window.READ_BOOKS=window.READ_BOOKS||{};window.READ_BOOKS["madame-bovary"]={"id":"madame-bovary","title":"Madame Bovary","titleZh":"包法利夫人","author":"Gustave Flaubert","translatorEn":"Eleanor Marx-Aveling","translatorZh":"李健吾","sourceEn":"Project Gutenberg #2413","hasZh":true,"chapters":[{"id":"1-1","part":1,"n":1,"title":"Part I · Chapter 1","titleZh":"上卷 · 1","paragraphs":[{"en":"We were in class when the head-master came in, followed by a “new fellow,” not wearing the school uniform, and a school servant carrying a large desk. Those who had been asleep woke up, and every one rose as if just surprised at his work.","sentences":[{"en":"We were in class when the head-master came in, followed by a “new fellow,” not wearing the school uniform, and a school servant carrying a large desk.","zh":"我们正上自习，校长进来了，后面跟着一个没有穿制服的新生和一个端着一张大书桌的校工。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Those who had been asleep woke up, and every one rose as if just surprised at his work.","zh":"正在睡觉的学生惊醒了，个个起立，像是用功被打断了的样子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The head-master made a sign to us to sit down. Then, turning to the class-master, he said to him in a low voice—","sentences":[{"en":"The head-master made a sign to us to sit down.","zh":"校长做手势叫我们坐下，然后转向班主任，对他低声道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, turning to the class-master, he said to him in a low voice—","zh":"校长做手势叫我们坐下，然后转向班主任，对他低声道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Monsieur Roger, here is a pupil whom I recommend to your care; he’ll be in the second. If his work and conduct are satisfactory, he will go into one of the upper classes, as becomes his age.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Monsieur Roger, here is a pupil whom I recommend to your care; he’ll be in the second.","zh":"“罗杰先生，我交给你一个学生，进五年级 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If his work and conduct are satisfactory, he will go into one of the upper classes, as becomes his age.”","zh":"学习和操行要是好的话，就按照年龄，把他升到高年级好了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The “new fellow,” standing in the corner behind the door so that he could hardly be seen, was a country lad of about fifteen, and taller than any of us. His hair was cut square on his forehead like a village chorister’s; he looked reliable, but very ill at ease. Although he was not broad-shouldered, his short school jacket of green cloth with black buttons must have been tight about the arm-holes, and showed at the opening of the cuffs red wrists accustomed to being bare. His legs, in blue stockings, looked out from beneath yellow trousers, drawn tight by braces, He wore stout, ill-cleaned, hob-nailed boots.","sentences":[{"en":"The “new fellow,” standing in the corner behind the door so that he could hardly be seen, was a country lad of about fifteen, and taller than any of us.","zh":"新生站在门后墙角，大家几乎看不见他。他是一个乡下孩子，十五岁光景，个子比我们哪一个人都高。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His hair was cut square on his forehead like a village chorister’s; he looked reliable, but very ill at ease.","zh":"他的神情又老实又拘谨。头发剪成平头，像教堂唱诗班的孩子那样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Although he was not broad-shouldered, his short school jacket of green cloth with black buttons must have been tight about the arm-holes, and showed at the opening of the cuffs red wrists accustomed to being bare.","zh":"肩膀不算宽，可是他的黑纽扣绿呢小外衣，台肩一定嫌紧，硬袖的袖口露出裸惯的红腕子。背带抽高了浅黄裤子，穿蓝袜的小腿露在外头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His legs, in blue stockings, looked out from beneath yellow trousers, drawn tight by braces, He wore stout, ill-cleaned, hob-nailed boots.","zh":"他穿一双鞋油没有怎么擦好的结实皮鞋，鞋底打钉子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"We began repeating the lesson. He listened with all his ears, as attentive as if at a sermon, not daring even to cross his legs or lean on his elbow; and when at two o’clock the bell rang, the master was obliged to tell him to fall into line with the rest of us.","sentences":[{"en":"We began repeating the lesson.","zh":"大家开始背书。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He listened with all his ears, as attentive as if at a sermon, not daring even to cross his legs or lean on his elbow; and when at two o’clock the bell rang, the master was obliged to tell him to fall into line with the rest of us.","zh":"他聚精会神，像听布道一样用心，连腿也不敢跷起来，胳膊肘也不敢支起来，两点钟的时候，下课钟响了，班主任要他和我们一道排队，不得不提醒他一声。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When we came back to work, we were in the habit of throwing our caps on the ground so as to have our hands more free; we used from the door to toss them under the form, so that they hit against the wall and made a lot of dust: it was “the thing.”","sentences":[{"en":"When we came back to work, we were in the habit of throwing our caps on the ground so as to have our hands more free; we used from the door to toss them under the form, so that they hit against the wall and made a lot of dust: it was “the thing.”","zh":"我们平时有一个习惯，一进教室，就拿制帽扔在地上，腾空了手好做功课；必须一到门槛，就拿制帽往凳子底下扔，还要恰好碰着墙，扬起一片尘土；这是规矩。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But, whether he had not noticed the trick, or did not dare to attempt it, the “new fellow,” was still holding his cap on his knees even after prayers were over. It was one of those head-gears of composite order, in which we can find traces of the bearskin, shako, billycock hat, sealskin cap, and cotton night-cap; one of those poor things, in fine, whose dumb ugliness has depths of expression, like an imbecile’s face. Oval, stiffened with whalebone, it began with three round knobs; then came in succession lozenges of velvet and rabbit-skin separated by a red band; after that a sort of bag that ended in a cardboard polygon covered with complicated braiding, from which hung, at the end of a long thin cord, small twisted gold threads in the manner of a tassel. The cap was new; its peak shone.","sentences":[{"en":"But, whether he had not noticed the trick, or did not dare to attempt it, the “new fellow,” was still holding his cap on his knees even after prayers were over.","zh":"可不知道他是没有注意这种做法，还是不敢照着做，祷告完了，新生还拿他的鸭舌帽放在他的两个膝盖上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was one of those head-gears of composite order, in which we can find traces of the bearskin, shako, billycock hat, sealskin cap, and cotton night-cap; one of those poor things, in fine, whose dumb ugliness has depths of expression, like an imbecile’s face.","zh":"这是一种混合式帽子 ，兼有熊皮帽、骑兵盔、圆筒帽、水獭鸭舌帽和睡帽的成分，总而言之，是一种不三不四的寒碜东西，它那不声不响的丑样子，活像一张表情莫名其妙的傻子的脸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oval, stiffened with whalebone, it began with three round knobs; then came in succession lozenges of velvet and rabbit-skin separated by a red band; after that a sort of bag that ended in a cardboard polygon covered with complicated braiding, from which hung, at the end of a long thin cord, small twisted gold threads in the manner of a tassel.","zh":"帽子外貌像鸡蛋，里面用鲸鱼骨支开了，帽口有三道粗圆绲边；往上是交错的菱形丝绒和兔子皮，一条红带子在中间隔开；再往上，是口袋似的帽筒，和硬纸板剪成的多角形的帽顶；帽顶蒙着一幅图案复杂的彩绣，上面垂下一条过分细的长绳，末端系着一个金线结成十字形花纹的坠子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The cap was new; its peak shone.","zh":"崭新的帽子，帽檐闪闪发光。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Rise,” said the master.","sentences":[{"en":"“Rise,” said the master.","zh":"教员道：“站起来。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He stood up; his cap fell. The whole class began to laugh. He stooped to pick it up. A neighbor knocked it down again with his elbow; he picked it up once more.","sentences":[{"en":"He stood up; his cap fell.","zh":"他站起身：帽子掉下去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The whole class began to laugh.","zh":"全班人笑了起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He stooped to pick it up.","zh":"他弯下腰去拾帽子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A neighbor knocked it down again with his elbow; he picked it up once more.","zh":"旁边一个学生一胳膊肘把它捅了下去；他又拾了一回。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Get rid of your helmet,” said the master, who was a bit of a wag.","sentences":[{"en":"“Get rid of your helmet,” said the master, who was a bit of a wag.","zh":"教员是一个风趣的人，就说：“拿开你的战盔吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"There was a burst of laughter from the boys, which so thoroughly put the poor lad out of countenance that he did not know whether to keep his cap in his hand, leave it on the ground, or put it on his head. He sat down again and placed it on his knee.","sentences":[{"en":"There was a burst of laughter from the boys, which so thoroughly put the poor lad out of countenance that he did not know whether to keep his cap in his hand, leave it on the ground, or put it on his head.","zh":"学生哄堂大笑，可怜的孩子大窘特窘，不知道应该拿着他的鸭舌帽好，还是放在地上好，或是戴在头上好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sat down again and placed it on his knee.","zh":"他又坐下，把它放在膝盖上。教员继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Rise,” repeated the master, “and tell me your name.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Rise,” repeated the master, “and tell me your name.”","zh":"“站起来，告诉我你叫什么名字。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The new boy articulated in a stammering voice an unintelligible name.","sentences":[{"en":"The new boy articulated in a stammering voice an unintelligible name.","zh":"新生叽里咕噜，说了一个听不清楚的名字。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Again!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Again!”","zh":"“再说一遍！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The same sputtering of syllables was heard, drowned by the tittering of the class.","sentences":[{"en":"The same sputtering of syllables was heard, drowned by the tittering of the class.","zh":"全班哗笑，照样听不出他叽里咕噜说的是什么字母。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Louder!” cried the master; “louder!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Louder!” cried the master; “louder!”","zh":"先生喊道：“大声说！大声！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The “new fellow” then took a supreme resolution, opened an inordinately large mouth, and shouted at the top of his voice as if calling someone in the word “Charbovari.”","sentences":[{"en":"The “new fellow” then took a supreme resolution, opened an inordinately large mouth, and shouted at the top of his voice as if calling someone in the word “Charbovari.”","zh":"于是新生下了最大的决心，张开大口，像喊什么人似的，扯嗓子嚷着这几个字：“查包法芮。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A hubbub broke out, rose in crescendo with bursts of shrill voices (they yelled, barked, stamped, repeated “Charbovari! Charbovari”), then died away into single notes, growing quieter only with great difficulty, and now and again suddenly recommencing along the line of a form whence rose here and there, like a damp cracker going off, a stifled laugh.","sentences":[{"en":"A hubbub broke out, rose in crescendo with bursts of shrill voices (they yelled, barked, stamped, repeated “Charbovari!","zh":"只听轰的一声，乱哄哄响成一片，渐强音 夹着尖叫（有人号，有人吠，有人跺脚，有人重复：“查包法芮！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charbovari”), then died away into single notes, growing quieter only with great difficulty, and now and again suddenly recommencing along the line of a form whence rose here and there, like a damp cracker going off, a stifled laugh.","zh":"查包法芮！”），跟着又变成零星音符，好不容易才静了下来。笑声是堵回去了，可有时候还沿着一排板凳，好像爆竹没有灭净一样，又东一声，西一声，响了起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"However, amid a rain of impositions, order was gradually re-established in the class; and the master having succeeded in catching the name of “Charles Bovary,” having had it dictated to him, spelt out, and re-read, at once ordered the poor devil to go and sit down on the punishment form at the foot of the master’s desk. He got up, but before going hesitated.","sentences":[{"en":"However, amid a rain of impositions, order was gradually re-established in the class; and the master having succeeded in catching the name of “Charles Bovary,” having had it dictated to him, spelt out, and re-read, at once ordered the poor devil to go and sit down on the punishment form at the foot of the master’s desk.","zh":"不过由于大罚功课，教室秩序逐渐恢复了；教员最后听出查理·包法利这个名字 ，经过默写、拼音、再读之后，立刻罚这可怜虫坐到讲桌底下的懒板凳。他立直了，可是行走以前，又逡巡起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He got up, but before going hesitated.","zh":"教员问道：“你找什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What are you looking for?” asked the master.","sentences":[{"en":"“What are you looking for?” asked the master.","zh":"新生向四围左张张，右张张，怯生生道：“我的鸭…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My c-a-p,” timidly said the “new fellow,” casting troubled looks round him.","sentences":[{"en":"“My c-a-p,” timidly said the “new fellow,” casting troubled looks round him.","zh":"“全班罚抄五百行诗！”一声怒吼，就像Quos ego 一样，止住新起的飓风。“不许闹！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Five hundred lines for all the class!” shouted in a furious voice stopped, like the Quos ego, a fresh outburst. “Silence!” continued the master indignantly, wiping his brow with his handkerchief, which he had just taken from his cap. “As to you, ‘new boy,’ you will conjugate ‘ridiculus sum’ twenty times.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Five hundred lines for all the class!” shouted in a furious voice stopped, like the Quos ego, a fresh outburst.","zh":"教员从瓜皮帽底下掏出手绢，一边擦额头的汗，一边气冲冲接下去道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Silence!” continued the master indignantly, wiping his brow with his handkerchief, which he had just taken from his cap.","zh":"“至于你，新生，罚你给我抄二十遍动词ridiculus sum 。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“As to you, ‘new boy,’ you will conjugate ‘ridiculus sum’ twenty times.”","zh":"然后声音变柔和一些：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, in a gentler tone, “Come, you’ll find your cap again; it hasn’t been stolen.”","sentences":[{"en":"Then, in a gentler tone, “Come, you’ll find your cap again; it hasn’t been stolen.”","zh":"“哎！你的鸭舌帽，你回头会找到的；没有人偷你的！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Quiet was restored. Heads bent over desks, and the “new fellow” remained for two hours in an exemplary attitude, although from time to time some paper pellet flipped from the tip of a pen came bang in his face. But he wiped his face with one hand and continued motionless, his eyes lowered.","sentences":[{"en":"Quiet was restored.","zh":"大伙又安静下来，头俯在笔记本上。新生端端正正坐了两小时，尽管不时有笔尖弹出的小纸球，飞来打他的脸，可是他擦擦脸，也就算了，低下眼睛，一动不动待到下课。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Heads bent over desks, and the “new fellow” remained for two hours in an exemplary attitude, although from time to time some paper pellet flipped from the tip of a pen came bang in his face.","zh":"大伙又安静下来，头俯在笔记本上。新生端端正正坐了两小时，尽管不时有笔尖弹出的小纸球，飞来打他的脸，可是他擦擦脸，也就算了，低下眼睛，一动不动待到下课。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But he wiped his face with one hand and continued motionless, his eyes lowered.","zh":"大伙又安静下来，头俯在笔记本上。新生端端正正坐了两小时，尽管不时有笔尖弹出的小纸球，飞来打他的脸，可是他擦擦脸，也就算了，低下眼睛，一动不动待到下课。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"In the evening, at preparation, he pulled out his pens from his desk, arranged his small belongings, and carefully ruled his paper. We saw him working conscientiously, looking up every word in the dictionary, and taking the greatest pains. Thanks, no doubt, to the willingness he showed, he had not to go down to the class below. But though he knew his rules passably, he had little finish in composition. It was the cure of his village who had taught him his first Latin; his parents, from motives of economy, having sent him to school as late as possible.","sentences":[{"en":"In the evening, at preparation, he pulled out his pens from his desk, arranged his small belongings, and carefully ruled his paper.","zh":"夜晚他在自习室，从书桌里取出他的套袖，把东西理齐，小心翼翼，拿尺在纸上打线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We saw him working conscientiously, looking up every word in the dictionary, and taking the greatest pains.","zh":"我们看见他学习认真，个个字查字典，很是辛苦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thanks, no doubt, to the willingness he showed, he had not to go down to the class below.","zh":"不用说，他就仗着这种坚强意志才不降班；因为他即使勉强懂了文法，造句并不高明。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But though he knew his rules passably, he had little finish in composition.","zh":"不用说，他就仗着这种坚强意志才不降班；因为他即使勉强懂了文法，造句并不高明。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was the cure of his village who had taught him his first Latin; his parents, from motives of economy, having sent him to school as late as possible.","zh":"他的拉丁文是本村堂长开的蒙，父母图省钱，尽迟送他上中学。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His father, Monsieur Charles Denis Bartolome Bovary, retired assistant-surgeon-major, compromised about 1812 in certain conscription scandals, and forced at this time to leave the service, had taken advantage of his fine figure to get hold of a dowry of sixty thousand francs that offered in the person of a hosier’s daughter who had fallen in love with his good looks. A fine man, a great talker, making his spurs ring as he walked, wearing whiskers that ran into his moustache, his fingers always garnished with rings and dressed in loud colours, he had the dash of a military man with the easy go of a commercial traveller.","sentences":[{"en":"His father, Monsieur Charles Denis Bartolome Bovary, retired assistant-surgeon-major, compromised about 1812 in certain conscription scandals, and forced at this time to leave the service, had taken advantage of his fine figure to get hold of a dowry of sixty thousand francs that offered in the person of a hosier’s daughter who had fallen in love with his good looks.","zh":"他的父亲查理·德尼·巴尔托洛梅·包法利先生，原来当军医副，一八一二年左右，在征兵事件上受了牵连，被迫在这期间离职，当时就利用他的长相漂亮，顺手牵羊，捞了六万法郎一笔嫁资：一个帽商姑娘爱上他的仪表，给他带过来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A fine man, a great talker, making his spurs ring as he walked, wearing whiskers that ran into his moustache, his fingers always garnished with rings and dressed in loud colours, he had the dash of a military man with the easy go of a commercial traveller.","zh":"美男子，说大话，好让他的刺马距发响声，络腮胡须连髭 ，手指总戴戒指，衣服要颜色鲜艳，外貌倒像一个勇士，说笑的兴致却像一个跑外的经纪人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Once married, he lived for three or four years on his wife’s fortune, dining well, rising late, smoking long porcelain pipes, not coming in at night till after the theatre, and haunting cafes. The father-in-law died, leaving little; he was indignant at this, “went in for the business,” lost some money in it, then retired to the country, where he thought he would make money.","sentences":[{"en":"Once married, he lived for three or four years on his wife’s fortune, dining well, rising late, smoking long porcelain pipes, not coming in at night till after the theatre, and haunting cafes.","zh":"结婚头两三年，他靠太太的财产过活，吃得好，起得迟，用大瓷烟斗吸烟，夜晚看过戏才回家，常到咖啡馆走动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The father-in-law died, leaving little; he was indignant at this, “went in for the business,” lost some money in it, then retired to the country, where he thought he would make money.","zh":"岳父死了，几乎没有留下什么来；他生了气，兴办实业，赔了些钱，随后退居乡野，想靠土地生利。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But, as he knew no more about farming than calico, as he rode his horses instead of sending them to plough, drank his cider in bottle instead of selling it in cask, ate the finest poultry in his farmyard, and greased his hunting-boots with the fat of his pigs, he was not long in finding out that he would do better to give up all speculation.","sentences":[{"en":"But, as he knew no more about farming than calico, as he rode his horses instead of sending them to plough, drank his cider in bottle instead of selling it in cask, ate the finest poultry in his farmyard, and greased his hunting-boots with the fat of his pigs, he was not long in finding out that he would do better to give up all speculation.","zh":"可是他不懂种田，正如不懂织布一样，他骑他的马，并不打发它们耕地，一瓶一瓶喝光他的苹果酒，并不一桶一桶卖掉，吃光院里最好的家禽，用猪油擦亮他的猎鞋，不久他看出来，顶好还是放弃一切投机。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For two hundred francs a year he managed to live on the border of the provinces of Caux and Picardy, in a kind of place half farm, half private house; and here, soured, eaten up with regrets, cursing his luck, jealous of everyone, he shut himself up at the age of forty-five, sick of men, he said, and determined to live at peace.","sentences":[{"en":"For two hundred francs a year he managed to live on the border of the provinces of Caux and Picardy, in a kind of place half farm, half private house; and here, soured, eaten up with regrets, cursing his luck, jealous of everyone, he shut himself up at the age of forty-five, sick of men, he said, and determined to live at peace.","zh":"所以他一年出两百法郎，在科 和庇卡底交界地方一个村子设法租了一所半田庄半住宅的房子；他从四十五岁起就闷闷不乐，懊恼万分，怪罪上天，妒忌每一个人，闭门不出，说是厌恶尘寰，决意不问世事。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His wife had adored him once on a time; she had bored him with a thousand servilities that had only estranged him the more. Lively once, expansive and affectionate, in growing older she had become (after the fashion of wine that, exposed to air, turns to vinegar) ill-tempered, grumbling, irritable. She had suffered so much without complaint at first, until she had seem him going after all the village drabs, and until a score of bad houses sent him back to her at night, weary, stinking drunk. Then her pride revolted. After that she was silent, burying her anger in a dumb stoicism that she maintained till her death. She was constantly going about looking after business matters. She called on the lawyers, the president, remembered when bills fell due, got them renewed, and at home ironed, sewed, washed, looked after the workmen, paid the accounts, while he, troubling himself about nothing, eternally besotted in sleepy sulkiness, whence he only roused himself to say disagreeable things to her, sat smoking by the fire and spitting into the cinders.","sentences":[{"en":"His wife had adored him once on a time; she had bored him with a thousand servilities that had only estranged him the more.","zh":"他的女人从前迷他，倾心相爱，百依百顺，结果他倒生了外心。早年她有说有笑，无话不谈，一心相与，上了岁数，性子就变得（好像酒走气，变成酸的一样）别别扭扭，嘁嘁喳喳，急急躁躁的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Lively once, expansive and affectionate, in growing older she had become (after the fashion of wine that, exposed to air, turns to vinegar) ill-tempered, grumbling, irritable.","zh":"他的女人从前迷他，倾心相爱，百依百顺，结果他倒生了外心。早年她有说有笑，无话不谈，一心相与，上了岁数，性子就变得（好像酒走气，变成酸的一样）别别扭扭，嘁嘁喳喳，急急躁躁的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She had suffered so much without complaint at first, until she had seem him going after all the village drabs, and until a score of bad houses sent him back to her at night, weary, stinking drunk.","zh":"她看见他追逐村里个个浪荡女人，夜晚不省人事，酒气冲天，多少下流地方叫人把他送回家来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then her pride revolted.","zh":"她受尽辛苦，起初并不抱怨，后来自尊心怎么也耐不下去了，索性不言语，忍气吞声，一直到死。","scope":"group"},{"en":"After that she was silent, burying her anger in a dumb stoicism that she maintained till her death.","zh":"她受尽辛苦，起初并不抱怨，后来自尊心怎么也耐不下去了，索性不言语，忍气吞声，一直到死。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was constantly going about looking after business matters.","zh":"她奔波、忙碌，一刻不停。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She called on the lawyers, the president, remembered when bills fell due, got them renewed, and at home ironed, sewed, washed, looked after the workmen, paid the accounts, while he, troubling himself about nothing, eternally besotted in sleepy sulkiness, whence he only roused himself to say disagreeable things to her, sat smoking by the fire and spitting into the cinders.","zh":"想起期票到期，她去见律师，见庭长，办理了缓期支付；在家里又是缝缝补补、洗洗熨熨，又是监督工人、开发工钱，而老爷无所事事，始终负气似的，昏天黑地挺尸，醒转来只对她说些无情无义的话，在炉火角落吸烟，往灰烬里吐痰。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When she had a child, it had to be sent out to nurse. When he came home, the lad was spoilt as if he were a prince. His mother stuffed him with jam; his father let him run about barefoot, and, playing the philosopher, even said he might as well go about quite naked like the young of animals. As opposed to the maternal ideas, he had a certain virile idea of childhood on which he sought to mould his son, wishing him to be brought up hardily, like a Spartan, to give him a strong constitution. He sent him to bed without any fire, taught him to drink off large draughts of rum and to jeer at religious processions. But, peaceable by nature, the lad answered only poorly to his notions. His mother always kept him near her; she cut out cardboard for him, told him tales, entertained him with endless monologues full of melancholy gaiety and charming nonsense. In her life’s isolation she centered on the child’s head all her shattered, broken little vanities. She dreamed of high station; she already saw him, tall, handsome, clever, settled as an engineer or in the law. She taught him to read, and even, on an old piano, she had taught him two or three little songs. But to all this Monsieur Bovary, caring little for letters, said, “It was not worth while. Would they ever have the means to send him to a public school, to buy him a practice, or start him in business? Besides, with cheek a man always gets on in the world.” Madame Bovary bit her lips, and the child knocked about the village.","sentences":[{"en":"When she had a child, it had to be sent out to nurse.","zh":"她生了一个男孩，必须交给别人乳养。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he came home, the lad was spoilt as if he were a prince.","zh":"小把戏回到家，惯得活像一个王子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His mother stuffed him with jam; his father let him run about barefoot, and, playing the philosopher, even said he might as well go about quite naked like the young of animals.","zh":"母亲喂他蜜饯；父亲叫他打赤脚，甚至冒充哲学家，说他可以学学幼畜，全身光着走路。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As opposed to the maternal ideas, he had a certain virile idea of childhood on which he sought to mould his son, wishing him to be brought up hardily, like a Spartan, to give him a strong constitution.","zh":"他对教育儿童有一种男性理想，所以排斥母亲的影响，试着按照这种理想训练，用斯巴达方式，从严管教。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sent him to bed without any fire, taught him to drink off large draughts of rum and to jeer at religious processions.","zh":"他打发他睡觉不生火，教他大口喝甘蔗酒和侮辱教堂行列。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But, peaceable by nature, the lad answered only poorly to his notions.","zh":"可是小孩子天性驯良，辜负了他的心力。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His mother always kept him near her; she cut out cardboard for him, told him tales, entertained him with endless monologues full of melancholy gaiety and charming nonsense.","zh":"母亲总把他拖在身边，帮他剪裁硬纸板，给他讲故事，喋喋不休，一个人和他谈古道今，充满了忧郁的欢乐和闲话三七的甜蜜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In her life’s isolation she centered on the child’s head all her shattered, broken little vanities.","zh":"日子过得孤零零的，好胜心支离破碎，她把希望统统集中在这孩子身上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She dreamed of high station; she already saw him, tall, handsome, clever, settled as an engineer or in the law.","zh":"她梦想高官厚禄，看见他已经长大成人，漂亮，有才情，成了土木工程师或者法官。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She taught him to read, and even, on an old piano, she had taught him two or three little songs.","zh":"她教他读书，甚至弹着她的一架旧钢琴，教他唱两三支小恋歌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But to all this Monsieur Bovary, caring little for letters, said, “It was not worth while.","zh":"可是包法利先生不重视文学，见她这样做，就说：“不值得！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Would they ever have the means to send him to a public school, to buy him a practice, or start him in business?","zh":"难道他们有钱让他上公立学校，给他顶进一个事务所 或者盘进一家店面？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, with cheek a man always gets on in the world.”","zh":"再说，“一个人只要脸皮厚，总会得意的”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Bovary bit her lips, and the child knocked about the village.","zh":"包法利夫人咬住了嘴唇，孩子在村里流浪着。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He went after the labourers, drove away with clods of earth the ravens that were flying about. He ate blackberries along the hedges, minded the geese with a long switch, went haymaking during harvest, ran about in the woods, played hop-scotch under the church porch on rainy days, and at great fetes begged the beadle to let him toll the bells, that he might hang all his weight on the long rope and feel himself borne upward by it in its swing. Meanwhile he grew like an oak; he was strong on hand, fresh of colour.","sentences":[{"en":"He went after the labourers, drove away with clods of earth the ravens that were flying about.","zh":"他跟在农夫后头，拾起碎土块，赶走飞来飞去的乌鸦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He ate blackberries along the hedges, minded the geese with a long switch, went haymaking during harvest, ran about in the woods, played hop-scotch under the church porch on rainy days, and at great fetes begged the beadle to let him toll the bells, that he might hang all his weight on the long rope and feel himself borne upward by it in its swing.","zh":"他吃沿沟的桑椹，拿一根竿子看守火鸡，收成期间翻谷子，在树林里跑来跑去，雨天在教堂门廊玩造房子，遇到盛大节日，就央求教堂听差让他敲钟，为的是整个身子吊住粗绳，上下来回摆动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Meanwhile he grew like an oak; he was strong on hand, fresh of colour.","zh":"所以他长得如同一棵橡树，手臂结实，肤色健康。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When he was twelve years old his mother had her own way; he began lessons. The curé took him in hand; but the lessons were so short and irregular that they could not be of much use. They were given at spare moments in the sacristy, standing up, hurriedly, between a baptism and a burial; or else the curé, if he had not to go out, sent for his pupil after the Angelus. They went up to his room and settled down; the flies and moths fluttered round the candle. It was close, the child fell asleep, and the good man, beginning to doze with his hands on his stomach, was soon snoring with his mouth wide open. On other occasions, when Monsieur le Curé, on his way back after administering the viaticum to some sick person in the neighbourhood, caught sight of Charles playing about the fields, he called him, lectured him for a quarter of an hour and took advantage of the occasion to make him conjugate his verb at the foot of a tree. The rain interrupted them or an acquaintance passed. All the same he was always pleased with him, and even said the “young man” had a very good memory.","sentences":[{"en":"When he was twelve years old his mother had her own way; he began lessons.","zh":"十二岁上，母亲给他争到开蒙，请教堂堂长教。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The curé took him in hand; but the lessons were so short and irregular that they could not be of much use.","zh":"可是上课的时间又短，又不固定，不起什么作用。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were given at spare moments in the sacristy, standing up, hurriedly, between a baptism and a burial; or else the curé, if he had not to go out, sent for his pupil after the Angelus.","zh":"功课不是忙里偷闲，站在圣衣室，匆匆忙忙，赶着行洗礼和出殡之间教，就是在做晚祷以后，堂长不出门，叫人把学生找过来教。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They went up to his room and settled down; the flies and moths fluttered round the candle.","zh":"他们上楼，到他的房间坐下；蚊子和蛾子兜着蜡烛飞翔。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was close, the child fell asleep, and the good man, beginning to doze with his hands on his stomach, was soon snoring with his mouth wide open.","zh":"天气热，孩子睡着了；老头子手搭在肚子上，昏昏沉沉，跟着也就张开嘴，打起鼾来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On other occasions, when Monsieur le Curé, on his way back after administering the viaticum to some sick person in the neighbourhood, caught sight of Charles playing about the fields, he called him, lectured him for a quarter of an hour and took advantage of the occasion to make him conjugate his verb at the foot of a tree.","zh":"有时候，堂长给邻近病人做临终圣事回来，望见查理在田里撒野，喊住他，开导他一刻钟，利用机会，叫他在树底下变化动词。落雨了，或者过来一位熟人，打断他们。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The rain interrupted them or an acquaintance passed.","zh":"有时候，堂长给邻近病人做临终圣事回来，望见查理在田里撒野，喊住他，开导他一刻钟，利用机会，叫他在树底下变化动词。落雨了，或者过来一位熟人，打断他们。","scope":"group"},{"en":"All the same he was always pleased with him, and even said the “young man” had a very good memory.","zh":"其实他一直对他满意，甚至说：年轻人记性很好。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles could not go on like this. Madame Bovary took strong steps. Ashamed, or rather tired out, Monsieur Bovary gave in without a struggle, and they waited one year longer, so that the lad should take his first communion.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles could not go on like this.","zh":"不能让查理这样下去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Bovary took strong steps.","zh":"太太下了决心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ashamed, or rather tired out, Monsieur Bovary gave in without a struggle, and they waited one year longer, so that the lad should take his first communion.","zh":"老爷惭愧了，或者不如说是疲倦了，不抗拒就让了步。他们又拖了一年，等孩子行过他的第一次圣体瞻礼。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Six months more passed, and the year after Charles was finally sent to school at Rouen, where his father took him towards the end of October, at the time of the St. Romain fair.","sentences":[{"en":"Six months more passed, and the year after Charles was finally sent to school at Rouen, where his father took him towards the end of October, at the time of the St. Romain fair.","zh":"一晃又是半年，第二年才决定把查理送进鲁昂的中学。约莫十月末，赶在圣罗曼节集市期间 ，父亲自己带他来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It would now be impossible for any of us to remember anything about him. He was a youth of even temperament, who played in playtime, worked in school-hours, was attentive in class, slept well in the dormitory, and ate well in the refectory. He had in loco parentis a wholesale ironmonger in the Rue Ganterie, who took him out once a month on Sundays after his shop was shut, sent him for a walk on the quay to look at the boats, and then brought him back to college at seven o’clock before supper. Every Thursday evening he wrote a long letter to his mother with red ink and three wafers; then he went over his history note-books, or read an old volume of “Anarchasis” that was knocking about the study. When he went for walks he talked to the servant, who, like himself, came from the country.","sentences":[{"en":"It would now be impossible for any of us to remember anything about him.","zh":"我们现在没有一个人能想起他当时的情形。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was a youth of even temperament, who played in playtime, worked in school-hours, was attentive in class, slept well in the dormitory, and ate well in the refectory.","zh":"他是一个性情温和的男孩子，游戏时间玩耍，自习时间用功，在教室听讲，在寝室睡得好，在饭厅吃得好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had in loco parentis a wholesale ironmonger in the Rue Ganterie, who took him out once a month on Sundays after his shop was shut, sent him for a walk on the quay to look at the boats, and then brought him back to college at seven o’clock before supper.","zh":"他的保证人是手套街一位铜铁器皿批发商，星期天铺子不做生意，每月一次，把他接出来，打发到码头散散步，看看船，然后一到七点，晚饭之前，送回学校。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Every Thursday evening he wrote a long letter to his mother with red ink and three wafers; then he went over his history note-books, or read an old volume of “Anarchasis” that was knocking about the study.","zh":"每星期四夜晚，他用红墨水给母亲写一封长信，拿三块小圆面团子封口；随后他就温习历史笔记，或者读一本扔在自习室的旧书《阿纳喀尔西斯》 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he went for walks he talked to the servant, who, like himself, came from the country.","zh":"散步中间，他和校工闲谈，校工像他一样，是乡下来的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"By dint of hard work he kept always about the middle of the class; once even he got a certificate in natural history. But at the end of his third year his parents withdrew him from the school to make him study medicine, convinced that he could even take his degree by himself.","sentences":[{"en":"By dint of hard work he kept always about the middle of the class; once even he got a certificate in natural history.","zh":"他靠死用功，在班上永远接近中等，也一直保持下来；甚至于有一次，他考博物，得到表扬。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But at the end of his third year his parents withdrew him from the school to make him study medicine, convinced that he could even take his degree by himself.","zh":"但是临到第三学年 末尾，父母叫他退学读医，深信他单靠自己，就会得到学位。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His mother chose a room for him on the fourth floor of a dyer’s she knew, overlooking the Eau-de-Robec. She made arrangements for his board, got him furniture, table and two chairs, sent home for an old cherry-tree bedstead, and bought besides a small cast-iron stove with the supply of wood that was to warm the poor child.","sentences":[{"en":"His mother chose a room for him on the fourth floor of a dyer’s she knew, overlooking the Eau-de-Robec.","zh":"母亲到罗拜克河附近相识的染匠家，给他在五楼挑了一间屋子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She made arrangements for his board, got him furniture, table and two chairs, sent home for an old cherry-tree bedstead, and bought besides a small cast-iron stove with the supply of wood that was to warm the poor child.","zh":"她讲定他的房饭钱，弄来几件木器：一张桌子，两把椅子，另外从家里运来一张樱桃木旧床，还买了一个小生铁炉子和一堆劈柴，为她可怜的孩子取暖用。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then at the end of a week she departed, after a thousand injunctions to be good now that he was going to be left to himself.","sentences":[{"en":"Then at the end of a week she departed, after a thousand injunctions to be good now that he was going to be left to himself.","zh":"随后她待了一星期，再三叮咛他正经做人，今后就只剩下他一个人了，这才回乡。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The syllabus that he read on the notice-board stunned him; lectures on anatomy, lectures on pathology, lectures on physiology, lectures on pharmacy, lectures on botany and clinical medicine, and therapeutics, without counting hygiene and materia medica—all names of whose etymologies he was ignorant, and that were to him as so many doors to sanctuaries filled with magnificent darkness.","sentences":[{"en":"The syllabus that he read on the notice-board stunned him; lectures on anatomy, lectures on pathology, lectures on physiology, lectures on pharmacy, lectures on botany and clinical medicine, and therapeutics, without counting hygiene and materia medica—all names of whose etymologies he was ignorant, and that were to him as so many doors to sanctuaries filled with magnificent darkness.","zh":"布告牌上的课程表，他一念，就觉得头昏脑涨；解剖学、病理学、生理学、药理学、化学、植物学、诊断学、治疗学，还不提卫生学、药材论，没有一个名词他晓得来源，一个一个全像庙门，里面庄严而又黑暗。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He understood nothing of it all; it was all very well to listen—he did not follow. Still he worked; he had bound note-books, he attended all the courses, never missed a single lecture. He did his little daily task like a mill-horse, who goes round and round with his eyes bandaged, not knowing what work he is doing.","sentences":[{"en":"He understood nothing of it all; it was all very well to listen—he did not follow.","zh":"他完全不懂；听也白听，他跟不上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Still he worked; he had bound note-books, he attended all the courses, never missed a single lecture.","zh":"可是他用功，他有成本的笔记。他每课必上，一次实习不缺。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He did his little daily task like a mill-horse, who goes round and round with his eyes bandaged, not knowing what work he is doing.","zh":"他干完一天的乏味工作，好像拉磨的马一样，两眼蒙住，兜着一个地方转，不知道磨了些什么。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To spare him expense his mother sent him every week by the carrier a piece of veal baked in the oven, with which he lunched when he came back from the hospital, while he sat kicking his feet against the wall. After this he had to run off to lectures, to the operation-room, to the hospital, and return to his home at the other end of the town. In the evening, after the poor dinner of his landlord, he went back to his room and set to work again in his wet clothes, which smoked as he sat in front of the hot stove.","sentences":[{"en":"To spare him expense his mother sent him every week by the carrier a piece of veal baked in the oven, with which he lunched when he came back from the hospital, while he sat kicking his feet against the wall.","zh":"母亲为他省钱，每星期托邮车给他带来一块灶火烤的小牛肉，他上午从医院回来，一边在墙上拍打鞋底，一边拿它就午饭吃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After this he had to run off to lectures, to the operation-room, to the hospital, and return to his home at the other end of the town.","zh":"用过午饭，他该朝教室、解剖室、救济院跑了，然后穿过一条又一条街，回到住所。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the evening, after the poor dinner of his landlord, he went back to his room and set to work again in his wet clothes, which smoked as he sat in front of the hot stove.","zh":"他用罢房东的菲薄晚饭，又上楼回到房间，埋头用功，他的湿衣服当着熊熊的炉火，直在身上冒气。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On the fine summer evenings, at the time when the close streets are empty, when the servants are playing shuttle-cock at the doors, he opened his window and leaned out. The river, that makes of this quarter of Rouen a wretched little Venice, flowed beneath him, between the bridges and the railings, yellow, violet, or blue. Working men, kneeling on the banks, washed their bare arms in the water. On poles projecting from the attics, skeins of cotton were drying in the air. Opposite, beyond the roots spread the pure heaven with the red sun setting. How pleasant it must be at home! How fresh under the beech-tree! And he expanded his nostrils to breathe in the sweet odours of the country which did not reach him.","sentences":[{"en":"On the fine summer evenings, at the time when the close streets are empty, when the servants are playing shuttle-cock at the doors, he opened his window and leaned out.","zh":"夏季黄昏美好，郁热的街巷空空落落，女用人在大门口踢毽子，他打开窗户，胳膊肘靠在上头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The river, that makes of this quarter of Rouen a wretched little Venice, flowed beneath him, between the bridges and the railings, yellow, violet, or blue.","zh":"小河 在他底下桥和栅栏之间流过，颜色发黄、发紫或者发蓝，把鲁昂这一区变成一个肮脏的小威尼斯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Working men, kneeling on the banks, washed their bare arms in the water.","zh":"有些工人，蹲在岸边，在水里洗胳膊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On poles projecting from the attics, skeins of cotton were drying in the air.","zh":"阁楼顶撑出去的竿子，晾着成把的棉线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Opposite, beyond the roots spread the pure heaven with the red sun setting.","zh":"从对面房顶望过去，一轮西沉的红日，衬着一片清澄的天空。","scope":"group"},{"en":"How pleasant it must be at home!","zh":"从对面房顶望过去，一轮西沉的红日，衬着一片清澄的天空。","scope":"group"},{"en":"How fresh under the beech-tree!","zh":"那边 该多好啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he expanded his nostrils to breathe in the sweet odours of the country which did not reach him.","zh":"山毛榉底下有多凉爽啊！他张开鼻孔去吸田野的清香味道，但是没有吸到。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He grew thin, his figure became taller, his face took a saddened look that made it nearly interesting. Naturally, through indifference, he abandoned all the resolutions he had made. Once he missed a lecture; the next day all the lectures; and, enjoying his idleness, little by little, he gave up work altogether. He got into the habit of going to the public-house, and had a passion for dominoes. To shut himself up every evening in the dirty public room, to push about on marble tables the small sheep bones with black dots, seemed to him a fine proof of his freedom, which raised him in his own esteem. It was beginning to see life, the sweetness of stolen pleasures; and when he entered, he put his hand on the door-handle with a joy almost sensual. Then many things hidden within him came out; he learnt couplets by heart and sang them to his boon companions, became enthusiastic about Beranger, learnt how to make punch, and, finally, how to make love.","sentences":[{"en":"He grew thin, his figure became taller, his face took a saddened look that made it nearly interesting.","zh":"他瘦了，个子长高了，脸上显出一种哀怨的表情，几乎能引起别人的几分兴趣。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Naturally, through indifference, he abandoned all the resolutions he had made.","zh":"自然而然，漫不经心地，他把早先下的决心统统丢到脑后。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once he missed a lecture; the next day all the lectures; and, enjoying his idleness, little by little, he gave up work altogether.","zh":"他有一次不实习，第二天不上课，尝出了偷懒的味道，索性渐渐不去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He got into the habit of going to the public-house, and had a passion for dominoes.","zh":"他养成坐酒馆的习惯，爱上了牙牌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To shut himself up every evening in the dirty public room, to push about on marble tables the small sheep bones with black dots, seemed to him a fine proof of his freedom, which raised him in his own esteem.","zh":"每天夜晚，钻进一家肮脏的赌窟，在大理石桌上，掷着有黑点的小羊骨头：他觉得这是他得到自由的一种珍贵凭据，提高他对自己的尊重。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was beginning to see life, the sweetness of stolen pleasures; and when he entered, he put his hand on the door-handle with a joy almost sensual.","zh":"这就像初入社会，初尝禁脔一样；他往里走，将手放在门的扶手上，心头兜起一种近乎肉感的喜悦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then many things hidden within him came out; he learnt couplets by heart and sang them to his boon companions, became enthusiastic about Beranger, learnt how to make punch, and, finally, how to make love.","zh":"于是心里许多被压抑的东西冒出来了：他学会几个小调，唱给女伴们听，迷上了贝朗瑞 ，能调五味酒，最后，懂得了爱情。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Thanks to these preparatory labours, he failed completely in his examination for an ordinary degree. He was expected home the same night to celebrate his success. He started on foot, stopped at the beginning of the village, sent for his mother, and told her all. She excused him, threw the blame of his failure on the injustice of the examiners, encouraged him a little, and took upon herself to set matters straight. It was only five years later that Monsieur Bovary knew the truth; it was old then, and he accepted it. Moreover, he could not believe that a man born of him could be a fool.","sentences":[{"en":"Thanks to these preparatory labours, he failed completely in his examination for an ordinary degree.","zh":"多亏这些准备工作，他的医生资格考试 完全失败。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was expected home the same night to celebrate his success.","zh":"当天黄昏，家里等他回来，庆贺他当上了医生！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He started on foot, stopped at the beginning of the village, sent for his mother, and told her all.","zh":"他一路走去，在村口停住，托人找母亲出来，一五一十，讲给她听。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She excused him, threw the blame of his failure on the injustice of the examiners, encouraged him a little, and took upon herself to set matters straight.","zh":"她原谅他，把失败推到主考人员身上，说他们不公道，勉励了他两句，负责安排一切。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was only five years later that Monsieur Bovary knew the truth; it was old then, and he accepted it.","zh":"五年以后，包法利先生才知道实情；过去的事，他也就由它去了，再说，他不能设想他生出来的孩子会是蠢材。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Moreover, he could not believe that a man born of him could be a fool.","zh":"五年以后，包法利先生才知道实情；过去的事，他也就由它去了，再说，他不能设想他生出来的孩子会是蠢材。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"So Charles set to work again and crammed for his examination, ceaselessly learning all the old questions by heart. He passed pretty well. What a happy day for his mother! They gave a grand dinner.","sentences":[{"en":"So Charles set to work again and crammed for his examination, ceaselessly learning all the old questions by heart.","zh":"于是查理埋头用功，坚持不懈，预备他的考试项目，事先记住全部问题。他录取了，分数相当高。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He passed pretty well.","zh":"这对他母亲来说，是一个了不起的大喜日子！","scope":"group"},{"en":"What a happy day for his mother!","zh":"这对他母亲来说，是一个了不起的大喜日子！","scope":"group"},{"en":"They gave a grand dinner.","zh":"他们大摆酒宴。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Where should he go to practice? To Tostes, where there was only one old doctor. For a long time Madame Bovary had been on the look-out for his death, and the old fellow had barely been packed off when Charles was installed, opposite his place, as his successor.","sentences":[{"en":"Where should he go to practice?","zh":"他到什么地方行医呢？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To Tostes, where there was only one old doctor.","zh":"道特 那边只有一个老医生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For a long time Madame Bovary had been on the look-out for his death, and the old fellow had barely been packed off when Charles was installed, opposite his place, as his successor.","zh":"许久以来，包法利夫人就盼着他死，老头子还没有卷铺盖，查理作为继承人，就在对面住下了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But it was not everything to have brought up a son, to have had him taught medicine, and discovered Tostes, where he could practice it; he must have a wife. She found him one—the widow of a bailiff at Dieppe—who was forty-five and had an income of twelve hundred francs. Though she was ugly, as dry as a bone, her face with as many pimples as the spring has buds, Madame Dubuc had no lack of suitors. To attain her ends Madame Bovary had to oust them all, and she even succeeded in very cleverly baffling the intrigues of a pork-butcher backed up by the priests.","sentences":[{"en":"But it was not everything to have brought up a son, to have had him taught medicine, and discovered Tostes, where he could practice it; he must have a wife.","zh":"但是把儿子教养成人，让他学医，帮他在道特挂牌行医，还不算完：他需要一位太太。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She found him one—the widow of a bailiff at Dieppe—who was forty-five and had an income of twelve hundred francs.","zh":"她给他找到一位：她是第厄普一个执达吏的寡妇，四十五岁，一年有一千二百法郎收入。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Though she was ugly, as dry as a bone, her face with as many pimples as the spring has buds, Madame Dubuc had no lack of suitors.","zh":"杜比克夫人尽管长得丑，像柴一样干，像春季发芽一样满脸疙瘩，可的确不缺人嫁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To attain her ends Madame Bovary had to oust them all, and she even succeeded in very cleverly baffling the intrigues of a pork-butcher backed up by the priests.","zh":"包法利太太为了达到目的，不得不一个一个挤掉，甚至于一个卖猪肉的，有教士们撑腰，她也想出办法，破坏了他的诡计。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles had seen in marriage the advent of an easier life, thinking he would be more free to do as he liked with himself and his money. But his wife was master; he had to say this and not say that in company, to fast every Friday, dress as she liked, harass at her bidding those patients who did not pay. She opened his letter, watched his comings and goings, and listened at the partition-wall when women came to consult him in his surgery.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles had seen in marriage the advent of an easier life, thinking he would be more free to do as he liked with himself and his money.","zh":"查理满以为结过婚，环境改善，他就自由了，身子可以自主，用钱可以随意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But his wife was master; he had to say this and not say that in company, to fast every Friday, dress as she liked, harass at her bidding those patients who did not pay.","zh":"然而当家做主的是他的太太；他在人面前，应该说这句话，不应该说那句话；每星期五吃素；顺她的心思穿衣服；照她的吩咐逼迫不付钱的病人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She opened his letter, watched his comings and goings, and listened at the partition-wall when women came to consult him in his surgery.","zh":"她拆他的信，窥伺他的行动，隔着板壁，听他在诊室给妇女看病。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She must have her chocolate every morning, attentions without end. She constantly complained of her nerves, her chest, her liver. The noise of footsteps made her ill; when people left her, solitude became odious to her; if they came back, it was doubtless to see her die. When Charles returned in the evening, she stretched forth two long thin arms from beneath the sheets, put them round his neck, and having made him sit down on the edge of the bed, began to talk to him of her troubles: he was neglecting her, he loved another. She had been warned she would be unhappy; and she ended by asking him for a dose of medicine and a little more love.","sentences":[{"en":"She must have her chocolate every morning, attentions without end.","zh":"她每天早晨要喝巧克力，要他一个劲儿疼她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She constantly complained of her nerves, her chest, her liver.","zh":"她不住口抱怨她的神经、她的肺、她的气血。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The noise of footsteps made her ill; when people left her, solitude became odious to her; if they came back, it was doubtless to see her die.","zh":"脚步声音刺激她；人走开了，她嫌寂寞；回到身旁，不用说，是为了看她死。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When Charles returned in the evening, she stretched forth two long thin arms from beneath the sheets, put them round his neck, and having made him sit down on the edge of the bed, began to talk to him of her troubles: he was neglecting her, he loved another.","zh":"查理夜晚回来，她从被窝底下伸出瘦长胳膊，搂住他的脖子，要他在床沿坐下，开始对他诉说她的苦恼：他忘掉了她，他爱别人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had been warned she would be unhappy; and she ended by asking him for a dose of medicine and a little more love.","zh":"人家先前同她讲过的，她会不幸的；说到最后，她为她的健康，向他要一点甜药水，再多来一点爱情。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"1-2","part":1,"n":2,"title":"Part I · Chapter 2","titleZh":"上卷 · 2","paragraphs":[{"en":"One night towards eleven o’clock they were awakened by the noise of a horse pulling up outside their door. The servant opened the garret-window and parleyed for some time with a man in the street below. He came for the doctor, had a letter for him. Natasie came downstairs shivering and undid the bars and bolts one after the other. The man left his horse, and, following the servant, suddenly came in behind her. He pulled out from his wool cap with grey top-knots a letter wrapped up in a rag and presented it gingerly to Charles, who rested on his elbow on the pillow to read it. Natasie, standing near the bed, held the light. Madame in modesty had turned to the wall and showed only her back.","sentences":[{"en":"One night towards eleven o’clock they were awakened by the noise of a horse pulling up outside their door.","zh":"一天夜晚，约莫十一点钟，来了一匹马，当门停住，响声吵醒他们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The servant opened the garret-window and parleyed for some time with a man in the street below.","zh":"女用人打开阁楼天窗，问明下面街上一个男子的来意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He came for the doctor, had a letter for him.","zh":"他带了一封信来请医生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Natasie came downstairs shivering and undid the bars and bolts one after the other.","zh":"娜丝塔西打着寒噤，走下楼梯，一道又一道，开锁，拔门闩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The man left his horse, and, following the servant, suddenly came in behind her.","zh":"来人下了马，跟着女用人，一直上来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He pulled out from his wool cap with grey top-knots a letter wrapped up in a rag and presented it gingerly to Charles, who rested on his elbow on the pillow to read it.","zh":"他从他的灰冠子毡帽，取出一封旧布包着的信，小心翼翼，呈上查理。查理拿胳膊肘支住枕头看信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Natasie, standing near the bed, held the light.","zh":"娜丝塔西在床边举着灯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame in modesty had turned to the wall and showed only her back.","zh":"太太害羞，脸转向墙，露出后背。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This letter, sealed with a small seal in blue wax, begged Monsieur Bovary to come immediately to the farm of the Bertaux to set a broken leg. Now from Tostes to the Bertaux was a good eighteen miles across country by way of Longueville and Saint-Victor. It was a dark night; Madame Bovary junior was afraid of accidents for her husband. So it was decided the stable-boy should go on first; Charles would start three hours later when the moon rose. A boy was to be sent to meet him, and show him the way to the farm, and open the gates for him.","sentences":[{"en":"This letter, sealed with a small seal in blue wax, begged Monsieur Bovary to come immediately to the farm of the Bertaux to set a broken leg.","zh":"这封信用一小块蓝漆封口，求包法利先生立刻就来拜尔托田庄，接一条断腿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now from Tostes to the Bertaux was a good eighteen miles across country by way of Longueville and Saint-Victor.","zh":"可是从道特到拜尔托，经过长镇和圣维克托，走小路也要十足六古里 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a dark night; Madame Bovary junior was afraid of accidents for her husband.","zh":"夜晚黑漆漆的，少奶奶担心丈夫遇到意外。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So it was decided the stable-boy should go on first; Charles would start three hours later when the moon rose.","zh":"所以决定，厩夫先打前站。查理等月亮上升，三小时后动身。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A boy was to be sent to meet him, and show him the way to the farm, and open the gates for him.","zh":"那边派一个小孩子迎他，帮他指点田庄道路，开栅栏门。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Towards four o’clock in the morning, Charles, well wrapped up in his cloak, set out for the Bertaux. Still sleepy from the warmth of his bed, he let himself be lulled by the quiet trot of his horse. When it stopped of its own accord in front of those holes surrounded with thorns that are dug on the margin of furrows, Charles awoke with a start, suddenly remembered the broken leg, and tried to call to mind all the fractures he knew. The rain had stopped, day was breaking, and on the branches of the leafless trees birds roosted motionless, their little feathers bristling in the cold morning wind. The flat country stretched as far as eye could see, and the tufts of trees round the farms at long intervals seemed like dark violet stains on the cast grey surface, that on the horizon faded into the gloom of the sky.","sentences":[{"en":"Towards four o’clock in the morning, Charles, well wrapped up in his cloak, set out for the Bertaux.","zh":"早晨四点钟左右，查理披好斗篷，向拜尔托出发。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Still sleepy from the warmth of his bed, he let himself be lulled by the quiet trot of his horse.","zh":"人刚离开暖被窝，还迷迷糊糊的，由着牲口的安详脚步，颠上颠下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When it stopped of its own accord in front of those holes surrounded with thorns that are dug on the margin of furrows, Charles awoke with a start, suddenly remembered the broken leg, and tried to call to mind all the fractures he knew.","zh":"靠近田垄处，掘了一些荆棘围着的窟窿，马走到跟前不走了，查理身子一耸，惊醒过来，立时想起断腿，试着回忆他知道的种种接骨方法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The rain had stopped, day was breaking, and on the branches of the leafless trees birds roosted motionless, their little feathers bristling in the cold morning wind.","zh":"雨已经不下了；天开始发亮，有些鸟动也不动，栖在苹果树的枯枝上，晨风料峭中，敛起它们小小的羽毛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The flat country stretched as far as eye could see, and the tufts of trees round the farms at long intervals seemed like dark violet stains on the cast grey surface, that on the horizon faded into the gloom of the sky.","zh":"平原展开，一望无际。田庄周围，一丛一丛树木远远隔开，在这灰灰的广大地面，形成若干黑紫点子。地面在天边没入天的阴暗色调。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles from time to time opened his eyes, his mind grew weary, and, sleep coming upon him, he soon fell into a doze wherein, his recent sensations blending with memories, he became conscious of a double self, at once student and married man, lying in his bed as but now, and crossing the operation theatre as of old. The warm smell of poultices mingled in his brain with the fresh odour of dew; he heard the iron rings rattling along the curtain-rods of the bed and saw his wife sleeping. As he passed Vassonville he came upon a boy sitting on the grass at the edge of a ditch.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles from time to time opened his eyes, his mind grew weary, and, sleep coming upon him, he soon fell into a doze wherein, his recent sensations blending with memories, he became conscious of a double self, at once student and married man, lying in his bed as but now, and crossing the operation theatre as of old.","zh":"查理不时睁开眼睛，但精神疲惫，困劲又上来了，没有多久，坠入一种昏迷境界，新近的感觉和记忆混淆在一起，看见自己变成两个：同时是学生，又是丈夫，就像方才一样躺在床上，又像往常一样走过一间手术室。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The warm smell of poultices mingled in his brain with the fresh odour of dew; he heard the iron rings rattling along the curtain-rods of the bed and saw his wife sleeping.","zh":"在他的意识上，药膏的暖香和露水的清香混合起来了；他听见床顶铁环在帐杆上滑动，太太睡着…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As he passed Vassonville he came upon a boy sitting on the grass at the edge of a ditch.","zh":"走过法松镇，他望见沟沿草地坐着一个小男孩。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are you the doctor?” asked the child.","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you the doctor?” asked the child.","zh":"小孩子问道：“您是医生吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And on Charles’s answer he took his wooden shoes in his hands and ran on in front of him.","sentences":[{"en":"And on Charles’s answer he took his wooden shoes in his hands and ran on in front of him.","zh":"查理回答一声“是”，他拿起木头套鞋，就在前面跑开了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The general practitioner, riding along, gathered from his guide’s talk that Monsieur Rouault must be one of the well-to-do farmers.","sentences":[{"en":"The general practitioner, riding along, gathered from his guide’s talk that Monsieur Rouault must be one of the well-to-do farmers.","zh":"路上听向导谈话，医生领会到卢欧先生一定是一位富裕的农民。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had broken his leg the evening before on his way home from a Twelfth-night feast at a neighbour’s. His wife had been dead for two years. There was with him only his daughter, who helped him to keep house.","sentences":[{"en":"He had broken his leg the evening before on his way home from a Twelfth-night feast at a neighbour’s.","zh":"昨天黄昏，他在邻居家里过三王 回来摔断了腿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His wife had been dead for two years.","zh":"太太死去两年，身边只有他的小姐帮他料理家务。","scope":"group"},{"en":"There was with him only his daughter, who helped him to keep house.","zh":"太太死去两年，身边只有他的小姐帮他料理家务。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The ruts were becoming deeper; they were approaching the Bertaux.","sentences":[{"en":"The ruts were becoming deeper; they were approaching the Bertaux.","zh":"车辙更深了。他们到了拜尔托。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The little lad, slipping through a hole in the hedge, disappeared; then he came back to the end of a courtyard to open the gate. The horse slipped on the wet grass; Charles had to stoop to pass under the branches. The watchdogs in their kennels barked, dragging at their chains. As he entered the Bertaux, the horse took fright and stumbled.","sentences":[{"en":"The little lad, slipping through a hole in the hedge, disappeared; then he came back to the end of a courtyard to open the gate.","zh":"只见小孩钻进一个篱笆窟窿，不见了，过后由一座院子尽里回来，开开栅栏门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The horse slipped on the wet grass; Charles had to stoop to pass under the branches.","zh":"马走湿草地，朝前滑溜；查理弯着腰，在树枝底下过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The watchdogs in their kennels barked, dragging at their chains.","zh":"看门的狗在狗舍拉起链子吠叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As he entered the Bertaux, the horse took fright and stumbled.","zh":"他走进拜尔托，马一害怕，来了一个大闪失。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was a substantial-looking farm. In the stables, over the top of the open doors, one could see great cart-horses quietly feeding from new racks. Right along the outbuildings extended a large dunghill, from which manure liquid oozed, while amidst fowls and turkeys, five or six peacocks, a luxury in Chauchois farmyards, were foraging on the top of it. The sheepfold was long, the barn high, with walls smooth as your hand. Under the cart-shed were two large carts and four ploughs, with their whips, shafts and harnesses complete, whose fleeces of blue wool were getting soiled by the fine dust that fell from the granaries. The courtyard sloped upwards, planted with trees set out symmetrically, and the chattering noise of a flock of geese was heard near the pond.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a substantial-looking farm.","zh":"这是一家外表殷实的田庄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the stables, over the top of the open doors, one could see great cart-horses quietly feeding from new racks.","zh":"马厩敞开，从门上望过去，就见耕田的大马，安安静静，吃着新槽的草料。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Right along the outbuildings extended a large dunghill, from which manure liquid oozed, while amidst fowls and turkeys, five or six peacocks, a luxury in Chauchois farmyards, were foraging on the top of it.","zh":"沿房有一大堆肥料，直冒水汽，五六只孔雀——科这地方田家的奢侈品，站在上头，在母鸡和火鸡当中，啄东西吃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sheepfold was long, the barn high, with walls smooth as your hand.","zh":"羊圈长长的，仓库高高的，墙光溜溜的，就像人手一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Under the cart-shed were two large carts and four ploughs, with their whips, shafts and harnesses complete, whose fleeces of blue wool were getting soiled by the fine dust that fell from the granaries.","zh":"车棚底下放着两辆老大的大车、四把犁，还有鞭子、套包、全副马具，楼上谷仓落下浮尘，污了马具的蓝羊毛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The courtyard sloped upwards, planted with trees set out symmetrically, and the chattering noise of a flock of geese was heard near the pond.","zh":"院子越上越高，种着行列整齐的树木，池塘附近，响彻一群鹅的欢叫。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A young woman in a blue merino dress with three flounces came to the threshold of the door to receive Monsieur Bovary, whom she led to the kitchen, where a large fire was blazing. The servant’s breakfast was boiling beside it in small pots of all sizes. Some damp clothes were drying inside the chimney-corner. The shovel, tongs, and the nozzle of the bellows, all of colossal size, shone like polished steel, while along the walls hung many pots and pans in which the clear flame of the hearth, mingling with the first rays of the sun coming in through the window, was mirrored fitfully.","sentences":[{"en":"A young woman in a blue merino dress with three flounces came to the threshold of the door to receive Monsieur Bovary, whom she led to the kitchen, where a large fire was blazing.","zh":"一个年轻女人，穿着镶了三道花边的美里奴 蓝袍，来到房门口，迎接包法利先生，让到厨房坐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The servant’s breakfast was boiling beside it in small pots of all sizes.","zh":"厨房生着旺火，伙计的早饭，盛入高低不齐的小闷罐，在四周沸滚。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Some damp clothes were drying inside the chimney-corner.","zh":"厨房生着旺火，伙计的早饭，盛入高低不齐的小闷罐，在四周沸滚。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The shovel, tongs, and the nozzle of the bellows, all of colossal size, shone like polished steel, while along the walls hung many pots and pans in which the clear flame of the hearth, mingling with the first rays of the sun coming in through the window, was mirrored fitfully.","zh":"灶头烘着几件湿衣服。铲子、钳子、吹筒，都大得不得了，明晃晃的，好像钢一样发亮，沿墙摆了许多厨房器皿，大小不等，映着通红的灶火和从玻璃窗那边射进来的曙光。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles went up the first floor to see the patient. He found him in his bed, sweating under his bed-clothes, having thrown his cotton nightcap right away from him. He was a fat little man of fifty, with white skin and blue eyes, the forepart of his head bald, and he wore earrings. By his side on a chair stood a large decanter of brandy, whence he poured himself a little from time to time to keep up his spirits; but as soon as he caught sight of the doctor his elation subsided, and instead of swearing, as he had been doing for the last twelve hours, began to groan freely.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles went up the first floor to see the patient.","zh":"查理上到二楼去看病人，就见他躺在床上，蒙着被窝出汗，睡帽扔得老远。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He found him in his bed, sweating under his bed-clothes, having thrown his cotton nightcap right away from him.","zh":"查理上到二楼去看病人，就见他躺在床上，蒙着被窝出汗，睡帽扔得老远。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was a fat little man of fifty, with white skin and blue eyes, the forepart of his head bald, and he wore earrings.","zh":"他是一个五十岁的矮胖子，白皮肤，蓝眼睛，秃额头，戴耳环。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By his side on a chair stood a large decanter of brandy, whence he poured himself a little from time to time to keep up his spirits; but as soon as he caught sight of the doctor his elation subsided, and instead of swearing, as he had been doing for the last twelve hours, began to groan freely.","zh":"旁边有一张椅子，上面放着一大瓶烧酒，不时喝一口，给自己打气；可是他一看见医生，就泄劲了，十二小时以来，他一直都在咒天骂地，如今却轻轻哼唧起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The fracture was a simple one, without any kind of complication.","sentences":[{"en":"The fracture was a simple one, without any kind of complication.","zh":"腿伤简单，情形并不复杂。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles could not have hoped for an easier case. Then calling to mind the devices of his masters at the bedsides of patients, he comforted the sufferer with all sorts of kindly remarks, those caresses of the surgeon that are like the oil they put on bistouries. In order to make some splints a bundle of laths was brought up from the cart-house. Charles selected one, cut it into two pieces and planed it with a fragment of windowpane, while the servant tore up sheets to make bandages, and Mademoiselle Emma tried to sew some pads. As she was a long time before she found her work-case, her father grew impatient; she did not answer, but as she sewed she pricked her fingers, which she then put to her mouth to suck them. Charles was surprised at the whiteness of her nails. They were shiny, delicate at the tips, more polished than the ivory of Dieppe, and almond-shaped. Yet her hand was not beautiful, perhaps not white enough, and a little hard at the knuckles; besides, it was too long, with no soft inflections in the outlines. Her real beauty was in her eyes. Although brown, they seemed black because of the lashes, and her look came at you frankly, with a candid boldness.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles could not have hoped for an easier case.","zh":"查理做梦也没有想到这么容易。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then calling to mind the devices of his masters at the bedsides of patients, he comforted the sufferer with all sorts of kindly remarks, those caresses of the surgeon that are like the oil they put on bistouries.","zh":"他于是想起师长在病床旁边的姿态，用各种好话安慰病人——外科医生的温存，就像抹手术刀的油一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In order to make some splints a bundle of laths was brought up from the cart-house.","zh":"有人到车棚底下找来一捆板条，当夹板用。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles selected one, cut it into two pieces and planed it with a fragment of windowpane, while the servant tore up sheets to make bandages, and Mademoiselle Emma tried to sew some pads.","zh":"查理挑了一块，劈成几小块，用碎玻璃磨光了，同时女用人撕开床单作绷带，爱玛小姐试着缝小垫子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As she was a long time before she found her work-case, her father grew impatient; she did not answer, but as she sewed she pricked her fingers, which she then put to her mouth to suck them.","zh":"父亲嫌她找针线盒找久了，一不耐烦，说了她两句；她没有顶嘴，不过，缝的中间，扎破手指头，然后放在嘴里嘬。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles was surprised at the whiteness of her nails.","zh":"指甲的白净使查理惊讶，亮晶晶的，尖头细细的，剪成杏仁样式，比第厄普的象牙还洁净。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were shiny, delicate at the tips, more polished than the ivory of Dieppe, and almond-shaped.","zh":"指甲的白净使查理惊讶，亮晶晶的，尖头细细的，剪成杏仁样式，比第厄普的象牙还洁净。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Yet her hand was not beautiful, perhaps not white enough, and a little hard at the knuckles; besides, it was too long, with no soft inflections in the outlines.","zh":"其实手并不美，也许不够白，关节瘦了一点；而且也太长了，周围的线条欠柔。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her real beauty was in her eyes.","zh":"她美在眼睛：由于睫毛缘故，棕颜色仿佛是黑颜色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Although brown, they seemed black because of the lashes, and her look came at you frankly, with a candid boldness.","zh":"眼睛朝你望来，毫无顾忌，有一种天真无邪的胆大神情。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The bandaging over, the doctor was invited by Monsieur Rouault himself to “pick a bit” before he left.","sentences":[{"en":"The bandaging over, the doctor was invited by Monsieur Rouault himself to “pick a bit” before he left.","zh":"包扎完了，卢欧先生亲自邀医生走前“用一口”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles went down into the room on the ground floor. Knives and forks and silver goblets were laid for two on a little table at the foot of a huge bed that had a canopy of printed cotton with figures representing Turks. There was an odour of iris-root and damp sheets that escaped from a large oak chest opposite the window. On the floor in corners were sacks of flour stuck upright in rows. These were the overflow from the neighbouring granary, to which three stone steps led. By way of decoration for the apartment, hanging to a nail in the middle of the wall, whose green paint scaled off from the effects of the saltpetre, was a crayon head of Minerva in gold frame, underneath which was written in Gothic letters “To dear Papa.”","sentences":[{"en":"Charles went down into the room on the ground floor.","zh":"查理下楼，来到底层厅房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Knives and forks and silver goblets were laid for two on a little table at the foot of a huge bed that had a canopy of printed cotton with figures representing Turks.","zh":"里头有一张华盖大床，挂着印花布帐子，帐子上画了土耳其人物 ；床脚放一张小桌，摆了两份刀叉和几只银杯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was an odour of iris-root and damp sheets that escaped from a large oak chest opposite the window.","zh":"他闻见蝴蝶花和面窗的橡木高橱散发出来的湿布气味。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the floor in corners were sacks of flour stuck upright in rows.","zh":"角落上，直挺挺排了几袋小麦，是谷仓装满剩下的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"These were the overflow from the neighbouring granary, to which three stone steps led.","zh":"谷仓就在近旁，有三层石头台阶通到那里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By way of decoration for the apartment, hanging to a nail in the middle of the wall, whose green paint scaled off from the effects of the saltpetre, was a crayon head of Minerva in gold frame, underneath which was written in Gothic letters “To dear Papa.”","zh":"墙上裱糊的绿纸受潮，剥落了；黑铅画的密涅瓦 头像装饰着房间，挂在墙当中钉子上，镶了镀金框子，下面用哥特字体 写着：“献给我亲爱的爸爸”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"First they spoke of the patient, then of the weather, of the great cold, of the wolves that infested the fields at night.","sentences":[{"en":"First they spoke of the patient, then of the weather, of the great cold, of the wolves that infested the fields at night.","zh":"他们起初讲病人，后来就谈天气、严寒、夜晚在田里跑东跑西的狼。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Mademoiselle Rouault did not at all like the country, especially now that she had to look after the farm almost alone. As the room was chilly, she shivered as she ate. This showed something of her full lips, that she had a habit of biting when silent.","sentences":[{"en":"Mademoiselle Rouault did not at all like the country, especially now that she had to look after the farm almost alone.","zh":"卢欧小姐在乡间并不开心，尤其是现在，田庄几乎归她一个人料理。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As the room was chilly, she shivered as she ate.","zh":"厅房冷凄凄的，她一边吃，一边打哆嗦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This showed something of her full lips, that she had a habit of biting when silent.","zh":"她一吃东西，就露出一点她丰腴的嘴唇。不说话的时候，她有咬嘴唇的习惯。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her neck stood out from a white turned-down collar. Her hair, whose two black folds seemed each of a single piece, so smooth were they, was parted in the middle by a delicate line that curved slightly with the curve of the head; and, just showing the tip of the ear, it was joined behind in a thick chignon, with a wavy movement at the temples that the country doctor saw now for the first time in his life. The upper part of her cheek was rose-coloured. She had, like a man, thrust in between two buttons of her bodice a tortoise-shell eyeglass.","sentences":[{"en":"Her neck stood out from a white turned-down collar.","zh":"白领子朝下翻，露出她的脖子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her hair, whose two black folds seemed each of a single piece, so smooth were they, was parted in the middle by a delicate line that curved slightly with the curve of the head; and, just showing the tip of the ear, it was joined behind in a thick chignon, with a wavy movement at the temples that the country doctor saw now for the first time in his life.","zh":"一条中缝顺着脑壳的弧线，轻轻下去，分开头发；头发黑乌乌、光溜溜的，两半边都像一整块东西一样，几乎盖住了耳朵尖，盘到后头，绾成一个大髻，又像波浪一样起伏，朝鬓角推了出去。这在乡下医生，还是有生以来头一回看见。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The upper part of her cheek was rose-coloured.","zh":"她的脸蛋是玫瑰红颜色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had, like a man, thrust in between two buttons of her bodice a tortoise-shell eyeglass.","zh":"她像男子一样，在上身衣服两颗纽扣中间，挂了一只玳瑁眼镜。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When Charles, after bidding farewell to old Rouault, returned to the room before leaving, he found her standing, her forehead against the window, looking into the garden, where the bean props had been knocked down by the wind. She turned round. “Are you looking for anything?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"When Charles, after bidding farewell to old Rouault, returned to the room before leaving, he found her standing, her forehead against the window, looking into the garden, where the bean props had been knocked down by the wind.","zh":"查理上楼，向卢欧老爹告辞，然后在走以前，又回到厅房。她站着朝花园望，额头贴住窗户。先前起风，吹倒园里的豆架。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She turned round.","zh":"查理上楼，向卢欧老爹告辞，然后在走以前，又回到厅房。她站着朝花园望，额头贴住窗户。先前起风，吹倒园里的豆架。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Are you looking for anything?” she asked.","zh":"她转回身，问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My whip, if you please,” he answered.","sentences":[{"en":"“My whip, if you please,” he answered.","zh":"“您找什么东西？”他答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He began rummaging on the bed, behind the doors, under the chairs. It had fallen to the floor, between the sacks and the wall. Mademoiselle Emma saw it, and bent over the flour sacks.","sentences":[{"en":"He began rummaging on the bed, behind the doors, under the chairs.","zh":"“对不住，我的鞭子。”他开始在床上、门背后、椅子底下寻找；原来掉在口袋和墙壁之间的地上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It had fallen to the floor, between the sacks and the wall.","zh":"“对不住，我的鞭子。”他开始在床上、门背后、椅子底下寻找；原来掉在口袋和墙壁之间的地上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Mademoiselle Emma saw it, and bent over the flour sacks.","zh":"爱玛小姐瞥见了；她伏到小麦口袋上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles out of politeness made a dash also, and as he stretched out his arm, at the same moment felt his breast brush against the back of the young girl bending beneath him. She drew herself up, scarlet, and looked at him over her shoulder as she handed him his whip.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles out of politeness made a dash also, and as he stretched out his arm, at the same moment felt his breast brush against the back of the young girl bending beneath him.","zh":"查理表示殷勤，连忙跑过去，也同样伸出胳膊，女孩子弯在底下，他觉出他的胸脯蹭到她的后背。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She drew herself up, scarlet, and looked at him over her shoulder as she handed him his whip.","zh":"她涨红了脸，立直了，朝后望，递鞭子给他。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Instead of returning to the Bertaux in three days as he had promised, he went back the very next day, then regularly twice a week, without counting the visits he paid now and then as if by accident.","sentences":[{"en":"Instead of returning to the Bertaux in three days as he had promised, he went back the very next day, then regularly twice a week, without counting the visits he paid now and then as if by accident.","zh":"原来答应三天过后再来拜尔托，但是第二天他就来了。此后，他一星期经常来两次，还不算他有时候意想不到的偶尔探望。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Everything, moreover, went well; the patient progressed favourably; and when, at the end of forty-six days, old Rouault was seen trying to walk alone in his “den,” Monsieur Bovary began to be looked upon as a man of great capacity. Old Rouault said that he could not have been cured better by the first doctor of Yvetot, or even of Rouen.","sentences":[{"en":"Everything, moreover, went well; the patient progressed favourably; and when, at the end of forty-six days, old Rouault was seen trying to walk alone in his “den,” Monsieur Bovary began to be looked upon as a man of great capacity.","zh":"其实，一切顺利，病按部就班好起来了；四十六天之后，大家看见卢欧老爹试着独自在他的破屋走路，他开始把包法利先生看成一位名医。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Old Rouault said that he could not have been cured better by the first doctor of Yvetot, or even of Rouen.","zh":"卢欧老爹说：伊弗托 ，就连鲁昂的头等医生，医病也不见其医得更好。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As to Charles, he did not stop to ask himself why it was a pleasure to him to go to the Bertaux. Had he done so, he would, no doubt, have attributed his zeal to the importance of the case, or perhaps to the money he hoped to make by it. Was it for this, however, that his visits to the farm formed a delightful exception to the meagre occupations of his life? On these days he rose early, set off at a gallop, urging on his horse, then got down to wipe his boots in the grass and put on black gloves before entering. He liked going into the courtyard, and noticing the gate turn against his shoulder, the cock crow on the wall, the lads run to meet him. He liked the granary and the stables; he liked old Rouault, who pressed his hand and called him his saviour; he liked the small wooden shoes of Mademoiselle Emma on the scoured flags of the kitchen—her high heels made her a little taller; and when she walked in front of him, the wooden soles springing up quickly struck with a sharp sound against the leather of her boots.","sentences":[{"en":"As to Charles, he did not stop to ask himself why it was a pleasure to him to go to the Bertaux.","zh":"至于查理，他并不细想他为什么喜欢去拜尔托。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Had he done so, he would, no doubt, have attributed his zeal to the importance of the case, or perhaps to the money he hoped to make by it.","zh":"万一想到这上头，不用说，他会把热忱说成患者病情严重，要不就说成想挣钱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Was it for this, however, that his visits to the farm formed a delightful exception to the meagre occupations of his life?","zh":"不过平日业务猥琐，难道去田庄看病成为可喜的例外，真就由于这些理由吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On these days he rose early, set off at a gallop, urging on his horse, then got down to wipe his boots in the grass and put on black gloves before entering.","zh":"去田庄的日子，他老早起来，骑上牲口，打着它跑；然后下马，在草地擦干净脚，进去之前，戴上黑手套。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He liked going into the courtyard, and noticing the gate turn against his shoulder, the cock crow on the wall, the lads run to meet him.","zh":"看见自己来到院子，觉得栅栏门随着肩膀转，公鸡在墙上啼，小伙计们过来迎他，他就欢喜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He liked the granary and the stables; he liked old Rouault, who pressed his hand and called him his saviour; he liked the small wooden shoes of Mademoiselle Emma on the scoured flags of the kitchen—her high heels made her a little taller; and when she walked in front of him, the wooden soles springing up quickly struck with a sharp sound against the leather of her boots.","zh":"他爱仓库和马厩；他爱卢欧老爹拍着他的肩膀，喊他救命恩人；他喜欢爱玛小姐的小木头套鞋，踩着厨房洗干净的石板地；她的高后跟托高了她一点点，她在前面走，木底飞快掀起，牵动女靴皮，嘎吱直响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She always accompanied him to the first step of the stairs. When his horse had not yet been brought round she stayed there. They had said “Good-bye”; there was no more talking. The open air wrapped her round, playing with the soft down on the back of her neck, or blew to and fro on her hips the apron-strings, that fluttered like streamers. Once, during a thaw the bark of the trees in the yard was oozing, the snow on the roofs of the outbuildings was melting; she stood on the threshold, and went to fetch her sunshade and opened it. The sunshade of silk of the colour of pigeons’ breasts, through which the sun shone, lighted up with shifting hues the white skin of her face. She smiled under the tender warmth, and drops of water could be heard falling one by one on the stretched silk.","sentences":[{"en":"She always accompanied him to the first step of the stairs.","zh":"她送他永远送到第一层台阶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When his horse had not yet been brought round she stayed there.","zh":"马要是还没有牵来，她就待在这里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They had said “Good-bye”; there was no more talking.","zh":"再会已经说过，他们也就不再言语；风兜住她，吹乱后颈新生的短发，或者吹起臀上围裙的带子，仿佛小旗，卷来卷去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The open air wrapped her round, playing with the soft down on the back of her neck, or blew to and fro on her hips the apron-strings, that fluttered like streamers.","zh":"再会已经说过，他们也就不再言语；风兜住她，吹乱后颈新生的短发，或者吹起臀上围裙的带子，仿佛小旗，卷来卷去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Once, during a thaw the bark of the trees in the yard was oozing, the snow on the roofs of the outbuildings was melting; she stood on the threshold, and went to fetch her sunshade and opened it.","zh":"有一次，时逢化冻，院里树木的皮在渗水，房顶的雪在融化。她站在门槛，找来她的阳伞，撑开了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sunshade of silk of the colour of pigeons’ breasts, through which the sun shone, lighted up with shifting hues the white skin of her face.","zh":"阳伞是缎子做的，鸽子咽喉颜色，阳光穿过，闪闪烁烁，照亮脸上的白净皮肤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She smiled under the tender warmth, and drops of water could be heard falling one by one on the stretched silk.","zh":"天气不冷不热，她在伞底下微笑；他们听见水点，一滴又一滴，打着紧绷绷的闪缎。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"During the first period of Charles’s visits to the Bertaux, Madame Bovary junior never failed to inquire after the invalid, and she had even chosen in the book that she kept on a system of double entry a clean blank page for Monsieur Rouault. But when she heard he had a daughter, she began to make inquiries, and she learnt the Mademoiselle Rouault, brought up at the Ursuline Convent, had received what is called “a good education”; and so knew dancing, geography, drawing, how to embroider and play the piano. That was the last straw.","sentences":[{"en":"During the first period of Charles’s visits to the Bertaux, Madame Bovary junior never failed to inquire after the invalid, and she had even chosen in the book that she kept on a system of double entry a clean blank page for Monsieur Rouault.","zh":"查理初去拜尔托，少奶奶免不了打听病人的底细，甚至于为卢欧先生，在她的复记账簿选了又白又干净的一页。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But when she heard he had a daughter, she began to make inquiries, and she learnt the Mademoiselle Rouault, brought up at the Ursuline Convent, had received what is called “a good education”; and so knew dancing, geography, drawing, how to embroider and play the piano.","zh":"但是她一听说他有一个女儿，就四下打探，得知卢欧小姐是在虞絮林修道院长大的，据说受过良好教育 ，自然也就懂得跳舞、地理、素描、刺绣和弹琴了，这还了得！","scope":"group"},{"en":"That was the last straw.","zh":"但是她一听说他有一个女儿，就四下打探，得知卢欧小姐是在虞絮林修道院长大的，据说受过良好教育 ，自然也就懂得跳舞、地理、素描、刺绣和弹琴了，这还了得！","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“So it is for this,” she said to herself, “that his face beams when he goes to see her, and that he puts on his new waistcoat at the risk of spoiling it with the rain. Ah! that woman! That woman!”","sentences":[{"en":"“So it is for this,” she said to herself, “that his face beams when he goes to see her, and that he puts on his new waistcoat at the risk of spoiling it with the rain.","zh":"她想：“那么，就是为了这个缘故，他去看她，这才脸上发光，这才穿上他的新背心，也不怕雨淋坏？啊！这个女人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! that woman!","zh":"这个女人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That woman!”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she detested her instinctively. At first she solaced herself by allusions that Charles did not understand, then by casual observations that he let pass for fear of a storm, finally by open apostrophes to which he knew not what to answer. “Why did he go back to the Bertaux now that Monsieur Rouault was cured and that these folks hadn’t paid yet? Ah! it was because a young lady was there, some one who knew how to talk, to embroider, to be witty. That was what he cared about; he wanted town misses.” And she went on—","sentences":[{"en":"And she detested her instinctively.","zh":"她本能地恨她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At first she solaced herself by allusions that Charles did not understand, then by casual observations that he let pass for fear of a storm, finally by open apostrophes to which he knew not what to answer.","zh":"起初她闷不下去，说暗话试他。查理听不懂；后来她偶尔挖苦几句，他怕吵闹，权当没有听见；最后，她当面指责，他不晓得怎么回答。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Why did he go back to the Bertaux now that Monsieur Rouault was cured and that these folks hadn’t paid yet?","zh":"——卢欧先生已经病好了，诊费又没有付，他凭什么还去拜尔托？啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! it was because a young lady was there, some one who knew how to talk, to embroider, to be witty.","zh":"因为那边有一个人儿、一位能说会道的人儿、一位刺绣家、一位女才子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That was what he cared about; he wanted town misses.”","zh":"他爱的就是这个：他要的是城里小姐！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And she went on—","zh":"她接着道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The daughter of old Rouault a town miss! Get out! Their grandfather was a shepherd, and they have a cousin who was almost had up at the assizes for a nasty blow in a quarrel. It is not worth while making such a fuss, or showing herself at church on Sundays in a silk gown like a countess. Besides, the poor old chap, if it hadn’t been for the colza last year, would have had much ado to pay up his arrears.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The daughter of old Rouault a town miss! Get out!","zh":"“卢欧老爹的女儿，一位城里小姐！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Their grandfather was a shepherd, and they have a cousin who was almost had up at the assizes for a nasty blow in a quarrel.","zh":"去她的吧！他们的祖父是放羊的，他们有一个亲戚，同人吵架，差点儿吃官司。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is not worth while making such a fuss, or showing herself at church on Sundays in a silk gown like a countess.","zh":"她犯不上那样瞎神气，也犯不上星期天上教堂，穿一件绸袍子，活像一位伯爵夫人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, the poor old chap, if it hadn’t been for the colza last year, would have had much ado to pay up his arrears.”","zh":"再说，可怜的老头子，去年要不是油菜收成好，兴许连地租都交不上！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For very weariness Charles left off going to the Bertaux. Heloise made him swear, his hand on the prayer-book, that he would go there no more after much sobbing and many kisses, in a great outburst of love. He obeyed then, but the strength of his desire protested against the servility of his conduct; and he thought, with a kind of naive hypocrisy, that his interdict to see her gave him a sort of right to love her. And then the widow was thin; she had long teeth; wore in all weathers a little black shawl, the edge of which hung down between her shoulder-blades; her bony figure was sheathed in her clothes as if they were a scabbard; they were too short, and displayed her ankles with the laces of her large boots crossed over grey stockings.","sentences":[{"en":"For very weariness Charles left off going to the Bertaux.","zh":"查理嫌烦，不去拜尔托了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Heloise made him swear, his hand on the prayer-book, that he would go there no more after much sobbing and many kisses, in a great outburst of love.","zh":"艾洛伊丝爱情大发作，哭了吻，吻了哭，之后，叫他赌咒，手放在弥撒书上，说他再也不去，他只得依顺；可是欲望强烈，他不甘心奴颜婢膝，就此屈服：这道禁止看她的阃令，通过一种天真的虚伪想法，在他看来反而成为爱她的权利。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He obeyed then, but the strength of his desire protested against the servility of his conduct; and he thought, with a kind of naive hypocrisy, that his interdict to see her gave him a sort of right to love her.","zh":"艾洛伊丝爱情大发作，哭了吻，吻了哭，之后，叫他赌咒，手放在弥撒书上，说他再也不去，他只得依顺；可是欲望强烈，他不甘心奴颜婢膝，就此屈服：这道禁止看她的阃令，通过一种天真的虚伪想法，在他看来反而成为爱她的权利。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And then the widow was thin; she had long teeth; wore in all weathers a little black shawl, the edge of which hung down between her shoulder-blades; her bony figure was sheathed in her clothes as if they were a scabbard; they were too short, and displayed her ankles with the laces of her large boots crossed over grey stockings.","zh":"而且寡妇瘦括括的，牙又长，整年披一件小黑披肩 ，尖尖头搭在肩胛骨之间；骨头一把，套上袍子，就像剑入了鞘一样；袍子又太短，露出踝骨和大皮鞋的交叉搭在灰袜上面的带子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles’s mother came to see them from time to time, but after a few days the daughter-in-law seemed to put her own edge on her, and then, like two knives, they scarified him with their reflections and observations. It was wrong of him to eat so much.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles’s mother came to see them from time to time, but after a few days the daughter-in-law seemed to put her own edge on her, and then, like two knives, they scarified him with their reflections and observations.","zh":"查理的母亲不时来看他们；可是待不了几天，刀口对刀口，媳妇像是把她磨快了一样，于是好比两把刀，你一言，我一语，她们扎过来，刺过去，拿他出气。他吃东西不该吃得那么多！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was wrong of him to eat so much.","zh":"为什么不管谁来，总请他喝酒？死不穿法兰绒背心，多固执！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Why did he always offer a glass of something to everyone who came? What obstinacy not to wear flannels! In the spring it came about that a notary at Ingouville, the holder of the widow Dubuc’s property, one fine day went off, taking with him all the money in his office. Heloise, it is true, still possessed, besides a share in a boat valued at six thousand francs, her house in the Rue St. Francois; and yet, with all this fortune that had been so trumpeted abroad, nothing, excepting perhaps a little furniture and a few clothes, had appeared in the household. The matter had to be gone into. The house at Dieppe was found to be eaten up with mortgages to its foundations; what she had placed with the notary God only knew, and her share in the boat did not exceed one thousand crowns. She had lied, the good lady! In his exasperation, Monsieur Bovary the elder, smashing a chair on the flags, accused his wife of having caused misfortune to the son by harnessing him to such a harridan, whose harness wasn’t worth her hide. They came to Tostes. Explanations followed. There were scenes. Heloise in tears, throwing her arms about her husband, implored him to defend her from his parents.","sentences":[{"en":"Why did he always offer a glass of something to everyone who came?","zh":"就在开春，安古镇一个公证人、杜比克寡妇财产的保管人，有一天带了他的事务所的全部现金，搭船卷逃了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"What obstinacy not to wear flannels!","zh":"就在开春，安古镇一个公证人、杜比克寡妇财产的保管人，有一天带了他的事务所的全部现金，搭船卷逃了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In the spring it came about that a notary at Ingouville, the holder of the widow Dubuc’s property, one fine day went off, taking with him all the money in his office.","zh":"就在开春，安古镇一个公证人、杜比克寡妇财产的保管人，有一天带了他的事务所的全部现金，搭船卷逃了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Heloise, it is true, still possessed, besides a share in a boat valued at six thousand francs, her house in the Rue St. Francois; and yet, with all this fortune that had been so trumpeted abroad, nothing, excepting perhaps a little furniture and a few clothes, had appeared in the household.","zh":"不错，除去值六千法郎的船股之外，艾洛伊丝还有她在圣弗朗索瓦街的房子；可是这份产业，尽管吹了个天花乱坠，除去几件家具和几件旧衣服之外，就没有别的再在家里露过面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The matter had to be gone into.","zh":"事情必须查究明白。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The house at Dieppe was found to be eaten up with mortgages to its foundations; what she had placed with the notary God only knew, and her share in the boat did not exceed one thousand crowns.","zh":"原来第厄普的房子，连打地基的桩子，都抵押掉了；她在公证人那边存了一些什么，只有上帝知道；船股也绝多不过一千埃居 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had lied, the good lady!","zh":"原来她撒谎来着，好娘儿们！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In his exasperation, Monsieur Bovary the elder, smashing a chair on the flags, accused his wife of having caused misfortune to the son by harnessing him to such a harridan, whose harness wasn’t worth her hide.","zh":"公公一怒，在石板地上摔坏一张椅子，骂老婆祸害儿子，给他套了这样一匹干瘪马，鞍韂不及马皮值钱，他们来到道特。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They came to Tostes.","zh":"公公一怒，在石板地上摔坏一张椅子，骂老婆祸害儿子，给他套了这样一匹干瘪马，鞍韂不及马皮值钱，他们来到道特。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Explanations followed.","zh":"话一扯穿，吵起来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"There were scenes.","zh":"话一扯穿，吵起来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Heloise in tears, throwing her arms about her husband, implored him to defend her from his parents.","zh":"艾洛伊丝哭着，扑到丈夫怀里，求他帮她对付公婆。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles tried to speak up for her. They grew angry and left the house.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles tried to speak up for her.","zh":"查理试着替她分辩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They grew angry and left the house.","zh":"父母一怒而去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But “the blow had struck home.” A week after, as she was hanging up some washing in her yard, she was seized with a spitting of blood, and the next day, while Charles had his back turned to her drawing the window-curtain, she said, “O God!” gave a sigh and fainted. She was dead! What a surprise! When all was over at the cemetery Charles went home. He found no one downstairs; he went up to the first floor to their room; saw her dress still hanging at the foot of the alcove; then, leaning against the writing-table, he stayed until the evening, buried in a sorrowful reverie. She had loved him after all!","sentences":[{"en":"But “the blow had struck home.”","zh":"但是病根扎下了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A week after, as she was hanging up some washing in her yard, she was seized with a spitting of blood, and the next day, while Charles had his back turned to her drawing the window-curtain, she said, “O God!” gave a sigh and fainted.","zh":"过了一星期，她在院子晾衣服，吐了一口血，第二天，查理转过背去拉窗帘，她说：“啊！我的上帝！”叹息一声，晕倒过去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was dead!","zh":"她死了，真想不到！","scope":"group"},{"en":"What a surprise!","zh":"她死了，真想不到！","scope":"group"},{"en":"When all was over at the cemetery Charles went home.","zh":"坟地的事一了，查理回到家，没有在底下遇见一个人，走上二楼卧室，看见她的袍子还挂在床头，于是靠住书桌，一直待到天黑，沉在痛苦的梦境。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He found no one downstairs; he went up to the first floor to their room; saw her dress still hanging at the foot of the alcove; then, leaning against the writing-table, he stayed until the evening, buried in a sorrowful reverie.","zh":"坟地的事一了，查理回到家，没有在底下遇见一个人，走上二楼卧室，看见她的袍子还挂在床头，于是靠住书桌，一直待到天黑，沉在痛苦的梦境。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She had loved him after all!","zh":"无论如何，她爱他来着。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"1-3","part":1,"n":3,"title":"Part I · Chapter 3","titleZh":"上卷 · 3","paragraphs":[{"en":"One morning old Rouault brought Charles the money for setting his leg—seventy-five francs in forty-sou pieces, and a turkey. He had heard of his loss, and consoled him as well as he could.","sentences":[{"en":"One morning old Rouault brought Charles the money for setting his leg—seventy-five francs in forty-sou pieces, and a turkey.","zh":"一天早晨，卢欧老爹来了，给查理带来医腿的诊费：七十五法郎，用的是四十苏 一枚的辅币 ，另外还有一只母火鸡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had heard of his loss, and consoled him as well as he could.","zh":"他听人说起他的不幸，就尽力安慰他，拍他的肩膀道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I know what it is,” said he, clapping him on the shoulder; “I’ve been through it. When I lost my dear departed, I went into the fields to be quite alone. I fell at the foot of a tree; I cried; I called on God; I talked nonsense to Him. I wanted to be like the moles that I saw on the branches, their insides swarming with worms, dead, and an end of it. And when I thought that there were others at that very moment with their nice little wives holding them in their embrace, I struck great blows on the earth with my stick. I was pretty well mad with not eating; the very idea of going to a cafe disgusted me—you wouldn’t believe it. Well, quite softly, one day following another, a spring on a winter, and an autumn after a summer, this wore away, piece by piece, crumb by crumb; it passed away, it is gone, I should say it has sunk; for something always remains at the bottom as one would say—a weight here, at one’s heart. But since it is the lot of all of us, one must not give way altogether, and, because others have died, want to die too. You must pull yourself together, Monsieur Bovary. It will pass away. Come to see us; my daughter thinks of you now and again, d’ye know, and she says you are forgetting her. Spring will soon be here. We’ll have some rabbit-shooting in the warrens to amuse you a bit.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I know what it is,” said he, clapping him on the shoulder; “I’ve been through it.","zh":"“我知道这是怎么一回事！我也像您一样，经过这事！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When I lost my dear departed, I went into the fields to be quite alone.","zh":"我丢了我的老伴儿，当时我走到田里，只想一个人待；我倒在一棵树旁边，又哭，又喊老天爷，直讲浑话；我真愿意像我看见的树枝上的田鼠一样，肚子里头长蛆，一句话，死了拉倒。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I fell at the foot of a tree; I cried; I called on God; I talked nonsense to Him.","zh":"我丢了我的老伴儿，当时我走到田里，只想一个人待；我倒在一棵树旁边，又哭，又喊老天爷，直讲浑话；我真愿意像我看见的树枝上的田鼠一样，肚子里头长蛆，一句话，死了拉倒。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I wanted to be like the moles that I saw on the branches, their insides swarming with worms, dead, and an end of it.","zh":"我丢了我的老伴儿，当时我走到田里，只想一个人待；我倒在一棵树旁边，又哭，又喊老天爷，直讲浑话；我真愿意像我看见的树枝上的田鼠一样，肚子里头长蛆，一句话，死了拉倒。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And when I thought that there were others at that very moment with their nice little wives holding them in their embrace, I struck great blows on the earth with my stick.","zh":"我一想到别人这期间，和他们的小媳妇亲热，搂得紧紧的，我就拿我的手杖拼命敲地；我差不多疯了，饭也不吃；您也许不相信，单只想到上咖啡馆，我就腻味。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I was pretty well mad with not eating; the very idea of going to a cafe disgusted me—you wouldn’t believe it.","zh":"我一想到别人这期间，和他们的小媳妇亲热，搂得紧紧的，我就拿我的手杖拼命敲地；我差不多疯了，饭也不吃；您也许不相信，单只想到上咖啡馆，我就腻味。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Well, quite softly, one day following another, a spring on a winter, and an autumn after a summer, this wore away, piece by piece, crumb by crumb; it passed away, it is gone, I should say it has sunk; for something always remains at the bottom as one would say—a weight here, at one’s heart.","zh":"好啦，慢条斯理，一天又一天，春天接冬天，秋天跟夏天，也就一星一点过去了，去远了，走开了，我的意思是说，沉下去了，因为您心里总有一点什么东西留下来，像人们说的…一块石头，在这儿，压着胸口！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But since it is the lot of all of us, one must not give way altogether, and, because others have died, want to die too.","zh":"不过，既然我们人人命当如此，就不该糟蹋自己，别因为伴儿死了，自己也想死…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You must pull yourself together, Monsieur Bovary.","zh":"包法利先生，应当打起精神来才是；这会过去的！","scope":"group"},{"en":"It will pass away.","zh":"包法利先生，应当打起精神来才是；这会过去的！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Come to see us; my daughter thinks of you now and again, d’ye know, and she says you are forgetting her.","zh":"看我们来吧；您明白，我女儿一来就想到您，说您忘了她啦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Spring will soon be here.","zh":"眼看春天要来了；我们陪您上林子里打野兔，也好散散心。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"We’ll have some rabbit-shooting in the warrens to amuse you a bit.”","zh":"眼看春天要来了；我们陪您上林子里打野兔，也好散散心。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles followed his advice. He went back to the Bertaux. He found all as he had left it, that is to say, as it was five months ago. The pear trees were already in blossom, and Farmer Rouault, on his legs again, came and went, making the farm more full of life.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles followed his advice.","zh":"查理听他劝，又去了拜尔托。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He went back to the Bertaux.","zh":"查理听他劝，又去了拜尔托。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He found all as he had left it, that is to say, as it was five months ago.","zh":"他发现一切如旧，就是说，和五个月以前一模一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The pear trees were already in blossom, and Farmer Rouault, on his legs again, came and went, making the farm more full of life.","zh":"梨树已经开花，卢欧老头子如今站起来了，走来走去，田庄也就因而越发生气蓬勃。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Thinking it his duty to heap the greatest attention upon the doctor because of his sad position, he begged him not to take his hat off, spoke to him in an undertone as if he had been ill, and even pretended to be angry because nothing rather lighter had been prepared for him than for the others, such as a little clotted cream or stewed pears. He told stories. Charles found himself laughing, but the remembrance of his wife suddenly coming back to him depressed him. Coffee was brought in; he thought no more about her.","sentences":[{"en":"Thinking it his duty to heap the greatest attention upon the doctor because of his sad position, he begged him not to take his hat off, spoke to him in an undertone as if he had been ill, and even pretended to be angry because nothing rather lighter had been prepared for him than for the others, such as a little clotted cream or stewed pears.","zh":"在卢欧老爹想来，医生遭逢不幸，尽可能体恤成了他的责任，所以他求他不要摘掉帽子，低声同他说话，仿佛他成了病人，甚至看见别人没有为他准备一点比较轻松的吃食，如小罐奶酪，或者烧熟的梨呀什么的，还假装生气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He told stories.","zh":"他讲故事，查理意料不到自己笑了；可是他忽然想起太太，就又郁郁不欢。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles found himself laughing, but the remembrance of his wife suddenly coming back to him depressed him.","zh":"他讲故事，查理意料不到自己笑了；可是他忽然想起太太，就又郁郁不欢。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Coffee was brought in; he thought no more about her.","zh":"咖啡端上来，他不再思念她了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He thought less of her as he grew accustomed to living alone. The new delight of independence soon made his loneliness bearable. He could now change his meal-times, go in or out without explanation, and when he was very tired stretch himself at full length on his bed. So he nursed and coddled himself and accepted the consolations that were offered him. On the other hand, the death of his wife had not served him ill in his business, since for a month people had been saying, “The poor young man! what a loss!” His name had been talked about, his practice had increased; and moreover, he could go to the Bertaux just as he liked. He had an aimless hope, and was vaguely happy; he thought himself better looking as he brushed his whiskers before the looking-glass.","sentences":[{"en":"He thought less of her as he grew accustomed to living alone.","zh":"过惯一个人的日子，他越来越不思念她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The new delight of independence soon made his loneliness bearable.","zh":"他有了自由自在这种新到手的快乐，不久反而觉得寂寞好受了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He could now change his meal-times, go in or out without explanation, and when he was very tired stretch himself at full length on his bed.","zh":"现在他可以改改用餐时间，出入不必举理由，人累狠了，就四肢一挺，躺到床上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So he nursed and coddled himself and accepted the consolations that were offered him.","zh":"他于是贪舒服，心疼自己，接受外人的慰唁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the other hand, the death of his wife had not served him ill in his business, since for a month people had been saying, “The poor young man! what a loss!”","zh":"再说太太一死，他的营业反而好转，因为一个月以来，大家总在说：“这可怜的年轻人！多不幸！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His name had been talked about, his practice had increased; and moreover, he could go to the Bertaux just as he liked.","zh":"他有了名气，主顾多了；而且他去拜尔托，无拘无束。他起了一种漫无目标的希望、一种模模糊糊的幸福；他理他的络腮胡须，照照镜子，觉得脸好看多了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He had an aimless hope, and was vaguely happy; he thought himself better looking as he brushed his whiskers before the looking-glass.","zh":"他有了名气，主顾多了；而且他去拜尔托，无拘无束。他起了一种漫无目标的希望、一种模模糊糊的幸福；他理他的络腮胡须，照照镜子，觉得脸好看多了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"One day he got there about three o’clock. Everybody was in the fields. He went into the kitchen, but did not at once catch sight of Emma; the outside shutters were closed. Through the chinks of the wood the sun sent across the flooring long fine rays that were broken at the corners of the furniture and trembled along the ceiling. Some flies on the table were crawling up the glasses that had been used, and buzzing as they drowned themselves in the dregs of the cider. The daylight that came in by the chimney made velvet of the soot at the back of the fireplace, and touched with blue the cold cinders. Between the window and the hearth Emma was sewing; she wore no fichu; he could see small drops of perspiration on her bare shoulders.","sentences":[{"en":"One day he got there about three o’clock.","zh":"有一天，三点钟上下，他来了；人全下地去了；他走进厨房，起初没有看见爱玛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Everybody was in the fields.","zh":"有一天，三点钟上下，他来了；人全下地去了；他走进厨房，起初没有看见爱玛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He went into the kitchen, but did not at once catch sight of Emma; the outside shutters were closed.","zh":"有一天，三点钟上下，他来了；人全下地去了；他走进厨房，起初没有看见爱玛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Through the chinks of the wood the sun sent across the flooring long fine rays that were broken at the corners of the furniture and trembled along the ceiling.","zh":"外头放下护窗板，阳光穿过板缝，在石板地上，变成一道一道又长又亮的细线，碰到家具犄角，一折为二，在天花板上颤抖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some flies on the table were crawling up the glasses that had been used, and buzzing as they drowned themselves in the dregs of the cider.","zh":"桌上放着用过的玻璃杯，有些苍蝇顺着往上爬，反而淹入杯底残苹果酒，嘤嘤作响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The daylight that came in by the chimney made velvet of the soot at the back of the fireplace, and touched with blue the cold cinders.","zh":"亮光从烟囱下来，掠过铁板上的烟灰，烟灰变成天鹅绒，冷却的灰烬映成淡蓝颜色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Between the window and the hearth Emma was sewing; she wore no fichu; he could see small drops of perspiration on her bare shoulders.","zh":"爱玛在窗、灶之间缝东西，没有披肩巾 ，只见光肩膀冒着小汗珠。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After the fashion of country folks she asked him to have something to drink. He said no; she insisted, and at last laughingly offered to have a glass of liqueur with him. So she went to fetch a bottle of curacao from the cupboard, reached down two small glasses, filled one to the brim, poured scarcely anything into the other, and, after having clinked glasses, carried hers to her mouth. As it was almost empty she bent back to drink, her head thrown back, her lips pouting, her neck on the strain. She laughed at getting none of it, while with the tip of her tongue passing between her small teeth she licked drop by drop the bottom of her glass.","sentences":[{"en":"After the fashion of country folks she asked him to have something to drink.","zh":"她按照乡间风俗，邀他喝酒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He said no; she insisted, and at last laughingly offered to have a glass of liqueur with him.","zh":"他不肯，她一定要他喝，最后一面笑，一面建议他陪她饮一杯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So she went to fetch a bottle of curacao from the cupboard, reached down two small glasses, filled one to the brim, poured scarcely anything into the other, and, after having clinked glasses, carried hers to her mouth.","zh":"于是她从碗橱找出一瓶橘皮酒，取下两只小玻璃杯，一杯斟得满满的，一杯等于没有斟，碰过了杯，端到嘴边喝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As it was almost empty she bent back to drink, her head thrown back, her lips pouting, her neck on the strain.","zh":"因为酒杯差不多是空的，她仰起身子来喝；头朝后，嘴唇向前，脖子伸长，她笑自己什么也没有喝到，同时舌尖穿过细白牙齿，一点一滴，舔着杯底。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She laughed at getting none of it, while with the tip of her tongue passing between her small teeth she licked drop by drop the bottom of her glass.","zh":"因为酒杯差不多是空的，她仰起身子来喝；头朝后，嘴唇向前，脖子伸长，她笑自己什么也没有喝到，同时舌尖穿过细白牙齿，一点一滴，舔着杯底。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She sat down again and took up her work, a white cotton stocking she was darning. She worked with her head bent down; she did not speak, nor did Charles. The air coming in under the door blew a little dust over the flags; he watched it drift along, and heard nothing but the throbbing in his head and the faint clucking of a hen that had laid an egg in the yard. Emma from time to time cooled her cheeks with the palms of her hands, and cooled these again on the knobs of the huge fire-dogs.","sentences":[{"en":"She sat down again and took up her work, a white cotton stocking she was darning.","zh":"她又坐下来，拾起女红，织补一只白线袜；她不言语，低下额头，只是织补。查理也不言语。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She worked with her head bent down; she did not speak, nor did Charles.","zh":"她又坐下来，拾起女红，织补一只白线袜；她不言语，低下额头，只是织补。查理也不言语。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The air coming in under the door blew a little dust over the flags; he watched it drift along, and heard nothing but the throbbing in his head and the faint clucking of a hen that had laid an egg in the yard.","zh":"空气从门底下吹进来，轻轻扬起石板地的灰尘；他看着灰尘散开，仅仅听见太阳穴跳动，还有远远一只母鸡在院子下了蛋啼叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma from time to time cooled her cheeks with the palms of her hands, and cooled these again on the knobs of the huge fire-dogs.","zh":"爱玛不时摊开手心冰脸，手心发热，放在火篦的铁球上再沁凉了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She complained of suffering since the beginning of the season from giddiness; she asked if sea-baths would do her any good; she began talking of her convent, Charles of his school; words came to them. They went up into her bedroom. She showed him her old music-books, the little prizes she had won, and the oak-leaf crowns, left at the bottom of a cupboard. She spoke to him, too, of her mother, of the country, and even showed him the bed in the garden where, on the first Friday of every month, she gathered flowers to put on her mother’s tomb. But the gardener they had never knew anything about it; servants are so stupid! She would have dearly liked, if only for the winter, to live in town, although the length of the fine days made the country perhaps even more wearisome in the summer. And, according to what she was saying, her voice was clear, sharp, or, on a sudden all languor, drawn out in modulations that ended almost in murmurs as she spoke to herself, now joyous, opening big naive eyes, then with her eyelids half closed, her look full of boredom, her thoughts wandering.","sentences":[{"en":"She complained of suffering since the beginning of the season from giddiness; she asked if sea-baths would do her any good; she began talking of her convent, Charles of his school; words came to them.","zh":"她诉说入夏以来，就感头晕；她问海水浴对她有没有用 ；她谈起修道院，查理谈起他的中学，他们有了话说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They went up into her bedroom.","zh":"他们上楼，来到她的卧室。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She showed him her old music-books, the little prizes she had won, and the oak-leaf crowns, left at the bottom of a cupboard.","zh":"她让他看她的旧音乐簿、她得奖的小书 和扔在衣橱底层的栎叶冠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She spoke to him, too, of her mother, of the country, and even showed him the bed in the garden where, on the first Friday of every month, she gathered flowers to put on her mother’s tomb.","zh":"她还说起她的母亲、坟地，甚至指给他看花园里的花畦，说她每个月的第一个星期五，都要掐下花来，放到母亲的坟头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the gardener they had never knew anything about it; servants are so stupid!","zh":"可是他们的花匠一点也不知道；用人简直不管事！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would have dearly liked, if only for the winter, to live in town, although the length of the fine days made the country perhaps even more wearisome in the summer.","zh":"她情愿住在城里，哪怕单是冬季也好，虽然夏季天长，住在乡间，也许更腻味；——依照说话的内容，她的声音一时清楚，一时尖锐，忽而懒洋洋，临了差不多变成自言自语时的呢喃——转眼之间，兴高采烈，睁开天真的眼睛，马上却又眼皮半闭，视线充满厌烦，不知想到什么地方去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And, according to what she was saying, her voice was clear, sharp, or, on a sudden all languor, drawn out in modulations that ended almost in murmurs as she spoke to herself, now joyous, opening big naive eyes, then with her eyelids half closed, her look full of boredom, her thoughts wandering.","zh":"她情愿住在城里，哪怕单是冬季也好，虽然夏季天长，住在乡间，也许更腻味；——依照说话的内容，她的声音一时清楚，一时尖锐，忽而懒洋洋，临了差不多变成自言自语时的呢喃——转眼之间，兴高采烈，睁开天真的眼睛，马上却又眼皮半闭，视线充满厌烦，不知想到什么地方去了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Going home at night, Charles went over her words one by one, trying to recall them, to fill out their sense, that he might piece out the life she had lived before he knew her. But he never saw her in his thoughts other than he had seen her the first time, or as he had just left her. Then he asked himself what would become of her—if she would be married, and to whom! Alas! Old Rouault was rich, and she!—so beautiful! But Emma’s face always rose before his eyes, and a monotone, like the humming of a top, sounded in his ears, “If you should marry after all! If you should marry!” At night he could not sleep; his throat was parched; he was athirst. He got up to drink from the water-bottle and opened the window. The night was covered with stars, a warm wind blowing in the distance; the dogs were barking. He turned his head towards the Bertaux.","sentences":[{"en":"Going home at night, Charles went over her words one by one, trying to recall them, to fill out their sense, that he might piece out the life she had lived before he knew her.","zh":"查理夜晚回来，一句一句掂量她说过的话，试着一面追忆，一面补足意思，想把他还不认识她的那段生活为自己编造出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But he never saw her in his thoughts other than he had seen her the first time, or as he had just left her.","zh":"不过他所能想象到的她，和他第一次看见的她，永远不差分毫，不然的话，也就是前不多久，他刚离开她时的模样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he asked himself what would become of her—if she would be married, and to whom!","zh":"随后他问自己：她结了婚，会变成什么模样？而且嫁谁？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Alas!","zh":"唉！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Old Rouault was rich, and she!—so beautiful!","zh":"卢欧老爹很有钱，她呀！又…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Emma’s face always rose before his eyes, and a monotone, like the humming of a top, sounded in his ears, “If you should marry after all!","zh":"那样美！不过爱玛的脸总在眼前出现，有种单调的声音，仿佛一只陀螺在耳边嗡嗡道：“可是，假如你结婚的话！","scope":"group"},{"en":"If you should marry!”","zh":"那样美！不过爱玛的脸总在眼前出现，有种单调的声音，仿佛一只陀螺在耳边嗡嗡道：“可是，假如你结婚的话！","scope":"group"},{"en":"At night he could not sleep; his throat was parched; he was athirst.","zh":"假如你结婚的话！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He got up to drink from the water-bottle and opened the window.","zh":"他夜晚睡不着，喉咙发干，直想喝水，下床走到水罐跟前，打开窗户；满天星斗，吹来一阵热风，狗在远处吠叫。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The night was covered with stars, a warm wind blowing in the distance; the dogs were barking.","zh":"他夜晚睡不着，喉咙发干，直想喝水，下床走到水罐跟前，打开窗户；满天星斗，吹来一阵热风，狗在远处吠叫。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He turned his head towards the Bertaux.","zh":"他的头不由地转向拜尔托。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Thinking that, after all, he should lose nothing, Charles promised himself to ask her in marriage as soon as occasion offered, but each time such occasion did offer the fear of not finding the right words sealed his lips.","sentences":[{"en":"Thinking that, after all, he should lose nothing, Charles promised himself to ask her in marriage as soon as occasion offered, but each time such occasion did offer the fear of not finding the right words sealed his lips.","zh":"查理一想，反正没有什么损失，决计一有机会就求婚；但是每次机会来了，他又牢牢闭拢嘴唇，害怕找不到适当的字句。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Old Rouault would not have been sorry to be rid of his daughter, who was of no use to him in the house. In his heart he excused her, thinking her too clever for farming, a calling under the ban of Heaven, since one never saw a millionaire in it. Far from having made a fortune by it, the good man was losing every year; for if he was good in bargaining, in which he enjoyed the dodges of the trade, on the other hand, agriculture properly so called, and the internal management of the farm, suited him less than most people. He did not willingly take his hands out of his pockets, and did not spare expense in all that concerned himself, liking to eat well, to have good fires, and to sleep well. He liked old cider, underdone legs of mutton, glorias well beaten up. He took his meals in the kitchen alone, opposite the fire, on a little table brought to him all ready laid as on the stage.","sentences":[{"en":"Old Rouault would not have been sorry to be rid of his daughter, who was of no use to him in the house.","zh":"女儿在家，帮不了他什么忙，有人把她带走，卢欧老爹不至于难过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In his heart he excused her, thinking her too clever for farming, a calling under the ban of Heaven, since one never saw a millionaire in it.","zh":"他私下原谅她，觉得她才情高，不宜稼穑——老天爷瞧不上的行业，从来没有见过出一位百万富翁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Far from having made a fortune by it, the good man was losing every year; for if he was good in bargaining, in which he enjoyed the dodges of the trade, on the other hand, agriculture properly so called, and the internal management of the farm, suited him less than most people.","zh":"老头子不但不发财，而且年年蚀本：因为他谈交易虽说精明，喜欢耍耍本行的花枪，可是稼穑本身，还有田庄内部管理，对他说来，却没有再不相宜的了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He did not willingly take his hands out of his pockets, and did not spare expense in all that concerned himself, liking to eat well, to have good fires, and to sleep well.","zh":"他不高兴操劳，生活方面，一钱不省，衣、食、住，样样考究。他喜欢酽苹果酒、带血的烤羊腿、拌匀的光荣酒 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He liked old cider, underdone legs of mutton, glorias well beaten up.","zh":"他一个人在厨房用饭，小桌端到跟前，当着灶火，菜统统摆好，如同在戏台上一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He took his meals in the kitchen alone, opposite the fire, on a little table brought to him all ready laid as on the stage.","zh":"他一个人在厨房用饭，小桌端到跟前，当着灶火，菜统统摆好，如同在戏台上一样。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"When, therefore, he perceived that Charles’s cheeks grew red if near his daughter, which meant that he would propose for her one of these days, he chewed the cud of the matter beforehand. He certainly thought him a little meagre, and not quite the son-in-law he would have liked, but he was said to be well brought-up, economical, very learned, and no doubt would not make too many difficulties about the dowry. Now, as old Rouault would soon be forced to sell twenty-two acres of “his property,” as he owed a good deal to the mason, to the harness-maker, and as the shaft of the cider-press wanted renewing, “If he asks for her,” he said to himself, “I’ll give her to him.”","sentences":[{"en":"When, therefore, he perceived that Charles’s cheeks grew red if near his daughter, which meant that he would propose for her one of these days, he chewed the cud of the matter beforehand.","zh":"所以看见查理挨近他女儿就脸红——意味有一天，对方会为了她向他求婚，他便前前后后先考虑了一番。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He certainly thought him a little meagre, and not quite the son-in-law he would have liked, but he was said to be well brought-up, economical, very learned, and no doubt would not make too many difficulties about the dowry.","zh":"他觉得查理人有些单薄，不是他一直想望的一位女婿；不过人家说他品行端正，省吃俭用，很有学问，不用说，不会太计较陪嫁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now, as old Rouault would soon be forced to sell twenty-two acres of “his property,” as he owed a good deal to the mason, to the harness-maker, and as the shaft of the cider-press wanted renewing, “If he asks for her,” he said to himself, “I’ll give her to him.”","zh":"何况卢欧老爹欠泥瓦匠、马具商许多钱，压榨器的大轴又该调换，他的产业非卖掉二十二英亩应付不了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At Michaelmas Charles went to spend three days at the Bertaux.","sentences":[{"en":"At Michaelmas Charles went to spend three days at the Bertaux.","zh":"他想：“他问我要她的话，我就给他。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The last had passed like the others in procrastinating from hour to hour. Old Rouault was seeing him off; they were walking along the road full of ruts; they were about to part. This was the time. Charles gave himself as far as to the corner of the hedge, and at last, when past it—","sentences":[{"en":"The last had passed like the others in procrastinating from hour to hour.","zh":"圣米迦勒期间 查理来拜尔托待三天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Old Rouault was seeing him off; they were walking along the road full of ruts; they were about to part.","zh":"末一天像前两天一样过掉，一刻又一刻拖延。卢欧老爹送他一程；他们走了一条坑坑洼洼的小道，眼看就要分手；是时候了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This was the time.","zh":"末一天像前两天一样过掉，一刻又一刻拖延。卢欧老爹送他一程；他们走了一条坑坑洼洼的小道，眼看就要分手；是时候了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles gave himself as far as to the corner of the hedge, and at last, when past it—","zh":"查理盘算，走到篱笆角落，一定开口，最后过都过去了，他唧哝道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Monsieur Rouault,” he murmured, “I should like to say something to you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Monsieur Rouault,” he murmured, “I should like to say something to you.”","zh":"“卢欧先生，我打算同您谈一点事。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They stopped. Charles was silent.","sentences":[{"en":"They stopped.","zh":"他们站住，查理又不吱声了。卢欧老爹笑微微道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles was silent.","zh":"他们站住，查理又不吱声了。卢欧老爹笑微微道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Well, tell me your story. Don’t I know all about it?” said old Rouault, laughing softly.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, tell me your story.","zh":"“把您的事说给我听吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Don’t I know all about it?” said old Rouault, laughing softly.","zh":"我还有什么不清楚的！”查理结结巴巴道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Monsieur Rouault—Monsieur Rouault,” stammered Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“Monsieur Rouault—Monsieur Rouault,” stammered Charles.","zh":"“卢欧老爹…卢欧老爹…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I ask nothing better”, the farmer went on. “Although, no doubt, the little one is of my mind, still we must ask her opinion. So you get off—I’ll go back home. If it is ‘yes’, you needn’t return because of all the people about, and besides it would upset her too much. But so that you mayn’t be eating your heart, I’ll open wide the outer shutter of the window against the wall; you can see it from the back by leaning over the hedge.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I ask nothing better”, the farmer went on.","zh":"佃农 继续道：“就我来说，我是求之不得。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Although, no doubt, the little one is of my mind, still we must ask her opinion.","zh":"不用说，闺女和我是一个心思，不过总该问问她，才好算数。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So you get off—I’ll go back home.","zh":"好，您走吧；我把话带回去就是了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If it is ‘yes’, you needn’t return because of all the people about, and besides it would upset her too much.","zh":"答应的话，您听明白，用不着回转来，一则人多口杂，再则，也太让她难为情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But so that you mayn’t be eating your heart, I’ll open wide the outer shutter of the window against the wall; you can see it from the back by leaning over the hedge.”","zh":"不过为了免得您心焦，我会推开护窗板，一直推得贴住墙：您趴在篱笆上，从后头就望见了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he went off.","sentences":[{"en":"And he went off.","zh":"他走开了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles fastened his horse to a tree; he ran into the road and waited. Half an hour passed, then he counted nineteen minutes by his watch. Suddenly a noise was heard against the wall; the shutter had been thrown back; the hook was still swinging.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles fastened his horse to a tree; he ran into the road and waited.","zh":"查理把马拴在树上，跑到小径等待。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Half an hour passed, then he counted nineteen minutes by his watch.","zh":"过了半小时，后来他数表又数了十几分钟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Suddenly a noise was heard against the wall; the shutter had been thrown back; the hook was still swinging.","zh":"墙那边忽然起了响声；护窗板推开，钩子还直摆动。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day by nine o’clock he was at the farm. Emma blushed as he entered, and she gave a little forced laugh to keep herself in countenance. Old Rouault embraced his future son-in-law. The discussion of money matters was put off; moreover, there was plenty of time before them, as the marriage could not decently take place till Charles was out of mourning, that is to say, about the spring of the next year.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day by nine o’clock he was at the farm.","zh":"第二天，才九点钟，他就到了田庄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma blushed as he entered, and she gave a little forced laugh to keep herself in countenance.","zh":"爱玛见他进来，脸红了，碍着面子，勉强笑了一笑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Old Rouault embraced his future son-in-law.","zh":"卢欧老爹吻抱未婚女婿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The discussion of money matters was put off; moreover, there was plenty of time before them, as the marriage could not decently take place till Charles was out of mourning, that is to say, about the spring of the next year.","zh":"银钱事项留到日后再谈；而且他们目前有的是时间，因为办喜事，照规矩说，也该等到查理除服，就是说，开春前后。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The winter passed waiting for this. Mademoiselle Rouault was busy with her trousseau. Part of it was ordered at Rouen, and she made herself chemises and nightcaps after fashion-plates that she borrowed. When Charles visited the farmer, the preparations for the wedding were talked over; they wondered in what room they should have dinner; they dreamed of the number of dishes that would be wanted, and what should be entrees.","sentences":[{"en":"The winter passed waiting for this.","zh":"大家在期待中过了冬天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mademoiselle Rouault was busy with her trousseau.","zh":"卢欧小姐忙着办嫁妆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Part of it was ordered at Rouen, and she made herself chemises and nightcaps after fashion-plates that she borrowed.","zh":"一部分到鲁昂定制；她照借来的时装图样，做了一些衬衣、睡帽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When Charles visited the farmer, the preparations for the wedding were talked over; they wondered in what room they should have dinner; they dreamed of the number of dishes that would be wanted, and what should be entrees.","zh":"查理一来田庄，他们就谈婚礼筹划，研究酒席摆在哪一间屋子；他们考虑必需的菜肴道数、上什么正菜。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma would, on the contrary, have preferred to have a midnight wedding with torches, but old Rouault could not understand such an idea. So there was a wedding at which forty-three persons were present, at which they remained sixteen hours at table, began again the next day, and to some extent on the days following.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma would, on the contrary, have preferred to have a midnight wedding with torches, but old Rouault could not understand such an idea.","zh":"爱玛希望点火炬，半夜成亲 ；不过卢欧老爹根本不懂这种想法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So there was a wedding at which forty-three persons were present, at which they remained sixteen hours at table, began again the next day, and to some extent on the days following.","zh":"婚礼举行了，来了四十三位客人，酒席用了十六小时，第二天又开始，拖拖拉拉，一连吃了几天。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"1-4","part":1,"n":4,"title":"Part I · Chapter 4","titleZh":"上卷 · 4","paragraphs":[{"en":"The guests arrived early in carriages, in one-horse chaises, two-wheeled cars, old open gigs, waggonettes with leather hoods, and the young people from the nearer villages in carts, in which they stood up in rows, holding on to the sides so as not to fall, going at a trot and well shaken up. Some came from a distance of thirty miles, from Goderville, from Normanville, and from Cany.","sentences":[{"en":"The guests arrived early in carriages, in one-horse chaises, two-wheeled cars, old open gigs, waggonettes with leather hoods, and the young people from the nearer villages in carts, in which they stood up in rows, holding on to the sides so as not to fall, going at a trot and well shaken up.","zh":"客人老早乘车来了：一匹马拉的小货车、一排一排板凳的双轮车、没有车篷的老式轻便马车、挂了皮篷的搬运车；邻近村庄的年轻人，一排一排，站在大车里头，扶住车栏杆，生怕摔倒，因为马放开蹄子，车颠得厉害。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some came from a distance of thirty miles, from Goderville, from Normanville, and from Cany.","zh":"有的从十古里以外的高代镇、诺曼镇和喀尼来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"All the relatives of both families had been invited, quarrels between friends arranged, acquaintances long since lost sight of written to.","sentences":[{"en":"All the relatives of both families had been invited, quarrels between friends arranged, acquaintances long since lost sight of written to.","zh":"两家亲戚邀遍了；绝了交的朋友，又和好如初；长久不见的故旧，也捎了信去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"From time to time one heard the crack of a whip behind the hedge; then the gates opened, a chaise entered. Galloping up to the foot of the steps, it stopped short and emptied its load. They got down from all sides, rubbing knees and stretching arms. The ladies, wearing bonnets, had on dresses in the town fashion, gold watch chains, pelerines with the ends tucked into belts, or little coloured fichus fastened down behind with a pin, and that left the back of the neck bare. The lads, dressed like their papas, seemed uncomfortable in their new clothes (many that day hand-sewed their first pair of boots), and by their sides, speaking never a work, wearing the white dress of their first communion lengthened for the occasion were some big girls of fourteen or sixteen, cousins or elder sisters no doubt, rubicund, bewildered, their hair greasy with rose pomade, and very much afraid of dirtying their gloves. As there were not enough stable-boys to unharness all the carriages, the gentlemen turned up their sleeves and set about it themselves. According to their different social positions they wore tail-coats, overcoats, shooting jackets, cutaway-coats; fine tail-coats, redolent of family respectability, that only came out of the wardrobe on state occasions; overcoats with long tails flapping in the wind and round capes and pockets like sacks; shooting jackets of coarse cloth, generally worn with a cap with a brass-bound peak; very short cutaway-coats with two small buttons in the back, close together like a pair of eyes, and the tails of which seemed cut out of one piece by a carpenter’s hatchet. Some, too (but these, you may be sure, would sit at the bottom of the table), wore their best blouses—that is to say, with collars turned down to the shoulders, the back gathered into small plaits and the waist fastened very low down with a worked belt.","sentences":[{"en":"From time to time one heard the crack of a whip behind the hedge; then the gates opened, a chaise entered.","zh":"篱笆外不时传来鞭子的响声，栅栏门紧跟着开开，便见进来一辆小货车，直奔台阶第一级，猛一下子停住。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Galloping up to the foot of the steps, it stopped short and emptied its load.","zh":"篱笆外不时传来鞭子的响声，栅栏门紧跟着开开，便见进来一辆小货车，直奔台阶第一级，猛一下子停住。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They got down from all sides, rubbing knees and stretching arms.","zh":"乘客四面八方下来，揉揉膝盖，挺挺胸脯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The ladies, wearing bonnets, had on dresses in the town fashion, gold watch chains, pelerines with the ends tucked into belts, or little coloured fichus fastened down behind with a pin, and that left the back of the neck bare.","zh":"妇女戴帽子，穿城里款式的长裙，挂金表链，披小斗篷，下摆掖在带子底下，或者披小花肩巾，拿别针在背后别住，露出后颈。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The lads, dressed like their papas, seemed uncomfortable in their new clothes (many that day hand-sewed their first pair of boots), and by their sides, speaking never a work, wearing the white dress of their first communion lengthened for the occasion were some big girls of fourteen or sixteen, cousins or elder sisters no doubt, rubicund, bewildered, their hair greasy with rose pomade, and very much afraid of dirtying their gloves.","zh":"男孩子照爸爸的模样打扮，穿新上衣，倒像添了拘束（这一天，许多孩子还是生平第一遭穿靴子），他们旁边，闷声不响坐着一个十四岁或者十六岁的大姑娘，不用说，是他们的姐姐或者堂姐，穿着第一次圣体瞻礼时穿的白袍，为了这趟做客才又放长了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As there were not enough stable-boys to unharness all the carriages, the gentlemen turned up their sleeves and set about it themselves.","zh":"她们脸红红的，心慌慌的，头发厚厚地抹了玫瑰油，直怕碰脏手套。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"According to their different social positions they wore tail-coats, overcoats, shooting jackets, cutaway-coats; fine tail-coats, redolent of family respectability, that only came out of the wardrobe on state occasions; overcoats with long tails flapping in the wind and round capes and pockets like sacks; shooting jackets of coarse cloth, generally worn with a cap with a brass-bound peak; very short cutaway-coats with two small buttons in the back, close together like a pair of eyes, and the tails of which seemed cut out of one piece by a carpenter’s hatchet.","zh":"厩夫少，车来不及卸，老爷们挽起袖子，亲自动手。他们依照不同的社会身份，有的穿燕尾服，有的穿大衣，有的穿制服，有的穿小礼服——讲究的燕尾服受到一家老小的敬重，不逢大典，不从衣橱里拿出来；大衣是随风飘扬的宽下摆，圆筒领子，口袋一般大小的衣袋；粗布制服，寻常还来一顶铜箍帽檐制帽；小礼服很短，后背有两个纽子，聚在一道，好似一双眼睛，对襟就像木匠一斧子从一整块料子上劈下来的一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some, too (but these, you may be sure, would sit at the bottom of the table), wore their best blouses—that is to say, with collars turned down to the shoulders, the back gathered into small plaits and the waist fastened very low down with a worked belt.","zh":"有些人（这种人，当然应该敬陪末座）穿着出门穿的工人服，就是说，领子翻在肩膀上，后背打小褶子，一条缝好的带子，在顶低的地方勒紧了腰。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the shirts stood out from the chests like cuirasses! Everyone had just had his hair cut; ears stood out from the heads; they had been close-shaved; a few, even, who had had to get up before daybreak, and not been able to see to shave, had diagonal gashes under their noses or cuts the size of a three-franc piece along the jaws, which the fresh air en route had enflamed, so that the great white beaming faces were mottled here and there with red dabs.","sentences":[{"en":"And the shirts stood out from the chests like cuirasses!","zh":"胸脯上的衬衣都胀鼓鼓的，仿佛铠甲！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everyone had just had his hair cut; ears stood out from the heads; they had been close-shaved; a few, even, who had had to get up before daybreak, and not been able to see to shave, had diagonal gashes under their noses or cuts the size of a three-franc piece along the jaws, which the fresh air en route had enflamed, so that the great white beaming faces were mottled here and there with red dabs.","zh":"人人新理的发，耳朵露出，脸刮得溜光；有些人天不亮就起床，刮胡须看不清，不是鼻子底下来几道垂直伤口，就是沿上下颚剃掉一块块埃居大小的皮，路上冷风一吹发了炎，于是那些容光焕发的大白脸，像大理石般添上了一片片小小的淡红色印记。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The mairie was a mile and a half from the farm, and they went thither on foot, returning in the same way after the ceremony in the church. The procession, first united like one long coloured scarf that undulated across the fields, along the narrow path winding amid the green corn, soon lengthened out, and broke up into different groups that loitered to talk. The fiddler walked in front with his violin, gay with ribbons at its pegs. Then came the married pair, the relations, the friends, all following pell-mell; the children stayed behind amusing themselves plucking the bell-flowers from oat-ears, or playing amongst themselves unseen. Emma’s dress, too long, trailed a little on the ground; from time to time she stopped to pull it up, and then delicately, with her gloved hands, she picked off the coarse grass and the thistledowns, while Charles, empty handed, waited till she had finished. Old Rouault, with a new silk hat and the cuffs of his black coat covering his hands up to the nails, gave his arm to Madame Bovary senior. As to Monsieur Bovary senior, who, heartily despising all these folk, had come simply in a frock-coat of military cut with one row of buttons—he was passing compliments of the bar to a fair young peasant. She bowed, blushed, and did not know what to say. The other wedding guests talked of their business or played tricks behind each other’s backs, egging one another on in advance to be jolly. Those who listened could always catch the squeaking of the fiddler, who went on playing across the fields. When he saw that the rest were far behind he stopped to take breath, slowly rosined his bow, so that the strings should sound more shrilly, then set off again, by turns lowering and raising his neck, the better to mark time for himself. The noise of the instrument drove away the little birds from afar.","sentences":[{"en":"The mairie was a mile and a half from the farm, and they went thither on foot, returning in the same way after the ceremony in the church.","zh":"镇公所离田庄半古里远，去时步行，教堂行礼回来，仍是步行。行列起初齐齐整整，走在绿油油小麦之间的狭窄阡陌，曲曲折折，好似一条花披肩，在田野动荡起伏，不久拉长了，三三两两，放慢步子闲谈。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The procession, first united like one long coloured scarf that undulated across the fields, along the narrow path winding amid the green corn, soon lengthened out, and broke up into different groups that loitered to talk.","zh":"镇公所离田庄半古里远，去时步行，教堂行礼回来，仍是步行。行列起初齐齐整整，走在绿油油小麦之间的狭窄阡陌，曲曲折折，好似一条花披肩，在田野动荡起伏，不久拉长了，三三两两，放慢步子闲谈。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The fiddler walked in front with his violin, gay with ribbons at its pegs.","zh":"前面走着提琴手，提琴的卷轴扎了彩带；新人跟在后头，亲友随便走动；孩子们待在末尾，掐荞麦秆子尖尖的花儿玩，要不然就瞒着大人，自己玩耍。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then came the married pair, the relations, the friends, all following pell-mell; the children stayed behind amusing themselves plucking the bell-flowers from oat-ears, or playing amongst themselves unseen.","zh":"前面走着提琴手，提琴的卷轴扎了彩带；新人跟在后头，亲友随便走动；孩子们待在末尾，掐荞麦秆子尖尖的花儿玩，要不然就瞒着大人，自己玩耍。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma’s dress, too long, trailed a little on the ground; from time to time she stopped to pull it up, and then delicately, with her gloved hands, she picked off the coarse grass and the thistledowns, while Charles, empty handed, waited till she had finished.","zh":"爱玛的袍子太长，下摆有些拖来拖去，她不时停住往上拉拉，然后用戴手套的手指，灵巧敏捷地除去野草和蓟的小刺，查理空着两手，在旁边等她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Old Rouault, with a new silk hat and the cuffs of his black coat covering his hands up to the nails, gave his arm to Madame Bovary senior.","zh":"卢欧老爹戴一顶新缎帽，青燕尾服的硬袖连手指甲也盖住了。他挽着包法利太太。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to Monsieur Bovary senior, who, heartily despising all these folk, had come simply in a frock-coat of military cut with one row of buttons—he was passing compliments of the bar to a fair young peasant.","zh":"至于包法利老爹，心下看不起这群人，来时只穿一件一排纽扣的军式大衣，向一个金黄头发乡下姑娘，卖弄咖啡馆流行的情话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She bowed, blushed, and did not know what to say.","zh":"她行着礼，红着脸，不知如何回答才好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The other wedding guests talked of their business or played tricks behind each other’s backs, egging one another on in advance to be jolly.","zh":"别的贺客，谈着自己的事，要不就兴致勃勃地彼此在背后捣乱；提琴手一直在田野拉琴，咯吱咯吱的声音总在大家耳边响。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Those who listened could always catch the squeaking of the fiddler, who went on playing across the fields.","zh":"别的贺客，谈着自己的事，要不就兴致勃勃地彼此在背后捣乱；提琴手一直在田野拉琴，咯吱咯吱的声音总在大家耳边响。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When he saw that the rest were far behind he stopped to take breath, slowly rosined his bow, so that the strings should sound more shrilly, then set off again, by turns lowering and raising his neck, the better to mark time for himself.","zh":"他一看大家落远了，就站住歇口气，仔细给弓子上松香，弦子吱嘎起来，也好听些，然后举步又走，琴柄忽高忽低，帮自己打拍子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The noise of the instrument drove away the little birds from afar.","zh":"乐器的声音惊起小鸟，远远飞去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The table was laid under the cart-shed. On it were four sirloins, six chicken fricassees, stewed veal, three legs of mutton, and in the middle a fine roast suckling pig, flanked by four chitterlings with sorrel. At the corners were decanters of brandy. Sweet bottled-cider frothed round the corks, and all the glasses had been filled to the brim with wine beforehand. Large dishes of yellow cream, that trembled with the least shake of the table, had designed on their smooth surface the initials of the newly wedded pair in nonpareil arabesques. A confectioner of Yvetot had been intrusted with the tarts and sweets. As he had only just set up on the place, he had taken a lot of trouble, and at dessert he himself brought in a set dish that evoked loud cries of wonderment. To begin with, at its base there was a square of blue cardboard, representing a temple with porticoes, colonnades, and stucco statuettes all round, and in the niches constellations of gilt paper stars; then on the second stage was a dungeon of Savoy cake, surrounded by many fortifications in candied angelica, almonds, raisins, and quarters of oranges; and finally, on the upper platform a green field with rocks set in lakes of jam, nutshell boats, and a small Cupid balancing himself in a chocolate swing whose two uprights ended in real roses for balls at the top.","sentences":[{"en":"The table was laid under the cart-shed.","zh":"酒席摆在车棚底下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On it were four sirloins, six chicken fricassees, stewed veal, three legs of mutton, and in the middle a fine roast suckling pig, flanked by four chitterlings with sorrel.","zh":"菜有四份牛里脊，六份炒仔鸡、煨小牛肉，三只羊腿，当中一只烤乳猪，边上四根酸模香肠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the corners were decanters of brandy.","zh":"犄角是盛烧酒的水晶瓶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sweet bottled-cider frothed round the corks, and all the glasses had been filled to the brim with wine beforehand.","zh":"一瓶瓶甜苹果酒，围着瓶塞冒沫子，个个玻璃杯先斟满了酒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Large dishes of yellow cream, that trembled with the least shake of the table, had designed on their smooth surface the initials of the newly wedded pair in nonpareil arabesques.","zh":"桌子轻轻一动，大盘的黄色奶油就晃荡，表皮光溜溜的，上面画着新人名姓的第一个字母，用糖渍小杏缀成图案。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A confectioner of Yvetot had been intrusted with the tarts and sweets.","zh":"他们到伊弗托找来一位点心师傅，专做馅饼和杏仁糕。他在当地初次亮相，特别当心，上点心时，亲自捧出颤巍巍一盘东西，人人惊叫。","scope":"group"},{"en":"As he had only just set up on the place, he had taken a lot of trouble, and at dessert he himself brought in a set dish that evoked loud cries of wonderment.","zh":"他们到伊弗托找来一位点心师傅，专做馅饼和杏仁糕。他在当地初次亮相，特别当心，上点心时，亲自捧出颤巍巍一盘东西，人人惊叫。","scope":"group"},{"en":"To begin with, at its base there was a square of blue cardboard, representing a temple with porticoes, colonnades, and stucco statuettes all round, and in the niches constellations of gilt paper stars; then on the second stage was a dungeon of Savoy cake, surrounded by many fortifications in candied angelica, almonds, raisins, and quarters of oranges; and finally, on the upper platform a green field with rocks set in lakes of jam, nutshell boats, and a small Cupid balancing himself in a chocolate swing whose two uprights ended in real roses for balls at the top.","zh":"首先，底层是方方一块蓝硬纸板，剪成一座有门廊有柱子的庙宇，四周龛子撒了金纸星宿，当中塑着小神像；其次，二层是一座萨瓦蛋糕 望楼，周围是独活、杏仁、葡萄干、橘瓣做的玲珑碉堡；最后，上层平台，绿油油一片草地，有山石，有蜜饯湖泊，有榛子船只，还看见一位小爱神在打秋千：巧克力秋千架，两边柱头一边放一个真玫瑰花球。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Until night they ate. When any of them were too tired of sitting, they went out for a stroll in the yard, or for a game with corks in the granary, and then returned to table. Some towards the finish went to sleep and snored. But with the coffee everyone woke up. Then they began songs, showed off tricks, raised heavy weights, performed feats with their fingers, then tried lifting carts on their shoulders, made broad jokes, kissed the women. At night when they left, the horses, stuffed up to the nostrils with oats, could hardly be got into the shafts; they kicked, reared, the harness broke, their masters laughed or swore; and all night in the light of the moon along country roads there were runaway carts at full gallop plunging into the ditches, jumping over yard after yard of stones, clambering up the hills, with women leaning out from the tilt to catch hold of the reins.","sentences":[{"en":"Until night they ate.","zh":"大家一直吃到天黑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When any of them were too tired of sitting, they went out for a stroll in the yard, or for a game with corks in the granary, and then returned to table.","zh":"坐得太累了，大家到院子散步，或者到仓库玩瓶塞 ，然后回来再吃。临到散席，有些人睡着了打鼾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some towards the finish went to sleep and snored.","zh":"不过咖啡一来，大家又都有了生气，有人唱歌，有人表演，有人举重，有人钻大拇指 ，有人试扛大车，有人说玩笑话，有人吻抱妇女。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But with the coffee everyone woke up.","zh":"不过咖啡一来，大家又都有了生气，有人唱歌，有人表演，有人举重，有人钻大拇指 ，有人试扛大车，有人说玩笑话，有人吻抱妇女。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then they began songs, showed off tricks, raised heavy weights, performed feats with their fingers, then tried lifting carts on their shoulders, made broad jokes, kissed the women.","zh":"不过咖啡一来，大家又都有了生气，有人唱歌，有人表演，有人举重，有人钻大拇指 ，有人试扛大车，有人说玩笑话，有人吻抱妇女。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At night when they left, the horses, stuffed up to the nostrils with oats, could hardly be got into the shafts; they kicked, reared, the harness broke, their masters laughed or swore; and all night in the light of the moon along country roads there were runaway carts at full gallop plunging into the ditches, jumping over yard after yard of stones, clambering up the hills, with women leaning out from the tilt to catch hold of the reins.","zh":"马吃荞麦，吃到鼻子眼儿都是，夜晚动身，左右不肯套车，又踢，又跳，鞁带也挣断了，主子骂着，要不然就是笑着；整整一夜，月光如水，小货车沿着乡间大道疯狂奔驰，蹦水沟，跳石子堆，爬险坡，妇女身子探出车门来抓缰绳。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Those who stayed at the Bertaux spent the night drinking in the kitchen. The children had fallen asleep under the seats.","sentences":[{"en":"Those who stayed at the Bertaux spent the night drinking in the kitchen.","zh":"留在拜尔托的那些人，在厨房饮酒消夜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The children had fallen asleep under the seats.","zh":"孩子们早在板凳底下睡着了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The bride had begged her father to be spared the usual marriage pleasantries. However, a fishmonger, one of their cousins (who had even brought a pair of soles for his wedding present), began to squirt water from his mouth through the keyhole, when old Rouault came up just in time to stop him, and explain to him that the distinguished position of his son-in-law would not allow of such liberties. The cousin all the same did not give in to these reasons readily. In his heart he accused old Rouault of being proud, and he joined four or five other guests in a corner, who having, through mere chance, been several times running served with the worst helps of meat, also were of opinion they had been badly used, and were whispering about their host, and with covered hints hoping he would ruin himself.","sentences":[{"en":"The bride had begged her father to be spared the usual marriage pleasantries.","zh":"新娘子事先央求父亲，免去闹房习俗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"However, a fishmonger, one of their cousins (who had even brought a pair of soles for his wedding present), began to squirt water from his mouth through the keyhole, when old Rouault came up just in time to stop him, and explain to him that the distinguished position of his son-in-law would not allow of such liberties.","zh":"不料亲戚当中，有一个海鱼贩子（还带了一对比目鱼作贺仪），对准钥匙眼儿，拿嘴往里喷水；正巧他要喷水，卢欧老爹过来拦住，对他解释：女婿有身份，这样闹是不可以的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The cousin all the same did not give in to these reasons readily.","zh":"亲戚勉强依了，可是心里直嫌卢欧老爹傲气，走到一个角落，和另外四五个客人打成一伙；这几个人偶尔一连几回在席上吃了次肉，也认为主人亏待他们，就嘀嘀咕咕，话里带刺，咒他败家。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In his heart he accused old Rouault of being proud, and he joined four or five other guests in a corner, who having, through mere chance, been several times running served with the worst helps of meat, also were of opinion they had been badly used, and were whispering about their host, and with covered hints hoping he would ruin himself.","zh":"亲戚勉强依了，可是心里直嫌卢欧老爹傲气，走到一个角落，和另外四五个客人打成一伙；这几个人偶尔一连几回在席上吃了次肉，也认为主人亏待他们，就嘀嘀咕咕，话里带刺，咒他败家。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary, senior, had not opened her mouth all day. She had been consulted neither as to the dress of her daughter-in-law nor as to the arrangement of the feast; she went to bed early. Her husband, instead of following her, sent to Saint-Victor for some cigars, and smoked till daybreak, drinking kirsch-punch, a mixture unknown to the company. This added greatly to the consideration in which he was held.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary, senior, had not opened her mouth all day.","zh":"包法利老太太整日没有开口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had been consulted neither as to the dress of her daughter-in-law nor as to the arrangement of the feast; she went to bed early.","zh":"媳妇的梳妆、酒席的安排，全没有同她商量；她老早上了床。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her husband, instead of following her, sent to Saint-Victor for some cigars, and smoked till daybreak, drinking kirsch-punch, a mixture unknown to the company.","zh":"她的丈夫非但不跟她安息，反而差人到圣维克托买雪茄，吸到天明，一边拿樱桃酒兑上柠檬酒喝——这种掺和方式，在座的人因为不懂，分外敬重他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This added greatly to the consideration in which he was held.","zh":"她的丈夫非但不跟她安息，反而差人到圣维克托买雪茄，吸到天明，一边拿樱桃酒兑上柠檬酒喝——这种掺和方式，在座的人因为不懂，分外敬重他。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles, who was not of a facetious turn, did not shine at the wedding. He answered feebly to the puns, doubles entendres, compliments, and chaff that it was felt a duty to let off at him as soon as the soup appeared.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles, who was not of a facetious turn, did not shine at the wedding.","zh":"查理生性不诙谐，婚礼期间，并不出色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He answered feebly to the puns, doubles entendres, compliments, and chaff that it was felt a duty to let off at him as soon as the soup appeared.","zh":"从上汤起，贺客作为一种责任，朝他直说俏皮话、同音字、双关语、恭维话和猥亵话，他也就是应付而已。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day, on the other hand, he seemed another man. It was he who might rather have been taken for the virgin of the evening before, whilst the bride gave no sign that revealed anything. The shrewdest did not know what to make of it, and they looked at her when she passed near them with an unbounded concentration of mind. But Charles concealed nothing. He called her “my wife”, tutoyéd her, asked for her of everyone, looked for her everywhere, and often he dragged her into the yards, where he could be seen from far between the trees, putting his arm around her waist, and walking half-bending over her, ruffling the chemisette of her bodice with his head.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day, on the other hand, he seemed another man.","zh":"第二天，异乎寻常，他仿佛成了另一个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was he who might rather have been taken for the virgin of the evening before, whilst the bride gave no sign that revealed anything.","zh":"大家简直把他看成昨天的女郎，而新娘子若无其事，讳莫如深，就连最狡黠的人也猜不透她的心思；她走过他们身边，他们打量她，显出万分紧张的心情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The shrewdest did not know what to make of it, and they looked at her when she passed near them with an unbounded concentration of mind.","zh":"大家简直把他看成昨天的女郎，而新娘子若无其事，讳莫如深，就连最狡黠的人也猜不透她的心思；她走过他们身边，他们打量她，显出万分紧张的心情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But Charles concealed nothing.","zh":"可是查理什么也不掩饰。他喊她“我的太太”，称呼亲热，逢人问她，到处找她，时常把她拉到院子，人远远望去，就见他在树木中间，搂住她的腰，继续行走，身子弯过去，头蹭乱她胸前的花边。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He called her “my wife”, tutoyéd her, asked for her of everyone, looked for her everywhere, and often he dragged her into the yards, where he could be seen from far between the trees, putting his arm around her waist, and walking half-bending over her, ruffling the chemisette of her bodice with his head.","zh":"可是查理什么也不掩饰。他喊她“我的太太”，称呼亲热，逢人问她，到处找她，时常把她拉到院子，人远远望去，就见他在树木中间，搂住她的腰，继续行走，身子弯过去，头蹭乱她胸前的花边。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Two days after the wedding the married pair left. Charles, on account of his patients, could not be away longer. Old Rouault had them driven back in his cart, and himself accompanied them as far as Vassonville. Here he embraced his daughter for the last time, got down, and went his way. When he had gone about a hundred paces he stopped, and as he saw the cart disappearing, its wheels turning in the dust, he gave a deep sigh. Then he remembered his wedding, the old times, the first pregnancy of his wife; he, too, had been very happy the day when he had taken her from her father to his home, and had carried her off on a pillion, trotting through the snow, for it was near Christmas-time, and the country was all white. She held him by one arm, her basket hanging from the other; the wind blew the long lace of her Cauchois headdress so that it sometimes flapped across his mouth, and when he turned his head he saw near him, on his shoulder, her little rosy face, smiling silently under the gold bands of her cap. To warm her hands she put them from time to time in his breast. How long ago it all was! Their son would have been thirty by now. Then he looked back and saw nothing on the road. He felt dreary as an empty house; and tender memories mingling with the sad thoughts in his brain, addled by the fumes of the feast, he felt inclined for a moment to take a turn towards the church. As he was afraid, however, that this sight would make him yet more sad, he went right away home.","sentences":[{"en":"Two days after the wedding the married pair left.","zh":"婚后过了两天，新夫妇动身，查理要看病人，不便多待。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles, on account of his patients, could not be away longer.","zh":"婚后过了两天，新夫妇动身，查理要看病人，不便多待。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Old Rouault had them driven back in his cart, and himself accompanied them as far as Vassonville.","zh":"卢欧老爹套上他的小货车送他们，又亲自陪到法松镇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Here he embraced his daughter for the last time, got down, and went his way.","zh":"他在这里最后吻抱一次女儿，下了车，往回走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he had gone about a hundred paces he stopped, and as he saw the cart disappearing, its wheels turning in the dust, he gave a deep sigh.","zh":"他走上百十来步，站住望着小货车走远，轮子在尘土中滚动，长叹了一口气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he remembered his wedding, the old times, the first pregnancy of his wife; he, too, had been very happy the day when he had taken her from her father to his home, and had carried her off on a pillion, trotting through the snow, for it was near Christmas-time, and the country was all white.","zh":"接着他想起他的婚礼、他的往事、太太第一次怀孕；他从岳父家带她回去，这一天，他也很快活来的，她骑在他的背后，马踏着雪；因为当时是在圣诞节前后，田野正好白茫茫一片；她一只胳膊抱牢他，一只胳膊挎着她的篮子；帽子是科地样式，风吹动花边长帽带，有时候飘到嘴上；他一回头，就见她的小红脸蛋，贴紧他的肩膀，在她的金黄帽檐底下，静悄悄微笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She held him by one arm, her basket hanging from the other; the wind blew the long lace of her Cauchois headdress so that it sometimes flapped across his mouth, and when he turned his head he saw near him, on his shoulder, her little rosy face, smiling silently under the gold bands of her cap.","zh":"接着他想起他的婚礼、他的往事、太太第一次怀孕；他从岳父家带她回去，这一天，他也很快活来的，她骑在他的背后，马踏着雪；因为当时是在圣诞节前后，田野正好白茫茫一片；她一只胳膊抱牢他，一只胳膊挎着她的篮子；帽子是科地样式，风吹动花边长帽带，有时候飘到嘴上；他一回头，就见她的小红脸蛋，贴紧他的肩膀，在她的金黄帽檐底下，静悄悄微笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"To warm her hands she put them from time to time in his breast.","zh":"她为了取暖，不时拿手指伸进他的胸怀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How long ago it all was!","zh":"这一切，都多么遥远！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Their son would have been thirty by now.","zh":"他们的儿子，活到如今，该三十岁了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he looked back and saw nothing on the road.","zh":"他不由得朝后望望。路上一无所有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He felt dreary as an empty house; and tender memories mingling with the sad thoughts in his brain, addled by the fumes of the feast, he felt inclined for a moment to take a turn towards the church.","zh":"他觉得自己好生凄凉，活像一所空房子；热气腾腾的酒菜，早已冲昏头脑，现在横添上动情的回忆和悲伤的心情，他一时真想到教堂旁边 转上一转。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As he was afraid, however, that this sight would make him yet more sad, he went right away home.","zh":"不过他怕去了愁上加愁，就一直回家去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Monsieur and Madame Charles arrived at Tostes about six o’clock.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur and Madame Charles arrived at Tostes about six o’clock.","zh":"约莫六点钟光景，查理夫妇到了道特。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The neighbors came to the windows to see their doctor’s new wife.","sentences":[{"en":"The neighbors came to the windows to see their doctor’s new wife.","zh":"邻居凑到窗户跟前，看他们的医生的新夫人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The old servant presented herself, curtsied to her, apologised for not having dinner ready, and suggested that madame, in the meantime, should look over her house.","sentences":[{"en":"The old servant presented herself, curtsied to her, apologised for not having dinner ready, and suggested that madame, in the meantime, should look over her house.","zh":"老女佣过来同她见礼，道歉晚饭没有备好，请太太先认认她的住宅。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"1-5","part":1,"n":5,"title":"Part I · Chapter 5","titleZh":"上卷 · 5","paragraphs":[{"en":"The brick front was just in a line with the street, or rather the road. Behind the door hung a cloak with a small collar, a bridle, and a black leather cap, and on the floor, in a corner, were a pair of leggings, still covered with dry mud. On the right was the one apartment, that was both dining and sitting room. A canary yellow paper, relieved at the top by a garland of pale flowers, was puckered everywhere over the badly stretched canvas; white calico curtains with a red border hung crossways at the length of the window; and on the narrow mantelpiece a clock with a head of Hippocrates shone resplendent between two plate candlesticks under oval shades. On the other side of the passage was Charles’s consulting room, a little room about six paces wide, with a table, three chairs, and an office chair. Volumes of the “Dictionary of Medical Science,” uncut, but the binding rather the worse for the successive sales through which they had gone, occupied almost along the six shelves of a deal bookcase.","sentences":[{"en":"The brick front was just in a line with the street, or rather the road.","zh":"房子前脸，一砖到顶，正好沿街，或者不如说是沿路。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Behind the door hung a cloak with a small collar, a bridle, and a black leather cap, and on the floor, in a corner, were a pair of leggings, still covered with dry mud.","zh":"门后挂一件小领斗篷、一副马笼头、一顶黑皮便帽，角落地上扔一双皮裹腿，上面还有干泥。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the right was the one apartment, that was both dining and sitting room.","zh":"右手是厅房，就是说，饮食起居所在。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A canary yellow paper, relieved at the top by a garland of pale flowers, was puckered everywhere over the badly stretched canvas; white calico curtains with a red border hung crossways at the length of the window; and on the narrow mantelpiece a clock with a head of Hippocrates shone resplendent between two plate candlesticks under oval shades.","zh":"金丝雀黄糊墙纸，高头镶一道暗花，由于帆布底子没有铺平，整个在颤动，压红边的白布窗帘，叉开挂在窗口；壁炉台窄窄的，上面放一只亮闪闪的座钟，上面饰有希波克拉底 的头像，一边一支椭圆形罩子扣着的包银蜡烛台。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the other side of the passage was Charles’s consulting room, a little room about six paces wide, with a table, three chairs, and an office chair.","zh":"过道对面是查理的诊室，六步来宽的小屋，里头有一张桌子、三张椅子和一张大靠背扶手椅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Volumes of the “Dictionary of Medical Science,” uncut, but the binding rather the worse for the successive sales through which they had gone, occupied almost along the six shelves of a deal bookcase.","zh":"一个六格松木书架，单是《医学辞典》 ，差不多就占满了。辞典没有裁开 ，但是一次一次出卖，几经转手，装订早已损坏。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The smell of melted butter penetrated through the walls when he saw patients, just as in the kitchen one could hear the people coughing in the consulting room and recounting their histories.","sentences":[{"en":"The smell of melted butter penetrated through the walls when he saw patients, just as in the kitchen one could hear the people coughing in the consulting room and recounting their histories.","zh":"看病时候，隔墙透过来牛油融化的味道；人在厨房，同样听见病人在诊室咳嗽，诉说他们的病历。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, opening on the yard, where the stable was, came a large dilapidated room with a stove, now used as a wood-house, cellar, and pantry, full of old rubbish, of empty casks, agricultural implements past service, and a mass of dusty things whose use it was impossible to guess.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, opening on the yard, where the stable was, came a large dilapidated room with a stove, now used as a wood-house, cellar, and pantry, full of old rubbish, of empty casks, agricultural implements past service, and a mass of dusty things whose use it was impossible to guess.","zh":"再往里去，正对院子和马棚，是一间有灶的破烂大屋，现在当柴房、堆房、库房用，搁满废铁、空桶、失修的农具和许多别的东西，布满灰尘，也摸不清做什么用。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The garden, longer than wide, ran between two mud walls with espaliered apricots, to a hawthorn hedge that separated it from the field. In the middle was a slate sundial on a brick pedestal; four flower beds with eglantines surrounded symmetrically the more useful kitchen garden bed. Right at the bottom, under the spruce bushes, was a cure in plaster reading his breviary.","sentences":[{"en":"The garden, longer than wide, ran between two mud walls with espaliered apricots, to a hawthorn hedge that separated it from the field.","zh":"花园长过于宽，夹在土墙当中，沿墙是果实累累的杏树，靠近田野，有一道荆棘篱笆隔开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the middle was a slate sundial on a brick pedestal; four flower beds with eglantines surrounded symmetrically the more useful kitchen garden bed.","zh":"当中是一个石座青石日晷。四畦瘦小野蔷薇，互相对称，环绕着一块较为实用的方菜地。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Right at the bottom, under the spruce bushes, was a cure in plaster reading his breviary.","zh":"院子深处云杉底下，有一座读祷告书的石膏堂长像。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma went upstairs. The first room was not furnished, but in the second, which was their bedroom, was a mahogany bedstead in an alcove with red drapery. A shell box adorned the chest of drawers, and on the secretary near the window a bouquet of orange blossoms tied with white satin ribbons stood in a bottle. It was a bride’s bouquet; it was the other one’s. She looked at it. Charles noticed it; he took it and carried it up to the attic, while Emma seated in an arm-chair (they were putting her things down around her) thought of her bridal flowers packed up in a bandbox, and wondered, dreaming, what would be done with them if she were to die.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma went upstairs.","zh":"爱玛来到楼上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The first room was not furnished, but in the second, which was their bedroom, was a mahogany bedstead in an alcove with red drapery.","zh":"第一间没有家具。第二间是卧室，尽里凹处有一张红幔桃花心木床；还有一只蚌壳盒子，点缀五斗柜；窗边一张书桌，上面放着一个水晶瓶，里头插了一把白绫带束扎的橘花。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A shell box adorned the chest of drawers, and on the secretary near the window a bouquet of orange blossoms tied with white satin ribbons stood in a bottle.","zh":"第一间没有家具。第二间是卧室，尽里凹处有一张红幔桃花心木床；还有一只蚌壳盒子，点缀五斗柜；窗边一张书桌，上面放着一个水晶瓶，里头插了一把白绫带束扎的橘花。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was a bride’s bouquet; it was the other one’s.","zh":"这是新娘子的花、前人的花！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She looked at it.","zh":"她看着花。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles noticed it; he took it and carried it up to the attic, while Emma seated in an arm-chair (they were putting her things down around her) thought of her bridal flowers packed up in a bandbox, and wondered, dreaming, what would be done with them if she were to die.","zh":"查理发觉了，拿花放到阁楼；爱玛坐在一张扶手椅上（她带来的东西放在周围），想着纸匣里她的结婚的花，凝神自问，万一她死了，这束花又将如何。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"During the first days she occupied herself in thinking about changes in the house. She took the shades off the candlesticks, had new wallpaper put up, the staircase repainted, and seats made in the garden round the sundial; she even inquired how she could get a basin with a jet fountain and fishes. Finally her husband, knowing that she liked to drive out, picked up a second-hand dogcart, which, with new lamps and splashboard in striped leather, looked almost like a tilbury.","sentences":[{"en":"During the first days she occupied herself in thinking about changes in the house.","zh":"开头几天，她盘算着改动家里的布置，去掉蜡台的罩子 ，换上新糊墙纸，又漆一遍楼梯，花园日晷四周，搁了几条板凳。她甚至打听怎样安装喷水鱼池。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She took the shades off the candlesticks, had new wallpaper put up, the staircase repainted, and seats made in the garden round the sundial; she even inquired how she could get a basin with a jet fountain and fishes.","zh":"开头几天，她盘算着改动家里的布置，去掉蜡台的罩子 ，换上新糊墙纸，又漆一遍楼梯，花园日晷四周，搁了几条板凳。她甚至打听怎样安装喷水鱼池。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Finally her husband, knowing that she liked to drive out, picked up a second-hand dogcart, which, with new lamps and splashboard in striped leather, looked almost like a tilbury.","zh":"最后，丈夫知道她喜欢乘马车散心，买了一辆廉价出让的包克 ，装上新灯和防泥的花皮护带，宛然就是一辆提耳玻里 。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was happy then, and without a care in the world. A meal together, a walk in the evening on the highroad, a gesture of her hands over her hair, the sight of her straw hat hanging from the window-fastener, and many another thing in which Charles had never dreamed of pleasure, now made up the endless round of his happiness. In bed, in the morning, by her side, on the pillow, he watched the sunlight sinking into the down on her fair cheek, half hidden by the lappets of her night-cap. Seen thus closely, her eyes looked to him enlarged, especially when, on waking up, she opened and shut them rapidly many times. Black in the shade, dark blue in broad daylight, they had, as it were, depths of different colours, that, darker in the centre, grew paler towards the surface of the eye. His own eyes lost themselves in these depths; he saw himself in miniature down to the shoulders, with his handkerchief round his head and the top of his shirt open. He rose. She came to the window to see him off, and stayed leaning on the sill between two pots of geranium, clad in her dressing gown hanging loosely about her. Charles, in the street buckled his spurs, his foot on the mounting stone, while she talked to him from above, picking with her mouth some scrap of flower or leaf that she blew out at him. Then this, eddying, floating, described semicircles in the air like a bird, and was caught before it reached the ground in the ill-groomed mane of the old white mare standing motionless at the door. Charles from horseback threw her a kiss; she answered with a nod; she shut the window, and he set off. And then along the highroad, spreading out its long ribbon of dust, along the deep lanes that the trees bent over as in arbours, along paths where the corn reached to the knees, with the sun on his back and the morning air in his nostrils, his heart full of the joys of the past night, his mind at rest, his flesh at ease, he went on, re-chewing his happiness, like those who after dinner taste again the truffles which they are digesting.","sentences":[{"en":"He was happy then, and without a care in the world.","zh":"于是他快乐，无忧无虑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A meal together, a walk in the evening on the highroad, a gesture of her hands over her hair, the sight of her straw hat hanging from the window-fastener, and many another thing in which Charles had never dreamed of pleasure, now made up the endless round of his happiness.","zh":"两个人面对面用饭、黄昏在大路散步、她的手整理头发的姿势、她的草帽挂在窗户开关上的形象和许多查理梦想不到的欢愉，如今都是他连绵不断的幸福的组成部分。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In bed, in the morning, by her side, on the pillow, he watched the sunlight sinking into the down on her fair cheek, half hidden by the lappets of her night-cap.","zh":"早晨他躺在床上，枕着枕头，在她旁边，看阳光射过她可爱的脸蛋的汗毛，睡帽带子有齿形缀饰，遮住一半她的脸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Seen thus closely, her eyes looked to him enlarged, especially when, on waking up, she opened and shut them rapidly many times.","zh":"看得这样近，他觉得她的眼睛大了，特别是她醒过来，一连几次睁开眼睑的时候；阴影过来，眼睛是黑的，阳光过来，成了深蓝，仿佛具有层层叠叠的颜色，深处最浓，越近珐琅质表面越淡。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Black in the shade, dark blue in broad daylight, they had, as it were, depths of different colours, that, darker in the centre, grew paler towards the surface of the eye.","zh":"看得这样近，他觉得她的眼睛大了，特别是她醒过来，一连几次睁开眼睑的时候；阴影过来，眼睛是黑的，阳光过来，成了深蓝，仿佛具有层层叠叠的颜色，深处最浓，越近珐琅质表面越淡。","scope":"group"},{"en":"His own eyes lost themselves in these depths; he saw himself in miniature down to the shoulders, with his handkerchief round his head and the top of his shirt open.","zh":"他自己的视线消失在颜色最深的地方，他看见里面有一个小我，到肩膀为止，另外还有包头帕子和他的衬衫领口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He rose.","zh":"他下了床。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She came to the window to see him off, and stayed leaning on the sill between two pots of geranium, clad in her dressing gown hanging loosely about her.","zh":"她来到窗前，看他动身，胳膊肘拄着窗台，一边放一盆天竺葵，穿着她的梳妆衣，松松的，搭在身子周围。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles, in the street buckled his spurs, his foot on the mounting stone, while she talked to him from above, picking with her mouth some scrap of flower or leaf that she blew out at him.","zh":"查理在街上蹬住界石，扣牢刺马距；她在楼上继续和他说话，咬下一瓣花或者一片叶来，朝他吹过去，鸟儿似的，一时飞翔，一时停顿，在空中形成一些半圆圈，飘向门口安详的老白牝马的蓬乱鬣毛，待了待，这才落到地上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then this, eddying, floating, described semicircles in the air like a bird, and was caught before it reached the ground in the ill-groomed mane of the old white mare standing motionless at the door.","zh":"查理在街上蹬住界石，扣牢刺马距；她在楼上继续和他说话，咬下一瓣花或者一片叶来，朝他吹过去，鸟儿似的，一时飞翔，一时停顿，在空中形成一些半圆圈，飘向门口安详的老白牝马的蓬乱鬣毛，待了待，这才落到地上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles from horseback threw her a kiss; she answered with a nod; she shut the window, and he set off.","zh":"查理在马上送她一个吻；她摆摆手，关上窗户，他便出发了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then along the highroad, spreading out its long ribbon of dust, along the deep lanes that the trees bent over as in arbours, along paths where the corn reached to the knees, with the sun on his back and the morning air in his nostrils, his heart full of the joys of the past night, his mind at rest, his flesh at ease, he went on, re-chewing his happiness, like those who after dinner taste again the truffles which they are digesting.","zh":"他走大路，路上尘土飞扬，如同一条长带子，无终无了；或者走坑坑洼洼的小道，树木弯弯曲曲，好似棚架一般；或者走田垄，小麦一直齐到腿弯子，他的双肩洒满阳光，鼻孔吸着早晨的空气，心中充满夜晚的欢愉，精神平静，肉体满足，他咀嚼他的幸福，就像饭后消化中还在回味口蘑的滋味一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Until now what good had he had of his life? His time at school, when he remained shut up within the high walls, alone, in the midst of companions richer than he or cleverer at their work, who laughed at his accent, who jeered at his clothes, and whose mothers came to the school with cakes in their muffs? Later on, when he studied medicine, and never had his purse full enough to treat some little work-girl who would have become his mistress? Afterwards, he had lived fourteen months with the widow, whose feet in bed were cold as icicles. But now he had for life this beautiful woman whom he adored. For him the universe did not extend beyond the circumference of her petticoat, and he reproached himself with not loving her. He wanted to see her again; he turned back quickly, ran up the stairs with a beating heart. Emma, in her room, was dressing; he came up on tiptoe, kissed her back; she gave a cry.","sentences":[{"en":"Until now what good had he had of his life?","zh":"在这以前，他生活哪一点称心如意？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His time at school, when he remained shut up within the high walls, alone, in the midst of companions richer than he or cleverer at their work, who laughed at his accent, who jeered at his clothes, and whose mothers came to the school with cakes in their muffs?","zh":"难道是中学时期？关在那些高墙中间，孤零零一个人，班上同学全比他有钱，有气力，他的口音逗他们发笑，他们奚落他的服装，他们的母亲来到会客室，皮手筒里带着点心。难道是后来学医的时期？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Later on, when he studied medicine, and never had his purse full enough to treat some little work-girl who would have become his mistress?","zh":"钱口袋永远瘪瘪的，一个做工的女孩子明明可以当他的姘头，因为她陪他跳双人舞的钱，他付不出，也告吹了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Afterwards, he had lived fourteen months with the widow, whose feet in bed were cold as icicles.","zh":"此后他和寡妇一道过了十四个月，她那双脚在床上就像冰块一样凉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But now he had for life this beautiful woman whom he adored.","zh":"可是现在，他心爱的这个标致女子，他能一辈子占有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For him the universe did not extend beyond the circumference of her petticoat, and he reproached himself with not loving her.","zh":"宇宙在他，不超过她的纺绸衬裙的幅员；他责备自己爱她爱得不够，想再回去看看她；他迅速回家，走上楼梯，心直扑腾。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He wanted to see her again; he turned back quickly, ran up the stairs with a beating heart.","zh":"宇宙在他，不超过她的纺绸衬裙的幅员；他责备自己爱她爱得不够，想再回去看看她；他迅速回家，走上楼梯，心直扑腾。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma, in her room, was dressing; he came up on tiptoe, kissed her back; she gave a cry.","zh":"爱玛正在房间梳洗；他潜着脚步，走到跟前，吻她的背，她猛吃一惊，叫了起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He could not keep from constantly touching her comb, her ring, her fichu; sometimes he gave her great sounding kisses with all his mouth on her cheeks, or else little kisses in a row all along her bare arm from the tip of her fingers up to her shoulder, and she put him away half-smiling, half-vexed, as you do a child who hangs about you.","sentences":[{"en":"He could not keep from constantly touching her comb, her ring, her fichu; sometimes he gave her great sounding kisses with all his mouth on her cheeks, or else little kisses in a row all along her bare arm from the tip of her fingers up to her shoulder, and she put him away half-smiling, half-vexed, as you do a child who hangs about you.","zh":"他一来就忍不住摸摸她的篦梳、她的戒指、她的肩巾；有时候他张开嘴，大吻她的脸蛋，要不然就顺着她的光胳膊，一路小吻下去，从手指尖一直吻到肩膀；她推开他，半微笑，半腻烦，好像对付一个死跟在你后头的小孩子一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Before marriage she thought herself in love; but the happiness that should have followed this love not having come, she must, she thought, have been mistaken. And Emma tried to find out what one meant exactly in life by the words felicity, passion, rapture, that had seemed to her so beautiful in books.","sentences":[{"en":"Before marriage she thought herself in love; but the happiness that should have followed this love not having come, she must, she thought, have been mistaken.","zh":"结婚以前，她以为自己有爱情；可是应当从这种爱情得到的幸福不见来，她想，一定是自己弄错了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And Emma tried to find out what one meant exactly in life by the words felicity, passion, rapture, that had seemed to her so beautiful in books.","zh":"欢愉、热情和迷恋这些字眼，从前在书上读到，她觉得那样美，那么在生活中，到底该怎样正确理解呢，爱玛极想知道。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"1-6","part":1,"n":6,"title":"Part I · Chapter 6","titleZh":"上卷 · 6","paragraphs":[{"en":"She had read “Paul and Virginia,” and she had dreamed of the little bamboo-house, the nigger Domingo, the dog Fidele, but above all of the sweet friendship of some dear little brother, who seeks red fruit for you on trees taller than steeples, or who runs barefoot over the sand, bringing you a bird’s nest.","sentences":[{"en":"She had read “Paul and Virginia,” and she had dreamed of the little bamboo-house, the nigger Domingo, the dog Fidele, but above all of the sweet friendship of some dear little brother, who seeks red fruit for you on trees taller than steeples, or who runs barefoot over the sand, bringing you a bird’s nest.","zh":"她读过《保尔和维吉妮》 ，梦见小竹房子、黑人多明戈、名唤“忠心”的狗，特别是，一个好心小哥哥，情意缠绵，爬上比钟楼还高的大树，给你摘红果子，或者赤脚在沙地跑，给你带来一个鸟窠。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When she was thirteen, her father himself took her to town to place her in the convent. They stopped at an inn in the St. Gervais quarter, where, at their supper, they used painted plates that set forth the story of Mademoiselle de la Valliere. The explanatory legends, chipped here and there by the scratching of knives, all glorified religion, the tendernesses of the heart, and the pomps of court.","sentences":[{"en":"When she was thirteen, her father himself took her to town to place her in the convent.","zh":"十三岁上，父亲送她去修道院，亲自带她进城 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They stopped at an inn in the St. Gervais quarter, where, at their supper, they used painted plates that set forth the story of Mademoiselle de la Valliere.","zh":"他们投宿在圣热尔韦区一家客店，晚饭用的盘子，画着拉瓦利埃尔小姐 的故事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The explanatory legends, chipped here and there by the scratching of knives, all glorified religion, the tendernesses of the heart, and the pomps of court.","zh":"解释传说的文字，句句宣扬宗教、心地的温柔以及宫廷的辉煌景象，可是东一道印，西一道印，划来划去，上下文连不起来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Far from being bored at first at the convent, she took pleasure in the society of the good sisters, who, to amuse her, took her to the chapel, which one entered from the refectory by a long corridor. She played very little during recreation hours, knew her catechism well, and it was she who always answered Monsieur le Vicaire’s difficult questions. Living thus, without ever leaving the warm atmosphere of the classrooms, and amid these pale-faced women wearing rosaries with brass crosses, she was softly lulled by the mystic languor exhaled in the perfumes of the altar, the freshness of the holy water, and the lights of the tapers. Instead of attending to mass, she looked at the pious vignettes with their azure borders in her book, and she loved the sick lamb, the sacred heart pierced with sharp arrows, or the poor Jesus sinking beneath the cross he carries. She tried, by way of mortification, to eat nothing a whole day. She puzzled her head to find some vow to fulfil.","sentences":[{"en":"Far from being bored at first at the convent, she took pleasure in the society of the good sisters, who, to amuse her, took her to the chapel, which one entered from the refectory by a long corridor.","zh":"她在修道院，起初不但不嫌憋闷，反而喜欢和修女们在一起相处。她们要她开心，领她穿过一条长廊，走出饭厅，去看礼拜堂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She played very little during recreation hours, knew her catechism well, and it was she who always answered Monsieur le Vicaire’s difficult questions.","zh":"休息时间，她很少游戏，把教理问答记得滚瓜烂熟，有了难题，总是由她回答主教助理先生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Living thus, without ever leaving the warm atmosphere of the classrooms, and amid these pale-faced women wearing rosaries with brass crosses, she was softly lulled by the mystic languor exhaled in the perfumes of the altar, the freshness of the holy water, and the lights of the tapers.","zh":"她终日生活在教室的温暖气氛里，在这些面色苍白、挂着铜十字架念珠的妇女中间，加之圣坛的芳香、圣水的清冽和蜡烛的光辉散发出一种神秘的魅力，日子一久，她也就逐渐绵软无力了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Instead of attending to mass, she looked at the pious vignettes with their azure borders in her book, and she loved the sick lamb, the sacred heart pierced with sharp arrows, or the poor Jesus sinking beneath the cross he carries.","zh":"她不听弥撒，只盯着书上天蓝框子的圣画；她爱害病的绵羊、利箭穿过的圣心或者边走边倒在十字架上的可怜的耶稣 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She tried, by way of mortification, to eat nothing a whole day.","zh":"她练习苦行，试着一天不吃饭，还左思右想，要许一个愿。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She puzzled her head to find some vow to fulfil.","zh":"她练习苦行，试着一天不吃饭，还左思右想，要许一个愿。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"When she went to confession, she invented little sins in order that she might stay there longer, kneeling in the shadow, her hands joined, her face against the grating beneath the whispering of the priest. The comparisons of betrothed, husband, celestial lover, and eternal marriage, that recur in sermons, stirred within her soul depths of unexpected sweetness.","sentences":[{"en":"When she went to confession, she invented little sins in order that she might stay there longer, kneeling in the shadow, her hands joined, her face against the grating beneath the whispering of the priest.","zh":"临到忏悔，她为了多待一会儿，便编造一些小罪过，跪在暗处，双手合十，脸贴住栅栏门，听教士喃喃低语。布道中间说起的那些比喻，诸如未婚夫、丈夫、天上的情人和永恒的婚姻等，总在她灵魂深处唤起意想不到的喜悦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The comparisons of betrothed, husband, celestial lover, and eternal marriage, that recur in sermons, stirred within her soul depths of unexpected sweetness.","zh":"临到忏悔，她为了多待一会儿，便编造一些小罪过，跪在暗处，双手合十，脸贴住栅栏门，听教士喃喃低语。布道中间说起的那些比喻，诸如未婚夫、丈夫、天上的情人和永恒的婚姻等，总在她灵魂深处唤起意想不到的喜悦。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"In the evening, before prayers, there was some religious reading in the study. On week-nights it was some abstract of sacred history or the Lectures of the Abbe Frayssinous, and on Sundays passages from the “Genie du Christianisme,” as a recreation. How she listened at first to the sonorous lamentations of its romantic melancholies reechoing through the world and eternity! If her childhood had been spent in the shop-parlour of some business quarter, she might perhaps have opened her heart to those lyrical invasions of Nature, which usually come to us only through translation in books. But she knew the country too well; she knew the lowing of cattle, the milking, the ploughs.","sentences":[{"en":"In the evening, before prayers, there was some religious reading in the study.","zh":"晚祷之前，在自习室读宗教作品。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On week-nights it was some abstract of sacred history or the Lectures of the Abbe Frayssinous, and on Sundays passages from the “Genie du Christianisme,” as a recreation.","zh":"星期一到星期六，读一些圣史节要，或者福雷西路斯院长的《讲演录》 ；星期日读几段《基督教真谛》 作为消遣。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How she listened at first to the sonorous lamentations of its romantic melancholies reechoing through the world and eternity!","zh":"浪漫主义的忧郁，回应大地和永生，随时随地，发出嘹亮的哭诉，她头几回听了，十分入神！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If her childhood had been spent in the shop-parlour of some business quarter, she might perhaps have opened her heart to those lyrical invasions of Nature, which usually come to us only through translation in books.","zh":"我们接受自然的感染，通常要靠作品做媒介，她的童年如果是在商业区店铺后屋度过，她也许容易受到感染，可是她太熟悉田野，熟悉牲畜的叫声，懂得乳品和犁铧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But she knew the country too well; she knew the lowing of cattle, the milking, the ploughs.","zh":"我们接受自然的感染，通常要靠作品做媒介，她的童年如果是在商业区店铺后屋度过，她也许容易受到感染，可是她太熟悉田野，熟悉牲畜的叫声，懂得乳品和犁铧。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Accustomed to calm aspects of life, she turned, on the contrary, to those of excitement. She loved the sea only for the sake of its storms, and the green fields only when broken up by ruins.","sentences":[{"en":"Accustomed to calm aspects of life, she turned, on the contrary, to those of excitement.","zh":"她看惯了安静的风物，反过来喜好刺激。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She loved the sea only for the sake of its storms, and the green fields only when broken up by ruins.","zh":"她爱海只爱海的惊涛骇浪，爱青草仅仅爱青草遍生于废墟之间。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She wanted to get some personal profit out of things, and she rejected as useless all that did not contribute to the immediate desires of her heart, being of a temperament more sentimental than artistic, looking for emotions, not landscapes.","sentences":[{"en":"She wanted to get some personal profit out of things, and she rejected as useless all that did not contribute to the immediate desires of her heart, being of a temperament more sentimental than artistic, looking for emotions, not landscapes.","zh":"她必须从事物得到某种好处；凡不能直接有助于她的感情发泄的，她就看成无用之物，弃置不顾——正因为天性多感，远在艺术爱好之上，她寻找的是情绪，并非风景。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At the convent there was an old maid who came for a week each month to mend the linen. Patronized by the clergy, because she belonged to an ancient family of noblemen ruined by the Revolution, she dined in the refectory at the table of the good sisters, and after the meal had a bit of chat with them before going back to her work. The girls often slipped out from the study to go and see her. She knew by heart the love songs of the last century, and sang them in a low voice as she stitched away.","sentences":[{"en":"At the convent there was an old maid who came for a week each month to mend the linen.","zh":"有一个老姑娘，每月来修道院，做一星期女红。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Patronized by the clergy, because she belonged to an ancient family of noblemen ruined by the Revolution, she dined in the refectory at the table of the good sisters, and after the meal had a bit of chat with them before going back to her work.","zh":"因为她是大革命摧毁的一个世家的后裔，有大主教保护，她和修女们一道在饭厅用饭，饭后和她们闲聊一会儿，再做女红。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The girls often slipped out from the study to go and see her.","zh":"住堂生常常溜出教室看她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She knew by heart the love songs of the last century, and sang them in a low voice as she stitched away.","zh":"前一世纪有些情歌，她还记得，一边捻针走线，一边曼声低唱起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She told stories, gave them news, went errands in the town, and on the sly lent the big girls some novel, that she always carried in the pockets of her apron, and of which the good lady herself swallowed long chapters in the intervals of her work. They were all love, lovers, sweethearts, persecuted ladies fainting in lonely pavilions, postilions killed at every stage, horses ridden to death on every page, sombre forests, heartaches, vows, sobs, tears and kisses, little skiffs by moonlight, nightingales in shady groves, “gentlemen” brave as lions, gentle as lambs, virtuous as no one ever was, always well dressed, and weeping like fountains. For six months, then, Emma, at fifteen years of age, made her hands dirty with books from old lending libraries.","sentences":[{"en":"She told stories, gave them news, went errands in the town, and on the sly lent the big girls some novel, that she always carried in the pockets of her apron, and of which the good lady herself swallowed long chapters in the intervals of her work.","zh":"她讲故事，报告新闻，替你上街买东西，围裙袋里总有一部传奇小说，私下借给大女孩子看，老姑娘休息的时候，自己也是一章一章拼命看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were all love, lovers, sweethearts, persecuted ladies fainting in lonely pavilions, postilions killed at every stage, horses ridden to death on every page, sombre forests, heartaches, vows, sobs, tears and kisses, little skiffs by moonlight, nightingales in shady groves, “gentlemen” brave as lions, gentle as lambs, virtuous as no one ever was, always well dressed, and weeping like fountains.","zh":"书上无非是恋爱、情男、情女、在冷清的亭子晕倒的落难命妇、站站遇害的驿夫、页页倒毙的马匹、阴暗的森林、心乱、立誓、呜咽、眼泪与吻、月下小艇、林中夜莺，公子勇敢如狮，温柔如羔羊，人品无双，永远衣冠楚楚，哭起来泪如泉涌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For six months, then, Emma, at fifteen years of age, made her hands dirty with books from old lending libraries.","zh":"就这样，爱玛在十五岁上，有半年之久，一双手沾满了古老书报租阅处的灰尘。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Through Walter Scott, later on, she fell in love with historical events, dreamed of old chests, guard-rooms and minstrels. She would have liked to live in some old manor-house, like those long-waisted chatelaines who, in the shade of pointed arches, spent their days leaning on the stone, chin in hand, watching a cavalier with white plume galloping on his black horse from the distant fields. At this time she had a cult for Mary Stuart and enthusiastic veneration for illustrious or unhappy women. Joan of Arc, Heloise, Agnes Sorel, the beautiful Ferroniere, and Clemence Isaure stood out to her like comets in the dark immensity of heaven, where also were seen, lost in shadow, and all unconnected, St. Louis with his oak, the dying Bayard, some cruelties of Louis XI, a little of St. Bartholomew’s Day, the plume of the Bearnais, and always the remembrance of the plates painted in honour of Louis XIV.","sentences":[{"en":"Through Walter Scott, later on, she fell in love with historical events, dreamed of old chests, guard-rooms and minstrels.","zh":"后来她读司各特 ，醉心历史事物，梦想着大皮柜、警卫室和行吟诗人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would have liked to live in some old manor-house, like those long-waisted chatelaines who, in the shade of pointed arches, spent their days leaning on the stone, chin in hand, watching a cavalier with white plume galloping on his black horse from the distant fields.","zh":"她巴不得自己也住在一所古老庄园，如同那些腰身细长的女庄主一样，整天在三叶形穹隆底下，胳膊肘支着石头，手托住下巴，遥望一位白羽骑士，胯下一匹黑马，从田野远处疾驰而来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At this time she had a cult for Mary Stuart and enthusiastic veneration for illustrious or unhappy women.","zh":"她当时崇拜玛丽·斯图亚特 ，衷心尊敬那些出名或者不幸的妇女。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Joan of Arc, Heloise, Agnes Sorel, the beautiful Ferroniere, and Clemence Isaure stood out to her like comets in the dark immensity of heaven, where also were seen, lost in shadow, and all unconnected, St. Louis with his oak, the dying Bayard, some cruelties of Louis XI, a little of St. Bartholomew’s Day, the plume of the Bearnais, and always the remembrance of the plates painted in honour of Louis XIV.","zh":"在她看来，贞德、爱洛伊丝、阿涅丝·索雷尔、美人拉弗隆与克莱芒丝·伊索尔， 超群出众，彗星一般，扫过历史的黑暗天空，而圣路易与他的橡树、临死的巴雅尔、路易十一的若干暴行、圣巴托罗缪的一些情况、贝恩人的羽翎和颂扬路易十四的彩盘的经久不忘的回忆， 虽然东一闪，西一闪，也在天空出现，但是彼此之间毫无关联，因而长夜漫漫，越发不见形迹。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the music class, in the ballads she sang, there was nothing but little angels with golden wings, madonnas, lagunes, gondoliers;-mild compositions that allowed her to catch a glimpse athwart the obscurity of style and the weakness of the music of the attractive phantasmagoria of sentimental realities. Some of her companions brought “keepsakes” given them as new year’s gifts to the convent. These had to be hidden; it was quite an undertaking; they were read in the dormitory. Delicately handling the beautiful satin bindings, Emma looked with dazzled eyes at the names of the unknown authors, who had signed their verses for the most part as counts or viscounts.","sentences":[{"en":"In the music class, in the ballads she sang, there was nothing but little angels with golden wings, madonnas, lagunes, gondoliers;-mild compositions that allowed her to catch a glimpse athwart the obscurity of style and the weakness of the music of the attractive phantasmagoria of sentimental realities.","zh":"她在音乐课上唱的歌，不外乎金翅膀的小天使、圣母、潟湖、贡多拉船夫， 全是一些悠闲之作，文字拙劣，曲调轻浮，她在这里，影影绰绰看见感情世界的动人形象。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some of her companions brought “keepsakes” given them as new year’s gifts to the convent.","zh":"有些同学，年节贺礼收到诗文并茂的画册，带到修道院来，必须藏好；查出来，非同小可；她们躲在寝室读。","scope":"group"},{"en":"These had to be hidden; it was quite an undertaking; they were read in the dormitory.","zh":"有些同学，年节贺礼收到诗文并茂的画册，带到修道院来，必须藏好；查出来，非同小可；她们躲在寝室读。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Delicately handling the beautiful satin bindings, Emma looked with dazzled eyes at the names of the unknown authors, who had signed their verses for the most part as counts or viscounts.","zh":"爱玛小心翼翼，掀开美丽的锦缎封面，就见每首诗文底下，陌生作家署名，大多数不是伯爵，就是子爵，这些名字让她看呆了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She trembled as she blew back the tissue paper over the engraving and saw it folded in two and fall gently against the page. Here behind the balustrade of a balcony was a young man in a short cloak, holding in his arms a young girl in a white dress wearing an alms-bag at her belt; or there were nameless portraits of English ladies with fair curls, who looked at you from under their round straw hats with their large clear eyes. Some there were lounging in their carriages, gliding through parks, a greyhound bounding along in front of the equipage driven at a trot by two midget postilions in white breeches. Others, dreaming on sofas with an open letter, gazed at the moon through a slightly open window half draped by a black curtain. The naive ones, a tear on their cheeks, were kissing doves through the bars of a Gothic cage, or, smiling, their heads on one side, were plucking the leaves of a marguerite with their taper fingers, that curved at the tips like peaked shoes. And you, too, were there, Sultans with long pipes reclining beneath arbours in the arms of Bayaderes; Djiaours, Turkish sabres, Greek caps; and you especially, pale landscapes of dithyrambic lands, that often show us at once palm trees and firs, tigers on the right, a lion to the left, Tartar minarets on the horizon; the whole framed by a very neat virgin forest, and with a great perpendicular sunbeam trembling in the water, where, standing out in relief like white excoriations on a steel-grey ground, swans are swimming about.","sentences":[{"en":"She trembled as she blew back the tissue paper over the engraving and saw it folded in two and fall gently against the page.","zh":"她战战兢兢，吹开保护画幅的绢纸；绢纸掀起一半，又轻轻落下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Here behind the balustrade of a balcony was a young man in a short cloak, holding in his arms a young girl in a white dress wearing an alms-bag at her belt; or there were nameless portraits of English ladies with fair curls, who looked at you from under their round straw hats with their large clear eyes.","zh":"上面画的是：阳台栏杆后面，一个穿短斗篷的青年男子，搂住一个腰带挂着布施袋的白袍少女；要不然就是英吉利贵妇的无名画像，金黄发环，戴圆草帽，睁开又大又亮的眼睛望你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some there were lounging in their carriages, gliding through parks, a greyhound bounding along in front of the equipage driven at a trot by two midget postilions in white breeches.","zh":"有的贵妇仰靠在马车内，驰骋草地，马前有一只猎犬跳跃，两个白裤小僮驭马。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Others, dreaming on sofas with an open letter, gazed at the moon through a slightly open window half draped by a black curtain.","zh":"有的贵妇坐在沙发上，身旁一封开口的信，仰首凝思，遥望月亮，窗户半开，还让黑幔挡住一半。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The naive ones, a tear on their cheeks, were kissing doves through the bars of a Gothic cage, or, smiling, their heads on one side, were plucking the leaves of a marguerite with their taper fingers, that curved at the tips like peaked shoes.","zh":"天真烂漫的贵妇，脸上一滴泪珠，隔着哥特式鸟笼的小柱，逗着笼中的斑鸠；要不就是偏着头微笑，十指尖尖，翘起如波兰式鞋 ，掐着雏菊的花瓣。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And you, too, were there, Sultans with long pipes reclining beneath arbours in the arms of Bayaderes; Djiaours, Turkish sabres, Greek caps; and you especially, pale landscapes of dithyrambic lands, that often show us at once palm trees and firs, tigers on the right, a lion to the left, Tartar minarets on the horizon; the whole framed by a very neat virgin forest, and with a great perpendicular sunbeam trembling in the water, where, standing out in relief like white excoriations on a steel-grey ground, swans are swimming about.","zh":"画上还有吸长烟袋的苏丹 ，在凉棚底下陶醉在印度舞姬的怀抱里；还有“邪教徒” 、土耳其刀、希腊帽；特别是酒神故乡暗淡的风景 ，我们经常在这里看到棕榈、冷杉，右边几只老虎，左边一只狮子，天边几座鞑靼尖塔，近景是罗马遗迹，稍远是几只蹲在地上的骆驼；——一片洁净的原始森林，像框子一样，环绕四周，同时一大道阳光，笔直下来，在水中荡漾，或远或近，青灰的湖面露出一些白痕，表示有几只天鹅在游动。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the shade of the argand lamp fastened to the wall above Emma’s head lighted up all these pictures of the world, that passed before her one by one in the silence of the dormitory, and to the distant noise of some belated carriage rolling over the Boulevards.","sentences":[{"en":"And the shade of the argand lamp fastened to the wall above Emma’s head lighted up all these pictures of the world, that passed before her one by one in the silence of the dormitory, and to the distant noise of some belated carriage rolling over the Boulevards.","zh":"挂在墙上的甘该灯 ，正在爱玛头上，罩子聚下光来，照亮这些人生画幅，一幅一幅，从眼前经过，寝室静悄悄的，远远传来一辆马车的响声，马车回来晚了，还在路上走动。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When her mother died she cried much the first few days. She had a funeral picture made with the hair of the deceased, and, in a letter sent to the Bertaux full of sad reflections on life, she asked to be buried later on in the same grave. The goodman thought she must be ill, and came to see her. Emma was secretly pleased that she had reached at a first attempt the rare ideal of pale lives, never attained by mediocre hearts. She let herself glide along with Lamartine meanderings, listened to harps on lakes, to all the songs of dying swans, to the falling of the leaves, the pure virgins ascending to heaven, and the voice of the Eternal discoursing down the valleys. She wearied of it, would not confess it, continued from habit, and at last was surprised to feel herself soothed, and with no more sadness at heart than wrinkles on her brow.","sentences":[{"en":"When her mother died she cried much the first few days.","zh":"母亲死的头几天，她哭得十分伤心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had a funeral picture made with the hair of the deceased, and, in a letter sent to the Bertaux full of sad reflections on life, she asked to be buried later on in the same grave.","zh":"她拿死者头发给自己编了一个纪念卡；她写了一封家信，满纸人生辛酸，要求日后把她也埋在母亲坟里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The goodman thought she must be ill, and came to see her.","zh":"老头子以为她病了，赶去看她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma was secretly pleased that she had reached at a first attempt the rare ideal of pale lives, never attained by mediocre hearts.","zh":"灰暗人生的稀有理想，庸人永远达不到，她觉得自己一下子就达到了这种境界，于是心满意足了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She let herself glide along with Lamartine meanderings, listened to harps on lakes, to all the songs of dying swans, to the falling of the leaves, the pure virgins ascending to heaven, and the voice of the Eternal discoursing down the valleys.","zh":"所以她由着自己滑入拉马丁的蜿蜒细流，谛听湖上的竖琴、天鹅死时的哀鸣、落叶的种种响声、升天的贞女和在溪谷布道的天父的声音 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wearied of it, would not confess it, continued from habit, and at last was surprised to feel herself soothed, and with no more sadness at heart than wrinkles on her brow.","zh":"她感到腻烦，却又绝口否认，先靠习惯，后靠虚荣心，总算撑持下来；她最后觉得自己平静下来，心中没有忧愁，就像额头没有皱纹一样，不由得大吃一惊。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The good nuns, who had been so sure of her vocation, perceived with great astonishment that Mademoiselle Rouault seemed to be slipping from them. They had indeed been so lavish to her of prayers, retreats, novenas, and sermons, they had so often preached the respect due to saints and martyrs, and given so much good advice as to the modesty of the body and the salvation of her soul, that she did as tightly reined horses; she pulled up short and the bit slipped from her teeth. This nature, positive in the midst of its enthusiasms, that had loved the church for the sake of the flowers, and music for the words of the songs, and literature for its passional stimulus, rebelled against the mysteries of faith as it grew irritated by discipline, a thing antipathetic to her constitution. When her father took her from school, no one was sorry to see her go. The Lady Superior even thought that she had latterly been somewhat irreverent to the community.","sentences":[{"en":"The good nuns, who had been so sure of her vocation, perceived with great astonishment that Mademoiselle Rouault seemed to be slipping from them.","zh":"女修士们从前一直认为卢欧小姐有灵性，有前程，如今发现她似乎辜负她们的爱护，惊奇万分。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They had indeed been so lavish to her of prayers, retreats, novenas, and sermons, they had so often preached the respect due to saints and martyrs, and given so much good advice as to the modesty of the body and the salvation of her soul, that she did as tightly reined horses; she pulled up short and the bit slipped from her teeth.","zh":"她们也确实在她身上尽过心。一再要她参加日课、静修、九日祈祷 、布道，一再宣讲应当尊敬先圣与殉教者，也谆谆劝诲应当克制肉体、拯救灵魂，可是她就像马一样，你拉紧缰绳，以为不会出事，岂知马猛然站住，马衔滑出嘴来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This nature, positive in the midst of its enthusiasms, that had loved the church for the sake of the flowers, and music for the words of the songs, and literature for its passional stimulus, rebelled against the mysteries of faith as it grew irritated by discipline, a thing antipathetic to her constitution.","zh":"她是热狂而又实际，爱教堂为了教堂的花卉，爱音乐为了歌的词句，爱文学为了文学的热情刺激，反抗信仰的神秘，好像院规同她的性情格格不入，她也越来越愤恨院规。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When her father took her from school, no one was sorry to see her go.","zh":"所以父亲接她出院，大家并不惜别。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The Lady Superior even thought that she had latterly been somewhat irreverent to the community.","zh":"院长甚至发觉，她在末期，不尊重修道院的共同生活。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma, at home once more, first took pleasure in looking after the servants, then grew disgusted with the country and missed her convent. When Charles came to the Bertaux for the first time, she thought herself quite disillusioned, with nothing more to learn, and nothing more to feel.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, at home once more, first took pleasure in looking after the servants, then grew disgusted with the country and missed her convent.","zh":"爱玛回家，起先还高兴管管仆人，过后却讨厌田野，又想念她的修道院了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When Charles came to the Bertaux for the first time, she thought herself quite disillusioned, with nothing more to learn, and nothing more to feel.","zh":"查理初来拜尔托，她正自以为万念俱灰，没有东西可学，也没有东西值得感受。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the uneasiness of her new position, or perhaps the disturbance caused by the presence of this man, had sufficed to make her believe that she at last felt that wondrous passion which, till then, like a great bird with rose-coloured wings, hung in the splendour of the skies of poesy; and now she could not think that the calm in which she lived was the happiness she had dreamed.","sentences":[{"en":"But the uneasiness of her new position, or perhaps the disturbance caused by the presence of this man, had sufficed to make her believe that she at last felt that wondrous passion which, till then, like a great bird with rose-coloured wings, hung in the splendour of the skies of poesy; and now she could not think that the calm in which she lived was the happiness she had dreamed.","zh":"但是对新生活的热望，或者也许是由于这个男人的存在而产生的刺激，足以使她相信：她终于得到了那种不可思议的爱情。在这以前，爱情仿佛一只玫瑰色羽毛的巨鸟，可望而不可即，在诗的灿烂天空翱翔；——可是现在她也不能想象，这种安静生活就是她早先梦想的幸福。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"1-7","part":1,"n":7,"title":"Part I · Chapter 7","titleZh":"上卷 · 7","paragraphs":[{"en":"She thought, sometimes, that, after all, this was the happiest time of her life—the honeymoon, as people called it. To taste the full sweetness of it, it would have been necessary doubtless to fly to those lands with sonorous names where the days after marriage are full of laziness most suave. In post chaises behind blue silken curtains to ride slowly up steep road, listening to the song of the postilion re-echoed by the mountains, along with the bells of goats and the muffled sound of a waterfall; at sunset on the shores of gulfs to breathe in the perfume of lemon trees; then in the evening on the villa-terraces above, hand in hand to look at the stars, making plans for the future. It seemed to her that certain places on earth must bring happiness, as a plant peculiar to the soil, and that cannot thrive elsewhere. Why could not she lean over balconies in Swiss chalets, or enshrine her melancholy in a Scotch cottage, with a husband dressed in a black velvet coat with long tails, and thin shoes, a pointed hat and frills? Perhaps she would have liked to confide all these things to someone. But how tell an undefinable uneasiness, variable as the clouds, unstable as the winds? Words failed her—the opportunity, the courage.","sentences":[{"en":"She thought, sometimes, that, after all, this was the happiest time of her life—the honeymoon, as people called it.","zh":"她有时候寻思，她一生最美好的时日，也就只有所谓蜜月。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To taste the full sweetness of it, it would have been necessary doubtless to fly to those lands with sonorous names where the days after marriage are full of laziness most suave.","zh":"领略蜜月味道，不用说，就该去那些名字响亮的地方 ，新婚夫妇在这些地方有最可人意的闲散！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In post chaises behind blue silken curtains to ride slowly up steep road, listening to the song of the postilion re-echoed by the mountains, along with the bells of goats and the muffled sound of a waterfall; at sunset on the shores of gulfs to breathe in the perfume of lemon trees; then in the evening on the villa-terraces above, hand in hand to look at the stars, making plans for the future.","zh":"人坐在驿车里，头上是蓝绸活动车篷，道路崎岖，一步一蹬，听驿夫的歌曲、山羊的铃铛和瀑布的喧豗，在大山之中，响成一片。夕阳西下，人在海湾岸边，吸着柠檬树的香味；过后天黑了，只有他们两个人，站在别墅平台，手指交错，一边做计划，一边眺望繁星。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It seemed to her that certain places on earth must bring happiness, as a plant peculiar to the soil, and that cannot thrive elsewhere.","zh":"她觉得某些地点应当出产幸福，就像一棵因地而异的植物一样，换了地方，便长不好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why could not she lean over balconies in Swiss chalets, or enshrine her melancholy in a Scotch cottage, with a husband dressed in a black velvet coat with long tails, and thin shoes, a pointed hat and frills?","zh":"她怎么就不能胳膊肘支着瑞士小木房的阳台，或者把她的忧愁关在一所苏格兰茅庐，丈夫穿一件花边袖口、长裾青绒燕尾服，踏一双软靴，戴一顶尖帽！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps she would have liked to confide all these things to someone.","zh":"她也许想对一个什么人，说说这些知心话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But how tell an undefinable uneasiness, variable as the clouds, unstable as the winds?","zh":"可是这种不安的心情，捉摸不定，云一样变幻，风一样旋转，怎么出口呢？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Words failed her—the opportunity, the courage.","zh":"她缺乏字句，也缺乏机会、胆量。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"If Charles had but wished it, if he had guessed it, if his look had but once met her thought, it seemed to her that a sudden plenty would have gone out from her heart, as the fruit falls from a tree when shaken by a hand. But as the intimacy of their life became deeper, the greater became the gulf that separated her from him.","sentences":[{"en":"If Charles had but wished it, if he had guessed it, if his look had but once met her thought, it seemed to her that a sudden plenty would have gone out from her heart, as the fruit falls from a tree when shaken by a hand.","zh":"不过假使查理愿意的话，诧异的话，看穿她的心思的话，哪怕一次也罢，她觉得，她的心头就会立时涌出滔滔不绝的话来，好比手一碰墙边果树，熟了的果子纷纷下坠一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But as the intimacy of their life became deeper, the greater became the gulf that separated her from him.","zh":"可是他们生活上越相近，她精神上离他却越远了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles’s conversation was commonplace as a street pavement, and everyone’s ideas trooped through it in their everyday garb, without exciting emotion, laughter, or thought. He had never had the curiosity, he said, while he lived at Rouen, to go to the theatre to see the actors from Paris. He could neither swim, nor fence, nor shoot, and one day he could not explain some term of horsemanship to her that she had come across in a novel.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles’s conversation was commonplace as a street pavement, and everyone’s ideas trooped through it in their everyday garb, without exciting emotion, laughter, or thought.","zh":"查理的谈吐就像人行道一样平板，见解庸俗，如同来往行人一般，衣着寻常，激不起情绪，也激不起笑或者梦想。他说，他在鲁昂居住的时候，从未动过上剧场看看巴黎演员的念头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He had never had the curiosity, he said, while he lived at Rouen, to go to the theatre to see the actors from Paris.","zh":"查理的谈吐就像人行道一样平板，见解庸俗，如同来往行人一般，衣着寻常，激不起情绪，也激不起笑或者梦想。他说，他在鲁昂居住的时候，从未动过上剧场看看巴黎演员的念头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He could neither swim, nor fence, nor shoot, and one day he could not explain some term of horsemanship to her that she had come across in a novel.","zh":"他不会游泳，不会比剑，不会放手枪，有一天，她拿传奇小说里遇到的一个骑马术语问他，他瞠目不知所对。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A man, on the contrary, should he not know everything, excel in manifold activities, initiate you into the energies of passion, the refinements of life, all mysteries? But this one taught nothing, knew nothing, wished nothing. He thought her happy; and she resented this easy calm, this serene heaviness, the very happiness she gave him.","sentences":[{"en":"A man, on the contrary, should he not know everything, excel in manifold activities, initiate you into the energies of passion, the refinements of life, all mysteries?","zh":"正相反，一个男子难道不该无所不知，无所不能，启发你领会热情的力量、生命的奥妙和一切秘密吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But this one taught nothing, knew nothing, wished nothing.","zh":"可是这位先生，一无所教，一无所知，一无所期。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He thought her happy; and she resented this easy calm, this serene heaviness, the very happiness she gave him.","zh":"他相信她快乐；然而她恨的正是他这种稳如磐石的安定，这种心平气和的迟钝，甚至她带给他的幸福。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Sometimes she would draw; and it was great amusement to Charles to stand there bolt upright and watch her bend over her cardboard, with eyes half-closed the better to see her work, or rolling, between her fingers, little bread-pellets. As to the piano, the more quickly her fingers glided over it the more he wondered. She struck the notes with aplomb, and ran from top to bottom of the keyboard without a break. Thus shaken up, the old instrument, whose strings buzzed, could be heard at the other end of the village when the window was open, and often the bailiff’s clerk, passing along the highroad bare-headed and in list slippers, stopped to listen, his sheet of paper in his hand.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes she would draw; and it was great amusement to Charles to stand there bolt upright and watch her bend over her cardboard, with eyes half-closed the better to see her work, or rolling, between her fingers, little bread-pellets.","zh":"有时候，她画素描，查理把这当作重要娱乐，直挺挺站在一旁，看她俯向画册，眨动眼睛，端详她的作品；要不然就在大拇指上，拿面包心子揉成小球 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to the piano, the more quickly her fingers glided over it the more he wondered.","zh":"说到钢琴，她的手越弹得快，他越觉得出奇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She struck the notes with aplomb, and ran from top to bottom of the keyboard without a break.","zh":"她弹音键，信心在握，上上下下，打遍键盘，停也不停。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus shaken up, the old instrument, whose strings buzzed, could be heard at the other end of the village when the window was open, and often the bailiff’s clerk, passing along the highroad bare-headed and in list slippers, stopped to listen, his sheet of paper in his hand.","zh":"这架旧乐器，钢丝倚里歪斜，经她一弹，响声震耳，只要窗户开开，村头也听得真切；执达吏的文书走过大路，光着头，穿着布鞋，手里拿着公文，也站住了听她弹琴。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma, on the other hand, knew how to look after her house. She sent the patients’ accounts in well-phrased letters that had no suggestion of a bill. When they had a neighbour to dinner on Sundays, she managed to have some tasty dish—piled up pyramids of greengages on vine leaves, served up preserves turned out into plates—and even spoke of buying finger-glasses for dessert. From all this much consideration was extended to Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, on the other hand, knew how to look after her house.","zh":"另一方面，爱玛懂得料理家务。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She sent the patients’ accounts in well-phrased letters that had no suggestion of a bill.","zh":"她送账单给病人，附一封信，措词婉转，不露索欠痕迹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When they had a neighbour to dinner on Sundays, she managed to have some tasty dish—piled up pyramids of greengages on vine leaves, served up preserves turned out into plates—and even spoke of buying finger-glasses for dessert.","zh":"星期六，有邻人来用饭，她设法烧一盘精致的菜，还会拿青梅在葡萄叶上摞成金字塔，蜜饯罐倒放在盘子上端出来，她甚至说起为用果点买几只玻璃盏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"From all this much consideration was extended to Bovary.","zh":"凡此种种，影响所及，提高了人们对包法利的敬重。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles finished by rising in his own esteem for possessing such a wife. He showed with pride in the sitting room two small pencil sketches by her that he had had framed in very large frames, and hung up against the wallpaper by long green cords. People returning from mass saw him at his door in his wool-work slippers.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles finished by rising in his own esteem for possessing such a wife.","zh":"娶到这样一位太太，查理临了也自视甚高了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He showed with pride in the sitting room two small pencil sketches by her that he had had framed in very large frames, and hung up against the wallpaper by long green cords.","zh":"她有两小幅铅画稿，他配上很宽的框子，用绿长绳挂在厅房墙上，傲形于色，指给人看。大家做完弥撒出来，就见他站在门口，穿一双漂亮绣花拖鞋。","scope":"group"},{"en":"People returning from mass saw him at his door in his wool-work slippers.","zh":"她有两小幅铅画稿，他配上很宽的框子，用绿长绳挂在厅房墙上，傲形于色，指给人看。大家做完弥撒出来，就见他站在门口，穿一双漂亮绣花拖鞋。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He came home late—at ten o’clock, at midnight sometimes. Then he asked for something to eat, and as the servant had gone to bed, Emma waited on him. He took off his coat to dine more at his ease. He told her, one after the other, the people he had met, the villages where he had been, the prescriptions he had written, and, well pleased with himself, he finished the remainder of the boiled beef and onions, picked pieces off the cheese, munched an apple, emptied his water-bottle, and then went to bed, and lay on his back and snored.","sentences":[{"en":"He came home late—at ten o’clock, at midnight sometimes.","zh":"他回家晚，十点钟，有时候半夜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he asked for something to eat, and as the servant had gone to bed, Emma waited on him.","zh":"他要东西吃，女仆睡了，只有爱玛伺候他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He took off his coat to dine more at his ease.","zh":"他要晚饭吃得自在，脱掉大衣。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He told her, one after the other, the people he had met, the villages where he had been, the prescriptions he had written, and, well pleased with himself, he finished the remainder of the boiled beef and onions, picked pieces off the cheese, munched an apple, emptied his water-bottle, and then went to bed, and lay on his back and snored.","zh":"他一个一个说起他遇见的人、去过的村子、开过的药方，心满意足，吃完洋葱烧牛肉，剥去干酪外皮，啃掉一只苹果，喝光他的水晶瓶，然后上床，身子一挺，打起鼾来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As he had been for a time accustomed to wear nightcaps, his handkerchief would not keep down over his ears, so that his hair in the morning was all tumbled pell-mell about his face and whitened with the feathers of the pillow, whose strings came untied during the night. He always wore thick boots that had two long creases over the instep running obliquely towards the ankle, while the rest of the upper continued in a straight line as if stretched on a wooden foot. He said that “was quite good enough for the country.”","sentences":[{"en":"As he had been for a time accustomed to wear nightcaps, his handkerchief would not keep down over his ears, so that his hair in the morning was all tumbled pell-mell about his face and whitened with the feathers of the pillow, whose strings came untied during the night.","zh":"他长久养成戴睡帽睡觉的习惯，包头帕子在耳边扣不牢实，一到早晨，头发就乱蓬蓬散了一脸，枕头带子夜晚松了，鸭绒搅白了他的头发。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He always wore thick boots that had two long creases over the instep running obliquely towards the ankle, while the rest of the upper continued in a straight line as if stretched on a wooden foot.","zh":"他总穿一双笨重靴子，脚背两个厚褶子，斜趋踝骨，靴筒笔直向上，紧绷绷的，活像一只木头脚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He said that “was quite good enough for the country.”","zh":"他说“这在乡下够好的啦”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His mother approved of his economy, for she came to see him as formerly when there had been some violent row at her place; and yet Madame Bovary senior seemed prejudiced against her daughter-in-law. She thought “her ways too fine for their position”; the wood, the sugar, and the candles disappeared as “at a grand establishment,” and the amount of firing in the kitchen would have been enough for twenty-five courses. She put her linen in order for her in the presses, and taught her to keep an eye on the butcher when he brought the meat. Emma put up with these lessons. Madame Bovary was lavish of them; and the words “daughter” and “mother” were exchanged all day long, accompanied by little quiverings of the lips, each one uttering gentle words in a voice trembling with anger.","sentences":[{"en":"His mother approved of his economy, for she came to see him as formerly when there had been some violent row at her place; and yet Madame Bovary senior seemed prejudiced against her daughter-in-law.","zh":"他母亲赞成他这样俭省；因为，自己家里吵凶了，她待不住，像往常一样来看他；可是老太太对儿媳妇似乎有成见。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She thought “her ways too fine for their position”; the wood, the sugar, and the candles disappeared as “at a grand establishment,” and the amount of firing in the kitchen would have been enough for twenty-five courses.","zh":"她觉得“他们的家境不衬她这种作风”；柴呀、糖呀，还有蜡烛，“就像高门大户一样糟蹋”，光是厨房烧的木炭，足可以上二十五道菜！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She put her linen in order for her in the presses, and taught her to keep an eye on the butcher when he brought the meat.","zh":"她帮她整理衣橱，教她监视屠户送肉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma put up with these lessons.","zh":"爱玛拜领这些教训，老太太的教训反而多了；两个人整天“媳妇呀”“妈呀”呼来唤去，嘴唇微微发抖，话说得很柔和，声音颤悠悠的，透着怒气。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Madame Bovary was lavish of them; and the words “daughter” and “mother” were exchanged all day long, accompanied by little quiverings of the lips, each one uttering gentle words in a voice trembling with anger.","zh":"爱玛拜领这些教训，老太太的教训反而多了；两个人整天“媳妇呀”“妈呀”呼来唤去，嘴唇微微发抖，话说得很柔和，声音颤悠悠的，透着怒气。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"In Madame Dubuc’s time the old woman felt that she was still the favorite; but now the love of Charles for Emma seemed to her a desertion from her tenderness, an encroachment upon what was hers, and she watched her son’s happiness in sad silence, as a ruined man looks through the windows at people dining in his old house. She recalled to him as remembrances her troubles and her sacrifices, and, comparing these with Emma’s negligence, came to the conclusion that it was not reasonable to adore her so exclusively.","sentences":[{"en":"In Madame Dubuc’s time the old woman felt that she was still the favorite; but now the love of Charles for Emma seemed to her a desertion from her tenderness, an encroachment upon what was hers, and she watched her son’s happiness in sad silence, as a ruined man looks through the windows at people dining in his old house.","zh":"杜比克夫人在的时候，老太太觉得自己还受儿子爱戴；可是现在，查理对爱玛的恩情在她看来，分明等于一种对她的慈爱的捐弃行为，一种取而代之的侵占行为；她注视儿子的幸福，闷不做声，仿佛一个人破了产，隔着玻璃窗，望见别人坐在自己的旧宅吃饭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She recalled to him as remembrances her troubles and her sacrifices, and, comparing these with Emma’s negligence, came to the conclusion that it was not reasonable to adore her so exclusively.","zh":"她用回想当年的方式，向他提起她的辛苦和她的牺牲，相形之下，爱玛心粗气浮，单宠爱玛一人，显然不合理。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles knew not what to answer: he respected his mother, and he loved his wife infinitely; he considered the judgment of the one infallible, and yet he thought the conduct of the other irreproachable. When Madam Bovary had gone, he tried timidly and in the same terms to hazard one or two of the more anodyne observations he had heard from his mamma. Emma proved to him with a word that he was mistaken, and sent him off to his patients.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles knew not what to answer: he respected his mother, and he loved his wife infinitely; he considered the judgment of the one infallible, and yet he thought the conduct of the other irreproachable.","zh":"查理不知道怎么样回答才好；他尊敬母亲，爱极了太太；他觉得前者判断正确，而后者无可贬责。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When Madam Bovary had gone, he tried timidly and in the same terms to hazard one or two of the more anodyne observations he had heard from his mamma.","zh":"老太太说过的最不痛不痒的指责，他在她走后，用同样话，畏畏缩缩，冒昧说了一两句；爱玛一句话就证明他错，打发他看病人去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma proved to him with a word that he was mistaken, and sent him off to his patients.","zh":"老太太说过的最不痛不痒的指责，他在她走后，用同样话，畏畏缩缩，冒昧说了一两句；爱玛一句话就证明他错，打发他看病人去了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And yet, in accord with theories she believed right, she wanted to make herself in love with him. By moonlight in the garden she recited all the passionate rhymes she knew by heart, and, sighing, sang to him many melancholy adagios; but she found herself as calm after as before, and Charles seemed no more amorous and no more moved.","sentences":[{"en":"And yet, in accord with theories she believed right, she wanted to make herself in love with him.","zh":"不过她根据自以为正确的原则，愿意表示自己的恩爱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By moonlight in the garden she recited all the passionate rhymes she knew by heart, and, sighing, sang to him many melancholy adagios; but she found herself as calm after as before, and Charles seemed no more amorous and no more moved.","zh":"于是月光皎洁之时，她在花园一首一首吟诵她记得起来的情诗，一面叹息，一面为他唱一些忧郁的慢调；可是吟唱之后，她发现自己如同吟唱之前一样平静，查理也似乎并不因而爱情加重，感动加深。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When she had thus for a while struck the flint on her heart without getting a spark, incapable, moreover, of understanding what she did not experience as of believing anything that did not present itself in conventional forms, she persuaded herself without difficulty that Charles’s passion was nothing very exorbitant. His outbursts became regular; he embraced her at certain fixed times. It was one habit among other habits, and, like a dessert, looked forward to after the monotony of dinner.","sentences":[{"en":"When she had thus for a while struck the flint on her heart without getting a spark, incapable, moreover, of understanding what she did not experience as of believing anything that did not present itself in conventional forms, she persuaded herself without difficulty that Charles’s passion was nothing very exorbitant.","zh":"仿佛火刀敲石子，她这样敲了一阵自己的心，不见冒出一颗火星来，而且经验不到的东西，她没有能力了解，正如不经传统形式表现的东西，也没有能力相信一样，她轻易就认定了查理的热情毫无惊人之处。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His outbursts became regular; he embraced her at certain fixed times.","zh":"感情流露，在他成了例行公事；他吻抱她，有一定时间。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was one habit among other habits, and, like a dessert, looked forward to after the monotony of dinner.","zh":"这是许多习惯之中的一个习惯，就像晚饭单调乏味，吃过以后，先晓得要上什么果点一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A gamekeeper, cured by the doctor of inflammation of the lungs, had given madame a little Italian greyhound; she took her out walking, for she went out sometimes in order to be alone for a moment, and not to see before her eyes the eternal garden and the dusty road. She went as far as the beeches of Banneville, near the deserted pavilion which forms an angle of the wall on the side of the country. Amidst the vegetation of the ditch there are long reeds with leaves that cut you.","sentences":[{"en":"A gamekeeper, cured by the doctor of inflammation of the lungs, had given madame a little Italian greyhound; she took her out walking, for she went out sometimes in order to be alone for a moment, and not to see before her eyes the eternal garden and the dusty road.","zh":"有一个猎警 ，害肺炎，经他医好，送了他太太一只意大利种小母猎犬；她带它散步，因为她有时候出去走走，独自待上一时，避免老看日久生厌的花园和尘土飞扬的大路。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She went as far as the beeches of Banneville, near the deserted pavilion which forms an angle of the wall on the side of the country.","zh":"她一直走到巴恩镇的山毛榉林子、田边墙角的荒亭子附近。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Amidst the vegetation of the ditch there are long reeds with leaves that cut you.","zh":"深沟乱草之中，有叶子锋利的高芦苇。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She began by looking round her to see if nothing had changed since last she had been there. She found again in the same places the foxgloves and wallflowers, the beds of nettles growing round the big stones, and the patches of lichen along the three windows, whose shutters, always closed, were rotting away on their rusty iron bars. Her thoughts, aimless at first, wandered at random, like her greyhound, who ran round and round in the fields, yelping after the yellow butterflies, chasing the shrew-mice, or nibbling the poppies on the edge of a cornfield.","sentences":[{"en":"She began by looking round her to see if nothing had changed since last she had been there.","zh":"她先望望周围，看和她上次来，有没有什么变动，她又在原来地点看到毛地黄和桂竹香，荨麻一丛一丛环绕大石块，地衣一片一片沿着三个窗户。护窗板永远关闭，腐烂的木屑落满了生锈的铁档。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She found again in the same places the foxgloves and wallflowers, the beds of nettles growing round the big stones, and the patches of lichen along the three windows, whose shutters, always closed, were rotting away on their rusty iron bars.","zh":"她先望望周围，看和她上次来，有没有什么变动，她又在原来地点看到毛地黄和桂竹香，荨麻一丛一丛环绕大石块，地衣一片一片沿着三个窗户。护窗板永远关闭，腐烂的木屑落满了生锈的铁档。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her thoughts, aimless at first, wandered at random, like her greyhound, who ran round and round in the fields, yelping after the yellow butterflies, chasing the shrew-mice, or nibbling the poppies on the edge of a cornfield.","zh":"她的思想起初漫无目的，忽来忽去，就像她的猎犬一样，在田野兜圈子，吠黄蝴蝶，追鼩鼱，咬小麦地边的野罂粟。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then gradually her ideas took definite shape, and, sitting on the grass that she dug up with little prods of her sunshade, Emma repeated to herself, “Good heavens! Why did I marry?”","sentences":[{"en":"Then gradually her ideas took definite shape, and, sitting on the grass that she dug up with little prods of her sunshade, Emma repeated to herself, “Good heavens!","zh":"随后，观念渐渐集中了，于是爱玛坐在草地，拿阳伞尖尖头轻轻刨土，向自己重复道：“我的上帝！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why did I marry?”","zh":"我为什么结婚？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She asked herself if by some other chance combination it would have not been possible to meet another man; and she tried to imagine what would have been these unrealised events, this different life, this unknown husband. All, surely, could not be like this one. He might have been handsome, witty, distinguished, attractive, such as, no doubt, her old companions of the convent had married. What were they doing now? In town, with the noise of the streets, the buzz of the theatres and the lights of the ballroom, they were living lives where the heart expands, the senses bourgeon out. But she—her life was cold as a garret whose dormer window looks on the north, and ennui, the silent spider, was weaving its web in the darkness in every corner of her heart.","sentences":[{"en":"She asked herself if by some other chance combination it would have not been possible to meet another man; and she tried to imagine what would have been these unrealised events, this different life, this unknown husband.","zh":"她问自己，她有没有方法，在其他巧合的机会，邂逅另外一个男子。她试着想象那些可能发生的事件、那种不同的生活、那个她不相识的丈夫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All, surely, could not be like this one.","zh":"人人一定不如他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He might have been handsome, witty, distinguished, attractive, such as, no doubt, her old companions of the convent had married.","zh":"他想必漂亮、聪明、英俊、夺目，不用说，就像他们一样，她那些修道院的老同学嫁的那些人一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"What were they doing now?","zh":"他想必漂亮、聪明、英俊、夺目，不用说，就像他们一样，她那些修道院的老同学嫁的那些人一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In town, with the noise of the streets, the buzz of the theatres and the lights of the ballroom, they were living lives where the heart expands, the senses bourgeon out.","zh":"她们如今在干什么？住在城里，市声喧杂，剧场一片音响，舞会灯火辉煌，她们过着心旷神怡的生活。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she—her life was cold as a garret whose dormer window looks on the north, and ennui, the silent spider, was weaving its web in the darkness in every corner of her heart.","zh":"可是她呀，生活好似天窗朝北的阁楼那样冷，而烦闷就像默不作声的蜘蛛，在暗地结网，爬过她的心的每个角落。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She recalled the prize days, when she mounted the platform to receive her little crowns, with her hair in long plaits. In her white frock and open prunella shoes she had a pretty way, and when she went back to her seat, the gentlemen bent over her to congratulate her; the courtyard was full of carriages; farewells were called to her through their windows; the music master with his violin case bowed in passing by. How far all of this! How far away! She called Djali, took her between her knees, and smoothed the long delicate head, saying, “Come, kiss mistress; you have no troubles.”","sentences":[{"en":"She recalled the prize days, when she mounted the platform to receive her little crowns, with her hair in long plaits.","zh":"她想起发奖的日子，她走上讲台，接受她的小花冠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In her white frock and open prunella shoes she had a pretty way, and when she went back to her seat, the gentlemen bent over her to congratulate her; the courtyard was full of carriages; farewells were called to her through their windows; the music master with his violin case bowed in passing by.","zh":"她梳着辫子，身穿白袍，脚上是开口黑毛线鞋，一副可爱模样；回到座位，男宾斜过身子向她致贺；满院车辆，大家在车门口同她话别，音乐教员挟着他的小提琴匣，边走，边打招呼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How far all of this!","zh":"这一切都多远啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How far away!","zh":"多远啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She called Djali, took her between her knees, and smoothed the long delicate head, saying, “Come, kiss mistress; you have no troubles.”","zh":"她喊加里过来，抱在膝盖当中，摸着它的细长头，对它道：“来，无忧无虑的东西，吻吻女主人。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then noting the melancholy face of the graceful animal, who yawned slowly, she softened, and comparing her to herself, spoke to her aloud as to somebody in trouble whom one is consoling.","sentences":[{"en":"Then noting the melancholy face of the graceful animal, who yawned slowly, she softened, and comparing her to herself, spoke to her aloud as to somebody in trouble whom one is consoling.","zh":"随后小狗慢悠悠打呵欠，她望着它忧郁的嘴脸，心软了，于是把它当成自己，好像安慰一个受苦人一样，大声同它说话。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Occasionally there came gusts of winds, breezes from the sea rolling in one sweep over the whole plateau of the Caux country, which brought even to these fields a salt freshness. The rushes, close to the ground, whistled; the branches trembled in a swift rustling, while their summits, ceaselessly swaying, kept up a deep murmur. Emma drew her shawl round her shoulders and rose.","sentences":[{"en":"Occasionally there came gusts of winds, breezes from the sea rolling in one sweep over the whole plateau of the Caux country, which brought even to these fields a salt freshness.","zh":"有时候，狂飙骤起，海风一跃而过科地的高原，就连远方田地、空气也有了盐水味道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The rushes, close to the ground, whistled; the branches trembled in a swift rustling, while their summits, ceaselessly swaying, kept up a deep murmur.","zh":"灯芯草伏在地面，簌簌作响，山毛榉的叶子立即打寒噤，发出响声，而树梢也总在摇来摆去，呼啸不已。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma drew her shawl round her shoulders and rose.","zh":"爱玛拉紧披肩站起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the avenue a green light dimmed by the leaves lit up the short moss that crackled softly beneath her feet. The sun was setting; the sky showed red between the branches, and the trunks of the trees, uniform, and planted in a straight line, seemed a brown colonnade standing out against a background of gold. A fear took hold of her; she called Djali, and hurriedly returned to Tostes by the high road, threw herself into an armchair, and for the rest of the evening did not speak.","sentences":[{"en":"In the avenue a green light dimmed by the leaves lit up the short moss that crackled softly beneath her feet.","zh":"林荫道的树叶，密密层层，映下一片绿光，照亮地面的青苔。青苔在她的脚底下，细声细气嘁喳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sun was setting; the sky showed red between the branches, and the trunks of the trees, uniform, and planted in a straight line, seemed a brown colonnade standing out against a background of gold.","zh":"夕阳西下，树枝之间的天变成红颜色，树身一般模样，排成一条直线，仿佛金色底子托着一排棕色圆柱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A fear took hold of her; she called Djali, and hurriedly returned to Tostes by the high road, threw herself into an armchair, and for the rest of the evening did not speak.","zh":"她怕起来了，呼喊加里，急忙走大路奔回道特，倒进扶手椅，整夜未曾开口。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But towards the end of September something extraordinary fell upon her life; she was invited by the Marquis d’Andervilliers to Vaubyessard.","sentences":[{"en":"But towards the end of September something extraordinary fell upon her life; she was invited by the Marquis d’Andervilliers to Vaubyessard.","zh":"但是九月梢左右，她的生活中出了一件大事：昂代维利耶侯爵邀她去渥毕萨尔。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Secretary of State under the Restoration, the Marquis, anxious to re-enter political life, set about preparing for his candidature to the Chamber of Deputies long beforehand. In the winter he distributed a great deal of wood, and in the Conseil General always enthusiastically demanded new roads for his arrondissement. During the dog-days he had suffered from an abscess, which Charles had cured as if by miracle by giving a timely little touch with the lancet. The steward sent to Tostes to pay for the operation reported in the evening that he had seen some superb cherries in the doctor’s little garden. Now cherry trees did not thrive at Vaubyessard; the Marquis asked Bovary for some slips; made it his business to thank his personally; saw Emma; thought she had a pretty figure, and that she did not bow like a peasant; so that he did not think he was going beyond the bounds of condescension, nor, on the other hand, making a mistake, in inviting the young couple.","sentences":[{"en":"Secretary of State under the Restoration, the Marquis, anxious to re-enter political life, set about preparing for his candidature to the Chamber of Deputies long beforehand.","zh":"复辟时期 ，侯爵是国务大臣，现在希望再过政治生涯，许久以来就在进行众议院选举的准备工作。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the winter he distributed a great deal of wood, and in the Conseil General always enthusiastically demanded new roads for his arrondissement.","zh":"冬天他分批大量馈送木柴；他在县议会总是慷慨激昂，为本区要求多修道路。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"During the dog-days he had suffered from an abscess, which Charles had cured as if by miracle by giving a timely little touch with the lancet.","zh":"大夏天他害口疮，查理凑巧一竹叶刀，奇迹似的治好了他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The steward sent to Tostes to pay for the operation reported in the evening that he had seen some superb cherries in the doctor’s little garden.","zh":"管家到道特送手术费，当天黄昏回来，说起他在医生小花园看见上品樱桃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now cherry trees did not thrive at Vaubyessard; the Marquis asked Bovary for some slips; made it his business to thank his personally; saw Emma; thought she had a pretty figure, and that she did not bow like a peasant; so that he did not think he was going beyond the bounds of condescension, nor, on the other hand, making a mistake, in inviting the young couple.","zh":"而樱桃树在渥毕萨尔就长不好，侯爵向包法利讨了一些接枝，觉得理应亲自道谢，恰巧看见爱玛，觉得她身材窈窕，行起礼来，决不似乡下女人；因为印象好，他相信请年轻夫妇到庄园来，既不失身份，也不至于使自己难堪。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On Wednesday at three o’clock, Monsieur and Madame Bovary, seated in their dog-cart, set out for Vaubyessard, with a great trunk strapped on behind and a bonnet-box in front of the apron. Besides these Charles held a bandbox between his knees.","sentences":[{"en":"On Wednesday at three o’clock, Monsieur and Madame Bovary, seated in their dog-cart, set out for Vaubyessard, with a great trunk strapped on behind and a bonnet-box in front of the apron.","zh":"有一天星期三，三点钟，包法利夫妇坐上他们的包克，去了渥毕萨尔，车后捆了老大一件行李，脚篷前面放了一个帽盒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides these Charles held a bandbox between his knees.","zh":"查理腿当中，还夹着一个纸匣。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They arrived at nightfall, just as the lamps in the park were being lit to show the way for the carriages.","sentences":[{"en":"They arrived at nightfall, just as the lamps in the park were being lit to show the way for the carriages.","zh":"他们到达时，正好天黑，有人在草地点起油灯，给马车照亮道路。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"1-8","part":1,"n":8,"title":"Part I · Chapter 8","titleZh":"上卷 · 8","paragraphs":[{"en":"The château, a modern building in Italian style, with two projecting wings and three flights of steps, lay at the foot of an immense green-sward, on which some cows were grazing among groups of large trees set out at regular intervals, while large beds of arbutus, rhododendron, syringas, and guelder roses bulged out their irregular clusters of green along the curve of the gravel path. A river flowed under a bridge; through the mist one could distinguish buildings with thatched roofs scattered over the field bordered by two gently sloping, well timbered hillocks, and in the background amid the trees rose in two parallel lines the coach houses and stables, all that was left of the ruined old château.","sentences":[{"en":"The château, a modern building in Italian style, with two projecting wings and three flights of steps, lay at the foot of an immense green-sward, on which some cows were grazing among groups of large trees set out at regular intervals, while large beds of arbutus, rhododendron, syringas, and guelder roses bulged out their irregular clusters of green along the curve of the gravel path.","zh":"侯爵府邸是近代建筑，意大利风格，两翼前伸，三座台阶，连着一片大草坪，有几只母牛在吃草，一丛一丛大树，距离相等，分列两旁，同时一簇一簇灌木、杜鹃花、紫丁香和雪球花，大小不等，沿着曲曲折折的沙砾小道，密密匝匝，朝外拱出它们的枝叶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A river flowed under a bridge; through the mist one could distinguish buildings with thatched roofs scattered over the field bordered by two gently sloping, well timbered hillocks, and in the background amid the trees rose in two parallel lines the coach houses and stables, all that was left of the ruined old château.","zh":"桥下流过一条小河；人隔着雾，隐约望见零零落落几所茅庐散布在草地上；两座山冈，坡度不大，树木蓊郁，环绕草地；再往里去，绿荫翳翳，车房和马厩，平列两线：它们是拆毁的旧庄园的残余部分。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles’s dog-cart pulled up before the middle flight of steps; servants appeared; the Marquis came forward, and, offering his arm to the doctor’s wife, conducted her to the vestibule.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles’s dog-cart pulled up before the middle flight of steps; servants appeared; the Marquis came forward, and, offering his arm to the doctor’s wife, conducted her to the vestibule.","zh":"查理的包克停在当中台阶前面；听差们露面了；侯爵迎上前，挎起医生太太的胳膊，领她走进过厅。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was paved with marble slabs, was very lofty, and the sound of footsteps and that of voices re-echoed through it as in a church.","sentences":[{"en":"It was paved with marble slabs, was very lofty, and the sound of footsteps and that of voices re-echoed through it as in a church.","zh":"过厅很高，大理石地，脚步响动和说话声音，像在教堂一样有回声。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Opposite rose a straight staircase, and on the left a gallery overlooking the garden led to the billiard room, through whose door one could hear the click of the ivory balls. As she crossed it to go to the drawing room, Emma saw standing round the table men with grave faces, their chins resting on high cravats. They all wore orders, and smiled silently as they made their strokes.","sentences":[{"en":"Opposite rose a straight staircase, and on the left a gallery overlooking the garden led to the billiard room, through whose door one could hear the click of the ivory balls.","zh":"正面笔直一座楼梯，左手一道走廊，对着花园，通到弹子间，人在门口，听见象牙球碰来碰去的响声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As she crossed it to go to the drawing room, Emma saw standing round the table men with grave faces, their chins resting on high cravats.","zh":"她穿过弹子间，走向客厅，看见几个男人，围住球台，面孔严肃，下巴贴着高领结，个个挂勋章，一脸微笑，不声不响，推动他们的球杆。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They all wore orders, and smiled silently as they made their strokes.","zh":"她穿过弹子间，走向客厅，看见几个男人，围住球台，面孔严肃，下巴贴着高领结，个个挂勋章，一脸微笑，不声不响，推动他们的球杆。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"On the dark wainscoting of the walls large gold frames bore at the bottom names written in black letters. She read: “Jean-Antoine d’Andervilliers d’Yvervonbille, Count de la Vaubyessard and Baron de la Fresnay, killed at the battle of Coutras on the 20th of October, 1587.” And on another: “Jean-Antoine-Henry-Guy d’Andervilliers de la Vaubyessard, Admiral of France and Chevalier of the Order of St. Michael, wounded at the battle of the Hougue-Saint-Vaast on the 29th of May, 1692; died at Vaubyessard on the 23rd of January 1693.” One could hardly make out those that followed, for the light of the lamps lowered over the green cloth threw a dim shadow round the room. Burnishing the horizontal pictures, it broke up against these in delicate lines where there were cracks in the varnish, and from all these great black squares framed in with gold stood out here and there some lighter portion of the painting—a pale brow, two eyes that looked at you, perukes flowing over and powdering red-coated shoulders, or the buckle of a garter above a well-rounded calf.","sentences":[{"en":"On the dark wainscoting of the walls large gold frames bore at the bottom names written in black letters.","zh":"板壁发暗，挂着几个镀金大框，框边靠下，黑字写着他们的名姓，上面是：“约翰·安东·昂代维利耶·伊维本维尔，渥毕萨尔伯爵、弗雷奈伊男爵，一五八七年十月二十日，殉于古特拉司之役 。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She read: “Jean-Antoine d’Andervilliers d’Yvervonbille, Count de la Vaubyessard and Baron de la Fresnay, killed at the battle of Coutras on the 20th of October, 1587.”","zh":"板壁发暗，挂着几个镀金大框，框边靠下，黑字写着他们的名姓，上面是：“约翰·安东·昂代维利耶·伊维本维尔，渥毕萨尔伯爵、弗雷奈伊男爵，一五八七年十月二十日，殉于古特拉司之役 。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"And on another: “Jean-Antoine-Henry-Guy d’Andervilliers de la Vaubyessard, Admiral of France and Chevalier of the Order of St. Michael, wounded at the battle of the Hougue-Saint-Vaast on the 29th of May, 1692; died at Vaubyessard on the 23rd of January 1693.”","zh":"另一个写着：“约翰·安东·亨利·昂代维利耶·渥毕萨尔，法兰西海军总司令、圣米迦勒骑士勋章获得者，一六九二年五月二十九日，虎格－圣法之战 负伤，一六九八年一月二十三日，在渥毕萨尔逝世。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One could hardly make out those that followed, for the light of the lamps lowered over the green cloth threw a dim shadow round the room.","zh":"再下去就辨认不清了，因为灯光聚在球台绿毡上，房间别的地方，阴影重重，灯光偶尔照到画像，碰上油漆裂口，分成一道一道细线，把画像变成棕色。所有这些金边大黑方幅，东一块，西一块，露出画上一些较亮的部分：一个苍白的额头、两只望人的眼睛、披在红燕尾服有粉的肩头的假发，或者丰满的小腿上部的一只吊袜带扣子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Burnishing the horizontal pictures, it broke up against these in delicate lines where there were cracks in the varnish, and from all these great black squares framed in with gold stood out here and there some lighter portion of the painting—a pale brow, two eyes that looked at you, perukes flowing over and powdering red-coated shoulders, or the buckle of a garter above a well-rounded calf.","zh":"再下去就辨认不清了，因为灯光聚在球台绿毡上，房间别的地方，阴影重重，灯光偶尔照到画像，碰上油漆裂口，分成一道一道细线，把画像变成棕色。所有这些金边大黑方幅，东一块，西一块，露出画上一些较亮的部分：一个苍白的额头、两只望人的眼睛、披在红燕尾服有粉的肩头的假发，或者丰满的小腿上部的一只吊袜带扣子。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The Marquis opened the drawing room door; one of the ladies (the Marchioness herself) came to meet Emma. She made her sit down by her on an ottoman, and began talking to her as amicably as if she had known her a long time. She was a woman of about forty, with fine shoulders, a hook nose, a drawling voice, and on this evening she wore over her brown hair a simple guipure fichu that fell in a point at the back. A fair young woman sat in a high-backed chair in a corner; and gentlemen with flowers in their buttonholes were talking to ladies round the fire.","sentences":[{"en":"The Marquis opened the drawing room door; one of the ladies (the Marchioness herself) came to meet Emma.","zh":"侯爵推开客厅门；一位贵妇（侯爵夫人本人）站起来迎接爱玛，请她靠近自己，坐在双人沙发上，和她亲亲热热谈话，如同旧相识一般。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She made her sit down by her on an ottoman, and began talking to her as amicably as if she had known her a long time.","zh":"侯爵推开客厅门；一位贵妇（侯爵夫人本人）站起来迎接爱玛，请她靠近自己，坐在双人沙发上，和她亲亲热热谈话，如同旧相识一般。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was a woman of about forty, with fine shoulders, a hook nose, a drawling voice, and on this evening she wore over her brown hair a simple guipure fichu that fell in a point at the back.","zh":"她是一个四十岁上下的女人，肩膀很好看，鹰嘴鼻子，声音拖长，栗色头发，当天夜晚，头上蒙了一条素花边肩巾，三角样式，垂在后背。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A fair young woman sat in a high-backed chair in a corner; and gentlemen with flowers in their buttonholes were talking to ladies round the fire.","zh":"一个金黄色头发女孩子，坐在旁边一张高背椅上；有几位绅士，翻领缀一朵小花，围着壁炉，和贵妇们闲谈。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At seven dinner was served. The men, who were in the majority, sat down at the first table in the vestibule; the ladies at the second in the dining room with the Marquis and Marchioness.","sentences":[{"en":"At seven dinner was served.","zh":"七点钟入席。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The men, who were in the majority, sat down at the first table in the vestibule; the ladies at the second in the dining room with the Marquis and Marchioness.","zh":"男宾较多，坐在过厅的第一桌；女宾坐在饭厅的第二桌，有侯爵夫妇相陪。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma, on entering, felt herself wrapped round by the warm air, a blending of the perfume of flowers and of the fine linen, of the fumes of the viands, and the odour of the truffles. The silver dish covers reflected the lighted wax candles in the candelabra, the cut crystal covered with light steam reflected from one to the other pale rays; bouquets were placed in a row the whole length of the table; and in the large-bordered plates each napkin, arranged after the fashion of a bishop’s mitre, held between its two gaping folds a small oval shaped roll. The red claws of lobsters hung over the dishes; rich fruit in open baskets was piled up on moss; there were quails in their plumage; smoke was rising; and in silk stockings, knee-breeches, white cravat, and frilled shirt, the steward, grave as a judge, offering ready carved dishes between the shoulders of the guests, with a touch of the spoon gave you the piece chosen. On the large stove of porcelain inlaid with copper baguettes the statue of a woman, draped to the chin, gazed motionless on the room full of life.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, on entering, felt herself wrapped round by the warm air, a blending of the perfume of flowers and of the fine linen, of the fumes of the viands, and the odour of the truffles.","zh":"爱玛一进去，就感到四周一股热气，兼有花香、肉香、口蘑味道和漂亮桌布气味的热气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The silver dish covers reflected the lighted wax candles in the candelabra, the cut crystal covered with light steam reflected from one to the other pale rays; bouquets were placed in a row the whole length of the table; and in the large-bordered plates each napkin, arranged after the fashion of a bishop’s mitre, held between its two gaping folds a small oval shaped roll.","zh":"烛焰映在银罩上，比原来显得长了；雕花的水晶，蒙了一层水汽，反射出微弱的光线；桌上一丛一丛花，排成一条直线；饭巾摆在宽边盘子里，叠成主教帽样式，每个折缝放着小小一块椭圆面包。龙虾的红爪伸出盘子；大水果一层又一层，压着敞口筐子的青苔；鹌鹑热气腾腾，还带着羽毛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The red claws of lobsters hung over the dishes; rich fruit in open baskets was piled up on moss; there were quails in their plumage; smoke was rising; and in silk stockings, knee-breeches, white cravat, and frilled shirt, the steward, grave as a judge, offering ready carved dishes between the shoulders of the guests, with a touch of the spoon gave you the piece chosen.","zh":"司膳是丝袜、短裤、白领结、镶花边衬衫，严肃如同法官，在宾客肩膀空间，端上切好的菜，一勺子就把你选的那块东西送到面前。带铜条的大瓷炉上，有一座女雕像，衣服宽宽适适的，从下巴裹起，一动不动，望着满屋的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the large stove of porcelain inlaid with copper baguettes the statue of a woman, draped to the chin, gazed motionless on the room full of life.","zh":"包法利夫人注意到，有几位贵妇，没有拿自己的手套放进她们的玻璃盏。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary noticed that many ladies had not put their gloves in their glasses.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary noticed that many ladies had not put their gloves in their glasses.","zh":"酒席上座是一个老头子，独自坐在全体妇女中间，伏在他的满盘菜上，饭巾挽在后背，仿佛一个小孩子，一面吃，一面嘴里一滴一滴流汤汁。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But at the upper end of the table, alone amongst all these women, bent over his full plate, and his napkin tied round his neck like a child, an old man sat eating, letting drops of gravy drip from his mouth. His eyes were bloodshot, and he wore a little queue tied with black ribbon. He was the Marquis’s father-in-law, the old Duke de Laverdiere, once on a time favourite of the Count d’Artois, in the days of the Vaudreuil hunting-parties at the Marquis de Conflans’, and had been, it was said, the lover of Queen Marie Antoinette, between Monsieur de Coigny and Monsieur de Lauzun. He had lived a life of noisy debauch, full of duels, bets, elopements; he had squandered his fortune and frightened all his family. A servant behind his chair named aloud to him in his ear the dishes that he pointed to stammering, and constantly Emma’s eyes turned involuntarily to this old man with hanging lips, as to something extraordinary. He had lived at court and slept in the bed of queens! Iced champagne was poured out. Emma shivered all over as she felt it cold in her mouth. She had never seen pomegranates nor tasted pineapples. The powdered sugar even seemed to her whiter and finer than elsewhere.","sentences":[{"en":"But at the upper end of the table, alone amongst all these women, bent over his full plate, and his napkin tied round his neck like a child, an old man sat eating, letting drops of gravy drip from his mouth.","zh":"酒席上座是一个老头子，独自坐在全体妇女中间，伏在他的满盘菜上，饭巾挽在后背，仿佛一个小孩子，一面吃，一面嘴里一滴一滴流汤汁。","scope":"group"},{"en":"His eyes were bloodshot, and he wore a little queue tied with black ribbon.","zh":"眼睛有红丝。他戴的小假发，用一条黑带子系牢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was the Marquis’s father-in-law, the old Duke de Laverdiere, once on a time favourite of the Count d’Artois, in the days of the Vaudreuil hunting-parties at the Marquis de Conflans’, and had been, it was said, the lover of Queen Marie Antoinette, between Monsieur de Coigny and Monsieur de Lauzun.","zh":"他是侯爵的岳父拉维迪耶尔老公爵，孔福朗侯爵在沃德勒伊举行猎会，他曾经一度得到阿图瓦伯爵的宠幸，据说他在柯瓦尼之后与洛赞之前，做过王后玛丽·安托瓦奈特的情人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had lived a life of noisy debauch, full of duels, bets, elopements; he had squandered his fortune and frightened all his family.","zh":"他一辈子荒唐，声名狼藉，不是决斗、打赌，就是抢夺妇女，荡尽财产，害得全家人担惊受怕。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A servant behind his chair named aloud to him in his ear the dishes that he pointed to stammering, and constantly Emma’s eyes turned involuntarily to this old man with hanging lips, as to something extraordinary.","zh":"他期期艾艾，指着盘子问，椅后一个听差，对着他的耳朵，大声告诉他菜的名目。爱玛不由自主，时时刻刻，望着这耷拉着嘴唇的老头子，像望着什么不同凡响的庄严事物。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had lived at court and slept in the bed of queens!","zh":"他在宫里待过，后妃床上睡过！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Iced champagne was poured out.","zh":"香槟酒冰镇过，爱玛经不起嘴里那么凉，浑身上下打颤。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma shivered all over as she felt it cold in her mouth.","zh":"香槟酒冰镇过，爱玛经不起嘴里那么凉，浑身上下打颤。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She had never seen pomegranates nor tasted pineapples.","zh":"她从来没有见过石榴，也没有吃过菠萝蜜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The powdered sugar even seemed to her whiter and finer than elsewhere.","zh":"就连砂糖，她也觉得比别处的砂糖更白更细。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The ladies afterwards went to their rooms to prepare for the ball.","sentences":[{"en":"The ladies afterwards went to their rooms to prepare for the ball.","zh":"晚饭用过，贵妇们上楼，回到房间，准备参加舞会。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma made her toilet with the fastidious care of an actress on her debut. She did her hair according to the directions of the hairdresser, and put on the barege dress spread out upon the bed.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma made her toilet with the fastidious care of an actress on her debut.","zh":"爱玛重新梳妆，小心在意，仔细从事，好像一个女演员初次登台一样。她照理发师的建议理好头发，穿上搭在床上的细呢袍。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She did her hair according to the directions of the hairdresser, and put on the barege dress spread out upon the bed.","zh":"爱玛重新梳妆，小心在意，仔细从事，好像一个女演员初次登台一样。她照理发师的建议理好头发，穿上搭在床上的细呢袍。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles’s trousers were tight across the belly.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles’s trousers were tight across the belly.","zh":"查理嫌裤腰紧，说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My trouser-straps will be rather awkward for dancing,” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"“My trouser-straps will be rather awkward for dancing,” he said.","zh":"“鞋底下的带子要妨碍我跳舞的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Dancing?” repeated Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Dancing?” repeated Emma.","zh":"爱玛反问道：“跳舞？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes!”","zh":"“是啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, you must be mad! They would make fun of you; keep your place. Besides, it is more becoming for a doctor,” she added.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, you must be mad!","zh":"“你发痴啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They would make fun of you; keep your place.","zh":"人家会笑话你的，你待着吧。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, it is more becoming for a doctor,” she added.","zh":"她添上一句话道：“再说，这更合医生身份。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles was silent. He walked up and down waiting for Emma to finish dressing.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles was silent.","zh":"查理住了口，走来走去，等爱玛穿衣服。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He walked up and down waiting for Emma to finish dressing.","zh":"查理住了口，走来走去，等爱玛穿衣服。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He saw her from behind in the glass between two lights. Her black eyes seemed blacker than ever. Her hair, undulating towards the ears, shone with a blue lustre; a rose in her chignon trembled on its mobile stalk, with artificial dewdrops on the tip of the leaves. She wore a gown of pale saffron trimmed with three bouquets of pompon roses mixed with green.","sentences":[{"en":"He saw her from behind in the glass between two lights.","zh":"他从背后，在一边一支蜡烛的镜子里看她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her black eyes seemed blacker than ever.","zh":"她的黑眼睛似乎更黑了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her hair, undulating towards the ears, shone with a blue lustre; a rose in her chignon trembled on its mobile stalk, with artificial dewdrops on the tip of the leaves.","zh":"靠耳朵那边，头发有一点蓬起来，放出一道蓝光；发髻插了一朵玫瑰，小枝子摇来摇去，花跟着晃荡，叶尖上有几滴人造露水。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wore a gown of pale saffron trimmed with three bouquets of pompon roses mixed with green.","zh":"她穿一件淡郁金香袍，上面点缀三簇有绿叶相衬的小玫瑰花。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles came and kissed her on her shoulder.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles came and kissed her on her shoulder.","zh":"查理过去吻她的肩膀。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Let me alone!” she said; “you are tumbling me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Let me alone!” she said; “you are tumbling me.”","zh":"“走开！当心弄皱我的衣裳。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One could hear the flourish of the violin and the notes of a horn. She went downstairs restraining herself from running.","sentences":[{"en":"One could hear the flourish of the violin and the notes of a horn.","zh":"他们听见小提琴的前奏曲和喇叭的声音。她下楼时真想跑下去，总算克制住了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She went downstairs restraining herself from running.","zh":"他们听见小提琴的前奏曲和喇叭的声音。她下楼时真想跑下去，总算克制住了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Dancing had begun. Guests were arriving. There was some crushing.","sentences":[{"en":"Dancing had begun.","zh":"四组舞已经开始。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Guests were arriving.","zh":"人们纷至沓来，向前拥挤。","scope":"group"},{"en":"There was some crushing.","zh":"人们纷至沓来，向前拥挤。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She sat down on a form near the door.","sentences":[{"en":"She sat down on a form near the door.","zh":"她坐在门边一条长凳上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The quadrille over, the floor was occupied by groups of men standing up and talking and servants in livery bearing large trays. Along the line of seated women painted fans were fluttering, bouquets half hid smiling faces, and gold stoppered scent-bottles were turned in partly-closed hands, whose white gloves outlined the nails and tightened on the flesh at the wrists. Lace trimmings, diamond brooches, medallion bracelets trembled on bodices, gleamed on breasts, clinked on bare arms.","sentences":[{"en":"The quadrille over, the floor was occupied by groups of men standing up and talking and servants in livery bearing large trays.","zh":"四组舞结束，舞场只有男人留下来，一群一群站着说话，听差穿着制服，端着大盘子，往来穿梭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Along the line of seated women painted fans were fluttering, bouquets half hid smiling faces, and gold stoppered scent-bottles were turned in partly-closed hands, whose white gloves outlined the nails and tightened on the flesh at the wrists.","zh":"妇女坐成一排，摇动画扇，微笑的面孔被花遮住一半，白手套显出指尖的轮廓，紧紧扣住腕上的肉，手松松攥着一个金塞鼻烟壶，在手心转来转去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lace trimmings, diamond brooches, medallion bracelets trembled on bodices, gleamed on breasts, clinked on bare arms.","zh":"花边缀饰在衣服上颤动，钻石别针在胸前闪烁，镶坠子的手镯在光胳膊上作响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The hair, well-smoothed over the temples and knotted at the nape, bore crowns, or bunches, or sprays of myosotis, jasmine, pomegranate blossoms, ears of corn, and corn-flowers. Calmly seated in their places, mothers with forbidding countenances were wearing red turbans.","sentences":[{"en":"The hair, well-smoothed over the temples and knotted at the nape, bore crowns, or bunches, or sprays of myosotis, jasmine, pomegranate blossoms, ears of corn, and corn-flowers.","zh":"头发贴在额头，盘在后颈，插着勿忘草、素馨花、石榴花、黍穗或者矢车菊，有王冠样子、花簇样子、树枝样子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Calmly seated in their places, mothers with forbidding countenances were wearing red turbans.","zh":"母亲们裹着红头巾 ，颦蹙着脸，安安详详，待在她们的座位里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma’s heart beat rather faster when, her partner holding her by the tips of the fingers, she took her place in a line with the dancers, and waited for the first note to start. But her emotion soon vanished, and, swaying to the rhythm of the orchestra, she glided forward with slight movements of the neck. A smile rose to her lips at certain delicate phrases of the violin, that sometimes played alone while the other instruments were silent; one could hear the clear clink of the louis d’or that were being thrown down upon the card tables in the next room; then all struck again, the cornet-a-piston uttered its sonorous note, feet marked time, skirts swelled and rustled, hands touched and parted; the same eyes falling before you met yours again.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma’s heart beat rather faster when, her partner holding her by the tips of the fingers, she took her place in a line with the dancers, and waited for the first note to start.","zh":"邀爱玛跳舞的男子，用指尖搂着她；她过去站好，等候音乐开始：这期间她有一点心跳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But her emotion soon vanished, and, swaying to the rhythm of the orchestra, she glided forward with slight movements of the neck.","zh":"不过她很快就镇定下来，随着乐队的节奏，左右摇曳，脚向前滑，颈项微微摆动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A smile rose to her lips at certain delicate phrases of the violin, that sometimes played alone while the other instruments were silent; one could hear the clear clink of the louis d’or that were being thrown down upon the card tables in the next room; then all struck again, the cornet-a-piston uttered its sonorous note, feet marked time, skirts swelled and rustled, hands touched and parted; the same eyes falling before you met yours again.","zh":"有时候，别的乐器停止，只有小提琴演奏，她听到妙处，嘴唇露出微笑；隔壁传来金路易 倒在桌毯上的叮当声；随后，乐器又全响了，铜号吹出嘹亮的声音。脚再合上拍子，裙子飘开，蹭了过去，手时而握在一起，时而分开，眼睛原来在你面前低下去，现在又仰起来，望你的眼睛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A few men (some fifteen or so), of twenty-five to forty, scattered here and there among the dancers or talking at the doorways, distinguished themselves from the crowd by a certain air of breeding, whatever their differences in age, dress, or face.","sentences":[{"en":"A few men (some fifteen or so), of twenty-five to forty, scattered here and there among the dancers or talking at the doorways, distinguished themselves from the crowd by a certain air of breeding, whatever their differences in age, dress, or face.","zh":"有些男子（约十四五位），二十五岁到四十岁不等，散见在舞客中，或者在门口闲谈，其年龄、衣着和面貌纵然各异，由于家世相近，一眼望去，就显出了与大家的不同。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Their clothes, better made, seemed of finer cloth, and their hair, brought forward in curls towards the temples, glossy with more delicate pomades. They had the complexion of wealth—that clear complexion that is heightened by the pallor of porcelain, the shimmer of satin, the veneer of old furniture, and that an ordered regimen of exquisite nurture maintains at its best. Their necks moved easily in their low cravats, their long whiskers fell over their turned-down collars, they wiped their lips upon handkerchiefs with embroidered initials that gave forth a subtle perfume. Those who were beginning to grow old had an air of youth, while there was something mature in the faces of the young. In their unconcerned looks was the calm of passions daily satiated, and through all their gentleness of manner pierced that peculiar brutality, the result of a command of half-easy things, in which force is exercised and vanity amused—the management of thoroughbred horses and the society of loose women.","sentences":[{"en":"Their clothes, better made, seemed of finer cloth, and their hair, brought forward in curls towards the temples, glossy with more delicate pomades.","zh":"他们的燕尾服，缝工分外考究，料子也特别柔软；头发一圈一圈压在太阳穴，亮光光的，抹了更好的生发油。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They had the complexion of wealth—that clear complexion that is heightened by the pallor of porcelain, the shimmer of satin, the veneer of old furniture, and that an ordered regimen of exquisite nurture maintains at its best.","zh":"肤色是阔人肤色，白白的，其所以能这样白而又白，显然是饮食讲究、善于摄生的结果，而瓷器的青白、锦缎的闪光、上等木器的油漆，越发衬白了肤色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Their necks moved easily in their low cravats, their long whiskers fell over their turned-down collars, they wiped their lips upon handkerchiefs with embroidered initials that gave forth a subtle perfume.","zh":"领结低低的，颈项旋转自如；领子朝下翻，络腮胡须长长的，搭在上头；他们揩嘴唇的手绢，有一股香气逸出，上面绣着姓名的第一个字母，绣得大大的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Those who were beginning to grow old had an air of youth, while there was something mature in the faces of the young.","zh":"开始走向老境的人，模样透着年轻，而年轻人的脸显着老成。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In their unconcerned looks was the calm of passions daily satiated, and through all their gentleness of manner pierced that peculiar brutality, the result of a command of half-easy things, in which force is exercised and vanity amused—the management of thoroughbred horses and the society of loose women.","zh":"情欲天天得到满足，所以他们的视线，有一种漠然和恬适的神情。他们举止虽然温文尔雅，却隐隐透出一种特殊的粗暴气息，借此控制那些易于驾驭的事物。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A few steps from Emma a gentleman in a blue coat was talking of Italy with a pale young woman wearing a parure of pearls.","sentences":[{"en":"A few steps from Emma a gentleman in a blue coat was talking of Italy with a pale young woman wearing a parure of pearls.","zh":"他们玩纯种马，追逐浪荡女人，以显示力量来满足虚荣心。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They were praising the breadth of the columns of St. Peter’s, Tivoly, Vesuvius, Castellamare, and Cassines, the roses of Genoa, the Coliseum by moonlight. With her other ear Emma was listening to a conversation full of words she did not understand. A circle gathered round a very young man who the week before had beaten “Miss Arabella” and “Romolus,” and won two thousand louis jumping a ditch in England. One complained that his racehorses were growing fat; another of the printers’ errors that had disfigured the name of his horse.","sentences":[{"en":"They were praising the breadth of the columns of St. Peter’s, Tivoly, Vesuvius, Castellamare, and Cassines, the roses of Genoa, the Coliseum by moonlight.","zh":"离爱玛三步远，有一位绅士，穿蓝燕尾服，和一位戴珍珠花钏、面色苍白的年轻妇女，闲谈意大利。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With her other ear Emma was listening to a conversation full of words she did not understand.","zh":"他们称赞圣彼得教堂柱子的粗大、热那亚的玫瑰、月光下的圆形剧场，也称赞蒂沃里、维苏威、斯塔比亚海堡和卡辛。爱玛另一只耳朵听来的话，有许多字句她听不懂。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A circle gathered round a very young man who the week before had beaten “Miss Arabella” and “Romolus,” and won two thousand louis jumping a ditch in England.","zh":"他们称赞圣彼得教堂柱子的粗大、热那亚的玫瑰、月光下的圆形剧场，也称赞蒂沃里、维苏威、斯塔比亚海堡和卡辛。爱玛另一只耳朵听来的话，有许多字句她听不懂。","scope":"group"},{"en":"One complained that his racehorses were growing fat; another of the printers’ errors that had disfigured the name of his horse.","zh":"大家围着一个年轻男子：他上星期赛马，赢了阿拉贝尔小姐和罗慕路， 在英吉利跳一道沟，赚了两千路易。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The atmosphere of the ball was heavy; the lamps were growing dim.","sentences":[{"en":"The atmosphere of the ball was heavy; the lamps were growing dim.","zh":"一个人叹息他的赛马长膘了，另一个人抱怨印错了他的马的名字。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Guests were flocking to the billiard room. A servant got upon a chair and broke the window-panes. At the crash of the glass Madame Bovary turned her head and saw in the garden the faces of peasants pressed against the window looking in at them. Then the memory of the Bertaux came back to her. She saw the farm again, the muddy pond, her father in a blouse under the apple trees, and she saw herself again as formerly, skimming with her finger the cream off the milk-pans in the dairy. But in the refulgence of the present hour her past life, so distinct until then, faded away completely, and she almost doubted having lived it. She was there; beyond the ball was only shadow overspreading all the rest. She was just eating a maraschino ice that she held with her left hand in a silver-gilt cup, her eyes half-closed, and the spoon between her teeth.","sentences":[{"en":"Guests were flocking to the billiard room.","zh":"舞场空气窒闷；灯暗下来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A servant got upon a chair and broke the window-panes.","zh":"人朝弹子间走。有一个听差，踩上椅子，砸破两块玻璃；包法利夫人听见玻璃碎，回过头去，望见花园里有一些乡下人，脸贴住窗玻璃，往里张望。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At the crash of the glass Madame Bovary turned her head and saw in the garden the faces of peasants pressed against the window looking in at them.","zh":"人朝弹子间走。有一个听差，踩上椅子，砸破两块玻璃；包法利夫人听见玻璃碎，回过头去，望见花园里有一些乡下人，脸贴住窗玻璃，往里张望。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then the memory of the Bertaux came back to her.","zh":"她不由得想起拜尔托。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She saw the farm again, the muddy pond, her father in a blouse under the apple trees, and she saw herself again as formerly, skimming with her finger the cream off the milk-pans in the dairy.","zh":"她又看见田庄、泥泞的池塘、苹果树下穿工人服的父亲；她也看见自己，像往常一样，在牛奶棚揭掉瓦盆里的乳皮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But in the refulgence of the present hour her past life, so distinct until then, faded away completely, and she almost doubted having lived it.","zh":"她过去的生活，虽然像在眼前一样，可是在现时五光十色之下，也就完全消逝了，她几乎不相信自己这样生活过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was there; beyond the ball was only shadow overspreading all the rest.","zh":"她在舞厅；舞厅之外，朦胧一片，统统盖在黑影底下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was just eating a maraschino ice that she held with her left hand in a silver-gilt cup, her eyes half-closed, and the spoon between her teeth.","zh":"她当时左手握着一只镀银介壳，正在吃里面的樱桃酒刨冰，眼睛半闭，勺子放在口中。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A lady near her dropped her fan. A gentlemen was passing.","sentences":[{"en":"A lady near her dropped her fan.","zh":"旁边一位贵妇，掉了扇子，正好过来一位舞客。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A gentlemen was passing.","zh":"旁边一位贵妇，掉了扇子，正好过来一位舞客。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Would you be so good,” said the lady, “as to pick up my fan that has fallen behind the sofa?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Would you be so good,” said the lady, “as to pick up my fan that has fallen behind the sofa?”","zh":"贵妇道：“先生，我的扇子掉在这张沙发后头，能不能劳驾拾起来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The gentleman bowed, and as he moved to stretch out his arm, Emma saw the hand of a young woman throw something white, folded in a triangle, into his hat. The gentleman, picking up the fan, offered it to the lady respectfully; she thanked him with an inclination of the head, and began smelling her bouquet.","sentences":[{"en":"The gentleman bowed, and as he moved to stretch out his arm, Emma saw the hand of a young woman throw something white, folded in a triangle, into his hat.","zh":"绅士弯下腰去，伸出胳膊，爱玛就见少妇乘机往他的帽子里扔进一点白东西，叠成三角形。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The gentleman, picking up the fan, offered it to the lady respectfully; she thanked him with an inclination of the head, and began smelling her bouquet.","zh":"他捡起扇子，恭恭敬敬，献给贵妇；她点点头，谢了谢他，开始嗅她的花。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After supper, where were plenty of Spanish and Rhine wines, soups à la bisque and au lait d’amandes, puddings à la Trafalgar, and all sorts of cold meats with jellies that trembled in the dishes, the carriages one after the other began to drive off. Raising the corners of the muslin curtain, one could see the light of their lanterns glimmering through the darkness. The seats began to empty, some card-players were still left; the musicians were cooling the tips of their fingers on their tongues. Charles was half asleep, his back propped against a door.","sentences":[{"en":"After supper, where were plenty of Spanish and Rhine wines, soups à la bisque and au lait d’amandes, puddings à la Trafalgar, and all sorts of cold meats with jellies that trembled in the dishes, the carriages one after the other began to drive off.","zh":"夜宵有大量西班牙酒和莱茵葡萄酒，虾糊汤和杏仁汤，特拉法尔加的布丁 ，还有各色冷肉，四边冻子直在盘里颤抖。用过夜宵之后，马车开始一辆一辆走动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Raising the corners of the muslin curtain, one could see the light of their lanterns glimmering through the darkness.","zh":"掀起一角纱帘，你就看见车灯的亮光，星星点点，在黑夜里消逝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The seats began to empty, some card-players were still left; the musicians were cooling the tips of their fingers on their tongues.","zh":"长凳空了；有几个赌徒，还没有走；乐师拿手指尖放在舌头上取凉；查理背靠一扇门，几乎睡着了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles was half asleep, his back propped against a door.","zh":"长凳空了；有几个赌徒，还没有走；乐师拿手指尖放在舌头上取凉；查理背靠一扇门，几乎睡着了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At three o’clock the cotillion began. Emma did not know how to waltz. Everyone was waltzing, Mademoiselle d’Andervilliers herself and the Marquis; only the guests staying at the castle were still there, about a dozen persons.","sentences":[{"en":"At three o’clock the cotillion began.","zh":"早晨三点钟，开始花色舞。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma did not know how to waltz.","zh":"爱玛不会华尔兹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everyone was waltzing, Mademoiselle d’Andervilliers herself and the Marquis; only the guests staying at the castle were still there, about a dozen persons.","zh":"人人跳华尔兹，侯爵夫人，连昂代维利耶小姐也跳。留下来的，只有住宿的客人，一共不过十二三位。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One of the waltzers, however, who was familiarly called Viscount, and whose low cut waistcoat seemed moulded to his chest, came a second time to ask Madame Bovary to dance, assuring her that he would guide her, and that she would get through it very well.","sentences":[{"en":"One of the waltzers, however, who was familiarly called Viscount, and whose low cut waistcoat seemed moulded to his chest, came a second time to ask Madame Bovary to dance, assuring her that he would guide her, and that she would get through it very well.","zh":"有一位跳华尔兹的，背心敞得开开的，就像照胸脯裁成的一样，大家顺口称他“子爵”，邀包法利夫人跳过一次舞，现在又来邀她，答应教她，还说她会跳得好的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They began slowly, then went more rapidly. They turned; all around them was turning—the lamps, the furniture, the wainscoting, the floor, like a disc on a pivot. On passing near the doors the bottom of Emma’s dress caught against his trousers.","sentences":[{"en":"They began slowly, then went more rapidly.","zh":"他们开始慢，后来快了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They turned; all around them was turning—the lamps, the furniture, the wainscoting, the floor, like a disc on a pivot.","zh":"他们旋转，样样东西围着他们旋转，灯、木器、板壁和拼花地板，就像一个圆盘在轴上旋转一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On passing near the doors the bottom of Emma’s dress caught against his trousers.","zh":"走过门边，爱玛的袍子，靠下飘了起来，蹭着对方的裤管；他们的腿，一来一去，轮流捣动；他朝下看她，她朝上看他；她觉得头昏眼花，连忙停住。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Their legs commingled; he looked down at her; she raised her eyes to his. A torpor seized her; she stopped. They started again, and with a more rapid movement; the Viscount, dragging her along disappeared with her to the end of the gallery, where panting, she almost fell, and for a moment rested her head upon his breast. And then, still turning, but more slowly, he guided her back to her seat. She leaned back against the wall and covered her eyes with her hands.","sentences":[{"en":"Their legs commingled; he looked down at her; she raised her eyes to his.","zh":"走过门边，爱玛的袍子，靠下飘了起来，蹭着对方的裤管；他们的腿，一来一去，轮流捣动；他朝下看她，她朝上看他；她觉得头昏眼花，连忙停住。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A torpor seized her; she stopped.","zh":"走过门边，爱玛的袍子，靠下飘了起来，蹭着对方的裤管；他们的腿，一来一去，轮流捣动；他朝下看她，她朝上看他；她觉得头昏眼花，连忙停住。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They started again, and with a more rapid movement; the Viscount, dragging her along disappeared with her to the end of the gallery, where panting, she almost fell, and for a moment rested her head upon his breast.","zh":"他们又跳起来，子爵转得越发快了，一直把她带到走廊尽头，离开众人；她气喘吁吁，险些跌倒，有一时，头倚着他的胸脯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then, still turning, but more slowly, he guided her back to her seat.","zh":"随后，他仍然转下去，不过慢了一些，送她回到原来座位；她朝墙一靠，手蒙住眼睛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She leaned back against the wall and covered her eyes with her hands.","zh":"随后，他仍然转下去，不过慢了一些，送她回到原来座位；她朝墙一靠，手蒙住眼睛。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"When she opened them again, in the middle of the drawing room three waltzers were kneeling before a lady sitting on a stool.","sentences":[{"en":"When she opened them again, in the middle of the drawing room three waltzers were kneeling before a lady sitting on a stool.","zh":"她睁开眼睛，就见客厅当中，有一位贵妇，坐在一张小凳上，三个跳华尔兹的男子跪在面前。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She chose the Viscount, and the violin struck up once more.","sentences":[{"en":"She chose the Viscount, and the violin struck up once more.","zh":"她挑选子爵，小提琴又响起来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Everyone looked at them. They passed and re-passed, she with rigid body, her chin bent down, and he always in the same pose, his figure curved, his elbow rounded, his chin thrown forward. That woman knew how to waltz! They kept up a long time, and tired out all the others.","sentences":[{"en":"Everyone looked at them.","zh":"大家望着他们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They passed and re-passed, she with rigid body, her chin bent down, and he always in the same pose, his figure curved, his elbow rounded, his chin thrown forward.","zh":"他们来了又去，去了又来，她低下头，身子一动不动，他也一直是一个姿势，身子有些类似一张弓，胳膊肘放圆，下巴向前。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That woman knew how to waltz!","zh":"这个女人，会跳华尔兹！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They kept up a long time, and tired out all the others.","zh":"他们跳了许久，人人累了，他们还在跳。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then they talked a few moments longer, and after the goodnights, or rather good mornings, the guests of the château retired to bed.","sentences":[{"en":"Then they talked a few moments longer, and after the goodnights, or rather good mornings, the guests of the château retired to bed.","zh":"客人们又闲谈了一阵，说过再会，或者不如说是早安，这才走开睡觉。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles dragged himself up by the balusters. His “knees were going up into his body.” He had spent five consecutive hours standing bolt upright at the card tables, watching them play whist, without understanding anything about it, and it was with a deep sigh of relief that he pulled off his boots.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles dragged himself up by the balusters.","zh":"查理扶着楼梯，累得腿也站不直了，一步一拖。","scope":"group"},{"en":"His “knees were going up into his body.”","zh":"查理扶着楼梯，累得腿也站不直了，一步一拖。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He had spent five consecutive hours standing bolt upright at the card tables, watching them play whist, without understanding anything about it, and it was with a deep sigh of relief that he pulled off his boots.","zh":"一连五小时，他站在牌桌前面，看人斗牌，自己一窍不通。所以临到他脱靴子，如释重负，舒了一口长气。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma threw a shawl over her shoulders, opened the window, and leant out.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma threw a shawl over her shoulders, opened the window, and leant out.","zh":"爱玛拿一条披肩盖住肩膀，打开窗户，胳膊肘支在上头。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The night was dark; some drops of rain were falling. She breathed in the damp wind that refreshed her eyelids. The music of the ball was still murmuring in her ears. And she tried to keep herself awake in order to prolong the illusion of this luxurious life that she would soon have to give up.","sentences":[{"en":"The night was dark; some drops of rain were falling.","zh":"黑漆漆的夜晚，细雨蒙蒙。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She breathed in the damp wind that refreshed her eyelids.","zh":"她吸着湿润的空气，风吹凉她的眼皮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The music of the ball was still murmuring in her ears.","zh":"跳舞的音乐还在她的耳边鸣响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And she tried to keep herself awake in order to prolong the illusion of this luxurious life that she would soon have to give up.","zh":"她尽力挣扎不睡，延长这种豪华生活的境界，因为没有多久，她就非放弃不可。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Day began to break. She looked long at the windows of the château, trying to guess which were the rooms of all those she had noticed the evening before. She would fain have known their lives, have penetrated, blended with them. But she was shivering with cold. She undressed, and cowered down between the sheets against Charles, who was asleep.","sentences":[{"en":"Day began to break.","zh":"天开始亮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She looked long at the windows of the château, trying to guess which were the rooms of all those she had noticed the evening before.","zh":"她望庄园窗户望了许久，试着猜测她这一夜注意的那些人睡在哪些房间。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would fain have known their lives, have penetrated, blended with them.","zh":"她巴不得知道他们的生平事迹，渗进去，打成一片。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she was shivering with cold.","zh":"但是她直打寒噤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She undressed, and cowered down between the sheets against Charles, who was asleep.","zh":"她脱去衣服，缩进被窝，躺在睡熟了的查理一旁。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"There were a great many people to luncheon. The repast lasted ten minutes; no liqueurs were served, which astonished the doctor.","sentences":[{"en":"There were a great many people to luncheon.","zh":"早饭有许多人用，十分钟了事；任何酒也没有，医生诧异了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The repast lasted ten minutes; no liqueurs were served, which astonished the doctor.","zh":"饭后，昂代维利耶小姐捡了一些蛋糕屑，放进一只小盘，带给池塘的天鹅吃。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Next, Mademoiselle d’Andervilliers collected some pieces of roll in a small basket to take them to the swans on the ornamental waters, and they went to walk in the hot-houses, where strange plants, bristling with hairs, rose in pyramids under hanging vases, whence, as from over-filled nests of serpents, fell long green cords interlacing. The orangery, which was at the other end, led by a covered way to the outhouses of the château. The Marquis, to amuse the young woman, took her to see the stables.","sentences":[{"en":"Next, Mademoiselle d’Andervilliers collected some pieces of roll in a small basket to take them to the swans on the ornamental waters, and they went to walk in the hot-houses, where strange plants, bristling with hairs, rose in pyramids under hanging vases, whence, as from over-filled nests of serpents, fell long green cords interlacing.","zh":"大家散步，来到花坞，里面有一些奇怪的植物，毛茸茸的，一层层垒在架子上，像金字塔一样，上面悬着一些花盆，仿佛蛇窟的蛇太多了，滴里耷拉，垂下几条绿油油的长枝子，盘在一起。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The orangery, which was at the other end, led by a covered way to the outhouses of the château.","zh":"花坞过去，就是橘林，密密层层，直到庄园的附属建筑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The Marquis, to amuse the young woman, took her to see the stables.","zh":"侯爵要少妇开心，带她去看马厩。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Above the basket-shaped racks porcelain slabs bore the names of the horses in black letters. Each animal in its stall whisked its tail when anyone went near and said “Tchk! tchk!” The boards of the harness room shone like the flooring of a drawing room. The carriage harness was piled up in the middle against two twisted columns, and the bits, the whips, the spurs, the curbs, were ranged in a line all along the wall.","sentences":[{"en":"Above the basket-shaped racks porcelain slabs bore the names of the horses in black letters.","zh":"马槽是篮子形状，上空挂了一些瓷牌，用黑字写着马的名字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Each animal in its stall whisked its tail when anyone went near and said “Tchk! tchk!”","zh":"每一匹马，见人走过，打舌头响，就在枥间骚动起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The boards of the harness room shone like the flooring of a drawing room.","zh":"马具间的地板如同客厅里拼花地板一样耀眼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The carriage harness was piled up in the middle against two twisted columns, and the bits, the whips, the spurs, the curbs, were ranged in a line all along the wall.","zh":"当中两根柱子，可以旋转，上面挂着鞍辔，沿墙是一长排马衔、马鞭、马镫和马勒。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles, meanwhile, went to ask a groom to put his horse to. The dog-cart was brought to the foot of the steps, and, all the parcels being crammed in, the Bovarys paid their respects to the Marquis and Marchioness and set out again for Tostes.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles, meanwhile, went to ask a groom to put his horse to.","zh":"查理这期间，烦劳一个听差，驾好他的包克。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The dog-cart was brought to the foot of the steps, and, all the parcels being crammed in, the Bovarys paid their respects to the Marquis and Marchioness and set out again for Tostes.","zh":"车停在台阶前面，包裹一件一件塞上车，包法利夫妇向侯爵夫妇辞过行，向道特出发了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma watched the turning wheels in silence. Charles, on the extreme edge of the seat, held the reins with his two arms wide apart, and the little horse ambled along in the shafts that were too big for him. The loose reins hanging over his crupper were wet with foam, and the box fastened on behind the chaise gave great regular bumps against it.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma watched the turning wheels in silence.","zh":"爱玛默不作声，望着车轮滚动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles, on the extreme edge of the seat, held the reins with his two arms wide apart, and the little horse ambled along in the shafts that were too big for him.","zh":"查理坐在长凳外沿，伸开两只胳膊赶车。马小，车辕太宽，马在当中，放开蹄子跑，缰绳软搭搭的，浸在汗水里，直打屁股。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The loose reins hanging over his crupper were wet with foam, and the box fastened on behind the chaise gave great regular bumps against it.","zh":"盒子捆在包克后头，不时撞着车厢，咕咚咕咚响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They were on the heights of Thibourville when suddenly some horsemen with cigars between their lips passed laughing. Emma thought she recognized the Viscount, turned back, and caught on the horizon only the movement of the heads rising or falling with the unequal cadence of the trot or gallop.","sentences":[{"en":"They were on the heights of Thibourville when suddenly some horsemen with cigars between their lips passed laughing.","zh":"他们上到狄布尔镇高坡，眼前忽然来了几个骑马的人，噙着雪茄笑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma thought she recognized the Viscount, turned back, and caught on the horizon only the movement of the heads rising or falling with the unequal cadence of the trot or gallop.","zh":"爱玛自以为认出了里面有子爵；她扭回头看，仅仅望见天边人头或高或低，依照奔驰快慢，起伏无定而已。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A mile farther on they had to stop to mend with some string the traces that had broken.","sentences":[{"en":"A mile farther on they had to stop to mend with some string the traces that had broken.","zh":"又走了四分之一古里，后 断了，他们只得停下来，用绳子接好。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Charles, giving a last look to the harness, saw something on the ground between his horse’s legs, and he picked up a cigar-case with a green silk border and beblazoned in the centre like the door of a carriage.","sentences":[{"en":"But Charles, giving a last look to the harness, saw something on the ground between his horse’s legs, and he picked up a cigar-case with a green silk border and beblazoned in the centre like the door of a carriage.","zh":"查理最后查看一眼马具，发现马腿之间，地上有什么东西；他捡起一只雪茄匣，绿绸镶边，当中家徽，好像大户人家马车的车门一样。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“There are even two cigars in it,” said he; “they’ll do for this evening after dinner.”","sentences":[{"en":"“There are even two cigars in it,” said he; “they’ll do for this evening after dinner.”","zh":"“里头还有两支雪茄，正好今天晚饭后用。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, do you smoke?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, do you smoke?” she asked.","zh":"她问道：“瞎说，你吸烟吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sometimes, when I get a chance.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sometimes, when I get a chance.”","zh":"“有时候，也看机会。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He put his find in his pocket and whipped up the nag.","sentences":[{"en":"He put his find in his pocket and whipped up the nag.","zh":"他拿拾来的东西放进衣袋，抽打小马。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When they reached home the dinner was not ready. Madame lost her temper. Nastasie answered rudely.","sentences":[{"en":"When they reached home the dinner was not ready.","zh":"他们回到家，发现晚饭还没有烧好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame lost her temper.","zh":"太太发脾气了，娜丝塔西顶嘴。爱玛说：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Nastasie answered rudely.","zh":"太太发脾气了，娜丝塔西顶嘴。爱玛说：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Leave the room!” said Emma. “You are forgetting yourself. I give you warning.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave the room!” said Emma.","zh":"太太发脾气了，娜丝塔西顶嘴。爱玛说：","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You are forgetting yourself.","zh":"“滚！岂有此理，你给我走。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I give you warning.”","zh":"“滚！岂有此理，你给我走。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"For dinner there was onion soup and a piece of veal with sorrel.","sentences":[{"en":"For dinner there was onion soup and a piece of veal with sorrel.","zh":"晚饭是葱汤和一块酸模小牛肉。查理坐在爱玛对面，一副快乐神气，搓着手道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles, seated opposite Emma, rubbed his hands gleefully.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles, seated opposite Emma, rubbed his hands gleefully.","zh":"晚饭是葱汤和一块酸模小牛肉。查理坐在爱玛对面，一副快乐神气，搓着手道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“How good it is to be at home again!”","sentences":[{"en":"“How good it is to be at home again!”","zh":"“回到家里，开心多了！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Nastasie could be heard crying. He was rather fond of the poor girl. She had formerly, during the wearisome time of his widowhood, kept him company many an evening. She had been his first patient, his oldest acquaintance in the place.","sentences":[{"en":"Nastasie could be heard crying.","zh":"他们听见娜丝塔西哭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was rather fond of the poor girl.","zh":"他有点喜欢这可怜的女仆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had formerly, during the wearisome time of his widowhood, kept him company many an evening.","zh":"从前鳏居无聊，她陪他消磨过许多黄昏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had been his first patient, his oldest acquaintance in the place.","zh":"她是他的第一个病人、当地最早的熟人，他终于道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Have you given her warning for good?” he asked at last.","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you given her warning for good?” he asked at last.","zh":"“你当真打发她走？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes. Who is to prevent me?” she replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.","zh":"她答道：“是啊。谁拦我不成？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Who is to prevent me?” she replied.","zh":"她答道：“是啊。谁拦我不成？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then they warmed themselves in the kitchen while their room was being made ready. Charles began to smoke. He smoked with lips protruding, spitting every moment, recoiling at every puff.","sentences":[{"en":"Then they warmed themselves in the kitchen while their room was being made ready.","zh":"女仆整理卧室时，他们来到厨房取暖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles began to smoke.","zh":"查理开始吸烟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He smoked with lips protruding, spitting every moment, recoiling at every puff.","zh":"他伸长嘴唇吸，不住吐痰，吐一口烟，闪开一回。她显出鄙夷的样子道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You’ll make yourself ill,” she said scornfully.","sentences":[{"en":"“You’ll make yourself ill,” she said scornfully.","zh":"“你要把自己弄病了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He put down his cigar and ran to swallow a glass of cold water at the pump. Emma seizing hold of the cigar case threw it quickly to the back of the cupboard.","sentences":[{"en":"He put down his cigar and ran to swallow a glass of cold water at the pump.","zh":"他放下雪茄，跑到水龙头跟前，喝了一口冷水。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma seizing hold of the cigar case threw it quickly to the back of the cupboard.","zh":"爱玛抓起雪茄匣，顺手丢进碗橱里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day was a long one. She walked about her little garden, up and down the same walks, stopping before the beds, before the espalier, before the plaster curate, looking with amazement at all these things of once-on-a-time that she knew so well. How far off the ball seemed already! What was it that thus set so far asunder the morning of the day before yesterday and the evening of to-day? Her journey to Vaubyessard had made a hole in her life, like one of those great crevices that a storm will sometimes make in one night in mountains. Still she was resigned. She devoutly put away in her drawers her beautiful dress, down to the satin shoes whose soles were yellowed with the slippery wax of the dancing floor. Her heart was like these. In its friction against wealth something had come over it that could not be effaced.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day was a long one.","zh":"第二天，日子长悠悠的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She walked about her little garden, up and down the same walks, stopping before the beds, before the espalier, before the plaster curate, looking with amazement at all these things of once-on-a-time that she knew so well.","zh":"她在她的小花园散步，在几条小径上走来走去，站在花畦前、贴墙的果树前、石膏神甫像前停一停。往日非常熟悉的这些东西，如今看在眼里却感到诧异。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How far off the ball seemed already!","zh":"舞会似乎已经离她很远！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was it that thus set so far asunder the morning of the day before yesterday and the evening of to-day?","zh":"前天早晨和今天黄昏，中间到底出了什么事，相隔如此遥远？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her journey to Vaubyessard had made a hole in her life, like one of those great crevices that a storm will sometimes make in one night in mountains.","zh":"渥毕萨尔之行，在她的生活上，凿了一个洞眼，如同山上那些大裂缝，一阵狂风暴雨，只一夜工夫，就成了这般模样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Still she was resigned.","zh":"渥毕萨尔之行，在她的生活上，凿了一个洞眼，如同山上那些大裂缝，一阵狂风暴雨，只一夜工夫，就成了这般模样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She devoutly put away in her drawers her beautiful dress, down to the satin shoes whose soles were yellowed with the slippery wax of the dancing floor.","zh":"她无可奈何，只得看开些，不过她的漂亮衣着，甚至她的缎鞋——拼花地板滑溜的蜡磨黄了鞋底，她都虔心虔意放入五斗柜。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her heart was like these.","zh":"她无可奈何，只得看开些，不过她的漂亮衣着，甚至她的缎鞋——拼花地板滑溜的蜡磨黄了鞋底，她都虔心虔意放入五斗柜。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In its friction against wealth something had come over it that could not be effaced.","zh":"她的心也像它们一样，和财富有过接触之后，添了一些磨蹭不掉的东西。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The memory of this ball, then, became an occupation for Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"The memory of this ball, then, became an occupation for Emma.","zh":"她的心也像它们一样，和财富有过接触之后，添了一些磨蹭不掉的东西。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Whenever the Wednesday came round she said to herself as she awoke, “Ah! I was there a week—a fortnight—three weeks ago.”","sentences":[{"en":"Whenever the Wednesday came round she said to herself as she awoke, “Ah!","zh":"于是对舞会的回忆，成了爱玛的重要生活内容。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was there a week—a fortnight—three weeks ago.”","zh":"每逢星期三，她醒过来，就问自己道：“啊！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And little by little the faces grew confused in her remembrance.","sentences":[{"en":"And little by little the faces grew confused in her remembrance.","zh":"一星期以前…两星期以前…三星期以前，我在那边！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She forgot the tune of the quadrilles; she no longer saw the liveries and appointments so distinctly; some details escaped her, but the regret remained with her.","sentences":[{"en":"She forgot the tune of the quadrilles; she no longer saw the liveries and appointments so distinctly; some details escaped her, but the regret remained with her.","zh":"然而在她的记忆之中，面貌渐渐混淆；她忘却了四组舞的曲调；她不再能真切地想起仆从的号衣和房间；若干细节淡忘了，可是心头留下了怅惘。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"1-9","part":1,"n":9,"title":"Part I · Chapter 9","titleZh":"上卷 · 9","paragraphs":[{"en":"Often when Charles was out she took from the cupboard, between the folds of the linen where she had left it, the green silk cigar case. She looked at it, opened it, and even smelt the odour of the lining—a mixture of verbena and tobacco. Whose was it? The Viscount’s? Perhaps it was a present from his mistress. It had been embroidered on some rosewood frame, a pretty little thing, hidden from all eyes, that had occupied many hours, and over which had fallen the soft curls of the pensive worker. A breath of love had passed over the stitches on the canvas; each prick of the needle had fixed there a hope or a memory, and all those interwoven threads of silk were but the continuity of the same silent passion. And then one morning the Viscount had taken it away with him. Of what had they spoken when it lay upon the wide-mantelled chimneys between flower-vases and Pompadour clocks? She was at Tostes; he was at Paris now, far away! What was this Paris like? What a vague name! She repeated it in a low voice, for the mere pleasure of it; it rang in her ears like a great cathedral bell; it shone before her eyes, even on the labels of her pomade-pots.","sentences":[{"en":"Often when Charles was out she took from the cupboard, between the folds of the linen where she had left it, the green silk cigar case.","zh":"查理不在家，她常常走到碗橱跟前，取出绿绸雪茄匣，她先前丢在叠好的饭巾一类东西当中。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She looked at it, opened it, and even smelt the odour of the lining—a mixture of verbena and tobacco.","zh":"她看了又看，开了又开，甚至还闻了闻衬里的味道：一种杂有美女樱与烟草的味道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Whose was it?","zh":"是谁的？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The Viscount’s?","zh":"子爵的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps it was a present from his mistress.","zh":"说不定是他的情妇用红木绷子绣出来，作为纪念送他的。绷子是一件细巧物件，藏起来不给人看，绣的人满腹心事，轻柔的发鬟搭在上面，一绣就好几小时，爱情的气息透过绣花底布上的针眼，每一针扎下去，不是扎下希望，便是扎下了回忆：这些交错的丝线，只是同一缄默的热情的延续。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It had been embroidered on some rosewood frame, a pretty little thing, hidden from all eyes, that had occupied many hours, and over which had fallen the soft curls of the pensive worker.","zh":"说不定是他的情妇用红木绷子绣出来，作为纪念送他的。绷子是一件细巧物件，藏起来不给人看，绣的人满腹心事，轻柔的发鬟搭在上面，一绣就好几小时，爱情的气息透过绣花底布上的针眼，每一针扎下去，不是扎下希望，便是扎下了回忆：这些交错的丝线，只是同一缄默的热情的延续。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A breath of love had passed over the stitches on the canvas; each prick of the needle had fixed there a hope or a memory, and all those interwoven threads of silk were but the continuity of the same silent passion.","zh":"说不定是他的情妇用红木绷子绣出来，作为纪念送他的。绷子是一件细巧物件，藏起来不给人看，绣的人满腹心事，轻柔的发鬟搭在上面，一绣就好几小时，爱情的气息透过绣花底布上的针眼，每一针扎下去，不是扎下希望，便是扎下了回忆：这些交错的丝线，只是同一缄默的热情的延续。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And then one morning the Viscount had taken it away with him.","zh":"绣成了，有一天早晨，子爵带走，放在宽炉台上，花瓶和彭巴杜尔式 座钟之间。他们这时候谈些什么？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Of what had they spoken when it lay upon the wide-mantelled chimneys between flower-vases and Pompadour clocks?","zh":"绣成了，有一天早晨，子爵带走，放在宽炉台上，花瓶和彭巴杜尔式 座钟之间。他们这时候谈些什么？","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was at Tostes; he was at Paris now, far away!","zh":"她在道特。他呀，如今在巴黎；在巴黎！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was this Paris like?","zh":"巴黎是个什么样子？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What a vague name!","zh":"名气多大！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She repeated it in a low voice, for the mere pleasure of it; it rang in her ears like a great cathedral bell; it shone before her eyes, even on the labels of her pomade-pots.","zh":"她为解闷，低声重复这两个字。它们像礼拜堂的钟声一样在耳边响，就连她的生发油瓶商标，也成了巴黎的化身，灼烁耀眼。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At night, when the carriers passed under her windows in their carts singing the “Marjolaine,” she awoke, and listened to the noise of the iron-bound wheels, which, as they gained the country road, was soon deadened by the soil. “They will be there to-morrow!” she said to herself.","sentences":[{"en":"At night, when the carriers passed under her windows in their carts singing the “Marjolaine,” she awoke, and listened to the noise of the iron-bound wheels, which, as they gained the country road, was soon deadened by the soil.","zh":"夜晚，海鱼贩子驾着大车，走过她的窗户底下，唱着牛至草 歌，铁轱辘转出村庄，很快就声音小了，她醒过来，听了听，自言自语道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“They will be there to-morrow!” she said to herself.","zh":"“他们明天就到了那边！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she followed them in thought up and down the hills, traversing villages, gliding along the highroads by the light of the stars. At the end of some indefinite distance there was always a confused spot, into which her dream died.","sentences":[{"en":"And she followed them in thought up and down the hills, traversing villages, gliding along the highroads by the light of the stars.","zh":"于是她在想象中，跟了他们上坡下岭，穿村越庄，星光熹微，顺着大路跋涉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the end of some indefinite distance there was always a confused spot, into which her dream died.","zh":"走过一段似近又远的道路，总有一个地点，模模糊糊，打断她的梦想。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She bought a plan of Paris, and with the tip of her finger on the map she walked about the capital. She went up the boulevards, stopping at every turning, between the lines of the streets, in front of the white squares that represented the houses. At last she would close the lids of her weary eyes, and see in the darkness the gas jets flaring in the wind and the steps of carriages lowered with much noise before the peristyles of theatres.","sentences":[{"en":"She bought a plan of Paris, and with the tip of her finger on the map she walked about the capital.","zh":"她买了一张巴黎地图，用手指指点点，游览纸上的京城。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She went up the boulevards, stopping at every turning, between the lines of the streets, in front of the white squares that represented the houses.","zh":"她走到大街，逗留在每个角落，在街与街之间表示房屋的白方块前面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last she would close the lids of her weary eyes, and see in the darkness the gas jets flaring in the wind and the steps of carriages lowered with much noise before the peristyles of theatres.","zh":"最后，她看累了，闭住眼睛，又见煤气灯在暗处随风摇曳，在剧院的柱廊前，一辆辆敞篷四轮马车，哗啦一声把踏板放下。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She took in “La Corbeille,” a lady’s journal, and the “Sylphe des Salons.” She devoured, without skipping a word, all the accounts of first nights, races, and soirees, took interest in the debut of a singer, in the opening of a new shop. She knew the latest fashions, the addresses of the best tailors, the days of the Bois and the Opera. In Eugene Sue she studied descriptions of furniture; she read Balzac and George Sand, seeking in them imaginary satisfaction for her own desires. Even at table she had her book by her, and turned over the pages while Charles ate and talked to her. The memory of the Viscount always returned as she read. Between him and the imaginary personages she made comparisons. But the circle of which he was the centre gradually widened round him, and the aureole that he bore, fading from his form, broadened out beyond, lighting up her other dreams.","sentences":[{"en":"She took in “La Corbeille,” a lady’s journal, and the “Sylphe des Salons.”","zh":"她订了一份妇女刊物《花篮》，又订了一份《沙龙精灵》。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She devoured, without skipping a word, all the accounts of first nights, races, and soirees, took interest in the debut of a singer, in the opening of a new shop.","zh":"她一字不漏，读完赛马、晚会和初次公演的全部报道，关心女歌唱家的首演和店铺的开张。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She knew the latest fashions, the addresses of the best tailors, the days of the Bois and the Opera.","zh":"她了解时装新款式、上等裁缝的地址、森林 和歌剧院的日程。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In Eugene Sue she studied descriptions of furniture; she read Balzac and George Sand, seeking in them imaginary satisfaction for her own desires.","zh":"她研究欧仁·苏的小说 中关于家具的描绘；她读巴尔扎克和乔治·桑的小说，寻找想象的愉快，满足本人的渴望。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Even at table she had her book by her, and turned over the pages while Charles ate and talked to her.","zh":"甚至用饭，她也带了书看，查理一边吃饭，一边同她谈话，她却只顾翻动书页。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The memory of the Viscount always returned as she read.","zh":"她一读书，总要想到子爵。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Between him and the imaginary personages she made comparisons.","zh":"她虚构了一些他和小说人物的关系。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the circle of which he was the centre gradually widened round him, and the aureole that he bore, fading from his form, broadened out beyond, lighting up her other dreams.","zh":"但是以他为中心的圆圈逐渐扩大，他的这种圆光也离开他的脸，到更远的地方，照亮别的梦想。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Paris, more vague than the ocean, glimmered before Emma’s eyes in an atmosphere of vermilion. The many lives that stirred amid this tumult were, however, divided into parts, classed as distinct pictures. Emma perceived only two or three that hid from her all the rest, and in themselves represented all humanity. The world of ambassadors moved over polished floors in drawing rooms lined with mirrors, round oval tables covered with velvet and gold-fringed cloths. There were dresses with trains, deep mysteries, anguish hidden beneath smiles. Then came the society of the duchesses; all were pale; all got up at four o’clock; the women, poor angels, wore English point on their petticoats; and the men, unappreciated geniuses under a frivolous outward seeming, rode horses to death at pleasure parties, spent the summer season at Baden, and towards the forties married heiresses. In the private rooms of restaurants, where one sups after midnight by the light of wax candles, laughed the motley crowd of men of letters and actresses. They were prodigal as kings, full of ideal, ambitious, fantastic frenzy. This was an existence outside that of all others, between heaven and earth, in the midst of storms, having something of the sublime. For the rest of the world it was lost, with no particular place and as if non-existent. The nearer things were, moreover, the more her thoughts turned away from them. All her immediate surroundings, the wearisome country, the middle-class imbeciles, the mediocrity of existence, seemed to her exceptional, a peculiar chance that had caught hold of her, while beyond stretched, as far as eye could see, an immense land of joys and passions. She confused in her desire the sensualities of luxury with the delights of the heart, elegance of manners with delicacy of sentiment. Did not love, like Indian plants, need a special soil, a particular temperature? Signs by moonlight, long embraces, tears flowing over yielded hands, all the fevers of the flesh and the languors of tenderness could not be separated from the balconies of great castles full of indolence, from boudoirs with silken curtains and thick carpets, well-filled flower-stands, a bed on a raised dias, nor from the flashing of precious stones and the shoulder-knots of liveries.","sentences":[{"en":"Paris, more vague than the ocean, glimmered before Emma’s eyes in an atmosphere of vermilion.","zh":"所以在爱玛看来，巴黎比海洋还大，到处金碧辉煌，闪闪发光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The many lives that stirred amid this tumult were, however, divided into parts, classed as distinct pictures.","zh":"活动在这翻腾的海洋中的芸芸众生，按景况的差异，分成不同的类别。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma perceived only two or three that hid from her all the rest, and in themselves represented all humanity.","zh":"爱玛只注意到两三种，便以为他们代表了全人类，再看不见其他人了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The world of ambassadors moved over polished floors in drawing rooms lined with mirrors, round oval tables covered with velvet and gold-fringed cloths.","zh":"一种是外交家社会，他们在四面全是镜子的客厅里，在铺有金穗天鹅绒桌毯的椭圆桌周围，人们穿着后摆长长的袍子，踩着闪亮的拼花地板，这里有重大的秘密，有用微笑来掩饰的焦虑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"There were dresses with trains, deep mysteries, anguish hidden beneath smiles.","zh":"一种是外交家社会，他们在四面全是镜子的客厅里，在铺有金穗天鹅绒桌毯的椭圆桌周围，人们穿着后摆长长的袍子，踩着闪亮的拼花地板，这里有重大的秘密，有用微笑来掩饰的焦虑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then came the society of the duchesses; all were pale; all got up at four o’clock; the women, poor angels, wore English point on their petticoats; and the men, unappreciated geniuses under a frivolous outward seeming, rode horses to death at pleasure parties, spent the summer season at Baden, and towards the forties married heiresses.","zh":"其次是公爵夫人的社会，这儿的人面色苍白，四点钟起床：女人们，可怜的天使！裙子下摆都镶着英吉利花边；男人们，外表平平，怀才不遇，为追寻欢乐，让马跑死了也不在乎，夏天到巴登 避暑，临了四十岁左右，娶一位女继承人拉倒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the private rooms of restaurants, where one sups after midnight by the light of wax candles, laughed the motley crowd of men of letters and actresses.","zh":"最后是餐馆的包间：一群文人和女演员，五颜六色，过了半夜来吃夜宵，烛光辉映，纵声狂笑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were prodigal as kings, full of ideal, ambitious, fantastic frenzy.","zh":"这些人挥霍如王侯，一腔没有着落的野心和荒唐无稽的狂热，傲然于天地之间、狂风暴雨之中，睥睨众人，不可一世。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This was an existence outside that of all others, between heaven and earth, in the midst of storms, having something of the sublime.","zh":"这些人挥霍如王侯，一腔没有着落的野心和荒唐无稽的狂热，傲然于天地之间、狂风暴雨之中，睥睨众人，不可一世。","scope":"group"},{"en":"For the rest of the world it was lost, with no particular place and as if non-existent.","zh":"至于人世的其他部分便不知去向了，没有明确的位置，就像不存在一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The nearer things were, moreover, the more her thoughts turned away from them.","zh":"而且离她越近的东西，她越回避。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All her immediate surroundings, the wearisome country, the middle-class imbeciles, the mediocrity of existence, seemed to her exceptional, a peculiar chance that had caught hold of her, while beyond stretched, as far as eye could see, an immense land of joys and passions.","zh":"身边的一切，沉闷的田野也好，愚蠢的小市民也好，平庸的生活也好，依她看来，都是一种例外，一种她不走运，偶然遇见的特殊情况，然而离开现实，浩渺无边，便是幸福和热情的广大地域。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She confused in her desire the sensualities of luxury with the delights of the heart, elegance of manners with delicacy of sentiment.","zh":"由于欲望强烈，她混淆了物质享受与精神愉悦、举止高雅与感情细致。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Did not love, like Indian plants, need a special soil, a particular temperature?","zh":"难道爱情不像印度植物一样，需要适宜的土地、特殊的气候？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Signs by moonlight, long embraces, tears flowing over yielded hands, all the fevers of the flesh and the languors of tenderness could not be separated from the balconies of great castles full of indolence, from boudoirs with silken curtains and thick carpets, well-filled flower-stands, a bed on a raised dias, nor from the flashing of precious stones and the shoulder-knots of liveries.","zh":"所以月下的叹息、长时间的拥抱、流在伸出来的手上的眼泪、肉体的种种不安和情意的种种缠绵，不但离不开终日悠闲的大庄园的阳台、铺着厚实地毯和有活动帘的绣房、枝叶茂密的盆景、放在台上的宝榻，也离不开珠玉的晶莹和号衣的饰带。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The lad from the posting house who came to groom the mare every morning passed through the passage with his heavy wooden shoes; there were holes in his blouse; his feet were bare in list slippers. And this was the groom in knee-britches with whom she had to be content! His work done, he did not come back again all day, for Charles on his return put up his horse himself, unsaddled him and put on the halter, while the servant-girl brought a bundle of straw and threw it as best she could into the manger.","sentences":[{"en":"The lad from the posting house who came to groom the mare every morning passed through the passage with his heavy wooden shoes; there were holes in his blouse; his feet were bare in list slippers.","zh":"驿站小伙计，每天早晨来刷洗母马，大木头套鞋在过道穿出穿进，工人服有窟窿，光脚穿一双布鞋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And this was the groom in knee-britches with whom she had to be content!","zh":"他就是她应当知足的短裤马僮！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His work done, he did not come back again all day, for Charles on his return put up his horse himself, unsaddled him and put on the halter, while the servant-girl brought a bundle of straw and threw it as best she could into the manger.","zh":"他做完活，一天就不来了。查理回来，亲自把马牵到马棚，卸下鞍子，戴上马笼头，女仆这期间抱来一捆草，使劲扔进槽头。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To replace Nastasie (who left Tostes shedding torrents of tears) Emma took into her service a young girl of fourteen, an orphan with a sweet face. She forbade her wearing cotton caps, taught her to address her in the third person, to bring a glass of water on a plate, to knock before coming into a room, to iron, starch, and to dress her—wanted to make a lady’s-maid of her. The new servant obeyed without a murmur, so as not to be sent away; and as madame usually left the key in the sideboard, Félicité every evening took a small supply of sugar that she ate alone in her bed after she had said her prayers.","sentences":[{"en":"To replace Nastasie (who left Tostes shedding torrents of tears) Emma took into her service a young girl of fourteen, an orphan with a sweet face.","zh":"爱玛找了一个十四岁小姑娘、面相善良的孤女，代替娜丝塔西（她哭得像开了河一样，终于离开了道特）。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She forbade her wearing cotton caps, taught her to address her in the third person, to bring a glass of water on a plate, to knock before coming into a room, to iron, starch, and to dress her—wanted to make a lady’s-maid of her.","zh":"她不许她戴软布帽，教她用第三人称 回话，端一杯水要用盘子，进来以前要先敲门，又教她浆衣服、熨衣服、伺候她穿衣服，一心一意，要把她训练成为她的贴身使女。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The new servant obeyed without a murmur, so as not to be sent away; and as madame usually left the key in the sideboard, Félicité every evening took a small supply of sugar that she ate alone in her bed after she had said her prayers.","zh":"新女仆怕被辞，服服帖帖，没有半点怨言；太太经常留下钥匙，不锁菜橱，全福每天晚晌偷一小包糖，做完祷告，一个人躺在床上吃。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Sometimes in the afternoon she went to chat with the postilions.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes in the afternoon she went to chat with the postilions.","zh":"下午有时候，她到对面和驿夫们闲谈，太太待在楼上自己的房间。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Madame was in her room upstairs. She wore an open dressing gown that showed between the shawl facings of her bodice a pleated chamisette with three gold buttons. Her belt was a corded girdle with great tassels, and her small garnet coloured slippers had a large knot of ribbon that fell over her instep. She had bought herself a blotting book, writing case, pen-holder, and envelopes, although she had no one to write to; she dusted her what-not, looked at herself in the glass, picked up a book, and then, dreaming between the lines, let it drop on her knees. She longed to travel or to go back to her convent. She wished at the same time to die and to live in Paris.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame was in her room upstairs.","zh":"下午有时候，她到对面和驿夫们闲谈，太太待在楼上自己的房间。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She wore an open dressing gown that showed between the shawl facings of her bodice a pleated chamisette with three gold buttons.","zh":"她穿一件敞口便服，披肩料子的翻领底下，露出一件打褶子的衬衫，有三粒金扣子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her belt was a corded girdle with great tassels, and her small garnet coloured slippers had a large knot of ribbon that fell over her instep.","zh":"腰带是一根坠着大流苏的绦带。石榴红小拖鞋，一簇宽带子披在脚面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had bought herself a blotting book, writing case, pen-holder, and envelopes, although she had no one to write to; she dusted her what-not, looked at herself in the glass, picked up a book, and then, dreaming between the lines, let it drop on her knees.","zh":"她给自己买了一本吸墨纸、一匣信纸、一支笔管和一些信封，虽然她没有一个人可以写信；她拂拭干净她的摆设架 ，照照镜子，拿起一本书，然后看着看着，想到别处，书掉在膝盖上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She longed to travel or to go back to her convent.","zh":"她巴望旅行，或者回到她的修道院。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wished at the same time to die and to live in Paris.","zh":"她希望死，又希望住到巴黎。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles in snow and rain trotted across country. He ate omelettes on farmhouse tables, poked his arm into damp beds, received the tepid spurt of blood-lettings in his face, listened to death-rattles, examined basins, turned over a good deal of dirty linen; but every evening he found a blazing fire, his dinner ready, easy-chairs, and a well-dressed woman, charming with an odour of freshness, though no one could say whence the perfume came, or if it were not her skin that made odorous her chemise.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles in snow and rain trotted across country.","zh":"查理风里来，雨里去，骑着马，四乡奔波。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He ate omelettes on farmhouse tables, poked his arm into damp beds, received the tepid spurt of blood-lettings in his face, listened to death-rattles, examined basins, turned over a good deal of dirty linen; but every evening he found a blazing fire, his dinner ready, easy-chairs, and a well-dressed woman, charming with an odour of freshness, though no one could say whence the perfume came, or if it were not her skin that made odorous her chemise.","zh":"他在田庄的饭桌上吃炒鸡蛋；胳膊伸进潮湿的床铺，给人放血，热血溅到脸上；听快死的人喘哮；检查洗脸盆；撩起肮脏的被单。但是每天黄昏回家，他就看到一炉旺火、饭菜摆好、家具舒服，还有一个衣着讲究的秀媚女人，一股清香，也不知道这种气味是从什么地方来的，说不定是她的皮肤熏香了她的衬衫。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She charmed him by numerous attentions; now it was some new way of arranging paper sconces for the candles, a flounce that she altered on her gown, or an extraordinary name for some very simple dish that the servant had spoilt, but that Charles swallowed with pleasure to the last mouthful. At Rouen she saw some ladies who wore a bunch of charms on the watch-chains; she bought some charms. She wanted for her mantelpiece two large blue glass vases, and some time after an ivory necessaire with a silver-gilt thimble. The less Charles understood these refinements the more they seduced him. They added something to the pleasure of the senses and to the comfort of his fireside. It was like a golden dust sanding all along the narrow path of his life.","sentences":[{"en":"She charmed him by numerous attentions; now it was some new way of arranging paper sconces for the candles, a flounce that she altered on her gown, or an extraordinary name for some very simple dish that the servant had spoilt, but that Charles swallowed with pleasure to the last mouthful.","zh":"她有许多别出心裁的地方使他入迷：她有时候花样翻新，给蜡烛剪些纸托盘，给她的袍子换一道压边，或者给简单的菜肴取一个动听的名字，女仆烧坏了，可是查理欢欢喜喜，一扫而光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At Rouen she saw some ladies who wore a bunch of charms on the watch-chains; she bought some charms.","zh":"她在鲁昂看见有些太太，表链来一串小玩意儿；她买了一串小玩意儿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wanted for her mantelpiece two large blue glass vases, and some time after an ivory necessaire with a silver-gilt thimble.","zh":"她要壁炉上摆一对碧琉璃大花瓶，过了一阵，她又要一个象牙针盒和一枚镀银顶针。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The less Charles understood these refinements the more they seduced him.","zh":"查理越不懂这些考究物品，越觉得可爱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They added something to the pleasure of the senses and to the comfort of his fireside.","zh":"它们增加他的官能的愉快和家室的安乐，仿佛金沙，一路洒遍他的生命小径。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was like a golden dust sanding all along the narrow path of his life.","zh":"它们增加他的官能的愉快和家室的安乐，仿佛金沙，一路洒遍他的生命小径。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He was well, looked well; his reputation was firmly established.","sentences":[{"en":"He was well, looked well; his reputation was firmly established.","zh":"他身体好，气色好，名誉也完全稳定了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The country-folk loved him because he was not proud. He petted the children, never went to the public house, and, moreover, his morals inspired confidence. He was specially successful with catarrhs and chest complaints. Being much afraid of killing his patients, Charles, in fact only prescribed sedatives, from time to time and emetic, a footbath, or leeches. It was not that he was afraid of surgery; he bled people copiously like horses, and for the taking out of teeth he had the “devil’s own wrist.”","sentences":[{"en":"The country-folk loved him because he was not proud.","zh":"乡下人喜欢他。因为他不骄傲。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He petted the children, never went to the public house, and, moreover, his morals inspired confidence.","zh":"他抚摸小孩子，从来不进酒店，而且他的人品得到大家信任。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was specially successful with catarrhs and chest complaints.","zh":"他的特长是治轻重伤风和胸腔内诸般炎症。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Being much afraid of killing his patients, Charles, in fact only prescribed sedatives, from time to time and emetic, a footbath, or leeches.","zh":"查理怕治死他的病人，实际开出来的方子，只是一些止痛剂，偶尔来一副呕吐剂，要不就是烫烫脚，或者放放血。他不畏惧外科，给人放血，好像给马放血一样，拔牙的手劲仿佛“铁腕子”。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was not that he was afraid of surgery; he bled people copiously like horses, and for the taking out of teeth he had the “devil’s own wrist.”","zh":"查理怕治死他的病人，实际开出来的方子，只是一些止痛剂，偶尔来一副呕吐剂，要不就是烫烫脚，或者放放血。他不畏惧外科，给人放血，好像给马放血一样，拔牙的手劲仿佛“铁腕子”。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Finally, to keep up with the times, he took in “La Ruche Medicale,” a new journal whose prospectus had been sent him. He read it a little after dinner, but in about five minutes the warmth of the room added to the effect of his dinner sent him to sleep; and he sat there, his chin on his two hands and his hair spreading like a mane to the foot of the lamp. Emma looked at him and shrugged her shoulders. Why, at least, was not her husband one of those men of taciturn passions who work at their books all night, and at last, when about sixty, the age of rheumatism sets in, wear a string of orders on their ill-fitting black coat? She could have wished this name of Bovary, which was hers, had been illustrious, to see it displayed at the booksellers’, repeated in the newspapers, known to all France. But Charles had no ambition.","sentences":[{"en":"Finally, to keep up with the times, he took in “La Ruche Medicale,” a new journal whose prospectus had been sent him.","zh":"他终于想赶上潮流，订了一份新刊物《医林》，他收到过要出版的广告，他用罢晚饭，读上一页两页，但是食物正在消化，加上房间热，不出五分钟，他就睡着了；于是他坐在那边，一双手托住下巴，头发披散下来，鬣毛一般，一直披散到灯座前头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He read it a little after dinner, but in about five minutes the warmth of the room added to the effect of his dinner sent him to sleep; and he sat there, his chin on his two hands and his hair spreading like a mane to the foot of the lamp.","zh":"他终于想赶上潮流，订了一份新刊物《医林》，他收到过要出版的广告，他用罢晚饭，读上一页两页，但是食物正在消化，加上房间热，不出五分钟，他就睡着了；于是他坐在那边，一双手托住下巴，头发披散下来，鬣毛一般，一直披散到灯座前头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma looked at him and shrugged her shoulders.","zh":"爱玛一见他这般模样，就耸肩膀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why, at least, was not her husband one of those men of taciturn passions who work at their books all night, and at last, when about sixty, the age of rheumatism sets in, wear a string of orders on their ill-fitting black coat?","zh":"单说嫁丈夫吧，她怎么连那样一个人也嫁不到：勤奋寡言，夜晚埋头著述，熬到六十岁上，风湿病的年龄来了，可是不合身的青燕尾服挂着一串勋章。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She could have wished this name of Bovary, which was hers, had been illustrious, to see it displayed at the booksellers’, repeated in the newspapers, known to all France.","zh":"她巴不得包法利这个姓——她现在姓这个姓——赫赫有名，在书店公开陈列，在报上经常出现，全法兰西知道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Charles had no ambition.","zh":"可是查理没有野心！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"An Yvetot doctor whom he had lately met in consultation had somewhat humiliated him at the very bedside of the patient, before the assembled relatives. When, in the evening, Charles told her this anecdote, Emma inveighed loudly against his colleague. Charles was much touched. He kissed her forehead with a tear in his eyes. But she was angered with shame; she felt a wild desire to strike him; she went to open the window in the passage and breathed in the fresh air to calm herself.","sentences":[{"en":"An Yvetot doctor whom he had lately met in consultation had somewhat humiliated him at the very bedside of the patient, before the assembled relatives.","zh":"伊弗托一个医生，新近会诊，简直就在病人床前，当着病人家属，多少给他难堪来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When, in the evening, Charles told her this anecdote, Emma inveighed loudly against his colleague.","zh":"查理夜晚讲给爱玛听，她气坏了，大骂这位同业。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles was much touched.","zh":"查理受了感动，挂着眼泪吻她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He kissed her forehead with a tear in his eyes.","zh":"可是她羞死了，恨不得打他一顿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she was angered with shame; she felt a wild desire to strike him; she went to open the window in the passage and breathed in the fresh air to calm herself.","zh":"她走到过道，打开窗户，吸新鲜空气，好让自己平下气来。她咬住嘴唇，低声道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What a man! What a man!” she said in a low voice, biting her lips.","sentences":[{"en":"“What a man!","zh":"“世上会有这种人！会有这种人！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"What a man!” she said in a low voice, biting her lips.","zh":"“世上会有这种人！会有这种人！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Besides, she was becoming more irritated with him. As he grew older his manner grew heavier; at dessert he cut the corks of the empty bottles; after eating he cleaned his teeth with his tongue; in taking soup he made a gurgling noise with every spoonful; and, as he was getting fatter, the puffed-out cheeks seemed to push the eyes, always small, up to the temples.","sentences":[{"en":"Besides, she was becoming more irritated with him.","zh":"再说，她越看他，越觉得有气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As he grew older his manner grew heavier; at dessert he cut the corks of the empty bottles; after eating he cleaned his teeth with his tongue; in taking soup he made a gurgling noise with every spoonful; and, as he was getting fatter, the puffed-out cheeks seemed to push the eyes, always small, up to the temples.","zh":"年纪一大，他举动也粗俗不文了：用果点的时候，他切空瓶的塞子；吃过东西，他拿舌头舔牙；喝起汤来，他咽一口，咕噜一声；而且他开始发福，眼睛本来就小，脸蛋胖虚虚的，像拿眼睛朝太阳穴挤。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Sometimes Emma tucked the red borders of his under-vest unto his waistcoat, rearranged his cravat, and threw away the dirty gloves he was going to put on; and this was not, as he fancied, for himself; it was for herself, by a diffusion of egotism, of nervous irritation. Sometimes, too, she told him of what she had read, such as a passage in a novel, of a new play, or an anecdote of the “upper ten” that she had seen in a feuilleton; for, after all, Charles was something, an ever-open ear, and ever-ready approbation. She confided many a thing to her greyhound. She would have done so to the logs in the fireplace or to the pendulum of the clock.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes Emma tucked the red borders of his under-vest unto his waistcoat, rearranged his cravat, and threw away the dirty gloves he was going to put on; and this was not, as he fancied, for himself; it was for herself, by a diffusion of egotism, of nervous irritation.","zh":"有时候，爱玛拿他的编结汗衫的红边掖到背心底下，帮他打好领结，或者手套旧了，他还想戴，她给扔开了；她这样做，并非像他想的，为了他，而是为了她自己，由于过分想着自己，由于嫌烦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes, too, she told him of what she had read, such as a passage in a novel, of a new play, or an anecdote of the “upper ten” that she had seen in a feuilleton; for, after all, Charles was something, an ever-open ear, and ever-ready approbation.","zh":"有时候，她也同他谈谈她读过的东西，诸如一节小说、一出新戏，或者副页上刊登的上流社会逸闻；因为话说回来，查理到底是一个人，总有耳朵听，总有嘴唯唯诺诺。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She confided many a thing to her greyhound.","zh":"她对她的猎犬不就无话不讲！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would have done so to the logs in the fireplace or to the pendulum of the clock.","zh":"即使是对钟摆和壁炉的木柴，她也一样会讲的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At the bottom of her heart, however, she was waiting for something to happen. Like shipwrecked sailors, she turned despairing eyes upon the solitude of her life, seeking afar off some white sail in the mists of the horizon. She did not know what this chance would be, what wind would bring it her, towards what shore it would drive her, if it would be a shallop or a three-decker, laden with anguish or full of bliss to the portholes. But each morning, as she awoke, she hoped it would come that day; she listened to every sound, sprang up with a start, wondered that it did not come; then at sunset, always more saddened, she longed for the morrow.","sentences":[{"en":"At the bottom of her heart, however, she was waiting for something to happen.","zh":"然而在她的灵魂深处，她一直期待意外发生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Like shipwrecked sailors, she turned despairing eyes upon the solitude of her life, seeking afar off some white sail in the mists of the horizon.","zh":"她睁大一双绝望的眼睛，观看她的生活的寂寞，好像沉了船的水手，在雾蒙蒙的天边，遥遥寻找白帆的踪影。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She did not know what this chance would be, what wind would bring it her, towards what shore it would drive her, if it would be a shallop or a three-decker, laden with anguish or full of bliss to the portholes.","zh":"她不知道什么地方有机会，哪一阵好风把机会吹到跟前，把她带到什么岸边，是小船还是三层甲板大船，满载忧虑还是满载幸福。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But each morning, as she awoke, she hoped it would come that day; she listened to every sound, sprang up with a start, wondered that it did not come; then at sunset, always more saddened, she longed for the morrow.","zh":"但是每天早晨，她醒过来，希望当天就会实现，细听种种响声，一骨碌跳下床，纳闷怎么还不见来，于是夕阳西下，永远愁上加愁，她又把希望寄托在明天。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Spring came round. With the first warm weather, when the pear trees began to blossom, she suffered from dyspnoea.","sentences":[{"en":"Spring came round.","zh":"春天又来了，梨树开花，暖洋洋的天气使她呼吸有些困难。","scope":"group"},{"en":"With the first warm weather, when the pear trees began to blossom, she suffered from dyspnoea.","zh":"春天又来了，梨树开花，暖洋洋的天气使她呼吸有些困难。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"From the beginning of July she counted how many weeks there were to October, thinking that perhaps the Marquis d’Andervilliers would give another ball at Vaubyessard. But all September passed without letters or visits.","sentences":[{"en":"From the beginning of July she counted how many weeks there were to October, thinking that perhaps the Marquis d’Andervilliers would give another ball at Vaubyessard.","zh":"一入七月，她就掐指计算，还有多少星期，才到十月，心想昂代维利耶侯爵，也许还会在渥毕萨尔举行舞会。然而整个九月过去了，不见信息，也不见有人拜访。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But all September passed without letters or visits.","zh":"失望之下，百无聊赖，她的心又空虚起来，于是类似的日子，一个连一个，重新开始。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After the ennui of this disappointment her heart once more remained empty, and then the same series of days recommenced. So now they would thus follow one another, always the same, immovable, and bringing nothing. Other lives, however flat, had at least the chance of some event. One adventure sometimes brought with it infinite consequences and the scene changed. But nothing happened to her; God had willed it so! The future was a dark corridor, with its door at the end shut fast.","sentences":[{"en":"After the ennui of this disappointment her heart once more remained empty, and then the same series of days recommenced.","zh":"日复一日，如今仿佛不断头的线，真要这样继续下去，永远一模一样，数又数不清，什么也带不来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So now they would thus follow one another, always the same, immovable, and bringing nothing.","zh":"别人的生活，再平板，起码也有机会碰到意外。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Other lives, however flat, had at least the chance of some event.","zh":"哪怕是一个偶然事件也好，有时候就会变化无穷，环境有了改动。可是上帝有意同她为难！","scope":"group"},{"en":"One adventure sometimes brought with it infinite consequences and the scene changed.","zh":"哪怕是一个偶然事件也好，有时候就会变化无穷，环境有了改动。可是上帝有意同她为难！","scope":"group"},{"en":"But nothing happened to her; God had willed it so!","zh":"她就偏偏什么事也碰不到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The future was a dark corridor, with its door at the end shut fast.","zh":"未来是一个过道，黑洞洞的，门在尽里关得严严的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She gave up music. What was the good of playing? Who would hear her? Since she could never, in a velvet gown with short sleeves, striking with her light fingers the ivory keys of an Erard at a concert, feel the murmur of ecstasy envelop her like a breeze, it was not worth while boring herself with practicing. Her drawing cardboard and her embroidery she left in the cupboard. What was the good? What was the good? Sewing irritated her. “I have read everything,” she said to herself. And she sat there making the tongs red-hot, or looked at the rain falling.","sentences":[{"en":"She gave up music.","zh":"她不弹钢琴了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was the good of playing?","zh":"弹它做什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who would hear her?","zh":"有谁听啊？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Since she could never, in a velvet gown with short sleeves, striking with her light fingers the ivory keys of an Erard at a concert, feel the murmur of ecstasy envelop her like a breeze, it was not worth while boring herself with practicing.","zh":"她没有机会穿短袖丝绒袍，到音乐会弹一架艾拉 钢琴，十指灵活，打象牙键，听见众口啧啧，如同一阵微风，在身边荡来荡去。既然如此，犯不上破费精力去学。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her drawing cardboard and her embroidery she left in the cupboard.","zh":"画册和刺绣，她丢在衣橱不管。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was the good?","zh":"有什么用？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was the good?","zh":"有什么用？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sewing irritated her.","zh":"缝纫惹她生气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I have read everything,” she said to herself.","zh":"她自言自语道：“书我全念啦。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And she sat there making the tongs red-hot, or looked at the rain falling.","zh":"于是闲来无事，她拿火钳烧得红红的，或者看下雨。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"How sad she was on Sundays when vespers sounded! She listened with dull attention to each stroke of the cracked bell. A cat slowly walking over some roof put up his back in the pale rays of the sun. The wind on the highroad blew up clouds of dust. Afar off a dog sometimes howled; and the bell, keeping time, continued its monotonous ringing that died away over the fields.","sentences":[{"en":"How sad she was on Sundays when vespers sounded!","zh":"星期日，晚祷钟声响了 ，她多愁闷！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She listened with dull attention to each stroke of the cracked bell.","zh":"她呆呆瞪瞪，细听钟声一下一下在响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A cat slowly walking over some roof put up his back in the pale rays of the sun.","zh":"日光黯淡，猫在屋顶耸起了背，慢条斯理地走动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The wind on the highroad blew up clouds of dust.","zh":"风在大路扬起一阵一阵尘土。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Afar off a dog sometimes howled; and the bell, keeping time, continued its monotonous ringing that died away over the fields.","zh":"有时候，远远传来一声犬吠；单调的钟声，按着均匀的拍子，响个不停，在田野里消散了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the people came out from church. The women in waxed clogs, the peasants in new blouses, the little bare-headed children skipping along in front of them, all were going home. And till nightfall, five or six men, always the same, stayed playing at corks in front of the large door of the inn.","sentences":[{"en":"But the people came out from church.","zh":"人们从教堂出来，女人穿着涂了蜡的木套鞋，男子穿着新工人服，小孩子光着头，在他们前面蹦跳，一个一个，回到家里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The women in waxed clogs, the peasants in new blouses, the little bare-headed children skipping along in front of them, all were going home.","zh":"人们从教堂出来，女人穿着涂了蜡的木套鞋，男子穿着新工人服，小孩子光着头，在他们前面蹦跳，一个一个，回到家里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And till nightfall, five or six men, always the same, stayed playing at corks in front of the large door of the inn.","zh":"有五六个男子，总是这几个人，在客店大门口玩瓶塞，一直玩到天黑。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The winter was severe. The windows every morning were covered with rime, and the light shining through them, dim as through ground-glass, sometimes did not change the whole day long. At four o’clock the lamp had to be lighted.","sentences":[{"en":"The winter was severe.","zh":"冬季严寒，每天早晨，玻璃窗凝一层霜，射过来的日光，灰灰的，像是从毛玻璃透过来的一样，有时候，整天不见变化。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The windows every morning were covered with rime, and the light shining through them, dim as through ground-glass, sometimes did not change the whole day long.","zh":"冬季严寒，每天早晨，玻璃窗凝一层霜，射过来的日光，灰灰的，像是从毛玻璃透过来的一样，有时候，整天不见变化。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At four o’clock the lamp had to be lighted.","zh":"一到下午四点钟，就得掌灯。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On fine days she went down into the garden. The dew had left on the cabbages a silver lace with long transparent threads spreading from one to the other. No birds were to be heard; everything seemed asleep, the espalier covered with straw, and the vine, like a great sick serpent under the coping of the wall, along which, on drawing near, one saw the many-footed woodlice crawling. Under the spruce by the hedgerow, the curé in the three-cornered hat reading his breviary had lost his right foot, and the very plaster, scaling off with the frost, had left white scabs on his face.","sentences":[{"en":"On fine days she went down into the garden.","zh":"每逢晴天，她下楼来到花园。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The dew had left on the cabbages a silver lace with long transparent threads spreading from one to the other.","zh":"露水在白菜上留下一些银线花边，有些长线明晃晃的，从这一棵白菜挂到另一棵白菜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No birds were to be heard; everything seemed asleep, the espalier covered with straw, and the vine, like a great sick serpent under the coping of the wall, along which, on drawing near, one saw the many-footed woodlice crawling.","zh":"听不见鸟声，好像全在睡觉一样，草盖住沿墙的果树，葡萄藤仿佛一条大蛇，有了病，盘在墙檐底下。走近了，就见爬着多足的鼠妇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Under the spruce by the hedgerow, the curé in the three-cornered hat reading his breviary had lost his right foot, and the very plaster, scaling off with the frost, had left white scabs on his face.","zh":"云杉底下，靠近篱笆，戴三角帽的堂长像掉了右脚，连石膏也冻脱了皮，脸上留下一些白癣，还在读他的祷告书。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she went up again, shut her door, put on coals, and fainting with the heat of the hearth, felt her boredom weigh more heavily than ever. She would have liked to go down and talk to the servant, but a sense of shame restrained her.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she went up again, shut her door, put on coals, and fainting with the heat of the hearth, felt her boredom weigh more heavily than ever.","zh":"随后她又上楼，关了屋门，剔剔炭，火旺旺的，她浑身无力，觉得心中分外烦闷。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would have liked to go down and talk to the servant, but a sense of shame restrained her.","zh":"她未尝不想下楼和女用人谈谈话，不过体面攸关，也就只好作罢。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Every day at the same time the schoolmaster in a black skullcap opened the shutters of his house, and the rural policeman, wearing his sabre over his blouse, passed by. Night and morning the post-horses, three by three, crossed the street to water at the pond. From time to time the bell of a public house door rang, and when it was windy one could hear the little brass basins that served as signs for the hairdresser’s shop creaking on their two rods. This shop had as decoration an old engraving of a fashion-plate stuck against a windowpane and the wax bust of a woman with yellow hair. He, too, the hairdresser, lamented his wasted calling, his hopeless future, and dreaming of some shop in a big town—at Rouen, for example, overlooking the harbour, near the theatre—he walked up and down all day from the mairie to the church, sombre and waiting for customers. When Madame Bovary looked up, she always saw him there, like a sentinel on duty, with his skullcap over his ears and his vest of lasting.","sentences":[{"en":"Every day at the same time the schoolmaster in a black skullcap opened the shutters of his house, and the rural policeman, wearing his sabre over his blouse, passed by.","zh":"每天在同一时间，小学校长戴一顶青缎小帽，推开他的护窗板；乡间警察走过，工人服上佩着刀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Night and morning the post-horses, three by three, crossed the street to water at the pond.","zh":"黄昏和早晨，驿站的马，穿街而过，三匹一起，到池塘饮水。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"From time to time the bell of a public house door rang, and when it was windy one could hear the little brass basins that served as signs for the hairdresser’s shop creaking on their two rods.","zh":"一家酒馆门铃不时在响；理发师的小铜脸盆，用作铺子的招牌，起了风，就见在两根铁杆上，吱嘎乱响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This shop had as decoration an old engraving of a fashion-plate stuck against a windowpane and the wax bust of a woman with yellow hair.","zh":"一张旧时装画，给铺子作装潢，贴在窗玻璃上，还有一座黄头发女人半身蜡像。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He, too, the hairdresser, lamented his wasted calling, his hopeless future, and dreaming of some shop in a big town—at Rouen, for example, overlooking the harbour, near the theatre—he walked up and down all day from the mairie to the church, sombre and waiting for customers.","zh":"理发师也直在自嗟自叹，一筹莫展，前途黯淡，梦想在大城市开铺子，比方说吧，鲁昂就好，在码头上，靠近剧场；他整天走来走去，从镇公所走到教堂，愁眉苦脸，等待顾客。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When Madame Bovary looked up, she always saw him there, like a sentinel on duty, with his skullcap over his ears and his vest of lasting.","zh":"包法利夫人仰起头来，总见他待在那边，仿佛一个值班哨兵，歪戴希腊小帽，穿着呢上身。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Sometimes in the afternoon outside the window of her room, the head of a man appeared, a swarthy head with black whiskers, smiling slowly, with a broad, gentle smile that showed his white teeth. A waltz immediately began and on the organ, in a little drawing room, dancers the size of a finger, women in pink turbans, Tyrolians in jackets, monkeys in frock coats, gentlemen in knee-breeches, turned and turned between the sofas, the consoles, multiplied in the bits of looking glass held together at their corners by a piece of gold paper. The man turned his handle, looking to the right and left, and up at the windows. Now and again, while he shot out a long squirt of brown saliva against the milestone, with his knee raised his instrument, whose hard straps tired his shoulder; and now, doleful and drawling, or gay and hurried, the music escaped from the box, droning through a curtain of pink taffeta under a brass claw in arabesque. They were airs played in other places at the theatres, sung in drawing rooms, danced to at night under lighted lustres, echoes of the world that reached even to Emma. Endless sarabands ran through her head, and, like an Indian dancing girl on the flowers of a carpet, her thoughts leapt with the notes, swung from dream to dream, from sadness to sadness. When the man had caught some coppers in his cap, he drew down an old cover of blue cloth, hitched his organ on to his back, and went off with a heavy tread. She watched him going.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes in the afternoon outside the window of her room, the head of a man appeared, a swarthy head with black whiskers, smiling slowly, with a broad, gentle smile that showed his white teeth.","zh":"到了下午，有时候，厅堂窗户外边，出现一个男人脑壳，脸晒得焦黄，黑络腮胡须，微笑起来，又慢，又随便，又柔和，露出一嘴白牙。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A waltz immediately began and on the organ, in a little drawing room, dancers the size of a finger, women in pink turbans, Tyrolians in jackets, monkeys in frock coats, gentlemen in knee-breeches, turned and turned between the sofas, the consoles, multiplied in the bits of looking glass held together at their corners by a piece of gold paper.","zh":"华尔兹舞跟着开始了；风琴上面，有一个小小客厅，里头是手指般高的舞俑、裹着玫瑰红包头巾的妇女、穿着背心的蒂罗尔人 、穿着青燕尾服的猴子、穿着短裤的绅士，在扶手椅、大沙发和茶几之间，转来转去，一道道金纸连接的镜片，映出他们的舞姿。这人一面旋转摇手，一面向左、向右、向窗户张望。他不时朝界石吐一口又长又黏的老黄痰。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The man turned his handle, looking to the right and left, and up at the windows.","zh":"乐器的硬皮带挂久了肩膀，肩膀支不住，他拿膝盖顶住乐器。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now and again, while he shot out a long squirt of brown saliva against the milestone, with his knee raised his instrument, whose hard straps tired his shoulder; and now, doleful and drawling, or gay and hurried, the music escaped from the box, droning through a curtain of pink taffeta under a brass claw in arabesque.","zh":"一个叶形铜钩吊起一幅玫瑰红缎幕，匣子里头传出呜哝呜哝的音乐，一时悲伤、徐缓，一时喜悦、急促，全是别处舞台上演奏的曲调、客厅歌唱的曲调、夜晚烛光下伴舞的曲调：这些社会回声，就这样一直传到爱玛耳边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were airs played in other places at the theatres, sung in drawing rooms, danced to at night under lighted lustres, echoes of the world that reached even to Emma.","zh":"萨拉邦德 舞曲，无尽无休，在她的脑内萦回。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Endless sarabands ran through her head, and, like an Indian dancing girl on the flowers of a carpet, her thoughts leapt with the notes, swung from dream to dream, from sadness to sadness.","zh":"她的思想随着音符跳跃，飘忽无定，一个梦去，一个梦来，旧忧未消，新忧又起，好像印度舞姬，在地毯的花卉上舞来舞去一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When the man had caught some coppers in his cap, he drew down an old cover of blue cloth, hitched his organ on to his back, and went off with a heavy tread.","zh":"那人摘下鸭舌帽，敛过了钱，拉下一幅旧蓝呢，蒙好风琴，扛在后背，拖着沉重的脚步走开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She watched him going.","zh":"她望着他走。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But it was above all the meal-times that were unbearable to her, in this small room on the ground floor, with its smoking stove, its creaking door, the walls that sweated, the damp flags; all the bitterness in life seemed served up on her plate, and with smoke of the boiled beef there rose from her secret soul whiffs of sickliness. Charles was a slow eater; she played with a few nuts, or, leaning on her elbow, amused herself with drawing lines along the oilcloth table cover with the point of her knife.","sentences":[{"en":"But it was above all the meal-times that were unbearable to her, in this small room on the ground floor, with its smoking stove, its creaking door, the walls that sweated, the damp flags; all the bitterness in life seemed served up on her plate, and with smoke of the boiled beef there rose from her secret soul whiffs of sickliness.","zh":"最让她受不了的是用饭的时间：楼下这间小厅房，壁炉冒烟，门吱嘎响，墙上渗水，石板地潮湿。她觉得人生的辛酸统统盛在她的盘子里，闻到肉味，她从灵魂深处泛起一阵恶心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles was a slow eater; she played with a few nuts, or, leaning on her elbow, amused herself with drawing lines along the oilcloth table cover with the point of her knife.","zh":"查理吃饭吃得慢；她不是嘎巴一声咬榛子，就是支起胳膊肘，用刀尖在油布上划小道道。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She now let everything in her household take care of itself, and Madame Bovary senior, when she came to spend part of Lent at Tostes, was much surprised at the change. She who was formerly so careful, so dainty, now passed whole days without dressing, wore grey cotton stockings, and burnt tallow candles. She kept saying they must be economical since they were not rich, adding that she was very contented, very happy, that Tostes pleased her very much, with other speeches that closed the mouth of her mother-in-law. Besides, Emma no longer seemed inclined to follow her advice; once even, Madame Bovary having thought fit to maintain that mistresses ought to keep an eye on the religion of their servants, she had answered with so angry a look and so cold a smile that the good woman did not interfere again.","sentences":[{"en":"She now let everything in her household take care of itself, and Madame Bovary senior, when she came to spend part of Lent at Tostes, was much surprised at the change.","zh":"家务她如今听其自然；四旬斋 期间，婆婆来道特住了几天，见她改了样，很是诧异。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She who was formerly so careful, so dainty, now passed whole days without dressing, wore grey cotton stockings, and burnt tallow candles.","zh":"说实话，她从前那样经心在意，如今整天乱发粗服，穿一双灰布袜，点一根油烛 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She kept saying they must be economical since they were not rich, adding that she was very contented, very happy, that Tostes pleased her very much, with other speeches that closed the mouth of her mother-in-law.","zh":"她一来就说，他们不是有钱人家，应该省吃俭用，还说什么她很称心、很快活，她非常喜欢道特和一些别的新调调，来堵老太太的口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, Emma no longer seemed inclined to follow her advice; once even, Madame Bovary having thought fit to maintain that mistresses ought to keep an eye on the religion of their servants, she had answered with so angry a look and so cold a smile that the good woman did not interfere again.","zh":"而且爱玛似乎没有听劝的意思；甚至有一回，老太太兴之所至，信口说起主人应当监督用人信教，她唯一的回答就是怒目而视，连声冷笑，老太太吓得再也不说起这类话了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma was growing difficult, capricious. She ordered dishes for herself, then she did not touch them; one day drank only pure milk, the next cups of tea by the dozen. Often she persisted in not going out, then, stifling, threw open the windows and put on light dresses. After she had well scolded her servant she gave her presents or sent her out to see neighbours, just as she sometimes threw beggars all the silver in her purse, although she was by no means tender-hearted or easily accessible to the feelings of others, like most country-bred people, who always retain in their souls something of the horny hardness of the paternal hands.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma was growing difficult, capricious.","zh":"爱玛越来越乖戾任性。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She ordered dishes for herself, then she did not touch them; one day drank only pure milk, the next cups of tea by the dozen.","zh":"她要了几样菜。菜来了，动也不动；今天光喝新鲜牛奶，明天就来几杯淡茶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often she persisted in not going out, then, stifling, threw open the windows and put on light dresses.","zh":"她常常赌气不出门，随后又嫌气闷，打开窗户，穿一件薄薄的袍子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After she had well scolded her servant she gave her presents or sent her out to see neighbours, just as she sometimes threw beggars all the silver in her purse, although she was by no means tender-hearted or easily accessible to the feelings of others, like most country-bred people, who always retain in their souls something of the horny hardness of the paternal hands.","zh":"万一恶声恶气申斥了女用人，事后她不是送她礼物，就是打发她到邻居家散心去。同样，她有时把口袋的银币统统给了穷人，一个子儿不剩。虽然她并不心软，也不那么容易被别人感动，正如大多数农村出身的人，灵魂之中，一直保留着父亲手上的膙子一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Towards the end of February old Rouault, in memory of his cure, himself brought his son-in-law a superb turkey, and stayed three days at Tostes. Charles being with his patients, Emma kept him company. He smoked in the room, spat on the firedogs, talked farming, calves, cows, poultry, and municipal council, so that when he left she closed the door on him with a feeling of satisfaction that surprised even herself. Moreover she no longer concealed her contempt for anything or anybody, and at times she set herself to express singular opinions, finding fault with that which others approved, and approving things perverse and immoral, all of which made her husband open his eyes widely.","sentences":[{"en":"Towards the end of February old Rouault, in memory of his cure, himself brought his son-in-law a superb turkey, and stayed three days at Tostes.","zh":"将近二月梢，卢欧老爹纪念女婿医好他的腿，亲自送来一只肥大的母火鸡，在道特住了三天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles being with his patients, Emma kept him company.","zh":"查理料理病人，只有爱玛陪他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He smoked in the room, spat on the firedogs, talked farming, calves, cows, poultry, and municipal council, so that when he left she closed the door on him with a feeling of satisfaction that surprised even herself.","zh":"他在卧室吸烟。朝火篦吐痰，说起庄稼、小牛、母牛、家禽和乡行政委员会，左说右说，临到他走，她把门一关，觉得松快，连她自己都没有想到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Moreover she no longer concealed her contempt for anything or anybody, and at times she set herself to express singular opinions, finding fault with that which others approved, and approving things perverse and immoral, all of which made her husband open his eyes widely.","zh":"再说，她看不起任何事、任何人的心情，也没有意思隐瞒；有时候，故意表示见解特别，别人称道的，她偏指摘，要不然就称道恶行败德：丈夫听了吃惊得睁大一双眼睛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Would this misery last for ever? Would she never issue from it? Yet she was as good as all the women who were living happily. She had seen duchesses at Vaubyessard with clumsier waists and commoner ways, and she execrated the injustice of God. She leant her head against the walls to weep; she envied lives of stir; longed for masked balls, for violent pleasures, with all the wildness that she did not know, but that these must surely yield.","sentences":[{"en":"Would this misery last for ever?","zh":"这可厌的生活，真就永远这样下去？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Would she never issue from it?","zh":"她有没有跳出去的一日？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yet she was as good as all the women who were living happily.","zh":"其实，生活快乐的妇女，她哪一个比不上！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had seen duchesses at Vaubyessard with clumsier waists and commoner ways, and she execrated the injustice of God.","zh":"她在渥毕萨尔，也曾见过几个公爵夫人，腰身比她粗笨，举止比她伧俗；她恨上帝不公道，头顶住墙哭；她歆羡动乱的生涯、戴假面具的晚会、闻所未闻的欢娱、一切她没有经历然而应当经历的疯狂爱情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She leant her head against the walls to weep; she envied lives of stir; longed for masked balls, for violent pleasures, with all the wildness that she did not know, but that these must surely yield.","zh":"她在渥毕萨尔，也曾见过几个公爵夫人，腰身比她粗笨，举止比她伧俗；她恨上帝不公道，头顶住墙哭；她歆羡动乱的生涯、戴假面具的晚会、闻所未闻的欢娱、一切她没有经历然而应当经历的疯狂爱情。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She grew pale and suffered from palpitations of the heart.","sentences":[{"en":"She grew pale and suffered from palpitations of the heart.","zh":"她脸色苍白，心跳也不正常。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles prescribed valerian and camphor baths. Everything that was tried only seemed to irritate her the more.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles prescribed valerian and camphor baths.","zh":"查理要她服缬草汤 洗樟脑澡，种种努力，似乎只是使她格外有气罢了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Everything that was tried only seemed to irritate her the more.","zh":"查理要她服缬草汤 洗樟脑澡，种种努力，似乎只是使她格外有气罢了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"On certain days she chatted with feverish rapidity, and this over-excitement was suddenly followed by a state of torpor, in which she remained without speaking, without moving. What then revived her was pouring a bottle of eau-de-cologne over her arms.","sentences":[{"en":"On certain days she chatted with feverish rapidity, and this over-excitement was suddenly followed by a state of torpor, in which she remained without speaking, without moving.","zh":"有些天，她像发高烧，说胡话一样，絮叨不完；兴奋过了，紧接着又像失去知觉一样，不言不动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What then revived her was pouring a bottle of eau-de-cologne over her arms.","zh":"她要自己振奋起来，便拿起一瓶科隆香水 ，朝胳膊上洒。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As she was constantly complaining about Tostes, Charles fancied that her illness was no doubt due to some local cause, and fixing on this idea, began to think seriously of setting up elsewhere.","sentences":[{"en":"As she was constantly complaining about Tostes, Charles fancied that her illness was no doubt due to some local cause, and fixing on this idea, began to think seriously of setting up elsewhere.","zh":"因为她一直抱怨道特不好，查理心想，她生病一定是水土不服之故；他存了这种心思，当真想着换一个地方行医了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"From that moment she drank vinegar, contracted a sharp little cough, and completely lost her appetite.","sentences":[{"en":"From that moment she drank vinegar, contracted a sharp little cough, and completely lost her appetite.","zh":"她从这时候起，喝醋要自己瘦，得了干咳小毛病，一点胃口也没有了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It cost Charles much to give up Tostes after living there four years and “when he was beginning to get on there.” Yet if it must be! He took her to Rouen to see his old master. It was a nervous complaint: change of air was needed.","sentences":[{"en":"It cost Charles much to give up Tostes after living there four years and “when he was beginning to get on there.”","zh":"待了四年，刚站稳脚跟，查理离开道特，并不合算。可是万一势在必行的话，也就顾不得了！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Yet if it must be!","zh":"待了四年，刚站稳脚跟，查理离开道特，并不合算。可是万一势在必行的话，也就顾不得了！","scope":"group"},{"en":"He took her to Rouen to see his old master.","zh":"他把她带到鲁昂，去看他的老师。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a nervous complaint: change of air was needed.","zh":"她害的是一种精神病：应该换换空气才是。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After looking about him on this side and on that, Charles learnt that in the Neufchâtel arrondissement there was a considerable market town called Yonville-l’Abbaye, whose doctor, a Polish refugee, had decamped a week before. Then he wrote to the chemist of the place to ask the number of the population, the distance from the nearest doctor, what his predecessor had made a year, and so forth; and the answer being satisfactory, he made up his mind to move towards the spring, if Emma’s health did not improve.","sentences":[{"en":"After looking about him on this side and on that, Charles learnt that in the Neufchâtel arrondissement there was a considerable market town called Yonville-l’Abbaye, whose doctor, a Polish refugee, had decamped a week before.","zh":"查理几方面进行打听，后来听说，新堡 区有一个殷实大镇叫永镇寺，医生是一个波兰难民 ，前一星期去了别处。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he wrote to the chemist of the place to ask the number of the population, the distance from the nearest doctor, what his predecessor had made a year, and so forth; and the answer being satisfactory, he made up his mind to move towards the spring, if Emma’s health did not improve.","zh":"他听到这话，写信给当地药剂师，询问人口数目、最近的同业的距离、前任每年进益等等；答复满意，爱玛的健康如果还不见好的话，他决计开春迁徙。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One day when, in view of her departure, she was tidying a drawer, something pricked her finger. It was a wire of her wedding bouquet. The orange blossoms were yellow with dust and the silver bordered satin ribbons frayed at the edges. She threw it into the fire. It flared up more quickly than dry straw. Then it was, like a red bush in the cinders, slowly devoured. She watched it burn.","sentences":[{"en":"One day when, in view of her departure, she was tidying a drawer, something pricked her finger.","zh":"有一天，预备动身，她清理抽屉，有什么东西扎了手指。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a wire of her wedding bouquet.","zh":"原来是一根铁丝，捆扎她的结婚的花用的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The orange blossoms were yellow with dust and the silver bordered satin ribbons frayed at the edges.","zh":"橘花已经在灰尘之中变黄了，银滚条缎带沿边也绽了线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She threw it into the fire.","zh":"她拿花扔进火里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It flared up more quickly than dry straw.","zh":"它烧起来，比干草还快，随后在灰烬里，仿佛一堆小红树，慢慢销毁。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then it was, like a red bush in the cinders, slowly devoured.","zh":"它烧起来，比干草还快，随后在灰烬里，仿佛一堆小红树，慢慢销毁。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She watched it burn.","zh":"她望着它燃烧。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The little pasteboard berries burst, the wire twisted, the gold lace melted; and the shriveled paper corollas, fluttering like black butterflies at the back of the stove, at last flew up the chimney.","sentences":[{"en":"The little pasteboard berries burst, the wire twisted, the gold lace melted; and the shriveled paper corollas, fluttering like black butterflies at the back of the stove, at last flew up the chimney.","zh":"小纸果裂开，铜丝弯弯扭扭，金银花带熔化；纸花瓣烧硬了。好像一只只黑蝴蝶，沿着壁炉，飘飘荡荡，最后，飞出烟筒去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When they left Tostes at the month of March, Madame Bovary was pregnant.","sentences":[{"en":"When they left Tostes at the month of March, Madame Bovary was pregnant.","zh":"临到三月，他们离开道特，包法利夫人这期间有了身孕。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-1","part":2,"n":1,"title":"Part II · Chapter 1","titleZh":"中卷 · 1","paragraphs":[{"en":"Yonville-l’Abbaye (so called from an old Capuchin abbey of which not even the ruins remain) is a market-town twenty-four miles from Rouen, between the Abbeville and Beauvais roads, at the foot of a valley watered by the Rieule, a little river that runs into the Andelle after turning three water-mills near its mouth, where there are a few trout that the lads amuse themselves by fishing for on Sundays.","sentences":[{"en":"Yonville-l’Abbaye (so called from an old Capuchin abbey of which not even the ruins remain) is a market-town twenty-four miles from Rouen, between the Abbeville and Beauvais roads, at the foot of a valley watered by the Rieule, a little river that runs into the Andelle after turning three water-mills near its mouth, where there are a few trout that the lads amuse themselves by fishing for on Sundays.","zh":"永镇寺（从前有一座嘉布遣 寺，所以才这样称呼，现在连遗址也看不见了）是一个离鲁昂八古里远的村镇，在阿柏镇大路和博韦大路之间，紧靠里厄河灌溉的一个盆地。小河在河口附近推动三座水磨，然后流入昂代尔河 ；水里有些鳟鱼，到了星期天，男孩子们就来钓鱼玩。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"We leave the highroad at La Boissiere and keep straight on to the top of the Leux hill, whence the valley is seen. The river that runs through it makes of it, as it were, two regions with distinct physiognomies—all on the left is pasture land, all of the right arable. The meadow stretches under a bulge of low hills to join at the back with the pasture land of the Bray country, while on the eastern side, the plain, gently rising, broadens out, showing as far as eye can follow its blond cornfields. The water, flowing by the grass, divides with a white line the colour of the roads and of the plains, and the country is like a great unfolded mantle with a green velvet cape bordered with a fringe of silver.","sentences":[{"en":"We leave the highroad at La Boissiere and keep straight on to the top of the Leux hill, whence the valley is seen.","zh":"人们在布瓦西耶离开大路，顺着平地，走到狼岭高头，就望见了盆地。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The river that runs through it makes of it, as it were, two regions with distinct physiognomies—all on the left is pasture land, all of the right arable.","zh":"河在中间流过，盆地一分为二，成了两块面貌不同的土地：左岸全是牧场，右岸全是农田。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The meadow stretches under a bulge of low hills to join at the back with the pasture land of the Bray country, while on the eastern side, the plain, gently rising, broadens out, showing as far as eye can follow its blond cornfields.","zh":"丘陵绵绵，草原迤逦蔓延，从山脚绕到后山，接上布赖 地区的牧场，同时平原在东边，一点一点高上去，向外扩展，金黄麦畦，一望无际。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The water, flowing by the grass, divides with a white line the colour of the roads and of the plains, and the country is like a great unfolded mantle with a green velvet cape bordered with a fringe of silver.","zh":"水在草边流过，仿佛一条白线，分开草地的颜色和田垄的颜色，整个田野看上去，就像一袭铺开的大斗篷，绿绒领子上镶了一道银边。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Before us, on the verge of the horizon, lie the oaks of the forest of Argueil, with the steeps of the Saint-Jean hills scarred from top to bottom with red irregular lines; they are rain tracks, and these brick-tones standing out in narrow streaks against the grey colour of the mountain are due to the quantity of iron springs that flow beyond in the neighboring country.","sentences":[{"en":"Before us, on the verge of the horizon, lie the oaks of the forest of Argueil, with the steeps of the Saint-Jean hills scarred from top to bottom with red irregular lines; they are rain tracks, and these brick-tones standing out in narrow streaks against the grey colour of the mountain are due to the quantity of iron springs that flow beyond in the neighboring country.","zh":"走到天边尽头，就有阿格伊森林 的橡树和圣约翰岭的巉岩，挡住去路。山坡自上而下，显出一些或宽或窄、又长又红的条纹，全是雨水冲洗的痕迹；许多含有铁质的泉水，四处流淌，流成那些红砖颜色，一道细线又一道细线，衬着山的灰底子，分外触目。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Here we are on the confines of Normandy, Picardy, and the Ile-de-France, a bastard land whose language is without accent and its landscape is without character. It is there that they make the worst Neufchâtel cheeses of all the arrondissement; and, on the other hand, farming is costly because so much manure is needed to enrich this friable soil full of sand and flints.","sentences":[{"en":"Here we are on the confines of Normandy, Picardy, and the Ile-de-France, a bastard land whose language is without accent and its landscape is without character.","zh":"这里是诺曼底、庇卡底和法兰西岛 交界处，一个三不管地区，语音没有高低轻重，就像风景没有特色一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is there that they make the worst Neufchâtel cheeses of all the arrondissement; and, on the other hand, farming is costly because so much manure is needed to enrich this friable soil full of sand and flints.","zh":"新堡全区干酪，数这地方做得最坏，另一方面，耕种费钱，因为土地充满沙砾、石子，毫无黏性，要施大量肥料才成。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Up to 1835 there was no practicable road for getting to Yonville, but about this time a cross-road was made which joins that of Abbeville to that of Amiens, and is occasionally used by the Rouen wagoners on their way to Flanders. Yonville-l’Abbaye has remained stationary in spite of its “new outlet.” Instead of improving the soil, they persist in keeping up the pasture lands, however depreciated they may be in value, and the lazy borough, growing away from the plain, has naturally spread riverwards. It is seen from afar sprawling along the banks like a cowherd taking a siesta by the water-side.","sentences":[{"en":"Up to 1835 there was no practicable road for getting to Yonville, but about this time a cross-road was made which joins that of Abbeville to that of Amiens, and is occasionally used by the Rouen wagoners on their way to Flanders.","zh":"直到一八三五年以前，人去永镇，没有好路可走；然而也就是在这期间，当地修了一条交通要道，连接阿柏镇大路和亚眠大路，车夫有时候从鲁昂送货到弗朗德勒 ，也走这条要道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yonville-l’Abbaye has remained stationary in spite of its “new outlet.”","zh":"永镇寺虽然有了新出路，照样驻足不前。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Instead of improving the soil, they persist in keeping up the pasture lands, however depreciated they may be in value, and the lazy borough, growing away from the plain, has naturally spread riverwards.","zh":"他们不改良土壤，只是死守牧场，不管收入坏到什么地步。懒惰的村镇，一成不变，看也不看平原一眼，继续朝河那边开拓，人从远处望去，只见它伸展在岸上，像一个放牛郎在水边睡午觉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It is seen from afar sprawling along the banks like a cowherd taking a siesta by the water-side.","zh":"他们不改良土壤，只是死守牧场，不管收入坏到什么地步。懒惰的村镇，一成不变，看也不看平原一眼，继续朝河那边开拓，人从远处望去，只见它伸展在岸上，像一个放牛郎在水边睡午觉。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At the foot of the hill beyond the bridge begins a roadway, planted with young aspens, that leads in a straight line to the first houses in the place. These, fenced in by hedges, are in the middle of courtyards full of straggling buildings, wine-presses, cart-sheds and distilleries scattered under thick trees, with ladders, poles, or scythes hung on to the branches. The thatched roofs, like fur caps drawn over eyes, reach down over about a third of the low windows, whose coarse convex glasses have knots in the middle like the bottoms of bottles. Against the plaster wall diagonally crossed by black joists, a meagre pear-tree sometimes leans and the ground-floors have at their door a small swing-gate to keep out the chicks that come pilfering crumbs of bread steeped in cider on the threshold. But the courtyards grow narrower, the houses closer together, and the fences disappear; a bundle of ferns swings under a window from the end of a broomstick; there is a blacksmith’s forge and then a wheelwright’s, with two or three new carts outside that partly block the way. Then across an open space appears a white house beyond a grass mound ornamented by a Cupid, his finger on his lips; two brass vases are at each end of a flight of steps; scutcheons blaze upon the door. It is the notary’s house, and the finest in the place.","sentences":[{"en":"At the foot of the hill beyond the bridge begins a roadway, planted with young aspens, that leads in a straight line to the first houses in the place.","zh":"过了桥，就在山脚，辟了一条垫高的堰路，栽着小白杨树，一直把你带到村子的头几家。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"These, fenced in by hedges, are in the middle of courtyards full of straggling buildings, wine-presses, cart-sheds and distilleries scattered under thick trees, with ladders, poles, or scythes hung on to the branches.","zh":"院子周围有一道篱笆，当中是住宅，还有许多零星小屋、压榨间、车棚、蒸馏间 ，在树木底下散开，枝叶茂密，中间挂着梯子、杆子或者镰刀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The thatched roofs, like fur caps drawn over eyes, reach down over about a third of the low windows, whose coarse convex glasses have knots in the middle like the bottoms of bottles.","zh":"窗矮矮的，玻璃又厚又鼓，仿佛瓶底，当中有一个圆疙瘩。泥草房顶几乎遮住窗户的三分之一，好像皮帽拉到眼睛上面一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Against the plaster wall diagonally crossed by black joists, a meagre pear-tree sometimes leans and the ground-floors have at their door a small swing-gate to keep out the chicks that come pilfering crumbs of bread steeped in cider on the threshold.","zh":"几根乌黑的龙骨，扯斜穿过石灰墙，偶尔有一棵瘦小的梨树，伸出墙头；小鸡站在底层的门槛上，啄着泡过苹果酒的黑面包屑，门口有活动小栅栏，防它们进屋里去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the courtyards grow narrower, the houses closer together, and the fences disappear; a bundle of ferns swings under a window from the end of a broomstick; there is a blacksmith’s forge and then a wheelwright’s, with two or three new carts outside that partly block the way.","zh":"再往前走，就见房屋密了，院子小了，篱笆不见了；窗户底下有一捆羊齿草 。绑在扫帚把的尖尖头，摇来摆去。过了一家马掌铺，就是一家车厂，外头搁着两三辆新车，堵住了路。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then across an open space appears a white house beyond a grass mound ornamented by a Cupid, his finger on his lips; two brass vases are at each end of a flight of steps; scutcheons blaze upon the door.","zh":"再过去，有一个栅栏门，望进去是一块圆草坪，点缀着一个小爱神，手指放在嘴上；再往里去，就是一所白房子，台阶两头一边一个铜瓶，门上钉着一块亮晶晶的事务所小牌：这是公证人的住宅，当地数它漂亮。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It is the notary’s house, and the finest in the place.","zh":"再过去，有一个栅栏门，望进去是一块圆草坪，点缀着一个小爱神，手指放在嘴上；再往里去，就是一所白房子，台阶两头一边一个铜瓶，门上钉着一块亮晶晶的事务所小牌：这是公证人的住宅，当地数它漂亮。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The Church is on the other side of the street, twenty paces farther down, at the entrance of the square. The little cemetery that surrounds it, closed in by a wall breast high, is so full of graves that the old stones, level with the ground, form a continuous pavement, on which the grass of itself has marked out regular green squares. The church was rebuilt during the last years of the reign of Charles X. The wooden roof is beginning to rot from the top, and here and there has black hollows in its blue colour. Over the door, where the organ should be, is a loft for the men, with a spiral staircase that reverberates under their wooden shoes.","sentences":[{"en":"The Church is on the other side of the street, twenty paces farther down, at the entrance of the square.","zh":"教堂在街的斜对面，离事务所有二十步远近，把着广场入口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The little cemetery that surrounds it, closed in by a wall breast high, is so full of graves that the old stones, level with the ground, form a continuous pavement, on which the grass of itself has marked out regular green squares.","zh":"公墓不大，环绕教堂，墙有大半个人高，里面墓冢累累，旧墓石倒在地上，块块相连，倒像铺的石板地，草长在夹缝，四四方方，绿茵成畦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The church was rebuilt during the last years of the reign of Charles X. The wooden roof is beginning to rot from the top, and here and there has black hollows in its blue colour.","zh":"查理十世在位的末年，教堂翻修一新 ，现在木头屋顶高处，开始腐烂，上面涂的蓝颜色，有些地方陷下去，成了黑颜色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Over the door, where the organ should be, is a loft for the men, with a spiral staircase that reverberates under their wooden shoes.","zh":"门上方搁风琴的地方，变成人们聚会的楼台，有一道楼梯盘旋而上，木头套鞋一踩，咯噔咯噔直响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The daylight coming through the plain glass windows falls obliquely upon the pews ranged along the walls, which are adorned here and there with a straw mat bearing beneath it the words in large letters, “Mr. So-and-so’s pew.” Farther on, at a spot where the building narrows, the confessional forms a pendant to a statuette of the Virgin, clothed in a satin robe, coifed with a tulle veil sprinkled with silver stars, and with red cheeks, like an idol of the Sandwich Islands; and, finally, a copy of the “Holy Family, presented by the Minister of the Interior,” overlooking the high altar, between four candlesticks, closes in the perspective. The choir stalls, of deal wood, have been left unpainted.","sentences":[{"en":"The daylight coming through the plain glass windows falls obliquely upon the pews ranged along the walls, which are adorned here and there with a straw mat bearing beneath it the words in large letters, “Mr. So-and-so’s pew.”","zh":"阳光透过匀净的玻璃窗，迤斜照亮顺墙排列的板凳；有的板凳放上一张草垫，钉牢了，底下写着几个大字：“某先生之凳”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Farther on, at a spot where the building narrows, the confessional forms a pendant to a statuette of the Virgin, clothed in a satin robe, coifed with a tulle veil sprinkled with silver stars, and with red cheeks, like an idol of the Sandwich Islands; and, finally, a copy of the “Holy Family, presented by the Minister of the Interior,” overlooking the high altar, between four candlesticks, closes in the perspective.","zh":"再往里去，在大厅狭窄的地方，有一个忏悔间，和一座小小的圣母像相对。圣母穿一件缎袍，头上蒙一幅银星点点的面网，朱红颜色脸蛋，活像夏威夷群岛的一尊神像；最后，靠里有一帧复制的《神圣家庭》，写明“内政部部长赠”，挂在圣坛上四支蜡烛当中，视野也就到此为止。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The choir stalls, of deal wood, have been left unpainted.","zh":"唱经堂是枞木做的，一直没有上过油漆。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The market, that is to say, a tiled roof supported by some twenty posts, occupies of itself about half the public square of Yonville. The town hall, constructed “from the designs of a Paris architect,” is a sort of Greek temple that forms the corner next to the chemist’s shop. On the ground-floor are three Ionic columns and on the first floor a semicircular gallery, while the dome that crowns it is occupied by a Gallic cock, resting one foot upon the “Charte” and holding in the other the scales of Justice.","sentences":[{"en":"The market, that is to say, a tiled roof supported by some twenty posts, occupies of itself about half the public square of Yonville.","zh":"菜市场占了永镇广场一半大小，其实也就是二十来根柱子撑起的一个瓦棚罢了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The town hall, constructed “from the designs of a Paris architect,” is a sort of Greek temple that forms the corner next to the chemist’s shop.","zh":"镇公所是“按照巴黎一位建筑师的图样”盖起来的，好似一座希腊神庙，紧挨着药房犄角，底层有三根爱奥尼亚圆柱，二楼有一条半圆穹隆长廊 ，横楣画了一只高卢公鸡 ，一只爪子踩住宪章，一只爪子举起公道天平。","scope":"group"},{"en":"On the ground-floor are three Ionic columns and on the first floor a semicircular gallery, while the dome that crowns it is occupied by a Gallic cock, resting one foot upon the “Charte” and holding in the other the scales of Justice.","zh":"镇公所是“按照巴黎一位建筑师的图样”盖起来的，好似一座希腊神庙，紧挨着药房犄角，底层有三根爱奥尼亚圆柱，二楼有一条半圆穹隆长廊 ，横楣画了一只高卢公鸡 ，一只爪子踩住宪章，一只爪子举起公道天平。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But that which most attracts the eye is opposite the Lion d’Or inn, the chemist’s shop of Monsieur Homais. In the evening especially its argand lamp is lit up and the red and green jars that embellish his shop-front throw far across the street their two streams of colour; then across them as if in Bengal lights is seen the shadow of the chemist leaning over his desk. His house from top to bottom is placarded with inscriptions written in large hand, round hand, printed hand: “Vichy, Seltzer, Barege waters, blood purifiers, Raspail patent medicine, Arabian racahout, Darcet lozenges, Regnault paste, trusses, baths, hygienic chocolate,” etc. And the signboard, which takes up all the breadth of the shop, bears in gold letters, “Homais, Chemist.” Then at the back of the shop, behind the great scales fixed to the counter, the word “Laboratory” appears on a scroll above a glass door, which about half-way up once more repeats “Homais” in gold letters on a black ground.","sentences":[{"en":"But that which most attracts the eye is opposite the Lion d’Or inn, the chemist’s shop of Monsieur Homais.","zh":"不过最引人注意的，却是金狮客店对面郝麦先生 的药房！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the evening especially its argand lamp is lit up and the red and green jars that embellish his shop-front throw far across the street their two streams of colour; then across them as if in Bengal lights is seen the shadow of the chemist leaning over his desk.","zh":"特别是夜晚，甘该灯点起来，装潢铺面的红、绿药瓶，朝地面投出两道彩色熠熠的亮光，便见影影绰绰，隔着亮光，如同隔着孟加拉烟火 一样，出现了药剂师伏几而坐的影子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His house from top to bottom is placarded with inscriptions written in large hand, round hand, printed hand: “Vichy, Seltzer, Barege waters, blood purifiers, Raspail patent medicine, Arabian racahout, Darcet lozenges, Regnault paste, trusses, baths, hygienic chocolate,” etc. And the signboard, which takes up all the breadth of the shop, bears in gold letters, “Homais, Chemist.”","zh":"他的住宅，由上到下，贴满招贴，有的是行书字体，有的是圆环字体，有的是铅印字体，写道：“维希水、塞兹水、巴赖吉水、清血汁、拉斯帕依药水、阿拉伯健身粉、达塞药糖、勒尼奥药膏、绷带、蒸馏器、卫生巧克力”等等， 不一而足。招牌像铺面一样长短，金字写着：郝麦药剂师。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then at the back of the shop, behind the great scales fixed to the counter, the word “Laboratory” appears on a scroll above a glass door, which about half-way up once more repeats “Homais” in gold letters on a black ground.","zh":"几架大天平，钉死在柜台上，天平后头铺子尽里，一扇玻璃门上，在一半高地方，黑底金字，“郝麦”这个名字又出现一次，同时横楣上，还写了实验室三个字。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Beyond this there is nothing to see at Yonville. The street (the only one) a gunshot in length and flanked by a few shops on either side stops short at the turn of the highroad. If it is left on the right hand and the foot of the Saint-Jean hills followed the cemetery is soon reached.","sentences":[{"en":"Beyond this there is nothing to see at Yonville.","zh":"此外，永镇也就没有什么可看的了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The street (the only one) a gunshot in length and flanked by a few shops on either side stops short at the turn of the highroad.","zh":"街道（唯一的一条街）有子弹射程那样长，两边几家店铺，在大路拐弯地方，收了形迹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If it is left on the right hand and the foot of the Saint-Jean hills followed the cemetery is soon reached.","zh":"出了街，往左转，沿圣约翰岭山脚走，很快就到了公墓。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At the time of the cholera, in order to enlarge this, a piece of wall was pulled down, and three acres of land by its side purchased; but all the new portion is almost tenantless; the tombs, as heretofore, continue to crowd together towards the gate. The keeper, who is at once gravedigger and church beadle (thus making a double profit out of the parish corpses), has taken advantage of the unused plot of ground to plant potatoes there. From year to year, however, his small field grows smaller, and when there is an epidemic, he does not know whether to rejoice at the deaths or regret the burials.","sentences":[{"en":"At the time of the cholera, in order to enlarge this, a piece of wall was pulled down, and three acres of land by its side purchased; but all the new portion is almost tenantless; the tombs, as heretofore, continue to crowd together towards the gate.","zh":"有一时期，霍乱流行 ，教堂扩大坟地，推倒一堵墙，在旁边买了三亩地；可是这块新开拓出来的地区，难得有人用，墓冢照常朝大门那边挤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The keeper, who is at once gravedigger and church beadle (thus making a double profit out of the parish corpses), has taken advantage of the unused plot of ground to plant potatoes there.","zh":"看守又管掘坟，又当教堂管事（这样就从教区死人身上得到两笔收益），利用空地，种了一些马铃薯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"From year to year, however, his small field grows smaller, and when there is an epidemic, he does not know whether to rejoice at the deaths or regret the burials.","zh":"不过他的田地本来就小，加之年复一年的收缩，所以他遇到传染病盛行的季节，便左右为难，不知道死人多了应当开心，还是坟墓多了应当难过才是。堂长先生终于有一天发话了：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You live on the dead, Lestiboudois!” the curé at last said to him one day. This grim remark made him reflect; it checked him for some time; but to this day he carries on the cultivation of his little tubers, and even maintains stoutly that they grow naturally.","sentences":[{"en":"“You live on the dead, Lestiboudois!” the curé at last said to him one day.","zh":"“赖斯地布杜瓦，你吃死人呢！”他听了这句话，觉得阴风惨惨，寻思之下，有一时期也就住了手，可是他今天照旧种他的块根，还硬说是野生的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This grim remark made him reflect; it checked him for some time; but to this day he carries on the cultivation of his little tubers, and even maintains stoutly that they grow naturally.","zh":"“赖斯地布杜瓦，你吃死人呢！”他听了这句话，觉得阴风惨惨，寻思之下，有一时期也就住了手，可是他今天照旧种他的块根，还硬说是野生的。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Since the events about to be narrated, nothing in fact has changed at Yonville. The tin tricolour flag still swings at the top of the church-steeple; the two chintz streamers still flutter in the wind from the linen-draper’s; the chemist’s fetuses, like lumps of white amadou, rot more and more in their turbid alcohol, and above the big door of the inn the old golden lion, faded by rain, still shows passers-by its poodle mane.","sentences":[{"en":"Since the events about to be narrated, nothing in fact has changed at Yonville.","zh":"自从下文说起的事故发生以来，事实上，永镇就没有什么改变。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The tin tricolour flag still swings at the top of the church-steeple; the two chintz streamers still flutter in the wind from the linen-draper’s; the chemist’s fetuses, like lumps of white amadou, rot more and more in their turbid alcohol, and above the big door of the inn the old golden lion, faded by rain, still shows passers-by its poodle mane.","zh":"马口铁三色旗，在教堂钟楼顶端，旋转如故；布庄两幅印花布幌子，依然迎风招展；药房的胎儿，仿佛一捆一捆白火绒，泡在浑浊的火酒里面，日渐腐烂；还有客店大门上头的老金狮子，风吹雨打，颜色褪掉，活像长毛犬，向过往行人露出它的鬈鬈毛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On the evening when the Bovarys were to arrive at Yonville, Widow Lefrancois, the landlady of this inn, was so very busy that she sweated great drops as she moved her saucepans. To-morrow was market-day. The meat had to be cut beforehand, the fowls drawn, the soup and coffee made. Moreover, she had the boarders’ meal to see to, and that of the doctor, his wife, and their servant; the billiard-room was echoing with bursts of laughter; three millers in a small parlour were calling for brandy; the wood was blazing, the brazen pan was hissing, and on the long kitchen table, amid the quarters of raw mutton, rose piles of plates that rattled with the shaking of the block on which spinach was being chopped.","sentences":[{"en":"On the evening when the Bovarys were to arrive at Yonville, Widow Lefrancois, the landlady of this inn, was so very busy that she sweated great drops as she moved her saucepans.","zh":"包法利夫妇要来永镇的那天黄昏，女店家勒弗朗索瓦寡妇，正忙得不可开交，一面烧菜，一面直冒大汗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To-morrow was market-day.","zh":"原来明天是镇上赶集的日子，必须先把肉切好，鸡开好膛，汤和咖啡煮好。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The meat had to be cut beforehand, the fowls drawn, the soup and coffee made.","zh":"原来明天是镇上赶集的日子，必须先把肉切好，鸡开好膛，汤和咖啡煮好。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Moreover, she had the boarders’ meal to see to, and that of the doctor, his wife, and their servant; the billiard-room was echoing with bursts of laughter; three millers in a small parlour were calling for brandy; the wood was blazing, the brazen pan was hissing, and on the long kitchen table, amid the quarters of raw mutton, rose piles of plates that rattled with the shaking of the block on which spinach was being chopped.","zh":"另外，还要做出包饭人的饭、医生夫妇和他们女用人的饭。弹子房传出一片震耳的笑声；小间有三位磨坊老板，喊人给他们拿烧酒去；劈柴在燃，焦炭在响，有人在案板上剁菠菜；厨房长桌上，盘子摞得高高的，和整块生羊肉夹杂在一起，案板一动，盘子就晃荡。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"From the poultry-yard was heard the screaming of the fowls whom the servant was chasing in order to wring their necks.","sentences":[{"en":"From the poultry-yard was heard the screaming of the fowls whom the servant was chasing in order to wring their necks.","zh":"偏院家禽咯咯叫唤，女用人在后头追赶，要宰它们。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A man slightly marked with small-pox, in green leather slippers, and wearing a velvet cap with a gold tassel, was warming his back at the chimney. His face expressed nothing but self-satisfaction, and he appeared to take life as calmly as the goldfinch suspended over his head in its wicker cage: this was the chemist.","sentences":[{"en":"A man slightly marked with small-pox, in green leather slippers, and wearing a velvet cap with a gold tassel, was warming his back at the chimney.","zh":"一个男人穿绿皮拖鞋，有几颗细麻子，戴一顶金坠小绒帽，背向壁炉烤火。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His face expressed nothing but self-satisfaction, and he appeared to take life as calmly as the goldfinch suspended over his head in its wicker cage: this was the chemist.","zh":"他一脸洋洋自得的表情，神态就像挂在他头上的柳条笼里的金翅雀那样安详，这人就是药剂师。女店家喊着：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Artémise!” shouted the landlady, “chop some wood, fill the water bottles, bring some brandy, look sharp! If only I knew what dessert to offer the guests you are expecting! Good heavens! Those furniture-movers are beginning their racket in the billiard-room again; and their van has been left before the front door! The ‘Hirondelle’ might run into it when it draws up. Call Polyte and tell him to put it up. Only think, Monsieur Homais, that since morning they have had about fifteen games, and drunk eight jars of cider! Why, they’ll tear my cloth for me,” she went on, looking at them from a distance, her strainer in her hand.","sentences":[{"en":"“Artémise!” shouted the landlady, “chop some wood, fill the water bottles, bring some brandy, look sharp!","zh":"“阿尔泰蜜丝！撅些细枝子，给水瓶装水，送烧酒去，快呀！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If only I knew what dessert to offer the guests you are expecting!","zh":"您等的客人，我单知道上什么果点，也就好了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good heavens!","zh":"老天爷！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Those furniture-movers are beginning their racket in the billiard-room again; and their van has been left before the front door!","zh":"帮搬家的那伙人，又在弹子房闹开了！他们的大车停在大门底下！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The ‘Hirondelle’ might run into it when it draws up.","zh":"燕子来了，兴许把它撞坏了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Call Polyte and tell him to put it up.","zh":"喊伊玻立特，把车搁好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Only think, Monsieur Homais, that since morning they have had about fifteen games, and drunk eight jars of cider!","zh":"说说看，郝麦先生，打早上起，他们打了约莫有十五盘球，喝了八坛苹果酒！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why, they’ll tear my cloth for me,” she went on, looking at them from a distance, her strainer in her hand.","zh":"他们要杵坏我的台球毡子的！”她拿着撇沫的勺子，边讲，边远远望他们。郝麦先生回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That wouldn’t be much of a loss,” replied Monsieur Homais. “You would buy another.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That wouldn’t be much of a loss,” replied Monsieur Homais.","zh":"“没有什么大不了，您买一张新的就是了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You would buy another.”","zh":"“没有什么大不了，您买一张新的就是了。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Another billiard-table!” exclaimed the widow.","sentences":[{"en":"“Another billiard-table!” exclaimed the widow.","zh":"寡妇一听这话，叫了起来：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Since that one is coming to pieces, Madame Lefrancois. I tell you again you are doing yourself harm, much harm! And besides, players now want narrow pockets and heavy cues. Hazards aren’t played now; everything is changed! One must keep pace with the times! Just look at Tellier!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Since that one is coming to pieces, Madame Lefrancois.","zh":"“再买一张台子！”“勒弗朗索瓦太太，旧的不去，新的不来；我早就对您说过了，您这是自己害自己！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I tell you again you are doing yourself harm, much harm!","zh":"“再买一张台子！”“勒弗朗索瓦太太，旧的不去，新的不来；我早就对您说过了，您这是自己害自己！","scope":"group"},{"en":"And besides, players now want narrow pockets and heavy cues.","zh":"大大地害了自己！再说，打弹子的人，如今讲究口袋窄，杆子重。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hazards aren’t played now; everything is changed!","zh":"人家不照老法子打啦，全变啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One must keep pace with the times!","zh":"必须跟着世道走！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just look at Tellier!”","zh":"看看泰里耶，宁可…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The hostess reddened with vexation. The chemist went on—","sentences":[{"en":"The hostess reddened with vexation.","zh":"女店家气红了脸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The chemist went on—","zh":"药剂师说下去：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You may say what you like; his table is better than yours; and if one were to think, for example, of getting up a patriotic pool for Poland or the sufferers from the Lyons floods—”","sentences":[{"en":"“You may say what you like; his table is better than yours; and if one were to think, for example, of getting up a patriotic pool for Poland or the sufferers from the Lyons floods—”","zh":"“他那张台子，随您怎么说，比您这张玲珑多了；好比说吧，人家就想得出来，帮波兰人募捐或者帮里昂遭水灾的人募捐 …”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It isn’t beggars like him that’ll frighten us,” interrupted the landlady, shrugging her fat shoulders. “Come, come, Monsieur Homais; as long as the ‘Lion d’Or’ exists people will come to it. We’ve feathered our nest; while one of these days you’ll find the ‘Cafe Francais’ closed with a big placard on the shutters. Change my billiard-table!” she went on, speaking to herself, “the table that comes in so handy for folding the washing, and on which, in the hunting season, I have slept six visitors! But that dawdler, Hivert, doesn’t come!”","sentences":[{"en":"“It isn’t beggars like him that’ll frighten us,” interrupted the landlady, shrugging her fat shoulders.","zh":"女店家耸着她的胖肩膀，打断他的话道：“像他那种叫花子，别想吓得了人！看吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Come, come, Monsieur Homais; as long as the ‘Lion d’Or’ exists people will come to it.","zh":"看吧！郝麦先生，金狮开一天，人来一天。我呀，有的是办法！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We’ve feathered our nest; while one of these days you’ll find the ‘Cafe Francais’ closed with a big placard on the shutters.","zh":"您看好了，总有一天早上，法兰西咖啡馆会关门大吉，窗板上贴封条的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Change my billiard-table!” she went on, speaking to herself, “the table that comes in so handy for folding the washing, and on which, in the hunting season, I have slept six visitors!","zh":"（她接下去，自言自语道）换掉我这张台子，可是搁搁我洗的衣服，有多方便！赶上打猎，我好让上头睡六个客人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But that dawdler, Hivert, doesn’t come!”","zh":"伊韦尔这慢腾鬼怎么还不来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are you waiting for him for your gentlemen’s dinner?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you waiting for him for your gentlemen’s dinner?”","zh":"药剂师问道：“您等他回来给客人开饭？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Wait for him! And what about Monsieur Binet? As the clock strikes six you’ll see him come in, for he hasn’t his equal under the sun for punctuality. He must always have his seat in the small parlour. He’d rather die than dine anywhere else. And so squeamish as he is, and so particular about the cider! Not like Monsieur Léon; he sometimes comes at seven, or even half-past, and he doesn’t so much as look at what he eats. Such a nice young man! Never speaks a rough word!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wait for him!","zh":"“等他回来？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And what about Monsieur Binet?","zh":"毕耐先生就不答应！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As the clock strikes six you’ll see him come in, for he hasn’t his equal under the sun for punctuality.","zh":"六点钟一敲，您看吧，他准进来，世上像他那样刻板的人，没有第二个。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He must always have his seat in the small parlour.","zh":"用饭也总要在小间用！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He’d rather die than dine anywhere else.","zh":"死也别想他换换地方！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And so squeamish as he is, and so particular about the cider!","zh":"又爱挑剔！又讲究喝好苹果酒！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Not like Monsieur Léon; he sometimes comes at seven, or even half-past, and he doesn’t so much as look at what he eats.","zh":"一点也不像赖昂先生；人家呀，有时候，七点钟来，连七点半钟的时候也有；有什么吃什么，看也不看一眼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Such a nice young man!","zh":"年轻人真好！从来说话斯斯文文的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Never speaks a rough word!”","zh":"年轻人真好！从来说话斯斯文文的。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Well, you see, there’s a great difference between an educated man and an old carabineer who is now a tax-collector.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, you see, there’s a great difference between an educated man and an old carabineer who is now a tax-collector.”","zh":"“这就因为呀，您明白，一个受过教育的人，和一个当过重骑兵的税务员，大有区别。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Six o’clock struck. Binet came in.","sentences":[{"en":"Six o’clock struck.","zh":"六点钟响了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Binet came in.","zh":"毕耐进来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He wore a blue frock-coat falling in a straight line round his thin body, and his leather cap, with its lappets knotted over the top of his head with string, showed under the turned-up peak a bald forehead, flattened by the constant wearing of a helmet. He wore a black cloth waistcoat, a hair collar, grey trousers, and, all the year round, well-blacked boots, that had two parallel swellings due to the sticking out of his big-toes. Not a hair stood out from the regular line of fair whiskers, which, encircling his jaws, framed, after the fashion of a garden border, his long, wan face, whose eyes were small and the nose hooked. Clever at all games of cards, a good hunter, and writing a fine hand, he had at home a lathe, and amused himself by turning napkin rings, with which he filled up his house, with the jealousy of an artist and the egotism of a bourgeois.","sentences":[{"en":"He wore a blue frock-coat falling in a straight line round his thin body, and his leather cap, with its lappets knotted over the top of his head with string, showed under the turned-up peak a bald forehead, flattened by the constant wearing of a helmet.","zh":"他穿一件蓝大衣，笔直下垂，裹住他的瘦身子，皮便帽的护耳，在顶门用小绳拴牢，帽檐朝上翻，底下露出光秃秃的额头，过去戴久了战盔，压出印子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He wore a black cloth waistcoat, a hair collar, grey trousers, and, all the year round, well-blacked boots, that had two parallel swellings due to the sticking out of his big-toes.","zh":"他穿一件青呢背心、一条灰裤，戴着硬领，一年四季，穿一双贼亮靴子，偏巧脚拇趾跷，脚面一边高起一块。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Not a hair stood out from the regular line of fair whiskers, which, encircling his jaws, framed, after the fashion of a garden border, his long, wan face, whose eyes were small and the nose hooked.","zh":"小眼睛，鹰嘴鼻，金黄络腮胡须，一根不乱，齐下巴兜住他少光无色的长脸，活像花圃的边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Clever at all games of cards, a good hunter, and writing a fine hand, he had at home a lathe, and amused himself by turning napkin rings, with which he filled up his house, with the jealousy of an artist and the egotism of a bourgeois.","zh":"他玩一手好牌，写一手好字，是一个打猎的好手，家里有一台旋床，闲来无事，他就旋餐巾环，怀着艺术家的爱心、资产者的私心，攒满了一屋。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He went to the small parlour, but the three millers had to be got out first, and during the whole time necessary for laying the cloth, Binet remained silent in his place near the stove. Then he shut the door and took off his cap in his usual way.","sentences":[{"en":"He went to the small parlour, but the three millers had to be got out first, and during the whole time necessary for laying the cloth, Binet remained silent in his place near the stove.","zh":"他朝小间走去；但是先得请出三位磨坊老板；他坐在炉火旁边，默不作声，等人给他摆好刀叉，然后像平日一样，关了门，摘掉便帽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he shut the door and took off his cap in his usual way.","zh":"药剂师一看就剩下他和女店家了，发话道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It isn’t with saying civil things that he’ll wear out his tongue,” said the chemist, as soon as he was along with the landlady.","sentences":[{"en":"“It isn’t with saying civil things that he’ll wear out his tongue,” said the chemist, as soon as he was along with the landlady.","zh":"“说上两句客气话，不见得就烂掉他的舌头！”她回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“He never talks more,” she replied. “Last week two travelers in the cloth line were here—such clever chaps who told such jokes in the evening, that I fairly cried with laughing; and he stood there like a dab fish and never said a word.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He never talks more,” she replied.","zh":"“他向来少言寡语；上星期，来了两个布贩；两个年轻人挺有才气，夜晚讲了许多笑话，可把我笑死啦。好，他呀，坐在那边，闷声不响，活活儿一条死鱼。”药剂师道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Last week two travelers in the cloth line were here—such clever chaps who told such jokes in the evening, that I fairly cried with laughing; and he stood there like a dab fish and never said a word.”","zh":"“他向来少言寡语；上星期，来了两个布贩；两个年轻人挺有才气，夜晚讲了许多笑话，可把我笑死啦。好，他呀，坐在那边，闷声不响，活活儿一条死鱼。”药剂师道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Yes,” observed the chemist; “no imagination, no sallies, nothing that makes the society-man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” observed the chemist; “no imagination, no sallies, nothing that makes the society-man.”","zh":"“是呀，没有想象，没有才情，一点应酬都不讲！”女店家驳他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet they say he has parts,” objected the landlady.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet they say he has parts,” objected the landlady.","zh":"“可是人家说他有本事啊。”郝麦回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Parts!” replied Monsieur Homais; “he, parts! In his own line it is possible,” he added in a calmer tone. And he went on—","sentences":[{"en":"“Parts!” replied Monsieur Homais; “he, parts!","zh":"“本事！他！本事？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In his own line it is possible,” he added in a calmer tone.","zh":"他换了一种比较平静的语气，接下去道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he went on—","zh":"“在他那一行，也许是吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! That a merchant, who has large connections, a jurisconsult, a doctor, a chemist, should be thus absent-minded, that they should become whimsical or even peevish, I can understand; such cases are cited in history. But at least it is because they are thinking of something. Myself, for example, how often has it happened to me to look on the bureau for my pen to write a label, and to find, after all, that I had put it behind my ear!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"于是他往下讲道：“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That a merchant, who has large connections, a jurisconsult, a doctor, a chemist, should be thus absent-minded, that they should become whimsical or even peevish, I can understand; such cases are cited in history.","zh":"一个场面大的商人、一个法学家、一个医生、一个药剂师，专心业务，人变古怪了，甚至于粗暴了，这我懂；历史上尽有这种事例！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But at least it is because they are thinking of something.","zh":"不过，那是因为，起码他们在想什么事情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Myself, for example, how often has it happened to me to look on the bureau for my pen to write a label, and to find, after all, that I had put it behind my ear!”","zh":"我，好比说吧，我写标签，在写字台上找钢笔，有许多回，找来找去找不到，临了发现夹在我的耳朵上头！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Lefrancois just then went to the door to see if the “Hirondelle” were not coming. She started. A man dressed in black suddenly came into the kitchen. By the last gleam of the twilight one could see that his face was rubicund and his form athletic.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Lefrancois just then went to the door to see if the “Hirondelle” were not coming.","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太走到门口，看看燕子到了没有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She started.","zh":"她吓一跳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A man dressed in black suddenly came into the kitchen.","zh":"一个穿一身黑的男子，突然走进厨房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By the last gleam of the twilight one could see that his face was rubicund and his form athletic.","zh":"黄昏一丝余光，照出他有一张赤红的脸和运动家的体格。“堂长先生，有事要我做吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What can I do for you, Monsieur le Curé?” asked the landlady, as she reached down from the chimney one of the copper candlesticks placed with their candles in a row. “Will you take something? A thimbleful of Cassis? A glass of wine?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What can I do for you, Monsieur le Curé?” asked the landlady, as she reached down from the chimney one of the copper candlesticks placed with their candles in a row.","zh":"女店家一面问，一面走向壁炉，去拿一支铜蜡烛台。铜蜡烛台和蜡烛并排摆在一起。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Will you take something?","zh":"“您要不要吃点东西？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A thimbleful of Cassis?","zh":"喝一小盅黑醋栗酒、一杯葡萄酒？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"A glass of wine?”","zh":"喝一小盅黑醋栗酒、一杯葡萄酒？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The priest declined very politely. He had come for his umbrella, that he had forgotten the other day at the Ernemont convent, and after asking Madame Lefrancois to have it sent to him at the presbytery in the evening, he left for the church, from which the Angelus was ringing.","sentences":[{"en":"The priest declined very politely.","zh":"教士十分客气地谢绝了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had come for his umbrella, that he had forgotten the other day at the Ernemont convent, and after asking Madame Lefrancois to have it sent to him at the presbytery in the evening, he left for the church, from which the Angelus was ringing.","zh":"他是来找他的雨伞的：他前一天把雨伞忘在艾讷蒙修道院了，所以来拜托勒弗朗索瓦太太，派人替他取回来，夜晚送到他的住处。晚祷的钟声在响，他回教堂去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When the chemist no longer heard the noise of his boots along the square, he thought the priest’s behaviour just now very unbecoming. This refusal to take any refreshment seemed to him the most odious hypocrisy; all priests tippled on the sly, and were trying to bring back the days of the tithe.","sentences":[{"en":"When the chemist no longer heard the noise of his boots along the square, he thought the priest’s behaviour just now very unbecoming.","zh":"药剂师听他的皮鞋声在广场消失以后，就批评说，方才他的行为，很不礼貌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This refusal to take any refreshment seemed to him the most odious hypocrisy; all priests tippled on the sly, and were trying to bring back the days of the tithe.","zh":"喝一杯酒，算得了什么，居然拒绝，在药剂师看来，是最要不得的一种虚伪。教士个个偷偷摸摸，大吃大喝，企图再过那种什一税 的日子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The landlady took up the defence of her curé.","sentences":[{"en":"The landlady took up the defence of her curé.","zh":"女店家帮她的堂长说话：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Besides, he could double up four men like you over his knee. Last year he helped our people to bring in the straw; he carried as many as six trusses at once, he is so strong.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Besides, he could double up four men like you over his knee.","zh":"“凭您怎么说，像您这样的男人，他在膝盖上，可以一撅四个。去年，他帮我们收麦秸，真结实啦，一趟扛六捆！”药剂师道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Last year he helped our people to bring in the straw; he carried as many as six trusses at once, he is so strong.”","zh":"“凭您怎么说，像您这样的男人，他在膝盖上，可以一撅四个。去年，他帮我们收麦秸，真结实啦，一趟扛六捆！”药剂师道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Bravo!” said the chemist. “Now just send your daughters to confess to fellows with such a temperament! I, if I were the Government, I’d have the priests bled once a month. Yes, Madame Lefrancois, every month—a good phlebotomy, in the interests of the police and morals.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Bravo!” said the chemist.","zh":"“妙啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Now just send your daughters to confess to fellows with such a temperament!","zh":"那么，打发你们的姑娘找有这般体格的小伙子忏悔去！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I, if I were the Government, I’d have the priests bled once a month.","zh":"我呀，我要是政府的话，我要教士一个月抽一次血。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yes, Madame Lefrancois, every month—a good phlebotomy, in the interests of the police and morals.”","zh":"是啊，勒弗朗索瓦太太，为了治安和风俗，每一个月，好好儿抽他们一回血！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Be quiet, Monsieur Homais. You are an infidel; you’ve no religion.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Be quiet, Monsieur Homais.","zh":"“别说了，郝麦先生！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are an infidel; you’ve no religion.”","zh":"您不敬神！不信教！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The chemist answered: “I have a religion, my religion, and I even have more than all these others with their mummeries and their juggling. I adore God, on the contrary. I believe in the Supreme Being, in a Creator, whatever he may be. I care little who has placed us here below to fulfil our duties as citizens and fathers of families; but I don’t need to go to church to kiss silver plates, and fatten, out of my pocket, a lot of good-for-nothings who live better than we do. For one can know Him as well in a wood, in a field, or even contemplating the eternal vault like the ancients. My God! Mine is the God of Socrates, of Franklin, of Voltaire, and of Beranger! I am for the profession of faith of the ‘Savoyard Vicar,’ and the immortal principles of ‘89! And I can’t admit of an old boy of a God who takes walks in his garden with a cane in his hand, who lodges his friends in the belly of whales, dies uttering a cry, and rises again at the end of three days; things absurd in themselves, and completely opposed, moreover, to all physical laws, which prove to us, by the way, that priests have always wallowed in turpid ignorance, in which they would fain engulf the people with them.”","sentences":[{"en":"The chemist answered: “I have a religion, my religion, and I even have more than all these others with their mummeries and their juggling.","zh":"药剂师还口道：“我信教，信我自己的教，别看他们装腔作势，像煞有介事，我比他们哪一个都有信仰！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I adore God, on the contrary.","zh":"正相反，我崇拜上帝！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I believe in the Supreme Being, in a Creator, whatever he may be.","zh":"我信奉上天，相信有一个造物主，随他是什么，我不在乎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I care little who has placed us here below to fulfil our duties as citizens and fathers of families; but I don’t need to go to church to kiss silver plates, and fatten, out of my pocket, a lot of good-for-nothings who live better than we do.","zh":"他要我们活在人世，尽我们的公民责任、家长责任；但是我用不着走进教室，吻银盘子，拿钱养肥一群小丑：他们吃得比我们好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For one can know Him as well in a wood, in a field, or even contemplating the eternal vault like the ancients.","zh":"人在树林，在田地，甚至像古人一样，望着苍天，一样可以敬仰上帝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My God!","zh":"我的上帝、我所敬礼的上帝，就是苏格拉底的上帝、富兰克林的上帝、伏尔泰和贝朗瑞的上帝！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Mine is the God of Socrates, of Franklin, of Voltaire, and of Beranger!","zh":"我的上帝、我所敬礼的上帝，就是苏格拉底的上帝、富兰克林的上帝、伏尔泰和贝朗瑞的上帝！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I am for the profession of faith of the ‘Savoyard Vicar,’ and the immortal principles of ‘89!","zh":"我拥护《萨瓦教务协理的信仰宣言》和八九年的不朽原则！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And I can’t admit of an old boy of a God who takes walks in his garden with a cane in his hand, who lodges his friends in the belly of whales, dies uttering a cry, and rises again at the end of three days; things absurd in themselves, and completely opposed, moreover, to all physical laws, which prove to us, by the way, that priests have always wallowed in turpid ignorance, in which they would fain engulf the people with them.”","zh":"所以我不承认什么糟老头子上帝，拄了拐杖，在他的花圃散步，让他的朋友住在鲸鱼肚子里，喊叫一声死去，三天之后再活过来。这些事本身就荒唐，还不说根本违反全部物理学原理；这顺便也就为我们证明：教士一向愚昧无知，厚颜无耻，还硬要世人和他们一样。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He ceased, looking round for an audience, for in his bubbling over the chemist had for a moment fancied himself in the midst of the town council. But the landlady no longer heeded him; she was listening to a distant rolling. One could distinguish the noise of a carriage mingled with the clattering of loose horseshoes that beat against the ground, and at last the “Hirondelle” stopped at the door.","sentences":[{"en":"He ceased, looking round for an audience, for in his bubbling over the chemist had for a moment fancied himself in the midst of the town council.","zh":"他住了口，目光炯炯，看周围有没有听众，因为药剂师一时兴起，忘乎所以，竟以为自己是在乡行政委员会了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the landlady no longer heeded him; she was listening to a distant rolling.","zh":"可是女店家已经心不在焉，伸长耳朵，听远处什么东西滚动的声音。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One could distinguish the noise of a carriage mingled with the clattering of loose horseshoes that beat against the ground, and at last the “Hirondelle” stopped at the door.","zh":"她听出是马车响，还掺杂着松了的马掌吧嗒吧嗒打地的声音。燕子终于在门前停住了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was a yellow box on two large wheels, that, reaching to the tilt, prevented travelers from seeing the road and dirtied their shoulders. The small panes of the narrow windows rattled in their sashes when the coach was closed, and retained here and there patches of mud amid the old layers of dust, that not even storms of rain had altogether washed away. It was drawn by three horses, the first a leader, and when it came down-hill its bottom jolted against the ground.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a yellow box on two large wheels, that, reaching to the tilt, prevented travelers from seeing the road and dirtied their shoulders.","zh":"这是一只黄箱子，夹在两个大轱轳当中，轱轳有车篷那样高，旅客看不见路，肩膀还要吃土。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The small panes of the narrow windows rattled in their sashes when the coach was closed, and retained here and there patches of mud amid the old layers of dust, that not even storms of rain had altogether washed away.","zh":"窗户窄小，车门一关，玻璃就在框子中间震动，上头灰尘已经够厚的了，还左一块，右一块，沾了好些泥点，即使倾盆大雨，一时也冲洗不掉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was drawn by three horses, the first a leader, and when it came down-hill its bottom jolted against the ground.","zh":"车套了三匹马，一匹打头，每逢下坡，车一颠簸，箱子底就碰了地。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Some of the inhabitants of Yonville came out into the square; they all spoke at once, asking for news, for explanations, for hampers. Hivert did not know whom to answer. It was he who did the errands of the place in town. He went to the shops and brought back rolls of leather for the shoemaker, old iron for the farrier, a barrel of herrings for his mistress, caps from the milliner’s, locks from the hair-dresser’s and all along the road on his return journey he distributed his parcels, which he threw, standing upright on his seat and shouting at the top of his voice, over the enclosures of the yards.","sentences":[{"en":"Some of the inhabitants of Yonville came out into the square; they all spoke at once, asking for news, for explanations, for hampers.","zh":"永镇有些市民，也到了广场，同时说话，七嘴八舌，问消息，要解释，找鸡鸭筐子，闹得伊韦尔不知道回答谁好。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Hivert did not know whom to answer.","zh":"永镇有些市民，也到了广场，同时说话，七嘴八舌，问消息，要解释，找鸡鸭筐子，闹得伊韦尔不知道回答谁好。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was he who did the errands of the place in town.","zh":"原因是他替本地人进城办货，到铺子买东西，给鞋匠带回几捆皮，给马掌匠带回一堆废铁，给店东家带回一桶鲱鱼，从女帽店带回几顶帽子，从理发店带回一些假发；他一路回来，一包一包分好，沿着各家的院墙扔进去，站在车座上，扯嗓子嚷嚷，马也不管了，由它们走去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He went to the shops and brought back rolls of leather for the shoemaker, old iron for the farrier, a barrel of herrings for his mistress, caps from the milliner’s, locks from the hair-dresser’s and all along the road on his return journey he distributed his parcels, which he threw, standing upright on his seat and shouting at the top of his voice, over the enclosures of the yards.","zh":"原因是他替本地人进城办货，到铺子买东西，给鞋匠带回几捆皮，给马掌匠带回一堆废铁，给店东家带回一桶鲱鱼，从女帽店带回几顶帽子，从理发店带回一些假发；他一路回来，一包一包分好，沿着各家的院墙扔进去，站在车座上，扯嗓子嚷嚷，马也不管了，由它们走去。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"An accident had delayed him. Madame Bovary’s greyhound had run across the field. They had whistled for him a quarter of an hour; Hivert had even gone back a mile and a half expecting every moment to catch sight of her; but it had been necessary to go on.","sentences":[{"en":"An accident had delayed him.","zh":"路上发生意外，车回来迟了；包法利夫人的猎犬，在田地迷失了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Madame Bovary’s greyhound had run across the field.","zh":"路上发生意外，车回来迟了；包法利夫人的猎犬，在田地迷失了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They had whistled for him a quarter of an hour; Hivert had even gone back a mile and a half expecting every moment to catch sight of her; but it had been necessary to go on.","zh":"大家足喊了一刻钟。伊韦尔甚至倒回了半古里路，时刻以为瞥见了，偏又不是；但是没有时间再找，非赶路不可。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma had wept, grown angry; she had accused Charles of this misfortune. Monsieur Lheureux, a draper, who happened to be in the coach with her, had tried to console her by a number of examples of lost dogs recognizing their masters at the end of long years. One, he said had been told of, who had come back to Paris from Constantinople. Another had gone one hundred and fifty miles in a straight line, and swum four rivers; and his own father had possessed a poodle, which, after twelve years of absence, had all of a sudden jumped on his back in the street as he was going to dine in town.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma had wept, grown angry; she had accused Charles of this misfortune.","zh":"爱玛又是哭，又是生气，直抱怨查理不好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Lheureux, a draper, who happened to be in the coach with her, had tried to console her by a number of examples of lost dogs recognizing their masters at the end of long years.","zh":"布商勒乐先生，凑巧同车，试着安慰她，举了许多例子：狗丢了，经过多年，又找到主人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One, he said had been told of, who had come back to Paris from Constantinople.","zh":"他听人讲起一条狗，从君士坦丁堡回到巴黎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Another had gone one hundred and fifty miles in a straight line, and swum four rivers; and his own father had possessed a poodle, which, after twelve years of absence, had all of a sudden jumped on his back in the street as he was going to dine in town.","zh":"还有一条狗，照直走了五十古里路，泅过四条河；他的父亲有一条长毛狗，不见了十二年，有一天黄昏，他到城里用饭，狗在街头冷不防跳上他的后背。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-2","part":2,"n":2,"title":"Part II · Chapter 2","titleZh":"中卷 · 2","paragraphs":[{"en":"Emma got out first, then Félicité, Monsieur Lheureux, and a nurse, and they had to wake up Charles in his corner, where he had slept soundly since night set in.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma got out first, then Félicité, Monsieur Lheureux, and a nurse, and they had to wake up Charles in his corner, where he had slept soundly since night set in.","zh":"爱玛头一个下车，全福、勒乐先生还有一个奶妈，跟着也下了车；天一黑，查理就在他的角落睡着了，临到下车，不得不喊醒他。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais introduced himself; he offered his homages to madame and his respects to monsieur; said he was charmed to have been able to render them some slight service, and added with a cordial air that he had ventured to invite himself, his wife being away.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais introduced himself; he offered his homages to madame and his respects to monsieur; said he was charmed to have been able to render them some slight service, and added with a cordial air that he had ventured to invite himself, his wife being away.","zh":"郝麦上前，介绍自己，向夫人表示他的热忱，向先生表示他的敬意，说他能稍尽绵薄，不胜荣幸。接着就悾悾款款，说他擅作主张，陪他们一道用饭，再说，他的太太又不在家。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"When Madame Bovary was in the kitchen she went up to the chimney.","sentences":[{"en":"When Madame Bovary was in the kitchen she went up to the chimney.","zh":"郝麦上前，介绍自己，向夫人表示他的热忱，向先生表示他的敬意，说他能稍尽绵薄，不胜荣幸。接着就悾悾款款，说他擅作主张，陪他们一道用饭，再说，他的太太又不在家。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"With the tips of her fingers she caught her dress at the knee, and having thus pulled it up to her ankle, held out her foot in its black boot to the fire above the revolving leg of mutton. The flame lit up the whole of her, penetrating with a crude light the woof of her gowns, the fine pores of her fair skin, and even her eyelids, which she blinked now and again. A great red glow passed over her with the blowing of the wind through the half-open door.","sentences":[{"en":"With the tips of her fingers she caught her dress at the knee, and having thus pulled it up to her ankle, held out her foot in its black boot to the fire above the revolving leg of mutton.","zh":"包法利夫人一进厨房，就走到壁炉跟前，伸出两个手指，在膝盖地方，把袍子提到踝骨上，露出一只穿黑靴子的脚，跨过烤来烤去的羊腿，伸向火焰。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The flame lit up the whole of her, penetrating with a crude light the woof of her gowns, the fine pores of her fair skin, and even her eyelids, which she blinked now and again.","zh":"火光照亮整个身子。一道强光射透袍料纬线、白净皮肤的细毛孔，甚至时时眨动的眼皮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A great red glow passed over her with the blowing of the wind through the half-open door.","zh":"门开了一半，风吹进来，一大片红颜色罩住她的身子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On the other side of the chimney a young man with fair hair watched her silently.","sentences":[{"en":"On the other side of the chimney a young man with fair hair watched her silently.","zh":"一个金黄头发青年，在壁炉另一边，不言不语地望她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As he was a good deal bored at Yonville, where he was a clerk at the notary’s, Monsieur Guillaumin, Monsieur Léon Dupuis (it was he who was the second habitue of the “Lion d’Or”) frequently put back his dinner-hour in hope that some traveler might come to the inn, with whom he could chat in the evening. On the days when his work was done early, he had, for want of something else to do, to come punctually, and endure from soup to cheese a tête-à-tête with Binet. It was therefore with delight that he accepted the landlady’s suggestion that he should dine in company with the newcomers, and they passed into the large parlour where Madame Lefrancois, for the purpose of showing off, had had the table laid for four.","sentences":[{"en":"As he was a good deal bored at Yonville, where he was a clerk at the notary’s, Monsieur Guillaumin, Monsieur Léon Dupuis (it was he who was the second habitue of the “Lion d’Or”) frequently put back his dinner-hour in hope that some traveler might come to the inn, with whom he could chat in the evening.","zh":"赖昂·迪皮伊先生（他是金狮客店第二个包饭客人），在公证人居由曼那边做文书，在永镇百无聊赖，推迟用饭的时间，希望客店来一位旅客，聊一黄昏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the days when his work was done early, he had, for want of something else to do, to come punctually, and endure from soup to cheese a tête-à-tête with Binet.","zh":"有些天，工作完毕，他不知道干什么好，只好准时前来，无可奈何，从头到尾，和毕耐一道吃饭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was therefore with delight that he accepted the landlady’s suggestion that he should dine in company with the newcomers, and they passed into the large parlour where Madame Lefrancois, for the purpose of showing off, had had the table laid for four.","zh":"所以女店家提议他陪新来的客人用饭，他就欢欢喜喜接受了。勒弗朗索瓦太太争体面，特意在大厅摆了四份刀叉。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais asked to be allowed to keep on his skull-cap, for fear of coryza; then, turning to his neighbour—","sentences":[{"en":"Homais asked to be allowed to keep on his skull-cap, for fear of coryza; then, turning to his neighbour—","zh":"大家走进大厅，郝麦怕伤风，请大家允许他戴他的希腊小帽，然后转向旁边的包法利夫人：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Madame is no doubt a little fatigued; one gets jolted so abominably in our ‘Hirondelle.’”","sentences":[{"en":"“Madame is no doubt a little fatigued; one gets jolted so abominably in our ‘Hirondelle.’”","zh":"“夫人，不用说，有点累了吧？我们这辆燕子，真要把人颠死！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That is true,” replied Emma; “but moving about always amuses me. I like change of place.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That is true,” replied Emma; “but moving about always amuses me.","zh":"爱玛答道：“是啊；不过我一向就觉得变动好玩，我喜欢出门。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I like change of place.”","zh":"爱玛答道：“是啊；不过我一向就觉得变动好玩，我喜欢出门。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“It is so tedious,” sighed the clerk, “to be always riveted to the same places.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is so tedious,” sighed the clerk, “to be always riveted to the same places.”","zh":"文书叹一口气，说：“老待在一个地方，简直把人腻死！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If you were like me,” said Charles, “constantly obliged to be in the saddle”—","sentences":[{"en":"“If you were like me,” said Charles, “constantly obliged to be in the saddle”—","zh":"查理道：“您要是也像我，老得骑着马来来去去…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But,” Léon went on, addressing himself to Madame Bovary, “nothing, it seems to me, is more pleasant—when one can,” he added.","sentences":[{"en":"“But,” Léon went on, addressing himself to Madame Bovary, “nothing, it seems to me, is more pleasant—when one can,” he added.","zh":"赖昂转向包法利夫人，接茬道：“可是，我觉得，这再有意思不过…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Moreover,” said the druggist, “the practice of medicine is not very hard work in our part of the world, for the state of our roads allows us the use of gigs, and generally, as the farmers are prosperous, they pay pretty well. We have, medically speaking, besides the ordinary cases of enteritis, bronchitis, bilious affections, etc., now and then a few intermittent fevers at harvest-time; but on the whole, little of a serious nature, nothing special to note, unless it be a great deal of scrofula, due, no doubt, to the deplorable hygienic conditions of our peasant dwellings. Ah! you will find many prejudices to combat, Monsieur Bovary, much obstinacy of routine, with which all the efforts of your science will daily come into collision; for people still have recourse to novenas, to relics, to the priest, rather than come straight to the doctor or the chemist. The climate, however, is not, truth to tell, bad, and we even have a few nonagenarians in our parish. The thermometer (I have made some observations) falls in winter to 4 degrees Centigrade at the outside, which gives us 24 degrees Reaumur as the maximum, or otherwise 54 degrees Fahrenheit (English scale), not more. And, as a matter of fact, we are sheltered from the north winds by the forest of Argueil on the one side, from the west winds by the St. Jean range on the other; and this heat, moreover, which, on account of the aqueous vapours given off by the river and the considerable number of cattle in the fields, which, as you know, exhale much ammonia, that is to say, nitrogen, hydrogen and oxygen (no, nitrogen and hydrogen alone), and which sucking up into itself the humus from the ground, mixing together all those different emanations, unites them into a stack, so to say, and combining with the electricity diffused through the atmosphere, when there is any, might in the long run, as in tropical countries, engender insalubrious miasmata—this heat, I say, finds itself perfectly tempered on the side whence it comes, or rather whence it should come—that is to say, the southern side—by the south-eastern winds, which, having cooled themselves passing over the Seine, reach us sometimes all at once like breezes from Russia.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Moreover,” said the druggist, “the practice of medicine is not very hard work in our part of the world, for the state of our roads allows us the use of gigs, and generally, as the farmers are prosperous, they pay pretty well.","zh":"“要能这样的话。”药剂师讲：“其实，在我们这地方行医，并不怎么辛苦；因为道路平坦，马车来往无阻，而且一般说来，农民生活富裕，酬金相当丰厚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We have, medically speaking, besides the ordinary cases of enteritis, bronchitis, bilious affections, etc., now and then a few intermittent fevers at harvest-time; but on the whole, little of a serious nature, nothing special to note, unless it be a great deal of scrofula, due, no doubt, to the deplorable hygienic conditions of our peasant dwellings.","zh":"就病而论，除去肠炎、气管炎、胆汁过多等等常见病例之外，我们也就是收获期间，偶尔害害疟疾，不过大体说来，情形并不严重，也没有特殊值得注意的地方，顶多爱生瘰疬罢了，这不用说，是我们乡下人居住不合卫生条件的缘故。啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! you will find many prejudices to combat, Monsieur Bovary, much obstinacy of routine, with which all the efforts of your science will daily come into collision; for people still have recourse to novenas, to relics, to the priest, rather than come straight to the doctor or the chemist.","zh":"包法利先生，到时您就知道，种种偏见，需要排除；顽固的旧习惯，天天和您的一切科学努力冲突；因为他们宁可求救于九日祈祷、圣骨、教堂堂长，也不按照常情，来看医生或者药剂师。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The climate, however, is not, truth to tell, bad, and we even have a few nonagenarians in our parish.","zh":"不过说实话，气候不坏，本乡就有几个九十岁的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The thermometer (I have made some observations) falls in winter to 4 degrees Centigrade at the outside, which gives us 24 degrees Reaumur as the maximum, or otherwise 54 degrees Fahrenheit (English scale), not more.","zh":"寒暑表（我观察过），冬季降到摄氏表四度，大夏天高到二十五度，顶多三十度，合成列氏表，最大限度也就是二十四度，或者华氏表（英国算法）五十四度 ，不会再高啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And, as a matter of fact, we are sheltered from the north winds by the forest of Argueil on the one side, from the west winds by the St. Jean range on the other; and this heat, moreover, which, on account of the aqueous vapours given off by the river and the considerable number of cattle in the fields, which, as you know, exhale much ammonia, that is to say, nitrogen, hydrogen and oxygen (no, nitrogen and hydrogen alone), and which sucking up into itself the humus from the ground, mixing together all those different emanations, unites them into a stack, so to say, and combining with the electricity diffused through the atmosphere, when there is any, might in the long run, as in tropical countries, engender insalubrious miasmata—this heat, I say, finds itself perfectly tempered on the side whence it comes, or rather whence it should come—that is to say, the southern side—by the south-eastern winds, which, having cooled themselves passing over the Seine, reach us sometimes all at once like breezes from Russia.”","zh":"——而且实际上，我们一方面有阿格伊森林，挡住北风，另一方面，又有圣约翰岭，挡住西风；不过河水蒸发，变成水汽，草原又有许多牲畜存在，你们知道，牲畜呼出大量阿莫尼亚，就是说，呼出氮气、氢气和氧气（不对，只有氮气和氢气），其所以热，就因为吸收了土地的腐烂植物，混合了所有这些不同种类的发散出来的东西，好比说，绑成一捆东西，遇到空气有电的时候，自动同电化合，时间久了，就像在热带一样，产生出妨害卫生的瘴气 ；——这种热，我说，在来的那边，或者不如说是可能来的那边，就是说，南方，经东南风一吹，也就好受了；风过塞纳河，已经凉爽了，有时候冷不防自天而降，就像俄罗斯小风一样。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“At any rate, you have some walks in the neighbourhood?” continued Madame Bovary, speaking to the young man.","sentences":[{"en":"“At any rate, you have some walks in the neighbourhood?” continued Madame Bovary, speaking to the young man.","zh":"包法利夫人继续向年轻人道：“附近总该有散步的地方吧？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, very few,” he answered. “There is a place they call La Pâture, on the top of the hill, on the edge of the forest. Sometimes, on Sundays, I go and stay there with a book, watching the sunset.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, very few,” he answered.","zh":"他回答道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“There is a place they call La Pâture, on the top of the hill, on the edge of the forest.","zh":"“简直没有！有一个地方，叫作牧场，在岭子高头，森林一旁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes, on Sundays, I go and stay there with a book, watching the sunset.”","zh":"星期天，我有时候去，带一本书，待在那边看日落。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I think there is nothing so admirable as sunsets,” she resumed; “but especially by the side of the sea.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I think there is nothing so admirable as sunsets,” she resumed; “but especially by the side of the sea.”","zh":"她接下去道：“我以为世上就数落日好看了，尤其是海边。”赖昂道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, I adore the sea!” said Monsieur Léon.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I adore the sea!” said Monsieur Léon.","zh":"“我就爱海！”包法利夫人回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And then, does it not seem to you,” continued Madame Bovary, “that the mind travels more freely on this limitless expanse, the contemplation of which elevates the soul, gives ideas of the infinite, the ideal?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And then, does it not seem to you,” continued Madame Bovary, “that the mind travels more freely on this limitless expanse, the contemplation of which elevates the soul, gives ideas of the infinite, the ideal?”","zh":"“汪洋一片，无边无涯，您不觉得精神更能自由翱翔？凝望大海，灵魂得以升华，不也引起对无限和理想的憧憬？”赖昂接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is the same with mountainous landscapes,” continued Léon. “A cousin of mine who travelled in Switzerland last year told me that one could not picture to oneself the poetry of the lakes, the charm of the waterfalls, the gigantic effect of the glaciers. One sees pines of incredible size across torrents, cottages suspended over precipices, and, a thousand feet below one, whole valleys when the clouds open. Such spectacles must stir to enthusiasm, incline to prayer, to ecstasy; and I no longer marvel at that celebrated musician who, the better to inspire his imagination, was in the habit of playing the piano before some imposing site.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is the same with mountainous landscapes,” continued Léon.","zh":"“山景也一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“A cousin of mine who travelled in Switzerland last year told me that one could not picture to oneself the poetry of the lakes, the charm of the waterfalls, the gigantic effect of the glaciers.","zh":"我有一位表兄，去年在瑞士旅行，对我讲，湖泊的诗意、瀑布的瑰丽、冰河的壮观，非常人所能想象。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One sees pines of incredible size across torrents, cottages suspended over precipices, and, a thousand feet below one, whole valleys when the clouds open.","zh":"松树高大无比，挺立湍流当中；茅屋草舍，悬于峭壁之上；在你脚下千尺之处，云雾微开，溪谷全部在望。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Such spectacles must stir to enthusiasm, incline to prayer, to ecstasy; and I no longer marvel at that celebrated musician who, the better to inspire his imagination, was in the habit of playing the piano before some imposing site.”","zh":"这些景象一定令人感动、令人神往，使人想到祈祷！所以那位出名的音乐家，为了激发想象，经常对着惊心动魄的景色弹琴，现在看来，也就不足为奇了。”她问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You play?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“You play?” she asked.","zh":"“您是音乐家？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, but I am very fond of music,” he replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“No, but I am very fond of music,” he replied.","zh":"他回答道：“不是，不过我很爱好。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! don’t you listen to him, Madame Bovary,” interrupted Homais, bending over his plate. “That’s sheer modesty. Why, my dear fellow, the other day in your room you were singing ‘L’Ange Gardien’ ravishingly. I heard you from the laboratory. You gave it like an actor.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! don’t you listen to him, Madame Bovary,” interrupted Homais, bending over his plate.","zh":"郝麦一边俯向盘子，一边插话道：“包法利夫人，别相信他，他说这话，完全由于谦虚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“That’s sheer modesty.","zh":"——怎么，好朋友！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why, my dear fellow, the other day in your room you were singing ‘L’Ange Gardien’ ravishingly.","zh":"那一天，您在您房间唱《守护天使》 ，实在好听。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I heard you from the laboratory.","zh":"我在实验室就听见了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You gave it like an actor.”","zh":"您像一位演员，说收就收。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon, in fact, lodged at the chemist’s where he had a small room on the second floor, overlooking the Place. He blushed at the compliment of his landlord, who had already turned to the doctor, and was enumerating to him, one after the other, all the principal inhabitants of Yonville. He was telling anecdotes, giving information; the fortune of the notary was not known exactly, and “there was the Tuvache household,” who made a good deal of show.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon, in fact, lodged at the chemist’s where he had a small room on the second floor, overlooking the Place.","zh":"赖昂的确住在药剂师家三楼一间小屋，面对广场。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He blushed at the compliment of his landlord, who had already turned to the doctor, and was enumerating to him, one after the other, all the principal inhabitants of Yonville.","zh":"听见房东这样恭维，他臊红了脸。郝麦已经转向医生，一个又一个，列举永镇的缙绅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was telling anecdotes, giving information; the fortune of the notary was not known exactly, and “there was the Tuvache household,” who made a good deal of show.","zh":"他叙述逸事，提供说明。公证人的财产，没有人知道准确数字；还有“杜法赦那一家人”，就爱摆架子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma continued, “And what music do you prefer?”","sentences":[{"en":"Emma continued, “And what music do you prefer?”","zh":"爱玛问下去道：“您喜欢什么音乐？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, German music; that which makes you dream.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, German music; that which makes you dream.”","zh":"“德国音乐；引人入梦的音乐。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Have you been to the opera?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you been to the opera?”","zh":"“您看过意大利歌剧吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Not yet; but I shall go next year, when I am living at Paris to finish reading for the bar.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not yet; but I shall go next year, when I am living at Paris to finish reading for the bar.”","zh":"“还没有；不过明年我要住到巴黎，把法科读完，那时候我就看到了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“As I had the honour of putting it to your husband,” said the chemist, “with regard to this poor Yanoda who has run away, you will find yourself, thanks to his extravagance, in the possession of one of the most comfortable houses of Yonville. Its greatest convenience for a doctor is a door giving on the Walk, where one can go in and out unseen. Moreover, it contains everything that is agreeable in a household—a laundry, kitchen with offices, sitting-room, fruit-room, and so on. He was a gay dog, who didn’t care what he spent. At the end of the garden, by the side of the water, he had an arbour built just for the purpose of drinking beer in summer; and if madame is fond of gardening she will be able—”","sentences":[{"en":"“As I had the honour of putting it to your husband,” said the chemist, “with regard to this poor Yanoda who has run away, you will find yourself, thanks to his extravagance, in the possession of one of the most comfortable houses of Yonville.","zh":"药剂师道：“方才我正对您丈夫说起那个跑了的、可怜的亚诺达；亏他瞎讲究，回头您就知道，您住的房子是永镇最舒服的一所房子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Its greatest convenience for a doctor is a door giving on the Walk, where one can go in and out unseen.","zh":"一个做医生的，特别觉得方便的是：巷子有一扇门，出入没有人看见。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Moreover, it contains everything that is agreeable in a household—a laundry, kitchen with offices, sitting-room, fruit-room, and so on.","zh":"再说，就居住而论，应有尽有：洗衣房、厨房带食具间、客厅、水果储藏室等等，不一而足。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was a gay dog, who didn’t care what he spent.","zh":"这家伙活活儿就是一位大爷，满不在乎！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the end of the garden, by the side of the water, he had an arbour built just for the purpose of drinking beer in summer; and if madame is fond of gardening she will be able—”","zh":"他在花园尽头近水的地方，搭了一座花棚，单单就为夏季喝喝啤酒！夫人要是爱好园艺的话，不妨…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My wife doesn’t care about it,” said Charles; “although she has been advised to take exercise, she prefers always sitting in her room reading.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My wife doesn’t care about it,” said Charles; “although she has been advised to take exercise, she prefers always sitting in her room reading.”","zh":"查理道：“内人对这不感兴趣，人家劝她活动活动，可是她就爱待在房间里看书。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Like me,” replied Léon. “And indeed, what is better than to sit by one’s fireside in the evening with a book, while the wind beats against the window and the lamp is burning?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Like me,” replied Léon.","zh":"赖昂插话道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“And indeed, what is better than to sit by one’s fireside in the evening with a book, while the wind beats against the window and the lamp is burning?”","zh":"“我也是这样；说实话，风吹打玻璃窗，灯点着，晚上在火旁一坐，拿起一本书…还有什么比这称心的？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What, indeed?” she said, fixing her large black eyes wide open upon him.","sentences":[{"en":"“What, indeed?” she said, fixing her large black eyes wide open upon him.","zh":"她睁大她的黑眼睛，看着他道：“可不是？”他继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“One thinks of nothing,” he continued; “the hours slip by. Motionless we traverse countries we fancy we see, and your thought, blending with the fiction, playing with the details, follows the outline of the adventures. It mingles with the characters, and it seems as if it were yourself palpitating beneath their costumes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“One thinks of nothing,” he continued; “the hours slip by.","zh":"“什么也不想，时间就过去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Motionless we traverse countries we fancy we see, and your thought, blending with the fiction, playing with the details, follows the outline of the adventures.","zh":"静静坐着，就在恍惚看见的地方漫游，你的思想和小说打成一片，不是玩味细节，就是探索奇遇的曲折起伏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It mingles with the characters, and it seems as if it were yourself palpitating beneath their costumes.”","zh":"思想化入人物，就像是你的心在他们的服装里面跳动一样。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That is true! That is true?” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“That is true!","zh":"她说：“对！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That is true?” she said.","zh":"对！”赖昂说下去：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Has it ever happened to you,” Léon went on, “to come across some vague idea of one’s own in a book, some dim image that comes back to you from afar, and as the completest expression of your own slightest sentiment?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Has it ever happened to you,” Léon went on, “to come across some vague idea of one’s own in a book, some dim image that comes back to you from afar, and as the completest expression of your own slightest sentiment?”","zh":"“您有没有这种经验：有时候看书，模模糊糊，遇见您也有过的想法，或者人影幢幢，遇见一个来自远方的形象，好像展示出来的，全是您最细微的感情一样？”她回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I have experienced it,” she replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“I have experienced it,” she replied.","zh":"“我有过这种体会。”他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That is why,” he said, “I especially love the poets. I think verse more tender than prose, and that it moves far more easily to tears.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That is why,” he said, “I especially love the poets.","zh":"“所以我特别喜爱诗人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I think verse more tender than prose, and that it moves far more easily to tears.”","zh":"我觉得诗词比散文温柔，更容易感人泪下。”爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Still in the long run it is tiring,” continued Emma. “Now I, on the contrary, adore stories that rush breathlessly along, that frighten one. I detest commonplace heroes and moderate sentiments, such as there are in nature.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Still in the long run it is tiring,” continued Emma.","zh":"“可是读久了也起腻；如今我就爱一气呵成、惊心动魄的故事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Now I, on the contrary, adore stories that rush breathlessly along, that frighten one.","zh":"我就恨人物庸俗、感情平缓，和日常见到的一样。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I detest commonplace heroes and moderate sentiments, such as there are in nature.”","zh":"文书发表意见道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“In fact,” observed the clerk, “these works, not touching the heart, miss, it seems to me, the true end of art. It is so sweet, amid all the disenchantments of life, to be able to dwell in thought upon noble characters, pure affections, and pictures of happiness. For myself, living here far from the world, this is my one distraction; but Yonville affords so few resources.”","sentences":[{"en":"“In fact,” observed the clerk, “these works, not touching the heart, miss, it seems to me, the true end of art.","zh":"“的确也是。这些作品既然不感动人，依我看来，就离开了艺术的真正目的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is so sweet, amid all the disenchantments of life, to be able to dwell in thought upon noble characters, pure affections, and pictures of happiness.","zh":"人生每多失望，能把思想寄托在高贵的性格、纯洁的感情和幸福的境界上，也就大可自慰了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For myself, living here far from the world, this is my one distraction; but Yonville affords so few resources.”","zh":"就我来说，住在这偏僻地方，远离社会，读书成了我唯一的消遣；因为永镇是什么也拿不出来的！”爱玛接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Like Tostes, no doubt,” replied Emma; “and so I always subscribed to a lending library.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Like Tostes, no doubt,” replied Emma; “and so I always subscribed to a lending library.”","zh":"“还用说，和道特一样；所以我从前总去一家书店租书看。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If madame will do me the honour of making use of it”, said the chemist, who had just caught the last words, “I have at her disposal a library composed of the best authors, Voltaire, Rousseau, Delille, Walter Scott, the ‘Echo des Feuilletons’; and in addition I receive various periodicals, among them the ‘Fanal de Rouen’ daily, having the advantage to be its correspondent for the districts of Buchy, Forges, Neufchâtel, Yonville, and vicinity.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If madame will do me the honour of making use of it”, said the chemist, who had just caught the last words, “I have at her disposal a library composed of the best authors, Voltaire, Rousseau, Delille, Walter Scott, the ‘Echo des Feuilletons’; and in addition I receive various periodicals, among them the ‘Fanal de Rouen’ daily, having the advantage to be its correspondent for the districts of Buchy, Forges, Neufchâtel, Yonville, and vicinity.”","zh":"药剂师听见这么几句话，就说：“我有一架书，都是最好的作家写的：伏尔泰啦，卢梭啦，德利尔 啦，瓦尔特·司各特啦，《回声报副刊》啦等等，而且我收到各种不同期刊，其中《鲁昂烽火》，天天送来，因为我是比西、福尔吉、新堡、永镇和附近一带的通讯员，所以只要夫人赏脸，我没有不乐意借的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For two hours and a half they had been at table; for the servant Artémis, carelessly dragging her old list slippers over the flags, brought one plate after the other, forgot everything, and constantly left the door of the billiard-room half open, so that it beat against the wall with its hooks.","sentences":[{"en":"For two hours and a half they had been at table; for the servant Artémis, carelessly dragging her old list slippers over the flags, brought one plate after the other, forgot everything, and constantly left the door of the billiard-room half open, so that it beat against the wall with its hooks.","zh":"他们的晚饭用了两小时半；因为女用人阿尔泰蜜丝，穿一双布条鞋 ，懒懒散散，在石板地上拖来拖去，端了一个盘子，再端一个盘子，丢三落四，样样不懂。弹子房的门，老是打开忘了关，门闩头直撞墙。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Unconsciously, Léon, while talking, had placed his foot on one of the bars of the chair on which Madame Bovary was sitting. She wore a small blue silk necktie, that kept up like a ruff a gauffered cambric collar, and with the movements of her head the lower part of her face gently sunk into the linen or came out from it. Thus side by side, while Charles and the chemist chatted, they entered into one of those vague conversations where the hazard of all that is said brings you back to the fixed centre of a common sympathy. The Paris theatres, titles of novels, new quadrilles, and the world they did not know; Tostes, where she had lived, and Yonville, where they were; they examined all, talked of everything till to the end of dinner.","sentences":[{"en":"Unconsciously, Léon, while talking, had placed his foot on one of the bars of the chair on which Madame Bovary was sitting.","zh":"赖昂一面说话，一面心不在焉，拿脚踩着包法利夫人坐的椅子的横档。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wore a small blue silk necktie, that kept up like a ruff a gauffered cambric collar, and with the movements of her head the lower part of her face gently sunk into the linen or came out from it.","zh":"她系一条蓝缎小领带，兜紧圆褶细麻布领，像花领箍 那样硬挺；头上下一动，她的小半个脸，也就跟着优雅地在领口出出进进。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus side by side, while Charles and the chemist chatted, they entered into one of those vague conversations where the hazard of all that is said brings you back to the fixed centre of a common sympathy.","zh":"查理和药剂师闲聊中间，他们就这样靠近了，泛泛而谈，东扯一句，西扯一句，但是总回到一个引起共鸣的中心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The Paris theatres, titles of novels, new quadrilles, and the world they did not know; Tostes, where she had lived, and Yonville, where they were; they examined all, talked of everything till to the end of dinner.","zh":"巴黎戏剧，小说的标题，新式四组舞，她住过的道特，他们现在待的永镇，以及他们没有见识过的社会，天上地下，无所不谈，一直谈到晚饭用罢，这才住口。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When coffee was served Félicité went away to get ready the room in the new house, and the guests soon raised the siege. Madame Lefrancois was asleep near the cinders, while the stable-boy, lantern in hand, was waiting to show Monsieur and Madame Bovary the way home. Bits of straw stuck in his red hair, and he limped with his left leg. When he had taken in his other hand the cure’s umbrella, they started.","sentences":[{"en":"When coffee was served Félicité went away to get ready the room in the new house, and the guests soon raised the siege.","zh":"上咖啡的时候，全福去新宅布置寝室。客人们没有多久，也就离席了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Lefrancois was asleep near the cinders, while the stable-boy, lantern in hand, was waiting to show Monsieur and Madame Bovary the way home.","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太在将熄的炉火旁睡着了。马夫提了一盏灯，守在一旁，送包法利夫妇去他们的新居，红头发沾着碎麦秸，左腿瘸着。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Bits of straw stuck in his red hair, and he limped with his left leg.","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太在将熄的炉火旁睡着了。马夫提了一盏灯，守在一旁，送包法利夫妇去他们的新居，红头发沾着碎麦秸，左腿瘸着。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When he had taken in his other hand the cure’s umbrella, they started.","zh":"大家等他另一只手拿好堂长先生的雨伞，就出发了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The town was asleep; the pillars of the market threw great shadows; the earth was all grey as on a summer’s night. But as the doctor’s house was only some fifty paces from the inn, they had to say good-night almost immediately, and the company dispersed.","sentences":[{"en":"The town was asleep; the pillars of the market threw great shadows; the earth was all grey as on a summer’s night.","zh":"全镇入睡。菜场的柱子投下长长的影子。像在夏天夜晚一样，地全是灰的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But as the doctor’s house was only some fifty paces from the inn, they had to say good-night almost immediately, and the company dispersed.","zh":"不过医生住宅离客店只有五十步远，大家差不多紧跟着就互道晚安分手了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As soon as she entered the passage, Emma felt the cold of the plaster fall about her shoulders like damp linen. The walls were new and the wooden stairs creaked. In their bedroom, on the first floor, a whitish light passed through the curtainless windows.","sentences":[{"en":"As soon as she entered the passage, Emma felt the cold of the plaster fall about her shoulders like damp linen.","zh":"爱玛一进门厅，就觉得冰冷的石灰，像湿布一样，落在她的肩头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The walls were new and the wooden stairs creaked.","zh":"墙是新刷的，木头梯子嘎吱直响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In their bedroom, on the first floor, a whitish light passed through the curtainless windows.","zh":"窗户没有挂窗帘，一道淡淡的白光射进二楼房间。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She could catch glimpses of tree tops, and beyond, the fields, half-drowned in the fog that lay reeking in the moonlight along the course of the river. In the middle of the room, pell-mell, were scattered drawers, bottles, curtain-rods, gilt poles, with mattresses on the chairs and basins on the ground—the two men who had brought the furniture had left everything about carelessly.","sentences":[{"en":"She could catch glimpses of tree tops, and beyond, the fields, half-drowned in the fog that lay reeking in the moonlight along the course of the river.","zh":"她影影绰绰，望见树梢，再往远去，还望见一半没在雾里的草原，月光皎洁，雾顺着河道冒气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the middle of the room, pell-mell, were scattered drawers, bottles, curtain-rods, gilt poles, with mattresses on the chairs and basins on the ground—the two men who had brought the furniture had left everything about carelessly.","zh":"房间里面，横七竖八，随地放着五斗柜的抽屉、瓶子、帐杆、镀金小棒，椅子上搁着褥垫，地板上搁着脸盆——搬家具的两个男人，漫不经心，信手扔了一地。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This was the fourth time that she had slept in a strange place.","sentences":[{"en":"This was the fourth time that she had slept in a strange place.","zh":"这是第四次，她睡在一个陌生地方，第一次是她进修道院的那一天；第二次是她到道特的那一天；第三次是她去渥毕萨尔的那一天；如今是第四次。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The first was the day of her going to the convent; the second, of her arrival at Tostes; the third, at Vaubyessard; and this was the fourth. And each one had marked, as it were, the inauguration of a new phase in her life. She did not believe that things could present themselves in the same way in different places, and since the portion of her life lived had been bad, no doubt that which remained to be lived would be better.","sentences":[{"en":"The first was the day of her going to the convent; the second, of her arrival at Tostes; the third, at Vaubyessard; and this was the fourth.","zh":"这是第四次，她睡在一个陌生地方，第一次是她进修道院的那一天；第二次是她到道特的那一天；第三次是她去渥毕萨尔的那一天；如今是第四次。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And each one had marked, as it were, the inauguration of a new phase in her life.","zh":"每次都像在她生命中间开始一个新局面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She did not believe that things could present themselves in the same way in different places, and since the portion of her life lived had been bad, no doubt that which remained to be lived would be better.","zh":"她不相信事物在不同地方，老是一个面目；活过的一部分既然坏，没有活过的一部分，当然会好多了。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-3","part":2,"n":3,"title":"Part II · Chapter 3","titleZh":"中卷 · 3","paragraphs":[{"en":"The next day, as she was getting up, she saw the clerk on the Place. She had on a dressing-gown. He looked up and bowed. She nodded quickly and reclosed the window.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day, as she was getting up, she saw the clerk on the Place.","zh":"第二天，她一下床，就望见文书在广场。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had on a dressing-gown.","zh":"她穿的是梳妆衣。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He looked up and bowed.","zh":"他仰起头，向她致敬。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She nodded quickly and reclosed the window.","zh":"她赶快点了点头，关上窗户。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon waited all day for six o’clock in the evening to come, but on going to the inn, he found no one but Monsieur Binet, already at table. The dinner of the evening before had been a considerable event for him; he had never till then talked for two hours consecutively to a “lady.” How then had he been able to explain, and in such language, the number of things that he could not have said so well before? He was usually shy, and maintained that reserve which partakes at once of modesty and dissimulation.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon waited all day for six o’clock in the evening to come, but on going to the inn, he found no one but Monsieur Binet, already at table.","zh":"赖昂整天在盼下午六点钟到，但是走进客店，仅仅看见毕耐坐在饭桌一旁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The dinner of the evening before had been a considerable event for him; he had never till then talked for two hours consecutively to a “lady.”","zh":"昨天那顿晚饭，对他来说，是一件大事；一连两小时，同一位太太谈话，他还从来没有过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How then had he been able to explain, and in such language, the number of things that he could not have said so well before?","zh":"这许多事，往常他说都说不清楚，和她一谈，怎么就会那样娓娓动听？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was usually shy, and maintained that reserve which partakes at once of modesty and dissimulation.","zh":"他一向胆怯，庄重自持，一半也是害羞，一半也是作假。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At Yonville he was considered “well-bred.” He listened to the arguments of the older people, and did not seem hot about politics—a remarkable thing for a young man. Then he had some accomplishments; he painted in water-colours, could read the key of G, and readily talked literature after dinner when he did not play cards. Monsieur Homais respected him for his education; Madame Homais liked him for his good-nature, for he often took the little Homais into the garden—little brats who were always dirty, very much spoilt, and somewhat lymphatic, like their mother. Besides the servant to look after them, they had Justin, the chemist’s apprentice, a second cousin of Monsieur Homais, who had been taken into the house from charity, and who was useful at the same time as a servant.","sentences":[{"en":"At Yonville he was considered “well-bred.”","zh":"永镇上人，认为他举止得体。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He listened to the arguments of the older people, and did not seem hot about politics—a remarkable thing for a young man.","zh":"成人高谈阔论，他洗耳恭听，不发一言，似乎并不热衷政治：对于一个年轻人说来，确实难得。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he had some accomplishments; he painted in water-colours, could read the key of G, and readily talked literature after dinner when he did not play cards.","zh":"而且他多才多艺，能画水彩画，能看乐谱，晚饭后不玩牌的时候，他就钻研文学。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Homais respected him for his education; Madame Homais liked him for his good-nature, for he often took the little Homais into the garden—little brats who were always dirty, very much spoilt, and somewhat lymphatic, like their mother.","zh":"郝麦先生看重他有知识；郝麦太太喜欢他为人随和，因为他常在花园陪伴那些小郝麦；这些小家伙，一向邋遢，缺乏管教，还有点迟钝，如同他们的母亲。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides the servant to look after them, they had Justin, the chemist’s apprentice, a second cousin of Monsieur Homais, who had been taken into the house from charity, and who was useful at the same time as a servant.","zh":"他们除去女用人照料之外，还有药房伙计朱斯丹照料他们：他是郝麦先生的远亲，郝麦先生行好，把他收留下来，同时当用人使唤。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The druggist proved the best of neighbours. He gave Madame Bovary information as to the trades-people, sent expressly for his own cider merchant, tasted the drink himself, and saw that the casks were properly placed in the cellar; he explained how to set about getting in a supply of butter cheap, and made an arrangement with Lestiboudois, the sacristan, who, besides his sacerdotal and funeral functions, looked after the principal gardens at Yonville by the hour or the year, according to the taste of the customers.","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist proved the best of neighbours.","zh":"为了表示他是最好的邻居，药剂师指点包法利夫人买谁家东西，特地把他照顾的苹果酒贩叫来，亲自尝酒，监视酒桶在地窖摆好。他又教她怎样买到便宜的牛油。教堂管事赖斯地布杜瓦，除去教会和殡葬两项职务之外，还随各家喜好，按年或者按钟点料理永镇的主要花园，药剂师也为她的花园接好了头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He gave Madame Bovary information as to the trades-people, sent expressly for his own cider merchant, tasted the drink himself, and saw that the casks were properly placed in the cellar; he explained how to set about getting in a supply of butter cheap, and made an arrangement with Lestiboudois, the sacristan, who, besides his sacerdotal and funeral functions, looked after the principal gardens at Yonville by the hour or the year, according to the taste of the customers.","zh":"为了表示他是最好的邻居，药剂师指点包法利夫人买谁家东西，特地把他照顾的苹果酒贩叫来，亲自尝酒，监视酒桶在地窖摆好。他又教她怎样买到便宜的牛油。教堂管事赖斯地布杜瓦，除去教会和殡葬两项职务之外，还随各家喜好，按年或者按钟点料理永镇的主要花园，药剂师也为她的花园接好了头。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The need of looking after others was not the only thing that urged the chemist to such obsequious cordiality; there was a plan underneath it all.","sentences":[{"en":"The need of looking after others was not the only thing that urged the chemist to such obsequious cordiality; there was a plan underneath it all.","zh":"药剂师曲意奉承，并非单为关怀别人，其中还有别的文章。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had infringed the law of the 19th Ventose, year xi., article I, which forbade all persons not having a diploma to practise medicine; so that, after certain anonymous denunciations, Homais had been summoned to Rouen to see the procurer of the king in his own private room; the magistrate receiving him standing up, ermine on shoulder and cap on head. It was in the morning, before the court opened. In the corridors one heard the heavy boots of the gendarmes walking past, and like a far-off noise great locks that were shut. The druggist’s ears tingled as if he were about to have an apoplectic stroke; he saw the depths of dungeons, his family in tears, his shop sold, all the jars dispersed; and he was obliged to enter a cafe and take a glass of rum and seltzer to recover his spirits.","sentences":[{"en":"He had infringed the law of the 19th Ventose, year xi., article I, which forbade all persons not having a diploma to practise medicine; so that, after certain anonymous denunciations, Homais had been summoned to Rouen to see the procurer of the king in his own private room; the magistrate receiving him standing up, ermine on shoulder and cap on head.","zh":"十一年风月 十九日法律，第一条规定：任何人没有执照，不得行医。他严重违反这一条法律，经人暗中告发，王家检察官传他到鲁昂问话。司法官穿了公服，肩膀上披一条白鼬皮，头上戴一顶瓜皮小帽，站着在办公室见他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was in the morning, before the court opened.","zh":"这在早晨开庭以前。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the corridors one heard the heavy boots of the gendarmes walking past, and like a far-off noise great locks that were shut.","zh":"他听见过道有宪兵的笨重靴子走动，远处像有大锁关闭的声音。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The druggist’s ears tingled as if he were about to have an apoplectic stroke; he saw the depths of dungeons, his family in tears, his shop sold, all the jars dispersed; and he was obliged to enter a cafe and take a glass of rum and seltzer to recover his spirits.","zh":"药剂师耳朵轰隆轰隆的，眼看自己像要中风一样；他恍惚看见自己被拘禁在地牢深处，一家大小号啕，药房出让，瓶瓶罐罐丢了一地；所以离开法院，他不得不走进一家咖啡馆，喝一杯掺塞兹水的甘蔗酒，恢复他的神志。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Little by little the memory of this reprimand grew fainter, and he continued, as heretofore, to give anodyne consultations in his back-parlour. But the mayor resented it, his colleagues were jealous, everything was to be feared; gaining over Monsieur Bovary by his attentions was to earn his gratitude, and prevent his speaking out later on, should he notice anything. So every morning Homais brought him “the paper,” and often in the afternoon left his shop for a few moments to have a chat with the Doctor.","sentences":[{"en":"Little by little the memory of this reprimand grew fainter, and he continued, as heretofore, to give anodyne consultations in his back-parlour.","zh":"日子一久，训斥的回忆渐渐淡了，他像往常一样，在铺面后间看病，开上一些无关紧要的方子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the mayor resented it, his colleagues were jealous, everything was to be feared; gaining over Monsieur Bovary by his attentions was to earn his gratitude, and prevent his speaking out later on, should he notice anything.","zh":"但是他有镇长作对，同行忌妒，必须加意小心；他之所以礼数频频，讨好包法利先生，就是为了使他感激在心，万一日后有所觉察，也就难以开口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So every morning Homais brought him “the paper,” and often in the afternoon left his shop for a few moments to have a chat with the Doctor.","zh":"所以每天早晨，郝麦送报纸给他看，下午常有一时离开药房，到医生那边聊天。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles was dull: patients did not come. He remained seated for hours without speaking, went into his consulting room to sleep, or watched his wife sewing. Then for diversion he employed himself at home as a workman; he even tried to do up the attic with some paint which had been left behind by the painters. But money matters worried him. He had spent so much for repairs at Tostes, for madame’s toilette, and for the moving, that the whole dowry, over three thousand crowns, had slipped away in two years.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles was dull: patients did not come.","zh":"查理愁眉不展：顾客不见上门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He remained seated for hours without speaking, went into his consulting room to sleep, or watched his wife sewing.","zh":"他不言不语，一坐好几小时，不是在他的诊室睡觉，就是看他的太太缝东西。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then for diversion he employed himself at home as a workman; he even tried to do up the attic with some paint which had been left behind by the painters.","zh":"他为了消遣，在家里学干粗活，甚至拿漆匠用剩下来的油漆，试着油漆阁楼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But money matters worried him.","zh":"不过他真正操心的，是银钱事务。修葺道特的房屋，太太添置化妆品，还有搬家，三千多埃居嫁资，两年下来，全花光了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He had spent so much for repairs at Tostes, for madame’s toilette, and for the moving, that the whole dowry, over three thousand crowns, had slipped away in two years.","zh":"不过他真正操心的，是银钱事务。修葺道特的房屋，太太添置化妆品，还有搬家，三千多埃居嫁资，两年下来，全花光了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then how many things had been spoilt or lost during their carriage from Tostes to Yonville, without counting the plaster cure, who falling out of the coach at an over-severe jolt, had been dashed into a thousand fragments on the pavements of Quincampoix! A pleasanter trouble came to distract him, namely, the pregnancy of his wife. As the time of her confinement approached he cherished her the more. It was another bond of the flesh establishing itself, and, as it were, a continued sentiment of a more complex union. When from afar he saw her languid walk, and her figure without stays turning softly on her hips; when opposite one another he looked at her at his ease, while she took tired poses in her armchair, then his happiness knew no bounds; he got up, embraced her, passed his hands over her face, called her little mamma, wanted to make her dance, and half-laughing, half-crying, uttered all kinds of caressing pleasantries that came into his head. The idea of having begotten a child delighted him. Now he wanted nothing. He knew human life from end to end, and he sat down to it with serenity.","sentences":[{"en":"Then how many things had been spoilt or lost during their carriage from Tostes to Yonville, without counting the plaster cure, who falling out of the coach at an over-severe jolt, had been dashed into a thousand fragments on the pavements of Quincampoix!","zh":"再说，从道特搬到永镇，东西不是损坏，就是遗失，还不算石膏堂长像，有一次车颠得太厉害，滚到大车底下，在甘冈普瓦的石路上摔碎了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A pleasanter trouble came to distract him, namely, the pregnancy of his wife.","zh":"有一件事，虽然担心，却也分忧，就是太太有喜了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As the time of her confinement approached he cherished her the more.","zh":"分娩期越近，他越疼她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was another bond of the flesh establishing itself, and, as it were, a continued sentiment of a more complex union.","zh":"另外一种血肉联系在建立，像是不断提醒一种更为复杂的结合。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When from afar he saw her languid walk, and her figure without stays turning softly on her hips; when opposite one another he looked at her at his ease, while she took tired poses in her armchair, then his happiness knew no bounds; he got up, embraced her, passed his hands over her face, called her little mamma, wanted to make her dance, and half-laughing, half-crying, uttered all kinds of caressing pleasantries that came into his head.","zh":"他远远望见她，走起路来，懒洋洋的，不穿胸衣，身子软绵绵的，在屁股上扭来扭去，要不然就是，坐在扶手椅里，一副慵倦模样，面对面，尽他饱看，他太幸福，再也憋不住，站起来，搂住她，摸她的脸，叫她小妈妈，想同她跳舞，于是半笑半哭，尽他想得起来的柔情蜜意的戏言戏语，说个不停。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The idea of having begotten a child delighted him.","zh":"他想到生孩子，心花怒放。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now he wanted nothing.","zh":"他现在什么也不缺了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He knew human life from end to end, and he sat down to it with serenity.","zh":"他经历到全部人生，于是坐在人生一旁，悠然自得，尽情享受。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma at first felt a great astonishment; then was anxious to be delivered that she might know what it was to be a mother. But not being able to spend as much as she would have liked, to have a swing-bassinette with rose silk curtains, and embroidered caps, in a fit of bitterness she gave up looking after the trousseau, and ordered the whole of it from a village needlewoman, without choosing or discussing anything. Thus she did not amuse herself with those preparations that stimulate the tenderness of mothers, and so her affection was from the very outset, perhaps, to some extent attenuated.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma at first felt a great astonishment; then was anxious to be delivered that she might know what it was to be a mother.","zh":"爱玛起先觉得很惊奇，后来想知道做母亲是怎么一回事，也就急于分娩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But not being able to spend as much as she would have liked, to have a swing-bassinette with rose silk curtains, and embroidered caps, in a fit of bitterness she gave up looking after the trousseau, and ordered the whole of it from a village needlewoman, without choosing or discussing anything.","zh":"不过她不能由着她的心思用钱，好比说，买一只玫瑰红缎帐摇篮、几顶绣花小帽，所以她一怄气，不加挑选，不和人讨论，什么也不料理，统统交给村里一个女工去做。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus she did not amuse herself with those preparations that stimulate the tenderness of mothers, and so her affection was from the very outset, perhaps, to some extent attenuated.","zh":"这样一来，引起母爱的准备工作的乐趣，她就体会不到了；也许是由于这个缘故吧，她的感情，从一开始，就欠深厚。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As Charles, however, spoke of the boy at every meal, she soon began to think of him more consecutively.","sentences":[{"en":"As Charles, however, spoke of the boy at every meal, she soon began to think of him more consecutively.","zh":"不过查理顿顿饭说起小把戏，她慢慢也就老想着这事。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She hoped for a son; he would be strong and dark; she would call him George; and this idea of having a male child was like an expected revenge for all her impotence in the past. A man, at least, is free; he may travel over passions and over countries, overcome obstacles, taste of the most far-away pleasures. But a woman is always hampered. At once inert and flexible, she has against her the weakness of the flesh and legal dependence. Her will, like the veil of her bonnet, held by a string, flutters in every wind; there is always some desire that draws her, some conventionality that restrains.","sentences":[{"en":"She hoped for a son; he would be strong and dark; she would call him George; and this idea of having a male child was like an expected revenge for all her impotence in the past.","zh":"她希望养一个儿子，身子结实，棕色头发，名字叫作乔治 ：她过去毫无作为，这种生一个男孩子的想法，就像预先弥补了似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A man, at least, is free; he may travel over passions and over countries, overcome obstacles, taste of the most far-away pleasures.","zh":"男人少说也是自由的；他可以尝遍热情，周游天下，克服困难，享受天涯海角的欢乐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But a woman is always hampered.","zh":"可是一个女人，就不断受到阻挠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At once inert and flexible, she has against her the weakness of the flesh and legal dependence.","zh":"她没有生气，没有主见，身体脆弱不说，还处处受到法律拘束。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her will, like the veil of her bonnet, held by a string, flutters in every wind; there is always some desire that draws her, some conventionality that restrains.","zh":"她的意志就像面网一样，一条细绳拴在帽子上头，随风飘荡。总有欲望引诱，却总有礼法限制。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was confined on a Sunday at about six o’clock, as the sun was rising.","sentences":[{"en":"She was confined on a Sunday at about six o’clock, as the sun was rising.","zh":"星期天早晨，六点钟左右，太阳正出来，她分娩了。查理道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is a girl!” said Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“It is a girl!” said Charles.","zh":"“是一个女孩子！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She turned her head away and fainted.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned her head away and fainted.","zh":"她转过头，晕过去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Homais, as well as Madame Lefrancois of the Lion d’Or, almost immediately came running in to embrace her. The chemist, as man of discretion, only offered a few provincial felicitations through the half-opened door. He wished to see the child and thought it well made.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Homais, as well as Madame Lefrancois of the Lion d’Or, almost immediately came running in to embrace her.","zh":"郝麦太太差不多跟着就跑过来吻她，勒弗朗索瓦太太离开金狮，也来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The chemist, as man of discretion, only offered a few provincial felicitations through the half-opened door.","zh":"药剂师不便进屋，只在门缝说了几句道喜的话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He wished to see the child and thought it well made.","zh":"他希望看看婴儿；他觉得相貌端正。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Whilst she was getting well she occupied herself much in seeking a name for her daughter. First she went over all those that have Italian endings, such as Clara, Louisa, Amanda, Atala; she liked Galsuinde pretty well, and Yseult or Leocadie still better.","sentences":[{"en":"Whilst she was getting well she occupied herself much in seeking a name for her daughter.","zh":"休养期间，她费了不少心思，给女儿想名字。她最先考虑所有那些有意大利字尾的名字，诸如克拉拉、路易莎、阿芒达、阿达娜；她相当喜欢嘉尔絮安德这个名字，尤其喜欢绮瑟和莱奥卡狄这两个名字。","scope":"group"},{"en":"First she went over all those that have Italian endings, such as Clara, Louisa, Amanda, Atala; she liked Galsuinde pretty well, and Yseult or Leocadie still better.","zh":"休养期间，她费了不少心思，给女儿想名字。她最先考虑所有那些有意大利字尾的名字，诸如克拉拉、路易莎、阿芒达、阿达娜；她相当喜欢嘉尔絮安德这个名字，尤其喜欢绮瑟和莱奥卡狄这两个名字。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles wanted the child to be called after her mother; Emma opposed this. They ran over the calendar from end to end, and then consulted outsiders.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles wanted the child to be called after her mother; Emma opposed this.","zh":"查理愿意小孩子叫母亲的名字；爱玛不赞成。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They ran over the calendar from end to end, and then consulted outsiders.","zh":"他们上下查历书 ，还向外人请教。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Monsieur Léon,” said the chemist, “with whom I was talking about it the other day, wonders you do not chose Madeleine. It is very much in fashion just now.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Monsieur Léon,” said the chemist, “with whom I was talking about it the other day, wonders you do not chose Madeleine.","zh":"药剂师道：“我和赖昂先生前一天说起这事，他奇怪你们为什么不取玛德兰娜这个名字，眼下非常时髦。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It is very much in fashion just now.”","zh":"药剂师道：“我和赖昂先生前一天说起这事，他奇怪你们为什么不取玛德兰娜这个名字，眼下非常时髦。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But Madame Bovary, senior, cried out loudly against this name of a sinner. As to Monsieur Homais, he had a preference for all those that recalled some great man, an illustrious fact, or a generous idea, and it was on this system that he had baptized his four children. Thus Napoleon represented glory and Franklin liberty; Irma was perhaps a concession to romanticism, but Athalie was a homage to the greatest masterpiece of the French stage. For his philosophical convictions did not interfere with his artistic tastes; in him the thinker did not stifle the man of sentiment; he could make distinctions, make allowances for imagination and fanaticism. In this tragedy, for example, he found fault with the ideas, but admired the style; he detested the conception, but applauded all the details, and loathed the characters while he grew enthusiastic over their dialogue. When he read the fine passages he was transported, but when he thought that mummers would get something out of them for their show, he was disconsolate; and in this confusion of sentiments in which he was involved he would have liked at once to crown Racine with both his hands and discuss with him for a good quarter of an hour.","sentences":[{"en":"But Madame Bovary, senior, cried out loudly against this name of a sinner.","zh":"但是包法利老太太坚决反对用这有罪女人的名字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to Monsieur Homais, he had a preference for all those that recalled some great man, an illustrious fact, or a generous idea, and it was on this system that he had baptized his four children.","zh":"至于郝麦先生，凡足以纪念大人物、光荣事件或者高贵思想的，他都特别喜爱；他给四个孩子取名字，根据的就是这种原理。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus Napoleon represented glory and Franklin liberty; Irma was perhaps a concession to romanticism, but Athalie was a homage to the greatest masterpiece of the French stage.","zh":"所以一个叫拿破仑，代表光荣；一个叫富兰克林，代表自由；一个叫伊尔玛，也许是对浪漫主义的一种让步 ；一个叫阿塔莉，却是对法兰西戏剧最不朽之作的敬意 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For his philosophical convictions did not interfere with his artistic tastes; in him the thinker did not stifle the man of sentiment; he could make distinctions, make allowances for imagination and fanaticism.","zh":"因为他的哲学信念并不妨碍他的艺术欣赏；他的思想家成分，也绝不抑制感情流露；他懂得怎么样加以区别，把想象和狂热的信仰分开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In this tragedy, for example, he found fault with the ideas, but admired the style; he detested the conception, but applauded all the details, and loathed the characters while he grew enthusiastic over their dialogue.","zh":"就拿《阿塔莉》这出悲剧来说，他指摘思想，但是欣赏风格；他诅咒概念，但是称道全部细节；他厌恶人物，然而热爱他们的对话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he read the fine passages he was transported, but when he thought that mummers would get something out of them for their show, he was disconsolate; and in this confusion of sentiments in which he was involved he would have liked at once to crown Racine with both his hands and discuss with him for a good quarter of an hour.","zh":"他读伟大篇什，神魂颠倒；但是一想到戴黑瓜皮帽之流 ，当作生意经用，他就伤心；于是百感交集，心困神惑，他一方面希望自己能亲手给拉辛戴上桂冠，一方面也希望和他认真地讨论一番。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last Emma remembered that at the château of Vaubyessard she had heard the Marchioness call a young lady Berthe; from that moment this name was chosen; and as old Rouault could not come, Monsieur Homais was requested to stand godfather. His gifts were all products from his establishment, to wit: six boxes of jujubes, a whole jar of racahout, three cakes of marshmallow paste, and six sticks of sugar-candy into the bargain that he had come across in a cupboard. On the evening of the ceremony there was a grand dinner; the cure was present; there was much excitement. Monsieur Homais towards liqueur-time began singing “Le Dieu des bonnes gens.” Monsieur Léon sang a barcarolle, and Madame Bovary, senior, who was godmother, a romance of the time of the Empire; finally, M. Bovary, senior, insisted on having the child brought down, and began baptizing it with a glass of champagne that he poured over its head. This mockery of the first of the sacraments made the Abbe Bournisien angry; old Bovary replied by a quotation from “La Guerre des Dieux”; the cure wanted to leave; the ladies implored, Homais interfered; and they succeeded in making the priest sit down again, and he quietly went on with the half-finished coffee in his saucer.","sentences":[{"en":"At last Emma remembered that at the château of Vaubyessard she had heard the Marchioness call a young lady Berthe; from that moment this name was chosen; and as old Rouault could not come, Monsieur Homais was requested to stand godfather.","zh":"最后还是爱玛想起，她在渥毕萨尔庄园，听见侯爵夫人喊一个年轻女人白尔特 ，就选定了这个名字。卢欧老爹不能来，他们请郝麦先生做教父。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His gifts were all products from his establishment, to wit: six boxes of jujubes, a whole jar of racahout, three cakes of marshmallow paste, and six sticks of sugar-candy into the bargain that he had come across in a cupboard.","zh":"他的礼物全是他的药房的出品，诸如：六匣黑枣、一整瓶健身粉、三筒药用蜀葵片，还有在壁橱里找到的六根冰糖棍。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the evening of the ceremony there was a grand dinner; the cure was present; there was much excitement.","zh":"举行洗礼的当天晚晌，摆了一桌酒席；教堂堂长也在座。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Homais towards liqueur-time began singing “Le Dieu des bonnes gens.”","zh":"大家兴高采烈，临到行酒，郝麦先生唱《好人们的上帝》 ，赖昂先生来了一首船夫曲，包法利老太太是教母，也唱了一首帝国时代流行的恋歌；闹到后来，老包法利硬要抱小孩子下来，举起一杯香槟酒，说是给她行洗礼，朝头上浇。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Léon sang a barcarolle, and Madame Bovary, senior, who was godmother, a romance of the time of the Empire; finally, M. Bovary, senior, insisted on having the child brought down, and began baptizing it with a glass of champagne that he poured over its head.","zh":"大家兴高采烈，临到行酒，郝麦先生唱《好人们的上帝》 ，赖昂先生来了一首船夫曲，包法利老太太是教母，也唱了一首帝国时代流行的恋歌；闹到后来，老包法利硬要抱小孩子下来，举起一杯香槟酒，说是给她行洗礼，朝头上浇。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This mockery of the first of the sacraments made the Abbe Bournisien angry; old Bovary replied by a quotation from “La Guerre des Dieux”; the cure wanted to leave; the ladies implored, Homais interfered; and they succeeded in making the priest sit down again, and he quietly went on with the half-finished coffee in his saucer.","zh":"布尔尼贤堂长见他取笑第一条圣事 ，未免有气；老包法利的答复是引证一句《众神之战》 ；堂长离席要走；太太们央求，郝麦解劝，才算留住教士又坐下来：他端起碟子，心平气和，又喝着他喝了一半的小杯咖啡。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Bovary, senior, stayed at Yonville a month, dazzling the natives by a superb policeman’s cap with silver tassels that he wore in the morning when he smoked his pipe in the square. Being also in the habit of drinking a good deal of brandy, he often sent the servant to the Lion d’Or to buy him a bottle, which was put down to his son’s account, and to perfume his handkerchiefs he used up his daughter-in-law’s whole supply of eau-de-cologne.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Bovary, senior, stayed at Yonville a month, dazzling the natives by a superb policeman’s cap with silver tassels that he wore in the morning when he smoked his pipe in the square.","zh":"老包法利在永镇住了一个月之久。早晨他到广场吸烟斗，戴一顶漂亮的银箍船形帽，居民还真让他给唬住了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Being also in the habit of drinking a good deal of brandy, he often sent the servant to the Lion d’Or to buy him a bottle, which was put down to his son’s account, and to perfume his handkerchiefs he used up his daughter-in-law’s whole supply of eau-de-cologne.","zh":"他喝烧酒有瘾，一来就差女用人到金狮替他买一瓶，写在儿子账上：他要手帕有香味，用光儿媳妇储藏的全部科隆香水。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The latter did not at all dislike his company. He had knocked about the world, he talked about Berlin, Vienna, and Strasbourg, of his soldier times, of the mistresses he had had, the grand luncheons of which he had partaken; then he was amiable, and sometimes even, either on the stairs, or in the garden, would seize hold of her waist, crying, “Charles, look out for yourself.”","sentences":[{"en":"The latter did not at all dislike his company.","zh":"儿媳妇并不讨厌他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had knocked about the world, he talked about Berlin, Vienna, and Strasbourg, of his soldier times, of the mistresses he had had, the grand luncheons of which he had partaken; then he was amiable, and sometimes even, either on the stairs, or in the garden, would seize hold of her waist, crying, “Charles, look out for yourself.”","zh":"他有阅历，讲起柏林、维也纳、斯特拉斯堡，还有他当军官的时期、他有过的情妇、他摆过的盛大午宴。而且他显出一副可爱模样，有时候甚至在楼梯上或者花园内，搂住她的腰，喊道：“查理，当心啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Madame Bovary, senior, became alarmed for her son’s happiness, and fearing that her husband might in the long-run have an immoral influence upon the ideas of the young woman, took care to hurry their departure. Perhaps she had more serious reasons for uneasiness. Monsieur Bovary was not the man to respect anything.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Madame Bovary, senior, became alarmed for her son’s happiness, and fearing that her husband might in the long-run have an immoral influence upon the ideas of the young woman, took care to hurry their departure.","zh":"这样一来，老太太不放心了，生怕丈夫会有一天对年轻女人起坏影响，连累儿子的幸福，急于要早走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps she had more serious reasons for uneasiness.","zh":"她也许有更严重的顾虑吧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Bovary was not the man to respect anything.","zh":"老包法利是个无法无天的人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One day Emma was suddenly seized with the desire to see her little girl, who had been put to nurse with the carpenter’s wife, and, without looking at the calendar to see whether the six weeks of the Virgin were yet passed, she set out for the Rollets’ house, situated at the extreme end of the village, between the highroad and the fields.","sentences":[{"en":"One day Emma was suddenly seized with the desire to see her little girl, who had been put to nurse with the carpenter’s wife, and, without looking at the calendar to see whether the six weeks of the Virgin were yet passed, she set out for the Rollets’ house, situated at the extreme end of the village, between the highroad and the fields.","zh":"小女儿交给木匠女人乳养，有一天，爱玛忽然动了看她的心思，也不看看历书，圣母的六个星期 过了没有，就朝罗莱住的地方走去。他住在岭下村子尽头，在大路和草原之间。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was mid-day, the shutters of the houses were closed and the slate roofs that glittered beneath the fierce light of the blue sky seemed to strike sparks from the crest of the gables. A heavy wind was blowing; Emma felt weak as she walked; the stones of the pavement hurt her; she was doubtful whether she would not go home again, or go in somewhere to rest.","sentences":[{"en":"It was mid-day, the shutters of the houses were closed and the slate roofs that glittered beneath the fierce light of the blue sky seemed to strike sparks from the crest of the gables.","zh":"正是中午，家家下了护窗板，碧空烈日，青石板屋顶明光闪闪，山墙头好像在冒火花。一阵热风吹来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A heavy wind was blowing; Emma felt weak as she walked; the stones of the pavement hurt her; she was doubtful whether she would not go home again, or go in somewhere to rest.","zh":"爱玛觉得行走乏力；人行道的石子磨脚；她拿不定主意回家好，还是进谁家歇歇好。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At this moment Monsieur Léon came out from a neighbouring door with a bundle of papers under his arm. He came to greet her, and stood in the shade in front of the Lheureux’s shop under the projecting grey awning.","sentences":[{"en":"At this moment Monsieur Léon came out from a neighbouring door with a bundle of papers under his arm.","zh":"正在这时，赖昂先生胳膊底下夹着一卷文件，从邻近一家大门出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He came to greet her, and stood in the shade in front of the Lheureux’s shop under the projecting grey awning.","zh":"他走过来问候她，站在勒乐铺子前面，灰帐篷底下的荫凉里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary said she was going to see her baby, but that she was beginning to grow tired.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary said she was going to see her baby, but that she was beginning to grow tired.","zh":"包法利夫人说她去看她的孩子，不过她已经觉得累了。“如果…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If—” said Léon, not daring to go on.","sentences":[{"en":"“If—” said Léon, not daring to go on.","zh":"赖昂嗫嚅一声，不敢再讲下去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Have you any business to attend to?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you any business to attend to?” she asked.","zh":"她问他：“您有事忙吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And on the clerk’s answer, she begged him to accompany her. That same evening this was known in Yonville, and Madame Tuvache, the mayor’s wife, declared in the presence of her servant that “Madame Bovary was compromising herself.”","sentences":[{"en":"And on the clerk’s answer, she begged him to accompany her.","zh":"文书说他没有事，她求他陪她一道去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That same evening this was known in Yonville, and Madame Tuvache, the mayor’s wife, declared in the presence of her servant that “Madame Bovary was compromising herself.”","zh":"一到黄昏，永镇传遍这事，镇长太太杜法赦夫人，当着女用人的面讲：“包法利太太惹火烧身。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To get to the nurse’s it was necessary to turn to the left on leaving the street, as if making for the cemetery, and to follow between little houses and yards a small path bordered with privet hedges. They were in bloom, and so were the speedwells, eglantines, thistles, and the sweetbriar that sprang up from the thickets. Through openings in the hedges one could see into the huts, some pigs on a dung-heap, or tethered cows rubbing their horns against the trunk of trees. The two, side by side walked slowly, she leaning upon him, and he restraining his pace, which he regulated by hers; in front of them a swarm of midges fluttered, buzzing in the warm air.","sentences":[{"en":"To get to the nurse’s it was necessary to turn to the left on leaving the street, as if making for the cemetery, and to follow between little houses and yards a small path bordered with privet hedges.","zh":"去奶妈家的路，就像去公墓的路一样，出了街，必须朝左转，穿过一些窄小的房屋和院落，走一条小径。道旁一排小女贞树，正在开花，还有威灵仙、野蔷薇、荨麻和在灌木丛上亭亭玉立的木莓，也不甘落后。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were in bloom, and so were the speedwells, eglantines, thistles, and the sweetbriar that sprang up from the thickets.","zh":"去奶妈家的路，就像去公墓的路一样，出了街，必须朝左转，穿过一些窄小的房屋和院落，走一条小径。道旁一排小女贞树，正在开花，还有威灵仙、野蔷薇、荨麻和在灌木丛上亭亭玉立的木莓，也不甘落后。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Through openings in the hedges one could see into the huts, some pigs on a dung-heap, or tethered cows rubbing their horns against the trunk of trees.","zh":"从篱笆窟窿望进去，就见草棚周围，不是猪在粪堆上爬，就是脖子套着夹板的母牛，拿犄角在蹭树身。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The two, side by side walked slowly, she leaning upon him, and he restraining his pace, which he regulated by hers; in front of them a swarm of midges fluttered, buzzing in the warm air.","zh":"两个人， 并肩漫步，她靠住他，他照她的脚步，放慢步子；空气燥热，一群苍蝇在他们前头飞来飞去，嘤嘤作响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They recognized the house by an old walnut-tree which shaded it.","sentences":[{"en":"They recognized the house by an old walnut-tree which shaded it.","zh":"他们看见一棵老胡桃树，知道到了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Low and covered with brown tiles, there hung outside it, beneath the dormer-window of the garret, a string of onions. Faggots upright against a thorn fence surrounded a bed of lettuce, a few square feet of lavender, and sweet peas strung on sticks. Dirty water was running here and there on the grass, and all round were several indefinite rags, knitted stockings, a red calico jacket, and a large sheet of coarse linen spread over the hedge. At the noise of the gate the nurse appeared with a baby she was suckling on one arm. With her other hand she was pulling along a poor puny little fellow, his face covered with scrofula, the son of a Rouen hosier, whom his parents, too taken up with their business, left in the country.","sentences":[{"en":"Low and covered with brown tiles, there hung outside it, beneath the dormer-window of the garret, a string of onions.","zh":"老胡桃树荫下，有一所棕色瓦房，矮矮的，阁楼天窗底下挂着一串大葱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Faggots upright against a thorn fence surrounded a bed of lettuce, a few square feet of lavender, and sweet peas strung on sticks.","zh":"一捆一捆小树枝，竖直了，靠住荆棘篱笆，圈着一畦生菜、一小片香草，架子支起正在开花的豌豆，泼在草上的脏水，东一摊、西一摊，房子周围有几件叫不出名堂的破衣烂裤，编织的袜子、一件红印花布短袖女衫和一大幅晾在篱笆上的厚帆布。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Dirty water was running here and there on the grass, and all round were several indefinite rags, knitted stockings, a red calico jacket, and a large sheet of coarse linen spread over the hedge.","zh":"一捆一捆小树枝，竖直了，靠住荆棘篱笆，圈着一畦生菜、一小片香草，架子支起正在开花的豌豆，泼在草上的脏水，东一摊、西一摊，房子周围有几件叫不出名堂的破衣烂裤，编织的袜子、一件红印花布短袖女衫和一大幅晾在篱笆上的厚帆布。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At the noise of the gate the nurse appeared with a baby she was suckling on one arm.","zh":"一捆一捆小树枝，竖直了，靠住荆棘篱笆，圈着一畦生菜、一小片香草，架子支起正在开花的豌豆，泼在草上的脏水，东一摊、西一摊，房子周围有几件叫不出名堂的破衣烂裤，编织的袜子、一件红印花布短袖女衫和一大幅晾在篱笆上的厚帆布。","scope":"group"},{"en":"With her other hand she was pulling along a poor puny little fellow, his face covered with scrofula, the son of a Rouen hosier, whom his parents, too taken up with their business, left in the country.","zh":"奶妈听见栅栏响，抱着一个吃奶的孩子出来，另一只手还牵着一个可怜的小瘦家伙，一脸瘰疬：鲁昂一个帽商的儿子，父母忙于做生意，把他留在乡下。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Go in,” she said; “your little one is there asleep.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go in,” she said; “your little one is there asleep.”","zh":"“进来吧，您的孩子在那边睡着呐。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The room on the ground-floor, the only one in the dwelling, had at its farther end, against the wall, a large bed without curtains, while a kneading-trough took up the side by the window, one pane of which was mended with a piece of blue paper. In the corner behind the door, shining hob-nailed shoes stood in a row under the slab of the washstand, near a bottle of oil with a feather stuck in its mouth; a Matthieu Laensberg lay on the dusty mantelpiece amid gunflints, candle-ends, and bits of amadou.","sentences":[{"en":"The room on the ground-floor, the only one in the dwelling, had at its farther end, against the wall, a large bed without curtains, while a kneading-trough took up the side by the window, one pane of which was mended with a piece of blue paper.","zh":"全楼唯一的卧室，就是下面的房间，尽里贴墙，有一张大床，不挂钩子；沿窗放着面盆；玻璃有一块裂开，拿蓝纸剪成一颗星星，粘在一道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the corner behind the door, shining hob-nailed shoes stood in a row under the slab of the washstand, near a bottle of oil with a feather stuck in its mouth; a Matthieu Laensberg lay on the dusty mantelpiece amid gunflints, candle-ends, and bits of amadou.","zh":"门后角落，水槽石板底下，摆着几只高筒靴子，靴底钉子发亮，旁边有一只瓶子，盛满了油，瓶口插着一根羽毛；炉架全是灰尘，上面扔着一本《马太·朗斯贝格》 ，夹杂在打火石、蜡烛头和零星火绒当中。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Finally, the last luxury in the apartment was a “Fame” blowing her trumpets, a picture cut out, no doubt, from some perfumer’s prospectus and nailed to the wall with six wooden shoe-pegs.","sentences":[{"en":"Finally, the last luxury in the apartment was a “Fame” blowing her trumpets, a picture cut out, no doubt, from some perfumer’s prospectus and nailed to the wall with six wooden shoe-pegs.","zh":"这间屋子最用不着的奢侈品是一幅画，画的是信息女神吹喇叭，不用说，一定是从什么香料广告画上剪下来的，拿六个木头套鞋钉子，钉在墙上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma’s child was asleep in a wicker-cradle. She took it up in the wrapping that enveloped it and began singing softly as she rocked herself to and fro.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma’s child was asleep in a wicker-cradle.","zh":"爱玛的小孩子睡在地上一个柳条摇篮里。她连被窝一道抱起来，一边摇晃身子，一边低声歌唱。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She took it up in the wrapping that enveloped it and began singing softly as she rocked herself to and fro.","zh":"爱玛的小孩子睡在地上一个柳条摇篮里。她连被窝一道抱起来，一边摇晃身子，一边低声歌唱。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Léon walked up and down the room; it seemed strange to him to see this beautiful woman in her nankeen dress in the midst of all this poverty. Madam Bovary reddened; he turned away, thinking perhaps there had been an impertinent look in his eyes. Then she put back the little girl, who had just been sick over her collar.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon walked up and down the room; it seemed strange to him to see this beautiful woman in her nankeen dress in the midst of all this poverty.","zh":"赖昂在屋里踱来踱去；这位漂亮太太，穿一件南京布 袍子，周围一片穷苦景象，他越看越觉得不伦不类。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madam Bovary reddened; he turned away, thinking perhaps there had been an impertinent look in his eyes.","zh":"包法利夫人脸红了；他转开身子，心想他这样看她，也许有些失礼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she put back the little girl, who had just been sick over her collar.","zh":"小孩子吐奶吐到她的领子上，她放她躺回去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The nurse at once came to dry her, protesting that it wouldn’t show.","sentences":[{"en":"The nurse at once came to dry her, protesting that it wouldn’t show.","zh":"奶妈赶忙过来揩，直说不会留下印子。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“She gives me other doses,” she said: “I am always a-washing of her. If you would have the goodness to order Camus, the grocer, to let me have a little soap, it would really be more convenient for you, as I needn’t trouble you then.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She gives me other doses,” she said: “I am always a-washing of her.","zh":"“她净朝我身上吐奶，我除去洗她，就甭想再干别的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If you would have the goodness to order Camus, the grocer, to let me have a little soap, it would really be more convenient for you, as I needn’t trouble you then.”","zh":"您可不可以吩咐杂货店卡穆一声，我缺肥皂用，许我拿上一块两块？往后我用不着吵扰您，对您也方便多了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Very well! very well!” said Emma. “Good morning, Madame Rollet,” and she went out, wiping her shoes at the door.","sentences":[{"en":"“Very well! very well!” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛道：“好吧！好吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Good morning, Madame Rollet,” and she went out, wiping her shoes at the door.","zh":"罗莱嫂子，再见！”她出来在门槛上揩了揩脚。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The good woman accompanied her to the end of the garden, talking all the time of the trouble she had getting up of nights.","sentences":[{"en":"The good woman accompanied her to the end of the garden, talking all the time of the trouble she had getting up of nights.","zh":"乡下女人陪她一直陪到院子尽头，诉说她夜晚不得不起床的苦处。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I’m that worn out sometimes as I drop asleep on my chair. I’m sure you might at least give me just a pound of ground coffee; that’d last me a month, and I’d take it of a morning with some milk.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’m that worn out sometimes as I drop asleep on my chair.","zh":"“我有时候累得要命，好端端坐在椅子上就睡着了；所以再不怎么，您也该赏我一磅磨好的咖啡，一磅够我一个月用的，早上我兑牛奶喝。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’m sure you might at least give me just a pound of ground coffee; that’d last me a month, and I’d take it of a morning with some milk.”","zh":"“我有时候累得要命，好端端坐在椅子上就睡着了；所以再不怎么，您也该赏我一磅磨好的咖啡，一磅够我一个月用的，早上我兑牛奶喝。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"After having submitted to her thanks, Madam Bovary left. She had gone a little way down the path when, at the sound of wooden shoes, she turned round. It was the nurse.","sentences":[{"en":"After having submitted to her thanks, Madam Bovary left.","zh":"包法利夫人勉强听完她的道谢，拔脚就走，眼看在小径已经走了一程，只听传来一片木头套鞋响声，回头一望：原来又是奶妈赶来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She had gone a little way down the path when, at the sound of wooden shoes, she turned round.","zh":"包法利夫人勉强听完她的道谢，拔脚就走，眼看在小径已经走了一程，只听传来一片木头套鞋响声，回头一望：原来又是奶妈赶来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was the nurse.","zh":"包法利夫人勉强听完她的道谢，拔脚就走，眼看在小径已经走了一程，只听传来一片木头套鞋响声，回头一望：原来又是奶妈赶来了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What is it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What is it?”","zh":"“又是什么事？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then the peasant woman, taking her aside behind an elm tree, began talking to her of her husband, who with his trade and six francs a year that the captain—","sentences":[{"en":"Then the peasant woman, taking her aside behind an elm tree, began talking to her of her husband, who with his trade and six francs a year that the captain—","zh":"于是乡下女人把她拽到一棵榆树后头，唠唠叨叨，说她的丈夫，干那行营生，一年六法郎，船长还…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, be quick!” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, be quick!” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛道：“快说吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well,” the nurse went on, heaving sighs between each word, “I’m afraid he’ll be put out seeing me have coffee alone, you know men—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well,” the nurse went on, heaving sighs between each word, “I’m afraid he’ll be put out seeing me have coffee alone, you know men—”","zh":"奶妈说一个字，叹一口气，接下去道：“可不，单我一个人有咖啡喝，我怕他看了会难过的；您知道，男人家…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But you are to have some,” Emma repeated; “I will give you some. You bother me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But you are to have some,” Emma repeated; “I will give you some.","zh":"爱玛一连几次道：“少不了您的，我给您就是了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You bother me!”","zh":"别跟我蘑菇！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, dear! my poor, dear lady! you see in consequence of his wounds he has terrible cramps in the chest. He even says that cider weakens him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, dear! my poor, dear lady! you see in consequence of his wounds he has terrible cramps in the chest.","zh":"“唉！我的善心太太，都只为他先前受伤，胸口死抽着疼。他讲，就连苹果酒也不顶事。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He even says that cider weakens him.”","zh":"“罗莱嫂子，有话快讲！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do make haste, Mere Rollet!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do make haste, Mere Rollet!”","zh":"后者行了一个大礼，接下去道：“那，您不嫌我太贫气…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well,” the latter continued, making a curtsey, “if it weren’t asking too much,” and she curtsied once more, “if you would”—and her eyes begged—“a jar of brandy,” she said at last, “and I’d rub your little one’s feet with it; they’re as tender as one’s tongue.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well,” the latter continued, making a curtsey, “if it weren’t asking too much,” and she curtsied once more, “if you would”—and her eyes begged—“a jar of brandy,” she said at last, “and I’d rub your little one’s feet with it; they’re as tender as one’s tongue.”","zh":"”一双眼睛哀求着，她终于说出了口：“一小坛烧酒，我拿它擦小姐的脚，她那小脚丫呀，嫩得就像舌头一样。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Once rid of the nurse, Emma again took Monsieur Léon’s arm. She walked fast for some time, then more slowly, and looking straight in front of her, her eyes rested on the shoulder of the young man, whose frock-coat had a black-velvety collar. His brown hair fell over it, straight and carefully arranged. She noticed his nails which were longer than one wore them at Yonville. It was one of the clerk’s chief occupations to trim them, and for this purpose he kept a special knife in his writing desk.","sentences":[{"en":"Once rid of the nurse, Emma again took Monsieur Léon’s arm.","zh":"爱玛打发掉奶妈，又挎上赖昂先生的胳膊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She walked fast for some time, then more slowly, and looking straight in front of her, her eyes rested on the shoulder of the young man, whose frock-coat had a black-velvety collar.","zh":"她放快脚步，走上一阵，又慢了下来，眼睛朝前望来望去，望到年轻人的肩膀。他的大衣有一条黑绒领子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His brown hair fell over it, straight and carefully arranged.","zh":"栗色头发，梳得又平又齐，搭在领子上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She noticed his nails which were longer than one wore them at Yonville.","zh":"她看出他的指甲，永镇谁也没有他长。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was one of the clerk’s chief occupations to trim them, and for this purpose he kept a special knife in his writing desk.","zh":"文书一件大事，就是保养指甲；他的文具盒里有一把小刀，专修指甲用。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They returned to Yonville by the water-side. In the warm season the bank, wider than at other times, showed to their foot the garden walls whence a few steps led to the river. It flowed noiselessly, swift, and cold to the eye; long, thin grasses huddled together in it as the current drove them, and spread themselves upon the limpid water like streaming hair; sometimes at the tip of the reeds or on the leaf of a water-lily an insect with fine legs crawled or rested. The sun pierced with a ray the small blue bubbles of the waves that, breaking, followed each other; branchless old willows mirrored their grey backs in the water; beyond, all around, the meadows seemed empty. It was the dinner-hour at the farms, and the young woman and her companion heard nothing as they walked but the fall of their steps on the earth of the path, the words they spoke, and the sound of Emma’s dress rustling round her.","sentences":[{"en":"They returned to Yonville by the water-side.","zh":"他们沿河岸回到永镇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the warm season the bank, wider than at other times, showed to their foot the garden walls whence a few steps led to the river.","zh":"到了夏季，河岸宽了，花园墙连墙基也露了出来。花园有一道台阶，通到水边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It flowed noiselessly, swift, and cold to the eye; long, thin grasses huddled together in it as the current drove them, and spread themselves upon the limpid water like streaming hair; sometimes at the tip of the reeds or on the leaf of a water-lily an insect with fine legs crawled or rested.","zh":"河水静静流着，望过去觉得水又急又凉；水草细长、顺流俯伏，仿佛松开的绿头发，在清澈的水里摊开了一样。有时候，一只细脚虫，在灯芯草尖端或者荷叶上面，爬来爬去，要不然就是待着不动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sun pierced with a ray the small blue bubbles of the waves that, breaking, followed each other; branchless old willows mirrored their grey backs in the water; beyond, all around, the meadows seemed empty.","zh":"波纹粼粼，一道阳光，像细丝一样，穿过蓝色的小气泡；小气泡一个接一个，朝前趱赶，随即又裂碎。缺枝断条的老柳树，在水里映出它们的灰色树皮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the dinner-hour at the farms, and the young woman and her companion heard nothing as they walked but the fall of their steps on the earth of the path, the words they spoke, and the sound of Emma’s dress rustling round her.","zh":"四周草原，远远望去，空空落落，好像一无所有。现在是田庄用饭的时辰，万籁俱寂，少妇和她的同伴就只听见他们自己的谈话、他们在小径行走的整齐步伐和爱玛袍子的窸窣响声。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The walls of the gardens with pieces of bottle on their coping were hot as the glass windows of a conservatory. Wallflowers had sprung up between the bricks, and with the tip of her open sunshade Madame Bovary, as she passed, made some of their faded flowers crumble into a yellow dust, or a spray of overhanging honeysuckle and clematis caught in its fringe and dangled for a moment over the silk.","sentences":[{"en":"The walls of the gardens with pieces of bottle on their coping were hot as the glass windows of a conservatory.","zh":"花园墙顶砌着碎玻璃，墙像暖房玻璃窗那样烫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Wallflowers had sprung up between the bricks, and with the tip of her open sunshade Madame Bovary, as she passed, made some of their faded flowers crumble into a yellow dust, or a spray of overhanging honeysuckle and clematis caught in its fringe and dangled for a moment over the silk.","zh":"砖缝长着桂竹香，有些花开败了，包法利夫人从旁走过，阳伞撑开，伞边一碰，就有黄粉撒了下来；要不然就是，有时，金银花和铁线莲的枝子，伸出墙外，和流苏绞在一起，在绸面上拖一阵。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They were talking of a troupe of Spanish dancers who were expected shortly at the Rouen theatre.","sentences":[{"en":"They were talking of a troupe of Spanish dancers who were expected shortly at the Rouen theatre.","zh":"他们谈起一家西班牙舞蹈团，不久要在鲁昂的剧场表演。她问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are you going?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you going?” she asked.","zh":"“您去不去看？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If I can,” he answered.","sentences":[{"en":"“If I can,” he answered.","zh":"他答道：“看情形。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Had they nothing else to say to one another? Yet their eyes were full of more serious speech, and while they forced themselves to find trivial phrases, they felt the same languor stealing over them both. It was the whisper of the soul, deep, continuous, dominating that of their voices. Surprised with wonder at this strange sweetness, they did not think of speaking of the sensation or of seeking its cause. Coming joys, like tropical shores, throw over the immensity before them their inborn softness, an odorous wind, and we are lulled by this intoxication without a thought of the horizon that we do not even know.","sentences":[{"en":"Had they nothing else to say to one another?","zh":"难道他们就没有别的话讲？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yet their eyes were full of more serious speech, and while they forced themselves to find trivial phrases, they felt the same languor stealing over them both.","zh":"然而他们的眼睛，有的是更传情的语言；每逢他们竭力搜寻无关紧要的话题，两个人就全感到一种相同的懒散心情，好像灵魂还有一种深沉、持久的呢喃，驾乎声音的呢喃之上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was the whisper of the soul, deep, continuous, dominating that of their voices.","zh":"然而他们的眼睛，有的是更传情的语言；每逢他们竭力搜寻无关紧要的话题，两个人就全感到一种相同的懒散心情，好像灵魂还有一种深沉、持久的呢喃，驾乎声音的呢喃之上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Surprised with wonder at this strange sweetness, they did not think of speaking of the sensation or of seeking its cause.","zh":"他们想不到自己会有这种甜蜜感受，惊愕之下，没有想到点破它的存在，或者寻找它的原因。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Coming joys, like tropical shores, throw over the immensity before them their inborn softness, an odorous wind, and we are lulled by this intoxication without a thought of the horizon that we do not even know.","zh":"未来的幸福好像热带的河岸，天性仁厚，滋润两旁的大地一样，放出阵阵香风，由他们尽情享受，他们也如醉如痴，乐在其中，什么顾虑都不搁在心上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In one place the ground had been trodden down by the cattle; they had to step on large green stones put here and there in the mud.","sentences":[{"en":"In one place the ground had been trodden down by the cattle; they had to step on large green stones put here and there in the mud.","zh":"有一个地方，牲畜踩来踩去，路陷下去，烂泥里搁着几块大绿石头，他们必须踩着石头过去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She often stopped a moment to look where to place her foot, and tottering on a stone that shook, her arms outspread, her form bent forward with a look of indecision, she would laugh, afraid of falling into the puddles of water.","sentences":[{"en":"She often stopped a moment to look where to place her foot, and tottering on a stone that shook, her arms outspread, her form bent forward with a look of indecision, she would laugh, afraid of falling into the puddles of water.","zh":"她一来就停住，看看下一步在什么地方落脚——于是石头活动，身子摇摆，胳膊伸在半空，胸脯朝前，眼睛犹疑不定，生怕掉进水坑，她笑了起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When they arrived in front of her garden, Madame Bovary opened the little gate, ran up the steps and disappeared.","sentences":[{"en":"When they arrived in front of her garden, Madame Bovary opened the little gate, ran up the steps and disappeared.","zh":"包法利夫人走到自己花园前面，推开小栅栏门，跑上台阶，就闪进去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon returned to his office. His chief was away; he just glanced at the briefs, then cut himself a pen, and at last took up his hat and went out.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon returned to his office.","zh":"赖昂回到办公室。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His chief was away; he just glanced at the briefs, then cut himself a pen, and at last took up his hat and went out.","zh":"老板不在；他望了一眼案卷，然后修了一支鹅毛笔，临了戴上帽子走了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He went to La Pâture at the top of the Argueil hills at the beginning of the forest; he threw himself upon the ground under the pines and watched the sky through his fingers.","sentences":[{"en":"He went to La Pâture at the top of the Argueil hills at the beginning of the forest; he threw himself upon the ground under the pines and watched the sky through his fingers.","zh":"他来到阿格伊岭上的牧场，躺在森林旁边冷杉底下，隔着手指望天。他自言自语道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How bored I am!” he said to himself, “how bored I am!”","sentences":[{"en":"“How bored I am!” he said to himself, “how bored I am!”","zh":"“真无聊！真无聊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He thought he was to be pitied for living in this village, with Homais for a friend and Monsieur Guillaumin for master. The latter, entirely absorbed by his business, wearing gold-rimmed spectacles and red whiskers over a white cravat, understood nothing of mental refinements, although he affected a stiff English manner, which in the beginning had impressed the clerk.","sentences":[{"en":"He thought he was to be pitied for living in this village, with Homais for a friend and Monsieur Guillaumin for master.","zh":"住这种村子，和郝麦做朋友，在居由曼先生手下做事，他觉得倒霉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The latter, entirely absorbed by his business, wearing gold-rimmed spectacles and red whiskers over a white cravat, understood nothing of mental refinements, although he affected a stiff English manner, which in the beginning had impressed the clerk.","zh":"后者心上只有事务，戴一副金丝眼镜，留一圈红络腮胡须，系一条白领带，摆出一副死板的英吉利派头，开头唬住了文书，其实，毫无精神生活。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As to the chemist’s spouse, she was the best wife in Normandy, gentle as a sheep, loving her children, her father, her mother, her cousins, weeping for other’s woes, letting everything go in her household, and detesting corsets; but so slow of movement, such a bore to listen to, so common in appearance, and of such restricted conversation, that although she was thirty, he only twenty, although they slept in rooms next each other and he spoke to her daily, he never thought that she might be a woman for another, or that she possessed anything else of her sex than the gown.","sentences":[{"en":"As to the chemist’s spouse, she was the best wife in Normandy, gentle as a sheep, loving her children, her father, her mother, her cousins, weeping for other’s woes, letting everything go in her household, and detesting corsets; but so slow of movement, such a bore to listen to, so common in appearance, and of such restricted conversation, that although she was thirty, he only twenty, although they slept in rooms next each other and he spoke to her daily, he never thought that she might be a woman for another, or that she possessed anything else of her sex than the gown.","zh":"至于药剂师的女人，她是诺曼底最贤德的太太，绵羊一般柔顺，爱护她的子女、她的父亲、她的母亲、她的亲戚，听见别人家出事就哭，家事概不过问，就恨穿胸衣；——但是行动那样迟缓，听她讲话那样乏味，面貌那样寻常，谈吐那样干巴，虽然她三十岁，他二十岁，他们睡觉门对门，他每天同她说话，他从来没有想到她对任何男子也是一个女人，除去袍子，看不出还有别的东西表示她是女性。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And what else was there? Binet, a few shopkeepers, two or three publicans, the cure, and finally, Monsieur Tuvache, the mayor, with his two sons, rich, crabbed, obtuse persons, who farmed their own lands and had feasts among themselves, bigoted to boot, and quite unbearable companions.","sentences":[{"en":"And what else was there?","zh":"此外，还有谁？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Binet, a few shopkeepers, two or three publicans, the cure, and finally, Monsieur Tuvache, the mayor, with his two sons, rich, crabbed, obtuse persons, who farmed their own lands and had feasts among themselves, bigoted to boot, and quite unbearable companions.","zh":"毕耐、几个生意人、两三个开小酒馆的、教堂堂长，最后还有，镇长杜法赦先生和他的两个儿子：他们是粗鲁、愚蠢的阔人，亲自下地，在家大吃大喝，而且虔心信教，根本没有可能待在一起。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But from the general background of all these human faces Emma’s stood out isolated and yet farthest off; for between her and him he seemed to see a vague abyss.","sentences":[{"en":"But from the general background of all these human faces Emma’s stood out isolated and yet farthest off; for between her and him he seemed to see a vague abyss.","zh":"但是在所有这些面目形成的共同背景之上，爱玛的形象，孤零零的，离他只有更远；因为他觉得在他和她之间，就像隔着好些一片模糊的深渊一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the beginning he had called on her several times along with the druggist. Charles had not appeared particularly anxious to see him again, and Léon did not know what to do between his fear of being indiscreet and the desire for an intimacy that seemed almost impossible.","sentences":[{"en":"In the beginning he had called on her several times along with the druggist.","zh":"起初他有几回，和药剂师一道到她家去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles had not appeared particularly anxious to see him again, and Léon did not know what to do between his fear of being indiscreet and the desire for an intimacy that seemed almost impossible.","zh":"查理似乎并不特别欢迎他；赖昂也不知道怎样才好，一面唯恐自己冒昧，一面却又希图亲近，然而说到亲近，照他估计，几乎就没有指望。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-4","part":2,"n":4,"title":"Part II · Chapter 4","titleZh":"中卷 · 4","paragraphs":[{"en":"When the first cold days set in Emma left her bedroom for the sitting-room, a long apartment with a low ceiling, in which there was on the mantelpiece a large bunch of coral spread out against the looking-glass. Seated in her arm chair near the window, she could see the villagers pass along the pavement.","sentences":[{"en":"When the first cold days set in Emma left her bedroom for the sitting-room, a long apartment with a low ceiling, in which there was on the mantelpiece a large bunch of coral spread out against the looking-glass.","zh":"天气一冷，爱玛就离开原来的卧室，住到楼下厅房：一间长屋，天花板低低的，壁炉镜子前面，有一盆多枝珊瑚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Seated in her arm chair near the window, she could see the villagers pass along the pavement.","zh":"她坐在窗边扶手椅里，看镇上的人从人行道走过。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Twice a day Léon went from his office to the Lion d’Or. Emma could hear him coming from afar; she leant forward listening, and the young man glided past the curtain, always dressed in the same way, and without turning his head. But in the twilight, when, her chin resting on her left hand, she let the embroidery she had begun fall on her knees, she often shuddered at the apparition of this shadow suddenly gliding past. She would get up and order the table to be laid.","sentences":[{"en":"Twice a day Léon went from his office to the Lion d’Or.","zh":"赖昂每天两趟，从事务所走到金狮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma could hear him coming from afar; she leant forward listening, and the young man glided past the curtain, always dressed in the same way, and without turning his head.","zh":"爱玛远远听见他来，斜过身子听脚步响；年轻人老是那么一身衣裳，在窗帘外，头也不回，溜了过去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But in the twilight, when, her chin resting on her left hand, she let the embroidery she had begun fall on her knees, she often shuddered at the apparition of this shadow suddenly gliding past.","zh":"爱玛远远听见他来，斜过身子听脚步响；年轻人老是那么一身衣裳，在窗帘外，头也不回，溜了过去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She would get up and order the table to be laid.","zh":"爱玛远远听见他来，斜过身子听脚步响；年轻人老是那么一身衣裳，在窗帘外，头也不回，溜了过去。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Homais called at dinner-time. Skull-cap in hand, he came in on tiptoe, in order to disturb no one, always repeating the same phrase, “Good evening, everybody.” Then, when he had taken his seat at the table between the pair, he asked the doctor about his patients, and the latter consulted his as to the probability of their payment. Next they talked of “what was in the paper.”","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Homais called at dinner-time.","zh":"傍晚，开了头的彩绣，她丢在膝盖上，左手支起下巴，正在出神，看见这个影子突然溜开，常常心里一紧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Skull-cap in hand, he came in on tiptoe, in order to disturb no one, always repeating the same phrase, “Good evening, everybody.”","zh":"傍晚，开了头的彩绣，她丢在膝盖上，左手支起下巴，正在出神，看见这个影子突然溜开，常常心里一紧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, when he had taken his seat at the table between the pair, he asked the doctor about his patients, and the latter consulted his as to the probability of their payment.","zh":"傍晚，开了头的彩绣，她丢在膝盖上，左手支起下巴，正在出神，看见这个影子突然溜开，常常心里一紧。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Next they talked of “what was in the paper.”","zh":"她站起来，吩咐开饭。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais by this hour knew it almost by heart, and he repeated it from end to end, with the reflections of the penny-a-liners, and all the stories of individual catastrophes that had occurred in France or abroad. But the subject becoming exhausted, he was not slow in throwing out some remarks on the dishes before him.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais by this hour knew it almost by heart, and he repeated it from end to end, with the reflections of the penny-a-liners, and all the stories of individual catastrophes that had occurred in France or abroad.","zh":"正吃晚饭，郝麦先生来了。他怕吵了他们，蹑着脚步进来，手里拿着希腊小帽，永远重复这句话：“各位晚安！”然后他挨近桌子，在他们夫妇之间的老位子一坐，向医生问起病人的消息，同时医生向他请教，诊费该多该少。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the subject becoming exhausted, he was not slow in throwing out some remarks on the dishes before him.","zh":"他们接下来就谈报纸上的新闻。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Sometimes even, half-rising, he delicately pointed out to madame the tenderest morsel, or turning to the servant, gave her some advice on the manipulation of stews and the hygiene of seasoning.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes even, half-rising, he delicately pointed out to madame the tenderest morsel, or turning to the servant, gave her some advice on the manipulation of stews and the hygiene of seasoning.","zh":"郝麦整天看报，赶到掌灯时分，差不多把新闻背也背下来了，讲起来有头有尾，一直讲到记者的议论、国内外个别人士的灾难，说到无可再说，就立时调转话头，谈论眼前的菜肴。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He talked aroma, osmazome, juices, and gelatine in a bewildering manner. Moreover, Homais, with his head fuller of recipes than his shop of jars, excelled in making all kinds of preserves, vinegars, and sweet liqueurs; he knew also all the latest inventions in economic stoves, together with the art of preserving cheese and of curing sick wines.","sentences":[{"en":"He talked aroma, osmazome, juices, and gelatine in a bewildering manner.","zh":"他有时甚至体贴入微，探起身子，给夫人指出最嫩的一块肉，要不然就转向女用人，教她烧菜的规程与合乎卫生的调味方法；他说起香料、味精、肉汁和胶质一类东西，头头是道。而且郝麦满脑方子，比他药房里的瓶子还多，他擅长酿造各色蜜饯、醋和香油，也知道种种新出的省煤的锅釜和保存干酪、料理坏酒的方法。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Moreover, Homais, with his head fuller of recipes than his shop of jars, excelled in making all kinds of preserves, vinegars, and sweet liqueurs; he knew also all the latest inventions in economic stoves, together with the art of preserving cheese and of curing sick wines.","zh":"他有时甚至体贴入微，探起身子，给夫人指出最嫩的一块肉，要不然就转向女用人，教她烧菜的规程与合乎卫生的调味方法；他说起香料、味精、肉汁和胶质一类东西，头头是道。而且郝麦满脑方子，比他药房里的瓶子还多，他擅长酿造各色蜜饯、醋和香油，也知道种种新出的省煤的锅釜和保存干酪、料理坏酒的方法。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At eight o’clock Justin came to fetch him to shut up the shop.","sentences":[{"en":"At eight o’clock Justin came to fetch him to shut up the shop.","zh":"一到八点，朱斯丹就来找他回去上门。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Monsieur Homais gave him a sly look, especially if Félicité was there, for he half noticed that his apprentice was fond of the doctor’s house.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Monsieur Homais gave him a sly look, especially if Félicité was there, for he half noticed that his apprentice was fond of the doctor’s house.","zh":"郝麦看出他的学徒好来医生家，所以显出嘲弄的眼神望他，特别是碰巧全福也在的时候。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The young dog,” he said, “is beginning to have ideas, and the devil take me if I don’t believe he’s in love with your servant!”","sentences":[{"en":"“The young dog,” he said, “is beginning to have ideas, and the devil take me if I don’t believe he’s in love with your servant!”","zh":"“我这小伙子，开始懂事啦，我敢说，他爱上了你们的丫头，不是才怪！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But a more serious fault with which he reproached Justin was his constantly listening to conversation. On Sunday, for example, one could not get him out of the drawing-room, whither Madame Homais had called him to fetch the children, who were falling asleep in the arm-chairs, and dragging down with their backs calico chair-covers that were too large.","sentences":[{"en":"But a more serious fault with which he reproached Justin was his constantly listening to conversation.","zh":"但是他责备他的，还有一个更大的过失，就是：老待下来听人谈话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On Sunday, for example, one could not get him out of the drawing-room, whither Madame Homais had called him to fetch the children, who were falling asleep in the arm-chairs, and dragging down with their backs calico chair-covers that were too large.","zh":"譬如说，星期天，在郝麦家的晚会上，孩子们在扶手椅里睡着了，椅子布套太宽，让后背拖得歪歪拧拧的，郝麦夫人把他叫了来，要他抱走，他愣在客厅，就没有办法让他离开。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Not many people came to these soirees at the chemist’s, his scandal-mongering and political opinions having successfully alienated various respectable persons from him. The clerk never failed to be there. As soon as he heard the bell he ran to meet Madame Bovary, took her shawl, and put away under the shop-counter the thick list shoes that she wore over her boots when there was snow.","sentences":[{"en":"Not many people came to these soirees at the chemist’s, his scandal-mongering and political opinions having successfully alienated various respectable persons from him.","zh":"药剂师这些晚会，没有多少人参加，士绅怕听他的闲言闲语和他的政治见解，陆陆续续，也就避而不来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The clerk never failed to be there.","zh":"但是文书绝不错过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As soon as he heard the bell he ran to meet Madame Bovary, took her shawl, and put away under the shop-counter the thick list shoes that she wore over her boots when there was snow.","zh":"他一听门铃响，就跑去迎接包法利夫人，接过她的披肩；碰到下雪，她在鞋上套一双布条大拖鞋，他也接过来，放在药房书桌底下。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"First they played some hands at trente-et-un; next Monsieur Homais played ecarte with Emma; Léon behind her gave her advice.","sentences":[{"en":"First they played some hands at trente-et-un; next Monsieur Homais played ecarte with Emma; Léon behind her gave her advice.","zh":"他一听门铃响，就跑去迎接包法利夫人，接过她的披肩；碰到下雪，她在鞋上套一双布条大拖鞋，他也接过来，放在药房书桌底下。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Standing up with his hands on the back of her chair he saw the teeth of her comb that bit into her chignon. With every movement that she made to throw her cards the right side of her dress was drawn up. From her turned-up hair a dark colour fell over her back, and growing gradually paler, lost itself little by little in the shade. Then her dress fell on both sides of her chair, puffing out full of folds, and reached the ground. When Léon occasionally felt the sole of his boot resting on it, he drew back as if he had trodden upon some one.","sentences":[{"en":"Standing up with his hands on the back of her chair he saw the teeth of her comb that bit into her chignon.","zh":"大家先玩几盘“三十一点”，接着郝麦先生就和爱玛玩“换牌”， 赖昂站在背后，帮她指点，手搭在椅背上，看着她插在发髻上的梳子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"With every movement that she made to throw her cards the right side of her dress was drawn up.","zh":"大家先玩几盘“三十一点”，接着郝麦先生就和爱玛玩“换牌”， 赖昂站在背后，帮她指点，手搭在椅背上，看着她插在发髻上的梳子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"From her turned-up hair a dark colour fell over her back, and growing gradually paler, lost itself little by little in the shade.","zh":"她每回出牌，右边袍子就往高里耸。头发向上卷，后背映成一片棕色，越来越淡，逐渐没入黑影。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then her dress fell on both sides of her chair, puffing out full of folds, and reached the ground.","zh":"她出过牌，往回一坐，衣服蓬蓬松松，全是褶子，搭在椅子两旁，垂到地上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When Léon occasionally felt the sole of his boot resting on it, he drew back as if he had trodden upon some one.","zh":"赖昂有时候觉出他的靴底踩到上头，连忙挪开，好像踩了人一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When the game of cards was over, the druggist and the Doctor played dominoes, and Emma, changing her place, leant her elbow on the table, turning over the leaves of “L’Illustration”. She had brought her ladies’ journal with her. Léon sat down near her; they looked at the engravings together, and waited for one another at the bottom of the pages. She often begged him to read her the verses; Léon declaimed them in a languid voice, to which he carefully gave a dying fall in the love passages. But the noise of the dominoes annoyed him. Monsieur Homais was strong at the game; he could beat Charles and give him a double-six. Then the three hundred finished, they both stretched themselves out in front of the fire, and were soon asleep. The fire was dying out in the cinders; the teapot was empty, Léon was still reading.","sentences":[{"en":"When the game of cards was over, the druggist and the Doctor played dominoes, and Emma, changing her place, leant her elbow on the table, turning over the leaves of “L’Illustration”.","zh":"斗过扑克，药剂师就和医生玩牙牌，爱玛换了座位，胳膊支着桌子，翻看《画报》 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had brought her ladies’ journal with her.","zh":"时装杂志是她带来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Léon sat down near her; they looked at the engravings together, and waited for one another at the bottom of the pages.","zh":"赖昂坐在旁边，和她一道看图，谁先看完，谁就等另一个人看完了再往下翻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She often begged him to read her the verses; Léon declaimed them in a languid voice, to which he carefully gave a dying fall in the love passages.","zh":"她一来就求他读几首诗给她听；赖昂拉长声音朗诵，念到爱情段落，用心煞尾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the noise of the dominoes annoyed him.","zh":"但是牙牌的声音吵他；郝麦先生是个中能手，查理输得一塌糊涂。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Homais was strong at the game; he could beat Charles and give him a double-six.","zh":"但是牙牌的声音吵他；郝麦先生是个中能手，查理输得一塌糊涂。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then the three hundred finished, they both stretched themselves out in front of the fire, and were soon asleep.","zh":"他们打满三个一百分，两个人全在壁炉前，伸直身子，很快也就睡着了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The fire was dying out in the cinders; the teapot was empty, Léon was still reading.","zh":"火灭了，茶壶空了，赖昂还在念。爱玛一边听他念，一边心不在焉，随手转动灯罩；纱罩上面，画了几个乘车的皮埃罗 和拿着平衡棒的走索姑娘。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma listened to him, mechanically turning around the lampshade, on the gauze of which were painted clowns in carriages, and tight-rope dances with their balancing-poles. Léon stopped, pointing with a gesture to his sleeping audience; then they talked in low tones, and their conversation seemed the more sweet to them because it was unheard.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma listened to him, mechanically turning around the lampshade, on the gauze of which were painted clowns in carriages, and tight-rope dances with their balancing-poles.","zh":"火灭了，茶壶空了，赖昂还在念。爱玛一边听他念，一边心不在焉，随手转动灯罩；纱罩上面，画了几个乘车的皮埃罗 和拿着平衡棒的走索姑娘。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Léon stopped, pointing with a gesture to his sleeping audience; then they talked in low tones, and their conversation seemed the more sweet to them because it was unheard.","zh":"赖昂住口不念，指着他的睡熟了的听众。于是他们低声说话，因为没有别人听，觉得谈话分外甜蜜。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Thus a kind of bond was established between them, a constant commerce of books and of romances. Monsieur Bovary, little given to jealousy, did not trouble himself about it.","sentences":[{"en":"Thus a kind of bond was established between them, a constant commerce of books and of romances.","zh":"他们之间，就这样建立了一种默契，不断交换书籍和歌曲；包法利先生难得忌妒，并不引以为怪。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Bovary, little given to jealousy, did not trouble himself about it.","zh":"他们之间，就这样建立了一种默契，不断交换书籍和歌曲；包法利先生难得忌妒，并不引以为怪。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"On his birthday he received a beautiful phrenological head, all marked with figures to the thorax and painted blue. This was an attention of the clerk’s. He showed him many others, even to doing errands for him at Rouen; and the book of a novelist having made the mania for cactuses fashionable, Léon bought some for Madame Bovary, bringing them back on his knees in the “Hirondelle,” pricking his fingers on their hard hairs.","sentences":[{"en":"On his birthday he received a beautiful phrenological head, all marked with figures to the thorax and painted blue.","zh":"生日那天，他收到一颗骨相学的漂亮人头，涂成蓝颜色，上上下下，写遍数字，连胸口也有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This was an attention of the clerk’s.","zh":"这是文书送的一份厚礼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He showed him many others, even to doing errands for him at Rouen; and the book of a novelist having made the mania for cactuses fashionable, Léon bought some for Madame Bovary, bringing them back on his knees in the “Hirondelle,” pricking his fingers on their hard hairs.","zh":"盛情不止于此，他甚至替医生到鲁昂买东西。有一部小说，引起爱好仙人掌科植物的风气，赖昂买了一盆，送医生太太，坐在燕子里面，捧在膝盖上，硬刺扎破他的手指。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She had a board with a balustrade fixed against her window to hold the pots. The clerk, too, had his small hanging garden; they saw each other tending their flowers at their windows.","sentences":[{"en":"She had a board with a balustrade fixed against her window to hold the pots.","zh":"她靠窗装了一个有栏杆的小木架，放她的小花盆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The clerk, too, had his small hanging garden; they saw each other tending their flowers at their windows.","zh":"文书也安了一个悬空的小花圃；他们彼此望见在窗口养花。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Of the windows of the village there was one yet more often occupied; for on Sundays from morning to night, and every morning when the weather was bright, one could see at the dormer-window of the garret the profile of Monsieur Binet bending over his lathe, whose monotonous humming could be heard at the Lion d’Or.","sentences":[{"en":"Of the windows of the village there was one yet more often occupied; for on Sundays from morning to night, and every morning when the weather was bright, one could see at the dormer-window of the garret the profile of Monsieur Binet bending over his lathe, whose monotonous humming could be heard at the Lion d’Or.","zh":"镇上有一扇窗户，望过去分外透着忙碌。如果天气晴和，每天下午，星期日甚至于从早到晚，就见一家阁楼的天窗，露出毕耐先生半张瘦脸，身子俯向他的旋床。旋床单调的响声，就连金狮那边也听得见。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One evening on coming home Léon found in his room a rug in velvet and wool with leaves on a pale ground. He called Madame Homais, Monsieur Homais, Justin, the children, the cook; he spoke of it to his chief; every one wanted to see this rug. Why did the doctor’s wife give the clerk presents? It looked queer. They decided that she must be his lover.","sentences":[{"en":"One evening on coming home Léon found in his room a rug in velvet and wool with leaves on a pale ground.","zh":"一天黄昏，赖昂回来，发现屋里有一条呢绒毯子，白底，树叶图案。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He called Madame Homais, Monsieur Homais, Justin, the children, the cook; he spoke of it to his chief; every one wanted to see this rug.","zh":"他喊郝麦太太、郝麦先生、朱斯丹、小孩子、女厨子；他告诉他的老板；人人想见识见识这条毯子；医生太太为什么送文书礼物？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Why did the doctor’s wife give the clerk presents?","zh":"他喊郝麦太太、郝麦先生、朱斯丹、小孩子、女厨子；他告诉他的老板；人人想见识见识这条毯子；医生太太为什么送文书礼物？","scope":"group"},{"en":"It looked queer.","zh":"未免出奇；大家断定她是他的相好。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They decided that she must be his lover.","zh":"未免出奇；大家断定她是他的相好。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He made this seem likely, so ceaselessly did he talk of her charms and of her wit; so much so, that Binet once roughly answered him—","sentences":[{"en":"He made this seem likely, so ceaselessly did he talk of her charms and of her wit; so much so, that Binet once roughly answered him—","zh":"也不由人不相信。他不住口夸她美貌多才，夸到后来，毕耐有一回老实不客气回他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What does it matter to me since I’m not in her set?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What does it matter to me since I’m not in her set?”","zh":"“关我什么事，我同她又没有来往！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He tortured himself to find out how he could make his declaration to her, and always halting between the fear of displeasing her and the shame of being such a coward, he wept with discouragement and desire. Then he took energetic resolutions, wrote letters that he tore up, put it off to times that he again deferred.","sentences":[{"en":"He tortured himself to find out how he could make his declaration to her, and always halting between the fear of displeasing her and the shame of being such a coward, he wept with discouragement and desire.","zh":"他绞尽脑汁，寻思对她表白心事的方法；他一方面怕她不高兴，一方面惭愧自己懦弱，瞻前顾后，永远迟疑不前，又是胆怯，又是相思，简直哭也要哭出来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he took energetic resolutions, wrote letters that he tore up, put it off to times that he again deferred.","zh":"他后来横了心，拿定主意，可是信写了，他又撕掉，时间确定了，他又延宕。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Often he set out with the determination to dare all; but this resolution soon deserted him in Emma’s presence, and when Charles, dropping in, invited him to jump into his chaise to go with him to see some patient in the neighbourhood, he at once accepted, bowed to madame, and went out. Her husband, was he not something belonging to her? As to Emma, she did not ask herself whether she loved. Love, she thought, must come suddenly, with great outbursts and lightnings—a hurricane of the skies, which falls upon life, revolutionises it, roots up the will like a leaf, and sweeps the whole heart into the abyss. She did not know that on the terrace of houses it makes lakes when the pipes are choked, and she would thus have remained in her security when she suddenly discovered a rent in the wall of it.","sentences":[{"en":"Often he set out with the determination to dare all; but this resolution soon deserted him in Emma’s presence, and when Charles, dropping in, invited him to jump into his chaise to go with him to see some patient in the neighbourhood, he at once accepted, bowed to madame, and went out.","zh":"他常常迈步向前，跃跃欲试，然而来到爱玛面前，这种决心很快就烟消云散，不知去向。查理蓦地出现，邀他坐上他的包克，一同到附近看看病人，他满口应承，向女主人一鞠躬，也就去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her husband, was he not something belonging to her?","zh":"她的丈夫，不也几乎等于她了吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to Emma, she did not ask herself whether she loved.","zh":"至于爱玛，她并不希望知道她是否爱他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Love, she thought, must come suddenly, with great outbursts and lightnings—a hurricane of the skies, which falls upon life, revolutionises it, roots up the will like a leaf, and sweeps the whole heart into the abyss.","zh":"她以为爱情应当骤然来临，电光闪闪，雷声隆隆，仿佛九霄云外的狂飙，吹过人世，颠覆生命，席卷意志，如同席卷落叶一般，把心整个带往深渊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She did not know that on the terrace of houses it makes lakes when the pipes are choked, and she would thus have remained in her security when she suddenly discovered a rent in the wall of it.","zh":"她不晓得，承溜堵塞，淫雨可以把房顶的平台变成湖泊。她这样住下去，自以为安全无事，不料事出意外，忽然发现墙上有了一条裂缝。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-5","part":2,"n":5,"title":"Part II · Chapter 5","titleZh":"中卷 · 5","paragraphs":[{"en":"It was a Sunday in February, an afternoon when the snow was falling.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a Sunday in February, an afternoon when the snow was falling.","zh":"二月，星期日，一个落雪的下午，包法利夫妇、郝麦和赖昂先生，全到离永镇半古里远的盆地，参观一家新建的麻纺厂。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"They had all, Monsieur and Madame Bovary, Homais, and Monsieur Léon, gone to see a yarn-mill that was being built in the valley a mile and a half from Yonville. The druggist had taken Napoleon and Athalie to give them some exercise, and Justin accompanied them, carrying the umbrellas on his shoulder.","sentences":[{"en":"They had all, Monsieur and Madame Bovary, Homais, and Monsieur Léon, gone to see a yarn-mill that was being built in the valley a mile and a half from Yonville.","zh":"二月，星期日，一个落雪的下午，包法利夫妇、郝麦和赖昂先生，全到离永镇半古里远的盆地，参观一家新建的麻纺厂。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The druggist had taken Napoleon and Athalie to give them some exercise, and Justin accompanied them, carrying the umbrellas on his shoulder.","zh":"药剂师要拿破仑和阿塔莉活动活动，也带了去，朱斯丹照管他们，肩头扛着雨伞。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Nothing, however, could be less curious than this curiosity. A great piece of waste ground, on which pell-mell, amid a mass of sand and stones, were a few break-wheels, already rusty, surrounded by a quadrangular building pierced by a number of little windows. The building was unfinished; the sky could be seen through the joists of the roofing. Attached to the stop-plank of the gable a bunch of straw mixed with corn-ears fluttered its tricoloured ribbons in the wind.","sentences":[{"en":"Nothing, however, could be less curious than this curiosity.","zh":"其实，他们要看的地方，根本不值得一看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A great piece of waste ground, on which pell-mell, amid a mass of sand and stones, were a few break-wheels, already rusty, surrounded by a quadrangular building pierced by a number of little windows.","zh":"一大片空地，乱七八糟，东一堆沙，西一堆石子，旁边撂着几个已经长锈的齿轮，当中一座长方形建筑，开着许多小窗，还没有盖好，隔着房椽，望见了天。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The building was unfinished; the sky could be seen through the joists of the roofing.","zh":"一大片空地，乱七八糟，东一堆沙，西一堆石子，旁边撂着几个已经长锈的齿轮，当中一座长方形建筑，开着许多小窗，还没有盖好，隔着房椽，望见了天。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Attached to the stop-plank of the gable a bunch of straw mixed with corn-ears fluttered its tricoloured ribbons in the wind.","zh":"山墙小梁绑着一捆掺杂麦穗的秸秆，尖头三色带子，迎风招展，呼呼直响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais was talking. He explained to the company the future importance of this establishment, computed the strength of the floorings, the thickness of the walls, and regretted extremely not having a yard-stick such as Monsieur Binet possessed for his own special use.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais was talking.","zh":"郝麦高谈阔论，向同伴解释这家厂房的重要性，计算地板的力量，墙壁的厚度，连声后悔没有带一管尺来，毕耐先生就有一管，供本人不时之需。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He explained to the company the future importance of this establishment, computed the strength of the floorings, the thickness of the walls, and regretted extremely not having a yard-stick such as Monsieur Binet possessed for his own special use.","zh":"郝麦高谈阔论，向同伴解释这家厂房的重要性，计算地板的力量，墙壁的厚度，连声后悔没有带一管尺来，毕耐先生就有一管，供本人不时之需。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma, who had taken his arm, bent lightly against his shoulder, and she looked at the sun’s disc shedding afar through the mist his pale splendour. She turned. Charles was there. His cap was drawn down over his eyebrows, and his two thick lips were trembling, which added a look of stupidity to his face; his very back, his calm back, was irritating to behold, and she saw written upon his coat all the platitude of the bearer.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, who had taken his arm, bent lightly against his shoulder, and she looked at the sun’s disc shedding afar through the mist his pale splendour.","zh":"爱玛挎住他的胳膊，微微靠着他的肩膀，遥望圆圆的太阳在雾里射出耀眼的白光；但是她一转脸，就看见了查理。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She turned.","zh":"爱玛挎住他的胳膊，微微靠着他的肩膀，遥望圆圆的太阳在雾里射出耀眼的白光；但是她一转脸，就看见了查理。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles was there.","zh":"爱玛挎住他的胳膊，微微靠着他的肩膀，遥望圆圆的太阳在雾里射出耀眼的白光；但是她一转脸，就看见了查理。","scope":"group"},{"en":"His cap was drawn down over his eyebrows, and his two thick lips were trembling, which added a look of stupidity to his face; his very back, his calm back, was irritating to behold, and she saw written upon his coat all the platitude of the bearer.","zh":"他的便帽低低盖住眉；上下厚嘴唇微微颤抖，脸格外显得蠢；就连他的背，他安详的背，也不顺眼；他穿的大衣亦如其人，俗不可耐。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"While she was considering him thus, tasting in her irritation a sort of depraved pleasure, Léon made a step forward. The cold that made him pale seemed to add a more gentle languor to his face; between his cravat and his neck the somewhat loose collar of his shirt showed the skin; the lobe of his ear looked out from beneath a lock of hair, and his large blue eyes, raised to the clouds, seemed to Emma more limpid and more beautiful than those mountain-lakes where the heavens are mirrored.","sentences":[{"en":"While she was considering him thus, tasting in her irritation a sort of depraved pleasure, Léon made a step forward.","zh":"她这样打量他，觉得有气，可是心头也起了一种变质的快感，赖昂这期间正好迈前一步。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The cold that made him pale seemed to add a more gentle languor to his face; between his cravat and his neck the somewhat loose collar of his shirt showed the skin; the lobe of his ear looked out from beneath a lock of hair, and his large blue eyes, raised to the clouds, seemed to Emma more limpid and more beautiful than those mountain-lakes where the heavens are mirrored.","zh":"由于天冷，他的脸变白了，似乎也更显得少气无力，温柔动人。衬衫领子有一点点松，在领带和颈项中间，露出皮肉；一绺头发盖住耳朵，耳朵尖露在外头，同时他的大蓝眼睛，望着浮云，爱玛觉得比起那些群山环绕、映照天日的湖泊，还要清，还要美。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Wretched boy!” suddenly cried the chemist.","sentences":[{"en":"“Wretched boy!” suddenly cried the chemist.","zh":"药剂师忽然喊了起来：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he ran to his son, who had just precipitated himself into a heap of lime in order to whiten his boots. At the reproaches with which he was being overwhelmed Napoleon began to roar, while Justin dried his shoes with a wisp of straw. But a knife was wanted; Charles offered his.","sentences":[{"en":"And he ran to his son, who had just precipitated himself into a heap of lime in order to whiten his boots.","zh":"“坏东西！”他的儿子正跳到石灰堆，打算把鞋抹白。他跑过去责备，拿破仑嚎叫起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the reproaches with which he was being overwhelmed Napoleon began to roar, while Justin dried his shoes with a wisp of straw.","zh":"朱斯丹找了一把麦秸帮他擦鞋，不过还需要一把小刀；查理掏出小刀，借给他用。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But a knife was wanted; Charles offered his.","zh":"朱斯丹找了一把麦秸帮他擦鞋，不过还需要一把小刀；查理掏出小刀，借给他用。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ah!” she said to herself, “he carried a knife in his pocket like a peasant.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!” she said to herself, “he carried a knife in his pocket like a peasant.”","zh":"她想：“啊！他像庄稼汉一样，衣服口袋里搁一把小刀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The hoar-frost was falling, and they turned back to Yonville.","sentences":[{"en":"The hoar-frost was falling, and they turned back to Yonville.","zh":"下霜了，他们走回永镇。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the evening Madame Bovary did not go to her neighbour’s, and when Charles had left and she felt herself alone, the comparison re-began with the clearness of a sensation almost actual, and with that lengthening of perspective which memory gives to things. Looking from her bed at the clean fire that was burning, she still saw, as she had down there, Léon standing up with one hand behind his cane, and with the other holding Athalie, who was quietly sucking a piece of ice. She thought him charming; she could not tear herself away from him; she recalled his other attitudes on other days, the words he had spoken, the sound of his voice, his whole person; and she repeated, pouting out her lips as if for a kiss—","sentences":[{"en":"In the evening Madame Bovary did not go to her neighbour’s, and when Charles had left and she felt herself alone, the comparison re-began with the clearness of a sensation almost actual, and with that lengthening of perspective which memory gives to things.","zh":"当天晚上，包法利夫人没有去邻居家，查理自去了。她觉得只剩她一个人，对比又在心头涌起，固然是一转眼的事，还历历在目；可到底是回忆，中间又隔着一段距离。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Looking from her bed at the clean fire that was burning, she still saw, as she had down there, Léon standing up with one hand behind his cane, and with the other holding Athalie, who was quietly sucking a piece of ice.","zh":"她躺在床上，望着明亮的旺火，就像还在那边一样，看见赖昂站着，一只手弄弯他的细手杖，另一只手领着阿塔莉。阿塔莉安安静静，咂一块冰。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She thought him charming; she could not tear herself away from him; she recalled his other attitudes on other days, the words he had spoken, the sound of his voice, his whole person; and she repeated, pouting out her lips as if for a kiss—","zh":"她觉得他可爱，就连不想也不成；她记起他在别的日子别的姿态、他说过的话、他说话的声音、他的一切，于是嘴唇向前，好像接吻一样，她重复道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, charming! charming! Is he not in love?” she asked herself; “but with whom? With me?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, charming! charming!","zh":"“是啊，可爱！可爱！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is he not in love?” she asked herself; “but with whom?","zh":"她问自己道：“他有心爱的人吗？是谁？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With me?”","zh":"是我呀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"All the proofs arose before her at once; her heart leapt. The flame of the fire threw a joyous light upon the ceiling; she turned on her back, stretching out her arms.","sentences":[{"en":"All the proofs arose before her at once; her heart leapt.","zh":"全部证据同时摊开，她心跳了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The flame of the fire threw a joyous light upon the ceiling; she turned on her back, stretching out her arms.","zh":"壁炉的火焰放出一道亮光，欢欢腾腾，在天花板上摇晃。她背转身子，伸出胳膊。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then began the eternal lamentation: “Oh, if Heaven had not willed it! And why not? What prevented it?”","sentences":[{"en":"Then began the eternal lamentation: “Oh, if Heaven had not willed it!","zh":"于是无终无了的哀怨开始了：“唉！只要天从人愿，也就好了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And why not?","zh":"凭什么不？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What prevented it?”","zh":"谁拦着了？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When Charles came home at midnight, she seemed to have just awakened, and as he made a noise undressing, she complained of a headache, then asked carelessly what had happened that evening.","sentences":[{"en":"When Charles came home at midnight, she seemed to have just awakened, and as he made a noise undressing, she complained of a headache, then asked carelessly what had happened that evening.","zh":"查理半夜回来，她装出才醒的模样，他脱衣服起了响声，她诉说头疼，然后随随便便，打听晚会的情形。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Monsieur Léon,” he said, “went to his room early.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Monsieur Léon,” he said, “went to his room early.”","zh":"“赖昂先生老早就上楼了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She could not help smiling, and she fell asleep, her soul filled with a new delight.","sentences":[{"en":"She could not help smiling, and she fell asleep, her soul filled with a new delight.","zh":"她不禁有了笑意，于是灵魂充满新的喜悦，她沉沉入睡了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day, at dusk, she received a visit from Monsieur Lheureux, the draper. He was a man of ability, was this shopkeeper. Born a Gascon but bred a Norman, he grafted upon his southern volubility the cunning of the Cauchois. His fat, flabby, beardless face seemed dyed by a decoction of liquorice, and his white hair made even more vivid the keen brilliance of his small black eyes. No one knew what he had been formerly; a pedlar said some, a banker at Routot according to others. What was certain was that he made complex calculations in his head that would have frightened Binet himself. Polite to obsequiousness, he always held himself with his back bent in the position of one who bows or who invites.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day, at dusk, she received a visit from Monsieur Lheureux, the draper.","zh":"第二天傍晚，时装商人勒乐看她来了。这位掌柜精明强干，是个做生意的能手。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was a man of ability, was this shopkeeper.","zh":"第二天傍晚，时装商人勒乐看她来了。这位掌柜精明强干，是个做生意的能手。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Born a Gascon but bred a Norman, he grafted upon his southern volubility the cunning of the Cauchois.","zh":"他生在南方加斯科涅，本来就爱说话，之后在诺曼底定居，又添上科地的狡黠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His fat, flabby, beardless face seemed dyed by a decoction of liquorice, and his white hair made even more vivid the keen brilliance of his small black eyes.","zh":"虚虚的胖脸，不留胡须，仿佛抹了一层薄薄的甘草汁；一双贼亮的小黑眼睛，衬上白头发，越发显得灵活。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No one knew what he had been formerly; a pedlar said some, a banker at Routot according to others.","zh":"人们不清楚他的来历，有人说是背包贩子，又有人说是鲁托 开钱庄的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was certain was that he made complex calculations in his head that would have frightened Binet himself.","zh":"确切的是，他工于心计，就连毕耐也怕。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Polite to obsequiousness, he always held himself with his back bent in the position of one who bows or who invites.","zh":"他礼貌，胁肩谄笑，腰一直哈着，姿势又像鞠躬，又像邀请。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After leaving at the door his hat surrounded with crape, he put down a green bandbox on the table, and began by complaining to madame, with many civilities, that he should have remained till that day without gaining her confidence. A poor shop like his was not made to attract a “fashionable lady”; he emphasized the words; yet she had only to command, and he would undertake to provide her with anything she might wish, either in haberdashery or linen, millinery or fancy goods, for he went to town regularly four times a month. He was connected with the best houses. You could speak of him at the “Trois Freres,” at the “Barbe d’Or,” or at the “Grand Sauvage”; all these gentlemen knew him as well as the insides of their pockets. To-day, then he had come to show madame, in passing, various articles he happened to have, thanks to the most rare opportunity. And he pulled out half-a-dozen embroidered collars from the box.","sentences":[{"en":"After leaving at the door his hat surrounded with crape, he put down a green bandbox on the table, and began by complaining to madame, with many civilities, that he should have remained till that day without gaining her confidence.","zh":"他把镶一道绉纱的毡帽留在门厅，然后走进屋来，往桌子上放下一个绿色硬纸匣，满嘴客套话，一开口就表示遗憾，说他直到现在，还没有承蒙太太赏光，像他开的那种小铺，吸引风雅妇女（他加重口气），本来不配。其实只要太太吩咐一声，他会尽心尽意，供应她的需要，不管是针线、衬衣、帽子或者新衣料，全有办法，因为他每月规定进城四趟。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A poor shop like his was not made to attract a “fashionable lady”; he emphasized the words; yet she had only to command, and he would undertake to provide her with anything she might wish, either in haberdashery or linen, millinery or fancy goods, for he went to town regularly four times a month.","zh":"他把镶一道绉纱的毡帽留在门厅，然后走进屋来，往桌子上放下一个绿色硬纸匣，满嘴客套话，一开口就表示遗憾，说他直到现在，还没有承蒙太太赏光，像他开的那种小铺，吸引风雅妇女（他加重口气），本来不配。其实只要太太吩咐一声，他会尽心尽意，供应她的需要，不管是针线、衬衣、帽子或者新衣料，全有办法，因为他每月规定进城四趟。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was connected with the best houses.","zh":"他和最大的行庄有联系。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You could speak of him at the “Trois Freres,” at the “Barbe d’Or,” or at the “Grand Sauvage”; all these gentlemen knew him as well as the insides of their pockets.","zh":"在三兄弟、金胡须或者大野人那边，提起他来，家家掌柜晓得，就像他们口袋里的东西一样熟！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To-day, then he had come to show madame, in passing, various articles he happened to have, thanks to the most rare opportunity.","zh":"所以他今天顺便给太太看几样货色，机会难得，凑巧他有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he pulled out half-a-dozen embroidered collars from the box.","zh":"说着说着，他从纸匣取出半打绣花领子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary examined them. “I do not require anything,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary examined them.","zh":"包法利夫人看了看，说：“我都用不着。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I do not require anything,” she said.","zh":"包法利夫人看了看，说：“我都用不着。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then Monsieur Lheureux delicately exhibited three Algerian scarves, several packets of English needles, a pair of straw slippers, and finally, four eggcups in cocoanut wood, carved in open work by convicts. Then, with both hands on the table, his neck stretched out, his figure bent forward, open-mouthed, he watched Emma’s look, who was walking up and down undecided amid these goods. From time to time, as if to remove some dust, he filliped with his nail the silk of the scarves spread out at full length, and they rustled with a little noise, making in the green twilight the gold spangles of their tissue scintillate like little stars.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Monsieur Lheureux delicately exhibited three Algerian scarves, several packets of English needles, a pair of straw slippers, and finally, four eggcups in cocoanut wood, carved in open work by convicts.","zh":"勒乐先生听了这话，小心在意，取出三条阿尔及利亚围巾 、几包英吉利针、一双草拖鞋，最后，四只由囚犯精镂细雕的吃蛋用的椰子小杯，然后他张开嘴，两只手搭在桌面，伸长脖子，身子向前，随着爱玛犹疑不决的视线，浏览这些货物。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, with both hands on the table, his neck stretched out, his figure bent forward, open-mouthed, he watched Emma’s look, who was walking up and down undecided amid these goods.","zh":"勒乐先生听了这话，小心在意，取出三条阿尔及利亚围巾 、几包英吉利针、一双草拖鞋，最后，四只由囚犯精镂细雕的吃蛋用的椰子小杯，然后他张开嘴，两只手搭在桌面，伸长脖子，身子向前，随着爱玛犹疑不决的视线，浏览这些货物。","scope":"group"},{"en":"From time to time, as if to remove some dust, he filliped with his nail the silk of the scarves spread out at full length, and they rustled with a little noise, making in the green twilight the gold spangles of their tissue scintillate like little stars.","zh":"围巾长长的，整个摊开，他似乎为了掸掉浮尘，不时拿指甲弹一下缎面，于是围巾窸窸窣窣，映着黄昏发绿的亮光，微微一动，就见上面的金点子，仿佛一颗一颗小星星，闪闪烁烁。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How much are they?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How much are they?”","zh":"“卖多少钱？”他回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“A mere nothing,” he replied, “a mere nothing. But there’s no hurry; whenever it’s convenient. We are not Jews.”","sentences":[{"en":"“A mere nothing,” he replied, “a mere nothing.","zh":"“没有几个钱，没有几个钱；也不必急着就给，随您方便；我们不是犹太人！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"But there’s no hurry; whenever it’s convenient.","zh":"“没有几个钱，没有几个钱；也不必急着就给，随您方便；我们不是犹太人！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"We are not Jews.”","zh":"“没有几个钱，没有几个钱；也不必急着就给，随您方便；我们不是犹太人！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She reflected for a few moments, and ended by again declining Monsieur Lheureux’s offer. He replied quite unconcernedly—","sentences":[{"en":"She reflected for a few moments, and ended by again declining Monsieur Lheureux’s offer.","zh":"她沉吟了一下，结局还是不买。勒乐先生满不在乎，答话道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He replied quite unconcernedly—","zh":"她沉吟了一下，结局还是不买。勒乐先生满不在乎，答话道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Very well. We shall understand one another by and by. I have always got on with ladies—if I didn’t with my own!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very well.","zh":"“好吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We shall understand one another by and by.","zh":"我们以后会相熟的；我一向凑合太太们，不过贱内可不在内！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I have always got on with ladies—if I didn’t with my own!”","zh":"我们以后会相熟的；我一向凑合太太们，不过贱内可不在内！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma smiled.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma smiled.","zh":"爱玛微笑了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I wanted to tell you,” he went on good-naturedly, after his joke, “that it isn’t the money I should trouble about. Why, I could give you some, if need be.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I wanted to tell you,” he went on good-naturedly, after his joke, “that it isn’t the money I should trouble about.","zh":"他说过这句趣话，就做出一副老实人模样，接下去道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why, I could give you some, if need be.”","zh":"“我讲这话，就是说，我不拿钱搁在心上…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She made a gesture of surprise.","sentences":[{"en":"She made a gesture of surprise.","zh":"您要是钱不凑手，我先借给您也行。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah!” said he quickly and in a low voice, “I shouldn’t have to go far to find you some, rely on that.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!” said he quickly and in a low voice, “I shouldn’t have to go far to find you some, rely on that.”","zh":"他连忙低声道：“啊！您用钱，近处就好周转；放心好了！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he began asking after Pere Tellier, the proprietor of the “Cafe Francais,” whom Monsieur Bovary was then attending.","sentences":[{"en":"And he began asking after Pere Tellier, the proprietor of the “Cafe Francais,” whom Monsieur Bovary was then attending.","zh":"他转过话头，问起法兰西咖啡馆的老板泰里耶老爹的消息，包法利当时正在给他看病。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What’s the matter with Pere Tellier? He coughs so that he shakes his whole house, and I’m afraid he’ll soon want a deal covering rather than a flannel vest. He was such a rake as a young man! Those sort of people, madame, have not the least regularity; he’s burnt up with brandy. Still it’s sad, all the same, to see an acquaintance go off.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s the matter with Pere Tellier?","zh":"“泰里耶老爹到底是怎么一回事？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He coughs so that he shakes his whole house, and I’m afraid he’ll soon want a deal covering rather than a flannel vest.","zh":"他一咳嗽，整个房子摇晃，我担心他过不了几天，不穿法兰绒内衣，会穿松木大衣 的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was such a rake as a young man!","zh":"年轻时候，他拼命荒唐！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Those sort of people, madame, have not the least regularity; he’s burnt up with brandy.","zh":"这种人呀，太太，一点儿也没有条理！光喝酒也把他喝干了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Still it’s sad, all the same, to see an acquaintance go off.”","zh":"不过眼睁睁看着相识的人死，不管怎么样，总不好过。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And while he fastened up his box he discoursed about the doctor’s patients.","sentences":[{"en":"And while he fastened up his box he discoursed about the doctor’s patients.","zh":"他一面扣硬纸匣，一面就这样议论医生的病人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It’s the weather, no doubt,” he said, looking frowningly at the floor, “that causes these illnesses. I, too, don’t feel the thing. One of these days I shall even have to consult the doctor for a pain I have in my back. Well, good-bye, Madame Bovary. At your service; your very humble servant.” And he closed the door gently.","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s the weather, no doubt,” he said, looking frowningly at the floor, “that causes these illnesses.","zh":"他望着玻璃窗，一脸不愉快的神情，说：“自然喽，时令不正，就生这些病。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I, too, don’t feel the thing.","zh":"他望着玻璃窗，一脸不愉快的神情，说：“自然喽，时令不正，就生这些病。","scope":"group"},{"en":"One of these days I shall even have to consult the doctor for a pain I have in my back.","zh":"我呀，我就觉得自己不怎么适意；我的后背有一个地方疼，改一天，我也许来看看大夫。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Well, good-bye, Madame Bovary.","zh":"我呀，我就觉得自己不怎么适意；我的后背有一个地方疼，改一天，我也许来看看大夫。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At your service; your very humble servant.”","zh":"可不，再见啦，包法利太太；有事尽管吩咐；在下一定伺候！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"And he closed the door gently.","zh":"可不，再见啦，包法利太太；有事尽管吩咐；在下一定伺候！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma had her dinner served in her bedroom on a tray by the fireside; she was a long time over it; everything was well with her.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma had her dinner served in her bedroom on a tray by the fireside; she was a long time over it; everything was well with her.","zh":"他轻轻把门带上。爱玛叫人把饭开到卧室，放在盘子里头；她坐在炉边，慢慢腾腾用饭，感到很舒坦。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How good I was!” she said to herself, thinking of the scarves.","sentences":[{"en":"“How good I was!” she said to herself, thinking of the scarves.","zh":"她想着围巾，自言自语道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She heard some steps on the stairs. It was Léon. She got up and took from the chest of drawers the first pile of dusters to be hemmed. When he came in she seemed very busy.","sentences":[{"en":"She heard some steps on the stairs.","zh":"“我真叫乖啦！”她听见楼梯上脚步响：赖昂来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was Léon.","zh":"“我真叫乖啦！”她听见楼梯上脚步响：赖昂来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She got up and took from the chest of drawers the first pile of dusters to be hemmed.","zh":"她站起来，五斗柜上放了几条抹布，等着缭边，她拿起头一条；他进来，她显得很忙。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When he came in she seemed very busy.","zh":"她站起来，五斗柜上放了几条抹布，等着缭边，她拿起头一条；他进来，她显得很忙。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The conversation languished; Madame Bovary gave it up every few minutes, whilst he himself seemed quite embarrassed. Seated on a low chair near the fire, he turned round in his fingers the ivory thimble-case. She stitched on, or from time to time turned down the hem of the cloth with her nail. She did not speak; he was silent, captivated by her silence, as he would have been by her speech.","sentences":[{"en":"The conversation languished; Madame Bovary gave it up every few minutes, whilst he himself seemed quite embarrassed.","zh":"谈话无精打采，包法利夫人有一句没一句，时时停顿，他自己也像有话难以出口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Seated on a low chair near the fire, he turned round in his fingers the ivory thimble-case.","zh":"他坐在炉边一张矮椅上，手里拿着象牙针盒，转来转去；她不是穿针引线，就是不时拿指甲压压布褶子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She stitched on, or from time to time turned down the hem of the cloth with her nail.","zh":"他坐在炉边一张矮椅上，手里拿着象牙针盒，转来转去；她不是穿针引线，就是不时拿指甲压压布褶子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She did not speak; he was silent, captivated by her silence, as he would have been by her speech.","zh":"她不说话，他也开不得口，她的沉默迷住了他，就像先前她的语言迷住了他一样。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Poor fellow!” she thought.","sentences":[{"en":"“Poor fellow!” she thought.","zh":"她不说话，他也开不得口，她的沉默迷住了他，就像先前她的语言迷住了他一样。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“How have I displeased her?” he asked himself.","sentences":[{"en":"“How have I displeased her?” he asked himself.","zh":"她心里想：“可怜的孩子！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last, however, Léon said that he should have, one of these days, to go to Rouen on some office business.","sentences":[{"en":"At last, however, Léon said that he should have, one of these days, to go to Rouen on some office business.","zh":"他问自己：“她嫌我什么？”临了还是赖昂说起，他有一天要去鲁昂，办理一件业务上的事。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Your music subscription is out; am I to renew it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Your music subscription is out; am I to renew it?”","zh":"“您订的音乐刊物满期了，要不要我续下去？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No,” she replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“No,” she replied.","zh":"她回道：“不要。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why?”","zh":"“为什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Because—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Because—”","zh":"“因为…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And pursing her lips she slowly drew a long stitch of grey thread.","sentences":[{"en":"And pursing her lips she slowly drew a long stitch of grey thread.","zh":"她闭紧嘴唇，慢条斯理，抽出一根长长的灰线。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This work irritated Léon. It seemed to roughen the ends of her fingers. A gallant phrase came into his head, but he did not risk it.","sentences":[{"en":"This work irritated Léon.","zh":"赖昂看着这件女活有气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It seemed to roughen the ends of her fingers.","zh":"爱玛的手指尖都像扎破了似的；他想起一句漂亮话，可是又不敢说出来。他接下去道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"A gallant phrase came into his head, but he did not risk it.","zh":"爱玛的手指尖都像扎破了似的；他想起一句漂亮话，可是又不敢说出来。他接下去道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Then you are giving it up?” he went on.","sentences":[{"en":"“Then you are giving it up?” he went on.","zh":"“您不学啦？”“什么？”她赶快改口道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What?” she asked hurriedly. “Music? Ah! yes! Have I not my house to look after, my husband to attend to, a thousand things, in fact, many duties that must be considered first?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?” she asked hurriedly.","zh":"“音乐？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Music?","zh":"啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! yes!","zh":"我的上帝，是啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Have I not my house to look after, my husband to attend to, a thousand things, in fact, many duties that must be considered first?”","zh":"难道我不要管家，不要照料丈夫，总之，手边还有一大堆活儿，许许多多分内事，要我先操心？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She looked at the clock. Charles was late. Then, she affected anxiety. Two or three times she even repeated, “He is so good!”","sentences":[{"en":"She looked at the clock.","zh":"她望望钟。查理回来迟了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles was late.","zh":"她望望钟。查理回来迟了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, she affected anxiety.","zh":"她不放心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Two or three times she even repeated, “He is so good!”","zh":"她重复了两三遍：“他人真好！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The clerk was fond of Monsieur Bovary. But this tenderness on his behalf astonished him unpleasantly; nevertheless he took up on his praises, which he said everyone was singing, especially the chemist.","sentences":[{"en":"The clerk was fond of Monsieur Bovary.","zh":"文书喜欢包法利先生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But this tenderness on his behalf astonished him unpleasantly; nevertheless he took up on his praises, which he said everyone was singing, especially the chemist.","zh":"可是他想不到她待他这样深情，听着未免别扭；不过他照样恭维他，他说，他听见人人夸他，尤其是药剂师。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! he is a good fellow,” continued Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! he is a good fellow,” continued Emma.","zh":"爱玛接下去道：“啊！他是一位好人！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Certainly,” replied the clerk.","sentences":[{"en":"“Certainly,” replied the clerk.","zh":"文书接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he began talking of Madame Homais, whose very untidy appearance generally made them laugh.","sentences":[{"en":"And he began talking of Madame Homais, whose very untidy appearance generally made them laugh.","zh":"“当然。”他调转话头，讲郝麦夫人，他们平时一来就笑她不修边幅。爱玛打断道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What does it matter?” interrupted Emma. “A good housewife does not trouble about her appearance.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What does it matter?” interrupted Emma.","zh":"“这有什么关系？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“A good housewife does not trouble about her appearance.”","zh":"做慈母的，没有心思打扮自己。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she relapsed into silence.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she relapsed into silence.","zh":"说过这话，她又默不作声了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was the same on the following days; her talks, her manners, everything changed. She took interest in the housework, went to church regularly, and looked after her servant with more severity.","sentences":[{"en":"It was the same on the following days; her talks, her manners, everything changed.","zh":"一连几天，都是如此；她的谈话、她的姿态，统统变了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She took interest in the housework, went to church regularly, and looked after her servant with more severity.","zh":"大家见她关心家务，按时上教堂，对女用人也管得更严了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She took Berthe from nurse. When visitors called, Félicité brought her in, and Madame Bovary undressed her to show off her limbs. She declared she adored children; this was her consolation, her joy, her passion, and she accompanied her caresses with lyrical outburst which would have reminded anyone but the Yonville people of Sachette in “Notre Dame de Paris.”","sentences":[{"en":"She took Berthe from nurse.","zh":"她从奶妈那边接回白尔特。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When visitors called, Félicité brought her in, and Madame Bovary undressed her to show off her limbs.","zh":"家里一有客人，全福就带她过来，包法利夫人撩起孩子的衣服，叫人看看她的小胳膊、小腿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She declared she adored children; this was her consolation, her joy, her passion, and she accompanied her caresses with lyrical outburst which would have reminded anyone but the Yonville people of Sachette in “Notre Dame de Paris.”","zh":"她讲她就爱小孩子；这是她的安慰、她的喜悦、她的迷恋；她的爱抚带有感情，除去永镇人，任何人看了，都会想到《巴黎圣母院》里的小麻袋 。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When Charles came home he found his slippers put to warm near the fire. His waistcoat now never wanted lining, nor his shirt buttons, and it was quite a pleasure to see in the cupboard the night-caps arranged in piles of the same height. She no longer grumbled as formerly at taking a turn in the garden; what he proposed was always done, although she did not understand the wishes to which she submitted without a murmur; and when Léon saw him by his fireside after dinner, his two hands on his stomach, his two feet on the fender, his two cheeks red with feeding, his eyes moist with happiness, the child crawling along the carpet, and this woman with the slender waist who came behind his arm-chair to kiss his forehead: “What madness!” he said to himself. “And how to reach her!”","sentences":[{"en":"When Charles came home he found his slippers put to warm near the fire.","zh":"查理回家，发现拖鞋放在炉火旁，烤得暖暖的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His waistcoat now never wanted lining, nor his shirt buttons, and it was quite a pleasure to see in the cupboard the night-caps arranged in piles of the same height.","zh":"现在，他的背心不再缺里子了。衬衫不再短纽扣了。甚至他的睡帽，也一顶一顶，整整齐齐，在橱里摞好，他看在眼里，觉得开心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She no longer grumbled as formerly at taking a turn in the garden; what he proposed was always done, although she did not understand the wishes to which she submitted without a murmur; and when Léon saw him by his fireside after dinner, his two hands on his stomach, his two feet on the fender, his two cheeks red with feeding, his eyes moist with happiness, the child crawling along the carpet, and this woman with the slender waist who came behind his arm-chair to kiss his forehead: “What madness!” he said to himself.","zh":"她不像往常，花园转转，就皱眉头；他有建议，她总同意，即使她猜不透他的意思，她也百依百顺，不露一丝抱怨。——赖昂看见他坐在炉边，用罢了饭，一双手搭在肚子上，两只脚搁在火篦上，脸蛋由于消化也发红了，眼睛由于幸福也润泽了，孩子在地毯上爬着，而这位细腰女子，就着椅背，吻他的额头。他向自己道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“And how to reach her!”","zh":"“简直胡闹！怎么接近得了她？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And thus she seemed so virtuous and inaccessible to him that he lost all hope, even the faintest. But by this renunciation he placed her on an extraordinary pinnacle. To him she stood outside those fleshly attributes from which he had nothing to obtain, and in his heart she rose ever, and became farther removed from him after the magnificent manner of an apotheosis that is taking wing. It was one of those pure feelings that do not interfere with life, that are cultivated because they are rare, and whose loss would afflict more than their passion rejoices.","sentences":[{"en":"And thus she seemed so virtuous and inaccessible to him that he lost all hope, even the faintest.","zh":"所以在他看来，她十分端庄，亲近不得，他连一星半点的希望也不存了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But by this renunciation he placed her on an extraordinary pinnacle.","zh":"可是意有所舍，心犹未甘，他只好把她放在非凡的境界。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To him she stood outside those fleshly attributes from which he had nothing to obtain, and in his heart she rose ever, and became farther removed from him after the magnificent manner of an apotheosis that is taking wing.","zh":"他在肉身方面既然一无所得，所以对他说来，她不具肉身，在他的心头扶摇直上，仿佛成仙得道，云脚冉冉，气象万千。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was one of those pure feelings that do not interfere with life, that are cultivated because they are rare, and whose loss would afflict more than their passion rejoices.","zh":"这是一种纯洁感情，并不妨碍日常生活，有了它，心里快活，一旦丢了，就会特别难过，正因为这种感情可贵，人才加以培养。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma grew thinner, her cheeks paler, her face longer. With her black hair, her large eyes, her aquiline nose, her birdlike walk, and always silent now, did she not seem to be passing through life scarcely touching it, and to bear on her brow the vague impress of some divine destiny? She was so sad and so calm, at once so gentle and so reserved, that near her one felt oneself seized by an icy charm, as we shudder in churches at the perfume of the flowers mingling with the cold of the marble. The others even did not escape from this seduction. The chemist said—","sentences":[{"en":"Emma grew thinner, her cheeks paler, her face longer.","zh":"爱玛瘦了，面色苍白，脸也长了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With her black hair, her large eyes, her aquiline nose, her birdlike walk, and always silent now, did she not seem to be passing through life scarcely touching it, and to bear on her brow the vague impress of some divine destiny?","zh":"大眼睛，直鼻子，一绺一绺黑头发，走路像鸟飞一样轻，而且现在永远静默：难道她不像亭亭玉立，经浊世而不染，额头隐隐约约，打着崇高宿命的印记？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was so sad and so calm, at once so gentle and so reserved, that near her one felt oneself seized by an icy charm, as we shudder in churches at the perfume of the flowers mingling with the cold of the marble.","zh":"她十分忧郁，而又十分安详；十分温柔，而又十分矜持。人在她旁边，感到一种冷冰冰的魅力，仿佛走进教堂，花香香的，大理石凉凉的，不禁寒颤起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The others even did not escape from this seduction.","zh":"就连别人也逃不出这种诱惑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The chemist said—","zh":"药剂师说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“She is a woman of great parts, who wouldn’t be misplaced in a sub-prefecture.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She is a woman of great parts, who wouldn’t be misplaced in a sub-prefecture.”","zh":"“她是一个天资卓绝的女子，做县长夫人也不过分。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The housewives admired her economy, the patients her politeness, the poor her charity.","sentences":[{"en":"The housewives admired her economy, the patients her politeness, the poor her charity.","zh":"太太们称赞她节省，病人们称赞她有礼貌，穷人们称赞她仁慈。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But she was eaten up with desires, with rage, with hate. That dress with the narrow folds hid a distracted fear, of whose torment those chaste lips said nothing. She was in love with Léon, and sought solitude that she might with the more ease delight in his image. The sight of his form troubled the voluptuousness of this mediation. Emma thrilled at the sound of his step; then in his presence the emotion subsided, and afterwards there remained to her only an immense astonishment that ended in sorrow.","sentences":[{"en":"But she was eaten up with desires, with rage, with hate.","zh":"但是她内心却充满欲念、愤怒和怨恨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That dress with the narrow folds hid a distracted fear, of whose torment those chaste lips said nothing.","zh":"衣褶平平正正，里头包藏着一颗骚乱的心；嘴唇娴静，并不讲出内心的苦恼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was in love with Léon, and sought solitude that she might with the more ease delight in his image.","zh":"她爱赖昂，追寻寂寞，为了能更自由自在地玩味他的形象。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sight of his form troubled the voluptuousness of this mediation.","zh":"真人当面，反而扰乱沉思的快感。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma thrilled at the sound of his step; then in his presence the emotion subsided, and afterwards there remained to her only an immense astonishment that ended in sorrow.","zh":"听见他的脚步，她就心跳；但是待在一起，心就沉下去了，她有的只是莫大的惊奇，临了又陷入忧郁。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon did not know that when he left her in despair she rose after he had gone to see him in the street. She concerned herself about his comings and goings; she watched his face; she invented quite a history to find an excuse for going to his room. The chemist’s wife seemed happy to her to sleep under the same roof, and her thoughts constantly centered upon this house, like the “Lion d’Or” pigeons, who came there to dip their red feet and white wings in its gutters. But the more Emma recognised her love, the more she crushed it down, that it might not be evident, that she might make it less. She would have liked Léon to guess it, and she imagined chances, catastrophes that should facilitate this.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon did not know that when he left her in despair she rose after he had gone to see him in the street.","zh":"赖昂走出她家，心灰意懒，却不知道她跟踪而起，看他在街上走动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She concerned herself about his comings and goings; she watched his face; she invented quite a history to find an excuse for going to his room.","zh":"她关心他的行止，窥伺他的脸色；她找借口看看他的房间，编了一个有头有尾的故事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The chemist’s wife seemed happy to her to sleep under the same roof, and her thoughts constantly centered upon this house, like the “Lion d’Or” pigeons, who came there to dip their red feet and white wings in its gutters.","zh":"药剂师女人和他住在同一房顶底下，在她看来，幸运之至。她一想就想到这家房屋，好像金狮的鸽子，一飞就飞到这家的承溜，在里头洗净它们的玫瑰红爪子和它们的白翅膀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the more Emma recognised her love, the more she crushed it down, that it might not be evident, that she might make it less.","zh":"可是爱玛越觉得自己有爱情，越加以抑制，为的是减弱它的声势，不要流露出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would have liked Léon to guess it, and she imagined chances, catastrophes that should facilitate this.","zh":"她巴不得赖昂猜破，也设想了一些促使赖昂猜破的机会、变故。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"What restrained her was, no doubt, idleness and fear, and a sense of shame also. She thought she had repulsed him too much, that the time was past, that all was lost. Then, pride, and joy of being able to say to herself, “I am virtuous,” and to look at herself in the glass taking resigned poses, consoled her a little for the sacrifice she believed she was making.","sentences":[{"en":"What restrained her was, no doubt, idleness and fear, and a sense of shame also.","zh":"她没有放手去做，不用说，是由于懒散或者畏惧的缘故。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She thought she had repulsed him too much, that the time was past, that all was lost.","zh":"还有羞耻的缘故。她寻思自己太拒人于千里之外，时机不再，无从补救了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, pride, and joy of being able to say to herself, “I am virtuous,” and to look at herself in the glass taking resigned poses, consoled her a little for the sacrifice she believed she was making.","zh":"她自以为牺牲很大，什么也安慰不了她，后来只能说说“我是贞洁女子”，还摆出听天由命的姿态照照镜子，显出一脸的骄傲和喜悦，心头才有一点点好受的味道。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then the lusts of the flesh, the longing for money, and the melancholy of passion all blended themselves into one suffering, and instead of turning her thoughts from it, she clave to it the more, urging herself to pain, and seeking everywhere occasion for it. She was irritated by an ill-served dish or by a half-open door; bewailed the velvets she had not, the happiness she had missed, her too exalted dreams, her narrow home.","sentences":[{"en":"Then the lusts of the flesh, the longing for money, and the melancholy of passion all blended themselves into one suffering, and instead of turning her thoughts from it, she clave to it the more, urging herself to pain, and seeking everywhere occasion for it.","zh":"于是肉体的需要、银钱的欠缺和热情的悒郁，揉成一团痛苦——她不但不设法摆脱，反而越陷越深，到处寻找机会加深她的痛苦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was irritated by an ill-served dish or by a half-open door; bewailed the velvets she had not, the happiness she had missed, her too exalted dreams, her narrow home.","zh":"一盘菜做坏了，或者一扇门没有关严，她就有气；想起自己没有丝绒衣衫，幸福插翅飞过，想望太高，居室太窄，她就难过。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"What exasperated her was that Charles did not seem to notice her anguish. His conviction that he was making her happy seemed to her an imbecile insult, and his sureness on this point ingratitude. For whose sake, then was she virtuous? Was it not for him, the obstacle to all felicity, the cause of all misery, and, as it were, the sharp clasp of that complex strap that bucked her in on all sides.","sentences":[{"en":"What exasperated her was that Charles did not seem to notice her anguish.","zh":"顶气人的是，她受折磨，查理似乎没有察觉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His conviction that he was making her happy seemed to her an imbecile insult, and his sureness on this point ingratitude.","zh":"他自以为使她幸福的信念，在她看来，就是一种岂有此理的侮辱；他那方面心安理得，就是忘恩负义。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For whose sake, then was she virtuous?","zh":"请问，她为谁贤惠？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Was it not for him, the obstacle to all felicity, the cause of all misery, and, as it were, the sharp clasp of that complex strap that bucked her in on all sides.","zh":"难道不正是他成为一切幸福的障碍、一切灾难的缘由，就像身上皮带的尖插头一样，把她扣得牢牢的，气也出不来一口？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On him alone, then, she concentrated all the various hatreds that resulted from her boredom, and every effort to diminish only augmented it; for this useless trouble was added to the other reasons for despair, and contributed still more to the separation between them. Her own gentleness to herself made her rebel against him. Domestic mediocrity drove her to lewd fancies, marriage tenderness to adulterous desires. She would have liked Charles to beat her, that she might have a better right to hate him, to revenge herself upon him. She was surprised sometimes at the atrocious conjectures that came into her thoughts, and she had to go on smiling, to hear repeated to her at all hours that she was happy, to pretend to be happy, to let it be believed.","sentences":[{"en":"On him alone, then, she concentrated all the various hatreds that resulted from her boredom, and every effort to diminish only augmented it; for this useless trouble was added to the other reasons for despair, and contributed still more to the separation between them.","zh":"所以种种怨恨，不管是不是从自己的烦闷来的，统统算在他的账上；她未尝不想减轻怨恨，可是回回努力，回回扑空，不但没有减轻，反而更深了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her own gentleness to herself made her rebel against him.","zh":"她这样白白辛苦一场，已经于心不快，加上使她痛苦的其他原因，彼此之间的隔膜，也就越发大了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Domestic mediocrity drove her to lewd fancies, marriage tenderness to adulterous desires.","zh":"她这样白白辛苦一场，已经于心不快，加上使她痛苦的其他原因，彼此之间的隔膜，也就越发大了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She would have liked Charles to beat her, that she might have a better right to hate him, to revenge herself upon him.","zh":"她对自己的柔顺起了反感。家庭生活的平庸使她向往奢华；夫妇之间的恩爱使她缅想奸淫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was surprised sometimes at the atrocious conjectures that came into her thoughts, and she had to go on smiling, to hear repeated to her at all hours that she was happy, to pretend to be happy, to let it be believed.","zh":"她巴不得查理打她一顿，她好抓住理由恨他、报复他。面对着自己想起的一些残酷的假设，她有时候不由一惊。然而她必须继续笑脸相向，听见自己重复说：她很快乐，而且装模作样，要人相信自己快乐。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Yet she had loathing of this hypocrisy. She was seized with the temptation to flee somewhere with Léon to try a new life; but at once a vague chasm full of darkness opened within her soul.","sentences":[{"en":"Yet she had loathing of this hypocrisy.","zh":"可是她厌恶这种虚伪行为。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was seized with the temptation to flee somewhere with Léon to try a new life; but at once a vague chasm full of darkness opened within her soul.","zh":"她有心和赖昂逃之夭夭，到天涯海角试试新的命运；不过一想到这上头，她立刻觉得有一道黑压压的大沟横在面前。她寻思道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Besides, he no longer loves me,” she thought. “What is to become of me? What help is to be hoped for, what consolation, what solace?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Besides, he no longer loves me,” she thought.","zh":"她有心和赖昂逃之夭夭，到天涯海角试试新的命运；不过一想到这上头，她立刻觉得有一道黑压压的大沟横在面前。她寻思道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"“What is to become of me?","zh":"“而且，他已经不爱我了；怎么办？指望谁帮助、谁安慰、谁搭救？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"What help is to be hoped for, what consolation, what solace?”","zh":"“而且，他已经不爱我了；怎么办？指望谁帮助、谁安慰、谁搭救？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She was left broken, breathless, inert, sobbing in a low voice, with flowing tears.","sentences":[{"en":"She was left broken, breathless, inert, sobbing in a low voice, with flowing tears.","zh":"她心碎了，气喘吁吁，痴痴呆呆，低声呜咽，满脸眼泪。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why don’t you tell master?” the servant asked her when she came in during these crises.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why don’t you tell master?” the servant asked her when she came in during these crises.","zh":"女用人有时候进来，赶上她犯病，就问她道：“为什么不告诉老爷？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is the nerves,” said Emma. “Do not speak to him of it; it would worry him.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is the nerves,” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛回答：“这是神经性的毛病；别告诉他，他要难过的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Do not speak to him of it; it would worry him.”","zh":"爱玛回答：“这是神经性的毛病；别告诉他，他要难过的。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ah! yes,” Félicité went on, “you are just like La Guerine, Pere Guerin’s daughter, the fisherman at Pollet, that I used to know at Dieppe before I came to you. She was so sad, so sad, to see her standing upright on the threshold of her house, she seemed to you like a winding-sheet spread out before the door. Her illness, it appears, was a kind of fog that she had in her head, and the doctors could not do anything, nor the priest either. When she was taken too bad she went off quite alone to the sea-shore, so that the customs officer, going his rounds, often found her lying flat on her face, crying on the shingle. Then, after her marriage, it went off, they say.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! yes,” Félicité went on, “you are just like La Guerine, Pere Guerin’s daughter, the fisherman at Pollet, that I used to know at Dieppe before I came to you.","zh":"全福接下去道：“啊！是啊，您就像小盖丽娜一样，波莱 的渔夫盖兰老爹的闺女，我来您家以前，在第厄普认识的，她呀，一天到晚，愁眉不展，站在她家门槛，看她那模样，真还以为是一条裹死人的布，挂在门前头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was so sad, so sad, to see her standing upright on the threshold of her house, she seemed to you like a winding-sheet spread out before the door.","zh":"全福接下去道：“啊！是啊，您就像小盖丽娜一样，波莱 的渔夫盖兰老爹的闺女，我来您家以前，在第厄普认识的，她呀，一天到晚，愁眉不展，站在她家门槛，看她那模样，真还以为是一条裹死人的布，挂在门前头。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her illness, it appears, was a kind of fog that she had in her head, and the doctors could not do anything, nor the priest either.","zh":"她害的病，看上去，就像脑子里头有了雾一样，大夫治不了，堂长也没有办法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When she was taken too bad she went off quite alone to the sea-shore, so that the customs officer, going his rounds, often found her lying flat on her face, crying on the shingle.","zh":"病狠了，她就一个人到海边待着，海关上的官儿巡逻，常常看见她脸朝下，趴在石子上头哭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, after her marriage, it went off, they say.”","zh":"后来，据说，嫁人以后，她就好啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But with me,” replied Emma, “it was after marriage that it began.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But with me,” replied Emma, “it was after marriage that it began.”","zh":"爱玛接下去道：“不过，我呀，我是嫁人以后得的。”","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-6","part":2,"n":6,"title":"Part II · Chapter 6","titleZh":"中卷 · 6","paragraphs":[{"en":"One evening when the window was open, and she, sitting by it, had been watching Lestiboudois, the beadle, trimming the box, she suddenly heard the Angelus ringing.","sentences":[{"en":"One evening when the window was open, and she, sitting by it, had been watching Lestiboudois, the beadle, trimming the box, she suddenly heard the Angelus ringing.","zh":"一天傍晚，打开窗户，她坐在窗口，刚才还望见教堂管事赖斯地布杜瓦在修剪黄杨，忽地听见晚祷的钟声响了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was the beginning of April, when the primroses are in bloom, and a warm wind blows over the flower-beds newly turned, and the gardens, like women, seem to be getting ready for the summer fetes. Through the bars of the arbour and away beyond the river seen in the fields, meandering through the grass in wandering curves. The evening vapours rose between the leafless poplars, touching their outlines with a violet tint, paler and more transparent than a subtle gauze caught athwart their branches. In the distance cattle moved about; neither their steps nor their lowing could be heard; and the bell, still ringing through the air, kept up its peaceful lamentation.","sentences":[{"en":"It was the beginning of April, when the primroses are in bloom, and a warm wind blows over the flower-beds newly turned, and the gardens, like women, seem to be getting ready for the summer fetes.","zh":"正当四月初旬，樱草开花，一阵熏风吹过新掘的花畦，花园如同妇女，着意修饰，迎接夏季的节日。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Through the bars of the arbour and away beyond the river seen in the fields, meandering through the grass in wandering curves.","zh":"从花棚的空隙望出去，就见河水曲曲折折，漫不经心，流过草原。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The evening vapours rose between the leafless poplars, touching their outlines with a violet tint, paler and more transparent than a subtle gauze caught athwart their branches.","zh":"黄昏的雾气，在光秃的白杨中间浮过，仿佛细纱挂在树枝，却比细纱还要白，还要透明，弥蒙一片，把白杨的轮廓勾成了堇色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the distance cattle moved about; neither their steps nor their lowing could be heard; and the bell, still ringing through the air, kept up its peaceful lamentation.","zh":"远处有牲畜走动，却听不见蹄声，也听不见叫唤。钟声含着淡淡的哀怨，在空中响个不停。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"With this repeated tinkling the thoughts of the young woman lost themselves in old memories of her youth and school-days. She remembered the great candlesticks that rose above the vases full of flowers on the altar, and the tabernacle with its small columns. She would have liked to be once more lost in the long line of white veils, marked off here and there by the stuff black hoods of the good sisters bending over their prie-Dieu. At mass on Sundays, when she looked up, she saw the gentle face of the Virgin amid the blue smoke of the rising incense. Then she was moved; she felt herself weak and quite deserted, like the down of a bird whirled by the tempest, and it was unconsciously that she went towards the church, included to no matter what devotions, so that her soul was absorbed and all existence lost in it.","sentences":[{"en":"With this repeated tinkling the thoughts of the young woman lost themselves in old memories of her youth and school-days.","zh":"钟声阵阵，唤起少妇对童年和寄宿时期的回忆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She remembered the great candlesticks that rose above the vases full of flowers on the altar, and the tabernacle with its small columns.","zh":"她想起圣坛的蜡烛台，高出花瓶和细柱神龛之上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would have liked to be once more lost in the long line of white veils, marked off here and there by the stuff black hoods of the good sisters bending over their prie-Dieu.","zh":"她真愿意像往常一样，混在修女们中间，伏在跪凳上，一长排白面网当中，东一块、西一块黑点，是修女们的硬风帽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At mass on Sundays, when she looked up, she saw the gentle face of the Virgin amid the blue smoke of the rising incense.","zh":"星期日望弥撒，她一抬头就望见淡蓝香云，环绕圣母慈容，冉冉上升。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she was moved; she felt herself weak and quite deserted, like the down of a bird whirled by the tempest, and it was unconsciously that she went towards the church, included to no matter what devotions, so that her soul was absorbed and all existence lost in it.","zh":"她的心被触动了，觉得自己柔弱无力，四处飘零，好像一根鸟羽，在狂风暴雨之中打转。她于是身不由己，不知不觉，去了教堂，准备虔心信教，什么方式都行，只求她的灵魂俯首帖耳，人间烦恼不再存在。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On the Place she met Lestivoudois on his way back, for, in order not to shorten his day’s labour, he preferred interrupting his work, then beginning it again, so that he rang the Angelus to suit his own convenience. Besides, the ringing over a little earlier warned the lads of catechism hour.","sentences":[{"en":"On the Place she met Lestivoudois on his way back, for, in order not to shorten his day’s labour, he preferred interrupting his work, then beginning it again, so that he rang the Angelus to suit his own convenience.","zh":"她在广场碰见赖斯地布杜瓦回来；他为了不影响收入，宁可中断工作，敲完钟再回来接着干。所以什么时候晚祷敲钟，只能趁他方便。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, the ringing over a little earlier warned the lads of catechism hour.","zh":"再说，提早敲钟，正好警告顽童：教理问答的时间到了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Already a few who had arrived were playing marbles on the stones of the cemetery. Others, astride the wall, swung their legs, kicking with their clogs the large nettles growing between the little enclosure and the newest graves. This was the only green spot. All the rest was but stones, always covered with a fine powder, despite the vestry-broom.","sentences":[{"en":"Already a few who had arrived were playing marbles on the stones of the cemetery.","zh":"有些孩子已经来了，在公墓的石板地玩弹子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Others, astride the wall, swung their legs, kicking with their clogs the large nettles growing between the little enclosure and the newest graves.","zh":"有的骑在墙头，腿荡来荡去，拿木头套鞋踢着墙和新坟之间高高的荨麻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This was the only green spot.","zh":"这块地方是此处仅有的绿地；此外都是石头，尽管经常打扫，总挡不住上头老有一层浮土。","scope":"group"},{"en":"All the rest was but stones, always covered with a fine powder, despite the vestry-broom.","zh":"这块地方是此处仅有的绿地；此外都是石头，尽管经常打扫，总挡不住上头老有一层浮土。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The children in list shoes ran about there as if it were an enclosure made for them. The shouts of their voices could be heard through the humming of the bell. This grew less and less with the swinging of the great rope that, hanging from the top of the belfry, dragged its end on the ground. Swallows flitted to and fro uttering little cries, cut the air with the edge of their wings, and swiftly returned to their yellow nests under the tiles of the coping. At the end of the church a lamp was burning, the wick of a night-light in a glass hung up. Its light from a distance looked like a white stain trembling in the oil. A long ray of the sun fell across the nave and seemed to darken the lower sides and the corners.","sentences":[{"en":"The children in list shoes ran about there as if it were an enclosure made for them.","zh":"似乎这就是孩子们的拼花地板，他们穿着布鞋，在里头跑来跑去，钟声再响，也听得见他们喧声如雷。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The shouts of their voices could be heard through the humming of the bell.","zh":"似乎这就是孩子们的拼花地板，他们穿着布鞋，在里头跑来跑去，钟声再响，也听得见他们喧声如雷。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This grew less and less with the swinging of the great rope that, hanging from the top of the belfry, dragged its end on the ground.","zh":"钟楼高空垂下一根粗绳，有一头搭在地上，钟绳摆幅缩短，钟声也就跟着小了下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Swallows flitted to and fro uttering little cries, cut the air with the edge of their wings, and swiftly returned to their yellow nests under the tiles of the coping.","zh":"燕子一面啁啾，一面掠空而过，迅速飞回檐瓦底下的黄窠。教堂尽里，点着一盏灯，就是说，玻璃盏挂在半空，里头有一根灯芯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the end of the church a lamp was burning, the wick of a night-light in a glass hung up.","zh":"远远望去，亮光仿佛一个灰白点子，漂在油上晃荡。一道细长的阳光，穿过教堂中部，相形之下，两侧和四周越发显得阴沉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Its light from a distance looked like a white stain trembling in the oil.","zh":"远远望去，亮光仿佛一个灰白点子，漂在油上晃荡。一道细长的阳光，穿过教堂中部，相形之下，两侧和四周越发显得阴沉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A long ray of the sun fell across the nave and seemed to darken the lower sides and the corners.","zh":"转门的轴已经松了，一个小孩还在摇着玩。包法利夫人问他：“堂长在哪儿？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where is the cure?” asked Madame Bovary of one of the lads, who was amusing himself by shaking a swivel in a hole too large for it.","sentences":[{"en":"“Where is the cure?” asked Madame Bovary of one of the lads, who was amusing himself by shaking a swivel in a hole too large for it.","zh":"“就快来啦 。”的确，门咯吱在响，布尔尼贤堂长走出住宅；孩子们一窝蜂似的逃进教室。教士唧咕道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“He is just coming,” he answered.","sentences":[{"en":"“He is just coming,” he answered.","zh":"“这些小家伙！总是这样！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And in fact the door of the presbytery grated; Abbe Bournisien appeared; the children, pell-mell, fled into the church.","sentences":[{"en":"And in fact the door of the presbytery grated; Abbe Bournisien appeared; the children, pell-mell, fled into the church.","zh":"他的脚碰到一本破烂的教理问答，他拾起来：“什么也不敬重！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“These young scamps!” murmured the priest, “always the same!”","sentences":[{"en":"“These young scamps!” murmured the priest, “always the same!”","zh":"他一瞥见包法利夫人，就说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, picking up a catechism all in rags that he had struck with his foot, “They respect nothing!” But as soon as he caught sight of Madame Bovary, “Excuse me,” he said; “I did not recognise you.”","sentences":[{"en":"Then, picking up a catechism all in rags that he had struck with his foot, “They respect nothing!”","zh":"“对不住，我没有认出您。”他把教理问答塞进衣袋，收住脚步，圣库的钥匙沉甸甸的，夹在两个手指当中，一直来回摇晃。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But as soon as he caught sight of Madame Bovary, “Excuse me,” he said; “I did not recognise you.”","zh":"“对不住，我没有认出您。”他把教理问答塞进衣袋，收住脚步，圣库的钥匙沉甸甸的，夹在两个手指当中，一直来回摇晃。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He thrust the catechism into his pocket, and stopped short, balancing the heavy vestry key between his two fingers.","sentences":[{"en":"He thrust the catechism into his pocket, and stopped short, balancing the heavy vestry key between his two fingers.","zh":"夕阳西下，余晖照亮他的整张脸，道袍下摆脱线，胳膊肘底下透亮，阳光掠过，毛呢颜色显得淡了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The light of the setting sun that fell full upon his face paled the lasting of his cassock, shiny at the elbows, unravelled at the hem. Grease and tobacco stains followed along his broad chest the lines of the buttons, and grew more numerous the farther they were from his neckcloth, in which the massive folds of his red chin rested; this was dotted with yellow spots, that disappeared beneath the coarse hair of his greyish beard. He had just dined and was breathing noisily.","sentences":[{"en":"The light of the setting sun that fell full upon his face paled the lasting of his cassock, shiny at the elbows, unravelled at the hem.","zh":"胸脯宽阔，沿着上面一排小纽扣，上上下下，全是油渍、烟污，离领巾越远，也就越多。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Grease and tobacco stains followed along his broad chest the lines of the buttons, and grew more numerous the farther they were from his neckcloth, in which the massive folds of his red chin rested; this was dotted with yellow spots, that disappeared beneath the coarse hair of his greyish beard.","zh":"颈项的红肉褶子搭在领巾上。皮肤上沥沥拉拉，撒着一些黄点子，直到鬣毛似的灰白胡须，才算看不见。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had just dined and was breathing noisily.","zh":"他刚用过晚饭，气咻咻的。他问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How are you?” he added.","sentences":[{"en":"“How are you?” he added.","zh":"“您好啊？”爱玛回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Not well,” replied Emma; “I am ill.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not well,” replied Emma; “I am ill.”","zh":"“不好，我难受。”教士接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, and so am I,” answered the priest. “These first warm days weaken one most remarkably, don’t they? But, after all, we are born to suffer, as St. Paul says. But what does Monsieur Bovary think of it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, and so am I,” answered the priest.","zh":"“可不！我也是。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“These first warm days weaken one most remarkably, don’t they?","zh":"这些日子，古里古怪，天刚热，人就四肢无力，您说对不对？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But, after all, we are born to suffer, as St. Paul says.","zh":"不过您要怎么着？圣保罗说得好，我们生下来就为受罪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But what does Monsieur Bovary think of it?”","zh":"倒是包法利先生，他是什么看法？”她做了一个轻蔑的手势，说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“He!” she said with a gesture of contempt.","sentences":[{"en":"“He!” she said with a gesture of contempt.","zh":"“他呀！”老好人吃了一惊，忙道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What!” replied the good fellow, quite astonished, “doesn’t he prescribe something for you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What!” replied the good fellow, quite astonished, “doesn’t he prescribe something for you?”","zh":"“什么！他不给您开方子，配一点药吃？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah!” said Emma, “it is no earthly remedy I need.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!” said Emma, “it is no earthly remedy I need.”","zh":"爱玛道：“啊！我要的不是人世的药。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the cure from time to time looked into the church, where the kneeling boys were shouldering one another, and tumbling over like packs of cards.","sentences":[{"en":"But the cure from time to time looked into the church, where the kneeling boys were shouldering one another, and tumbling over like packs of cards.","zh":"但是堂长不时朝教堂张望。孩子们全在里头跪着，你拿肩膀推我，我拿肩膀推你，好像一排纸人，倒了头一个，连串往下倒。她接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I should like to know—” she went on.","sentences":[{"en":"“I should like to know—” she went on.","zh":"“我想知道…”教士声音带怒，喊叫道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You look out, Riboudet,” cried the priest in an angry voice; “I’ll warm your ears, you imp!” Then turning to Emma, “He’s Boudet the carpenter’s son; his parents are well off, and let him do just as he pleases. Yet he could learn quickly if he would, for he is very sharp. And so sometimes for a joke I call him Riboudet (like the road one takes to go to Maromme) and I even say ‘Mon Riboudet.’ Ha! Ha! ‘Mont Riboudet.’ The other day I repeated that just to Monsignor, and he laughed at it; he condescended to laugh at it. And how is Monsieur Bovary?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You look out, Riboudet,” cried the priest in an angry voice; “I’ll warm your ears, you imp!”","zh":"“好，好，里布代，看我不打你耳光，捣蛋鬼！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then turning to Emma, “He’s Boudet the carpenter’s son; his parents are well off, and let him do just as he pleases.","zh":"随后转向爱玛道：“他是木匠布代的儿子；父母有钱，惯坏了他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yet he could learn quickly if he would, for he is very sharp.","zh":"不过只要他用功，他会学得快的，因为他很聪明。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And so sometimes for a joke I call him Riboudet (like the road one takes to go to Maromme) and I even say ‘Mon Riboudet.’","zh":"我呐，有时候打趣，就叫他里布代（去马罗默经过的岭子这样叫），我甚至说：‘蒙里布代’。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ha!","zh":"啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ha! ‘Mont Riboudet.’","zh":"啊！蒙里布代！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The other day I repeated that just to Monsignor, and he laughed at it; he condescended to laugh at it.","zh":"前一天，我把这话讲给主教听，他笑起来了…居然赏脸，笑起来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And how is Monsieur Bovary?”","zh":"——倒是，包法利先生，他好吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She seemed not to hear him. And he went on—","sentences":[{"en":"She seemed not to hear him.","zh":"她仿佛没有听见。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he went on—","zh":"他继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Always very busy, no doubt; for he and I are certainly the busiest people in the parish. But he is doctor of the body,” he added with a thick laugh, “and I of the soul.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Always very busy, no doubt; for he and I are certainly the busiest people in the parish.","zh":"“不用说，总在忙喽？因为他跟我的确是本教区最忙的两个人了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But he is doctor of the body,” he added with a thick laugh, “and I of the soul.”","zh":"不过他呀，是身体的医生（他放声笑着），而我呀，是灵魂的医生！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She fixed her pleading eyes upon the priest. “Yes,” she said, “you solace all sorrows.”","sentences":[{"en":"She fixed her pleading eyes upon the priest.","zh":"她显出一种哀求的眼神盯着教士道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Yes,” she said, “you solace all sorrows.”","zh":"“是啊…您解除所有的苦难。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! don’t talk to me of it, Madame Bovary. This morning I had to go to Bas-Diauville for a cow that was ill; they thought it was under a spell. All their cows, I don’t know how it is—But pardon me! Longuemarre and Boudet! Bless me! Will you leave off?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! don’t talk to me of it, Madame Bovary.","zh":"“啊！说的是呀，包法利太太！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This morning I had to go to Bas-Diauville for a cow that was ill; they thought it was under a spell.","zh":"就在今天早晨，有一条母牛吃了飞虫 ，我不得不去下狄欧镇一趟；他们以为牛中了邪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All their cows, I don’t know how it is—But pardon me!","zh":"他们的母牛，我不晓得是怎么一回事，头头…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Longuemarre and Boudet!","zh":"不过，对不起！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bless me!","zh":"龙格马尔，还有布代！家伙！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Will you leave off?”","zh":"你们有完没完？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And with a bound he ran into the church.","sentences":[{"en":"And with a bound he ran into the church.","zh":"他于是一步跳进教堂。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The boys were just then clustering round the large desk, climbing over the precentor’s footstool, opening the missal; and others on tiptoe were just about to venture into the confessional. But the priest suddenly distributed a shower of cuffs among them. Seizing them by the collars of their coats, he lifted them from the ground, and deposited them on their knees on the stones of the choir, firmly, as if he meant planting them there.","sentences":[{"en":"The boys were just then clustering round the large desk, climbing over the precentor’s footstool, opening the missal; and others on tiptoe were just about to venture into the confessional.","zh":"顽童们正兜着大讲经台，前推后拥，打开弥撒书，爬上唱诗班领队的凳子；有的蹑手蹑脚，眼看就要溜进告解座 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the priest suddenly distributed a shower of cuffs among them.","zh":"但是堂长冷不防赏了大家一顿巴掌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Seizing them by the collars of their coats, he lifted them from the ground, and deposited them on their knees on the stones of the choir, firmly, as if he meant planting them there.","zh":"他抓起他们的上衣领子，提到半空，使劲往唱经堂的石板地一按，让他们双膝下跪，像要将他们活活栽进地里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes,” said he, when he returned to Emma, unfolding his large cotton handkerchief, one corner of which he put between his teeth, “farmers are much to be pitied.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” said he, when he returned to Emma, unfolding his large cotton handkerchief, one corner of which he put between his teeth, “farmers are much to be pitied.”","zh":"他回到爱玛身边，摊开他的大印花布手帕，拿一个犄角塞到他的上下牙中间，说：“真的，庄稼人实在可怜！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Others, too,” she replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“Others, too,” she replied.","zh":"她回答道：“还有别人。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Assuredly. Town-labourers, for example.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Assuredly.","zh":"“当然！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Town-labourers, for example.”","zh":"比方说，城市的工人。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is not they—”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is not they—”","zh":"“我说的不是他们…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Pardon! I’ve there known poor mothers of families, virtuous women, I assure you, real saints, who wanted even bread.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Pardon!","zh":"“您说得对！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve there known poor mothers of families, virtuous women, I assure you, real saints, who wanted even bread.”","zh":"我就晓得有些可怜的母亲，身边一堆孩子，全是贤德妇女，您听我说，全是道地女圣人，连面包也没有。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But those,” replied Emma, and the corners of her mouth twitched as she spoke, “those, Monsieur le Cure, who have bread and have no—”","sentences":[{"en":"“But those,” replied Emma, and the corners of her mouth twitched as she spoke, “those, Monsieur le Cure, who have bread and have no—”","zh":"爱玛（说话之间，嘴角抽搐）接下去道：“不过有些人，有些人，堂长先生，有面包，却没有…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Fire in the winter,” said the priest.","sentences":[{"en":"“Fire in the winter,” said the priest.","zh":"教士道：“冬天没有火。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, what does that matter?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, what does that matter?”","zh":"“哎呀！有什么关系？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What! What does it matter? It seems to me that when one has firing and food—for, after all—”","sentences":[{"en":"“What!","zh":"“怎么！有什么关系？我觉得，一个人只要温、饱，就…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What does it matter?","zh":"因为，说到临了…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It seems to me that when one has firing and food—for, after all—”","zh":"”她叹气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My God! my God!” she sighed.","sentences":[{"en":"“My God! my God!” she sighed.","zh":"“我的上帝！我的上帝！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is indigestion, no doubt? You must get home, Madame Bovary; drink a little tea, that will strengthen you, or else a glass of fresh water with a little moist sugar.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is indigestion, no doubt?","zh":"他显出关心，走前一步，问道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You must get home, Madame Bovary; drink a little tea, that will strengthen you, or else a glass of fresh water with a little moist sugar.”","zh":"“您觉得难受？想必是，消化不良吧？包法利太太，您应当回家，喝一点茶；这您就有精神了；要不然，喝一杯清水，放一点红糖也行。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why?” And she looked like one awaking from a dream.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why?”","zh":"“为什么？”她的模样如同一个人做梦方醒。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And she looked like one awaking from a dream.","zh":"“为什么？”她的模样如同一个人做梦方醒。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Well, you see, you were putting your hand to your forehead. I thought you felt faint.” Then, bethinking himself, “But you were asking me something? What was it? I really don’t remember.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, you see, you were putting your hand to your forehead.","zh":"“因为您拿手搁在额头上。我以为您头晕。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought you felt faint.”","zh":"随后改变话题道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, bethinking himself, “But you were asking me something?","zh":"“不过您有话要问我来着？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was it?","zh":"到底是什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I really don’t remember.”","zh":"我忘记啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I? Nothing! nothing!” repeated Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“I? Nothing! nothing!” repeated Emma.","zh":"爱玛重复道：“我？没有…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the glance she cast round her slowly fell upon the old man in the cassock. They looked at one another face to face without speaking.","sentences":[{"en":"And the glance she cast round her slowly fell upon the old man in the cassock.","zh":"她的眼睛望着四周，慢悠悠落在穿法衣的老人身上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They looked at one another face to face without speaking.","zh":"他们面对面，不言不语，两个人互相打量，最后他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Then, Madame Bovary,” he said at last, “excuse me, but duty first, you know; I must look after my good-for-nothings. The first communion will soon be upon us, and I fear we shall be behind after all. So after Ascension Day I keep them recta an extra hour every Wednesday. Poor children! One cannot lead them too soon into the path of the Lord, as, moreover, he has himself recommended us to do by the mouth of his Divine Son. Good health to you, madame; my respects to your husband.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Then, Madame Bovary,” he said at last, “excuse me, but duty first, you know; I must look after my good-for-nothings.","zh":"“那么，包法利太太，原谅我，您知道，责任第一；我得伺候我那些宝贝家伙。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The first communion will soon be upon us, and I fear we shall be behind after all.","zh":"孩子们的第一次圣体瞻礼，眼看就要到了。我们又要临时抓瞎啦，我还真担心！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So after Ascension Day I keep them recta an extra hour every Wednesday.","zh":"所以从升天节起，我要他们准备每星期三多上一小时课。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Poor children!","zh":"所以从升天节起，我要他们准备每星期三多上一小时课。","scope":"group"},{"en":"One cannot lead them too soon into the path of the Lord, as, moreover, he has himself recommended us to do by the mouth of his Divine Son.","zh":"这些可怜的孩子！指点他们走上我主的大道，只有嫌晚，我主通过圣子的口，就是这样劝诫我们的…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good health to you, madame; my respects to your husband.”","zh":"希望您身体好，太太；替我向您丈夫致意。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he went into the church making a genuflexion as soon as he reached the door.","sentences":[{"en":"And he went into the church making a genuflexion as soon as he reached the door.","zh":"他走进教堂，才到门口，就做了一个下跪的姿势。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma saw him disappear between the double row of forms, walking with a heavy tread, his head a little bent over his shoulder, and with his two hands half-open behind him.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma saw him disappear between the double row of forms, walking with a heavy tread, his head a little bent over his shoulder, and with his two hands half-open behind him.","zh":"爱玛看他脚步沉重，头朝一边歪，两只手张开一半，手心朝外，在两排长凳中间不见了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she turned on her heel all of one piece, like a statue on a pivot, and went homewards. But the loud voice of the priest, the clear voices of the boys still reached her ears, and went on behind her.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she turned on her heel all of one piece, like a statue on a pivot, and went homewards.","zh":"她接着掉转脚跟，又笨又重，如同一座雕像顺着中轴挪动一样，走上回家的道路。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the loud voice of the priest, the clear voices of the boys still reached her ears, and went on behind her.","zh":"堂长严肃而又洪亮的声音、顽童们清脆的声音，依然传进她的耳朵，在背后继续响着：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are you a Christian?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you a Christian?”","zh":"“你是基督徒？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, I am a Christian.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, I am a Christian.”","zh":"“是，我是基督徒。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What is a Christian?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What is a Christian?”","zh":"“什么叫作基督徒？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“He who, being baptized-baptized-baptized—”","sentences":[{"en":"“He who, being baptized-baptized-baptized—”","zh":"“基督徒就是一个人领了洗…领了洗…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She went up the steps of the staircase holding on to the banisters, and when she was in her room threw herself into an arm-chair.","sentences":[{"en":"She went up the steps of the staircase holding on to the banisters, and when she was in her room threw herself into an arm-chair.","zh":"领了洗…领了洗。”她抓住栏杆，一步一步蹭上楼梯，走进卧室，倒在一张扶手椅里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The whitish light of the window-panes fell with soft undulations.","sentences":[{"en":"The whitish light of the window-panes fell with soft undulations.","zh":"玻璃窗映过来的夕照，漪澜成波，悠悠下降。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The furniture in its place seemed to have become more immobile, and to lose itself in the shadow as in an ocean of darkness. The fire was out, the clock went on ticking, and Emma vaguely marvelled at this calm of all things while within herself was such tumult. But little Berthe was there, between the window and the work-table, tottering on her knitted shoes, and trying to come to her mother to catch hold of the ends of her apron-strings.","sentences":[{"en":"The furniture in its place seemed to have become more immobile, and to lose itself in the shadow as in an ocean of darkness.","zh":"家具待在原来地方，似乎越发死板了，阴影笼罩，好像沉入漆黑的大洋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The fire was out, the clock went on ticking, and Emma vaguely marvelled at this calm of all things while within herself was such tumult.","zh":"壁炉熄了，钟总在敲打，爱玛心潮翻滚，看见事物这样安静，感到说不出的惊愕。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But little Berthe was there, between the window and the work-table, tottering on her knitted shoes, and trying to come to her mother to catch hold of the ends of her apron-strings.","zh":"但是小白尔特站在窗户和女红桌子中间，穿着编织的小靴，摇摇晃晃，打算来到母亲跟前，揪她的围裙带子。母亲拿手一推，说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Leave me alone,” said the latter, putting her from her with her hand.","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave me alone,” said the latter, putting her from her with her hand.","zh":"“走开！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The little girl soon came up closer against her knees, and leaning on them with her arms, she looked up with her large blue eyes, while a small thread of pure saliva dribbled from her lips on to the silk apron.","sentences":[{"en":"The little girl soon came up closer against her knees, and leaning on them with her arms, she looked up with her large blue eyes, while a small thread of pure saliva dribbled from her lips on to the silk apron.","zh":"没有多久，小姑娘又来了，越发靠近母亲的膝盖；她拿胳膊支在上面，朝她仰起她的大蓝眼睛，嘴里流下一道晶莹的口水，滴在绸围裙上。少妇烦了，重复道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Leave me alone,” repeated the young woman quite irritably.","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave me alone,” repeated the young woman quite irritably.","zh":"“走开！”小孩子望着她的脸，一害怕，哭起来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her face frightened the child, who began to scream.","sentences":[{"en":"Her face frightened the child, who began to scream.","zh":"她拿胳膊肘把孩子往外一搡，道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Will you leave me alone?” she said, pushing her with her elbow.","sentences":[{"en":"“Will you leave me alone?” she said, pushing her with her elbow.","zh":"“哎呀！倒是走开啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Berthe fell at the foot of the drawers against the brass handle, cutting her cheek, which began to bleed, against it. Madame Bovary sprang to lift her up, broke the bell-rope, called for the servant with all her might, and she was just going to curse herself when Charles appeared. It was the dinner-hour; he had come home.","sentences":[{"en":"Berthe fell at the foot of the drawers against the brass handle, cutting her cheek, which began to bleed, against it.","zh":"白尔特一跤掼在五斗柜前头，脸蛋碰到抽屉的铜拉手，划破了，流血。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Bovary sprang to lift her up, broke the bell-rope, called for the servant with all her might, and she was just going to curse herself when Charles appeared.","zh":"包法利夫人赶上前去，扶起她来，拼命拉铃叫用人，把铃绳都揪断了，正要咒骂自己，就见查理出现了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the dinner-hour; he had come home.","zh":"晚饭时辰到了，他回转家来。爱玛不动声色地说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Look, dear!” said Emma, in a calm voice, “the little one fell down while she was playing, and has hurt herself.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look, dear!” said Emma, in a calm voice, “the little one fell down while she was playing, and has hurt herself.”","zh":"“看呀，亲爱的朋友，小东西玩着玩着，就在地上摔破了脸。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles reassured her; the case was not a serious one, and he went for some sticking plaster.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles reassured her; the case was not a serious one, and he went for some sticking plaster.","zh":"查理叫她放心，情形并不严重，说完话，就找橡皮膏去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary did not go downstairs to the dining-room; she wished to remain alone to look after the child. Then watching her sleep, the little anxiety she felt gradually wore off, and she seemed very stupid to herself, and very good to have been so worried just now at so little. Berthe, in fact, no longer sobbed.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary did not go downstairs to the dining-room; she wished to remain alone to look after the child.","zh":"包法利夫人愿意一个人看守她的孩子，没有下楼用饭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then watching her sleep, the little anxiety she felt gradually wore off, and she seemed very stupid to herself, and very good to have been so worried just now at so little.","zh":"她看她睡熟了，这才一点一点放下心来。这么一丁点小事，她就慌了神，回想起来，觉得自己又善良，又傻气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Berthe, in fact, no longer sobbed.","zh":"的确，白尔特已经不哭了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her breathing now imperceptibly raised the cotton covering. Big tears lay in the corner of the half-closed eyelids, through whose lashes one could see two pale sunken pupils; the plaster stuck on her cheek drew the skin obliquely.","sentences":[{"en":"Her breathing now imperceptibly raised the cotton covering.","zh":"现在已经看不大出她的呼吸掀动棉被。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Big tears lay in the corner of the half-closed eyelids, through whose lashes one could see two pale sunken pupils; the plaster stuck on her cheek drew the skin obliquely.","zh":"大颗泪珠停在眼角，眼皮闭了一半，睫毛当中，露出两个深黝黝的没有光彩的瞳孔。橡皮膏贴在脸上，紧绷绷的，把脸蛋拉歪了。爱玛寻思：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is very strange,” thought Emma, “how ugly this child is!”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is very strange,” thought Emma, “how ugly this child is!”","zh":"“也真怪，这孩子多丑！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When at eleven o’clock Charles came back from the chemist’s shop, whither he had gone after dinner to return the remainder of the sticking-plaster, he found his wife standing by the cradle.","sentences":[{"en":"When at eleven o’clock Charles came back from the chemist’s shop, whither he had gone after dinner to return the remainder of the sticking-plaster, he found his wife standing by the cradle.","zh":"夜里十一点钟，查理从药房回来（他饭后去归还用剩下来的橡皮膏），发现太太站在摇篮一旁。他吻她的额头道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I assure you it’s nothing.” he said, kissing her on the forehead. “Don’t worry, my poor darling; you will make yourself ill.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I assure you it’s nothing.” he said, kissing her on the forehead.","zh":"“我不是叫你放心，说不碍事么；别心焦，小可怜，你这样会生病的！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Don’t worry, my poor darling; you will make yourself ill.”","zh":"“我不是叫你放心，说不碍事么；别心焦，小可怜，你这样会生病的！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He had stayed a long time at the chemist’s. Although he had not seemed much moved, Homais, nevertheless, had exerted himself to buoy him up, to “keep up his spirits.” Then they had talked of the various dangers that threaten childhood, of the carelessness of servants. Madame Homais knew something of it, having still upon her chest the marks left by a basin full of soup that a cook had formerly dropped on her pinafore, and her good parents took no end of trouble for her. The knives were not sharpened, nor the floors waxed; there were iron gratings to the windows and strong bars across the fireplace; the little Homais, in spite of their spirit, could not stir without someone watching them; at the slightest cold their father stuffed them with pectorals; and until they were turned four they all, without pity, had to wear wadded head-protectors. This, it is true, was a fancy of Madame Homais’; her husband was inwardly afflicted at it. Fearing the possible consequences of such compression to the intellectual organs. He even went so far as to say to her, “Do you want to make Caribs or Botocudos of them?”","sentences":[{"en":"He had stayed a long time at the chemist’s.","zh":"原来他在药房待了许久。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Although he had not seemed much moved, Homais, nevertheless, had exerted himself to buoy him up, to “keep up his spirits.”","zh":"他并没有显出很着急的样子，可是郝麦先生照样鼓舞他，要他打起精神来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then they had talked of the various dangers that threaten childhood, of the carelessness of servants.","zh":"于是他们说起种种威胁儿童的危险和用人的鲁莽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Homais knew something of it, having still upon her chest the marks left by a basin full of soup that a cook had formerly dropped on her pinafore, and her good parents took no end of trouble for her.","zh":"郝麦夫人知道这是怎么一回事：她小的时候，一个厨娘把一碗汤，打翻在她的小围嘴上，现在胸脯还有痕迹。所以她慈爱的双亲，也就处处当心，小刀从来不磨，地板从来不打蜡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The knives were not sharpened, nor the floors waxed; there were iron gratings to the windows and strong bars across the fireplace; the little Homais, in spite of their spirit, could not stir without someone watching them; at the slightest cold their father stuffed them with pectorals; and until they were turned four they all, without pity, had to wear wadded head-protectors.","zh":"窗户装上铁栅，壁炉前头安上结实的护栏。郝麦的小孩子，别看是无拘无束的，也一动就有人跟在后头；一点点伤风，父亲就灌他们药汁，直到四岁多了，也不可怜他们，还让他们一人戴一顶棉箍 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This, it is true, was a fancy of Madame Homais’; her husband was inwardly afflicted at it.","zh":"说实话，这是郝麦夫人的怪主意；她的丈夫私下发愁，怕戴久了，可能理智器官受伤，所以不免脱口冲她说：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Fearing the possible consequences of such compression to the intellectual organs.","zh":"说实话，这是郝麦夫人的怪主意；她的丈夫私下发愁，怕戴久了，可能理智器官受伤，所以不免脱口冲她说：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He even went so far as to say to her, “Do you want to make Caribs or Botocudos of them?”","zh":"“难道你真要他们当加勒比人或者包陶库道斯人？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles, however, had several times tried to interrupt the conversation. “I should like to speak to you,” he had whispered in the clerk’s ear, who went upstairs in front of him.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles, however, had several times tried to interrupt the conversation.","zh":"其实，查理有好几次，试着想打断谈话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I should like to speak to you,” he had whispered in the clerk’s ear, who went upstairs in front of him.","zh":"文书正要上楼，走在前头，查理附耳低声对他说：“我想同您谈谈。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Can he suspect anything?” Léon asked himself. His heart beat, and he racked his brain with surmises.","sentences":[{"en":"“Can he suspect anything?”","zh":"赖昂心跳了，左猜右想，暗自纳闷：难道他看出什么破绽来啦？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Léon asked himself.","zh":"赖昂心跳了，左猜右想，暗自纳闷：难道他看出什么破绽来啦？","scope":"group"},{"en":"His heart beat, and he racked his brain with surmises.","zh":"赖昂心跳了，左猜右想，暗自纳闷：难道他看出什么破绽来啦？","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At last, Charles, having shut the door, asked him to see himself what would be the price at Rouen of a fine daguerreotypes. It was a sentimental surprise he intended for his wife, a delicate attention—his portrait in a frock-coat. But he wanted first to know “how much it would be.” The inquiries would not put Monsieur Léon out, since he went to town almost every week.","sentences":[{"en":"At last, Charles, having shut the door, asked him to see himself what would be the price at Rouen of a fine daguerreotypes.","zh":"查理最后关上门，央他到鲁昂打听一下达盖尔摄影法 照一张相要多少钱；他想照一张青燕尾服肖像，送给他的太太，这是一件表示感情的礼物，一种细心的体贴。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was a sentimental surprise he intended for his wife, a delicate attention—his portrait in a frock-coat.","zh":"查理最后关上门，央他到鲁昂打听一下达盖尔摄影法 照一张相要多少钱；他想照一张青燕尾服肖像，送给他的太太，这是一件表示感情的礼物，一种细心的体贴。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But he wanted first to know “how much it would be.”","zh":"不过他愿意先知道价钱；这大概不会给赖昂添太多麻烦，因为他差不多每星期进一趟城。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The inquiries would not put Monsieur Léon out, since he went to town almost every week.","zh":"不过他愿意先知道价钱；这大概不会给赖昂添太多麻烦，因为他差不多每星期进一趟城。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Why? Monsieur Homais suspected some “young man’s affair” at the bottom of it, an intrigue. But he was mistaken. Léon was after no love-making. He was sadder than ever, as Madame Lefrancois saw from the amount of food he left on his plate. To find out more about it she questioned the tax-collector. Binet answered roughly that he “wasn’t paid by the police.”","sentences":[{"en":"Why?","zh":"进城干什么？郝麦疑心他年轻荒唐，搞女人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Homais suspected some “young man’s affair” at the bottom of it, an intrigue.","zh":"进城干什么？郝麦疑心他年轻荒唐，搞女人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But he was mistaken.","zh":"不过他猜错了；赖昂并不拈花惹草。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Léon was after no love-making.","zh":"不过他猜错了；赖昂并不拈花惹草。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was sadder than ever, as Madame Lefrancois saw from the amount of food he left on his plate.","zh":"他反而更忧郁了，留在盘里的菜，现在也多起来了，勒弗朗索瓦太太一眼就看出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To find out more about it she questioned the tax-collector.","zh":"她想知道底细，问税务员；毕耐显出一副傲慢的样子，粗声粗气回答道“警察没有支薪水”给他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Binet answered roughly that he “wasn’t paid by the police.”","zh":"她想知道底细，问税务员；毕耐显出一副傲慢的样子，粗声粗气回答道“警察没有支薪水”给他。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"All the same, his companion seemed very strange to him, for Léon often threw himself back in his chair, and stretching out his arms, complained vaguely of life.","sentences":[{"en":"All the same, his companion seemed very strange to him, for Léon often threw himself back in his chair, and stretching out his arms, complained vaguely of life.","zh":"可是他觉得他的餐伴十分古怪；因为赖昂常常摊开胳膊，人朝椅背一仰，泛泛抱怨人生。税务员说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It’s because you don’t take enough recreation,” said the collector.","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s because you don’t take enough recreation,” said the collector.","zh":"“这是因为您消遣不够。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What recreation?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What recreation?”","zh":"“什么消遣？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If I were you I’d have a lathe.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If I were you I’d have a lathe.”","zh":"“我要是您呀，就来一台旋床！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But I don’t know how to turn,” answered the clerk.","sentences":[{"en":"“But I don’t know how to turn,” answered the clerk.","zh":"文书回答：“可是我不会旋东西。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! that’s true,” said the other, rubbing his chin with an air of mingled contempt and satisfaction.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! that’s true,” said the other, rubbing his chin with an air of mingled contempt and satisfaction.","zh":"“这倒是真的！”对方摸摸下巴，显出蔑视而又得意的神情。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon was weary of loving without any result; moreover he was beginning to feel that depression caused by the repetition of the same kind of life, when no interest inspires and no hope sustains it. He was so bored with Yonville and its inhabitants, that the sight of certain persons, of certain houses, irritated him beyond endurance; and the chemist, good fellow though he was, was becoming absolutely unbearable to him. Yet the prospect of a new condition of life frightened as much as it seduced him.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon was weary of loving without any result; moreover he was beginning to feel that depression caused by the repetition of the same kind of life, when no interest inspires and no hope sustains it.","zh":"毫无结果的爱情，赖昂疲倦了；生活千篇一律，没有乐趣，没有希望，他开始感到苦闷。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was so bored with Yonville and its inhabitants, that the sight of certain persons, of certain houses, irritated him beyond endurance; and the chemist, good fellow though he was, was becoming absolutely unbearable to him.","zh":"他讨厌永镇和永镇人，有些人、有些房屋，他一看就有气，简直耐不下去；药剂师为人再好，他也忍受不了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yet the prospect of a new condition of life frightened as much as it seduced him.","zh":"另一方面，改变环境的远景固然引诱他，却也使他畏惧。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This apprehension soon changed into impatience, and then Paris from afar sounded its fanfare of masked balls with the laugh of grisettes. As he was to finish reading there, why not set out at once? What prevented him? And he began making home-preparations; he arranged his occupations beforehand. He furnished in his head an apartment. He would lead an artist’s life there! He would take lessons on the guitar! He would have a dressing-gown, a Basque cap, blue velvet slippers! He even already was admiring two crossed foils over his chimney-piece, with a death’s head on the guitar above them.","sentences":[{"en":"This apprehension soon changed into impatience, and then Paris from afar sounded its fanfare of masked balls with the laugh of grisettes.","zh":"害怕很快变成了烦躁：巴黎遥遥向他招手，化装舞会的铜管乐吹响了，姑娘们的笑声起来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As he was to finish reading there, why not set out at once?","zh":"他既然要到那边读完法科，为什么不去？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What prevented him?","zh":"谁拦着他？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he began making home-preparations; he arranged his occupations beforehand.","zh":"他心里开始筹划，预作远游期间的生活安排。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He furnished in his head an apartment.","zh":"他设想自己那边有一间屋子，布置着家具。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He would lead an artist’s life there!","zh":"他要在那边过艺术家生活！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He would take lessons on the guitar!","zh":"他要在那边学六弦琴！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He would have a dressing-gown, a Basque cap, blue velvet slippers!","zh":"他要穿一件室内穿的长便袍，戴一顶巴斯克人戴的圆便帽， 拖一双蓝绒拖鞋！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He even already was admiring two crossed foils over his chimney-piece, with a death’s head on the guitar above them.","zh":"壁炉墙上交叉插着两把花剑，再往高去，是六弦琴和一颗死人脑壳，而且他已然在赞赏了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The difficulty was the consent of his mother; nothing, however, seemed more reasonable. Even his employer advised him to go to some other chambers where he could advance more rapidly. Taking a middle course, then, Léon looked for some place as second clerk at Rouen; found none, and at last wrote his mother a long letter full of details, in which he set forth the reasons for going to live at Paris immediately. She consented.","sentences":[{"en":"The difficulty was the consent of his mother; nothing, however, seemed more reasonable.","zh":"困难在于母亲是否同意；不过，看上去，也没有比这再合理的了。连他的老板也劝他换事务所，谋求发展。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Even his employer advised him to go to some other chambers where he could advance more rapidly.","zh":"困难在于母亲是否同意；不过，看上去，也没有比这再合理的了。连他的老板也劝他换事务所，谋求发展。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Taking a middle course, then, Léon looked for some place as second clerk at Rouen; found none, and at last wrote his mother a long letter full of details, in which he set forth the reasons for going to live at Paris immediately.","zh":"于是赖昂采取折中办法，到鲁昂谋一个二等文书的职位，但是没有成功，最后他给母亲写了一封长信，详详细细，说明他立刻要去巴黎的理由。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She consented.","zh":"她同意了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He did not hurry. Every day for a month Hivert carried boxes, valises, parcels for him from Yonville to Rouen and from Rouen to Yonville; and when Léon had packed up his wardrobe, had his three arm-chairs restuffed, bought a stock of neckties, in a word, had made more preparations than for a voyage around the world, he put it off from week to week, until he received a second letter from his mother urging him to leave, since he wanted to pass his examination before the vacation.","sentences":[{"en":"He did not hurry.","zh":"他并不急着要去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Every day for a month Hivert carried boxes, valises, parcels for him from Yonville to Rouen and from Rouen to Yonville; and when Léon had packed up his wardrobe, had his three arm-chairs restuffed, bought a stock of neckties, in a word, had made more preparations than for a voyage around the world, he put it off from week to week, until he received a second letter from his mother urging him to leave, since he wanted to pass his examination before the vacation.","zh":"足有一个月，伊韦尔每天从永镇到鲁昂，从鲁昂到永镇，帮他运送箱箧包裹。赖昂添置衣服，修理三只扶手椅，选购大批手绢，总而言之，准备的东西，周游世界也嫌多，但是他一星期又一星期，拖延行期，直到后来，母亲两次来信，催他动身，既然他希望在放假之前通过考试。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When the moment for the farewells had come, Madame Homais wept, Justin sobbed; Homais, as a man of nerve, concealed his emotion; he wished to carry his friend’s overcoat himself as far as the gate of the notary, who was taking Léon to Rouen in his carriage.","sentences":[{"en":"When the moment for the farewells had come, Madame Homais wept, Justin sobbed; Homais, as a man of nerve, concealed his emotion; he wished to carry his friend’s overcoat himself as far as the gate of the notary, who was taking Léon to Rouen in his carriage.","zh":"辞行的时间到了，郝麦夫人啼哭，朱斯丹呜咽，郝麦是男子汉，藏起悲痛，要亲自拿着朋友的大衣，送到公证人门口。公证人乘自己的车，送赖昂到鲁昂去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The latter had just time to bid farewell to Monsieur Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"The latter had just time to bid farewell to Monsieur Bovary.","zh":"留下的时间，正够向包法利先生告别。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When he reached the head of the stairs, he stopped, he was so out of breath. As he came in, Madame Bovary arose hurriedly.","sentences":[{"en":"When he reached the head of the stairs, he stopped, he was so out of breath.","zh":"走到楼梯高头，他觉得自己气喘吁吁，只好停步。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As he came in, Madame Bovary arose hurriedly.","zh":"他一进来，包法利夫人连忙立起。赖昂道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is I again!” said Léon.","sentences":[{"en":"“It is I again!” said Léon.","zh":"“我又来啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I was sure of it!”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was sure of it!”","zh":"“我早料到了！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She bit her lips, and a rush of blood flowing under her skin made her red from the roots of her hair to the top of her collar. She remained standing, leaning with her shoulder against the wainscot.","sentences":[{"en":"She bit her lips, and a rush of blood flowing under her skin made her red from the roots of her hair to the top of her collar.","zh":"她咬紧嘴唇，血往上涌，脸一直红到耳朵梢。她站直了，肩膀靠住墙壁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She remained standing, leaning with her shoulder against the wainscot.","zh":"他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The doctor is not here?” he went on.","sentences":[{"en":"“The doctor is not here?” he went on.","zh":"“先生不在家？”“他出去了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“He is out.” She repeated, “He is out.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He is out.”","zh":"她又说一遍：“他出去了。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She repeated, “He is out.”","zh":"她又说一遍：“他出去了。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then there was silence. They looked at one another and their thoughts, confounded in the same agony, clung close together like two throbbing breasts.","sentences":[{"en":"Then there was silence.","zh":"于是你望我，我望你，沉默下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They looked at one another and their thoughts, confounded in the same agony, clung close together like two throbbing breasts.","zh":"他们的思想，感到同一痛苦，好像两个上下起伏的胸脯，紧紧搂在一起。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I should like to kiss Berthe,” said Léon.","sentences":[{"en":"“I should like to kiss Berthe,” said Léon.","zh":"赖昂道：“我挺想亲亲白尔特。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma went down a few steps and called Félicité.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma went down a few steps and called Félicité.","zh":"爱玛走下几级楼梯，呼唤全福。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He threw one long look around him that took in the walls, the decorations, the fireplace, as if to penetrate everything, carry away everything. But she returned, and the servant brought Berthe, who was swinging a windmill roof downwards at the end of a string. Léon kissed her several times on the neck.","sentences":[{"en":"He threw one long look around him that took in the walls, the decorations, the fireplace, as if to penetrate everything, carry away everything.","zh":"他向周围迅速扫视，一眼望过墙壁、摆设架、壁炉，依依不舍，像是想要钻进一切，带走一切。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she returned, and the servant brought Berthe, who was swinging a windmill roof downwards at the end of a string.","zh":"她又进来了，女用人带着白尔特。孩子甩动一根绳子，绳子一头是一架风车，尖头朝下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Léon kissed her several times on the neck.","zh":"赖昂吻了几遍她的颈项。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Good-bye, poor child! good-bye, dear little one! good-bye!” And he gave her back to her mother.","sentences":[{"en":"“Good-bye, poor child! good-bye, dear little one! good-bye!”","zh":"“再会，好孩子！再会，小宝贝，再会！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he gave her back to her mother.","zh":"他把她交还给她母亲。后者说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Take her away,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Take her away,” she said.","zh":"“带她下楼吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They remained alone—Madame Bovary, her back turned, her face pressed against a window-pane; Léon held his cap in his hand, knocking it softly against his thigh.","sentences":[{"en":"They remained alone—Madame Bovary, her back turned, her face pressed against a window-pane; Léon held his cap in his hand, knocking it softly against his thigh.","zh":"就留下他们两个人了。包法利夫人背过脸去，贴住一块窗玻璃；赖昂拿起他的便帽，轻轻拍打臀部。爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is going to rain,” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“It is going to rain,” said Emma.","zh":"“就要下雨。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I have a cloak,” he answered.","sentences":[{"en":"“I have a cloak,” he answered.","zh":"他回答：“我有斗篷。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!”","zh":"“啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She turned around, her chin lowered, her forehead bent forward.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned around, her chin lowered, her forehead bent forward.","zh":"她转回身来，额头向前，下巴朝下。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The light fell on it as on a piece of marble, to the curve of the eyebrows, without one’s being able to guess what Emma was seeing on the horizon or what she was thinking within herself.","sentences":[{"en":"The light fell on it as on a piece of marble, to the curve of the eyebrows, without one’s being able to guess what Emma was seeing on the horizon or what she was thinking within herself.","zh":"阳光掠过额头，照到眉毛的弧线，犹如一块大理石，猜不出爱玛望天边望见了什么，也猜不出她心里到底在想什么。他叹气道：“好，再会！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, good-bye,” he sighed.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, good-bye,” he sighed.","zh":"头骤然一扬，她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She raised her head with a quick movement.","sentences":[{"en":"She raised her head with a quick movement.","zh":"“是啊，再会…您走吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, good-bye—go!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, good-bye—go!”","zh":"两个人全朝前走，他伸出手，她迟疑了一下，这才伸过手去，勉强笑着说：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"They advanced towards each other; he held out his hand; she hesitated.","sentences":[{"en":"They advanced towards each other; he held out his hand; she hesitated.","zh":"两个人全朝前走，他伸出手，她迟疑了一下，这才伸过手去，勉强笑着说：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“In the English fashion, then,” she said, giving her own hand wholly to him, and forcing a laugh.","sentences":[{"en":"“In the English fashion, then,” she said, giving her own hand wholly to him, and forcing a laugh.","zh":"“照英国人规矩。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon felt it between his fingers, and the very essence of all his being seemed to pass down into that moist palm. Then he opened his hand; their eyes met again, and he disappeared.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon felt it between his fingers, and the very essence of all his being seemed to pass down into that moist palm.","zh":"赖昂觉出他的手指握住她的手，似乎他的全部生命，顺着胳膊，集中在这只湿津津的手心。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he opened his hand; their eyes met again, and he disappeared.","zh":"赖昂觉出他的手指握住她的手，似乎他的全部生命，顺着胳膊，集中在这只湿津津的手心。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"When he reached the market-place, he stopped and hid behind a pillar to look for the last time at this white house with the four green blinds. He thought he saw a shadow behind the window in the room; but the curtain, sliding along the pole as though no one were touching it, slowly opened its long oblique folds that spread out with a single movement, and thus hung straight and motionless as a plaster wall. Léon set off running.","sentences":[{"en":"When he reached the market-place, he stopped and hid behind a pillar to look for the last time at this white house with the four green blinds.","zh":"他随后松开手；他们的眼睛又遇到一起；他走了。他在菜场站住，躲到柱子后头，最后一次，望望这所白房子和它的四块绿色窗帘。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He thought he saw a shadow behind the window in the room; but the curtain, sliding along the pole as though no one were touching it, slowly opened its long oblique folds that spread out with a single movement, and thus hung straight and motionless as a plaster wall.","zh":"他依稀望见卧室窗口有一个人影；但是窗幔似乎没有人碰，就离开钩子，扯斜的长褶，慢慢移动，一下子就全平整了，比一堵石灰墙还要硬挺。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Léon set off running.","zh":"赖昂只好跑开。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"From afar he saw his employer’s gig in the road, and by it a man in a coarse apron holding the horse. Homais and Monsieur Guillaumin were talking. They were waiting for him.","sentences":[{"en":"From afar he saw his employer’s gig in the road, and by it a man in a coarse apron holding the horse.","zh":"他远远望见老板的轻便马车，停在大路，旁边有一个男人，前胸系一条粗布围裙，手拉住马。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais and Monsieur Guillaumin were talking.","zh":"郝麦和居由曼先生一边闲谈，一边在等他来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were waiting for him.","zh":"郝麦和居由曼先生一边闲谈，一边在等他来。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Embrace me,” said the druggist with tears in his eyes. “Here is your coat, my good friend. Mind the cold; take care of yourself; look after yourself.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Embrace me,” said the druggist with tears in his eyes.","zh":"药剂师眼泪汪汪，说：“搂搂我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Here is your coat, my good friend.","zh":"这是你的大衣，我的好朋友，当心别着凉！保重身体！凡事经心！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Mind the cold; take care of yourself; look after yourself.”","zh":"这是你的大衣，我的好朋友，当心别着凉！保重身体！凡事经心！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Come, Léon, jump in,” said the notary.","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, Léon, jump in,” said the notary.","zh":"公证人道：“来吧，赖昂，上车！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais bent over the splash-board, and in a voice broken by sobs uttered these three sad words—","sentences":[{"en":"Homais bent over the splash-board, and in a voice broken by sobs uttered these three sad words—","zh":"郝麦俯在防泥板上，声音夹杂呜咽，好不容易说出这四个伤心的字眼：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“A pleasant journey!”","sentences":[{"en":"“A pleasant journey!”","zh":"“一路平安！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Good-night,” said Monsieur Guillaumin. “Give him his head.” They set out, and Homais went back.","sentences":[{"en":"“Good-night,” said Monsieur Guillaumin.","zh":"居由曼先生回答道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Give him his head.”","zh":"“晚安。放马！走！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They set out, and Homais went back.","zh":"他们出发了，郝麦也回家去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary had opened her window overlooking the garden and watched the clouds. They gathered around the sunset on the side of Rouen and then swiftly rolled back their black columns, behind which the great rays of the sun looked out like the golden arrows of a suspended trophy, while the rest of the empty heavens was white as porcelain. But a gust of wind bowed the poplars, and suddenly the rain fell; it pattered against the green leaves.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary had opened her window overlooking the garden and watched the clouds.","zh":"包法利夫人打开面向花园的窗户，眺望浮云。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They gathered around the sunset on the side of Rouen and then swiftly rolled back their black columns, behind which the great rays of the sun looked out like the golden arrows of a suspended trophy, while the rest of the empty heavens was white as porcelain.","zh":"西边鲁昂那个方向，起了乌云，波涛汹涌，前推后拥，太阳放出长线，却又金箭一般，赶过云头，同时天空别的地方，空空落落，如同瓷器一般白净。一阵狂风吹来，白杨弯腰，骤雨急降，滴滴答答，敲打绿叶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But a gust of wind bowed the poplars, and suddenly the rain fell; it pattered against the green leaves.","zh":"太阳跟着又出来，母鸡啼叫，麻雀在湿漉漉的小树丛拍打翅膀，沙地上一摊摊积水朝低处流，带走一棵合欢树粉红色的落花。她寻思：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then the sun reappeared, the hens clucked, sparrows shook their wings in the damp thickets, and the pools of water on the gravel as they flowed away carried off the pink flowers of an acacia.","sentences":[{"en":"Then the sun reappeared, the hens clucked, sparrows shook their wings in the damp thickets, and the pools of water on the gravel as they flowed away carried off the pink flowers of an acacia.","zh":"他一定已经走远啦！”郝麦先生照旧在六点半钟用晚饭的时间过来。他坐下来道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! how far off he must be already!” she thought.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! how far off he must be already!” she thought.","zh":"“好！我们的年轻人，这会儿该上船了吧？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Homais, as usual, came at half-past six during dinner.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Homais, as usual, came at half-past six during dinner.","zh":"医生回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well,” said he, “so we’ve sent off our young friend!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well,” said he, “so we’ve sent off our young friend!”","zh":"“大概吧！”然后他在椅子上转过身子：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“So it seems,” replied the doctor. Then turning on his chair; “Any news at home?”","sentences":[{"en":"“So it seems,” replied the doctor.","zh":"“府上没有什么？”“没有什么。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then turning on his chair; “Any news at home?”","zh":"也就是我太太，今天下午，有一点难过。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Nothing much. Only my wife was a little moved this afternoon. You know women—a nothing upsets them, especially my wife. And we should be wrong to object to that, since their nervous organization is much more malleable than ours.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nothing much.","zh":"也就是我太太，今天下午，有一点难过。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Only my wife was a little moved this afternoon.","zh":"您知道女人们，芝麻大的小事，也架不住！尤其是我那一口子！","scope":"group"},{"en":"You know women—a nothing upsets them, especially my wife.","zh":"您知道女人们，芝麻大的小事，也架不住！尤其是我那一口子！","scope":"group"},{"en":"And we should be wrong to object to that, since their nervous organization is much more malleable than ours.”","zh":"这也不能怪她们，因为她们的脑神经组织，本来就比我们脆弱。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Poor Léon!” said Charles. “How will he live at Paris? Will he get used to it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Poor Léon!” said Charles.","zh":"查理道：“可怜的赖昂！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“How will he live at Paris?","zh":"他在巴黎怎么过活！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Will he get used to it?”","zh":"他待得惯吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary sighed.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary sighed.","zh":"包法利夫人叹了一口气。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Get along!” said the chemist, smacking his lips. “The outings at restaurants, the masked balls, the champagne—all that’ll be jolly enough, I assure you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Get along!” said the chemist, smacking his lips.","zh":"药剂师打了个响舌，道：“哪儿的话！聚餐游戏呀！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“The outings at restaurants, the masked balls, the champagne—all that’ll be jolly enough, I assure you.”","zh":"化装舞会呀！香槟酒呀！告诉您，样样称心！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I don’t think he’ll go wrong,” objected Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t think he’ll go wrong,” objected Bovary.","zh":"包法利反驳道：“我不相信他会胡闹。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Nor do I,” said Monsieur Homais quickly; “although he’ll have to do like the rest for fear of passing for a Jesuit. And you don’t know what a life those dogs lead in the Latin quarter with actresses. Besides, students are thought a great deal of in Paris. Provided they have a few accomplishments, they are received in the best society; there are even ladies of the Faubourg Saint-Germain who fall in love with them, which subsequently furnishes them opportunities for making very good matches.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nor do I,” said Monsieur Homais quickly; “although he’ll have to do like the rest for fear of passing for a Jesuit.","zh":"郝麦先生连忙接下去道：“我也不相信！不过，除非他不怕别人把他看成耶稣会会士 ，否则，他将来就得同流合污。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And you don’t know what a life those dogs lead in the Latin quarter with actresses.","zh":"您不知道这些小荒唐鬼在拉丁区 ，和女戏子过的是什么生活！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, students are thought a great deal of in Paris.","zh":"再说，学生在巴黎很吃香。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Provided they have a few accomplishments, they are received in the best society; there are even ladies of the Faubourg Saint-Germain who fall in love with them, which subsequently furnishes them opportunities for making very good matches.”","zh":"只要他们有一点点作乐的才分，上流社会就欢迎他们，甚至圣日耳曼区 的贵妇们也爱他们，机会到手，岂可错过，他们自然就当上了豪门贵婿。”医生道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But,” said the doctor, “I fear for him that down there—”","sentences":[{"en":"“But,” said the doctor, “I fear for him that down there—”","zh":"“不过我担心他…在那边…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are right,” interrupted the chemist; “that is the reverse of the medal. And one is constantly obliged to keep one’s hand in one’s pocket there. Thus, we will suppose you are in a public garden. An individual presents himself, well dressed, even wearing an order, and whom one would take for a diplomatist. He approaches you, he insinuates himself; offers you a pinch of snuff, or picks up your hat. Then you become more intimate; he takes you to a cafe, invites you to his country-house, introduces you, between two drinks, to all sorts of people; and three-fourths of the time it’s only to plunder your watch or lead you into some pernicious step.","sentences":[{"en":"“You are right,” interrupted the chemist; “that is the reverse of the medal.","zh":"“您说得对，事情还有另一面！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And one is constantly obliged to keep one’s hand in one’s pocket there.","zh":"人到了那边，不得不老拿手攥住腰包。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus, we will suppose you are in a public garden.","zh":"好比说吧，您在一座公园里，来了一个陌生人，衣着考究，甚至挂着勋章，您以为是一位外交官；他走到您跟前；你们聊起来了，他摸熟您的脾气，请您吸鼻烟，或者替您拾帽子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"An individual presents himself, well dressed, even wearing an order, and whom one would take for a diplomatist.","zh":"好比说吧，您在一座公园里，来了一个陌生人，衣着考究，甚至挂着勋章，您以为是一位外交官；他走到您跟前；你们聊起来了，他摸熟您的脾气，请您吸鼻烟，或者替您拾帽子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He approaches you, he insinuates himself; offers you a pinch of snuff, or picks up your hat.","zh":"好比说吧，您在一座公园里，来了一个陌生人，衣着考究，甚至挂着勋章，您以为是一位外交官；他走到您跟前；你们聊起来了，他摸熟您的脾气，请您吸鼻烟，或者替您拾帽子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then you become more intimate; he takes you to a cafe, invites you to his country-house, introduces you, between two drinks, to all sorts of people; and three-fourths of the time it’s only to plunder your watch or lead you into some pernicious step.","zh":"后来两个人谈出了交情，他带您上咖啡馆，请您去他的别墅，喝酒之间，介绍各色人等和您相识，而十之八九，不是为了抢您的钱袋，就是拉您去干坏事。”查理回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That is true,” said Charles; “but I was thinking especially of illnesses—of typhoid fever, for example, that attacks students from the provinces.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That is true,” said Charles; “but I was thinking especially of illnesses—of typhoid fever, for example, that attacks students from the provinces.”","zh":"“话是对的；不过我担心的，倒是生病，譬如，伤寒，外省去的学生就爱害这种病。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma shuddered.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma shuddered.","zh":"爱玛不寒而栗了。药剂师继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Because of the change of regimen,” continued the chemist, “and of the perturbation that results therefrom in the whole system. And then the water at Paris, don’t you know! The dishes at restaurants, all the spiced food, end by heating the blood, and are not worth, whatever people may say of them, a good soup. For my own part, I have always preferred plain living; it is more healthy. So when I was studying pharmacy at Rouen, I boarded in a boarding house; I dined with the professors.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Because of the change of regimen,” continued the chemist, “and of the perturbation that results therefrom in the whole system.","zh":"“这是由于饮食改变，人的整个机体产生紊乱的缘故。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then the water at Paris, don’t you know!","zh":"再说，巴黎的水，您晓得是怎么一回事！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The dishes at restaurants, all the spiced food, end by heating the blood, and are not worth, whatever people may say of them, a good soup.","zh":"还有饭馆的菜，样样吃食加香料，临了把你的血烧得滚烫，其实，说什么也抵不上一锅肉汤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For my own part, I have always preferred plain living; it is more healthy.","zh":"我呀，一向就喜欢家常菜：卫生多了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So when I was studying pharmacy at Rouen, I boarded in a boarding house; I dined with the professors.”","zh":"所以过去我在鲁昂念药剂学，我就住到私人家里吃包饭，和教师们一道用饭。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And thus he went on, expounding his opinions generally and his personal likings, until Justin came to fetch him for a mulled egg that was wanted.","sentences":[{"en":"And thus he went on, expounding his opinions generally and his personal likings, until Justin came to fetch him for a mulled egg that was wanted.","zh":"他就这样继续发表他的一般意见和他的个别爱好，直到朱斯丹来，找他回去配制蛋黄橘汁糖水，这才喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Not a moment’s peace!” he cried; “always at it! I can’t go out for a minute! Like a plough-horse, I have always to be moiling and toiling. What drudgery!” Then, when he was at the door, “By the way, do you know the news?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not a moment’s peace!” he cried; “always at it!","zh":"“就没有一刻休息！永远拴得牢牢的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I can’t go out for a minute!","zh":"我就不能走开一分钟！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Like a plough-horse, I have always to be moiling and toiling.","zh":"像下地的马一样，累死了也得做！多苦的命哟！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"What drudgery!”","zh":"像下地的马一样，累死了也得做！多苦的命哟！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, when he was at the door, “By the way, do you know the news?”","zh":"已经走到门口了，他道：“对了，您听到消息没有？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What news?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What news?”","zh":"“什么消息？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That it is very likely,” Homais went on, raising his eyebrows and assuming one of his most serious expression, “that the agricultural meeting of the Seine-Inferieure will be held this year at Yonville-l’Abbaye. The rumour, at all events, is going the round. This morning the paper alluded to it. It would be of the utmost importance for our district. But we’ll talk it over later on. I can see, thank you; Justin has the lantern.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That it is very likely,” Homais went on, raising his eyebrows and assuming one of his most serious expression, “that the agricultural meeting of the Seine-Inferieure will be held this year at Yonville-l’Abbaye.","zh":"郝麦竖起眉毛，一脸像煞有介事的表情，接下去道：“塞纳河下游州的农业展览会，今年要在永镇寺举行。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The rumour, at all events, is going the round.","zh":"至少，有这种风声。今天早晨，报上还提起过。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This morning the paper alluded to it.","zh":"至少，有这种风声。今天早晨，报上还提起过。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It would be of the utmost importance for our district.","zh":"这对本县太重要了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But we’ll talk it over later on.","zh":"不过我们改天谈吧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I can see, thank you; Justin has the lantern.”","zh":"谢谢，我看得见；朱斯丹有灯。”","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-7","part":2,"n":7,"title":"Part II · Chapter 7","titleZh":"中卷 · 7","paragraphs":[{"en":"The next day was a dreary one for Emma. Everything seemed to her enveloped in a black atmosphere floating confusedly over the exterior of things, and sorrow was engulfed within her soul with soft shrieks such as the winter wind makes in ruined castles. It was that reverie which we give to things that will not return, the lassitude that seizes you after everything was done; that pain, in fine, that the interruption of every wonted movement, the sudden cessation of any prolonged vibration, brings on.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day was a dreary one for Emma.","zh":"第二天对爱玛成了一个死气沉沉的日子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everything seemed to her enveloped in a black atmosphere floating confusedly over the exterior of things, and sorrow was engulfed within her soul with soft shrieks such as the winter wind makes in ruined castles.","zh":"她只觉一片愁云惨雾，弥漫天空，乱腾腾浮游在事物的外部，而悲痛沉入心底，低哭轻号，仿佛冬天的风，在荒凉的庄园啸叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was that reverie which we give to things that will not return, the lassitude that seizes you after everything was done; that pain, in fine, that the interruption of every wonted movement, the sudden cessation of any prolonged vibration, brings on.","zh":"这好像韶光一去不返，魂牵梦萦，又像做完一件事，身心疲劳，更像习惯动作中断，或者经久不停的摆，骤然停止。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As on the return from Vaubyessard, when the quadrilles were running in her head, she was full of a gloomy melancholy, of a numb despair. Léon reappeared, taller, handsomer, more charming, more vague. Though separated from her, he had not left her; he was there, and the walls of the house seemed to hold his shadow.","sentences":[{"en":"As on the return from Vaubyessard, when the quadrilles were running in her head, she was full of a gloomy melancholy, of a numb despair.","zh":"她的心情好像往年从渥毕萨尔回来、四组舞还在脑子里转来转去，悒悒寡欢，昏昏沉沉，只是一味难受。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Léon reappeared, taller, handsomer, more charming, more vague.","zh":"她的心情好像往年从渥毕萨尔回来、四组舞还在脑子里转来转去，悒悒寡欢，昏昏沉沉，只是一味难受。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Though separated from her, he had not left her; he was there, and the walls of the house seemed to hold his shadow.","zh":"赖昂似乎又出现了，人也显得更高、更美、更温柔、更模糊；他虽然走了，可是没有离开她，就在眼前，房子的墙好像把他的影子留下来了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She could not detach her eyes from the carpet where he had walked, from those empty chairs where he had sat. The river still flowed on, and slowly drove its ripples along the slippery banks.","sentences":[{"en":"She could not detach her eyes from the carpet where he had walked, from those empty chairs where he had sat.","zh":"赖昂似乎又出现了，人也显得更高、更美、更温柔、更模糊；他虽然走了，可是没有离开她，就在眼前，房子的墙好像把他的影子留下来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The river still flowed on, and slowly drove its ripples along the slippery banks.","zh":"她看不厌他走过的地毯、他坐过的空椅子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They had often walked there to the murmur of the waves over the moss-covered pebbles. How bright the sun had been! What happy afternoons they had seen alone in the shade at the end of the garden! He read aloud, bareheaded, sitting on a footstool of dry sticks; the fresh wind of the meadow set trembling the leaves of the book and the nasturtiums of the arbour. Ah! he was gone, the only charm of her life, the only possible hope of joy. Why had she not seized this happiness when it came to her? Why not have kept hold of it with both hands, with both knees, when it was about to flee from her? And she cursed herself for not having loved Léon. She thirsted for his lips. The wish took possession of her to run after and rejoin him, throw herself into his arms and say to him, “It is I; I am yours.” But Emma recoiled beforehand at the difficulties of the enterprise, and her desires, increased by regret, became only the more acute.","sentences":[{"en":"They had often walked there to the murmur of the waves over the moss-covered pebbles.","zh":"河水一直在流，顺着滑溜溜的河堤，慢慢悠悠，涟漪成纹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How bright the sun had been!","zh":"他们有许多次在这里散步，石子遍体青苔，水波流过，照样潺湲作响。头上太阳多好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What happy afternoons they had seen alone in the shade at the end of the garden!","zh":"下午单单两个人待在花园尽头有阴凉的地方，多有意思！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He read aloud, bareheaded, sitting on a footstool of dry sticks; the fresh wind of the meadow set trembling the leaves of the book and the nasturtiums of the arbour.","zh":"他坐在一张干木条凳子上，不戴帽子，高声朗诵；草原清风徐来，书页颤动，棚上的旱金莲摇摆…啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! he was gone, the only charm of her life, the only possible hope of joy.","zh":"他走了，她的生命的唯一欢乐，幸福的唯一有可能实现的希望！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why had she not seized this happiness when it came to her?","zh":"幸福当前，她怎么就不抓住！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why not have kept hold of it with both hands, with both knees, when it was about to flee from her?","zh":"眼看幸福远扬，为什么就不双手伸出，双膝下跪，一把揪牢？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And she cursed herself for not having loved Léon.","zh":"她诅咒自己没有向赖昂表示爱情；她想念他的嘴唇。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She thirsted for his lips.","zh":"她诅咒自己没有向赖昂表示爱情；她想念他的嘴唇。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The wish took possession of her to run after and rejoin him, throw herself into his arms and say to him, “It is I; I am yours.”","zh":"她恨不得追上他，扑进他的胸怀，对他说：“是我；我是你的！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Emma recoiled beforehand at the difficulties of the enterprise, and her desires, increased by regret, became only the more acute.","zh":"可是爱玛想到困难重重，先失了张本；她一起懊恼之心，欲望便越发活跃了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Henceforth the memory of Léon was the centre of her boredom; it burnt there more brightly than the fire travellers have left on the snow of a Russian steppe. She sprang towards him, she pressed against him, she stirred carefully the dying embers, sought all around her anything that could revive it; and the most distant reminiscences, like the most immediate occasions, what she experienced as well as what she imagined, her voluptuous desires that were unsatisfied, her projects of happiness that crackled in the wind like dead boughs, her sterile virtue, her lost hopes, the domestic tête-à-tête—she gathered it all up, took everything, and made it all serve as fuel for her melancholy.","sentences":[{"en":"Henceforth the memory of Léon was the centre of her boredom; it burnt there more brightly than the fire travellers have left on the snow of a Russian steppe.","zh":"从这时候起，回忆赖昂成了她的愁闷的中心；回忆的火星噼啪作响，比旅客在俄罗斯大草原雪地上留下的火堆还闪烁不定。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She sprang towards him, she pressed against him, she stirred carefully the dying embers, sought all around her anything that could revive it; and the most distant reminiscences, like the most immediate occasions, what she experienced as well as what she imagined, her voluptuous desires that were unsatisfied, her projects of happiness that crackled in the wind like dead boughs, her sterile virtue, her lost hopes, the domestic tête-à-tête—she gathered it all up, took everything, and made it all serve as fuel for her melancholy.","zh":"她扑过去，蹲在一旁，小心在意，拨弄这要灭的火，前后左右寻找，看有没有东西能把火弄旺；于是最远的回忆和最近的会晤、她感觉到的和她想象到的、她对欢愉的落空的期待、她的枯枝一般在风中哽咽的幸福、她的劳而无获的道德、她的幻灭的希望、家庭的牺牲，细大不捐，她全拣过来，拾起来，聚在一起，烘暖她的忧郁。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The flames, however, subsided, either because the supply had exhausted itself, or because it had been piled up too much. Love, little by little, was quelled by absence; regret stifled beneath habit; and this incendiary light that had empurpled her pale sky was overspread and faded by degrees. In the supineness of her conscience she even took her repugnance towards her husband for aspirations towards her lover, the burning of hate for the warmth of tenderness; but as the tempest still raged, and as passion burnt itself down to the very cinders, and no help came, no sun rose, there was night on all sides, and she was lost in the terrible cold that pierced her.","sentences":[{"en":"The flames, however, subsided, either because the supply had exhausted itself, or because it had been piled up too much.","zh":"然而不知道是供应不足，还是堆积过多，火苗弱了下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Love, little by little, was quelled by absence; regret stifled beneath habit; and this incendiary light that had empurpled her pale sky was overspread and faded by degrees.","zh":"别离渐渐泯灭了爱情，久而久之，怅惘也就窒息了。这道火光先前照亮她的灰色的天空，如今越来越暗，慢慢消失了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the supineness of her conscience she even took her repugnance towards her husband for aspirations towards her lover, the burning of hate for the warmth of tenderness; but as the tempest still raged, and as passion burnt itself down to the very cinders, and no help came, no sun rose, there was night on all sides, and she was lost in the terrible cold that pierced her.","zh":"昏昏沉沉中，甚至厌恶丈夫的心，她也颠三倒四，当作思念情人的表现；甚至憎恨的炙伤，她也糊里糊涂，看成恩爱的缠绵。可是狂风一直在吹，热情烧成灰烬，无可挽救，也不见太阳出来，黑漆漆的夜晚，四面八方，重锁密布，她觉得自己无路可走，寒气逼人，冷彻骨髓。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then the evil days of Tostes began again. She thought herself now far more unhappy; for she had the experience of grief, with the certainty that it would not end.","sentences":[{"en":"Then the evil days of Tostes began again.","zh":"于是道特的坏日子又开始了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She thought herself now far more unhappy; for she had the experience of grief, with the certainty that it would not end.","zh":"她觉得现在比过去还要糟，因为她经过伤心事，而且确信要一直伤心下去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A woman who had laid on herself such sacrifices could well allow herself certain whims. She bought a Gothic prie-dieu, and in a month spent fourteen francs on lemons for polishing her nails; she wrote to Rouen for a blue cashmere gown; she chose one of Lheureux’s finest scarves, and wore it knotted around her waist over her dressing-gown; and, with closed blinds and a book in her hand, she lay stretched out on a couch in this garb.","sentences":[{"en":"A woman who had laid on herself such sacrifices could well allow herself certain whims.","zh":"一个女人强迫自己做出这样大的牺牲，生活上很可以看开一些。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She bought a Gothic prie-dieu, and in a month spent fourteen francs on lemons for polishing her nails; she wrote to Rouen for a blue cashmere gown; she chose one of Lheureux’s finest scarves, and wore it knotted around her waist over her dressing-gown; and, with closed blinds and a book in her hand, she lay stretched out on a couch in this garb.","zh":"她买了一只哥特式跪凳；她一个月花十四法郎买柠檬，洗指甲；她写信给鲁昂，要一件克什米尔呢 蓝袍；她到勒乐那边，挑了一条顶好的围巾，当腰扎在室内穿的便袍上，然后关上屋里的护窗板，拿起一本书，就这样一身装束，躺在一张大沙发上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She often changed her coiffure; she did her hair a la Chinoise, in flowing curls, in plaited coils; she parted in on one side and rolled it under like a man’s.","sentences":[{"en":"She often changed her coiffure; she did her hair a la Chinoise, in flowing curls, in plaited coils; she parted in on one side and rolled it under like a man’s.","zh":"她常常改换头发样式；她照中国样式梳头，不是柔软的圈圈，就是辫子；头发靠旁边挑一条缝，像男人一样朝下卷。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She wanted to learn Italian; she bought dictionaries, a grammar, and a supply of white paper. She tried serious reading, history, and philosophy. Sometimes in the night Charles woke up with a start, thinking he was being called to a patient. “I’m coming,” he stammered; and it was the noise of a match Emma had struck to relight the lamp. But her reading fared like her piece of embroidery, all of which, only just begun, filled her cupboard; she took it up, left it, passed on to other books.","sentences":[{"en":"She wanted to learn Italian; she bought dictionaries, a grammar, and a supply of white paper.","zh":"她想学意大利文，买了几本字典、一本文法、一叠白纸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She tried serious reading, history, and philosophy.","zh":"她试着看正经书：历史和哲学。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes in the night Charles woke up with a start, thinking he was being called to a patient.","zh":"查理夜晚睡得沉沉的，有时候惊醒了，跳下床来，以为有人找他看病，咕哝道：“我就去。”原来只是爱玛擦火柴点灯的响声。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I’m coming,” he stammered; and it was the noise of a match Emma had struck to relight the lamp.","zh":"查理夜晚睡得沉沉的，有时候惊醒了，跳下床来，以为有人找他看病，咕哝道：“我就去。”原来只是爱玛擦火柴点灯的响声。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But her reading fared like her piece of embroidery, all of which, only just begun, filled her cupboard; she took it up, left it, passed on to other books.","zh":"不过她念书就像她刺绣一样，开了一个头，就全丢进衣橱了。她拿起来，放下去，又换别的活做、别的书读。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She had attacks in which she could easily have been driven to commit any folly. She maintained one day, in opposition to her husband, that she could drink off a large glass of brandy, and, as Charles was stupid enough to dare her to, she swallowed the brandy to the last drop.","sentences":[{"en":"She had attacks in which she could easily have been driven to commit any folly.","zh":"赶上怄气，别人不过三言两语，她就失了分寸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She maintained one day, in opposition to her husband, that she could drink off a large glass of brandy, and, as Charles was stupid enough to dare her to, she swallowed the brandy to the last drop.","zh":"有一天，她和丈夫打赌，说她可以喝大半杯烧酒，查理一时糊涂，说他不信，她便一口气喝光。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In spite of her vapourish airs (as the housewives of Yonville called them), Emma, all the same, never seemed gay, and usually she had at the corners of her mouth that immobile contraction that puckers the faces of old maids, and those of men whose ambition has failed. She was pale all over, white as a sheet; the skin of her nose was drawn at the nostrils, her eyes looked at you vaguely. After discovering three grey hairs on her temples, she talked much of her old age.","sentences":[{"en":"In spite of her vapourish airs (as the housewives of Yonville called them), Emma, all the same, never seemed gay, and usually she had at the corners of her mouth that immobile contraction that puckers the faces of old maids, and those of men whose ambition has failed.","zh":"爱玛虽说作风轻狂（永镇的太太们这样说她），却不显得快活。她的嘴角常有一条纹路， 呆呆，像老姑娘，也像失意政客，由于这条纹路，脸都皱了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was pale all over, white as a sheet; the skin of her nose was drawn at the nostrils, her eyes looked at you vaguely.","zh":"她面无血色，布单一般白，鼻子的皮朝鼻孔抽搐，眼睛望着你，一副神不守舍的模样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After discovering three grey hairs on her temples, she talked much of her old age.","zh":"她在鬓角见到三根灰头发，便说自己老了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She often fainted. One day she even spat blood, and, as Charles fussed around her showing his anxiety—","sentences":[{"en":"She often fainted.","zh":"她常常晕倒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One day she even spat blood, and, as Charles fussed around her showing his anxiety—","zh":"有一天，她甚至咯出一口血来，查理着急，显出焦灼不安，她回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Bah!” she answered, “what does it matter?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Bah!” she answered, “what does it matter?”","zh":"“得啦！这算得了什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles fled to his study and wept there, both his elbows on the table, sitting in an arm-chair at his bureau under the phrenological head.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles fled to his study and wept there, both his elbows on the table, sitting in an arm-chair at his bureau under the phrenological head.","zh":"查理躲到他的诊室，坐在他的大靠背扶手椅上，两只胳膊肘拄着桌子，对着骨相学人头，哭了起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he wrote to his mother begging her to come, and they had many long consultations together on the subject of Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"Then he wrote to his mother begging her to come, and they had many long consultations together on the subject of Emma.","zh":"他给母亲捎信，求她来一趟。他们商量爱玛的事，谈了好长时间。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"What should they decide? What was to be done since she rejected all medical treatment? “Do you know what your wife wants?” replied Madame Bovary senior.","sentences":[{"en":"What should they decide?","zh":"这事怎么解决？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was to be done since she rejected all medical treatment?","zh":"她拒绝医治，怎么办？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do you know what your wife wants?” replied Madame Bovary senior.","zh":"老太太说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“She wants to be forced to occupy herself with some manual work. If she were obliged, like so many others, to earn her living, she wouldn’t have these vapours, that come to her from a lot of ideas she stuffs into her head, and from the idleness in which she lives.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She wants to be forced to occupy herself with some manual work.","zh":"“你知道你女人需要什么？就是逼她操劳，手不闲着！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If she were obliged, like so many others, to earn her living, she wouldn’t have these vapours, that come to her from a lot of ideas she stuffs into her head, and from the idleness in which she lives.”","zh":"只要她多少像别人一样，非自食其力不可，她就不会犯神经了。这都是因为她整天没事干，脑子净胡思乱想的缘故。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet she is always busy,” said Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet she is always busy,” said Charles.","zh":"查理道：“可是她也很忙呀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! always busy at what? Reading novels, bad books, works against religion, and in which they mock at priests in speeches taken from Voltaire. But all that leads you far astray, my poor child. Anyone who has no religion always ends by turning out badly.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! always busy at what?","zh":"“啊！忙！忙什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Reading novels, bad books, works against religion, and in which they mock at priests in speeches taken from Voltaire.","zh":"看小说；看坏书；看反对宗教的书；看用伏尔泰的语言讥笑教士的书。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But all that leads you far astray, my poor child.","zh":"不过，我可怜的孩子，糟的还在后头，不信教的人，结局总是坏的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Anyone who has no religion always ends by turning out badly.”","zh":"不过，我可怜的孩子，糟的还在后头，不信教的人，结局总是坏的。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"So it was decided to stop Emma reading novels. The enterprise did not seem easy. The good lady undertook it. She was, when she passed through Rouen, to go herself to the lending-library and represent that Emma had discontinued her subscription. Would they not have a right to apply to the police if the librarian persisted all the same in his poisonous trade? The farewells of mother and daughter-in-law were cold. During the three weeks that they had been together they had not exchanged half-a-dozen words apart from the inquiries and phrases when they met at table and in the evening before going to bed.","sentences":[{"en":"So it was decided to stop Emma reading novels.","zh":"于是他们决定阻止爱玛看小说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The enterprise did not seem easy.","zh":"事情看来不大好办。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The good lady undertook it.","zh":"老太太自告奋勇说她路过鲁昂，可以亲自到租书的地方，声明爱玛停止订阅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was, when she passed through Rouen, to go herself to the lending-library and represent that Emma had discontinued her subscription.","zh":"老太太自告奋勇说她路过鲁昂，可以亲自到租书的地方，声明爱玛停止订阅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Would they not have a right to apply to the police if the librarian persisted all the same in his poisonous trade?","zh":"万一书局坚持这种害人的生意，难道他们没有权利通知警察？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The farewells of mother and daughter-in-law were cold.","zh":"婆媳并不惜别。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"During the three weeks that they had been together they had not exchanged half-a-dozen words apart from the inquiries and phrases when they met at table and in the evening before going to bed.","zh":"她们在一起待了三星期，没有说过几句话，除去用餐时和睡前的问讯和问候。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary left on a Wednesday, the market-day at Yonville.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary left on a Wednesday, the market-day at Yonville.","zh":"老太太星期三走，这一天是永镇有集的日子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The Place since morning had been blocked by a row of carts, which, on end and their shafts in the air, spread all along the line of houses from the church to the inn. On the other side there were canvas booths, where cotton checks, blankets, and woollen stockings were sold, together with harness for horses, and packets of blue ribbon, whose ends fluttered in the wind. The coarse hardware was spread out on the ground between pyramids of eggs and hampers of cheeses, from which sticky straw stuck out.","sentences":[{"en":"The Place since morning had been blocked by a row of carts, which, on end and their shafts in the air, spread all along the line of houses from the church to the inn.","zh":"从早晨起，广场堆满大车，个个车辕朝天，由教堂到客店，顺着房屋，摆了一排。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the other side there were canvas booths, where cotton checks, blankets, and woollen stockings were sold, together with harness for horses, and packets of blue ribbon, whose ends fluttered in the wind.","zh":"对面是帆布摊子，出卖布帛、被褥、毛袜、马络和成包的蓝带子；带子露出一头，随风飘扬。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The coarse hardware was spread out on the ground between pyramids of eggs and hampers of cheeses, from which sticky straw stuck out.","zh":"地上是粗笨的铜铁器皿，一边是高高摞起的鸡蛋，一边是小柳条筐，里头放着干酪，干酪外皮还有黏黏的草。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Near the corn-machines clucking hens passed their necks through the bars of flat cages. The people, crowding in the same place and unwilling to move thence, sometimes threatened to smash the shop front of the chemist. On Wednesdays his shop was never empty, and the people pushed in less to buy drugs than for consultations. So great was Homais’ reputation in the neighbouring villages. His robust aplomb had fascinated the rustics. They considered him a greater doctor than all the doctors.","sentences":[{"en":"Near the corn-machines clucking hens passed their necks through the bars of flat cages.","zh":"好些母鸡，靠近打麦机，头探出笼子，咯咯叫唤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The people, crowding in the same place and unwilling to move thence, sometimes threatened to smash the shop front of the chemist.","zh":"人群有时候险些挤破药房门面，聚在一个地点，谁也不肯走动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On Wednesdays his shop was never empty, and the people pushed in less to buy drugs than for consultations.","zh":"星期三，药房整天不空，人挤进去，说是为了买药，不如说是为了看病，郝麦先生的名气传遍四乡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So great was Homais’ reputation in the neighbouring villages.","zh":"他坚定的口吻迷住了乡下佬。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His robust aplomb had fascinated the rustics.","zh":"他们把他看成一个比任何医生都伟大的医生。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They considered him a greater doctor than all the doctors.","zh":"他们把他看成一个比任何医生都伟大的医生。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma was leaning out at the window; she was often there. The window in the provinces replaces the theatre and the promenade, she was amusing herself with watching the crowd of boors when she saw a gentleman in a green velvet coat. He had on yellow gloves, although he wore heavy gaiters; he was coming towards the doctor’s house, followed by a peasant walking with a bent head and quite a thoughtful air.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma was leaning out at the window; she was often there.","zh":"爱玛倚着窗户（她常常待在这儿，外省窗户有代替看戏和散步的作用），瞧着乱哄哄的乡下佬解闷，却见一位绅士，穿一件绿绒大衣，戴一副黄手套，而又套着一双厚皮护腿，一直走向医生住宅，后面跟着一个庄稼汉，耷拉着头，若有所思的模样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The window in the provinces replaces the theatre and the promenade, she was amusing herself with watching the crowd of boors when she saw a gentleman in a green velvet coat.","zh":"爱玛倚着窗户（她常常待在这儿，外省窗户有代替看戏和散步的作用），瞧着乱哄哄的乡下佬解闷，却见一位绅士，穿一件绿绒大衣，戴一副黄手套，而又套着一双厚皮护腿，一直走向医生住宅，后面跟着一个庄稼汉，耷拉着头，若有所思的模样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He had on yellow gloves, although he wore heavy gaiters; he was coming towards the doctor’s house, followed by a peasant walking with a bent head and quite a thoughtful air.","zh":"爱玛倚着窗户（她常常待在这儿，外省窗户有代替看戏和散步的作用），瞧着乱哄哄的乡下佬解闷，却见一位绅士，穿一件绿绒大衣，戴一副黄手套，而又套着一双厚皮护腿，一直走向医生住宅，后面跟着一个庄稼汉，耷拉着头，若有所思的模样。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Can I see the doctor?” he asked Justin, who was talking on the doorsteps with Félicité, and, taking him for a servant of the house—“Tell him that Monsieur Rodolphe Boulanger of La Huchette is here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Can I see the doctor?” he asked Justin, who was talking on the doorsteps with Félicité, and, taking him for a servant of the house—“Tell him that Monsieur Rodolphe Boulanger of La Huchette is here.”","zh":"他问在门口和全福闲谈的朱斯丹道：“医生在家吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was not from territorial vanity that the new arrival added “of La Huchette” to his name, but to make himself the better known.","sentences":[{"en":"It was not from territorial vanity that the new arrival added “of La Huchette” to his name, but to make himself the better known.","zh":"他把他看成医生的男用人：“请告诉他，于歇特的罗道耳弗·布朗热先生要见他。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"La Huchette, in fact, was an estate near Yonville, where he had just bought the château and two farms that he cultivated himself, without, however, troubling very much about them. He lived as a bachelor, and was supposed to have “at least fifteen thousand francs a year.”","sentences":[{"en":"La Huchette, in fact, was an estate near Yonville, where he had just bought the château and two farms that he cultivated himself, without, however, troubling very much about them.","zh":"新来的人并非为了夸耀他有土地，才拿于歇特放在姓名前头，不过是让人知道他是谁罢了。于歇特确实是永镇附近的产业，他新近买下庄园，有两块庄田，亲自耕种，可是并不过分经心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He lived as a bachelor, and was supposed to have “at least fifteen thousand francs a year.”","zh":"他过的是独身生活，据说一年起码有一万五千法郎收入！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles came into the room. Monsieur Boulanger introduced his man, who wanted to be bled because he felt “a tingling all over.”","sentences":[{"en":"Charles came into the room.","zh":"查理走进厅房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Boulanger introduced his man, who wanted to be bled because he felt “a tingling all over.”","zh":"布朗热先生向他解释，他的用人想放放血，因为他觉得“浑身痒痒”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That’ll purge me,” he urged as an objection to all reasoning.","sentences":[{"en":"“That’ll purge me,” he urged as an objection to all reasoning.","zh":"别人怎么劝说，他也不听，只是讲：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"So Bovary ordered a bandage and a basin, and asked Justin to hold it. Then addressing the peasant, who was already pale—","sentences":[{"en":"So Bovary ordered a bandage and a basin, and asked Justin to hold it.","zh":"“出出血，我就干净啦。”包法利听了这话，先取来一捆绷带和一只脸盆。他求朱斯丹端好脸盆，然后转向面色已经发白的乡下人道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then addressing the peasant, who was already pale—","zh":"“出出血，我就干净啦。”包法利听了这话，先取来一捆绷带和一只脸盆。他求朱斯丹端好脸盆，然后转向面色已经发白的乡下人道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Don’t be afraid, my lad.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t be afraid, my lad.”","zh":"“老乡，别害怕。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no, sir,” said the other; “get on.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no, sir,” said the other; “get on.”","zh":"另一位回答道：“不，不，您动手好啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And with an air of bravado he held out his great arm. At the prick of the lancet the blood spurted out, splashing against the looking-glass.","sentences":[{"en":"And with an air of bravado he held out his great arm.","zh":"他伸出他的粗胳膊，摆出一种若无其事的姿势。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the prick of the lancet the blood spurted out, splashing against the looking-glass.","zh":"竹叶刀刺了一下，血涌出来，溅到镜子上。查理喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Hold the basin nearer,” exclaimed Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“Hold the basin nearer,” exclaimed Charles.","zh":"“盆子端到跟前！”乡下人道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Lor!” said the peasant, “one would swear it was a little fountain flowing. How red my blood is! That’s a good sign, isn’t it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Lor!” said the peasant, “one would swear it was a little fountain flowing.","zh":"“瞅！活像一道小泉眼在流！我的血多红！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How red my blood is!","zh":"这该是好现象，对不对？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That’s a good sign, isn’t it?”","zh":"医生接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sometimes,” answered the doctor, “one feels nothing at first, and then syncope sets in, and more especially with people of strong constitution like this man.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sometimes,” answered the doctor, “one feels nothing at first, and then syncope sets in, and more especially with people of strong constitution like this man.”","zh":"“有时候，开头不觉得怎么样，过后说晕倒就晕倒，尤其是像这种人，身子骨儿结实。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At these words the rustic let go the lancet-case he was twisting between his fingers. A shudder of his shoulders made the chair-back creak. His hat fell off.","sentences":[{"en":"At these words the rustic let go the lancet-case he was twisting between his fingers.","zh":"乡下佬手指捏着竹叶刀的匣子，转来转去，一听这话，松开了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A shudder of his shoulders made the chair-back creak.","zh":"肩膀猛然一动，椅背嘎吱响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His hat fell off.","zh":"帽子掉下去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I thought as much,” said Bovary, pressing his finger on the vein.","sentences":[{"en":"“I thought as much,” said Bovary, pressing his finger on the vein.","zh":"包法利拿手指捺住血管，道：“我说什么来着。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The basin was beginning to tremble in Justin’s hands; his knees shook, he turned pale.","sentences":[{"en":"The basin was beginning to tremble in Justin’s hands; his knees shook, he turned pale.","zh":"朱斯丹两手直抖，脸盆开始摇晃；脸成了白的，腿也站立不住。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Emma! Emma!” called Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“Emma!","zh":"朱斯丹两手直抖，脸盆开始摇晃；脸成了白的，腿也站立不住。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma!” called Charles.","zh":"查理喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"With one bound she came down the staircase.","sentences":[{"en":"With one bound she came down the staircase.","zh":"“太太！太太！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Some vinegar,” he cried. “O dear! two at once!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Some vinegar,” he cried.","zh":"她一步跳下楼梯。他嚷道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"“O dear! two at once!”","zh":"她一步跳下楼梯。他嚷道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And in his emotion he could hardly put on the compress.","sentences":[{"en":"And in his emotion he could hardly put on the compress.","zh":"啊！我的上帝！一下子两个人！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is nothing,” said Monsieur Boulanger quietly, taking Justin in his arms. He seated him on the table with his back resting against the wall.","sentences":[{"en":"“It is nothing,” said Monsieur Boulanger quietly, taking Justin in his arms.","zh":"他一激动，连紧压布也几乎放不平稳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He seated him on the table with his back resting against the wall.","zh":"布朗热先生抱起朱斯丹，镇定地说：“不要紧的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary began taking off his cravat. The strings of his shirt had got into a knot, and she was for some minutes moving her light fingers about the young fellow’s neck. Then she poured some vinegar on her cambric handkerchief; she moistened his temples with little dabs, and then blew upon them softly. The ploughman revived, but Justin’s syncope still lasted, and his eyeballs disappeared in the pale sclerotics like blue flowers in milk.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary began taking off his cravat.","zh":"他叫他背靠墙，坐在桌子上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The strings of his shirt had got into a knot, and she was for some minutes moving her light fingers about the young fellow’s neck.","zh":"包法利夫人解开他的领带。衬衫绳子挽了一个死结；她灵活的手指，在年轻人的颈项，停了几分钟；然后她拿醋倒在她的麻纱手绢上，轻轻拍湿他的太阳穴，还小心在意，往上嘘气。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she poured some vinegar on her cambric handkerchief; she moistened his temples with little dabs, and then blew upon them softly.","zh":"包法利夫人解开他的领带。衬衫绳子挽了一个死结；她灵活的手指，在年轻人的颈项，停了几分钟；然后她拿醋倒在她的麻纱手绢上，轻轻拍湿他的太阳穴，还小心在意，往上嘘气。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The ploughman revived, but Justin’s syncope still lasted, and his eyeballs disappeared in the pale sclerotics like blue flowers in milk.","zh":"赶大车的乡下人醒过来了；朱斯丹仍然不省人事，瞳仁在眼白中间消散，就像蓝花在牛乳中间消散一样。查理道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We must hide this from him,” said Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“We must hide this from him,” said Charles.","zh":"“别叫他看见这个。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary took the basin to put it under the table. With the movement she made in bending down, her dress (it was a summer dress with four flounces, yellow, long in the waist and wide in the skirt) spread out around her on the flags of the room; and as Emma stooping, staggered a little as she stretched out her arms.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary took the basin to put it under the table.","zh":"包法利夫人拿起脸盆，放到桌子底下；她一弯腰，袍子（一件夏天袍子，滚了四道花边，黄颜色，腰身长，裙幅宽大）就在周围的方石板地上摊开；同时，爱玛弯腰，伸开胳膊，有一点摇晃，膨起的衣裙有些地方随着身体的曲线陷下去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"With the movement she made in bending down, her dress (it was a summer dress with four flounces, yellow, long in the waist and wide in the skirt) spread out around her on the flags of the room; and as Emma stooping, staggered a little as she stretched out her arms.","zh":"包法利夫人拿起脸盆，放到桌子底下；她一弯腰，袍子（一件夏天袍子，滚了四道花边，黄颜色，腰身长，裙幅宽大）就在周围的方石板地上摊开；同时，爱玛弯腰，伸开胳膊，有一点摇晃，膨起的衣裙有些地方随着身体的曲线陷下去了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The stuff here and there gave with the inflections of her bust.","sentences":[{"en":"The stuff here and there gave with the inflections of her bust.","zh":"她接着取来一瓶水，溶化几块糖。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she went to fetch a bottle of water, and she was melting some pieces of sugar when the chemist arrived. The servant had been to fetch him in the tumult. Seeing his pupil’s eyes staring he drew a long breath; then going around him he looked at him from head to foot.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she went to fetch a bottle of water, and she was melting some pieces of sugar when the chemist arrived.","zh":"药剂师到了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The servant had been to fetch him in the tumult.","zh":"女用人找他，他正在大发雷霆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Seeing his pupil’s eyes staring he drew a long breath; then going around him he looked at him from head to foot.","zh":"看见学徒睁开眼睛，他这才放心。跟着他就兜过来，兜过去，上上下下，打量他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Fool!” he said, “really a little fool! A fool in four letters! A phlebotomy’s a big affair, isn’t it! And a fellow who isn’t afraid of anything; a kind of squirrel, just as he is who climbs to vertiginous heights to shake down nuts. Oh, yes! you just talk to me, boast about yourself! Here’s a fine fitness for practising pharmacy later on; for under serious circumstances you may be called before the tribunals in order to enlighten the minds of the magistrates, and you would have to keep your head then, to reason, show yourself a man, or else pass for an imbecile.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Fool!” he said, “really a little fool!","zh":"“废物！一点不差，小废物！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A fool in four letters!","zh":"十足的废物！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A phlebotomy’s a big affair, isn’t it!","zh":"放放血，算得了什么！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And a fellow who isn’t afraid of anything; a kind of squirrel, just as he is who climbs to vertiginous heights to shake down nuts.","zh":"好一个顶天立地的汉子！你们看呀，这就是那只松鼠，不怕头晕，爬到树梢摇核桃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, yes! you just talk to me, boast about yourself!","zh":"啊！是的，说呀，夸嘴呀！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Here’s a fine fitness for practising pharmacy later on; for under serious circumstances you may be called before the tribunals in order to enlighten the minds of the magistrates, and you would have to keep your head then, to reason, show yourself a man, or else pass for an imbecile.”","zh":"真是块好料，赶明儿还要当药剂师呢；兴许有一天，情况严重，法院传你，要你指点指点法官们的良心；这时你就该头脑冷静，讲得头头是道，像一个男子汉大丈夫，不然的话，只好让人当傻瓜看！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Justin did not answer. The chemist went on—","sentences":[{"en":"Justin did not answer.","zh":"朱斯丹不回答。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The chemist went on—","zh":"药剂师继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Who asked you to come? You are always pestering the doctor and madame. On Wednesday, moreover, your presence is indispensable to me. There are now twenty people in the shop. I left everything because of the interest I take in you. Come, get along! Sharp! Wait for me, and keep an eye on the jars.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who asked you to come?","zh":"“谁请你来的？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are always pestering the doctor and madame.","zh":"你总在麻烦包法利先生和包法利太太！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On Wednesday, moreover, your presence is indispensable to me.","zh":"再说，星期三，我离不开你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There are now twenty people in the shop.","zh":"药房现在就有一大堆人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I left everything because of the interest I take in you.","zh":"为了你的缘故，我只好丢开他们不管。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Come, get along!","zh":"好啦，滚！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sharp!","zh":"跑！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Wait for me, and keep an eye on the jars.”","zh":"等我来，看好瓶子！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When Justin, who was rearranging his dress, had gone, they talked for a little while about fainting-fits. Madame Bovary had never fainted.","sentences":[{"en":"When Justin, who was rearranging his dress, had gone, they talked for a little while about fainting-fits.","zh":"朱斯丹穿好衣服，走了以后，大家谈起昏厥的事。包法利夫人从来没有昏厥过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Bovary had never fainted.","zh":"布朗热先生道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That is extraordinary for a lady,” said Monsieur Boulanger; “but some people are very susceptible. Thus in a duel, I have seen a second lose consciousness at the mere sound of the loading of pistols.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That is extraordinary for a lady,” said Monsieur Boulanger; “but some people are very susceptible.","zh":"“女人能不昏厥，的确了不起！其实，有些男人就很脆弱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus in a duel, I have seen a second lose consciousness at the mere sound of the loading of pistols.”","zh":"有一回决斗，我见到一位证人，听见手枪装子弹，就失了知觉。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For my part,” said the chemist, “the sight of other people’s blood doesn’t affect me at all, but the mere thought of my own flowing would make me faint if I reflected upon it too much.”","sentences":[{"en":"“For my part,” said the chemist, “the sight of other people’s blood doesn’t affect me at all, but the mere thought of my own flowing would make me faint if I reflected upon it too much.”","zh":"药剂师道：“我呀，看见别人淌血，一点也不在乎；可是单只一想自己淌血，要是想过了头，我就难免会晕过去。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Boulanger, however, dismissed his servant, advising him to calm himself, since his fancy was over.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Boulanger, however, dismissed his servant, advising him to calm himself, since his fancy was over.","zh":"布朗热先生打发走他的听差，劝他安心，好在已经照他的想法放过血了。他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It procured me the advantage of making your acquaintance,” he added, and he looked at Emma as he said this. Then he put three francs on the corner of the table, bowed negligently, and went out.","sentences":[{"en":"“It procured me the advantage of making your acquaintance,” he added, and he looked at Emma as he said this.","zh":"“有机会认识你们，我很高兴。”说这句话的时候，他望着爱玛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he put three francs on the corner of the table, bowed negligently, and went out.","zh":"然后他在桌角放下三法郎，随便一鞠躬，扬长去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was soon on the other side of the river (this was his way back to La Huchette), and Emma saw him in the meadow, walking under the poplars, slackening his pace now and then as one who reflects.","sentences":[{"en":"He was soon on the other side of the river (this was his way back to La Huchette), and Emma saw him in the meadow, walking under the poplars, slackening his pace now and then as one who reflects.","zh":"过了一刻，他走到河对岸（他回于歇特的小路）；爱玛望见他在草原白杨底下行走，仿佛一个人想心事，走着走着，就走慢了。他自言自语道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“She is very pretty,” he said to himself; “she is very pretty, this doctor’s wife. Fine teeth, black eyes, a dainty foot, a figure like a Parisienne’s. Where the devil does she come from? Wherever did that fat fellow pick her up?”","sentences":[{"en":"“She is very pretty,” he said to himself; “she is very pretty, this doctor’s wife.","zh":"“她很可爱！这位医生太太，很可爱！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Fine teeth, black eyes, a dainty foot, a figure like a Parisienne’s.","zh":"牙齿美，眼睛黑，脚轻俏，长得如同一个巴黎女子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where the devil does she come from?","zh":"家伙，她打哪儿来的？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Wherever did that fat fellow pick her up?”","zh":"那笨小子打哪儿找到她的？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Rodolphe Boulanger was thirty-four; he was of brutal temperament and intelligent perspicacity, having, moreover, had much to do with women, and knowing them well. This one had seemed pretty to him; so he was thinking about her and her husband.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Rodolphe Boulanger was thirty-four; he was of brutal temperament and intelligent perspicacity, having, moreover, had much to do with women, and knowing them well.","zh":"罗道耳弗·布朗热先生，三十四岁，性情粗暴，思路敏捷，而且常和妇女往来，是一位风月老手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This one had seemed pretty to him; so he was thinking about her and her husband.","zh":"他觉得这个女人标致，所以一心思念她和她的丈夫。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I think he is very stupid. She is tired of him, no doubt. He has dirty nails, and hasn’t shaved for three days. While he is trotting after his patients, she sits there botching socks. And she gets bored! She would like to live in town and dance polkas every evening. Poor little woman! She is gaping after love like a carp after water on a kitchen-table. With three words of gallantry she’d adore one, I’m sure of it. She’d be tender, charming. Yes; but how to get rid of her afterwards?”","sentences":[{"en":"“I think he is very stupid.","zh":"“我想，他一定很蠢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She is tired of him, no doubt.","zh":"不用说，她讨厌他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He has dirty nails, and hasn’t shaved for three days.","zh":"指甲长，三天不刮胡子。他在外头跑来跑去看病人，她待在家里补短袜子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"While he is trotting after his patients, she sits there botching socks.","zh":"指甲长，三天不刮胡子。他在外头跑来跑去看病人，她待在家里补短袜子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And she gets bored!","zh":"她一定闷居无聊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would like to live in town and dance polkas every evening.","zh":"一定愿意住到城里，每天夜晚跳波兰舞！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Poor little woman!","zh":"小可怜儿！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She is gaping after love like a carp after water on a kitchen-table.","zh":"巴望爱情，活像厨房桌子上一条鲤鱼巴望水。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With three words of gallantry she’d adore one, I’m sure of it.","zh":"来上三句情话，我拿稳了她会膜拜你！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She’d be tender, charming.","zh":"一定温柔！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yes; but how to get rid of her afterwards?”","zh":"销魂！是的，不过事后怎么甩掉？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then the difficulties of love-making seen in the distance made him by contrast think of his mistress. She was an actress at Rouen, whom he kept; and when he had pondered over this image, with which, even in remembrance, he was satiated—","sentences":[{"en":"Then the difficulties of love-making seen in the distance made him by contrast think of his mistress.","zh":"想到寻欢作乐，却又阻碍多端，他只好掉转方向，回味自己的情妇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was an actress at Rouen, whom he kept; and when he had pondered over this image, with which, even in remembrance, he was satiated—","zh":"她是他贴养的一个鲁昂女戏子；单单一想，他就对这女人感到腻味。他寻思道：“啊！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! Madame Bovary,” he thought, “is much prettier, especially fresher. Virginie is decidedly beginning to grow fat. She is so finiky about her pleasures; and, besides, she has a mania for prawns.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"包法利夫人比她漂亮多了，尤其是，鲜妍多了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Madame Bovary,” he thought, “is much prettier, especially fresher.","zh":"包法利夫人比她漂亮多了，尤其是，鲜妍多了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Virginie is decidedly beginning to grow fat.","zh":"维吉妮显然在发胖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She is so finiky about her pleasures; and, besides, she has a mania for prawns.”","zh":"她玩也玩得那样乏味！再说，吃斑节虾吃成了瘾！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The fields were empty, and around him Rodolphe only heard the regular beating of the grass striking against his boots, with a cry of the grasshopper hidden at a distance among the oats. He again saw Emma in her room, dressed as he had seen her, and he undressed her.","sentences":[{"en":"The fields were empty, and around him Rodolphe only heard the regular beating of the grass striking against his boots, with a cry of the grasshopper hidden at a distance among the oats.","zh":"田野空旷，罗道耳弗四顾无人，仅仅听见草拂打着鞋，动作有致，蟋蟀远远伏在荞麦底下，唧唧鸣叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He again saw Emma in her room, dressed as he had seen her, and he undressed her.","zh":"他恍惚又在厅房看见爱玛，穿的衣服和他方才见到的一模一样：他脱掉她的衣服。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, I will have her,” he cried, striking a blow with his stick at a clod in front of him. And he at once began to consider the political part of the enterprise. He asked himself—","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I will have her,” he cried, striking a blow with his stick at a clod in front of him.","zh":"他恍惚又在厅房看见爱玛，穿的衣服和他方才见到的一模一样：他脱掉她的衣服。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And he at once began to consider the political part of the enterprise.","zh":"他抡起手杖，敲碎前面一块土，喊道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He asked himself—","zh":"“我一定要把她弄到手！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where shall we meet? By what means? We shall always be having the brat on our hands, and the servant, the neighbours, and husband, all sorts of worries. Pshaw! one would lose too much time over it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Where shall we meet?","zh":"他立即考虑进行的策略。","scope":"group"},{"en":"By what means?","zh":"他立即考虑进行的策略。","scope":"group"},{"en":"We shall always be having the brat on our hands, and the servant, the neighbours, and husband, all sorts of worries.","zh":"他问自己：“到什么地方相会？用什么方法？小孩子死钉在后头，女用人、邻居、丈夫、形形色色的麻烦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Pshaw! one would lose too much time over it.”","zh":"——去他妈的！”他说：“太糟蹋时间！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he resumed, “She really has eyes that pierce one’s heart like a gimlet. And that pale complexion! I adore pale women!”","sentences":[{"en":"Then he resumed, “She really has eyes that pierce one’s heart like a gimlet.","zh":"“她那双眼睛就像钻子一样，一直旋进你的心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And that pale complexion!","zh":"还有脸色发白…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I adore pale women!”","zh":"我就爱脸色发白的女子！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When he reached the top of the Arguiel hills he had made up his mind. “It’s only finding the opportunities. Well, I will call in now and then. I’ll send them venison, poultry; I’ll have myself bled, if need be. We shall become friends; I’ll invite them to my place. By Jove!” added he, “there’s the agricultural show coming on. She’ll be there. I shall see her. We’ll begin boldly, for that’s the surest way.”","sentences":[{"en":"When he reached the top of the Arguiel hills he had made up his mind.","zh":"上到阿格伊岭，他下了决心：“问题只在寻找机会。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“It’s only finding the opportunities.","zh":"好啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, I will call in now and then.","zh":"我偶尔拜访两趟，送他们几只野味、几只家禽；必要的话，我去放放血；我们变成朋友，我请他们到家里来…啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll send them venison, poultry; I’ll have myself bled, if need be.","zh":"我偶尔拜访两趟，送他们几只野味、几只家禽；必要的话，我去放放血；我们变成朋友，我请他们到家里来…啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"We shall become friends; I’ll invite them to my place.","zh":"我偶尔拜访两趟，送他们几只野味、几只家禽；必要的话，我去放放血；我们变成朋友，我请他们到家里来…啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"By Jove!” added he, “there’s the agricultural show coming on.","zh":"有啦！”他灵机一动，道：“展览会不久就要举行；她会来的，我会看见她的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She’ll be there.","zh":"有啦！”他灵机一动，道：“展览会不久就要举行；她会来的，我会看见她的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I shall see her.","zh":"有啦！”他灵机一动，道：“展览会不久就要举行；她会来的，我会看见她的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"We’ll begin boldly, for that’s the surest way.”","zh":"趁热打铁，勇往直前，一定成功。”","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-8","part":2,"n":8,"title":"Part II · Chapter 8","titleZh":"中卷 · 8","paragraphs":[{"en":"At last it came, the famous agricultural show. On the morning of the solemnity all the inhabitants at their doors were chatting over the preparations. The pediment of the town hall had been hung with garlands of ivy; a tent had been erected in a meadow for the banquet; and in the middle of the Place, in front of the church, a kind of bombarde was to announce the arrival of the prefect and the names of the successful farmers who had obtained prizes. The National Guard of Buchy (there was none at Yonville) had come to join the corps of firemen, of whom Binet was captain. On that day he wore a collar even higher than usual; and, tightly buttoned in his tunic, his figure was so stiff and motionless that the whole vital portion of his person seemed to have descended into his legs, which rose in a cadence of set steps with a single movement. As there was some rivalry between the tax-collector and the colonel, both, to show off their talents, drilled their men separately. One saw the red epaulettes and the black breastplates pass and re-pass alternately; there was no end to it, and it constantly began again. There had never been such a display of pomp. Several citizens had scoured their houses the evening before; tri-coloured flags hung from half-open windows; all the public-houses were full; and in the lovely weather the starched caps, the golden crosses, and the coloured neckerchiefs seemed whiter than snow, shone in the sun, and relieved with the motley colours the sombre monotony of the frock-coats and blue smocks. The neighbouring farmers’ wives, when they got off their horses, pulled out the long pins that fastened around them their dresses, turned up for fear of mud; and the husbands, for their part, in order to save their hats, kept their handkerchiefs around them, holding one corner between their teeth.","sentences":[{"en":"At last it came, the famous agricultural show.","zh":"这有名的展览会确实到了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the morning of the solemnity all the inhabitants at their doors were chatting over the preparations.","zh":"从节日早晨起，居民就全站在门口，谈论应有的准备工作；镇公所正面缀着常春藤；草地搭起一座帐篷摆酒席；广场当中，教堂前面，有一架旧炮，到时宣告州长驾到和得奖的农民的姓名。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The pediment of the town hall had been hung with garlands of ivy; a tent had been erected in a meadow for the banquet; and in the middle of the Place, in front of the church, a kind of bombarde was to announce the arrival of the prefect and the names of the successful farmers who had obtained prizes.","zh":"从节日早晨起，居民就全站在门口，谈论应有的准备工作；镇公所正面缀着常春藤；草地搭起一座帐篷摆酒席；广场当中，教堂前面，有一架旧炮，到时宣告州长驾到和得奖的农民的姓名。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The National Guard of Buchy (there was none at Yonville) had come to join the corps of firemen, of whom Binet was captain.","zh":"比西的国民自卫军（永镇没有）开来参加毕耐率领的消防队。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On that day he wore a collar even higher than usual; and, tightly buttoned in his tunic, his figure was so stiff and motionless that the whole vital portion of his person seemed to have descended into his legs, which rose in a cadence of set steps with a single movement.","zh":"他这一天戴一条比平日还高的领子；制服紧绷绷的，上身直挺挺的，一动不动，就像气血统统移到下边两条腿里一样；他按照节奏，抬高两条腿，步伐合拍，起落一致。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As there was some rivalry between the tax-collector and the colonel, both, to show off their talents, drilled their men separately.","zh":"税务员和联队长，争强好胜，炫耀才能，分别率领部下，在一旁操练，就见红肩章和黑胸甲 ，过来过去，川流不息，简直没完没了！","scope":"group"},{"en":"One saw the red epaulettes and the black breastplates pass and re-pass alternately; there was no end to it, and it constantly began again.","zh":"税务员和联队长，争强好胜，炫耀才能，分别率领部下，在一旁操练，就见红肩章和黑胸甲 ，过来过去，川流不息，简直没完没了！","scope":"group"},{"en":"There had never been such a display of pomp.","zh":"如此庄严景象，从未见过！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Several citizens had scoured their houses the evening before; tri-coloured flags hung from half-open windows; all the public-houses were full; and in the lovely weather the starched caps, the golden crosses, and the coloured neckerchiefs seemed whiter than snow, shone in the sun, and relieved with the motley colours the sombre monotony of the frock-coats and blue smocks.","zh":"有些人家，前一天刷洗干净房屋，窗户开开一半，三色旗挂在外头；家家酒店客满；天气晴和，上浆的帽子、金十字架和花肩巾，仿佛比雪还白，在明亮的阳光下，熠熠发光，同时五颜六色，星星点点，衬得一般颜色较深的大衣和蓝布工人服也醒目了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The neighbouring farmers’ wives, when they got off their horses, pulled out the long pins that fastened around them their dresses, turned up for fear of mud; and the husbands, for their part, in order to save their hats, kept their handkerchiefs around them, holding one corner between their teeth.","zh":"四乡佃农妇女，生怕袍子沾上泥点，兜身撩起，拿大别针别好，临到下马，再解下来；丈夫相反，爱惜帽子，用手绢从上包住，拿牙咬牢手绢的一个犄角。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The crowd came into the main street from both ends of the village. People poured in from the lanes, the alleys, the houses; and from time to time one heard knockers banging against doors closing behind women with their gloves, who were going out to see the fete. What was most admired were two long lamp-stands covered with lanterns, that flanked a platform on which the authorities were to sit. Besides this there were against the four columns of the town hall four kinds of poles, each bearing a small standard of greenish cloth, embellished with inscriptions in gold letters.","sentences":[{"en":"The crowd came into the main street from both ends of the village.","zh":"人们从村子两头涌进大街。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People poured in from the lanes, the alleys, the houses; and from time to time one heard knockers banging against doors closing behind women with their gloves, who were going out to see the fete.","zh":"小巷、夹道、远房近舍，到处有人出来；门环时刻响动，太太们戴上线手套，去看热闹。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was most admired were two long lamp-stands covered with lanterns, that flanked a platform on which the authorities were to sit.","zh":"一对尖塔似的长三脚架，立在司令台两侧，上上下下全是花灯，特别为人称道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides this there were against the four columns of the town hall four kinds of poles, each bearing a small standard of greenish cloth, embellished with inscriptions in gold letters.","zh":"此外还有四根竿子，绑在镇公所四根圆柱 上，各自挑起一幅淡绿小布幡，金字标语，一幅写着：“商业”；另一幅写着：“农业”；第三幅写着：“工业”；第四幅写着：“艺术”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On one was written, “To Commerce”; on the other, “To Agriculture”; on the third, “To Industry”; and on the fourth, “To the Fine Arts.”","sentences":[{"en":"On one was written, “To Commerce”; on the other, “To Agriculture”; on the third, “To Industry”; and on the fourth, “To the Fine Arts.”","zh":"人人笑逐颜开，只有女店家勒弗朗索瓦太太，显得愁眉苦脸，站在厨房台阶，嘴里咕咕哝哝道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the jubilation that brightened all faces seemed to darken that of Madame Lefrancois, the innkeeper. Standing on her kitchen-steps she muttered to herself, “What rubbish! what rubbish! With their canvas booth! Do they think the prefect will be glad to dine down there under a tent like a gipsy? They call all this fussing doing good to the place! Then it wasn’t worth while sending to Neufchâtel for the keeper of a cookshop! And for whom? For cowherds! tatterdemalions!”","sentences":[{"en":"But the jubilation that brightened all faces seemed to darken that of Madame Lefrancois, the innkeeper.","zh":"“简直胡闹！帆布摊子，简直胡闹！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Standing on her kitchen-steps she muttered to herself, “What rubbish! what rubbish!","zh":"难道他们以为州长也像一个卖艺的，喜欢坐在棚子底下吃饭吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"With their canvas booth!","zh":"难道他们以为州长也像一个卖艺的，喜欢坐在棚子底下吃饭吗？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Do they think the prefect will be glad to dine down there under a tent like a gipsy?","zh":"这些碍手碍脚的东西，也好说成给本乡增光！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They call all this fussing doing good to the place!","zh":"所以啊，根本就犯不上到新堡找一个糟厨子来！而且为谁找？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then it wasn’t worth while sending to Neufchâtel for the keeper of a cookshop!","zh":"所以啊，根本就犯不上到新堡找一个糟厨子来！而且为谁找？","scope":"group"},{"en":"And for whom?","zh":"为些放牛的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For cowherds! tatterdemalions!”","zh":"一些叫花子！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The druggist was passing. He had on a frock-coat, nankeen trousers, beaver shoes, and, for a wonder, a hat with a low crown.","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist was passing.","zh":"药剂师过来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had on a frock-coat, nankeen trousers, beaver shoes, and, for a wonder, a hat with a low crown.","zh":"他穿一件青燕尾服、一条南京布裤、一双海狸皮鞋，还戴一顶毡帽——一顶矮筒毡帽，真正难得。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Your servant! Excuse me, I am in a hurry.” And as the fat widow asked where he was going—","sentences":[{"en":"“Your servant!","zh":"“您好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Excuse me, I am in a hurry.”","zh":"对不住，我有急事。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And as the fat widow asked where he was going—","zh":"胖寡妇问他去什么地方，他回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It seems odd to you, doesn’t it, I who am always more cooped up in my laboratory than the man’s rat in his cheese.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It seems odd to you, doesn’t it, I who am always more cooped up in my laboratory than the man’s rat in his cheese.”","zh":"“您觉得好笑，是不是？我一直关在我的实验室，比老鼠在好好先生的干酪里 待得还久。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What cheese?” asked the landlady.","sentences":[{"en":"“What cheese?” asked the landlady.","zh":"女店家道：“什么干酪？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, nothing! nothing!” Homais continued. “I merely wished to convey to you, Madame Lefrancois, that I usually live at home like a recluse. To-day, however, considering the circumstances, it is necessary—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, nothing! nothing!”","zh":"郝麦接下去道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais continued.","zh":"“没有什么！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I merely wished to convey to you, Madame Lefrancois, that I usually live at home like a recluse.","zh":"没有什么！我只是告诉您，勒弗朗索瓦太太，我经常闭门不出，可是今天，情形特殊，我必须…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"To-day, however, considering the circumstances, it is necessary—”","zh":"没有什么！我只是告诉您，勒弗朗索瓦太太，我经常闭门不出，可是今天，情形特殊，我必须…”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, you’re going down there!” she said contemptuously.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, you’re going down there!” she said contemptuously.","zh":"她显出一副蔑视的神气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, I am going,” replied the druggist, astonished. “Am I not a member of the consulting commission?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, I am going,” replied the druggist, astonished.","zh":"“啊！您到那边去？”药剂师诧异了，回答道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Am I not a member of the consulting commission?”","zh":"“是呀，那边去；我不是咨询委员会的委员吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Mere Lefrancois looked at him for a few moments, and ended by saying with a smile—","sentences":[{"en":"Mere Lefrancois looked at him for a few moments, and ended by saying with a smile—","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太打量了他几分钟，最后笑吟吟回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That’s another pair of shoes! But what does agriculture matter to you? Do you understand anything about it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s another pair of shoes!","zh":"“原来是这样！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But what does agriculture matter to you?","zh":"不过耕地关您什么事？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you understand anything about it?”","zh":"难道您懂这个？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Certainly I understand it, since I am a druggist—that is to say, a chemist. And the object of chemistry, Madame Lefrancois, being the knowledge of the reciprocal and molecular action of all natural bodies, it follows that agriculture is comprised within its domain. And, in fact, the composition of the manure, the fermentation of liquids, the analyses of gases, and the influence of miasmata, what, I ask you, is all this, if it isn’t chemistry, pure and simple?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Certainly I understand it, since I am a druggist—that is to say, a chemist.","zh":"“当然懂，因为我是药剂师，就是说，化学家！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And the object of chemistry, Madame Lefrancois, being the knowledge of the reciprocal and molecular action of all natural bodies, it follows that agriculture is comprised within its domain.","zh":"而化学，勒弗朗索瓦太太，目的就在认识自然界一切物体的分子的相互作用，农业自然也就包括在它的范围内！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And, in fact, the composition of the manure, the fermentation of liquids, the analyses of gases, and the influence of miasmata, what, I ask you, is all this, if it isn’t chemistry, pure and simple?”","zh":"事实上，肥料的配合、酒的发酵、煤气的分析和瘴气的影响，我问您，这一切，不是化学，又是什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The landlady did not answer. Homais went on—","sentences":[{"en":"The landlady did not answer.","zh":"女店家并不回答。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais went on—","zh":"郝麦继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do you think that to be an agriculturist it is necessary to have tilled the earth or fattened fowls oneself? It is necessary rather to know the composition of the substances in question—the geological strata, the atmospheric actions, the quality of the soil, the minerals, the waters, the density of the different bodies, their capillarity, and what not. And one must be master of all the principles of hygiene in order to direct, criticize the construction of buildings, the feeding of animals, the diet of domestics. And, moreover, Madame Lefrancois, one must know botany, be able to distinguish between plants, you understand, which are the wholesome and those that are deleterious, which are unproductive and which nutritive, if it is well to pull them up here and re-sow them there, to propagate some, destroy others; in brief, one must keep pace with science by means of pamphlets and public papers, be always on the alert to find out improvements.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you think that to be an agriculturist it is necessary to have tilled the earth or fattened fowls oneself?","zh":"“难道您以为做农学家，本人就该耕田、喂家禽吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is necessary rather to know the composition of the substances in question—the geological strata, the atmospheric actions, the quality of the soil, the minerals, the waters, the density of the different bodies, their capillarity, and what not.","zh":"他首先应当知道的，倒是有关物质的成分，地层的次序，大气的作用，土地、矿石和雨水的性质，不同物体的密度和它们的毛细管现象！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And one must be master of all the principles of hygiene in order to direct, criticize the construction of buildings, the feeding of animals, the diet of domestics.","zh":"等等，等等。他应该彻底掌握全部卫生原则，以便指导、批评房屋的构造、牲畜的管理、仆人的饮食！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And, moreover, Madame Lefrancois, one must know botany, be able to distinguish between plants, you understand, which are the wholesome and those that are deleterious, which are unproductive and which nutritive, if it is well to pull them up here and re-sow them there, to propagate some, destroy others; in brief, one must keep pace with science by means of pamphlets and public papers, be always on the alert to find out improvements.”","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太，还应当掌握植物学，学会辨别草木。您明白不？哪些对身体有益、哪些对身体有害；哪些产量低、哪些有营养；这里是否该拔掉，那里是否该补种，是否推广这个，消灭那个；总而言之，应当读小册子，看出版物，迎头赶上科学潮流，永远有准备，随时指出改良的道路…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The landlady never took her eyes off the “Cafe Francois” and the chemist went on—","sentences":[{"en":"The landlady never took her eyes off the “Cafe Francois” and the chemist went on—","zh":"女店家的眼睛不离开法兰西咖啡馆的门。药剂师继续发挥道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Would to God our agriculturists were chemists, or that at least they would pay more attention to the counsels of science. Thus lately I myself wrote a considerable tract, a memoir of over seventy-two pages, entitled, ‘Cider, its Manufacture and its Effects, together with some New Reflections on the Subject,’ that I sent to the Agricultural Society of Rouen, and which even procured me the honour of being received among its members—Section, Agriculture; Class, Pomological. Well, if my work had been given to the public—” But the druggist stopped, Madame Lefrancois seemed so preoccupied.","sentences":[{"en":"“Would to God our agriculturists were chemists, or that at least they would pay more attention to the counsels of science.","zh":"“但愿我们的农民都是化学家，或者起码多听听科学建议，也就好了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus lately I myself wrote a considerable tract, a memoir of over seventy-two pages, entitled, ‘Cider, its Manufacture and its Effects, together with some New Reflections on the Subject,’ that I sent to the Agricultural Society of Rouen, and which even procured me the honour of being received among its members—Section, Agriculture; Class, Pomological.","zh":"所以我最近写了一部出色的小书，一篇七十二页之多的论文，题目是：《论苹果酒及其酿造与效用，附有新见解》，我送到鲁昂农学会去了；他们接受我当会员，分在农学组果学类；是啊，我的作品如果公之于世…”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, if my work had been given to the public—” But the druggist stopped, Madame Lefrancois seemed so preoccupied.","zh":"但是药剂师一看勒弗朗索瓦太太心在别处，也就住了口。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Just look at them!” she said. “It’s past comprehension! Such a cookshop as that!” And with a shrug of the shoulders that stretched out over her breast the stitches of her knitted bodice, she pointed with both hands at her rival’s inn, whence songs were heard issuing. “Well, it won’t last long,” she added. “It’ll be over before a week.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Just look at them!” she said.","zh":"“看他们哎！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“It’s past comprehension!","zh":"简直不像话！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Such a cookshop as that!”","zh":"成了饭摊子！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And with a shrug of the shoulders that stretched out over her breast the stitches of her knitted bodice, she pointed with both hands at her rival’s inn, whence songs were heard issuing.","zh":"她一耸肩膀，胸脯上毛衣的网眼也绷开了。她的对头酒馆传出歌唱的声音。她伸出一双手，边指点，边接下去道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Well, it won’t last long,” she added.","zh":"“其实，也长不了；不到一星期，整个完蛋。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’ll be over before a week.”","zh":"“其实，也长不了；不到一星期，整个完蛋。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Homais drew back with stupefaction. She came down three steps and whispered in his ear—","sentences":[{"en":"Homais drew back with stupefaction.","zh":"郝麦听了这话，大吃一惊，往后倒退。她走下三级台阶，俯耳向他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"She came down three steps and whispered in his ear—","zh":"郝麦听了这话，大吃一惊，往后倒退。她走下三级台阶，俯耳向他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What! you didn’t know it? There is to be an execution in next week. It’s Lheureux who is selling him out; he has killed him with bills.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What! you didn’t know it?","zh":"“怎么！您不知道？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There is to be an execution in next week.","zh":"本星期就要执行扣押。是勒乐坑了他。他出借票害了他。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It’s Lheureux who is selling him out; he has killed him with bills.”","zh":"世上任何情况，只要想得出来，药剂师总有词句配合，所以他就嚷道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What a terrible catastrophe!” cried the druggist, who always found expressions in harmony with all imaginable circumstances.","sentences":[{"en":"“What a terrible catastrophe!” cried the druggist, who always found expressions in harmony with all imaginable circumstances.","zh":"“有这等惊人的祸事！”女店家于是讲起这件事的来龙去脉。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then the landlady began telling him the story that she had heard from Theodore, Monsieur Guillaumin’s servant, and although she detested Tellier, she blamed Lheureux. He was “a wheedler, a sneak.”","sentences":[{"en":"Then the landlady began telling him the story that she had heard from Theodore, Monsieur Guillaumin’s servant, and although she detested Tellier, she blamed Lheureux.","zh":"她是听居由曼先生的听差泰奥多尔说的。她恨泰里耶，可是她也怪罪勒乐：他是个佞口骗子、一个卑鄙小人。她道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was “a wheedler, a sneak.”","zh":"她是听居由曼先生的听差泰奥多尔说的。她恨泰里耶，可是她也怪罪勒乐：他是个佞口骗子、一个卑鄙小人。她道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“There!” she said. “Look at him! he is in the market; he is bowing to Madame Bovary, who’s got on a green bonnet. Why, she’s taking Monsieur Boulanger’s arm.”","sentences":[{"en":"“There!” she said.","zh":"“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Look at him! he is in the market; he is bowing to Madame Bovary, who’s got on a green bonnet.","zh":"您看，他在菜场，冲包法利太太行礼。包法利太太戴一顶绿帽子，还挎着布朗热先生的胳膊。”郝麦道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Why, she’s taking Monsieur Boulanger’s arm.”","zh":"您看，他在菜场，冲包法利太太行礼。包法利太太戴一顶绿帽子，还挎着布朗热先生的胳膊。”郝麦道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Madame Bovary!” exclaimed Homais. “I must go at once and pay her my respects. Perhaps she’ll be very glad to have a seat in the enclosure under the peristyle.” And, without heeding Madame Lefrancois, who was calling him back to tell him more about it, the druggist walked off rapidly with a smile on his lips, with straight knees, bowing copiously to right and left, and taking up much room with the large tails of his frock-coat that fluttered behind him in the wind.","sentences":[{"en":"“Madame Bovary!” exclaimed Homais.","zh":"“包法利太太！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I must go at once and pay her my respects.","zh":"我要赶过去，表示一下我的敬意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps she’ll be very glad to have a seat in the enclosure under the peristyle.”","zh":"她也许高兴在近处廊子底下来一个座位。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And, without heeding Madame Lefrancois, who was calling him back to tell him more about it, the druggist walked off rapidly with a smile on his lips, with straight knees, bowing copiously to right and left, and taking up much room with the large tails of his frock-coat that fluttered behind him in the wind.","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太喊他回来，还要一五一十讲下去，可是药剂师不理睬，快步走开。他左一躬，右一躬，笑容可掬，后腿弯子蹬直，青燕尾服的大小摆在后头随风飘荡，占了好大地方。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe, having caught sight of him from afar, hurried on, but Madame Bovary lost her breath; so he walked more slowly, and, smiling at her, said in a rough tone—","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe, having caught sight of him from afar, hurried on, but Madame Bovary lost her breath; so he walked more slowly, and, smiling at her, said in a rough tone—","zh":"罗道耳弗远远望见他来，也走快了，不过包法利夫人气喘，他只好放慢步子，粗声粗气，笑微微向她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It’s only to get away from that fat fellow, you know, the druggist.” She pressed his elbow.","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s only to get away from that fat fellow, you know, the druggist.”","zh":"“我是为了避开那个胖家伙，您知道，药剂师。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She pressed his elbow.","zh":"“我是为了避开那个胖家伙，您知道，药剂师。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What’s the meaning of that?” he asked himself. And he looked at her out of the corner of his eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s the meaning of that?” he asked himself.","zh":"她拿胳膊肘捅了他一下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he looked at her out of the corner of his eyes.","zh":"他暗琢磨：她这是什么意思？他边走，边乜斜眼睛打量她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her profile was so calm that one could guess nothing from it. It stood out in the light from the oval of her bonnet, with pale ribbons on it like the leaves of weeds. Her eyes with their long curved lashes looked straight before her, and though wide open, they seemed slightly puckered by the cheek-bones, because of the blood pulsing gently under the delicate skin. A pink line ran along the partition between her nostrils. Her head was bent upon her shoulder, and the pearl tips of her white teeth were seen between her lips.","sentences":[{"en":"Her profile was so calm that one could guess nothing from it.","zh":"看她的侧面，十分安详，简直什么也看不出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It stood out in the light from the oval of her bonnet, with pale ribbons on it like the leaves of weeds.","zh":"她戴的帽子是椭圆形，白帽带仿佛芦苇叶子，阳光灿烂，把脸照得特别清楚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her eyes with their long curved lashes looked straight before her, and though wide open, they seemed slightly puckered by the cheek-bones, because of the blood pulsing gently under the delicate skin.","zh":"长睫毛弯弯的，眼睛虽然睁开了朝前望，可是由于血在白净皮肤底下轻轻跳动的缘故，看上去睁得还不够痛快，有一点像是颧骨在拘着眼睛似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A pink line ran along the partition between her nostrils.","zh":"一道玫瑰红颜色照亮鼻孔之间的中隔。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her head was bent upon her shoulder, and the pearl tips of her white teeth were seen between her lips.","zh":"头朝一边歪，嘴唇当中露出皓白牙齿的珍珠似的尖梢。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Is she making fun of me?” thought Rodolphe.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is she making fun of me?” thought Rodolphe.","zh":"罗道耳弗心想：难道她是讥笑我？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma’s gesture, however, had only been meant for a warning; for Monsieur Lheureux was accompanying them, and spoke now and again as if to enter into the conversation.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma’s gesture, however, had only been meant for a warning; for Monsieur Lheureux was accompanying them, and spoke now and again as if to enter into the conversation.","zh":"其实，爱玛捅他，只是一种警告；因为勒乐先生陪伴他们，像煞有意搭话似的，不时插上一句：“今天可真好！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What a superb day! Everybody is out! The wind is east!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What a superb day!","zh":"其实，爱玛捅他，只是一种警告；因为勒乐先生陪伴他们，像煞有意搭话似的，不时插上一句：“今天可真好！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Everybody is out!","zh":"“人人上街！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The wind is east!”","zh":"“风打东来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And neither Madame Bovary nor Rodolphe answered him, whilst at the slightest movement made by them he drew near, saying, “I beg your pardon!” and raised his hat.","sentences":[{"en":"And neither Madame Bovary nor Rodolphe answered him, whilst at the slightest movement made by them he drew near, saying, “I beg your pardon!” and raised his hat.","zh":"包法利夫人，还有罗道耳弗，并不理他，可是他们稍微一动，他就碰碰帽子，凑到近边，说：“什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When they reached the farrier’s house, instead of following the road up to the fence, Rodolphe suddenly turned down a path, drawing with him Madame Bovary. He called out—","sentences":[{"en":"When they reached the farrier’s house, instead of following the road up to the fence, Rodolphe suddenly turned down a path, drawing with him Madame Bovary.","zh":"来到马掌铺前面，罗道耳弗不沿大路去栅栏门，却骤然带了包法利夫人，拐进小径，喊道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He called out—","zh":"来到马掌铺前面，罗道耳弗不沿大路去栅栏门，却骤然带了包法利夫人，拐进小径，喊道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Good evening, Monsieur Lheureux! See you again presently.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Good evening, Monsieur Lheureux!","zh":"“晚安，勒乐先生！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"See you again presently.”","zh":"再见！”她笑道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How you got rid of him!” she said, laughing.","sentences":[{"en":"“How you got rid of him!” she said, laughing.","zh":"“您怎么这样打发他！”他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why,” he went on, “allow oneself to be intruded upon by others? And as to-day I have the happiness of being with you—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why,” he went on, “allow oneself to be intruded upon by others?","zh":"“为什么让人打搅？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And as to-day I have the happiness of being with you—”","zh":"何况今天，我有福分同您…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma blushed. He did not finish his sentence. Then he talked of the fine weather and of the pleasure of walking on the grass. A few daisies had sprung up again.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma blushed.","zh":"爱玛红了脸。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He did not finish his sentence.","zh":"爱玛红了脸。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he talked of the fine weather and of the pleasure of walking on the grass.","zh":"他掉转话头，说起天气晴好和草地上散步的愉快。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A few daisies had sprung up again.","zh":"有些春白菊又长出来了。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Here are some pretty Easter daisies,” he said, “and enough of them to furnish oracles to all the amorous maids in the place.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Here are some pretty Easter daisies,” he said, “and enough of them to furnish oracles to all the amorous maids in the place.”","zh":"“这里有好看的延命菊，大可以供本地全部害相思病的姑娘们问卜了。”紧跟着他又说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He added, “Shall I pick some? What do you think?”","sentences":[{"en":"He added, “Shall I pick some?","zh":"“要是我也掐一朵，您看怎么样？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"What do you think?”","zh":"“要是我也掐一朵，您看怎么样？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Are you in love?” she asked, coughing a little.","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you in love?” she asked, coughing a little.","zh":"她微微咳嗽道：“您闹恋爱？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“H’m, h’m! who knows?” answered Rodolphe.","sentences":[{"en":"“H’m, h’m! who knows?” answered Rodolphe.","zh":"罗道耳弗回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The meadow began to fill, and the housewives hustled you with their great umbrellas, their baskets, and their babies. One had often to get out of the way of a long file of country folk, servant-maids with blue stockings, flat shoes, silver rings, and who smelt of milk, when one passed close to them. They walked along holding one another by the hand, and thus they spread over the whole field from the row of open trees to the banquet tent.","sentences":[{"en":"The meadow began to fill, and the housewives hustled you with their great umbrellas, their baskets, and their babies.","zh":"“哎！哎！谁知道？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One had often to get out of the way of a long file of country folk, servant-maids with blue stockings, flat shoes, silver rings, and who smelt of milk, when one passed close to them.","zh":"草地上开始拥挤。管家婆挟着大雨伞，提着盒子，拖着孩子，朝你身上撞。还得经常回避一长列乡下妇人、女用人，她们穿蓝袜子、平底鞋，戴银戒指，你从旁边走过，闻见一股牛奶气味。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They walked along holding one another by the hand, and thus they spread over the whole field from the row of open trees to the banquet tent.","zh":"她们走路手拉手，从那排白杨起，到宴会的帐篷为止，熙熙攘攘，满草原全是。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But this was the examination time, and the farmers one after the other entered a kind of enclosure formed by a long cord supported on sticks.","sentences":[{"en":"But this was the examination time, and the farmers one after the other entered a kind of enclosure formed by a long cord supported on sticks.","zh":"不过审查时间到了，农民一个跟一个，走进一个赛马场似的地点：一条长绳，拴在桩子上，圈出这样一块空地。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The beasts were there, their noses towards the cord, and making a confused line with their unequal rumps. Drowsy pigs were burrowing in the earth with their snouts, calves were bleating, lambs baaing; the cows, on knees folded in, were stretching their bellies on the grass, slowly chewing the cud, and blinking their heavy eyelids at the gnats that buzzed round them. Plough-men with bare arms were holding by the halter prancing stallions that neighed with dilated nostrils looking towards the mares. These stood quietly, stretching out their heads and flowing manes, while their foals rested in their shadow, or now and then came and sucked them. And above the long undulation of these crowded animals one saw some white mane rising in the wind like a wave, or some sharp horns sticking out, and the heads of men running about. Apart, outside the enclosure, a hundred paces off, was a large black bull, muzzled, with an iron ring in its nostrils, and who moved no more than if he had been in bronze. A child in rags was holding him by a rope.","sentences":[{"en":"The beasts were there, their noses towards the cord, and making a confused line with their unequal rumps.","zh":"里头是牲口，鼻子冲着绳子，屁股有大有小，乱乱腾腾，排一长条。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Drowsy pigs were burrowing in the earth with their snouts, calves were bleating, lambs baaing; the cows, on knees folded in, were stretching their bellies on the grass, slowly chewing the cud, and blinking their heavy eyelids at the gnats that buzzed round them.","zh":"猪昏头昏脑，拿嘴拱土；牛犊叫；羊羔咩；母牛曲起后腿弯子，肚皮贴着草地，也不管牛蝇围住身子嗡嗡乱飞，眨巴着沉重的眼皮，慢条斯理，来回嚼嘴里的东西。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Plough-men with bare arms were holding by the halter prancing stallions that neighed with dilated nostrils looking towards the mares.","zh":"种马尥起蹶子，朝母马扯嗓子嘶鸣，赶大车的光着胳膊，揪住种马的缰绳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"These stood quietly, stretching out their heads and flowing manes, while their foals rested in their shadow, or now and then came and sucked them.","zh":"母马安安静静，伸长头和耷拉下来的鬣毛，马驹不是躺在母马身影里，就是偶尔凑到底下吮奶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And above the long undulation of these crowded animals one saw some white mane rising in the wind like a wave, or some sharp horns sticking out, and the heads of men running about.","zh":"这些牲口挤作一团，起伏无定，不是雪白的鬣毛波涛一般随风扬起，就是东露出一堆尖犄角，西露出一堆人头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Apart, outside the enclosure, a hundred paces off, was a large black bull, muzzled, with an iron ring in its nostrils, and who moved no more than if he had been in bronze.","zh":"人在里头跑来跑去。围场外边，百步远近，单有一只大黑公牛，戴上嘴套，鼻孔挂着一个铁环环，像青铜铸出来的，站着一动不动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A child in rags was holding him by a rope.","zh":"一个衣服破烂的小孩子牵着它，揪住一条绳子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Between the two lines the committee-men were walking with heavy steps, examining each animal, then consulting one another in a low voice. One who seemed of more importance now and then took notes in a book as he walked along. This was the president of the jury, Monsieur Derozerays de la Panville. As soon as he recognised Rodolphe he came forward quickly, and smiling amiably, said—","sentences":[{"en":"Between the two lines the committee-men were walking with heavy steps, examining each animal, then consulting one another in a low voice.","zh":"大人先生们夹在两排牲口当中，步伐沉重，一面前进，一面一只一只检查，检查过后，就彼此会商，声音相当低。其中一位，似乎地位更高，边走边记。","scope":"group"},{"en":"One who seemed of more importance now and then took notes in a book as he walked along.","zh":"大人先生们夹在两排牲口当中，步伐沉重，一面前进，一面一只一只检查，检查过后，就彼此会商，声音相当低。其中一位，似乎地位更高，边走边记。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This was the president of the jury, Monsieur Derozerays de la Panville.","zh":"他是评判委员会主席、邦镇的德罗兹赖先生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As soon as he recognised Rodolphe he came forward quickly, and smiling amiably, said—","zh":"他一看见罗道耳弗，就快步向前，和颜悦色，笑吟吟向他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What! Monsieur Boulanger, you are deserting us?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What!","zh":"“布朗热先生，您怎么放下大家伙儿的事不管？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Boulanger, you are deserting us?”","zh":"“布朗热先生，您怎么放下大家伙儿的事不管？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe protested that he was just coming. But when the president had disappeared—","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe protested that he was just coming.","zh":"罗道耳弗保证他来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But when the president had disappeared—","zh":"可是主席刚走远，他就说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ma foi!” said he, “I shall not go. Your company is better than his.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ma foi!” said he, “I shall not go.","zh":"“家伙，我才不去，同您在一起，比同他在一起好得多。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Your company is better than his.”","zh":"“家伙，我才不去，同您在一起，比同他在一起好得多。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And while poking fun at the show, Rodolphe, to move about more easily, showed the gendarme his blue card, and even stopped now and then in front of some fine beast, which Madame Bovary did not at all admire. He noticed this, and began jeering at the Yonville ladies and their dresses; then he apologised for the negligence of his own. He had that incongruity of common and elegant in which the habitually vulgar think they see the revelation of an eccentric existence, of the perturbations of sentiment, the tyrannies of art, and always a certain contempt for social conventions, that seduces or exasperates them. Thus his cambric shirt with plaited cuffs was blown out by the wind in the opening of his waistcoat of grey ticking, and his broad-striped trousers disclosed at the ankle nankeen boots with patent leather gaiters.","sentences":[{"en":"And while poking fun at the show, Rodolphe, to move about more easily, showed the gendarme his blue card, and even stopped now and then in front of some fine beast, which Madame Bovary did not at all admire.","zh":"罗道耳弗一面打趣展览会，一面却也为了通行无阻起见，掏出他的蓝帖子给宪兵看，有时候甚至看见一件好展品，停住脚步。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He noticed this, and began jeering at the Yonville ladies and their dresses; then he apologised for the negligence of his own.","zh":"可是他一见包法利夫人不感兴趣，就拿装束作题目，取笑永镇的太太们。跟着他就为他的衣着马虎道歉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had that incongruity of common and elegant in which the habitually vulgar think they see the revelation of an eccentric existence, of the perturbations of sentiment, the tyrannies of art, and always a certain contempt for social conventions, that seduces or exasperates them.","zh":"他的衣着又随俗，又考究，显出不协调的情调，一般人看了，有的会受吸引，有的会感到愤慨，因为他们总觉得这种装束，表示生活离奇、感情纷乱、艺术的强大影响以及某种永远蔑视社会习俗的心理。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus his cambric shirt with plaited cuffs was blown out by the wind in the opening of his waistcoat of grey ticking, and his broad-striped trousers disclosed at the ankle nankeen boots with patent leather gaiters.","zh":"细麻布衬衫的袖口缀着褶纹纱，风吹过来，衬衫就在灰夏布背心领口地方鼓了起来；宽道道裤子，脚踝地方，露出一双南京布靴子，靴筒底下有一圈漆皮，亮堂堂的，草也照了出来。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"These were so polished that they reflected the grass. He trampled on horses’s dung with them, one hand in the pocket of his jacket and his straw hat on one side.","sentences":[{"en":"These were so polished that they reflected the grass.","zh":"细麻布衬衫的袖口缀着褶纹纱，风吹过来，衬衫就在灰夏布背心领口地方鼓了起来；宽道道裤子，脚踝地方，露出一双南京布靴子，靴筒底下有一圈漆皮，亮堂堂的，草也照了出来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He trampled on horses’s dung with them, one hand in the pocket of his jacket and his straw hat on one side.","zh":"他穿着这样一双靴子，践踏马粪，一只手插在上衣口袋，草帽歪戴一旁。他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Besides,” added he, “when one lives in the country—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Besides,” added he, “when one lives in the country—”","zh":"“再说，一个人住在乡下…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It’s waste of time,” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s waste of time,” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛道：“什么也是枉然。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That is true,” replied Rodolphe. “To think that not one of these people is capable of understanding even the cut of a coat!”","sentences":[{"en":"“That is true,” replied Rodolphe.","zh":"罗道耳弗回答道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“To think that not one of these people is capable of understanding even the cut of a coat!”","zh":"“说得是呀！想想看，这些老好人，就连燕尾服的式样，也没有一个人能懂！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then they talked about provincial mediocrity, of the lives it crushed, the illusions lost there.","sentences":[{"en":"Then they talked about provincial mediocrity, of the lives it crushed, the illusions lost there.","zh":"于是他们谈起内地的庸俗、生活的窒闷、理想的毁灭。罗道耳弗道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And I too,” said Rodolphe, “am drifting into depression.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And I too,” said Rodolphe, “am drifting into depression.”","zh":"“所以我郁闷到了极点…”她诧异道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You!” she said in astonishment; “I thought you very light-hearted.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You!” she said in astonishment; “I thought you very light-hearted.”","zh":"“您！我一直以为您很快活，不是吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! yes. I seem so, because in the midst of the world I know how to wear the mask of a scoffer upon my face; and yet, how many a time at the sight of a cemetery by moonlight have I not asked myself whether it were not better to join those sleeping there!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! yes.","zh":"“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I seem so, because in the midst of the world I know how to wear the mask of a scoffer upon my face; and yet, how many a time at the sight of a cemetery by moonlight have I not asked myself whether it were not better to join those sleeping there!”","zh":"是的，单看外表；因为我对社会戴了一副玩世不恭的面具。其实，月光之下，看见公墓，有多少回，我问自己：我是不是顶好还是追踪那些长眠地下的人…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh! and your friends?” she said. “You do not think of them.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh! and your friends?” she said.","zh":"她道：“哎呀！您那些朋友呢？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“You do not think of them.”","zh":"您就不想想他们？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My friends! What friends? Have I any? Who cares for me?” And he accompanied the last words with a kind of whistling of the lips.","sentences":[{"en":"“My friends!","zh":"“我那些朋友？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What friends?","zh":"都是谁？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Have I any?","zh":"我有朋友吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who cares for me?”","zh":"谁关心我？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he accompanied the last words with a kind of whistling of the lips.","zh":"说到末一句话，嘴里同时吹出一种类似口哨的声音。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But they were obliged to separate from each other because of a great pile of chairs that a man was carrying behind them. He was so overladen with them that one could only see the tips of his wooden shoes and the ends of his two outstretched arms. It was Lestiboudois, the gravedigger, who was carrying the church chairs about amongst the people. Alive to all that concerned his interests, he had hit upon this means of turning the show to account; and his idea was succeeding, for he no longer knew which way to turn. In fact, the villagers, who were hot, quarreled for these seats, whose straw smelt of incense, and they leant against the thick backs, stained with the wax of candles, with a certain veneration.","sentences":[{"en":"But they were obliged to separate from each other because of a great pile of chairs that a man was carrying behind them.","zh":"不过后头走来一个人，抱了高高一摞椅子，他们只好分在两下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was so overladen with them that one could only see the tips of his wooden shoes and the ends of his two outstretched arms.","zh":"左也椅子，右也椅子，除去他的木头套鞋的尖尖头露在外面以外，就只看见他的胳膊伸得开开的，露出两只手来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Lestiboudois, the gravedigger, who was carrying the church chairs about amongst the people.","zh":"原来是那个掘坟的赖斯地布杜瓦，把教堂椅子搬到外头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Alive to all that concerned his interests, he had hit upon this means of turning the show to account; and his idea was succeeding, for he no longer knew which way to turn.","zh":"他想挣外快，结果想出这种利用展览会的方法，而且获得成功，因为生意兴隆，他应付不过来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In fact, the villagers, who were hot, quarreled for these seats, whose straw smelt of incense, and they leant against the thick backs, stained with the wax of candles, with a certain veneration.","zh":"说实话，乡下人热得受不了，全抢椅子坐，草垫有香料气味，厚椅背沾着蜡渍，他们恭而敬之，往上一靠。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary again took Rodolphe’s arm; he went on as if speaking to himself—","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary again took Rodolphe’s arm; he went on as if speaking to himself—","zh":"包法利夫人又挽起罗道耳弗的胳膊。他像是自言自语，继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, I have missed so many things. Always alone! Ah! if I had some aim in life, if I had met some love, if I had found someone! Oh, how I would have spent all the energy of which I am capable, surmounted everything, overcome everything!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, I have missed so many things.","zh":"“是啊！我错过许多机会！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Always alone!","zh":"总是一个人，啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! if I had some aim in life, if I had met some love, if I had found someone!","zh":"我活着要是有一个目的，我要是遇到真心相待的人，我要是发现有人…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, how I would have spent all the energy of which I am capable, surmounted everything, overcome everything!”","zh":"哎呀！我会竭尽全力，我会克服一切困难，粉碎一切困难！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet it seems to me,” said Emma, “that you are not to be pitied.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet it seems to me,” said Emma, “that you are not to be pitied.”","zh":"爱玛道：“不过我觉得您不该让人可怜。”罗道耳弗道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! you think so?” said Rodolphe.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! you think so?” said Rodolphe.","zh":"“啊！您觉得？”她接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For, after all,” she went on, “you are free—” she hesitated, “rich—”","sentences":[{"en":"“For, after all,” she went on, “you are free—” she hesitated, “rich—”","zh":"“因为说到临了…您自由。”她迟疑了一下：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do not mock me,” he replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do not mock me,” he replied.","zh":"“又有钱。”他回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she protested that she was not mocking him, when the report of a cannon resounded. Immediately all began hustling one another pell-mell towards the village.","sentences":[{"en":"And she protested that she was not mocking him, when the report of a cannon resounded.","zh":"“别取笑我啦。”她赌咒不是取笑，这期间只听轰然一声炮响，大家立刻你拥我挤，乱乱腾腾，往村里跑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Immediately all began hustling one another pell-mell towards the village.","zh":"“别取笑我啦。”她赌咒不是取笑，这期间只听轰然一声炮响，大家立刻你拥我挤，乱乱腾腾，往村里跑。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"It was a false alarm. The prefect seemed not to be coming, and the members of the jury felt much embarrassed, not knowing if they ought to begin the meeting or still wait.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a false alarm.","zh":"原来炮发错了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The prefect seemed not to be coming, and the members of the jury felt much embarrassed, not knowing if they ought to begin the meeting or still wait.","zh":"州长大人并没有来；这就开会，还是再等下去，评判委员们左右为难，不知道怎么办才好。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last at the end of the Place a large hired landau appeared, drawn by two thin horses, which a coachman in a white hat was whipping lustily. Binet had only just time to shout, “Present arms!” and the colonel to imitate him. All ran towards the enclosure; everyone pushed forward. A few even forgot their collars; but the equipage of the prefect seemed to anticipate the crowd, and the two yoked jades, trapesing in their harness, came up at a little trot in front of the peristyle of the town hall at the very moment when the National Guard and firemen deployed, beating drums and marking time.","sentences":[{"en":"At last at the end of the Place a large hired landau appeared, drawn by two thin horses, which a coachman in a white hat was whipping lustily.","zh":"最后，广场尽头，来了一辆前后有活篷的四轮出租大马车，驾着两匹瘦马，一个白帽车夫，狠命抽打。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Binet had only just time to shout, “Present arms!” and the colonel to imitate him.","zh":"毕耐急忙喊：“举枪！”联队长急忙学他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All ran towards the enclosure; everyone pushed forward.","zh":"人人朝枪位跑。人人向前抢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A few even forgot their collars; but the equipage of the prefect seemed to anticipate the crowd, and the two yoked jades, trapesing in their harness, came up at a little trot in front of the peristyle of the town hall at the very moment when the National Guard and firemen deployed, beating drums and marking time.","zh":"有些人连硬领也忘记戴了。但是州长的马车，似乎意会到这种困难局面，两匹并驾的羸马，拉起辕木链子，摇摇晃晃，小步紧跑，来到镇公所前面，正好赶上国民自卫军和消防队打着鼓，大踏步，摆队相迎。毕耐喊着：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Present!” shouted Binet.","sentences":[{"en":"“Present!” shouted Binet.","zh":"“齐步走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Halt!” shouted the colonel. “Left about, march.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Halt!” shouted the colonel.","zh":"联队长喊着：“立正！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Left about, march.”","zh":"向左看齐！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And after presenting arms, during which the clang of the band, letting loose, rang out like a brass kettle rolling downstairs, all the guns were lowered. Then was seen stepping down from the carriage a gentleman in a short coat with silver braiding, with bald brow, and wearing a tuft of hair at the back of his head, of a sallow complexion and the most benign appearance. His eyes, very large and covered by heavy lids, were half-closed to look at the crowd, while at the same time he raised his sharp nose, and forced a smile upon his sunken mouth. He recognised the mayor by his scarf, and explained to him that the prefect was not able to come. He himself was a councillor at the prefecture; then he added a few apologies. Monsieur Tuvache answered them with compliments; the other confessed himself nervous; and they remained thus, face to face, their foreheads almost touching, with the members of the jury all round, the municipal council, the notable personages, the National Guard and the crowd. The councillor pressing his little cocked hat to his breast repeated his bows, while Tuvache, bent like a bow, also smiled, stammered, tried to say something, protested his devotion to the monarchy and the honour that was being done to Yonville.","sentences":[{"en":"And after presenting arms, during which the clang of the band, letting loose, rang out like a brass kettle rolling downstairs, all the guns were lowered.","zh":"接着就是举枪敬礼，枪箍扳开，踢里当啷，响声好似一只铜锅滚下楼梯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then was seen stepping down from the carriage a gentleman in a short coat with silver braiding, with bald brow, and wearing a tuft of hair at the back of his head, of a sallow complexion and the most benign appearance.","zh":"敬礼已毕，枪又统统放下。只见一位先生，穿一件银线绣花短燕尾服，秃额头，后脑勺一撮头发，脸色灰白，外貌极其和善，走下马车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His eyes, very large and covered by heavy lids, were half-closed to look at the crowd, while at the same time he raised his sharp nose, and forced a smile upon his sunken mouth.","zh":"眼睛很大，厚眼皮半睁半闭，打量着群众，同时仰起他的尖鼻子，瘪嘴露出一丝笑意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He recognised the mayor by his scarf, and explained to him that the prefect was not able to come.","zh":"镇长系着绶带，他认出他来，对他解释：州长有事来不了，本人是州行政委员，接着还讲了几句抱歉的话。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He himself was a councillor at the prefecture; then he added a few apologies.","zh":"镇长系着绶带，他认出他来，对他解释：州长有事来不了，本人是州行政委员，接着还讲了几句抱歉的话。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Tuvache answered them with compliments; the other confessed himself nervous; and they remained thus, face to face, their foreheads almost touching, with the members of the jury all round, the municipal council, the notable personages, the National Guard and the crowd.","zh":"杜法赦的回答只是一味恭维，另一位表示愧不敢当：两个人就这样站着，面对面，额头几乎碰额头，周围是评判委员、乡行政委员、缙绅、国民自卫军和群众。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The councillor pressing his little cocked hat to his breast repeated his bows, while Tuvache, bent like a bow, also smiled, stammered, tried to say something, protested his devotion to the monarchy and the honour that was being done to Yonville.","zh":"州行政委员先生，三角小黑帽贴住胸脯 ，频频还礼，同时杜法赦哈下腰来，仿佛一张弓，也是笑盈盈的，结结巴巴，寻找字句，一面表示自己忠心王室 ，一面为永镇得到的荣誉表示感激。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Hippolyte, the groom from the inn, took the head of the horses from the coachman, and, limping along with his club-foot, led them to the door of the “Lion d’Or”, where a number of peasants collected to look at the carriage. The drum beat, the howitzer thundered, and the gentlemen one by one mounted the platform, where they sat down in red utrecht velvet arm-chairs that had been lent by Madame Tuvache.","sentences":[{"en":"Hippolyte, the groom from the inn, took the head of the horses from the coachman, and, limping along with his club-foot, led them to the door of the “Lion d’Or”, where a number of peasants collected to look at the carriage.","zh":"客店伙计伊玻立特走到车夫跟前，接过缰绳，一只脚跛着，把马牵到金狮门廊底下。许多乡下人，聚在门廊，瞻仰马车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The drum beat, the howitzer thundered, and the gentlemen one by one mounted the platform, where they sat down in red utrecht velvet arm-chairs that had been lent by Madame Tuvache.","zh":"鼓在敲，炮在响，先生们鱼贯而行，走上主席台，坐在杜法赦夫人借出来的乌特勒支 红绒大扶手椅上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"All these people looked alike. Their fair flabby faces, somewhat tanned by the sun, were the colour of sweet cider, and their puffy whiskers emerged from stiff collars, kept up by white cravats with broad bows. All the waist-coats were of velvet, double-breasted; all the watches had, at the end of a long ribbon, an oval cornelian seal; everyone rested his two hands on his thighs, carefully stretching the stride of their trousers, whose unsponged glossy cloth shone more brilliantly than the leather of their heavy boots.","sentences":[{"en":"All these people looked alike.","zh":"这些人像是一个模子塑出来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Their fair flabby faces, somewhat tanned by the sun, were the colour of sweet cider, and their puffy whiskers emerged from stiff collars, kept up by white cravats with broad bows.","zh":"软搭搭的脸，新苹果酒颜色，亮堂堂的，太阳晒得有点发黑，络腮胡须尨尨茸茸，拱出高硬领外；白领带箍紧硬领，匀匀停停，结着一个鼓囊囊的领花。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All the waist-coats were of velvet, double-breasted; all the watches had, at the end of a long ribbon, an oval cornelian seal; everyone rested his two hands on his thighs, carefully stretching the stride of their trousers, whose unsponged glossy cloth shone more brilliantly than the leather of their heavy boots.","zh":"背心有压边，全是丝绒料子，表有一根长带，尖尖头全坠着一颗深红玛瑙椭圆印章；人人是一双手搭在两条大腿上，仔细分开裤裆，裤料没有磨掉光泽，比靴子的厚皮还亮。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The ladies of the company stood at the back under the vestibule between the pillars while the common herd was opposite, standing up or sitting on chairs. As a matter of fact, Lestiboudois had brought thither all those that he had moved from the field, and he even kept running back every minute to fetch others from the church. He caused such confusion with this piece of business that one had great difficulty in getting to the small steps of the platform.","sentences":[{"en":"The ladies of the company stood at the back under the vestibule between the pillars while the common herd was opposite, standing up or sitting on chairs.","zh":"上流妇女坐在后头过厅底下和圆柱中间，大多数群众站在对面，或者坐在椅子上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As a matter of fact, Lestiboudois had brought thither all those that he had moved from the field, and he even kept running back every minute to fetch others from the church.","zh":"说实话，赖斯地布杜瓦把椅子全从草场搬过来了，甚至时时刻刻跑进教堂去找椅子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He caused such confusion with this piece of business that one had great difficulty in getting to the small steps of the platform.","zh":"人们想靠近司令台的小梯子，因为他这样一做生意，交通堵塞，也就很难过去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I think,” said Monsieur Lheureux to the chemist, who was passing to his place, “that they ought to have put up two Venetian masts with something rather severe and rich for ornaments; it would have been a very pretty effect.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I think,” said Monsieur Lheureux to the chemist, who was passing to his place, “that they ought to have put up two Venetian masts with something rather severe and rich for ornaments; it would have been a very pretty effect.”","zh":"勒乐先生向药剂师（他正要到他的座位上去）道：“我以为应当竖两根威尼斯旗杆，弄点新鲜东西挂在上头，又富丽，又有一点威严，望过去，就很美观了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“To be sure,” replied Homais; “but what can you expect? The mayor took everything on his own shoulders. He hasn’t much taste. Poor Tuvache! and he is even completely destitute of what is called the genius of art.”","sentences":[{"en":"“To be sure,” replied Homais; “but what can you expect?","zh":"郝麦回答道：“的确是的。不过有什么办法！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The mayor took everything on his own shoulders.","zh":"这是镇长一手包办的结果。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He hasn’t much taste.","zh":"可怜的杜法赦，这人没有多少鉴赏力；根本缺乏所谓艺术天分。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Poor Tuvache! and he is even completely destitute of what is called the genius of art.”","zh":"可怜的杜法赦，这人没有多少鉴赏力；根本缺乏所谓艺术天分。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe, meanwhile, with Madame Bovary, had gone up to the first floor of the town hall, to the “council-room,” and, as it was empty, he declared that they could enjoy the sight there more comfortably. He fetched three stools from the round table under the bust of the monarch, and having carried them to one of the windows, they sat down by each other.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe, meanwhile, with Madame Bovary, had gone up to the first floor of the town hall, to the “council-room,” and, as it was empty, he declared that they could enjoy the sight there more comfortably.","zh":"罗道耳弗这时陪伴包法利夫人，走上镇公所二楼，来到会议厅，看见没有一个人，就讲：他们在这里瞭望，尽兴多了，国王半身像底下有一张椭圆桌子，他到旁边搬了三张凳子，放到一个窗口跟前，然后他们挨挨挤挤，并肩坐下。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He fetched three stools from the round table under the bust of the monarch, and having carried them to one of the windows, they sat down by each other.","zh":"罗道耳弗这时陪伴包法利夫人，走上镇公所二楼，来到会议厅，看见没有一个人，就讲：他们在这里瞭望，尽兴多了，国王半身像底下有一张椭圆桌子，他到旁边搬了三张凳子，放到一个窗口跟前，然后他们挨挨挤挤，并肩坐下。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"There was commotion on the platform, long whisperings, much parleying. At last the councillor got up. They knew now that his name was Lieuvain, and in the crowd the name was passed from one to the other. After he had collated a few pages, and bent over them to see better, he began—","sentences":[{"en":"There was commotion on the platform, long whisperings, much parleying.","zh":"主席台上起了一阵骚动：长久耳语和交换意见。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last the councillor got up.","zh":"主席台上起了一阵骚动：长久耳语和交换意见。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They knew now that his name was Lieuvain, and in the crowd the name was passed from one to the other.","zh":"最后还是州行政委员先生站起。大家现在晓得他姓廖万，群众一个传一个，说起他的名姓。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After he had collated a few pages, and bent over them to see better, he began—","zh":"于是他掏出几张纸，凑近眼睛细看了看，这才开口道：诸位先生：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Gentlemen! May I be permitted first of all (before addressing you on the object of our meeting to-day, and this sentiment will, I am sure, be shared by you all), may I be permitted, I say, to pay a tribute to the higher administration, to the government to the monarch, gentle men, our sovereign, to that beloved king, to whom no branch of public or private prosperity is a matter of indifference, and who directs with a hand at once so firm and wise the chariot of the state amid the incessant perils of a stormy sea, knowing, moreover, how to make peace respected as well as war, industry, commerce, agriculture, and the fine arts?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Gentlemen!","zh":"首先请允许我，在没有和你们谈起今天的盛会之前——我相信，你们全有这种感情，我说，首先请允许我赞扬一下最高当局、政府、国君，诸位先生，赞扬一下我们的主上、万民爱戴的国王。大家知道，事关繁荣，不问公私，圣上一律关怀，即使怒海狂涛，危险百出，圣上也坚定审慎，稳步行车，何况圣上谋求和平，重视战争、工业、商业、农业与艺术。","scope":"group"},{"en":"May I be permitted first of all (before addressing you on the object of our meeting to-day, and this sentiment will, I am sure, be shared by you all), may I be permitted, I say, to pay a tribute to the higher administration, to the government to the monarch, gentle men, our sovereign, to that beloved king, to whom no branch of public or private prosperity is a matter of indifference, and who directs with a hand at once so firm and wise the chariot of the state amid the incessant perils of a stormy sea, knowing, moreover, how to make peace respected as well as war, industry, commerce, agriculture, and the fine arts?”","zh":"首先请允许我，在没有和你们谈起今天的盛会之前——我相信，你们全有这种感情，我说，首先请允许我赞扬一下最高当局、政府、国君，诸位先生，赞扬一下我们的主上、万民爱戴的国王。大家知道，事关繁荣，不问公私，圣上一律关怀，即使怒海狂涛，危险百出，圣上也坚定审慎，稳步行车，何况圣上谋求和平，重视战争、工业、商业、农业与艺术。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I ought,” said Rodolphe, “to get back a little further.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I ought,” said Rodolphe, “to get back a little further.”","zh":"罗道耳弗道：“我该退后一点坐。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why?” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why?” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But at this moment the voice of the councillor rose to an extraordinary pitch. He declaimed—","sentences":[{"en":"But at this moment the voice of the councillor rose to an extraordinary pitch.","zh":"“为什么？”不过州行政委员的声音分外高了，他朗诵道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He declaimed—","zh":"“为什么？”不过州行政委员的声音分外高了，他朗诵道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“This is no longer the time, gentlemen, when civil discord ensanguined our public places, when the landlord, the business-man, the working-man himself, falling asleep at night, lying down to peaceful sleep, trembled lest he should be awakened suddenly by the noise of incendiary tocsins, when the most subversive doctrines audaciously sapped foundations.”","sentences":[{"en":"“This is no longer the time, gentlemen, when civil discord ensanguined our public places, when the landlord, the business-man, the working-man himself, falling asleep at night, lying down to peaceful sleep, trembled lest he should be awakened suddenly by the noise of incendiary tocsins, when the most subversive doctrines audaciously sapped foundations.”","zh":"诸位先生，兄弟阋于墙，血染公众广场的时期，已经一去不复返了；业主、商人，甚至于工人，夜晚安眠，听见警钟齐鸣，忽然惊醒的时期，已经一去不复返了；邪说横行，擅敢颠覆社稷的时期，已经一去不复返了…罗道耳弗接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, someone down there might see me,” Rodolphe resumed, “then I should have to invent excuses for a fortnight; and with my bad reputation—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, someone down there might see me,” Rodolphe resumed, “then I should have to invent excuses for a fortnight; and with my bad reputation—”","zh":"“因为下面也许有人望见我；这样一来，我就要一连两星期道歉，像我这样的坏名声…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, you are slandering yourself,” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, you are slandering yourself,” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛道：“哎呀！您成心糟蹋自己。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No! It is dreadful, I assure you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No! It is dreadful, I assure you.”","zh":"“不，不，您听我讲，坏极了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But, gentlemen,” continued the councillor, “if, banishing from my memory the remembrance of these sad pictures, I carry my eyes back to the actual situation of our dear country, what do I see there? Everywhere commerce and the arts are flourishing; everywhere new means of communication, like so many new arteries in the body of the state, establish within it new relations. Our great industrial centres have recovered all their activity; religion, more consolidated, smiles in all hearts; our ports are full, confidence is born again, and France breathes once more!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But, gentlemen,” continued the councillor, “if, banishing from my memory the remembrance of these sad pictures, I carry my eyes back to the actual situation of our dear country, what do I see there?","zh":"州行政委员继续道：可是，诸位先生，放下这些暗无天日的画面不去回想，转过眼睛，浏览一下我们美丽祖国的现状，我又看见了什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everywhere commerce and the arts are flourishing; everywhere new means of communication, like so many new arteries in the body of the state, establish within it new relations.","zh":"处处商业繁盛，艺术发达，处处兴修新的道路，仿佛国家添了许多新的动脉，构成新的联系；我们伟大的工业中心又活跃起来；宗教得到巩固，法光普照；我们的码头堆满货物，信心再起，法兰西终于得到了新生…罗道耳弗又道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Our great industrial centres have recovered all their activity; religion, more consolidated, smiles in all hearts; our ports are full, confidence is born again, and France breathes once more!”","zh":"处处商业繁盛，艺术发达，处处兴修新的道路，仿佛国家添了许多新的动脉，构成新的联系；我们伟大的工业中心又活跃起来；宗教得到巩固，法光普照；我们的码头堆满货物，信心再起，法兰西终于得到了新生…罗道耳弗又道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Besides,” added Rodolphe, “perhaps from the world’s point of view they are right.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Besides,” added Rodolphe, “perhaps from the world’s point of view they are right.”","zh":"“其实，就社会观点看来，他们也许有道理。”她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How so?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“How so?” she asked.","zh":"“什么道理？”他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What!” said he. “Do you not know that there are souls constantly tormented? They need by turns to dream and to act, the purest passions and the most turbulent joys, and thus they fling themselves into all sorts of fantasies, of follies.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What!” said he.","zh":"“怎么！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do you not know that there are souls constantly tormented?","zh":"难道您不知道，有人无时无刻不在苦恼？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They need by turns to dream and to act, the purest passions and the most turbulent joys, and thus they fling themselves into all sorts of fantasies, of follies.”","zh":"他们一时需要梦想，一时需要行动，一时需要最纯洁的热情，一时需要最疯狂的欢乐，人就这样来来去去，过着形形色色荒唐、怪诞的生活。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she looked at him as one looks at a traveller who has voyaged over strange lands, and went on—","sentences":[{"en":"Then she looked at him as one looks at a traveller who has voyaged over strange lands, and went on—","zh":"于是她看着他，就像一个人打量一个到过奇土异域的旅客一样，接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We have not even this distraction, we poor women!”","sentences":[{"en":"“We have not even this distraction, we poor women!”","zh":"“我们这些可怜的妇女，就连这种消遣也没有！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“A sad distraction, for happiness isn’t found in it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“A sad distraction, for happiness isn’t found in it.”","zh":"“微不足道的消遣，因为人们在这里找不到幸福。”她问道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“But is it ever found?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“But is it ever found?” she asked.","zh":"“微不足道的消遣，因为人们在这里找不到幸福。”她问道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Yes; one day it comes,” he answered.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes; one day it comes,” he answered.","zh":"“可是人们找得到吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And this is what you have understood,” said the councillor.","sentences":[{"en":"“And this is what you have understood,” said the councillor.","zh":"他回答道：“是的，会有一天遇到的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You, farmers, agricultural labourers! you pacific pioneers of a work that belongs wholly to civilization! you, men of progress and morality, you have understood, I say, that political storms are even more redoubtable than atmospheric disturbances!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You, farmers, agricultural labourers! you pacific pioneers of a work that belongs wholly to civilization! you, men of progress and morality, you have understood, I say, that political storms are even more redoubtable than atmospheric disturbances!”","zh":"你们是农民和田野的工人；你们是真正为文化而工作的和平的先驱！你们是进步和道德人士！我说，你们明白，政治风暴，比起大气紊乱，确实可怕得多…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It comes one day,” repeated Rodolphe, “one day suddenly, and when one is despairing of it. Then the horizon expands; it is as if a voice cried, ‘It is here!’ You feel the need of confiding the whole of your life, of giving everything, sacrificing everything to this being. There is no need for explanations; they understand one another. They have seen each other in dreams!”","sentences":[{"en":"“It comes one day,” repeated Rodolphe, “one day suddenly, and when one is despairing of it.","zh":"罗道耳弗重复道：“有一天，有一天赶巧万念俱灰，会忽然遇到的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the horizon expands; it is as if a voice cried, ‘It is here!’","zh":"于是云散天开，好像有一个声音在喊：‘这就是！’","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You feel the need of confiding the whole of your life, of giving everything, sacrificing everything to this being.","zh":"您觉得需要向这个人诉说衷情，把一切给他，为他牺牲一切！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There is no need for explanations; they understand one another.","zh":"用不着烦言解释，彼此就一见如故，似曾梦里相逢。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They have seen each other in dreams!”","zh":"用不着烦言解释，彼此就一见如故，似曾梦里相逢。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"(And he looked at her.) “In fine, here it is, this treasure so sought after, here before you. It glitters, it flashes; yet one still doubts, one does not believe it; one remains dazzled, as if one went out from darkness into light.”","sentences":[{"en":"(And he looked at her.) “In fine, here it is, this treasure so sought after, here before you.","zh":"（他看着她）总之，就在眼前，四处寻觅的珠宝就在眼前，光华灿烂，火星迸射。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It glitters, it flashes; yet one still doubts, one does not believe it; one remains dazzled, as if one went out from darkness into light.”","zh":"可是仍然怀疑，仍然不敢相信；眼花缭乱，好像走出黑暗，乍见亮光一样。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And as he ended Rodolphe suited the action to the word. He passed his hand over his face, like a man seized with giddiness. Then he let it fall on Emma’s. She took hers away.","sentences":[{"en":"And as he ended Rodolphe suited the action to the word.","zh":"罗道耳弗说到末了这几句话，添上手势。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He passed his hand over his face, like a man seized with giddiness.","zh":"他拿一只手放在脸上，就像一个人晕眩一样，然后落下来搭在爱玛手上。她抽回她的手。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he let it fall on Emma’s.","zh":"他拿一只手放在脸上，就像一个人晕眩一样，然后落下来搭在爱玛手上。她抽回她的手。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She took hers away.","zh":"可是州行政委员总在读着：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And who would be surprised at it, gentlemen? He only who is so blind, so plunged (I do not fear to say it), so plunged in the prejudices of another age as still to misunderstand the spirit of agricultural populations. Where, indeed, is to be found more patriotism than in the country, greater devotion to the public welfare, more intelligence, in a word? And, gentlemen, I do not mean that superficial intelligence, vain ornament of idle minds, but rather that profound and balanced intelligence that applies itself above all else to useful objects, thus contributing to the good of all, to the common amelioration and to the support of the state, born of respect for law and the practice of duty—”","sentences":[{"en":"“And who would be surprised at it, gentlemen?","zh":"诸位先生，有谁惊奇吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He only who is so blind, so plunged (I do not fear to say it), so plunged in the prejudices of another age as still to misunderstand the spirit of agricultural populations.","zh":"也只有他们惊奇：就是那种瞎了眼的人、那种沉溺于（我不怕说出口来）前一世纪的偏见，照旧否认农民是有头脑的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where, indeed, is to be found more patriotism than in the country, greater devotion to the public welfare, more intelligence, in a word?","zh":"说实话，寻找爱国精神、热心公众事业，一言以蔽之，智慧，除去田野，还有什么地方更多？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And, gentlemen, I do not mean that superficial intelligence, vain ornament of idle minds, but rather that profound and balanced intelligence that applies itself above all else to useful objects, thus contributing to the good of all, to the common amelioration and to the support of the state, born of respect for law and the practice of duty—”","zh":"诸位先生，我说的不是那种表面的智慧、那种闲汉的点缀。我说的是那种深刻、稳健的智慧，专心致志于追求那些有用之物，因而有助于个人福利、一般改善与支援国家，它是——尊重法律和完成任务的收获…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! again!” said Rodolphe. “Always ‘duty.’ I am sick of the word. They are a lot of old blockheads in flannel vests and of old women with foot-warmers and rosaries who constantly drone into our ears ‘Duty, duty!’ Ah! by Jove! one’s duty is to feel what is great, cherish the beautiful, and not accept all the conventions of society with the ignominy that it imposes upon us.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! again!” said Rodolphe.","zh":"罗道耳弗道：“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Always ‘duty.’","zh":"又是这个。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am sick of the word.","zh":"总是任务，我听也听腻了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They are a lot of old blockheads in flannel vests and of old women with foot-warmers and rosaries who constantly drone into our ears ‘Duty, duty!’","zh":"他们一堆穿法兰绒背心的老昏聩、一堆离不开脚炉和念珠的假虔婆，不住口在我们的耳梢唠叨：‘任务！任务！’","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! by Jove! one’s duty is to feel what is great, cherish the beautiful, and not accept all the conventions of society with the ignominy that it imposes upon us.”","zh":"哎！家伙！任务呀，任务是感受高贵事物、珍爱美丽事物，并非接受社会全部约束和硬加在我们身上的种种耻辱。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet—yet—” objected Madame Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet—yet—” objected Madame Bovary.","zh":"包法利夫人反驳道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no! Why cry out against the passions? Are they not the one beautiful thing on the earth, the source of heroism, of enthusiasm, of poetry, music, the arts, of everything, in a word?”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no! Why cry out against the passions?","zh":"不过…”“哎，不！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Are they not the one beautiful thing on the earth, the source of heroism, of enthusiasm, of poetry, music, the arts, of everything, in a word?”","zh":"凭什么反对热情？难道它不是世上唯一美丽的东西？难道它不是英勇、热忱、诗歌、音乐、艺术以及其他一切的根源？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But one must,” said Emma, “to some extent bow to the opinion of the world and accept its moral code.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But one must,” said Emma, “to some extent bow to the opinion of the world and accept its moral code.”","zh":"爱玛道：“可是也该听听世人的意见，遵守一般立身处世之道。”他回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! but there are two,” he replied. “The small, the conventional, that of men, that which constantly changes, that brays out so loudly, that makes such a commotion here below, of the earth earthly, like the mass of imbeciles you see down there. But the other, the eternal, that is about us and above, like the landscape that surrounds us, and the blue heavens that give us light.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! but there are two,” he replied.","zh":"“啊！立身处世之道有两种。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“The small, the conventional, that of men, that which constantly changes, that brays out so loudly, that makes such a commotion here below, of the earth earthly, like the mass of imbeciles you see down there.","zh":"一种是渺小的、众人公认的处世之道，因时而异，目光如豆，吵吵嚷嚷，低级庸俗，就像眼前这群蠢家伙一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the other, the eternal, that is about us and above, like the landscape that surrounds us, and the blue heavens that give us light.”","zh":"另一种是万古长存之道，在周围，也在上空，风景一般环绕我们，碧天一般照耀我们。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Lieuvain had just wiped his mouth with a pocket-handkerchief. He continued—","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Lieuvain had just wiped his mouth with a pocket-handkerchief.","zh":"廖万先生方才掏出手绢擦过嘴，接下去道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He continued—","zh":"廖万先生方才掏出手绢擦过嘴，接下去道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“And what should I do here gentlemen, pointing out to you the uses of agriculture? Who supplies our wants? Who provides our means of subsistence? Is it not the agriculturist? The agriculturist, gentlemen, who, sowing with laborious hand the fertile furrows of the country, brings forth the corn, which, being ground, is made into a powder by means of ingenious machinery, comes out thence under the name of flour, and from there, transported to our cities, is soon delivered at the baker’s, who makes it into food for poor and rich alike. Again, is it not the agriculturist who fattens, for our clothes, his abundant flocks in the pastures? For how should we clothe ourselves, how nourish ourselves, without the agriculturist? And, gentlemen, is it even necessary to go so far for examples? Who has not frequently reflected on all the momentous things that we get out of that modest animal, the ornament of poultry-yards, that provides us at once with a soft pillow for our bed, with succulent flesh for our tables, and eggs? But I should never end if I were to enumerate one after the other all the different products which the earth, well cultivated, like a generous mother, lavishes upon her children. Here it is the vine, elsewhere the apple tree for cider, there colza, farther on cheeses and flax. Gentlemen, let us not forget flax, which has made such great strides of late years, and to which I will more particularly call your attention.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And what should I do here gentlemen, pointing out to you the uses of agriculture?","zh":"诸位先生，农业的重要，还用得着我在这里向你们指出来吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who supplies our wants?","zh":"请问，谁供应我们的需要？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who provides our means of subsistence?","zh":"谁接济我们的生活？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is it not the agriculturist?","zh":"难道不是农民？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The agriculturist, gentlemen, who, sowing with laborious hand the fertile furrows of the country, brings forth the corn, which, being ground, is made into a powder by means of ingenious machinery, comes out thence under the name of flour, and from there, transported to our cities, is soon delivered at the baker’s, who makes it into food for poor and rich alike.","zh":"诸位先生，农民拿一双勤劳的手，把种子撒在肥沃的田地里，种子长成麦子，麦子被精巧的机器磨成细末，以面粉的名称运到城市，没有多久，就进了面包房，制成食品，不分贫富，一概供应。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Again, is it not the agriculturist who fattens, for our clothes, his abundant flocks in the pastures?","zh":"为了我们有衣服穿，难道不又是农民养肥牧场众多的羊群？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For how should we clothe ourselves, how nourish ourselves, without the agriculturist?","zh":"没有农民，我们穿什么，我们吃什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And, gentlemen, is it even necessary to go so far for examples?","zh":"诸位先生，我们有必要到老远的地方寻找例证吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who has not frequently reflected on all the momentous things that we get out of that modest animal, the ornament of poultry-yards, that provides us at once with a soft pillow for our bed, with succulent flesh for our tables, and eggs?","zh":"谁不常常想到那只羞怯的动物、我们家禽群里值得骄傲的珍品？它一方面长毛给我们做绵软的枕头，一方面有丰美的肉给我们吃，一方面还下蛋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But I should never end if I were to enumerate one after the other all the different products which the earth, well cultivated, like a generous mother, lavishes upon her children.","zh":"地耕好了，出产种种物品，好比慈母心疼儿女，尽量供应，我要是一一枚举的话，就要不胜其举了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Here it is the vine, elsewhere the apple tree for cider, there colza, farther on cheeses and flax.","zh":"这边是葡萄藤；那边是苹果树；远望，是油菜；再往远望，是干酪；还有麻，诸位先生，千万不要忘记麻 ！近年以来，麻的产量增加了许多，我特别希望你们注意。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Gentlemen, let us not forget flax, which has made such great strides of late years, and to which I will more particularly call your attention.”","zh":"这边是葡萄藤；那边是苹果树；远望，是油菜；再往远望，是干酪；还有麻，诸位先生，千万不要忘记麻 ！近年以来，麻的产量增加了许多，我特别希望你们注意。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He had no need to call it, for all the mouths of the multitude were wide open, as if to drink in his words. Tuvache by his side listened to him with staring eyes. Monsieur Derozerays from time to time softly closed his eyelids, and farther on the chemist, with his son Napoleon between his knees, put his hand behind his ear in order not to lose a syllable. The chins of the other members of the jury went slowly up and down in their waistcoats in sign of approval. The firemen at the foot of the platform rested on their bayonets; and Binet, motionless, stood with out-turned elbows, the point of his sabre in the air. Perhaps he could hear, but certainly he could see nothing, because of the visor of his helmet, that fell down on his nose. His lieutenant, the youngest son of Monsieur Tuvache, had a bigger one, for his was enormous, and shook on his head, and from it an end of his cotton scarf peeped out. He smiled beneath it with a perfectly infantine sweetness, and his pale little face, whence drops were running, wore an expression of enjoyment and sleepiness.","sentences":[{"en":"He had no need to call it, for all the mouths of the multitude were wide open, as if to drink in his words.","zh":"他不必希望；因为群众个个张大了嘴，好像要喝掉他的话一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tuvache by his side listened to him with staring eyes.","zh":"杜法赦在他一旁，睁大了眼睛听；德罗兹赖先生，有时候，微微合上眼皮；再过去，药剂师两腿夹住他的儿子拿破仑，拿手张在耳边，一个字音不叫漏掉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Derozerays from time to time softly closed his eyelids, and farther on the chemist, with his son Napoleon between his knees, put his hand behind his ear in order not to lose a syllable.","zh":"杜法赦在他一旁，睁大了眼睛听；德罗兹赖先生，有时候，微微合上眼皮；再过去，药剂师两腿夹住他的儿子拿破仑，拿手张在耳边，一个字音不叫漏掉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The chins of the other members of the jury went slowly up and down in their waistcoats in sign of approval.","zh":"别的评判委员表示赞同，慢慢悠悠，上下摇摆背心里的下巴。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The firemen at the foot of the platform rested on their bayonets; and Binet, motionless, stood with out-turned elbows, the point of his sabre in the air.","zh":"消防队员站在主席台底下，靠住他们的刺刀；毕耐一丝不动，胳膊肘朝外，刀尖向上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps he could hear, but certainly he could see nothing, because of the visor of his helmet, that fell down on his nose.","zh":"他也许在听，不过他一定什么也看不见，由于他的盔檐太低，一直罩到鼻子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His lieutenant, the youngest son of Monsieur Tuvache, had a bigger one, for his was enormous, and shook on his head, and from it an end of his cotton scarf peeped out.","zh":"副队长是杜法赦先生的小儿子，盔檐低得出奇；因为他戴了一顶绝大的战盔，在头上晃来晃去，花布手绢垫在底下，有一头露出来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He smiled beneath it with a perfectly infantine sweetness, and his pale little face, whence drops were running, wore an expression of enjoyment and sleepiness.","zh":"他在战盔底下，笑嘻嘻的，一副小孩子的可爱模样，小白脸蛋淌着汗，流露出一种欢愉、疲倦和睡眠的表情。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The square as far as the houses was crowded with people. One saw folk leaning on their elbows at all the windows, others standing at doors, and Justin, in front of the chemist’s shop, seemed quite transfixed by the sight of what he was looking at. In spite of the silence Monsieur Lieuvain’s voice was lost in the air. It reached you in fragments of phrases, and interrupted here and there by the creaking of chairs in the crowd; then you suddenly heard the long bellowing of an ox, or else the bleating of the lambs, who answered one another at street corners. In fact, the cowherds and shepherds had driven their beasts thus far, and these lowed from time to time, while with their tongues they tore down some scrap of foliage that hung above their mouths.","sentences":[{"en":"The square as far as the houses was crowded with people.","zh":"广场两边的房屋都挤满了人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One saw folk leaning on their elbows at all the windows, others standing at doors, and Justin, in front of the chemist’s shop, seemed quite transfixed by the sight of what he was looking at.","zh":"家家有人靠着窗户，有人站在门口。朱斯丹站在药房前面，似乎看愣了，动弹不得。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In spite of the silence Monsieur Lieuvain’s voice was lost in the air.","zh":"虽说安静，廖万先生的声音照样听不清楚：群众中间，椅子出了响声，东一打岔，西一打岔，截断演说，只有一句半句传到耳朵；接着就是背后，冷不防起了漫长一声牛鸣，或者就是街角羊羔咩咩叫唤。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It reached you in fragments of phrases, and interrupted here and there by the creaking of chairs in the crowd; then you suddenly heard the long bellowing of an ox, or else the bleating of the lambs, who answered one another at street corners.","zh":"虽说安静，廖万先生的声音照样听不清楚：群众中间，椅子出了响声，东一打岔，西一打岔，截断演说，只有一句半句传到耳朵；接着就是背后，冷不防起了漫长一声牛鸣，或者就是街角羊羔咩咩叫唤。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In fact, the cowherds and shepherds had driven their beasts thus far, and these lowed from time to time, while with their tongues they tore down some scrap of foliage that hung above their mouths.","zh":"说实话，放牛的和放羊的，一直把牲口赶到这边，它们有时候你一声，我一声，一面还吐长舌头，拉曳挂在脸上的三两片树叶。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe had drawn nearer to Emma, and said to her in a low voice, speaking rapidly—","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe had drawn nearer to Emma, and said to her in a low voice, speaking rapidly—","zh":"罗道耳弗更挨近爱玛了，声音压低，急促地说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Does not this conspiracy of the world revolt you? Is there a single sentiment it does not condemn? The noblest instincts, the purest sympathies are persecuted, slandered; and if at length two poor souls do meet, all is so organised that they cannot blend together. Yet they will make the attempt; they will flutter their wings; they will call upon each other. Oh! no matter. Sooner or later, in six months, ten years, they will come together, will love; for fate has decreed it, and they are born one for the other.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Does not this conspiracy of the world revolt you?","zh":"“人世这种阴谋，您不愤恨？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is there a single sentiment it does not condemn?","zh":"哪一样感情它不谴责？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The noblest instincts, the purest sympathies are persecuted, slandered; and if at length two poor souls do meet, all is so organised that they cannot blend together.","zh":"最高贵的本能、最纯洁的同情，也逃不脱迫害、诽谤；一对可怜虫要是碰在一起的话，就组织一切力量来拆散他们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yet they will make the attempt; they will flutter their wings; they will call upon each other.","zh":"不过他们偏要试试，扇扇翅膀，你呼唤我，我呼唤你：是啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh! no matter.","zh":"迟早有什么关系，半年，十年，他们照样结合，照样相爱，因为命里注定这样，彼此天生就是一对。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Sooner or later, in six months, ten years, they will come together, will love; for fate has decreed it, and they are born one for the other.”","zh":"迟早有什么关系，半年，十年，他们照样结合，照样相爱，因为命里注定这样，彼此天生就是一对。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"His arms were folded across his knees, and thus lifting his face towards Emma, close by her, he looked fixedly at her. She noticed in his eyes small golden lines radiating from black pupils; she even smelt the perfume of the pomade that made his hair glossy.","sentences":[{"en":"His arms were folded across his knees, and thus lifting his face towards Emma, close by her, he looked fixedly at her.","zh":"两只胳膊横在膝盖上，他仰起脸，凑到近边，死盯着看爱玛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She noticed in his eyes small golden lines radiating from black pupils; she even smelt the perfume of the pomade that made his hair glossy.","zh":"她看见纤细的金光，一道又一道，兜着他的黑瞳仁，从眼睛里面朝外放射。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then a faintness came over her; she recalled the Viscount who had waltzed with her at Vaubyessard, and his beard exhaled like this air an odour of vanilla and citron, and mechanically she half-closed her eyes the better to breathe it in. But in making this movement, as she leant back in her chair, she saw in the distance, right on the line of the horizon, the old diligence, the “Hirondelle,” that was slowly descending the hill of Leux, dragging after it a long trail of dust. It was in this yellow carriage that Léon had so often come back to her, and by this route down there that he had gone for ever. She fancied she saw him opposite at his windows; then all grew confused; clouds gathered; it seemed to her that she was again turning in the waltz under the light of the lustres on the arm of the Viscount, and that Léon was not far away, that he was coming; and yet all the time she was conscious of the scent of Rodolphe’s head by her side. This sweetness of sensation pierced through her old desires, and these, like grains of sand under a gust of wind, eddied to and fro in the subtle breath of the perfume which suffused her soul. She opened wide her nostrils several times to drink in the freshness of the ivy round the capitals. She took off her gloves, she wiped her hands, then fanned her face with her handkerchief, while athwart the throbbing of her temples she heard the murmur of the crowd and the voice of the councillor intoning his phrases. He said—“Continue, persevere; listen neither to the suggestions of routine, nor to the over-hasty councils of a rash empiricism.","sentences":[{"en":"Then a faintness came over her; she recalled the Viscount who had waltzed with her at Vaubyessard, and his beard exhaled like this air an odour of vanilla and citron, and mechanically she half-closed her eyes the better to breathe it in.","zh":"她甚至于闻见他抹亮头发的生发油的香味，于是心荡神驰，不由想起在渥毕萨尔陪她跳华尔兹的子爵，他的胡须就像这些头发，放出这种香草和柠檬气息；她不由自己，闭了一半眼皮往里吸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But in making this movement, as she leant back in her chair, she saw in the distance, right on the line of the horizon, the old diligence, the “Hirondelle,” that was slowly descending the hill of Leux, dragging after it a long trail of dust.","zh":"但是她坐在椅子 上，身子往后一仰，恍惚远远望见驿车燕子，在天边尽头，慢慢腾腾，走下狼岭，车后扬起长悠悠的灰尘。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was in this yellow carriage that Léon had so often come back to her, and by this route down there that he had gone for ever.","zh":"赖昂就是乘了这辆黄车，时刻来到她的身边；也就是经这条路，他又一去不回！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She fancied she saw him opposite at his windows; then all grew confused; clouds gathered; it seemed to her that she was again turning in the waltz under the light of the lustres on the arm of the Viscount, and that Léon was not far away, that he was coming; and yet all the time she was conscious of the scent of Rodolphe’s head by her side.","zh":"她仿佛看见他在对面窗口，接着就又一片模糊，满天浮云，她觉得吊灯照耀，她还像在跳华尔兹，挎着子爵的胳膊，同时赖昂离得也不远，眼看就要过来…但是她总觉得罗道耳弗的头在她旁边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This sweetness of sensation pierced through her old desires, and these, like grains of sand under a gust of wind, eddied to and fro in the subtle breath of the perfume which suffused her soul.","zh":"这种甜蜜的感觉就这样渗透从前她那些欲望，好像一阵狂飙，掀起了沙砾，香风习习，吹遍她的灵魂，幽渺的氤氲卷起了欲望旋转。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She opened wide her nostrils several times to drink in the freshness of the ivy round the capitals.","zh":"她好几回用力张开鼻孔，吸入柱头常春藤的清新气息。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She took off her gloves, she wiped her hands, then fanned her face with her handkerchief, while athwart the throbbing of her temples she heard the murmur of the crowd and the voice of the councillor intoning his phrases.","zh":"她摘去手套，擦了擦手，然后拿起手绢扇脸，太阳穴虽说跳动，她照样听见群众叽里咕噜、州行政委员说来说去的单调声音：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He said—“Continue, persevere; listen neither to the suggestions of routine, nor to the over-hasty councils of a rash empiricism.","zh":"她摘去手套，擦了擦手，然后拿起手绢扇脸，太阳穴虽说跳动，她照样听见群众叽里咕噜、州行政委员说来说去的单调声音：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Apply yourselves, above all, to the amelioration of the soil, to good manures, to the development of the equine, bovine, ovine, and porcine races. Let these shows be to you pacific arenas, where the victor in leaving it will hold forth a hand to the vanquished, and will fraternise with him in the hope of better success. And you, aged servants, humble domestics, whose hard labour no Government up to this day has taken into consideration, come hither to receive the reward of your silent virtues, and be assured that the state henceforward has its eye upon you; that it encourages you, protects you; that it will accede to your just demands, and alleviate as much as in it lies the burden of your painful sacrifices.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Apply yourselves, above all, to the amelioration of the soil, to good manures, to the development of the equine, bovine, ovine, and porcine races.","zh":"继续努力！坚持不懈！既不要墨守成规，也不要采纳过分莽撞急躁的建议！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let these shows be to you pacific arenas, where the victor in leaving it will hold forth a hand to the vanquished, and will fraternise with him in the hope of better success.","zh":"尤其要致力于改良土壤、施用优质肥料，发展马、牛、羊、猪的优良品种！让展览会成为你们充满和平景象的比武场，胜利者向战败者伸出友爱之手，希望他下一次竞赛成功！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And you, aged servants, humble domestics, whose hard labour no Government up to this day has taken into consideration, come hither to receive the reward of your silent virtues, and be assured that the state henceforward has its eye upon you; that it encourages you, protects you; that it will accede to your just demands, and alleviate as much as in it lies the burden of your painful sacrifices.”","zh":"可敬的臣民！谦逊的仆人，你们辛勤劳苦，往日得不到任何政府重视，现在就来接受你们默默无闻的道德的酬劳吧。而且你们相信政府从今以后，一定会注视你们，鼓励你们，保护你们，满足你们的正当要求，尽一切可能，减轻你们痛苦牺牲的负担！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Lieuvain then sat down; Monsieur Derozerays got up, beginning another speech. His was not perhaps so florid as that of the councillor, but it recommended itself by a more direct style, that is to say, by more special knowledge and more elevated considerations. Thus the praise of the Government took up less space in it; religion and agriculture more. He showed in it the relations of these two, and how they had always contributed to civilisation. Rodolphe with Madame Bovary was talking dreams, presentiments, magnetism. Going back to the cradle of society, the orator painted those fierce times when men lived on acorns in the heart of woods. Then they had left off the skins of beasts, had put on cloth, tilled the soil, planted the vine. Was this a good, and in this discovery was there not more of injury than of gain? Monsieur Derozerays set himself this problem. From magnetism little by little Rodolphe had come to affinities, and while the president was citing Cincinnatus and his plough, Diocletian, planting his cabbages, and the Emperors of China inaugurating the year by the sowing of seed, the young man was explaining to the young woman that these irresistible attractions find their cause in some previous state of existence.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Lieuvain then sat down; Monsieur Derozerays got up, beginning another speech.","zh":"廖万先生终于坐下。德罗兹赖先生站起，开始另一篇演说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His was not perhaps so florid as that of the councillor, but it recommended itself by a more direct style, that is to say, by more special knowledge and more elevated considerations.","zh":"他的讲演也许不像州行政委员的讲演那样华丽；不过他有他的特点：风格切实，就是说，学识比较专门，议论比较高超，少了一些颂扬政府的话，宗教和农业分到更多的地位，二者息息相关，一向就同心协力，促进文化。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus the praise of the Government took up less space in it; religion and agriculture more.","zh":"罗道耳弗和包法利夫人谈着梦、预感、催眠术。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He showed in it the relations of these two, and how they had always contributed to civilisation.","zh":"演说家追溯到原始社会，形容野蛮时代，人在树林深处，靠橡实过活；后来人们扔掉兽皮，改穿布帛，耕田犁地，种植葡萄。这算不算幸福？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe with Madame Bovary was talking dreams, presentiments, magnetism.","zh":"这种发现会不会弊多于利？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Going back to the cradle of society, the orator painted those fierce times when men lived on acorns in the heart of woods.","zh":"德罗兹赖先生对自己提出这个问题。罗道耳弗由催眠术一点一点谈到亲和力。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then they had left off the skins of beasts, had put on cloth, tilled the soil, planted the vine.","zh":"主席引证：辛辛纳图斯掌犁，戴克里先种菜， 中国皇帝立春播种。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Was this a good, and in this discovery was there not more of injury than of gain?","zh":"年轻人这期间向少妇解释：吸引之所以难以抗拒，就是前生的缘故。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Derozerays set himself this problem.","zh":"年轻人这期间向少妇解释：吸引之所以难以抗拒，就是前生的缘故。","scope":"group"},{"en":"From magnetism little by little Rodolphe had come to affinities, and while the president was citing Cincinnatus and his plough, Diocletian, planting his cabbages, and the Emperors of China inaugurating the year by the sowing of seed, the young man was explaining to the young woman that these irresistible attractions find their cause in some previous state of existence.","zh":"他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Thus we,” he said, “why did we come to know one another? What chance willed it? It was because across the infinite, like two streams that flow but to unite; our special bents of mind had driven us towards each other.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Thus we,” he said, “why did we come to know one another?","zh":"“所以，就拿您我来说，我们为什么相识？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What chance willed it?","zh":"出于什么机缘？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was because across the infinite, like two streams that flow but to unite; our special bents of mind had driven us towards each other.”","zh":"我们各自的天性，您朝我推，我朝您推，毫无疑问，像两条河一样，经过千山万水，合流为一。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he seized her hand; she did not withdraw it.","sentences":[{"en":"And he seized her hand; she did not withdraw it.","zh":"他握住她的手；她没有抽回去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For good farming generally!” cried the president.","sentences":[{"en":"“For good farming generally!” cried the president.","zh":"主席喊道：“一般种植奖！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Just now, for example, when I went to your house.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Just now, for example, when I went to your house.”","zh":"“譬方说，方才我到府上…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“To Monsieur Bizat of Quincampoix.”","sentences":[{"en":"“To Monsieur Bizat of Quincampoix.”","zh":"“甘冈普瓦的比内先生。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Did I know I should accompany you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Did I know I should accompany you?”","zh":"“我怎么晓得我会陪伴您？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Seventy francs.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Seventy francs.”","zh":"“七十法郎！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“A hundred times I wished to go; and I followed you—I remained.”","sentences":[{"en":"“A hundred times I wished to go; and I followed you—I remained.”","zh":"“有许多回，我想走开，可是我跟着您，待了下来。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Manures!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Manures!”","zh":"“肥料奖。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And I shall remain to-night, to-morrow, all other days, all my life!”","sentences":[{"en":"“And I shall remain to-night, to-morrow, all other days, all my life!”","zh":"“既然今天黄昏会待了下来，明天、别的日子、我一辈子，也会待了下来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“To Monsieur Caron of Argueil, a gold medal!”","sentences":[{"en":"“To Monsieur Caron of Argueil, a gold medal!”","zh":"“阿格伊的卡隆先生，金质奖章一枚！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For I have never in the society of any other person found so complete a charm.”","sentences":[{"en":"“For I have never in the society of any other person found so complete a charm.”","zh":"“因为我和别人在一道，从来没有感到这样大的魅力。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“To Monsieur Bain of Givry-Saint-Martin.”","sentences":[{"en":"“To Monsieur Bain of Givry-Saint-Martin.”","zh":"“基弗里－圣马丹的班先生！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And I shall carry away with me the remembrance of you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And I shall carry away with me the remembrance of you.”","zh":"“所以我呐，我会永远想念您的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For a merino ram!”","sentences":[{"en":"“For a merino ram!”","zh":"“一只美里奴种公羊…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But you will forget me; I shall pass away like a shadow.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But you will forget me; I shall pass away like a shadow.”","zh":"“不过您要忘记我的，我会像一个影子般消逝的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“To Monsieur Belot of Notre-Dame.”","sentences":[{"en":"“To Monsieur Belot of Notre-Dame.”","zh":"“圣母村的…柏劳先生。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, no! I shall be something in your thought, in your life, shall I not?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, no! I shall be something in your thought, in your life, shall I not?”","zh":"“哎呀！不会的。我会不会成为您的思想、您的生命的一部分？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Porcine race; prizes—equal, to Messrs. Leherisse and Cullembourg, sixty francs!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Porcine race; prizes—equal, to Messrs. Leherisse and Cullembourg, sixty francs!”","zh":"“猪种奖两名：勒埃里塞先生与居朗布尔先生；平分六十法郎！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe was pressing her hand, and he felt it all warm and quivering like a captive dove that wants to fly away; but, whether she was trying to take it away or whether she was answering his pressure; she made a movement with her fingers. He exclaimed—","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe was pressing her hand, and he felt it all warm and quivering like a captive dove that wants to fly away; but, whether she was trying to take it away or whether she was answering his pressure; she made a movement with her fingers.","zh":"罗道耳弗捏住她的手，觉得又温暖，又颤抖，如同一只斑鸠，虽然被捉住了，还想飞走；但是不知道是她试着抽出手来，还是响应这种压抑，她动了动手指；他喊道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He exclaimed—","zh":"罗道耳弗捏住她的手，觉得又温暖，又颤抖，如同一只斑鸠，虽然被捉住了，还想飞走；但是不知道是她试着抽出手来，还是响应这种压抑，她动了动手指；他喊道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, I thank you! You do not repulse me! You are good! You understand that I am yours! Let me look at you; let me contemplate you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I thank you!","zh":"“谢谢！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You do not repulse me!","zh":"您不拒绝我！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are good!","zh":"您真好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You understand that I am yours!","zh":"您明白我是您的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let me look at you; let me contemplate you!”","zh":"让我看您，让我端详您！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A gust of wind that blew in at the window ruffled the cloth on the table, and in the square below all the great caps of the peasant women were uplifted by it like the wings of white butterflies fluttering.","sentences":[{"en":"A gust of wind that blew in at the window ruffled the cloth on the table, and in the square below all the great caps of the peasant women were uplifted by it like the wings of white butterflies fluttering.","zh":"一阵风飘进窗户，吹皱了桌毯，同时底下广场，乡下女人的大帽子，像白蝴蝶扇动翅膀一样，个个翘了起来。主席继续道：“豆饼的使用。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Use of oil-cakes,” continued the president. He was hurrying on: “Flemish manure-flax-growing-drainage-long leases-domestic service.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Use of oil-cakes,” continued the president.","zh":"他加快道：“养粪池，——种麻，——排水，——长期租赁，——家庭服务。”罗道耳弗不再说话。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was hurrying on: “Flemish manure-flax-growing-drainage-long leases-domestic service.”","zh":"他加快道：“养粪池，——种麻，——排水，——长期租赁，——家庭服务。”罗道耳弗不再说话。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe was no longer speaking. They looked at one another. A supreme desire made their dry lips tremble, and wearily, without an effort, their fingers intertwined.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe was no longer speaking.","zh":"两个人你望我，我望你，欲火如焚，干嘴唇直打哆嗦，于是心旌摇摇，手指不用力，就揉在一道。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They looked at one another.","zh":"两个人你望我，我望你，欲火如焚，干嘴唇直打哆嗦，于是心旌摇摇，手指不用力，就揉在一道。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A supreme desire made their dry lips tremble, and wearily, without an effort, their fingers intertwined.","zh":"两个人你望我，我望你，欲火如焚，干嘴唇直打哆嗦，于是心旌摇摇，手指不用力，就揉在一道。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Catherine Nicaise Elizabeth Leroux, of Sassetot-la-Guerriere, for fifty-four years of service at the same farm, a silver medal—value, twenty-five francs!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Catherine Nicaise Elizabeth Leroux, of Sassetot-la-Guerriere, for fifty-four years of service at the same farm, a silver medal—value, twenty-five francs!”","zh":"“萨司托－拉盖里耶的卡特琳－妮凯丝－伊莉莎白·勒鲁，在一家田庄连续服务五十四年，银质奖章一枚——值二十五法郎！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where is Catherine Leroux?” repeated the councillor.","sentences":[{"en":"“Where is Catherine Leroux?” repeated the councillor.","zh":"州行政委员重复道：“卡特琳·勒鲁，在什么地方？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She did not present herself, and one could hear voices whispering—","sentences":[{"en":"She did not present herself, and one could hear voices whispering—","zh":"不见她的踪影。只听见好些声音窃窃私语道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Go up!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go up!”","zh":"“去呀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Don’t be afraid!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t be afraid!”","zh":"“不。”“左边走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, how stupid she is!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, how stupid she is!”","zh":"“别害怕！”“啊！看她多蠢！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, is she there?” cried Tuvache.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, is she there?” cried Tuvache.","zh":"杜法赦喊道：“她到底在不在？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes; here she is.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes; here she is.”","zh":"“在！那不是！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Then let her come up!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Then let her come up!”","zh":"“那么，到前面来呀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then there came forward on the platform a little old woman with timid bearing, who seemed to shrink within her poor clothes. On her feet she wore heavy wooden clogs, and from her hips hung a large blue apron. Her pale face framed in a borderless cap was more wrinkled than a withered russet apple. And from the sleeves of her red jacket looked out two large hands with knotty joints, the dust of barns, the potash of washing the grease of wools had so encrusted, roughened, hardened these that they seemed dirty, although they had been rinsed in clear water; and by dint of long service they remained half open, as if to bear humble witness for themselves of so much suffering endured. Something of monastic rigidity dignified her face. Nothing of sadness or of emotion weakened that pale look. In her constant living with animals she had caught their dumbness and their calm. It was the first time that she found herself in the midst of so large a company, and inwardly scared by the flags, the drums, the gentlemen in frock-coats, and the order of the councillor, she stood motionless, not knowing whether to advance or run away, nor why the crowd was pushing her and the jury were smiling at her.","sentences":[{"en":"Then there came forward on the platform a little old woman with timid bearing, who seemed to shrink within her poor clothes.","zh":"这时人们看见一个矮小的老妇人，走上主席台，神情畏缩，好像和身上的破烂衣服皱成了一团一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On her feet she wore heavy wooden clogs, and from her hips hung a large blue apron.","zh":"她脚上蹬一双大木头套鞋，腰里系一条大蓝围裙，一顶没有镶边的小风帽兜住她的瘦脸；一脸老皱纹，风干的苹果也没有她的多。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her pale face framed in a borderless cap was more wrinkled than a withered russet apple.","zh":"她脚上蹬一双大木头套鞋，腰里系一条大蓝围裙，一顶没有镶边的小风帽兜住她的瘦脸；一脸老皱纹，风干的苹果也没有她的多。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And from the sleeves of her red jacket looked out two large hands with knotty joints, the dust of barns, the potash of washing the grease of wools had so encrusted, roughened, hardened these that they seemed dirty, although they had been rinsed in clear water; and by dint of long service they remained half open, as if to bear humble witness for themselves of so much suffering endured.","zh":"红上衣的袖筒伸出两只长手，关节疙里疙瘩；谷仓的灰尘、洗衣服的碱水、羊毛的油脂在手上留下一层厚皮，全是裂缝，指节发僵；清水再洗，也显着肮脏；苦干多年，合也合不拢来：好像明摆着这一双手，就是千辛万苦的卑微的凭证一样。脸上的表情，如同一个修行的道姑那样呆滞。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Something of monastic rigidity dignified her face.","zh":"任何喜怒哀乐也软化不了她那黯淡的视线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nothing of sadness or of emotion weakened that pale look.","zh":"她和牲畜待在一起，也像它们一样喑哑、安详。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In her constant living with animals she had caught their dumbness and their calm.","zh":"她还是第一次看见自己在这样大的一群人当中，眼前又是旗，又是鼓，又是青燕尾服的先生们，又是州行政委员的十字勋章，心中惶恐，一步不敢移动，不知道该往前走，还是该向后逃，也不知道群众为什么推她，审查员为什么朝她微笑。这干了半世纪劳役的苦婆子，就这样站在这些喜笑颜开的资产者面前。州行政委员从主席手上接过得奖人员的名单，然后道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was the first time that she found herself in the midst of so large a company, and inwardly scared by the flags, the drums, the gentlemen in frock-coats, and the order of the councillor, she stood motionless, not knowing whether to advance or run away, nor why the crowd was pushing her and the jury were smiling at her.","zh":"她还是第一次看见自己在这样大的一群人当中，眼前又是旗，又是鼓，又是青燕尾服的先生们，又是州行政委员的十字勋章，心中惶恐，一步不敢移动，不知道该往前走，还是该向后逃，也不知道群众为什么推她，审查员为什么朝她微笑。这干了半世纪劳役的苦婆子，就这样站在这些喜笑颜开的资产者面前。州行政委员从主席手上接过得奖人员的名单，然后道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Thus stood before these radiant bourgeois this half-century of servitude.","sentences":[{"en":"Thus stood before these radiant bourgeois this half-century of servitude.","zh":"“过来，可敬的卡特琳－妮凯丝－伊莉莎白·勒鲁！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Approach, venerable Catherine Nicaise Elizabeth Leroux!” said the councillor, who had taken the list of prize-winners from the president; and, looking at the piece of paper and the old woman by turns, he repeated in a fatherly tone—“Approach! approach!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Approach, venerable Catherine Nicaise Elizabeth Leroux!” said the councillor, who had taken the list of prize-winners from the president; and, looking at the piece of paper and the old woman by turns, he repeated in a fatherly tone—“Approach! approach!”","zh":"他看一遍名单，看一遍老妇人，用慈父的声音，重复道：“过来，过来！”杜法赦在扶手椅上跳道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are you deaf?” said Tuvache, fidgeting in his armchair; and he began shouting in her ear, “Fifty-four years of service. A silver medal! Twenty-five francs! For you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you deaf?” said Tuvache, fidgeting in his armchair; and he began shouting in her ear, “Fifty-four years of service.","zh":"“您聋了吗？”他朝她的耳朵喊道：“五十四年服务！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A silver medal!","zh":"银质奖章一枚！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Twenty-five francs!","zh":"银质奖章一枚！","scope":"group"},{"en":"For you!”","zh":"二十五法郎！是给您的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, when she had her medal, she looked at it, and a smile of beatitude spread over her face; and as she walked away they could hear her muttering “I’ll give it to our cure up home, to say some masses for me!”","sentences":[{"en":"Then, when she had her medal, she looked at it, and a smile of beatitude spread over her face; and as she walked away they could hear her muttering “I’ll give it to our cure up home, to say some masses for me!”","zh":"她接过奖章，仔细打量，随即一脸幸福的微笑，径自走开；大家听见她咕哝道：“我拿这送给我们的教堂堂长，给我做弥撒。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What fanaticism!” exclaimed the chemist, leaning across to the notary.","sentences":[{"en":"“What fanaticism!” exclaimed the chemist, leaning across to the notary.","zh":"药剂师朝公证人俯过身子，喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The meeting was over, the crowd dispersed, and now that the speeches had been read, each one fell back into his place again, and everything into the old grooves; the masters bullied the servants, and these struck the animals, indolent victors, going back to the stalls, a green-crown on their horns.","sentences":[{"en":"The meeting was over, the crowd dispersed, and now that the speeches had been read, each one fell back into his place again, and everything into the old grooves; the masters bullied the servants, and these struck the animals, indolent victors, going back to the stalls, a green-crown on their horns.","zh":"“信教信到这步田地！”大会开完，群众散去；现在，演说词读过了，人人回到原来地位，一切照旧：主子谩骂下人，下人鞭打牲畜；得奖的牲畜，犄角挂着一顶绿冠，漠不关心，又回槽头去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The National Guards, however, had gone up to the first floor of the town hall with buns spitted on their bayonets, and the drummer of the battalion carried a basket with bottles. Madame Bovary took Rodolphe’s arm; he saw her home; they separated at her door; then he walked about alone in the meadow while he waited for the time of the banquet.","sentences":[{"en":"The National Guards, however, had gone up to the first floor of the town hall with buns spitted on their bayonets, and the drummer of the battalion carried a basket with bottles.","zh":"国民自卫军这期间上到镇公所二楼，刺刀扎了一串点心，大队鼓手提着一篮酒瓶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Bovary took Rodolphe’s arm; he saw her home; they separated at her door; then he walked about alone in the meadow while he waited for the time of the banquet.","zh":"包法利夫人挎着罗道耳弗的胳膊；他送她回家；他们在她的门前分手；然后他一个人在田野散步，等候到入席的时间。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The feast was long, noisy, ill served; the guests were so crowded that they could hardly move their elbows; and the narrow planks used for forms almost broke down under their weight. They ate hugely. Each one stuffed himself on his own account. Sweat stood on every brow, and a whitish steam, like the vapour of a stream on an autumn morning, floated above the table between the hanging lamps. Rodolphe, leaning against the calico of the tent was thinking so earnestly of Emma that he heard nothing. Behind him on the grass the servants were piling up the dirty plates, his neighbours were talking; he did not answer them; they filled his glass, and there was silence in his thoughts in spite of the growing noise. He was dreaming of what she had said, of the line of her lips; her face, as in a magic mirror, shone on the plates of the shakos, the folds of her gown fell along the walls, and days of love unrolled to all infinity before him in the vistas of the future.","sentences":[{"en":"The feast was long, noisy, ill served; the guests were so crowded that they could hardly move their elbows; and the narrow planks used for forms almost broke down under their weight.","zh":"宴会又长又闹，而且侍奉不周；根本就人山人海，移动不得，窄木板变成临时条凳，人坐多了，险些压断。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They ate hugely.","zh":"菜肴丰盛，人人狠命吃喝自己名下的一份，个个额头冒汗。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Each one stuffed himself on his own account.","zh":"菜肴丰盛，人人狠命吃喝自己名下的一份，个个额头冒汗。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Sweat stood on every brow, and a whitish steam, like the vapour of a stream on an autumn morning, floated above the table between the hanging lamps.","zh":"桌面上高悬的甘该灯之间，浮起白蒙蒙一片热气，好像秋天早晨河水的雾气一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe, leaning against the calico of the tent was thinking so earnestly of Emma that he heard nothing.","zh":"罗道耳弗一心在想爱玛，背靠篷布，什么也没有听见。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Behind him on the grass the servants were piling up the dirty plates, his neighbours were talking; he did not answer them; they filled his glass, and there was silence in his thoughts in spite of the growing noise.","zh":"背后好些听差，在草地上摞脏盘子；邻座同他讲话，他不回答；有人给他斟酒；嘈杂的声音越来越响，可是他心里静静的，追忆她说过的话和她的嘴唇的形态；军帽的徽章仿佛一面照妖镜，照出她的脸来；她的打褶的袍子恍惚沿墙而下；遥望未来，恩爱的日月悠悠展开，好像没有尽期一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was dreaming of what she had said, of the line of her lips; her face, as in a magic mirror, shone on the plates of the shakos, the folds of her gown fell along the walls, and days of love unrolled to all infinity before him in the vistas of the future.","zh":"背后好些听差，在草地上摞脏盘子；邻座同他讲话，他不回答；有人给他斟酒；嘈杂的声音越来越响，可是他心里静静的，追忆她说过的话和她的嘴唇的形态；军帽的徽章仿佛一面照妖镜，照出她的脸来；她的打褶的袍子恍惚沿墙而下；遥望未来，恩爱的日月悠悠展开，好像没有尽期一样。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He saw her again in the evening during the fireworks, but she was with her husband, Madame Homais, and the druggist, who was worrying about the danger of stray rockets, and every moment he left the company to go and give some advice to Binet.","sentences":[{"en":"He saw her again in the evening during the fireworks, but she was with her husband, Madame Homais, and the druggist, who was worrying about the danger of stray rockets, and every moment he left the company to go and give some advice to Binet.","zh":"夜晚放烟火，他又见到她；但是她和丈夫，还有郝麦夫妇在一起。火花四射，药剂师十分担心会出危险，他时刻走开，过去关照毕耐几句。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The pyrotechnic pieces sent to Monsieur Tuvache had, through an excess of caution, been shut up in his cellar, and so the damp powder would not light, and the principal set piece, that was to represent a dragon biting his tail, failed completely. Now and then a meagre Roman-candle went off; then the gaping crowd sent up a shout that mingled with the cry of the women, whose waists were being squeezed in the darkness. Emma silently nestled against Charles’s shoulder; then, raising her chin, she watched the luminous rays of the rockets against the dark sky. Rodolphe gazed at her in the light of the burning lanterns.","sentences":[{"en":"The pyrotechnic pieces sent to Monsieur Tuvache had, through an excess of caution, been shut up in his cellar, and so the damp powder would not light, and the principal set piece, that was to represent a dragon biting his tail, failed completely.","zh":"爆竹送到杜法赦先生那边，他过分小心，放在他的地窖里，所以火药受潮，根本点不着，主要节目应当表现一条龙咬自己的尾巴，又完全失败。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now and then a meagre Roman-candle went off; then the gaping crowd sent up a shout that mingled with the cry of the women, whose waists were being squeezed in the darkness.","zh":"天空偶尔出现一串不值一看的罗马蜡烛 ，群众张口凝望，喊成一片，里面还掺杂着在黑地里腰让胳肢了的妇女的叫唤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma silently nestled against Charles’s shoulder; then, raising her chin, she watched the luminous rays of the rockets against the dark sky.","zh":"爱玛悄不做声，缩成一团，轻轻靠住查理的肩膀，然后仰起下巴，望着射出来的火花在黑黝黝的天空掠过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe gazed at her in the light of the burning lanterns.","zh":"罗道耳弗借着花灯亮光张望她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They went out one by one. The stars shone out. A few crops of rain began to fall. She knotted her fichu round her bare head.","sentences":[{"en":"They went out one by one.","zh":"花灯渐渐熄灭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The stars shone out.","zh":"天上出来星星。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A few crops of rain began to fall.","zh":"飘下一丝半点细雨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She knotted her fichu round her bare head.","zh":"她拿肩巾挽在头上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At this moment the councillor’s carriage came out from the inn.","sentences":[{"en":"At this moment the councillor’s carriage came out from the inn.","zh":"就在这时，州行政委员的马车走出客店。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His coachman, who was drunk, suddenly dozed off, and one could see from the distance, above the hood, between the two lanterns, the mass of his body, that swayed from right to left with the giving of the traces.","sentences":[{"en":"His coachman, who was drunk, suddenly dozed off, and one could see from the distance, above the hood, between the two lanterns, the mass of his body, that swayed from right to left with the giving of the traces.","zh":"车夫喝醉了酒，立刻昏昏沉沉，打起盹来了。大家远远望见他，坐在两盏车灯中间，大半个身子耸出车篷，车厢前后一动，也就左右摇晃起来。药剂师道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Truly,” said the druggist, “one ought to proceed most rigorously against drunkenness! I should like to see written up weekly at the door of the town hall on a board ad hoc the names of all those who during the week got intoxicated on alcohol. Besides, with regard to statistics, one would thus have, as it were, public records that one could refer to in case of need. But excuse me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Truly,” said the druggist, “one ought to proceed most rigorously against drunkenness!","zh":"“真的，应当严厉反对酗酒！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I should like to see written up weekly at the door of the town hall on a board ad hoc the names of all those who during the week got intoxicated on alcohol.","zh":"我希望镇公所门口，每星期专挂一块牌子，写出这一星期喝酒喝醉了的人的名姓。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, with regard to statistics, one would thus have, as it were, public records that one could refer to in case of need.","zh":"再说，有统计报告，好比年鉴一类东西，遇到必要，不妨拿来参考参考…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But excuse me!”","zh":"对不住。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he once more ran off to the captain. The latter was going back to see his lathe again.","sentences":[{"en":"And he once more ran off to the captain.","zh":"他又朝队长跑过去了。队长惦记他的旋床，正要回家看看。郝麦向他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"The latter was going back to see his lathe again.","zh":"他又朝队长跑过去了。队长惦记他的旋床，正要回家看看。郝麦向他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Perhaps you would not do ill,” Homais said to him, “to send one of your men, or to go yourself—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Perhaps you would not do ill,” Homais said to him, “to send one of your men, or to go yourself—”","zh":"“也许碍不了您什么事，打发您的部下，要不您就亲自去…”税务员回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Leave me alone!” answered the tax-collector. “It’s all right!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave me alone!” answered the tax-collector.","zh":"“什么事也没有，您就别跟我捣乱了吧！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It’s all right!”","zh":"“什么事也没有，您就别跟我捣乱了吧！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Do not be uneasy,” said the druggist, when he returned to his friends. “Monsieur Binet has assured me that all precautions have been taken. No sparks have fallen; the pumps are full. Let us go to rest.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do not be uneasy,” said the druggist, when he returned to his friends.","zh":"药剂师回到他的朋友旁边，道：“你们放心好啦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Monsieur Binet has assured me that all precautions have been taken.","zh":"毕耐先生告诉我，已经有了防备。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No sparks have fallen; the pumps are full.","zh":"火花不会落下来的。水龙装得满满的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let us go to rest.”","zh":"我们睡觉去吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ma foi! I want it,” said Madame Homais, yawning at large. “But never mind; we’ve had a beautiful day for our fete.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ma foi!","zh":"郝麦夫人大打呵欠，道：“说的是呀！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I want it,” said Madame Homais, yawning at large.","zh":"郝麦夫人大打呵欠，道：“说的是呀！","scope":"group"},{"en":"“But never mind; we’ve had a beautiful day for our fete.”","zh":"我尽想睡；不过没有关系，我们这一天过得好极啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe repeated in a low voice, and with a tender look, “Oh, yes! very beautiful!”","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe repeated in a low voice, and with a tender look, “Oh, yes! very beautiful!”","zh":"罗道耳弗放低声音，眼睛充满感情，道：“是啊！好极啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And having bowed to one another, they separated.","sentences":[{"en":"And having bowed to one another, they separated.","zh":"大家道过晚安，各走各的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Two days later, in the “Final de Rouen,” there was a long article on the show. Homais had composed it with verve the very next morning.","sentences":[{"en":"Two days later, in the “Final de Rouen,” there was a long article on the show.","zh":"两天以后，《鲁昂烽火》登出一篇报道展览会的大文章。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais had composed it with verve the very next morning.","zh":"郝麦兴之所至，第二天就把它写出来了：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why these festoons, these flowers, these garlands? Whither hurries this crowd like the waves of a furious sea under the torrents of a tropical sun pouring its heat upon our heads?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why these festoons, these flowers, these garlands?","zh":"为什么张灯？为什么悬花？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Whither hurries this crowd like the waves of a furious sea under the torrents of a tropical sun pouring its heat upon our heads?”","zh":"为什么结彩？一种热带的太阳，直射我们的阡陌。这群人仿佛怒海巨涛，冒着头上的热流，朝什么地方跑？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he spoke of the condition of the peasants. Certainly the Government was doing much, but not enough. “Courage!” he cried to it; “a thousand reforms are indispensable; let us accomplish them!” Then touching on the entry of the councillor, he did not forget “the martial air of our militia;” nor “our most merry village maidens;” nor the “bald-headed old men like patriarchs who were there, and of whom some, the remnants of our phalanxes, still felt their hearts beat at the manly sound of the drums.” He cited himself among the first of the members of the jury, and he even called attention in a note to the fact that Monsieur Homais, chemist, had sent a memoir on cider to the agricultural society.","sentences":[{"en":"Then he spoke of the condition of the peasants.","zh":"接着他就谈起农民的情况。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Certainly the Government was doing much, but not enough.","zh":"政府的确尽了大力，但是不够！他向政府呼喊道：“勇敢！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Courage!” he cried to it; “a thousand reforms are indispensable; let us accomplish them!”","zh":"千千万万的改革需要着手，我们就来完成这些改革吧。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then touching on the entry of the councillor, he did not forget “the martial air of our militia;” nor “our most merry village maidens;” nor the “bald-headed old men like patriarchs who were there, and of whom some, the remnants of our phalanxes, still felt their hearts beat at the manly sound of the drums.”","zh":"随后他写到州行政委员驾到，没有忘记“我们军队的武士气概”，也没有忘记“我们最活泼的乡村妇女”，也没有忘记秃了头的老年人，“仿佛古代族长，岸然而立，其中有几位，曾经置身于我们不朽的行伍，听见雄壮的鼓声，觉得心还在跳”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He cited himself among the first of the members of the jury, and he even called attention in a note to the fact that Monsieur Homais, chemist, had sent a memoir on cider to the agricultural society.","zh":"他列举重要的评判委员，还说到自己；甚至在一个小注里，也提醒读者：药剂师郝麦先生，曾经给农学会送去一篇关于苹果酒的论文。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When he came to the distribution of the prizes, he painted the joy of the prize-winners in dithyrambic strophes. “The father embraced the son, the brother the brother, the husband his consort. More than one showed his humble medal with pride; and no doubt when he got home to his good housewife, he hung it up weeping on the modest walls of his cot.","sentences":[{"en":"When he came to the distribution of the prizes, he painted the joy of the prize-winners in dithyrambic strophes.","zh":"他写到赠奖，形容得奖者的喜悦，运用抒情笔调：“父亲吻抱儿子，哥哥吻抱兄弟，丈夫吻抱妻子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“The father embraced the son, the brother the brother, the husband his consort.","zh":"他写到赠奖，形容得奖者的喜悦，运用抒情笔调：“父亲吻抱儿子，哥哥吻抱兄弟，丈夫吻抱妻子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"More than one showed his humble medal with pride; and no doubt when he got home to his good housewife, he hung it up weeping on the modest walls of his cot.","zh":"许多人傲形于色，指着他们的小小奖章，不用说，回到家中，在贤内助身旁，边哭边拿它挂到茅庐的缄默的墙头。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“About six o’clock a banquet prepared in the meadow of Monsieur Leigeard brought together the principal personages of the fete. The greatest cordiality reigned here. Divers toasts were proposed: Monsieur Lieuvain, the King; Monsieur Tuvache, the Prefect; Monsieur Derozerays, Agriculture; Monsieur Homais, Industry and the Fine Arts, those twin sisters; Monsieur Leplichey, Progress. In the evening some brilliant fireworks on a sudden illumined the air. One would have called it a veritable kaleidoscope, a real operatic scene; and for a moment our little locality might have thought itself transported into the midst of a dream of the ‘Thousand and One Nights.’ Let us state that no untoward event disturbed this family meeting.” And he added “Only the absence of the clergy was remarked. No doubt the priests understand progress in another fashion. Just as you please, messieurs the followers of Loyola!”","sentences":[{"en":"“About six o’clock a banquet prepared in the meadow of Monsieur Leigeard brought together the principal personages of the fete.","zh":"“六点钟左右，酒席摆在利艾加尔先生的牧场，参加大会的主要人物聚在一道，自始至终，充满着发自内心的最大热忱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The greatest cordiality reigned here.","zh":"宴会中间，不时举杯致敬：廖万先生提议，为国君的健康干杯！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Divers toasts were proposed: Monsieur Lieuvain, the King; Monsieur Tuvache, the Prefect; Monsieur Derozerays, Agriculture; Monsieur Homais, Industry and the Fine Arts, those twin sisters; Monsieur Leplichey, Progress.","zh":"杜法赦先生提议，为州长的健康干杯！德罗兹赖先生提议，为农业干杯！郝麦先生提议，为工业和艺术这一对姊妹干杯！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the evening some brilliant fireworks on a sudden illumined the air.","zh":"勒普利谢先生提议，为进步干杯！到了夜晚，烟火忽然照亮天空。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One would have called it a veritable kaleidoscope, a real operatic scene; and for a moment our little locality might have thought itself transported into the midst of a dream of the ‘Thousand and One Nights.’","zh":"五彩缤纷，简直像是真正的歌剧布景。一时间我们这小镇，竟如同进入了《天方夜谭》的梦境。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let us state that no untoward event disturbed this family meeting.”","zh":"“这次家庭集会，可以说，没有任何不愉快的事发生。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he added “Only the absence of the clergy was remarked.","zh":"他还加上一句：“此次教士不露面，特别惹人注目。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No doubt the priests understand progress in another fashion.","zh":"不用说，教会对进步别有看法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Just as you please, messieurs the followers of Loyola!”","zh":"罗耀拉 的信徒们，请便！”","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-9","part":2,"n":9,"title":"Part II · Chapter 9","titleZh":"中卷 · 9","paragraphs":[{"en":"Six weeks passed. Rodolphe did not come again. At last one evening he appeared.","sentences":[{"en":"Six weeks passed.","zh":"六个星期过去了，还不见罗道耳弗来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Rodolphe did not come again.","zh":"六个星期过去了，还不见罗道耳弗来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last one evening he appeared.","zh":"最后有一天黄昏，他露面了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The day after the show he had said to himself—“We mustn’t go back too soon; that would be a mistake.”","sentences":[{"en":"The day after the show he had said to himself—“We mustn’t go back too soon; that would be a mistake.”","zh":"展览会的第二天，他对自己讲：“别去早了；去早了反而坏事。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And at the end of a week he had gone off hunting. After the hunting he had thought it was too late, and then he reasoned thus—","sentences":[{"en":"And at the end of a week he had gone off hunting.","zh":"头一个星期，过到末尾，他打猎去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"After the hunting he had thought it was too late, and then he reasoned thus—","zh":"打过猎，他一想，去也太晚了，接着他又这样理论道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If from the first day she loved me, she must from impatience to see me again love me more. Let’s go on with it!”","sentences":[{"en":"“If from the first day she loved me, she must from impatience to see me again love me more.","zh":"“不过如果头一天她就爱上了我的话，她一定盼望我去，她越情急，越会爱我。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let’s go on with it!”","zh":"还是继续下去吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he knew that his calculation had been right when, on entering the room, he saw Emma turn pale.","sentences":[{"en":"And he knew that his calculation had been right when, on entering the room, he saw Emma turn pale.","zh":"他走进厅房，望见爱玛脸色变白，明白他划算对了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was alone. The day was drawing in. The small muslin curtain along the windows deepened the twilight, and the gilding of the barometer, on which the rays of the sun fell, shone in the looking-glass between the meshes of the coral.","sentences":[{"en":"She was alone.","zh":"只她一个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The day was drawing in.","zh":"天色向晚，小纱窗帘遮着玻璃，越发显得阴暗。阳光一线，照亮晴雨计的镀金；金光闪闪，穿过珊瑚丫杈的空隙，在镜子里变成了一团火。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The small muslin curtain along the windows deepened the twilight, and the gilding of the barometer, on which the rays of the sun fell, shone in the looking-glass between the meshes of the coral.","zh":"天色向晚，小纱窗帘遮着玻璃，越发显得阴暗。阳光一线，照亮晴雨计的镀金；金光闪闪，穿过珊瑚丫杈的空隙，在镜子里变成了一团火。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe remained standing, and Emma hardly answered his first conventional phrases.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe remained standing, and Emma hardly answered his first conventional phrases.","zh":"罗道耳弗一直站着；爱玛几乎等于没有回答他的问候。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I,” he said, “have been busy. I have been ill.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I,” he said, “have been busy.","zh":"“我呀，有事忙，又害了一场病。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I have been ill.”","zh":"“我呀，有事忙，又害了一场病。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Seriously?” she cried.","sentences":[{"en":"“Seriously?” she cried.","zh":"她着急道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well,” said Rodolphe, sitting down at her side on a footstool, “no; it was because I did not want to come back.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well,” said Rodolphe, sitting down at her side on a footstool, “no; it was because I did not want to come back.”","zh":"“病重吗？”罗道耳弗坐到她身旁一张凳子上，道：“啊！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why?”","zh":"“为什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Can you not guess?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Can you not guess?”","zh":"“您猜不出来？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He looked at her again, but so hard that she lowered her head, blushing. He went on—","sentences":[{"en":"He looked at her again, but so hard that she lowered her head, blushing.","zh":"他又看了她一眼，但是神色热烈，她涨红了脸，低下头去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He went on—","zh":"他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Emma!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Emma!”","zh":"“爱玛…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sir,” she said, drawing back a little.","sentences":[{"en":"“Sir,” she said, drawing back a little.","zh":"她稍稍走开，道：“先生！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! you see,” replied he in a melancholy voice, “that I was right not to come back; for this name, this name that fills my whole soul, and that escaped me, you forbid me to use! Madame Bovary! why all the world calls you thus! Besides, it is not your name; it is the name of another!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! you see,” replied he in a melancholy voice, “that I was right not to come back; for this name, this name that fills my whole soul, and that escaped me, you forbid me to use!","zh":"他用一种忧伤的声音对答道：“啊！您看，我不想来，我有道理；因为您这名字，您这名字充满我的灵魂，可是脱口而出，您又禁止！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Bovary! why all the world calls you thus!","zh":"包法利太太！哎！人人这样称呼您！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, it is not your name; it is the name of another!”","zh":"其实，这不是您的姓；这是别人的姓！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He repeated, “of another!” And he hid his face in his hands.","sentences":[{"en":"He repeated, “of another!”","zh":"他重复一遍：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he hid his face in his hands.","zh":"“别人的姓！”他拿脸藏到两只手里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, I think of you constantly. The memory of you drives me to despair. Ah! forgive me! I will leave you! Farewell! I will go far away, so far that you will never hear of me again; and yet—to-day—I know not what force impelled me towards you. For one does not struggle against Heaven; one cannot resist the smile of angels; one is carried away by that which is beautiful, charming, adorable.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, I think of you constantly.","zh":"“是的，我时时刻刻想您！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The memory of you drives me to despair.","zh":"我一想到您就难过！啊！对不住！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! forgive me!","zh":"我离开您…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I will leave you!","zh":"永别了！我要到远地方去…远到您再也不会听见有人说起我来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Farewell!","zh":"可是…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I will go far away, so far that you will never hear of me again; and yet—to-day—I know not what force impelled me towards you.","zh":"今天…我不知道又是什么力量把我朝您推过来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For one does not struggle against Heaven; one cannot resist the smile of angels; one is carried away by that which is beautiful, charming, adorable.”","zh":"因为人斗不过天，人拗不过天使们的微笑！人不由自主，就跟着美丽、愉快、值得热爱的事物走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was the first time that Emma had heard such words spoken to herself, and her pride, like one who reposes bathed in warmth, expanded softly and fully at this glowing language.","sentences":[{"en":"It was the first time that Emma had heard such words spoken to herself, and her pride, like one who reposes bathed in warmth, expanded softly and fully at this glowing language.","zh":"爱玛还是第一次听见这种话，她的骄傲好似一个人在蒸汽浴室，养息精神，伸开四肢，驱除疲劳，把自己整个儿交给这热雾腾腾的语言。他继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But if I did not come,” he continued, “if I could not see you, at least I have gazed long on all that surrounds you. At night-every night-I arose; I came hither; I watched your house, its glimmering in the moon, the trees in the garden swaying before your window, and the little lamp, a gleam shining through the window-panes in the darkness. Ah! you never knew that there, so near you, so far from you, was a poor wretch!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But if I did not come,” he continued, “if I could not see you, at least I have gazed long on all that surrounds you.","zh":"“可是就算我不来，就算我不来看您，啊！至少您周围的东西，我尽饱看的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At night-every night-I arose; I came hither; I watched your house, its glimmering in the moon, the trees in the garden swaying before your window, and the little lamp, a gleam shining through the window-panes in the darkness.","zh":"夜晚，每天夜晚，我爬起床，一直走到这儿，望着您的房屋：月光照亮屋顶，花园树木在您的窗前摇来晃去，窗玻璃里，阴影中间，点着一盏小灯，透出一丝亮光。啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! you never knew that there, so near you, so far from you, was a poor wretch!”","zh":"您说什么也不知道，那边有一个可怜人，说近也算近，说远可真远…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She turned towards him with a sob.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned towards him with a sob.","zh":"她朝他转过身子，呜咽道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, you are good!” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, you are good!” she said.","zh":"“啊！您真好！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, I love you, that is all! You do not doubt that! Tell me—one word—only one word!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, I love you, that is all!","zh":"“不对，我爱您，就是这个！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You do not doubt that!","zh":"您相信我！说给我听！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tell me—one word—only one word!”","zh":"一句话！只一句话也就成了！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And Rodolphe imperceptibly glided from the footstool to the ground; but a sound of wooden shoes was heard in the kitchen, and he noticed the door of the room was not closed.","sentences":[{"en":"And Rodolphe imperceptibly glided from the footstool to the ground; but a sound of wooden shoes was heard in the kitchen, and he noticed the door of the room was not closed.","zh":"罗道耳弗不知不觉，就从凳子溜到地上；厨房传来木头套鞋的响声，同时他望见厅房门也没有关。他站起来，讲下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How kind it would be of you,” he went on, rising, “if you would humour a whim of mine.” It was to go over her house; he wanted to know it; and Madame Bovary seeing no objection to this, they both rose, when Charles came in.","sentences":[{"en":"“How kind it would be of you,” he went on, rising, “if you would humour a whim of mine.”","zh":"“我有一个怪心思，您行行好，满足满足吧！”原来是带他看看房屋；他想熟识熟识；包法利夫人看不出有什么不合适，两下方才站起，正好查理进来。罗道耳弗向他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was to go over her house; he wanted to know it; and Madame Bovary seeing no objection to this, they both rose, when Charles came in.","zh":"“我有一个怪心思，您行行好，满足满足吧！”原来是带他看看房屋；他想熟识熟识；包法利夫人看不出有什么不合适，两下方才站起，正好查理进来。罗道耳弗向他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Good morning, doctor,” Rodolphe said to him.","sentences":[{"en":"“Good morning, doctor,” Rodolphe said to him.","zh":"“您好，博士。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The doctor, flattered at this unexpected title, launched out into obsequious phrases. Of this the other took advantage to pull himself together a little.","sentences":[{"en":"The doctor, flattered at this unexpected title, launched out into obsequious phrases.","zh":"医生听了这天外飞来的头衔，受宠若惊，殷勤趋奉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Of this the other took advantage to pull himself together a little.","zh":"另一位利用这期间定了定神，就说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Madame was speaking to me,” he then said, “about her health.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Madame was speaking to me,” he then said, “about her health.”","zh":"“尊夫人同我谈起她的健康…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles interrupted him; he had indeed a thousand anxieties; his wife’s palpitations of the heart were beginning again. Then Rodolphe asked if riding would not be good.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles interrupted him; he had indeed a thousand anxieties; his wife’s palpitations of the heart were beginning again.","zh":"查理插话道：他的确担心到了万分；他的女人又开始感到郁闷。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Rodolphe asked if riding would not be good.","zh":"罗道耳弗于是问，骑马有没有用处。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Certainly! excellent! just the thing! There’s an idea! You ought to follow it up.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Certainly! excellent! just the thing!","zh":"“当然！很好，对！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There’s an idea!","zh":"这倒是一个好办法！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You ought to follow it up.”","zh":"你应当照这话做。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And as she objected that she had no horse, Monsieur Rodolphe offered one. She refused his offer; he did not insist. Then to explain his visit he said that his ploughman, the man of the blood-letting, still suffered from giddiness.","sentences":[{"en":"And as she objected that she had no horse, Monsieur Rodolphe offered one.","zh":"她说困难在于没有马。罗道耳弗愿意借她一匹，她谢绝了，他也并不坚持。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She refused his offer; he did not insist.","zh":"她说困难在于没有马。罗道耳弗愿意借她一匹，她谢绝了，他也并不坚持。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then to explain his visit he said that his ploughman, the man of the blood-letting, still suffered from giddiness.","zh":"他随后解释他的来意，说他的赶大车的、前次放血的那个家伙，总觉得头晕眼花。包法利道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I’ll call around,” said Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll call around,” said Bovary.","zh":"“改天我去看看。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no! I’ll send him to you; we’ll come; that will be more convenient for you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no! I’ll send him to you; we’ll come; that will be more convenient for you.”","zh":"“不，不，我打发他来；我们来，您方便多了。”“啊！很好。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! very good! I thank you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! very good!","zh":"罗道耳弗一走，查理就说：","scope":"group"},{"en":"I thank you.”","zh":"罗道耳弗一走，查理就说：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And as soon as they were alone, “Why don’t you accept Monsieur Boulanger’s kind offer?”","sentences":[{"en":"And as soon as they were alone, “Why don’t you accept Monsieur Boulanger’s kind offer?”","zh":"“布朗热先生好意借马，你为什么不应下来？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She assumed a sulky air, invented a thousand excuses, and finally declared that perhaps it would look odd.","sentences":[{"en":"She assumed a sulky air, invented a thousand excuses, and finally declared that perhaps it would look odd.","zh":"她摆出噘嘴模样，找了许多话推托，最后才讲：“我也许会惹人笑话。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, what the deuce do I care for that?” said Charles, making a pirouette. “Health before everything! You are wrong.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, what the deuce do I care for that?” said Charles, making a pirouette.","zh":"查理打了一个转身，道：“啊！我不在乎！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Health before everything!","zh":"健康第一！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are wrong.”","zh":"你错啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And how do you think I can ride when I haven’t got a habit?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And how do you think I can ride when I haven’t got a habit?”","zh":"“哎呀！我没有骑马衣服，你怎么好叫我骑马呀？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You must order one,” he answered.","sentences":[{"en":"“You must order one,” he answered.","zh":"他回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The riding-habit decided her.","sentences":[{"en":"The riding-habit decided her.","zh":"“你就该添置一身！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When the habit was ready, Charles wrote to Monsieur Boulanger that his wife was at his command, and that they counted on his good-nature.","sentences":[{"en":"When the habit was ready, Charles wrote to Monsieur Boulanger that his wife was at his command, and that they counted on his good-nature.","zh":"她看在骑马衣服分上，同意了。衣服做成，查理写信给布朗热先生，说：盛意可感，拙荆待命，不胜翘企。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day at noon Rodolphe appeared at Charles’s door with two saddle-horses. One had pink rosettes at his ears and a deerskin side-saddle.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day at noon Rodolphe appeared at Charles’s door with two saddle-horses.","zh":"第二天正午，罗道耳弗带了两匹鞍韂齐备的马，来到查理门前。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One had pink rosettes at his ears and a deerskin side-saddle.","zh":"有一匹耳朵还系着玫瑰红小绒球，背上搭了一副鹿皮女鞍。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe had put on high soft boots, saying to himself that no doubt she had never seen anything like them. In fact, Emma was charmed with his appearance as he stood on the landing in his great velvet coat and white corduroy breeches. She was ready; she was waiting for him.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe had put on high soft boots, saying to himself that no doubt she had never seen anything like them.","zh":"罗道耳弗穿了一双软皮长靴，心想这样东西，她从前一定没有见过；事实上，他在楼梯口一出现，身上是丝绒长燕尾服，腿上是灯芯绒白裤，爱玛就已经在欣赏他的翩翩风度了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In fact, Emma was charmed with his appearance as he stood on the landing in his great velvet coat and white corduroy breeches.","zh":"罗道耳弗穿了一双软皮长靴，心想这样东西，她从前一定没有见过；事实上，他在楼梯口一出现，身上是丝绒长燕尾服，腿上是灯芯绒白裤，爱玛就已经在欣赏他的翩翩风度了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was ready; she was waiting for him.","zh":"她打扮停当，正等他来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Justin escaped from the chemist’s to see her start, and the chemist also came out. He was giving Monsieur Boulanger a little good advice.","sentences":[{"en":"Justin escaped from the chemist’s to see her start, and the chemist also came out.","zh":"朱斯丹溜出药房看她，连药剂师也惊动出来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was giving Monsieur Boulanger a little good advice.","zh":"他一再叮咛布朗热先生：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“An accident happens so easily. Be careful! Your horses perhaps are mettlesome.”","sentences":[{"en":"“An accident happens so easily.","zh":"“意外说来就来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Be careful!","zh":"千万当心！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Your horses perhaps are mettlesome.”","zh":"您的马也许性烈！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She heard a noise above her; it was Félicité drumming on the windowpanes to amuse little Berthe. The child blew her a kiss; her mother answered with a wave of her whip.","sentences":[{"en":"She heard a noise above her; it was Félicité drumming on the windowpanes to amuse little Berthe.","zh":"她听见头上有响声：原来是全福哄小白尔特，敲打玻璃窗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The child blew her a kiss; her mother answered with a wave of her whip.","zh":"小孩子远远递了她一个吻；母亲的回答是摇摇鞭子把儿。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“A pleasant ride!” cried Monsieur Homais. “Prudence! above all, prudence!” And he flourished his newspaper as he saw them disappear.","sentences":[{"en":"“A pleasant ride!” cried Monsieur Homais.","zh":"郝麦先生喊道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Prudence! above all, prudence!”","zh":"“一路快乐！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he flourished his newspaper as he saw them disappear.","zh":"千万小心！小心！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As soon as he felt the ground, Emma’s horse set off at a gallop.","sentences":[{"en":"As soon as he felt the ground, Emma’s horse set off at a gallop.","zh":"他摇动他的报纸，望着他们走远。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe galloped by her side. Now and then they exchanged a word. Her figure slightly bent, her hand well up, and her right arm stretched out, she gave herself up to the cadence of the movement that rocked her in her saddle. At the bottom of the hill Rodolphe gave his horse its head; they started together at a bound, then at the top suddenly the horses stopped, and her large blue veil fell about her.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe galloped by her side.","zh":"爱玛的马一出镇子，就小跑起来，罗道耳弗的马跟在一旁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now and then they exchanged a word.","zh":"他们偶尔交谈一句。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her figure slightly bent, her hand well up, and her right arm stretched out, she gave herself up to the cadence of the movement that rocked her in her saddle.","zh":"她坐在鞍子上，脸微微向下，手举起来，右胳膊伸开，由着马上下颠簸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the bottom of the hill Rodolphe gave his horse its head; they started together at a bound, then at the top suddenly the horses stopped, and her large blue veil fell about her.","zh":"来到岭下，罗道耳弗放松缰绳，他们一道驰骋；随后跑上岭，马猛然站住，她的大蓝面网坠了下来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was early in October. There was fog over the land. Hazy clouds hovered on the horizon between the outlines of the hills; others, rent asunder, floated up and disappeared. Sometimes through a rift in the clouds, beneath a ray of sunshine, gleamed from afar the roots of Yonville, with the gardens at the water’s edge, the yards, the walls and the church steeple. Emma half closed her eyes to pick out her house, and never had this poor village where she lived appeared so small. From the height on which they were the whole valley seemed an immense pale lake sending off its vapour into the air. Clumps of trees here and there stood out like black rocks, and the tall lines of the poplars that rose above the mist were like a beach stirred by the wind.","sentences":[{"en":"It was early in October.","zh":"正当十月上旬，田野有雾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was fog over the land.","zh":"雾气沿着丘陵的边缘，弥漫在天边，有的地方云雾裂开，升上天空消失了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Hazy clouds hovered on the horizon between the outlines of the hills; others, rent asunder, floated up and disappeared.","zh":"雾气沿着丘陵的边缘，弥漫在天边，有的地方云雾裂开，升上天空消失了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Sometimes through a rift in the clouds, beneath a ray of sunshine, gleamed from afar the roots of Yonville, with the gardens at the water’s edge, the yards, the walls and the church steeple.","zh":"有时候，一道阳光破云而出，让他们远远望见永镇的屋顶、水边的花园、院落、墙壁和教堂的钟楼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma half closed her eyes to pick out her house, and never had this poor village where she lived appeared so small.","zh":"爱玛眯着眼睛，寻认她的住宅；她住的这可怜的小镇，从来没显得这样小。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"From the height on which they were the whole valley seemed an immense pale lake sending off its vapour into the air.","zh":"他们站在高处，觉得整个盆地就像一座白茫茫的大湖，在半空化成雾气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Clumps of trees here and there stood out like black rocks, and the tall lines of the poplars that rose above the mist were like a beach stirred by the wind.","zh":"左一丛树木，右一丛树木，黑岩似的，兀立一侧；白杨高耸雾上，齐齐一排，好像风卷沙移的海滩。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"By the side, on the turf between the pines, a brown light shimmered in the warm atmosphere. The earth, ruddy like the powder of tobacco, deadened the noise of their steps, and with the edge of their shoes the horses as they walked kicked the fallen fir cones in front of them.","sentences":[{"en":"By the side, on the turf between the pines, a brown light shimmered in the warm atmosphere.","zh":"他们旁边，冷杉蓊郁，中间一块草坪，上空有一道褐光，在温暖的大气里游来游去。土像烟草屑一样的颜色，近似红褐，马走上去，听不见蹄子响。马朝前走，铁掌踢开遍地的松实。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The earth, ruddy like the powder of tobacco, deadened the noise of their steps, and with the edge of their shoes the horses as they walked kicked the fallen fir cones in front of them.","zh":"他们旁边，冷杉蓊郁，中间一块草坪，上空有一道褐光，在温暖的大气里游来游去。土像烟草屑一样的颜色，近似红褐，马走上去，听不见蹄子响。马朝前走，铁掌踢开遍地的松实。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe and Emma thus went along the skirt of the wood. She turned away from time to time to avoid his look, and then she saw only the pine trunks in lines, whose monotonous succession made her a little giddy. The horses were panting; the leather of the saddles creaked.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe and Emma thus went along the skirt of the wood.","zh":"罗道耳弗和爱玛就这样兜着树林边沿走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She turned away from time to time to avoid his look, and then she saw only the pine trunks in lines, whose monotonous succession made her a little giddy.","zh":"她回避他的视线，不时转过头去，可是这样一来，就只看见一排一排冷杉树干，络绎不绝，看到后来，未免头晕眼花。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The horses were panting; the leather of the saddles creaked.","zh":"马在喘气。鞍皮咯吱咯吱直响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Just as they were entering the forest the sun shone out.","sentences":[{"en":"Just as they were entering the forest the sun shone out.","zh":"他们走进森林，太阳正好出来。罗道耳弗道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“God protects us!” said Rodolphe.","sentences":[{"en":"“God protects us!” said Rodolphe.","zh":"“上帝保佑我们！”她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do you think so?” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you think so?” she said.","zh":"“您相信？”他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Forward! forward!” he continued.","sentences":[{"en":"“Forward! forward!” he continued.","zh":"“再往前！往前走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He “tchk’d” with his tongue. The two beasts set off at a trot.","sentences":[{"en":"He “tchk’d” with his tongue.","zh":"他打响舌；两匹马跑了起来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The two beasts set off at a trot.","zh":"他打响舌；两匹马跑了起来。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Long ferns by the roadside caught in Emma’s stirrup.","sentences":[{"en":"Long ferns by the roadside caught in Emma’s stirrup.","zh":"道旁的羊齿草，横拦竖遮，一来就卷进爱玛的脚镫。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe leant forward and removed them as they rode along. At other times, to turn aside the branches, he passed close to her, and Emma felt his knee brushing against her leg. The sky was now blue, the leaves no longer stirred. There were spaces full of heather in flower, and plots of violets alternated with the confused patches of the trees that were grey, fawn, or golden coloured, according to the nature of their leaves. Often in the thicket was heard the fluttering of wings, or else the hoarse, soft cry of the ravens flying off amidst the oaks.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe leant forward and removed them as they rode along.","zh":"罗道耳弗一面纵马跑，一面斜过身子，一根又一根，把羊齿草抽出来。有的时候，他靠近了，推开树枝，爱玛觉得他的膝盖蹭到她的腿。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At other times, to turn aside the branches, he passed close to her, and Emma felt his knee brushing against her leg.","zh":"罗道耳弗一面纵马跑，一面斜过身子，一根又一根，把羊齿草抽出来。有的时候，他靠近了，推开树枝，爱玛觉得他的膝盖蹭到她的腿。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The sky was now blue, the leaves no longer stirred.","zh":"天变成蓝色。树叶一动不动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There were spaces full of heather in flower, and plots of violets alternated with the confused patches of the trees that were grey, fawn, or golden coloured, according to the nature of their leaves.","zh":"许多空地长满正在开花的映山红；一片片紫罗兰夹杂在树丛中，这些树丛枝叶各异，有的呈灰色，有的呈灰褐色，有的呈金黄色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often in the thicket was heard the fluttering of wings, or else the hoarse, soft cry of the ravens flying off amidst the oaks.","zh":"灌木丛中，他们不时听见翅膀轻轻扑扇，或者乌鸦在橡树之间盘旋，哑哑哀鸣。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They dismounted. Rodolphe fastened up the horses. She walked on in front on the moss between the paths. But her long habit got in her way, although she held it up by the skirt; and Rodolphe, walking behind her, saw between the black cloth and the black shoe the fineness of her white stocking, that seemed to him as if it were a part of her nakedness.","sentences":[{"en":"They dismounted.","zh":"他们下了马。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe fastened up the horses.","zh":"罗道耳弗拴马，她在车辙之间的青苔上漫步前行。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She walked on in front on the moss between the paths.","zh":"罗道耳弗拴马，她在车辙之间的青苔上漫步前行。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But her long habit got in her way, although she held it up by the skirt; and Rodolphe, walking behind her, saw between the black cloth and the black shoe the fineness of her white stocking, that seemed to him as if it were a part of her nakedness.","zh":"但是袍子太长，她虽说撩起后摆，仍然妨碍走路。罗道耳弗跟在后头，望着她细致的白袜，在黑衣料和黑靴之间，像是她的一部分光光的皮肉似的。她站住道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She stopped. “I am tired,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"She stopped.","zh":"“我累啦。”他回答道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I am tired,” she said.","zh":"“我累啦。”他回答道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Come, try again,” he went on. “Courage!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, try again,” he went on.","zh":"“来，再走走看！加油！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Courage!”","zh":"“来，再走走看！加油！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then some hundred paces farther on she again stopped, and through her veil, that fell sideways from her man’s hat over her hips, her face appeared in a bluish transparency as if she were floating under azure waves.","sentences":[{"en":"Then some hundred paces farther on she again stopped, and through her veil, that fell sideways from her man’s hat over her hips, her face appeared in a bluish transparency as if she were floating under azure waves.","zh":"又走了百来步远，她又站住。她戴一顶男人帽子，面网坠下来，斜搭在臀部，看上去像在碧波底下游泳一样，隔着透明的浅蓝颜色，他依稀认出她的脸相。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But where are we going?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But where are we going?”","zh":"“我们到底去什么地方？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He did not answer. She was breathing irregularly. Rodolphe looked round him biting his moustache. They came to a larger space where the coppice had been cut. They sat down on the trunk of a fallen tree, and Rodolphe began speaking to her of his love. He did not begin by frightening her with compliments. He was calm, serious, melancholy.","sentences":[{"en":"He did not answer.","zh":"他不回答。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was breathing irregularly.","zh":"她的呼吸急促了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe looked round him biting his moustache.","zh":"罗道耳弗向周围扫了一眼，咬着上嘴唇的髭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They came to a larger space where the coppice had been cut.","zh":"他们来到一个地点，小树砍去，比较宽阔。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They sat down on the trunk of a fallen tree, and Rodolphe began speaking to her of his love.","zh":"他们坐在一个放倒了的树干上，罗道耳弗对她谈起他的爱情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He did not begin by frightening her with compliments.","zh":"他生怕吓着了她，一入手，先收起恭维话不说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was calm, serious, melancholy.","zh":"他安静、严肃、忧郁。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma listened to him with bowed head, and stirred the bits of wood on the ground with the tip of her foot. But at the words, “Are not our destinies now one?”","sentences":[{"en":"Emma listened to him with bowed head, and stirred the bits of wood on the ground with the tip of her foot.","zh":"爱玛低着头听，一边还拿脚尖翻动地上的碎木片。“难道我们的命运如今不是同一个？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But at the words, “Are not our destinies now one?”","zh":"她一听这话，就驳道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, no!” she replied. “You know that well. It is impossible!” She rose to go. He seized her by the wrist. She stopped. Then, having gazed at him for a few moments with an amorous and humid look, she said hurriedly—","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, no!” she replied.","zh":"“不是同一个！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“You know that well.","zh":"您清楚的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is impossible!”","zh":"不可能。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She rose to go.","zh":"她站起来要走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He seized her by the wrist.","zh":"他揪住她的手腕。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She stopped.","zh":"她只好站住。然后她用湿润的媚眼打量了他几分钟，急忙道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, having gazed at him for a few moments with an amorous and humid look, she said hurriedly—","zh":"她只好站住。然后她用湿润的媚眼打量了他几分钟，急忙道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ah! do not speak of it again! Where are the horses? Let us go back.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! do not speak of it again!","zh":"“啊！好，别说下去啦…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where are the horses?","zh":"马在什么地方？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let us go back.”","zh":"回去吧。”他做了一个又生气又苦恼的手势。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He made a gesture of anger and annoyance. She repeated:","sentences":[{"en":"He made a gesture of anger and annoyance.","zh":"回去吧。”他做了一个又生气又苦恼的手势。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She repeated:","zh":"她重复道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where are the horses? Where are the horses?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Where are the horses?","zh":"“马在什么地方？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where are the horses?”","zh":"马在什么地方？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then smiling a strange smile, his pupil fixed, his teeth set, he advanced with outstretched arms. She recoiled trembling. She stammered:","sentences":[{"en":"Then smiling a strange smile, his pupil fixed, his teeth set, he advanced with outstretched arms.","zh":"他于是目不转睛，咬紧牙关，透出一种奇怪的微笑，伸开胳膊，逼向她来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She recoiled trembling.","zh":"她一边哆嗦，一边倒退，期期艾艾道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"She stammered:","zh":"她一边哆嗦，一边倒退，期期艾艾道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, you frighten me! You hurt me! Let me go!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, you frighten me!","zh":"“您让我害怕！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You hurt me!","zh":"您让我难过！走吧！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Let me go!”","zh":"您让我难过！走吧！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“If it must be,” he went on, his face changing; and he again became respectful, caressing, timid. She gave him her arm. They went back. He said—","sentences":[{"en":"“If it must be,” he went on, his face changing; and he again became respectful, caressing, timid.","zh":"他改变面貌，回答道：“您一定要走…”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She gave him her arm.","zh":"他立时就又变得敬重、温存、懦怯。她挎住他的胳膊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They went back.","zh":"他们往回走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He said—","zh":"他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What was the matter with you? Why? I do not understand. You were mistaken, no doubt. In my soul you are as a Madonna on a pedestal, in a place lofty, secure, immaculate. But I need you to live! I must have your eyes, your voice, your thought! Be my friend, my sister, my angel!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What was the matter with you?","zh":"“您到底怎么啦？为什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why?","zh":"我不明白。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I do not understand.","zh":"我不明白。","scope":"group"},{"en":"You were mistaken, no doubt.","zh":"想来您是误会了吧？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In my soul you are as a Madonna on a pedestal, in a place lofty, secure, immaculate.","zh":"您在我心里，就像一位圣母娘娘，高高待在底座上，又坚固，又纯洁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But I need you to live!","zh":"不过没有您，我活不下去！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I must have your eyes, your voice, your thought!","zh":"我需要您的眼睛、您的声音、您的思想。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Be my friend, my sister, my angel!”","zh":"做我的朋友、我的妹妹、我的天使吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he put out his arm round her waist. She feebly tried to disengage herself. He supported her thus as they walked along.","sentences":[{"en":"And he put out his arm round her waist.","zh":"他于是伸长胳膊，搂住她的腰肢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She feebly tried to disengage herself.","zh":"她半推半就，试着挣扎出来。他边走，边这样搂着她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He supported her thus as they walked along.","zh":"她半推半就，试着挣扎出来。他边走，边这样搂着她。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But they heard the two horses browsing on the leaves.","sentences":[{"en":"But they heard the two horses browsing on the leaves.","zh":"他们听见两匹马在吃树叶。罗道耳弗道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh! one moment!” said Rodolphe. “Do not let us go! Stay!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh! one moment!” said Rodolphe.","zh":"“再待一会儿！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do not let us go!","zh":"别就走！停下来吧！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Stay!”","zh":"别就走！停下来吧！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He drew her farther on to a small pool where duckweeds made a greenness on the water. Faded water lilies lay motionless between the reeds. At the noise of their steps in the grass, frogs jumped away to hide themselves.","sentences":[{"en":"He drew her farther on to a small pool where duckweeds made a greenness on the water.","zh":"他把她带到更远的地方，兜着一口小水塘转悠。满地浮萍，绿波如茵。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Faded water lilies lay motionless between the reeds.","zh":"残荷安安静静，夹在灯芯草中间。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the noise of their steps in the grass, frogs jumped away to hide themselves.","zh":"他们走在草上，青蛙听见脚步，跳开了躲藏起来。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I am wrong! I am wrong!” she said. “I am mad to listen to you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“I am wrong!","zh":"“我错了，我错了，我不该听您的话。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I am wrong!” she said.","zh":"“我错了，我错了，我不该听您的话。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I am mad to listen to you!”","zh":"“为什么？爱玛！爱玛！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why? Emma! Emma!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why?","zh":"少妇一面倒向他的肩膀，一面慢悠悠道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma!","zh":"少妇一面倒向他的肩膀，一面慢悠悠道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma!”","zh":"“唉！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, Rodolphe!” said the young woman slowly, leaning on his shoulder.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, Rodolphe!” said the young woman slowly, leaning on his shoulder.","zh":"罗道耳弗！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The cloth of her habit caught against the velvet of his coat. She threw back her white neck, swelling with a sigh, and faltering, in tears, with a long shudder and hiding her face, she gave herself up to him—","sentences":[{"en":"The cloth of her habit caught against the velvet of his coat.","zh":"她的衣裙贴紧他的丝绒燕尾服。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She threw back her white neck, swelling with a sigh, and faltering, in tears, with a long shudder and hiding her face, she gave herself up to him—","zh":"她仰起白生生的颈项，颈项由于叹息而胀圆了。她于是软弱无力，满脸眼泪，浑身打颤，将脸藏起，依顺了他。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The shades of night were falling; the horizontal sun passing between the branches dazzled the eyes. Here and there around her, in the leaves or on the ground, trembled luminous patches, as if hummingbirds flying about had scattered their feathers. Silence was everywhere; something sweet seemed to come forth from the trees; she felt her heart, whose beating had begun again, and the blood coursing through her flesh like a stream of milk. Then far away, beyond the wood, on the other hills, she heard a vague prolonged cry, a voice which lingered, and in silence she heard it mingling like music with the last pulsations of her throbbing nerves. Rodolphe, a cigar between his lips, was mending with his penknife one of the two broken bridles.","sentences":[{"en":"The shades of night were falling; the horizontal sun passing between the branches dazzled the eyes.","zh":"天已薄暮，落日穿过树枝，照花她的眼睛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Here and there around her, in the leaves or on the ground, trembled luminous patches, as if hummingbirds flying about had scattered their feathers.","zh":"周围或远或近，有些亮点在树叶当中或者地面晃来晃去，好像蜂鸟飞翔，抖落羽毛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Silence was everywhere; something sweet seemed to come forth from the trees; she felt her heart, whose beating had begun again, and the blood coursing through her flesh like a stream of milk.","zh":"一片幽静，树木像有香气散到外头。她觉得心又开始跳跃，血液仿佛一条奶河，在皮肤底下流动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then far away, beyond the wood, on the other hills, she heard a vague prolonged cry, a voice which lingered, and in silence she heard it mingling like music with the last pulsations of her throbbing nerves.","zh":"她听见一种模糊而悠长的叫喊，一种拉长的声音，从树林外面别的丘陵传出，她静静听来，就像乐曲一样，与她激动的神经的最后震颤交织在一起。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe, a cigar between his lips, was mending with his penknife one of the two broken bridles.","zh":"断了一根缰绳，罗道耳弗噙着雪茄，拿小刀修理。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They returned to Yonville by the same road. On the mud they saw again the traces of their horses side by side, the same thickets, the same stones to the grass; nothing around them seemed changed; and yet for her something had happened more stupendous than if the mountains had moved in their places. Rodolphe now and again bent forward and took her hand to kiss it.","sentences":[{"en":"They returned to Yonville by the same road.","zh":"他们走原路回到永镇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the mud they saw again the traces of their horses side by side, the same thickets, the same stones to the grass; nothing around them seemed changed; and yet for her something had happened more stupendous than if the mountains had moved in their places.","zh":"他们又在泥地看见马的并排蹄印，又看见小树丛和草里的石子。周围什么也没有改变；可是就她来说，却发生了好比大山移位般的大事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe now and again bent forward and took her hand to kiss it.","zh":"罗道耳弗不时斜过身子，举起她的手吻。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was charming on horseback—upright, with her slender waist, her knee bent on the mane of her horse, her face somewhat flushed by the fresh air in the red of the evening.","sentences":[{"en":"She was charming on horseback—upright, with her slender waist, her knee bent on the mane of her horse, her face somewhat flushed by the fresh air in the red of the evening.","zh":"她骑在马上，婀娜多姿！挺直细腰，膝盖齐着马鬣弯下去，晚霞和新鲜空气在脸上薄薄敷了一层颜色。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On entering Yonville she made her horse prance in the road. People looked at her from the windows.","sentences":[{"en":"On entering Yonville she made her horse prance in the road.","zh":"走进永镇，马打着石头地，左右回旋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People looked at her from the windows.","zh":"大家在窗口望她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At dinner her husband thought she looked well, but she pretended not to hear him when he inquired about her ride, and she remained sitting there with her elbow at the side of her plate between the two lighted candles.","sentences":[{"en":"At dinner her husband thought she looked well, but she pretended not to hear him when he inquired about her ride, and she remained sitting there with her elbow at the side of her plate between the two lighted candles.","zh":"晚饭时节，她的丈夫觉得她气色很好，但是问起出游情形，她装出没有听见的模样，胳膊肘拄在盘子一旁，两边一边点着一支蜡烛。他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Emma!” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Emma!” he said.","zh":"“爱玛！”“什么事？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“爱玛！”“什么事？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Well, I spent the afternoon at Monsieur Alexandre’s. He has an old cob, still very fine, only a little broken-kneed, and that could be bought; I am sure, for a hundred crowns.” He added, “And thinking it might please you, I have bespoken it—bought it. Have I done right? Do tell me?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I spent the afternoon at Monsieur Alexandre’s.","zh":"“喏，今天下午，我是在亚历山大先生家里过的；他有一匹老母马，看上去还很英挺，只有膝盖磕掉一小块皮，不长毛，我拿稳了，出一百埃居，准能买下…","scope":"group"},{"en":"He has an old cob, still very fine, only a little broken-kneed, and that could be bought; I am sure, for a hundred crowns.”","zh":"“喏，今天下午，我是在亚历山大先生家里过的；他有一匹老母马，看上去还很英挺，只有膝盖磕掉一小块皮，不长毛，我拿稳了，出一百埃居，准能买下…","scope":"group"},{"en":"He added, “And thinking it might please you, I have bespoken it—bought it.","zh":"“喏，今天下午，我是在亚历山大先生家里过的；他有一匹老母马，看上去还很英挺，只有膝盖磕掉一小块皮，不长毛，我拿稳了，出一百埃居，准能买下…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Have I done right?","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do tell me?”","zh":"他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She nodded her head in assent; then a quarter of an hour later—","sentences":[{"en":"She nodded her head in assent; then a quarter of an hour later—","zh":"“我一想，你会喜欢的，我就留下它…把它买过来了…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are you going out to-night?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you going out to-night?” she asked.","zh":"我办得好吧？你说呢。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes. Why?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.","zh":"她点了点头，表示赞成，过了一刻钟，她问道：“你晚晌出去吗？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Why?”","zh":"她点了点头，表示赞成，过了一刻钟，她问道：“你晚晌出去吗？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, nothing, nothing, my dear!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, nothing, nothing, my dear!”","zh":"“出去。你问这干什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And as soon as she had got rid of Charles she went and shut herself up in her room.","sentences":[{"en":"And as soon as she had got rid of Charles she went and shut herself up in her room.","zh":"“啊！好人，没有什么，没有什么。”她打发掉查理，上楼来到卧室，把门关了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At first she felt stunned; she saw the trees, the paths, the ditches, Rodolphe, and she again felt the pressure of his arm, while the leaves rustled and the reeds whistled.","sentences":[{"en":"At first she felt stunned; she saw the trees, the paths, the ditches, Rodolphe, and she again felt the pressure of his arm, while the leaves rustled and the reeds whistled.","zh":"开头就像头晕眼花了一样，她又看见树木、小道、沟渠、罗道耳弗，照样感到他的搂抱，听见树叶摇摆、灯心草呼呼吹动。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But when she saw herself in the glass she wondered at her face. Never had her eyes been so large, so black, of so profound a depth. Something subtle about her being transfigured her. She repeated, “I have a lover! a lover!” delighting at the idea as if a second puberty had come to her. So at last she was to know those joys of love, that fever of happiness of which she had despaired! She was entering upon marvels where all would be passion, ecstasy, delirium. An azure infinity encompassed her, the heights of sentiment sparkled under her thought, and ordinary existence appeared only afar off, down below in the shade, through the interspaces of these heights.","sentences":[{"en":"But when she saw herself in the glass she wondered at her face.","zh":"但是一照镜子，她惊异起来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Never had her eyes been so large, so black, of so profound a depth.","zh":"她从来没有见过她的眼睛这样大，这样黑，这样深。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Something subtle about her being transfigured her.","zh":"她像服过什么仙方一样，人变美了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She repeated, “I have a lover! a lover!” delighting at the idea as if a second puberty had come to her.","zh":"她三番两次自言自语道：“我有一个情人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So at last she was to know those joys of love, that fever of happiness of which she had despaired!","zh":"一个情人！”她一想到这上头，就心花怒放，好像刹那间又返老还童了一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was entering upon marvels where all would be passion, ecstasy, delirium.","zh":"她想不到的那种神仙欢愉、那种风月乐趣，终于就要到手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"An azure infinity encompassed her, the heights of sentiment sparkled under her thought, and ordinary existence appeared only afar off, down below in the shade, through the interspaces of these heights.","zh":"她走进一个只有热情、销魂、酩酊的神奇世界，周围是一望无涯的碧空，感情的极峰在心头闪闪发光，而日常生活只在遥远、低洼、阴暗的山隙出现。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she recalled the heroines of the books that she had read, and the lyric legion of these adulterous women began to sing in her memory with the voice of sisters that charmed her. She became herself, as it were, an actual part of these imaginings, and realised the love-dream of her youth as she saw herself in this type of amorous women whom she had so envied. Besides, Emma felt a satisfaction of revenge. Had she not suffered enough? But now she triumphed, and the love so long pent up burst forth in full joyous bubblings. She tasted it without remorse, without anxiety, without trouble.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she recalled the heroines of the books that she had read, and the lyric legion of these adulterous women began to sing in her memory with the voice of sisters that charmed her.","zh":"她于是想起她读过的书中的女主人公，这些淫妇多感善歌，开始成群结队，在她的记忆之中咏唱，意气相投，使她陶醉，就像自己变成这些幻象的真正一部分一样，实现了少女时期的长梦，从前神往的多情女典型，如今她也成为其中的一个。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She became herself, as it were, an actual part of these imaginings, and realised the love-dream of her youth as she saw herself in this type of amorous women whom she had so envied.","zh":"她于是想起她读过的书中的女主人公，这些淫妇多感善歌，开始成群结队，在她的记忆之中咏唱，意气相投，使她陶醉，就像自己变成这些幻象的真正一部分一样，实现了少女时期的长梦，从前神往的多情女典型，如今她也成为其中的一个。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Besides, Emma felt a satisfaction of revenge.","zh":"再说，爱玛还感觉到报复的满足。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Had she not suffered enough?","zh":"难道她没有受够折磨！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But now she triumphed, and the love so long pent up burst forth in full joyous bubblings.","zh":"可是现在，她胜利了。久经压制的感情，一涌而出，欢跃沸腾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She tasted it without remorse, without anxiety, without trouble.","zh":"她领略到了爱情，不后悔，不担忧，不心乱。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The day following passed with a new sweetness. They made vows to one another. She told him of her sorrows. Rodolphe interrupted her with kisses; and she looking at him through half-closed eyes, asked him to call her again by her name—to say that he loved her. They were in the forest, as yesterday, in the shed of some woodenshoe maker. The walls were of straw, and the roof so low they had to stoop. They were seated side by side on a bed of dry leaves.","sentences":[{"en":"The day following passed with a new sweetness.","zh":"第二天，整天沉入新的欢乐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They made vows to one another.","zh":"他们海誓山盟。她对他说起她的种种哀愁。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She told him of her sorrows.","zh":"他们海誓山盟。她对他说起她的种种哀愁。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Rodolphe interrupted her with kisses; and she looking at him through half-closed eyes, asked him to call her again by her name—to say that he loved her.","zh":"罗道耳弗用吻打断她；她闭住一半眼皮，目不转睛，要他再叫一遍她的名字，再说一遍他爱她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were in the forest, as yesterday, in the shed of some woodenshoe maker.","zh":"他们像昨天一样，走进森林，待在一个做木头套鞋的人的小屋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The walls were of straw, and the roof so low they had to stoop.","zh":"墙是草堆成的，屋顶低极了，他们不得不弯下腰来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were seated side by side on a bed of dry leaves.","zh":"他们相倚相偎，坐在一张干树叶床上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"From that day forth they wrote to one another regularly every evening. Emma placed her letter at the end of the garden, by the river, in a fissure of the wall. Rodolphe came to fetch it, and put another there, that she always found fault with as too short.","sentences":[{"en":"From that day forth they wrote to one another regularly every evening.","zh":"从这一天起，他们没有例外，天天晚晌写信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma placed her letter at the end of the garden, by the river, in a fissure of the wall.","zh":"爱玛来到花园尽头，把信放在河边墙缝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe came to fetch it, and put another there, that she always found fault with as too short.","zh":"罗道耳弗拿到信，另放一封进去。她总嫌他的信太短。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One morning, when Charles had gone out before day break, she was seized with the fancy to see Rodolphe at once. She would go quickly to La Huchette, stay there an hour, and be back again at Yonville while everyone was still asleep. This idea made her pant with desire, and she soon found herself in the middle of the field, walking with rapid steps, without looking behind her.","sentences":[{"en":"One morning, when Charles had gone out before day break, she was seized with the fancy to see Rodolphe at once.","zh":"有一天早晨，不等天亮，查理就出门了，她忽然异想天开，起了立刻看见罗道耳弗的念头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would go quickly to La Huchette, stay there an hour, and be back again at Yonville while everyone was still asleep.","zh":"她可以赶到于歇特，待一小时，回到永镇，人人还在睡梦之中。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This idea made her pant with desire, and she soon found herself in the middle of the field, walking with rapid steps, without looking behind her.","zh":"她这样一想，心急欲炽，气也短促了。没有多久，她就到了草原，头也不回，只是快步趱行。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Day was just breaking. Emma from afar recognised her lover’s house. Its two dove-tailed weathercocks stood out black against the pale dawn.","sentences":[{"en":"Day was just breaking.","zh":"天方破晓，爱玛远远望到情人的住宅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma from afar recognised her lover’s house.","zh":"天方破晓，爱玛远远望到情人的住宅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Its two dove-tailed weathercocks stood out black against the pale dawn.","zh":"两只燕尾风标，迎着白蒙蒙的曙光，显得黑乎乎的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Beyond the farmyard there was a detached building that she thought must be the château. She entered—it was if the doors at her approach had opened wide of their own accord. A large straight staircase led up to the corridor. Emma raised the latch of a door, and suddenly at the end of the room she saw a man sleeping. It was Rodolphe. She uttered a cry.","sentences":[{"en":"Beyond the farmyard there was a detached building that she thought must be the château.","zh":"穿过院落，便是一所房子，想必就是庄邸。她走进去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She entered—it was if the doors at her approach had opened wide of their own accord.","zh":"墙壁一见她来，像是自动闪到一旁一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A large straight staircase led up to the corridor.","zh":"一座大楼梯笔直通到过道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma raised the latch of a door, and suddenly at the end of the room she saw a man sleeping.","zh":"爱玛挑起门闩，骤然望见一个男人，在屋子尽里睡觉。原来就是罗道耳弗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Rodolphe.","zh":"她叫了起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She uttered a cry.","zh":"他说了几遍：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You here? You here?” he repeated. “How did you manage to come? Ah! your dress is damp.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You here?","zh":"“是你！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You here?” he repeated.","zh":"是你！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“How did you manage to come?","zh":"你怎么来的？啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! your dress is damp.”","zh":"你的袍子也湿啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I love you,” she answered, throwing her arms about his neck.","sentences":[{"en":"“I love you,” she answered, throwing her arms about his neck.","zh":"她拿胳膊搂住他的颈项，回答道：“我爱你！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This first piece of daring successful, now every time Charles went out early Emma dressed quickly and slipped on tiptoe down the steps that led to the waterside.","sentences":[{"en":"This first piece of daring successful, now every time Charles went out early Emma dressed quickly and slipped on tiptoe down the steps that led to the waterside.","zh":"这大胆的举动，头一次成功，以后每逢查理早出，爱玛就连忙穿好衣服，蹑着脚步，走下通到水边的台阶。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But when the plank for the cows was taken up, she had to go by the walls alongside of the river; the bank was slippery; in order not to fall she caught hold of the tufts of faded wallflowers. Then she went across ploughed fields, in which she sank, stumbling; and clogging her thin shoes. Her scarf, knotted round her head, fluttered to the wind in the meadows. She was afraid of the oxen; she began to run; she arrived out of breath, with rosy cheeks, and breathing out from her whole person a fresh perfume of sap, of verdure, of the open air. At this hour Rodolphe still slept. It was like a spring morning coming into his room.","sentences":[{"en":"But when the plank for the cows was taken up, she had to go by the walls alongside of the river; the bank was slippery; in order not to fall she caught hold of the tufts of faded wallflowers.","zh":"但是遇到牛走的便桥抽掉，就得沿着河旁的墙走，堤是滑的，她抓住一把残了的桂竹香，生怕跌倒。她随后穿越犁过的田，陷在里头，绊了脚，好不容易才拔出她的小靴。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she went across ploughed fields, in which she sank, stumbling; and clogging her thin shoes.","zh":"但是遇到牛走的便桥抽掉，就得沿着河旁的墙走，堤是滑的，她抓住一把残了的桂竹香，生怕跌倒。她随后穿越犁过的田，陷在里头，绊了脚，好不容易才拔出她的小靴。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her scarf, knotted round her head, fluttered to the wind in the meadows.","zh":"风吹动她的包头帕子，在牧场翻来卷去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was afraid of the oxen; she began to run; she arrived out of breath, with rosy cheeks, and breathing out from her whole person a fresh perfume of sap, of verdure, of the open air.","zh":"遇到了牛，她又害怕，提脚就跑，跑到了，直喘气，脸庞通红，浑身发出一种树液、青草和新鲜空气的清香气味。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At this hour Rodolphe still slept.","zh":"罗道耳弗这期间还在睡觉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was like a spring morning coming into his room.","zh":"她像春天的早晨一样来到他的房间。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The yellow curtains along the windows let a heavy, whitish light enter softly. Emma felt about, opening and closing her eyes, while the drops of dew hanging from her hair formed, as it were, a topaz aureole around her face. Rodolphe, laughing, drew her to him, and pressed her to his breast.","sentences":[{"en":"The yellow curtains along the windows let a heavy, whitish light enter softly.","zh":"一道沉重的金光悄悄透过沿窗的黄幔。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma felt about, opening and closing her eyes, while the drops of dew hanging from her hair formed, as it were, a topaz aureole around her face.","zh":"爱玛眨巴眼睛，边走边摸索，露珠挂在头发上，一圈黄玉圆光似的，环绕脸蛋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe, laughing, drew her to him, and pressed her to his breast.","zh":"罗道耳弗一面笑，一面把她拉到身边，搂在怀里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she examined the apartment, opened the drawers of the tables, combed her hair with his comb, and looked at herself in his shaving-glass. Often she even put between her teeth the big pipe that lay on the table by the bed, amongst lemons and pieces of sugar near a bottle of water.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she examined the apartment, opened the drawers of the tables, combed her hair with his comb, and looked at herself in his shaving-glass.","zh":"过后，她就检查房间，打开抽屉，用他的梳子梳头，用他刮脸的镜子刮脸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often she even put between her teeth the big pipe that lay on the table by the bed, amongst lemons and pieces of sugar near a bottle of water.","zh":"床几上放着柠檬和方糖，靠近水瓶，还有一支大烟斗，她经常叼在嘴里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It took them a good quarter of an hour to say goodbye. Then Emma cried. She would have wished never to leave Rodolphe. Something stronger than herself forced her to him; so much so, that one day, seeing her come unexpectedly, he frowned as one put out.","sentences":[{"en":"It took them a good quarter of an hour to say goodbye.","zh":"他们分手足足需要一刻钟。爱玛哭着，希望永不离开罗道耳弗。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then Emma cried.","zh":"他们分手足足需要一刻钟。爱玛哭着，希望永不离开罗道耳弗。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She would have wished never to leave Rodolphe.","zh":"有什么东西把她朝他推过来，一点由不得她，连他也嫌欠妥。有一天，他见她不期而至，皱起眉头，模样像是很不以为然。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Something stronger than herself forced her to him; so much so, that one day, seeing her come unexpectedly, he frowned as one put out.","zh":"有什么东西把她朝他推过来，一点由不得她，连他也嫌欠妥。有一天，他见她不期而至，皱起眉头，模样像是很不以为然。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What is the matter with you?” she said. “Are you ill? Tell me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What is the matter with you?” she said.","zh":"她道：“你怎么啦？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Are you ill?","zh":"难受吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tell me!”","zh":"说给我听！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last he declared with a serious air that her visits were becoming imprudent—that she was compromising herself.","sentences":[{"en":"At last he declared with a serious air that her visits were becoming imprudent—that she was compromising herself.","zh":"他最后神色严肃，对她说：她来看他，粗心大意，会给自己惹乱子的。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-10","part":2,"n":10,"title":"Part II · Chapter 10","titleZh":"中卷 · 10","paragraphs":[{"en":"Gradually Rodolphe’s fears took possession of her. At first, love had intoxicated her; and she had thought of nothing beyond. But now that he was indispensable to her life, she feared to lose anything of this, or even that it should be disturbed. When she came back from his house she looked all about her, anxiously watching every form that passed in the horizon, and every village window from which she could be seen. She listened for steps, cries, the noise of the ploughs, and she stopped short, white, and trembling more than the aspen leaves swaying overhead.","sentences":[{"en":"Gradually Rodolphe’s fears took possession of her.","zh":"她也像罗道耳弗一样，渐渐有了畏惧心理。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At first, love had intoxicated her; and she had thought of nothing beyond.","zh":"她起初什么也不放在心上，一味陶醉在爱情之中。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But now that he was indispensable to her life, she feared to lose anything of this, or even that it should be disturbed.","zh":"可是如今她的生命少不了它，她生怕失落一星半点，或者受到意外干扰。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When she came back from his house she looked all about her, anxiously watching every form that passed in the horizon, and every village window from which she could be seen.","zh":"所以她走出他的庄园，东张西望，忐忑不安，天边走过的每一个身影、镇子里可能望见她的每一个天窗，都要看个明白，脚步、叫喊、犁的响声，也要听一个分晓；她站住不动，头上摇来摇去的白杨叶子，也不及她的脸色白，也不像她的身子抖得那么厉害。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She listened for steps, cries, the noise of the ploughs, and she stopped short, white, and trembling more than the aspen leaves swaying overhead.","zh":"所以她走出他的庄园，东张西望，忐忑不安，天边走过的每一个身影、镇子里可能望见她的每一个天窗，都要看个明白，脚步、叫喊、犁的响声，也要听一个分晓；她站住不动，头上摇来摇去的白杨叶子，也不及她的脸色白，也不像她的身子抖得那么厉害。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"One morning as she was thus returning, she suddenly thought she saw the long barrel of a carbine that seemed to be aimed at her. It stuck out sideways from the end of a small tub half-buried in the grass on the edge of a ditch. Emma, half-fainting with terror, nevertheless walked on, and a man stepped out of the tub like a Jack-in-the-box. He had gaiters buckled up to the knees, his cap pulled down over his eyes, trembling lips, and a red nose. It was Captain Binet lying in ambush for wild ducks.","sentences":[{"en":"One morning as she was thus returning, she suddenly thought she saw the long barrel of a carbine that seemed to be aimed at her.","zh":"有一天早晨，她正提心吊胆，转回家去，眼睛一晃，忽然看见一管猎枪似乎瞄准了她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It stuck out sideways from the end of a small tub half-buried in the grass on the edge of a ditch.","zh":"枪筒长长的，扯斜露在一只小木桶的外沿。小木桶有一半埋在沟边草里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma, half-fainting with terror, nevertheless walked on, and a man stepped out of the tub like a Jack-in-the-box.","zh":"爱玛吓得魂飞魄散。正待朝前走去，就见一个男人爬出桶来，活像盒子打开，弹簧人往上一跳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had gaiters buckled up to the knees, his cap pulled down over his eyes, trembling lips, and a red nose.","zh":"皮护腿裹到膝盖，便帽盖住眼睛，鼻子通红，嘴唇颤抖：原来是毕耐队长埋伏好了等野鸭打。他嚷嚷道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was Captain Binet lying in ambush for wild ducks.","zh":"皮护腿裹到膝盖，便帽盖住眼睛，鼻子通红，嘴唇颤抖：原来是毕耐队长埋伏好了等野鸭打。他嚷嚷道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You ought to have called out long ago!” he exclaimed; “When one sees a gun, one should always give warning.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You ought to have called out long ago!” he exclaimed; “When one sees a gun, one should always give warning.”","zh":"“您老远就该说话！望见枪，总得嚷一声才好。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The tax-collector was thus trying to hide the fright he had had, for a prefectorial order having prohibited duckhunting except in boats, Monsieur Binet, despite his respect for the laws, was infringing them, and so he every moment expected to see the rural guard turn up. But this anxiety whetted his pleasure, and, all alone in his tub, he congratulated himself on his luck and on his cuteness. At sight of Emma he seemed relieved from a great weight, and at once entered upon a conversation.","sentences":[{"en":"The tax-collector was thus trying to hide the fright he had had, for a prefectorial order having prohibited duckhunting except in boats, Monsieur Binet, despite his respect for the laws, was infringing them, and so he every moment expected to see the rural guard turn up.","zh":"税务员说这话，打算掩盖方才的恐惧。因为州长有令，除去船上许可猎鸭以外，禁止在别处猎鸭，毕耐先生虽然守法，在这上头，偏巧违禁。所以他心中有鬼，时时刻刻，以为听见猎警过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But this anxiety whetted his pleasure, and, all alone in his tub, he congratulated himself on his luck and on his cuteness.","zh":"但是这种杌陧心情刺激他的乐趣，一个人缩在木桶，妙法在握，自以为得计。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At sight of Emma he seemed relieved from a great weight, and at once entered upon a conversation.","zh":"他看见爱玛，一块石头落地，显得松快了，跟着就闲谈起来：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It isn’t warm; it’s nipping.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It isn’t warm; it’s nipping.”","zh":"“天不暖和，凉飕飕的！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma answered nothing. He went on—","sentences":[{"en":"Emma answered nothing.","zh":"爱玛一句话也不回答。他讲下去：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He went on—","zh":"爱玛一句话也不回答。他讲下去：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“And you’re out so early?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And you’re out so early?”","zh":"“您出门真早啊？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes,” she said stammering; “I am just coming from the nurse where my child is.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” she said stammering; “I am just coming from the nurse where my child is.”","zh":"她结结巴巴道：“是的；小孩在奶妈家，我才看她来着。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! very good! very good! For myself, I am here, just as you see me, since break of day; but the weather is so muggy, that unless one had the bird at the mouth of the gun—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! very good! very good!","zh":"“啊！很好！很好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For myself, I am here, just as you see me, since break of day; but the weather is so muggy, that unless one had the bird at the mouth of the gun—”","zh":"拿我来说，您看见的，天刚一亮，就到了这儿。不过天气死沉沉的，除非飞到枪口…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Good evening, Monsieur Binet,” she interrupted him, turning on her heel.","sentences":[{"en":"“Good evening, Monsieur Binet,” she interrupted him, turning on her heel.","zh":"她转过脚跟，打断他道：“毕耐先生，再会。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Your servant, madame,” he replied drily; and he went back into his tub.","sentences":[{"en":"“Your servant, madame,” he replied drily; and he went back into his tub.","zh":"他冷冷回了一句：“请便，太太。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma regretted having left the tax-collector so abruptly. No doubt he would form unfavourable conjectures. The story about the nurse was the worst possible excuse, everyone at Yonville knowing that the little Bovary had been at home with her parents for a year. Besides, no one was living in this direction; this path led only to La Huchette. Binet, then, would guess whence she came, and he would not keep silence; he would talk, that was certain. She remained until evening racking her brain with every conceivable lying project, and had constantly before her eyes that imbecile with the game-bag.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma regretted having left the tax-collector so abruptly.","zh":"接着他又钻回木桶去了。爱玛后悔这样干巴巴就离开了税务员。","scope":"group"},{"en":"No doubt he would form unfavourable conjectures.","zh":"接着他又钻回木桶去了。爱玛后悔这样干巴巴就离开了税务员。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The story about the nurse was the worst possible excuse, everyone at Yonville knowing that the little Bovary had been at home with her parents for a year.","zh":"不用说，他要往坏事上想的。永镇上人人晓得，包法利家小女孩子，接回家来，已经一年了，去看奶妈的说法，糟不可言。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, no one was living in this direction; this path led only to La Huchette.","zh":"再说，周围没有人家，这条小道只通于歇特；这样一来，毕耐猜出她从什么地方回来，不会秘而不宣的；逢人就讲，是必然的了！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Binet, then, would guess whence she came, and he would not keep silence; he would talk, that was certain.","zh":"再说，周围没有人家，这条小道只通于歇特；这样一来，毕耐猜出她从什么地方回来，不会秘而不宣的；逢人就讲，是必然的了！","scope":"group"},{"en":"She remained until evening racking her brain with every conceivable lying project, and had constantly before her eyes that imbecile with the game-bag.","zh":"直到天黑，她还在煞费苦心，思前想后，编排种种谎话，可是这挂猎囊的蠢人，总在眼前晃来晃去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles after dinner, seeing her gloomy, proposed, by way of distraction, to take her to the chemist’s, and the first person she caught sight of in the shop was the taxcollector again. He was standing in front of the counter, lit up by the gleams of the red bottle, and was saying—","sentences":[{"en":"Charles after dinner, seeing her gloomy, proposed, by way of distraction, to take her to the chemist’s, and the first person she caught sight of in the shop was the taxcollector again.","zh":"查理用罢晚饭，见她愁眉不展，提议带她到药剂师家消遣消遣。她在药房遇见的头一个人，偏偏又是税务员！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was standing in front of the counter, lit up by the gleams of the red bottle, and was saying—","zh":"他站在柜台前面，红药瓶的亮光照着，他说：“请您给我半两矾。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Please give me half an ounce of vitriol.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Please give me half an ounce of vitriol.”","zh":"药剂师喊道：“朱斯丹，拿硫酸来。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Justin,” cried the druggist, “bring us the sulphuric acid.” Then to Emma, who was going up to Madame Homais’ room, “No, stay here; it isn’t worth while going up; she is just coming down. Warm yourself at the stove in the meantime. Excuse me. Good-day, doctor,” (for the chemist much enjoyed pronouncing the word “doctor,” as if addressing another by it reflected on himself some of the grandeur that he found in it). “Now, take care not to upset the mortars! You’d better fetch some chairs from the little room; you know very well that the arm-chairs are not to be taken out of the drawing-room.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Justin,” cried the druggist, “bring us the sulphuric acid.”","zh":"爱玛想上楼去看郝麦夫人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then to Emma, who was going up to Madame Homais’ room, “No, stay here; it isn’t worth while going up; she is just coming down.","zh":"他拦住道：“不必了，用不着，她就下来，还是在底下坐吧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Warm yourself at the stove in the meantime.","zh":"您在炉子那边烤烤火，等她下来…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Excuse me.","zh":"对不住…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good-day, doctor,” (for the chemist much enjoyed pronouncing the word “doctor,” as if addressing another by it reflected on himself some of the grandeur that he found in it).","zh":"好啊，博士（因为药剂师非常爱说博士这两个字，好像这样称呼另一个人，自己也就跟着体面了似的）…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Now, take care not to upset the mortars!","zh":"当心打翻那些臼！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You’d better fetch some chairs from the little room; you know very well that the arm-chairs are not to be taken out of the drawing-room.”","zh":"到小房间搬些椅子来；客厅的扶手椅不许乱动，你不是不知道。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And to put his arm-chair back in its place he was darting away from the counter, when Binet asked him for half an ounce of sugar acid.","sentences":[{"en":"And to put his arm-chair back in its place he was darting away from the counter, when Binet asked him for half an ounce of sugar acid.","zh":"药剂师正要跑出柜台，放好他的扶手椅，就见毕耐问他要半两糖酸。药剂师鄙夷地说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sugar acid!” said the chemist contemptuously, “don’t know it; I’m ignorant of it! But perhaps you want oxalic acid. It is oxalic acid, isn’t it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sugar acid!” said the chemist contemptuously, “don’t know it; I’m ignorant of it!","zh":"“糖酸？我不晓得，没听说过！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But perhaps you want oxalic acid.","zh":"您要的也许是草酸吧？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is oxalic acid, isn’t it?”","zh":"是草，不是糖，对不对？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Binet explained that he wanted a corrosive to make himself some copperwater with which to remove rust from his hunting things.","sentences":[{"en":"Binet explained that he wanted a corrosive to make himself some copperwater with which to remove rust from his hunting things.","zh":"毕耐解释，他要一种腐蚀剂，配成一种搽铜药水，去掉各种猎具的锈。爱玛听了这话，直打哆嗦。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma shuddered. The chemist began saying—","sentences":[{"en":"Emma shuddered.","zh":"毕耐解释，他要一种腐蚀剂，配成一种搽铜药水，去掉各种猎具的锈。爱玛听了这话，直打哆嗦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The chemist began saying—","zh":"药剂师道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Indeed the weather is not propitious on account of the damp.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Indeed the weather is not propitious on account of the damp.”","zh":"“的确也是，天湿，不相宜。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Nevertheless,” replied the tax-collector, with a sly look, “there are people who like it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nevertheless,” replied the tax-collector, with a sly look, “there are people who like it.”","zh":"税务员透出狡黠的神色，回答道：“不过有人就不在乎。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was stifling.","sentences":[{"en":"She was stifling.","zh":"她连气也不敢出。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And give me—”","sentences":[{"en":"“And give me—”","zh":"“再给我…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Will he never go?” thought she.","sentences":[{"en":"“Will he never go?” thought she.","zh":"她想：他就永远不走！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Half an ounce of resin and turpentine, four ounces of yellow wax, and three half ounces of animal charcoal, if you please, to clean the varnished leather of my togs.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Half an ounce of resin and turpentine, four ounces of yellow wax, and three half ounces of animal charcoal, if you please, to clean the varnished leather of my togs.”","zh":"“半两松香和树胶，四两黄蜡，再给我一两半骨炭，搽我的装备上的漆皮用。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The druggist was beginning to cut the wax when Madame Homais appeared, Irma in her arms, Napoleon by her side, and Athalie following. She sat down on the velvet seat by the window, and the lad squatted down on a footstool, while his eldest sister hovered round the jujube box near her papa. The latter was filling funnels and corking phials, sticking on labels, making up parcels. Around him all were silent; only from time to time, were heard the weights jingling in the balance, and a few low words from the chemist giving directions to his pupil.","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist was beginning to cut the wax when Madame Homais appeared, Irma in her arms, Napoleon by her side, and Athalie following.","zh":"药剂师正在切蜡，郝麦太太出现了，怀里抱着伊尔玛，旁边走着拿破仑，后头跟着阿塔莉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She sat down on the velvet seat by the window, and the lad squatted down on a footstool, while his eldest sister hovered round the jujube box near her papa.","zh":"她过去坐到窗边丝绒长凳上，男孩子蹲到一张凳子上，大姊兜着她的小爸爸旁边的枣匣转悠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The latter was filling funnels and corking phials, sticking on labels, making up parcels.","zh":"后者灌漏斗，封瓶口，贴标签，打小包。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Around him all were silent; only from time to time, were heard the weights jingling in the balance, and a few low words from the chemist giving directions to his pupil.","zh":"周围鸦雀无声，仅仅不时听见天平的砝码响，还有药剂师吩咐他的学徒，偶尔唧咕几句。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And how’s the little woman?” suddenly asked Madame Homais.","sentences":[{"en":"“And how’s the little woman?” suddenly asked Madame Homais.","zh":"郝麦太太忽然问道：“您的小宝宝好吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Silence!” exclaimed her husband, who was writing down some figures in his waste-book.","sentences":[{"en":"“Silence!” exclaimed her husband, who was writing down some figures in his waste-book.","zh":"她的丈夫正在流水簿上写账，喊道：“别做声！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why didn’t you bring her?” she went on in a low voice.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why didn’t you bring her?” she went on in a low voice.","zh":"她低声又道：“您怎么不带她来呀？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Hush! hush!” said Emma, pointing with her finger to the druggist.","sentences":[{"en":"“Hush! hush!” said Emma, pointing with her finger to the druggist.","zh":"爱玛指着药剂师道：“嘘！嘘！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Binet, quite absorbed in looking over his bill, had probably heard nothing. At last he went out. Then Emma, relieved, uttered a deep sigh.","sentences":[{"en":"But Binet, quite absorbed in looking over his bill, had probably heard nothing.","zh":"不过毕耐一心在看账，大概什么也没有听见。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last he went out.","zh":"他终于出去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Emma, relieved, uttered a deep sigh.","zh":"爱玛如释重负，出了一口长气。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How hard you are breathing!” said Madame Homais.","sentences":[{"en":"“How hard you are breathing!” said Madame Homais.","zh":"郝麦夫人道：“您出气出得好粗！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, you see, it’s rather warm,” she replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, you see, it’s rather warm,” she replied.","zh":"她回答道：“啊！因为天热呀。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"So the next day they talked over how to arrange their rendezvous. Emma wanted to bribe her servant with a present, but it would be better to find some safe house at Yonville. Rodolphe promised to look for one.","sentences":[{"en":"So the next day they talked over how to arrange their rendezvous.","zh":"这样一来，他们的幽会地点，第二天只好另作打算。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma wanted to bribe her servant with a present, but it would be better to find some safe house at Yonville.","zh":"爱玛想送一件礼物，把女用人收买过来；不过顶好还是在永镇找一所稳便的房子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe promised to look for one.","zh":"罗道耳弗答应去找。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"All through the winter, three or four times a week, in the dead of night he came to the garden. Emma had on purpose taken away the key of the gate, which Charles thought lost.","sentences":[{"en":"All through the winter, three or four times a week, in the dead of night he came to the garden.","zh":"一整冬天，每星期有三四回，他趁黑夜来到花园。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma had on purpose taken away the key of the gate, which Charles thought lost.","zh":"爱玛故意拿掉栅栏门的钥匙，查理还当丢了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To call her, Rodolphe threw a sprinkle of sand at the shutters. She jumped up with a start; but sometimes he had to wait, for Charles had a mania for chatting by the fireside, and he would not stop. She was wild with impatience; if her eyes could have done it, she would have hurled him out at the window. At last she would begin to undress, then take up a book, and go on reading very quietly as if the book amused her. But Charles, who was in bed, called to her to come too.","sentences":[{"en":"To call her, Rodolphe threw a sprinkle of sand at the shutters.","zh":"为通知她，罗道耳弗抓起一把沙子扔到百叶窗上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She jumped up with a start; but sometimes he had to wait, for Charles had a mania for chatting by the fireside, and he would not stop.","zh":"她跳下床；不过有时候，她必须等待，因为查理喜欢围炉闲谈，谈起来就没完没了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was wild with impatience; if her eyes could have done it, she would have hurled him out at the window.","zh":"她急死了：假如她的眼睛办得到的话，一定会让他从窗户跳进来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last she would begin to undress, then take up a book, and go on reading very quietly as if the book amused her.","zh":"她最后开始卸妆，接着拿起一本书，心平气和，安安静静读下去，好像津津有味一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Charles, who was in bed, called to her to come too.","zh":"但是查理躺在床上，喊她睡觉。他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come, now, Emma,” he said, “it is time.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, now, Emma,” he said, “it is time.”","zh":"“来呀，爱玛，是时候啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, I am coming,” she answered.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, I am coming,” she answered.","zh":"她回答道：“是啊，就来啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, as the candles dazzled him; he turned to the wall and fell asleep. She escaped, smiling, palpitating, undressed. Rodolphe had a large cloak; he wrapped her in it, and putting his arm round her waist, he drew her without a word to the end of the garden.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, as the candles dazzled him; he turned to the wall and fell asleep.","zh":"不过蜡烛耀眼，他转向墙壁睡着了。她屏住呼吸，微笑着，心跳着，不穿衣服，溜了出去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She escaped, smiling, palpitating, undressed.","zh":"不过蜡烛耀眼，他转向墙壁睡着了。她屏住呼吸，微笑着，心跳着，不穿衣服，溜了出去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Rodolphe had a large cloak; he wrapped her in it, and putting his arm round her waist, he drew her without a word to the end of the garden.","zh":"罗道耳弗披一件大斗篷，上下裹好了她，然后胳膊搂住她的腰，不言不语，把她带到花园深处。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was in the arbour, on the same seat of old sticks where formerly Léon had looked at her so amorously on the summer evenings. She never thought of him now.","sentences":[{"en":"It was in the arbour, on the same seat of old sticks where formerly Léon had looked at her so amorously on the summer evenings.","zh":"他们来到花棚底下，坐在那张烂木条长凳上，从前夏天黄昏，赖昂就在这里，情意绵绵地望着她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She never thought of him now.","zh":"她现在想不到他了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The stars shone through the leafless jasmine branches. Behind them they heard the river flowing, and now and again on the bank the rustling of the dry reeds. Masses of shadow here and there loomed out in the darkness, and sometimes, vibrating with one movement, they rose up and swayed like immense black waves pressing forward to engulf them. The cold of the nights made them clasp closer; the sighs of their lips seemed to them deeper; their eyes that they could hardly see, larger; and in the midst of the silence low words were spoken that fell on their souls sonorous, crystalline, and that reverberated in multiplied vibrations.","sentences":[{"en":"The stars shone through the leafless jasmine branches.","zh":"星光闪烁，映照素馨的枯枝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Behind them they heard the river flowing, and now and again on the bank the rustling of the dry reeds.","zh":"他们听见背后河水潺潺，堤上的枯苇不时簌簌作响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Masses of shadow here and there loomed out in the darkness, and sometimes, vibrating with one movement, they rose up and swayed like immense black waves pressing forward to engulf them.","zh":"黑暗中影影绰绰，东鼓一堆，西鼓一堆，有时候不约而同，摇曳披拂，忽而竖直，忽而倾斜，仿佛巨大的黑浪，翻滚向前，要淹没他们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The cold of the nights made them clasp closer; the sighs of their lips seemed to them deeper; their eyes that they could hardly see, larger; and in the midst of the silence low words were spoken that fell on their souls sonorous, crystalline, and that reverberated in multiplied vibrations.","zh":"夜晚寒冷，他们越发搂紧，叹起气来，也像更响了，眼睛隐约可辨，彼此觉得似乎更大了。万籁无声，有些话低低说出，落在心头，水晶声音似的响亮，上下回旋，震颤不止。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When the night was rainy, they took refuge in the consulting-room between the cart-shed and the stable. She lighted one of the kitchen candles that she had hidden behind the books. Rodolphe settled down there as if at home. The sight of the library, of the bureau, of the whole apartment, in fine, excited his merriment, and he could not refrain from making jokes about Charles, which rather embarrassed Emma. She would have liked to see him more serious, and even on occasions more dramatic; as, for example, when she thought she heard a noise of approaching steps in the alley.","sentences":[{"en":"When the night was rainy, they took refuge in the consulting-room between the cart-shed and the stable.","zh":"夜晚落雨，他们避到车房马棚之间的诊室。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She lighted one of the kitchen candles that she had hidden behind the books.","zh":"厨房的蜡烛，她先在书后藏好，这时取出一支来点亮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe settled down there as if at home.","zh":"罗道耳弗坐在这里，如同待在自己家里一样。书架、书桌，总而言之，整个房间，在他看来，好笑异常，不由自己，就大开查理的玩笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The sight of the library, of the bureau, of the whole apartment, in fine, excited his merriment, and he could not refrain from making jokes about Charles, which rather embarrassed Emma.","zh":"罗道耳弗坐在这里，如同待在自己家里一样。书架、书桌，总而言之，整个房间，在他看来，好笑异常，不由自己，就大开查理的玩笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She would have liked to see him more serious, and even on occasions more dramatic; as, for example, when she thought she heard a noise of approaching steps in the alley.","zh":"爱玛听了，未免窘促，她希望他分外严肃，甚至必要时，分外紧张，就像有一回，她觉得小巷有脚步走近的响声，言道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Someone is coming!” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Someone is coming!” she said.","zh":"“有人来！”他吹灭蜡烛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He blew out the light.","sentences":[{"en":"He blew out the light.","zh":"“你带手枪了没有？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Have you your pistols?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you your pistols?”","zh":"“做什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why?”","zh":"爱玛回答道：“为…自卫呀。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Why, to defend yourself,” replied Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, to defend yourself,” replied Emma.","zh":"爱玛回答道：“为…自卫呀。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“From your husband? Oh, poor devil!” And Rodolphe finished his sentence with a gesture that said, “I could crush him with a flip of my finger.”","sentences":[{"en":"“From your husband?","zh":"“对付你丈夫？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, poor devil!”","zh":"啊！可怜的孩子！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And Rodolphe finished his sentence with a gesture that said, “I could crush him with a flip of my finger.”","zh":"说完这句话，罗道耳弗做了一个手势，意思是：“我一弹手指，他就完蛋。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was wonder-stricken at his bravery, although she felt in it a sort of indecency and a naive coarseness that scandalised her.","sentences":[{"en":"She was wonder-stricken at his bravery, although she felt in it a sort of indecency and a naive coarseness that scandalised her.","zh":"他的勇敢使她吃惊，可是语气不文，用词粗野，也令她反感。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe reflected a good deal on the affair of the pistols. If she had spoken seriously, it was very ridiculous, he thought, even odious; for he had no reason to hate the good Charles, not being what is called devoured by jealousy; and on this subject Emma had taken a great vow that he did not think in the best of taste.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe reflected a good deal on the affair of the pistols.","zh":"手枪这句话，罗道耳弗寻思了许久，心想：万一她说话当真，这就非常可笑，甚至于可憎了，因为他本人毫无理由怨恨善良的查理，他不是那类忌妒成性的人——爱玛说起他不忌妒，怕他不信，还赌了大咒，他也嫌她有伤大雅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"If she had spoken seriously, it was very ridiculous, he thought, even odious; for he had no reason to hate the good Charles, not being what is called devoured by jealousy; and on this subject Emma had taken a great vow that he did not think in the best of taste.","zh":"手枪这句话，罗道耳弗寻思了许久，心想：万一她说话当真，这就非常可笑，甚至于可憎了，因为他本人毫无理由怨恨善良的查理，他不是那类忌妒成性的人——爱玛说起他不忌妒，怕他不信，还赌了大咒，他也嫌她有伤大雅。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Besides, she was growing very sentimental. She had insisted on exchanging miniatures; they had cut off handfuls of hair, and now she was asking for a ring—a real wedding-ring, in sign of an eternal union. She often spoke to him of the evening chimes, of the voices of nature. Then she talked to him of her mother—hers! and of his mother—his! Rodolphe had lost his twenty years ago. Emma none the less consoled him with caressing words as one would have done a lost child, and she sometimes even said to him, gazing at the moon—","sentences":[{"en":"Besides, she was growing very sentimental.","zh":"而且她越来越重感情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had insisted on exchanging miniatures; they had cut off handfuls of hair, and now she was asking for a ring—a real wedding-ring, in sign of an eternal union.","zh":"先是一定要交换小照，剪一绺头发相送；现在她要一枚戒指、一枚真的结婚戒指，表示百年相好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She often spoke to him of the evening chimes, of the voices of nature.","zh":"她动不动同他谈起晚钟或者天籁，接着又说到自己的母亲，问起他的母亲。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she talked to him of her mother—hers! and of his mother—his!","zh":"她动不动同他谈起晚钟或者天籁，接着又说到自己的母亲，问起他的母亲。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Rodolphe had lost his twenty years ago.","zh":"罗道耳弗的母亲已经死了二十年了。爱玛还要婉言安慰他，好像他是个弃儿，甚至有时候，她望着月亮对他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma none the less consoled him with caressing words as one would have done a lost child, and she sometimes even said to him, gazing at the moon—","zh":"罗道耳弗的母亲已经死了二十年了。爱玛还要婉言安慰他，好像他是个弃儿，甚至有时候，她望着月亮对他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I am sure that above there together they approve of our love.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I am sure that above there together they approve of our love.”","zh":"“我拿稳了，她们在天上全都赞成我们相爱。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But she was so pretty. He had possessed so few women of such ingenuousness. This love without debauchery was a new experience for him, and, drawing him out of his lazy habits, caressed at once his pride and his sensuality. Emma’s enthusiasm, which his bourgeois good sense disdained, seemed to him in his heart of hearts charming, since it was lavished on him. Then, sure of being loved, he no longer kept up appearances, and insensibly his ways changed.","sentences":[{"en":"But she was so pretty.","zh":"可是她长得也真标致！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had possessed so few women of such ingenuousness.","zh":"他玩过的女人，像她这样爽快的，也少有过！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This love without debauchery was a new experience for him, and, drawing him out of his lazy habits, caressed at once his pride and his sensuality.","zh":"就他来说，这种不放荡的恋爱，不但新鲜，而且逼他走出老一套习惯，让他又骄傲又动兴。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma’s enthusiasm, which his bourgeois good sense disdained, seemed to him in his heart of hearts charming, since it was lavished on him.","zh":"爱玛的兴奋，根据他的资产阶级见识，他看不上眼，可这是冲他来的，所以心下又觉得滋味不错。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, sure of being loved, he no longer kept up appearances, and insensibly his ways changed.","zh":"于是他拿稳了她爱他，疏忽大意之下，不知不觉，变了态度。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had no longer, as formerly, words so gentle that they made her cry, nor passionate caresses that made her mad, so that their great love, which engrossed her life, seemed to lessen beneath her like the water of a stream absorbed into its channel, and she could see the bed of it. She would not believe it; she redoubled in tenderness, and Rodolphe concealed his indifference less and less.","sentences":[{"en":"He had no longer, as formerly, words so gentle that they made her cry, nor passionate caresses that made her mad, so that their great love, which engrossed her life, seemed to lessen beneath her like the water of a stream absorbed into its channel, and she could see the bed of it.","zh":"他不像往常那样，一来就甜言蜜语，感动得她直哭，也不像往常那样，一来就热吻紧抱，使她发疯。他们的伟大爱情，从前仿佛长江大河，她在里面优游自得，现在一天涸似一天，河床少水，她看见了污泥。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would not believe it; she redoubled in tenderness, and Rodolphe concealed his indifference less and less.","zh":"她不肯相信，加倍温存。罗道耳弗却越来越不掩饰他的冷淡。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She did not know if she regretted having yielded to him, or whether she did not wish, on the contrary, to enjoy him the more. The humiliation of feeling herself weak was turning to rancour, tempered by their voluptuous pleasures. It was not affection; it was like a continual seduction. He subjugated her; she almost feared him.","sentences":[{"en":"She did not know if she regretted having yielded to him, or whether she did not wish, on the contrary, to enjoy him the more.","zh":"她不知道她是后悔不该依顺了他，还是相反，她不希望再爱下去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The humiliation of feeling herself weak was turning to rancour, tempered by their voluptuous pleasures.","zh":"她嫌自己软弱；羞愧慢慢变成怨恨；癫狂又减轻了怨恨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was not affection; it was like a continual seduction.","zh":"这不是热恋，倒像一种长远的诱惑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He subjugated her; she almost feared him.","zh":"他制住了她。她简直怕起他来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Appearances, nevertheless, were calmer than ever, Rodolphe having succeeded in carrying out the adultery after his own fancy; and at the end of six months, when the spring-time came, they were to one another like a married couple, tranquilly keeping up a domestic flame.","sentences":[{"en":"Appearances, nevertheless, were calmer than ever, Rodolphe having succeeded in carrying out the adultery after his own fancy; and at the end of six months, when the spring-time came, they were to one another like a married couple, tranquilly keeping up a domestic flame.","zh":"罗道耳弗顺利地按照自己的心意支配奸情，所以表面也就分外平静。一晃半年，到了春天，他们发现自己面对面，好像一对夫妇，家居无事，但求爱火不灭一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was the time of year when old Rouault sent his turkey in remembrance of the setting of his leg. The present always arrived with a letter. Emma cut the string that tied it to the basket, and read the following lines:—","sentences":[{"en":"It was the time of year when old Rouault sent his turkey in remembrance of the setting of his leg.","zh":"又到了卢欧老爹纪念治好他的腿，送母火鸡的时期。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The present always arrived with a letter.","zh":"礼物之外，照例有一封信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma cut the string that tied it to the basket, and read the following lines:—","zh":"爱玛剪掉筐子上拴着的绳子，读着下面的词句：我亲爱的孩子们，","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My Dear Children—I hope this will find you well, and that this one will be as good as the others. For it seems to me a little more tender, if I may venture to say so, and heavier. But next time, for a change, I’ll give you a turkeycock, unless you have a preference for some dabs; and send me back the hamper, if you please, with the two old ones. I have had an accident with my cart-sheds, whose covering flew off one windy night among the trees. The harvest has not been overgood either. Finally, I don’t know when I shall come to see you. It is so difficult now to leave the house since I am alone, my poor Emma.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My Dear Children—I hope this will find you well, and that this one will be as good as the others.","zh":"我希望信到时，你们身体康健，这只火鸡像往年一样好；因为如果我敢这么说的话，我觉得它更嫩一点，个儿也大些。","scope":"group"},{"en":"For it seems to me a little more tender, if I may venture to say so, and heavier.","zh":"我希望信到时，你们身体康健，这只火鸡像往年一样好；因为如果我敢这么说的话，我觉得它更嫩一点，个儿也大些。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But next time, for a change, I’ll give you a turkeycock, unless you have a preference for some dabs; and send me back the hamper, if you please, with the two old ones.","zh":"不过下一次，变变花样，我要送你们一只公的，除非你们偏喜欢母的。请你们把鸡筐子送还我，还有两只旧的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I have had an accident with my cart-sheds, whose covering flew off one windy night among the trees.","zh":"有天晚上，起了大风，我不走运，车房的顶子给刮到树林里去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The harvest has not been overgood either.","zh":"收成也不太争气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Finally, I don’t know when I shall come to see you.","zh":"总之，我不知道我什么时候去看你们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is so difficult now to leave the house since I am alone, my poor Emma.”","zh":"自从我成了一个人以来，可怜的爱玛，我如今就很难离开家啦！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Here there was a break in the lines, as if the old fellow had dropped his pen to dream a little while.","sentences":[{"en":"Here there was a break in the lines, as if the old fellow had dropped his pen to dream a little while.","zh":"紧跟着两行之间，有一个空当，好像老头子想心事，笔掉下去了一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For myself, I am very well, except for a cold I caught the other day at the fair at Yvetot, where I had gone to hire a shepherd, having turned away mine because he was too dainty. How we are to be pitied with such a lot of thieves! Besides, he was also rude. I heard from a pedlar, who, travelling through your part of the country this winter, had a tooth drawn, that Bovary was as usual working hard. That doesn’t surprise me; and he showed me his tooth; we had some coffee together. I asked him if he had seen you, and he said not, but that he had seen two horses in the stables, from which I conclude that business is looking up. So much the better, my dear children, and may God send you every imaginable happiness! It grieves me not yet to have seen my dear little grand-daughter, Berthe Bovary. I have planted an Orleans plum-tree for her in the garden under your room, and I won’t have it touched unless it is to have jam made for her by and bye, that I will keep in the cupboard for her when she comes.","sentences":[{"en":"“For myself, I am very well, except for a cold I caught the other day at the fair at Yvetot, where I had gone to hire a shepherd, having turned away mine because he was too dainty.","zh":"我本人，除去前不久到伊弗托赶集，着凉之外，身子倒也结实。我歇掉我那放羊的，原因是他太讲究吃食了，所以我才去伊弗托，另雇一个。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How we are to be pitied with such a lot of thieves!","zh":"人就对付不了这些家伙，个个全是强盗！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, he was also rude.","zh":"再说，他也不老实。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I heard from a pedlar, who, travelling through your part of the country this winter, had a tooth drawn, that Bovary was as usual working hard.","zh":"有一个小贩，去冬在你们那地方跑生意，拔掉一颗牙，我听他讲，包法利总在辛苦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That doesn’t surprise me; and he showed me his tooth; we had some coffee together.","zh":"我不觉得奇怪。他拿牙给我看；我们一道喝了一杯咖啡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I asked him if he had seen you, and he said not, but that he had seen two horses in the stables, from which I conclude that business is looking up.","zh":"我问他看见你没有，他说没有，不过他看见马棚有两匹牲口，这样看来，生意还有起色。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So much the better, my dear children, and may God send you every imaginable happiness!","zh":"这就好，我亲爱的孩子们，人间至福，愿上帝全给你们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It grieves me not yet to have seen my dear little grand-daughter, Berthe Bovary.","zh":"直到如今，我还不认识我心爱的小外孙女白尔特·包法利，难过就不必说了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I have planted an Orleans plum-tree for her in the garden under your room, and I won’t have it touched unless it is to have jam made for her by and bye, that I will keep in the cupboard for her when she comes.","zh":"我在花园你的屋子窗户底下，栽了一棵“奥尔良”种李子树。我不许人碰树上的李子，除非将来摘下来给她做蜜饯，就是蜜饯，我也留在橱里，单单等她来吃。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Good-bye, my dear children. I kiss you, my girl, you too, my son-in-law, and the little one on both cheeks. I am, with best compliments, your loving father.","sentences":[{"en":"“Good-bye, my dear children.","zh":"再见，我亲爱的孩子们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I kiss you, my girl, you too, my son-in-law, and the little one on both cheeks.","zh":"我吻你，我的女儿，还有你，我的女婿，还有宝宝，吻两个脸蛋儿。愿你们快乐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am, with best compliments, your loving father.","zh":"你们慈爱的父亲泰奥多尔·卢欧","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Theodore Rouault.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Theodore Rouault.”","zh":"你们慈爱的父亲泰奥多尔·卢欧","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She held the coarse paper in her fingers for some minutes. The spelling mistakes were interwoven one with the other, and Emma followed the kindly thought that cackled right through it like a hen half hidden in the hedge of thorns. The writing had been dried with ashes from the hearth, for a little grey powder slipped from the letter on to her dress, and she almost thought she saw her father bending over the hearth to take up the tongs. How long since she had been with him, sitting on the footstool in the chimney-corner, where she used to burn the end of a bit of wood in the great flame of the sea-sedges! She remembered the summer evenings all full of sunshine. The colts neighed when anyone passed by, and galloped, galloped. Under her window there was a beehive, and sometimes the bees wheeling round in the light struck against her window like rebounding balls of gold. What happiness there had been at that time, what freedom, what hope! What an abundance of illusions! Nothing was left of them now. She had got rid of them all in her soul’s life, in all her successive conditions of life, maidenhood, her marriage, and her love—thus constantly losing them all her life through, like a traveller who leaves something of his wealth at every inn along his road.","sentences":[{"en":"She held the coarse paper in her fingers for some minutes.","zh":"这张粗纸，她捏在手心，捏了好几分钟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The spelling mistakes were interwoven one with the other, and Emma followed the kindly thought that cackled right through it like a hen half hidden in the hedge of thorns.","zh":"连篇错字，可是思想厚道，在字里行间，揪着爱玛的心，仿佛一只母鸡，躲躲闪闪，藏在荆棘篱笆里头，咯咯叫唤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The writing had been dried with ashes from the hearth, for a little grey powder slipped from the letter on to her dress, and she almost thought she saw her father bending over the hearth to take up the tongs.","zh":"墨水是炉灰吸干的，因为信上有一些灰颜色屑子，落在她的袍子上。她差不多隐约望见父亲，朝灶头弯下了腰，去拿火钳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How long since she had been with him, sitting on the footstool in the chimney-corner, where she used to burn the end of a bit of wood in the great flame of the sea-sedges!","zh":"她好久不在他跟前了！黄刺条噼里啪啦，冒出老高的火焰，她坐在壁炉角落的方凳上，拿起一根火柴，就着火烧…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She remembered the summer evenings all full of sunshine.","zh":"她想起夏季黄昏，阳光灿烂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The colts neighed when anyone passed by, and galloped, galloped.","zh":"有人走过，马驹全在嘶叫，奔驰，奔驰…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Under her window there was a beehive, and sometimes the bees wheeling round in the light struck against her window like rebounding balls of gold.","zh":"她的窗户底下有一个蜂房，有时候，蜜蜂在阳光里飞来飞去，碰着玻璃窗，好像金球一样跳跃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What happiness there had been at that time, what freedom, what hope!","zh":"当时多幸福！多自由！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What an abundance of illusions!","zh":"多少希望！多少绮梦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nothing was left of them now.","zh":"现在什么也没有！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had got rid of them all in her soul’s life, in all her successive conditions of life, maidenhood, her marriage, and her love—thus constantly losing them all her life through, like a traveller who leaves something of his wealth at every inn along his road.","zh":"她已经把它们耗光了，耗在她灵魂的高低波澜上，环境的前后变动上，处女、婚姻和恋爱的各个阶段上——它们就这样跟着她的生命，一路丢光，好像一位旅客，在沿途家家小店，留下一点他的财物一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But what then, made her so unhappy? What was the extraordinary catastrophe that had transformed her? And she raised her head, looking round as if to seek the cause of that which made her suffer.","sentences":[{"en":"But what then, made her so unhappy?","zh":"那么，她怎么会这样不快乐呢？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What was the extraordinary catastrophe that had transformed her?","zh":"出了什么大变动，使她坠入了苦海？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And she raised her head, looking round as if to seek the cause of that which made her suffer.","zh":"她仰起头来，四下眺望，像在寻找她落难的原因。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"An April ray was dancing on the china of the whatnot; the fire burned; beneath her slippers she felt the softness of the carpet; the day was bright, the air warm, and she heard her child shouting with laughter.","sentences":[{"en":"An April ray was dancing on the china of the whatnot; the fire burned; beneath her slippers she felt the softness of the carpet; the day was bright, the air warm, and she heard her child shouting with laughter.","zh":"一道四月的阳光，照着摆设架的瓷器，晶莹耀眼。炉火燃烧。她穿着拖鞋，觉出地毯的绵软。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In fact, the little girl was just then rolling on the lawn in the midst of the grass that was being turned. She was lying flat on her stomach at the top of a rick. The servant was holding her by her skirt. Lestiboudois was raking by her side, and every time he came near she lent forward, beating the air with both her arms.","sentences":[{"en":"In fact, the little girl was just then rolling on the lawn in the midst of the grass that was being turned.","zh":"果然，草割下来要晒，她正在上面打滚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was lying flat on her stomach at the top of a rick.","zh":"她趴在草堆高头，脸朝下，女用人揪住她的下摆，赖斯地布杜瓦在旁边除草，每次他一凑近，她就斜过身子，抡起两只胳膊，在空里乱打。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The servant was holding her by her skirt.","zh":"她趴在草堆高头，脸朝下，女用人揪住她的下摆，赖斯地布杜瓦在旁边除草，每次他一凑近，她就斜过身子，抡起两只胳膊，在空里乱打。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Lestiboudois was raking by her side, and every time he came near she lent forward, beating the air with both her arms.","zh":"她趴在草堆高头，脸朝下，女用人揪住她的下摆，赖斯地布杜瓦在旁边除草，每次他一凑近，她就斜过身子，抡起两只胳膊，在空里乱打。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Bring her to me,” said her mother, rushing to embrace her. “How I love you, my poor child! How I love you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Bring her to me,” said her mother, rushing to embrace her.","zh":"她的母亲跑过去吻她，道：“带她过来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“How I love you, my poor child!","zh":"我多爱你，我的小可怜儿！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How I love you!”","zh":"我多爱你！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then noticing that the tips of her ears were rather dirty, she rang at once for warm water, and washed her, changed her linen, her stockings, her shoes, asked a thousand questions about her health, as if on the return from a long journey, and finally, kissing her again and crying a little, she gave her back to the servant, who stood quite thunderstricken at this excess of tenderness.","sentences":[{"en":"Then noticing that the tips of her ears were rather dirty, she rang at once for warm water, and washed her, changed her linen, her stockings, her shoes, asked a thousand questions about her health, as if on the return from a long journey, and finally, kissing her again and crying a little, she gave her back to the servant, who stood quite thunderstricken at this excess of tenderness.","zh":"她看见她的耳梢有一点脏，赶快拉铃，要来热水，帮她洗干净，给她换衬衫，换袜子，换鞋，问起她的身子好坏，一遍又一遍，好像出远门才回来一样，最后又吻了一回，这才挂着眼泪，交还女用人，女用人看她疼孩子疼到这步田地，惊得话也说不出来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"That evening Rodolphe found her more serious than usual.","sentences":[{"en":"That evening Rodolphe found her more serious than usual.","zh":"当天晚晌，罗道耳弗发现她比平时严肃多了。他盘算道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That will pass over,” he concluded; “it’s a whim:”","sentences":[{"en":"“That will pass over,” he concluded; “it’s a whim:”","zh":"“就会好的；她在闹脾气。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he missed three rendezvous running. When he did come, she showed herself cold and almost contemptuous.","sentences":[{"en":"And he missed three rendezvous running.","zh":"他一连三天爽约。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he did come, she showed herself cold and almost contemptuous.","zh":"等他再来，她显出一副冷淡、差不多鄙夷的神情。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! you’re losing your time, my lady!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! you’re losing your time, my lady!”","zh":"“啊！我的小心肝，你这叫白糟蹋时候…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he pretended not to notice her melancholy sighs, nor the handkerchief she took out.","sentences":[{"en":"And he pretended not to notice her melancholy sighs, nor the handkerchief she took out.","zh":"他心里这样想着，同时装模作样，就像没有注意到她伤心叹气，掏她的手绢一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Emma repented. She even asked herself why she detested Charles; if it had not been better to have been able to love him? But he gave her no opportunities for such a revival of sentiment, so that she was much embarrassed by her desire for sacrifice, when the druggist came just in time to provide her with an opportunity.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Emma repented.","zh":"原来是爱玛忏悔了！她甚至问自己：她凭什么痛恨查理，是不是还是顶好想法子爱他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She even asked herself why she detested Charles; if it had not been better to have been able to love him?","zh":"原来是爱玛忏悔了！她甚至问自己：她凭什么痛恨查理，是不是还是顶好想法子爱他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But he gave her no opportunities for such a revival of sentiment, so that she was much embarrassed by her desire for sacrifice, when the druggist came just in time to provide her with an opportunity.","zh":"然而她改变心情，他并不理会，所以她虽然有心奉献，却不知从何着手；正在此时，药剂师适逢其会，给她提供了一个机会。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-11","part":2,"n":11,"title":"Part II · Chapter 11","titleZh":"中卷 · 11","paragraphs":[{"en":"He had recently read a eulogy on a new method for curing club-foot, and as he was a partisan of progress, he conceived the patriotic idea that Yonville, in order to keep to the fore, ought to have some operations for strephopody or club-foot.","sentences":[{"en":"He had recently read a eulogy on a new method for curing club-foot, and as he was a partisan of progress, he conceived the patriotic idea that Yonville, in order to keep to the fore, ought to have some operations for strephopody or club-foot.","zh":"他新近读到一篇表扬新法治疗跷脚的文章；他一向拥护进步，所以就起了这种爱乡的想法：永镇为了看齐起见，也应当施行畸形足手术。他对爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For,” said he to Emma, “what risk is there? See—” (and he enumerated on his fingers the advantages of the attempt), “success, almost certain relief and beautifying of the patient, celebrity acquired by the operator. Why, for example, should not your husband relieve poor Hippolyte of the ‘Lion d’Or’? Note that he would not fail to tell about his cure to all the travellers, and then” (Homais lowered his voice and looked round him) “who is to prevent me from sending a short paragraph on the subject to the paper? Eh! goodness me! an article gets about; it is talked of; it ends by making a snowball! And who knows? who knows?”","sentences":[{"en":"“For,” said he to Emma, “what risk is there?","zh":"“因为，有什么不好？您合计合计（他用手指数着尝试的利益）：成功十拿九稳；病人消除痛苦，增加美观；施手术的人立时出名。","scope":"group"},{"en":"See—” (and he enumerated on his fingers the advantages of the attempt), “success, almost certain relief and beautifying of the patient, celebrity acquired by the operator.","zh":"“因为，有什么不好？您合计合计（他用手指数着尝试的利益）：成功十拿九稳；病人消除痛苦，增加美观；施手术的人立时出名。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Why, for example, should not your husband relieve poor Hippolyte of the ‘Lion d’Or’?","zh":"比方说，您丈夫为什么不救救金狮的伙计、可怜的伊玻立特？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Note that he would not fail to tell about his cure to all the travellers, and then” (Homais lowered his voice and looked round him) “who is to prevent me from sending a short paragraph on the subject to the paper?","zh":"看吧，病治好了，他不会不对个个旅客讲的，再说（郝麦放低声音，四下张望），谁拦着我不往报上送一小段新闻，谈谈这事？是啊！我的上帝！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Eh! goodness me! an article gets about; it is talked of; it ends by making a snowball!","zh":"人手一篇…个个说起…结局就名扬天下！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And who knows? who knows?”","zh":"谁知道？谁知道？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In fact, Bovary might succeed. Nothing proved to Emma that he was not clever; and what a satisfaction for her to have urged him to a step by which his reputation and fortune would be increased! She only wished to lean on something more solid than love.","sentences":[{"en":"In fact, Bovary might succeed.","zh":"包法利的确可以成功；爱玛还没有看见什么证明他做不了的手术；一件事名利双收，又是她撺掇他做的，她该怎么称心啊？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Nothing proved to Emma that he was not clever; and what a satisfaction for her to have urged him to a step by which his reputation and fortune would be increased!","zh":"包法利的确可以成功；爱玛还没有看见什么证明他做不了的手术；一件事名利双收，又是她撺掇他做的，她该怎么称心啊？","scope":"group"},{"en":"She only wished to lean on something more solid than love.","zh":"她但求有某种比爱情更坚实的东西作自己的支柱。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles, urged by the druggist and by her, allowed himself to be persuaded. He sent to Rouen for Dr. Duval’s volume, and every evening, holding his head between both hands, plunged into the reading of it.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles, urged by the druggist and by her, allowed himself to be persuaded.","zh":"经不起药剂师和她双管齐下，查理也就听从了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sent to Rouen for Dr. Duval’s volume, and every evening, holding his head between both hands, plunged into the reading of it.","zh":"他托人到鲁昂取来杜瓦尔博士 的论文，每天晚晌，手捧住头，用心研读。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"While he was studying equinus, varus, and valgus, that is to say, katastrephopody, endostrephopody, and exostrephopody (or better, the various turnings of the foot downwards, inwards, and outwards, with the hypostrephopody and anastrephopody), otherwise torsion downwards and upwards, Monsier Homais, with all sorts of arguments, was exhorting the lad at the inn to submit to the operation.","sentences":[{"en":"While he was studying equinus, varus, and valgus, that is to say, katastrephopody, endostrephopody, and exostrephopody (or better, the various turnings of the foot downwards, inwards, and outwards, with the hypostrephopody and anastrephopody), otherwise torsion downwards and upwards, Monsier Homais, with all sorts of arguments, was exhorting the lad at the inn to submit to the operation.","zh":"他研究马蹄型、外拐型、里拐型，就是说，趾畸形足、内畸形足、外畸形足（或者说明白些，就是形形色色的跷脚：跷后跟、里跷、外跷），以及底畸形足和踵畸形足（也就是平脚底板和跷脚尖），同时郝麦先生千方百计怂恿客店伙计动手术。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You will scarcely feel, probably, a slight pain; it is a simple prick, like a little blood-letting, less than the extraction of certain corns.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You will scarcely feel, probably, a slight pain; it is a simple prick, like a little blood-letting, less than the extraction of certain corns.”","zh":"“你也许连一点点疼都觉不出来；也就是像放血一样，扎一下子，比去脚膙子还好受。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Hippolyte, reflecting, rolled his stupid eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"Hippolyte, reflecting, rolled his stupid eyes.","zh":"伊玻立特沉吟不语，傻瓜似的，转动眼睛。药剂师接下去道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“However,” continued the chemist, “it doesn’t concern me. It’s for your sake, for pure humanity! I should like to see you, my friend, rid of your hideous caudication, together with that waddling of the lumbar regions which, whatever you say, must considerably interfere with you in the exercise of your calling.”","sentences":[{"en":"“However,” continued the chemist, “it doesn’t concern me.","zh":"伊玻立特沉吟不语，傻瓜似的，转动眼睛。药剂师接下去道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s for your sake, for pure humanity!","zh":"“其实不关我的事！为的是你！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I should like to see you, my friend, rid of your hideous caudication, together with that waddling of the lumbar regions which, whatever you say, must considerably interfere with you in the exercise of your calling.”","zh":"纯粹是人道观点！一瘸一拐的，走路难看，后腰摆过来摆过去，你再嘴硬，干起活儿来，也一定很碍事，我的朋友，我是指望你好。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Homais represented to him how much jollier and brisker he would feel afterwards, and even gave him to understand that he would be more likely to please the women; and the stable-boy began to smile heavily. Then he attacked him through his vanity:","sentences":[{"en":"Then Homais represented to him how much jollier and brisker he would feel afterwards, and even gave him to understand that he would be more likely to please the women; and the stable-boy began to smile heavily.","zh":"郝麦于是帮他指出：好了以后，他会觉得自己更快活，更灵活；甚至还暗示：他博女人欢心，也会容易些。马夫听了这话，不由得一脸蠢相，有了笑意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he attacked him through his vanity:","zh":"郝麦接着拿话激他：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Aren’t you a man? Hang it! what would you have done if you had had to go into the army, to go and fight beneath the standard? Ah! Hippolyte!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Aren’t you a man?","zh":"“家伙！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hang it! what would you have done if you had had to go into the army, to go and fight beneath the standard?","zh":"你是不是男子汉？万一祖国要你应征，到前线打仗的话，你怎么着？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah!","zh":"啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hippolyte!”","zh":"伊玻立特！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And Homais retired, declaring that he could not understand this obstinacy, this blindness in refusing the benefactions of science.","sentences":[{"en":"And Homais retired, declaring that he could not understand this obstinacy, this blindness in refusing the benefactions of science.","zh":"郝麦边走开边讲：一个人拒绝科学的恩典，居然这样固执，这样盲目，真是不可思议。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The poor fellow gave way, for it was like a conspiracy. Binet, who never interfered with other people’s business, Madame Lefrancois, Artémise, the neighbours, even the mayor, Monsieur Tuvache—everyone persuaded him, lectured him, shamed him; but what finally decided him was that it would cost him nothing. Bovary even undertook to provide the machine for the operation. This generosity was an idea of Emma’s, and Charles consented to it, thinking in his heart of hearts that his wife was an angel.","sentences":[{"en":"The poor fellow gave way, for it was like a conspiracy.","zh":"可怜虫让步了，因为人们好像串通好了对付他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Binet, who never interfered with other people’s business, Madame Lefrancois, Artémise, the neighbours, even the mayor, Monsieur Tuvache—everyone persuaded him, lectured him, shamed him; but what finally decided him was that it would cost him nothing.","zh":"从来闭门不问世事的毕耐，还有勒弗朗索瓦太太、阿尔泰蜜丝、邻居们，甚至镇长杜法赦先生，也伙在一起，个个劝他，说他，臊他；不过最后起决定作用的，却是：这不要花他一个钱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bovary even undertook to provide the machine for the operation.","zh":"包法利甚至答应供应手术机器。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This generosity was an idea of Emma’s, and Charles consented to it, thinking in his heart of hearts that his wife was an angel.","zh":"做好事是爱玛的主意；查理同意了，私下直说他女人是一位天使。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"So by the advice of the chemist, and after three fresh starts, he had a kind of box made by the carpenter, with the aid of the locksmith, that weighed about eight pounds, and in which iron, wood, sheer-iron, leather, screws, and nuts had not been spared.","sentences":[{"en":"So by the advice of the chemist, and after three fresh starts, he had a kind of box made by the carpenter, with the aid of the locksmith, that weighed about eight pounds, and in which iron, wood, sheer-iron, leather, screws, and nuts had not been spared.","zh":"于是他结合药剂师的意见，还有锁匠帮忙，叫木匠做了一个盒子样式的东西，开头做错了两回，第三回总算做成了，约摸八磅重，铁、木、皮、铅皮、螺丝钉和螺丝口，应有尽有，绝不偷工减料。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But to know which of Hippolyte’s tendons to cut, it was necessary first of all to find out what kind of club-foot he had.","sentences":[{"en":"But to know which of Hippolyte’s tendons to cut, it was necessary first of all to find out what kind of club-foot he had.","zh":"但是割哪一条筋，先该知道伊玻立特是哪一类跷脚。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had a foot forming almost a straight line with the leg, which, however, did not prevent it from being turned in, so that it was an equinus together with something of a varus, or else a slight varus with a strong tendency to equinus. But with this equinus, wide in foot like a horse’s hoof, with rugose skin, dry tendons, and large toes, on which the black nails looked as if made of iron, the clubfoot ran about like a deer from morn till night. He was constantly to be seen on the Place, jumping round the carts, thrusting his limping foot forwards. He seemed even stronger on that leg than the other. By dint of hard service it had acquired, as it were, moral qualities of patience and energy; and when he was given some heavy work, he stood on it in preference to its fellow.","sentences":[{"en":"He had a foot forming almost a straight line with the leg, which, however, did not prevent it from being turned in, so that it was an equinus together with something of a varus, or else a slight varus with a strong tendency to equinus.","zh":"他的脚差不多和腿成为一条直线，同时还朝里歪，看上去是马蹄型，兼一点外拐型，或者也可以说成轻微的外拐型，结合严重的马蹄型。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But with this equinus, wide in foot like a horse’s hoof, with rugose skin, dry tendons, and large toes, on which the black nails looked as if made of iron, the clubfoot ran about like a deer from morn till night.","zh":"这只马蹄型脚，确实也有马蹄大小，疙瘩皮，硬筋，粗脚趾，趾甲黑得像马掌钉子一样，可是跛子从早到晚，快步如飞。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was constantly to be seen on the Place, jumping round the carts, thrusting his limping foot forwards.","zh":"大家看见他，时刻在广场跳跳蹦蹦，兜着大车转。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He seemed even stronger on that leg than the other.","zh":"这条坏脚朝前一甩，简直像比那条好腿还要得力。侍应日久，它通达灵性，养成忍耐和刚强的品质，赶上重活，他信赖的，总归是它。","scope":"group"},{"en":"By dint of hard service it had acquired, as it were, moral qualities of patience and energy; and when he was given some heavy work, he stood on it in preference to its fellow.","zh":"这条坏脚朝前一甩，简直像比那条好腿还要得力。侍应日久，它通达灵性，养成忍耐和刚强的品质，赶上重活，他信赖的，总归是它。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Now, as it was an equinus, it was necessary to cut the tendon of Achilles, and, if need were, the anterior tibial muscle could be seen to afterwards for getting rid of the varus; for the doctor did not dare to risk both operations at once; he was even trembling already for fear of injuring some important region that he did not know.","sentences":[{"en":"Now, as it was an equinus, it was necessary to cut the tendon of Achilles, and, if need were, the anterior tibial muscle could be seen to afterwards for getting rid of the varus; for the doctor did not dare to risk both operations at once; he was even trembling already for fear of injuring some important region that he did not know.","zh":"既然是马蹄型，就该切断后跟的大腱；医治外拐型，要动前胫筋，只有留到以后再做：因为医生不敢一下子冒险开两次刀，其实行第一次手术 ，他已经打哆嗦了，直怕伤着什么他不清楚的重要部位。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Neither Ambrose Pare, applying for the first time since Celsus, after an interval of fifteen centuries, a ligature to an artery, nor Dupuytren, about to open an abscess in the brain, nor Gensoul when he first took away the superior maxilla, had hearts that trembled, hands that shook, minds so strained as Monsieur Bovary when he approached Hippolyte, his tenotome between his fingers. And as at hospitals, near by on a table lay a heap of lint, with waxed thread, many bandages—a pyramid of bandages—every bandage to be found at the druggist’s. It was Monsieur Homais who since morning had been organising all these preparations, as much to dazzle the multitude as to keep up his illusions. Charles pierced the skin; a dry crackling was heard. The tendon was cut, the operation over. Hippolyte could not get over his surprise, but bent over Bovary’s hands to cover them with kisses.","sentences":[{"en":"Neither Ambrose Pare, applying for the first time since Celsus, after an interval of fifteen centuries, a ligature to an artery, nor Dupuytren, about to open an abscess in the brain, nor Gensoul when he first took away the superior maxilla, had hearts that trembled, hands that shook, minds so strained as Monsieur Bovary when he approached Hippolyte, his tenotome between his fingers.","zh":"自从塞尔苏斯行医以来，经一千五百年而有昂布瓦斯·帕雷，他第一次紧急接合动脉，或者如迪皮特伦，穿过老厚一层脑髓，割治脓疮，或者如冉苏，第一次移动上颚骨， 都没有像包法利拿着他的截腱刀来到伊玻立特跟前，心那样跳，手那样抖，人那样紧张。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And as at hospitals, near by on a table lay a heap of lint, with waxed thread, many bandages—a pyramid of bandages—every bandage to be found at the druggist’s.","zh":"好像在医院一样，就见旁边桌子上，放着一堆旧布条、蜡线、许多绷带——金字塔一般高的绷带、药房的全部绷带。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Monsieur Homais who since morning had been organising all these preparations, as much to dazzle the multitude as to keep up his illusions.","zh":"郝麦先生从早晨起，就在料理一切，一方面为了向公众炫耀，另方面也为了自己心上受用。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles pierced the skin; a dry crackling was heard.","zh":"查理扎破肉皮，只听嘎吱一声，腱就断了，手术完成。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The tendon was cut, the operation over.","zh":"伊玻立特还在心惊肉跳，不料已经完事大吉；他朝包法利弯过身子，吻他的手。药剂师道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Hippolyte could not get over his surprise, but bent over Bovary’s hands to cover them with kisses.","zh":"伊玻立特还在心惊肉跳，不料已经完事大吉；他朝包法利弯过身子，吻他的手。药剂师道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Come, be calm,” said the druggist; “later on you will show your gratitude to your benefactor.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, be calm,” said the druggist; “later on you will show your gratitude to your benefactor.”","zh":"“好啦，放安静吧，改天谢你的恩人不迟！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he went down to tell the result to five or six inquirers who were waiting in the yard, and who fancied that Hippolyte would reappear walking properly. Then Charles, having buckled his patient into the machine, went home, where Emma, all anxiety, awaited him at the door. She threw herself on his neck; they sat down to table; he ate much, and at dessert he even wanted to take a cup of coffee, a luxury he only permitted himself on Sundays when there was company.","sentences":[{"en":"And he went down to tell the result to five or six inquirers who were waiting in the yard, and who fancied that Hippolyte would reappear walking properly.","zh":"院里站着五六个好事的，郝麦下来告诉他们结果，原来他们满以为伊玻立特会像常人一样走出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Charles, having buckled his patient into the machine, went home, where Emma, all anxiety, awaited him at the door.","zh":"查理接着就把病人的腿装进机关，回家去了。爱玛焦灼不安，正在门口盼他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She threw herself on his neck; they sat down to table; he ate much, and at dessert he even wanted to take a cup of coffee, a luxury he only permitted himself on Sundays when there was company.","zh":"她搂住他的脖子。饭开上来，他饱餐一顿，甚至想在饭后喝一杯咖啡：这样的奢侈，除非是星期天有客人，他才偶尔为之。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The evening was charming, full of prattle, of dreams together. They talked about their future fortune, of the improvements to be made in their house; he saw people’s estimation of him growing, his comforts increasing, his wife always loving him; and she was happy to refresh herself with a new sentiment, healthier, better, to feel at last some tenderness for this poor fellow who adored her. The thought of Rodolphe for one moment passed through her mind, but her eyes turned again to Charles; she even noticed with surprise that he had not bad teeth.","sentences":[{"en":"The evening was charming, full of prattle, of dreams together.","zh":"这是个愉快的夜晚，他们谈天说地，闲话共同的梦想、未来的财富、家中应有的改良。他看见自己名扬四海，生活稳定，太太永远爱他；她也发觉自己心旷神怡，通过更健康、更美好的感情，取得新生，对这爱她的可怜的孩子，终于有了若干恩情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They talked about their future fortune, of the improvements to be made in their house; he saw people’s estimation of him growing, his comforts increasing, his wife always loving him; and she was happy to refresh herself with a new sentiment, healthier, better, to feel at last some tenderness for this poor fellow who adored her.","zh":"这是个愉快的夜晚，他们谈天说地，闲话共同的梦想、未来的财富、家中应有的改良。他看见自己名扬四海，生活稳定，太太永远爱他；她也发觉自己心旷神怡，通过更健康、更美好的感情，取得新生，对这爱她的可怜的孩子，终于有了若干恩情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The thought of Rodolphe for one moment passed through her mind, but her eyes turned again to Charles; she even noticed with surprise that he had not bad teeth.","zh":"她偶尔想到罗道耳弗，并不留恋，望着查理，甚至发现他的牙齿并不难看，未免一惊。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They were in bed when Monsieur Homais, in spite of the servant, suddenly entered the room, holding in his hand a sheet of paper just written. It was the paragraph he intended for the “Fanal de Rouen.” He brought it for them to read.","sentences":[{"en":"They were in bed when Monsieur Homais, in spite of the servant, suddenly entered the room, holding in his hand a sheet of paper just written.","zh":"他们还在床上，郝麦先生不顾女用人阻拦，就突然走进卧室，拿着一张方才写成的稿纸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the paragraph he intended for the “Fanal de Rouen.”","zh":"原来是他给《鲁昂烽火》写的宣传文章。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He brought it for them to read.","zh":"他带过来给他们看。包法利说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Read it yourself,” said Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"“Read it yourself,” said Bovary.","zh":"“您自己念。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He read—","sentences":[{"en":"He read—","zh":"他读道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“‘Despite the prejudices that still invest a part of the face of Europe like a net, the light nevertheless begins to penetrate our country places. Thus on Tuesday our little town of Yonville found itself the scene of a surgical operation which is at the same time an act of loftiest philanthropy. Monsieur Bovary, one of our most distinguished practitioners—’”","sentences":[{"en":"“‘Despite the prejudices that still invest a part of the face of Europe like a net, the light nevertheless begins to penetrate our country places.","zh":"成见好似一张网，依然盖着欧洲一部分土地，尽管如此，光明却也开始照到我们的田野。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus on Tuesday our little town of Yonville found itself the scene of a surgical operation which is at the same time an act of loftiest philanthropy.","zh":"例如我们永镇，就在星期二，看到试验外科手术，同时还是高尚的人道行为。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Bovary, one of our most distinguished practitioners—’”","zh":"我们一位最知名的手术家包法利先生…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, that is too much! too much!” said Charles, choking with emotion.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, that is too much! too much!” said Charles, choking with emotion.","zh":"查理好生激动，连说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no! not at all! What next!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no! not at all!","zh":"“啊！言过其实！言过其实！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"What next!”","zh":"“啊！言过其实！言过其实！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“‘—Performed an operation on a club-footed man.’ I have not used the scientific term, because you know in a newspaper everyone would not perhaps understand. The masses must—’”","sentences":[{"en":"“‘—Performed an operation on a club-footed man.’","zh":"“不！一点也不！正该这样！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I have not used the scientific term, because you know in a newspaper everyone would not perhaps understand.","zh":"‘割治一个跷脚…’我没有用科学名词，因为您知道，报纸…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The masses must—’”","zh":"不见得人人都懂；群众必须…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No doubt,” said Bovary; “go on!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No doubt,” said Bovary; “go on!”","zh":"包法利道：“当然。念吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I proceed,” said the chemist. “‘Monsieur Bovary, one of our most distinguished practitioners, performed an operation on a club-footed man called Hippolyte Tautain, stableman for the last twenty-five years at the hotel of the “Lion d’Or,” kept by Widow Lefrancois, at the Place d’Armes. The novelty of the attempt, and the interest incident to the subject, had attracted such a concourse of persons that there was a veritable obstruction on the threshold of the establishment. The operation, moreover, was performed as if by magic, and barely a few drops of blood appeared on the skin, as though to say that the rebellious tendon had at last given way beneath the efforts of art. The patient, strangely enough—we affirm it as an eye-witness—complained of no pain. His condition up to the present time leaves nothing to be desired. Everything tends to show that his convelescence will be brief; and who knows even if at our next village festivity we shall not see our good Hippolyte figuring in the bacchic dance in the midst of a chorus of joyous boon-companions, and thus proving to all eyes by his verve and his capers his complete cure? Honour, then, to the generous savants! Honour to those indefatigable spirits who consecrate their vigils to the amelioration or to the alleviation of their kind! Honour, thrice honour! Is it not time to cry that the blind shall see, the deaf hear, the lame walk? But that which fanaticism formerly promised to its elect, science now accomplishes for all men. We shall keep our readers informed as to the successive phases of this remarkable cure.’”","sentences":[{"en":"“I proceed,” said the chemist.","zh":"“我往下念。”药剂师道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“‘Monsieur Bovary, one of our most distinguished practitioners, performed an operation on a club-footed man called Hippolyte Tautain, stableman for the last twenty-five years at the hotel of the “Lion d’Or,” kept by Widow Lefrancois, at the Place d’Armes.","zh":"我们一位最知名的手术家包法利先生割治一个跷脚患者。他是寡妇勒弗朗索瓦太太在阅兵广场开的金狮饭店用了二十年的马夫，名叫伊玻立特·托坦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The novelty of the attempt, and the interest incident to the subject, had attracted such a concourse of persons that there was a veritable obstruction on the threshold of the establishment.","zh":"无数居民由于事属创举，与对病人的关心，聚在饭店门首，前拥后挤，水泄不通。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The operation, moreover, was performed as if by magic, and barely a few drops of blood appeared on the skin, as though to say that the rebellious tendon had at last given way beneath the efforts of art.","zh":"施行手术，好像仙家作法一样，几乎没有血冒出来，证明倔强的大腱，终于向技艺之门纳降。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The patient, strangely enough—we affirm it as an eye-witness—complained of no pain.","zh":"说来也怪，病人并不感到疼痛（我们亲眼看见，可以作证）。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His condition up to the present time leaves nothing to be desired.","zh":"到现在为止，情形良好，相信他不久就会复元。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everything tends to show that his convelescence will be brief; and who knows even if at our next village festivity we shall not see our good Hippolyte figuring in the bacchic dance in the midst of a chorus of joyous boon-companions, and thus proving to all eyes by his verve and his capers his complete cure?","zh":"下次镇上过节，谁能说我们看不见勇敢的伊玻立特，夹在寻欢作乐的伙伴中间，大跳其酒神之舞，兴会淋漓，步伐便捷，向众人证明，脚完全治好了呢？所以光荣属于高贵的学者！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Honour, then, to the generous savants!","zh":"光荣属于夜以继日、增进同胞的幸福或者减轻同胞痛苦的那些人！光荣！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Honour to those indefatigable spirits who consecrate their vigils to the amelioration or to the alleviation of their kind!","zh":"光荣属于夜以继日、增进同胞的幸福或者减轻同胞痛苦的那些人！光荣！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Honour, thrice honour!","zh":"三倍的光荣！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is it not time to cry that the blind shall see, the deaf hear, the lame walk?","zh":"难道我们不该高声呐喊：瞎子将要看见，聋子将要听见，跛子将要行走如常？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But that which fanaticism formerly promised to its elect, science now accomplishes for all men.","zh":"上天先前许给它的选民的，科学如今为全人类完成！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We shall keep our readers informed as to the successive phases of this remarkable cure.’”","zh":"这不可思议的医治的经过，我们将随时向读者报告。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This did not prevent Mere Lefrancois, from coming five days after, scared, and crying out—","sentences":[{"en":"This did not prevent Mere Lefrancois, from coming five days after, scared, and crying out—","zh":"这挡不住五天以后，勒弗朗索瓦太太惊惶失措，走来叫喊：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Help! he is dying! I am going crazy!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Help! he is dying!","zh":"“救命呀！他要死啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am going crazy!”","zh":"我不晓得怎么办才好！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles rushed to the “Lion d’Or,” and the chemist, who caught sight of him passing along the Place hatless, abandoned his shop. He appeared himself breathless, red, anxious, and asking everyone who was going up the stairs—","sentences":[{"en":"Charles rushed to the “Lion d’Or,” and the chemist, who caught sight of him passing along the Place hatless, abandoned his shop.","zh":"查理拔腿就朝金狮跑；药剂师望见他走过广场，不戴帽子，也离开药房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He appeared himself breathless, red, anxious, and asking everyone who was going up the stairs—","zh":"他赶到了，喘着气，脸通红，不放心，问起个个上楼的人：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, what’s the matter with our interesting strephopode?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, what’s the matter with our interesting strephopode?”","zh":"“我们的畸形足患者，到底怎么啦？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The strephopode was writhing in hideous convulsions, so that the machine in which his leg was enclosed was knocked against the wall enough to break it.","sentences":[{"en":"The strephopode was writhing in hideous convulsions, so that the machine in which his leg was enclosed was knocked against the wall enough to break it.","zh":"畸形足患者正在疯狂抽搐，裹腿的机关打着墙，简直要把墙打穿了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"With many precautions, in order not to disturb the position of the limb, the box was removed, and an awful sight presented itself. The outlines of the foot disappeared in such a swelling that the entire skin seemed about to burst, and it was covered with ecchymosis, caused by the famous machine. Hippolyte had already complained of suffering from it. No attention had been paid to him; they had to acknowledge that he had not been altogether wrong, and he was freed for a few hours. But, hardly had the oedema gone down to some extent, than the two savants thought fit to put back the limb in the apparatus, strapping it tighter to hasten matters. At last, three days after, Hippolyte being unable to endure it any longer, they once more removed the machine, and were much surprised at the result they saw. The livid tumefaction spread over the leg, with blisters here and there, whence there oozed a black liquid. Matters were taking a serious turn. Hippolyte began to worry himself, and Mere Lefrancois, had him installed in the little room near the kitchen, so that he might at least have some distraction.","sentences":[{"en":"With many precautions, in order not to disturb the position of the limb, the box was removed, and an awful sight presented itself.","zh":"他们不移动腿的部位，小心翼翼，去掉盒子，看到一种可怕的景象。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The outlines of the foot disappeared in such a swelling that the entire skin seemed about to burst, and it was covered with ecchymosis, caused by the famous machine.","zh":"脚肿得连脚样都没有了，整个肉皮像要胀破了似的，上面全是有名的机器弄出来的瘀血点子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hippolyte had already complained of suffering from it.","zh":"伊玻立特早就喊疼了，没有人在意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No attention had been paid to him; they had to acknowledge that he had not been altogether wrong, and he was freed for a few hours.","zh":"现在他们不得不承认，他叫喊，也有部分道理。他们让腿晾了几小时。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But, hardly had the oedema gone down to some extent, than the two savants thought fit to put back the limb in the apparatus, strapping it tighter to hasten matters.","zh":"可是浮肿刚有一点消散，两位学者认为应当再拿腿装进机关，而且为了促进治疗效果，捆得还要紧些。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, three days after, Hippolyte being unable to endure it any longer, they once more removed the machine, and were much surprised at the result they saw.","zh":"过了三天，伊玻立特说什么也受不住了，他们又挪开机器，面对结果，触目惊心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The livid tumefaction spread over the leg, with blisters here and there, whence there oozed a black liquid.","zh":"腿肿成铅皮似的，东一个水泡，西一个水泡，往外冒黑水。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Matters were taking a serious turn.","zh":"情况显然严重。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hippolyte began to worry himself, and Mere Lefrancois, had him installed in the little room near the kitchen, so that he might at least have some distraction.","zh":"伊玻立特心焦了，勒弗朗索瓦太太把他搬进挨近厨房的小间，好歹也能散散心。不过税务员，天天在这里用饭，坚决反对，只好又把伊玻立特移到弹子房。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the tax-collector, who dined there every day, complained bitterly of such companionship. Then Hippolyte was removed to the billiard-room. He lay there moaning under his heavy coverings, pale with long beard, sunken eyes, and from time to time turning his perspiring head on the dirty pillow, where the flies alighted. Madame Bovary went to see him. She brought him linen for his poultices; she comforted, and encouraged him. Besides, he did not want for company, especially on market-days, when the peasants were knocking about the billiard-balls round him, fenced with the cues, smoked, drank, sang, and brawled.","sentences":[{"en":"But the tax-collector, who dined there every day, complained bitterly of such companionship.","zh":"他躺在这里，哼哼唧唧，蒙着他的厚被窝，面无血色，胡须长长的，眼睛陷下去，头直冒汗，不时在落苍蝇的脏枕头上来回挪动。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then Hippolyte was removed to the billiard-room.","zh":"他躺在这里，哼哼唧唧，蒙着他的厚被窝，面无血色，胡须长长的，眼睛陷下去，头直冒汗，不时在落苍蝇的脏枕头上来回挪动。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He lay there moaning under his heavy coverings, pale with long beard, sunken eyes, and from time to time turning his perspiring head on the dirty pillow, where the flies alighted.","zh":"包法利夫人看望他，还给他带了敷药的布来，一边安慰他，一边鼓励他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Madame Bovary went to see him.","zh":"包法利夫人看望他，还给他带了敷药的布来，一边安慰他，一边鼓励他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She brought him linen for his poultices; she comforted, and encouraged him.","zh":"其实他不缺人陪伴，尤其是赶集的日子，乡下人在他的周围打弹子，拿起杆子比剑，吸着烟，喝着酒，又唱歌，又嚷嚷。他们拍着他的肩膀道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Besides, he did not want for company, especially on market-days, when the peasants were knocking about the billiard-balls round him, fenced with the cues, smoked, drank, sang, and brawled.","zh":"其实他不缺人陪伴，尤其是赶集的日子，乡下人在他的周围打弹子，拿起杆子比剑，吸着烟，喝着酒，又唱歌，又嚷嚷。他们拍着他的肩膀道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“How are you?” they said, clapping him on the shoulder. “Ah! you’re not up to much, it seems, but it’s your own fault. You should do this! do that!” And then they told him stories of people who had all been cured by other remedies than his. Then by way of consolation they added—","sentences":[{"en":"“How are you?” they said, clapping him on the shoulder.","zh":"“怎么样？啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Ah! you’re not up to much, it seems, but it’s your own fault.","zh":"看样子，你情绪不高呀！不过是你不对。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You should do this! do that!”","zh":"你该这么的，那么的。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then they told him stories of people who had all been cured by other remedies than his.","zh":"于是他们同他讲起别人，不用他的法子，用旁的法子，都治好了，接着，像安慰他似的，又讲道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then by way of consolation they added—","zh":"于是他们同他讲起别人，不用他的法子，用旁的法子，都治好了，接着，像安慰他似的，又讲道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You give way too much! Get up! You coddle yourself like a king! All the same, old chap, you don’t smell nice!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You give way too much!","zh":"“你太迁就自己啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Get up!","zh":"起来吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You coddle yourself like a king!","zh":"你把自己娇养得活像一位国王！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All the same, old chap, you don’t smell nice!”","zh":"啊！坏小子！你身上气味可不好闻。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Gangrene, in fact, was spreading more and more. Bovary himself turned sick at it. He came every hour, every moment. Hippolyte looked at him with eyes full of terror, sobbing—","sentences":[{"en":"Gangrene, in fact, was spreading more and more.","zh":"痈确实越来越往上走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bovary himself turned sick at it.","zh":"包法利自己也像病了一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He came every hour, every moment.","zh":"他时时刻刻来。伊玻立特望着他，一双眼睛惊恐万分，期期艾艾，呜呜咽咽道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Hippolyte looked at him with eyes full of terror, sobbing—","zh":"他时时刻刻来。伊玻立特望着他，一双眼睛惊恐万分，期期艾艾，呜呜咽咽道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“When shall I get well? Oh, save me! How unfortunate I am! How unfortunate I am!”","sentences":[{"en":"“When shall I get well?","zh":"“我什么时候可以好？啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, save me!","zh":"救救我！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How unfortunate I am!","zh":"我真倒霉！我真倒霉！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How unfortunate I am!”","zh":"医生临走，总劝他少吃东西。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the doctor left, always recommending him to diet himself.","sentences":[{"en":"And the doctor left, always recommending him to diet himself.","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太等他走了，就说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Don’t listen to him, my lad,” said Mere Lefrancois, “Haven’t they tortured you enough already? You’ll grow still weaker. Here! swallow this.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t listen to him, my lad,” said Mere Lefrancois, “Haven’t they tortured you enough already?","zh":"“别听他的话，我的孩子；他们已经把你害够了！吃得少你只会虚弱下去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"You’ll grow still weaker.","zh":"“别听他的话，我的孩子；他们已经把你害够了！吃得少你只会虚弱下去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Here! swallow this.”","zh":"来，大口吃吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she gave him some good beef-tea, a slice of mutton, a piece of bacon, and sometimes small glasses of brandy, that he had not the strength to put to his lips.","sentences":[{"en":"And she gave him some good beef-tea, a slice of mutton, a piece of bacon, and sometimes small glasses of brandy, that he had not the strength to put to his lips.","zh":"她于是给他端来好肉汤、几片羊肉、几块腌肉，偶尔还来几小杯酒，不过他没有勇气端到嘴唇跟前。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Abbe Bournisien, hearing that he was growing worse, asked to see him. He began by pitying his sufferings, declaring at the same time that he ought to rejoice at them since it was the will of the Lord, and take advantage of the occasion to reconcile himself to Heaven.","sentences":[{"en":"Abbe Bournisien, hearing that he was growing worse, asked to see him.","zh":"布尔尼贤堂长听说他病转重了，希望看看他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He began by pitying his sufferings, declaring at the same time that he ought to rejoice at them since it was the will of the Lord, and take advantage of the occasion to reconcile himself to Heaven.","zh":"开头他表示同情，不过又讲：既然主要他病，他就该欢喜才是，同时就该赶快利用机会，请求上天饶恕。教士用严父口吻道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For,” said the ecclesiastic in a paternal tone, “you rather neglected your duties; you were rarely seen at divine worship. How many years is it since you approached the holy table? I understand that your work, that the whirl of the world may have kept you from care for your salvation. But now is the time to reflect. Yet don’t despair. I have known great sinners, who, about to appear before God (you are not yet at this point I know), had implored His mercy, and who certainly died in the best frame of mind. Let us hope that, like them, you will set us a good example. Thus, as a precaution, what is to prevent you from saying morning and evening a ‘Hail Mary, full of grace,’ and ‘Our Father which art in heaven’? Yes, do that, for my sake, to oblige me. That won’t cost you anything. Will you promise me?”","sentences":[{"en":"“For,” said the ecclesiastic in a paternal tone, “you rather neglected your duties; you were rarely seen at divine worship.","zh":"“因为你不怎么尽本分；我很少看见你做礼拜；你领圣体以来，又有多少年没有来啦？","scope":"group"},{"en":"How many years is it since you approached the holy table?","zh":"“因为你不怎么尽本分；我很少看见你做礼拜；你领圣体以来，又有多少年没有来啦？","scope":"group"},{"en":"I understand that your work, that the whirl of the world may have kept you from care for your salvation.","zh":"我晓得你生活忙碌，尘事纷扰，你一时想不到拯救灵魂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But now is the time to reflect.","zh":"不过现在，该是想想这个的时候了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Yet don’t despair.","zh":"不过现在，该是想想这个的时候了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I have known great sinners, who, about to appear before God (you are not yet at this point I know), had implored His mercy, and who certainly died in the best frame of mind.","zh":"可是也不必难过；我就认识好些人，犯过大罪，快到上帝面前受审时（我知道，你还没有到这一步），再三求他开恩，过后当然也就心到福到，安安宁宁咽了气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let us hope that, like them, you will set us a good example.","zh":"希望你像他们一样，也给大家做个好榜样！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus, as a precaution, what is to prevent you from saying morning and evening a ‘Hail Mary, full of grace,’ and ‘Our Father which art in heaven’?","zh":"所以就该早作准备才是。那么，谁拦着你每天早晚，先说一遍，‘敬礼马利亚’和‘我们在天上的父’ ？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yes, do that, for my sake, to oblige me.","zh":"是啊，做吧！就算为了我，为了讨我欢喜！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That won’t cost you anything.","zh":"这又费得了什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Will you promise me?”","zh":"你答应不答应？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The poor devil promised. The cure came back day after day. He chatted with the landlady; and even told anecdotes interspersed with jokes and puns that Hippolyte did not understand. Then, as soon as he could, he fell back upon matters of religion, putting on an appropriate expression of face.","sentences":[{"en":"The poor devil promised.","zh":"可怜虫答应了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The cure came back day after day.","zh":"堂长接连来了几天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He chatted with the landlady; and even told anecdotes interspersed with jokes and puns that Hippolyte did not understand.","zh":"他和女店家闲话三七，甚至还讲掌故，夹杂一些逗哏的话和伊玻立特听不懂的双关语。情形一许可，他就换上一副合适的脸相，又谈宗教问题。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, as soon as he could, he fell back upon matters of religion, putting on an appropriate expression of face.","zh":"他和女店家闲话三七，甚至还讲掌故，夹杂一些逗哏的话和伊玻立特听不懂的双关语。情形一许可，他就换上一副合适的脸相，又谈宗教问题。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"His zeal seemed successful, for the club-foot soon manifested a desire to go on a pilgrimage to Bon-Secours if he were cured; to which Monsieur Bournisien replied that he saw no objection; two precautions were better than one; it was no risk anyhow.","sentences":[{"en":"His zeal seemed successful, for the club-foot soon manifested a desire to go on a pilgrimage to Bon-Secours if he were cured; to which Monsieur Bournisien replied that he saw no objection; two precautions were better than one; it was no risk anyhow.","zh":"他的热心似乎有了收获；因为畸形足患者不久表示：他要是病好了的话，愿意朝拜普济 去。布尔尼贤先生听了这话，回答：他看不出这有什么不妥；采取两项措施，总比一项措施强。反正没坏处。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The druggist was indignant at what he called the manoeuvres of the priest; they were prejudicial, he said, to Hippolyte’s convalescence, and he kept repeating to Madame Lefrancois, “Leave him alone! leave him alone! You perturb his morals with your mysticism.” But the good woman would no longer listen to him; he was the cause of it all. From a spirit of contradiction she hung up near the bedside of the patient a basin filled with holy-water and a branch of box.","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist was indignant at what he called the manoeuvres of the priest; they were prejudicial, he said, to Hippolyte’s convalescence, and he kept repeating to Madame Lefrancois, “Leave him alone! leave him alone!","zh":"药剂师愤恨他所谓的“教士策略”，认为妨碍伊玻立特复元，再三劝勒弗朗索瓦太太道：“别吵他！别吵他！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You perturb his morals with your mysticism.”","zh":"你的神秘主义只会扰乱他的精神！”但是善心的太太不理会他这一套。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But the good woman would no longer listen to him; he was the cause of it all.","zh":"你的神秘主义只会扰乱他的精神！”但是善心的太太不理会他这一套。","scope":"group"},{"en":"From a spirit of contradiction she hung up near the bedside of the patient a basin filled with holy-water and a branch of box.","zh":"他是祸根。她有意作对，在病人床头挂了一个满满的圣水瓶，里头插一枝黄杨。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Religion, however, seemed no more able to succour him than surgery, and the invincible gangrene still spread from the extremities towards the stomach. It was all very well to vary the potions and change the poultices; the muscles each day rotted more and more; and at last Charles replied by an affirmative nod of the head when Mere Lefrancois, asked him if she could not, as a forlorn hope, send for Monsieur Canivet of Neufchâtel, who was a celebrity.","sentences":[{"en":"Religion, however, seemed no more able to succour him than surgery, and the invincible gangrene still spread from the extremities towards the stomach.","zh":"然而宗教也像外科一样，似乎无能为力，坏疽所向无敌，一直在朝肚子蔓延。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was all very well to vary the potions and change the poultices; the muscles each day rotted more and more; and at last Charles replied by an affirmative nod of the head when Mere Lefrancois, asked him if she could not, as a forlorn hope, send for Monsieur Canivet of Neufchâtel, who was a celebrity.","zh":"改药水，换药膏，一无用处，眼看肌肉一天天烂下去，最后，勒弗朗索瓦太太请教查理：她好不好尽尽人事，邀一下新堡的名医卡尼韦？查理只好点点头，表示赞成。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A doctor of medicine, fifty years of age, enjoying a good position and self-possessed, Charles’s colleague did not refrain from laughing disdainfully when he had uncovered the leg, mortified to the knee. Then having flatly declared that it must be amputated, he went off to the chemist’s to rail at the asses who could have reduced a poor man to such a state. Shaking Monsieur Homais by the button of his coat, he shouted out in the shop—","sentences":[{"en":"A doctor of medicine, fifty years of age, enjoying a good position and self-possessed, Charles’s colleague did not refrain from laughing disdainfully when he had uncovered the leg, mortified to the knee.","zh":"这位同业是一位医学博士，五十岁，有地位，自信心强，发现这条腿一直烂到膝盖，毫无克制地发出鄙夷的笑声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then having flatly declared that it must be amputated, he went off to the chemist’s to rail at the asses who could have reduced a poor man to such a state.","zh":"他宣布必须把腿割掉，然后去了药房，臭骂那些蠢材，把一个倒霉蛋坑到这步田地。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Shaking Monsieur Homais by the button of his coat, he shouted out in the shop—","zh":"他抓住郝麦先生的大衣纽扣，边摇，边在药房谩骂道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“These are the inventions of Paris! These are the ideas of those gentry of the capital! It is like strabismus, chloroform, lithotrity, a heap of monstrosities that the Government ought to prohibit. But they want to do the clever, and they cram you with remedies without, troubling about the consequences. We are not so clever, not we! We are not savants, coxcombs, fops! We are practitioners; we cure people, and we should not dream of operating on anyone who is in perfect health. Straighten club-feet! As if one could straighten club-feet! It is as if one wished, for example, to make a hunchback straight!”","sentences":[{"en":"“These are the inventions of Paris!","zh":"“这就是巴黎的发明！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"These are the ideas of those gentry of the capital!","zh":"京城先生们的高见！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is like strabismus, chloroform, lithotrity, a heap of monstrosities that the Government ought to prohibit.","zh":"这和斜视、麻醉药、膀胱石扫除手术 一样，荒诞不经，政府应该加以禁止！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But they want to do the clever, and they cram you with remedies without, troubling about the consequences.","zh":"可是人家假装内行，不问结果，乱塞药给你吃！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We are not so clever, not we!","zh":"我们不像人家那样有本领；我们不是学者；我们不会异想天开，给大好一个常人行手术！","scope":"group"},{"en":"We are not savants, coxcombs, fops!","zh":"我们不像人家那样有本领；我们不是学者；我们不会异想天开，给大好一个常人行手术！","scope":"group"},{"en":"We are practitioners; we cure people, and we should not dream of operating on anyone who is in perfect health.","zh":"我们不像人家那样有本领；我们不是学者；我们不会异想天开，给大好一个常人行手术！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Straighten club-feet!","zh":"治好跷脚？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As if one could straighten club-feet!","zh":"谁能治好跷脚？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is as if one wished, for example, to make a hunchback straight!”","zh":"简直就像，好比说，叫驼背挺直脊梁骨！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais suffered as he listened to this discourse, and he concealed his discomfort beneath a courtier’s smile; for he needed to humour Monsier Canivet, whose prescriptions sometimes came as far as Yonville. So he did not take up the defence of Bovary; he did not even make a single remark, and, renouncing his principles, he sacrificed his dignity to the more serious interests of his business.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais suffered as he listened to this discourse, and he concealed his discomfort beneath a courtier’s smile; for he needed to humour Monsier Canivet, whose prescriptions sometimes came as far as Yonville.","zh":"郝麦听这篇演说，起了一身鸡皮疙瘩，不过心里尽管不自在，照样满脸谄媚的笑容，因为卡尼韦先生的药方有时候也在永镇出现，非拉拢不可；所以他也就不帮包法利辩护，甚至不发一言，放弃原则，为了商业上更重大的利益，牺牲他的尊严。","scope":"group"},{"en":"So he did not take up the defence of Bovary; he did not even make a single remark, and, renouncing his principles, he sacrificed his dignity to the more serious interests of his business.","zh":"郝麦听这篇演说，起了一身鸡皮疙瘩，不过心里尽管不自在，照样满脸谄媚的笑容，因为卡尼韦先生的药方有时候也在永镇出现，非拉拢不可；所以他也就不帮包法利辩护，甚至不发一言，放弃原则，为了商业上更重大的利益，牺牲他的尊严。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"This amputation of the thigh by Doctor Canivet was a great event in the village. On that day all the inhabitants got up earlier, and the Grande Rue, although full of people, had something lugubrious about it, as if an execution had been expected. At the grocer’s they discussed Hippolyte’s illness; the shops did no business, and Madame Tuvache, the mayor’s wife, did not stir from her window, such was her impatience to see the operator arrive.","sentences":[{"en":"This amputation of the thigh by Doctor Canivet was a great event in the village.","zh":"卡尼韦博士割大腿，成了镇上一件大事！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On that day all the inhabitants got up earlier, and the Grande Rue, although full of people, had something lugubrious about it, as if an execution had been expected.","zh":"这一天，个个居民早起。大街挤满了人，不过景象有些凄惨，好像观看死刑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the grocer’s they discussed Hippolyte’s illness; the shops did no business, and Madame Tuvache, the mayor’s wife, did not stir from her window, such was her impatience to see the operator arrive.","zh":"杂货铺有人讨论伊玻立特的病；商店停止营业；镇长太太杜法赦夫人，害怕看不到外科医生路过，守着窗户，只是不走。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He came in his gig, which he drove himself. But the springs of the right side having at length given way beneath the weight of his corpulence, it happened that the carriage as it rolled along leaned over a little, and on the other cushion near him could be seen a large box covered in red sheep-leather, whose three brass clasps shone grandly.","sentences":[{"en":"He came in his gig, which he drove himself.","zh":"他亲自吆喝着他的轻便马车来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the springs of the right side having at length given way beneath the weight of his corpulence, it happened that the carriage as it rolled along leaned over a little, and on the other cushion near him could be seen a large box covered in red sheep-leather, whose three brass clasps shone grandly.","zh":"但是马车走起来，有一点歪斜，原因是他身子沉重，日子久了，右边弹簧压了下去。旁边另一只坐垫，放着一个老大盒子，上面盖着红羊皮，三个铜襻，亮光光的，威仪凛凛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After he had entered like a whirlwind the porch of the “Lion d’Or,” the doctor, shouting very loud, ordered them to unharness his horse. Then he went into the stable to see that she was eating her oats all right; for on arriving at a patient’s he first of all looked after his mare and his gig. People even said about this—","sentences":[{"en":"After he had entered like a whirlwind the porch of the “Lion d’Or,” the doctor, shouting very loud, ordered them to unharness his horse.","zh":"马车旋风似的，进了金狮门厅，博士大喊大叫，要人卸马，然后走进马棚，看是不是喂它荞麦；因为他出诊时，首先挂心的，总是他的母马和他的轻便马车。提起这话，大家就说：“啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he went into the stable to see that she was eating her oats all right; for on arriving at a patient’s he first of all looked after his mare and his gig.","zh":"马车旋风似的，进了金狮门厅，博士大喊大叫，要人卸马，然后走进马棚，看是不是喂它荞麦；因为他出诊时，首先挂心的，总是他的母马和他的轻便马车。提起这话，大家就说：“啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"People even said about this—","zh":"卡尼韦先生呀，他是一个怪人！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ah! Monsieur Canivet’s a character!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"卡尼韦先生呀，他是一个怪人！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Canivet’s a character!”","zh":"卡尼韦先生呀，他是一个怪人！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And he was the more esteemed for this imperturbable coolness. The universe to the last man might have died, and he would not have missed the smallest of his habits.","sentences":[{"en":"And he was the more esteemed for this imperturbable coolness.","zh":"你别看他泰然自若，旁若无人，可是大家反而更敬重他。世上人即使死绝了，他的习惯也不会有丝毫改变。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The universe to the last man might have died, and he would not have missed the smallest of his habits.","zh":"你别看他泰然自若，旁若无人，可是大家反而更敬重他。世上人即使死绝了，他的习惯也不会有丝毫改变。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Homais presented himself.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais presented himself.","zh":"郝麦露面了，博士道：“我正需要你。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I count on you,” said the doctor. “Are we ready? Come along!”","sentences":[{"en":"“I count on you,” said the doctor.","zh":"郝麦露面了，博士道：“我正需要你。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Are we ready?","zh":"齐备了吧？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Come along!”","zh":"开步走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the druggist, turning red, confessed that he was too sensitive to assist at such an operation.","sentences":[{"en":"But the druggist, turning red, confessed that he was too sensitive to assist at such an operation.","zh":"但是药剂师面红耳赤，不打自招，说他过于敏感，不便参与这种手术。他讲：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“When one is a simple spectator,” he said, “the imagination, you know, is impressed. And then I have such a nervous system!”","sentences":[{"en":"“When one is a simple spectator,” he said, “the imagination, you know, is impressed.","zh":"“一个人光在旁边看，您知道，想象容易受到刺激！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then I have such a nervous system!”","zh":"再说，我的神经组织非常…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Pshaw!” interrupted Canivet; “on the contrary, you seem to me inclined to apoplexy. Besides, that doesn’t astonish me, for you chemist fellows are always poking about your kitchens, which must end by spoiling your constitutions. Now just look at me. I get up every day at four o’clock; I shave with cold water (and am never cold). I don’t wear flannels, and I never catch cold; my carcass is good enough! I live now in one way, now in another, like a philosopher, taking pot-luck; that is why I am not squeamish like you, and it is as indifferent to me to carve a Christian as the first fowl that turns up. Then, perhaps, you will say, habit! habit!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Pshaw!” interrupted Canivet; “on the contrary, you seem to me inclined to apoplexy.","zh":"卡尼韦打断道：“得啦！依我看，恰巧相反，您容易中风。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, that doesn’t astonish me, for you chemist fellows are always poking about your kitchens, which must end by spoiling your constitutions.","zh":"其实，不足为奇；因为你们药剂师先生，老是蹲在配方室，久而久之，体质必然受损害。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Now just look at me.","zh":"其实，不足为奇；因为你们药剂师先生，老是蹲在配方室，久而久之，体质必然受损害。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I get up every day at four o’clock; I shave with cold water (and am never cold).","zh":"您看我：天天四点钟起床，拿凉水刮胡子（我从来不怕冷），不穿法兰绒，也不害感冒，身子骨儿才叫棒！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I don’t wear flannels, and I never catch cold; my carcass is good enough!","zh":"您看我：天天四点钟起床，拿凉水刮胡子（我从来不怕冷），不穿法兰绒，也不害感冒，身子骨儿才叫棒！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I live now in one way, now in another, like a philosopher, taking pot-luck; that is why I am not squeamish like you, and it is as indifferent to me to carve a Christian as the first fowl that turns up.","zh":"东一顿，西一顿，有什么吃什么，绝不挑剔。所以我也就不像你们这样娇嫩，拿刀割起基督徒来，才像宰鸡宰鸭一样，根本不放在心上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, perhaps, you will say, habit! habit!”","zh":"你们听了这话，要说啦，习惯…习惯…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, without any consideration for Hippolyte, who was sweating with agony between his sheets, these gentlemen entered into a conversation, in which the druggist compared the coolness of a surgeon to that of a general; and this comparison was pleasing to Canivet, who launched out on the exigencies of his art. He looked upon, it as a sacred office, although the ordinary practitioners dishonoured it. At last, coming back to the patient, he examined the bandages brought by Homais, the same that had appeared for the club-foot, and asked for someone to hold the limb for him. Lestiboudois was sent for, and Monsieur Canivet having turned up his sleeves, passed into the billiard-room, while the druggist stayed with Artémise and the landlady, both whiter than their aprons, and with ears strained towards the door.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, without any consideration for Hippolyte, who was sweating with agony between his sheets, these gentlemen entered into a conversation, in which the druggist compared the coolness of a surgeon to that of a general; and this comparison was pleasing to Canivet, who launched out on the exigencies of his art.","zh":"于是两位先生一点也不管伊玻立特在被窝里头焦急出汗，大谈特谈起来。一位外科医生，在药剂师看来，就和一位将军同样冷静。卡尼韦爱听这种比较，滔滔不绝，谈论行医的条件，把医道看成一种神圣事业，虽然普通考试出身的医生玷辱了它。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He looked upon, it as a sacred office, although the ordinary practitioners dishonoured it.","zh":"于是两位先生一点也不管伊玻立特在被窝里头焦急出汗，大谈特谈起来。一位外科医生，在药剂师看来，就和一位将军同样冷静。卡尼韦爱听这种比较，滔滔不绝，谈论行医的条件，把医道看成一种神圣事业，虽然普通考试出身的医生玷辱了它。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last, coming back to the patient, he examined the bandages brought by Homais, the same that had appeared for the club-foot, and asked for someone to hold the limb for him.","zh":"最后，谈到眼前的病人，他检查郝麦带来的绷带、作跷脚手术用过的绷带，要一个人帮他捧住坏腿。他们派人去找赖斯地布杜瓦来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lestiboudois was sent for, and Monsieur Canivet having turned up his sleeves, passed into the billiard-room, while the druggist stayed with Artémise and the landlady, both whiter than their aprons, and with ears strained towards the door.","zh":"卡尼韦先生卷起袖管，走进弹子房，药剂师在这期间，和阿尔泰蜜丝、女店家待在一起。两个女人全拿耳朵贴住门，脸比她们的围裙还白。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Bovary during this time did not dare to stir from his house.","sentences":[{"en":"Bovary during this time did not dare to stir from his house.","zh":"包法利在这期间，一步不敢走出家门。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He kept downstairs in the sitting-room by the side of the fireless chimney, his chin on his breast, his hands clasped, his eyes staring. “What a mishap!” he thought, “what a mishap!” Perhaps, after all, he had made some slip. He thought it over, but could hit upon nothing. But the most famous surgeons also made mistakes; and that is what no one would ever believe! People, on the contrary, would laugh, jeer! It would spread as far as Forges, as Neufchâtel, as Rouen, everywhere! Who could say if his colleagues would not write against him. Polemics would ensue; he would have to answer in the papers. Hippolyte might even prosecute him. He saw himself dishonoured, ruined, lost; and his imagination, assailed by a world of hypotheses, tossed amongst them like an empty cask borne by the sea and floating upon the waves.","sentences":[{"en":"He kept downstairs in the sitting-room by the side of the fireless chimney, his chin on his breast, his hands clasped, his eyes staring.","zh":"他坐在底下厅房，靠近没有生火的壁炉，下巴搭在胸口，手握在一起，两眼发直。他寻思道：真不走运！真是失望！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“What a mishap!” he thought, “what a mishap!”","zh":"其实，事前的预防工作，应有尽有，他也全做到了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps, after all, he had made some slip.","zh":"命该如此。有什么关系？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He thought it over, but could hit upon nothing.","zh":"万一伊玻立特死了的话，害他的还不就是自己？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the most famous surgeons also made mistakes; and that is what no one would ever believe!","zh":"再说，看病中间，有人问起，他拿什么话对答？难道他真有什么地方错了不成？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People, on the contrary, would laugh, jeer!","zh":"左思右想，他想不出错在什么地方。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It would spread as far as Forges, as Neufchâtel, as Rouen, everywhere!","zh":"名望最高的外科医生，照样也犯错误。可是人们偏偏不肯相信？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who could say if his colleagues would not write against him.","zh":"而且相反，人家要笑他，骂他！话会传到福尔吉！新堡！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Polemics would ensue; he would have to answer in the papers.","zh":"鲁昂！天涯海角！谁知道同业中间，会不会有人写文章攻击他？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hippolyte might even prosecute him.","zh":"笔战一出现，他就得在报上回答。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He saw himself dishonoured, ruined, lost; and his imagination, assailed by a world of hypotheses, tossed amongst them like an empty cask borne by the sea and floating upon the waves.","zh":"伊玻立特很可能告他一状。他看见自己出丑、破产、毁灭！心里左一个假定，右一个假定，他的想象在中间忽上忽下，仿佛一只空桶，随波逐浪，翻来滚去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma, opposite, watched him; she did not share his humiliation; she felt another—that of having supposed such a man was worth anything. As if twenty times already she had not sufficiently perceived his mediocrity.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, opposite, watched him; she did not share his humiliation; she felt another—that of having supposed such a man was worth anything.","zh":"爱玛坐在对面望他；她并没感觉到他的耻辱，她感到的是另一种耻辱：这样一个人，她先前怎么会指望他有出息，好像他庸碌无能，她看了二十回，还没有看透一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"As if twenty times already she had not sufficiently perceived his mediocrity.","zh":"爱玛坐在对面望他；她并没感觉到他的耻辱，她感到的是另一种耻辱：这样一个人，她先前怎么会指望他有出息，好像他庸碌无能，她看了二十回，还没有看透一样。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles was walking up and down the room; his boots creaked on the floor.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles was walking up and down the room; his boots creaked on the floor.","zh":"查理在房里踱来踱去。靴子嘎吱直响。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sit down,” she said; “you fidget me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sit down,” she said; “you fidget me.”","zh":"“坐下吧，把人烦死！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He sat down again.","sentences":[{"en":"He sat down again.","zh":"他又坐下。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"How was it that she—she, who was so intelligent—could have allowed herself to be deceived again? and through what deplorable madness had she thus ruined her life by continual sacrifices? She recalled all her instincts of luxury, all the privations of her soul, the sordidness of marriage, of the household, her dream sinking into the mire like wounded swallows; all that she had longed for, all that she had denied herself, all that she might have had! And for what? for what?","sentences":[{"en":"How was it that she—she, who was so intelligent—could have allowed herself to be deceived again? and through what deplorable madness had she thus ruined her life by continual sacrifices?","zh":"她怎么会（她这样聪明的人！）又做错了事的？再说，她怎么会天差地错，痴心妄想，就这样一而再，再而三，白白牺牲她的一生的？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She recalled all her instincts of luxury, all the privations of her soul, the sordidness of marriage, of the household, her dream sinking into the mire like wounded swallows; all that she had longed for, all that she had denied herself, all that she might have had!","zh":"她想起她爱好奢华的种种本能、她心灵上享受不到的种种东西、婚姻和家庭生活的微贱、她那像受伤的燕子跌进泥淖般的绮梦、她向往的一切、她放弃的一切、她可能得到的一切！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And for what? for what?","zh":"为什么她得不到，为什么？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the midst of the silence that hung over the village a heart-rending cry rose on the air. Bovary turned white to fainting. She knit her brows with a nervous gesture, then went on. And it was for him, for this creature, for this man, who understood nothing, who felt nothing! For he was there quite quiet, not even suspecting that the ridicule of his name would henceforth sully hers as well as his. She had made efforts to love him, and she had repented with tears for having yielded to another!","sentences":[{"en":"In the midst of the silence that hung over the village a heart-rending cry rose on the air.","zh":"安安静静的镇子，破空起了一声尖叫。包法利脸色转白，险些晕倒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bovary turned white to fainting.","zh":"她做了一个心烦的手势，皱紧眉头，接着又寻思下去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She knit her brows with a nervous gesture, then went on.","zh":"她做了一个心烦的手势，皱紧眉头，接着又寻思下去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And it was for him, for this creature, for this man, who understood nothing, who felt nothing!","zh":"然而就是为了他，为了这家伙，为了这个什么也不懂、什么也感觉不到的男子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For he was there quite quiet, not even suspecting that the ridicule of his name would henceforth sully hers as well as his.","zh":"因为他坐在那边，安安静静，想也不想，从今以后，他的可笑的名姓不但玷辱他，而且还玷辱她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had made efforts to love him, and she had repented with tears for having yielded to another!","zh":"她曾经试着爱他来着，她曾经哭哭啼啼，后悔顺从另一个男子来的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But it was perhaps a valgus!” suddenly exclaimed Bovary, who was meditating.","sentences":[{"en":"“But it was perhaps a valgus!” suddenly exclaimed Bovary, who was meditating.","zh":"包法利出神冥想，忽然喊道：“也许是里拐型吧？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At the unexpected shock of this phrase falling on her thought like a leaden bullet on a silver plate, Emma, shuddering, raised her head in order to find out what he meant to say; and they looked at the other in silence, almost amazed to see each other, so far sundered were they by their inner thoughts. Charles gazed at her with the dull look of a drunken man, while he listened motionless to the last cries of the sufferer, that followed each other in long-drawn modulations, broken by sharp spasms like the far-off howling of some beast being slaughtered. Emma bit her wan lips, and rolling between her fingers a piece of coral that she had broken, fixed on Charles the burning glance of her eyes like two arrows of fire about to dart forth. Everything in him irritated her now; his face, his dress, what he did not say, his whole person, his existence, in fine. She repented of her past virtue as of a crime, and what still remained of it rumbled away beneath the furious blows of her pride. She revelled in all the evil ironies of triumphant adultery. The memory of her lover came back to her with dazzling attractions; she threw her whole soul into it, borne away towards this image with a fresh enthusiasm; and Charles seemed to her as much removed from her life, as absent forever, as impossible and annihilated, as if he had been about to die and were passing under her eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"At the unexpected shock of this phrase falling on her thought like a leaden bullet on a silver plate, Emma, shuddering, raised her head in order to find out what he meant to say; and they looked at the other in silence, almost amazed to see each other, so far sundered were they by their inner thoughts.","zh":"这句话脱口而出，冲撞她的思想，如同一颗铅球落在一只银盘，爱玛大吃一惊，仰起头来，猜他是什么意思。于是他们悄不做声，你望我，我望你，也正因为各想各的，忽然发觉身边有人，就几乎惊呆了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles gazed at her with the dull look of a drunken man, while he listened motionless to the last cries of the sufferer, that followed each other in long-drawn modulations, broken by sharp spasms like the far-off howling of some beast being slaughtered.","zh":"查理打量她，仿佛一个醉鬼，视线模糊，同时一动不动，听着病人割腿，发出最后的嘶喊，好像屠宰什么牲口一样，远远吼号，拉长声音，冷不防中间来一声尖叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma bit her wan lips, and rolling between her fingers a piece of coral that she had broken, fixed on Charles the burning glance of her eyes like two arrows of fire about to dart forth.","zh":"爱玛咬着她青灰的嘴唇，掰断一个珊瑚枝子，在手心搓来搓去，瞳仁亮晃晃的，仿佛两支就要射出去的火箭，目光炯炯，盯牢查理。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everything in him irritated her now; his face, his dress, what he did not say, his whole person, his existence, in fine.","zh":"他的脸、他的衣服、他没说出来的话、他的整个身子，总而言之，他的存在，如今她样样看了有气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She repented of her past virtue as of a crime, and what still remained of it rumbled away beneath the furious blows of her pride.","zh":"她后悔早先不该守身如玉，像后悔不该犯罪一样。残留的一点妇德，禁不住她的骄傲狂抽乱打，终于倒塌了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She revelled in all the evil ironies of triumphant adultery.","zh":"她欣赏胜利的奸淫的种种恶意揶揄。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The memory of her lover came back to her with dazzling attractions; she threw her whole soul into it, borne away towards this image with a fresh enthusiasm; and Charles seemed to her as much removed from her life, as absent forever, as impossible and annihilated, as if he had been about to die and were passing under her eyes.","zh":"情人的形象回到她的心头，光采奕奕。销魂动魄，一股新的热情卷带着她，不由她不献出她的灵魂。她觉得查理离开她的生命，永远走出，不再回来，杳无形迹，就像她眼睁睁看着他确实在死、在咽气一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"There was a sound of steps on the pavement. Charles looked up, and through the lowered blinds he saw at the corner of the market in the broad sunshine Dr. Canivet, who was wiping his brow with his handkerchief. Homais, behind him, was carrying a large red box in his hand, and both were going towards the chemist’s.","sentences":[{"en":"There was a sound of steps on the pavement.","zh":"便道响起了脚步声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles looked up, and through the lowered blinds he saw at the corner of the market in the broad sunshine Dr. Canivet, who was wiping his brow with his handkerchief.","zh":"查理从放下来的活动窗帘望出去，就见卡尼韦医生在菜场一旁太阳地，拿手绢擦额头的汗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais, behind him, was carrying a large red box in his hand, and both were going towards the chemist’s.","zh":"郝麦跟在后面，捧着一个大红盒子。两个人全朝药房走去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then with a feeling of sudden tenderness and discouragement Charles turned to his wife saying to her—","sentences":[{"en":"Then with a feeling of sudden tenderness and discouragement Charles turned to his wife saying to her—","zh":"于是查理心灰意懒，觉得自己忽然需要温暖，转向他的女人道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, kiss me, my own!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, kiss me, my own!”","zh":"“好人，亲亲我！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Leave me!” she said, red with anger.","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave me!” she said, red with anger.","zh":"她心头火起，气红了脸道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What is the matter?” he asked, stupefied. “Be calm; compose yourself. You know well enough that I love you. Come!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What is the matter?” he asked, stupefied.","zh":"“走开！”他一惊之下，做声不得，一遍又一遍重复道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Be calm; compose yourself.","zh":"“你怎么啦？你怎么啦？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You know well enough that I love you.","zh":"别急！想想看！你知道我爱你…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Come!”","zh":"来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Enough!” she cried with a terrible look.","sentences":[{"en":"“Enough!” she cried with a terrible look.","zh":"她气势汹汹，大声嚷道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And escaping from the room, Emma closed the door so violently that the barometer fell from the wall and smashed on the floor.","sentences":[{"en":"And escaping from the room, Emma closed the door so violently that the barometer fell from the wall and smashed on the floor.","zh":"“够啦！”爱玛溜出厅房，使劲拿门一带，墙上的晴雨计震到地上，摔碎了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles sank back into his arm-chair overwhelmed, trying to discover what could be wrong with her, fancying some nervous illness, weeping, and vaguely feeling something fatal and incomprehensible whirling round him.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles sank back into his arm-chair overwhelmed, trying to discover what could be wrong with her, fancying some nervous illness, weeping, and vaguely feeling something fatal and incomprehensible whirling round him.","zh":"查理倒进扶手椅，栖栖惶惶，寻思个中缘故，以为她是精神失常，眼泪纵横，觉得周围阴风惨惨，隐约感到有什么不可理解的不祥的东西在周围游来荡去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When Rodolphe came to the garden that evening, he found his mistress waiting for him at the foot of the steps on the lowest stair. They threw their arms round one another, and all their rancour melted like snow beneath the warmth of that kiss.","sentences":[{"en":"When Rodolphe came to the garden that evening, he found his mistress waiting for him at the foot of the steps on the lowest stair.","zh":"罗道耳弗晚上来到花园，发现他的情妇在台阶底下第一级等他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They threw their arms round one another, and all their rancour melted like snow beneath the warmth of that kiss.","zh":"他们搂成一团，怨恨像雪一样，在热吻之下消融了。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-12","part":2,"n":12,"title":"Part II · Chapter 12","titleZh":"中卷 · 12","paragraphs":[{"en":"They began to love one another again. Often, even in the middle of the day, Emma suddenly wrote to him, then from the window made a sign to Justin, who, taking his apron off, quickly ran to La Huchette. Rodolphe would come; she had sent for him to tell him that she was bored, that her husband was odious, her life frightful.","sentences":[{"en":"They began to love one another again.","zh":"他们又开始相爱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often, even in the middle of the day, Emma suddenly wrote to him, then from the window made a sign to Justin, who, taking his apron off, quickly ran to La Huchette.","zh":"甚至大白天，爱玛也心血来潮，动不动给他写信；信写好了，她隔着玻璃窗，朝朱斯丹做手势。朱斯丹连忙解开粗布围裙，飞也似的去了于歇特。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe would come; she had sent for him to tell him that she was bored, that her husband was odious, her life frightful.","zh":"罗道耳弗来了；原来就为告诉他：日子过得气闷，丈夫可憎，生活太不称心！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But what can I do?” he cried one day impatiently.","sentences":[{"en":"“But what can I do?” he cried one day impatiently.","zh":"他有一天不耐烦了，喊道：“我能有什么办法？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! if you would—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! if you would—”","zh":"“啊！只要你肯！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was sitting on the floor between his knees, her hair loose, her look lost.","sentences":[{"en":"She was sitting on the floor between his knees, her hair loose, her look lost.","zh":"她坐在地上他的两腿当中，头发辫子解开，视线恍恍惚惚。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, what?” said Rodolphe.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, what?” said Rodolphe.","zh":"罗道耳弗问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She sighed.","sentences":[{"en":"She sighed.","zh":"“肯什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We would go and live elsewhere—somewhere!”","sentences":[{"en":"“We would go and live elsewhere—somewhere!”","zh":"她叹气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are really mad!” he said laughing. “How could that be possible?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are really mad!” he said laughing.","zh":"“我们可以去别的地方过活…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“How could that be possible?”","zh":"随便一个地方…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She returned to the subject; he pretended not to understand, and turned the conversation.","sentences":[{"en":"She returned to the subject; he pretended not to understand, and turned the conversation.","zh":"他笑道：“真的，你疯啦！这怎么成？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"What he did not understand was all this worry about so simple an affair as love. She had a motive, a reason, and, as it were, a pendant to her affection.","sentences":[{"en":"What he did not understand was all this worry about so simple an affair as love.","zh":"她第二回又谈这话，他假装不懂，另找话讲，恋爱这事，再简单不过，他不明白怎么会这样混乱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had a motive, a reason, and, as it were, a pendant to her affection.","zh":"原来她另有一种动机、原因；这仿佛一支援军，接应她的眷恋。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her tenderness, in fact, grew each day with her repulsion to her husband. The more she gave up herself to the one, the more she loathed the other. Never had Charles seemed to her so disagreeable, to have such stodgy fingers, such vulgar ways, to be so dull as when they found themselves together after her meeting with Rodolphe. Then, while playing the spouse and virtue, she was burning at the thought of that head whose black hair fell in a curl over the sunburnt brow, of that form at once so strong and elegant, of that man, in a word, who had such experience in his reasoning, such passion in his desires. It was for him that she filed her nails with the care of a chaser, and that there was never enough cold-cream for her skin, nor of patchouli for her handkerchiefs. She loaded herself with bracelets, rings, and necklaces. When he was coming she filled the two large blue glass vases with roses, and prepared her room and her person like a courtesan expecting a prince. The servant had to be constantly washing linen, and all day Félicité did not stir from the kitchen, where little Justin, who often kept her company, watched her at work.","sentences":[{"en":"Her tenderness, in fact, grew each day with her repulsion to her husband.","zh":"这种恩情的确每天见长。缘故是她厌恶丈夫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The more she gave up herself to the one, the more she loathed the other.","zh":"她越倒向这一个，就越憎恨另一个；她同罗道耳弗幽会之后，再和查理在一起，分外嫌他讨厌，指头特别显得粗，人特别显得笨，举止特别显得庸俗。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Never had Charles seemed to her so disagreeable, to have such stodgy fingers, such vulgar ways, to be so dull as when they found themselves together after her meeting with Rodolphe.","zh":"她越倒向这一个，就越憎恨另一个；她同罗道耳弗幽会之后，再和查理在一起，分外嫌他讨厌，指头特别显得粗，人特别显得笨，举止特别显得庸俗。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, while playing the spouse and virtue, she was burning at the thought of that head whose black hair fell in a curl over the sunburnt brow, of that form at once so strong and elegant, of that man, in a word, who had such experience in his reasoning, such passion in his desires.","zh":"所以她虽然装出贤妻模样，可是想到另一个男子，她就淫心荡漾，按捺不住。人家是黑乌乌头发，梳成一个圈圈，朝太阳晒黑了的额头卷过去，腰身又结实，又俊雅，总而言之，判事富有经验，情之所至，却又如醉如痴！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was for him that she filed her nails with the care of a chaser, and that there was never enough cold-cream for her skin, nor of patchouli for her handkerchiefs.","zh":"也就是为了他，她才像镂刻匠一样，细心修剪指甲，皮肤上的冷霜，手帕上的香精，永远嫌少。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She loaded herself with bracelets, rings, and necklaces.","zh":"她戴镯子、戒指、项圈。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he was coming she filled the two large blue glass vases with roses, and prepared her room and her person like a courtesan expecting a prince.","zh":"她估量他要来了，两只碧琉璃大花瓶插满玫瑰花，收拾房间，打扮自己，活像一个妓女等候一位大贵人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The servant had to be constantly washing linen, and all day Félicité did not stir from the kitchen, where little Justin, who often kept her company, watched her at work.","zh":"女用人一天到晚洗呀浆的。全福从早到晚待在厨房，小朱斯丹常来陪她，看她做活。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"With his elbows on the long board on which she was ironing, he greedily watched all these women’s clothes spread about him, the dimity petticoats, the fichus, the collars, and the drawers with running strings, wide at the hips and growing narrower below.","sentences":[{"en":"With his elbows on the long board on which she was ironing, he greedily watched all these women’s clothes spread about him, the dimity petticoats, the fichus, the collars, and the drawers with running strings, wide at the hips and growing narrower below.","zh":"胳膊肘支着她熨衣服的长木板，他瞪直了眼，打量这些扔在四周的妇女什物：方格线呢裙子、肩巾、领披、屁股大裤管窄的连腰带女裤。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What is that for?” asked the young fellow, passing his hand over the crinoline or the hooks and eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"“What is that for?” asked the young fellow, passing his hand over the crinoline or the hooks and eyes.","zh":"小伙计拿手摸着硬衬或者挂钩，问道：“这做什么用？”全福带笑回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, haven’t you ever seen anything?” Félicité answered laughing. “As if your mistress, Madame Homais, didn’t wear the same.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, haven’t you ever seen anything?”","zh":"“你真就从来没有见过？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Félicité answered laughing.","zh":"倒像你的女东家，郝麦太太不穿这些东西似的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“As if your mistress, Madame Homais, didn’t wear the same.”","zh":"倒像你的女东家，郝麦太太不穿这些东西似的。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, I daresay! Madame Homais!” And he added with a meditative air, “As if she were a lady like madame!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I daresay!","zh":"“啊！是的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Homais!”","zh":"郝麦太太！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he added with a meditative air, “As if she were a lady like madame!”","zh":"他想了想，又道：“难道她像你家太太，也是贵妇人？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Félicité grew impatient of seeing him hanging round her. She was six years older than he, and Theodore, Monsieur Guillaumin’s servant, was beginning to pay court to her.","sentences":[{"en":"But Félicité grew impatient of seeing him hanging round her.","zh":"但是全福见他这样兜着自己打转，直不耐烦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was six years older than he, and Theodore, Monsieur Guillaumin’s servant, was beginning to pay court to her.","zh":"她比他大六岁多，居由曼的听差泰奥多尔开始向她求爱。她挪开糨糊缸道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Let me alone,” she said, moving her pot of starch. “You’d better be off and pound almonds; you are always dangling about women. Before you meddle with such things, bad boy, wait till you’ve got a beard to your chin.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Let me alone,” she said, moving her pot of starch.","zh":"“别搅我！你不如捣你的杏子去；你总是夹在女人堆里捣乱；小坏蛋，你想在女人堆里混呀，等你下巴颏长了胡子再说。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You’d better be off and pound almonds; you are always dangling about women.","zh":"“别搅我！你不如捣你的杏子去；你总是夹在女人堆里捣乱；小坏蛋，你想在女人堆里混呀，等你下巴颏长了胡子再说。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Before you meddle with such things, bad boy, wait till you’ve got a beard to your chin.”","zh":"“别搅我！你不如捣你的杏子去；你总是夹在女人堆里捣乱；小坏蛋，你想在女人堆里混呀，等你下巴颏长了胡子再说。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, don’t be cross! I’ll go and clean her boots.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, don’t be cross!","zh":"“得啦，别生气，我来替你擦干净她的小靴子去。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll go and clean her boots.”","zh":"“得啦，别生气，我来替你擦干净她的小靴子去。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And he at once took down from the shelf Emma’s boots, all coated with mud, the mud of the rendezvous, that crumbled into powder beneath his fingers, and that he watched as it gently rose in a ray of sunlight.","sentences":[{"en":"And he at once took down from the shelf Emma’s boots, all coated with mud, the mud of the rendezvous, that crumbled into powder beneath his fingers, and that he watched as it gently rose in a ray of sunlight.","zh":"他立时从架子上拿下爱玛的鞋来，上面沾满了泥——幽会的泥，他拿手一掰，就掉下来了，他望着屑子在阳光里慢慢上扬。女厨子道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How afraid you are of spoiling them!” said the servant, who wasn’t so particular when she cleaned them herself, because as soon as the stuff of the boots was no longer fresh madame handed them over to her.","sentences":[{"en":"“How afraid you are of spoiling them!” said the servant, who wasn’t so particular when she cleaned them herself, because as soon as the stuff of the boots was no longer fresh madame handed them over to her.","zh":"“你可真怕弄坏了鞋！”轮到她擦鞋，绝不在意，因为太太一看料子发旧，就送给她穿。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma had a number in her cupboard that she squandered one after the other, without Charles allowing himself the slightest observation. So also he disbursed three hundred francs for a wooden leg that she thought proper to make a present of to Hippolyte. Its top was covered with cork, and it had spring joints, a complicated mechanism, covered over by black trousers ending in a patent-leather boot. But Hippolyte, not daring to use such a handsome leg every day, begged Madame Bovary to get him another more convenient one. The doctor, of course, had again to defray the expense of this purchase.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma had a number in her cupboard that she squandered one after the other, without Charles allowing himself the slightest observation.","zh":"爱玛的衣橱里放着一大堆鞋，她一双一双糟蹋，查理从来没有说过半句闲话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So also he disbursed three hundred francs for a wooden leg that she thought proper to make a present of to Hippolyte.","zh":"她认为应当送伊玻立特一条木腿，他同样一声不吭，掏出三百法郎，买了一条木腿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Its top was covered with cork, and it had spring joints, a complicated mechanism, covered over by black trousers ending in a patent-leather boot.","zh":"木腿是一个复杂的机器，软木包头，弹簧关节，外头罩了一条黑裤，底下是一只漆皮靴子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Hippolyte, not daring to use such a handsome leg every day, begged Madame Bovary to get him another more convenient one.","zh":"可是这样漂亮的一条腿，伊玻立特不敢天天用，所以就求包法利夫人，帮他另弄一条平常好用的。当然又是医生出钱买了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The doctor, of course, had again to defray the expense of this purchase.","zh":"可是这样漂亮的一条腿，伊玻立特不敢天天用，所以就求包法利夫人，帮他另弄一条平常好用的。当然又是医生出钱买了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"So little by little the stable-man took up his work again. One saw him running about the village as before, and when Charles heard from afar the sharp noise of the wooden leg, he at once went in another direction.","sentences":[{"en":"So little by little the stable-man took up his work again.","zh":"马夫渐渐又忙活起来，只见他像早先一样，在村子里跑来跑去。查理一听见他的木腿顿石板路响，就赶快换一条路走。","scope":"group"},{"en":"One saw him running about the village as before, and when Charles heard from afar the sharp noise of the wooden leg, he at once went in another direction.","zh":"马夫渐渐又忙活起来，只见他像早先一样，在村子里跑来跑去。查理一听见他的木腿顿石板路响，就赶快换一条路走。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"It was Monsieur Lheureux, the shopkeeper, who had undertaken the order; this provided him with an excuse for visiting Emma. He chatted with her about the new goods from Paris, about a thousand feminine trifles, made himself very obliging, and never asked for his money. Emma yielded to this lazy mode of satisfying all her caprices. Thus she wanted to have a very handsome ridding-whip that was at an umbrella-maker’s at Rouen to give to Rodolphe. The week after Monsieur Lheureux placed it on her table.","sentences":[{"en":"It was Monsieur Lheureux, the shopkeeper, who had undertaken the order; this provided him with an excuse for visiting Emma.","zh":"商人勒乐先生自告奋勇，接受木腿订货：这给他带来接近爱玛的机会。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He chatted with her about the new goods from Paris, about a thousand feminine trifles, made himself very obliging, and never asked for his money.","zh":"他同她谈起巴黎新出品、形形色色的妇女饰物，态度非常谦和，从不开口要钱。爱玛一时一种喜好，因为容易得到满足，也就由它去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma yielded to this lazy mode of satisfying all her caprices.","zh":"他同她谈起巴黎新出品、形形色色的妇女饰物，态度非常谦和，从不开口要钱。爱玛一时一种喜好，因为容易得到满足，也就由它去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Thus she wanted to have a very handsome ridding-whip that was at an umbrella-maker’s at Rouen to give to Rodolphe.","zh":"例如鲁昂一家伞庄，有一条极其漂亮的马鞭，她直想买下来，送罗道耳弗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The week after Monsieur Lheureux placed it on her table.","zh":"一星期后，勒乐先生就把马鞭放在她的桌子上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the next day he called on her with a bill for two hundred and seventy francs, not counting the centimes. Emma was much embarrassed; all the drawers of the writing-table were empty; they owed over a fortnight’s wages to Lestiboudois, two quarters to the servant, for any quantity of other things, and Bovary was impatiently expecting Monsieur Derozeray’s account, which he was in the habit of paying every year about Midsummer.","sentences":[{"en":"But the next day he called on her with a bill for two hundred and seventy francs, not counting the centimes.","zh":"但是第二天，他送过来一份账单，二百七十法郎，尾数不计。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma was much embarrassed; all the drawers of the writing-table were empty; they owed over a fortnight’s wages to Lestiboudois, two quarters to the servant, for any quantity of other things, and Bovary was impatiently expecting Monsieur Derozeray’s account, which he was in the habit of paying every year about Midsummer.","zh":"爱玛窘极了：只只抽屉是空的；他们还欠赖斯地布杜瓦半个月工资、女用人半年工资，有许多还不算计在内；包法利盼望德罗兹赖先生送钱，盼得两眼发直，因为他每年付清诊费，照例总在圣彼得节 前后。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She succeeded at first in putting off Lheureux. At last he lost patience; he was being sued; his capital was out, and unless he got some in he should be forced to take back all the goods she had received.","sentences":[{"en":"She succeeded at first in putting off Lheureux.","zh":"开头她总算把勒乐对付开了，可是后来他发急了，说是有人逼他，他缺现款，现款如果收不回一部分，她买下的货物，只好全部取走。爱玛道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last he lost patience; he was being sued; his capital was out, and unless he got some in he should be forced to take back all the goods she had received.","zh":"开头她总算把勒乐对付开了，可是后来他发急了，说是有人逼他，他缺现款，现款如果收不回一部分，她买下的货物，只好全部取走。爱玛道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, very well, take them!” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, very well, take them!” said Emma.","zh":"“取走好了！”他回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I was only joking,” he replied; “the only thing I regret is the whip. My word! I’ll ask monsieur to return it to me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was only joking,” he replied; “the only thing I regret is the whip.","zh":"“我是说着玩儿的！其实我也就是舍不得马鞭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My word!","zh":"好吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ll ask monsieur to return it to me.”","zh":"我向先生讨好了。”她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no!” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no!” she said.","zh":"“不！别向他讨！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! I’ve got you!” thought Lheureux.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"勒乐寻思道：这下子你跑不了啦！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ve got you!” thought Lheureux.","zh":"勒乐寻思道：这下子你跑不了啦！","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And, certain of his discovery, he went out repeating to himself in an undertone, and with his usual low whistle—","sentences":[{"en":"And, certain of his discovery, he went out repeating to himself in an undertone, and with his usual low whistle—","zh":"他于是成竹在胸，抓住她的把柄，一面朝外走，一面低声重复，照老习惯，嘴里发出微微的嘘嘘声：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Good! we shall see! we shall see!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Good! we shall see! we shall see!”","zh":"“就这么着！再说吧！再说吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was thinking how to get out of this when the servant coming in put on the mantelpiece a small roll of blue paper “from Monsieur Derozeray’s.” Emma pounced upon and opened it. It contained fifteen napoleons; it was the account. She heard Charles on the stairs; threw the gold to the back of her drawer, and took out the key.","sentences":[{"en":"She was thinking how to get out of this when the servant coming in put on the mantelpiece a small roll of blue paper “from Monsieur Derozeray’s.”","zh":"她正在寻思解围办法，女用人进来，拿一小卷蓝纸放在壁炉上：“德罗兹赖先生送来的。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma pounced upon and opened it.","zh":"爱玛扑过去，打开了，里面是他的诊费、十五块拿破仑 。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It contained fifteen napoleons; it was the account.","zh":"爱玛扑过去，打开了，里面是他的诊费、十五块拿破仑 。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She heard Charles on the stairs; threw the gold to the back of her drawer, and took out the key.","zh":"她听见查理走上楼梯；她拿钱丢进她的抽屉，锁好了，拔去钥匙。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Three days after Lheureux reappeared.","sentences":[{"en":"Three days after Lheureux reappeared.","zh":"三天之后，勒乐又出现了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I have an arrangement to suggest to you,” he said. “If, instead of the sum agreed on, you would take—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I have an arrangement to suggest to you,” he said.","zh":"他说：“我有一个办法；过去的账付不出就付不出，只要您肯借…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“If, instead of the sum agreed on, you would take—”","zh":"他说：“我有一个办法；过去的账付不出就付不出，只要您肯借…”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Here it is,” she said placing fourteen napoleons in his hand.","sentences":[{"en":"“Here it is,” she said placing fourteen napoleons in his hand.","zh":"她往他手里放下十四块拿破仑，道：“这不是！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The tradesman was dumfounded. Then, to conceal his disappointment, he was profuse in apologies and proffers of service, all of which Emma declined; then she remained a few moments fingering in the pocket of her apron the two five-franc pieces that he had given her in change. She promised herself she would economise in order to pay back later on. “Pshaw!” she thought, “he won’t think about it again.”","sentences":[{"en":"The tradesman was dumfounded.","zh":"商人惊呆了，于是掩饰失望，连声道歉，请她赏光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, to conceal his disappointment, he was profuse in apologies and proffers of service, all of which Emma declined; then she remained a few moments fingering in the pocket of her apron the two five-franc pieces that he had given her in change.","zh":"爱玛完全拒绝，然后手放在围裙袋里，摸着找回来的两个五法郎一枚的辅币，决心节省，将来好还…她转念道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She promised herself she would economise in order to pay back later on.","zh":"“啊！由它去！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Pshaw!” she thought, “he won’t think about it again.”","zh":"他想不到这上头的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Besides the riding-whip with its silver-gilt handle, Rodolphe had received a seal with the motto Amor nel cor; furthermore, a scarf for a muffler, and, finally, a cigar-case exactly like the Viscount’s, that Charles had formerly picked up in the road, and that Emma had kept. These presents, however, humiliated him; he refused several; she insisted, and he ended by obeying, thinking her tyrannical and overexacting.","sentences":[{"en":"Besides the riding-whip with its silver-gilt handle, Rodolphe had received a seal with the motto Amor nel cor; furthermore, a scarf for a muffler, and, finally, a cigar-case exactly like the Viscount’s, that Charles had formerly picked up in the road, and that Emma had kept.","zh":"除去银头镀金马鞭之外，罗道耳弗还收下一颗印章，上面刻着这句格言：“心心相印” 。另外还有一条围巾料子，最后还有一只雪茄匣，和子爵的雪茄匣一般模样，查理先前在路上捡到的，爱玛还保存着。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"These presents, however, humiliated him; he refused several; she insisted, and he ended by obeying, thinking her tyrannical and overexacting.","zh":"不过这些礼物使他难堪，有几件就谢绝了，她一坚持，罗道耳弗结局收是收了，不过嫌她盛气凌人，过分强人所难。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she had strange ideas.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she had strange ideas.","zh":"再说，她净是一些古怪念头。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“When midnight strikes,” she said, “you must think of me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“When midnight strikes,” she said, “you must think of me.”","zh":"“半夜听见钟响，你要想着我！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And if he confessed that he had not thought of her, there were floods of reproaches that always ended with the eternal question—","sentences":[{"en":"And if he confessed that he had not thought of her, there were floods of reproaches that always ended with the eternal question—","zh":"万一他老实说他没有想她的话，她就百般责备，临了总是这么一句话收场：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do you love me?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you love me?”","zh":"“你爱我吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, of course I love you,” he answered.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, of course I love you,” he answered.","zh":"他回答道：“是呀，我爱你！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“A great deal?”","sentences":[{"en":"“A great deal?”","zh":"“爱得厉害？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Certainly!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Certainly!”","zh":"“当然！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You haven’t loved any others?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You haven’t loved any others?”","zh":"“你没有爱过别的女人，嗯？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Did you think you’d got a virgin?” he exclaimed laughing.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you think you’d got a virgin?” he exclaimed laughing.","zh":"他笑嚷道：“你以为我当初是童男啊？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma cried, and he tried to console her, adorning his protestations with puns.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma cried, and he tried to console her, adorning his protestations with puns.","zh":"爱玛哭了；他竭力安慰她，一面对天明心，一面说些俏皮话，调剂气氛。她讲道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh,” she went on, “I love you! I love you so that I could not live without you, do you see? There are times when I long to see you again, when I am torn by all the anger of love. I ask myself, Where is he? Perhaps he is talking to other women. They smile upon him; he approaches. Oh no; no one else pleases you. There are some more beautiful, but I love you best. I know how to love best. I am your servant, your concubine! You are my king, my idol! You are good, you are beautiful, you are clever, you are strong!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh,” she went on, “I love you!","zh":"“因为我爱你啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I love you so that I could not live without you, do you see?","zh":"爱到离开你，我就活不成，你可知道？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There are times when I long to see you again, when I am torn by all the anger of love.","zh":"有时候，我一心就想再看到你，心里酸溜溜的，好不难过。我问自己：‘他如今在什么地方？","scope":"group"},{"en":"I ask myself, Where is he?","zh":"有时候，我一心就想再看到你，心里酸溜溜的，好不难过。我问自己：‘他如今在什么地方？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Perhaps he is talking to other women.","zh":"也许在同别的女人说话吧？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They smile upon him; he approaches.","zh":"她们笑嘻嘻看着他，他走过去…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Oh no; no one else pleases you.","zh":"她们笑嘻嘻看着他，他走过去…","scope":"group"},{"en":"There are some more beautiful, but I love you best.","zh":"’不，你哪一个女人也不喜欢，对不对？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I know how to love best.","zh":"比我好看的女人有的是，可是我呀，我懂得爱！我是你的奴才、你的姘头！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am your servant, your concubine!","zh":"你是我的王爷、我的偶像！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are my king, my idol!","zh":"你好，你美！你聪明！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are good, you are beautiful, you are clever, you are strong!”","zh":"你强壮！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had so often heard these things said that they did not strike him as original. Emma was like all his mistresses; and the charm of novelty, gradually falling away like a garment, laid bare the eternal monotony of passion, that has always the same forms and the same language. He did not distinguish, this man of so much experience, the difference of sentiment beneath the sameness of expression. Because lips libertine and venal had murmured such words to him, he believed but little in the candour of hers; exaggerated speeches hiding mediocre affections must be discounted; as if the fullness of the soul did not sometimes overflow in the emptiest metaphors, since no one can ever give the exact measure of his needs, nor of his conceptions, nor of his sorrows; and since human speech is like a cracked tin kettle, on which we hammer out tunes to make bears dance when we long to move the stars.","sentences":[{"en":"He had so often heard these things said that they did not strike him as original.","zh":"这话他听了千百遍，丝毫不觉新奇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma was like all his mistresses; and the charm of novelty, gradually falling away like a garment, laid bare the eternal monotony of passion, that has always the same forms and the same language.","zh":"爱玛类似所有的情妇；这像脱衣服一样，新鲜劲儿过去了，赤裸裸露出了热情，永远千篇一律，形象和语言老是那么一套。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He did not distinguish, this man of so much experience, the difference of sentiment beneath the sameness of expression.","zh":"别看这位先生是风月老手，他辨别不出同一表现的不同感情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Because lips libertine and venal had murmured such words to him, he believed but little in the candour of hers; exaggerated speeches hiding mediocre affections must be discounted; as if the fullness of the soul did not sometimes overflow in the emptiest metaphors, since no one can ever give the exact measure of his needs, nor of his conceptions, nor of his sorrows; and since human speech is like a cracked tin kettle, on which we hammer out tunes to make bears dance when we long to move the stars.","zh":"因为他听见放荡或者卖淫女子，唧唧哝哝，对他说过相同的话，他也就不大相信她那些话出自本心了。在他看来，言辞浮夸，感情贫乏，就该非议，倒像灵魂涨满，有时候就不免涌出最空洞的隐喻来。因为人对自己的需要、自己的理解、自己的痛苦，永远缺乏准确的尺寸，何况人类语言就像一只破锅，我们敲敲打打，希望音响铿锵，感动星宿，实际只有狗熊闻声起舞而已。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But with that superior critical judgment that belongs to him who, in no matter what circumstance, holds back, Rodolphe saw other delights to be got out of this love. He thought all modesty in the way. He treated her quite sans façon. He made of her something supple and corrupt. Hers was an idiotic sort of attachment, full of admiration for him, of voluptuousness for her, a beatitude that benumbed her; her soul sank into this drunkenness, shrivelled up, drowned in it, like Clarence in his butt of Malmsey.","sentences":[{"en":"But with that superior critical judgment that belongs to him who, in no matter what circumstance, holds back, Rodolphe saw other delights to be got out of this love.","zh":"但是罗道耳弗有那种遇事退一步考虑的明智眼光，他发现这种爱情，可发掘的乐趣还很多，尽好享受。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He thought all modesty in the way.","zh":"他嫌廉耻掣肘，待她不但没有礼貌，还把她训练成了一个又服帖、又淫荡的女人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He treated her quite sans façon.","zh":"他嫌廉耻掣肘，待她不但没有礼貌，还把她训练成了一个又服帖、又淫荡的女人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He made of her something supple and corrupt.","zh":"这成了一种不可理喻的依恋，她对他一味倾倒，自己也是一个劲儿癫狂；一种极乐世界，她待在里头，昏昏沉沉；这类似一种酒，她喝得醉醺醺，灵魂泡在里头，皱成一团，好像克拉伦斯公爵，泡在马尔法兹酒桶里一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Hers was an idiotic sort of attachment, full of admiration for him, of voluptuousness for her, a beatitude that benumbed her; her soul sank into this drunkenness, shrivelled up, drowned in it, like Clarence in his butt of Malmsey.","zh":"这成了一种不可理喻的依恋，她对他一味倾倒，自己也是一个劲儿癫狂；一种极乐世界，她待在里头，昏昏沉沉；这类似一种酒，她喝得醉醺醺，灵魂泡在里头，皱成一团，好像克拉伦斯公爵，泡在马尔法兹酒桶里一样。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"By the mere effect of her love Madame Bovary’s manners changed. Her looks grew bolder, her speech more free; she even committed the impropriety of walking out with Monsieur Rodolphe, a cigarette in her mouth, “as if to defy the people.” At last, those who still doubted doubted no longer when one day they saw her getting out of the “Hirondelle,” her waist squeezed into a waistcoat like a man; and Madame Bovary senior, who, after a fearful scene with her husband, had taken refuge at her son’s, was not the least scandalised of the women-folk. Many other things displeased her. First, Charles had not attended to her advice about the forbidding of novels; then the “ways of the house” annoyed her; she allowed herself to make some remarks, and there were quarrels, especially one on account of Félicité.","sentences":[{"en":"By the mere effect of her love Madame Bovary’s manners changed.","zh":"包法利夫人纵情声色，积习难返，姿态也起了变化。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her looks grew bolder, her speech more free; she even committed the impropriety of walking out with Monsieur Rodolphe, a cigarette in her mouth, “as if to defy the people.”","zh":"视线更无忌惮，语言也更放肆；她甚至甘冒不韪，和罗道耳弗先生一同散步，口噙香烟，旁若无人；有一天，见她走下燕子，学男人穿一件背心，最后就连还不相信的那些人，也不再怀疑了。包法利老太太和丈夫大闹一场之后，躲到儿子家来，见她这般模样，反感已极。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last, those who still doubted doubted no longer when one day they saw her getting out of the “Hirondelle,” her waist squeezed into a waistcoat like a man; and Madame Bovary senior, who, after a fearful scene with her husband, had taken refuge at her son’s, was not the least scandalised of the women-folk.","zh":"视线更无忌惮，语言也更放肆；她甚至甘冒不韪，和罗道耳弗先生一同散步，口噙香烟，旁若无人；有一天，见她走下燕子，学男人穿一件背心，最后就连还不相信的那些人，也不再怀疑了。包法利老太太和丈夫大闹一场之后，躲到儿子家来，见她这般模样，反感已极。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Many other things displeased her.","zh":"另外还有许多事，也不顺她的心思：首先，查理没有听劝，制止她看小说；其次，她不喜欢这种治家之道，不管三七二十一，说了几句，尤其有一回，说到全福，她们闹翻了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"First, Charles had not attended to her advice about the forbidding of novels; then the “ways of the house” annoyed her; she allowed herself to make some remarks, and there were quarrels, especially one on account of Félicité.","zh":"另外还有许多事，也不顺她的心思：首先，查理没有听劝，制止她看小说；其次，她不喜欢这种治家之道，不管三七二十一，说了几句，尤其有一回，说到全福，她们闹翻了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary senior, the evening before, passing along the passage, had surprised her in company of a man—a man with a brown collar, about forty years old, who, at the sound of her step, had quickly escaped through the kitchen. Then Emma began to laugh, but the good lady grew angry, declaring that unless morals were to be laughed at one ought to look after those of one’s servants.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary senior, the evening before, passing along the passage, had surprised her in company of a man—a man with a brown collar, about forty years old, who, at the sound of her step, had quickly escaped through the kitchen.","zh":"吵架的前一晚上，老太太穿过道走，发现全福和一个男人待在一起，那人一圈棕色胡须，四十岁上下，听见她的脚步，赶快从厨房溜掉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Emma began to laugh, but the good lady grew angry, declaring that unless morals were to be laughed at one ought to look after those of one’s servants.","zh":"爱玛一听这话，笑了起来，可是老太太动了肝火，就讲：一个人除非不拿规矩当事，否则就该监视用人才是。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where were you brought up?” asked the daughter-in-law, with so impertinent a look that Madame Bovary asked her if she were not perhaps defending her own case.","sentences":[{"en":"“Where were you brought up?” asked the daughter-in-law, with so impertinent a look that Madame Bovary asked her if she were not perhaps defending her own case.","zh":"“您算是哪类人？”儿媳妇说这话，视线万分无礼，老太太不由地问，她是不是回护她自己的事。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Leave the room!” said the young woman, springing up with a bound.","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave the room!” said the young woman, springing up with a bound.","zh":"少妇跳起来道：“滚出去！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Emma! Mamma!” cried Charles, trying to reconcile them.","sentences":[{"en":"“Emma!","zh":"查理在中间劝解，喊道：“爱玛！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mamma!” cried Charles, trying to reconcile them.","zh":"妈！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But both had fled in their exasperation. Emma was stamping her feet as she repeated—","sentences":[{"en":"But both had fled in their exasperation.","zh":"但是两个女人一赌气，全走开了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma was stamping her feet as she repeated—","zh":"但是两个女人一赌气，全走开了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh! what manners! What a peasant!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh! what manners!","zh":"爱玛跺着脚，说过来说过去：","scope":"group"},{"en":"What a peasant!”","zh":"爱玛跺着脚，说过来说过去：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He ran to his mother; she was beside herself. She stammered","sentences":[{"en":"He ran to his mother; she was beside herself.","zh":"“啊！真懂规矩啦！活活一个庄稼女人！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She stammered","zh":"“啊！真懂规矩啦！活活一个庄稼女人！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“She is an insolent, giddy-headed thing, or perhaps worse!”","sentences":[{"en":"“She is an insolent, giddy-headed thing, or perhaps worse!”","zh":"他跑到母亲跟前，她气糊涂了，结结巴巴道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she was for leaving at once if the other did not apologise. So Charles went back again to his wife and implored her to give way; he knelt to her; she ended by saying—","sentences":[{"en":"And she was for leaving at once if the other did not apologise.","zh":"“目无尊长的东西！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So Charles went back again to his wife and implored her to give way; he knelt to her; she ended by saying—","zh":"轻狂的东西！也许更坏！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Very well! I’ll go to her.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very well!","zh":"儿媳妇不对她赔不是，她要马上就走。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll go to her.”","zh":"儿媳妇不对她赔不是，她要马上就走。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And in fact she held out her hand to her mother-in-law with the dignity of a marchioness as she said—","sentences":[{"en":"And in fact she held out her hand to her mother-in-law with the dignity of a marchioness as she said—","zh":"查理回到太太跟前，求她让步：他下跪了。临了她回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Excuse me, madame.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Excuse me, madame.”","zh":"“好吧！我去！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, having gone up again to her room, she threw herself flat on her bed and cried there like a child, her face buried in the pillow.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, having gone up again to her room, she threw herself flat on her bed and cried there like a child, her face buried in the pillow.","zh":"她的确拿手伸给婆婆，如同一位侯爵夫人那样尊严，向她道：“原谅我，夫人。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She and Rodolphe had agreed that in the event of anything extraordinary occurring, she should fasten a small piece of white paper to the blind, so that if by chance he happened to be in Yonville, he could hurry to the lane behind the house. Emma made the signal; she had been waiting three-quarters of an hour when she suddenly caught sight of Rodolphe at the corner of the market. She felt tempted to open the window and call him, but he had already disappeared. She fell back in despair.","sentences":[{"en":"She and Rodolphe had agreed that in the event of anything extraordinary occurring, she should fasten a small piece of white paper to the blind, so that if by chance he happened to be in Yonville, he could hurry to the lane behind the house.","zh":"然后爱玛走上楼，扑倒在床，脸埋在枕头里，哭得像小孩子一样。她和罗道耳弗约好了，遇到大事，就在窗上贴一小张白纸，万一凑巧他在永镇，望见暗号，就跑到房后小巷会她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma made the signal; she had been waiting three-quarters of an hour when she suddenly caught sight of Rodolphe at the corner of the market.","zh":"爱玛这样做了；她等了三刻钟，忽然望见罗道耳弗在菜场一角。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She felt tempted to open the window and call him, but he had already disappeared.","zh":"她有心打开窗户喊他；可是他已经不见了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She fell back in despair.","zh":"她一难过，又倒了下去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Soon, however, it seemed to her that someone was walking on the pavement. It was he, no doubt. She went downstairs, crossed the yard. He was there outside. She threw herself into his arms.","sentences":[{"en":"Soon, however, it seemed to her that someone was walking on the pavement.","zh":"不过没有多久，她觉得有人在人行道上走动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was he, no doubt.","zh":"不用说，是他；她走下楼梯，穿过院落。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She went downstairs, crossed the yard.","zh":"不用说，是他；她走下楼梯，穿过院落。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was there outside.","zh":"他站在外头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She threw herself into his arms.","zh":"她扑到他的怀里。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do take care!” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do take care!” he said.","zh":"“小心有人看见！”她回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! if you knew!” she replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! if you knew!” she replied.","zh":"“啊！你知道也就好啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she began telling him everything, hurriedly, disjointedly, exaggerating the facts, inventing many, and so prodigal of parentheses that he understood nothing of it.","sentences":[{"en":"And she began telling him everything, hurriedly, disjointedly, exaggerating the facts, inventing many, and so prodigal of parentheses that he understood nothing of it.","zh":"她一五一十，同他讲起，又急促，又上气不接下气，夸张事实，还捏造了一些事实，添了不少按语，絮絮叨叨，讲到后来，他一句也没有听懂。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come, my poor angel, courage! Be comforted! be patient!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, my poor angel, courage!","zh":"“得啦，我可怜的天使，拿出勇气来，看开些，凡事忍耐！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Be comforted! be patient!”","zh":"“得啦，我可怜的天使，拿出勇气来，看开些，凡事忍耐！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“But I have been patient; I have suffered for four years. A love like ours ought to show itself in the face of heaven. They torture me! I can bear it no longer! Save me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But I have been patient; I have suffered for four years.","zh":"“可是我已经忍耐、煎熬了四年！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A love like ours ought to show itself in the face of heaven.","zh":"像我们这样相爱，就该公之于世！他们快把我折磨死了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They torture me!","zh":"像我们这样相爱，就该公之于世！他们快把我折磨死了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I can bear it no longer!","zh":"我受不了啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Save me!”","zh":"救救我！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She clung to Rodolphe. Her eyes, full of tears, flashed like flames beneath a wave; her breast heaved; he had never loved her so much, so that he lost his head and said “What is, it? What do you wish?”","sentences":[{"en":"She clung to Rodolphe.","zh":"她贴紧罗道耳弗：满眼泪水，闪闪发光，就像波浪底下的火焰一样；胸脯一上一下喘气，又急又快。他从来没有这样爱过她；他一时没了主张，问她道：“该怎么办？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her eyes, full of tears, flashed like flames beneath a wave; her breast heaved; he had never loved her so much, so that he lost his head and said “What is, it?","zh":"她贴紧罗道耳弗：满眼泪水，闪闪发光，就像波浪底下的火焰一样；胸脯一上一下喘气，又急又快。他从来没有这样爱过她；他一时没了主张，问她道：“该怎么办？","scope":"group"},{"en":"What do you wish?”","zh":"你打算怎么着？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Take me away,” she cried, “carry me off! Oh, I pray you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Take me away,” she cried, “carry me off!","zh":"她喊道：“把我带走！抢走！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, I pray you!”","zh":"哎呀！我求你啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she threw herself upon his mouth, as if to seize there the unexpected consent if breathed forth in a kiss.","sentences":[{"en":"And she threw herself upon his mouth, as if to seize there the unexpected consent if breathed forth in a kiss.","zh":"她连忙凑到他的嘴跟前，好像要在这里捉住意想不到的同意一样。他用吻表示同意。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But—” Rodolphe resumed.","sentences":[{"en":"“But—” Rodolphe resumed.","zh":"罗道耳弗又讲：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"罗道耳弗又讲：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Your little girl!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Your little girl!”","zh":"“不过…”“什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She reflected a few moments, then replied—","sentences":[{"en":"She reflected a few moments, then replied—","zh":"“你女儿怎么办？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We will take her! It can’t be helped!”","sentences":[{"en":"“We will take her!","zh":"她沉吟了几分钟后，回答道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"It can’t be helped!”","zh":"她沉吟了几分钟后，回答道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What a woman!” he said to himself, watching her as she went. For she had run into the garden. Someone was calling her.","sentences":[{"en":"“What a woman!” he said to himself, watching her as she went.","zh":"“只好带她走！”他望着她走开，心想：“有这种女人！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"For she had run into the garden.","zh":"“只好带她走！”他望着她走开，心想：“有这种女人！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Someone was calling her.","zh":"“只好带她走！”他望着她走开，心想：“有这种女人！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"On the following days Madame Bovary senior was much surprised at the change in her daughter-in-law. Emma, in fact, was showing herself more docile, and even carried her deference so far as to ask for a recipe for pickling gherkins.","sentences":[{"en":"On the following days Madame Bovary senior was much surprised at the change in her daughter-in-law.","zh":"她朝花园溜过去了。原来是有人喊她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma, in fact, was showing herself more docile, and even carried her deference so far as to ask for a recipe for pickling gherkins.","zh":"一连几天，儿媳妇改了模样，老太太好生纳罕。爱玛的确和顺多了，甚至低声下气，向她请教腌黄瓜的方法。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Was it the better to deceive them both? Or did she wish by a sort of voluptuous stoicism to feel the more profoundly the bitterness of the things she was about to leave?","sentences":[{"en":"Was it the better to deceive them both?","zh":"她这样做，是为了更好地欺骗他们母子？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Or did she wish by a sort of voluptuous stoicism to feel the more profoundly the bitterness of the things she was about to leave?","zh":"还是就要分手了，她以一种无上的坚忍精神，愿意再进一步，体会体会生活的辛酸？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But she paid no heed to them; on the contrary, she lived as lost in the anticipated delight of her coming happiness.","sentences":[{"en":"But she paid no heed to them; on the contrary, she lived as lost in the anticipated delight of her coming happiness.","zh":"可是不，她没有存这种心思。她是想着她的幸福快到手了，醉醺醺的，就像预先闻到了酒味一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was an eternal subject for conversation with Rodolphe. She leant on his shoulder murmuring—","sentences":[{"en":"It was an eternal subject for conversation with Rodolphe.","zh":"她和罗道耳弗谈话，三句不离本题。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She leant on his shoulder murmuring—","zh":"她靠着他的肩膀，嘀咕道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! when we are in the mail-coach! Do you think about it? Can it be? It seems to me that the moment I feel the carriage start, it will be as if we were rising in a balloon, as if we were setting out for the clouds. Do you know that I count the hours? And you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! when we are in the mail-coach!","zh":"“嗯！我们一上邮车呀！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you think about it?","zh":"你想到这上头没有？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Can it be?","zh":"你想到这上头没有？","scope":"group"},{"en":"It seems to me that the moment I feel the carriage start, it will be as if we were rising in a balloon, as if we were setting out for the clouds.","zh":"这会是真的？我觉得，车出发的一刹那，我们就像乘了气球一样，就像要上九天云霄去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you know that I count the hours?","zh":"你知道我在计算日子吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And you?”","zh":"你呢？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Never had Madame Bovary been so beautiful as at this period; she had that indefinable beauty that results from joy, from enthusiasm, from success, and that is only the harmony of temperament with circumstances. Her desires, her sorrows, the experience of pleasure, and her ever-young illusions, that had, as soil and rain and winds and the sun make flowers grow, gradually developed her, and she at length blossomed forth in all the plenitude of her nature. Her eyelids seemed chiselled expressly for her long amorous looks in which the pupil disappeared, while a strong inspiration expanded her delicate nostrils and raised the fleshy corner of her lips, shaded in the light by a little black down. One would have thought that an artist apt in conception had arranged the curls of hair upon her neck; they fell in a thick mass, negligently, and with the changing chances of their adultery, that unbound them every day. Her voice now took more mellow infections, her figure also; something subtle and penetrating escaped even from the folds of her gown and from the line of her foot. Charles, as when they were first married, thought her delicious and quite irresistible.","sentences":[{"en":"Never had Madame Bovary been so beautiful as at this period; she had that indefinable beauty that results from joy, from enthusiasm, from success, and that is only the harmony of temperament with circumstances.","zh":"包法利夫人从来没有像这期间这样好看过。这种难以形容的美丽，来自喜悦、兴奋和成功，来自环境和气质的协调。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her desires, her sorrows, the experience of pleasure, and her ever-young illusions, that had, as soil and rain and winds and the sun make flowers grow, gradually developed her, and she at length blossomed forth in all the plenitude of her nature.","zh":"就像风、雨、阳光和肥料供花木生长一样，她的贪欲、苦恼、风月经验和她那永远生气勃勃的空想，使她的本性逐步发展丰满，终于绽苞盛开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her eyelids seemed chiselled expressly for her long amorous looks in which the pupil disappeared, while a strong inspiration expanded her delicate nostrils and raised the fleshy corner of her lips, shaded in the light by a little black down.","zh":"眼皮像是特地为她的视线剪裁的，看上去又杳渺又妩媚，瞳仁沉在里头，不见踪影。气出急了，玲珑的鼻孔分开，丰盈的嘴唇翘起，同时薄薄一层黑毛，影影绰绰，盖住她的嘴唇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One would have thought that an artist apt in conception had arranged the curls of hair upon her neck; they fell in a thick mass, negligently, and with the changing chances of their adultery, that unbound them every day.","zh":"头发像是由一位专会诱人堕落的艺人挽成的一个肥肥的圆髻，随随便便，盘在后颈，又因为幽会，天天散开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her voice now took more mellow infections, her figure also; something subtle and penetrating escaped even from the folds of her gown and from the line of her foot.","zh":"她的声音如今越发柔和动听，身材越发袅娜可爱，甚至她的袍褶和她弓起的脚面，也妙不可言，沁人心脾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles, as when they were first married, thought her delicious and quite irresistible.","zh":"查理又像在新婚期间一样，觉得她赏心悦目，难以抗拒。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When he came home in the middle of the night, he did not dare to wake her. The porcelain night-light threw a round trembling gleam upon the ceiling, and the drawn curtains of the little cot formed as it were a white hut standing out in the shade, and by the bedside Charles looked at them. He seemed to hear the light breathing of his child. She would grow big now; every season would bring rapid progress. He already saw her coming from school as the day drew in, laughing, with ink-stains on her jacket, and carrying her basket on her arm. Then she would have to be sent to the boarding-school; that would cost much; how was it to be done? Then he reflected. He thought of hiring a small farm in the neighbourhood, that he would superintend every morning on his way to his patients. He would save up what he brought in; he would put it in the savings-bank. Then he would buy shares somewhere, no matter where; besides, his practice would increase; he counted upon that, for he wanted Berthe to be well-educated, to be accomplished, to learn to play the piano. Ah! how pretty she would be later on when she was fifteen, when, resembling her mother, she would, like her, wear large straw hats in the summer-time; from a distance they would be taken for two sisters. He pictured her to himself working in the evening by their side beneath the light of the lamp; she would embroider him slippers; she would look after the house; she would fill all the home with her charm and her gaiety. At last, they would think of her marriage; they would find her some good young fellow with a steady business; he would make her happy; this would last for ever.","sentences":[{"en":"When he came home in the middle of the night, he did not dare to wake her.","zh":"他深夜回来，不敢叫醒她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The porcelain night-light threw a round trembling gleam upon the ceiling, and the drawn curtains of the little cot formed as it were a white hut standing out in the shade, and by the bedside Charles looked at them.","zh":"过夜的瓷灯，哆哆嗦嗦，在天花板上，聚成一个亮圈；床边摇篮放下帐子，仿佛一间小白屋，在黑影里特别明显。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He seemed to hear the light breathing of his child.","zh":"查理望过去，恍惚听见孩子的细微呼吸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would grow big now; every season would bring rapid progress.","zh":"她如今正长个子，一季一蹿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He already saw her coming from school as the day drew in, laughing, with ink-stains on her jacket, and carrying her basket on her arm.","zh":"他像已经看见日落西山，她放学回家，满脸的笑，衣服上有墨水点子，胳膊挎着她的小篮子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she would have to be sent to the boarding-school; that would cost much; how was it to be done?","zh":"以后还得进寄宿学校，要花许多钱；怎么办？他不由得沉吟起来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he reflected.","zh":"以后还得进寄宿学校，要花许多钱；怎么办？他不由得沉吟起来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He thought of hiring a small farm in the neighbourhood, that he would superintend every morning on his way to his patients.","zh":"他想在附近佃一小块田，每天早晨去看病人，亲自监督。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He would save up what he brought in; he would put it in the savings-bank.","zh":"他省下田里收入，存在储蓄银行；然后买上一些股票，随便哪一家公司都成；再说，主顾会多起来的；他这样希望，因为他要白尔特受到良好教育，有才分，会弹钢琴。啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he would buy shares somewhere, no matter where; besides, his practice would increase; he counted upon that, for he wanted Berthe to be well-educated, to be accomplished, to learn to play the piano.","zh":"他省下田里收入，存在储蓄银行；然后买上一些股票，随便哪一家公司都成；再说，主顾会多起来的；他这样希望，因为他要白尔特受到良好教育，有才分，会弹钢琴。啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Ah! how pretty she would be later on when she was fifteen, when, resembling her mother, she would, like her, wear large straw hats in the summer-time; from a distance they would be taken for two sisters.","zh":"等她长到十五岁，像她的母亲一样，在夏天也戴大草帽，该多好看！人们会老远把她们看成一对姊妹花的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He pictured her to himself working in the evening by their side beneath the light of the lamp; she would embroider him slippers; she would look after the house; she would fill all the home with her charm and her gaiety.","zh":"他想象她夜晚在灯光底下，靠近他们做活，她会为他绣拖鞋，会料理家务，个个房间洋溢着她的可爱和她的快活。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, they would think of her marriage; they would find her some good young fellow with a steady business; he would make her happy; this would last for ever.","zh":"最后，他们会照料她的终身，为她挑一个殷实可靠的好丈夫；他会使她快乐，而且永远快乐。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma was not asleep; she pretended to be; and while he dozed off by her side she awakened to other dreams.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma was not asleep; she pretended to be; and while he dozed off by her side she awakened to other dreams.","zh":"爱玛没有睡，也就是装睡；他躺在旁边，昏昏沉沉，她却醒过来，做别的梦。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To the gallop of four horses she was carried away for a week towards a new land, whence they would return no more. They went on and on, their arms entwined, without a word. Often from the top of a mountain there suddenly glimpsed some splendid city with domes, and bridges, and ships, forests of citron trees, and cathedrals of white marble, on whose pointed steeples were storks’ nests. They went at a walking-pace because of the great flag-stones, and on the ground there were bouquets of flowers, offered you by women dressed in red bodices. They heard the chiming of bells, the neighing of mules, together with the murmur of guitars and the noise of fountains, whose rising spray refreshed heaps of fruit arranged like a pyramid at the foot of pale statues that smiled beneath playing waters. And then, one night they came to a fishing village, where brown nets were drying in the wind along the cliffs and in front of the huts. It was there that they would stay; they would live in a low, flat-roofed house, shaded by a palm-tree, in the heart of a gulf, by the sea. They would row in gondolas, swing in hammocks, and their existence would be easy and large as their silk gowns, warm and star-spangled as the nights they would contemplate. However, in the immensity of this future that she conjured up, nothing special stood forth; the days, all magnificent, resembled each other like waves; and it swayed in the horizon, infinite, harmonised, azure, and bathed in sunshine. But the child began to cough in her cot or Bovary snored more loudly, and Emma did not fall asleep till morning, when the dawn whitened the windows, and when little Justin was already in the square taking down the shutters of the chemist’s shop.","sentences":[{"en":"To the gallop of four horses she was carried away for a week towards a new land, whence they would return no more.","zh":"她乘了驿车，四匹马放开蹄子，驰往新国度，已经有一星期了；他们到了那边，不再回来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They went on and on, their arms entwined, without a word.","zh":"他们走呀走的，胳膊挽在一起，不言不语。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often from the top of a mountain there suddenly glimpsed some splendid city with domes, and bridges, and ships, forests of citron trees, and cathedrals of white marble, on whose pointed steeples were storks’ nests.","zh":"他们站在山头，常常意想不到，望见一座壮丽的大城，有圆顶，有桥，有船，有柠檬林和白大理石教堂，教堂的尖钟楼有鹳巢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They went at a walking-pace because of the great flag-stones, and on the ground there were bouquets of flowers, offered you by women dressed in red bodices.","zh":"大石板地，他们只好步行；妇女穿着红紧身，举起地上的花一把一把献给你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They heard the chiming of bells, the neighing of mules, together with the murmur of guitars and the noise of fountains, whose rising spray refreshed heaps of fruit arranged like a pyramid at the foot of pale statues that smiled beneath playing waters.","zh":"他们听见钟响、骡鸣、六弦琴低吟、泉水淙淙；白雕像笑微微立在喷泉底下，脚边摆着成堆的水果，摞得金字塔似的，水花溅上去，个个新鲜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then, one night they came to a fishing village, where brown nets were drying in the wind along the cliffs and in front of the huts.","zh":"随后，有一天黄昏，他们来到一个渔村，沿着峭壁和茅屋，迎风晾着一些棕色渔网。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was there that they would stay; they would live in a low, flat-roofed house, shaded by a palm-tree, in the heart of a gulf, by the sea.","zh":"他们就在这里待下来，在海边港湾深处，住一所在棕榈树的浓荫覆盖下的平顶矮房。他们驾着小船游荡，躺在吊床上摇摆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They would row in gondolas, swing in hammocks, and their existence would be easy and large as their silk gowns, warm and star-spangled as the nights they would contemplate.","zh":"生活又方便，又宽裕，就像他们的绸缎衣服一样；又暖和，又皎洁，就像他们观赏的温馨的星夜一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"However, in the immensity of this future that she conjured up, nothing special stood forth; the days, all magnificent, resembled each other like waves; and it swayed in the horizon, infinite, harmonised, azure, and bathed in sunshine.","zh":"不过她给自己设想的未来，浩瀚渺茫，绝少明确的形象出现：每天全都相仿，绚烂一片，好像波浪一样，起伏动荡，与天际相连，和谐、蔚蓝、充满阳光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the child began to cough in her cot or Bovary snored more loudly, and Emma did not fall asleep till morning, when the dawn whitened the windows, and when little Justin was already in the square taking down the shutters of the chemist’s shop.","zh":"但是小孩子开始在摇篮里咳嗽，要不就是包法利鼾声更响了，直到早晨，爱玛才入睡，玻璃窗已经发白，小朱斯丹已经在广场打开药房的护窗板。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She had sent for Monsieur Lheureux, and had said to him—","sentences":[{"en":"She had sent for Monsieur Lheureux, and had said to him—","zh":"她把勒乐先生找来，向他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I want a cloak—a large lined cloak with a deep collar.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I want a cloak—a large lined cloak with a deep collar.”","zh":"“我要一件斗篷，一件大斗篷，长领披，有夹里的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are going on a journey?” he asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“You are going on a journey?” he asked.","zh":"他问道：“您出远门？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No; but—never mind. I may count on you, may I not, and quickly?”","sentences":[{"en":"“No; but—never mind.","zh":"“不是的！不过…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I may count on you, may I not, and quickly?”","zh":"管它呐，我信得过您，对不对？要快！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He bowed.","sentences":[{"en":"He bowed.","zh":"他鞠躬。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Besides, I shall want,” she went on, “a trunk—not too heavy—handy.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Besides, I shall want,” she went on, “a trunk—not too heavy—handy.”","zh":"她接下去道：“我还要一只箱子…不要太重…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, yes, I understand. About three feet by a foot and a half, as they are being made just now.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, yes, I understand.","zh":"“对，对，我懂，约莫九十二公分长，五十公分宽，眼下的新样子。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"About three feet by a foot and a half, as they are being made just now.”","zh":"“对，对，我懂，约莫九十二公分长，五十公分宽，眼下的新样子。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“And a travelling bag.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And a travelling bag.”","zh":"“还要一只旅行袋。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Decidedly,” thought Lheureux, “there’s a row on here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Decidedly,” thought Lheureux, “there’s a row on here.”","zh":"勒乐寻思：“这里头一定有把戏。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And,” said Madame Bovary, taking her watch from her belt, “take this; you can pay yourself out of it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And,” said Madame Bovary, taking her watch from her belt, “take this; you can pay yourself out of it.”","zh":"包法利夫人边解腰带上的表，边道：“好，拿去，用这抵账好了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the tradesman cried out that she was wrong; they knew one another; did he doubt her? What childishness!","sentences":[{"en":"But the tradesman cried out that she was wrong; they knew one another; did he doubt her?","zh":"可是商人嚷了起来！她这就不对了，他们彼此了解，难道她有什么不相信他的？","scope":"group"},{"en":"What childishness!","zh":"可是商人嚷了起来！她这就不对了，他们彼此了解，难道她有什么不相信他的？","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She insisted, however, on his taking at least the chain, and Lheureux had already put it in his pocket and was going, when she called him back.","sentences":[{"en":"She insisted, however, on his taking at least the chain, and Lheureux had already put it in his pocket and was going, when she called him back.","zh":"真是想到哪儿去啦！她坚持要他拿，少说也要拿链子去，眼看勒乐已经把链子放进口袋要走了，她又喊他回来：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You will leave everything at your place. As to the cloak”—she seemed to be reflecting—“do not bring it either; you can give me the maker’s address, and tell him to have it ready for me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You will leave everything at your place.","zh":"“您全留在铺子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to the cloak”—she seemed to be reflecting—“do not bring it either; you can give me the maker’s address, and tell him to have it ready for me.”","zh":"至于斗篷（她显出思索的神情），也不用送来；您只要把裁缝住址给我，叫他们等我来取就是了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was the next month that they were to run away. She was to leave Yonville as if she was going on some business to Rouen. Rodolphe would have booked the seats, procured the passports, and even have written to Paris in order to have the whole mail-coach reserved for them as far as Marseilles, where they would buy a carriage, and go on thence without stopping to Genoa. She would take care to send her luggage to Lheureux whence it would be taken direct to the “Hirondelle,” so that no one would have any suspicion. And in all this there never was any allusion to the child. Rodolphe avoided speaking of her; perhaps he no longer thought about it.","sentences":[{"en":"It was the next month that they were to run away.","zh":"他们打算下月逃走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was to leave Yonville as if she was going on some business to Rouen.","zh":"她离开永镇，装出上鲁昂买东西的模样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe would have booked the seats, procured the passports, and even have written to Paris in order to have the whole mail-coach reserved for them as far as Marseilles, where they would buy a carriage, and go on thence without stopping to Genoa.","zh":"罗道耳弗先订好座位，办好护照，甚至去信巴黎，包一辆直达马赛的驿车；到了马赛，他们买一辆有活动车篷的四轮敞篷车，马不停蹄，直奔热那亚而去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would take care to send her luggage to Lheureux whence it would be taken direct to the “Hirondelle,” so that no one would have any suspicion.","zh":"她的行李，她小心在意，先送到勒乐那边，再直接装上燕子，这样一来，就免得人疑心了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And in all this there never was any allusion to the child.","zh":"她左右安排，只有她的小孩子，她忘了安排。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe avoided speaking of her; perhaps he no longer thought about it.","zh":"罗道耳弗对此避而不谈，她也许没有想到这上头。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He wished to have two more weeks before him to arrange some affairs; then at the end of a week he wanted two more; then he said he was ill; next he went on a journey. The month of August passed, and, after all these delays, they decided that it was to be irrevocably fixed for the 4th September—a Monday.","sentences":[{"en":"He wished to have two more weeks before him to arrange some affairs; then at the end of a week he wanted two more; then he said he was ill; next he went on a journey.","zh":"有些布置，他还需要两个星期才能结束；过了一个星期，他要再来两个星期；后来，说他有病；过后，他又出门有事；八月过去了，经过种种延宕，他们决定在九月四日，星期一出奔，再也不改日期。星期六，出奔的前两天，终于到了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The month of August passed, and, after all these delays, they decided that it was to be irrevocably fixed for the 4th September—a Monday.","zh":"有些布置，他还需要两个星期才能结束；过了一个星期，他要再来两个星期；后来，说他有病；过后，他又出门有事；八月过去了，经过种种延宕，他们决定在九月四日，星期一出奔，再也不改日期。星期六，出奔的前两天，终于到了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At length the Saturday before arrived.","sentences":[{"en":"At length the Saturday before arrived.","zh":"天一黑，罗道耳弗就来了，比平日都早。她问他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe came in the evening earlier than usual.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe came in the evening earlier than usual.","zh":"天一黑，罗道耳弗就来了，比平日都早。她问他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Everything is ready?” she asked him.","sentences":[{"en":"“Everything is ready?” she asked him.","zh":"“全齐备啦？”“齐备啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"于是他们顺着花圃兜了一圈，过去坐到平台近旁的墙头。爱玛道：“你怎么愁眉不展的？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then they walked round a garden-bed, and went to sit down near the terrace on the kerb-stone of the wall.","sentences":[{"en":"Then they walked round a garden-bed, and went to sit down near the terrace on the kerb-stone of the wall.","zh":"于是他们顺着花圃兜了一圈，过去坐到平台近旁的墙头。爱玛道：“你怎么愁眉不展的？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You are sad,” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“You are sad,” said Emma.","zh":"“没有。为什么呀？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No; why?”","sentences":[{"en":"“No; why?”","zh":"可是他古怪地看着她，一副多情的模样。她接着问道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And yet he looked at her strangely in a tender fashion.","sentences":[{"en":"And yet he looked at her strangely in a tender fashion.","zh":"可是他古怪地看着她，一副多情的模样。她接着问道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“It is because you are going away?” she went on; “because you are leaving what is dear to you—your life? Ah! I understand. I have nothing in the world! you are all to me; so shall I be to you. I will be your people, your country; I will tend, I will love you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is because you are going away?” she went on; “because you are leaving what is dear to you—your life?","zh":"“是不是为了上路？为了抛弃你心爱的东西、你的生活？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah!","zh":"啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I understand.","zh":"我明白…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I have nothing in the world! you are all to me; so shall I be to you.","zh":"可是我呀，我在世上就什么也没有！你是我的一切。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I will be your people, your country; I will tend, I will love you!”","zh":"所以我也要是你的一切，我也要是你的家、你的国：我照料你，我爱你。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How sweet you are!” he said, seizing her in his arms.","sentences":[{"en":"“How sweet you are!” he said, seizing her in his arms.","zh":"他搂紧了她道：“你真可爱！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Really!” she said with a voluptuous laugh. “Do you love me? Swear it then!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Really!” she said with a voluptuous laugh.","zh":"她心花怒放地笑道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do you love me?","zh":"“当真？你爱我吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Swear it then!”","zh":"发发誓看！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do I love you—love you? I adore you, my love.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do I love you—love you?","zh":"“我爱你不爱？爱你不爱？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I adore you, my love.”","zh":"可是，我的心肝！我膜拜你呢！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The moon, full and purple-coloured, was rising right out of the earth at the end of the meadow. She rose quickly between the branches of the poplars, that hid her here and there like a black curtain pierced with holes. Then she appeared dazzling with whiteness in the empty heavens that she lit up, and now sailing more slowly along, let fall upon the river a great stain that broke up into an infinity of stars; and the silver sheen seemed to writhe through the very depths like a heedless serpent covered with luminous scales; it also resembled some monster candelabra all along which sparkled drops of diamonds running together. The soft night was about them; masses of shadow filled the branches. Emma, her eyes half closed, breathed in with deep sighs the fresh wind that was blowing. They did not speak, lost as they were in the rush of their reverie. The tenderness of the old days came back to their hearts, full and silent as the flowing river, with the softness of the perfume of the syringas, and threw across their memories shadows more immense and more sombre than those of the still willows that lengthened out over the grass. Often some night-animal, hedgehog or weasel, setting out on the hunt, disturbed the lovers, or sometimes they heard a ripe peach falling all alone from the espalier.","sentences":[{"en":"The moon, full and purple-coloured, was rising right out of the earth at the end of the meadow.","zh":"草原尽头，月亮就地升起，又圆又红，很快上到白杨树的枝叶当中，这些枝叶仿佛一面有破口的黑幕，左遮遮，右露露，月亮最后升到冷清清的天空，白晃晃一片晶莹，它放慢步子，朝河面洒下一片白光，变成万千星宿。这道银光好似一条无头蛇，遍体明鳞，盘来盘去，一直盘到河底，又好似一支奇大无比的蜡烛台，点点滴滴，流下不可胜数的金刚石颗粒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She rose quickly between the branches of the poplars, that hid her here and there like a black curtain pierced with holes.","zh":"温馨的夜晚裹住他们；树叶布满阴影。爱玛半闭眼睛，随着大声叹息，吸进吹来的清风。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she appeared dazzling with whiteness in the empty heavens that she lit up, and now sailing more slowly along, let fall upon the river a great stain that broke up into an infinity of stars; and the silver sheen seemed to writhe through the very depths like a heedless serpent covered with luminous scales; it also resembled some monster candelabra all along which sparkled drops of diamonds running together.","zh":"绮梦弥漫他们的心灵，两个人一时无话。过去的恩情，满满的，静静的，仿佛一条河，又流回他们的心来；同时香喷喷的，也像山梅花一样，芬芳醉人；同时又软绵绵的，朝回忆投下它的影子，比安静的柳树铺在草上的影子还要宽阔，还要忧悒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The soft night was about them; masses of shadow filled the branches.","zh":"刺猬或者黄鼠狼，这类夜间动物，常常搅动树叶，追赶什么东西。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma, her eyes half closed, breathed in with deep sighs the fresh wind that was blowing.","zh":"他们不时还听见一只熟了的桃子，自行从墙边桃树落下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They did not speak, lost as they were in the rush of their reverie.","zh":"罗道耳弗道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The tenderness of the old days came back to their hearts, full and silent as the flowing river, with the softness of the perfume of the syringas, and threw across their memories shadows more immense and more sombre than those of the still willows that lengthened out over the grass.","zh":"“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often some night-animal, hedgehog or weasel, setting out on the hunt, disturbed the lovers, or sometimes they heard a ripe peach falling all alone from the espalier.","zh":"多美的夜晚！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! what a lovely night!” said Rodolphe.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! what a lovely night!” said Rodolphe.","zh":"爱玛回答道：“我们以后有的是！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We shall have others,” replied Emma; and, as if speaking to herself: “Yet, it will be good to travel. And yet, why should my heart be so heavy? Is it dread of the unknown? The effect of habits left? Or rather—? No; it is the excess of happiness. How weak I am, am I not? Forgive me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“We shall have others,” replied Emma; and, as if speaking to herself: “Yet, it will be good to travel.","zh":"于是她自言自语似的说：“是啊，能旅行，再好没有…不过，为什么我感到凄凉？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And yet, why should my heart be so heavy?","zh":"难道是怕陌生…是改变习惯的结果…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is it dread of the unknown?","zh":"还是别的什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The effect of habits left?","zh":"不，是太幸福的缘故！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Or rather—?","zh":"我真软弱，是不是？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No; it is the excess of happiness.","zh":"饶恕我吧！”他喊道：“还来得及！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How weak I am, am I not?","zh":"再想想看，你说不定要后悔的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Forgive me!”","zh":"再想想看，你说不定要后悔的。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“There is still time!” he cried. “Reflect! perhaps you may repent!”","sentences":[{"en":"“There is still time!” he cried.","zh":"她抢嘴道：“决不！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Reflect! perhaps you may repent!”","zh":"然后又靠近他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Never!” she cried impetuously. And coming closer to him: “What ill could come to me? There is no desert, no precipice, no ocean I would not traverse with you. The longer we live together the more it will be like an embrace, every day closer, more heart to heart. There will be nothing to trouble us, no cares, no obstacle. We shall be alone, all to ourselves eternally. Oh, speak! Answer me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Never!” she cried impetuously.","zh":"“我怕什么风险？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And coming closer to him: “What ill could come to me?","zh":"沙漠、深渊、大洋，只要和你在一起，我就能过得去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There is no desert, no precipice, no ocean I would not traverse with you.","zh":"我们在一起生活，就像搂抱一样，一天比一天紧，一天比一天美满！我们没有顾虑，没有困难，什么也搅扰不了我们！","scope":"group"},{"en":"The longer we live together the more it will be like an embrace, every day closer, more heart to heart.","zh":"我们在一起生活，就像搂抱一样，一天比一天紧，一天比一天美满！我们没有顾虑，没有困难，什么也搅扰不了我们！","scope":"group"},{"en":"There will be nothing to trouble us, no cares, no obstacle.","zh":"我们只有自己，除去你和我，就是你和我，永远这样…","scope":"group"},{"en":"We shall be alone, all to ourselves eternally.","zh":"我们只有自己，除去你和我，就是你和我，永远这样…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Oh, speak!","zh":"说话呀，回答我呀。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Answer me!”","zh":"说话呀，回答我呀。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At regular intervals he answered, “Yes—Yes—” She had passed her hands through his hair, and she repeated in a childlike voice, despite the big tears which were falling, “Rodolphe! Rodolphe! Ah! Rodolphe! dear little Rodolphe!”","sentences":[{"en":"At regular intervals he answered, “Yes—Yes—” She had passed her hands through his hair, and she repeated in a childlike voice, despite the big tears which were falling, “Rodolphe!","zh":"他一会儿回答一声：“是呀…是呀…”她拿手摩挲他的头发，老大的泪珠往下淌，可是还用小孩子的声音一遍又一遍地说：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe!","zh":"“罗道耳弗！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Ah!","zh":"“罗道耳弗！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Rodolphe! dear little Rodolphe!”","zh":"罗道耳弗！啊！罗道耳弗，亲爱的小罗道耳弗！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Midnight struck.","sentences":[{"en":"Midnight struck.","zh":"钟声在响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Midnight!” said she. “Come, it is to-morrow. One day more!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Midnight!” said she.","zh":"她道：“半夜！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Come, it is to-morrow.","zh":"好，我们明天走！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One day more!”","zh":"还有一天！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He rose to go; and as if the movement he made had been the signal for their flight, Emma said, suddenly assuming a gay air—","sentences":[{"en":"He rose to go; and as if the movement he made had been the signal for their flight, Emma said, suddenly assuming a gay air—","zh":"他站起来要走；他这一动，仿佛就是他们逃走的暗号，爱玛忽然显出一副快活的模样：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You have the passports?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You have the passports?”","zh":"“你拿到护照了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“拿到啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are forgetting nothing?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are forgetting nothing?”","zh":"“你没有忘记什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No.”","zh":"“没有。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are you sure?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Are you sure?”","zh":"“你拿稳啦？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Certainly.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Certainly.”","zh":"“当然。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is at the Hotel de Provence, is it not, that you will wait for me at midday?”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is at the Hotel de Provence, is it not, that you will wait for me at midday?”","zh":"“你在普罗旺斯旅馆等我，对不对？正午？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He nodded.","sentences":[{"en":"He nodded.","zh":"他点了点头。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Till to-morrow then!” said Emma in a last caress; and she watched him go.","sentences":[{"en":"“Till to-morrow then!” said Emma in a last caress; and she watched him go.","zh":"爱玛最后吻了他一回道：“好，明天见！”她望着他走开。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He did not turn round. She ran after him, and, leaning over the water’s edge between the bulrushes—","sentences":[{"en":"He did not turn round.","zh":"他不回头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She ran after him, and, leaning over the water’s edge between the bulrushes—","zh":"她追过去，站在乱草当中，身子俯在水边，喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“To-morrow!” she cried.","sentences":[{"en":"“To-morrow!” she cried.","zh":"“明天见！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was already on the other side of the river and walking fast across the meadow.","sentences":[{"en":"He was already on the other side of the river and walking fast across the meadow.","zh":"他已经来到对岸，快步走进草原。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After a few moments Rodolphe stopped; and when he saw her with her white gown gradually fade away in the shade like a ghost, he was seized with such a beating of the heart that he leant against a tree lest he should fall.","sentences":[{"en":"After a few moments Rodolphe stopped; and when he saw her with her white gown gradually fade away in the shade like a ghost, he was seized with such a beating of the heart that he leant against a tree lest he should fall.","zh":"过了几分钟，罗道耳弗站住，看见她一身白，仿佛幽灵，在黑暗中渐渐消逝，他觉得心扑腾扑腾直跳，唯恐摔倒，连忙靠住一棵树。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What an imbecile I am!” he said with a fearful oath. “No matter! She was a pretty mistress!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What an imbecile I am!” he said with a fearful oath.","zh":"“我真蠢！”他骂了一句脏话，又道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“No matter!","zh":"“不管怎么说，她是个漂亮情妇！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was a pretty mistress!”","zh":"“不管怎么说，她是个漂亮情妇！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And immediately Emma’s beauty, with all the pleasures of their love, came back to him. For a moment he softened; then he rebelled against her.","sentences":[{"en":"And immediately Emma’s beauty, with all the pleasures of their love, came back to him.","zh":"于是爱玛的美丽，以及这种恋爱的种种欢乐，一下子又涌到他的心头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For a moment he softened; then he rebelled against her.","zh":"起初他还心软，后来他又恨起她来，指手画脚嚷嚷道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For, after all,” he exclaimed, gesticulating, “I can’t exile myself—have a child on my hands.”","sentences":[{"en":"“For, after all,” he exclaimed, gesticulating, “I can’t exile myself—have a child on my hands.”","zh":"“话说回来，我不能远走高飞，再带一个小女孩子。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was saying these things to give himself firmness.","sentences":[{"en":"He was saying these things to give himself firmness.","zh":"他说这些话加强他的信心：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And besides, the worry, the expense! Ah! no, no, no, no! a thousand times no! That would be too stupid.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And besides, the worry, the expense!","zh":"“再说，麻烦，开销…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! no, no, no, no! a thousand times no! That would be too stupid.”","zh":"啊！不，不，一千个不！傻瓜才干这事！”","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-13","part":2,"n":13,"title":"Part II · Chapter 13","titleZh":"中卷 · 13","paragraphs":[{"en":"No sooner was Rodolphe at home than he sat down quickly at his bureau under the stag’s head that hung as a trophy on the wall. But when he had the pen between his fingers, he could think of nothing, so that, resting on his elbows, he began to reflect. Emma seemed to him to have receded into a far-off past, as if the resolution he had taken had suddenly placed a distance between them.","sentences":[{"en":"No sooner was Rodolphe at home than he sat down quickly at his bureau under the stag’s head that hung as a trophy on the wall.","zh":"罗道耳弗一回到家，就急急忙忙坐到书桌面前，正好就在墙上战利品似的公鹿头底下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But when he had the pen between his fingers, he could think of nothing, so that, resting on his elbows, he began to reflect.","zh":"可是他拿起笔，想不出词，只好支着两个胳膊肘思索。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma seemed to him to have receded into a far-off past, as if the resolution he had taken had suddenly placed a distance between them.","zh":"他觉得爱玛仿佛退到遥远的过去，好像是他方才下的决心把他们忽然隔得老远一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To get back something of her, he fetched from the cupboard at the bedside an old Rheims biscuit-box, in which he usually kept his letters from women, and from it came an odour of dry dust and withered roses. First he saw a handkerchief with pale little spots. It was a handkerchief of hers. Once when they were walking her nose had bled; he had forgotten it. Near it, chipped at all the corners, was a miniature given him by Emma: her toilette seemed to him pretentious, and her languishing look in the worst possible taste. Then, from looking at this image and recalling the memory of its original, Emma’s features little by little grew confused in his remembrance, as if the living and the painted face, rubbing one against the other, had effaced each other. Finally, he read some of her letters; they were full of explanations relating to their journey, short, technical, and urgent, like business notes. He wanted to see the long ones again, those of old times. In order to find them at the bottom of the box, Rodolphe disturbed all the others, and mechanically began rummaging amidst this mass of papers and things, finding pell-mell bouquets, garters, a black mask, pins, and hair—hair! dark and fair, some even, catching in the hinges of the box, broke when it was opened.","sentences":[{"en":"To get back something of her, he fetched from the cupboard at the bedside an old Rheims biscuit-box, in which he usually kept his letters from women, and from it came an odour of dry dust and withered roses.","zh":"为了追回一点她的印象，他走到床头，从衣橱取出一个兰斯 饼干旧匣子，里面平日放着女人的书信。一股受潮的尘土和凋谢的玫瑰的气味散了出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"First he saw a handkerchief with pale little spots.","zh":"他首先看到一条有小暗点的手绢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a handkerchief of hers.","zh":"手绢是她的；有一回散步，她流鼻血用过。他已经忘记这回事了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Once when they were walking her nose had bled; he had forgotten it.","zh":"手绢是她的；有一回散步，她流鼻血用过。他已经忘记这回事了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Near it, chipped at all the corners, was a miniature given him by Emma: her toilette seemed to him pretentious, and her languishing look in the worst possible taste.","zh":"旁边有爱玛送他的小像，四角统统破损了；他嫌她装束不得当，斜眼看人的效果也极糟糕；他想多看两眼肖像，帮他回忆本人的模样，可是他想起来的爱玛的面貌，反而越来越模糊，好像活人的脸和画出来的脸，彼此对称，就这样抵消了似的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, from looking at this image and recalling the memory of its original, Emma’s features little by little grew confused in his remembrance, as if the living and the painted face, rubbing one against the other, had effaced each other.","zh":"旁边有爱玛送他的小像，四角统统破损了；他嫌她装束不得当，斜眼看人的效果也极糟糕；他想多看两眼肖像，帮他回忆本人的模样，可是他想起来的爱玛的面貌，反而越来越模糊，好像活人的脸和画出来的脸，彼此对称，就这样抵消了似的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Finally, he read some of her letters; they were full of explanations relating to their journey, short, technical, and urgent, like business notes.","zh":"最后，他念她的信；信上全是关于他们旅行的解说，简短、实际、急促，倒像生意人的单子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He wanted to see the long ones again, those of old times.","zh":"他希望看看长信、先前的信；罗道耳弗到尽底找，翻乱所有的信。他在这堆纸张和什物里头，伸手乱摸，七颠八倒，摸出了几把花、一只袜带、一个黑面具、几根别针和几缕头发——头发！棕色的、金黄色的；有的挂在铁片上，开匣子的时候绞断了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In order to find them at the bottom of the box, Rodolphe disturbed all the others, and mechanically began rummaging amidst this mass of papers and things, finding pell-mell bouquets, garters, a black mask, pins, and hair—hair! dark and fair, some even, catching in the hinges of the box, broke when it was opened.","zh":"他希望看看长信、先前的信；罗道耳弗到尽底找，翻乱所有的信。他在这堆纸张和什物里头，伸手乱摸，七颠八倒，摸出了几把花、一只袜带、一个黑面具、几根别针和几缕头发——头发！棕色的、金黄色的；有的挂在铁片上，开匣子的时候绞断了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Thus dallying with his souvenirs, he examined the writing and the style of the letters, as varied as their orthography. They were tender or jovial, facetious, melancholy; there were some that asked for love, others that asked for money. A word recalled faces to him, certain gestures, the sound of a voice; sometimes, however, he remembered nothing at all.","sentences":[{"en":"Thus dallying with his souvenirs, he examined the writing and the style of the letters, as varied as their orthography.","zh":"他就这样回忆过去，查看书信的字体和风格；它们和拼写一样错综复杂，意思温柔，要不就是愉快、滑稽、忧郁；有的书信要爱情，有的书信要钱。可是有时候，他什么也想不起来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were tender or jovial, facetious, melancholy; there were some that asked for love, others that asked for money.","zh":"他就这样回忆过去，查看书信的字体和风格；它们和拼写一样错综复杂，意思温柔，要不就是愉快、滑稽、忧郁；有的书信要爱情，有的书信要钱。可是有时候，他什么也想不起来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A word recalled faces to him, certain gestures, the sound of a voice; sometimes, however, he remembered nothing at all.","zh":"他就这样回忆过去，查看书信的字体和风格；它们和拼写一样错综复杂，意思温柔，要不就是愉快、滑稽、忧郁；有的书信要爱情，有的书信要钱。可是有时候，他什么也想不起来。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"In fact, these women, rushing at once into his thoughts, cramped each other and lessened, as reduced to a uniform level of love that equalised them all. So taking handfuls of the mixed-up letters, he amused himself for some moments with letting them fall in cascades from his right into his left hand. At last, bored and weary, Rodolphe took back the box to the cupboard, saying to himself, “What a lot of rubbish!” Which summed up his opinion; for pleasures, like schoolboys in a school courtyard, had so trampled upon his heart that no green thing grew there, and that which passed through it, more heedless than children, did not even, like them, leave a name carved upon the wall.","sentences":[{"en":"In fact, these women, rushing at once into his thoughts, cramped each other and lessened, as reduced to a uniform level of love that equalised them all.","zh":"说实话，这些女人同时跑进他的思想，互相妨碍，仿佛拘在同一爱情水平底下，截长补短，统统变小了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So taking handfuls of the mixed-up letters, he amused himself for some moments with letting them fall in cascades from his right into his left hand.","zh":"所以右手抓起一把弄乱了的书信，他好几分钟，看它们瀑布似的往下倾泻，再用左手接住玩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, bored and weary, Rodolphe took back the box to the cupboard, saying to himself, “What a lot of rubbish!”","zh":"最后，罗道耳弗腻了，困了，又拿匣子放进衣橱，自言自语道：“简直扯淡！”这句话说明他的见解。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Which summed up his opinion; for pleasures, like schoolboys in a school courtyard, had so trampled upon his heart that no green thing grew there, and that which passed through it, more heedless than children, did not even, like them, leave a name carved upon the wall.","zh":"他是风月老手，欢娱在他的心头踏来踏去，好像小学生在学校院子把地踏硬了，弄得寸草不生，女人经过他的心头，比孩子们还漫不经心，连名姓也没有留下一个，不像孩子们，还把姓名刻在墙上。他向自己道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come,” said he, “let’s begin.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come,” said he, “let’s begin.”","zh":"“好，开始吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He wrote—","sentences":[{"en":"He wrote—","zh":"他写道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Courage, Emma! courage! I would not bring misery into your life.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Courage, Emma! courage!","zh":"拿出勇气来，爱玛！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I would not bring misery into your life.”","zh":"拿出勇气来！我不希望害您一辈子…罗道耳弗寻思：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“After all, that’s true,” thought Rodolphe. “I am acting in her interest; I am honest.”","sentences":[{"en":"“After all, that’s true,” thought Rodolphe.","zh":"“其实，真是这样；我这是为她好；我这人再厚道不过。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I am acting in her interest; I am honest.”","zh":"“其实，真是这样；我这是为她好；我这人再厚道不过。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Have you carefully weighed your resolution? Do you know to what an abyss I was dragging you, poor angel? No, you do not, do you? You were coming confident and fearless, believing in happiness in the future. Ah! unhappy that we are—insensate!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you carefully weighed your resolution?","zh":"您下决心以前，可曾好好想过？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you know to what an abyss I was dragging you, poor angel?","zh":"可怜的天使，您知道我把您拖到怎样的深渊吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No, you do not, do you?","zh":"不知道，对不对？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You were coming confident and fearless, believing in happiness in the future.","zh":"您满怀信心，不顾一切，只是相信幸福、未来…啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! unhappy that we are—insensate!”","zh":"我们真不幸！也真不懂事！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe stopped here to think of some good excuse.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe stopped here to think of some good excuse.","zh":"罗道耳弗写到这里，停住笔，寻找漂亮借口。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If I told her all my fortune is lost? No! Besides, that would stop nothing. It would all have to be begun over again later on. As if one could make women like that listen to reason!” He reflected, then went on—","sentences":[{"en":"“If I told her all my fortune is lost?","zh":"告诉她我破产了，怎么样？啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No! Besides, that would stop nothing.","zh":"不好，再说，这不顶事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It would all have to be begun over again later on.","zh":"过后又要重新耍这一套。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As if one could make women like that listen to reason!”","zh":"难道同这样的女人能谈得通吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He reflected, then went on—","zh":"他想了想，续下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I shall not forget you, oh believe it; and I shall ever have a profound devotion for you; but some day, sooner or later, this ardour (such is the fate of human things) would have grown less, no doubt. Lassitude would have come to us, and who knows if I should not even have had the atrocious pain of witnessing your remorse, of sharing it myself, since I should have been its cause? The mere idea of the grief that would come to you tortures me, Emma. Forget me! Why did I ever know you? Why were you so beautiful? Is it my fault? O my God! No, no! Accuse only fate.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I shall not forget you, oh believe it; and I shall ever have a profound devotion for you; but some day, sooner or later, this ardour (such is the fate of human things) would have grown less, no doubt.","zh":"请相信，我忘不了您；我对您将永远忠诚。不过迟早有一天，不用说，这种热情（人间的事注定是这样的）要冷却的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lassitude would have come to us, and who knows if I should not even have had the atrocious pain of witnessing your remorse, of sharing it myself, since I should have been its cause?","zh":"我们会厌倦的。谁知道我会不会痛苦万分，看到您有一天后悔，也看自己后悔，因为我是您后悔的原因。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The mere idea of the grief that would come to you tortures me, Emma.","zh":"单单想到您要难过，爱玛！我就如坐针毡！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Forget me!","zh":"忘了我吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why did I ever know you?","zh":"为什么我偏认识了您？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why were you so beautiful?","zh":"为什么您生得这样美？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Is it my fault?","zh":"难道这是我的错？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"O my God!","zh":"我的上帝！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No, no! Accuse only fate.”","zh":"不，不，怨也只好怨命！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That’s a word that always tells,” he said to himself.","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s a word that always tells,” he said to himself.","zh":"他自言自语道：“命这个字永远打动人。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah, if you had been one of those frivolous women that one sees, certainly I might, through egotism, have tried an experiment, in that case without danger for you. But that delicious exaltation, at once your charm and your torment, has prevented you from understanding, adorable woman that you are, the falseness of our future position. Nor had I reflected upon this at first, and I rested in the shade of that ideal happiness as beneath that of the manchineel tree, without foreseeing the consequences.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah, if you had been one of those frivolous women that one sees, certainly I might, through egotism, have tried an experiment, in that case without danger for you.","zh":"啊！如果您是一个水性杨花的女人，像常见的那些女人一样，当然，我就可以自私自利，照眼前的安排做，因为这就不会害您了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But that delicious exaltation, at once your charm and your torment, has prevented you from understanding, adorable woman that you are, the falseness of our future position.","zh":"您动人的狂热既做成您的魅力，也做成您的痛苦，且妨碍了您这样一位令人膜拜的女子看清我们将来处境的险恶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nor had I reflected upon this at first, and I rested in the shade of that ideal happiness as beneath that of the manchineel tree, without foreseeing the consequences.”","zh":"我也一样，开头没有多加考虑。我躺在这种理想的幸福的影子里，就像躺在芒色尼耶树 的影子里一样，安安逸逸，不管后果有多可怕。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Perhaps she’ll think I’m giving it up from avarice. Ah, well! so much the worse; it must be stopped!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Perhaps she’ll think I’m giving it up from avarice.","zh":"“她也许以为我是舍不得花钱才不出走…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah, well! so much the worse; it must be stopped!”","zh":"啊！管它呐，她爱怎样想就怎样想，反正得散伙！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The world is cruel, Emma. Wherever we might have gone, it would have persecuted us. You would have had to put up with indiscreet questions, calumny, contempt, insult perhaps. Insult to you! Oh! And I, who would place you on a throne! I who bear with me your memory as a talisman! For I am going to punish myself by exile for all the ill I have done you. I am going away. Whither I know not. I am mad. Adieu! Be good always. Preserve the memory of the unfortunate who has lost you. Teach my name to your child; let her repeat it in her prayers.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The world is cruel, Emma.","zh":"爱玛，人世冷酷，我们走到天涯海角，也不会放过我们。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Wherever we might have gone, it would have persecuted us.","zh":"爱玛，人世冷酷，我们走到天涯海角，也不会放过我们。","scope":"group"},{"en":"You would have had to put up with indiscreet questions, calumny, contempt, insult perhaps.","zh":"您得忍受无礼的盘问、诽谤、蔑视，甚至于侮辱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Insult to you!","zh":"侮辱您！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh!","zh":"哦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And I, who would place you on a throne!","zh":"而我却要您坐上宝座！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I who bear with me your memory as a talisman!","zh":"而我却在心目中把您看成护符！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For I am going to punish myself by exile for all the ill I have done you.","zh":"因为我要亡命异乡，这样来惩罚我带给您的一切祸殃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am going away.","zh":"我走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Whither I know not.","zh":"去什么地方？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am mad.","zh":"我不知道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Adieu!","zh":"我疯啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Be good always.","zh":"永别了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Preserve the memory of the unfortunate who has lost you.","zh":"愿您永远善良！想着失去您的不幸男子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Teach my name to your child; let her repeat it in her prayers.”","zh":"把我的名字告诉您的孩子，让她为我祈祷吧。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The wicks of the candles flickered. Rodolphe got up to, shut the window, and when he had sat down again—","sentences":[{"en":"The wicks of the candles flickered.","zh":"两支蜡烛心子直摇晃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe got up to, shut the window, and when he had sat down again—","zh":"罗道耳弗站起，过去关上窗户，又回来坐好了，道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I think it’s all right. Ah! and this for fear she should come and hunt me up.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I think it’s all right.","zh":"“我看，也就是这些了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! and this for fear she should come and hunt me up.”","zh":"啊，添两句话，免得再来找我捣乱。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I shall be far away when you read these sad lines, for I have wished to flee as quickly as possible to shun the temptation of seeing you again. No weakness! I shall return, and perhaps later on we shall talk together very coldly of our old love. Adieu!”","sentences":[{"en":"“I shall be far away when you read these sad lines, for I have wished to flee as quickly as possible to shun the temptation of seeing you again.","zh":"您读这封忧郁的信的时候，我已经走远了；因为我要尽快逃走，免得心思不定，再去看您。不要软弱！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No weakness!","zh":"我会回来的；说不定将来有一天，我们会在一起，心如古井，谈起我们的旧情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I shall return, and perhaps later on we shall talk together very coldly of our old love.","zh":"我会回来的；说不定将来有一天，我们会在一起，心如古井，谈起我们的旧情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Adieu!”","zh":"永别了！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And there was a last “adieu” divided into two words! “A Dieu!” which he thought in very excellent taste.","sentences":[{"en":"And there was a last “adieu” divided into two words!","zh":"最后又来了一个“永别了”，分成两截：“永——别了！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“A Dieu!” which he thought in very excellent taste.","zh":"认为十分得体。他自言自语道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Now how am I to sign?” he said to himself. “‘Yours devotedly?’ No! ‘Your friend?’ Yes, that’s it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now how am I to sign?” he said to himself.","zh":"“现在，落什么款好？‘您最忠心的’…不好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“‘Yours devotedly?’","zh":"‘您的朋友’？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No! ‘Your friend?’","zh":"对，就是它。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yes, that’s it.”","zh":"您的朋友","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Your friend.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Your friend.”","zh":"他又念了一遍信，觉得很好。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He re-read his letter. He considered it very good.","sentences":[{"en":"He re-read his letter.","zh":"他又念了一遍信，觉得很好。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He considered it very good.","zh":"他带着感情，寻思道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Poor little woman!” he thought with emotion. “She’ll think me harder than a rock. There ought to have been some tears on this; but I can’t cry; it isn’t my fault.” Then, having emptied some water into a glass, Rodolphe dipped his finger into it, and let a big drop fall on the paper, that made a pale stain on the ink. Then looking for a seal, he came upon the one “Amor nel cor.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Poor little woman!” he thought with emotion.","zh":"“可怜的小女人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“She’ll think me harder than a rock.","zh":"她以为我的心肠比石头还硬了；应当来几滴眼泪才对；不过我呀，我哭不出来；这不是我的错。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"There ought to have been some tears on this; but I can’t cry; it isn’t my fault.”","zh":"她以为我的心肠比石头还硬了；应当来几滴眼泪才对；不过我呀，我哭不出来；这不是我的错。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, having emptied some water into a glass, Rodolphe dipped his finger into it, and let a big drop fall on the paper, that made a pale stain on the ink.","zh":"罗道耳弗于是倒了一杯水，沾湿手指，在半空丢下一大滴水，冲淡一个地方的墨水。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then looking for a seal, he came upon the one “Amor nel cor.”","zh":"随后，他找印章封信，摸到的印章偏偏就是那颗“心心相印”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That doesn’t at all fit in with the circumstances. Pshaw! never mind!”","sentences":[{"en":"“That doesn’t at all fit in with the circumstances.","zh":"“这不很协调…啊！算啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Pshaw! never mind!”","zh":"有什么关系！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After which he smoked three pipes and went to bed.","sentences":[{"en":"After which he smoked three pipes and went to bed.","zh":"盖过章，封好信，他吸了三烟斗烟，睡觉去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day when he was up (at about two o’clock—he had slept late), Rodolphe had a basket of apricots picked. He put his letter at the bottom under some vine leaves, and at once ordered Girard, his ploughman, to take it with care to Madame Bovary. He made use of this means for corresponding with her, sending according to the season fruits or game.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day when he was up (at about two o’clock—he had slept late), Rodolphe had a basket of apricots picked.","zh":"第二天，罗道耳弗起床（下午两点左右：他睡迟了），叫人摘了一篮杏子，信放在尽底，盖上几片葡萄叶，马上吩咐犁地的吉拉尔，小心在意，送给包法利夫人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He put his letter at the bottom under some vine leaves, and at once ordered Girard, his ploughman, to take it with care to Madame Bovary.","zh":"第二天，罗道耳弗起床（下午两点左右：他睡迟了），叫人摘了一篮杏子，信放在尽底，盖上几片葡萄叶，马上吩咐犁地的吉拉尔，小心在意，送给包法利夫人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He made use of this means for corresponding with her, sending according to the season fruits or game.","zh":"他平日就是用这个方法和她通信的，依照季节，送她水果或者打猎得来的野味。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If she asks after me,” he said, “you will tell her that I have gone on a journey. You must give the basket to her herself, into her own hands. Get along and take care!”","sentences":[{"en":"“If she asks after me,” he said, “you will tell her that I have gone on a journey.","zh":"“她要是问起我的消息，你就回答，我出远门去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You must give the basket to her herself, into her own hands.","zh":"篮子一定要当面交给本人…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Get along and take care!”","zh":"去吧，当心！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Girard put on his new blouse, knotted his handkerchief round the apricots, and walking with great heavy steps in his thick iron-bound galoshes, made his way to Yonville.","sentences":[{"en":"Girard put on his new blouse, knotted his handkerchief round the apricots, and walking with great heavy steps in his thick iron-bound galoshes, made his way to Yonville.","zh":"吉拉尔穿上新工人服，拿手帕兜住杏子挽了一个结，蹬起他的铁钉大木底皮鞋，迈开大步，从容不迫，去了永镇。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary, when he got to her house, was arranging a bundle of linen on the kitchen-table with Félicité.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary, when he got to her house, was arranging a bundle of linen on the kitchen-table with Félicité.","zh":"他来到包法利夫人家，见她正和全福在厨房桌子上料理一包要洗的东西。伙计说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Here,” said the ploughboy, “is something for you—from the master.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Here,” said the ploughboy, “is something for you—from the master.”","zh":"“这是我们主人送您的东西。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was seized with apprehension, and as she sought in her pocket for some coppers, she looked at the peasant with haggard eyes, while he himself looked at her with amazement, not understanding how such a present could so move anyone. At last he went out. Félicité remained. She could bear it no longer; she ran into the sitting room as if to take the apricots there, overturned the basket, tore away the leaves, found the letter, opened it, and, as if some fearful fire were behind her, Emma flew to her room terrified.","sentences":[{"en":"She was seized with apprehension, and as she sought in her pocket for some coppers, she looked at the peasant with haggard eyes, while he himself looked at her with amazement, not understanding how such a present could so move anyone.","zh":"她惶惑了，一面在衣袋摸零钱，一面瞪圆眼睛打量农夫，同时他纳罕这么一件礼物怎会使人那样感动，望定了她，也在吃惊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last he went out.","zh":"他终于走了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Félicité remained.","zh":"全福还在身边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She could bear it no longer; she ran into the sitting room as if to take the apricots there, overturned the basket, tore away the leaves, found the letter, opened it, and, as if some fearful fire were behind her, Emma flew to her room terrified.","zh":"爱玛憋不住了，跑进厅房，模样像要去放杏子。她倒翻篮子，抓去叶子，找到书信，拆开了，好像背后起了大火一样，爱玛惊惶失措，朝她的卧室逃跑。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles was there; she saw him; he spoke to her; she heard nothing, and she went on quickly up the stairs, breathless, distraught, dumb, and ever holding this horrible piece of paper, that crackled between her fingers like a plate of sheet-iron. On the second floor she stopped before the attic door, which was closed.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles was there; she saw him; he spoke to her; she heard nothing, and she went on quickly up the stairs, breathless, distraught, dumb, and ever holding this horrible piece of paper, that crackled between her fingers like a plate of sheet-iron.","zh":"她望见查理在里头；他同她说话，她一句也听不见，急急忙忙，继续走上楼梯，气喘吁吁，慌里慌张，颠三倒四，总拿着那张可怕的信纸，信纸仿佛一张铁皮， ，在手里直响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the second floor she stopped before the attic door, which was closed.","zh":"她上到三楼，在阁楼前面站住。门关着。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she tried to calm herself; she recalled the letter; she must finish it; she did not dare to. And where? How? She would be seen! “Ah, no! here,” she thought, “I shall be all right.”","sentences":[{"en":"Then she tried to calm herself; she recalled the letter; she must finish it; she did not dare to.","zh":"她这时打算静下心来。她想起了信；应该念完信，可是她不敢。再说，到什么地方念？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And where?","zh":"怎么念？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How?","zh":"人家会看见她的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She would be seen!","zh":"人家会看见她的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Ah, no! here,” she thought, “I shall be all right.”","zh":"她想道：“啊！不，这儿就好。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma pushed open the door and went in.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma pushed open the door and went in.","zh":"爱玛推开门，走进阁楼。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The slates threw straight down a heavy heat that gripped her temples, stifled her; she dragged herself to the closed garret-window. She drew back the bolt, and the dazzling light burst in with a leap.","sentences":[{"en":"The slates threw straight down a heavy heat that gripped her temples, stifled her; she dragged herself to the closed garret-window.","zh":"空气闷热：热气笔直从石瓦下来，压抑太阳穴，阻塞呼吸。她好不容易走到天窗跟前，拔去窗闩，打开窗户，阳光一涌而入，照花了眼。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She drew back the bolt, and the dazzling light burst in with a leap.","zh":"空气闷热：热气笔直从石瓦下来，压抑太阳穴，阻塞呼吸。她好不容易走到天窗跟前，拔去窗闩，打开窗户，阳光一涌而入，照花了眼。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Opposite, beyond the roofs, stretched the open country till it was lost to sight. Down below, underneath her, the village square was empty; the stones of the pavement glittered, the weathercocks on the houses were motionless. At the corner of the street, from a lower storey, rose a kind of humming with strident modulations. It was Binet turning.","sentences":[{"en":"Opposite, beyond the roofs, stretched the open country till it was lost to sight.","zh":"隔着房顶，就见对面的原野，一望无际。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Down below, underneath her, the village square was empty; the stones of the pavement glittered, the weathercocks on the houses were motionless.","zh":"下面广场空空落落，人行道的石子闪闪烁烁，房上风标一动不动，街角有一家二楼传出呜隆呜隆的响声，还夹杂一些刺耳的音响。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At the corner of the street, from a lower storey, rose a kind of humming with strident modulations.","zh":"下面广场空空落落，人行道的石子闪闪烁烁，房上风标一动不动，街角有一家二楼传出呜隆呜隆的响声，还夹杂一些刺耳的音响。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was Binet turning.","zh":"那是毕耐先生在旋东西。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She leant against the embrasure of the window, and reread the letter with angry sneers. But the more she fixed her attention upon it, the more confused were her ideas. She saw him again, heard him, encircled him with her arms, and throbs of her heart, that beat against her breast like blows of a sledge-hammer, grew faster and faster, with uneven intervals. She looked about her with the wish that the earth might crumble into pieces. Why not end it all? What restrained her? She was free. She advanced, looking at the paving-stones, saying to herself, “Come! come!”","sentences":[{"en":"She leant against the embrasure of the window, and reread the letter with angry sneers.","zh":"她靠着窗台，拿起信来又念，气得直发冷笑。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the more she fixed her attention upon it, the more confused were her ideas.","zh":"不过她越用心看信，心越乱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She saw him again, heard him, encircled him with her arms, and throbs of her heart, that beat against her breast like blows of a sledge-hammer, grew faster and faster, with uneven intervals.","zh":"她恍惚又看见他，听他说话，两只胳膊还搂住她。心在胸脯里跳得像大杠子使劲撞城门一样，不但不匀，而且一次紧似一次。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She looked about her with the wish that the earth might crumble into pieces.","zh":"她向四周扫了一眼，恨不得地陷下去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why not end it all?","zh":"为什么不死了拉倒？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What restrained her?","zh":"谁拦着她了？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was free.","zh":"只有她一个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She advanced, looking at the paving-stones, saying to herself, “Come! come!”","zh":"她朝前走，望着石板路，向自己说：“跳吧！跳吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The luminous ray that came straight up from below drew the weight of her body towards the abyss. It seemed to her that the ground of the oscillating square went up the walls and that the floor dipped on end like a tossing boat. She was right at the edge, almost hanging, surrounded by vast space. The blue of the heavens suffused her, the air was whirling in her hollow head; she had but to yield, to let herself be taken; and the humming of the lathe never ceased, like an angry voice calling her.","sentences":[{"en":"The luminous ray that came straight up from below drew the weight of her body towards the abyss.","zh":"明晃晃的阳光，从底下笔直反射上来，裹住她的身体，往深渊拉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It seemed to her that the ground of the oscillating square went up the walls and that the floor dipped on end like a tossing boat.","zh":"她觉得广场土地晃晃悠悠，齐墙凸起，地板向一边倾斜，好像船只前后摆动一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was right at the edge, almost hanging, surrounded by vast space.","zh":"她站在窗口，仿佛挂在半空，四周一无所有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The blue of the heavens suffused her, the air was whirling in her hollow head; she had but to yield, to let herself be taken; and the humming of the lathe never ceased, like an angry voice calling her.","zh":"碧天近在身边，空气在她空洞的脑袋里流来流去，她只要就势一跳，朝前一纵，也就成了。旋床呜隆呜隆，并不中断，活像一个发怒的声音在叫她一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Emma! Emma!” cried Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“Emma!","zh":"查理喊着：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma!” cried Charles.","zh":"查理喊着：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She stopped.","sentences":[{"en":"She stopped.","zh":"“太太！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Wherever are you? Come!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Wherever are you?","zh":"太太！”她站住了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Come!”","zh":"太太！”她站住了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The thought that she had just escaped from death almost made her faint with terror. She closed her eyes; then she shivered at the touch of a hand on her sleeve; it was Félicité.","sentences":[{"en":"The thought that she had just escaped from death almost made her faint with terror.","zh":"“你在哪儿？来呀！”想起自己险些死掉，她一害怕，几乎晕倒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She closed her eyes; then she shivered at the touch of a hand on her sleeve; it was Félicité.","zh":"她闭住眼睛；有一只手拉她的衣袖，她发抖了：原来是全福。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Master is waiting for you, madame; the soup is on the table.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Master is waiting for you, madame; the soup is on the table.”","zh":"“太太，老爷等您，汤端上啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she had to go down to sit at table.","sentences":[{"en":"And she had to go down to sit at table.","zh":"必须下楼！必须用饭！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She tried to eat. The food choked her. Then she unfolded her napkin as if to examine the darns, and she really thought of applying herself to this work, counting the threads in the linen. Suddenly the remembrance of the letter returned to her. How had she lost it? Where could she find it? But she felt such weariness of spirit that she could not even invent a pretext for leaving the table. Then she became a coward; she was afraid of Charles; he knew all, that was certain! Indeed he pronounced these words in a strange manner:","sentences":[{"en":"She tried to eat.","zh":"她勉强吃了几口，东西堵着喉咙。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The food choked her.","zh":"她勉强吃了几口，东西堵着喉咙。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she unfolded her napkin as if to examine the darns, and she really thought of applying herself to this work, counting the threads in the linen.","zh":"于是她摊开饭巾，仿佛查看补缀好了没有，而且专心致志，当真数起上面的线来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Suddenly the remembrance of the letter returned to her.","zh":"她忽然想到书信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How had she lost it?","zh":"难道她把它丢了？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where could she find it?","zh":"到哪儿找去？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she felt such weariness of spirit that she could not even invent a pretext for leaving the table.","zh":"可是她觉得自己一百二十分劳累，就连捏造借口，离开饭桌，也没有这份心思。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she became a coward; she was afraid of Charles; he knew all, that was certain!","zh":"而且她变得胆怯起来，害怕查理：毫无疑问，他全知道！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Indeed he pronounced these words in a strange manner:","zh":"说实话，他这几句话就讲得古怪：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We are not likely to see Monsieur Rodolphe soon again, it seems.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We are not likely to see Monsieur Rodolphe soon again, it seems.”","zh":"“看样子，我们有一阵子，要见不着罗道耳弗先生了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Who told you?” she said, shuddering.","sentences":[{"en":"“Who told you?” she said, shuddering.","zh":"她战栗着问：“谁告诉你的？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Who told me!” he replied, rather astonished at her abrupt tone. “Why, Girard, whom I met just now at the door of the Cafe Francais. He has gone on a journey, or is to go.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who told me!” he replied, rather astonished at her abrupt tone.","zh":"口吻尖利，他听了有点吃惊，回答道：“谁告诉我的？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Why, Girard, whom I met just now at the door of the Cafe Francais.","zh":"是吉拉尔呀。我方才在法兰西咖啡馆门口遇到他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He has gone on a journey, or is to go.”","zh":"罗道耳弗先生旅行去了，要不，也快去了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She gave a sob.","sentences":[{"en":"She gave a sob.","zh":"她抽噎了一下。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What surprises you in that? He absents himself like that from time to time for a change, and, ma foi, I think he’s right, when one has a fortune and is a bachelor. Besides, he has jolly times, has our friend. He’s a bit of a rake. Monsieur Langlois told me—”","sentences":[{"en":"“What surprises you in that?","zh":"“这有什么好奇怪的？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He absents himself like that from time to time for a change, and, ma foi, I think he’s right, when one has a fortune and is a bachelor.","zh":"他动不动就出门找消遣去，真的！我赞成。一个人有钱，又是单身汉！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, he has jolly times, has our friend.","zh":"——再说，他也善于寻欢作乐，我们的朋友！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He’s a bit of a rake.","zh":"他是一个浮浪子弟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Langlois told me—”","zh":"朗格洛瓦先生告诉我…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He stopped for propriety’s sake because the servant came in. She put back into the basket the apricots scattered on the sideboard. Charles, without noticing his wife’s colour, had them brought to him, took one, and bit into it.","sentences":[{"en":"He stopped for propriety’s sake because the servant came in.","zh":"女用人进来，他只好住口不讲。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She put back into the basket the apricots scattered on the sideboard.","zh":"杏子散在摆设架上，全福又全收到篮子里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles, without noticing his wife’s colour, had them brought to him, took one, and bit into it.","zh":"查理没有注意太太脸红，叫她端过篮子，拿起一个咬着，还说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! perfect!” said he; “just taste!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! perfect!” said he; “just taste!”","zh":"“啊！好吃极啦！来，尝尝。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he handed her the basket, which she put away from her gently.","sentences":[{"en":"And he handed her the basket, which she put away from her gently.","zh":"他递篮子给她，她轻轻推开了。他一连在她鼻子底下递了几回，说道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do just smell! What an odour!” he remarked, passing it under her nose several times.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do just smell!","zh":"“闻闻看：真香！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What an odour!” he remarked, passing it under her nose several times.","zh":"她跳起来道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I am choking,” she cried, leaping up. But by an effort of will the spasm passed; then—","sentences":[{"en":"“I am choking,” she cried, leaping up.","zh":"“我出不来气！”可是她使劲一挣，这阵痉挛也就过去了。她道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"But by an effort of will the spasm passed; then—","zh":"“我出不来气！”可是她使劲一挣，这阵痉挛也就过去了。她道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“It is nothing,” she said, “it is nothing! It is nervousness. Sit down and go on eating.” For she dreaded lest he should begin questioning her, attending to her, that she should not be left alone.","sentences":[{"en":"“It is nothing,” she said, “it is nothing!","zh":"“没有什么！没有什么！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is nervousness.","zh":"是神经作怪！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sit down and go on eating.”","zh":"坐下吧，吃你的！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For she dreaded lest he should begin questioning her, attending to her, that she should not be left alone.","zh":"因为她就怕他盘问她，照料她，不离开她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles, to obey her, sat down again, and he spat the stones of the apricots into his hands, afterwards putting them on his plate.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles, to obey her, sat down again, and he spat the stones of the apricots into his hands, afterwards putting them on his plate.","zh":"查理听话，又坐下来了。他把杏核吐在手心，再搁到他的盘子里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Suddenly a blue tilbury passed across the square at a rapid trot. Emma uttered a cry and fell back rigid to the ground.","sentences":[{"en":"Suddenly a blue tilbury passed across the square at a rapid trot.","zh":"忽见一辆蓝色提耳玻里，驰过广场。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma uttered a cry and fell back rigid to the ground.","zh":"爱玛喊了一声，直挺挺仰面倒在地上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In fact, Rodolphe, after many reflections, had decided to set out for Rouen. Now, as from La Huchette to Buchy there is no other way than by Yonville, he had to go through the village, and Emma had recognised him by the rays of the lanterns, which like lightning flashed through the twilight.","sentences":[{"en":"In fact, Rodolphe, after many reflections, had decided to set out for Rouen.","zh":"说实话，罗道耳弗考虑再三，决计还是到鲁昂去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now, as from La Huchette to Buchy there is no other way than by Yonville, he had to go through the village, and Emma had recognised him by the rays of the lanterns, which like lightning flashed through the twilight.","zh":"可是从于歇特去比西，除去永镇这条路之外，就没有别的路可走。他只好穿过村子。天色昏黑，车灯如电，一闪而过。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The chemist, at the tumult which broke out in the house ran thither. The table with all the plates was upset; sauce, meat, knives, the salt, and cruet-stand were strewn over the room; Charles was calling for help; Berthe, scared, was crying; and Félicité, whose hands trembled, was unlacing her mistress, whose whole body shivered convulsively.","sentences":[{"en":"The chemist, at the tumult which broke out in the house ran thither.","zh":"药剂师听见医生家乱成一团，跑了过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The table with all the plates was upset; sauce, meat, knives, the salt, and cruet-stand were strewn over the room; Charles was calling for help; Berthe, scared, was crying; and Félicité, whose hands trembled, was unlacing her mistress, whose whole body shivered convulsively.","zh":"桌子连同盘子，统统打翻了；酱油、肉、刀子、盐瓶和油瓶，扔了一地；查理连声喊救；白尔特吓得直哭；全福手在哆嗦，给太太解衣服。爱玛浑身上下都在抽搐。药剂师道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I’ll run to my laboratory for some aromatic vinegar,” said the druggist.","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll run to my laboratory for some aromatic vinegar,” said the druggist.","zh":"“我到我的实验室找一点香醋来。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then as she opened her eyes on smelling the bottle—","sentences":[{"en":"Then as she opened her eyes on smelling the bottle—","zh":"随后，她闻着小醋瓶，睁开眼睛，他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I was sure of it,” he remarked; “that would wake any dead person for you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was sure of it,” he remarked; “that would wake any dead person for you!”","zh":"“我拿稳了有用；死人也能一闻就醒。”查理道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Speak to us,” said Charles; “collect yourself; it is your Charles, who loves you. Do you know me? See! here is your little girl! Oh, kiss her!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Speak to us,” said Charles; “collect yourself; it is your Charles, who loves you.","zh":"“说话！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you know me?","zh":"说话！醒醒！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"See! here is your little girl!","zh":"是我，爱你的查理！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, kiss her!”","zh":"你认得我吗？看，这是你的小女儿：亲亲她！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The child stretched out her arms to her mother to cling to her neck. But turning away her head, Emma said in a broken voice “No, no! no one!”","sentences":[{"en":"The child stretched out her arms to her mother to cling to her neck.","zh":"小女孩子朝母亲伸出胳膊，想搂她的脖子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But turning away her head, Emma said in a broken voice “No, no! no one!”","zh":"但是爱玛转开了头，声音一喘一喘的：“不，不…什么人也不要！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She fainted again. They carried her to her bed. She lay there stretched at full length, her lips apart, her eyelids closed, her hands open, motionless, and white as a waxen image. Two streams of tears flowed from her eyes and fell slowly upon the pillow.","sentences":[{"en":"She fainted again.","zh":"她又晕过去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They carried her to her bed.","zh":"大家把她抬到床上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She lay there stretched at full length, her lips apart, her eyelids closed, her hands open, motionless, and white as a waxen image.","zh":"她躺着动也不动，嘴张开，眼皮闭住，手放平，脸白白的，活像一座蜡像。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Two streams of tears flowed from her eyes and fell slowly upon the pillow.","zh":"两道眼泪慢慢流到枕头上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles, standing up, was at the back of the alcove, and the chemist, near him, maintained that meditative silence that is becoming on the serious occasions of life.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles, standing up, was at the back of the alcove, and the chemist, near him, maintained that meditative silence that is becoming on the serious occasions of life.","zh":"查理直挺挺待在靠里床头，药剂师站在一旁，保持着人在重要关头应有的思维的静默。他拿胳膊肘杵了他一下道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do not be uneasy,” he said, touching his elbow; “I think the paroxysm is past.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do not be uneasy,” he said, touching his elbow; “I think the paroxysm is past.”","zh":"“放心好了，我想危险过去啦。”查理看着她睡，回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, she is resting a little now,” answered Charles, watching her sleep. “Poor girl! poor girl! She had gone off now!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, she is resting a little now,” answered Charles, watching her sleep.","zh":"“是的，她现在安静多了！可怜的女人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Poor girl! poor girl!","zh":"可怜的女人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had gone off now!”","zh":"她又病啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Homais asked how the accident had come about. Charles answered that she had been taken ill suddenly while she was eating some apricots.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Homais asked how the accident had come about.","zh":"郝麦于是问起发病的原委。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles answered that she had been taken ill suddenly while she was eating some apricots.","zh":"查理回答，她正吃杏子，病就突然发作了。药剂师道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Extraordinary!” continued the chemist. “But it might be that the apricots had brought on the syncope. Some natures are so sensitive to certain smells; and it would even be a very fine question to study both in its pathological and physiological relation. The priests know the importance of it, they who have introduced aromatics into all their ceremonies. It is to stupefy the senses and to bring on ecstasies—a thing, moreover, very easy in persons of the weaker sex, who are more delicate than the other. Some are cited who faint at the smell of burnt hartshorn, of new bread—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Extraordinary!” continued the chemist.","zh":"“怪事！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“But it might be that the apricots had brought on the syncope.","zh":"不过也很可能就是杏子引起昏迷的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some natures are so sensitive to certain smells; and it would even be a very fine question to study both in its pathological and physiological relation.","zh":"有些人对某种气味，生来非常敏感！就病理学和生理学而言，这是一个值得研究的有趣题目。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The priests know the importance of it, they who have introduced aromatics into all their ceremonies.","zh":"教士懂得香味的重要性，举行仪式，总要掺和香料。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is to stupefy the senses and to bring on ecstasies—a thing, moreover, very easy in persons of the weaker sex, who are more delicate than the other.","zh":"这也就是麻醉智力，使人入迷而已，其实，女性比男性脆弱，收效也并不难。有人引证，妇女闻见烧过的鹿角气味、新鲜面包气味…就晕了过去。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Some are cited who faint at the smell of burnt hartshorn, of new bread—”","zh":"这也就是麻醉智力，使人入迷而已，其实，女性比男性脆弱，收效也并不难。有人引证，妇女闻见烧过的鹿角气味、新鲜面包气味…就晕了过去。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Take care; you’ll wake her!” said Bovary in a low voice.","sentences":[{"en":"“Take care; you’ll wake her!” said Bovary in a low voice.","zh":"包法利低声道：“当心吵醒她！”药剂师继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And not only,” the druggist went on, “are human beings subject to such anomalies, but animals also. Thus you are not ignorant of the singularly aphrodisiac effect produced by the Nepeta cataria, vulgarly called catmint, on the feline race; and, on the other hand, to quote an example whose authenticity I can answer for. Bridaux (one of my old comrades, at present established in the Rue Malpalu) possesses a dog that falls into convulsions as soon as you hold out a snuff-box to him. He often even makes the experiment before his friends at his summer-house at Guillaume Wood. Would anyone believe that a simple sternutation could produce such ravages on a quadrupedal organism? It is extremely curious, is it not?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And not only,” the druggist went on, “are human beings subject to such anomalies, but animals also.","zh":"“不光人有这种反常现象，走兽也有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus you are not ignorant of the singularly aphrodisiac effect produced by the Nepeta cataria, vulgarly called catmint, on the feline race; and, on the other hand, to quote an example whose authenticity I can answer for.","zh":"比方说，您一定知道，有一种花草，学名荆芥，俗名猫儿草，对猫类动物，具有强烈春药效果；另一方面，不妨举一个我保证确实的例子，布里杜（我的一个老同学，眼下住在马耳巴吕街）有一条狗，一见人掏鼻烟盒给它闻，就倒在地上抽搐。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Bridaux (one of my old comrades, at present established in the Rue Malpalu) possesses a dog that falls into convulsions as soon as you hold out a snuff-box to him.","zh":"比方说，您一定知道，有一种花草，学名荆芥，俗名猫儿草，对猫类动物，具有强烈春药效果；另一方面，不妨举一个我保证确实的例子，布里杜（我的一个老同学，眼下住在马耳巴吕街）有一条狗，一见人掏鼻烟盒给它闻，就倒在地上抽搐。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He often even makes the experiment before his friends at his summer-house at Guillaume Wood.","zh":"在他的纪尧姆树林的别墅，他常常当着朋友做实验。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Would anyone believe that a simple sternutation could produce such ravages on a quadrupedal organism?","zh":"谁相信普通一副催喷嚏的药，居然会对四足动物的机体起这样大的破坏作用？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is extremely curious, is it not?”","zh":"真是奇闻，对不对？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes,” said Charles, who was not listening to him.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” said Charles, who was not listening to him.","zh":"查理没有听，信口答道：“对。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“This shows us,” went on the other, smiling with benign self-sufficiency, “the innumerable irregularities of the nervous system. With regard to madame, she has always seemed to me, I confess, very susceptible. And so I should by no means recommend to you, my dear friend, any of those so-called remedies that, under the pretence of attacking the symptoms, attack the constitution. No; no useless physicking! Diet, that is all; sedatives, emollients, dulcification. Then, don’t you think that perhaps her imagination should be worked upon?”","sentences":[{"en":"“This shows us,” went on the other, smiling with benign self-sufficiency, “the innumerable irregularities of the nervous system.","zh":"药剂师显出一副洋洋自得的神气，笑吟吟道：“这证明神经系统的不规则现象，数也无从数起。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With regard to madame, she has always seemed to me, I confess, very susceptible.","zh":"至于嫂夫人这方面，我承认，我一直觉得，属于真正的敏感型。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And so I should by no means recommend to you, my dear friend, any of those so-called remedies that, under the pretence of attacking the symptoms, attack the constitution.","zh":"所以，我的好朋友，那些自命不凡的方子，我一个也不劝您用，说是对症下药，其实是伤害体质。不，别乱吃药！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No; no useless physicking!","zh":"注意饮食，就是这个！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Diet, that is all; sedatives, emollients, dulcification.","zh":"用镇静剂、缓和剂、糖剂就成。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, don’t you think that perhaps her imagination should be worked upon?”","zh":"然后，也许需要刺激一下想象，您看怎么样？”包法利道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“In what way? How?” said Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"“In what way?","zh":"“用什么刺激？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How?” said Bovary.","zh":"怎么刺激？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! that is it. Such is indeed the question. ‘That is the question,’ as I lately read in a newspaper.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! that is it.","zh":"“啊！问题就在这儿！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Such is indeed the question. ‘That is the question,’ as I lately read in a newspaper.”","zh":"这正是问题所在：That is the question！像我新近在报上读到的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Emma, awaking, cried out—","sentences":[{"en":"But Emma, awaking, cried out—","zh":"但是爱玛醒了，喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The letter! the letter!”","sentences":[{"en":"“The letter! the letter!”","zh":"“信呢？信呢？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They thought she was delirious; and she was by midnight. Brain-fever had set in.","sentences":[{"en":"They thought she was delirious; and she was by midnight.","zh":"大家以为她精神错乱；从半夜起，她果然精神错乱了：她的脑神经有了病。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Brain-fever had set in.","zh":"大家以为她精神错乱；从半夜起，她果然精神错乱了：她的脑神经有了病。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"For forty-three days Charles did not leave her. He gave up all his patients; he no longer went to bed; he was constantly feeling her pulse, putting on sinapisms and cold-water compresses. He sent Justin as far as Neufchâtel for ice; the ice melted on the way; he sent him back again. He called Monsieur Canivet into consultation; he sent for Dr. Lariviere, his old master, from Rouen; he was in despair. What alarmed him most was Emma’s prostration, for she did not speak, did not listen, did not even seem to suffer, as if her body and soul were both resting together after all their troubles.","sentences":[{"en":"For forty-three days Charles did not leave her.","zh":"一连四十三天，查理不离开她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He gave up all his patients; he no longer went to bed; he was constantly feeling her pulse, putting on sinapisms and cold-water compresses.","zh":"别的病人他全不看了，觉也不睡，总在听脉，贴芥子膏，换冷水布。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sent Justin as far as Neufchâtel for ice; the ice melted on the way; he sent him back again.","zh":"他差朱斯丹到新堡去找冰；冰在路上化了；他差他再去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He called Monsieur Canivet into consultation; he sent for Dr. Lariviere, his old master, from Rouen; he was in despair.","zh":"他约卡尼韦先生会诊；他派人到鲁昂请他的老师拉里维耶尔博士来；他万分焦急，最担心的是爱玛萎靡不振；因为她不说，也不听，看样子也并不痛苦，好像她的身体和她的灵魂先前激动够了，现在一同进入休眠状态。","scope":"group"},{"en":"What alarmed him most was Emma’s prostration, for she did not speak, did not listen, did not even seem to suffer, as if her body and soul were both resting together after all their troubles.","zh":"他约卡尼韦先生会诊；他派人到鲁昂请他的老师拉里维耶尔博士来；他万分焦急，最担心的是爱玛萎靡不振；因为她不说，也不听，看样子也并不痛苦，好像她的身体和她的灵魂先前激动够了，现在一同进入休眠状态。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"About the middle of October she could sit up in bed supported by pillows. Charles wept when he saw her eat her first bread-and-jelly. Her strength returned to her; she got up for a few hours of an afternoon, and one day, when she felt better, he tried to take her, leaning on his arm, for a walk round the garden. The sand of the paths was disappearing beneath the dead leaves; she walked slowly, dragging along her slippers, and leaning against Charles’s shoulder. She smiled all the time.","sentences":[{"en":"About the middle of October she could sit up in bed supported by pillows.","zh":"十月中旬前后，她可以靠着枕头，在床上坐起。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles wept when he saw her eat her first bread-and-jelly.","zh":"查理看见她第一次吃一片面包抹果酱，哭起来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her strength returned to her; she got up for a few hours of an afternoon, and one day, when she felt better, he tried to take her, leaning on his arm, for a walk round the garden.","zh":"她有了气力；下午她起来几小时，有一天她觉得大好了，他试着让她挎起他的胳膊，兜着花园散步。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sand of the paths was disappearing beneath the dead leaves; she walked slowly, dragging along her slippers, and leaning against Charles’s shoulder.","zh":"枯落的树叶盖着小径的沙砾；她穿着拖鞋，悠悠走去，肩膀贴紧查理，一直笑容满面。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She smiled all the time.","zh":"枯落的树叶盖着小径的沙砾；她穿着拖鞋，悠悠走去，肩膀贴紧查理，一直笑容满面。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"They went thus to the bottom of the garden near the terrace. She drew herself up slowly, shading her eyes with her hand to look. She looked far off, as far as she could, but on the horizon were only great bonfires of grass smoking on the hills.","sentences":[{"en":"They went thus to the bottom of the garden near the terrace.","zh":"他们这样走到花园尽头平台旁边，她慢慢直起身子，手放在眼前眺望：她远远望去，朝最远的地方望；但是天边只有几大堆草，在岭上冒烟。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She drew herself up slowly, shading her eyes with her hand to look.","zh":"他们这样走到花园尽头平台旁边，她慢慢直起身子，手放在眼前眺望：她远远望去，朝最远的地方望；但是天边只有几大堆草，在岭上冒烟。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She looked far off, as far as she could, but on the horizon were only great bonfires of grass smoking on the hills.","zh":"包法利道：“亲爱的，你要累了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You will tire yourself, my darling!” said Bovary. And, pushing her gently to make her go into the arbour, “Sit down on this seat; you’ll be comfortable.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You will tire yourself, my darling!” said Bovary.","zh":"他轻轻推她走到花棚底下：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And, pushing her gently to make her go into the arbour, “Sit down on this seat; you’ll be comfortable.”","zh":"“坐到这条长凳上，你就适意了。”声音没有力量，她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh! no; not there!” she said in a faltering voice.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh! no; not there!” she said in a faltering voice.","zh":"“啊！不，不去那儿，不去那儿！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was seized with giddiness, and from that evening her illness recommenced, with a more uncertain character, it is true, and more complex symptoms. Now she suffered in her heart, then in the chest, the head, the limbs; she had vomitings, in which Charles thought he saw the first signs of cancer.","sentences":[{"en":"She was seized with giddiness, and from that evening her illness recommenced, with a more uncertain character, it is true, and more complex symptoms.","zh":"她觉得头晕。当天黄昏，病又犯了，而且情形暧昧，显见复杂了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now she suffered in her heart, then in the chest, the head, the limbs; she had vomitings, in which Charles thought he saw the first signs of cancer.","zh":"她一时心里难过，一时胸口难过，一时头里难过，一时四肢难过；她添上了呕吐，查理以为这是癌症的早期症状。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And besides this, the poor fellow was worried about money matters.","sentences":[{"en":"And besides this, the poor fellow was worried about money matters.","zh":"除此以外，可怜人还愁钱不够用！","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"2-14","part":2,"n":14,"title":"Part II · Chapter 14","titleZh":"中卷 · 14","paragraphs":[{"en":"To begin with, he did not know how he could pay Monsieur Homais for all the physic supplied by him, and though, as a medical man, he was not obliged to pay for it, he nevertheless blushed a little at such an obligation. Then the expenses of the household, now that the servant was mistress, became terrible. Bills rained in upon the house; the tradesmen grumbled; Monsieur Lheureux especially harassed him. In fact, at the height of Emma’s illness, the latter, taking advantage of the circumstances to make his bill larger, had hurriedly brought the cloak, the travelling-bag, two trunks instead of one, and a number of other things. It was very well for Charles to say he did not want them. The tradesman answered arrogantly that these articles had been ordered, and that he would not take them back; besides, it would vex madame in her convalescence; the doctor had better think it over; in short, he was resolved to sue him rather than give up his rights and take back his goods. Charles subsequently ordered them to be sent back to the shop. Félicité forgot; he had other things to attend to; then thought no more about them. Monsieur Lheureux returned to the charge, and, by turns threatening and whining, so managed that Bovary ended by signing a bill at six months. But hardly had he signed this bill than a bold idea occurred to him: it was to borrow a thousand francs from Lheureux. So, with an embarrassed air, he asked if it were possible to get them, adding that it would be for a year, at any interest he wished. Lheureux ran off to his shop, brought back the money, and dictated another bill, by which Bovary undertook to pay to his order on the 1st of September next the sum of one thousand and seventy francs, which, with the hundred and eighty already agreed to, made just twelve hundred and fifty, thus lending at six per cent in addition to one-fourth for commission: and the things bringing him in a good third at the least, this ought in twelve months to give him a profit of a hundred and thirty francs. He hoped that the business would not stop there; that the bills would not be paid; that they would be renewed; and that his poor little money, having thriven at the doctor’s as at a hospital, would come back to him one day considerably more plump, and fat enough to burst his bag.","sentences":[{"en":"To begin with, he did not know how he could pay Monsieur Homais for all the physic supplied by him, and though, as a medical man, he was not obliged to pay for it, he nevertheless blushed a little at such an obligation.","zh":"郝麦先生药房的药，他用了许许多多，先就不知道怎么样补报才是；他是医生，固然可以不付钱，但是过分承情，他这方面到底有些难堪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the expenses of the household, now that the servant was mistress, became terrible.","zh":"其次就是家里如今由女厨子当家，开销大得惊人；账单漫天飞来，生意人闲言闲语，直不满意，勒乐先生尤其纠缠不清。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Bills rained in upon the house; the tradesmen grumbled; Monsieur Lheureux especially harassed him.","zh":"其次就是家里如今由女厨子当家，开销大得惊人；账单漫天飞来，生意人闲言闲语，直不满意，勒乐先生尤其纠缠不清。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In fact, at the height of Emma’s illness, the latter, taking advantage of the circumstances to make his bill larger, had hurriedly brought the cloak, the travelling-bag, two trunks instead of one, and a number of other things.","zh":"说实话，爱玛病危期间，后者利用机会，滥开账单，急忙送来斗篷、旅行袋、箱子两只（原定一只），还有许多别的东西。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was very well for Charles to say he did not want them.","zh":"查理白说他用不着这些东西；商人盛气凌人，还口道：全是订货，他拿不回去；再说，太太知道了，或许妨碍身子复元，先生再考虑考虑看；总而言之，他下定决心，宁可起诉，也不放弃权利，收回货物。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The tradesman answered arrogantly that these articles had been ordered, and that he would not take them back; besides, it would vex madame in her convalescence; the doctor had better think it over; in short, he was resolved to sue him rather than give up his rights and take back his goods.","zh":"查理白说他用不着这些东西；商人盛气凌人，还口道：全是订货，他拿不回去；再说，太太知道了，或许妨碍身子复元，先生再考虑考虑看；总而言之，他下定决心，宁可起诉，也不放弃权利，收回货物。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles subsequently ordered them to be sent back to the shop.","zh":"查理事后吩咐全福，给他送回商店去；偏偏全福忘了，他愁着别的事，也没有往这上头想。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Félicité forgot; he had other things to attend to; then thought no more about them.","zh":"查理事后吩咐全福，给他送回商店去；偏偏全福忘了，他愁着别的事，也没有往这上头想。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Lheureux returned to the charge, and, by turns threatening and whining, so managed that Bovary ended by signing a bill at six months.","zh":"勒乐先生又讨账来了，一会儿吓唬，一会儿诉苦，逼来逼去，包法利最后只得写了一张半年借据。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But hardly had he signed this bill than a bold idea occurred to him: it was to borrow a thousand francs from Lheureux.","zh":"但是他还没有在借据上签好名，就起了一个大胆的念头，向勒乐先生借一千法郎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So, with an embarrassed air, he asked if it were possible to get them, adding that it would be for a year, at any interest he wished.","zh":"他于是一副窘相，问他有没有方法弄到这笔钱，又说一年为期，利息听便。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lheureux ran off to his shop, brought back the money, and dictated another bill, by which Bovary undertook to pay to his order on the 1st of September next the sum of one thousand and seventy francs, which, with the hundred and eighty already agreed to, made just twelve hundred and fifty, thus lending at six per cent in addition to one-fourth for commission: and the things bringing him in a good third at the least, this ought in twelve months to give him a profit of a hundred and thirty francs.","zh":"勒乐一听这话，跑回商店，取来现款，要他再写一张借据，包法利在这上面写明：来年九月一日，付清一千零七十法郎，加上先前议定一百八十法郎，正好一千二百五十法郎。这样一来，六厘利，外加四分之一佣金，货物起码有三分之一赚头，一年下来，他有一百三十法郎利息，而且他并不指望就此结束：借据到期不付，就会延期，于是他的小小资本，在医生家就像在疗养院一样，足吃足喝，有一天，回到身边，肉亸亸的，撑破钱口袋。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He hoped that the business would not stop there; that the bills would not be paid; that they would be renewed; and that his poor little money, having thriven at the doctor’s as at a hospital, would come back to him one day considerably more plump, and fat enough to burst his bag.","zh":"勒乐一听这话，跑回商店，取来现款，要他再写一张借据，包法利在这上面写明：来年九月一日，付清一千零七十法郎，加上先前议定一百八十法郎，正好一千二百五十法郎。这样一来，六厘利，外加四分之一佣金，货物起码有三分之一赚头，一年下来，他有一百三十法郎利息，而且他并不指望就此结束：借据到期不付，就会延期，于是他的小小资本，在医生家就像在疗养院一样，足吃足喝，有一天，回到身边，肉亸亸的，撑破钱口袋。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Everything, moreover, succeeded with him. He was adjudicator for a supply of cider to the hospital at Neufchâtel; Monsieur Guillaumin promised him some shares in the turf-pits of Gaumesnil, and he dreamt of establishing a new diligence service between Arcueil and Rouen, which no doubt would not be long in ruining the ramshackle van of the “Lion d’Or,” and that, travelling faster, at a cheaper rate, and carrying more luggage, would thus put into his hands the whole commerce of Yonville.","sentences":[{"en":"Everything, moreover, succeeded with him.","zh":"而且他一帆风顺，凡事如意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was adjudicator for a supply of cider to the hospital at Neufchâtel; Monsieur Guillaumin promised him some shares in the turf-pits of Gaumesnil, and he dreamt of establishing a new diligence service between Arcueil and Rouen, which no doubt would not be long in ruining the ramshackle van of the “Lion d’Or,” and that, travelling faster, at a cheaper rate, and carrying more luggage, would thus put into his hands the whole commerce of Yonville.","zh":"他和新堡医院订立合同，由他供应苹果酒；居由曼先生答应卖给他格吕梅尼泥炭矿的股票；他打算在阿格伊和鲁昂之间再开一班公共马车，走得更快，票价更低，行李载得更多，这样一来，永镇的商业便完全落入他的手心，不用说，金狮的破车也就跟着完蛋。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles several times asked himself by what means he should next year be able to pay back so much money. He reflected, imagined expedients, such as applying to his father or selling something. But his father would be deaf, and he—he had nothing to sell. Then he foresaw such worries that he quickly dismissed so disagreeable a subject of meditation from his mind. He reproached himself with forgetting Emma, as if, all his thoughts belonging to this woman, it was robbing her of something not to be constantly thinking of her.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles several times asked himself by what means he should next year be able to pay back so much money.","zh":"查理几次问自己，偌大的债，来年他拿什么还，左思右想，一筹莫展。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He reflected, imagined expedients, such as applying to his father or selling something.","zh":"求父亲帮助，父亲不会答应；卖东西，他又没有东西可卖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But his father would be deaf, and he—he had nothing to sell.","zh":"他一看束手无策，想也想不出个所以然来，反而越想越不愉快，很快也就丢开不想了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he foresaw such worries that he quickly dismissed so disagreeable a subject of meditation from his mind.","zh":"他一看束手无策，想也想不出个所以然来，反而越想越不愉快，很快也就丢开不想了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He reproached himself with forgetting Emma, as if, all his thoughts belonging to this woman, it was robbing her of something not to be constantly thinking of her.","zh":"他责备自己分心外务，忘了爱玛，好像他的思想全部属于这个女人，不往她身上想，等于偷她什么东西似的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The winter was severe, Madame Bovary’s convalescence slow. When it was fine they wheeled her arm-chair to the window that overlooked the square, for she now had an antipathy to the garden, and the blinds on that side were always down. She wished the horse to be sold; what she formerly liked now displeased her. All her ideas seemed to be limited to the care of herself. She stayed in bed taking little meals, rang for the servant to inquire about her gruel or to chat with her. The snow on the market-roof threw a white, still light into the room; then the rain began to fall; and Emma waited daily with a mind full of eagerness for the inevitable return of some trifling events which nevertheless had no relation to her. The most important was the arrival of the “Hirondelle” in the evening. Then the landlady shouted out, and other voices answered, while Hippolyte’s lantern, as he fetched the boxes from the boot, was like a star in the darkness. At mid-day Charles came in; then he went out again; next she took some beef-tea, and towards five o’clock, as the day drew in, the children coming back from school, dragging their wooden shoes along the pavement, knocked the clapper of the shutters with their rulers one after the other.","sentences":[{"en":"The winter was severe, Madame Bovary’s convalescence slow.","zh":"冬季凄楚，太太慢慢悠悠复元，赶上天晴，她坐在扶手椅里，推到窗口，张望广场，因为她如今厌恶花园，那一面的百叶窗一直关着。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When it was fine they wheeled her arm-chair to the window that overlooked the square, for she now had an antipathy to the garden, and the blinds on that side were always down.","zh":"冬季凄楚，太太慢慢悠悠复元，赶上天晴，她坐在扶手椅里，推到窗口，张望广场，因为她如今厌恶花园，那一面的百叶窗一直关着。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She wished the horse to be sold; what she formerly liked now displeased her.","zh":"她要人把马卖掉；往常她喜爱的东西，现在她样样讨厌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All her ideas seemed to be limited to the care of herself.","zh":"她一心似乎只是想着料理自己。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She stayed in bed taking little meals, rang for the servant to inquire about her gruel or to chat with her.","zh":"她坐在床上用点心，揿铃叫女用人来，问汤药煎好没有，或者就为和她聊聊家常。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The snow on the market-roof threw a white, still light into the room; then the rain began to fall; and Emma waited daily with a mind full of eagerness for the inevitable return of some trifling events which nevertheless had no relation to her.","zh":"菜场棚顶的雪，朝屋里反射过来一片雅静的白光。过些日子，又是下雨。有些小事，到时必然重复，虽然同她毫无关系，她也仿佛望眼欲穿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The most important was the arrival of the “Hirondelle” in the evening.","zh":"最重大的事是燕子黄昏来到，女店家喊叫，别的声音回应，伊玻立特在车篷上寻找箱笼，手提灯在黑夜如同一颗星星。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then the landlady shouted out, and other voices answered, while Hippolyte’s lantern, as he fetched the boxes from the boot, was like a star in the darkness.","zh":"最重大的事是燕子黄昏来到，女店家喊叫，别的声音回应，伊玻立特在车篷上寻找箱笼，手提灯在黑夜如同一颗星星。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At mid-day Charles came in; then he went out again; next she took some beef-tea, and towards five o’clock, as the day drew in, the children coming back from school, dragging their wooden shoes along the pavement, knocked the clapper of the shutters with their rulers one after the other.","zh":"查理中午回来，接着就又出去；然后她喝点汤，五点钟左右，日落西山，孩子们放学回家，在人行道上拖着木头套鞋，个个拿着尺，一扇又一扇地敲打窗板钩子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was at this hour that Monsieur Bournisien came to see her. He inquired after her health, gave her news, exhorted her to religion, in a coaxing little prattle that was not without its charm. The mere thought of his cassock comforted her.","sentences":[{"en":"It was at this hour that Monsieur Bournisien came to see her.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生就在这时过来看她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He inquired after her health, gave her news, exhorted her to religion, in a coaxing little prattle that was not without its charm.","zh":"他问起她的健康，谈起一些新闻，劝她信教，娓娓道来，倒也委婉动听。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The mere thought of his cassock comforted her.","zh":"单单看见他的道袍，她就感到安慰。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One day, when at the height of her illness, she had thought herself dying, and had asked for the communion; and, while they were making the preparations in her room for the sacrament, while they were turning the night table covered with syrups into an altar, and while Félicité was strewing dahlia flowers on the floor, Emma felt some power passing over her that freed her from her pains, from all perception, from all feeling. Her body, relieved, no longer thought; another life was beginning; it seemed to her that her being, mounting toward God, would be annihilated in that love like a burning incense that melts into vapour. The bed-clothes were sprinkled with holy water, the priest drew from the holy pyx the white wafer; and it was fainting with a celestial joy that she put out her lips to accept the body of the Saviour presented to her. The curtains of the alcove floated gently round her like clouds, and the rays of the two tapers burning on the night-table seemed to shine like dazzling halos. Then she let her head fall back, fancying she heard in space the music of seraphic harps, and perceived in an azure sky, on a golden throne in the midst of saints holding green palms, God the Father, resplendent with majesty, who with a sign sent to earth angels with wings of fire to carry her away in their arms.","sentences":[{"en":"One day, when at the height of her illness, she had thought herself dying, and had asked for the communion; and, while they were making the preparations in her room for the sacrament, while they were turning the night table covered with syrups into an altar, and while Félicité was strewing dahlia flowers on the floor, Emma felt some power passing over her that freed her from her pains, from all perception, from all feeling.","zh":"她有一天，病势危急，以为自己要死，请领圣体。大家在她的房间布置圣事，堆满药瓶的五斗柜改成圣坛，全福在地板上撒了一些大丽花，爱玛这期间，觉得就像有什么强有力的东西，飘过身体，帮她解除痛苦、一切知觉、一切情感。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her body, relieved, no longer thought; another life was beginning; it seemed to her that her being, mounting toward God, would be annihilated in that love like a burning incense that melts into vapour.","zh":"她的肉身轻松愉快，不再思想，开始新的生命；她觉得她的灵魂奔向上帝，仿佛香点着了，化成一道青烟，眼看就要融入天上的爱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The bed-clothes were sprinkled with holy water, the priest drew from the holy pyx the white wafer; and it was fainting with a celestial joy that she put out her lips to accept the body of the Saviour presented to her.","zh":"床单洒了圣水；教士从圣盒取出面饼，送到她的嘴边；她努出嘴唇，领受救主身体，感到无上的愉悦，停在昏迷的状态。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The curtains of the alcove floated gently round her like clouds, and the rays of the two tapers burning on the night-table seemed to shine like dazzling halos.","zh":"床帏轻轻飘起，环绕四周，如同浮云；五斗柜上点着两支蜡烛，在她眼里，仿佛耀眼的圆光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she let her head fall back, fancying she heard in space the music of seraphic harps, and perceived in an azure sky, on a golden throne in the midst of saints holding green palms, God the Father, resplendent with majesty, who with a sign sent to earth angels with wings of fire to carry her away in their arms.","zh":"于是她又倒下头去，恍惚听见空中仙乐铿锵，隐约望见天父坐在碧霄的金座，威仪万千，诸圣侍立两侧，拿着绿棕榈枝，只见天父摆了摆手，就有火焰翅膀的天使飞下地来，伸出两只胳膊，托她上天。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This splendid vision dwelt in her memory as the most beautiful thing that it was possible to dream, so that now she strove to recall her sensation. That still lasted, however, but in a less exclusive fashion and with a deeper sweetness. Her soul, tortured by pride, at length found rest in Christian humility, and, tasting the joy of weakness, she saw within herself the destruction of her will, that must have left a wide entrance for the inroads of heavenly grace. There existed, then, in the place of happiness, still greater joys—another love beyond all loves, without pause and without end, one that would grow eternally! She saw amid the illusions of her hope a state of purity floating above the earth mingling with heaven, to which she aspired. She wanted to become a saint. She bought chaplets and wore amulets; she wished to have in her room, by the side of her bed, a reliquary set in emeralds that she might kiss it every evening.","sentences":[{"en":"This splendid vision dwelt in her memory as the most beautiful thing that it was possible to dream, so that now she strove to recall her sensation.","zh":"这种壮丽的景象，留在她的记忆中，就像难得梦见的最美的梦一样；现在感觉继续存在，她努力追寻，味道照样隽永，不过不那样弥漫心灵。","scope":"group"},{"en":"That still lasted, however, but in a less exclusive fashion and with a deeper sweetness.","zh":"这种壮丽的景象，留在她的记忆中，就像难得梦见的最美的梦一样；现在感觉继续存在，她努力追寻，味道照样隽永，不过不那样弥漫心灵。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her soul, tortured by pride, at length found rest in Christian humility, and, tasting the joy of weakness, she saw within herself the destruction of her will, that must have left a wide entrance for the inroads of heavenly grace.","zh":"爱玛一向好胜，如今终于领会基督的谦逊精神，心平气和，体味凡事退让的愉快，欣赏意志在内心摧毁，腾出一片空地，迎接上天怜悯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There existed, then, in the place of happiness, still greater joys—another love beyond all loves, without pause and without end, one that would grow eternally!","zh":"原来幸福之外，还有更大的福祉，还有一种爱，凌驾世俗之爱，不间断，不结束，永远增长！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She saw amid the illusions of her hope a state of purity floating above the earth mingling with heaven, to which she aspired.","zh":"希望给她带来幻境，她隐约看见她憧憬的极乐世界，浮游半空，和天成为一体。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wanted to become a saint.","zh":"她愿意变成一位圣者。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She bought chaplets and wore amulets; she wished to have in her room, by the side of her bed, a reliquary set in emeralds that she might kiss it every evening.","zh":"她买念珠，她戴符咒；她希望床头挂一个镶翡翠的圣骨匣，每天夜晚吻着。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The cure marvelled at this humour, although Emma’s religion, he thought, might, from its fervour, end by touching on heresy, extravagance. But not being much versed in these matters, as soon as they went beyond a certain limit he wrote to Monsieur Boulard, bookseller to Monsignor, to send him “something good for a lady who was very clever.” The bookseller, with as much indifference as if he had been sending off hardware to niggers, packed up, pellmell, everything that was then the fashion in the pious book trade. There were little manuals in questions and answers, pamphlets of aggressive tone after the manner of Monsieur de Maistre, and certain novels in rose-coloured bindings and with a honied style, manufactured by troubadour seminarists or penitent blue-stockings. There were the “Think of it; the Man of the World at Mary’s Feet, by Monsieur de ***, decorated with many Orders”; “The Errors of Voltaire, for the Use of the Young,” etc.","sentences":[{"en":"The cure marvelled at this humour, although Emma’s religion, he thought, might, from its fervour, end by touching on heresy, extravagance.","zh":"爱玛这些心情，堂长看成奇迹，惊异不止，虽然他也嫌她的信仰热心过分，有一天可能走火入魔，甚至做出荒唐事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But not being much versed in these matters, as soon as they went beyond a certain limit he wrote to Monsieur Boulard, bookseller to Monsignor, to send him “something good for a lady who was very clever.”","zh":"但这方面，自己不太了然，把握不住，所以他写信给主教的书商布拉尔先生，请他寄来“一些大作，供一位绝顶聪明的女子读”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The bookseller, with as much indifference as if he had been sending off hardware to niggers, packed up, pellmell, everything that was then the fashion in the pious book trade.","zh":"书商漫不经心，就像给黑人寄铜铁器皿一样，把当时流行的善书，不管三七二十一，统统寄了过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There were little manuals in questions and answers, pamphlets of aggressive tone after the manner of Monsieur de Maistre, and certain novels in rose-coloured bindings and with a honied style, manufactured by troubadour seminarists or penitent blue-stockings.","zh":"其中有问答手册、像德·迈斯特 先生那样口气傲慢的布道小书，还有一些类似小说的东西，玫瑰红封皮，风格近似且俗，不是初级修道院学生诗人的手笔，就是洗心革面的所谓女作家的手笔，例如《三思而行》、曾得各种奖章的德…先生写的《社交男子拜倒在圣母脚下》、少年读物《伏尔泰的谬误》等等。","scope":"group"},{"en":"There were the “Think of it; the Man of the World at Mary’s Feet, by Monsieur de ***, decorated with many Orders”; “The Errors of Voltaire, for the Use of the Young,” etc.","zh":"其中有问答手册、像德·迈斯特 先生那样口气傲慢的布道小书，还有一些类似小说的东西，玫瑰红封皮，风格近似且俗，不是初级修道院学生诗人的手笔，就是洗心革面的所谓女作家的手笔，例如《三思而行》、曾得各种奖章的德…先生写的《社交男子拜倒在圣母脚下》、少年读物《伏尔泰的谬误》等等。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary’s mind was not yet sufficiently clear to apply herself seriously to anything; moreover, she began this reading in too much hurry. She grew provoked at the doctrines of religion; the arrogance of the polemic writings displeased her by their inveteracy in attacking people she did not know; and the secular stories, relieved with religion, seemed to her written in such ignorance of the world, that they insensibly estranged her from the truths for whose proof she was looking. Nevertheless, she persevered; and when the volume slipped from her hands, she fancied herself seized with the finest Catholic melancholy that an ethereal soul could conceive.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary’s mind was not yet sufficiently clear to apply herself seriously to anything; moreover, she began this reading in too much hurry.","zh":"包法利夫人的智力没有完全恢复，还不能认真读书；再说，她看这些书，也未免过于急促。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She grew provoked at the doctrines of religion; the arrogance of the polemic writings displeased her by their inveteracy in attacking people she did not know; and the secular stories, relieved with religion, seemed to her written in such ignorance of the world, that they insensibly estranged her from the truths for whose proof she was looking.","zh":"她嫌教条苛细；她厌恶论战文字高高在上，攻击她不认识的那些人，毫不容情；宗教气息浓厚的世俗故事，在她看来，根本就不了解人生，她原来希望看到真理的具体事实，但是这样一来，她反而不知不觉离开了真理。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nevertheless, she persevered; and when the volume slipped from her hands, she fancied herself seized with the finest Catholic melancholy that an ethereal soul could conceive.","zh":"可是她照样坚持下去，甚至于书离开手，一个纯洁的灵魂可能感到的最优美的正当忧郁，她也以为自己有了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As for the memory of Rodolphe, she had thrust it back to the bottom of her heart, and it remained there more solemn and more motionless than a king’s mummy in a catacomb. An exhalation escaped from this embalmed love, that, penetrating through everything, perfumed with tenderness the immaculate atmosphere in which she longed to live. When she knelt on her Gothic prie-Dieu, she addressed to the Lord the same suave words that she had murmured formerly to her lover in the outpourings of adultery. It was to make faith come; but no delights descended from the heavens, and she arose with tired limbs and with a vague feeling of a gigantic dupery.","sentences":[{"en":"As for the memory of Rodolphe, she had thrust it back to the bottom of her heart, and it remained there more solemn and more motionless than a king’s mummy in a catacomb.","zh":"至于罗道耳弗，她已经不思念他了，他停在她的心灵深处，比一位国王的木乃伊在陵墓里还要尊严，还要安静。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"An exhalation escaped from this embalmed love, that, penetrating through everything, perfumed with tenderness the immaculate atmosphere in which she longed to live.","zh":"这伟大的爱情如同加了防腐香料一般，散出一股气味，透过一切，甚至她愿意在里面过活的圣洁空气，也香喷喷的，有了柔情蜜意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When she knelt on her Gothic prie-Dieu, she addressed to the Lord the same suave words that she had murmured formerly to her lover in the outpourings of adultery.","zh":"她从前醉心奸情，甜言蜜语，唧唧哝哝，说给她的情人听，如今她跪在哥特式跪凳上，一丝不走，向救主重复。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was to make faith come; but no delights descended from the heavens, and she arose with tired limbs and with a vague feeling of a gigantic dupery.","zh":"她这样做，为了滋生信念。可是不见天上有任何快乐来到心头，她又站了起来，四肢疲乏，隐隐约约觉得像是上了当。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This searching after faith, she thought, was only one merit the more, and in the pride of her devoutness Emma compared herself to those grand ladies of long ago whose glory she had dreamed of over a portrait of La Valliere, and who, trailing with so much majesty the lace-trimmed trains of their long gowns, retired into solitudes to shed at the feet of Christ all the tears of hearts that life had wounded.","sentences":[{"en":"This searching after faith, she thought, was only one merit the more, and in the pride of her devoutness Emma compared herself to those grand ladies of long ago whose glory she had dreamed of over a portrait of La Valliere, and who, trailing with so much majesty the lace-trimmed trains of their long gowns, retired into solitudes to shed at the feet of Christ all the tears of hearts that life had wounded.","zh":"她想，她这样苦心向道，一定会有好报。于是爱玛自负信仰虔诚，拿自己和过去那些贵妇相比，她先前对着一幅拉瓦利埃尔的画像，缅想她们的光荣：她们显出不可一世的庄重气派，曳起长袍花团锦簇的后摆，谢却荣华，遁入空门，把一颗受伤的心的满腔眼泪，倾泻在基督脚前。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she gave herself up to excessive charity. She sewed clothes for the poor, she sent wood to women in childbed; and Charles one day, on coming home, found three good-for-nothings in the kitchen seated at the table eating soup. She had her little girl, whom during her illness her husband had sent back to the nurse, brought home. She wanted to teach her to read; even when Berthe cried, she was not vexed. She had made up her mind to resignation, to universal indulgence. Her language about everything was full of ideal expressions. She said to her child, “Is your stomach-ache better, my angel?”","sentences":[{"en":"Then she gave herself up to excessive charity.","zh":"她于是大行善事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She sewed clothes for the poor, she sent wood to women in childbed; and Charles one day, on coming home, found three good-for-nothings in the kitchen seated at the table eating soup.","zh":"她给穷人缝衣服，给产妇送木柴；查理有一天回来，看见三个无赖汉坐在厨房喝汤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had her little girl, whom during her illness her husband had sent back to the nurse, brought home.","zh":"她生病期间，丈夫把小女儿送到奶妈那边照管，她如今又接回家来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wanted to teach her to read; even when Berthe cried, she was not vexed.","zh":"她想教她认字，白尔特再哭，她也不发脾气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had made up her mind to resignation, to universal indulgence.","zh":"她打定主意凡事退让，一概宽容。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her language about everything was full of ideal expressions.","zh":"随便什么事，她说起来，也充满了理想的词句。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She said to her child, “Is your stomach-ache better, my angel?”","zh":"她问她的小女儿：“我的天使，你的肚子还疼不疼？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary senior found nothing to censure except perhaps this mania of knitting jackets for orphans instead of mending her own house-linen; but, harassed with domestic quarrels, the good woman took pleasure in this quiet house, and she even stayed there till after Easter, to escape the sarcasms of old Bovary, who never failed on Good Friday to order chitterlings.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary senior found nothing to censure except perhaps this mania of knitting jackets for orphans instead of mending her own house-linen; but, harassed with domestic quarrels, the good woman took pleasure in this quiet house, and she even stayed there till after Easter, to escape the sarcasms of old Bovary, who never failed on Good Friday to order chitterlings.","zh":"婆婆无话可说，除非也许嫌她家事不理，一味给孤儿编织衣服。但是老太太在家吵嘴受气，却也喜欢儿子这边清静，她一直住到复活节，免得回去听包法利老爹挖苦，他不管斋戒不斋戒，每逢星期五，就要香肠吃。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Besides the companionship of her mother-in-law, who strengthened her a little by the rectitude of her judgment and her grave ways, Emma almost every day had other visitors. These were Madame Langlois, Madame Caron, Madame Dubreuil, Madame Tuvache, and regularly from two to five o’clock the excellent Madame Homais, who, for her part, had never believed any of the tittle-tattle about her neighbour. The little Homais also came to see her; Justin accompanied them. He went up with them to her bedroom, and remained standing near the door, motionless and mute. Often even Madame Bovary; taking no heed of him, began her toilette. She began by taking out her comb, shaking her head with a quick movement, and when he for the first time saw all this mass of hair that fell to her knees unrolling in black ringlets, it was to him, poor child! like a sudden entrance into something new and strange, whose splendour terrified him.","sentences":[{"en":"Besides the companionship of her mother-in-law, who strengthened her a little by the rectitude of her judgment and her grave ways, Emma almost every day had other visitors.","zh":"婆婆判事正确，举止端庄，给了爱玛一点力量。除去婆婆做伴之外，她几乎天天有人相陪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"These were Madame Langlois, Madame Caron, Madame Dubreuil, Madame Tuvache, and regularly from two to five o’clock the excellent Madame Homais, who, for her part, had never believed any of the tittle-tattle about her neighbour.","zh":"其中有朗格洛瓦夫人、卡隆夫人、杜勃勒伊夫人、杜法赦夫人；还有善心的郝麦夫人，两点到五点，一定来看她，从来不肯相信任何关于女邻居的闲话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The little Homais also came to see her; Justin accompanied them.","zh":"小郝麦们也来看她；朱斯丹陪他们来，一同上楼，走进她的房间。他站在门外，不言不语，安安静静。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He went up with them to her bedroom, and remained standing near the door, motionless and mute.","zh":"小郝麦们也来看她；朱斯丹陪他们来，一同上楼，走进她的房间。他站在门外，不言不语，安安静静。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Often even Madame Bovary; taking no heed of him, began her toilette.","zh":"包法利夫人常常不在意，当着他梳头打扮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She began by taking out her comb, shaking her head with a quick movement, and when he for the first time saw all this mass of hair that fell to her knees unrolling in black ringlets, it was to him, poor child! like a sudden entrance into something new and strange, whose splendour terrified him.","zh":"她猛一摇头，先取下梳子；他头一回看见她这一圈一圈的黑头发散开，全部垂下来，一直搭到膝盖，仿佛忽然走进什么新奇的世界，富丽堂皇，吓坏了这可怜的孩子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma, no doubt, did not notice his silent attentions or his timidity. She had no suspicion that the love vanished from her life was there, palpitating by her side, beneath that coarse holland shirt, in that youthful heart open to the emanations of her beauty. Besides, she now enveloped all things with such indifference, she had words so affectionate with looks so haughty, such contradictory ways, that one could no longer distinguish egotism from charity, or corruption from virtue. One evening, for example, she was angry with the servant, who had asked to go out, and stammered as she tried to find some pretext. Then suddenly—","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, no doubt, did not notice his silent attentions or his timidity.","zh":"爱玛当然不注意他的默默的殷勤和他的懦怯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had no suspicion that the love vanished from her life was there, palpitating by her side, beneath that coarse holland shirt, in that youthful heart open to the emanations of her beauty.","zh":"她一点也没有想到，花容月貌，风魔人心，爱情走出她的生命，却又来到近旁，穿着粗布衬衫，在这少年的心头跳动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, she now enveloped all things with such indifference, she had words so affectionate with looks so haughty, such contradictory ways, that one could no longer distinguish egotism from charity, or corruption from virtue.","zh":"而且她如今凡事漠不关心，言词亲热，目光冷淡，姿态多变，以致人们区别不出是自私还是慈悲、是恶行还是美德。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One evening, for example, she was angry with the servant, who had asked to go out, and stammered as she tried to find some pretext.","zh":"譬如有一天黄昏，女用人请假出去，期期艾艾，寻找借口，她先在生气，忽然问道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then suddenly—","zh":"譬如有一天黄昏，女用人请假出去，期期艾艾，寻找借口，她先在生气，忽然问道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“So you love him?” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“So you love him?” she said.","zh":"“你真就爱上了他？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And without waiting for any answer from Félicité, who was blushing, she added, “There! run along; enjoy yourself!”","sentences":[{"en":"And without waiting for any answer from Félicité, who was blushing, she added, “There! run along; enjoy yourself!”","zh":"全福脸红了。她不等全福回答，就显出一副忧悒的神情，说下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the beginning of spring she had the garden turned up from end to end, despite Bovary’s remonstrances. However, he was glad to see her at last manifest a wish of any kind. As she grew stronger she displayed more wilfulness. First, she found occasion to expel Mere Rollet, the nurse, who during her convalescence had contracted the habit of coming too often to the kitchen with her two nurslings and her boarder, better off for teeth than a cannibal. Then she got rid of the Homais family, successively dismissed all the other visitors, and even frequented church less assiduously, to the great approval of the druggist, who said to her in a friendly way—","sentences":[{"en":"In the beginning of spring she had the garden turned up from end to end, despite Bovary’s remonstrances.","zh":"“好，快跑！开心去吧！”开春前后，她不听查理劝说，叫人前前后后，把花园翻腾一遍。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"However, he was glad to see her at last manifest a wish of any kind.","zh":"查理见她终于有了振作的表示，倒也高兴。她一天比一天见好，也就一天比一天振作。","scope":"group"},{"en":"As she grew stronger she displayed more wilfulness.","zh":"查理见她终于有了振作的表示，倒也高兴。她一天比一天见好，也就一天比一天振作。","scope":"group"},{"en":"First, she found occasion to expel Mere Rollet, the nurse, who during her convalescence had contracted the habit of coming too often to the kitchen with her two nurslings and her boarder, better off for teeth than a cannibal.","zh":"在她养病期间，奶妈罗莱女人，肆无忌惮，带来两个奶孩子，经常待在厨房，另外还带着一个寄居的孩子，吃起饭来，狼吞虎咽，一扫而光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she got rid of the Homais family, successively dismissed all the other visitors, and even frequented church less assiduously, to the great approval of the druggist, who said to her in a friendly way—","zh":"她先想办法把她撵走，然后摆脱郝麦一家大小，再陆续辞谢众人的看望，甚至教堂，她去得也不怎么勤了。药剂师大加称道，立时表示好感，对她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You were going in a bit for the cassock!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You were going in a bit for the cassock!”","zh":"“您先前有点迷过了头！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As formerly, Monsieur Bournisien dropped in every day when he came out after catechism class. He preferred staying out of doors to taking the air “in the grove,” as he called the arbour. This was the time when Charles came home. They were hot; some sweet cider was brought out, and they drank together to madame’s complete restoration.","sentences":[{"en":"As formerly, Monsieur Bournisien dropped in every day when he came out after catechism class.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生，像往常一样，上过教理问答，每天必来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He preferred staying out of doors to taking the air “in the grove,” as he called the arbour.","zh":"他喜欢待在外边林荫中间，吸吸新鲜空气：他这样称呼花棚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This was the time when Charles came home.","zh":"查理正在这时回家。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were hot; some sweet cider was brought out, and they drank together to madame’s complete restoration.","zh":"他们觉得天热，一道喝着新苹果酒，预祝太太完全康复。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Binet was there; that is to say, a little lower down against the terrace wall, fishing for crayfish. Bovary invited him to have a drink, and he thoroughly understood the uncorking of the stone bottles.","sentences":[{"en":"Binet was there; that is to say, a little lower down against the terrace wall, fishing for crayfish.","zh":"毕耐也在那儿，就是说，稍靠下，在平台墙外，打捞蝲蛄。包法利请他喝酒，开坛子他完全在行。他望了四周一眼，心满意足，一直望到天边，然后道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Bovary invited him to have a drink, and he thoroughly understood the uncorking of the stone bottles.","zh":"毕耐也在那儿，就是说，稍靠下，在平台墙外，打捞蝲蛄。包法利请他喝酒，开坛子他完全在行。他望了四周一眼，心满意足，一直望到天边，然后道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You must,” he said, throwing a satisfied glance all round him, even to the very extremity of the landscape, “hold the bottle perpendicularly on the table, and after the strings are cut, press up the cork with little thrusts, gently, gently, as indeed they do seltzer-water at restaurants.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You must,” he said, throwing a satisfied glance all round him, even to the very extremity of the landscape, “hold the bottle perpendicularly on the table, and after the strings are cut, press up the cork with little thrusts, gently, gently, as indeed they do seltzer-water at restaurants.”","zh":"“应当像这样，在桌子上拿直瓶子，绳子剪断以后，一点一点拔软木塞，轻轻地，轻轻地，就像人在饭后开塞兹水一样。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But during his demonstration the cider often spurted right into their faces, and then the ecclesiastic, with a thick laugh, never missed this joke—","sentences":[{"en":"But during his demonstration the cider often spurted right into their faces, and then the ecclesiastic, with a thick laugh, never missed this joke—","zh":"但是在他讲解中间，苹果酒常常溅他们一脸，于是教士格格笑着，重复一遍这句趣话道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Its goodness strikes the eye!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Its goodness strikes the eye!”","zh":"“好酒打眼！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was, in fact, a good fellow and one day he was not even scandalised at the chemist, who advised Charles to give madame some distraction by taking her to the theatre at Rouen to hear the illustrious tenor, Lagardy. Homais, surprised at this silence, wanted to know his opinion, and the priest declared that he considered music less dangerous for morals than literature.","sentences":[{"en":"He was, in fact, a good fellow and one day he was not even scandalised at the chemist, who advised Charles to give madame some distraction by taking her to the theatre at Rouen to hear the illustrious tenor, Lagardy.","zh":"他的确是一个老好人，甚至有一天，药剂师劝查理带太太散散心，到鲁昂剧场去听有名的男高音拉嘉尔狄，他也并不大惊小怪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais, surprised at this silence, wanted to know his opinion, and the priest declared that he considered music less dangerous for morals than literature.","zh":"郝麦见他默不作声，反而诧异了，问他有什么意见。教士讲：在他看来，音乐不像文学那样伤风败俗。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the chemist took up the defence of letters. The theatre, he contended, served for railing at prejudices, and, beneath a mask of pleasure, taught virtue.","sentences":[{"en":"But the chemist took up the defence of letters.","zh":"但是药剂师为文学辩护。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The theatre, he contended, served for railing at prejudices, and, beneath a mask of pleasure, taught virtue.","zh":"他认为戏剧有益，不但责难偏见，而且利用娱乐，启迪道德。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Castigat ridendo mores, Monsieur Bournisien! Thus consider the greater part of Voltaire’s tragedies; they are cleverly strewn with philosophical reflections, that made them a vast school of morals and diplomacy for the people.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Castigat ridendo mores, Monsieur Bournisien!","zh":"“布尔尼贤先生，‘在笑中移风易俗’ ！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus consider the greater part of Voltaire’s tragedies; they are cleverly strewn with philosophical reflections, that made them a vast school of morals and diplomacy for the people.”","zh":"例如，看看伏尔泰大部分的悲剧；他用巧妙的手法，把哲学见解撒在戏里，因而这些悲剧就成了人民在道德上、外交上，真正受教育的地方。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I,” said Binet, “once saw a piece called the ‘Gamin de Paris,’ in which there was the character of an old general that is really hit off to a T. He sets down a young swell who had seduced a working girl, who at the ending—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I,” said Binet, “once saw a piece called the ‘Gamin de Paris,’ in which there was the character of an old general that is really hit off to a T. He sets down a young swell who had seduced a working girl, who at the ending—”","zh":"毕耐道：“我从前看过一出戏，名字叫《巴黎的野孩子》 ，里面有老将军那么一个人物，简直绝妙！一位少爷勾引一个女工，挨了他一顿教训，女工后来…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Certainly,” continued Homais, “there is bad literature as there is bad pharmacy, but to condemn in a lump the most important of the fine arts seems to me a stupidity, a Gothic idea, worthy of the abominable times that imprisoned Galileo.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Certainly,” continued Homais, “there is bad literature as there is bad pharmacy, but to condemn in a lump the most important of the fine arts seems to me a stupidity, a Gothic idea, worthy of the abominable times that imprisoned Galileo.”","zh":"“当然，有坏文学，就像有坏药房一样；不过，不问青红皂白，一笔抹杀最重要的艺术，我觉得是一种蠢事，一种落伍的想法，可憎可恨，不亚于监禁伽利略的时代。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I know very well,” objected the cure, “that there are good works, good authors. However, if it were only those persons of different sexes united in a bewitching apartment, decorated rouge, those lights, those effeminate voices, all this must, in the long-run, engender a certain mental libertinage, give rise to immodest thoughts and impure temptations. Such, at any rate, is the opinion of all the Fathers. Finally,” he added, suddenly assuming a mystic tone of voice while he rolled a pinch of snuff between his fingers, “if the Church has condemned the theatre, she must be right; we must submit to her decrees.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I know very well,” objected the cure, “that there are good works, good authors.","zh":"堂长反驳道：“我知道，世上有好作品、好作家；可是不分男女，聚在一个光怪陆离的房间，陈设浮华，人又打扮得妖形怪状，搽粉抹胭脂，点着灯，嗲声嗲气，结局必然使人想入非非，心思不正，受到非礼的诱惑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"However, if it were only those persons of different sexes united in a bewitching apartment, decorated rouge, those lights, those effeminate voices, all this must, in the long-run, engender a certain mental libertinage, give rise to immodest thoughts and impure temptations.","zh":"堂长反驳道：“我知道，世上有好作品、好作家；可是不分男女，聚在一个光怪陆离的房间，陈设浮华，人又打扮得妖形怪状，搽粉抹胭脂，点着灯，嗲声嗲气，结局必然使人想入非非，心思不正，受到非礼的诱惑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Such, at any rate, is the opinion of all the Fathers.","zh":"至少圣父们 全是这样说的。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Finally,” he added, suddenly assuming a mystic tone of voice while he rolled a pinch of snuff between his fingers, “if the Church has condemned the theatre, she must be right; we must submit to her decrees.”","zh":"他忽然换成神秘的声调，同时大拇指搓着一撮鼻烟，接下去道：“总之，教会谴责戏剧，有谴责的理由，旨令下来，我们就该服从才是。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why,” asked the druggist, “should she excommunicate actors? For formerly they openly took part in religious ceremonies. Yes, in the middle of the chancel they acted; they performed a kind of farce called ‘Mysteries,’ which often offended against the laws of decency.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why,” asked the druggist, “should she excommunicate actors?","zh":"药剂师问道：“教会为什么驱逐演员出教？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For formerly they openly took part in religious ceremonies.","zh":"他们从前是公开参加宗教仪式的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yes, in the middle of the chancel they acted; they performed a kind of farce called ‘Mysteries,’ which often offended against the laws of decency.”","zh":"是的，他们在唱经堂当中搬演叫作圣迹剧的一类闹剧 ，戏里一来就奚落礼法。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The ecclesiastic contented himself with uttering a groan, and the chemist went on—","sentences":[{"en":"The ecclesiastic contented himself with uttering a groan, and the chemist went on—","zh":"教士做声不得，只好叹气了事。药剂师继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It’s like it is in the Bible; there there are, you know, more than one piquant detail, matters really libidinous!”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s like it is in the Bible; there there are, you know, more than one piquant detail, matters really libidinous!”","zh":"“《圣经》也一样；里头…您知道…不止一个地方…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And on a gesture of irritation from Monsieur Bournisien—","sentences":[{"en":"And on a gesture of irritation from Monsieur Bournisien—","zh":"他见布尔尼贤先生做了一个恼怒的手势，就说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! you’ll admit that it is not a book to place in the hands of a young girl, and I should be sorry if Athalie—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! you’ll admit that it is not a book to place in the hands of a young girl, and I should be sorry if Athalie—”","zh":"“啊！你同意吧，这不是一本女孩子应该看的书。我会难过的，我要是看见阿塔莉…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But it is the Protestants, and not we,” cried the other impatiently, “who recommend the Bible.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But it is the Protestants, and not we,” cried the other impatiently, “who recommend the Bible.”","zh":"“可是劝人读《圣经》的是耶稣教教徒，不是我们天主教教徒！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No matter,” said Homais. “I am surprised that in our days, in this century of enlightenment, anyone should still persist in proscribing an intellectual relaxation that is inoffensive, moralising, and sometimes even hygienic; is it not, doctor?”","sentences":[{"en":"“No matter,” said Homais.","zh":"郝麦道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I am surprised that in our days, in this century of enlightenment, anyone should still persist in proscribing an intellectual relaxation that is inoffensive, moralising, and sometimes even hygienic; is it not, doctor?”","zh":"“不管怎么样，一种精神娱乐，无害于人，而又劝善惩恶，有时候甚至还对卫生有益，到了我们今天这个光明的世纪，还有人执意禁止去看，我觉得奇怪。不是吗，博士？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No doubt,” replied the doctor carelessly, either because, sharing the same ideas, he wished to offend no one, or else because he had not any ideas.","sentences":[{"en":"“No doubt,” replied the doctor carelessly, either because, sharing the same ideas, he wished to offend no one, or else because he had not any ideas.","zh":"医生的想法也许和他一样，然而不愿意得罪人，要么就是什么想法也没有，所以勉强回答了一句：“还用说。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The conversation seemed at an end when the chemist thought fit to shoot a Parthian arrow.","sentences":[{"en":"The conversation seemed at an end when the chemist thought fit to shoot a Parthian arrow.","zh":"谈话似乎结束了，但是药剂师觉得不妨最后再踢一脚：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I’ve known priests who put on ordinary clothes to go and see dancers kicking about.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve known priests who put on ordinary clothes to go and see dancers kicking about.”","zh":"“我就认识有些教士，俗家打扮，去看舞女跳舞。”堂长道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come, come!” said the cure.","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, come!” said the cure.","zh":"“瞎扯！”“啊！我就认识！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! I’ve known some!” And separating the words of his sentence, Homais repeated, “I—have—known—some!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"郝麦一字一顿，重复道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve known some!”","zh":"“我——就——认识。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And separating the words of his sentence, Homais repeated, “I—have—known—some!”","zh":"布尔尼贤逆来顺受，只好道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, they were wrong,” said Bournisien, resigned to anything.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, they were wrong,” said Bournisien, resigned to anything.","zh":"“好吧！他们不对。”药剂师喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“By Jove! they go in for more than that,” exclaimed the druggist.","sentences":[{"en":"“By Jove! they go in for more than that,” exclaimed the druggist.","zh":"“家伙！他们还有别的花样！”教士站起来道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sir!” replied the ecclesiastic, with such angry eyes that the druggist was intimidated by them.","sentences":[{"en":"“Sir!” replied the ecclesiastic, with such angry eyes that the druggist was intimidated by them.","zh":"“先生！”同时眼睛冒火，连药剂师也害怕了，声调放柔，解释道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I only mean to say,” he replied in less brutal a tone, “that toleration is the surest way to draw people to religion.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I only mean to say,” he replied in less brutal a tone, “that toleration is the surest way to draw people to religion.”","zh":"“我不过是说，宽容才是使人信教的最稳当的方法。”老实人又坐下来，让步道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That is true! that is true!” agreed the good fellow, sitting down again on his chair. But he stayed only a few moments.","sentences":[{"en":"“That is true! that is true!” agreed the good fellow, sitting down again on his chair.","zh":"“这话对！这话对！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"But he stayed only a few moments.","zh":"“这话对！这话对！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then, as soon as he had gone, Monsieur Homais said to the doctor—","sentences":[{"en":"Then, as soon as he had gone, Monsieur Homais said to the doctor—","zh":"但是他只待了两分钟就走了。他一走开，郝麦就向医生道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That’s what I call a cock-fight. I beat him, did you see, in a way!—Now take my advice. Take madame to the theatre, if it were only for once in your life, to enrage one of these ravens, hang it! If anyone could take my place, I would accompany you myself. Be quick about it. Lagardy is only going to give one performance; he’s engaged to go to England at a high salary. From what I hear, he’s a regular dog; he’s rolling in money; he’s taking three mistresses and a cook along with him. All these great artists burn the candle at both ends; they require a dissolute life, that suits the imagination to some extent. But they die at the hospital, because they haven’t the sense when young to lay by. Well, a pleasant dinner! Goodbye till to-morrow.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That’s what I call a cock-fight.","zh":"“这就叫作斗嘴！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I beat him, did you see, in a way!—Now take my advice.","zh":"您看见的，我老实不客气，咬了他几口…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Take madame to the theatre, if it were only for once in your life, to enrage one of these ravens, hang it!","zh":"话说回来，听我的话，带太太去看看戏吧，哪怕单为您这辈子，气一回一只这样的黑老鸹 ，也是好的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If anyone could take my place, I would accompany you myself.","zh":"要是有人能替我的话，我愿意亲自陪你们走走。快！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Be quick about it.","zh":"要是有人能替我的话，我愿意亲自陪你们走走。快！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Lagardy is only going to give one performance; he’s engaged to go to England at a high salary.","zh":"拉嘉尔狄只演一场；英国出高薪聘了他。据说，很有两下子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"From what I hear, he’s a regular dog; he’s rolling in money; he’s taking three mistresses and a cook along with him.","zh":"发了大财！他随身就带三个姘头、一个厨子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All these great artists burn the candle at both ends; they require a dissolute life, that suits the imagination to some extent.","zh":"大艺术家个个拿钱不当钱花；他们需要生活放荡不羁，刺激刺激想象。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But they die at the hospital, because they haven’t the sense when young to lay by.","zh":"临了他们死在救济院，因为他们年轻的时候，不懂得攒钱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, a pleasant dinner!","zh":"好，祝您晚饭用得好；明天见！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Goodbye till to-morrow.”","zh":"好，祝您晚饭用得好；明天见！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The idea of the theatre quickly germinated in Bovary’s head, for he at once communicated it to his wife, who at first refused, alleging the fatigue, the worry, the expense; but, for a wonder, Charles did not give in, so sure was he that this recreation would be good for her. He saw nothing to prevent it: his mother had sent them three hundred francs which he had no longer expected; the current debts were not very large, and the falling in of Lheureux’s bills was still so far off that there was no need to think about them. Besides, imagining that she was refusing from delicacy, he insisted the more; so that by dint of worrying her she at last made up her mind, and the next day at eight o’clock they set out in the “Hirondelle.”","sentences":[{"en":"The idea of the theatre quickly germinated in Bovary’s head, for he at once communicated it to his wife, who at first refused, alleging the fatigue, the worry, the expense; but, for a wonder, Charles did not give in, so sure was he that this recreation would be good for her.","zh":"看戏这个意思，很快在包法利心里生了根，他没有多久就说给太太知道。她起初反对，理由是疲倦、麻烦、花钱；但是出乎意料，查理并不让步，他以为看戏散心，对她有好处。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He saw nothing to prevent it: his mother had sent them three hundred francs which he had no longer expected; the current debts were not very large, and the falling in of Lheureux’s bills was still so far off that there was no need to think about them.","zh":"他看不出有什么障碍；他已经不指望母亲给他们汇钱了，可是还汇了三百法郎来；眼前的债又不怎么大，勒乐先生的借据离到期还远，不必为这担心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, imagining that she was refusing from delicacy, he insisted the more; so that by dint of worrying her she at last made up her mind, and the next day at eight o’clock they set out in the “Hirondelle.”","zh":"尤其是，查理以为她不去看戏，只是为了他好，更坚持要去了；她最后经不起再三麻烦，只得答应。于是第二天，上午八点，他们上了燕子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The druggist, whom nothing whatever kept at Yonville, but who thought himself bound not to budge from it, sighed as he saw them go.","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist, whom nothing whatever kept at Yonville, but who thought himself bound not to budge from it, sighed as he saw them go.","zh":"药剂师随时可以离开永镇，不过他自以为有事在身，离开不得，所以看见他们走，边叹气边道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, a pleasant journey!” he said to them; “happy mortals that you are!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, a pleasant journey!” he said to them; “happy mortals that you are!”","zh":"“好，一路平安！你们真有福气！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then addressing himself to Emma, who was wearing a blue silk gown with four flounces—","sentences":[{"en":"Then addressing himself to Emma, who was wearing a blue silk gown with four flounces—","zh":"随后看见爱玛穿一件有四道绲边的蓝缎袍，就说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are as lovely as a Venus. You’ll cut a figure at Rouen.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are as lovely as a Venus.","zh":"“您标致得活像一朵鲜花！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You’ll cut a figure at Rouen.”","zh":"您要轰动鲁昂啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The diligence stopped at the “Croix-Rouge” in the Place Beauvoisine. It was the inn that is in every provincial faubourg, with large stables and small bedrooms, where one sees in the middle of the court chickens pilfering the oats under the muddy gigs of the commercial travellers—a good old house, with worm-eaten balconies that creak in the wind on winter nights, always full of people, noise, and feeding, whose black tables are sticky with coffee and brandy, the thick windows made yellow by the flies, the damp napkins stained with cheap wine, and that always smells of the village, like ploughboys dressed in Sundayclothes, has a cafe on the street, and towards the countryside a kitchen-garden. Charles at once set out. He muddled up the stage-boxes with the gallery, the pit with the boxes; asked for explanations, did not understand them; was sent from the box-office to the acting-manager; came back to the inn, returned to the theatre, and thus several times traversed the whole length of the town from the theatre to the boulevard.","sentences":[{"en":"The diligence stopped at the “Croix-Rouge” in the Place Beauvoisine.","zh":"驿车停在芳邻广场的红十字旅馆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the inn that is in every provincial faubourg, with large stables and small bedrooms, where one sees in the middle of the court chickens pilfering the oats under the muddy gigs of the commercial travellers—a good old house, with worm-eaten balconies that creak in the wind on winter nights, always full of people, noise, and feeding, whose black tables are sticky with coffee and brandy, the thick windows made yellow by the flies, the damp napkins stained with cheap wine, and that always smells of the village, like ploughboys dressed in Sundayclothes, has a cafe on the street, and towards the countryside a kitchen-garden.","zh":"这家客店类似外省所有的城郊客店，马棚大，卧室小，站在屋里往外望，就见院子当中，放着推销员的轻便马车，浑身是泥，母鸡在车底下啄荞麦吃。舒舒服服的老屋子，虫蛀的木栏杆，冬季夜晚风吹着，嘎吱直响；里头总住满了人，喊声喧天，要东要西；黑饭桌子黏黏的，沾满了光荣酒；苍蝇叮黄了厚玻璃窗；潮湿的饭巾，斑斑点点，都是廉价酒的污迹。客店总有乡村气息，好像田庄的伙计穿上过节的衣服一样，靠街有一座咖啡馆，田野那边有一座菜园。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles at once set out.","zh":"查理一下车就去了剧场 。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He muddled up the stage-boxes with the gallery, the pit with the boxes; asked for explanations, did not understand them; was sent from the box-office to the acting-manager; came back to the inn, returned to the theatre, and thus several times traversed the whole length of the town from the theatre to the boulevard.","zh":"他分不清花楼和楼座、前厅和包厢，请教完了，还是莫名其妙，票房请他去问经理室，回到客店，又去剧场，这样来回跑了几趟，从剧场到马路，跑熟了城南城北。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary bought a bonnet, gloves, and a bouquet. The doctor was much afraid of missing the beginning, and, without having had time to swallow a plate of soup, they presented themselves at the doors of the theatre, which were still closed.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary bought a bonnet, gloves, and a bouquet.","zh":"太太买了一顶帽子、一副手套、一把花。先生直怕错过开场戏；他们来不及喝汤，就赶到剧场门前。门还关着。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The doctor was much afraid of missing the beginning, and, without having had time to swallow a plate of soup, they presented themselves at the doors of the theatre, which were still closed.","zh":"太太买了一顶帽子、一副手套、一把花。先生直怕错过开场戏；他们来不及喝汤，就赶到剧场门前。门还关着。","scope":"group"}]}]},{"id":"2-15","part":2,"n":15,"title":"Part II · Chapter 15","titleZh":"中卷 · 15","paragraphs":[{"en":"The crowd was waiting against the wall, symmetrically enclosed between the balustrades. At the corner of the neighbouring streets huge bills repeated in quaint letters “Lucie de Lammermoor-Lagardy-Opera-etc.” The weather was fine, the people were hot, perspiration trickled amid the curls, and handkerchiefs taken from pockets were mopping red foreheads; and now and then a warm wind that blew from the river gently stirred the border of the tick awnings hanging from the doors of the public-houses. A little lower down, however, one was refreshed by a current of icy air that smelt of tallow, leather, and oil. This was an exhalation from the Rue des Charrettes, full of large black warehouses where they made casks.","sentences":[{"en":"The crowd was waiting against the wall, symmetrically enclosed between the balustrades.","zh":"观众站在栏杆当中，靠墙排成两行。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At the corner of the neighbouring streets huge bills repeated in quaint letters “Lucie de Lammermoor-Lagardy-Opera-etc.”","zh":"邻街拐角地方，大幅广告写着奇形怪状的字体：“《吕西·德·拉麦穆尔》 …拉嘉尔狄…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The weather was fine, the people were hot, perspiration trickled amid the curls, and handkerchiefs taken from pockets were mopping red foreheads; and now and then a warm wind that blew from the river gently stirred the border of the tick awnings hanging from the doors of the public-houses.","zh":"歌剧”等等。天晴气暖，头发里热汗直淌，人人掏出手绢擦红额头。有时候，河上吹来一阵热风，轻轻吹动小咖啡馆门口细布凉棚的外沿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A little lower down, however, one was refreshed by a current of icy air that smelt of tallow, leather, and oil.","zh":"再往下走，又来一股凉风，夹带着脂肪、皮和油的味道。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This was an exhalation from the Rue des Charrettes, full of large black warehouses where they made casks.","zh":"这是大车街的气味，那条街满街都是黑洞洞的大货栈，大桶在里头滚来滚去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For fear of seeming ridiculous, Emma before going in wished to have a little stroll in the harbour, and Bovary prudently kept his tickets in his hand, in the pocket of his trousers, which he pressed against his stomach.","sentences":[{"en":"For fear of seeming ridiculous, Emma before going in wished to have a little stroll in the harbour, and Bovary prudently kept his tickets in his hand, in the pocket of his trousers, which he pressed against his stomach.","zh":"爱玛怕人笑话，要在进去以前，先到码头散散步。包法利小心翼翼，手捏住戏票，插在裤袋里，顶住他的肚皮。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her heart began to beat as soon as she reached the vestibule. She involuntarily smiled with vanity on seeing the crowd rushing to the right by the other corridor while she went up the staircase to the reserved seats. She was as pleased as a child to push with her finger the large tapestried door. She breathed in with all her might the dusty smell of the lobbies, and when she was seated in her box she bent forward with the air of a duchess.","sentences":[{"en":"Her heart began to beat as soon as she reached the vestibule.","zh":"她一进过厅就心跳，看见观众急急向右，走进另外一条过道，自己却踏上包厢的楼梯，不由得眉飞色舞，有了笑容。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She involuntarily smiled with vanity on seeing the crowd rushing to the right by the other corridor while she went up the staircase to the reserved seats.","zh":"她一进过厅就心跳，看见观众急急向右，走进另外一条过道，自己却踏上包厢的楼梯，不由得眉飞色舞，有了笑容。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was as pleased as a child to push with her finger the large tapestried door.","zh":"门宽宽的，挂着幔子，她像小孩子一样，推开了门，觉得快乐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She breathed in with all her might the dusty smell of the lobbies, and when she was seated in her box she bent forward with the air of a duchess.","zh":"夹道的灰尘气味，她使劲往里吸。她坐在包厢里，微微前俯，潇洒自若，宛然一位公爵夫人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The theatre was beginning to fill; opera-glasses were taken from their cases, and the subscribers, catching sight of one another, were bowing. They came to seek relaxation in the fine arts after the anxieties of business; but “business” was not forgotten; they still talked cottons, spirits of wine, or indigo. The heads of old men were to be seen, inexpressive and peaceful, with their hair and complexions looking like silver medals tarnished by steam of lead. The young beaux were strutting about in the pit, showing in the opening of their waistcoats their pink or applegreen cravats, and Madame Bovary from above admired them leaning on their canes with golden knobs in the open palm of their yellow gloves.","sentences":[{"en":"The theatre was beginning to fill; opera-glasses were taken from their cases, and the subscribers, catching sight of one another, were bowing.","zh":"剧场渐渐坐满。有人取出望远镜；长期观众，远远望见，互相致意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They came to seek relaxation in the fine arts after the anxieties of business; but “business” was not forgotten; they still talked cottons, spirits of wine, or indigo.","zh":"他们整日操心买卖，此刻到艺术中来消除疲劳，但是并没忘记生意，谈的照样是棉花、酒精或者蓝靛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The heads of old men were to be seen, inexpressive and peaceful, with their hair and complexions looking like silver medals tarnished by steam of lead.","zh":"其中有些老人，脸上没有表情，模样安详，灰白头发，灰白皮肤，好像银质奖章蒙着一层铅气，失了光泽一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The young beaux were strutting about in the pit, showing in the opening of their waistcoats their pink or applegreen cravats, and Madame Bovary from above admired them leaning on their canes with golden knobs in the open palm of their yellow gloves.","zh":"包法利夫人往下望，欣赏前厅一些美少年：他们洋洋自得，背心领口露出玫瑰红或者苹果绿领带，黄手套绷紧手掌，身子靠住金头手杖。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Now the lights of the orchestra were lit, the lustre, let down from the ceiling, throwing by the glimmering of its facets a sudden gaiety over the theatre; then the musicians came in one after the other; and first there was the protracted hubbub of the basses grumbling, violins squeaking, cornets trumpeting, flutes and flageolets fifing. But three knocks were heard on the stage, a rolling of drums began, the brass instruments played some chords, and the curtain rising, discovered a country-scene.","sentences":[{"en":"Now the lights of the orchestra were lit, the lustre, let down from the ceiling, throwing by the glimmering of its facets a sudden gaiety over the theatre; then the musicians came in one after the other; and first there was the protracted hubbub of the basses grumbling, violins squeaking, cornets trumpeting, flutes and flageolets fifing.","zh":"乐池的蜡烛点亮了；天花板上挂的多枝烛台也放了下来，上面的小玻璃片光芒四射，剧场忽然显出一片快活气象。乐师接着鱼贯而入，先是低音呜隆，跟着是小提琴吱喳，小铜号滴滴答答，长笛和短笛咿咿唔唔，乱响了一大阵。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But three knocks were heard on the stage, a rolling of drums began, the brass instruments played some chords, and the curtain rising, discovered a country-scene.","zh":"但是舞台上连响三声，定音鼓咚咚敲了起来，接着就是铜乐合鸣，幕升上去，露出一片风景。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was the cross-roads of a wood, with a fountain shaded by an oak to the left. Peasants and lords with plaids on their shoulders were singing a hunting-song together; then a captain suddenly came on, who evoked the spirit of evil by lifting both his arms to heaven. Another appeared; they went away, and the hunters started afresh. She felt herself transported to the reading of her youth, into the midst of Walter Scott. She seemed to hear through the mist the sound of the Scotch bagpipes re-echoing over the heather. Then her remembrance of the novel helping her to understand the libretto, she followed the story phrase by phrase, while vague thoughts that came back to her dispersed at once again with the bursts of music. She gave herself up to the lullaby of the melodies, and felt all her being vibrate as if the violin bows were drawn over her nerves. She had not eyes enough to look at the costumes, the scenery, the actors, the painted trees that shook when anyone walked, and the velvet caps, cloaks, swords—all those imaginary things that floated amid the harmony as in the atmosphere of another world. But a young woman stepped forward, throwing a purse to a squire in green. She was left alone, and the flute was heard like the murmur of a fountain or the warbling of birds. Lucie attacked her cavatina in G major bravely. She plained of love; she longed for wings. Emma, too, fleeing from life, would have liked to fly away in an embrace. Suddenly Edgar-Lagardy appeared.","sentences":[{"en":"It was the cross-roads of a wood, with a fountain shaded by an oak to the left.","zh":"这是一座树林的十字路口，左边橡树浓荫下，有一股喷泉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Peasants and lords with plaids on their shoulders were singing a hunting-song together; then a captain suddenly came on, who evoked the spirit of evil by lifting both his arms to heaven.","zh":"农民和领主，肩膀搭着苏格兰式斗篷，不分贵贱，一同唱着猎歌；随后上来一位队长，朝天伸出胳膊，呼吁恶魔下凡；又来了一位；他们一走，猎人们就又唱起歌来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Another appeared; they went away, and the hunters started afresh.","zh":"农民和领主，肩膀搭着苏格兰式斗篷，不分贵贱，一同唱着猎歌；随后上来一位队长，朝天伸出胳膊，呼吁恶魔下凡；又来了一位；他们一走，猎人们就又唱起歌来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She felt herself transported to the reading of her youth, into the midst of Walter Scott.","zh":"她回到童年的读物中间，活在司各特小说的氛围里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She seemed to hear through the mist the sound of the Scotch bagpipes re-echoing over the heather.","zh":"她隐约听见苏格兰风笛的声音，透过浓雾，飘过映山红，反复回荡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then her remembrance of the novel helping her to understand the libretto, she followed the story phrase by phrase, while vague thoughts that came back to her dispersed at once again with the bursts of music.","zh":"她有对小说的记忆，很容易了解唱词，一句又一句，跟着唱词往下听。她那些朦胧的回忆，经不起音乐急吹猛打，没有多久，也就不知去向。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She gave herself up to the lullaby of the melodies, and felt all her being vibrate as if the violin bows were drawn over her nerves.","zh":"她随着旋律摇曳，觉得自己全身心都在颤动，仿佛提琴的弓弦在拉她的神经一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had not eyes enough to look at the costumes, the scenery, the actors, the painted trees that shook when anyone walked, and the velvet caps, cloaks, swords—all those imaginary things that floated amid the harmony as in the atmosphere of another world.","zh":"服装、风景、人物，还有人一走过就震动的画出来的树木，五光十色，使她应接不暇；小绒帽、斗篷、宝剑：所有这些虚构的事物，在音乐之中动荡，就像在另一个世界的氛围之中。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But a young woman stepped forward, throwing a purse to a squire in green.","zh":"一个年轻女子走向前来，拿钱包丢向一个穿绿衣服的侍从。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was left alone, and the flute was heard like the murmur of a fountain or the warbling of birds.","zh":"然后舞台上留下她一个人，只听一支长笛在响，仿佛泉水潺潺，或者飞鸟啁啾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lucie attacked her cavatina in G major bravely.","zh":"吕西神色严肃，唱着她的G大调短歌；她抱怨爱情，希望生长翅膀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She plained of love; she longed for wings.","zh":"吕西神色严肃，唱着她的G大调短歌；她抱怨爱情，希望生长翅膀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma, too, fleeing from life, would have liked to fly away in an embrace.","zh":"爱玛同样希望离开人生，在相抱之中飞逝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Suddenly Edgar-Lagardy appeared.","zh":"突然拉嘉尔狄扮演的艾德嘉尔出现了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had that splendid pallor that gives something of the majesty of marble to the ardent races of the South. His vigorous form was tightly clad in a brown-coloured doublet; a small chiselled poniard hung against his left thigh, and he cast round laughing looks showing his white teeth. They said that a Polish princess having heard him sing one night on the beach at Biarritz, where he mended boats, had fallen in love with him. She had ruined herself for him. He had deserted her for other women, and this sentimental celebrity did not fail to enhance his artistic reputation. The diplomatic mummer took care always to slip into his advertisements some poetic phrase on the fascination of his person and the susceptibility of his soul. A fine organ, imperturbable coolness, more temperament than intelligence, more power of emphasis than of real singing, made up the charm of this admirable charlatan nature, in which there was something of the hairdresser and the toreador.","sentences":[{"en":"He had that splendid pallor that gives something of the majesty of marble to the ardent races of the South.","zh":"他的肤色白皙，神采奕奕：一般说来，气质热情的南方人有了这种皮肤，看上去便像大理石雕像一样尊严。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His vigorous form was tightly clad in a brown-coloured doublet; a small chiselled poniard hung against his left thigh, and he cast round laughing looks showing his white teeth.","zh":"一件棕色紧上衣裹着他强壮的身体；左臀挂着一把雕镂的小刺刀。他露出一口白牙，同时旋转眼睛，恹恹无力，仿佛在爱情上受尽折磨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They said that a Polish princess having heard him sing one night on the beach at Biarritz, where he mended boats, had fallen in love with him.","zh":"据说一位波兰公主，有一天黄昏，听见他在比阿里茨海滨 唱着歌修理小艇，爱上了他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had ruined herself for him.","zh":"她为他抛弃一切。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had deserted her for other women, and this sentimental celebrity did not fail to enhance his artistic reputation.","zh":"他却抛弃了她，另爱别的女人：爱情上的名气越发提高了他艺术上的声誉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The diplomatic mummer took care always to slip into his advertisements some poetic phrase on the fascination of his person and the susceptibility of his soul.","zh":"擅长外交手腕的戏子，甚至留意广告，经常添上一个诗意的句子，夸耀自己形象动人，心灵善感。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A fine organ, imperturbable coolness, more temperament than intelligence, more power of emphasis than of real singing, made up the charm of this admirable charlatan nature, in which there was something of the hairdresser and the toreador.","zh":"一副好嗓子、一颗冷静的心，情绪多于理智、夸张多于诗意，做成这位有理发师与斗牛士气质的江湖艺人的叫座本钱。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"From the first scene he evoked enthusiasm. He pressed Lucy in his arms, he left her, he came back, he seemed desperate; he had outbursts of rage, then elegiac gurglings of infinite sweetness, and the notes escaped from his bare neck full of sobs and kisses. Emma leant forward to see him, clutching the velvet of the box with her nails. She was filling her heart with these melodious lamentations that were drawn out to the accompaniment of the double-basses, like the cries of the drowning in the tumult of a tempest. She recognised all the intoxication and the anguish that had almost killed her. The voice of a prima donna seemed to her to be but echoes of her conscience, and this illusion that charmed her as some very thing of her own life. But no one on earth had loved her with such love. He had not wept like Edgar that last moonlit night when they said, “To-morrow! to-morrow!” The theatre rang with cheers; they recommenced the entire movement; the lovers spoke of the flowers on their tomb, of vows, exile, fate, hopes; and when they uttered the final adieu, Emma gave a sharp cry that mingled with the vibrations of the last chords.","sentences":[{"en":"From the first scene he evoked enthusiasm.","zh":"他一进场就激起观众的热情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He pressed Lucy in his arms, he left her, he came back, he seemed desperate; he had outbursts of rage, then elegiac gurglings of infinite sweetness, and the notes escaped from his bare neck full of sobs and kisses.","zh":"他拥抱吕西，离开了，又回来，像是难过到了极点。他一时暴怒，一时又无限温柔，唱挽歌似的呻吟；他光着颈项，音符从里面逸出，一个又一个，像是充满呜咽和热吻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma leant forward to see him, clutching the velvet of the box with her nails.","zh":"爱玛看他，身子向前，指甲抓挠包厢的丝绒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was filling her heart with these melodious lamentations that were drawn out to the accompaniment of the double-basses, like the cries of the drowning in the tumult of a tempest.","zh":"这些抑扬动听的哀歌，伴奏的低音提琴加以延长！就像狂风暴雨之中翻了船的人呼救一样。她心中充满这些哀歌，而且原本就熟悉这种种沉醉和焦虑的感情，且几乎为之死去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She recognised all the intoxication and the anguish that had almost killed her.","zh":"这些抑扬动听的哀歌，伴奏的低音提琴加以延长！就像狂风暴雨之中翻了船的人呼救一样。她心中充满这些哀歌，而且原本就熟悉这种种沉醉和焦虑的感情，且几乎为之死去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The voice of a prima donna seemed to her to be but echoes of her conscience, and this illusion that charmed her as some very thing of her own life.","zh":"女音在她听来，似乎只是她内心的回声；她着迷的形象，也似乎只是她生命的某一部分。可是世上就没有人这样爱过她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But no one on earth had loved her with such love.","zh":"他们最后一晚，月色溶溶，互相说起：“明天见！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had not wept like Edgar that last moonlit night when they said, “To-morrow! to-morrow!”","zh":"明天见！”他就不像艾德嘉尔哭得这样伤心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The theatre rang with cheers; they recommenced the entire movement; the lovers spoke of the flowers on their tomb, of vows, exile, fate, hopes; and when they uttered the final adieu, Emma gave a sharp cry that mingled with the vibrations of the last chords.","zh":"剧场一片喊好的声音；末一节全部又唱了一遍；一对情人说起他们坟上的花、誓言、流放、厄运、希望，唱到最后告别，爱玛尖叫起来，和煞尾的音乐响成一片。包法利问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But why,” asked Bovary, “does that gentleman persecute her?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But why,” asked Bovary, “does that gentleman persecute her?”","zh":"“这位贵人为什么欺负她？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no!” she answered; “he is her lover!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no!” she answered; “he is her lover!”","zh":"她回答道：“不对；他是她的情人。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet he vows vengeance on her family, while the other one who came on before said, ‘I love Lucie and she loves me!’ Besides, he went off with her father arm in arm. For he certainly is her father, isn’t he—the ugly little man with a cock’s feather in his hat?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet he vows vengeance on her family, while the other one who came on before said, ‘I love Lucie and she loves me!’","zh":"“可是他赌咒复仇，害她一家人，而另一位，方才来过的那一位，又说：‘我爱吕西，我相信她也爱我。’","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, he went off with her father arm in arm.","zh":"再说，他和她的父亲，胳膊挎胳膊，一道走出去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For he certainly is her father, isn’t he—the ugly little man with a cock’s feather in his hat?”","zh":"因为那是她的父亲，那个丑矮子，帽子插一根鸡毛，对不对？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Despite Emma’s explanations, as soon as the recitative duet began in which Gilbert lays bare his abominable machinations to his master Ashton, Charles, seeing the false troth-ring that is to deceive Lucie, thought it was a love-gift sent by Edgar. He confessed, moreover, that he did not understand the story because of the music, which interfered very much with the words.","sentences":[{"en":"Despite Emma’s explanations, as soon as the recitative duet began in which Gilbert lays bare his abominable machinations to his master Ashton, Charles, seeing the false troth-ring that is to deceive Lucie, thought it was a love-gift sent by Edgar.","zh":"临到宣叙调二重唱，吉尔拜特对他的主人阿什屯讲起他狠毒的计谋，查理看见欺骗吕西的假订婚戒指，任爱玛左解说，右解说，他还是说成艾德嘉尔送来的爱情纪念品。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He confessed, moreover, that he did not understand the story because of the music, which interfered very much with the words.","zh":"他承认他听不明白故事——由于音乐的缘故；对话不大听得出来。爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What does it matter?” said Emma. “Do be quiet!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What does it matter?” said Emma.","zh":"“有什么关系？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do be quiet!”","zh":"别说啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, but you know,” he went on, leaning against her shoulder, “I like to understand things.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, but you know,” he went on, leaning against her shoulder, “I like to understand things.”","zh":"他俯向她的肩膀，又道：“原因是，你知道，我喜欢了解透彻。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Be quiet! be quiet!” she cried impatiently.","sentences":[{"en":"“Be quiet! be quiet!” she cried impatiently.","zh":"她不耐烦道：“别说啦！别说啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Lucie advanced, half supported by her women, a wreath of orange blossoms in her hair, and paler than the white satin of her gown. Emma dreamed of her marriage day; she saw herself at home again amid the corn in the little path as they walked to the church. Oh, why had not she, like this woman, resisted, implored? She, on the contrary, had been joyous, without seeing the abyss into which she was throwing herself. Ah! if in the freshness of her beauty, before the soiling of marriage and the disillusions of adultery, she could have anchored her life upon some great, strong heart, then virtue, tenderness, voluptuousness, and duty blending, she would never have fallen from so high a happiness. But that happiness, no doubt, was a lie invented for the despair of all desire. She now knew the smallness of the passions that art exaggerated. So, striving to divert her thoughts, Emma determined now to see in this reproduction of her sorrows only a plastic fantasy, well enough to please the eye, and she even smiled internally with disdainful pity when at the back of the stage under the velvet hangings a man appeared in a black cloak.","sentences":[{"en":"Lucie advanced, half supported by her women, a wreath of orange blossoms in her hair, and paler than the white satin of her gown.","zh":"吕西半倚着侍女们，走向前来，头上戴一顶橘花冠，脸色比她的白缎袍子还白。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma dreamed of her marriage day; she saw herself at home again amid the corn in the little path as they walked to the church.","zh":"爱玛想起她的大喜日子，恍惚又看见自己在麦田当中，沿着小径，走向教堂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, why had not she, like this woman, resisted, implored?","zh":"为什么她当时不像吕西，又是拒绝，又是哀求？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She, on the contrary, had been joyous, without seeing the abyss into which she was throwing herself.","zh":"正相反，她当时兴高采烈，根本不领会她在投入深渊…啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! if in the freshness of her beauty, before the soiling of marriage and the disillusions of adultery, she could have anchored her life upon some great, strong heart, then virtue, tenderness, voluptuousness, and duty blending, she would never have fallen from so high a happiness.","zh":"在她如花似玉的年龄，尚未跌入婚姻的泥淖、陷进通奸的幻灭之前，她要是能把终身许给一位心地坚定的伟大灵魂，而贞操、恩情、欢愉和责任也集于一人之身，她绝不至于从那样高的幸福之巅摔了下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But that happiness, no doubt, was a lie invented for the despair of all desire.","zh":"毫无疑问，这种幸福只是一种谎言，编排出来抚慰人心的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She now knew the smallness of the passions that art exaggerated.","zh":"艺术夸大的热情，她如今知道何等渺小了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So, striving to divert her thoughts, Emma determined now to see in this reproduction of her sorrows only a plastic fantasy, well enough to please the eye, and she even smiled internally with disdainful pity when at the back of the stage under the velvet hangings a man appeared in a black cloak.","zh":"于是爱玛努力不朝这方面想：她自身痛苦的这种再现，她一意看成游戏之作，仅供耳目之娱，她甚至怀着鄙夷和怜悯的心理笑了起来。这时就见舞台尽里，绒门帘底下，走出一个披黑斗篷的男子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His large Spanish hat fell at a gesture he made, and immediately the instruments and the singers began the sextet. Edgar, flashing with fury, dominated all the others with his clearer voice; Ashton hurled homicidal provocations at him in deep notes; Lucie uttered her shrill plaint, Arthur at one side, his modulated tones in the middle register, and the bass of the minister pealed forth like an organ, while the voices of the women repeating his words took them up in chorus delightfully. They were all in a row gesticulating, and anger, vengeance, jealousy, terror, and stupefaction breathed forth at once from their half-opened mouths. The outraged lover brandished his naked sword; his guipure ruffle rose with jerks to the movements of his chest, and he walked from right to left with long strides, clanking against the boards the silver-gilt spurs of his soft boots, widening out at the ankles. He, she thought must have an inexhaustible love to lavish it upon the crowd with such effusion. All her small fault-findings faded before the poetry of the part that absorbed her; and, drawn towards this man by the illusion of the character, she tried to imagine to herself his life—that life resonant, extraordinary, splendid, and that might have been hers if fate had willed it. They would have known one another, loved one another. With him, through all the kingdoms of Europe she would have travelled from capital to capital, sharing his fatigues and his pride, picking up the flowers thrown to him, herself embroidering his costumes. Then each evening, at the back of a box, behind the golden trellis-work she would have drunk in eagerly the expansions of this soul that would have sung for her alone; from the stage, even as he acted, he would have looked at her. But the mad idea seized her that he was looking at her; it was certain. She longed to run to his arms, to take refuge in his strength, as in the incarnation of love itself, and to say to him, to cry out, “Take me away! carry me with you! let us go! Thine, thine! all my ardour and all my dreams!”","sentences":[{"en":"His large Spanish hat fell at a gesture he made, and immediately the instruments and the singers began the sextet.","zh":"他做了一个手势，他戴的宽边西班牙式帽子就掉下来了，乐器和歌手马上开始六重奏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Edgar, flashing with fury, dominated all the others with his clearer voice; Ashton hurled homicidal provocations at him in deep notes; Lucie uttered her shrill plaint, Arthur at one side, his modulated tones in the middle register, and the bass of the minister pealed forth like an organ, while the voices of the women repeating his words took them up in chorus delightfully.","zh":"艾德嘉尔大怒之下，声音分外嘹亮，压倒全场，阿什屯音调低沉，唱着凶话激他；吕西尖声哀诉；阿尔色闪在一旁，用中音歌唱；牧师的次中音，唔咿唔呀，好似一架风琴；侍女们的声音，合唱一般重复他的语言，十分悦耳。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were all in a row gesticulating, and anger, vengeance, jealousy, terror, and stupefaction breathed forth at once from their half-opened mouths.","zh":"他们全都站在一排做手势，半张着嘴，同时倾吐愤怒、报复、忌妒、恐怖、慈悲和惊惧的语言。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The outraged lover brandished his naked sword; his guipure ruffle rose with jerks to the movements of his chest, and he walked from right to left with long strides, clanking against the boards the silver-gilt spurs of his soft boots, widening out at the ankles.","zh":"情人气愤不过，拔出宝剑挥舞；胸脯一动，花边领披就跟着上下起伏；他迈开大步，左走走，右走走，软皮靴在踝骨地方开口，朱红刺马距打着地板直响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He, she thought must have an inexhaustible love to lavish it upon the crowd with such effusion.","zh":"她心想他的爱情一定用之不竭，才会这样向观众大量倾泻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All her small fault-findings faded before the poetry of the part that absorbed her; and, drawn towards this man by the illusion of the character, she tried to imagine to herself his life—that life resonant, extraordinary, splendid, and that might have been hers if fate had willed it.","zh":"角色的诗意感染了她，揶揄的心理完全消失，剧中人的假象使她对演员本人产生好感，她试着想象他的生活——那种轰动远近、世间少有的辉煌生活，机缘凑巧，她兴许也能过它一过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They would have known one another, loved one another.","zh":"这样一来，他们就会相识、相爱了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With him, through all the kingdoms of Europe she would have travelled from capital to capital, sharing his fatigues and his pride, picking up the flowers thrown to him, herself embroidering his costumes.","zh":"她同他在一起，游遍欧洲的王国，一个京城又一个京城，分享他的疲劳和他的骄傲，拾起那些朝他丢过来的花，亲自刺绣他的服装；然后每天夜晚，坐在包厢尽里，待在金栅栏后面，如醉如痴，领会这只为她一个人歌唱的心灵的倾诉；他在舞台上也边演边望她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then each evening, at the back of a box, behind the golden trellis-work she would have drunk in eagerly the expansions of this soul that would have sung for her alone; from the stage, even as he acted, he would have looked at her.","zh":"她同他在一起，游遍欧洲的王国，一个京城又一个京城，分享他的疲劳和他的骄傲，拾起那些朝他丢过来的花，亲自刺绣他的服装；然后每天夜晚，坐在包厢尽里，待在金栅栏后面，如醉如痴，领会这只为她一个人歌唱的心灵的倾诉；他在舞台上也边演边望她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But the mad idea seized her that he was looking at her; it was certain.","zh":"但是她起了一种怪念头：他如今就在望她，一定的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She longed to run to his arms, to take refuge in his strength, as in the incarnation of love itself, and to say to him, to cry out, “Take me away! carry me with you! let us go!","zh":"她真想扑进他的胸怀，受到他的力量的庇护，如同受到爱情化身的庇护，对他说，对他喊：“把我抢走，把我带走，一同走！我是你的，你的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thine, thine! all my ardour and all my dreams!”","zh":"我的热情、我的梦想，全都属于你！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The curtain fell.","sentences":[{"en":"The curtain fell.","zh":"幕落了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The smell of the gas mingled with that of the breaths, the waving of the fans, made the air more suffocating. Emma wanted to go out; the crowd filled the corridors, and she fell back in her arm-chair with palpitations that choked her. Charles, fearing that she would faint, ran to the refreshment-room to get a glass of barley-water.","sentences":[{"en":"The smell of the gas mingled with that of the breaths, the waving of the fans, made the air more suffocating.","zh":"煤气灯的气味和人呼出的气息混在一起；扇子的风反而增加空气的窒闷。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma wanted to go out; the crowd filled the corridors, and she fell back in her arm-chair with palpitations that choked her.","zh":"爱玛想出去走走；群众拥在夹道，堵住了路，她倒进扶手椅，心跳得气也喘不过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles, fearing that she would faint, ran to the refreshment-room to get a glass of barley-water.","zh":"查理怕她晕倒，跑到茶食部，给她弄来一杯杏仁露。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had great difficulty in getting back to his seat, for his elbows were jerked at every step because of the glass he held in his hands, and he even spilt three-fourths on the shoulders of a Rouen lady in short sleeves, who feeling the cold liquid running down to her loins, uttered cries like a peacock, as if she were being assassinated. Her husband, who was a millowner, railed at the clumsy fellow, and while she was with her handkerchief wiping up the stains from her handsome cherry-coloured taffeta gown, he angrily muttered about indemnity, costs, reimbursement. At last Charles reached his wife, saying to her, quite out of breath—","sentences":[{"en":"He had great difficulty in getting back to his seat, for his elbows were jerked at every step because of the glass he held in his hands, and he even spilt three-fourths on the shoulders of a Rouen lady in short sleeves, who feeling the cold liquid running down to her loins, uttered cries like a peacock, as if she were being assassinated.","zh":"他费了老大气力，回到原来地方；因为他两手捧着杯子，每走一步路，都有人碰他的胳膊肘，甚至于有四分之三，他倒在一位穿短袖袍子的鲁昂女人的肩膀上。她觉得冷水往腰里灌，叫得活像一只孔雀，如同有人杀她一般。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her husband, who was a millowner, railed at the clumsy fellow, and while she was with her handkerchief wiping up the stains from her handsome cherry-coloured taffeta gown, he angrily muttered about indemnity, costs, reimbursement.","zh":"丈夫是一个开纱厂的，对笨蛋大发脾气。她拿手绢揩着她漂亮的樱桃红缎袍的水渍，他粗声粗气，咕咕哝哝，说起赔偿、开支、归还这些字眼。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last Charles reached his wife, saying to her, quite out of breath—","zh":"查理好不容易来到太太身旁，喘着气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ma foi! I thought I should have had to stay there. There is such a crowd—SUCH a crowd!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ma foi!","zh":"“老天！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought I should have had to stay there.","zh":"我以为我过不来了！到处是人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There is such a crowd—SUCH a crowd!”","zh":"是人！”他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He added—","sentences":[{"en":"He added—","zh":"“你猜我在上头遇到谁了？","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Just guess whom I met up there! Monsieur Léon!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Just guess whom I met up there!","zh":"“你猜我在上头遇到谁了？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Léon!”","zh":"遇到赖昂先生！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Léon?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Léon?”","zh":"“赖昂？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Himself! He’s coming along to pay his respects.” And as he finished these words the ex-clerk of Yonville entered the box.","sentences":[{"en":"“Himself!","zh":"“正是！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He’s coming along to pay his respects.”","zh":"他这就过来看你。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And as he finished these words the ex-clerk of Yonville entered the box.","zh":"他才说完话，永镇往日的文书就进了包厢。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He held out his hand with the ease of a gentleman; and Madame Bovary extended hers, without doubt obeying the attraction of a stronger will. She had not felt it since that spring evening when the rain fell upon the green leaves, and they had said good-bye standing at the window. But soon recalling herself to the necessities of the situation, with an effort she shook off the torpor of her memories, and began stammering a few hurried words.","sentences":[{"en":"He held out his hand with the ease of a gentleman; and Madame Bovary extended hers, without doubt obeying the attraction of a stronger will.","zh":"他伸出手来，贵人一样爽快；包法利夫人不由自己，也伸出了手，不用说，由于一种更强有力的意志的吸引。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had not felt it since that spring evening when the rain fell upon the green leaves, and they had said good-bye standing at the window.","zh":"自从春季那天黄昏，雨打着绿叶，他们站在窗边道别以来，她没有再碰到这只手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But soon recalling herself to the necessities of the situation, with an effort she shook off the torpor of her memories, and began stammering a few hurried words.","zh":"可是她很快就想到不该这样出神，努力从回忆之中摆脱出来，期期艾艾，说出一些简短的字句：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah, good-day! What! you here?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah, good-day!","zh":"“啊！您好…怎么！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What! you here?”","zh":"您也在这儿？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Silence!” cried a voice from the pit, for the third act was beginning.","sentences":[{"en":"“Silence!” cried a voice from the pit, for the third act was beginning.","zh":"第三幕开始了，后厅有人喊道：“别说话！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“So you are at Rouen?”","sentences":[{"en":"“So you are at Rouen?”","zh":"“您又回鲁昂啦？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“是的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And since when?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And since when?”","zh":"“什么时候回来的？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Turn them out! turn them out!” People were looking at them. They were silent.","sentences":[{"en":"“Turn them out! turn them out!”","zh":"“出去讲话！出去！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People were looking at them.","zh":"大家朝他们望，他们只好住口。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were silent.","zh":"大家朝他们望，他们只好住口。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But from that moment she listened no more; and the chorus of the guests, the scene between Ashton and his servant, the grand duet in D major, all were for her as far off as if the instruments had grown less sonorous and the characters more remote. She remembered the games at cards at the druggist’s, and the walk to the nurse’s, the reading in the arbour, the tête-à-tête by the fireside—all that poor love, so calm and so protracted, so discreet, so tender, and that she had nevertheless forgotten. And why had he come back? What combination of circumstances had brought him back into her life? He was standing behind her, leaning with his shoulder against the wall of the box; now and again she felt herself shuddering beneath the hot breath from his nostrils falling upon her hair.","sentences":[{"en":"But from that moment she listened no more; and the chorus of the guests, the scene between Ashton and his servant, the grand duet in D major, all were for her as far off as if the instruments had grown less sonorous and the characters more remote.","zh":"但是从这时候起，她就听而不闻了；来宾的合唱、阿什屯和他的跟班的场面、伟大的D大调二重唱，在她看来，都离得很远，就像乐器不够响亮，人物退到远处一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She remembered the games at cards at the druggist’s, and the walk to the nurse’s, the reading in the arbour, the tête-à-tête by the fireside—all that poor love, so calm and so protracted, so discreet, so tender, and that she had nevertheless forgotten.","zh":"她想起药房斗牌、去奶妈家散步、花棚底下读书、炉边谈话，那可怜的恋爱，又安静，又悠长，又矜持，又温存，然而她全忘光了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And why had he come back?","zh":"他为什么回来？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What combination of circumstances had brought him back into her life?","zh":"是什么机缘，他又走进她的生命？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was standing behind her, leaning with his shoulder against the wall of the box; now and again she felt herself shuddering beneath the hot breath from his nostrils falling upon her hair.","zh":"他站在背后，肩膀靠住板壁，鼻孔呼出的热气正好扑进她的头发，她不时感到一阵战栗。他朝她俯下身子，髭尖几乎触到她的脸，问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Does this amuse you?” said he, bending over her so closely that the end of his moustache brushed her cheek. She replied carelessly—","sentences":[{"en":"“Does this amuse you?” said he, bending over her so closely that the end of his moustache brushed her cheek.","zh":"“您爱看这个？”她信口应道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"She replied carelessly—","zh":"“您爱看这个？”她信口应道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, dear me, no, not much.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, dear me, no, not much.”","zh":"“我的上帝，不！不怎么爱看。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he proposed that they should leave the theatre and go and take an ice somewhere.","sentences":[{"en":"Then he proposed that they should leave the theatre and go and take an ice somewhere.","zh":"他听见这话，提议到剧场外头饮冰水去。包法利道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, not yet; let us stay,” said Bovary. “Her hair’s undone; this is going to be tragic.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, not yet; let us stay,” said Bovary.","zh":"“啊！别就走！待下来吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Her hair’s undone; this is going to be tragic.”","zh":"她的头发散开啦，看样子要演苦戏了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the mad scene did not at all interest Emma, and the acting of the singer seemed to her exaggerated.","sentences":[{"en":"But the mad scene did not at all interest Emma, and the acting of the singer seemed to her exaggerated.","zh":"但是爱玛对发疯的场面不感兴趣，她嫌女歌手的表演过火，转向正在听戏的查理道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“She screams too loud,” said she, turning to Charles, who was listening.","sentences":[{"en":"“She screams too loud,” said she, turning to Charles, who was listening.","zh":"“她叫得太厉害。”他回答道：“是的…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes—a little,” he replied, undecided between the frankness of his pleasure and his respect for his wife’s opinion.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes—a little,” he replied, undecided between the frankness of his pleasure and his respect for his wife’s opinion.","zh":"他一方面觉得真有意思，一方面又尊重太太的意见，说起话来，未免模棱两可。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then with a sigh Léon said—","sentences":[{"en":"Then with a sigh Léon said—","zh":"赖昂接着就叹息道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The heat is—”","sentences":[{"en":"“The heat is—”","zh":"“这儿热得…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Unbearable! Yes!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Unbearable!","zh":"“受不了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yes!”","zh":"真是这样。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do you feel unwell?” asked Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you feel unwell?” asked Bovary.","zh":"包法利问道：“你热得难过？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, I am stifling; let us go.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, I am stifling; let us go.”","zh":"“是啊，我出不来气；我们走吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Léon put her long lace shawl carefully about her shoulders, and all three went off to sit down in the harbour, in the open air, outside the windows of a cafe.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Léon put her long lace shawl carefully about her shoulders, and all three went off to sit down in the harbour, in the open air, outside the windows of a cafe.","zh":"赖昂先生拿起她的长花边披肩，轻轻放在她的肩头。他们三个人走到码头，坐在一家咖啡馆外面的空地上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"First they spoke of her illness, although Emma interrupted Charles from time to time, for fear, she said, of boring Monsieur Léon; and the latter told them that he had come to spend two years at Rouen in a large office, in order to get practice in his profession, which was different in Normandy and Paris. Then he inquired after Berthe, the Homais, Mere Lefrancois, and as they had, in the husband’s presence, nothing more to say to one another, the conversation soon came to an end.","sentences":[{"en":"First they spoke of her illness, although Emma interrupted Charles from time to time, for fear, she said, of boring Monsieur Léon; and the latter told them that he had come to spend two years at Rouen in a large office, in order to get practice in his profession, which was different in Normandy and Paris.","zh":"起初谈她的病，爱玛不时打断查理的话，她说，怕赖昂听了腻烦。后者告诉他们，他来鲁昂，在一家大事务所熟习两年，因为人们在诺曼底处理业务，和巴黎大不相同。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he inquired after Berthe, the Homais, Mere Lefrancois, and as they had, in the husband’s presence, nothing more to say to one another, the conversation soon came to an end.","zh":"他接着问起白尔特、郝麦一家大小、勒弗朗索瓦太太；他们当着丈夫，没有多少话讲，谈话不久也就断了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"People coming out of the theatre passed along the pavement, humming or shouting at the top of their voices, “O bel ange, ma Lucie!” Then Léon, playing the dilettante, began to talk music. He had seen Tambourini, Rubini, Persiani, Grisi, and, compared with them, Lagardy, despite his grand outbursts, was nowhere.","sentences":[{"en":"People coming out of the theatre passed along the pavement, humming or shouting at the top of their voices, “O bel ange, ma Lucie!”","zh":"有些人看完戏，走过人行道，不是哼唧，就是乱喊：“美丽的天使、我的吕西！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Léon, playing the dilettante, began to talk music.","zh":"于是赖昂表示他是行家，谈起音乐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had seen Tambourini, Rubini, Persiani, Grisi, and, compared with them, Lagardy, despite his grand outbursts, was nowhere.","zh":"他看过唐比里尼、吕比尼、佩尔西阿尼、格里西 ；拉嘉尔狄虽然热情奔放，同他们一比，也就不值一文了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet,” interrupted Charles, who was slowly sipping his rum-sherbet, “they say that he is quite admirable in the last act. I regret leaving before the end, because it was beginning to amuse me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet,” interrupted Charles, who was slowly sipping his rum-sherbet, “they say that he is quite admirable in the last act.","zh":"查理一小口，一小口啜饮冰镇甘蔗酒，打断道：“不过人家讲，他末一幕特别好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I regret leaving before the end, because it was beginning to amuse me.”","zh":"我后悔没有看完就走，因为我开始觉得好玩起来。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why,” said the clerk, “he will soon give another performance.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why,” said the clerk, “he will soon give another performance.”","zh":"文书接下去道：“其实，他不久还要再演一回。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Charles replied that they were going back next day. “Unless,” he added, turning to his wife, “you would like to stay alone, kitten?”","sentences":[{"en":"But Charles replied that they were going back next day.","zh":"但是查理回答，他们明天就走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Unless,” he added, turning to his wife, “you would like to stay alone, kitten?”","zh":"他转向太太，又道：“除非是你愿意一个人留下来，我的小猫？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And changing his tactics at this unexpected opportunity that presented itself to his hopes, the young man sang the praises of Lagardy in the last number. It was really superb, sublime. Then Charles insisted—","sentences":[{"en":"And changing his tactics at this unexpected opportunity that presented itself to his hopes, the young man sang the praises of Lagardy in the last number.","zh":"年轻人想不到有这样一个机会迎合他的希望，改变策略，恭维拉嘉尔狄末一幕的成就。简直是出神入化，难以言传！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was really superb, sublime.","zh":"查理一听这话，坚持道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then Charles insisted—","zh":"查理一听这话，坚持道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You would get back on Sunday. Come, make up your mind. You are wrong if you feel that this is doing you the least good.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You would get back on Sunday.","zh":"“你星期天回去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Come, make up your mind.","zh":"好，决定了吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are wrong if you feel that this is doing you the least good.”","zh":"你只要觉得对你有一点点好处，你就不该不看。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The tables round them, however, were emptying; a waiter came and stood discreetly near them. Charles, who understood, took out his purse; the clerk held back his arm, and did not forget to leave two more pieces of silver that he made chink on the marble.","sentences":[{"en":"The tables round them, however, were emptying; a waiter came and stood discreetly near them.","zh":"可是周围的桌子撤空了，过来一个伙计，意在言外，站到他们旁边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles, who understood, took out his purse; the clerk held back his arm, and did not forget to leave two more pieces of silver that he made chink on the marble.","zh":"查理明白是催他们走，掏出钱包；文书拉住他的胳膊，甚至没有忘记外赏两枚银币，得朗朗扔在大理石桌面上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I am really sorry,” said Bovary, “about the money which you are—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I am really sorry,” said Bovary, “about the money which you are—”","zh":"包法利呢喃道：“真的，您不该付…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The other made a careless gesture full of cordiality, and taking his hat said—","sentences":[{"en":"The other made a careless gesture full of cordiality, and taking his hat said—","zh":"文书做了一个无所谓而又亲热的手势，拿起他的帽子：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is settled, isn’t it? To-morrow at six o’clock?”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is settled, isn’t it?","zh":"“明天六点钟，讲定了，是不是？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"To-morrow at six o’clock?”","zh":"“明天六点钟，讲定了，是不是？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles explained once more that he could not absent himself longer, but that nothing prevented Emma—","sentences":[{"en":"Charles explained once more that he could not absent himself longer, but that nothing prevented Emma—","zh":"查理依然说起他不能久离，不过爱玛没有理由不…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But,” she stammered, with a strange smile, “I am not sure—”","sentences":[{"en":"“But,” she stammered, with a strange smile, “I am not sure—”","zh":"她显出一种奇怪的微笑，期期艾艾道：“原因是…我不太知道…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, you must think it over. We’ll see. Night brings counsel.” Then to Léon, who was walking along with them, “Now that you are in our part of the world, I hope you’ll come and ask us for some dinner now and then.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, you must think it over.","zh":"“好吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We’ll see.","zh":"你再想想看，睡上一夜，也许你就改变主意了…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Night brings counsel.”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then to Léon, who was walking along with them, “Now that you are in our part of the world, I hope you’ll come and ask us for some dinner now and then.”","zh":"然后转向陪伴他们的赖昂：“您如今回到家乡了，我希望，您随时会来舍下用用便饭吧？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The clerk declared he would not fail to do so, being obliged, moreover, to go to Yonville on some business for his office. And they parted before the Saint-Herbland Passage just as the clock in the cathedral struck half-past eleven.","sentences":[{"en":"The clerk declared he would not fail to do so, being obliged, moreover, to go to Yonville on some business for his office.","zh":"文书说他会打扰的，而且事务所有一宗业务，他也非去永镇不可。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And they parted before the Saint-Herbland Passage just as the clock in the cathedral struck half-past eleven.","zh":"他们在圣艾尔柏朗夹道前面分手，礼拜堂的大钟正敲十一点半。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-1","part":3,"n":1,"title":"Part III · Chapter 1","titleZh":"下卷 · 1","paragraphs":[{"en":"Monsieur Léon, while studying law, had gone pretty often to the dancing-rooms, where he was even a great success amongst the grisettes, who thought he had a distinguished air. He was the best-mannered of the students; he wore his hair neither too long nor too short, didn’t spend all his quarter’s money on the first day of the month, and kept on good terms with his professors. As for excesses, he had always abstained from them, as much from cowardice as from refinement.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Léon, while studying law, had gone pretty often to the dancing-rooms, where he was even a great success amongst the grisettes, who thought he had a distinguished air.","zh":"赖昂先生一面钻研法律，准备学位考试，一面却也相当照顾茅庐 。他在这里得到绝大成功，爱漂亮的小女工觉得他气宇轩昂，另眼看待。学生里面，数他正派：头发不太长，也不太短；一季的钱，他不在月初花光；和教授保持友好关系。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was the best-mannered of the students; he wore his hair neither too long nor too short, didn’t spend all his quarter’s money on the first day of the month, and kept on good terms with his professors.","zh":"赖昂先生一面钻研法律，准备学位考试，一面却也相当照顾茅庐 。他在这里得到绝大成功，爱漂亮的小女工觉得他气宇轩昂，另眼看待。学生里面，数他正派：头发不太长，也不太短；一季的钱，他不在月初花光；和教授保持友好关系。","scope":"group"},{"en":"As for excesses, he had always abstained from them, as much from cowardice as from refinement.","zh":"说到荒唐，他永远适可而止，不是为了害羞，就是由于怕事。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Often when he stayed in his room to read, or else when sitting of an evening under the lime-trees of the Luxembourg, he let his Code fall to the ground, and the memory of Emma came back to him. But gradually this feeling grew weaker, and other desires gathered over it, although it still persisted through them all. For Léon did not lose all hope; there was for him, as it were, a vague promise floating in the future, like a golden fruit suspended from some fantastic tree.","sentences":[{"en":"Often when he stayed in his room to read, or else when sitting of an evening under the lime-trees of the Luxembourg, he let his Code fall to the ground, and the memory of Emma came back to him.","zh":"他待在房间读书，或者黄昏坐在卢森堡 菩提树底下，想起爱玛，他的法典常常掉在地上。但是日久天长，情感也就渐渐淡了，他有了别的欲望；不过尽管上面压着别的欲望，这种情感照样活了下来，因为赖昂并不死心，就像一线希望，在未来摇摇晃晃，又像一枚金果，挂在怪树枝头，还有到口的可能一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But gradually this feeling grew weaker, and other desires gathered over it, although it still persisted through them all.","zh":"他待在房间读书，或者黄昏坐在卢森堡 菩提树底下，想起爱玛，他的法典常常掉在地上。但是日久天长，情感也就渐渐淡了，他有了别的欲望；不过尽管上面压着别的欲望，这种情感照样活了下来，因为赖昂并不死心，就像一线希望，在未来摇摇晃晃，又像一枚金果，挂在怪树枝头，还有到口的可能一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"For Léon did not lose all hope; there was for him, as it were, a vague promise floating in the future, like a golden fruit suspended from some fantastic tree.","zh":"他待在房间读书，或者黄昏坐在卢森堡 菩提树底下，想起爱玛，他的法典常常掉在地上。但是日久天长，情感也就渐渐淡了，他有了别的欲望；不过尽管上面压着别的欲望，这种情感照样活了下来，因为赖昂并不死心，就像一线希望，在未来摇摇晃晃，又像一枚金果，挂在怪树枝头，还有到口的可能一样。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then, seeing her again after three years of absence his passion reawakened. He must, he thought, at last make up his mind to possess her. Moreover, his timidity had worn off by contact with his gay companions, and he returned to the provinces despising everyone who had not with varnished shoes trodden the asphalt of the boulevards. By the side of a Parisienne in her laces, in the drawing-room of some illustrious physician, a person driving his carriage and wearing many orders, the poor clerk would no doubt have trembled like a child; but here, at Rouen, on the harbour, with the wife of this small doctor he felt at his ease, sure beforehand he would shine. Self-possession depends on its environment. We don’t speak on the first floor as on the fourth; and the wealthy woman seems to have, about her, to guard her virtue, all her banknotes, like a cuirass in the lining of her corset.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, seeing her again after three years of absence his passion reawakened.","zh":"所以别离三年，他再看见她，热情又苏醒过来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He must, he thought, at last make up his mind to possess her.","zh":"他寻思道：事不宜迟，现在必须决心下手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Moreover, his timidity had worn off by contact with his gay companions, and he returned to the provinces despising everyone who had not with varnished shoes trodden the asphalt of the boulevards.","zh":"再说，常和轻浮子弟厮混，畏怯之心早已不知去向，回到内地，高视阔步，他根本就看不起那些没有穿过漆皮鞋、没有走过沥青马路的人们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By the side of a Parisienne in her laces, in the drawing-room of some illustrious physician, a person driving his carriage and wearing many orders, the poor clerk would no doubt have trembled like a child; but here, at Rouen, on the harbour, with the wife of this small doctor he felt at his ease, sure beforehand he would shine.","zh":"倘若在一位名闻四海的博士（得过勋章，出门有车的人物）的客厅，挨近一位遍体绫罗的巴黎女子，毫无疑问，可怜的文书，会像小孩子一样打哆嗦；不过如今是在鲁昂码头，眼前是这小医生的太太，他先拿稳了，胜利在握，自然也就觉得行若无事了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Self-possession depends on its environment.","zh":"倘若在一位名闻四海的博士（得过勋章，出门有车的人物）的客厅，挨近一位遍体绫罗的巴黎女子，毫无疑问，可怜的文书，会像小孩子一样打哆嗦；不过如今是在鲁昂码头，眼前是这小医生的太太，他先拿稳了，胜利在握，自然也就觉得行若无事了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"We don’t speak on the first floor as on the fourth; and the wealthy woman seems to have, about her, to guard her virtue, all her banknotes, like a cuirass in the lining of her corset.","zh":"信心因际遇而异：人在大厅说话，和在阁楼说话不同；阔太太保护贞操，在他看来，似乎胸衣衬里放满了钞票，如同披上了铠甲一样，无从下手。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On leaving the Bovarys the night before, Léon had followed them through the streets at a distance; then having seen them stop at the “Croix-Rouge,” he turned on his heel, and spent the night meditating a plan.","sentences":[{"en":"On leaving the Bovarys the night before, Léon had followed them through the streets at a distance; then having seen them stop at the “Croix-Rouge,” he turned on his heel, and spent the night meditating a plan.","zh":"头天夜晚，赖昂和包法利夫妇分手之后，远远跟着，看见他们走进红十字旅馆，他才转身回去，整整一夜，思索进行的计划。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"So the next day about five o’clock he walked into the kitchen of the inn, with a choking sensation in his throat, pale cheeks, and that resolution of cowards that stops at nothing.","sentences":[{"en":"So the next day about five o’clock he walked into the kitchen of the inn, with a choking sensation in his throat, pale cheeks, and that resolution of cowards that stops at nothing.","zh":"所以第二天下午五点钟左右，他走进客店厨房，喉咙发紧，脸色发白，活像胆小鬼横了心，要硬干到底。有一个听差回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The gentleman isn’t in,” answered a servant.","sentences":[{"en":"“The gentleman isn’t in,” answered a servant.","zh":"“先生不在。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This seemed to him a good omen. He went upstairs.","sentences":[{"en":"This seemed to him a good omen.","zh":"这是吉兆。他上了楼。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He went upstairs.","zh":"这是吉兆。他上了楼。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She was not disturbed at his approach; on the contrary, she apologised for having neglected to tell him where they were staying.","sentences":[{"en":"She was not disturbed at his approach; on the contrary, she apologised for having neglected to tell him where they were staying.","zh":"她看见他来，并不感到慌乱。正相反，她向他道歉，他们忘记告诉他，他们的住址了。赖昂道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, I divined it!” said Léon.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I divined it!” said Léon.","zh":"“可是我猜出来了。”“怎么会的？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He pretended he had been guided towards her by chance, by, instinct. She began to smile; and at once, to repair his folly, Léon told her that he had spent his morning in looking for her in all the hotels in the town one after the other.","sentences":[{"en":"He pretended he had been guided towards her by chance, by, instinct.","zh":"他说成是有缘相会，本能引导。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She began to smile; and at once, to repair his folly, Léon told her that he had spent his morning in looking for her in all the hotels in the town one after the other.","zh":"她听了这话，微微一笑。赖昂一看话笨，连忙改正，说他一上午都在找她，一家又一家，问遍全城旅馆。他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“So you have made up your mind to stay?” he added.","sentences":[{"en":"“So you have made up your mind to stay?” he added.","zh":"“那么，您决定待下来啦？”她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes,” she said, “and I am wrong. One ought not to accustom oneself to impossible pleasures when there are a thousand demands upon one.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” she said, “and I am wrong.","zh":"“是的。我真不应该。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One ought not to accustom oneself to impossible pleasures when there are a thousand demands upon one.”","zh":"手边一大堆事，忙都忙不过来，真不该寻什么不切实际的娱乐…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, I can imagine!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I can imagine!”","zh":"“啊！我心想…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! no; for you, you are a man!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! no; for you, you are a man!”","zh":"“哎呀！心想不来的，因为您呀，您不是女人。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But men too had had their trials, and the conversation went off into certain philosophical reflections. Emma expatiated much on the misery of earthly affections, and the eternal isolation in which the heart remains entombed.","sentences":[{"en":"But men too had had their trials, and the conversation went off into certain philosophical reflections.","zh":"不过男子也有男子的苦恼，谈话带上了哲理意味。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma expatiated much on the misery of earthly affections, and the eternal isolation in which the heart remains entombed.","zh":"爱玛大谈特谈人事无常，长年寂寞，心像活埋了一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To show off, or from a naive imitation of this melancholy which called forth his, the young man declared that he had been awfully bored during the whole course of his studies. The law irritated him, other vocations attracted him, and his mother never ceased worrying him in every one of her letters. As they talked they explained more and more fully the motives of their sadness, working themselves up in their progressive confidence. But they sometimes stopped short of the complete exposition of their thought, and then sought to invent a phrase that might express it all the same. She did not confess her passion for another; he did not say that he had forgotten her.","sentences":[{"en":"To show off, or from a naive imitation of this melancholy which called forth his, the young man declared that he had been awfully bored during the whole course of his studies.","zh":"年轻人为了取得好感，或者受了熏染，天真烂漫，模仿这种忧郁，讲起他在学校，一年四季，万分无聊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The law irritated him, other vocations attracted him, and his mother never ceased worrying him in every one of her letters.","zh":"他嫌诉讼程序烦琐，直想改行，母亲写信给他，封封使他难过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As they talked they explained more and more fully the motives of their sadness, working themselves up in their progressive confidence.","zh":"他们谈到痛苦的原因，越谈越细致，倾筐倒箧，畅所欲言，说到后来，全无一点兴奋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But they sometimes stopped short of the complete exposition of their thought, and then sought to invent a phrase that might express it all the same.","zh":"不过他们没有把话全说出来，有时候就沉吟不语，寻思一句能表达心意的话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She did not confess her passion for another; he did not say that he had forgotten her.","zh":"她绝口不提她对另一个男子的热情；他也瞒住不说他曾经把她忘了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Perhaps he no longer remembered his suppers with girls after masked balls; and no doubt she did not recollect the rendezvous of old when she ran across the fields in the morning to her lover’s house. The noises of the town hardly reached them, and the room seemed small, as if on purpose to hem in their solitude more closely. Emma, in a dimity dressing-gown, leant her head against the back of the old arm-chair; the yellow wall-paper formed, as it were, a golden background behind her, and her bare head was mirrored in the glass with the white parting in the middle, and the tip of her ears peeping out from the folds of her hair.","sentences":[{"en":"Perhaps he no longer remembered his suppers with girls after masked balls; and no doubt she did not recollect the rendezvous of old when she ran across the fields in the morning to her lover’s house.","zh":"他或许已记不起舞会后和姑娘们吃夜宵的情景；不用说，她也把清晨在草地上奔往情人的庄园去幽会之事忘在九霄云外。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The noises of the town hardly reached them, and the room seemed small, as if on purpose to hem in their solitude more closely.","zh":"城市的喧嚣差不多传不到他们的耳朵；房间很小，仿佛特意造成这样，缩小他们的寂寞。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma, in a dimity dressing-gown, leant her head against the back of the old arm-chair; the yellow wall-paper formed, as it were, a golden background behind her, and her bare head was mirrored in the glass with the white parting in the middle, and the tip of her ears peeping out from the folds of her hair.","zh":"爱玛穿一件条纹布梳头衣服，头发靠着扶手椅的椅背；黄墙纸像金色背景似的托着她；镜子照出她头上梳的白线似的中缝，耳朵梢露在头发外面。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But pardon me!” she said. “It is wrong of me. I weary you with my eternal complaints.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But pardon me!” she said.","zh":"“不过，对不住，我错了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“It is wrong of me.","zh":"我左诉苦，右诉苦，诉来诉去，您听也听腻烦了！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I weary you with my eternal complaints.”","zh":"我左诉苦，右诉苦，诉来诉去，您听也听腻烦了！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“No, never, never!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, never, never!”","zh":"“不，不！没有的事！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If you knew,” she went on, raising to the ceiling her beautiful eyes, in which a tear was trembling, “all that I had dreamed!”","sentences":[{"en":"“If you knew,” she went on, raising to the ceiling her beautiful eyes, in which a tear was trembling, “all that I had dreamed!”","zh":"她仰起眼睛望天花板，眼里包着一滴眼泪，接下去道：“您知道我一向梦想些什么也就好了！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And I! Oh, I too have suffered! Often I went out; I went away. I dragged myself along the quays, seeking distraction amid the din of the crowd without being able to banish the heaviness that weighed upon me. In an engraver’s shop on the boulevard there is an Italian print of one of the Muses. She is draped in a tunic, and she is looking at the moon, with forget-me-nots in her flowing hair. Something drove me there continually; I stayed there hours together.” Then in a trembling voice, “She resembled you a little.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And I! Oh, I too have suffered!","zh":"“我也一样！哎呀！我受够了罪！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often I went out; I went away.","zh":"我常常走出房间，来到街上，沿着河岸，一步一步拖着身子，想在嘈杂人群里忘记自己，可是心事重重，我就没有法子做到。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I dragged myself along the quays, seeking distraction amid the din of the crowd without being able to banish the heaviness that weighed upon me.","zh":"我常常走出房间，来到街上，沿着河岸，一步一步拖着身子，想在嘈杂人群里忘记自己，可是心事重重，我就没有法子做到。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In an engraver’s shop on the boulevard there is an Italian print of one of the Muses.","zh":"路旁有一家画店，橱窗里挂着一张意大利版画，上面画着一位文艺女神，披了一件贴身衣服，眼睛望着月亮，头发散开，簪着勿忘草。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She is draped in a tunic, and she is looking at the moon, with forget-me-nots in her flowing hair.","zh":"路旁有一家画店，橱窗里挂着一张意大利版画，上面画着一位文艺女神，披了一件贴身衣服，眼睛望着月亮，头发散开，簪着勿忘草。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Something drove me there continually; I stayed there hours together.”","zh":"有什么东西不住地吸引我过去；我在那边一待就是几小时。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then in a trembling voice, “She resembled you a little.”","zh":"然后声音发颤，他说：“她有一点像您。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary turned away her head that he might not see the irrepressible smile she felt rising to her lips.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary turned away her head that he might not see the irrepressible smile she felt rising to her lips.","zh":"包法利夫人转过头去，因为她挡不住自己微笑，却又不希望他看见。他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Often,” he went on, “I wrote you letters that I tore up.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Often,” he went on, “I wrote you letters that I tore up.”","zh":"“我常常给您写信，写好了，又撕掉。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She did not answer. He continued—","sentences":[{"en":"She did not answer.","zh":"她不回答。他继续说：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He continued—","zh":"她不回答。他继续说：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I sometimes fancied that some chance would bring you. I thought I recognised you at street-corners, and I ran after all the carriages through whose windows I saw a shawl fluttering, a veil like yours.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I sometimes fancied that some chance would bring you.","zh":"“我有时候心想，机缘凑巧我会遇见您。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought I recognised you at street-corners, and I ran after all the carriages through whose windows I saw a shawl fluttering, a veil like yours.”","zh":"别人走过街角，我错以为是您；我追赶所有的马车，只要看见车门飘出一条披肩、一幅面网，和您的一样…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She seemed resolved to let him go on speaking without interruption. Crossing her arms and bending down her face, she looked at the rosettes on her slippers, and at intervals made little movements inside the satin of them with her toes.","sentences":[{"en":"She seemed resolved to let him go on speaking without interruption.","zh":"她似乎打定主意，由他说去，并不打断。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Crossing her arms and bending down her face, she looked at the rosettes on her slippers, and at intervals made little movements inside the satin of them with her toes.","zh":"她交叉胳膊，垂下脸来，望着拖鞋的鞋花，偶尔脚尖在缎面里头微微一动。不过她叹了一口气：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At last she sighed.","sentences":[{"en":"At last she sighed.","zh":"她交叉胳膊，垂下脸来，望着拖鞋的鞋花，偶尔脚尖在缎面里头微微一动。不过她叹了一口气：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“But the most wretched thing, is it not—is to drag out, as I do, a useless existence. If our pains were only of some use to someone, we should find consolation in the thought of the sacrifice.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But the most wretched thing, is it not—is to drag out, as I do, a useless existence.","zh":"“世上最伤心的事，难道不是像我一样，一辈子没有正经用处？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If our pains were only of some use to someone, we should find consolation in the thought of the sacrifice.”","zh":"我们的痛苦如果能对别人有用的话，想着是牺牲，倒也可以自慰了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He started off in praise of virtue, duty, and silent immolation, having himself an incredible longing for self-sacrifice that he could not satisfy.","sentences":[{"en":"He started off in praise of virtue, duty, and silent immolation, having himself an incredible longing for self-sacrifice that he could not satisfy.","zh":"他开始赞扬道德、责任和默默无闻的牺牲，说来也不见得相信，不过这是实情，他自己就有一片忠心，得不到机会满足。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I should much like,” she said, “to be a nurse at a hospital.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I should much like,” she said, “to be a nurse at a hospital.”","zh":"“我真愿意做一名医院的护士，看护病人。”他回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Alas! men have none of these holy missions, and I see nowhere any calling—unless perhaps that of a doctor.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Alas! men have none of these holy missions, and I see nowhere any calling—unless perhaps that of a doctor.”","zh":"“嗐！男子就没有这一类神圣使命，我就看不出我有什么事好做…除非也许是，做做医生…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"With a slight shrug of her shoulders, Emma interrupted him to speak of her illness, which had almost killed her. What a pity! She should not be suffering now! Léon at once envied the calm of the tomb, and one evening he had even made his will, asking to be buried in that beautiful rug with velvet stripes he had received from her. For this was how they would have wished to be, each setting up an ideal to which they were now adapting their past life. Besides, speech is a rolling-mill that always thins out the sentiment.","sentences":[{"en":"With a slight shrug of her shoulders, Emma interrupted him to speak of her illness, which had almost killed her.","zh":"爱玛轻轻耸了一下肩膀，打断他的话，抱怨自己害了一场大病，偏偏不死；真是可惜！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What a pity!","zh":"死了的话，她现在也就不至于再受罪了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She should not be suffering now!","zh":"死了的话，她现在也就不至于再受罪了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Léon at once envied the calm of the tomb, and one evening he had even made his will, asking to be buried in that beautiful rug with velvet stripes he had received from her.","zh":"赖昂马上就说，他羡慕坟墓的宁静，甚至有一晚，他立遗嘱，要人埋他时用她送他的那条有绒道道的漂亮脚毯裹他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For this was how they would have wished to be, each setting up an ideal to which they were now adapting their past life.","zh":"他们未尝不希望自己曾经这样生活，所以如今做出一种理想的安排，补充到过去的生活中去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, speech is a rolling-mill that always thins out the sentiment.","zh":"再说，语言就是一架展延机，永远拉长感情。但是听到关于脚毯的鬼话，她问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But at this invention of the rug she asked, “But why?”","sentences":[{"en":"But at this invention of the rug she asked, “But why?”","zh":"“这是为什么？”“为什么？”他迟疑了一下：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why?” He hesitated. “Because I loved you so!” And congratulating himself at having surmounted the difficulty, Léon watched her face out of the corner of his eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why?”","zh":"“因为我爱您啊！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He hesitated.","zh":"“因为我爱您啊！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Because I loved you so!”","zh":"“因为我爱您啊！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"And congratulating himself at having surmounted the difficulty, Léon watched her face out of the corner of his eyes.","zh":"赖昂一面庆幸自己跳过难关，一面乜斜着眼睛，观察她的脸色。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was like the sky when a gust of wind drives the clouds across. The mass of sad thoughts that darkened them seemed to be lifted from her blue eyes; her whole face shone. He waited. At last she replied—","sentences":[{"en":"It was like the sky when a gust of wind drives the clouds across.","zh":"她的脸色仿佛天空，一阵风刮走了乌云。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The mass of sad thoughts that darkened them seemed to be lifted from her blue eyes; her whole face shone.","zh":"黑压压的忧郁思想，似乎走出她的蓝眼睛 ，整个脸熠熠发光。他等候反应。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He waited.","zh":"她最后回答道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last she replied—","zh":"“我从前也一直这么觉得…”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I always suspected it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I always suspected it.”","zh":"“我从前也一直这么觉得…”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then they went over all the trifling events of that far-off existence, whose joys and sorrows they had just summed up in one word. They recalled the arbour with clematis, the dresses she had worn, the furniture of her room, the whole of her house.","sentences":[{"en":"Then they went over all the trifling events of that far-off existence, whose joys and sorrows they had just summed up in one word.","zh":"于是他们谈起过去发生的那些琐细事件，其中或苦或乐，他们方才已经用一个字眼总括过了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They recalled the arbour with clematis, the dresses she had worn, the furniture of her room, the whole of her house.","zh":"他想起铁线莲的架子、她往常穿的袍子、她的卧室家具、她的整所房子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And our poor cactuses, where are they?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And our poor cactuses, where are they?”","zh":"“我们可怜的仙人掌怎么样了？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The cold killed them this winter.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The cold killed them this winter.”","zh":"“去年冬天冻死了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! how I have thought of them, do you know? I often saw them again as of yore, when on the summer mornings the sun beat down upon your blinds, and I saw your two bare arms passing out amongst the flowers.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! how I have thought of them, do you know?","zh":"“啊！您知道我多想念它们吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I often saw them again as of yore, when on the summer mornings the sun beat down upon your blinds, and I saw your two bare arms passing out amongst the flowers.”","zh":"我常常看见它们像从前一样，夏天早晨，太阳照着窗帘…我望见您的两只光胳膊，在花草当中，过来过去。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Poor friend!” she said, holding out her hand to him.","sentences":[{"en":"“Poor friend!” she said, holding out her hand to him.","zh":"“可怜的朋友！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon swiftly pressed his lips to it. Then, when he had taken a deep breath—","sentences":[{"en":"Léon swiftly pressed his lips to it.","zh":"她朝他伸出手去，赖昂连忙凑上嘴唇，然后深深吸了一口气道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, when he had taken a deep breath—","zh":"她朝他伸出手去，赖昂连忙凑上嘴唇，然后深深吸了一口气道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“At that time you were to me I know not what incomprehensible force that took captive my life. Once, for instance, I went to see you; but you, no doubt, do not remember it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“At that time you were to me I know not what incomprehensible force that took captive my life.","zh":"“就我来说，我不知道您当时有什么不可思议的力量把我俘虏了过去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once, for instance, I went to see you; but you, no doubt, do not remember it.”","zh":"有一回，好比说，我来到您家；不过，不用说，您不记得了吧？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I do,” she said; “go on.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I do,” she said; “go on.”","zh":"她说：“记得。讲下去。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You were downstairs in the ante-room, ready to go out, standing on the last stair; you were wearing a bonnet with small blue flowers; and without any invitation from you, in spite of myself, I went with you. Every moment, however, I grew more and more conscious of my folly, and I went on walking by you, not daring to follow you completely, and unwilling to leave you. When you went into a shop, I waited in the street, and I watched you through the window taking off your gloves and counting the change on the counter. Then you rang at Madame Tuvache’s; you were let in, and I stood like an idiot in front of the great heavy door that had closed after you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You were downstairs in the ante-room, ready to go out, standing on the last stair; you were wearing a bonnet with small blue flowers; and without any invitation from you, in spite of myself, I went with you.","zh":"“您在楼下前厅，正要出门，站在末一道台阶——您还戴了一顶小蓝花帽子；您没有邀我，可是我不由自主，陪着您走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Every moment, however, I grew more and more conscious of my folly, and I went on walking by you, not daring to follow you completely, and unwilling to leave you.","zh":"每一分钟，我越来越觉得自己犯傻，可是我照样在您旁边走动，不敢太靠近，可又不愿意离开您。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When you went into a shop, I waited in the street, and I watched you through the window taking off your gloves and counting the change on the counter.","zh":"您走进铺子，我待在街上，隔着玻璃窗，看您摘掉手套，在柜台上数钱。过后您在杜法赦门口拉铃，有人给您开门，门又重又大，您一进去，就又关上了，我待在外头，活像一个傻瓜。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then you rang at Madame Tuvache’s; you were let in, and I stood like an idiot in front of the great heavy door that had closed after you.”","zh":"您走进铺子，我待在街上，隔着玻璃窗，看您摘掉手套，在柜台上数钱。过后您在杜法赦门口拉铃，有人给您开门，门又重又大，您一进去，就又关上了，我待在外头，活像一个傻瓜。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary, as she listened to him, wondered that she was so old. All these things reappearing before her seemed to widen out her life; it was like some sentimental immensity to which she returned; and from time to time she said in a low voice, her eyes half closed—","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary, as she listened to him, wondered that she was so old.","zh":"包法利夫人听他讲，惊讶自己竟这样老了；这些花花絮絮的事情，仿佛扩展了她的生命，形成一片感情的海洋任她遨游。她半闭着眼，不时低声道：“是啊，真是这样！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All these things reappearing before her seemed to widen out her life; it was like some sentimental immensity to which she returned; and from time to time she said in a low voice, her eyes half closed—","zh":"真是这样！真是这样！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, it is true—true—true!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, it is true—true—true!”","zh":"芳邻区很有一些寄宿学校、教堂和无人居住的大公馆，形形色色的大钟在响。他们听见钟敲八点。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"They heard eight strike on the different clocks of the Beauvoisine quarter, which is full of schools, churches, and large empty hotels. They no longer spoke, but they felt as they looked upon each other a buzzing in their heads, as if something sonorous had escaped from the fixed eyes of each of them. They were hand in hand now, and the past, the future, reminiscences and dreams, all were confounded in the sweetness of this ecstasy. Night was darkening over the walls, on which still shone, half hidden in the shade, the coarse colours of four bills representing four scenes from the “Tour de Nesle,” with a motto in Spanish and French at the bottom. Through the sash-window a patch of dark sky was seen between the pointed roofs.","sentences":[{"en":"They heard eight strike on the different clocks of the Beauvoisine quarter, which is full of schools, churches, and large empty hotels.","zh":"芳邻区很有一些寄宿学校、教堂和无人居住的大公馆，形形色色的大钟在响。他们听见钟敲八点。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They no longer spoke, but they felt as they looked upon each other a buzzing in their heads, as if something sonorous had escaped from the fixed eyes of each of them.","zh":"他们不再言语；但是你看着我，我看着你，觉得脑子里扑扇扑扇的，像有什么出声的东西，顺着他们一动不动的瞳孔流过来流过去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were hand in hand now, and the past, the future, reminiscences and dreams, all were confounded in the sweetness of this ecstasy.","zh":"他们握着手，只见过去、未来、回忆和梦想，全部融化在这销魂的优美境界。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Night was darkening over the walls, on which still shone, half hidden in the shade, the coarse colours of four bills representing four scenes from the “Tour de Nesle,” with a motto in Spanish and French at the bottom.","zh":"夜渐渐深了，墙上挂的四幅版画，画着《奈勒塔》 四个场面，底下有西班牙文和法文说明，在阴影里，已经看不大清了，浓浓的颜色还在闪烁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Through the sash-window a patch of dark sky was seen between the pointed roofs.","zh":"从往上推的窗户望出去，尖房顶之间，露出一角黑暗的天空。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She rose to light two wax-candles on the drawers, then she sat down again.","sentences":[{"en":"She rose to light two wax-candles on the drawers, then she sat down again.","zh":"她站起来，点亮五斗柜上的两支蜡烛，回来坐下。赖昂道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well!” said Léon.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well!” said Léon.","zh":"“什么？”她回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well!” she replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well!” she replied.","zh":"“什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was thinking how to resume the interrupted conversation, when she said to him—","sentences":[{"en":"He was thinking how to resume the interrupted conversation, when she said to him—","zh":"断了的谈话，他正寻思怎样才能接上，就见她对他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How is it that no one until now has ever expressed such sentiments to me?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How is it that no one until now has ever expressed such sentiments to me?”","zh":"“到目前为止，从来没有人对我表示过这种感情，又是什么缘故？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The clerk said that ideal natures were difficult to understand. He from the first moment had loved her, and he despaired when he thought of the happiness that would have been theirs, if thanks to fortune, meeting her earlier, they had been indissolubly bound to one another.","sentences":[{"en":"The clerk said that ideal natures were difficult to understand.","zh":"文书指出：人的精神活动是不容易理解的。他爱她就是一见钟情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He from the first moment had loved her, and he despaired when he thought of the happiness that would have been theirs, if thanks to fortune, meeting her earlier, they had been indissolubly bound to one another.","zh":"如果天假良缘，他们得以早日相逢的话，彼此一定好合无间，恩爱到老，所以他一想到他们实现不了这种幸福，就万分痛苦。她接下去道：“我有时候也这样想来着。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I have sometimes thought of it,” she went on.","sentences":[{"en":"“I have sometimes thought of it,” she went on.","zh":"赖昂呢喃道：“多好的梦啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What a dream!” murmured Léon. And fingering gently the blue binding of her long white sash, he added, “And who prevents us from beginning now?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What a dream!” murmured Léon.","zh":"他轻轻抚摸着她的又长又白的腰带的蓝压边，继续道：“那么，有什么阻拦我们重新开始呢？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"And fingering gently the blue binding of her long white sash, he added, “And who prevents us from beginning now?”","zh":"他轻轻抚摸着她的又长又白的腰带的蓝压边，继续道：“那么，有什么阻拦我们重新开始呢？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“No, my friend,” she replied; “I am too old; you are too young. Forget me! Others will love you; you will love them.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, my friend,” she replied; “I am too old; you are too young.","zh":"她回答道：“不成，我的朋友。我太老…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Forget me!","zh":"您太年轻…忘了我吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Others will love you; you will love them.”","zh":"会有别人爱你…您也会爱她们的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Not as you!” he cried.","sentences":[{"en":"“Not as you!” he cried.","zh":"他喊道：“不像爱您一样！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What a child you are! Come, let us be sensible. I wish it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What a child you are!","zh":"“您真成了小孩子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Come, let us be sensible.","zh":"好啦，放乖些，我要您这样！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I wish it.”","zh":"好啦，放乖些，我要您这样！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She showed him the impossibility of their love, and that they must remain, as formerly, on the simple terms of a fraternal friendship.","sentences":[{"en":"She showed him the impossibility of their love, and that they must remain, as formerly, on the simple terms of a fraternal friendship.","zh":"她指出他们不可能相爱，他们应当永远像往常一样，仅仅保持友谊。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Was she speaking thus seriously? No doubt Emma did not herself know, quite absorbed as she was by the charm of the seduction, and the necessity of defending herself from it; and contemplating the young man with a moved look, she gently repulsed the timid caresses that his trembling hands attempted.","sentences":[{"en":"Was she speaking thus seriously?","zh":"她说这话认真不认真？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No doubt Emma did not herself know, quite absorbed as she was by the charm of the seduction, and the necessity of defending herself from it; and contemplating the young man with a moved look, she gently repulsed the timid caresses that his trembling hands attempted.","zh":"毫无疑问，她心里充满了被诱惑的愉快，却又必须防止被他诱惑，连自己也不晓得是不是认真。他的手畏畏缩缩，试着抚摸她；她望着年轻人，眼睛充满怜惜，轻轻推开他的哆哆嗦嗦的手。他后退道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! forgive me!” he cried, drawing back.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! forgive me!” he cried, drawing back.","zh":"“啊！对不住。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma was seized with a vague fear at this shyness, more dangerous to her than the boldness of Rodolphe when he advanced to her open-armed. No man had ever seemed to her so beautiful. An exquisite candour emanated from his being. He lowered his long fine eyelashes, that curled upwards. His cheek, with the soft skin reddened, she thought, with desire of her person, and Emma felt an invincible longing to press her lips to it. Then, leaning towards the clock as if to see the time—","sentences":[{"en":"Emma was seized with a vague fear at this shyness, more dangerous to her than the boldness of Rodolphe when he advanced to her open-armed.","zh":"爱玛觉得这种畏缩，比起罗道耳弗色胆包天、伸出胳膊搂她还要危险，不由起了一种无名的畏惧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No man had ever seemed to her so beautiful.","zh":"她觉得从来没有一个男子，长得像他这样美。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"An exquisite candour emanated from his being.","zh":"他的举止之间，流露出一种天真无邪的可爱神态。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He lowered his long fine eyelashes, that curled upwards.","zh":"他垂着他的又细又长的弯弯的睫毛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His cheek, with the soft skin reddened, she thought, with desire of her person, and Emma felt an invincible longing to press her lips to it.","zh":"他的细皮嫩肉的脸庞也因为欲火如焚——她想——涨得通红，爱玛心荡神驰，恨不得贴上嘴唇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, leaning towards the clock as if to see the time—","zh":"她于是看时间似的，朝钟俯下身子，道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! how late it is!” she said; “how we do chatter!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! how late it is!” she said; “how we do chatter!”","zh":"“我的上帝！我们尽说话，可不早啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He understood the hint and took up his hat.","sentences":[{"en":"He understood the hint and took up his hat.","zh":"他听出她的意思，寻找帽子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It has even made me forget the theatre. And poor Bovary has left me here especially for that. Monsieur Lormeaux, of the Rue Grand-Pont, was to take me and his wife.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It has even made me forget the theatre.","zh":"“我连戏也忘记看了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And poor Bovary has left me here especially for that.","zh":"可怜的包法利，把我留下来，就为了看戏！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Lormeaux, of the Rue Grand-Pont, was to take me and his wife.”","zh":"大桥街的洛尔莫先生和他的太太陪我一道去。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the opportunity was lost, as she was to leave the next day.","sentences":[{"en":"And the opportunity was lost, as she was to leave the next day.","zh":"机会错过了，因为她明天就动身回乡下去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Really!” said Léon.","sentences":[{"en":"“Really!” said Léon.","zh":"赖昂道：“当真？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“是的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But I must see you again,” he went on. “I wanted to tell you—”","sentences":[{"en":"“But I must see you again,” he went on.","zh":"他接着就说：“不过我还得和您见一面，我有话告诉您…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I wanted to tell you—”","zh":"他接着就说：“不过我还得和您见一面，我有话告诉您…”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“什么话？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Something—important—serious. Oh, no! Besides, you will not go; it is impossible. If you should—listen to me. Then you have not understood me; you have not guessed—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Something—important—serious.","zh":"“一件事…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, no! Besides, you will not go; it is impossible.","zh":"又要紧，又重大。哎！不，可不，您不要走，千万别走！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If you should—listen to me.","zh":"您要是知道…听我讲…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then you have not understood me; you have not guessed—”","zh":"您真就不懂我的意思？您真就猜不出来？”爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet you speak plainly,” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet you speak plainly,” said Emma.","zh":"“其实，您话说得很清楚。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! you can jest. Enough! enough! Oh, for pity’s sake, let me see you once—only once!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! you can jest.","zh":"“哎呀！您还取笑人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Enough! enough!","zh":"够啦，够啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, for pity’s sake, let me see you once—only once!”","zh":"您就可怜可怜我，让我和您再见一面…一面…只一面。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well—” She stopped; then, as if thinking better of it, “Oh, not here!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well—” She stopped; then, as if thinking better of it, “Oh, not here!”","zh":"“好吧！”她住了口，随后，仿佛想到什么：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where you will.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Where you will.”","zh":"“不在这儿！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Will you—” She seemed to reflect; then abruptly, “To-morrow at eleven o’clock in the cathedral.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Will you—” She seemed to reflect; then abruptly, “To-morrow at eleven o’clock in the cathedral.”","zh":"“您愿不愿意…”她想了想，一口气说完道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I shall be there,” he cried, seizing her hands, which she disengaged.","sentences":[{"en":"“I shall be there,” he cried, seizing her hands, which she disengaged.","zh":"“明天，十一点钟，在礼拜堂。”他抓住她的手，喊了一声：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And as they were both standing up, he behind her, and Emma with her head bent, he stooped over her and pressed long kisses on her neck.","sentences":[{"en":"And as they were both standing up, he behind her, and Emma with her head bent, he stooped over her and pressed long kisses on her neck.","zh":"“我一定来！”她抽出手，低下了头。两个人全站直了，他在她的背后，弯过身子，吻她的后颈，吻了许久。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are mad! Ah! you are mad!” she said, with sounding little laughs, while the kisses multiplied.","sentences":[{"en":"“You are mad!","zh":"“您疯啦！啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! you are mad!” she said, with sounding little laughs, while the kisses multiplied.","zh":"您疯啦！”她边说，边叽叽嘎嘎直笑。吻越发多了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then bending his head over her shoulder, he seemed to beg the consent of her eyes. They fell upon him full of an icy dignity.","sentences":[{"en":"Then bending his head over her shoulder, he seemed to beg the consent of her eyes.","zh":"他于是拿头探过她的肩膀，仿佛从她的眼睛征求同意一般。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They fell upon him full of an icy dignity.","zh":"她的眼睛望着他，冷冰冰的，充满庄严。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon stepped back to go out. He stopped on the threshold; then he whispered with a trembling voice, “Tomorrow!”","sentences":[{"en":"Léon stepped back to go out.","zh":"赖昂倒退三步，准备出去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He stopped on the threshold; then he whispered with a trembling voice, “Tomorrow!”","zh":"他在门边停住，然后声音颤抖着，低声说道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She answered with a nod, and disappeared like a bird into the next room.","sentences":[{"en":"She answered with a nod, and disappeared like a bird into the next room.","zh":"“明天见。”她点点头，飞鸟一样去了里间。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the evening Emma wrote the clerk an interminable letter, in which she cancelled the rendezvous; all was over; they must not, for the sake of their happiness, meet again. But when the letter was finished, as she did not know Léon’s address, she was puzzled.","sentences":[{"en":"In the evening Emma wrote the clerk an interminable letter, in which she cancelled the rendezvous; all was over; they must not, for the sake of their happiness, meet again.","zh":"爱玛当晚给文书写了一封拖拖拉拉的长信，谢绝约会；往事如烟，他们如今为了自己的幸福，不该相会。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But when the letter was finished, as she did not know Léon’s address, she was puzzled.","zh":"但是封好了信，她才想起不知道赖昂的住址，无从投递。她为难了一时，向自己道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I’ll give it to him myself,” she said; “he will come.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll give it to him myself,” she said; “he will come.”","zh":"“我当面给他。他会去的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next morning, at the open window, and humming on his balcony, Léon himself varnished his pumps with several coatings. He put on white trousers, fine socks, a green coat, emptied all the scent he had into his handkerchief, then having had his hair curled, he uncurled it again, in order to give it a more natural elegance.","sentences":[{"en":"The next morning, at the open window, and humming on his balcony, Léon himself varnished his pumps with several coatings.","zh":"第二天，赖昂打开窗户，在阳台上低声唱歌，亲自刷亮皮鞋，一连刷了几遍。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He put on white trousers, fine socks, a green coat, emptied all the scent he had into his handkerchief, then having had his hair curled, he uncurled it again, in order to give it a more natural elegance.","zh":"他穿上白裤、上等短袜、绿燕尾服，把他所有的香水统统洒在手帕上，然后头发卷成鬈鬈，再打散了，让头发具有一种自然的优雅。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is still too early,” he thought, looking at the hairdresser’s cuckoo-clock, that pointed to the hour of nine. He read an old fashion journal, went out, smoked a cigar, walked up three streets, thought it was time, and went slowly towards the porch of Notre Dame.","sentences":[{"en":"“It is still too early,” he thought, looking at the hairdresser’s cuckoo-clock, that pointed to the hour of nine.","zh":"他发现理发店的杜鹃钟正指九点，心想：“还太早！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He read an old fashion journal, went out, smoked a cigar, walked up three streets, thought it was time, and went slowly towards the porch of Notre Dame.","zh":"他拿起一本旧时装杂志看了看，这才出去，吸着一支雪茄，荡过三条马路，心想是时候了，慢悠悠朝礼拜堂走去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was a beautiful summer morning. Silver plate sparkled in the jeweller’s windows, and the light falling obliquely on the cathedral made mirrors of the corners of the grey stones; a flock of birds fluttered in the grey sky round the trefoil bell-turrets; the square, resounding with cries, was fragrant with the flowers that bordered its pavement, roses, jasmines, pinks, narcissi, and tube-roses, unevenly spaced out between moist grasses, catmint, and chickweed for the birds; the fountains gurgled in the centre, and under large umbrellas, amidst melons, piled up in heaps, flower-women, bare-headed, were twisting paper round bunches of violets.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a beautiful summer morning.","zh":"夏季早晨，风和日丽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Silver plate sparkled in the jeweller’s windows, and the light falling obliquely on the cathedral made mirrors of the corners of the grey stones; a flock of birds fluttered in the grey sky round the trefoil bell-turrets; the square, resounding with cries, was fragrant with the flowers that bordered its pavement, roses, jasmines, pinks, narcissi, and tube-roses, unevenly spaced out between moist grasses, catmint, and chickweed for the birds; the fountains gurgled in the centre, and under large umbrellas, amidst melons, piled up in heaps, flower-women, bare-headed, were twisting paper round bunches of violets.","zh":"银楼的银器晶莹耀眼；阳光斜照礼拜堂，灰色石头的断口闪闪烁烁；一群鸟绕着有三叶花饰的小钟楼，在碧空飞来飞去；广场一片喧哗，花香扑鼻：沿石板路种有玫瑰花、素馨花、石竹花、水仙花和晚香玉，中间远近不等，夹杂着一些湿漉漉的绿叶、猫尾草和喂鸟用的鹅肠菜；喷泉在当中淙淙琤琤直响；大伞底下有些没戴帽子的妇女，站在摞成金字塔似的疙瘩皮西瓜当中，拿纸包扎紫罗兰花束。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The young man took one. It was the first time that he had bought flowers for a woman, and his breast, as he smelt them, swelled with pride, as if this homage that he meant for another had recoiled upon himself.","sentences":[{"en":"The young man took one.","zh":"年轻人买了一把。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the first time that he had bought flowers for a woman, and his breast, as he smelt them, swelled with pride, as if this homage that he meant for another had recoiled upon himself.","zh":"他这是头一次为女人买花；他闻着花香，傲形于色，胸脯也挺起来了，倒像他这花不是送别人而是送自己的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But he was afraid of being seen; he resolutely entered the church. The beadle, who was just then standing on the threshold in the middle of the left doorway, under the “Dancing Marianne,” with feather cap, and rapier dangling against his calves, came in, more majestic than a cardinal, and as shining as a saint on a holy pyx.","sentences":[{"en":"But he was afraid of being seen; he resolutely entered the church.","zh":"不过他怕有人看见，只好硬起头皮，走进教堂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The beadle, who was just then standing on the threshold in the middle of the left doorway, under the “Dancing Marianne,” with feather cap, and rapier dangling against his calves, came in, more majestic than a cardinal, and as shining as a saint on a holy pyx.","zh":"左门当中，在翩翩起舞的玛丽亚娜 底下，守卫当时正好站在门槛，头戴羽盔，腰挎长剑，手持拄杖，比红衣主教还庄严，像圣体盒那样耀眼。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He came towards Léon, and, with that smile of wheedling benignity assumed by ecclesiastics when they question children—","sentences":[{"en":"He came towards Léon, and, with that smile of wheedling benignity assumed by ecclesiastics when they question children—","zh":"他满脸笑容，和善狡黠，仿佛教士盘问小孩子，走向赖昂：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The gentleman, no doubt, does not belong to these parts? The gentleman would like to see the curiosities of the church?”","sentences":[{"en":"“The gentleman, no doubt, does not belong to these parts?","zh":"“先生想必不是本地人吧？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The gentleman would like to see the curiosities of the church?”","zh":"先生有意观光观光教堂？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No!” said the other.","sentences":[{"en":"“No!” said the other.","zh":"赖昂说：“不要。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he first went round the lower aisles. Then he went out to look at the Place. Emma was not coming yet. He went up again to the choir.","sentences":[{"en":"And he first went round the lower aisles.","zh":"他先沿着两侧，走了一匝，然后回到广场张望。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he went out to look at the Place.","zh":"他先沿着两侧，走了一匝，然后回到广场张望。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma was not coming yet.","zh":"他不见爱玛，又上来，一直走到唱经堂。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He went up again to the choir.","zh":"他不见爱玛，又上来，一直走到唱经堂。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The nave was reflected in the full fonts with the beginning of the arches and some portions of the glass windows. But the reflections of the paintings, broken by the marble rim, were continued farther on upon the flag-stones, like a many-coloured carpet. The broad daylight from without streamed into the church in three enormous rays from the three opened portals. From time to time at the upper end a sacristan passed, making the oblique genuflexion of devout persons in a hurry. The crystal lustres hung motionless. In the choir a silver lamp was burning, and from the side chapels and dark places of the church sometimes rose sounds like sighs, with the clang of a closing grating, its echo reverberating under the lofty vault.","sentences":[{"en":"The nave was reflected in the full fonts with the beginning of the arches and some portions of the glass windows.","zh":"大殿屋顶、拱券上部和玻璃窗，倒映在满满的圣水盘里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the reflections of the paintings, broken by the marble rim, were continued farther on upon the flag-stones, like a many-coloured carpet.","zh":"花玻璃的反光，在大理石的边沿虽然断掉，反而射得更远了，摊在石地上，活像一条花花绿绿的地毯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The broad daylight from without streamed into the church in three enormous rays from the three opened portals.","zh":"强烈的阳光，顺着三座敞开的拱门，变成三道巨光，一直射到教堂里头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"From time to time at the upper end a sacristan passed, making the oblique genuflexion of devout persons in a hurry.","zh":"尽里不时走出一位司库，经过圣坛，斜身一跪，站起就走，好像行色匆忙的信士。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The crystal lustres hung motionless.","zh":"水晶烛台，安安静静，挂在半空。唱经堂点着一盏银灯；偏殿、教堂的阴暗部分，有时候发出一声叹息，加上关栅栏门的声音，在高耸的穹隆底下，发出回响。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In the choir a silver lamp was burning, and from the side chapels and dark places of the church sometimes rose sounds like sighs, with the clang of a closing grating, its echo reverberating under the lofty vault.","zh":"水晶烛台，安安静静，挂在半空。唱经堂点着一盏银灯；偏殿、教堂的阴暗部分，有时候发出一声叹息，加上关栅栏门的声音，在高耸的穹隆底下，发出回响。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Léon with solemn steps walked along by the walls. Life had never seemed so good to him. She would come directly, charming, agitated, looking back at the glances that followed her, and with her flounced dress, her gold eyeglass, her thin shoes, with all sorts of elegant trifles that he had never enjoyed, and with the ineffable seduction of yielding virtue. The church like a huge boudoir spread around her; the arches bent down to gather in the shade the confession of her love; the windows shone resplendent to illumine her face, and the censers would burn that she might appear like an angel amid the fumes of the sweet-smelling odours.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon with solemn steps walked along by the walls.","zh":"赖昂踱着庄严的步伐，在墙边徘徊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Life had never seemed so good to him.","zh":"他觉得人生对他从来没有这样好过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would come directly, charming, agitated, looking back at the glances that followed her, and with her flounced dress, her gold eyeglass, her thin shoes, with all sorts of elegant trifles that he had never enjoyed, and with the ineffable seduction of yielding virtue.","zh":"再过一会儿，她就来了，她一定是一副迷人的模样，心神不宁，偷眼张望背后看她的男女——穿着她的有花边道道的袍子，举着她的金丝眼镜，蹬着她的玲珑小靴：种种装饰，他见也没有见过，显出贞节将要失去时难以言传的魅力。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The church like a huge boudoir spread around her; the arches bent down to gather in the shade the confession of her love; the windows shone resplendent to illumine her face, and the censers would burn that she might appear like an angel amid the fumes of the sweet-smelling odours.","zh":"教堂好似一间广大的绣房，迎她进来。穹隆弯下身子，在阴影里头，听取她的爱情的自白。花玻璃窗明光闪闪，就为照亮她的脸，而香炉燃烧，就为香云缭绕，她像天使一样出现。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But she did not come. He sat down on a chair, and his eyes fell upon a blue stained window representing boatmen carrying baskets. He looked at it long, attentively, and he counted the scales of the fishes and the button-holes of the doublets, while his thoughts wandered off towards Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"But she did not come.","zh":"然而就是不见她来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sat down on a chair, and his eyes fell upon a blue stained window representing boatmen carrying baskets.","zh":"他坐在一张椅子上，望着一扇蓝玻璃窗，上面画了一些提筐携篮的船夫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He looked at it long, attentively, and he counted the scales of the fishes and the button-holes of the doublets, while his thoughts wandered off towards Emma.","zh":"他集中注意力，望了许久，计算鱼鳞和小领紧身短袄的钮孔的数目，思想却漫无目的，四下寻找爱玛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The beadle, standing aloof, was inwardly angry at this individual who took the liberty of admiring the cathedral by himself. He seemed to him to be conducting himself in a monstrous fashion, to be robbing him in a sort, and almost committing sacrilege.","sentences":[{"en":"The beadle, standing aloof, was inwardly angry at this individual who took the liberty of admiring the cathedral by himself.","zh":"守卫站在一旁，心里直生这人的气：他居然独自观赏礼拜堂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He seemed to him to be conducting himself in a monstrous fashion, to be robbing him in a sort, and almost committing sacrilege.","zh":"在守卫看来，他行事荒唐，近乎剽窃，几乎是渎圣了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But a rustle of silk on the flags, the tip of a bonnet, a lined cloak—it was she! Léon rose and ran to meet her.","sentences":[{"en":"But a rustle of silk on the flags, the tip of a bonnet, a lined cloak—it was she!","zh":"但是石板路上响起了丝绸窸窣的声音，半空露出一顶帽子的边沿、一件小黑披风…是她！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Léon rose and ran to meet her.","zh":"但是石板路上响起了丝绸窸窣的声音，半空露出一顶帽子的边沿、一件小黑披风…是她！","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma was pale. She walked fast.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma was pale.","zh":"赖昂一跃而起，奔了过去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She walked fast.","zh":"赖昂一跃而起，奔了过去。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Read!” she said, holding out a paper to him. “Oh, no!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Read!” she said, holding out a paper to him.","zh":"爱玛面无血色，快步走来。她递给他一张纸道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Oh, no!”","zh":"爱玛面无血色，快步走来。她递给他一张纸道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And she abruptly withdrew her hand to enter the chapel of the Virgin, where, kneeling on a chair, she began to pray.","sentences":[{"en":"And she abruptly withdrew her hand to enter the chapel of the Virgin, where, kneeling on a chair, she began to pray.","zh":"啊！不！”她急忙缩回手，走进圣母堂，靠住一张椅子跪下来，开始祷告。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The young man was irritated at this bigot fancy; then he nevertheless experienced a certain charm in seeing her, in the middle of a rendezvous, thus lost in her devotions, like an Andalusian marchioness; then he grew bored, for she seemed never coming to an end.","sentences":[{"en":"The young man was irritated at this bigot fancy; then he nevertheless experienced a certain charm in seeing her, in the middle of a rendezvous, thus lost in her devotions, like an Andalusian marchioness; then he grew bored, for she seemed never coming to an end.","zh":"年轻人恼恨她这心血来潮的虔诚，然而见她在幽会地点，仿佛安达卢西亚的一位侯爵夫人 ，一心一意在祈祷，倒也感到有趣，没有多久，却又不耐烦了，因为她祷告下去，没完没了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma prayed, or rather strove to pray, hoping that some sudden resolution might descend to her from heaven; and to draw down divine aid she filled full her eyes with the splendours of the tabernacle. She breathed in the perfumes of the full-blown flowers in the large vases, and listened to the stillness of the church, that only heightened the tumult of her heart.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma prayed, or rather strove to pray, hoping that some sudden resolution might descend to her from heaven; and to draw down divine aid she filled full her eyes with the splendours of the tabernacle.","zh":"爱玛在祷告，或者不如说是努力在祷告，希望上天迅速帮她做出决定来；她为了得到神助，就望着光辉的圣龛，吸着插在大瓶里的开白花的南芥菜的香味，感受着教堂的一片静默：结果心倒越发乱了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She breathed in the perfumes of the full-blown flowers in the large vases, and listened to the stillness of the church, that only heightened the tumult of her heart.","zh":"爱玛在祷告，或者不如说是努力在祷告，希望上天迅速帮她做出决定来；她为了得到神助，就望着光辉的圣龛，吸着插在大瓶里的开白花的南芥菜的香味，感受着教堂的一片静默：结果心倒越发乱了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She rose, and they were about to leave, when the beadle came forward, hurriedly saying—","sentences":[{"en":"She rose, and they were about to leave, when the beadle came forward, hurriedly saying—","zh":"她站起来。他们正要走出，就见守卫急忙凑近道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Madame, no doubt, does not belong to these parts? Madame would like to see the curiosities of the church?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Madame, no doubt, does not belong to these parts?","zh":"“太太想必不是本地人吧？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame would like to see the curiosities of the church?”","zh":"太太有意观光观光教堂吗？”文书喊道：“不要！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, no!” cried the clerk.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, no!” cried the clerk.","zh":"她回答：“为什么不？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why not?” said she. For she clung with her expiring virtue to the Virgin, the sculptures, the tombs—anything.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why not?” said she.","zh":"因为眼看贞节要守不住，她只好求助于圣母、雕像、墓冢、任何机缘。","scope":"group"},{"en":"For she clung with her expiring virtue to the Virgin, the sculptures, the tombs—anything.","zh":"因为眼看贞节要守不住，她只好求助于圣母、雕像、墓冢、任何机缘。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then, in order to proceed “by rule,” the beadle conducted them right to the entrance near the square, where, pointing out with his cane a large circle of block-stones without inscription or carving—","sentences":[{"en":"Then, in order to proceed “by rule,” the beadle conducted them right to the entrance near the square, where, pointing out with his cane a large circle of block-stones without inscription or carving—","zh":"于是按顺序进行，守卫把他们一直领到靠近广场的入口，手杖指着黑石头铺成的一个大圆圈，上面没有铭记，也没有花纹，摆出一副庄严的模样道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“This,” he said majestically, “is the circumference of the beautiful bell of Ambroise. It weighed forty thousand pounds. There was not its equal in all Europe. The workman who cast it died of the joy—”","sentences":[{"en":"“This,” he said majestically, “is the circumference of the beautiful bell of Ambroise.","zh":"“这儿就是昂布瓦斯大钟的钟口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It weighed forty thousand pounds.","zh":"钟重四万磅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was not its equal in all Europe.","zh":"全欧洲没有第二只。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The workman who cast it died of the joy—”","zh":"铸钟的工人一开心，闭过气去，死了…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Let us go on,” said Léon.","sentences":[{"en":"“Let us go on,” said Léon.","zh":"赖昂道：“走吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The old fellow started off again; then, having got back to the chapel of the Virgin, he stretched forth his arm with an all-embracing gesture of demonstration, and, prouder than a country squire showing you his espaliers, went on—","sentences":[{"en":"The old fellow started off again; then, having got back to the chapel of the Virgin, he stretched forth his arm with an all-embracing gesture of demonstration, and, prouder than a country squire showing you his espaliers, went on—","zh":"老好人往里走，回到圣母堂，伸出双臂，做了一个概括的解释姿势，比乡绅带你看他的墙边果木还要得意：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“This simple stone covers Pierre de Breze, lord of Varenne and of Brissac, grand marshal of Poitou, and governor of Normandy, who died at the battle of Montlhery on the 16th of July, 1465.”","sentences":[{"en":"“This simple stone covers Pierre de Breze, lord of Varenne and of Brissac, grand marshal of Poitou, and governor of Normandy, who died at the battle of Montlhery on the 16th of July, 1465.”","zh":"“这块石头底下，埋着彼埃尔·德·勃雷泽，法奈纳和布里萨克的领主、普瓦图大元帅和诺曼底总督，一四六五年七月十六日，死于孟来里之役。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon bit his lips, fuming.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon bit his lips, fuming.","zh":"赖昂咬嘴唇，跺脚。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And on the right, this gentleman all encased in iron, on the prancing horse, is his grandson, Louis de Breze, lord of Breval and of Montchauvet, Count de Maulevrier, Baron de Mauny, chamberlain to the king, Knight of the Order, and also governor of Normandy; died on the 23rd of July, 1531—a Sunday, as the inscription specifies; and below, this figure, about to descend into the tomb, portrays the same person. It is not possible, is it, to see a more perfect representation of annihilation?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And on the right, this gentleman all encased in iron, on the prancing horse, is his grandson, Louis de Breze, lord of Breval and of Montchauvet, Count de Maulevrier, Baron de Mauny, chamberlain to the king, Knight of the Order, and also governor of Normandy; died on the 23rd of July, 1531—a Sunday, as the inscription specifies; and below, this figure, about to descend into the tomb, portrays the same person.","zh":"“右面这位贵人，全身铠甲，骑着一匹前腿举起的马，是他的孙子路易·德·勃雷泽，勃雷瓦尔和蒙绍韦的领主、莫勒弗里耶伯爵、莫尼男爵、御前大臣、功勋骑士，也是诺曼底总督，碑文写着：死于一五三一年七月二十三日，一个星期天；下面雕的这个男子正要葬入墓穴，面孔和他本人一模一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is not possible, is it, to see a more perfect representation of annihilation?”","zh":"死人雕塑得这样逼真，世上找不出第二份了，是不是？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary put up her eyeglasses. Léon, motionless, looked at her, no longer even attempting to speak a single word, to make a gesture, so discouraged was he at this two-fold obstinacy of gossip and indifference.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary put up her eyeglasses.","zh":"包法利夫人举起单柄眼镜细看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Léon, motionless, looked at her, no longer even attempting to speak a single word, to make a gesture, so discouraged was he at this two-fold obstinacy of gossip and indifference.","zh":"赖昂看见一个口若悬河，一个冷若冰霜，执意作对，觉得心灰意懒，呆呆望着她，话也懒得说，手势也懒得做了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The everlasting guide went on—","sentences":[{"en":"The everlasting guide went on—","zh":"絮絮叨叨的向导继续下去：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Near him, this kneeling woman who weeps is his spouse, Diane de Poitiers, Countess de Breze, Duchess de Valentinois, born in 1499, died in 1566, and to the left, the one with the child is the Holy Virgin. Now turn to this side; here are the tombs of the Ambroise. They were both cardinals and archbishops of Rouen. That one was minister under Louis XII. He did a great deal for the cathedral. In his will he left thirty thousand gold crowns for the poor.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Near him, this kneeling woman who weeps is his spouse, Diane de Poitiers, Countess de Breze, Duchess de Valentinois, born in 1499, died in 1566, and to the left, the one with the child is the Holy Virgin.","zh":"“旁边这个女人，跪在地上哭，是他的太太狄安娜·德·普瓦蒂埃，勃雷泽伯爵夫人、瓦朗蒂诺公爵夫人，生于一四九九年，死于一五六六年。左边抱孩子的这个女人，是圣母娘娘。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now turn to this side; here are the tombs of the Ambroise.","zh":"请看这边：这儿就是昂布瓦斯家的坟墓。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were both cardinals and archbishops of Rouen.","zh":"这两位是鲁昂的红衣主教和大主教。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That one was minister under Louis XII.","zh":"那一位是国王路易十二的一位大臣。他给了礼拜堂许多好处。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He did a great deal for the cathedral.","zh":"那一位是国王路易十二的一位大臣。他给了礼拜堂许多好处。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In his will he left thirty thousand gold crowns for the poor.”","zh":"他在遗嘱里给穷人留下三万金埃居。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And without stopping, still talking, he pushed them into a chapel full of balustrades, some put away, and disclosed a kind of block that certainly might once have been an ill-made statue.","sentences":[{"en":"And without stopping, still talking, he pushed them into a chapel full of balustrades, some put away, and disclosed a kind of block that certainly might once have been an ill-made statue.","zh":"他娓娓道来，一刻不停，又把他们带到一间堆放栏杆的偏殿，挪开几个栏杆，露出一块笨重东西，很可能是一座雕坏了的石像。他深深叹一口气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Truly,” he said with a groan, “it adorned the tomb of Richard Coeur de Lion, King of England and Duke of Normandy. It was the Calvinists, sir, who reduced it to this condition. They had buried it for spite in the earth, under the episcopal seat of Monsignor. See! this is the door by which Monsignor passes to his house. Let us pass on quickly to see the gargoyle windows.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Truly,” he said with a groan, “it adorned the tomb of Richard Coeur de Lion, King of England and Duke of Normandy.","zh":"“这原是装饰英国国王和诺曼底公爵‘狮心’理查 的陵墓的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the Calvinists, sir, who reduced it to this condition.","zh":"先生，都是加尔文信徒把它毁成这个样子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They had buried it for spite in the earth, under the episcopal seat of Monsignor.","zh":"他们不安好心，把它埋在大主教宝座底下的地里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"See! this is the door by which Monsignor passes to his house.","zh":"看，大主教回府，就走这座门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let us pass on quickly to see the gargoyle windows.”","zh":"我们来看看画有毒蟒的花玻璃窗 。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Léon hastily took some silver from his pocket and seized Emma’s arm. The beadle stood dumfounded, not able to understand this untimely munificence when there were still so many things for the stranger to see. So calling him back, he cried—","sentences":[{"en":"But Léon hastily took some silver from his pocket and seized Emma’s arm.","zh":"但是赖昂连忙从衣袋摸出一块银币丢给他，抓住爱玛的胳膊就走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The beadle stood dumfounded, not able to understand this untimely munificence when there were still so many things for the stranger to see.","zh":"守卫目瞪口呆，不明白为什么提早赏钱，因为还有许多东西值得外乡人观光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So calling him back, he cried—","zh":"所以他喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sir! sir! The steeple! the steeple!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sir! sir!","zh":"“喂！先生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The steeple! the steeple!”","zh":"钟塔！钟塔！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, thank you!” said Léon.","sentences":[{"en":"“No, thank you!” said Léon.","zh":"赖昂道：“不看啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are wrong, sir! It is four hundred and forty feet high, nine less than the great pyramid of Egypt. It is all cast; it—”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are wrong, sir!","zh":"“先生不该不看！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is four hundred and forty feet high, nine less than the great pyramid of Egypt.","zh":"钟塔有四百四十尺高，比埃及的大金字塔才低九尺。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is all cast; it—”","zh":"整个儿是铁铸成的，钟塔…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon was fleeing, for it seemed to him that his love, that for nearly two hours now had become petrified in the church like the stones, would vanish like a vapour through that sort of truncated funnel, of oblong cage, of open chimney that rises so grotesquely from the cathedral like the extravagant attempt of some fantastic brazier.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon was fleeing, for it seemed to him that his love, that for nearly two hours now had become petrified in the church like the stones, would vanish like a vapour through that sort of truncated funnel, of oblong cage, of open chimney that rises so grotesquely from the cathedral like the extravagant attempt of some fantastic brazier.","zh":"赖昂拔脚就跑；因为两小时以来，他觉得他的爱情，眼看在教堂就要变成石头，现在又要化成一道烟，穿过那个半截管子似的、长方鸟笼似的、有孔烟筒似的东西（居然不嫌难看，架在礼拜堂上头，倒像一个异想天开的锅匠，在做什么古怪试验） ，不知去向。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But where are we going?” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“But where are we going?” she said.","zh":"“我们去什么地方啊？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Making no answer, he walked on with a rapid step; and Madame Bovary was already, dipping her finger in the holy water when behind them they heard a panting breath interrupted by the regular sound of a cane. Léon turned back.","sentences":[{"en":"Making no answer, he walked on with a rapid step; and Madame Bovary was already, dipping her finger in the holy water when behind them they heard a panting breath interrupted by the regular sound of a cane.","zh":"他不回答，继续快步走去；包法利夫人已经把手指泡在圣水里了，听见背后气喘吁吁，夹杂手杖顿地的有规律的响声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Léon turned back.","zh":"赖昂转回身子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sir!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sir!”","zh":"“先生！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What is it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What is it?”","zh":"“什么事？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he recognised the beadle, holding under his arms and balancing against his stomach some twenty large sewn volumes. They were works “which treated of the cathedral.”","sentences":[{"en":"And he recognised the beadle, holding under his arms and balancing against his stomach some twenty large sewn volumes.","zh":"原来是守卫，胳膊底下抱着二十来本装订好的大书，顶住肚皮，怕掉下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were works “which treated of the cathedral.”","zh":"全是“关于礼拜堂”的著述。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Idiot!” growled Léon, rushing out of the church.","sentences":[{"en":"“Idiot!” growled Léon, rushing out of the church.","zh":"赖昂跑出教堂，咕哝道：“浑蛋！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A lad was playing about the close.","sentences":[{"en":"A lad was playing about the close.","zh":"一个野孩子在广场玩耍。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Go and get me a cab!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go and get me a cab!”","zh":"“去给我找一辆马车来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The child bounded off like a ball by the Rue Quatre-Vents; then they were alone a few minutes, face to face, and a little embarrassed.","sentences":[{"en":"The child bounded off like a ball by the Rue Quatre-Vents; then they were alone a few minutes, face to face, and a little embarrassed.","zh":"小孩子像皮球一样去了四风街；于是他们面对面，单独在一起待了几分钟，全有一点窘。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! Léon! Really—I don’t know—if I ought,” she whispered. Then with a more serious air, “Do you know, it is very improper—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Léon!","zh":"赖昂…真的…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Really—I don’t know—if I ought,” she whispered.","zh":"我不知道…我该不该…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then with a more serious air, “Do you know, it is very improper—”","zh":"”先是娇声娇气，故作媚态，接着就又摆出一副庄重的神气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How so?” replied the clerk. “It is done at Paris.”","sentences":[{"en":"“How so?” replied the clerk.","zh":"“这不合适，您知道吗？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“It is done at Paris.”","zh":"文书反驳道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And that, as an irresistible argument, decided her.","sentences":[{"en":"And that, as an irresistible argument, decided her.","zh":"“有什么不合适？巴黎就这样做！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Still the cab did not come. Léon was afraid she might go back into the church. At last the cab appeared.","sentences":[{"en":"Still the cab did not come.","zh":"这句话仿佛无可驳辩的论据，说服了她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Léon was afraid she might go back into the church.","zh":"马车还不见来。赖昂直怕她再进教堂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last the cab appeared.","zh":"马车终于来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“At all events, go out by the north porch,” cried the beadle, who was left alone on the threshold, “so as to see the Resurrection, the Last Judgment, Paradise, King David, and the Condemned in Hell-flames.”","sentences":[{"en":"“At all events, go out by the north porch,” cried the beadle, who was left alone on the threshold, “so as to see the Resurrection, the Last Judgment, Paradise, King David, and the Condemned in Hell-flames.”","zh":"守卫站在门槛，朝他们喊道：“再怎么也该走北门出去！看看《复活》《最后的审判》《天堂》《大卫王》和《火焰地狱的罪人》。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where to, sir?” asked the coachman.","sentences":[{"en":"“Where to, sir?” asked the coachman.","zh":"车夫问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where you like,” said Léon, forcing Emma into the cab.","sentences":[{"en":"“Where you like,” said Léon, forcing Emma into the cab.","zh":"“先生去什么地方？”赖昂推爱玛上车道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the lumbering machine set out. It went down the Rue Grand-Pont, crossed the Place des Arts, the Quai Napoleon, the Pont Neuf, and stopped short before the statue of Pierre Corneille.","sentences":[{"en":"And the lumbering machine set out.","zh":"“随你！”笨重的马车出发了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It went down the Rue Grand-Pont, crossed the Place des Arts, the Quai Napoleon, the Pont Neuf, and stopped short before the statue of Pierre Corneille.","zh":"它下了大桥街，走过艺术广场、拿破仑码头、新桥，在彼埃尔·高乃依的雕像前面停住 。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Go on,” cried a voice that came from within.","sentences":[{"en":"“Go on,” cried a voice that came from within.","zh":"车里发出声音道：“往前走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The cab went on again, and as soon as it reached the Carrefour Lafayette, set off down-hill, and entered the station at a gallop.","sentences":[{"en":"The cab went on again, and as soon as it reached the Carrefour Lafayette, set off down-hill, and entered the station at a gallop.","zh":"马车又走动，穿过拉法夷特十字路口，走下坡路，一直奔到车站 。同一声音喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, straight on!” cried the same voice.","sentences":[{"en":"“No, straight on!” cried the same voice.","zh":"“别停，一直走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The cab came out by the gate, and soon having reached the Cours, trotted quietly beneath the elm-trees. The coachman wiped his brow, put his leather hat between his knees, and drove his carriage beyond the side alley by the meadow to the margin of the waters.","sentences":[{"en":"The cab came out by the gate, and soon having reached the Cours, trotted quietly beneath the elm-trees.","zh":"马车走出栅栏门，不久来到林荫道，在夹道的大榆树之间，放慢了速度。车夫擦擦额头，皮帽夹在腿当中，把车赶到道旁水边的草地上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The coachman wiped his brow, put his leather hat between his knees, and drove his carriage beyond the side alley by the meadow to the margin of the waters.","zh":"马车走出栅栏门，不久来到林荫道，在夹道的大榆树之间，放慢了速度。车夫擦擦额头，皮帽夹在腿当中，把车赶到道旁水边的草地上。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"It went along by the river, along the towing-path paved with sharp pebbles, and for a long while in the direction of Oyssel, beyond the isles.","sentences":[{"en":"It went along by the river, along the towing-path paved with sharp pebbles, and for a long while in the direction of Oyssel, beyond the isles.","zh":"它沿河走着碎石铺的纤道，从瓦塞尔往前走了许久，一直走过河心那些小岛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But suddenly it turned with a dash across Quatremares, Sotteville, La Grande-Chaussee, the Rue d’Elbeuf, and made its third halt in front of the Jardin des Plantes.","sentences":[{"en":"But suddenly it turned with a dash across Quatremares, Sotteville, La Grande-Chaussee, the Rue d’Elbeuf, and made its third halt in front of the Jardin des Plantes.","zh":"但是它猛然加快速度，驰过四塘、扫特镇、大坝、艾耳伯夫街，在植物园前第三次停了下来。声音越发暴躁了，喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Get on, will you?” cried the voice more furiously.","sentences":[{"en":"“Get on, will you?” cried the voice more furiously.","zh":"“走啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And at once resuming its course, it passed by Saint-Sever, by the Quai’des Curandiers, the Quai aux Meules, once more over the bridge, by the Place du Champ de Mars, and behind the hospital gardens, where old men in black coats were walking in the sun along the terrace all green with ivy. It went up the Boulevard Bouvreuil, along the Boulevard Cauchoise, then the whole of Mont-Riboudet to the Deville hills.","sentences":[{"en":"And at once resuming its course, it passed by Saint-Sever, by the Quai’des Curandiers, the Quai aux Meules, once more over the bridge, by the Place du Champ de Mars, and behind the hospital gardens, where old men in black coats were walking in the sun along the terrace all green with ivy.","zh":"它立刻就又上路，走过圣赛韦尔、居朗迪耶码头、磨石码头，再一次过桥，走过阅兵场，来到广济医院的花园后面：花园里有些穿黑上衣的老年人，沿着绿藤蔓生的平台，在太阳地散步。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It went up the Boulevard Bouvreuil, along the Boulevard Cauchoise, then the whole of Mont-Riboudet to the Deville hills.","zh":"它走上布弗勒依路，驰过苟什瓦兹，兜了一圈里布代岭，一直来到德镇岭。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It came back; and then, without any fixed plan or direction, wandered about at hazard. The cab was seen at Saint-Pol, at Lescure, at Mont Gargan, at La Rougue-Marc and Place du Gaillardbois; in the Rue Maladrerie, Rue Dinanderie, before Saint-Romain, Saint-Vivien, Saint-Maclou, Saint-Nicaise—in front of the Customs, at the “Vieille Tour,” the “Trois Pipes,” and the Monumental Cemetery. From time to time the coachman, on his box cast despairing eyes at the public-houses. He could not understand what furious desire for locomotion urged these individuals never to wish to stop. He tried to now and then, and at once exclamations of anger burst forth behind him. Then he lashed his perspiring jades afresh, but indifferent to their jolting, running up against things here and there, not caring if he did, demoralised, and almost weeping with thirst, fatigue, and depression.","sentences":[{"en":"It came back; and then, without any fixed plan or direction, wandered about at hazard.","zh":"它往回走，漫无目的，由着马走。有人在圣波、莱斯居尔、嘉尔刚岭、红塘和快活林见到它；有人在癞病医院街、铜器街、圣罗曼教堂、圣维维安教堂、圣马克卢教堂、圣尼凯斯教堂前面、海关前面、下老三塔、三烟斗和纪念公墓见到它。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The cab was seen at Saint-Pol, at Lescure, at Mont Gargan, at La Rougue-Marc and Place du Gaillardbois; in the Rue Maladrerie, Rue Dinanderie, before Saint-Romain, Saint-Vivien, Saint-Maclou, Saint-Nicaise—in front of the Customs, at the “Vieille Tour,” the “Trois Pipes,” and the Monumental Cemetery.","zh":"它往回走，漫无目的，由着马走。有人在圣波、莱斯居尔、嘉尔刚岭、红塘和快活林见到它；有人在癞病医院街、铜器街、圣罗曼教堂、圣维维安教堂、圣马克卢教堂、圣尼凯斯教堂前面、海关前面、下老三塔、三烟斗和纪念公墓见到它。","scope":"group"},{"en":"From time to time the coachman, on his box cast despairing eyes at the public-houses.","zh":"车夫坐在车座上，不时望望小酒馆，懊恼万状。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He could not understand what furious desire for locomotion urged these individuals never to wish to stop.","zh":"他不明白，这两位乘客犯了什么转运迷，不要车停。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He tried to now and then, and at once exclamations of anger burst forth behind him.","zh":"他有时候想停停看，马上听见背后狂吼怒叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he lashed his perspiring jades afresh, but indifferent to their jolting, running up against things here and there, not caring if he did, demoralised, and almost weeping with thirst, fatigue, and depression.","zh":"于是他不管两匹驽马流不流汗，拼命抽打，也不管颠不颠，心不在焉，由着它东一撞，西一撞，垂头丧气，又渴，又倦，又愁，简直要哭出来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And on the harbour, in the midst of the drays and casks, and in the streets, at the corners, the good folk opened large wonder-stricken eyes at this sight, so extraordinary in the provinces, a cab with blinds drawn, and which appeared thus constantly shut more closely than a tomb, and tossing about like a vessel.","sentences":[{"en":"And on the harbour, in the midst of the drays and casks, and in the streets, at the corners, the good folk opened large wonder-stricken eyes at this sight, so extraordinary in the provinces, a cab with blinds drawn, and which appeared thus constantly shut more closely than a tomb, and tossing about like a vessel.","zh":"码头上，货车和大车之间，街头，拐角，市民睁大眼睛，望着这个内地罕见的怪物发愣：一辆马车，放下窗帘，一直这样行走，比坟墓还严密，像船一样摇晃。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Once in the middle of the day, in the open country, just as the sun beat most fiercely against the old plated lanterns, a bared hand passed beneath the small blinds of yellow canvas, and threw out some scraps of paper that scattered in the wind, and farther off lighted like white butterflies on a field of red clover all in bloom.","sentences":[{"en":"Once in the middle of the day, in the open country, just as the sun beat most fiercely against the old plated lanterns, a bared hand passed beneath the small blinds of yellow canvas, and threw out some scraps of paper that scattered in the wind, and farther off lighted like white butterflies on a field of red clover all in bloom.","zh":"有一回，时当中午，马车来到田野，太阳直射着包银的旧灯，就见黄布小帘探出一只光手，扔掉一些碎纸片，随风散开，远远飘下，好像白蝴蝶落在绚烂一片的红三叶田上一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At about six o’clock the carriage stopped in a back street of the Beauvoisine Quarter, and a woman got out, who walked with her veil down, and without turning her head.","sentences":[{"en":"At about six o’clock the carriage stopped in a back street of the Beauvoisine Quarter, and a woman got out, who walked with her veil down, and without turning her head.","zh":"最后，六点钟左右，马车停在芳邻区一条小巷，下来一位妇人，面网下垂，头也不回，照直走了下去。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-2","part":3,"n":2,"title":"Part III · Chapter 2","titleZh":"下卷 · 2","paragraphs":[{"en":"On reaching the inn, Madame Bovary was surprised not to see the diligence. Hivert, who had waited for her fifty-three minutes, had at last started.","sentences":[{"en":"On reaching the inn, Madame Bovary was surprised not to see the diligence.","zh":"包法利夫人回到客店，一看驿车不在，大吃一惊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hivert, who had waited for her fifty-three minutes, had at last started.","zh":"伊韦尔等她等了五十三分钟，不见她来，只好出发了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Yet nothing forced her to go; but she had given her word that she would return that same evening. Moreover, Charles expected her, and in her heart she felt already that cowardly docility that is for some women at once the chastisement and atonement of adultery.","sentences":[{"en":"Yet nothing forced her to go; but she had given her word that she would return that same evening.","zh":"其实，她也不是非回去不可；不过她有话在先，说她当天黄昏到家。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Moreover, Charles expected her, and in her heart she felt already that cowardly docility that is for some women at once the chastisement and atonement of adultery.","zh":"再说，查理在等她回来；她心里已经起了那种唯命是从的胆怯感：对于许多妇女，犯了奸淫，这种感觉就是惩罚，也就是所付的代价。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She packed her box quickly, paid her bill, took a cab in the yard, hurrying on the driver, urging him on, every moment inquiring about the time and the miles traversed. He succeeded in catching up the “Hirondelle” as it neared the first houses of Quincampoix.","sentences":[{"en":"She packed her box quickly, paid her bill, took a cab in the yard, hurrying on the driver, urging him on, every moment inquiring about the time and the miles traversed.","zh":"她连忙收拾行李、算账，到院子雇了一辆轻便马车，又是催促，又是鼓励，时时刻刻向马夫打听：用了多少时间，走了多少里路，终于在甘冈普瓦入口，追上燕子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He succeeded in catching up the “Hirondelle” as it neared the first houses of Quincampoix.","zh":"她连忙收拾行李、算账，到院子雇了一辆轻便马车，又是催促，又是鼓励，时时刻刻向马夫打听：用了多少时间，走了多少里路，终于在甘冈普瓦入口，追上燕子。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Hardly was she seated in her corner than she closed her eyes, and opened them at the foot of the hill, when from afar she recognised Félicité, who was on the lookout in front of the farrier’s shop. Hivert pulled in his horses and, the servant, climbing up to the window, said mysteriously—","sentences":[{"en":"Hardly was she seated in her corner than she closed her eyes, and opened them at the foot of the hill, when from afar she recognised Félicité, who was on the lookout in front of the farrier’s shop.","zh":"她一坐到她的角落，立刻闭上眼睛，直到挨近岭下，才又睁开。她远远望见全福，站在马掌铺前瞭望。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hivert pulled in his horses and, the servant, climbing up to the window, said mysteriously—","zh":"伊韦尔把马勒住，女用人攀着窗口，鬼鬼祟祟道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Madame, you must go at once to Monsieur Homais. It’s for something important.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Madame, you must go at once to Monsieur Homais.","zh":"“太太，您得马上去郝麦先生家一趟，有急事。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s for something important.”","zh":"“太太，您得马上去郝麦先生家一趟，有急事。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The village was silent as usual. At the corner of the streets were small pink heaps that smoked in the air, for this was the time for jam-making, and everyone at Yonville prepared his supply on the same day. But in front of the chemist’s shop one might admire a far larger heap, and that surpassed the others with the superiority that a laboratory must have over ordinary stores, a general need over individual fancy.","sentences":[{"en":"The village was silent as usual.","zh":"村子静静落落，和平日一样。街角有一堆堆玫瑰色的东西冒热气，因为眼下到了做果酱的时期，永镇家家在同一天酿造。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At the corner of the streets were small pink heaps that smoked in the air, for this was the time for jam-making, and everyone at Yonville prepared his supply on the same day.","zh":"村子静静落落，和平日一样。街角有一堆堆玫瑰色的东西冒热气，因为眼下到了做果酱的时期，永镇家家在同一天酿造。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But in front of the chemist’s shop one might admire a far larger heap, and that surpassed the others with the superiority that a laboratory must have over ordinary stores, a general need over individual fancy.","zh":"大家称道药房前面那一堆，不但分外大，也特别考究，药房理当压倒寻常人家，公众需要应该重于个人爱好。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She went in. The large arm-chair was upset, and even the “Fanal de Rouen” lay on the ground, outspread between two pestles. She pushed open the lobby door, and in the middle of the kitchen, amid brown jars full of picked currants, of powdered sugar and lump sugar, of the scales on the table, and of the pans on the fire, she saw all the Homais, small and large, with aprons reaching to their chins, and with forks in their hands. Justin was standing up with bowed head, and the chemist was screaming—","sentences":[{"en":"She went in.","zh":"她走进药房，只见大扶手椅翻倒，连《鲁昂烽火》也扔在地上，摊在两只杵当中。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The large arm-chair was upset, and even the “Fanal de Rouen” lay on the ground, outspread between two pestles.","zh":"她走进药房，只见大扶手椅翻倒，连《鲁昂烽火》也扔在地上，摊在两只杵当中。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She pushed open the lobby door, and in the middle of the kitchen, amid brown jars full of picked currants, of powdered sugar and lump sugar, of the scales on the table, and of the pans on the fire, she saw all the Homais, small and large, with aprons reaching to their chins, and with forks in their hands.","zh":"她推开过道门，望见郝麦一家大小，全在厨房，个个拿着叉，系围裙系到下巴，周围有砂糖、方糖、装满一颗一颗红醋栗的棕色坛子，桌上有天平，火上有锅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Justin was standing up with bowed head, and the chemist was screaming—","zh":"朱斯丹站着，耷拉着头，药剂师冲他嚷道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Who told you to go and fetch it in the Capharnaum.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Who told you to go and fetch it in the Capharnaum.”","zh":"“谁叫你到堆置间找它的？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What is it? What is the matter?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What is it?","zh":"“怎么啦？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What is the matter?”","zh":"出了什么事？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What is it?” replied the druggist. “We are making preserves; they are simmering; but they were about to boil over, because there is too much juice, and I ordered another pan. Then he, from indolence, from laziness, went and took, hanging on its nail in my laboratory, the key of the Capharnaum.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What is it?” replied the druggist.","zh":"药剂师回答道：“什么事？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“We are making preserves; they are simmering; but they were about to boil over, because there is too much juice, and I ordered another pan.","zh":"我们在做果酱，已经煮上了，可是汤太多，眼看要流到外头，我叫他另取一只锅来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he, from indolence, from laziness, went and took, hanging on its nail in my laboratory, the key of the Capharnaum.”","zh":"也不知他是不起劲，还是偷懒，走到我的实验室，把挂在钉子上的堆置间的钥匙拿了下来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was thus the druggist called a small room under the leads, full of the utensils and the goods of his trade. He often spent long hours there alone, labelling, decanting, and doing up again; and he looked upon it not as a simple store, but as a veritable sanctuary, whence there afterwards issued, elaborated by his hands, all sorts of pills, boluses, infusions, lotions, and potions, that would bear far and wide his celebrity. No one in the world set foot there, and he respected it so, that he swept it himself. Finally, if the pharmacy, open to all comers, was the spot where he displayed his pride, the Capharnaum was the refuge where, egoistically concentrating himself, Homais delighted in the exercise of his predilections, so that Justin’s thoughtlessness seemed to him a monstrous piece of irreverence, and, redder than the currants, he repeated—","sentences":[{"en":"It was thus the druggist called a small room under the leads, full of the utensils and the goods of his trade.","zh":"药剂师这样称呼顶楼的一间小屋，里头全是他那一行的器皿和商品。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He often spent long hours there alone, labelling, decanting, and doing up again; and he looked upon it not as a simple store, but as a veritable sanctuary, whence there afterwards issued, elaborated by his hands, all sorts of pills, boluses, infusions, lotions, and potions, that would bear far and wide his celebrity.","zh":"他常常一个人待在里头，一待就是几小时，不是贴标签、倒瓶子，就是捆扎包装。他不单单把它看成一间堆房，而是看成一间真正的内殿，出去的全是他亲手制成的形形色色的药品：丹药、丸药、煎药、洗药和水药，到四乡宣扬他的大名。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No one in the world set foot there, and he respected it so, that he swept it himself.","zh":"谁也不许进去；他尊重它尊重到了这般地步，亲自打扫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Finally, if the pharmacy, open to all comers, was the spot where he displayed his pride, the Capharnaum was the refuge where, egoistically concentrating himself, Homais delighted in the exercise of his predilections, so that Justin’s thoughtlessness seemed to him a monstrous piece of irreverence, and, redder than the currants, he repeated—","zh":"总之，药房店面是他满足自尊心的地方，向公众开放；堆置间却是郝麦的隐居所，他在这里聚精会神，玩味个人所好。所以朱斯丹的轻举妄动，在他看来便是大不敬。他的脸涨得比红醋栗还红，反复道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, from the Capharnaum! The key that locks up the acids and caustic alkalies! To go and get a spare pan! a pan with a lid! and that I shall perhaps never use! Everything is of importance in the delicate operations of our art! But, devil take it! one must make distinctions, and not employ for almost domestic purposes that which is meant for pharmaceutical! It is as if one were to carve a fowl with a scalpel; as if a magistrate—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, from the Capharnaum!","zh":"“是啊，堆置间！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The key that locks up the acids and caustic alkalies!","zh":"锁着酸类和苛性碱类的钥匙！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To go and get a spare pan! a pan with a lid! and that I shall perhaps never use!","zh":"去取一只备而不用的锅！一只有盖的锅！一只我自己也许永远不用的锅！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everything is of importance in the delicate operations of our art!","zh":"我们医学实验，奥妙入微，样样重要！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But, devil take it! one must make distinctions, and not employ for almost domestic purposes that which is meant for pharmaceutical!","zh":"家伙！一定要分清界限！用于制药的器皿绝不能用在家务上！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is as if one were to carve a fowl with a scalpel; as if a magistrate—”","zh":"这就像拿手术刀宰填肥的仔鸡一样，就像当官的…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Now be calm,” said Madame Homais.","sentences":[{"en":"“Now be calm,” said Madame Homais.","zh":"郝麦夫人道：“你先平平气！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And Athalie, pulling at his coat, cried “Papa! papa!”","sentences":[{"en":"And Athalie, pulling at his coat, cried “Papa! papa!”","zh":"同时阿塔莉揪住他的大衣：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, let me alone,” went on the druggist “let me alone, hang it! My word! One might as well set up for a grocer. That’s it! go it! respect nothing! break, smash, let loose the leeches, burn the mallow-paste, pickle the gherkins in the window jars, tear up the bandages!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, let me alone,” went on the druggist “let me alone, hang it!","zh":"“爸爸！爸爸！”药剂师继续发作道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My word!","zh":"“不！走开！走开！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One might as well set up for a grocer.","zh":"好，来吧！什么也不尊重！砸吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That’s it! go it! respect nothing! break, smash, let loose the leeches, burn the mallow-paste, pickle the gherkins in the window jars, tear up the bandages!”","zh":"烧掉蜀葵！药瓶腌黄瓜！绷带撕烂了！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I thought you had—” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“I thought you had—” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛道：“不过您有话…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Presently! Do you know to what you exposed yourself? Didn’t you see anything in the corner, on the left, on the third shelf? Speak, answer, articulate something.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Presently!","zh":"“等一等！——你知道你惹了多大乱子？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Do you know to what you exposed yourself?","zh":"“等一等！——你知道你惹了多大乱子？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Didn’t you see anything in the corner, on the left, on the third shelf?","zh":"你就没有看见，左边犄角，第三槅架的东西？说呀，回话呀，哼唧一句说出来呀！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Speak, answer, articulate something.”","zh":"你就没有看见，左边犄角，第三槅架的东西？说呀，回话呀，哼唧一句说出来呀！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I—don’t—know,” stammered the young fellow.","sentences":[{"en":"“I—don’t—know,” stammered the young fellow.","zh":"年轻伙计结结巴巴道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! you don’t know! Well, then, I do know! You saw a bottle of blue glass, sealed with yellow wax, that contains a white powder, on which I have even written ‘Dangerous!’ And do you know what is in it? Arsenic! And you go and touch it! You take a pan that was next to it!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! you don’t know!","zh":"“我不…知道。”“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, then, I do know!","zh":"你不知道。好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You saw a bottle of blue glass, sealed with yellow wax, that contains a white powder, on which I have even written ‘Dangerous!’","zh":"我呀，我知道！你没有看见一只蓝玻璃瓶子 ，黄蜡封口，里头装着白粉，我亲自在外头写着：危险！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And do you know what is in it?","zh":"你知道里头是什么吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Arsenic!","zh":"砒霜！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And you go and touch it!","zh":"你去碰这个！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You take a pan that was next to it!”","zh":"到旁边去拿一只锅！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Next to it!” cried Madame Homais, clasping her hands. “Arsenic! You might have poisoned us all.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Next to it!” cried Madame Homais, clasping her hands.","zh":"郝麦夫人合起双手，嚷道：“旁边！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Arsenic!","zh":"砒霜？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You might have poisoned us all.”","zh":"你简直要把我们统统毒死！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the children began howling as if they already had frightful pains in their entrails.","sentences":[{"en":"And the children began howling as if they already had frightful pains in their entrails.","zh":"孩子们又是哭，又是叫，好像他们已经感到肠子剧疼。药剂师继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Or poison a patient!” continued the druggist. “Do you want to see me in the prisoner’s dock with criminals, in a court of justice? To see me dragged to the scaffold? Don’t you know what care I take in managing things, although I am so thoroughly used to it? Often I am horrified myself when I think of my responsibility; for the Government persecutes us, and the absurd legislation that rules us is a veritable Damocles’ sword over our heads.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Or poison a patient!” continued the druggist.","zh":"“要不然就是毒死病人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do you want to see me in the prisoner’s dock with criminals, in a court of justice?","zh":"你莫非是希望我站到刑事庭的罪犯席？看我上断头台？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To see me dragged to the scaffold?","zh":"难道你不知道，我轻车熟路，照样得小心操作？想到我的责任，我都胆战心惊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Don’t you know what care I take in managing things, although I am so thoroughly used to it?","zh":"难道你不知道，我轻车熟路，照样得小心操作？想到我的责任，我都胆战心惊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Often I am horrified myself when I think of my responsibility; for the Government persecutes us, and the absurd legislation that rules us is a veritable Damocles’ sword over our heads.”","zh":"因为政府迫害我们、管制我们的可笑法规活活就是悬在达摩克利斯头上的利剑 ，挂在我们的头上！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma no longer dreamed of asking what they wanted her for, and the druggist went on in breathless phrases—","sentences":[{"en":"Emma no longer dreamed of asking what they wanted her for, and the druggist went on in breathless phrases—","zh":"爱玛不再指望问清要她来做什么了，药剂师又是喘，又是急，一句紧跟一句道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That is your return for all the kindness we have shown you! That is how you recompense me for the really paternal care that I lavish on you! For without me where would you be? What would you be doing? Who provides you with food, education, clothes, and all the means of figuring one day with honour in the ranks of society? But you must pull hard at the oar if you’re to do that, and get, as, people say, callosities upon your hands. Fabricando fit faber, age quod agis.”","sentences":[{"en":"“That is your return for all the kindness we have shown you!","zh":"“这就是你报答我的恩德！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That is how you recompense me for the really paternal care that I lavish on you!","zh":"我像父亲一样照料你，这就是你的酬谢！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For without me where would you be?","zh":"要不是我，你在什么地方？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What would you be doing?","zh":"你做什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who provides you with food, education, clothes, and all the means of figuring one day with honour in the ranks of society?","zh":"谁供你饮食、教育、衣着？谁供你种种便利，将来体体面面，置身于社会之中？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But you must pull hard at the oar if you’re to do that, and get, as, people say, callosities upon your hands.","zh":"可是为了这个呀，你就该吃苦耐劳，像人家说的，手上长膙子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Fabricando fit faber, age quod agis.”","zh":"Fabricando fit faber， age quod agis. ”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was so exasperated he quoted Latin. He would have quoted Chinese or Greenlandish had he known those two languages, for he was in one of those crises in which the whole soul shows indistinctly what it contains, like the ocean, which, in the storm, opens itself from the seaweeds on its shores down to the sands of its abysses.","sentences":[{"en":"He was so exasperated he quoted Latin.","zh":"他在气头上，引证起拉丁文来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He would have quoted Chinese or Greenlandish had he known those two languages, for he was in one of those crises in which the whole soul shows indistinctly what it contains, like the ocean, which, in the storm, opens itself from the seaweeds on its shores down to the sands of its abysses.","zh":"他要是懂得中文和格陵兰文的话，他也会引证的。因为他已经无法控制自己，心中所有，倾囊吐出，就像大洋一样，遇到狂风暴雨，不但露出岸边的马尾藻，就连海底的沙砾也露出来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he went on—","sentences":[{"en":"And he went on—","zh":"他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I am beginning to repent terribly of having taken you up! I should certainly have done better to have left you to rot in your poverty and the dirt in which you were born. Oh, you’ll never be fit for anything but to herd animals with horns! You have no aptitude for science! You hardly know how to stick on a label! And there you are, dwelling with me snug as a parson, living in clover, taking your ease!”","sentences":[{"en":"“I am beginning to repent terribly of having taken you up!","zh":"“我可真后悔不该照管你！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I should certainly have done better to have left you to rot in your poverty and the dirt in which you were born.","zh":"我顶好还是让你像从前一样，回到你生长的脏地方，过穷日子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, you’ll never be fit for anything but to herd animals with horns!","zh":"你呀，一辈子不会有出息，顶多也就是放放牛！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You have no aptitude for science!","zh":"你没有一点点才分学科学！你连贴标签也干不好！","scope":"group"},{"en":"You hardly know how to stick on a label!","zh":"你没有一点点才分学科学！你连贴标签也干不好！","scope":"group"},{"en":"And there you are, dwelling with me snug as a parson, living in clover, taking your ease!”","zh":"你待在我家，养尊处优，倒像一个教士、一只大肥公鸡，光会吃喝玩乐！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Emma, turning to Madame Homais, “I was told to come here—”","sentences":[{"en":"But Emma, turning to Madame Homais, “I was told to come here—”","zh":"但是爱玛不耐烦等下去，转向郝麦夫人道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, dear me!” interrupted the good woman, with a sad air, “how am I to tell you? It is a misfortune!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, dear me!” interrupted the good woman, with a sad air, “how am I to tell you?","zh":"“有人叫我来…”这位太太神色悲伤，打断道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"It is a misfortune!”","zh":"“有人叫我来…”这位太太神色悲伤，打断道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She could not finish, the druggist was thundering—“Empty it! Clean it! Take it back! Be quick!”","sentences":[{"en":"She could not finish, the druggist was thundering—“Empty it!","zh":"“啊！我的上帝！我怎么对您说才好？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Clean it!","zh":"“啊！我的上帝！我怎么对您说才好？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Take it back!","zh":"是一个坏消息！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Be quick!”","zh":"是一个坏消息！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And seizing Justin by the collar of his blouse, he shook a book out of his pocket. The lad stooped, but Homais was the quicker, and, having picked up the volume, contemplated it with staring eyes and open mouth.","sentences":[{"en":"And seizing Justin by the collar of his blouse, he shook a book out of his pocket.","zh":"话没有说完，药剂师就打断她，吼声震天道：“倒空它！洗干净！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The lad stooped, but Homais was the quicker, and, having picked up the volume, contemplated it with staring eyes and open mouth.","zh":"拿走！快呀！”他抓住朱斯丹的衣领，摇了两摇，就见衣袋掉出一本书来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“CONJUGAL—LOVE!” he said, slowly separating the two words. “Ah! very good! very good! very pretty! And illustrations! Oh, this is too much!”","sentences":[{"en":"“CONJUGAL—LOVE!” he said, slowly separating the two words.","zh":"年轻人弯下腰拾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Ah! very good! very good! very pretty!","zh":"郝麦比他快，抢过来一看，眼睛瞪圆，下巴也耷拉下来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And illustrations!","zh":"郝麦比他快，抢过来一看，眼睛瞪圆，下巴也耷拉下来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Oh, this is too much!”","zh":"郝麦比他快，抢过来一看，眼睛瞪圆，下巴也耷拉下来。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Madame Homais came forward.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Homais came forward.","zh":"他分成两截，慢慢读道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, do not touch it!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, do not touch it!”","zh":"“《夫妇…之爱》！啊！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The children wanted to look at the pictures.","sentences":[{"en":"The children wanted to look at the pictures.","zh":"郝麦夫人走过来看。“不！别动！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Leave the room,” he said imperiously; and they went out.","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave the room,” he said imperiously; and they went out.","zh":"孩子们想看看图。他气冲冲道：“出去！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"First he walked up and down with the open volume in his hand, rolling his eyes, choking, tumid, apoplectic. Then he came straight to his pupil, and, planting himself in front of him with crossed arms—","sentences":[{"en":"First he walked up and down with the open volume in his hand, rolling his eyes, choking, tumid, apoplectic.","zh":"他们出去了。他起初迈开大步，来回乱走，手捏着翻开的书，转动眼睛，怒气填胸，说不出话，像要中风。随后，他一直走到学徒跟前，交叉胳膊，当前一站：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he came straight to his pupil, and, planting himself in front of him with crossed arms—","zh":"他们出去了。他起初迈开大步，来回乱走，手捏着翻开的书，转动眼睛，怒气填胸，说不出话，像要中风。随后，他一直走到学徒跟前，交叉胳膊，当前一站：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Have you every vice, then, little wretch? Take care! you are on a downward path. Did not you reflect that this infamous book might fall in the hands of my children, kindle a spark in their minds, tarnish the purity of Athalie, corrupt Napoleon. He is already formed like a man. Are you quite sure, anyhow, that they have not read it? Can you certify to me—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Have you every vice, then, little wretch?","zh":"“小坏蛋，原来你样样恶习都有啊？当心滚进泥坑！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Take care! you are on a downward path.","zh":"“小坏蛋，原来你样样恶习都有啊？当心滚进泥坑！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Did not you reflect that this infamous book might fall in the hands of my children, kindle a spark in their minds, tarnish the purity of Athalie, corrupt Napoleon.","zh":"难道你想也不想，这本坏书会落到我的孩子的手里，刺激他们的头脑，损伤阿塔莉的纯洁，败坏拿破仑！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He is already formed like a man.","zh":"眼看他就要长成大人了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Are you quite sure, anyhow, that they have not read it?","zh":"至少，你拿得稳，他们没有看到？你能不能保证…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Can you certify to me—”","zh":"”爱玛问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But really, sir,” said Emma, “you wished to tell me—”","sentences":[{"en":"“But really, sir,” said Emma, “you wished to tell me—”","zh":"“不过，先生，到底您有没有话同我讲？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah, yes! madame. Your father-in-law is dead.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah, yes! madame.","zh":"“我有话讲，夫人…你的公公死了！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Your father-in-law is dead.”","zh":"“我有话讲，夫人…你的公公死了！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"In fact, Monsieur Bovary senior had expired the evening before suddenly from an attack of apoplexy as he got up from table, and by way of greater precaution, on account of Emma’s sensibility, Charles had begged Homais to break the horrible news to her gradually. Homais had thought over his speech; he had rounded, polished it, made it rhythmical; it was a masterpiece of prudence and transitions, of subtle turns and delicacy; but anger had got the better of rhetoric.","sentences":[{"en":"In fact, Monsieur Bovary senior had expired the evening before suddenly from an attack of apoplexy as he got up from table, and by way of greater precaution, on account of Emma’s sensibility, Charles had begged Homais to break the horrible news to her gradually.","zh":"老包法利饭后中风，的确在前天去世了；查理过分担心爱玛感情重，央求郝麦先生，把这可怕的消息婉转通知她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais had thought over his speech; he had rounded, polished it, made it rhythmical; it was a masterpiece of prudence and transitions, of subtle turns and delicacy; but anger had got the better of rhetoric.","zh":"他说什么，他也仔细想过；他要语句工整、精致、富有节奏，成为一篇审慎、委婉、措词讲究而细腻的杰作；但是愤怒战胜了修辞学。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma, giving up all chance of hearing any details, left the pharmacy; for Monsieur Homais had taken up the thread of his vituperations. However, he was growing calmer, and was now grumbling in a paternal tone whilst he fanned himself with his skull-cap.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, giving up all chance of hearing any details, left the pharmacy; for Monsieur Homais had taken up the thread of his vituperations.","zh":"爱玛一看听不到详情，便离开了药房；因为郝麦先生又数落起来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"However, he was growing calmer, and was now grumbling in a paternal tone whilst he fanned himself with his skull-cap.","zh":"不过他现在平下气来，一面拿他的希腊小帽扇风，一面用严父的口吻唧咕道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is not that I entirely disapprove of the work. Its author was a doctor! There are certain scientific points in it that it is not ill a man should know, and I would even venture to say that a man must know. But later—later! At any rate, not till you are man yourself and your temperament is formed.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is not that I entirely disapprove of the work.","zh":"“并非我完全不赞成这本书！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Its author was a doctor!","zh":"作者是医生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There are certain scientific points in it that it is not ill a man should know, and I would even venture to say that a man must know.","zh":"里头有些科学知识，知道一下也是好的；我敢说，一个人也应当知道。不过，迟些日子，迟些日子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But later—later!","zh":"起码也要等你自己长大成人，性格稳定下来才成。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"At any rate, not till you are man yourself and your temperament is formed.”","zh":"起码也要等你自己长大成人，性格稳定下来才成。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"When Emma knocked at the door. Charles, who was waiting for her, came forward with open arms and said to her with tears in his voice—","sentences":[{"en":"When Emma knocked at the door.","zh":"查理在等爱玛回来，听见门环响，走上前去，伸出胳膊，两眼含泪，向她道：“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles, who was waiting for her, came forward with open arms and said to her with tears in his voice—","zh":"我亲爱的朋友…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! my dear!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! my dear!”","zh":"他慢悠悠躬下身子吻她。但是她碰到他的嘴唇，想起另一个男子，她摩挲着脸，颤抖起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he bent over her gently to kiss her. But at the contact of his lips the memory of the other seized her, and she passed her hand over her face shuddering.","sentences":[{"en":"And he bent over her gently to kiss her.","zh":"她回答他道：“是啊，我知道了…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But at the contact of his lips the memory of the other seized her, and she passed her hand over her face shuddering.","zh":"知道了…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But she made answer, “Yes, I know, I know!”","sentences":[{"en":"But she made answer, “Yes, I know, I know!”","zh":"他掏出母亲的来信给她看：信上说起丧事，没有一点假惺惺哀恸的意思。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He showed her the letter in which his mother told the event without any sentimental hypocrisy. She only regretted her husband had not received the consolations of religion, as he had died at Daudeville, in the street, at the door of a cafe after a patriotic dinner with some ex-officers.","sentences":[{"en":"He showed her the letter in which his mother told the event without any sentimental hypocrisy.","zh":"他掏出母亲的来信给她看：信上说起丧事，没有一点假惺惺哀恸的意思。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She only regretted her husband had not received the consolations of religion, as he had died at Daudeville, in the street, at the door of a cafe after a patriotic dinner with some ex-officers.","zh":"他和几位旧日袍泽，在杜德镇一家咖啡馆举行爱国聚餐，过后倒在门口街上死了。她唯一的遗憾是他没有接受宗教救助。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma gave him back the letter; then at dinner, for appearance’s sake, she affected a certain repugnance. But as he urged her to try, she resolutely began eating, while Charles opposite her sat motionless in a dejected attitude.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma gave him back the letter; then at dinner, for appearance’s sake, she affected a certain repugnance.","zh":"爱玛拿信还给他。过后开上晚饭，她照顾人情，装出不要吃的样子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But as he urged her to try, she resolutely began eating, while Charles opposite her sat motionless in a dejected attitude.","zh":"但是经不起他再三劝，她只好不管三七二十一，吃起来了，而查理坐在对面，没有动静，显出一副哀恸的姿势。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Now and then he raised his head and gave her a long look full of distress. Once he sighed, “I should have liked to see him again!”","sentences":[{"en":"Now and then he raised his head and gave her a long look full of distress.","zh":"他不时仰起脸来看她。一看就是老半天，目光充满悲伤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once he sighed, “I should have liked to see him again!”","zh":"他有一回叹气道：“我真想再见他一面！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was silent. At last, understanding that she must say something, “How old was your father?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"She was silent.","zh":"她不做声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, understanding that she must say something, “How old was your father?” she asked.","zh":"她最后明白自己非说话不可了，就问：“你父亲多大年纪？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Fifty-eight.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Fifty-eight.”","zh":"“五十八岁！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!”","zh":"“啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And that was all.","sentences":[{"en":"And that was all.","zh":"她没有话了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A quarter of an hour after he added, “My poor mother! what will become of her now?”","sentences":[{"en":"A quarter of an hour after he added, “My poor mother! what will become of her now?”","zh":"他过了一刻钟又道：“我可怜的母亲？她如今怎么办？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She made a gesture that signified she did not know. Seeing her so taciturn, Charles imagined her much affected, and forced himself to say nothing, not to reawaken this sorrow which moved him. And, shaking off his own—","sentences":[{"en":"She made a gesture that signified she did not know.","zh":"她做了一个不知道的手势。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Seeing her so taciturn, Charles imagined her much affected, and forced himself to say nothing, not to reawaken this sorrow which moved him.","zh":"查理看她默默无言，以为她在难过，唯恐加深她的痛苦，压制自己不再说下去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And, shaking off his own—","zh":"他于是丢开自己的痛苦，问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Did you enjoy yourself yesterday?” he asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“Did you enjoy yourself yesterday?” he asked.","zh":"“你昨天玩得开心吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“开心。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When the cloth was removed, Bovary did not rise, nor did Emma; and as she looked at him, the monotony of the spectacle drove little by little all pity from her heart. He seemed to her paltry, weak, a cipher—in a word, a poor thing in every way. How to get rid of him? What an interminable evening! Something stupefying like the fumes of opium seized her.","sentences":[{"en":"When the cloth was removed, Bovary did not rise, nor did Emma; and as she looked at him, the monotony of the spectacle drove little by little all pity from her heart.","zh":"桌布撤掉，包法利没有起身，爱玛也没有；她常看他这种单调的形象，怜悯心也逐渐消失了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He seemed to her paltry, weak, a cipher—in a word, a poor thing in every way.","zh":"她嫌他寒酸、软弱、无能，总之，是一个地道可怜虫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How to get rid of him?","zh":"怎样才能摆脱他？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What an interminable evening!","zh":"夜晚过得真慢！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Something stupefying like the fumes of opium seized her.","zh":"有什么东西像鸦片气味一样，使她昏昏沉沉。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They heard in the passage the sharp noise of a wooden leg on the boards. It was Hippolyte bringing back Emma’s luggage. In order to put it down he described painfully a quarter of a circle with his stump.","sentences":[{"en":"They heard in the passage the sharp noise of a wooden leg on the boards.","zh":"他们听见一根棍子在门道顿地板响。原来是伊玻立特给太太送行李来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was Hippolyte bringing back Emma’s luggage.","zh":"他们听见一根棍子在门道顿地板响。原来是伊玻立特给太太送行李来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In order to put it down he described painfully a quarter of a circle with his stump.","zh":"他用假腿好不容易画了一个四分之一的圆圈，才把行李放下，满头的红头发在淌汗。她望着可怜人想道：“他已经忘得一干二净！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“He doesn’t even remember any more about it,” she thought, looking at the poor devil, whose coarse red hair was wet with perspiration.","sentences":[{"en":"“He doesn’t even remember any more about it,” she thought, looking at the poor devil, whose coarse red hair was wet with perspiration.","zh":"他用假腿好不容易画了一个四分之一的圆圈，才把行李放下，满头的红头发在淌汗。她望着可怜人想道：“他已经忘得一干二净！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Bovary was searching at the bottom of his purse for a centime, and without appearing to understand all there was of humiliation for him in the mere presence of this man, who stood there like a personified reproach to his incurable incapacity.","sentences":[{"en":"Bovary was searching at the bottom of his purse for a centime, and without appearing to understand all there was of humiliation for him in the mere presence of this man, who stood there like a personified reproach to his incurable incapacity.","zh":"包法利在钱包尽底摸一个小钱；伊玻立特站在眼前，如同当面谴责他的不可挽救的无能一样，可是他似乎并不感到耻辱，望着壁炉上赖昂的紫罗兰道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Hallo! you’ve a pretty bouquet,” he said, noticing Léon’s violets on the chimney.","sentences":[{"en":"“Hallo! you’ve a pretty bouquet,” he said, noticing Léon’s violets on the chimney.","zh":"“你这把花真好看！”她信口答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes,” she replied indifferently; “it’s a bouquet I bought just now from a beggar.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” she replied indifferently; “it’s a bouquet I bought just now from a beggar.”","zh":"“是啊；是我方才买的…一个女叫花子卖给我的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles picked up the flowers, and freshening his eyes, red with tears, against them, smelt them delicately.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles picked up the flowers, and freshening his eyes, red with tears, against them, smelt them delicately.","zh":"查理拿起紫罗兰，小心在意，闻着香气，哭红了的眼睛也凑到上头。她赶快抢过来，放到水杯里。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She took them quickly from his hand and put them in a glass of water.","sentences":[{"en":"She took them quickly from his hand and put them in a glass of water.","zh":"查理拿起紫罗兰，小心在意，闻着香气，哭红了的眼睛也凑到上头。她赶快抢过来，放到水杯里。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The next day Madame Bovary senior arrived. She and her son wept much. Emma, on the pretext of giving orders, disappeared. The following day they had a talk over the mourning. They went and sat down with their workboxes by the waterside under the arbour.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day Madame Bovary senior arrived.","zh":"第二天，包法利老太太来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She and her son wept much.","zh":"她和儿子哭了许久。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma, on the pretext of giving orders, disappeared.","zh":"爱玛借口安排家务，走开了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The following day they had a talk over the mourning.","zh":"过了这天，他们也该一道谈谈丧事了，就带了女红盒子，坐到水边花棚底下。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They went and sat down with their workboxes by the waterside under the arbour.","zh":"过了这天，他们也该一道谈谈丧事了，就带了女红盒子，坐到水边花棚底下。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles was thinking of his father, and was surprised to feel so much affection for this man, whom till then he had thought he cared little about. Madame Bovary senior was thinking of her husband. The worst days of the past seemed enviable to her. All was forgotten beneath the instinctive regret of such a long habit, and from time to time whilst she sewed, a big tear rolled along her nose and hung suspended there a moment. Emma was thinking that it was scarcely forty-eight hours since they had been together, far from the world, all in a frenzy of joy, and not having eyes enough to gaze upon each other. She tried to recall the slightest details of that past day. But the presence of her husband and mother-in-law worried her. She would have liked to hear nothing, to see nothing, so as not to disturb the meditation on her love, that, do what she would, became lost in external sensations.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles was thinking of his father, and was surprised to feel so much affection for this man, whom till then he had thought he cared little about.","zh":"查理直在想念父亲；他惊讶自己对父亲感情会这样重，先前他以为自己爱他，也不过极其平常罢了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Bovary senior was thinking of her husband.","zh":"包法利老太太也在想丈夫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The worst days of the past seemed enviable to her.","zh":"往常最坏的年月，也像值得留恋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All was forgotten beneath the instinctive regret of such a long habit, and from time to time whilst she sewed, a big tear rolled along her nose and hung suspended there a moment.","zh":"日子久了，成了习惯，自然而然，也就没有怨尤，只有怀念了。针缝来缝去，可是不时有一大颗眼泪，顺着鼻梁往下流，有一时还在半道停住不流。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma was thinking that it was scarcely forty-eight hours since they had been together, far from the world, all in a frenzy of joy, and not having eyes enough to gaze upon each other.","zh":"爱玛却在想：不到四十八小时以前，没有别人，只有他们单独待在一起，心荡神驰，恨不得多生几只眼睛对看才好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She tried to recall the slightest details of that past day.","zh":"这一天追是追不回来了，她试着回忆当天的细枝末节。不过婆婆和丈夫的存在拘束她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But the presence of her husband and mother-in-law worried her.","zh":"这一天追是追不回来了，她试着回忆当天的细枝末节。不过婆婆和丈夫的存在拘束她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She would have liked to hear nothing, to see nothing, so as not to disturb the meditation on her love, that, do what she would, became lost in external sensations.","zh":"她希望什么也听不见，什么也看不见，没有东西扰乱自己回味爱情，因为尽管集中力量，沉思冥想，外来的感觉眼看就要把它挤掉了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was unpicking the lining of a dress, and the strips were scattered around her. Madame Bovary senior was plying her scissor without looking up, and Charles, in his list slippers and his old brown surtout that he used as a dressing-gown, sat with both hands in his pockets, and did not speak either; near them Berthe, in a little white pinafore, was raking sand in the walks with her spade. Suddenly she saw Monsieur Lheureux, the linendraper, come in through the gate.","sentences":[{"en":"She was unpicking the lining of a dress, and the strips were scattered around her.","zh":"她在拆一件袍子夹里，周围全是零幅、断线；老太太低着眼睛剪裁；查理穿着他的布头拖鞋和他当便服用的棕色旧大衣，两只手插在衣袋，也不言语；白尔特系着小白围裙，拿起她的小铲，在旁边小径刮沙子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Madame Bovary senior was plying her scissor without looking up, and Charles, in his list slippers and his old brown surtout that he used as a dressing-gown, sat with both hands in his pockets, and did not speak either; near them Berthe, in a little white pinafore, was raking sand in the walks with her spade.","zh":"她在拆一件袍子夹里，周围全是零幅、断线；老太太低着眼睛剪裁；查理穿着他的布头拖鞋和他当便服用的棕色旧大衣，两只手插在衣袋，也不言语；白尔特系着小白围裙，拿起她的小铲，在旁边小径刮沙子。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Suddenly she saw Monsieur Lheureux, the linendraper, come in through the gate.","zh":"忽然就见布商勒乐先生走进了栅栏门。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He came to offer his services “under the sad circumstances.” Emma answered that she thought she could do without. The shopkeeper was not to be beaten.","sentences":[{"en":"He came to offer his services “under the sad circumstances.”","zh":"他们遭逢大故，他效劳来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma answered that she thought she could do without.","zh":"爱玛回答，她相信不要添置东西。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The shopkeeper was not to be beaten.","zh":"商人并不认输，说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I beg your pardon,” he said, “but I should like to have a private talk with you.” Then in a low voice, “It’s about that affair—you know.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I beg your pardon,” he said, “but I should like to have a private talk with you.”","zh":"“对不住，我有两句话，希望私下谈谈。”接着就放低声音：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then in a low voice, “It’s about that affair—you know.”","zh":"“关于那件事…您知道？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles crimsoned to his ears. “Oh, yes! certainly.” And in his confusion, turning to his wife, “Couldn’t you, my darling?”","sentences":[{"en":"Charles crimsoned to his ears.","zh":"查理的脸一直红到耳梢。“啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Oh, yes! certainly.”","zh":"查理的脸一直红到耳梢。“啊！","scope":"group"},{"en":"And in his confusion, turning to his wife, “Couldn’t you, my darling?”","zh":"对…当然。”他心慌意乱，转向太太道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She seemed to understand him, for she rose; and Charles said to his mother, “It is nothing particular. No doubt, some household trifle.” He did not want her to know the story of the bill, fearing her reproaches.","sentences":[{"en":"She seemed to understand him, for she rose; and Charles said to his mother, “It is nothing particular.","zh":"我亲爱的？”她似乎领会他的意思，因为她站起来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No doubt, some household trifle.”","zh":"查理又对母亲道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He did not want her to know the story of the bill, fearing her reproaches.","zh":"“没有什么！不过是家里一些鸡毛蒜皮的事。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As soon as they were alone, Monsieur Lheureux in sufficiently clear terms began to congratulate Emma on the inheritance, then to talk of indifferent matters, of the espaliers, of the harvest, and of his own health, which was always so-so, always having ups and downs. In fact, he had to work devilish hard, although he didn’t make enough, in spite of all people said, to find butter for his bread.","sentences":[{"en":"As soon as they were alone, Monsieur Lheureux in sufficiently clear terms began to congratulate Emma on the inheritance, then to talk of indifferent matters, of the espaliers, of the harvest, and of his own health, which was always so-so, always having ups and downs.","zh":"他不愿意母亲知道借据的事，怕她训他一顿。勒乐先生一见没有别人，就单刀直入，恭喜爱玛有遗产承继，接着谈了一些不相干的事：墙边果木呐，收成呐，还有他本人的健康，总是“不好不歹”，“好上一阵，坏上一阵”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In fact, he had to work devilish hard, although he didn’t make enough, in spite of all people said, to find butter for his bread.","zh":"说实在的，话由人说，可是他卖足了力气，什么也赚不到手，就连抹面包的牛油也吃不起。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma let him talk on. She had bored herself so prodigiously the last two days.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma let him talk on.","zh":"爱玛尽他讲去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had bored herself so prodigiously the last two days.","zh":"两天以来，她正闷得要死！他继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And so you’re quite well again?” he went on. “Ma foi! I saw your husband in a sad state. He’s a good fellow, though we did have a little misunderstanding.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And so you’re quite well again?” he went on.","zh":"“您现在大好啦？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Ma foi!","zh":"真的，您丈夫当时那份焦急，我可看见啦！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I saw your husband in a sad state.","zh":"真的，您丈夫当时那份焦急，我可看见啦！","scope":"group"},{"en":"He’s a good fellow, though we did have a little misunderstanding.”","zh":"他是一个好人，别看我们之间有点纠葛。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She asked what misunderstanding, for Charles had said nothing of the dispute about the goods supplied to her.","sentences":[{"en":"She asked what misunderstanding, for Charles had said nothing of the dispute about the goods supplied to her.","zh":"她问什么纠葛，因为查理瞒她，没有讲起关于货物的争执。勒乐道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, you know well enough,” cried Lheureux. “It was about your little fancies—the travelling trunks.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, you know well enough,” cried Lheureux.","zh":"“您再明白不过！就是您一时高兴，想要的那些旅行箱子啊。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It was about your little fancies—the travelling trunks.”","zh":"“您再明白不过！就是您一时高兴，想要的那些旅行箱子啊。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He had drawn his hat over his eyes, and, with his hands behind his back, smiling and whistling, he looked straight at her in an unbearable manner. Did he suspect anything?","sentences":[{"en":"He had drawn his hat over his eyes, and, with his hands behind his back, smiling and whistling, he looked straight at her in an unbearable manner.","zh":"帽子压着眼睛，一双手搭在背后，他笑吟吟的，吹着口哨，做出一副令人难堪的神气，盯住她看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Did he suspect anything?","zh":"他疑心什么不成？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was lost in all kinds of apprehensions. At last, however, he went on—","sentences":[{"en":"She was lost in all kinds of apprehensions.","zh":"她神不守舍，非常杌陧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, however, he went on—","zh":"可是临了他却改口道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We made it up, all the same, and I’ve come again to propose another arrangement.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We made it up, all the same, and I’ve come again to propose another arrangement.”","zh":"“我们又谈妥啦。我来是有一个新安排和他商量。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This was to renew the bill Bovary had signed. The doctor, of course, would do as he pleased; he was not to trouble himself, especially just now, when he would have a lot of worry. “And he would do better to give it over to someone else—to you, for example. With a power of attorney it could be easily managed, and then we (you and I) would have our little business transactions together.”","sentences":[{"en":"This was to renew the bill Bovary had signed.","zh":"他指的是延长包法利立的借据。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The doctor, of course, would do as he pleased; he was not to trouble himself, especially just now, when he would have a lot of worry.","zh":"当然，先生可以按自己的心意行事；不过这样一来，他就不必在这方面操心了，特别是现在，他手上有许多事要办。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“And he would do better to give it over to someone else—to you, for example.","zh":"“其实，他最好把事情委托给别人料理，比如说，让您来料理；您有了代理人权力，方便多了，我们也好在一起打些小交道…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"With a power of attorney it could be easily managed, and then we (you and I) would have our little business transactions together.”","zh":"“其实，他最好把事情委托给别人料理，比如说，让您来料理；您有了代理人权力，方便多了，我们也好在一起打些小交道…”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She did not understand. He was silent. Then, passing to his trade, Lheureux declared that madame must require something. He would send her a black barege, twelve yards, just enough to make a gown.","sentences":[{"en":"She did not understand.","zh":"她听不懂他的意思，偏偏他又不明说。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was silent.","zh":"她听不懂他的意思，偏偏他又不明说。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, passing to his trade, Lheureux declared that madame must require something.","zh":"勒乐随后谈到生意，就说：太太不买他点东西也不成。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He would send her a black barege, twelve yards, just enough to make a gown.","zh":"他回头给她送一块青哔叽来，十二米长，正好做一件袍子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The one you’ve on is good enough for the house, but you want another for calls. I saw that the very moment that I came in. I’ve the eye of an American!”","sentences":[{"en":"“The one you’ve on is good enough for the house, but you want another for calls.","zh":"“您身上这件只好家里穿穿。出门做客，您该另来一件才好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I saw that the very moment that I came in.","zh":"我一进门，头一眼就看出来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve the eye of an American!”","zh":"我的眼睛尖着呐。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He did not send the stuff; he brought it. Then he came again to measure it; he came again on other pretexts, always trying to make himself agreeable, useful, “enfeoffing himself,” as Homais would have said, and always dropping some hint to Emma about the power of attorney. He never mentioned the bill; she did not think of it. Charles, at the beginning of her convalescence, had certainly said something about it to her, but so many emotions had passed through her head that she no longer remembered it. Besides, she took care not to talk of any money questions. Madame Bovary seemed surprised at this, and attributed the change in her ways to the religious sentiments she had contracted during her illness.","sentences":[{"en":"He did not send the stuff; he brought it.","zh":"他不是派人送衣料，而是亲自送来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he came again to measure it; he came again on other pretexts, always trying to make himself agreeable, useful, “enfeoffing himself,” as Homais would have said, and always dropping some hint to Emma about the power of attorney.","zh":"过后他又带尺来量；又找别的借口来，每回都竭力做出热心、殷勤的样子，或者学郝麦的说法，趋奉唯谨的样子，总在爱玛耳边来上一言半语，提醒代理人权力问题。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He never mentioned the bill; she did not think of it.","zh":"过后他又带尺来量；又找别的借口来，每回都竭力做出热心、殷勤的样子，或者学郝麦的说法，趋奉唯谨的样子，总在爱玛耳边来上一言半语，提醒代理人权力问题。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles, at the beginning of her convalescence, had certainly said something about it to her, but so many emotions had passed through her head that she no longer remembered it.","zh":"他绝口不提借据。她也不往这上头想；查理在她复元初期，露出两句口风，可是她一脑子事由，早不记得了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, she took care not to talk of any money questions.","zh":"再说，银钱事项，她有意避而不谈；老太太想不到她会这样不关心，把她的转变看成她病中信奉宗教的结果。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Madame Bovary seemed surprised at this, and attributed the change in her ways to the religious sentiments she had contracted during her illness.","zh":"再说，银钱事项，她有意避而不谈；老太太想不到她会这样不关心，把她的转变看成她病中信奉宗教的结果。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But as soon as she was gone, Emma greatly astounded Bovary by her practical good sense. It would be necessary to make inquiries, to look into mortgages, and see if there were any occasion for a sale by auction or a liquidation. She quoted technical terms casually, pronounced the grand words of order, the future, foresight, and constantly exaggerated the difficulties of settling his father’s affairs so much, that at last one day she showed him the rough draft of a power of attorney to manage and administer his business, arrange all loans, sign and endorse all bills, pay all sums, etc. She had profited by Lheureux’s lessons. Charles naively asked her where this paper came from.","sentences":[{"en":"But as soon as she was gone, Emma greatly astounded Bovary by her practical good sense.","zh":"但老太太一动身，爱玛立刻表现出她有何等清醒而实际的头脑，使包法利大为赞叹。她提出应当多方打听，验明抵押物品，看看是否需要拍卖或者清算。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It would be necessary to make inquiries, to look into mortgages, and see if there were any occasion for a sale by auction or a liquidation.","zh":"但老太太一动身，爱玛立刻表现出她有何等清醒而实际的头脑，使包法利大为赞叹。她提出应当多方打听，验明抵押物品，看看是否需要拍卖或者清算。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She quoted technical terms casually, pronounced the grand words of order, the future, foresight, and constantly exaggerated the difficulties of settling his father’s affairs so much, that at last one day she showed him the rough draft of a power of attorney to manage and administer his business, arrange all loans, sign and endorse all bills, pay all sums, etc. She had profited by Lheureux’s lessons.","zh":"她随口引用专门名词，说起“程序”“未来”“预见”这些辉煌的字眼，不断夸大承继的困难，最后有一天，她掏出一张委托书样本给他看，上面写着“经管代理他的事务，处理一切债款，签发所有票据，偿付全部银钱”等等。勒乐的指示，她算充分利用了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles naively asked her where this paper came from.","zh":"查理天真烂漫，问她这张纸是哪儿来的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Monsieur Guillaumin”; and with the utmost coolness she added, “I don’t trust him overmuch. Notaries have such a bad reputation. Perhaps we ought to consult—we only know—no one.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Monsieur Guillaumin”; and with the utmost coolness she added, “I don’t trust him overmuch.","zh":"“居由曼先生那边。”她显得异常镇静，继续道：“我不太信任他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Notaries have such a bad reputation.","zh":"这些公证人，没有好名声！也许应该请教…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps we ought to consult—we only know—no one.”","zh":"我们就只认识…唉！谁也不认识！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Unless Léon—” replied Charles, who was reflecting. But it was difficult to explain matters by letter. Then she offered to make the journey, but he thanked her. She insisted. It was quite a contest of mutual consideration. At last she cried with affected waywardness—","sentences":[{"en":"“Unless Léon—” replied Charles, who was reflecting.","zh":"查理沉吟了一下，回答道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But it was difficult to explain matters by letter.","zh":"“除非是赖昂…”不过写信不抵事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she offered to make the journey, but he thanked her.","zh":"她提议她走一趟。他不要她去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She insisted.","zh":"她一定要去。两个人抢着表示好意。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was quite a contest of mutual consideration.","zh":"她一定要去。两个人抢着表示好意。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last she cried with affected waywardness—","zh":"她最后用假惺惺的反抗口吻嚷道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, I will go!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, I will go!”","zh":"“得，我求你啦，我一定去。”他吻着她的额头道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“How good you are!” he said, kissing her forehead.","sentences":[{"en":"“How good you are!” he said, kissing her forehead.","zh":"“得，我求你啦，我一定去。”他吻着她的额头道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The next morning she set out in the “Hirondelle” to go to Rouen to consult Monsieur Léon, and she stayed there three days.","sentences":[{"en":"The next morning she set out in the “Hirondelle” to go to Rouen to consult Monsieur Léon, and she stayed there three days.","zh":"“你真好！”第二天，她乘燕子去了鲁昂，向赖昂先生请教；她一住就是三天。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-3","part":3,"n":3,"title":"Part III · Chapter 3","titleZh":"下卷 · 3","paragraphs":[{"en":"They were three full, exquisite days—a true honeymoon. They were at the Hotel-de-Boulogne, on the harbour; and they lived there, with drawn blinds and closed doors, with flowers on the floor, and iced syrups were brought them early in the morning.","sentences":[{"en":"They were three full, exquisite days—a true honeymoon.","zh":"这三天才是真正的蜜月，妙趣无穷且又丰富多彩。他们住在靠码头的布洛涅旅馆，待在里头，闭了窗板，锁上了门，地上撒遍鲜花，冰镇果露清早就送过来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were at the Hotel-de-Boulogne, on the harbour; and they lived there, with drawn blinds and closed doors, with flowers on the floor, and iced syrups were brought them early in the morning.","zh":"这三天才是真正的蜜月，妙趣无穷且又丰富多彩。他们住在靠码头的布洛涅旅馆，待在里头，闭了窗板，锁上了门，地上撒遍鲜花，冰镇果露清早就送过来。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Towards evening they took a covered boat and went to dine on one of the islands. It was the time when one hears by the side of the dockyard the caulking-mallets sounding against the hull of vessels. The smoke of the tar rose up between the trees; there were large fatty drops on the water, undulating in the purple colour of the sun, like floating plaques of Florentine bronze.","sentences":[{"en":"Towards evening they took a covered boat and went to dine on one of the islands.","zh":"将近黄昏，他们乘一只遮蔽严密的游艇，到一座小岛用晚饭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the time when one hears by the side of the dockyard the caulking-mallets sounding against the hull of vessels.","zh":"沿着船坞，这里正好听见一片嵌抹船缝的工人敲打船身的响声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The smoke of the tar rose up between the trees; there were large fatty drops on the water, undulating in the purple colour of the sun, like floating plaques of Florentine bronze.","zh":"柏油烟在树木间袅袅上升；大片的油渍在绯红的夕阳照耀下起伏荡漾，好像佛罗伦萨的古铜奖章在漂浮一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They rowed down in the midst of moored boats, whose long oblique cables grazed lightly against the bottom of the boat. The din of the town gradually grew distant; the rolling of carriages, the tumult of voices, the yelping of dogs on the decks of vessels. She took off her bonnet, and they landed on their island.","sentences":[{"en":"They rowed down in the midst of moored boats, whose long oblique cables grazed lightly against the bottom of the boat.","zh":"他们从停泊的船只间穿过，游艇上部轻轻擦过长而又斜的缆索。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The din of the town gradually grew distant; the rolling of carriages, the tumult of voices, the yelping of dogs on the decks of vessels.","zh":"城里的喧嚣——大车的滚动、语声的嘈杂、甲板上的吠声，不知不觉就听不真切了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She took off her bonnet, and they landed on their island.","zh":"她摘下帽子，他们在小岛上岸。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They sat down in the low-ceilinged room of a tavern, at whose door hung black nets. They ate fried smelts, cream and cherries. They lay down upon the grass; they kissed behind the poplars; and they would fain, like two Robinsons, have lived for ever in this little place, which seemed to them in their beatitude the most magnificent on earth. It was not the first time that they had seen trees, a blue sky, meadows; that they had heard the water flowing and the wind blowing in the leaves; but, no doubt, they had never admired all this, as if Nature had not existed before, or had only begun to be beautiful since the gratification of their desires.","sentences":[{"en":"They sat down in the low-ceilinged room of a tavern, at whose door hung black nets.","zh":"他们坐在一家酒馆的低厅里，门口挂着黑网。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They ate fried smelts, cream and cherries.","zh":"他们吃煎胡瓜鱼、奶酪和樱桃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They lay down upon the grass; they kissed behind the poplars; and they would fain, like two Robinsons, have lived for ever in this little place, which seemed to them in their beatitude the most magnificent on earth.","zh":"他们睡在草地，躲到白杨树底下吻抱。他们未尝不希望一生一世住在这小地方，就像两个鲁宾孙一样，心旷神怡，觉得这里福天洞地，不啻世外桃源。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was not the first time that they had seen trees, a blue sky, meadows; that they had heard the water flowing and the wind blowing in the leaves; but, no doubt, they had never admired all this, as if Nature had not existed before, or had only begun to be beautiful since the gratification of their desires.","zh":"他们不是头一回看见树木、蓝天、青草，也不是头一回听见水声潺潺、微风在枝叶之间吹拂，不过毫无疑问，他们从来没有加以赞赏，好像大自然先前并不存在，或者只在他们的欲望满足之后，才开始美丽一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At night they returned. The boat glided along the shores of the islands. They sat at the bottom, both hidden by the shade, in silence. The square oars rang in the iron thwarts, and, in the stillness, seemed to mark time, like the beating of a metronome, while at the stern the rudder that trailed behind never ceased its gentle splash against the water.","sentences":[{"en":"At night they returned.","zh":"他们夜晚回去，沿着岛屿行驶，两个人待在船心，躲在阴影里，不言不语。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The boat glided along the shores of the islands.","zh":"他们夜晚回去，沿着岛屿行驶，两个人待在船心，躲在阴影里，不言不语。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They sat at the bottom, both hidden by the shade, in silence.","zh":"他们夜晚回去，沿着岛屿行驶，两个人待在船心，躲在阴影里，不言不语。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The square oars rang in the iron thwarts, and, in the stillness, seemed to mark time, like the beating of a metronome, while at the stern the rudder that trailed behind never ceased its gentle splash against the water.","zh":"方桨在铁榫中间吱嘎响动，静寂中仿佛节奏计的敲打，同时舵在船尾，无休无止，轻轻拍着水响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Once the moon rose; they did not fail to make fine phrases, finding the orb melancholy and full of poetry. She even began to sing—","sentences":[{"en":"Once the moon rose; they did not fail to make fine phrases, finding the orb melancholy and full of poetry.","zh":"有一回，月亮出来，他们不免搜索词句，加以形容，觉得充满诗意，悒郁感人；她甚至唱着：","scope":"group"},{"en":"She even began to sing—","zh":"有一回，月亮出来，他们不免搜索词句，加以形容，觉得充满诗意，悒郁感人；她甚至唱着：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“One night, do you remember, we were sailing,” etc.","sentences":[{"en":"“One night, do you remember, we were sailing,” etc.","zh":"你可记得，有一夜，我们摇船…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her musical but weak voice died away along the waves, and the winds carried off the trills that Léon heard pass like the flapping of wings about him.","sentences":[{"en":"Her musical but weak voice died away along the waves, and the winds carried off the trills that Léon heard pass like the flapping of wings about him.","zh":"她柔和的歌声，散到水上，风带走颤音，从赖昂身边掠过，他听上去，仿佛翅膀扇动。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was opposite him, leaning against the partition of the shallop, through one of whose raised blinds the moon streamed in. Her black dress, whose drapery spread out like a fan, made her seem more slender, taller. Her head was raised, her hands clasped, her eyes turned towards heaven. At times the shadow of the willows hid her completely; then she reappeared suddenly, like a vision in the moonlight.","sentences":[{"en":"She was opposite him, leaning against the partition of the shallop, through one of whose raised blinds the moon streamed in.","zh":"她坐在对面，靠着板壁，月光照进一面开着的窗板。她穿一件黑袍，褶幅摊开，如开一把扇子，衬得她更苗条，更颀长。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her black dress, whose drapery spread out like a fan, made her seem more slender, taller.","zh":"她坐在对面，靠着板壁，月光照进一面开着的窗板。她穿一件黑袍，褶幅摊开，如开一把扇子，衬得她更苗条，更颀长。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her head was raised, her hands clasped, her eyes turned towards heaven.","zh":"她仰起了脸，合着手，眼睛望天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At times the shadow of the willows hid her completely; then she reappeared suddenly, like a vision in the moonlight.","zh":"有时候，柳树影子完全遮住了她，忽而她又出现了，月光融融，恍若仙子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon, on the floor by her side, found under his hand a ribbon of scarlet silk. The boatman looked at it, and at last said—","sentences":[{"en":"Léon, on the floor by her side, found under his hand a ribbon of scarlet silk.","zh":"赖昂坐在她的脚边，手底下碰到一条虞美人红的缎带。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The boatman looked at it, and at last said—","zh":"船夫端详了一会儿道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Perhaps it belongs to the party I took out the other day. A lot of jolly folk, gentlemen and ladies, with cakes, champagne, cornets—everything in style! There was one especially, a tall handsome man with small moustaches, who was that funny! And they all kept saying, ‘Now tell us something, Adolphe—Dolpe,’ I think.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Perhaps it belongs to the party I took out the other day.","zh":"“啊！这也许是前一天我摇的那群人的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A lot of jolly folk, gentlemen and ladies, with cakes, champagne, cornets—everything in style!","zh":"有男有女，一群年轻荒唐鬼，带着点心、香槟、短号，样样齐全！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was one especially, a tall handsome man with small moustaches, who was that funny!","zh":"当中有一位先生，又高，又漂亮，一溜短髭，特别逗哏！他们一来就说：‘来吧，给我们讲讲别的…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And they all kept saying, ‘Now tell us something, Adolphe—Dolpe,’ I think.”","zh":"阿道耳弗…道道耳弗…’我想他就叫这个名字吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She shivered.","sentences":[{"en":"She shivered.","zh":"她哆嗦着。赖昂挨到旁边问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are in pain?” asked Léon, coming closer to her.","sentences":[{"en":"“You are in pain?” asked Léon, coming closer to her.","zh":"“你不舒服？”“没有什么。一定是夜晚的寒气。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, it’s nothing! No doubt, it is only the night air.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it’s nothing!","zh":"老水手以为说话讨客人欢喜，就慢悠悠道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"No doubt, it is only the night air.”","zh":"老水手以为说话讨客人欢喜，就慢悠悠道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“And who doesn’t want for women, either,” softly added the sailor, thinking he was paying the stranger a compliment.","sentences":[{"en":"“And who doesn’t want for women, either,” softly added the sailor, thinking he was paying the stranger a compliment.","zh":"“看样子，有的是女人迷他。”他说过这话，唾唾手掌，又摇起桨来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, spitting on his hands, he took the oars again.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, spitting on his hands, he took the oars again.","zh":"可是好景不长，终有一别！分离是凄凉的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Yet they had to part. The adieux were sad. He was to send his letters to Mere Rollet, and she gave him such precise instructions about a double envelope that he admired greatly her amorous astuteness.","sentences":[{"en":"Yet they had to part.","zh":"他有信可以交罗莱嫂子转；她教他用两个信封装信，她的偷情打算，清楚明白，不由得他五体投地，佩服之至。她最后吻他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"The adieux were sad.","zh":"他有信可以交罗莱嫂子转；她教他用两个信封装信，她的偷情打算，清楚明白，不由得他五体投地，佩服之至。她最后吻他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was to send his letters to Mere Rollet, and she gave him such precise instructions about a double envelope that he admired greatly her amorous astuteness.","zh":"他有信可以交罗莱嫂子转；她教他用两个信封装信，她的偷情打算，清楚明白，不由得他五体投地，佩服之至。她最后吻他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“So you can assure me it is all right?” she said with her last kiss.","sentences":[{"en":"“So you can assure me it is all right?” she said with her last kiss.","zh":"“那么，你可以让我完全放心啦？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, certainly.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, certainly.”","zh":"“当然！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But why,” he thought afterwards as he came back through the streets alone, “is she so very anxious to get this power of attorney?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But why,” he thought afterwards as he came back through the streets alone, “is she so very anxious to get this power of attorney?”","zh":"他随后独自回家，在街上寻思道：“可是她为什么那样关心代理人权力这个问题啊？”","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-4","part":3,"n":4,"title":"Part III · Chapter 4","titleZh":"下卷 · 4","paragraphs":[{"en":"Léon soon put on an air of superiority before his comrades, avoided their company, and completely neglected his work.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon soon put on an air of superiority before his comrades, avoided their company, and completely neglected his work.","zh":"没有多久，赖昂在朋友面前，神气十足，不但疏远了他们，连业务也丢开不管了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He waited for her letters; he re-read them; he wrote to her. He called her to mind with all the strength of his desires and of his memories. Instead of lessening with absence, this longing to see her again grew, so that at last on Saturday morning he escaped from his office.","sentences":[{"en":"He waited for her letters; he re-read them; he wrote to her.","zh":"他盼信；信来了，他左看右看，看个没完。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He called her to mind with all the strength of his desires and of his memories.","zh":"他写回信，他用全部欲望和回忆的力量唤起她的形象。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Instead of lessening with absence, this longing to see her again grew, so that at last on Saturday morning he escaped from his office.","zh":"那种再见她的心愿，非但不因为别离淡薄，反而越来越强，他按捺不住，有一个星期六早晨，溜出了事务所。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When, from the summit of the hill, he saw in the valley below the church-spire with its tin flag swinging in the wind, he felt that delight mingled with triumphant vanity and egoistic tenderness that millionaires must experience when they come back to their native village.","sentences":[{"en":"When, from the summit of the hill, he saw in the valley below the church-spire with its tin flag swinging in the wind, he felt that delight mingled with triumphant vanity and egoistic tenderness that millionaires must experience when they come back to their native village.","zh":"他在岭上望见盆地教堂的钟楼，还有它的马口铁做的旗子，随风旋转，就像百万富翁荣归故里一样，心头涌起一股喜悦之情，里头有诗意，也有感慨。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He went rambling round her house. A light was burning in the kitchen. He watched for her shadow behind the curtains, but nothing appeared.","sentences":[{"en":"He went rambling round her house.","zh":"他围绕她的住宅徘徊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A light was burning in the kitchen.","zh":"厨房闪出一道亮光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He watched for her shadow behind the curtains, but nothing appeared.","zh":"他等候窗帘后头露出她的影子。什么也没有出来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Mere Lefrancois, when she saw him, uttered many exclamations. She thought he “had grown and was thinner,” while Artémise, on the contrary, thought him stouter and darker.","sentences":[{"en":"Mere Lefrancois, when she saw him, uttered many exclamations.","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太一看见他，就大喊大叫，觉得他“高啦，瘦啦”，不过阿尔泰蜜丝不这样想，觉得他“壮啦，黑啦”。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She thought he “had grown and was thinner,” while Artémise, on the contrary, thought him stouter and darker.","zh":"勒弗朗索瓦太太一看见他，就大喊大叫，觉得他“高啦，瘦啦”，不过阿尔泰蜜丝不这样想，觉得他“壮啦，黑啦”。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He dined in the little room as of yore, but alone, without the tax-gatherer; for Binet, tired of waiting for the “Hirondelle,” had definitely put forward his meal one hour, and now he dined punctually at five, and yet he declared usually the rickety old concern “was late.”","sentences":[{"en":"He dined in the little room as of yore, but alone, without the tax-gatherer; for Binet, tired of waiting for the “Hirondelle,” had definitely put forward his meal one hour, and now he dined punctually at five, and yet he declared usually the rickety old concern “was late.”","zh":"他像往常一样，在小间用饭，不过只有一个人，没有税务员；因为毕耐等燕子等累了，决定提前一小时用饭，如今他准五点钟用晚饭，可是照样一来就说：“破车到晚了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon, however, made up his mind, and knocked at the doctor’s door. Madame was in her room, and did not come down for a quarter of an hour. The doctor seemed delighted to see him, but he never stirred out that evening, nor all the next day.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon, however, made up his mind, and knocked at the doctor’s door.","zh":"赖昂下定决心去敲医生的门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame was in her room, and did not come down for a quarter of an hour.","zh":"太太在卧室，要一刻钟以后下楼。老爷似乎高兴又见到他；但是他一整黄昏不见动静，第二天又是一天待在家里。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The doctor seemed delighted to see him, but he never stirred out that evening, nor all the next day.","zh":"太太在卧室，要一刻钟以后下楼。老爷似乎高兴又见到他；但是他一整黄昏不见动静，第二天又是一天待在家里。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He saw her alone in the evening, very late, behind the garden in the lane; in the lane, as she had the other one! It was a stormy night, and they talked under an umbrella by lightning flashes.","sentences":[{"en":"He saw her alone in the evening, very late, behind the garden in the lane; in the lane, as she had the other one!","zh":"第二天黄昏，很晚了，他才在花园后头小巷，单独见到她——小巷，像和另一个男子一样！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a stormy night, and they talked under an umbrella by lightning flashes.","zh":"赶上雷雨，电光一闪一闪的，照着他们在一把雨伞底下谈话。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Their separation was becoming intolerable. “I would rather die!” said Emma. She was writhing in his arms, weeping. “Adieu! adieu! When shall I see you again?”","sentences":[{"en":"Their separation was becoming intolerable.","zh":"他们难割难舍，爱玛道：“宁可死！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I would rather die!” said Emma.","zh":"他们难割难舍，爱玛道：“宁可死！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was writhing in his arms, weeping.","zh":"她边哭，边在他的胸前扭来扭去：","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Adieu! adieu!","zh":"她边哭，边在他的胸前扭来扭去：","scope":"group"},{"en":"When shall I see you again?”","zh":"她边哭，边在他的胸前扭来扭去：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"They came back again to embrace once more, and it was then that she promised him to find soon, by no matter what means, a regular opportunity for seeing one another in freedom at least once a week. Emma never doubted she should be able to do this. Besides, she was full of hope. Some money was coming to her.","sentences":[{"en":"They came back again to embrace once more, and it was then that she promised him to find soon, by no matter what means, a regular opportunity for seeing one another in freedom at least once a week.","zh":"“再见！再见！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma never doubted she should be able to do this.","zh":"我什么时候再见到你啊？”他们走开了又回转来吻抱；这一回，她答应他，不拘什么方法，她不久会想出一个长远的机会，自由相会，起码也要每星期一次，爱玛相信有办法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, she was full of hope.","zh":"而且她满怀希望。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some money was coming to her.","zh":"她就要有钱了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On the strength of it she bought a pair of yellow curtains with large stripes for her room, whose cheapness Monsieur Lheureux had commended; she dreamed of getting a carpet, and Lheureux, declaring that it wasn’t “drinking the sea,” politely undertook to supply her with one. She could no longer do without his services. Twenty times a day she sent for him, and he at once put by his business without a murmur. People could not understand either why Mere Rollet breakfasted with her every day, and even paid her private visits.","sentences":[{"en":"On the strength of it she bought a pair of yellow curtains with large stripes for her room, whose cheapness Monsieur Lheureux had commended; she dreamed of getting a carpet, and Lheureux, declaring that it wasn’t “drinking the sea,” politely undertook to supply her with one.","zh":"所以她给卧室买了一对宽道道的黄窗帘，勒乐先生早就对她吹嘘便宜来着。她梦想有一条地毯，勒乐说：“这又不是月中桂。”彬彬有礼，决定帮她弄一条来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She could no longer do without his services.","zh":"他成了她的左右手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Twenty times a day she sent for him, and he at once put by his business without a murmur.","zh":"一天里头，她尽叫人找他；他听说她找，丢下手边的事，马上奔了过去，不出一句怨言。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People could not understand either why Mere Rollet breakfasted with her every day, and even paid her private visits.","zh":"大家也不明白，罗莱嫂子为什么天天在她家用午饭，甚至还私下看望她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was about this time, that is to say, the beginning of winter, that she seemed seized with great musical fervour.","sentences":[{"en":"It was about this time, that is to say, the beginning of winter, that she seemed seized with great musical fervour.","zh":"也就是在这期间，就是说，交冬前后，她对音乐似乎有了热烈感情。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One evening when Charles was listening to her, she began the same piece four times over, each time with much vexation, while he, not noticing any difference, cried—","sentences":[{"en":"One evening when Charles was listening to her, she began the same piece four times over, each time with much vexation, while he, not noticing any difference, cried—","zh":"有一天傍晚，查理听她弹琴，同一琴谱，她一连弹了四次，一次比一次生气，然而他看不出有什么不同，却喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Bravo! very goodl You are wrong to stop. Go on!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Bravo! very goodl You are wrong to stop.","zh":"“真好！好极了！你不该停下来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Go on!”","zh":"弹吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, no; it is execrable! My fingers are quite rusty.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, no; it is execrable!","zh":"“嗐！不成！糟不可言！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My fingers are quite rusty.”","zh":"我的手指全像长了锈一样！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day he begged her to play him something again.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day he begged her to play him something again.","zh":"第二天，他求她“再弹点什么给他听”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Very well; to please you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very well; to please you!”","zh":"“好吧，你要听，我弹给你听！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And Charles confessed she had gone off a little. She played wrong notes and blundered; then, stopping short—","sentences":[{"en":"And Charles confessed she had gone off a little.","zh":"查理承认她有一点生疏。她弹错琴键，东碰碰，西碰碰，最后干脆住了手：","scope":"group"},{"en":"She played wrong notes and blundered; then, stopping short—","zh":"查理承认她有一点生疏。她弹错琴键，东碰碰，西碰碰，最后干脆住了手：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ah! it is no use. I ought to take some lessons; but—” She bit her lips and added, “Twenty francs a lesson, that’s too dear!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! it is no use.","zh":"“啊！没有救！我应该跟人学琴去，不过…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I ought to take some lessons; but—” She bit her lips and added, “Twenty francs a lesson, that’s too dear!”","zh":"”她咬了咬嘴唇，接下去道：“二十法郎一次，太贵啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, so it is—rather,” said Charles, giggling stupidly. “But it seems to me that one might be able to do it for less; for there are artists of no reputation, and who are often better than the celebrities.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, so it is—rather,” said Charles, giggling stupidly.","zh":"查理似笑非笑，蠢模蠢样道：“是啊，的确…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“But it seems to me that one might be able to do it for less; for there are artists of no reputation, and who are often better than the celebrities.”","zh":"有一点…其实，少出些钱，我看，也许一样好学；因为有些艺术家，别看没有名气，往往比名流高多了。”爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Find them!” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“Find them!” said Emma.","zh":"“你打听打听看。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day when he came home he looked at her shyly, and at last could no longer keep back the words.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day when he came home he looked at her shyly, and at last could no longer keep back the words.","zh":"第二天，他回到家，一副狡黠模样打量她，临了憋不住，还是把话说出来了：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How obstinate you are sometimes! I went to Barfucheres to-day. Well, Madame Liegard assured me that her three young ladies who are at La Misericorde have lessons at fifty sous apiece, and that from an excellent mistress!”","sentences":[{"en":"“How obstinate you are sometimes!","zh":"“你有时候可真固执！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I went to Barfucheres to-day.","zh":"今天我到巴尔弗舍尔去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, Madame Liegard assured me that her three young ladies who are at La Misericorde have lessons at fifty sous apiece, and that from an excellent mistress!”","zh":"好！利埃热尔太太对我讲：她那两位小姐，在慈悲修道院学琴，教一次两个半法郎，还是一位有名的女教师！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She shrugged her shoulders and did not open her piano again. But when she passed by it (if Bovary were there), she sighed—","sentences":[{"en":"She shrugged her shoulders and did not open her piano again.","zh":"她耸耸肩膀，索性琴也不弹了。但是她从钢琴旁边走过（万一包法利也在旁边的话），她就叹气道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"But when she passed by it (if Bovary were there), she sighed—","zh":"她耸耸肩膀，索性琴也不弹了。但是她从钢琴旁边走过（万一包法利也在旁边的话），她就叹气道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ah! my poor piano!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! my poor piano!”","zh":"“哎！我可怜的钢琴！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And when anyone came to see her, she did not fail to inform them she had given up music, and could not begin again now for important reasons. Then people commiserated her—","sentences":[{"en":"And when anyone came to see her, she did not fail to inform them she had given up music, and could not begin again now for important reasons.","zh":"你去看望她，她少不了告诉你，她早已放弃音乐不学了，由于环境关系，现在也不可能再学了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then people commiserated her—","zh":"她得到外人的同情。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What a pity! she had so much talent!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What a pity! she had so much talent!”","zh":"真可惜！她那样有才分！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They even spoke to Bovary about it. They put him to shame, and especially the chemist.","sentences":[{"en":"They even spoke to Bovary about it.","zh":"有人甚至同包法利谈起，说他不该不让她学，特别是药剂师：","scope":"group"},{"en":"They put him to shame, and especially the chemist.","zh":"有人甚至同包法利谈起，说他不该不让她学，特别是药剂师：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You are wrong. One should never let any of the faculties of nature lie fallow. Besides, just think, my good friend, that by inducing madame to study; you are economising on the subsequent musical education of your child. For my own part, I think that mothers ought themselves to instruct their children. That is an idea of Rousseau’s, still rather new perhaps, but that will end by triumphing, I am certain of it, like mothers nursing their own children and vaccination.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are wrong.","zh":"“这就是您的不是了！一个人有天分，说什么也不该耽搁。","scope":"group"},{"en":"One should never let any of the faculties of nature lie fallow.","zh":"“这就是您的不是了！一个人有天分，说什么也不该耽搁。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Besides, just think, my good friend, that by inducing madame to study; you are economising on the subsequent musical education of your child.","zh":"再说，您想想看，我的好朋友，放太太去学琴，以后您孩子的音乐教育，不就替您省下来了吗！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For my own part, I think that mothers ought themselves to instruct their children.","zh":"我认为母亲应当亲自教育子女。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That is an idea of Rousseau’s, still rather new perhaps, but that will end by triumphing, I am certain of it, like mothers nursing their own children and vaccination.”","zh":"这是卢梭的见解，也许眼下还有一点新，不过我拿稳了，迟早会盛行的，就像母亲喂奶和种牛痘一样。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"So Charles returned once more to this question of the piano. Emma replied bitterly that it would be better to sell it. This poor piano, that had given her vanity so much satisfaction—to see it go was to Bovary like the indefinable suicide of a part of herself.","sentences":[{"en":"So Charles returned once more to this question of the piano.","zh":"所以查理再度谈起钢琴的问题。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma replied bitterly that it would be better to sell it.","zh":"爱玛一听，就酸溜溜地回答：顶好拿它卖掉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This poor piano, that had given her vanity so much satisfaction—to see it go was to Bovary like the indefinable suicide of a part of herself.","zh":"这架可怜的钢琴，曾经多次满足她的虚荣心，如今卖掉，在包法利看来，就像她亲手处死她的某一部分一样，他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If you liked,” he said, “a lesson from time to time, that wouldn’t after all be very ruinous.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If you liked,” he said, “a lesson from time to time, that wouldn’t after all be very ruinous.”","zh":"“万一你愿意的话…偶尔学一次钢琴，话说回来，也不见得有多大破费。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But lessons,” she replied, “are only of use when followed up.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But lessons,” she replied, “are only of use when followed up.”","zh":"她就这样设法得到丈夫允许，每星期进城一趟，会晤她的情人。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And thus it was she set about obtaining her husband’s permission to go to town once a week to see her lover. At the end of a month she was even considered to have made considerable progress.","sentences":[{"en":"And thus it was she set about obtaining her husband’s permission to go to town once a week to see her lover.","zh":"她就这样设法得到丈夫允许，每星期进城一趟，会晤她的情人。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At the end of a month she was even considered to have made considerable progress.","zh":"一个月下来，居然有人以为她弹琴很有进步。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-5","part":3,"n":5,"title":"Part III · Chapter 5","titleZh":"下卷 · 5","paragraphs":[{"en":"She went on Thursdays. She got up and dressed silently, in order not to awaken Charles, who would have made remarks about her getting ready too early. Next she walked up and down, went to the windows, and looked out at the Place. The early dawn was broadening between the pillars of the market, and the chemist’s shop, with the shutters still up, showed in the pale light of the dawn the large letters of his signboard.","sentences":[{"en":"She went on Thursdays.","zh":"她每星期四去，从床上爬起来，悄不做声，穿好衣服，就怕惊醒查理，来上两句闲话，说她不必太早出门。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She got up and dressed silently, in order not to awaken Charles, who would have made remarks about her getting ready too early.","zh":"她每星期四去，从床上爬起来，悄不做声，穿好衣服，就怕惊醒查理，来上两句闲话，说她不必太早出门。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Next she walked up and down, went to the windows, and looked out at the Place.","zh":"她打扮消停，走来走去，要不然就站在窗前，瞭望广场。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The early dawn was broadening between the pillars of the market, and the chemist’s shop, with the shutters still up, showed in the pale light of the dawn the large letters of his signboard.","zh":"曙光在菜场柱子的空当转动，药房的窗板关着，招牌上的大写字母，衬着黎明的灰白颜色，隐约可辨。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When the clock pointed to a quarter past seven, she went off to the “Lion d’Or,” whose door Artémise opened yawning. The girl then made up the coals covered by the cinders, and Emma remained alone in the kitchen. Now and again she went out. Hivert was leisurely harnessing his horses, listening, moreover, to Mere Lefrancois, who, passing her head and nightcap through a grating, was charging him with commissions and giving him explanations that would have confused anyone else. Emma kept beating the soles of her boots against the pavement of the yard.","sentences":[{"en":"When the clock pointed to a quarter past seven, she went off to the “Lion d’Or,” whose door Artémise opened yawning.","zh":"钟针指到七点一刻，她去了金狮，阿尔泰蜜丝打着呵欠，过来给她开门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The girl then made up the coals covered by the cinders, and Emma remained alone in the kitchen.","zh":"炭埋在灰烬里头，阿尔泰蜜丝为她剔红了。爱玛一个人待在厅房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now and again she went out.","zh":"她不时走到院子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hivert was leisurely harnessing his horses, listening, moreover, to Mere Lefrancois, who, passing her head and nightcap through a grating, was charging him with commissions and giving him explanations that would have confused anyone else.","zh":"伊韦尔不慌不忙套车，勒弗朗索瓦太太戴着睡帽，探出小窗口，交代任务，絮絮叨叨，对他解说来解说去，换了别人，早不耐烦了，可是伊韦尔一边套车，还一边在听。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma kept beating the soles of her boots against the pavement of the yard.","zh":"爱玛的靴跟打着院子石头地响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last, when he had eaten his soup, put on his cloak, lighted his pipe, and grasped his whip, he calmly installed himself on his seat.","sentences":[{"en":"At last, when he had eaten his soup, put on his cloak, lighted his pipe, and grasped his whip, he calmly installed himself on his seat.","zh":"他用过早点，披上粗毛斗篷，点起烟斗，拿起鞭子，终于安闲无事，坐到他的座位。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The “Hirondelle” started at a slow trot, and for about a mile stopped here and there to pick up passengers who waited for it, standing at the border of the road, in front of their yard gates.","sentences":[{"en":"The “Hirondelle” started at a slow trot, and for about a mile stopped here and there to pick up passengers who waited for it, standing at the border of the road, in front of their yard gates.","zh":"燕子悠悠走去，第一古里有四分之三，随地停留，等旅客上车。有的站在路旁，院子栅栏门前，守候它来；有的头一天约好了，由着车等；有的甚至还在家里床上；伊韦尔连喊带叫，骂过不算，还走下车来，拼命砸门。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Those who had secured seats the evening before kept it waiting; some even were still in bed in their houses. Hivert called, shouted, swore; then he got down from his seat and went and knocked loudly at the doors. The wind blew through the cracked windows.","sentences":[{"en":"Those who had secured seats the evening before kept it waiting; some even were still in bed in their houses.","zh":"燕子悠悠走去，第一古里有四分之三，随地停留，等旅客上车。有的站在路旁，院子栅栏门前，守候它来；有的头一天约好了，由着车等；有的甚至还在家里床上；伊韦尔连喊带叫，骂过不算，还走下车来，拼命砸门。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Hivert called, shouted, swore; then he got down from his seat and went and knocked loudly at the doors.","zh":"燕子悠悠走去，第一古里有四分之三，随地停留，等旅客上车。有的站在路旁，院子栅栏门前，守候它来；有的头一天约好了，由着车等；有的甚至还在家里床上；伊韦尔连喊带叫，骂过不算，还走下车来，拼命砸门。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The wind blew through the cracked windows.","zh":"冷风吹进车窗的裂缝。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The four seats, however, filled up. The carriage rolled off; rows of apple-trees followed one upon another, and the road between its two long ditches, full of yellow water, rose, constantly narrowing towards the horizon.","sentences":[{"en":"The four seats, however, filled up.","zh":"四条长凳坐满，车朝前驶去，苹果树一棵接连一棵，一闪而过；两道长沟，盛满黄水，夹着大路；大路越靠近天边，越显得窄小。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The carriage rolled off; rows of apple-trees followed one upon another, and the road between its two long ditches, full of yellow water, rose, constantly narrowing towards the horizon.","zh":"四条长凳坐满，车朝前驶去，苹果树一棵接连一棵，一闪而过；两道长沟，盛满黄水，夹着大路；大路越靠近天边，越显得窄小。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma knew it from end to end; she knew that after a meadow there was a sign-post, next an elm, a barn, or the hut of a lime-kiln tender. Sometimes even, in the hope of getting some surprise, she shut her eyes, but she never lost the clear perception of the distance to be traversed.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma knew it from end to end; she knew that after a meadow there was a sign-post, next an elm, a barn, or the hut of a lime-kiln tender.","zh":"爱玛对这条路，拐弯抹角，没有一个地方不熟，知道过了一家牧场，就有一根桩子，再下去又是一棵榆树、一座谷仓，或者一间路工小屋；有时候，她甚至闭上眼睛，过一会儿再睁开，奇怪到了什么地方，但是还有多少路要走，她再清楚不过。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Sometimes even, in the hope of getting some surprise, she shut her eyes, but she never lost the clear perception of the distance to be traversed.","zh":"爱玛对这条路，拐弯抹角，没有一个地方不熟，知道过了一家牧场，就有一根桩子，再下去又是一棵榆树、一座谷仓，或者一间路工小屋；有时候，她甚至闭上眼睛，过一会儿再睁开，奇怪到了什么地方，但是还有多少路要走，她再清楚不过。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At last the brick houses began to follow one another more closely, the earth resounded beneath the wheels, the “Hirondelle” glided between the gardens, where through an opening one saw statues, a periwinkle plant, clipped yews, and a swing. Then on a sudden the town appeared. Sloping down like an amphitheatre, and drowned in the fog, it widened out beyond the bridges confusedly. Then the open country spread away with a monotonous movement till it touched in the distance the vague line of the pale sky. Seen thus from above, the whole landscape looked immovable as a picture; the anchored ships were massed in one corner, the river curved round the foot of the green hills, and the isles, oblique in shape, lay on the water, like large, motionless, black fishes. The factory chimneys belched forth immense brown fumes that were blown away at the top. One heard the rumbling of the foundries, together with the clear chimes of the churches that stood out in the mist. The leafless trees on the boulevards made violet thickets in the midst of the houses, and the roofs, all shining with the rain, threw back unequal reflections, according to the height of the quarters in which they were. Sometimes a gust of wind drove the clouds towards the Saint Catherine hills, like aerial waves that broke silently against a cliff.","sentences":[{"en":"At last the brick houses began to follow one another more closely, the earth resounded beneath the wheels, the “Hirondelle” glided between the gardens, where through an opening one saw statues, a periwinkle plant, clipped yews, and a swing.","zh":"砖房终于到了眼前，地在车轮底下起了响声，燕子穿过两旁花园，人在开口的地方望到几座雕像、一座葡萄台 、几棵剪齐了的罗汉松和一架秋千。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then on a sudden the town appeared.","zh":"紧跟着一眨眼工夫，城出现了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sloping down like an amphitheatre, and drowned in the fog, it widened out beyond the bridges confusedly.","zh":"城像圆剧场，一步比一步低，雾气笼罩，直到过了桥，才乱纷纷展开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the open country spread away with a monotonous movement till it touched in the distance the vague line of the pale sky.","zh":"再过去又是旷野，形象单调，越远越高，最后碰上灰色天空的模糊的基线。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Seen thus from above, the whole landscape looked immovable as a picture; the anchored ships were massed in one corner, the river curved round the foot of the green hills, and the isles, oblique in shape, lay on the water, like large, motionless, black fishes.","zh":"全部风景，这样从高处望去，平平静静，像煞一幅画。停锚的船只，堆在一个角落；河顺着绿岭弯来弯去；长方形的岛屿，如同几条大黑鱼，停在水面，一动不动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The factory chimneys belched forth immense brown fumes that were blown away at the top.","zh":"工厂的烟筒冒出大团棕色的烟，随风飘散。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One heard the rumbling of the foundries, together with the clear chimes of the churches that stood out in the mist.","zh":"教堂的尖顶突破浓雾，清越的钟声有冶铸厂轰隆轰隆的响声伴奏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The leafless trees on the boulevards made violet thickets in the midst of the houses, and the roofs, all shining with the rain, threw back unequal reflections, according to the height of the quarters in which they were.","zh":"马路的枯树，站在房屋中间，好像成堆的紫色荆棘。雨洗过的屋顶，由于市区有高有低，光色参差不齐。有时候，吹来一阵劲风，浮云漂向圣卡特琳岭，仿佛空气凝成波涛，冲击岸边绝崖，先是气势汹汹，转瞬就又销声匿迹了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Sometimes a gust of wind drove the clouds towards the Saint Catherine hills, like aerial waves that broke silently against a cliff.","zh":"马路的枯树，站在房屋中间，好像成堆的紫色荆棘。雨洗过的屋顶，由于市区有高有低，光色参差不齐。有时候，吹来一阵劲风，浮云漂向圣卡特琳岭，仿佛空气凝成波涛，冲击岸边绝崖，先是气势汹汹，转瞬就又销声匿迹了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"A giddiness seemed to her to detach itself from this mass of existence, and her heart swelled as if the hundred and twenty thousand souls that palpitated there had all at once sent into it the vapour of the passions she fancied theirs. Her love grew in the presence of this vastness, and expanded with tumult to the vague murmurings that rose towards her. She poured it out upon the square, on the walks, on the streets, and the old Norman city outspread before her eyes as an enormous capital, as a Babylon into which she was entering. She leant with both hands against the window, drinking in the breeze; the three horses galloped, the stones grated in the mud, the diligence rocked, and Hivert, from afar, hailed the carts on the road, while the bourgeois who had spent the night at the Guillaume woods came quietly down the hill in their little family carriages.","sentences":[{"en":"A giddiness seemed to her to detach itself from this mass of existence, and her heart swelled as if the hundred and twenty thousand souls that palpitated there had all at once sent into it the vapour of the passions she fancied theirs.","zh":"这些人口密集的地方似乎有什么令人晕眩的东西，使她心潮澎湃，按她的设想，仿佛活在这里的十二万人，个个热情洋溢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her love grew in the presence of this vastness, and expanded with tumult to the vague murmurings that rose towards her.","zh":"她的爱情在这种地方益发高涨起来，城市的喧腾填入她的爱情，使之膨胀，随即她又朝广场、林荫道、街头把爱倾泻出来。诺曼底的这座古城，在她看来，成了一座奇大无比的京城，一座等她进去的巴比伦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She poured it out upon the square, on the walks, on the streets, and the old Norman city outspread before her eyes as an enormous capital, as a Babylon into which she was entering.","zh":"她的爱情在这种地方益发高涨起来，城市的喧腾填入她的爱情，使之膨胀，随即她又朝广场、林荫道、街头把爱倾泻出来。诺曼底的这座古城，在她看来，成了一座奇大无比的京城，一座等她进去的巴比伦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She leant with both hands against the window, drinking in the breeze; the three horses galloped, the stones grated in the mud, the diligence rocked, and Hivert, from afar, hailed the carts on the road, while the bourgeois who had spent the night at the Guillaume woods came quietly down the hill in their little family carriages.","zh":"两只手靠住车窗，她吸着吹来的微风。三匹马奔驰，泥里的石头嘎吱在响，车在摇晃，伊韦尔老远就喊路上小货车闪开，同时在纪尧姆树林过夜的资产者，乘着家里的小马车，安安详详下岭。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They stopped at the barrier; Emma undid her overshoes, put on other gloves, rearranged her shawl, and some twenty paces farther she got down from the “Hirondelle.”","sentences":[{"en":"They stopped at the barrier; Emma undid her overshoes, put on other gloves, rearranged her shawl, and some twenty paces farther she got down from the “Hirondelle.”","zh":"车在城门跟前停住；爱玛脱下木头套鞋，换过手套，理好披肩，在二十步开外，走下燕子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The town was then awakening. Shop-boys in caps were cleaning up the shop-fronts, and women with baskets against their hips, at intervals uttered sonorous cries at the corners of streets. She walked with downcast eyes, close to the walls, and smiling with pleasure under her lowered black veil.","sentences":[{"en":"The town was then awakening.","zh":"全城正苏醒过来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Shop-boys in caps were cleaning up the shop-fronts, and women with baskets against their hips, at intervals uttered sonorous cries at the corners of streets.","zh":"有些伙计戴着希腊小帽，擦亮店面；有些妇女，屁股顶着篮子，隔一会儿，在街角吆喝一声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She walked with downcast eyes, close to the walls, and smiling with pleasure under her lowered black veil.","zh":"她贴墙走，眼睛望地，黑面网拉下来，喜滋滋的，笑容满面。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For fear of being seen, she did not usually take the most direct road. She plunged into dark alleys, and, all perspiring, reached the bottom of the Rue Nationale, near the fountain that stands there. It is the quarter for theatres, public-houses, and whores. Often a cart would pass near her, bearing some shaking scenery. Waiters in aprons were sprinkling sand on the flagstones between green shrubs. It all smelt of absinthe, cigars, and oysters.","sentences":[{"en":"For fear of being seen, she did not usually take the most direct road.","zh":"她怕人看见，一般不走最近的路。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She plunged into dark alleys, and, all perspiring, reached the bottom of the Rue Nationale, near the fountain that stands there.","zh":"她钻进不见阳光的小巷，浑身是汗，从国民街的街口，喷泉附近出来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is the quarter for theatres, public-houses, and whores.","zh":"这里是剧场、咖啡馆和妓院区。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often a cart would pass near her, bearing some shaking scenery.","zh":"常常一辆大车，载着晃晃悠悠的布景，从她旁边走过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Waiters in aprons were sprinkling sand on the flagstones between green shrubs.","zh":"有些系围裙的伙计，往绿色灌木丛之间的石板路上撒沙子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It all smelt of absinthe, cigars, and oysters.","zh":"她闻见洋艾酒、雪茄和牡蛎的气味。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She turned down a street; she recognised him by his curling hair that escaped from beneath his hat.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned down a street; she recognised him by his curling hair that escaped from beneath his hat.","zh":"她转过一条街，看见一个人，帽子底下露出一圈一圈头发，认出了他。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon walked along the pavement. She followed him to the hotel. He went up, opened the door, entered—What an embrace!","sentences":[{"en":"Léon walked along the pavement.","zh":"赖昂在人行道上继续行走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She followed him to the hotel.","zh":"她一直跟到旅馆；他走上楼，开开门，进去…热烈地吻抱！","scope":"group"},{"en":"He went up, opened the door, entered—What an embrace!","zh":"她一直跟到旅馆；他走上楼，开开门，进去…热烈地吻抱！","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then, after the kisses, the words gushed forth. They told each other the sorrows of the week, the presentiments, the anxiety for the letters; but now everything was forgotten; they gazed into each other’s faces with voluptuous laughs, and tender names.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, after the kisses, the words gushed forth.","zh":"吻过以后，话像激流一样，滔滔不绝。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They told each other the sorrows of the week, the presentiments, the anxiety for the letters; but now everything was forgotten; they gazed into each other’s faces with voluptuous laughs, and tender names.","zh":"他们互相倾诉一星期来的愁闷、忧虑和盼信的焦灼；但是如今，统统烟消云散了，他们面对面望着，开心地笑着，恩恩爱爱地叫着。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The bed was large, of mahogany, in the shape of a boat. The curtains were in red levantine, that hung from the ceiling and bulged out too much towards the bell-shaped bedside; and nothing in the world was so lovely as her brown head and white skin standing out against this purple colour, when, with a movement of shame, she crossed her bare arms, hiding her face in her hands.","sentences":[{"en":"The bed was large, of mahogany, in the shape of a boat.","zh":"床是一张船形桃花心木大床。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The curtains were in red levantine, that hung from the ceiling and bulged out too much towards the bell-shaped bedside; and nothing in the world was so lovely as her brown head and white skin standing out against this purple colour, when, with a movement of shame, she crossed her bare arms, hiding her face in her hands.","zh":"天花板挂着素红缎幔帐，低低下垂，兜着敞口床头——世上没有比这再美的了：红颜色衬着她的棕色头发、她的白色皮肤，同时她羞答答的，缩拢两条光胳膊，脸藏在手心。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The warm room, with its discreet carpet, its gay ornaments, and its calm light, seemed made for the intimacies of passion. The curtain-rods, ending in arrows, their brass pegs, and the great balls of the fire-dogs shone suddenly when the sun came in. On the chimney between the candelabra there were two of those pink shells in which one hears the murmur of the sea if one holds them to the ear.","sentences":[{"en":"The warm room, with its discreet carpet, its gay ornaments, and its calm light, seemed made for the intimacies of passion.","zh":"房间暖和，地毯没有声息，陈设轻狎，光线柔和，似乎一切专为颠鸾倒凤而设。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The curtain-rods, ending in arrows, their brass pegs, and the great balls of the fire-dogs shone suddenly when the sun came in.","zh":"太阳进来，箭头帐竿、铜床钩、火篦的大球，马上发出亮光。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the chimney between the candelabra there were two of those pink shells in which one hears the murmur of the sea if one holds them to the ear.","zh":"两只玫瑰红大蚌壳，放在壁炉上两支蜡烛当中，举到耳边，可以听见海啸。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"How they loved that dear room, so full of gaiety, despite its rather faded splendour! They always found the furniture in the same place, and sometimes hairpins, that she had forgotten the Thursday before, under the pedestal of the clock. They lunched by the fireside on a little round table, inlaid with rosewood. Emma carved, put bits on his plate with all sorts of coquettish ways, and she laughed with a sonorous and libertine laugh when the froth of the champagne ran over from the glass to the rings on her fingers. They were so completely lost in the possession of each other that they thought themselves in their own house, and that they would live there till death, like two spouses eternally young. They said “our room,” “our carpet,” she even said “my slippers,” a gift of Léon’s, a whim she had had. They were pink satin, bordered with swansdown. When she sat on his knees, her leg, then too short, hung in the air, and the dainty shoe, that had no back to it, was held only by the toes to her bare foot.","sentences":[{"en":"How they loved that dear room, so full of gaiety, despite its rather faded splendour!","zh":"他们多爱这间亲密的卧室！装潢虽然有一点过时，但是充满欢愉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They always found the furniture in the same place, and sometimes hairpins, that she had forgotten the Thursday before, under the pedestal of the clock.","zh":"他们过一个星期再来，发现木器照样待在原来的地方，有时候，她上星期四忘记的头发针又在钟座底下看到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They lunched by the fireside on a little round table, inlaid with rosewood.","zh":"他们围着一张独腿紫檀小圆桌，在炉边用午饭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma carved, put bits on his plate with all sorts of coquettish ways, and she laughed with a sonorous and libertine laugh when the froth of the champagne ran over from the glass to the rings on her fingers.","zh":"爱玛把肉切成薄片，给他放在盘子里，一边千娇百媚，卖弄风骚。香槟酒倒进精致的玻璃杯，沫子溅上她的戒指，她笑了起来，清脆动听，无拘无束。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were so completely lost in the possession of each other that they thought themselves in their own house, and that they would live there till death, like two spouses eternally young.","zh":"他们两下色授魂与，如胶似漆，错把旅馆当作家园，要在这里活到老死，宛如一对神仙夫妇，永远少艾。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They said “our room,” “our carpet,” she even said “my slippers,” a gift of Léon’s, a whim she had had.","zh":"他们说起“我们的房间”“我们的地毯”“我们的扶手椅”；她甚至说起“我的拖鞋”——这是赖昂的礼物，天鹅毛沿口。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were pink satin, bordered with swansdown.","zh":"他们说起“我们的房间”“我们的地毯”“我们的扶手椅”；她甚至说起“我的拖鞋”——这是赖昂的礼物，天鹅毛沿口。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When she sat on his knees, her leg, then too short, hung in the air, and the dainty shoe, that had no back to it, was held only by the toes to her bare foot.","zh":"她坐在他的膝上，她的腿太短，悬在半空，于是没有后跟的玲珑拖鞋，就只套在她的光脚的脚趾。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He for the first time enjoyed the inexpressible delicacy of feminine refinements. He had never met this grace of language, this reserve of clothing, these poses of the weary dove. He admired the exaltation of her soul and the lace on her petticoat. Besides, was she not “a lady” and a married woman—a real mistress, in fine?","sentences":[{"en":"He for the first time enjoyed the inexpressible delicacy of feminine refinements.","zh":"女性生活的不可言传的美妙，他有生以来，还是头一回玩味。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had never met this grace of language, this reserve of clothing, these poses of the weary dove.","zh":"他从来没有领略过这种雅致的语言、这种考究的服装、这种睡鸽似的姿态。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He admired the exaltation of her soul and the lace on her petticoat.","zh":"他赞赏她火热的感情和裙子的花边。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, was she not “a lady” and a married woman—a real mistress, in fine?","zh":"再说，她不正是一位社交之花、一位有夫之妇！总而言之，一位真正的情妇！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"By the diversity of her humour, in turn mystical or mirthful, talkative, taciturn, passionate, careless, she awakened in him a thousand desires, called up instincts or memories. She was the mistress of all the novels, the heroine of all the dramas, the vague “she” of all the volumes of verse. He found again on her shoulder the amber colouring of the “Odalisque Bathing”; she had the long waist of feudal chatelaines, and she resembled the “Pale Woman of Barcelona.” But above all she was the Angel!","sentences":[{"en":"By the diversity of her humour, in turn mystical or mirthful, talkative, taciturn, passionate, careless, she awakened in him a thousand desires, called up instincts or memories.","zh":"由于性情多变，一时幽深，一时快活，一时絮叨，一时缄默，一时激愤，一时冷淡，她激发出来的欲望，在他也是无穷的，不唤起本能，就唤起回忆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was the mistress of all the novels, the heroine of all the dramas, the vague “she” of all the volumes of verse.","zh":"她是所有传奇小说里的情人、一切剧本里的女主人公、任何诗集泛指的她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He found again on her shoulder the amber colouring of the “Odalisque Bathing”; she had the long waist of feudal chatelaines, and she resembled the “Pale Woman of Barcelona.”","zh":"他在她的肩头又看见了《土耳其嫔妃入浴图》的琥珀颜色；她有封建时代女庄主的细长腰肢；她也很像“巴塞罗那的面色苍白的妇人”，但首先她是天使！","scope":"group"},{"en":"But above all she was the Angel!","zh":"他在她的肩头又看见了《土耳其嫔妃入浴图》的琥珀颜色；她有封建时代女庄主的细长腰肢；她也很像“巴塞罗那的面色苍白的妇人”，但首先她是天使！","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Often looking at her, it seemed to him that his soul, escaping towards her, spread like a wave about the outline of her head, and descended drawn down into the whiteness of her breast. He knelt on the ground before her, and with both elbows on her knees looked at her with a smile, his face upturned.","sentences":[{"en":"Often looking at her, it seemed to him that his soul, escaping towards her, spread like a wave about the outline of her head, and descended drawn down into the whiteness of her breast.","zh":"他常常一边看她，一边觉得他的灵魂离开自己，变成波浪，顺着她的头部往下流，不由自主，流进她的白净的胸脯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He knelt on the ground before her, and with both elbows on her knees looked at her with a smile, his face upturned.","zh":"他坐在她面前的地上，一对胳膊肘搭在膝盖上，仰起脸来，笑眯眯打量她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She bent over him, and murmured, as if choking with intoxication—","sentences":[{"en":"She bent over him, and murmured, as if choking with intoxication—","zh":"她朝他弯下身子，仿佛神魂颠倒，话也说不出来了，唧唧哝哝道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, do not move! do not speak! look at me! Something so sweet comes from your eyes that helps me so much!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, do not move! do not speak! look at me!","zh":"“别动！别说话！看着我！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Something so sweet comes from your eyes that helps me so much!”","zh":"你的眼睛像有什么东西放射出来，那样甜，那样让我惬意！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She called him “child.” “Child, do you love me?”","sentences":[{"en":"She called him “child.”","zh":"她叫他“孩子”：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Child, do you love me?”","zh":"“孩子，你爱我吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she did not listen for his answer in the haste of her lips that fastened to his mouth.","sentences":[{"en":"And she did not listen for his answer in the haste of her lips that fastened to his mouth.","zh":"她简直听不见他的答话，因为他的嘴唇很快就上来封住了她的嘴。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On the clock there was a bronze cupid, who smirked as he bent his arm beneath a golden garland. They had laughed at it many a time, but when they had to part everything seemed serious to them.","sentences":[{"en":"On the clock there was a bronze cupid, who smirked as he bent his arm beneath a golden garland.","zh":"钟上有一个丘比特 小铜像，一脸媚态，弯起两只胳膊，托住一个镀金花环。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They had laughed at it many a time, but when they had to part everything seemed serious to them.","zh":"他们笑他笑了许多次。但是临到非分手不可，他们觉得样样严肃了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Motionless in front of each other, they kept repeating, “Till Thursday, till Thursday.”","sentences":[{"en":"Motionless in front of each other, they kept repeating, “Till Thursday, till Thursday.”","zh":"两个人面对面，一动不动，再三重复：“下星期四见！下星期四见…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Suddenly she seized his head between her hands, kissed him hurriedly on the forehead, crying, “Adieu!” and rushed down the stairs.","sentences":[{"en":"Suddenly she seized his head between her hands, kissed him hurriedly on the forehead, crying, “Adieu!” and rushed down the stairs.","zh":"她伸出两只手，猛然搂住他的头，骤风急雨般吻着他的前额，喊一声“再会！”奔下楼梯。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She went to a hairdresser’s in the Rue de la Comedie to have her hair arranged. Night fell; the gas was lighted in the shop. She heard the bell at the theatre calling the mummers to the performance, and she saw, passing opposite, men with white faces and women in faded gowns going in at the stage-door.","sentences":[{"en":"She went to a hairdresser’s in the Rue de la Comedie to have her hair arranged.","zh":"她走到剧场街，在一家理发馆整理头发。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Night fell; the gas was lighted in the shop.","zh":"天黑了；铺子点亮煤气灯。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She heard the bell at the theatre calling the mummers to the performance, and she saw, passing opposite, men with white faces and women in faded gowns going in at the stage-door.","zh":"她听见剧场摇铃，召集演员上戏；她看见对面走过白脸的男子和装束过时的女子，从后台门进去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was hot in the room, small, and too low where the stove was hissing in the midst of wigs and pomades. The smell of the tongs, together with the greasy hands that handled her head, soon stunned her, and she dozed a little in her wrapper. Often, as he did her hair, the man offered her tickets for a masked ball.","sentences":[{"en":"It was hot in the room, small, and too low where the stove was hissing in the midst of wigs and pomades.","zh":"这间小屋本来太低，加上假发和生发油之间，生着熊熊的炉火，显得特别暖和。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The smell of the tongs, together with the greasy hands that handled her head, soon stunned her, and she dozed a little in her wrapper.","zh":"她闻着铁的气味，还有那双给她梳理头发的油手，很快就昏昏沉沉，披着她的梳头衣服，眯瞪了一小会儿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often, as he did her hair, the man offered her tickets for a masked ball.","zh":"伙计常常一边给她梳头，一边问她要不要化装舞会的门票。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she went away. She went up the streets; reached the Croix-Rouge, put on her overshoes, that she had hidden in the morning under the seat, and sank into her place among the impatient passengers. Some got out at the foot of the hill. She remained alone in the carriage. At every turning all the lights of the town were seen more and more completely, making a great luminous vapour about the dim houses. Emma knelt on the cushions and her eyes wandered over the dazzling light. She sobbed; called on Léon, sent him tender words and kisses lost in the wind.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she went away.","zh":"她终于走开了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She went up the streets; reached the Croix-Rouge, put on her overshoes, that she had hidden in the morning under the seat, and sank into her place among the impatient passengers.","zh":"穿街越巷，来到红十字旅馆，早晨她把木头套鞋藏在长凳底下，现在又取出来穿上，挨着不耐烦的乘客，坐到她的座位。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some got out at the foot of the hill.","zh":"有的乘客在岭下就下了车，她一个人留在车上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She remained alone in the carriage.","zh":"有的乘客在岭下就下了车，她一个人留在车上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At every turning all the lights of the town were seen more and more completely, making a great luminous vapour about the dim houses.","zh":"每拐一次弯，遥望城里灯火，也就一次比一次多，仿佛一大片通明的水汽，浮在杂乱的房屋上空。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma knelt on the cushions and her eyes wandered over the dazzling light.","zh":"爱玛跪在垫子上，茫然望着这照花了眼的景象。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She sobbed; called on Léon, sent him tender words and kisses lost in the wind.","zh":"她呜咽了，叫着赖昂，朝他送去一些情意绵绵的话和随风而逝的吻。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On the hillside a poor devil wandered about with his stick in the midst of the diligences. A mass of rags covered his shoulders, and an old staved-in beaver, turned out like a basin, hid his face; but when he took it off he discovered in the place of eyelids empty and bloody orbits. The flesh hung in red shreds, and there flowed from it liquids that congealed into green scale down to the nose, whose black nostrils sniffed convulsively. To speak to you he threw back his head with an idiotic laugh; then his bluish eyeballs, rolling constantly, at the temples beat against the edge of the open wound. He sang a little song as he followed the carriages—","sentences":[{"en":"On the hillside a poor devil wandered about with his stick in the midst of the diligences.","zh":"有一个乞丐，拄着拐杖，不顾山路崎岖，在驿车中间奔走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A mass of rags covered his shoulders, and an old staved-in beaver, turned out like a basin, hid his face; but when he took it off he discovered in the place of eyelids empty and bloody orbits.","zh":"肩膀蒙着一堆破布。一只旧獭皮帽，没有顶子，圆圆的仿佛一个脸盆，扣住他的脸，可是他一摘掉，就见眼皮地方，有两个血窟窿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The flesh hung in red shreds, and there flowed from it liquids that congealed into green scale down to the nose, whose black nostrils sniffed convulsively.","zh":"皮肉开裂，形成一道道红皮瓣，脓液淌下来，凝成绿痂，一直到鼻子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To speak to you he threw back his head with an idiotic laugh; then his bluish eyeballs, rolling constantly, at the temples beat against the edge of the open wound.","zh":"黑鼻孔痉挛似的往里吸气。说话先要仰起头来傻笑——于是他的淡蓝瞳仁，不住朝太阳穴滚过去，一直滚到脓疮外沿。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He sang a little song as he followed the carriages—","zh":"黑鼻孔痉挛似的往里吸气。说话先要仰起头来傻笑——于是他的淡蓝瞳仁，不住朝太阳穴滚过去，一直滚到脓疮外沿。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Maids an the warmth of a summer day Dream of love, and of love always”","sentences":[{"en":"“Maids an the warmth of a summer day Dream of love, and of love always”","zh":"他跟在车辆后面，唱着一首小歌：火红的太阳暖烘烘，","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And all the rest was about birds and sunshine and green leaves.","sentences":[{"en":"And all the rest was about birds and sunshine and green leaves.","zh":"小姑娘正做爱情的梦。下边唱到飞鸟、太阳和绿叶。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Sometimes he appeared suddenly behind Emma, bareheaded, and she drew back with a cry. Hivert made fun of him. He would advise him to get a booth at the Saint Romain fair, or else ask him, laughing, how his young woman was.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes he appeared suddenly behind Emma, bareheaded, and she drew back with a cry.","zh":"有时候，他光着头，冷不防来到爱玛背后。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hivert made fun of him.","zh":"她叫一声，就往后退。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He would advise him to get a booth at the Saint Romain fair, or else ask him, laughing, how his young woman was.","zh":"伊韦尔寻他开心，叫他赶圣罗曼集摆一个摊子，要不然就笑嘻嘻问他，他的情人一向可好。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Often they had started when, with a sudden movement, his hat entered the diligence through the small window, while he clung with his other arm to the footboard, between the wheels splashing mud. His voice, feeble at first and quavering, grew sharp; it resounded in the night like the indistinct moan of a vague distress; and through the ringing of the bells, the murmur of the trees, and the rumbling of the empty vehicle, it had a far-off sound that disturbed Emma. It went to the bottom of her soul, like a whirlwind in an abyss, and carried her away into the distances of a boundless melancholy. But Hivert, noticing a weight behind, gave the blind man sharp cuts with his whip. The thong lashed his wounds, and he fell back into the mud with a yell. Then the passengers in the “Hirondelle” ended by falling asleep, some with open mouths, others with lowered chins, leaning against their neighbour’s shoulder, or with their arm passed through the strap, oscillating regularly with the jolting of the carriage; and the reflection of the lantern swinging without, on the crupper of the wheeler; penetrating into the interior through the chocolate calico curtains, threw sanguineous shadows over all these motionless people. Emma, drunk with grief, shivered in her clothes, feeling her feet grow colder and colder, and death in her soul.","sentences":[{"en":"Often they had started when, with a sudden movement, his hat entered the diligence through the small window, while he clung with his other arm to the footboard, between the wheels splashing mud.","zh":"常常车正在走，就见他的帽子突然塞进车窗，另一只胳膊抓住脚凳，车轮泥水再溅，他也揪牢不放。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His voice, feeble at first and quavering, grew sharp; it resounded in the night like the indistinct moan of a vague distress; and through the ringing of the bells, the murmur of the trees, and the rumbling of the empty vehicle, it had a far-off sound that disturbed Emma.","zh":"他的声音先是哀婉，如同婴儿啼哭，慢慢变尖了，在夜色中拖长，好像一个人说不出来为什么伤心，抽抽噎噎，听不真切哭些什么，可是透过铃铛的响声、树木的吹动和空车的轰隆，隐隐传来什么力量，扰乱爱玛的心情，好像一阵旋风进了深渊一样，沉入她的灵魂深处，又把她带到无边无涯的忧郁世界。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It went to the bottom of her soul, like a whirlwind in an abyss, and carried her away into the distances of a boundless melancholy.","zh":"他的声音先是哀婉，如同婴儿啼哭，慢慢变尖了，在夜色中拖长，好像一个人说不出来为什么伤心，抽抽噎噎，听不真切哭些什么，可是透过铃铛的响声、树木的吹动和空车的轰隆，隐隐传来什么力量，扰乱爱玛的心情，好像一阵旋风进了深渊一样，沉入她的灵魂深处，又把她带到无边无涯的忧郁世界。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But Hivert, noticing a weight behind, gave the blind man sharp cuts with his whip.","zh":"不过伊韦尔觉出一边偏重来了，抡起鞭子，使劲抽打瞎子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The thong lashed his wounds, and he fell back into the mud with a yell.","zh":"鞭梢抽到他的烂疮，他摔在泥里，疼得扯嗓子乱叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the passengers in the “Hirondelle” ended by falling asleep, some with open mouths, others with lowered chins, leaning against their neighbour’s shoulder, or with their arm passed through the strap, oscillating regularly with the jolting of the carriage; and the reflection of the lantern swinging without, on the crupper of the wheeler; penetrating into the interior through the chocolate calico curtains, threw sanguineous shadows over all these motionless people.","zh":"燕子的乘客终于睡着了，有人张开嘴，有人低下头，不是靠住邻人的肩膀，就是胳膊穿进车上的皮带，随着马车的颠簸，摇来晃去。灯在车外摆来摆去，照着辕马的屁股，透过巧克力色的布帘，撒下一片血红的影子，笼罩着这些安静的男女。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma, drunk with grief, shivered in her clothes, feeling her feet grow colder and colder, and death in her soul.","zh":"爱玛一阵紧似一阵凄凉，穿着衣服，直打寒噤，越来越觉得脚冷，心像死了一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles at home was waiting for her; the “Hirondelle” was always late on Thursdays. Madame arrived at last, and scarcely kissed the child. The dinner was not ready. No matter! She excused the servant. This girl now seemed allowed to do just as she liked.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles at home was waiting for her; the “Hirondelle” was always late on Thursdays.","zh":"查理在家等她回来；燕子星期四总是姗姗来迟。太太终于回来了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame arrived at last, and scarcely kissed the child.","zh":"她勉强吻抱了一下小女孩子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The dinner was not ready.","zh":"晚饭没有预备好，没有关系！","scope":"group"},{"en":"No matter!","zh":"晚饭没有预备好，没有关系！","scope":"group"},{"en":"She excused the servant.","zh":"她原谅女厨子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This girl now seemed allowed to do just as she liked.","zh":"现在似乎全尽这丫头做。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Often her husband, noting her pallor, asked if she were unwell.","sentences":[{"en":"Often her husband, noting her pallor, asked if she were unwell.","zh":"丈夫看出她面色苍白，常常问她是否难受。爱玛说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No,” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“No,” said Emma.","zh":"“不难受。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But,” he replied, “you seem so strange this evening.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But,” he replied, “you seem so strange this evening.”","zh":"他反驳：“可是你不觉得你今天晚上有点异样？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, it’s nothing! nothing!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it’s nothing! nothing!”","zh":"他反驳：“可是你不觉得你今天晚上有点异样？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"There were even days when she had no sooner come in than she went up to her room; and Justin, happening to be there, moved about noiselessly, quicker at helping her than the best of maids. He put the matches ready, the candlestick, a book, arranged her nightgown, turned back the bedclothes.","sentences":[{"en":"There were even days when she had no sooner come in than she went up to her room; and Justin, happening to be there, moved about noiselessly, quicker at helping her than the best of maids.","zh":"没有什么！”甚至有些天，她一到家，就先上楼，去了卧室。朱斯丹凑巧也在，潜着脚步，奔走伺候，比一个精明的宫女还要得心应手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He put the matches ready, the candlestick, a book, arranged her nightgown, turned back the bedclothes.","zh":"他理齐火柴、蜡烛盘和一本书，放好她的睡衣，摊开被窝。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come!” said she, “that will do. Now you can go.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come!” said she, “that will do.","zh":"“好，行啦，去吧！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Now you can go.”","zh":"“好，行啦，去吧！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"For he stood there, his hands hanging down and his eyes wide open, as if enmeshed in the innumerable threads of a sudden reverie.","sentences":[{"en":"For he stood there, his hands hanging down and his eyes wide open, as if enmeshed in the innumerable threads of a sudden reverie.","zh":"因为他站在一旁，两手下垂，眼睛睁开，就像忽然沉入绮梦，千丝万缕，缠在里面无法自拔。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The following day was frightful, and those that came after still more unbearable, because of her impatience to once again seize her happiness; an ardent lust, inflamed by the images of past experience, and that burst forth freely on the seventh day beneath Léon’s caresses. His ardours were hidden beneath outbursts of wonder and gratitude. Emma tasted this love in a discreet, absorbed fashion, maintained it by all the artifices of her tenderness, and trembled a little lest it should be lost later on.","sentences":[{"en":"The following day was frightful, and those that came after still more unbearable, because of her impatience to once again seize her happiness; an ardent lust, inflamed by the images of past experience, and that burst forth freely on the seventh day beneath Léon’s caresses.","zh":"第二天阴沉可怕，以后几天，还要难熬，因为爱玛急于重温她的幸福，大有迫不及待之势——正因深谙其味，越发贪得无厌，所以她熬到第七天，见到赖昂，就尽情缱绻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His ardours were hidden beneath outbursts of wonder and gratitude.","zh":"他的热情表现首先是惊奇和感激。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma tasted this love in a discreet, absorbed fashion, maintained it by all the artifices of her tenderness, and trembled a little lest it should be lost later on.","zh":"爱玛享受这种爱情，审慎而专注，温存体贴，花样翻新，唯恐有什么闪失，爱情不翼而飞。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She often said to him, with her sweet, melancholy voice—","sentences":[{"en":"She often said to him, with her sweet, melancholy voice—","zh":"她常常声音柔和，悒悒寡欢，对他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! you too, you will leave me! You will marry! You will be like all the others.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! you too, you will leave me!","zh":"“啊！你！你会离开我的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You will marry!","zh":"你要结婚的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You will be like all the others.”","zh":"你要和别人一样的。”他问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He asked, “What others?”","sentences":[{"en":"He asked, “What others?”","zh":"“哪些别人？”她回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, like all men,” she replied. Then added, repulsing him with a languid movement—","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, like all men,” she replied.","zh":"“还不都是男人。”然后她做出娇嗔的手势，推开他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then added, repulsing him with a languid movement—","zh":"“还不都是男人。”然后她做出娇嗔的手势，推开他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You are all evil!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are all evil!”","zh":"“你们全是负心的货！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One day, as they were talking philosophically of earthly disillusions, to experiment on his jealousy, or yielding, perhaps, to an over-strong need to pour out her heart, she told him that formerly, before him, she had loved someone.","sentences":[{"en":"One day, as they were talking philosophically of earthly disillusions, to experiment on his jealousy, or yielding, perhaps, to an over-strong need to pour out her heart, she told him that formerly, before him, she had loved someone.","zh":"他们有一天，心平气和，漫谈人事无常，她随便说起（为了试验他的忌妒，或者也许由于一种过分强烈的吐露心情的要求）往日，她在他之前，爱过一个男子，“并不像你！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Not like you,” she went on quickly, protesting by the head of her child that “nothing had passed between them.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not like you,” she went on quickly, protesting by the head of her child that “nothing had passed between them.”","zh":"她赶快补上一句，还用女儿的终身赌咒，说：“没有发生关系。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The young man believed her, but none the less questioned her to find out what he was.","sentences":[{"en":"The young man believed her, but none the less questioned her to find out what he was.","zh":"年轻人信以为真，问起他的职业。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“He was a ship’s captain, my dear.”","sentences":[{"en":"“He was a ship’s captain, my dear.”","zh":"“我的朋友，他是一位船长。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Was this not preventing any inquiry, and, at the same time, assuming a higher ground through this pretended fascination exercised over a man who must have been of warlike nature and accustomed to receive homage?","sentences":[{"en":"Was this not preventing any inquiry, and, at the same time, assuming a higher ground through this pretended fascination exercised over a man who must have been of warlike nature and accustomed to receive homage?","zh":"这不免去任何追究，同时不也抬高她的身份？——因为一个男人，天性好斗，听惯恭维，居然受她支配，无形之中，也就说明她的魅力。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The clerk then felt the lowliness of his position; he longed for epaulettes, crosses, titles. All that would please her—he gathered that from her spendthrift habits.","sentences":[{"en":"The clerk then felt the lowliness of his position; he longed for epaulettes, crosses, titles.","zh":"可是文书听了这话，很嫌自己卑微。他羡慕肩章、勋章、官衔。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All that would please her—he gathered that from her spendthrift habits.","zh":"她一定喜欢这类东西，从她爱挥霍的习惯上就能看出来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma nevertheless concealed many of these extravagant fancies, such as her wish to have a blue tilbury to drive into Rouen, drawn by an English horse and driven by a groom in top-boots. It was Justin who had inspired her with this whim, by begging her to take him into her service as valet-de-chambre, and if the privation of it did not lessen the pleasure of her arrival at each rendezvous, it certainly augmented the bitterness of the return.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma nevertheless concealed many of these extravagant fancies, such as her wish to have a blue tilbury to drive into Rouen, drawn by an English horse and driven by a groom in top-boots.","zh":"其实爱玛有许多异想天开的事，还没有说出口来，例如她来鲁昂，希望能乘一辆蓝色提耳玻里，驾一匹英吉利马，有一个穿翻口长靴的马僮驭马。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Justin who had inspired her with this whim, by begging her to take him into her service as valet-de-chambre, and if the privation of it did not lessen the pleasure of her arrival at each rendezvous, it certainly augmented the bitterness of the return.","zh":"勾起她这种怪想法的是朱斯丹，他曾求她收他当一名跟班。短少这辆马车，并不减轻她每次赴幽会的快感，然而增加回去的辛酸，也是真的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Often, when they talked together of Paris, she ended by murmuring, “Ah! how happy we should be there!”","sentences":[{"en":"Often, when they talked together of Paris, she ended by murmuring, “Ah! how happy we should be there!”","zh":"他们一道谈起巴黎，她临了总嘀咕道：“啊！我们住在那边，要有多好！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are we not happy?” gently answered the young man passing his hands over her hair.","sentences":[{"en":"“Are we not happy?” gently answered the young man passing his hands over her hair.","zh":"年轻人摸着她的头发，柔声柔气问道：“难道我们不快活？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, that is true,” she said. “I am mad. Kiss me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, that is true,” she said.","zh":"她道：“是啊，的确快活，我把话说得没有边儿啦；亲亲我！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I am mad.","zh":"她道：“是啊，的确快活，我把话说得没有边儿啦；亲亲我！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Kiss me!”","zh":"她道：“是啊，的确快活，我把话说得没有边儿啦；亲亲我！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"To her husband she was more charming than ever. She made him pistachio-creams, and played him waltzes after dinner. So he thought himself the most fortunate of men and Emma was without uneasiness, when, one evening suddenly he said—","sentences":[{"en":"To her husband she was more charming than ever.","zh":"她待丈夫也可爱多了：给他做“阿月浑子”奶酪，晚饭后弹华尔兹舞曲。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She made him pistachio-creams, and played him waltzes after dinner.","zh":"她待丈夫也可爱多了：给他做“阿月浑子”奶酪，晚饭后弹华尔兹舞曲。","scope":"group"},{"en":"So he thought himself the most fortunate of men and Emma was without uneasiness, when, one evening suddenly he said—","zh":"他把自己看成最走运的人，爱玛日子也过得无忧无虑的，可是有一天黄昏，他冷不防问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is Mademoiselle Lempereur, isn’t it, who gives you lessons?”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is Mademoiselle Lempereur, isn’t it, who gives you lessons?”","zh":"“教你弹琴的，是不是朗玻乐小姐？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“是她。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, I saw her just now,” Charles went on, “at Madame Liegeard’s. I spoke to her about you, and she doesn’t know you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I saw her just now,” Charles went on, “at Madame Liegeard’s.","zh":"查理接下去道：“噢！我方才在利埃热尔太太家里看见了她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I spoke to her about you, and she doesn’t know you.”","zh":"我同她谈起你来，她说她不认识。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This was like a thunderclap. However, she replied quite naturally—","sentences":[{"en":"This was like a thunderclap.","zh":"她像遭了雷殛一样，不过还装出若无其事的模样，回答道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"However, she replied quite naturally—","zh":"她像遭了雷殛一样，不过还装出若无其事的模样，回答道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ah! no doubt she forgot my name.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! no doubt she forgot my name.”","zh":"“啊！想必是她忘记我的名姓啦！”医生道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But perhaps,” said the doctor, “there are several Demoiselles Lempereur at Rouen who are music-mistresses.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But perhaps,” said the doctor, “there are several Demoiselles Lempereur at Rouen who are music-mistresses.”","zh":"“不过鲁昂也许有几位朗玻乐小姐教钢琴吧？”“很有可能。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Possibly!” Then quickly—“But I have my receipts here. See!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Possibly!”","zh":"然后连忙道：“可是我有她的收据，可不！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then quickly—“But I have my receipts here.","zh":"然后连忙道：“可是我有她的收据，可不！","scope":"group"},{"en":"See!”","zh":"你看。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she went to the writing-table, ransacked all the drawers, rummaged the papers, and at last lost her head so completely that Charles earnestly begged her not to take so much trouble about those wretched receipts.","sentences":[{"en":"And she went to the writing-table, ransacked all the drawers, rummaged the papers, and at last lost her head so completely that Charles earnestly begged her not to take so much trouble about those wretched receipts.","zh":"她走到书桌跟前，翻遍抽屉，搅乱纸张，临了头昏脑涨，还是不见踪影，查理再三劝她住手，犯不上为了这些无聊收据，自讨苦吃。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, I will find them,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I will find them,” she said.","zh":"“嗐！我会找到的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And, in fact, on the following Friday, as Charles was putting on one of his boots in the dark cabinet where his clothes were kept, he felt a piece of paper between the leather and his sock. He took it out and read—","sentences":[{"en":"And, in fact, on the following Friday, as Charles was putting on one of his boots in the dark cabinet where his clothes were kept, he felt a piece of paper between the leather and his sock.","zh":"果不其然，到了下星期五，他在存放衣服的黑小间换靴子，发现在一只靴子的皮和袜子之间，有一张纸，他取出来读道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He took it out and read—","zh":"果不其然，到了下星期五，他在存放衣服的黑小间换靴子，发现在一只靴子的皮和袜子之间，有一张纸，他取出来读道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Received, for three months’ lessons and several pieces of music, the sum of sixty-three francs.—Felicie Lempereur, professor of music.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Received, for three months’ lessons and several pieces of music, the sum of sixty-three francs.—Felicie Lempereur, professor of music.”","zh":"兹收到三个月教琴费及杂费共六十五法郎。音乐教师费莉西·朗玻乐。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How the devil did it get into my boots?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How the devil did it get into my boots?”","zh":"“家伙！这怎么会在我的靴子里头？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It must,” she replied, “have fallen from the old box of bills that is on the edge of the shelf.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It must,” she replied, “have fallen from the old box of bills that is on the edge of the shelf.”","zh":"她回答道：“想必是从放账单的旧纸盒里掉出去的。纸盒放在架子的边边上。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"From that moment her existence was but one long tissue of lies, in which she enveloped her love as in veils to hide it. It was a want, a mania, a pleasure carried to such an extent that if she said she had the day before walked on the right side of a road, one might know she had taken the left.","sentences":[{"en":"From that moment her existence was but one long tissue of lies, in which she enveloped her love as in veils to hide it.","zh":"从这时起，她的生活只是一连串谎话，好像面网一样，用来包藏她的爱情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a want, a mania, a pleasure carried to such an extent that if she said she had the day before walked on the right side of a road, one might know she had taken the left.","zh":"这变成一种需要、一种癖好、一种快感，以致她若说她昨天在一条街道的右侧行走的话，必须听成她在左侧行走。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One morning, when she had gone, as usual, rather lightly clothed, it suddenly began to snow, and as Charles was watching the weather from the window, he caught sight of Monsieur Bournisien in the chaise of Monsieur Tuvache, who was driving him to Rouen. Then he went down to give the priest a thick shawl that he was to hand over to Emma as soon as he reached the “Croix-Rouge.” When he got to the inn, Monsieur Bournisien asked for the wife of the Yonville doctor. The landlady replied that she very rarely came to her establishment. So that evening, when he recognised Madame Bovary in the “Hirondelle,” the cure told her his dilemma, without, however, appearing to attach much importance to it, for he began praising a preacher who was doing wonders at the Cathedral, and whom all the ladies were rushing to hear.","sentences":[{"en":"One morning, when she had gone, as usual, rather lightly clothed, it suddenly began to snow, and as Charles was watching the weather from the window, he caught sight of Monsieur Bournisien in the chaise of Monsieur Tuvache, who was driving him to Rouen.","zh":"有一天早晨，她像平时一样，衣着相当单薄，去了鲁昂，可是才一动身，天空忽然飘起雪来了；查理正在窗口看雪，望见布尔尼贤先生坐了杜法赦先生的包克到鲁昂去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he went down to give the priest a thick shawl that he was to hand over to Emma as soon as he reached the “Croix-Rouge.”","zh":"他于是跑下楼梯，拿了一条厚披肩，拜托教士，一到红十字旅馆，就递给太太。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When he got to the inn, Monsieur Bournisien asked for the wife of the Yonville doctor.","zh":"布尔尼贤前脚才进客店，就打听永镇医生太太在什么地方。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The landlady replied that she very rarely came to her establishment.","zh":"女店家回答：她很少来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So that evening, when he recognised Madame Bovary in the “Hirondelle,” the cure told her his dilemma, without, however, appearing to attach much importance to it, for he began praising a preacher who was doing wonders at the Cathedral, and whom all the ladies were rushing to hear.","zh":"临到黄昏，堂长在燕子里遇见包法利夫人，对她说起他的尴尬，不过似乎也并不怎么看重，因为他马上改口恭维一位布道师，在礼拜堂讲演，效果很好，阔太太全争先恐后来听。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Still, if he did not ask for any explanation, others, later on, might prove less discreet. So she thought well to get down each time at the “Croix-Rouge,” so that the good folk of her village who saw her on the stairs should suspect nothing.","sentences":[{"en":"Still, if he did not ask for any explanation, others, later on, might prove less discreet.","zh":"他不追根究底，难保将来别人不管闲事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So she thought well to get down each time at the “Croix-Rouge,” so that the good folk of her village who saw her on the stairs should suspect nothing.","zh":"她这样一想，觉得每次还是在“红十字”下车的好，本村正经的男女上下楼梯看见她，也就不起疑心了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One day, however, Monsieur Lheureux met her coming out of the Hotel de Boulogne on Léon’s arm; and she was frightened, thinking he would gossip. He was not such a fool. But three days after he came to her room, shut the door, and said, “I must have some money.”","sentences":[{"en":"One day, however, Monsieur Lheureux met her coming out of the Hotel de Boulogne on Léon’s arm; and she was frightened, thinking he would gossip.","zh":"但是有一天，勒乐先生遇见她走出布洛涅旅馆，挎着赖昂的胳膊。她怕起来了，以为他会张扬出去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was not such a fool.","zh":"但是有一天，勒乐先生遇见她走出布洛涅旅馆，挎着赖昂的胳膊。她怕起来了，以为他会张扬出去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But three days after he came to her room, shut the door, and said, “I must have some money.”","zh":"他不那样蠢。可是三天之后，他走进她的房间，把门关好，说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She declared she could not give him any. Lheureux burst into lamentations and reminded her of all the kindnesses he had shown her.","sentences":[{"en":"She declared she could not give him any.","zh":"“我等钱用。”她说她付不出。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lheureux burst into lamentations and reminded her of all the kindnesses he had shown her.","zh":"勒乐唉声叹气了一大阵，提起他过去待她的种种好处。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In fact, of the two bills signed by Charles, Emma up to the present had paid only one. As to the second, the shopkeeper, at her request, had consented to replace it by another, which again had been renewed for a long date. Then he drew from his pocket a list of goods not paid for; to wit, the curtains, the carpet, the material for the armchairs, several dresses, and divers articles of dress, the bills for which amounted to about two thousand francs.","sentences":[{"en":"In fact, of the two bills signed by Charles, Emma up to the present had paid only one.","zh":"查理签的两张借据，的确，爱玛直到如今，只付过一张。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to the second, the shopkeeper, at her request, had consented to replace it by another, which again had been renewed for a long date.","zh":"至于第二张，她请商人换成两张，付款日期还放得老远老远的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he drew from his pocket a list of goods not paid for; to wit, the curtains, the carpet, the material for the armchairs, several dresses, and divers articles of dress, the bills for which amounted to about two thousand francs.","zh":"他说起这话，从衣袋取出一张欠付的货单，例如窗帘、地毯、沙发料、几件衣服和一些梳洗用的零星东西，一共约莫有两千法郎。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She bowed her head. He went on—","sentences":[{"en":"She bowed her head.","zh":"她低下了头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He went on—","zh":"他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But if you haven’t any ready money, you have an estate.” And he reminded her of a miserable little hovel situated at Barneville, near Aumale, that brought in almost nothing. It had formerly been part of a small farm sold by Monsieur Bovary senior; for Lheureux knew everything, even to the number of acres and the names of the neighbours.","sentences":[{"en":"“But if you haven’t any ready money, you have an estate.”","zh":"“您没有现钱，可是您有房产呀。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he reminded her of a miserable little hovel situated at Barneville, near Aumale, that brought in almost nothing.","zh":"他说起奥马尔附近一所破烂房屋，根本没什么收益，坐落在巴恩镇，从前属于老包法利卖掉的一所小田庄。勒乐居然了如指掌，连公顷数目、邻居姓名，也都知道。他说：","scope":"group"},{"en":"It had formerly been part of a small farm sold by Monsieur Bovary senior; for Lheureux knew everything, even to the number of acres and the names of the neighbours.","zh":"他说起奥马尔附近一所破烂房屋，根本没什么收益，坐落在巴恩镇，从前属于老包法利卖掉的一所小田庄。勒乐居然了如指掌，连公顷数目、邻居姓名，也都知道。他说：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“If I were in your place,” he said, “I should clear myself of my debts, and have money left over.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If I were in your place,” he said, “I should clear myself of my debts, and have money left over.”","zh":"“我要是您呀，拿它还清债，还有多余。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She pointed out the difficulty of getting a purchaser. He held out the hope of finding one; but she asked him how she should manage to sell it.","sentences":[{"en":"She pointed out the difficulty of getting a purchaser.","zh":"她说找不到买主；他说有希望找到。她问怎么样她才能做主出卖。他回答道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He held out the hope of finding one; but she asked him how she should manage to sell it.","zh":"她说找不到买主；他说有希望找到。她问怎么样她才能做主出卖。他回答道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Haven’t you your power of attorney?” he replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“Haven’t you your power of attorney?” he replied.","zh":"“难道您没有代理人权力？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The phrase came to her like a breath of fresh air. “Leave me the bill,” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"The phrase came to her like a breath of fresh air.","zh":"她听到这话，就像一阵清风吹来一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Leave me the bill,” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛道：“您把账单留给我。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, it isn’t worth while,” answered Lheureux.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it isn’t worth while,” answered Lheureux.","zh":"勒乐回答说：“哎呀！操这份心干什么！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He came back the following week and boasted of having, after much trouble, at last discovered a certain Langlois, who, for a long time, had had an eye on the property, but without mentioning his price.","sentences":[{"en":"He came back the following week and boasted of having, after much trouble, at last discovered a certain Langlois, who, for a long time, had had an eye on the property, but without mentioning his price.","zh":"下星期他又来了，自吹自擂，说他千辛万苦，终于发现了一个人，叫朗格洛瓦的，许久以来，就在觊觎那所房产，不过没有说出买价来。她喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Never mind the price!” she cried.","sentences":[{"en":"“Never mind the price!” she cried.","zh":"“什么价钱都成！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But they would, on the contrary, have to wait, to sound the fellow. The thing was worth a journey, and, as she could not undertake it, he offered to go to the place to have an interview with Langlois. On his return he announced that the purchaser proposed four thousand francs.","sentences":[{"en":"But they would, on the contrary, have to wait, to sound the fellow.","zh":"正相反，必须等候，试探试探这家伙。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The thing was worth a journey, and, as she could not undertake it, he offered to go to the place to have an interview with Langlois.","zh":"为了这事，值得走一趟，她既然去不了，他愿意代劳，当面和朗格洛瓦讲定。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On his return he announced that the purchaser proposed four thousand francs.","zh":"待他回来，就讲：买主出到四千法郎。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma was radiant at this news.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma was radiant at this news.","zh":"爱玛听见这消息，眉飞色舞。他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Frankly,” he added, “that’s a good price.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Frankly,” he added, “that’s a good price.”","zh":"“老实讲，出价够高的啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She drew half the sum at once, and when she was about to pay her account the shopkeeper said—","sentences":[{"en":"She drew half the sum at once, and when she was about to pay her account the shopkeeper said—","zh":"她立刻收到一半议价。商人看见她要付账，又向她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It really grieves me, on my word! to see you depriving yourself all at once of such a big sum as that.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It really grieves me, on my word! to see you depriving yourself all at once of such a big sum as that.”","zh":"“这样大一笔款子，您一下子用光，天地良心，我看了可真不好受。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she looked at the bank-notes, and dreaming of the unlimited number of rendezvous represented by those two thousand francs, she stammered—","sentences":[{"en":"Then she looked at the bank-notes, and dreaming of the unlimited number of rendezvous represented by those two thousand francs, she stammered—","zh":"于是她望着钞票，想着这两千法郎能作成不计其数的幽会，不由得期期艾艾道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What! what!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What! what!”","zh":"“怎么！怎么！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh!” he went on, laughing good-naturedly, “one puts anything one likes on receipts. Don’t you think I know what household affairs are?” And he looked at her fixedly, while in his hand he held two long papers that he slid between his nails. At last, opening his pocket-book, he spread out on the table four bills to order, each for a thousand francs.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh!” he went on, laughing good-naturedly, “one puts anything one likes on receipts.","zh":"他装出一副老好人的模样，笑道：“哎呀！随便什么，全好记账的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Don’t you think I know what household affairs are?”","zh":"家里的事，我有什么不知道的。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he looked at her fixedly, while in his hand he held two long papers that he slid between his nails.","zh":"他一边盯着她看，一边捏住两张长纸，在指甲中间滑来滑去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, opening his pocket-book, he spread out on the table four bills to order, each for a thousand francs.","zh":"他最后打开皮夹，掏出四张期票，每张票面一千法郎，放在桌上。他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sign these,” he said, “and keep it all!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sign these,” he said, “and keep it all!”","zh":"“您签一个字，钱就留着用吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She cried out, scandalised.","sentences":[{"en":"She cried out, scandalised.","zh":"她觉得太不像话，叫起来了。勒乐先生厚着脸皮回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But if I give you the surplus,” replied Monsieur Lheureux impudently, “is that not helping you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But if I give you the surplus,” replied Monsieur Lheureux impudently, “is that not helping you?”","zh":"“我把多出来的差额给您，您也好说不是成全您？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And taking a pen he wrote at the bottom of the account, “Received of Madame Bovary four thousand francs.”","sentences":[{"en":"And taking a pen he wrote at the bottom of the account, “Received of Madame Bovary four thousand francs.”","zh":"于是他拿起一支笔，在货单底下写了一句：“兹收到包法利夫人四千法郎。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Now who can trouble you, since in six months you’ll draw the arrears for your cottage, and I don’t make the last bill due till after you’ve been paid?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now who can trouble you, since in six months you’ll draw the arrears for your cottage, and I don’t make the last bill due till after you’ve been paid?”","zh":"“您卖破房子的尾数，半年内可以拿到，我再把末一张期票的日期挪到付清之后，您有什么不放心的？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma grew rather confused in her calculations, and her ears tingled as if gold pieces, bursting from their bags, rang all round her on the floor. At last Lheureux explained that he had a very good friend, Vincart, a broker at Rouen, who would discount these four bills. Then he himself would hand over to madame the remainder after the actual debt was paid.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma grew rather confused in her calculations, and her ears tingled as if gold pieces, bursting from their bags, rang all round her on the floor.","zh":"爱玛计算来，计算去，绕在里头，绕不出来了，耳边听见叮叮当当，好像金币撑破口袋，在地板上围住她响个不停。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last Lheureux explained that he had a very good friend, Vincart, a broker at Rouen, who would discount these four bills.","zh":"勒乐最后解释：他有一位朋友，叫万萨的，在鲁昂开了一家银行，可以照这四张期票的数字，先行代付，等他那边付过了，扣去实际欠款，他会亲自把多余的差额给太太送过来的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he himself would hand over to madame the remainder after the actual debt was paid.","zh":"勒乐最后解释：他有一位朋友，叫万萨的，在鲁昂开了一家银行，可以照这四张期票的数字，先行代付，等他那边付过了，扣去实际欠款，他会亲自把多余的差额给太太送过来的。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But instead of two thousand francs he brought only eighteen hundred, for the friend Vincart (which was only fair) had deducted two hundred francs for commission and discount. Then he carelessly asked for a receipt.","sentences":[{"en":"But instead of two thousand francs he brought only eighteen hundred, for the friend Vincart (which was only fair) had deducted two hundred francs for commission and discount.","zh":"但是他送来的不是两千法郎，而是一千八百法郎，因为朋友万萨（按照规矩），作为佣金和回扣，扣下了两百法郎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he carelessly asked for a receipt.","zh":"接着他就漫不经心的样子，要一张收据。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You understand—in business—sometimes. And with the date, if you please, with the date.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You understand—in business—sometimes.","zh":"“您明白…交易上…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And with the date, if you please, with the date.”","zh":"有时候…写上日期，费心写上日期。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A horizon of realisable whims opened out before Emma. She was prudent enough to lay by a thousand crowns, with which the first three bills were paid when they fell due; but the fourth, by chance, came to the house on a Thursday, and Charles, quite upset, patiently awaited his wife’s return for an explanation.","sentences":[{"en":"A horizon of realisable whims opened out before Emma.","zh":"梦想可以实现了，爱玛眼前展开一片好景。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was prudent enough to lay by a thousand crowns, with which the first three bills were paid when they fell due; but the fourth, by chance, came to the house on a Thursday, and Charles, quite upset, patiently awaited his wife’s return for an explanation.","zh":"不过她也相当小心，留下一千埃居不用，按期付清头三张期票；可是第四张偏巧在星期四送来，查理栖栖惶惶，耐下心来，等太太回家解释。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"If she had not told him about this bill, it was only to spare him such domestic worries; she sat on his knees, caressed him, cooed to him, gave him a long enumeration of all the indispensable things that had been got on credit.","sentences":[{"en":"If she had not told him about this bill, it was only to spare him such domestic worries; she sat on his knees, caressed him, cooed to him, gave him a long enumeration of all the indispensable things that had been got on credit.","zh":"她先前没有告诉他这张期票的来历，只是怕他操劳家事；她坐在他的膝盖上，疼他，哄他，一桩又一桩，列举欠了账也非买不可的东西。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Really, you must confess, considering the quantity, it isn’t too dear.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Really, you must confess, considering the quantity, it isn’t too dear.”","zh":"“其实你也看得出来，买了这么多东西，要价不算太高。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles, at his wit’s end, soon had recourse to the eternal Lheureux, who swore he would arrange matters if the doctor would sign him two bills, one of which was for seven hundred francs, payable in three months. In order to arrange for this he wrote his mother a pathetic letter. Instead of sending a reply she came herself; and when Emma wanted to know whether he had got anything out of her, “Yes,” he replied; “but she wants to see the account.” The next morning at daybreak Emma ran to Lheureux to beg him to make out another account for not more than a thousand francs, for to show the one for four thousand it would be necessary to say that she had paid two-thirds, and confess, consequently, the sale of the estate—a negotiation admirably carried out by the shopkeeper, and which, in fact, was only actually known later on.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles, at his wit’s end, soon had recourse to the eternal Lheureux, who swore he would arrange matters if the doctor would sign him two bills, one of which was for seven hundred francs, payable in three months.","zh":"查理无路可走，想来想去，只得再求勒乐帮忙。他对天赌咒，说他一定息事宁人，只要老爷另立两张期票就成。一张是七百法郎，三个月付清。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In order to arrange for this he wrote his mother a pathetic letter.","zh":"他预作绸缪之计，给母亲写了一封求告的家书。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Instead of sending a reply she came herself; and when Emma wanted to know whether he had got anything out of her, “Yes,” he replied; “but she wants to see the account.”","zh":"她不写回信，亲自来了；爱玛问他有没有从她那方面挤出钱来，他回答道：“钱有。不过她先要看账。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The next morning at daybreak Emma ran to Lheureux to beg him to make out another account for not more than a thousand francs, for to show the one for four thousand it would be necessary to say that she had paid two-thirds, and confess, consequently, the sale of the estate—a negotiation admirably carried out by the shopkeeper, and which, in fact, was only actually known later on.","zh":"第二天，天才破晓，爱玛就跑到勒乐先生那边，求他另写一份账，不要超出一千法郎；因为她拿出四千法郎的账单来，就是说出她已经付过四分之三，那样一来，势必非承认变卖房产不可。交易是商人从中拉成的，直到后来，人才知道。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Despite the low price of each article, Madame Bovary senior, of course, thought the expenditure extravagant.","sentences":[{"en":"Despite the low price of each article, Madame Bovary senior, of course, thought the expenditure extravagant.","zh":"买的东西虽然件件便宜，老太太还嫌浪费。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Couldn’t you do without a carpet? Why have recovered the arm-chairs? In my time there was a single arm-chair in a house, for elderly persons—at any rate it was so at my mother’s, who was a good woman, I can tell you. Everybody can’t be rich! No fortune can hold out against waste! I should be ashamed to coddle myself as you do! And yet I am old. I need looking after. And there! there! fitting up gowns! fallals! What! silk for lining at two francs, when you can get jaconet for ten sous, or even for eight, that would do well enough!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Couldn’t you do without a carpet?","zh":"“你不好不用地毯？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why have recovered the arm-chairs?","zh":"为什么要换椅套？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In my time there was a single arm-chair in a house, for elderly persons—at any rate it was so at my mother’s, who was a good woman, I can tell you.","zh":"我那时候，家里只有一张扶手椅，还是为老年人预备的——至少我母亲是这样过来的，她可是一位正经女人，我告诉你。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everybody can’t be rich!","zh":"——世人不见得个个有钱！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No fortune can hold out against waste!","zh":"再有钱，也经不起乱花！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I should be ashamed to coddle myself as you do!","zh":"我要是像你这样贪舒服，就要脸红的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And yet I am old.","zh":"可是我上了年纪，倒正需要将息…","scope":"group"},{"en":"I need looking after.","zh":"可是我上了年纪，倒正需要将息…","scope":"group"},{"en":"And there! there! fitting up gowns! fallals!","zh":"看啊！看啊，修改衣服！摆阔！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What! silk for lining at two francs, when you can get jaconet for ten sous, or even for eight, that would do well enough!”","zh":"怎么！绸夹里，两法郎一米！其实纱布就挺好，才半法郎一米，还有八个苏一米的！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma, lying on a lounge, replied as quietly as possible—“Ah! Madame, enough! enough!”","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, lying on a lounge, replied as quietly as possible—“Ah!","zh":"爱玛仰靠在长椅上，尽最大可能，平心静气回答道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Madame, enough! enough!”","zh":"爱玛仰靠在长椅上，尽最大可能，平心静气回答道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The other went on lecturing her, predicting they would end in the workhouse. But it was Bovary’s fault. Luckily he had promised to destroy that power of attorney.","sentences":[{"en":"The other went on lecturing her, predicting they would end in the workhouse.","zh":"“哎呀！老太太，够啦！够啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But it was Bovary’s fault.","zh":"”老太太偏不住嘴，继续教训她，预先断定他们会流落到救济院的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Luckily he had promised to destroy that power of attorney.","zh":"说来说去，都是包法利的不是。幸而他答应取消那张代理书…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“怎么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! he swore he would,” went on the good woman.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! he swore he would,” went on the good woman.","zh":"老太太回答道：“啊！他赌了咒的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma opened the window, called Charles, and the poor fellow was obliged to confess the promise torn from him by his mother.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma opened the window, called Charles, and the poor fellow was obliged to confess the promise torn from him by his mother.","zh":"爱玛打开窗户，喊查理来。三面对证，可怜人只好承认是母亲逼的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma disappeared, then came back quickly, and majestically handed her a thick piece of paper.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma disappeared, then came back quickly, and majestically handed her a thick piece of paper.","zh":"爱玛跑开了，很快就又回来，气焰十足，拿一张厚纸递给她。老太太道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Thank you,” said the old woman. And she threw the power of attorney into the fire.","sentences":[{"en":"“Thank you,” said the old woman.","zh":"“我谢谢你。”她一丢就把代理书丢到火里去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And she threw the power of attorney into the fire.","zh":"“我谢谢你。”她一丢就把代理书丢到火里去了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma began to laugh, a strident, piercing, continuous laugh; she had an attack of hysterics.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma began to laugh, a strident, piercing, continuous laugh; she had an attack of hysterics.","zh":"爱玛笑了起来，笑声又尖，又响，又长：她又精神失常了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, my God!” cried Charles. “Ah! you really are wrong! You come here and make scenes with her!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, my God!” cried Charles.","zh":"查理喊道：“啊！我的上帝！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Ah! you really are wrong!","zh":"哎呀！妈，你也不对！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You come here and make scenes with her!”","zh":"你来了就跟她吵…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His mother, shrugging her shoulders, declared it was “all put on.”","sentences":[{"en":"His mother, shrugging her shoulders, declared it was “all put on.”","zh":"母亲耸耸肩膀，硬说：“这全是假招子。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Charles, rebelling for the first time, took his wife’s part, so that Madame Bovary, senior, said she would leave. She went the very next day, and on the threshold, as he was trying to detain her, she replied—","sentences":[{"en":"But Charles, rebelling for the first time, took his wife’s part, so that Madame Bovary, senior, said she would leave.","zh":"可是查理第一次反抗，找话护卫太太，老太太听不下去，不肯待了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She went the very next day, and on the threshold, as he was trying to detain her, she replied—","zh":"她第二天就走，他试着留她，她站在门口回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no! You love her better than me, and you are right. It is natural. For the rest, so much the worse! You will see. Good day—for I am not likely to come soon again, as you say, to make scenes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no! You love her better than me, and you are right.","zh":"“不必，不必啦！你爱她，胜过爱我，你对，这是天性。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It is natural.","zh":"“不必，不必啦！你爱她，胜过爱我，你对，这是天性。","scope":"group"},{"en":"For the rest, so much the worse!","zh":"反正，好不了！你等着瞧吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You will see.","zh":"当心身子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good day—for I am not likely to come soon again, as you say, to make scenes.”","zh":"因为我不会冒冒失失，再像你说的，来跟她吵的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles nevertheless was very crestfallen before Emma, who did not hide the resentment she still felt at his want of confidence, and it needed many prayers before she would consent to have another power of attorney. He even accompanied her to Monsieur Guillaumin to have a second one, just like the other, drawn up.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles nevertheless was very crestfallen before Emma, who did not hide the resentment she still felt at his want of confidence, and it needed many prayers before she would consent to have another power of attorney.","zh":"查理得罪了母亲，可是在爱玛面前，照样十分尴尬。他不信任她，她绝不隐藏她的怨恨。他左求右求，求到后来，她才勉强同意收回代理人权力。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He even accompanied her to Monsieur Guillaumin to have a second one, just like the other, drawn up.","zh":"他亲自陪她到居由曼先生的事务所，另立一份代理书，和先前的一份完全一样。公证人道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I understand,” said the notary; “a man of science can’t be worried with the practical details of life.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I understand,” said the notary; “a man of science can’t be worried with the practical details of life.”","zh":"“我明白。一位科学工作者，分不出心照管琐碎的实际生活。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And Charles felt relieved by this comfortable reflection, which gave his weakness the flattering appearance of higher pre-occupation.","sentences":[{"en":"And Charles felt relieved by this comfortable reflection, which gave his weakness the flattering appearance of higher pre-occupation.","zh":"查理听了这句奉承话，觉得心下一宽：经过恭维，他的弱点改头换面，似乎另有崇高的任务在身了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And what an outburst the next Thursday at the hotel in their room with Léon! She laughed, cried, sang, sent for sherbets, wanted to smoke cigarettes, seemed to him wild and extravagant, but adorable, superb.","sentences":[{"en":"And what an outburst the next Thursday at the hotel in their room with Léon!","zh":"下星期四，她来到旅馆他们的房间，和赖昂在一起，是怎样地热情奔放！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She laughed, cried, sang, sent for sherbets, wanted to smoke cigarettes, seemed to him wild and extravagant, but adorable, superb.","zh":"又是笑，又是哭，又是唱，又是舞，要冰镇柠檬水喝，要香烟吸，他嫌她放肆，可是又觉得她娇娆动人，出尘绝世。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He did not know what recreation of her whole being drove her more and more to plunge into the pleasures of life. She was becoming irritable, greedy, voluptuous; and she walked about the streets with him carrying her head high, without fear, so she said, of compromising herself. At times, however, Emma shuddered at the sudden thought of meeting Rodolphe, for it seemed to her that, although they were separated forever, she was not completely free from her subjugation to him.","sentences":[{"en":"He did not know what recreation of her whole being drove her more and more to plunge into the pleasures of life.","zh":"他不知道她的内心起了什么反应，越来越使她追逐人生的享乐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was becoming irritable, greedy, voluptuous; and she walked about the streets with him carrying her head high, without fear, so she said, of compromising herself.","zh":"她变得好生气，爱吃嘴，喜刺激。她和他在街上散步，扬起头来，她说，不怕出事。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At times, however, Emma shuddered at the sudden thought of meeting Rodolphe, for it seemed to her that, although they were separated forever, she was not completely free from her subjugation to him.","zh":"不过有时候，她猛然想到遇见罗道耳弗，却也畏缩起来；因为他们虽然永远分手，她觉得她还没有完全摆脱他的影响。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One night she did not return to Yonville at all. Charles lost his head with anxiety, and little Berthe would not go to bed without her mamma, and sobbed enough to break her heart. Justin had gone out searching the road at random. Monsieur Homais even had left his pharmacy.","sentences":[{"en":"One night she did not return to Yonville at all.","zh":"有一天黄昏，她没有回永镇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles lost his head with anxiety, and little Berthe would not go to bed without her mamma, and sobbed enough to break her heart.","zh":"查理急得走投无路，小白尔特没有妈妈，不肯睡觉，抽抽噎噎，心也要哭出来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Justin had gone out searching the road at random.","zh":"朱斯丹赶到大路张望。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Homais even had left his pharmacy.","zh":"郝麦先生走出了药房。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last, at eleven o’clock, able to bear it no longer, Charles harnessed his chaise, jumped in, whipped up his horse, and reached the “Croix-Rouge” about two o’clock in the morning. No one there! He thought that the clerk had perhaps seen her; but where did he live? Happily, Charles remembered his employer’s address, and rushed off there.","sentences":[{"en":"At last, at eleven o’clock, able to bear it no longer, Charles harnessed his chaise, jumped in, whipped up his horse, and reached the “Croix-Rouge” about two o’clock in the morning.","zh":"最后，等到十一点钟，查理不见她回来，再也耐不下去了，驾起他的包克，跳上去，抽打牲口，早晨两点钟左右，到了红十字旅馆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No one there!","zh":"她不在。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He thought that the clerk had perhaps seen her; but where did he live?","zh":"他心想文书也许见到她，不过他住在什么地方？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Happily, Charles remembered his employer’s address, and rushed off there.","zh":"查理幸而记起他的老板的地址。他奔去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Day was breaking, and he could distinguish the escutcheons over the door, and knocked. Someone, without opening the door, shouted out the required information, adding a few insults to those who disturb people in the middle of the night.","sentences":[{"en":"Day was breaking, and he could distinguish the escutcheons over the door, and knocked.","zh":"天才破晓。他在一家门首，看见几个牌子，就去打门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Someone, without opening the door, shouted out the required information, adding a few insults to those who disturb people in the middle of the night.","zh":"没有人开门，他问的话，有人喊着回答，还直骂那些夜晚搅扰别人的人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The house inhabited by the clerk had neither bell, knocker, nor porter. Charles knocked loudly at the shutters with his hands. A policeman happened to pass by. Then he was frightened, and went away.","sentences":[{"en":"The house inhabited by the clerk had neither bell, knocker, nor porter.","zh":"文书住的房子没有门铃，没有门环，也没有门房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles knocked loudly at the shutters with his hands.","zh":"查理握起拳头，拼命砸窗板。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A policeman happened to pass by.","zh":"过来一位巡警；查理心虚了，只好走开。他自言自语：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he was frightened, and went away.","zh":"过来一位巡警；查理心虚了，只好走开。他自言自语：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I am mad,” he said; “no doubt they kept her to dinner at Monsieur Lormeaux’.” But the Lormeaux no longer lived at Rouen.","sentences":[{"en":"“I am mad,” he said; “no doubt they kept her to dinner at Monsieur Lormeaux’.”","zh":"“我真叫傻；毫无疑问，洛尔莫先生留她用晚饭来着。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the Lormeaux no longer lived at Rouen.","zh":"洛尔莫一家已经离开鲁昂了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“She probably stayed to look after Madame Dubreuil. Why, Madame Dubreuil has been dead these ten months! Where can she be?”","sentences":[{"en":"“She probably stayed to look after Madame Dubreuil.","zh":"“她大概是待下来看护杜普勒依太太。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why, Madame Dubreuil has been dead these ten months!","zh":"哎呀！杜普勒依太太死了有十个月了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where can she be?”","zh":"她到底在什么地方？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"An idea occurred to him. At a cafe he asked for a Directory, and hurriedly looked for the name of Mademoiselle Lempereur, who lived at No. 74 Rue de la Renelle-des-Maroquiniers.","sentences":[{"en":"An idea occurred to him.","zh":"他灵机一动，走进一家咖啡馆，要《年鉴》看，很快就找到朗玻乐小姐的名字，她住在皮缰街七十四号。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At a cafe he asked for a Directory, and hurriedly looked for the name of Mademoiselle Lempereur, who lived at No. 74 Rue de la Renelle-des-Maroquiniers.","zh":"他灵机一动，走进一家咖啡馆，要《年鉴》看，很快就找到朗玻乐小姐的名字，她住在皮缰街七十四号。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"As he was turning into the street, Emma herself appeared at the other end of it. He threw himself upon her rather than embraced her, crying—","sentences":[{"en":"As he was turning into the street, Emma herself appeared at the other end of it.","zh":"他走进这条街，爱玛本人正好从另一头出来；他不是吻抱，而是扑到她身上，一边喊道：“昨天谁留住你啦？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"He threw himself upon her rather than embraced her, crying—","zh":"他走进这条街，爱玛本人正好从另一头出来；他不是吻抱，而是扑到她身上，一边喊道：“昨天谁留住你啦？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“What kept you yesterday?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What kept you yesterday?”","zh":"“我生病来着。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I was not well.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was not well.”","zh":"“什么病？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What was it? Where? How?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What was it?","zh":"住在什么地方？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where?","zh":"怎么会的？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How?”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She passed her hand over her forehead and answered, “At Mademoiselle Lempereur’s.”","sentences":[{"en":"She passed her hand over her forehead and answered, “At Mademoiselle Lempereur’s.”","zh":"她摸了摸额头，回答道：“在朗玻乐小姐家。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I was sure of it! I was going there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I was sure of it!","zh":"“我晓得是她家！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was going there.”","zh":"我正要去。”爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, it isn’t worth while,” said Emma. “She went out just now; but for the future don’t worry. I do not feel free, you see, if I know that the least delay upsets you like this.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it isn’t worth while,” said Emma.","zh":"“不必去，她方才出的门；不过以后再有这类事，你放心好了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“She went out just now; but for the future don’t worry.","zh":"“不必去，她方才出的门；不过以后再有这类事，你放心好了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I do not feel free, you see, if I know that the least delay upsets you like this.”","zh":"我回来晚一点点，你就急成这样，这么一来，你明白，我就不敢出门走动啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This was a sort of permission that she gave herself, so as to get perfect freedom in her escapades. And she profited by it freely, fully. When she was seized with the desire to see Léon, she set out upon any pretext; and as he was not expecting her on that day, she went to fetch him at his office.","sentences":[{"en":"This was a sort of permission that she gave herself, so as to get perfect freedom in her escapades.","zh":"话说在前头，以后再赴幽会，她可以毫无顾虑，为所欲为。所以她也就由着性子，加以充分利用。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And she profited by it freely, fully.","zh":"话说在前头，以后再赴幽会，她可以毫无顾虑，为所欲为。所以她也就由着性子，加以充分利用。","scope":"group"},{"en":"When she was seized with the desire to see Léon, she set out upon any pretext; and as he was not expecting her on that day, she went to fetch him at his office.","zh":"只要心血来潮，想看赖昂，她马上就随便找一个借口，去了鲁昂。他想不到她来，这一天没有在旅馆等她，她到他的事务所找他。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was a great delight at first, but soon he no longer concealed the truth, which was, that his master complained very much about these interruptions.","sentences":[{"en":"It was a great delight at first, but soon he no longer concealed the truth, which was, that his master complained very much about these interruptions.","zh":"开头几回，欢乐异常。但是没有多久，他说出了实情，就是他的老板极不赞成有人打搅。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Pshaw! come along,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Pshaw! come along,” she said.","zh":"“得啦，走吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he slipped out.","sentences":[{"en":"And he slipped out.","zh":"于是他溜出来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She wanted him to dress all in black, and grow a pointed beard, to look like the portraits of Louis XIII. She wanted to see his lodgings; thought them poor. He blushed at them, but she did not notice this, then advised him to buy some curtains like hers, and as he objected to the expense—","sentences":[{"en":"She wanted him to dress all in black, and grow a pointed beard, to look like the portraits of Louis XIII.","zh":"她要他穿一身黑，下巴留一撮尖胡须，模仿路易十三的肖像。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wanted to see his lodgings; thought them poor.","zh":"她想认识他的住处，看过以后，嫌它寒酸；他一听这话，臊红了脸，她满不在乎。随后她劝他买些和她家里一样的窗帘，他嫌浪费，她笑道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He blushed at them, but she did not notice this, then advised him to buy some curtains like hers, and as he objected to the expense—","zh":"她想认识他的住处，看过以后，嫌它寒酸；他一听这话，臊红了脸，她满不在乎。随后她劝他买些和她家里一样的窗帘，他嫌浪费，她笑道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ah! ah! you care for your money,” she said laughing.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! ah! you care for your money,” she said laughing.","zh":"“哈！哈！你舍不得你的宝贝钱啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Each time Léon had to tell her everything that he had done since their last meeting. She asked him for some verses—some verses “for herself,” a “love poem” in honour of her. But he never succeeded in getting a rhyme for the second verse; and at last ended by copying a sonnet in a “Keepsake.” This was less from vanity than from the one desire of pleasing her. He did not question her ideas; he accepted all her tastes; he was rather becoming her mistress than she his. She had tender words and kisses that thrilled his soul. Where could she have learnt this corruption almost incorporeal in the strength of its profanity and dissimulation?","sentences":[{"en":"Each time Léon had to tell her everything that he had done since their last meeting.","zh":"赖昂必须回回向她报告：从上次幽会起，他这期间，都做了些什么。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She asked him for some verses—some verses “for herself,” a “love poem” in honour of her.","zh":"她问他要诗、一首为她写出来的诗、一首献给她的情诗；第二行韵脚，他搜索枯肠，也配对不出，结局就是从纪念册上抄一首十四行诗交卷。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But he never succeeded in getting a rhyme for the second verse; and at last ended by copying a sonnet in a “Keepsake.”","zh":"她问他要诗、一首为她写出来的诗、一首献给她的情诗；第二行韵脚，他搜索枯肠，也配对不出，结局就是从纪念册上抄一首十四行诗交卷。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This was less from vanity than from the one desire of pleasing her.","zh":"他这样做，不是出于虚荣，而是为了讨她的欢心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He did not question her ideas; he accepted all her tastes; he was rather becoming her mistress than she his.","zh":"他不反驳她的见解；他接受她的一切爱好；与其说她是他的情妇，倒不如说，他变成她的情夫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had tender words and kisses that thrilled his soul.","zh":"她有温存的语言和销魂的吻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where could she have learnt this corruption almost incorporeal in the strength of its profanity and dissimulation?","zh":"这种妖媚，表面上看不出什么，实际上出神入化，到了无迹可寻的地步，奇怪，她从什么地方学来的？","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-6","part":3,"n":6,"title":"Part III · Chapter 6","titleZh":"下卷 · 6","paragraphs":[{"en":"During the journeys he made to see her, Léon had often dined at the chemist’s, and he felt obliged from politeness to invite him in turn.","sentences":[{"en":"During the journeys he made to see her, Léon had often dined at the chemist’s, and he felt obliged from politeness to invite him in turn.","zh":"赖昂下乡看她，常在药剂师家用晚饭，觉得应当还请才对。郝麦先生回答他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“With pleasure!” Monsieur Homais replied; “besides, I must invigorate my mind, for I am getting rusty here. We’ll go to the theatre, to the restaurant; we’ll make a night of it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“With pleasure!”","zh":"“愿意之至！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Homais replied; “besides, I must invigorate my mind, for I am getting rusty here.","zh":"再说，我老待在这里，快要长锈了，也该活动活动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We’ll go to the theatre, to the restaurant; we’ll make a night of it.”","zh":"我们去看看戏，吃吃馆子，玩它一个痛快！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, my dear!” tenderly murmured Madame Homais, alarmed at the vague perils he was preparing to brave.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, my dear!” tenderly murmured Madame Homais, alarmed at the vague perils he was preparing to brave.","zh":"郝麦太太一听他有意去冒那些无名的危险，心惊胆战，情之所至，低声阻拦道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, what? Do you think I’m not sufficiently ruining my health living here amid the continual emanations of the pharmacy? But there! that is the way with women! They are jealous of science, and then are opposed to our taking the most legitimate distractions. No matter! Count upon me. One of these days I shall turn up at Rouen, and we’ll go the pace together.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, what?","zh":"“啊！好人！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Do you think I’m not sufficiently ruining my health living here amid the continual emanations of the pharmacy?","zh":"“嗐，这有什么？你以为我经年待在药房，一天到晚闻气味，就不糟蹋我的身子啦？","scope":"group"},{"en":"But there! that is the way with women!","zh":"“嗐，这有什么？你以为我经年待在药房，一天到晚闻气味，就不糟蹋我的身子啦？","scope":"group"},{"en":"They are jealous of science, and then are opposed to our taking the most legitimate distractions.","zh":"可不，这就是女人的特征：她们忌妒科学，然后就反对最正当的娱乐。","scope":"group"},{"en":"No matter!","zh":"可不，这就是女人的特征：她们忌妒科学，然后就反对最正当的娱乐。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Count upon me.","zh":"没有关系，我一定来，我说不定哪一天就来鲁昂，我们一道把洋钱用光算数。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"One of these days I shall turn up at Rouen, and we’ll go the pace together.”","zh":"没有关系，我一定来，我说不定哪一天就来鲁昂，我们一道把洋钱用光算数。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The druggist would formerly have taken good care not to use such an expression, but he was cultivating a gay Parisian style, which he thought in the best taste; and, like his neighbour, Madame Bovary, he questioned the clerk curiously about the customs of the capital; he even talked slang to dazzle the bourgeois, saying bender, crummy, dandy, macaroni, the cheese, cut my stick and “I’ll hook it,” for “I am going.”","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist would formerly have taken good care not to use such an expression, but he was cultivating a gay Parisian style, which he thought in the best taste; and, like his neighbour, Madame Bovary, he questioned the clerk curiously about the customs of the capital; he even talked slang to dazzle the bourgeois, saying bender, crummy, dandy, macaroni, the cheese, cut my stick and “I’ll hook it,” for “I am going.”","zh":"这样的话，药剂师先前没有说过；然而他如今看中快活的巴黎派头，认为最得风气之先，所以也像他的邻居包法利夫人一样，向文书再三打听京城风俗，甚至于话里掺上切口，来唬…资产者，说窝、摊、新潮、摩登、柏奈达路，还有，不说“我去了”，而说“我颠儿了”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"So one Thursday Emma was surprised to meet Monsieur Homais in the kitchen of the “Lion d’Or,” wearing a traveller’s costume, that is to say, wrapped in an old cloak which no one knew he had, while he carried a valise in one hand and the foot-warmer of his establishment in the other. He had confided his intentions to no one, for fear of causing the public anxiety by his absence.","sentences":[{"en":"So one Thursday Emma was surprised to meet Monsieur Homais in the kitchen of the “Lion d’Or,” wearing a traveller’s costume, that is to say, wrapped in an old cloak which no one knew he had, while he carried a valise in one hand and the foot-warmer of his establishment in the other.","zh":"果然有一个星期四，爱玛她意想不到会在金狮的厨房遇见郝麦先生，穿着旅行装，就是说，披一件谁也没有见过的旧斗篷，一只手提一只小箱，另一只手提了一只药房的脚炉，他唯恐公众见他不在，大惊小怪，因而没有同任何人讲起他的计划。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He had confided his intentions to no one, for fear of causing the public anxiety by his absence.","zh":"果然有一个星期四，爱玛她意想不到会在金狮的厨房遇见郝麦先生，穿着旅行装，就是说，披一件谁也没有见过的旧斗篷，一只手提一只小箱，另一只手提了一只药房的脚炉，他唯恐公众见他不在，大惊小怪，因而没有同任何人讲起他的计划。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The idea of seeing again the place where his youth had been spent no doubt excited him, for during the whole journey he never ceased talking, and as soon as he had arrived, he jumped quickly out of the diligence to go in search of Léon. In vain the clerk tried to get rid of him. Monsieur Homais dragged him off to the large Cafe de la Normandie, which he entered majestically, not raising his hat, thinking it very provincial to uncover in any public place.","sentences":[{"en":"The idea of seeing again the place where his youth had been spent no doubt excited him, for during the whole journey he never ceased talking, and as soon as he had arrived, he jumped quickly out of the diligence to go in search of Léon.","zh":"重游旧地的想法，毫无疑问，使他意兴盎然，所以一路上话不绝口。他不等车停，连忙跳下，寻找赖昂；文书推托不去，经不起郝麦先生强拉，还是把他拉到诺曼底咖啡馆去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In vain the clerk tried to get rid of him.","zh":"重游旧地的想法，毫无疑问，使他意兴盎然，所以一路上话不绝口。他不等车停，连忙跳下，寻找赖昂；文书推托不去，经不起郝麦先生强拉，还是把他拉到诺曼底咖啡馆去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Homais dragged him off to the large Cafe de la Normandie, which he entered majestically, not raising his hat, thinking it very provincial to uncover in any public place.","zh":"药剂师大摇大摆，走进咖啡馆，帽子不摘，以为在公共场所露出光头，十分土气。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma waited for Léon three quarters of an hour. At last she ran to his office; and, lost in all sorts of conjectures, accusing him of indifference, and reproaching herself for her weakness, she spent the afternoon, her face pressed against the window-panes.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma waited for Léon three quarters of an hour.","zh":"爱玛等赖昂等了三刻钟，不见他来，跑到事务所找他，照样无影无踪，猜来猜去，莫名其妙。她骂他无情，怨自己心软，额头贴住玻璃，气闷了一下午。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last she ran to his office; and, lost in all sorts of conjectures, accusing him of indifference, and reproaching herself for her weakness, she spent the afternoon, her face pressed against the window-panes.","zh":"爱玛等赖昂等了三刻钟，不见他来，跑到事务所找他，照样无影无踪，猜来猜去，莫名其妙。她骂他无情，怨自己心软，额头贴住玻璃，气闷了一下午。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"At two o’clock they were still at a table opposite each other. The large room was emptying; the stove-pipe, in the shape of a palm-tree, spread its gilt leaves over the white ceiling, and near them, outside the window, in the bright sunshine, a little fountain gurgled in a white basin, where; in the midst of watercress and asparagus, three torpid lobsters stretched across to some quails that lay heaped up in a pile on their sides.","sentences":[{"en":"At two o’clock they were still at a table opposite each other.","zh":"已经两点钟了，他们面对面，坐在桌子前。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The large room was emptying; the stove-pipe, in the shape of a palm-tree, spread its gilt leaves over the white ceiling, and near them, outside the window, in the bright sunshine, a little fountain gurgled in a white basin, where; in the midst of watercress and asparagus, three torpid lobsters stretched across to some quails that lay heaped up in a pile on their sides.","zh":"大厅空空落落；炉管是棕榈树模样，枝叶镀金，在白色天花板上散成绚烂一片；靠近他们，玻璃窗外，太阳地里，有一个小喷泉，淙淙琤琤，流在大理石水池：池里有水芹和石刀柏，当中爬着三条龙虾，昏昏沉沉，躺在一堆侧卧的鹌鹑旁边。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais was enjoying himself. Although he was even more intoxicated with the luxury than the rich fare, the Pommard wine all the same rather excited his faculties; and when the omelette au rhum appeared, he began propounding immoral theories about women. What seduced him above all else was chic. He admired an elegant toilette in a well-furnished apartment, and as to bodily qualities, he didn’t dislike a young girl.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais was enjoying himself.","zh":"郝麦兴高采烈，其乐陶陶，虽说使他有了醉意的，与其说是美酒盛馔，不如说是豪华气派。不过喝到波马尔葡萄酒 ，他也有点飘飘然了，甘蔗酒煎鸡蛋端来的时候，他正在发挥关于女人的有伤风化的理论。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Although he was even more intoxicated with the luxury than the rich fare, the Pommard wine all the same rather excited his faculties; and when the omelette au rhum appeared, he began propounding immoral theories about women.","zh":"郝麦兴高采烈，其乐陶陶，虽说使他有了醉意的，与其说是美酒盛馔，不如说是豪华气派。不过喝到波马尔葡萄酒 ，他也有点飘飘然了，甘蔗酒煎鸡蛋端来的时候，他正在发挥关于女人的有伤风化的理论。","scope":"group"},{"en":"What seduced him above all else was chic.","zh":"郝麦兴高采烈，其乐陶陶，虽说使他有了醉意的，与其说是美酒盛馔，不如说是豪华气派。不过喝到波马尔葡萄酒 ，他也有点飘飘然了，甘蔗酒煎鸡蛋端来的时候，他正在发挥关于女人的有伤风化的理论。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He admired an elegant toilette in a well-furnished apartment, and as to bodily qualities, he didn’t dislike a young girl.","zh":"最打动他的就是俏。他醉心于服装优雅和家具高贵的房间。至于形体，他不讨厌小巧玲珑。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon watched the clock in despair. The druggist went on drinking, eating, and talking.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon watched the clock in despair.","zh":"赖昂望着挂钟，内心如捣。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The druggist went on drinking, eating, and talking.","zh":"药剂师喝着，吃着，说着，无限快活。他忽然道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You must be very lonely,” he said suddenly, “here at Rouen. To be sure your lady-love doesn’t live far away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You must be very lonely,” he said suddenly, “here at Rouen.","zh":"“您在鲁昂，一定很感寂寞。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To be sure your lady-love doesn’t live far away.”","zh":"其实您的对象住得也并不远。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the other blushed—","sentences":[{"en":"And the other blushed—","zh":"看见对方脸红，他问下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come now, be frank. Can you deny that at Yonville—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come now, be frank.","zh":"“好，坦白吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Can you deny that at Yonville—”","zh":"您能否认您在永镇…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The young man stammered something.","sentences":[{"en":"The young man stammered something.","zh":"年轻人期期艾艾，不知所云。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“At Madame Bovary’s, you’re not making love to—”","sentences":[{"en":"“At Madame Bovary’s, you’re not making love to—”","zh":"“您在包法利太太家，不是追…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“To whom?”","sentences":[{"en":"“To whom?”","zh":"“追谁？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The servant!”","sentences":[{"en":"“The servant!”","zh":"“丫头！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was not joking; but vanity getting the better of all prudence, Léon, in spite of himself protested. Besides, he only liked dark women.","sentences":[{"en":"He was not joking; but vanity getting the better of all prudence, Léon, in spite of himself protested.","zh":"他不说笑；但在赖昂，虚荣心压倒了一切谨慎，冒冒失失，就绝口否认了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, he only liked dark women.","zh":"再说，他只爱棕色头发女人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I approve of that,” said the chemist; “they have more passion.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I approve of that,” said the chemist; “they have more passion.”","zh":"药剂师道：“我同意；她们比较淫荡。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And whispering into his friend’s ear, he pointed out the symptoms by which one could find out if a woman had passion. He even launched into an ethnographic digression: the German was vapourish, the French woman licentious, the Italian passionate.","sentences":[{"en":"And whispering into his friend’s ear, he pointed out the symptoms by which one could find out if a woman had passion.","zh":"他于是俯在朋友耳边，列举辨别女人淫荡的标志。他甚至于掉转话锋，大谈人种学：德意志女人悒郁，法兰西女人轻佻，意大利女人热情。文书问道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He even launched into an ethnographic digression: the German was vapourish, the French woman licentious, the Italian passionate.","zh":"他于是俯在朋友耳边，列举辨别女人淫荡的标志。他甚至于掉转话锋，大谈人种学：德意志女人悒郁，法兰西女人轻佻，意大利女人热情。文书问道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“And negresses?” asked the clerk.","sentences":[{"en":"“And negresses?” asked the clerk.","zh":"“黑种女人呢？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“They are an artistic taste!” said Homais. “Waiter! two cups of coffee!”","sentences":[{"en":"“They are an artistic taste!” said Homais.","zh":"郝麦道：“这是艺术家的雅好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Waiter! two cups of coffee!”","zh":"伙计！两小杯咖啡！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Are we going?” at last asked Léon impatiently.","sentences":[{"en":"“Are we going?” at last asked Léon impatiently.","zh":"赖昂不耐烦了，终于说道：“我们走吧？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Ja!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ja!”","zh":"赖昂不耐烦了，终于说道：“我们走吧？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But before leaving he wanted to see the proprietor of the establishment and made him a few compliments. Then the young man, to be alone, alleged he had some business engagement.","sentences":[{"en":"But before leaving he wanted to see the proprietor of the establishment and made him a few compliments.","zh":"“Yes. ”不过他走以前，要见见老板，夸奖两句酒菜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the young man, to be alone, alleged he had some business engagement.","zh":"年轻人一听这话，就说有事，希望借机溜掉。郝麦道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! I will escort you,” said Homais.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"“好啊，我护送你走！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I will escort you,” said Homais.","zh":"“好啊，我护送你走！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And all the while he was walking through the streets with him he talked of his wife, his children; of their future, and of his business; told him in what a decayed condition it had formerly been, and to what a degree of perfection he had raised it.","sentences":[{"en":"And all the while he was walking through the streets with him he talked of his wife, his children; of their future, and of his business; told him in what a decayed condition it had formerly been, and to what a degree of perfection he had raised it.","zh":"他一边陪他在街上行走，一边说起他的太太、他的子女、他们的未来和他的药房，讲它先前如何不景气，经他历年整顿，达到了完善的地步。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Arrived in front of the Hotel de Boulogne, Léon left him abruptly, ran up the stairs, and found his mistress in great excitement. At mention of the chemist she flew into a passion. He, however, piled up good reasons; it wasn’t his fault; didn’t she know Homais—did she believe that he would prefer his company? But she turned away; he drew her back, and, sinking on his knees, clasped her waist with his arms in a languorous pose, full of concupiscence and supplication.","sentences":[{"en":"Arrived in front of the Hotel de Boulogne, Léon left him abruptly, ran up the stairs, and found his mistress in great excitement.","zh":"走到布洛涅旅馆前面，赖昂出其不意，丢下了他，跑上楼梯，发现他的情妇焦灼惶惑，百无聊赖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At mention of the chemist she flew into a passion.","zh":"不提药剂师还好，提起他来，她就冒火。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He, however, piled up good reasons; it wasn’t his fault; didn’t she know Homais—did she believe that he would prefer his company?","zh":"然而错不在他，他举出种种理由解说：难道她不了解郝麦先生？难道她会相信他喜欢和他在一起？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she turned away; he drew her back, and, sinking on his knees, clasped her waist with his arms in a languorous pose, full of concupiscence and supplication.","zh":"但是她不理他，转开了身子；他拉她回来，跪在地上，搂住她的腰，一副撒娇的可怜相，充满情欲和哀求。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was standing up, her large flashing eyes looked at him seriously, almost terribly. Then tears obscured them, her red eyelids were lowered, she gave him her hands, and Léon was pressing them to his lips when a servant appeared to tell the gentleman that he was wanted.","sentences":[{"en":"She was standing up, her large flashing eyes looked at him seriously, almost terribly.","zh":"她站直了，眼睛冒火，睁大了望他，模样不但严肃，简直有些可怕了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then tears obscured them, her red eyelids were lowered, she gave him her hands, and Léon was pressing them to his lips when a servant appeared to tell the gentleman that he was wanted.","zh":"接着她就泪眼模糊，红眼皮耷拉下来，把两只手给了他。赖昂正在吻手，就见进来一个茶房，回禀先生：有人找他。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You will come back?” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“You will come back?” she said.","zh":"“你还回来？”“对。”“什么时候？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.”","zh":"“这就回来。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“But when?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But when?”","zh":"“这就回来。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Immediately.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Immediately.”","zh":"药剂师一见赖昂就道：“我用的是计。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“It’s a trick,” said the chemist, when he saw Léon. “I wanted to interrupt this visit, that seemed to me to annoy you. Let’s go and have a glass of garus at Bridoux’.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It’s a trick,” said the chemist, when he saw Léon.","zh":"药剂师一见赖昂就道：“我用的是计。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“I wanted to interrupt this visit, that seemed to me to annoy you.","zh":"我想你也不高兴见别人，还是帮你打断了的好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let’s go and have a glass of garus at Bridoux’.”","zh":"我们到布里杜那儿喝一杯嘉吕斯 去。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon vowed that he must get back to his office. Then the druggist joked him about quill-drivers and the law.","sentences":[{"en":"Léon vowed that he must get back to his office.","zh":"赖昂赌咒发誓，说他非回事务所不可。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the druggist joked him about quill-drivers and the law.","zh":"药剂师听见这话，就打趣公文、诉讼手续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Leave Cujas and Barthole alone a bit. Who the devil prevents you? Be a man! Let’s go to Bridoux’. You’ll see his dog. It’s very interesting.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Leave Cujas and Barthole alone a bit.","zh":"“去他妈的居雅斯和巴尔托勒 吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who the devil prevents you?","zh":"谁拦着你？大丈夫，说走就走！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Be a man!","zh":"谁拦着你？大丈夫，说走就走！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Let’s go to Bridoux’.","zh":"去布里杜家！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You’ll see his dog.","zh":"看看他的狗，有趣极了！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s very interesting.”","zh":"看看他的狗，有趣极了！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And as the clerk still insisted—","sentences":[{"en":"And as the clerk still insisted—","zh":"他看文书执意不肯，就改口道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I’ll go with you. I’ll read a paper while I wait for you, or turn over the leaves of a ‘Code.’”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ll go with you.","zh":"他看文书执意不肯，就改口道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll read a paper while I wait for you, or turn over the leaves of a ‘Code.’”","zh":"“我也到你的事务所去，我看报等你，要不然就翻翻法典也好。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Léon, bewildered by Emma’s anger, Monsieur Homais’ chatter, and, perhaps, by the heaviness of the luncheon, was undecided, and, as it were, fascinated by the chemist, who kept repeating—","sentences":[{"en":"Léon, bewildered by Emma’s anger, Monsieur Homais’ chatter, and, perhaps, by the heaviness of the luncheon, was undecided, and, as it were, fascinated by the chemist, who kept repeating—","zh":"爱玛的愤怒、郝麦先生的絮叨，或许还有午饭的饱胀，把赖昂折腾得迷迷糊糊，现在经他这样一来，简直失了主张。他像受了蛊惑一样，听见药剂师重复：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Let’s go to Bridoux’. It’s just by here, in the Rue Malpalu.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Let’s go to Bridoux’.","zh":"“去马耳巴吕街布里杜家，也就是两步路。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s just by here, in the Rue Malpalu.”","zh":"“去马耳巴吕街布里杜家，也就是两步路。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then, through cowardice, through stupidity, through that indefinable feeling that drags us into the most distasteful acts, he allowed himself to be led off to Bridoux’, whom they found in his small yard, superintending three workmen, who panted as they turned the large wheel of a machine for making seltzer-water. Homais gave them some good advice. He embraced Bridoux; they took some garus. Twenty times Léon tried to escape, but the other seized him by the arm saying—","sentences":[{"en":"Then, through cowardice, through stupidity, through that indefinable feeling that drags us into the most distasteful acts, he allowed himself to be led off to Bridoux’, whom they found in his small yard, superintending three workmen, who panted as they turned the large wheel of a machine for making seltzer-water.","zh":"由于懦弱、愚蠢和导致人们做违心之事的卑怯，他到底还是让他拉到布里杜家去了。他们在他的小院看见他，监督三个伙计，喘着气，转动一架酿造塞兹水的机器的大轮子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais gave them some good advice.","zh":"郝麦帮他们出主意，吻抱布里杜，要嘉吕斯喝。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He embraced Bridoux; they took some garus.","zh":"郝麦帮他们出主意，吻抱布里杜，要嘉吕斯喝。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Twenty times Léon tried to escape, but the other seized him by the arm saying—","zh":"赖昂一连二十次想走；可是另一位揪住他的胳膊，对他讲：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Presently! I’m coming! We’ll go to the ‘Fanal de Rouen’ to see the fellows there. I’ll introduce you to Thornassin.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Presently!","zh":"“一会儿工夫！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’m coming!","zh":"“一会儿工夫！","scope":"group"},{"en":"We’ll go to the ‘Fanal de Rouen’ to see the fellows there.","zh":"我这就走，我们去《鲁昂烽火》，看看报社的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ll introduce you to Thornassin.”","zh":"我介绍您认识托玛散。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last he managed to get rid of him, and rushed straight to the hotel. Emma was no longer there. She had just gone in a fit of anger. She detested him now. This failing to keep their rendezvous seemed to her an insult, and she tried to rake up other reasons to separate herself from him. He was incapable of heroism, weak, banal, more spiritless than a woman, avaricious too, and cowardly.","sentences":[{"en":"At last he managed to get rid of him, and rushed straight to the hotel.","zh":"他总算甩掉了他，一口气跑到旅馆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma was no longer there.","zh":"爱玛已经不在了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had just gone in a fit of anger.","zh":"她怒火冲天，方才离开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She detested him now.","zh":"她如今恨他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This failing to keep their rendezvous seemed to her an insult, and she tried to rake up other reasons to separate herself from him.","zh":"在她看来，爽约是一种侮辱。她想多找一些借口，索性摆脱他：他没有英雄气概，软弱，平庸，不及女人刚强，而且吝啬，胆小如鼠。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was incapable of heroism, weak, banal, more spiritless than a woman, avaricious too, and cowardly.","zh":"在她看来，爽约是一种侮辱。她想多找一些借口，索性摆脱他：他没有英雄气概，软弱，平庸，不及女人刚强，而且吝啬，胆小如鼠。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then, growing calmer, she at length discovered that she had, no doubt, calumniated him. But the disparaging of those we love always alienates us from them to some extent. We must not touch our idols; the gilt sticks to our fingers.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, growing calmer, she at length discovered that she had, no doubt, calumniated him.","zh":"接着她又平静下来，终于觉得自己无疑冤枉了他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the disparaging of those we love always alienates us from them to some extent.","zh":"不过一旦贬责我们心爱的人，或多或少总要形成彼此之间的隔阂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We must not touch our idols; the gilt sticks to our fingers.","zh":"偶像是碰不得的：一碰之后，就有金粉留在手上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They gradually came to talking more frequently of matters outside their love, and in the letters that Emma wrote him she spoke of flowers, verses, the moon and the stars, naive resources of a waning passion striving to keep itself alive by all external aids. She was constantly promising herself a profound felicity on her next journey. Then she confessed to herself that she felt nothing extraordinary. This disappointment quickly gave way to a new hope, and Emma returned to him more inflamed, more eager than ever. She undressed brutally, tearing off the thin laces of her corset that nestled around her hips like a gliding snake. She went on tiptoe, barefooted, to see once more that the door was closed, then, pale, serious, and, without speaking, with one movement, she threw herself upon his breast with a long shudder.","sentences":[{"en":"They gradually came to talking more frequently of matters outside their love, and in the letters that Emma wrote him she spoke of flowers, verses, the moon and the stars, naive resources of a waning passion striving to keep itself alive by all external aids.","zh":"他们的谈话越来越和爱情无关。爱玛给他写信，离不开花、诗、月亮、星星——热情衰退之后的这些稚拙手段，无非是借重外援来使热情复苏。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was constantly promising herself a profound felicity on her next journey.","zh":"她总在期许下次幽会无限幸福，事后却承认毫无惊人之处。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she confessed to herself that she felt nothing extraordinary.","zh":"她总在期许下次幽会无限幸福，事后却承认毫无惊人之处。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This disappointment quickly gave way to a new hope, and Emma returned to him more inflamed, more eager than ever.","zh":"爱玛觉得扫兴，可是一种新的希望又很快起而代之，回到他的身旁，分外炽热，分外情急。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She undressed brutally, tearing off the thin laces of her corset that nestled around her hips like a gliding snake.","zh":"她脱衣服，说脱就脱，揪开束腰的细带，细带兜着她的屁股，窸窸窣窣，像一条蛇，溜来溜去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She went on tiptoe, barefooted, to see once more that the door was closed, then, pale, serious, and, without speaking, with one movement, she threw herself upon his breast with a long shudder.","zh":"她光着脚，踮起脚尖，走到门边，再看一回关好了没有；一看关好了，她一下子把衣服脱得一丝不挂，然后——脸色苍白，不言不语，神情严肃，贴住他的胸脯，浑身打颤，久久不已。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Yet there was upon that brow covered with cold drops, on those quivering lips, in those wild eyes, in the strain of those arms, something vague and dreary that seemed to Léon to glide between them subtly as if to separate them.","sentences":[{"en":"Yet there was upon that brow covered with cold drops, on those quivering lips, in those wild eyes, in the strain of those arms, something vague and dreary that seemed to Léon to glide between them subtly as if to separate them.","zh":"但是在这冷汗涔涔的额头上，在这期期艾艾的嘴唇上，在这双迷惘的瞳仁里，在这两只胳膊搂抱之中，赖昂觉得像有什么极端的，模模糊糊、凄惨悲切的东西，神不知鬼不觉地，轻悠悠来到他们中间，要把他们分开。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He did not dare to question her; but, seeing her so skilled, she must have passed, he thought, through every experience of suffering and of pleasure. What had once charmed now frightened him a little. Besides, he rebelled against his absorption, daily more marked, by her personality. He begrudged Emma this constant victory. He even strove not to love her; then, when he heard the creaking of her boots, he turned coward, like drunkards at the sight of strong drinks.","sentences":[{"en":"He did not dare to question her; but, seeing her so skilled, she must have passed, he thought, through every experience of suffering and of pleasure.","zh":"他不敢盘问她；不过他见她经验丰富，总觉得她过去一定经过各色苦乐的考验。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What had once charmed now frightened him a little.","zh":"一样风情，从前倾倒，现在他有一点害怕了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, he rebelled against his absorption, daily more marked, by her personality.","zh":"而且他反抗她的一天大似一天的统治，这种持久的胜利使他怨恨爱玛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He begrudged Emma this constant victory.","zh":"而且他反抗她的一天大似一天的统治，这种持久的胜利使他怨恨爱玛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He even strove not to love her; then, when he heard the creaking of her boots, he turned coward, like drunkards at the sight of strong drinks.","zh":"他甚至企图不再爱她；可是她的小靴一咯噔，他便把持不住，就像醉鬼见到了烈酒一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She did not fail, in truth, to lavish all sorts of attentions upon him, from the delicacies of food to the coquettries of dress and languishing looks. She brought roses to her breast from Yonville, which she threw into his face; was anxious about his health, gave him advice as to his conduct; and, in order the more surely to keep her hold on him, hoping perhaps that heaven would take her part, she tied a medal of the Virgin round his neck. She inquired like a virtuous mother about his companions. She said to him—","sentences":[{"en":"She did not fail, in truth, to lavish all sorts of attentions upon him, from the delicacies of food to the coquettries of dress and languishing looks.","zh":"的确，她对他的关心，从菜肴的精美，直到服装的俏丽和视线的缠绵，无所不包，无微不至。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She brought roses to her breast from Yonville, which she threw into his face; was anxious about his health, gave him advice as to his conduct; and, in order the more surely to keep her hold on him, hoping perhaps that heaven would take her part, she tied a medal of the Virgin round his neck.","zh":"她从永镇来，怀里揣着玫瑰，见了他，朝他脸上一丢。她担心他的健康，指点他的行为。她要他一心和她相好，希望得到上天协助，往他的脖子挂了一个圣母像牌。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She inquired like a virtuous mother about his companions.","zh":"她仿佛一位圣洁的母亲，问起他的朋友。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She said to him—","zh":"她对他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Don’t see them; don’t go out; think only of ourselves; love me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t see them; don’t go out; think only of ourselves; love me!”","zh":"“别见他们，别出去，就想着我们自己；爱我！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She would have liked to be able to watch over his life; and the idea occurred to her of having him followed in the streets. Near the hotel there was always a kind of loafer who accosted travellers, and who would not refuse. But her pride revolted at this.","sentences":[{"en":"She would have liked to be able to watch over his life; and the idea occurred to her of having him followed in the streets.","zh":"她希望自己能监视他的生活，又想派人到街上盯他的梢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Near the hotel there was always a kind of loafer who accosted travellers, and who would not refuse.","zh":"旅馆附近，总有一个流氓似的人招呼旅客，他不会不肯的…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But her pride revolted at this.","zh":"不过她的自尊心不许她这样做。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Bah! so much the worse. Let him deceive me! What does it matter to me? As If I cared for him!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Bah! so much the worse.","zh":"“嗐，活该！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Let him deceive me!","zh":"他要是欺骗我，由他去！","scope":"group"},{"en":"What does it matter to me?","zh":"他要是欺骗我，由他去！","scope":"group"},{"en":"As If I cared for him!”","zh":"难道我在乎？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One day, when they had parted early and she was returning alone along the boulevard, she saw the walls of her convent; then she sat down on a form in the shade of the elm-trees. How calm that time had been! How she longed for the ineffable sentiments of love that she had tried to figure to herself out of books! The first month of her marriage, her rides in the wood, the viscount that waltzed, and Lagardy singing, all repassed before her eyes. And Léon suddenly appeared to her as far off as the others.","sentences":[{"en":"One day, when they had parted early and she was returning alone along the boulevard, she saw the walls of her convent; then she sat down on a form in the shade of the elm-trees.","zh":"有一天，他们散得早，她独自在马路溜达，望见她的修道院的墙壁；她坐在榆树树荫下一条长凳上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How calm that time had been!","zh":"当年有多安静！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How she longed for the ineffable sentiments of love that she had tried to figure to herself out of books!","zh":"那些不能言喻的恋爱心情，她试着照书本虚构出来的心情，她如今又多向往！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The first month of her marriage, her rides in the wood, the viscount that waltzed, and Lagardy singing, all repassed before her eyes.","zh":"她的新婚期间、她骑马在森林的漫游、跳华尔兹的子爵和歌唱的拉嘉尔狄…又都在她的眼前出现。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And Léon suddenly appeared to her as far off as the others.","zh":"赖昂犹如别人，她忽然觉得同样遥远。她问自己道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet I love him,” she said to herself.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet I love him,” she said to herself.","zh":"“可是我在爱着他啊！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"No matter! She was not happy—she never had been. Whence came this insufficiency in life—this instantaneous turning to decay of everything on which she leant? But if there were somewhere a being strong and beautiful, a valiant nature, full at once of exaltation and refinement, a poet’s heart in an angel’s form, a lyre with sounding chords ringing out elegiac epithalamia to heaven, why, perchance, should she not find him? Ah! how impossible! Besides, nothing was worth the trouble of seeking it; everything was a lie. Every smile hid a yawn of boredom, every joy a curse, all pleasure satiety, and the sweetest kisses left upon your lips only the unattainable desire for a greater delight.","sentences":[{"en":"No matter!","zh":"有什么关系！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was not happy—she never had been.","zh":"反正她不快乐，也从来没有快乐过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Whence came this insufficiency in life—this instantaneous turning to decay of everything on which she leant?","zh":"何以人生总不如意？何以她信赖的事物，时刻腐朽？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But if there were somewhere a being strong and beautiful, a valiant nature, full at once of exaltation and refinement, a poet’s heart in an angel’s form, a lyre with sounding chords ringing out elegiac epithalamia to heaven, why, perchance, should she not find him?","zh":"可是假如有一个强壮、漂亮的男子，天生英武，而又细腻多情，天使的形象，诗人的心，抱着七弦琴，演奏哀婉的祝婚歌，响彻九霄，何以她就不会凑巧遇到？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Ah! how impossible!","zh":"哦！永远扑空！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, nothing was worth the trouble of seeking it; everything was a lie.","zh":"再说，也不值得追寻；处处是谎！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Every smile hid a yawn of boredom, every joy a curse, all pleasure satiety, and the sweetest kisses left upon your lips only the unattainable desire for a greater delight.","zh":"声声微笑隐伏着因腻烦而起的呵欠，回回喜悦隐伏着诅咒，任何欢乐免不了餍足。最香的吻，在你唇上留下来的，也只是一种实现不了而又向往更甜蜜的销魂境界的热望。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A metallic clang droned through the air, and four strokes were heard from the convent-clock. Four o’clock! And it seemed to her that she had been there on that form an eternity. But an infinity of passions may be contained in a minute, like a crowd in a small space.","sentences":[{"en":"A metallic clang droned through the air, and four strokes were heard from the convent-clock.","zh":"空中荡漾着铿锵的响声，修道院的钟敲了四下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Four o’clock!","zh":"四点钟，她觉得自己好像有生以来，就一直坐在这条长凳上似的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And it seemed to her that she had been there on that form an eternity.","zh":"四点钟，她觉得自己好像有生以来，就一直坐在这条长凳上似的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But an infinity of passions may be contained in a minute, like a crowd in a small space.","zh":"不过一分钟能容纳千变万化的热情，正如小小空间能容纳一大群人一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma lived all absorbed in hers, and troubled no more about money matters than an archduchess.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma lived all absorbed in hers, and troubled no more about money matters than an archduchess.","zh":"爱玛一心一意活在她的热情里，仿佛一位大公爵夫人，不拿银钱搁在心上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Once, however, a wretched-looking man, rubicund and bald, came to her house, saying he had been sent by Monsieur Vincart of Rouen. He took out the pins that held together the side-pockets of his long green overcoat, stuck them into his sleeve, and politely handed her a paper.","sentences":[{"en":"Once, however, a wretched-looking man, rubicund and bald, came to her house, saying he had been sent by Monsieur Vincart of Rouen.","zh":"但是有一回，家里来了一个红脸、秃顶的男子，举止猥琐，说是鲁昂的万萨先生差来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He took out the pins that held together the side-pockets of his long green overcoat, stuck them into his sleeve, and politely handed her a paper.","zh":"他穿一件绿长大衣，别针别住旁边的衣袋；他取下别针，插在袖子上，恭恭敬敬，递来一张纸。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was a bill for seven hundred francs, signed by her, and which Lheureux, in spite of all his professions, had paid away to Vincart. She sent her servant for him. He could not come. Then the stranger, who had remained standing, casting right and left curious glances, that his thick, fair eyebrows hid, asked with a naive air—","sentences":[{"en":"It was a bill for seven hundred francs, signed by her, and which Lheureux, in spite of all his professions, had paid away to Vincart.","zh":"这是她立的一张七百法郎的借据，勒乐嘴上说得好听，结局还是给了万萨。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She sent her servant for him.","zh":"她打发女用人去找他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He could not come.","zh":"他不能来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the stranger, who had remained standing, casting right and left curious glances, that his thick, fair eyebrows hid, asked with a naive air—","zh":"来人一直站着，东张西望，金黄颜色的粗眉毛遮住他好奇的视线，看见女用人徒劳往返，就一副天真的模样问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What answer am I to take Monsieur Vincart?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What answer am I to take Monsieur Vincart?”","zh":"“我拿什么话回万萨先生？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh,” said Emma, “tell him that I haven’t it. I will send next week; he must wait; yes, till next week.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh,” said Emma, “tell him that I haven’t it.","zh":"爱玛回答道：“好吧！告诉他…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I will send next week; he must wait; yes, till next week.”","zh":"下星期才有…他等着好了…是的，下星期。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the fellow went without another word.","sentences":[{"en":"And the fellow went without another word.","zh":"来人不发一言，拔脚就走。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the next day at twelve o’clock she received a summons, and the sight of the stamped paper, on which appeared several times in large letters, “Maitre Hareng, bailiff at Buchy,” so frightened her that she rushed in hot haste to the linendraper’s. She found him in his shop, doing up a parcel.","sentences":[{"en":"But the next day at twelve o’clock she received a summons, and the sight of the stamped paper, on which appeared several times in large letters, “Maitre Hareng, bailiff at Buchy,” so frightened her that she rushed in hot haste to the linendraper’s.","zh":"但是第二天正午，她收到一份拒付通知书，上面贴着印花，用大字写着“比西执达吏哈朗律师”的字样。她看见这张公文，害怕极了，慌慌张张，急忙奔往布商家里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She found him in his shop, doing up a parcel.","zh":"她在他的店里找到他，他正在捆扎一个小包。他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Your obedient!” he said; “I am at your service.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Your obedient!” he said; “I am at your service.”","zh":"“啊，有事见教？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But Lheureux, all the same, went on with his work, helped by a young girl of about thirteen, somewhat hunch-backed, who was at once his clerk and his servant.","sentences":[{"en":"But Lheureux, all the same, went on with his work, helped by a young girl of about thirteen, somewhat hunch-backed, who was at once his clerk and his servant.","zh":"勒乐并不因为她来，就中断工作。一个十三岁上下的女孩子在旁相帮；她有一点驼背，既是伙计，又是厨子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then, his clogs clattering on the shop-boards, he went up in front of Madame Bovary to the first door, and introduced her into a narrow closet, where, in a large bureau in sapon-wood, lay some ledgers, protected by a horizontal padlocked iron bar. Against the wall, under some remnants of calico, one glimpsed a safe, but of such dimensions that it must contain something besides bills and money. Monsieur Lheureux, in fact, went in for pawnbroking, and it was there that he had put Madame Bovary’s gold chain, together with the earrings of poor old Tellier, who, at last forced to sell out, had bought a meagre store of grocery at Quincampoix, where he was dying of catarrh amongst his candles, that were less yellow than his face.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, his clogs clattering on the shop-boards, he went up in front of Madame Bovary to the first door, and introduced her into a narrow closet, where, in a large bureau in sapon-wood, lay some ledgers, protected by a horizontal padlocked iron bar.","zh":"然后他在前走，大头套鞋呱嗒呱嗒，蹬着地板，把包法利夫人带到二楼，请进一间窄窄的小屋，里头有一张大松木书桌，桌面放着几本账簿，横里压着一根上了锁的细铁棍。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Against the wall, under some remnants of calico, one glimpsed a safe, but of such dimensions that it must contain something besides bills and money.","zh":"靠墙堆着一些零头印花布，底下隐隐约约露出一只保险箱，但是容积不小，似乎盛的不只是票据、银钱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Lheureux, in fact, went in for pawnbroking, and it was there that he had put Madame Bovary’s gold chain, together with the earrings of poor old Tellier, who, at last forced to sell out, had bought a meagre store of grocery at Quincampoix, where he was dying of catarrh amongst his candles, that were less yellow than his face.","zh":"原来勒乐先生兼营当铺生意，里面放的有包法利夫人的金表链和泰里耶老爹的耳环。可怜的老头走投无路，临了拍卖家什，又到甘冈普瓦盘了一家空无所有的小杂货铺，害黏膜炎死掉，脸比四周的蜡烛还黄。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Lheureux sat down in a large cane arm-chair, saying: “What news?”","sentences":[{"en":"Lheureux sat down in a large cane arm-chair, saying: “What news?”","zh":"勒乐坐到他的大藤扶手椅上，一边说：“您有什么事？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“See!”","sentences":[{"en":"“See!”","zh":"“请看。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she showed him the paper.","sentences":[{"en":"And she showed him the paper.","zh":"她拿公文给他看。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well how can I help it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well how can I help it?”","zh":"“哦！我有什么办法？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she grew angry, reminding him of the promise he had given not to pay away her bills. He acknowledged it.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she grew angry, reminding him of the promise he had given not to pay away her bills.","zh":"她一听这话，愤愤不平，提醒他不转让她的期票的约言。他承认说过这话。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He acknowledged it.","zh":"她一听这话，愤愤不平，提醒他不转让她的期票的约言。他承认说过这话。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“But I was pressed myself; the knife was at my own throat.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But I was pressed myself; the knife was at my own throat.”","zh":"“不过我也是走投无路，叫人逼的。”她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And what will happen now?” she went on.","sentences":[{"en":"“And what will happen now?” she went on.","zh":"“那，以后呢？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, it’s very simple; a judgment and then a distraint—that’s about it!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it’s very simple; a judgment and then a distraint—that’s about it!”","zh":"“哎呀！很简单嘛：法院裁决，再来一个扣押…完事大吉。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma kept down a desire to strike him, and asked gently if there was no way of quieting Monsieur Vincart.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma kept down a desire to strike him, and asked gently if there was no way of quieting Monsieur Vincart.","zh":"爱玛恨不得打他一顿。她忍下这口气，和颜悦色问他：“有没有办法疏通疏通万萨先生？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I dare say! Quiet Vincart! You don’t know him; he’s more ferocious than an Arab!”","sentences":[{"en":"“I dare say!","zh":"“好啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Quiet Vincart!","zh":"疏通万萨；您不晓得这个人；他比什么人都心狠。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"You don’t know him; he’s more ferocious than an Arab!”","zh":"疏通万萨；您不晓得这个人；他比什么人都心狠。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Still Monsieur Lheureux must interfere.","sentences":[{"en":"Still Monsieur Lheureux must interfere.","zh":"不过勒乐先生必须在中间尽尽力。“您听我讲，我觉得，截至目前，我对您够客气的啦！”他打开一本账簿道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, listen. It seems to me so far I’ve been very good to you.” And opening one of his ledgers, “See,” he said. Then running up the page with his finger, “Let’s see! let’s see! August 3d, two hundred francs; June 17th, a hundred and fifty; March 23d, forty-six. In April—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, listen.","zh":"“看！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It seems to me so far I’ve been very good to you.”","zh":"然后，手指朝上指：“看…看…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And opening one of his ledgers, “See,” he said.","zh":"八月三日，两百法郎…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then running up the page with his finger, “Let’s see! let’s see!","zh":"六月十七日，一百五十法郎…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"August 3d, two hundred francs; June 17th, a hundred and fifty; March 23d, forty-six.","zh":"三月二十三日，四十六法郎…四月…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In April—”","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He stopped, as if afraid of making some mistake.","sentences":[{"en":"He stopped, as if afraid of making some mistake.","zh":"他住了口，好像怕说错了话一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Not to speak of the bills signed by Monsieur Bovary, one for seven hundred francs, and another for three hundred. As to your little installments, with the interest, why, there’s no end to ‘em; one gets quite muddled over ‘em. I’ll have nothing more to do with it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not to speak of the bills signed by Monsieur Bovary, one for seven hundred francs, and another for three hundred.","zh":"“我还不提您丈夫立的期票，一张七百法郎，一张三百法郎！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to your little installments, with the interest, why, there’s no end to ‘em; one gets quite muddled over ‘em.","zh":"还有您那些零星账，连本带利，算也算不清，根本就是一篇糊涂账。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ll have nothing more to do with it.”","zh":"我可再也不上这个当啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She wept; she even called him “her good Monsieur Lheureux.” But he always fell back upon “that rascal Vincart.” Besides, he hadn’t a brass farthing; no one was paying him now-a-days; they were eating his coat off his back; a poor shopkeeper like him couldn’t advance money.","sentences":[{"en":"She wept; she even called him “her good Monsieur Lheureux.”","zh":"她哭，甚至于喊他“好勒乐先生”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But he always fell back upon “that rascal Vincart.”","zh":"可是他统统推到“万萨这个狗东西”身上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, he hadn’t a brass farthing; no one was paying him now-a-days; they were eating his coat off his back; a poor shopkeeper like him couldn’t advance money.","zh":"而且他一个小钱也没有，现在没有人还账，可把他坑苦了，像他这样一个可怜的开铺子的，就没有力量放账。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma was silent, and Monsieur Lheureux, who was biting the feathers of a quill, no doubt became uneasy at her silence, for he went on—","sentences":[{"en":"Emma was silent, and Monsieur Lheureux, who was biting the feathers of a quill, no doubt became uneasy at her silence, for he went on—","zh":"爱玛无话可说；勒乐先生在咬笔毛，见她默不作声，不用说，感到不安了，因为他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Unless one of these days I have something coming in, I might—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Unless one of these days I have something coming in, I might—”","zh":"“起码也得有一天，只要我多少有一点进项…我才可以…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Besides,” said she, “as soon as the balance of Barneville—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Besides,” said she, “as soon as the balance of Barneville—”","zh":"她道：“其实，巴恩镇的尾数一到…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What!”","zh":"“怎么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And on hearing that Langlois had not yet paid he seemed much surprised. Then in a honied voice—","sentences":[{"en":"And on hearing that Langlois had not yet paid he seemed much surprised.","zh":"听说朗格洛瓦还没有付清买房子的钱，他似乎吃了一惊，然后声音甜甜地道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then in a honied voice—","zh":"听说朗格洛瓦还没有付清买房子的钱，他似乎吃了一惊，然后声音甜甜地道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“And we agree, you say?”","sentences":[{"en":"“And we agree, you say?”","zh":"听说朗格洛瓦还没有付清买房子的钱，他似乎吃了一惊，然后声音甜甜地道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh! to anything you like.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh! to anything you like.”","zh":"“您说，条件是…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On this he closed his eyes to reflect, wrote down a few figures, and declaring it would be very difficult for him, that the affair was shady, and that he was being bled, he wrote out four bills for two hundred and fifty francs each, to fall due month by month.","sentences":[{"en":"On this he closed his eyes to reflect, wrote down a few figures, and declaring it would be very difficult for him, that the affair was shady, and that he was being bled, he wrote out four bills for two hundred and fifty francs each, to fall due month by month.","zh":"“唉！条件随您。”他于是闭上眼睛想了想，写了几个数字，一边说他很不合算，这是蚀本生意，他在赌性命，一边写了四张期票，每张二百五十法郎，各自相隔一个月到期。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Provided that Vincart will listen to me! However, it’s settled. I don’t play the fool; I’m straight enough.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Provided that Vincart will listen to me!","zh":"“但愿万萨答应！其实，决定的事，我不反悔！","scope":"group"},{"en":"However, it’s settled.","zh":"“但愿万萨答应！其实，决定的事，我不反悔！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I don’t play the fool; I’m straight enough.”","zh":"我这人顶诚恳不过。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Next he carelessly showed her several new goods, not one of which, however, was in his opinion worthy of madame.","sentences":[{"en":"Next he carelessly showed her several new goods, not one of which, however, was in his opinion worthy of madame.","zh":"他接着就手拿了几件新货给她看，不过依他看来，不会有一件合太太的意。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“When I think that there’s a dress at threepence-halfpenny a yard, and warranted fast colours! And yet they actually swallow it! Of course you understand one doesn’t tell them what it really is!” He hoped by this confession of dishonesty to others to quite convince her of his probity to her.","sentences":[{"en":"“When I think that there’s a dress at threepence-halfpenny a yard, and warranted fast colours!","zh":"“这件衣料，我说七个苏一米，保不褪色，好啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And yet they actually swallow it!","zh":"大家抢着买！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Of course you understand one doesn’t tell them what it really is!”","zh":"您明白，我才不拿真话告诉他们！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He hoped by this confession of dishonesty to others to quite convince her of his probity to her.","zh":"说出欺哄别人，他想，她就一定相信他为人正直了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he called her back to show her three yards of guipure that he had lately picked up “at a sale.”","sentences":[{"en":"Then he called her back to show her three yards of guipure that he had lately picked up “at a sale.”","zh":"接着他又喊她回来，让她看一幅三米多长的花边，他最近从一家拍卖行弄来的。勒乐道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Isn’t it lovely?” said Lheureux. “It is very much used now for the backs of arm-chairs. It’s quite the rage.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Isn’t it lovely?” said Lheureux.","zh":"“多好看！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“It is very much used now for the backs of arm-chairs.","zh":"现在用的人多着呢，搭在沙发背上，非常时兴。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s quite the rage.”","zh":"现在用的人多着呢，搭在沙发背上，非常时兴。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And, more ready than a juggler, he wrapped up the guipure in some blue paper and put it in Emma’s hands.","sentences":[{"en":"And, more ready than a juggler, he wrapped up the guipure in some blue paper and put it in Emma’s hands.","zh":"他拿蓝纸卷起花边，放在爱玛手心，比变戏法还快。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But at least let me know—”","sentences":[{"en":"“But at least let me know—”","zh":"“您倒是告诉我…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, another time,” he replied, turning on his heel.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, another time,” he replied, turning on his heel.","zh":"他接下去道：“啊！以后再说吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"That same evening she urged Bovary to write to his mother, to ask her to send as quickly as possible the whole of the balance due from the father’s estate. The mother-in-law replied that she had nothing more, the winding up was over, and there was due to them besides Barneville an income of six hundred francs, that she would pay them punctually.","sentences":[{"en":"That same evening she urged Bovary to write to his mother, to ask her to send as quickly as possible the whole of the balance due from the father’s estate.","zh":"转回身子往里去了。当天黄昏，她就催促包法利给母亲写信，要她把继承的钱财的全部尾数，尽快给他们汇来，婆婆回信说，钱没有了，清算已经结束，他们除掉巴恩镇房产之外，每年还有六百法郎进项，到时她会汇来的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The mother-in-law replied that she had nothing more, the winding up was over, and there was due to them besides Barneville an income of six hundred francs, that she would pay them punctually.","zh":"转回身子往里去了。当天黄昏，她就催促包法利给母亲写信，要她把继承的钱财的全部尾数，尽快给他们汇来，婆婆回信说，钱没有了，清算已经结束，他们除掉巴恩镇房产之外，每年还有六百法郎进项，到时她会汇来的。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then Madame Bovary sent in accounts to two or three patients, and she made large use of this method, which was very successful. She was always careful to add a postscript: “Do not mention this to my husband; you know how proud he is. Excuse me. Yours obediently.” There were some complaints; she intercepted them.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Madame Bovary sent in accounts to two or three patients, and she made large use of this method, which was very successful.","zh":"包法利夫人一看婆婆那方面没有指望，就给两三家病人送账单，收诊费，看见这个法子有效，不久就大用起来。她在账单后头，总当心加上一句：“拙夫性傲，万勿向其道及…","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was always careful to add a postscript: “Do not mention this to my husband; you know how proud he is.","zh":"包法利夫人一看婆婆那方面没有指望，就给两三家病人送账单，收诊费，看见这个法子有效，不久就大用起来。她在账单后头，总当心加上一句：“拙夫性傲，万勿向其道及…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Excuse me.","zh":"尚祈原宥…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Yours obediently.”","zh":"尚祈原宥…","scope":"group"},{"en":"There were some complaints; she intercepted them.","zh":"”有人写信抱怨；她截去来信。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To get money she began selling her old gloves, her old hats, the old odds and ends, and she bargained rapaciously, her peasant blood standing her in good stead. Then on her journey to town she picked up nick-nacks secondhand, that, in default of anyone else, Monsieur Lheureux would certainly take off her hands. She bought ostrich feathers, Chinese porcelain, and trunks; she borrowed from Félicité, from Madame Lefrancois, from the landlady at the Croix-Rouge, from everybody, no matter where.","sentences":[{"en":"To get money she began selling her old gloves, her old hats, the old odds and ends, and she bargained rapaciously, her peasant blood standing her in good stead.","zh":"她为了弄钱，卖掉她的旧手套、旧帽子、废铜烂铁，无所不卖，讲起价来，锱铢必较——她的农民的血使她连蝇头小利也在所必争。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then on her journey to town she picked up nick-nacks secondhand, that, in default of anyone else, Monsieur Lheureux would certainly take off her hands.","zh":"城里遇见便宜货，心想别人不收，勒乐先生一定会收，她就买下来。她还买鸵鸟羽毛、中国瓷器和木箱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She bought ostrich feathers, Chinese porcelain, and trunks; she borrowed from Félicité, from Madame Lefrancois, from the landlady at the Croix-Rouge, from everybody, no matter where.","zh":"她向全福、红十字女掌柜、勒弗朗索瓦太太借钱，不管张三李四，见人就借。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"With the money she at last received from Barneville she paid two bills; the other fifteen hundred francs fell due. She renewed the bills, and thus it was continually.","sentences":[{"en":"With the money she at last received from Barneville she paid two bills; the other fifteen hundred francs fell due.","zh":"最后，她收到巴恩镇的钱，付清两张期票，另外一千五百法郎又到期了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She renewed the bills, and thus it was continually.","zh":"她再续下去，永远续下去！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Sometimes, it is true, she tried to make a calculation, but she discovered things so exorbitant that she could not believe them possible. Then she recommenced, soon got confused, gave it all up, and thought no more about it.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes, it is true, she tried to make a calculation, but she discovered things so exorbitant that she could not believe them possible.","zh":"有时候她的确也试着计算来的，可是她发现数字庞大无边，连自己也信不过，于是她再计算，很快就糊涂了，只好丢在一旁，再也不去理睬。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she recommenced, soon got confused, gave it all up, and thought no more about it.","zh":"有时候她的确也试着计算来的，可是她发现数字庞大无边，连自己也信不过，于是她再计算，很快就糊涂了，只好丢在一旁，再也不去理睬。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The house was very dreary now. Tradesmen were seen leaving it with angry faces. Handkerchiefs were lying about on the stoves, and little Berthe, to the great scandal of Madame Homais, wore stockings with holes in them. If Charles timidly ventured a remark, she answered roughly that it wasn’t her fault.","sentences":[{"en":"The house was very dreary now.","zh":"家里如今才叫凄凉！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tradesmen were seen leaving it with angry faces.","zh":"供应商人走出大门，个个怒容满面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Handkerchiefs were lying about on the stoves, and little Berthe, to the great scandal of Madame Homais, wore stockings with holes in them.","zh":"手绢堆在灶头；小白尔特穿着破袜子，郝麦太太觉得太不像话。万一查理赔小心，偶尔说上一言半语，她就蛮不讲理，回答一句：不是她错！","scope":"group"},{"en":"If Charles timidly ventured a remark, she answered roughly that it wasn’t her fault.","zh":"手绢堆在灶头；小白尔特穿着破袜子，郝麦太太觉得太不像话。万一查理赔小心，偶尔说上一言半语，她就蛮不讲理，回答一句：不是她错！","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"What was the meaning of all these fits of temper? He explained everything through her old nervous illness, and reproaching himself with having taken her infirmities for faults, accused himself of egotism, and longed to go and take her in his arms.","sentences":[{"en":"What was the meaning of all these fits of temper?","zh":"为什么这样大发脾气？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He explained everything through her old nervous illness, and reproaching himself with having taken her infirmities for faults, accused himself of egotism, and longed to go and take her in his arms.","zh":"他认为全是她的神经旧病的缘故；他怪自己自私，不该拿病看成过失，心里抱歉，直想跑过去吻她。他向自己道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah, no!” he said to himself; “I should worry her.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah, no!” he said to himself; “I should worry her.”","zh":"“不必了，我会惹她讨厌的！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he did not stir.","sentences":[{"en":"And he did not stir.","zh":"他于是待下来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After dinner he walked about alone in the garden; he took little Berthe on his knees, and unfolding his medical journal, tried to teach her to read. But the child, who never had any lessons, soon looked up with large, sad eyes and began to cry. Then he comforted her; went to fetch water in her can to make rivers on the sand path, or broke off branches from the privet hedges to plant trees in the beds. This did not spoil the garden much, all choked now with long weeds. They owed Lestiboudois for so many days. Then the child grew cold and asked for her mother.","sentences":[{"en":"After dinner he walked about alone in the garden; he took little Berthe on his knees, and unfolding his medical journal, tried to teach her to read.","zh":"他用过晚饭，独自在花园散步；他把小白尔特放在膝盖上，打开他的医学杂志，试着教她认字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the child, who never had any lessons, soon looked up with large, sad eyes and began to cry.","zh":"小孩子从来没有经过文字教育，没有多久，就愁眉苦脸，睁大眼睛，啼哭起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he comforted her; went to fetch water in her can to make rivers on the sand path, or broke off branches from the privet hedges to plant trees in the beds.","zh":"他只好又来哄她，倒出喷壶的水，在沙地开河，或者掰断小女贞树的枝子，当作树栽在花圃：花园到处是杂草，所以这也没怎么破坏花园的美观。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This did not spoil the garden much, all choked now with long weeds.","zh":"赖斯地布杜瓦的工钱，他们有好些日子没有付了！","scope":"group"},{"en":"They owed Lestiboudois for so many days.","zh":"赖斯地布杜瓦的工钱，他们有好些日子没有付了！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then the child grew cold and asked for her mother.","zh":"随后小孩子冷了，要找母亲，查理道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Call the servant,” said Charles. “You know, dearie, that mamma does not like to be disturbed.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Call the servant,” said Charles.","zh":"“叫姨姨好了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“You know, dearie, that mamma does not like to be disturbed.”","zh":"你知道，乖乖，妈妈不要人吵她。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Autumn was setting in, and the leaves were already falling, as they did two years ago when she was ill. Where would it all end? And he walked up and down, his hands behind his back.","sentences":[{"en":"Autumn was setting in, and the leaves were already falling, as they did two years ago when she was ill.","zh":"转眼入秋，落叶又已纷纷——同她两年前生病一般光景！——到底什么时候才好得起来啊？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Where would it all end?","zh":"转眼入秋，落叶又已纷纷——同她两年前生病一般光景！——到底什么时候才好得起来啊？","scope":"group"},{"en":"And he walked up and down, his hands behind his back.","zh":"两只手搭在背后，他继续行走。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame was in her room, which no one entered. She stayed there all day long, torpid, half dressed, and from time to time burning Turkish pastilles which she had bought at Rouen in an Algerian’s shop. In order not to have at night this sleeping man stretched at her side, by dint of manoeuvring, she at last succeeded in banishing him to the second floor, while she read till morning extravagant books, full of pictures of orgies and thrilling situations. Often, seized with fear, she cried out, and Charles hurried to her.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame was in her room, which no one entered.","zh":"太太待在房间。没有人上去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She stayed there all day long, torpid, half dressed, and from time to time burning Turkish pastilles which she had bought at Rouen in an Algerian’s shop.","zh":"她整天待在卧室，昏昏沉沉，衣服几乎不穿，有时候还点起她在鲁昂一家阿尔及利亚商店买来的宫香。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In order not to have at night this sleeping man stretched at her side, by dint of manoeuvring, she at last succeeded in banishing him to the second floor, while she read till morning extravagant books, full of pictures of orgies and thrilling situations.","zh":"丈夫夜晚就知道挺尸，她不要他睡在身旁，最后硬是把他贬到三楼。她看些荒诞不经的小说，里头不是穷奢极欲，就是流血杀人，一看就看到天亮，常常心惊肉颤，大声喊叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often, seized with fear, she cried out, and Charles hurried to her.","zh":"查理跑进屋来看她。她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, go away!” she would say.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, go away!” she would say.","zh":"“啊！走开！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Or at other times, consumed more ardently than ever by that inner flame to which adultery added fuel, panting, tremulous, all desire, she threw open her window, breathed in the cold air, shook loose in the wind her masses of hair, too heavy, and, gazing upon the stars, longed for some princely love. She thought of him, of Léon. She would then have given anything for a single one of those meetings that surfeited her.","sentences":[{"en":"Or at other times, consumed more ardently than ever by that inner flame to which adultery added fuel, panting, tremulous, all desire, she threw open her window, breathed in the cold air, shook loose in the wind her masses of hair, too heavy, and, gazing upon the stars, longed for some princely love.","zh":"别的时候，她想起奸情，欲火烧身，又是气喘，又是心跳，无可奈何，过去打开窗户，吸冷空气，迎风抖散她的过于沉重的头发，仰观星星，希望会有贵人相爱。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She thought of him, of Léon.","zh":"她思念他，思念赖昂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would then have given anything for a single one of those meetings that surfeited her.","zh":"她这时候恨不得捐弃一切，换取一次幽会，得到满足。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"These were her gala days. She wanted them to be sumptuous, and when he alone could not pay the expenses, she made up the deficit liberally, which happened pretty well every time. He tried to make her understand that they would be quite as comfortable somewhere else, in a smaller hotel, but she always found some objection.","sentences":[{"en":"These were her gala days.","zh":"幽会成了她的节日。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wanted them to be sumptuous, and when he alone could not pay the expenses, she made up the deficit liberally, which happened pretty well every time.","zh":"她要排场！他一个人应付不了开销，她就大大方方来补足：几乎回回如此。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He tried to make her understand that they would be quite as comfortable somewhere else, in a smaller hotel, but she always found some objection.","zh":"他试着要她明白：换一个地方、一个比较便宜的旅馆，他们一样会快活的，可是她举出理由反对。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One day she drew six small silver-gilt spoons from her bag (they were old Roualt’s wedding present), begging him to pawn them at once for her, and Léon obeyed, though the proceeding annoyed him. He was afraid of compromising himself.","sentences":[{"en":"One day she drew six small silver-gilt spoons from her bag (they were old Roualt’s wedding present), begging him to pawn them at once for her, and Léon obeyed, though the proceeding annoyed him.","zh":"有一天，她从提包取出六把镀金小银匙（卢欧老爹送她的结婚礼物），求他为她立刻送到当铺。赖昂害怕连累名声，不高兴去，不过还是去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was afraid of compromising himself.","zh":"有一天，她从提包取出六把镀金小银匙（卢欧老爹送她的结婚礼物），求他为她立刻送到当铺。赖昂害怕连累名声，不高兴去，不过还是去了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then, on, reflection, he began to think his mistress’s ways were growing odd, and that they were perhaps not wrong in wishing to separate him from her.","sentences":[{"en":"Then, on, reflection, he began to think his mistress’s ways were growing odd, and that they were perhaps not wrong in wishing to separate him from her.","zh":"事后他细想，觉得他的情妇行为乖张，就此分手，也许不错。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In fact someone had sent his mother a long anonymous letter to warn her that he was “ruining himself with a married woman,” and the good lady at once conjuring up the eternal bugbear of families, the vague pernicious creature, the siren, the monster, who dwells fantastically in depths of love, wrote to Lawyer Dubocage, his employer, who behaved perfectly in the affair. He kept him for three quarters of an hour trying to open his eyes, to warn him of the abyss into which he was falling. Such an intrigue would damage him later on, when he set up for himself. He implored him to break with her, and, if he would not make this sacrifice in his own interest, to do it at least for his, Dubocage’s sake.","sentences":[{"en":"In fact someone had sent his mother a long anonymous letter to warn her that he was “ruining himself with a married woman,” and the good lady at once conjuring up the eternal bugbear of families, the vague pernicious creature, the siren, the monster, who dwells fantastically in depths of love, wrote to Lawyer Dubocage, his employer, who behaved perfectly in the affair.","zh":"的确也有人给他母亲写了一封匿名长信，警告她：他“与一有夫之妇相好，前途堪忧”。老太太影影绰绰，就见眼前站了一个败家精，就是说，那个隐在爱情深处的怪物、妖妇、叫不出名目的害人精，她马上通知他的老板杜包卡吉律师。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He kept him for three quarters of an hour trying to open his eyes, to warn him of the abyss into which he was falling.","zh":"律师办这种事，再精明不过，找他谈了三刻钟话，希望他看清是非，悬崖勒马。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Such an intrigue would damage him later on, when he set up for himself.","zh":"这种暧昧行为将来要给他的事业带来损害的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He implored him to break with her, and, if he would not make this sacrifice in his own interest, to do it at least for his, Dubocage’s sake.","zh":"他求他断绝关系，万一不为自己着想，至少也该为他着想，为杜包卡吉着想！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last Léon swore he would not see Emma again, and he reproached himself with not having kept his word, considering all the worry and lectures this woman might still draw down upon him, without reckoning the jokes made by his companions as they sat round the stove in the morning. Besides, he was soon to be head clerk; it was time to settle down. So he gave up his flute, exalted sentiments, and poetry; for every bourgeois in the flush of his youth, were it but for a day, a moment, has believed himself capable of immense passions, of lofty enterprises. The most mediocre libertine has dreamed of sultanas; every notary bears within him the debris of a poet.","sentences":[{"en":"At last Léon swore he would not see Emma again, and he reproached himself with not having kept his word, considering all the worry and lectures this woman might still draw down upon him, without reckoning the jokes made by his companions as they sat round the stove in the morning.","zh":"赖昂最后发誓，不再和爱玛会面，但没有做到。一想到这个女人可能给他招惹麻烦和闲话，还不算同事早晨围着炉子的打趣，他就责备自己，不该没有做到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, he was soon to be head clerk; it was time to settle down.","zh":"再说，他就要升为首席文书，是该严肃的时候了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So he gave up his flute, exalted sentiments, and poetry; for every bourgeois in the flush of his youth, were it but for a day, a moment, has believed himself capable of immense passions, of lofty enterprises.","zh":"所以他放弃旧习惯、激昂的情绪和想象——因为个个资产者，年轻时候，血气方刚，就算是一天、一小时也罢，都自以为抱有海阔天空的热情，会干出轰轰烈烈的事业来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The most mediocre libertine has dreamed of sultanas; every notary bears within him the debris of a poet.","zh":"最庸俗的登徒子念念不忘东方皇后；个个公证人心里全有诗人的残膏剩馥。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was bored now when Emma suddenly began to sob on his breast, and his heart, like the people who can only stand a certain amount of music, dozed to the sound of a love whose delicacies he no longer noted.","sentences":[{"en":"He was bored now when Emma suddenly began to sob on his breast, and his heart, like the people who can only stand a certain amount of music, dozed to the sound of a love whose delicacies he no longer noted.","zh":"如今一见爱玛贴住他的胸脯，忽然呜咽上来，他就厌烦；他的心好像那些只能忍受一定强度的音乐的人们一样，爱情过分喧闹反使人麻木淡漠，再也辨别不出爱情的妙趣。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They knew one another too well for any of those surprises of possession that increase its joys a hundred-fold. She was as sick of him as he was weary of her. Emma found again in adultery all the platitudes of marriage.","sentences":[{"en":"They knew one another too well for any of those surprises of possession that increase its joys a hundred-fold.","zh":"他们太相熟了，颠鸾倒凤，并不又惊又喜，欢好百倍。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was as sick of him as he was weary of her.","zh":"她腻味他正如他厌倦她。爱玛又在通奸中发现婚姻的平淡无奇了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma found again in adultery all the platitudes of marriage.","zh":"她腻味他正如他厌倦她。爱玛又在通奸中发现婚姻的平淡无奇了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But how to get rid of him? Then, though she might feel humiliated at the baseness of such enjoyment, she clung to it from habit or from corruption, and each day she hungered after them the more, exhausting all felicity in wishing for too much of it. She accused Léon of her baffled hopes, as if he had betrayed her; and she even longed for some catastrophe that would bring about their separation, since she had not the courage to make up her mind to it herself.","sentences":[{"en":"But how to get rid of him?","zh":"可是怎么才能把他甩掉？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, though she might feel humiliated at the baseness of such enjoyment, she clung to it from habit or from corruption, and each day she hungered after them the more, exhausting all felicity in wishing for too much of it.","zh":"这种幸福她虽然觉得鄙不足道，不过习惯成自然，或者积恶成癖，她不唯安之若素，而且一天比一天迷恋，也正因为竭泽而渔，幸福反倒成为无水之池了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She accused Léon of her baffled hopes, as if he had betrayed her; and she even longed for some catastrophe that would bring about their separation, since she had not the courage to make up her mind to it herself.","zh":"希望落空，她怪罪赖昂，好像他欺骗了她一样；她甚至于希望祸起萧墙，造成他们的分离，因为她没有勇气做出分离的决定。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She none the less went on writing him love letters, in virtue of the notion that a woman must write to her lover.","sentences":[{"en":"She none the less went on writing him love letters, in virtue of the notion that a woman must write to her lover.","zh":"她并不因而就中止给他写情书，因为她认为一个女人应当永远给她的情人写信。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But whilst she wrote it was another man she saw, a phantom fashioned out of her most ardent memories, of her finest reading, her strongest lusts, and at last he became so real, so tangible, that she palpitated wondering, without, however, the power to imagine him clearly, so lost was he, like a god, beneath the abundance of his attributes. He dwelt in that azure land where silk ladders hang from balconies under the breath of flowers, in the light of the moon. She felt him near her; he was coming, and would carry her right away in a kiss.","sentences":[{"en":"But whilst she wrote it was another man she saw, a phantom fashioned out of her most ardent memories, of her finest reading, her strongest lusts, and at last he became so real, so tangible, that she palpitated wondering, without, however, the power to imagine him clearly, so lost was he, like a god, beneath the abundance of his attributes.","zh":"但是她在写信中间，见到的恍惚是另一个男子，一个她最热烈的回忆、最美好的读物和最殷切的愿望所形成的幻影。他最后变得十分真实、靠近，但是她自己目夺神移，描写不出他的确切形象：他仿佛一尊天神，众相纷纷，隐去真身。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He dwelt in that azure land where silk ladders hang from balconies under the breath of flowers, in the light of the moon.","zh":"他住在天色淡蓝的国度，月明花香，丝梯悬在阳台上，摆来摆去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She felt him near her; he was coming, and would carry her right away in a kiss.","zh":"她觉得他近在咫尺，凌空下来，一个热吻就会把她活活带走，紧跟着她又跌到地面，心身交瘁；因为这些爱情的遐想，比起淫欲无度，还要使她疲倦。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then she fell back exhausted, for these transports of vague love wearied her more than great debauchery.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she fell back exhausted, for these transports of vague love wearied her more than great debauchery.","zh":"她觉得他近在咫尺，凌空下来，一个热吻就会把她活活带走，紧跟着她又跌到地面，心身交瘁；因为这些爱情的遐想，比起淫欲无度，还要使她疲倦。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She now felt constant ache all over her. Often she even received summonses, stamped paper that she barely looked at. She would have liked not to be alive, or to be always asleep.","sentences":[{"en":"She now felt constant ache all over her.","zh":"爱玛如今即使什么都不干，也时刻感到劳累。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Often she even received summonses, stamped paper that she barely looked at.","zh":"她经常收到传票、贴印花的公文，她却看也不看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would have liked not to be alive, or to be always asleep.","zh":"她还真想不活了，要不然就睡过去，再也不醒过来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On Mid-Lent she did not return to Yonville, but in the evening went to a masked ball. She wore velvet breeches, red stockings, a club wig, and three-cornered hat cocked on one side. She danced all night to the wild tones of the trombones; people gathered round her, and in the morning she found herself on the steps of the theatre together with five or six masks, débardeuses and sailors, Léon’s comrades, who were talking about having supper.","sentences":[{"en":"On Mid-Lent she did not return to Yonville, but in the evening went to a masked ball.","zh":"四旬斋狂欢节 ，她不回永镇，黄昏去了化装跳舞会。她穿一条丝绒长裤和一双红袜子，梳一条打结辫子，一顶小三角帽戴在一只耳朵上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She wore velvet breeches, red stockings, a club wig, and three-cornered hat cocked on one side.","zh":"四旬斋狂欢节 ，她不回永镇，黄昏去了化装跳舞会。她穿一条丝绒长裤和一双红袜子，梳一条打结辫子，一顶小三角帽戴在一只耳朵上。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She danced all night to the wild tones of the trombones; people gathered round her, and in the morning she found herself on the steps of the theatre together with five or six masks, débardeuses and sailors, Léon’s comrades, who were talking about having supper.","zh":"她跟着双管喇叭的疯狂响声跳了整整一夜。人们拿她作中心，围了一个圈子。早晨她在剧场回廊，发现自己和五六个扮成卸船女人和水手的男子待在一起；他们是赖昂的同事，说要去用夜宵。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The neighbouring cafes were full. They caught sight of one on the harbour, a very indifferent restaurant, whose proprietor showed them to a little room on the fourth floor.","sentences":[{"en":"The neighbouring cafes were full.","zh":"附近咖啡馆，人山人海。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They caught sight of one on the harbour, a very indifferent restaurant, whose proprietor showed them to a little room on the fourth floor.","zh":"他们在码头望见一家顶不像样的小饭馆，主人把他们带到五楼一间小屋。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The men were whispering in a corner, no doubt consorting about expenses. There were a clerk, two medical students, and a shopman—what company for her! As to the women, Emma soon perceived from the tone of their voices that they must almost belong to the lowest class. Then she was frightened, pushed back her chair, and cast down her eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"The men were whispering in a corner, no doubt consorting about expenses.","zh":"男子聚在一个角落嘀咕，毫无疑问，是在磋商开销。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There were a clerk, two medical students, and a shopman—what company for her!","zh":"他们是一个文书、两个医学生和一个商店伙计：这就是她的伴侣！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to the women, Emma soon perceived from the tone of their voices that they must almost belong to the lowest class.","zh":"至于女人，爱玛一听她们的声调，马上看出她们十有八九属于末流社会。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she was frightened, pushed back her chair, and cast down her eyes.","zh":"她胆战心惊了，抽开椅子，低下眼睛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The others began to eat; she ate nothing. Her head was on fire, her eyes smarted, and her skin was ice-cold. In her head she seemed to feel the floor of the ball-room rebounding again beneath the rhythmical pulsation of the thousands of dancing feet. And now the smell of the punch, the smoke of the cigars, made her giddy. She fainted, and they carried her to the window.","sentences":[{"en":"The others began to eat; she ate nothing.","zh":"别人都在用饭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her head was on fire, her eyes smarted, and her skin was ice-cold.","zh":"她吃不下去，额头滚烫，眼皮酸痛，皮肤冰凉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In her head she seemed to feel the floor of the ball-room rebounding again beneath the rhythmical pulsation of the thousands of dancing feet.","zh":"她觉得舞厅地板，随着千百只脚的有节奏的起伏，还在她脑子里跳动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And now the smell of the punch, the smoke of the cigars, made her giddy.","zh":"五味酒的气味，加上雪茄的烟雾，熏得她晕头转向。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She fainted, and they carried her to the window.","zh":"她晕过去了：大家把她抱到窗口。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Day was breaking, and a great stain of purple colour broadened out in the pale horizon over the St. Catherine hills. The livid river was shivering in the wind; there was no one on the bridges; the street lamps were going out.","sentences":[{"en":"Day was breaking, and a great stain of purple colour broadened out in the pale horizon over the St. Catherine hills.","zh":"曙光开始显现，圣卡特琳方向，灰白色的天空有一抹红色，逐渐扩大。铅色河水，随风荡漾；桥上没有人；街灯熄了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The livid river was shivering in the wind; there was no one on the bridges; the street lamps were going out.","zh":"曙光开始显现，圣卡特琳方向，灰白色的天空有一抹红色，逐渐扩大。铅色河水，随风荡漾；桥上没有人；街灯熄了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She revived, and began thinking of Berthe asleep yonder in the servant’s room. Then a cart filled with long strips of iron passed by, and made a deafening metallic vibration against the walls of the houses.","sentences":[{"en":"She revived, and began thinking of Berthe asleep yonder in the servant’s room.","zh":"她终于清醒过来，想起白尔特在女用人的下房睡觉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then a cart filled with long strips of iron passed by, and made a deafening metallic vibration against the walls of the houses.","zh":"这时过来一辆满载长铁条的大车，顺墙传来铁条颠动的响声，震耳欲聋。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She slipped away suddenly, threw off her costume, told Léon she must get back, and at last was alone at the Hotel de Boulogne. Everything, even herself, was now unbearable to her. She wished that, taking wing like a bird, she could fly somewhere, far away to regions of purity, and there grow young again.","sentences":[{"en":"She slipped away suddenly, threw off her costume, told Léon she must get back, and at last was alone at the Hotel de Boulogne.","zh":"她急忙溜出来，脱去服装，告诉赖昂：她有事要先回去。她终于一个人待在布洛涅旅馆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everything, even herself, was now unbearable to her.","zh":"连自己在内，她什么也忍受不了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She wished that, taking wing like a bird, she could fly somewhere, far away to regions of purity, and there grow young again.","zh":"她巴不得变成一只鸟，返老还童，飞到什么遥远的仙境。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She went out, crossed the Boulevard, the Place Cauchoise, and the Faubourg, as far as an open street that overlooked some gardens. She walked rapidly; the fresh air calming her; and, little by little, the faces of the crowd, the masks, the quadrilles, the lights, the supper, those women, all disappeared like mists fading away. Then, reaching the “Croix-Rouge,” she threw herself on the bed in her little room on the second floor, where there were pictures of the “Tour de Nesle.” At four o’clock Hivert awoke her.","sentences":[{"en":"She went out, crossed the Boulevard, the Place Cauchoise, and the Faubourg, as far as an open street that overlooked some gardens.","zh":"她离开旅馆，穿过马路、科镇广场和城郊，快步行走，来到一条两边全是花园的大路。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She walked rapidly; the fresh air calming her; and, little by little, the faces of the crowd, the masks, the quadrilles, the lights, the supper, those women, all disappeared like mists fading away.","zh":"空气新鲜，她安静下来了；群众的面孔、假面具、对舞、蜡烛架、夜宵和那些妇女，好像雾去云开一样，全都逐渐消失了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, reaching the “Croix-Rouge,” she threw herself on the bed in her little room on the second floor, where there were pictures of the “Tour de Nesle.”","zh":"她来到红十字，走进三楼有《奈勒塔》版画的小屋，倒在床上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At four o’clock Hivert awoke her.","zh":"下午四点钟，伊韦尔喊醒她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When she got home, Félicité showed her behind the clock a grey paper. She read—","sentences":[{"en":"When she got home, Félicité showed her behind the clock a grey paper.","zh":"回到家，全福指着钟后一张灰纸给她看，上面写着：","scope":"group"},{"en":"She read—","zh":"回到家，全福指着钟后一张灰纸给她看，上面写着：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“In virtue of the seizure in execution of a judgment.”","sentences":[{"en":"“In virtue of the seizure in execution of a judgment.”","zh":"兹经判决执行…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"What judgment? As a matter of fact, the evening before another paper had been brought that she had not yet seen, and she was stunned by these words—","sentences":[{"en":"What judgment?","zh":"判决什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As a matter of fact, the evening before another paper had been brought that she had not yet seen, and she was stunned by these words—","zh":"不错，昨天送来一张公文，她没有看懂，所以读到今天这一张，看见这样的字句，她像遭了雷殛：“遵奉圣谕，依照法令，包法利夫人必须…","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“By order of the king, law, and justice, to Madame Bovary.” Then, skipping several lines, she read, “Within twenty-four hours, without fail—” But what? “To pay the sum of eight thousand francs.” And there was even at the bottom, “She will be constrained thereto by every form of law, and notably by a writ of distraint on her furniture and effects.”","sentences":[{"en":"“By order of the king, law, and justice, to Madame Bovary.”","zh":"不错，昨天送来一张公文，她没有看懂，所以读到今天这一张，看见这样的字句，她像遭了雷殛：“遵奉圣谕，依照法令，包法利夫人必须…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then, skipping several lines, she read, “Within twenty-four hours, without fail—” But what?","zh":"”她跳过几行，就见上面写着：“限期二十四小时，不得拖延。”——什么意思？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“To pay the sum of eight thousand francs.”","zh":"“清偿全部债款八千法郎。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And there was even at the bottom, “She will be constrained thereto by every form of law, and notably by a writ of distraint on her furniture and effects.”","zh":"再往下，她还读到：“过期不付，当即依法执行，扣押其家具与衣物。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"What was to be done? In twenty-four hours—tomorrow. Lheureux, she thought, wanted to frighten her again; for she saw through all his devices, the object of his kindnesses. What reassured her was the very magnitude of the sum.","sentences":[{"en":"What was to be done?","zh":"怎么办？限定二十四小时；就是明天！","scope":"group"},{"en":"In twenty-four hours—tomorrow.","zh":"怎么办？限定二十四小时；就是明天！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Lheureux, she thought, wanted to frighten her again; for she saw through all his devices, the object of his kindnesses.","zh":"她寻思：毫无疑问，勒乐又想吓唬她了；因为她一下子看穿了他的种种策略、他的殷勤的目标。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What reassured her was the very magnitude of the sum.","zh":"所以看见数字庞大惊人，她倒放心了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"However, by dint of buying and not paying, of borrowing, signing bills, and renewing these bills that grew at each new falling-in, she had ended by preparing a capital for Monsieur Lheureux which he was impatiently awaiting for his speculations.","sentences":[{"en":"However, by dint of buying and not paying, of borrowing, signing bills, and renewing these bills that grew at each new falling-in, she had ended by preparing a capital for Monsieur Lheureux which he was impatiently awaiting for his speculations.","zh":"但是她一味买，一味欠，一味借，一味出票据，续票据，每次到期又往上滚，结局就是：她给勒乐先生积累好了一笔资金，他急不能待，直盼用在他的投机买卖上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She presented herself at his place with an offhand air.","sentences":[{"en":"She presented herself at his place with an offhand air.","zh":"她装出一副若无其事的模样去看他。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You know what has happened to me? No doubt it’s a joke!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You know what has happened to me?","zh":"“您知道我出了什么事吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No doubt it’s a joke!”","zh":"不用说，是开玩笑！”“不是。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How so?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How so?”","zh":"“怎么会呢？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He turned away slowly, and, folding his arms, said to her—","sentences":[{"en":"He turned away slowly, and, folding his arms, said to her—","zh":"他慢条斯理转过身子，交叉胳膊，向她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My good lady, did you think I should go on to all eternity being your purveyor and banker, for the love of God? Now be just. I must get back what I’ve laid out. Now be just.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My good lady, did you think I should go on to all eternity being your purveyor and banker, for the love of God?","zh":"“我的少奶奶，您以为我单为行好，供货供钱，真就白白供您供到世纪末日？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now be just.","zh":"放出去的账，我应该收回来，我们要公道！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I must get back what I’ve laid out.","zh":"放出去的账，我应该收回来，我们要公道！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Now be just.”","zh":"放出去的账，我应该收回来，我们要公道！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She cried out against the debt.","sentences":[{"en":"She cried out against the debt.","zh":"她说她欠也欠不了这许多。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! so much the worse. The court has admitted it. There’s a judgment. It’s been notified to you. Besides, it isn’t my fault. It’s Vincart’s.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! so much the worse.","zh":"“啊！错不了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The court has admitted it.","zh":"法院承认！有判决书！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There’s a judgment.","zh":"有通知书！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It’s been notified to you.","zh":"再说，不是我要这样做，是万萨要这样做的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Besides, it isn’t my fault.","zh":"再说，不是我要这样做，是万萨要这样做的。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s Vincart’s.”","zh":"再说，不是我要这样做，是万萨要这样做的。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Could you not—?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Could you not—?”","zh":"“您能不能…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, nothing whatever.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, nothing whatever.”","zh":"“嗐，无法可想。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But still, now talk it over.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But still, now talk it over.”","zh":"“可是…不过…再想想看。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she began beating about the bush; she had known nothing about it; it was a surprise.","sentences":[{"en":"And she began beating about the bush; she had known nothing about it; it was a surprise.","zh":"她放下正文不谈，只谈她事先一无所知…出乎意外…勒乐揶揄似的鞠躬道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Whose fault is that?” said Lheureux, bowing ironically. “While I’m slaving like a nigger, you go gallivanting about.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Whose fault is that?” said Lheureux, bowing ironically.","zh":"“怪谁？我像黑人一样吃苦卖力气，您这期间，寻欢作乐。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“While I’m slaving like a nigger, you go gallivanting about.”","zh":"“啊！用不着教训！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! no lecturing.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! no lecturing.”","zh":"他反驳道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It never does any harm,” he replied.","sentences":[{"en":"“It never does any harm,” he replied.","zh":"“这永远没有害处。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She turned coward; she implored him; she even pressed her pretty white and slender hand against the shopkeeper’s knee.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned coward; she implored him; she even pressed her pretty white and slender hand against the shopkeeper’s knee.","zh":"她胆怯，她央求，甚至于拿她又白又长的玉手放在商人的膝盖上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“There, that’ll do! Anyone’d think you wanted to seduce me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“There, that’ll do!","zh":"“请吧！人家会以为您有心勾引我呐！”她喊道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Anyone’d think you wanted to seduce me!”","zh":"“请吧！人家会以为您有心勾引我呐！”她喊道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You are a wretch!” she cried.","sentences":[{"en":"“You are a wretch!” she cried.","zh":"“您这个无赖！”他笑道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, oh! go it! go it!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, oh! go it! go it!”","zh":"“哈！哈！您倒冒起火来啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I will show you up. I shall tell my husband.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I will show you up.","zh":"“我要叫人知道您是什么样的人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I shall tell my husband.”","zh":"我要告诉我丈夫…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“All right! I too. I’ll show your husband something.”","sentences":[{"en":"“All right!","zh":"“好吧！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I too.","zh":"我呀，也有东西给您丈夫看！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll show your husband something.”","zh":"我呀，也有东西给您丈夫看！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And Lheureux drew from his strong box the receipt for eighteen hundred francs that she had given him when Vincart had discounted the bills.","sentences":[{"en":"And Lheureux drew from his strong box the receipt for eighteen hundred francs that she had given him when Vincart had discounted the bills.","zh":"勒乐从他的保险箱取出一张一千八百法郎的收据：万萨预支现金的时候，她写给他的。他接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do you think,” he added, “that he’ll not understand your little theft, the poor dear man?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you think,” he added, “that he’ll not understand your little theft, the poor dear man?”","zh":"“您以为这可怜的好人，真就不明白您的小偷行为吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She collapsed, more overcome than if felled by the blow of a pole-axe. He was walking up and down from the window to the bureau, repeating all the while—","sentences":[{"en":"She collapsed, more overcome than if felled by the blow of a pole-axe.","zh":"这比挨了一棍还厉害，她整个瘫下来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was walking up and down from the window to the bureau, repeating all the while—","zh":"他在窗户和书桌之间走来走去，三番四次说着：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! I’ll show him! I’ll show him!” Then he approached her, and in a soft voice said—","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ll show him!","zh":"我要给他看的…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ll show him!”","zh":"我要给他看的…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he approached her, and in a soft voice said—","zh":"”随后走到她跟前，柔声道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It isn’t pleasant, I know; but, after all, no bones are broken, and, since that is the only way that is left for you paying back my money—”","sentences":[{"en":"“It isn’t pleasant, I know; but, after all, no bones are broken, and, since that is the only way that is left for you paying back my money—”","zh":"“我知道，这不好玩；不过话说回来，也没有人为这死掉。既然这是唯一使您还我的钱的办法…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But where am I to get any?” said Emma, wringing her hands.","sentences":[{"en":"“But where am I to get any?” said Emma, wringing her hands.","zh":"爱玛扭绞着手道：“可是我到哪儿去弄钱啊？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Bah! when one has friends like you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Bah! when one has friends like you!”","zh":"“得啦，您有朋友，怕什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he looked at her in so keen, so terrible a fashion, that she shuddered to her very heart.","sentences":[{"en":"And he looked at her in so keen, so terrible a fashion, that she shuddered to her very heart.","zh":"他盯住她看，眼睛又亮，又吓人，她从里到外打起哆嗦来。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I promise you,” she said, “to sign—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I promise you,” she said, “to sign—”","zh":"“我答应您一定归还，我签字…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I’ve enough of your signatures.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I’ve enough of your signatures.”","zh":"“您签的字，我有的是！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I will sell something.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I will sell something.”","zh":"“我再卖…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Get along!” he said, shrugging his shoulders; “you’ve not got anything.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Get along!” he said, shrugging his shoulders; “you’ve not got anything.”","zh":"他耸肩膀道：“算了吧，您卖不出什么东西来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he called through the peep-hole that looked down into the shop—","sentences":[{"en":"And he called through the peep-hole that looked down into the shop—","zh":"他对准接连铺面的小洞喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Annette, don’t forget the three coupons of No. 14.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Annette, don’t forget the three coupons of No. 14.”","zh":"“阿奈特！别忘记十四号的三块零头布。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The servant appeared. Emma understood, and asked how much money would be wanted to put a stop to the proceedings.","sentences":[{"en":"The servant appeared.","zh":"爱玛看见女用人露面，明白是撵她走的意思，就问：“停止诉讼，要多少钱？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma understood, and asked how much money would be wanted to put a stop to the proceedings.","zh":"爱玛看见女用人露面，明白是撵她走的意思，就问：“停止诉讼，要多少钱？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“It is too late.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is too late.”","zh":"“太迟了！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But if I brought you several thousand francs—a quarter of the sum—a third—perhaps the whole?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But if I brought you several thousand francs—a quarter of the sum—a third—perhaps the whole?”","zh":"“可是如果我弄来几千法郎、四分之一、三分之一、几乎全部，又怎么样？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No; it’s no use!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No; it’s no use!”","zh":"“哎呀！用不着，没有用！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he pushed her gently towards the staircase.","sentences":[{"en":"And he pushed her gently towards the staircase.","zh":"他轻轻朝楼梯口推她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I implore you, Monsieur Lheureux, just a few days more!” She was sobbing.","sentences":[{"en":"“I implore you, Monsieur Lheureux, just a few days more!”","zh":"“我求您了，勒乐先生，再宽限几天！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was sobbing.","zh":"“我求您了，勒乐先生，再宽限几天！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“There! tears now!”","sentences":[{"en":"“There! tears now!”","zh":"她呜咽了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are driving me to despair!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are driving me to despair!”","zh":"“嘿！眼泪也使出来啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What do I care?” said he, shutting the door.","sentences":[{"en":"“What do I care?” said he, shutting the door.","zh":"“您是朝死路逼我！”他关了门道：“关我屁事！”","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-7","part":3,"n":7,"title":"Part III · Chapter 7","titleZh":"下卷 · 7","paragraphs":[{"en":"She was stoical the next day when Maitre Hareng, the bailiff, with two assistants, presented himself at her house to draw up the inventory for the distraint.","sentences":[{"en":"She was stoical the next day when Maitre Hareng, the bailiff, with two assistants, presented himself at her house to draw up the inventory for the distraint.","zh":"第二天，执达吏哈朗律师带了两位见证人，来到她家，她硬着头皮，由他记录扣押的物品。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They began with Bovary’s consulting-room, and did not write down the phrenological head, which was considered an “instrument of his profession”; but in the kitchen they counted the plates; the saucepans, the chairs, the candlesticks, and in the bedroom all the nick-nacks on the whatnot. They examined her dresses, the linen, the dressing-room; and her whole existence to its most intimate details, was, like a corpse on whom a post-mortem is made, outspread before the eyes of these three men.","sentences":[{"en":"They began with Bovary’s consulting-room, and did not write down the phrenological head, which was considered an “instrument of his profession”; but in the kitchen they counted the plates; the saucepans, the chairs, the candlesticks, and in the bedroom all the nick-nacks on the whatnot.","zh":"他们先从包法利的诊室看起，骨相学人头作为“开业工具”，不在登记之列；但是厨房的盘子、锅子、椅子、蜡烛台，卧室摆设架的种种摆设，他们一一点过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They examined her dresses, the linen, the dressing-room; and her whole existence to its most intimate details, was, like a corpse on whom a post-mortem is made, outspread before the eyes of these three men.","zh":"他们检查她的衣服、床单和桌布一类东西，还有梳洗间；她的生活仿佛一具被解剖的尸体，连最秘密的角落也露到外面，尽这三个人上上下下饱看。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Maitre Hareng, buttoned up in his thin black coat, wearing a white choker and very tight foot-straps, repeated from time to time—“Allow me, madame. You allow me?” Often he uttered exclamations. “Charming! very pretty.” Then he began writing again, dipping his pen into the horn inkstand in his left hand.","sentences":[{"en":"Maitre Hareng, buttoned up in his thin black coat, wearing a white choker and very tight foot-straps, repeated from time to time—“Allow me, madame.","zh":"哈朗律师穿一件薄青燕尾服，系一条白领带，鞋底下的带子绑得死紧，不时重复道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"You allow me?”","zh":"哈朗律师穿一件薄青燕尾服，系一条白领带，鞋底下的带子绑得死紧，不时重复道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Often he uttered exclamations.","zh":"“可以看吗，太太？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Charming! very pretty.”","zh":"“可以看吗，太太？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he began writing again, dipping his pen into the horn inkstand in his left hand.","zh":"可以看吗？”他动不动就叫唤：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When they had done with the rooms they went up to the attic. She kept a desk there in which Rodolphe’s letters were locked. It had to be opened.","sentences":[{"en":"When they had done with the rooms they went up to the attic.","zh":"“真好！漂亮极了！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She kept a desk there in which Rodolphe’s letters were locked.","zh":"然后他拿笔蘸蘸左手的牛角墨水瓶，又写下去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It had to be opened.","zh":"他们记完起居室，走上阁楼。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! a correspondence,” said Maitre Hareng, with a discreet smile. “But allow me, for I must make sure the box contains nothing else.” And he tipped up the papers lightly, as if to shake out napoleons. Then she grew angered to see this coarse hand, with fingers red and pulpy like slugs, touching these pages against which her heart had beaten.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! a correspondence,” said Maitre Hareng, with a discreet smile.","zh":"这里有她一张书几，里头锁着罗道耳弗的书信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“But allow me, for I must make sure the box contains nothing else.”","zh":"他们一定要她开开。哈朗律师意有所会，微笑道：“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And he tipped up the papers lightly, as if to shake out napoleons.","zh":"来往信件！不过，对不住！抽屉里有没有别的东西，我得看看仔细。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she grew angered to see this coarse hand, with fingers red and pulpy like slugs, touching these pages against which her heart had beaten.","zh":"他于是轻轻举起信纸，斜着一抖，好像会有金币抖出来一样。她看见这只大手，红手指柔柔的活像蛞蝓，捏住这些曾经让她心跳的信纸，止不住心头火起。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They went at last. Félicité came back. Emma had sent her out to watch for Bovary in order to keep him off, and they hurriedly installed the man in possession under the roof, where he swore he would remain.","sentences":[{"en":"They went at last.","zh":"他们终于走了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Félicité came back.","zh":"她怕包法利撞上，打发全福到外头守望，准备拿话骗开。全福看见他们走了，也就进来。留下来的看管人，她们赶快让他藏在顶楼；他答应待在那儿不出来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma had sent her out to watch for Bovary in order to keep him off, and they hurriedly installed the man in possession under the roof, where he swore he would remain.","zh":"她怕包法利撞上，打发全福到外头守望，准备拿话骗开。全福看见他们走了，也就进来。留下来的看管人，她们赶快让他藏在顶楼；他答应待在那儿不出来。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"During the evening Charles seemed to her careworn. Emma watched him with a look of anguish, fancying she saw an accusation in every line of his face. Then, when her eyes wandered over the chimney-piece ornamented with Chinese screens, over the large curtains, the armchairs, all those things, in a word, that had, softened the bitterness of her life, remorse seized her or rather an immense regret, that, far from crushing, irritated her passion. Charles placidly poked the fire, both his feet on the fire-dogs.","sentences":[{"en":"During the evening Charles seemed to her careworn.","zh":"一整黄昏，她觉得查理愁眉不展。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma watched him with a look of anguish, fancying she saw an accusation in every line of his face.","zh":"爱玛焦灼不安，偷眼看他：脸上的皱纹活像一张诉状。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, when her eyes wandered over the chimney-piece ornamented with Chinese screens, over the large curtains, the armchairs, all those things, in a word, that had, softened the bitterness of her life, remorse seized her or rather an immense regret, that, far from crushing, irritated her passion.","zh":"她的眼睛落在有中国屏风的壁炉上、大窗帘上、扶手椅上，总而言之，样样曾经帮她消磨岁月的什物上，她起了内疚，或者不如说是巨大的遗憾——不但不扑灭热情，反而激起热情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles placidly poked the fire, both his feet on the fire-dogs.","zh":"查理把脚搁在火篦上，静静地拨弄炉火。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Once the man, no doubt bored in his hiding-place, made a slight noise.","sentences":[{"en":"Once the man, no doubt bored in his hiding-place, made a slight noise.","zh":"看管人待在躲藏的地方，不用说，有一时待腻了，出了一点响声。查理问道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Is anyone walking upstairs?” said Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is anyone walking upstairs?” said Charles.","zh":"看管人待在躲藏的地方，不用说，有一时待腻了，出了一点响声。查理问道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“No,” she replied; “it is a window that has been left open, and is rattling in the wind.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No,” she replied; “it is a window that has been left open, and is rattling in the wind.”","zh":"“上头有人走动？”她回答道：“没人，一扇天窗没有关，风刮动了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day, Sunday, she went to Rouen to call on all the brokers whose names she knew. They were at their country-places or on journeys. She was not discouraged; and those whom she did manage to see she asked for money, declaring she must have some, and that she would pay it back. Some laughed in her face; all refused.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day, Sunday, she went to Rouen to call on all the brokers whose names she knew.","zh":"第二天是星期日，她去鲁昂，访问她知道名姓的个个银行家。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were at their country-places or on journeys.","zh":"他们不是下乡，就是旅行去了，她不灰心，凡是她能见到的银行家，她就开口借钱，说她到了非借不可的地步，保证归还。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was not discouraged; and those whom she did manage to see she asked for money, declaring she must have some, and that she would pay it back.","zh":"他们不是下乡，就是旅行去了，她不灰心，凡是她能见到的银行家，她就开口借钱，说她到了非借不可的地步，保证归还。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Some laughed in her face; all refused.","zh":"有的当面笑她；个个不借。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At two o’clock she hurried to Léon, and knocked at the door. No one answered. At length he appeared.","sentences":[{"en":"At two o’clock she hurried to Léon, and knocked at the door.","zh":"下午两点钟，她跑到赖昂住的地方。她叩门，门不开。","scope":"group"},{"en":"No one answered.","zh":"下午两点钟，她跑到赖昂住的地方。她叩门，门不开。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At length he appeared.","zh":"最后，他露面了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What brings you here?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What brings you here?”","zh":"“你怎么来了？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do I disturb you?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do I disturb you?”","zh":"“我打搅你啦？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No; but—” And he admitted that his landlord didn’t like his having “women” there.","sentences":[{"en":"“No; but—” And he admitted that his landlord didn’t like his having “women” there.","zh":"“没有…没有…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I must speak to you,” she went on.","sentences":[{"en":"“I must speak to you,” she went on.","zh":"他说房东不喜欢房客招待女人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he took down the key, but she stopped him.","sentences":[{"en":"Then he took down the key, but she stopped him.","zh":"她回答道：“我有话和你讲。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no! Down there, in our home!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no! Down there, in our home!”","zh":"他掏钥匙，她拦住他。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And they went to their room at the Hotel de Boulogne.","sentences":[{"en":"And they went to their room at the Hotel de Boulogne.","zh":"“不必！到那边我们住的地方去。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On arriving she drank off a large glass of water. She was very pale. She said to him—","sentences":[{"en":"On arriving she drank off a large glass of water.","zh":"他们于是去了布洛涅旅馆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was very pale.","zh":"她一走进房间，就喝了一大杯水。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She said to him—","zh":"她一走进房间，就喝了一大杯水。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Léon, you will do me a service?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Léon, you will do me a service?”","zh":"她脸上没有一丝血色。她向他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And, shaking him by both hands that she grasped tightly, she added—","sentences":[{"en":"And, shaking him by both hands that she grasped tightly, she added—","zh":"“赖昂，我要你帮忙。”于是捏紧他的手，摇他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Listen, I want eight thousand francs.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Listen, I want eight thousand francs.”","zh":"“听我讲，我需要八千法郎！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But you are mad!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But you are mad!”","zh":"“你疯啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Not yet.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Not yet.”","zh":"“还没有！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And thereupon, telling him the story of the distraint, she explained her distress to him; for Charles knew nothing of it; her mother-in-law detested her; old Rouault could do nothing; but he, Léon, he would set about finding this indispensable sum.","sentences":[{"en":"And thereupon, telling him the story of the distraint, she explained her distress to him; for Charles knew nothing of it; her mother-in-law detested her; old Rouault could do nothing; but he, Léon, he would set about finding this indispensable sum.","zh":"她立刻说起扣押和她的窘境；因为查理完全不知道；她的婆婆恨她，卢欧老爹又无济于事；可是这笔钱少了又不行，他，赖昂，帮她奔走奔走看…“你怎么指望…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How on earth can I?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How on earth can I?”","zh":"“你可真没有种！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What a coward you are!” she cried.","sentences":[{"en":"“What a coward you are!” she cried.","zh":"他听了这话，蠢头蠢脑道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he said stupidly, “You are exaggerating the difficulty. Perhaps, with a thousand crowns or so the fellow could be stopped.”","sentences":[{"en":"Then he said stupidly, “You are exaggerating the difficulty.","zh":"“事情不像你说得那样严重。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps, with a thousand crowns or so the fellow could be stopped.”","zh":"也许有一千埃居，对方就不闹了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"All the greater reason to try and do something; it was impossible that they could not find three thousand francs. Besides, Léon, could be security instead of her.","sentences":[{"en":"All the greater reason to try and do something; it was impossible that they could not find three thousand francs.","zh":"正是这个缘故，更该设法；绝不至于找不到一千埃居。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, Léon, could be security instead of her.","zh":"再说，她做不了担保，赖昂可以做。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Go, try, try! I will love you so!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go, try, try!","zh":"“去吧！试试看！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I will love you so!”","zh":"非钱不可！快！哎呀！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He went out, and came back at the end of an hour, saying, with solemn face—","sentences":[{"en":"He went out, and came back at the end of an hour, saying, with solemn face—","zh":"试试看！我会更爱你的！”他去了一小时回来，满脸严肃地说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I have been to three people with no success.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I have been to three people with no success.”","zh":"“我找了三个人…没有用！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then they remained sitting face to face at the two chimney corners, motionless, in silence. Emma shrugged her shoulders as she stamped her feet. He heard her murmuring—","sentences":[{"en":"Then they remained sitting face to face at the two chimney corners, motionless, in silence.","zh":"他们面对面，坐在壁炉两角，不言不语，一动不动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma shrugged her shoulders as she stamped her feet.","zh":"爱玛又是顿脚，又是耸肩，他听见她咕哝道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"He heard her murmuring—","zh":"爱玛又是顿脚，又是耸肩，他听见她咕哝道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“If I were in your place I should soon get some.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If I were in your place I should soon get some.”","zh":"“我要是你呀，就能找得到。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But where?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But where?”","zh":"“到哪儿去？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“At your office.” And she looked at him.","sentences":[{"en":"“At your office.”","zh":"“你的事务所！”她看着他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And she looked at him.","zh":"“你的事务所！”她看着他。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"An infernal boldness looked out from her burning eyes, and their lids drew close together with a lascivious and encouraging look, so that the young man felt himself growing weak beneath the mute will of this woman who was urging him to a crime. Then he was afraid, and to avoid any explanation he smote his forehead, crying—","sentences":[{"en":"An infernal boldness looked out from her burning eyes, and their lids drew close together with a lascivious and encouraging look, so that the young man felt himself growing weak beneath the mute will of this woman who was urging him to a crime.","zh":"她火热的瞳孔显出一种魔鬼般的胆量，眯缝着眼，模样又淫荡，又挑唆；这勾引他犯罪的女人的意志，顽强无比，虽然喑哑无声，也有力量鼓动年轻人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he was afraid, and to avoid any explanation he smote his forehead, crying—","zh":"他害怕了，为防止她细说下去，他敲打着额头，喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Morel is to come back to-night; he will not refuse me, I hope” (this was one of his friends, the son of a very rich merchant); “and I will bring it you to-morrow,” he added.","sentences":[{"en":"“Morel is to come back to-night; he will not refuse me, I hope” (this was one of his friends, the son of a very rich merchant); “and I will bring it you to-morrow,” he added.","zh":"“毛赖耳今天夜晚回来！我想，他不会不借的（他是他的一个朋友、一个大富商的儿子），我明天给你送来。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma did not seem to welcome this hope with all the joy he had expected. Did she suspect the lie? He went on, blushing—","sentences":[{"en":"Emma did not seem to welcome this hope with all the joy he had expected.","zh":"他说这话，心想她听了会喜出望外，可是爱玛的神色，并未热烈欢迎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Did she suspect the lie?","zh":"难道她猜出了他是撒谎吗？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He went on, blushing—","zh":"他臊红了脸，继续道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“However, if you don’t see me by three o’clock do not wait for me, my darling. I must be off now; forgive me! Goodbye!”","sentences":[{"en":"“However, if you don’t see me by three o’clock do not wait for me, my darling.","zh":"“不过你要是下午三点钟还不见我来的话，心肝，就别等我了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I must be off now; forgive me!","zh":"对不住，我该走了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Goodbye!”","zh":"再见！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He pressed her hand, but it felt quite lifeless. Emma had no strength left for any sentiment.","sentences":[{"en":"He pressed her hand, but it felt quite lifeless.","zh":"他握她的手，觉得毫无生气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma had no strength left for any sentiment.","zh":"爱玛已经没有气力感受了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Four o’clock struck, and she rose to return to Yonville, mechanically obeying the force of old habits.","sentences":[{"en":"Four o’clock struck, and she rose to return to Yonville, mechanically obeying the force of old habits.","zh":"钟敲四点；她站起来，想回永镇，机器人一样，服从习惯的动力。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The weather was fine. It was one of those March days, clear and sharp, when the sun shines in a perfectly white sky. The Rouen folk, in Sunday-clothes, were walking about with happy looks. She reached the Place du Parvis. People were coming out after vespers; the crowd flowed out through the three doors like a stream through the three arches of a bridge, and in the middle one, more motionless than a rock, stood the beadle.","sentences":[{"en":"The weather was fine.","zh":"天气晴朗；这是三月的明亮而又寒冽的好天，白茫茫的天空，只有太阳照耀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was one of those March days, clear and sharp, when the sun shines in a perfectly white sky.","zh":"天气晴朗；这是三月的明亮而又寒冽的好天，白茫茫的天空，只有太阳照耀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The Rouen folk, in Sunday-clothes, were walking about with happy looks.","zh":"有些鲁昂居民，穿了节日服装，潇洒自如，漫步街头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She reached the Place du Parvis.","zh":"她走到礼拜堂广场。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"People were coming out after vespers; the crowd flowed out through the three doors like a stream through the three arches of a bridge, and in the middle one, more motionless than a rock, stood the beadle.","zh":"晚祷方过，群众挨挨挤挤，涌出三座拱门，好像一条河流过三个桥洞一样，守卫站在当中，一动不动，赛过一块石头。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she remembered the day when, all anxious and full of hope, she had entered beneath this large nave, that had opened out before her, less profound than her love; and she walked on weeping beneath her veil, giddy, staggering, almost fainting.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she remembered the day when, all anxious and full of hope, she had entered beneath this large nave, that had opened out before her, less profound than her love; and she walked on weeping beneath her veil, giddy, staggering, almost fainting.","zh":"她不由得想起那一天，她又是焦急，又是满怀希望，走进高大的教堂：当时一眼望去，正殿还不及她的爱情深长。她继续行走，一溜歪斜，眼泪在面网底下直淌，头昏脑涨，眼看就要软瘫下来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Take care!” cried a voice issuing from the gate of a courtyard that was thrown open.","sentences":[{"en":"“Take care!” cried a voice issuing from the gate of a courtyard that was thrown open.","zh":"一辆马车的车门正好开开，里头有人喊道：“当心！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She stopped to let pass a black horse, pawing the ground between the shafts of a tilbury, driven by a gentleman in sable furs. Who was it? She knew him. The carriage darted by and disappeared.","sentences":[{"en":"She stopped to let pass a black horse, pawing the ground between the shafts of a tilbury, driven by a gentleman in sable furs.","zh":"她收住脚步，让过一辆提耳玻里，当辕一匹黑马，一位穿貂皮的绅士赶车。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Who was it?","zh":"这人是谁？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She knew him.","zh":"她认识他…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The carriage darted by and disappeared.","zh":"马车向前驰去，转眼不见了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Why, it was he—the Viscount. She turned away; the street was empty. She was so overwhelmed, so sad, that she had to lean against a wall to keep herself from falling.","sentences":[{"en":"Why, it was he—the Viscount.","zh":"这人就是他，子爵！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She turned away; the street was empty.","zh":"她转回身子；街空空的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was so overwhelmed, so sad, that she had to lean against a wall to keep herself from falling.","zh":"她又难过，又伤心，靠住一堵墙，免得跌倒。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she thought she had been mistaken. Anyhow, she did not know. All within her and around her was abandoning her. She felt lost, sinking at random into indefinable abysses, and it was almost with joy that, on reaching the “Croix-Rouge,” she saw the good Homais, who was watching a large box full of pharmaceutical stores being hoisted on to the “Hirondelle.” In his hand he held tied in a silk handkerchief six cheminots for his wife.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she thought she had been mistaken.","zh":"她再一想，是她看错了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Anyhow, she did not know.","zh":"她再一想，是她看错了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"All within her and around her was abandoning her.","zh":"再说，她什么都不清楚。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She felt lost, sinking at random into indefinable abysses, and it was almost with joy that, on reaching the “Croix-Rouge,” she saw the good Homais, who was watching a large box full of pharmaceutical stores being hoisted on to the “Hirondelle.”","zh":"外界的一切，连同她自己统统把她抛弃了。她像在神秘莫测的深渊里乱滚，眼看就要毁灭，所以来到红十字，望见那位善心的郝麦先生，她几乎高兴起来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"In his hand he held tied in a silk handkerchief six cheminots for his wife.","zh":"外界的一切，连同她自己统统把她抛弃了。她像在神秘莫测的深渊里乱滚，眼看就要毁灭，所以来到红十字，望见那位善心的郝麦先生，她几乎高兴起来。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Madame Homais was very fond of these small, heavy turban-shaped loaves, that are eaten in Lent with salt butter; a last vestige of Gothic food that goes back, perhaps, to the time of the Crusades, and with which the robust Normans gorged themselves of yore, fancying they saw on the table, in the light of the yellow torches, between tankards of hippocras and huge boars’ heads, the heads of Saracens to be devoured. The druggist’s wife crunched them up as they had done—heroically, despite her wretched teeth. And so whenever Homais journeyed to town, he never failed to bring her home some that he bought at the great baker’s in the Rue Massacre.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Homais was very fond of these small, heavy turban-shaped loaves, that are eaten in Lent with salt butter; a last vestige of Gothic food that goes back, perhaps, to the time of the Crusades, and with which the robust Normans gorged themselves of yore, fancying they saw on the table, in the light of the yellow torches, between tankards of hippocras and huge boars’ heads, the heads of Saracens to be devoured.","zh":"他看着一大箱药品装上燕子，手里拿着一条绸手绢，里头是给太太买的六块干粮。郝麦太太很喜欢这些包头巾似的又小又重的面包，抹上咸牛油，在四旬斋吃：这是哥特人传到今天的吃食，也许是十字军时代的发明，从前放在桌子上，两旁是桂皮酒坛子和大块猪肉，照着火把的黄光，豪壮的诺曼人以为看见的是伊斯兰教徒的头颅，狼吞虎咽，大吃一顿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The druggist’s wife crunched them up as they had done—heroically, despite her wretched teeth.","zh":"药剂师太太的牙齿很坏，不过也是一派英雄作风，像他们一样啃着。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And so whenever Homais journeyed to town, he never failed to bring her home some that he bought at the great baker’s in the Rue Massacre.","zh":"所以郝麦先生每次进城，总要到屠杀街大面包房买些，给她带回去。他看见爱玛，搀她上车道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Charmed to see you,” he said, offering Emma a hand to help her into the “Hirondelle.” Then he hung up his cheminots to the cords of the netting, and remained bare-headed in an attitude pensive and Napoleonic.","sentences":[{"en":"“Charmed to see you,” he said, offering Emma a hand to help her into the “Hirondelle.”","zh":"“看见您，我很高兴！”接着他拿干粮挂在车顶的网条上，摘下帽子，坐好了，交叉胳膊，摆出一副拿破仑似的思考的姿态。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he hung up his cheminots to the cords of the netting, and remained bare-headed in an attitude pensive and Napoleonic.","zh":"“看见您，我很高兴！”接着他拿干粮挂在车顶的网条上，摘下帽子，坐好了，交叉胳膊，摆出一副拿破仑似的思考的姿态。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But when the blind man appeared as usual at the foot of the hill he exclaimed—","sentences":[{"en":"But when the blind man appeared as usual at the foot of the hill he exclaimed—","zh":"但是临到瞎子像平常一样，又在岭下露面，他就嚷嚷道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I can’t understand why the authorities tolerate such culpable industries. Such unfortunates should be locked up and forced to work. Progress, my word! creeps at a snail’s pace. We are floundering about in mere barbarism.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I can’t understand why the authorities tolerate such culpable industries.","zh":"“这种生活方式，罪实难逭，我不明白，政府怎么会容忍到现在！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Such unfortunates should be locked up and forced to work.","zh":"应当把这些坏蛋关起来，强迫劳动才是！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Progress, my word! creeps at a snail’s pace.","zh":"说实话，进步走的是蜗牛步子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We are floundering about in mere barbarism.”","zh":"我们活在野蛮时代！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The blind man held out his hat, that flapped about at the door, as if it were a bag in the lining that had come unnailed.","sentences":[{"en":"The blind man held out his hat, that flapped about at the door, as if it were a bag in the lining that had come unnailed.","zh":"瞎子伸出他的帽子，在车门旁边摇来摇去，如同一只离开钉子的布袋。药剂师道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“This,” said the chemist, “is a scrofulous affection.”","sentences":[{"en":"“This,” said the chemist, “is a scrofulous affection.”","zh":"“他害的是瘰疬！”他见过这可怜虫，不过他装出第一回看到的模样，低声说着角膜、不透明角膜、巩膜、面孔这些字眼，然后用严父口吻问他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And though he knew the poor devil, he pretended to see him for the first time, murmured something about “cornea,” “opaque cornea,” “sclerotic,” “facies,” then asked him in a paternal tone—","sentences":[{"en":"And though he knew the poor devil, he pretended to see him for the first time, murmured something about “cornea,” “opaque cornea,” “sclerotic,” “facies,” then asked him in a paternal tone—","zh":"“他害的是瘰疬！”他见过这可怜虫，不过他装出第一回看到的模样，低声说着角膜、不透明角膜、巩膜、面孔这些字眼，然后用严父口吻问他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“My friend, have you long had this terrible infirmity? Instead of getting drunk at the public, you’d do better to die yourself.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My friend, have you long had this terrible infirmity?","zh":"“朋友，这可怕的毛病，你害了有多久啦？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Instead of getting drunk at the public, you’d do better to die yourself.”","zh":"别净在酒馆喝酒啦，顶好还是节制节制饮食吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He advised him to take good wine, good beer, and good joints. The blind man went on with his song; he seemed, moreover, almost idiotic. At last Monsieur Homais opened his purse—","sentences":[{"en":"He advised him to take good wine, good beer, and good joints.","zh":"他劝他喝上等葡萄酒、上等啤酒，吃上等烤肉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The blind man went on with his song; he seemed, moreover, almost idiotic.","zh":"瞎子一直在唱歌，那副神气，简直就像白痴。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last Monsieur Homais opened his purse—","zh":"郝麦先生最后打开他的钱包道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Now there’s a sou; give me back two lairds, and don’t forget my advice: you’ll be the better for it.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now there’s a sou; give me back two lairds, and don’t forget my advice: you’ll be the better for it.”","zh":"“好，这里是一个苏，找我两个里亚 。我的建议别忘了，会把你的病治好的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Hivert openly cast some doubt on the efficacy of it. But the druggist said that he would cure himself with an antiphlogistic pomade of his own composition, and he gave his address—“Monsieur Homais, near the market, pretty well known.”","sentences":[{"en":"Hivert openly cast some doubt on the efficacy of it.","zh":"伊韦尔不管三七二十一，公开怀疑这些办法是否有效。可是药剂师担保用他配的一种消炎膏能治好他。他把地址给了可怜虫：","scope":"group"},{"en":"But the druggist said that he would cure himself with an antiphlogistic pomade of his own composition, and he gave his address—“Monsieur Homais, near the market, pretty well known.”","zh":"伊韦尔不管三七二十一，公开怀疑这些办法是否有效。可是药剂师担保用他配的一种消炎膏能治好他。他把地址给了可怜虫：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Now,” said Hivert, “for all this trouble you’ll give us your performance.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now,” said Hivert, “for all this trouble you’ll give us your performance.”","zh":"“郝麦先生，挨近菜场，一问就晓得。”伊韦尔道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The blind man sank down on his haunches, with his head thrown back, whilst he rolled his greenish eyes, lolled out his tongue, and rubbed his stomach with both hands as he uttered a kind of hollow yell like a famished dog. Emma, filled with disgust, threw him over her shoulder a five-franc piece. It was all her fortune. It seemed to her very fine thus to throw it away.","sentences":[{"en":"The blind man sank down on his haunches, with his head thrown back, whilst he rolled his greenish eyes, lolled out his tongue, and rubbed his stomach with both hands as he uttered a kind of hollow yell like a famished dog.","zh":"“得啦！不顶事，您也就是给我们做戏。”瞎子往下一蹲，头朝上仰，转动他的淡绿眼睛，吐出舌头，两只手搓揉胸脯，好像一只饿狗一样，发出一种低沉的嗥叫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma, filled with disgust, threw him over her shoulder a five-franc piece.","zh":"爱玛觉得恶心，背转脸，拿一枚五法郎的辅币朝他丢了过去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was all her fortune.","zh":"这是她的全部财产。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It seemed to her very fine thus to throw it away.","zh":"她觉得这样扔了倒也痛快。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The coach had gone on again when suddenly Monsieur Homais leant out through the window, crying—","sentences":[{"en":"The coach had gone on again when suddenly Monsieur Homais leant out through the window, crying—","zh":"车又走动了，郝麦先生忽然探出窗外喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No farinaceous or milk food, wear wool next the skin, and expose the diseased parts to the smoke of juniper berries.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No farinaceous or milk food, wear wool next the skin, and expose the diseased parts to the smoke of juniper berries.”","zh":"“不要吃淀粉质、乳质一类东西！拿羊毛贴身穿，拿杜松子的烟熏有病的地方！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The sight of the well-known objects that defiled before her eyes gradually diverted Emma from her present trouble. An intolerable fatigue overwhelmed her, and she reached her home stupefied, discouraged, almost asleep.","sentences":[{"en":"The sight of the well-known objects that defiled before her eyes gradually diverted Emma from her present trouble.","zh":"爱玛熟悉眼前景物。它们一个连一个，渐渐转移她的痛苦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"An intolerable fatigue overwhelmed her, and she reached her home stupefied, discouraged, almost asleep.","zh":"她疲倦到了极点，回到家来，心灰意懒，呆呆瞪瞪，快要睡着了。她自言自语道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come what may come!” she said to herself. “And then, who knows? Why, at any moment could not some extraordinary event occur? Lheureux even might die!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come what may come!” she said to herself.","zh":"“要来的就来吧！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“And then, who knows?","zh":"而且谁知道？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why, at any moment could not some extraordinary event occur?","zh":"时刻都有出现奇迹的可能，凭什么不？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lheureux even might die!”","zh":"勒乐兴许会死掉。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At nine o’clock in the morning she was awakened by the sound of voices in the Place. There was a crowd round the market reading a large bill fixed to one of the posts, and she saw Justin, who was climbing on to a stone and tearing down the bill. But at this moment the rural guard seized him by the collar. Monsieur Homais came out of his shop, and Mere Lefrançois, in the midst of the crowd, seemed to be perorating.","sentences":[{"en":"At nine o’clock in the morning she was awakened by the sound of voices in the Place.","zh":"早晨九点钟，广场那边，人声嘈杂，吵醒了她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was a crowd round the market reading a large bill fixed to one of the posts, and she saw Justin, who was climbing on to a stone and tearing down the bill.","zh":"一大群人围住菜场，读着柱子上张贴的大告示。她望见朱斯丹蹬上界石撕它。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But at this moment the rural guard seized him by the collar.","zh":"可是就在这时，猎警抓住了他的肩膀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Homais came out of his shop, and Mere Lefrançois, in the midst of the crowd, seemed to be perorating.","zh":"郝麦先生走出药房；勒弗朗索瓦太太站在人群中，模样像在讲说什么。全福边喊，边进来道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Madame! madame!” cried Félicité, running in, “it’s abominable!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Madame! madame!” cried Félicité, running in, “it’s abominable!”","zh":"“太太！太太！太可恨啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And the poor girl, deeply moved, handed her a yellow paper that she had just torn off the door. Emma read with a glance that all her furniture was for sale.","sentences":[{"en":"And the poor girl, deeply moved, handed her a yellow paper that she had just torn off the door.","zh":"可怜的姑娘，慌里慌张，递给她一张刚在门口撕下的黄纸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma read with a glance that all her furniture was for sale.","zh":"爱玛一眼就看清上面写着：出卖她的全部动产。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then they looked at one another silently. The servant and mistress had no secret one from the other. At last Félicité sighed—","sentences":[{"en":"Then they looked at one another silently.","zh":"她们于是不声不响，你看着我，我看着你。她们主仆之间没有相瞒的事情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The servant and mistress had no secret one from the other.","zh":"她们于是不声不响，你看着我，我看着你。她们主仆之间没有相瞒的事情。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last Félicité sighed—","zh":"全福最后叹气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If I were you, madame, I should go to Monsieur Guillaumin.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If I were you, madame, I should go to Monsieur Guillaumin.”","zh":"“我要是您的话，太太，我会找居由曼先生的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do you think—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you think—”","zh":"“你看行？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And this question meant to say—","sentences":[{"en":"And this question meant to say—","zh":"这句问话的意思是：“你和听差好，清楚底细，莫非主人有时候说起我？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You who know the house through the servant, has the master spoken sometimes of me?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You who know the house through the servant, has the master spoken sometimes of me?”","zh":"这句问话的意思是：“你和听差好，清楚底细，莫非主人有时候说起我？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Yes, you’d do well to go there.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, you’d do well to go there.”","zh":"“行，去吧，有好处的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She dressed, put on her black gown, and her hood with jet beads, and that she might not be seen (there was still a crowd on the Place), she took the path by the river, outside the village.","sentences":[{"en":"She dressed, put on her black gown, and her hood with jet beads, and that she might not be seen (there was still a crowd on the Place), she took the path by the river, outside the village.","zh":"她穿上她的黑袍子，戴上她有黑星星的帽子；她怕人看见（广场总有许多人），绕到村外，走河边小径。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She reached the notary’s gate quite breathless. The sky was sombre, and a little snow was falling. At the sound of the bell, Theodore in a red waistcoat appeared on the steps; he came to open the door almost familiarly, as to an acquaintance, and showed her into the dining-room.","sentences":[{"en":"She reached the notary’s gate quite breathless.","zh":"她气喘吁吁，来到公证人栅栏门前；天色阴沉，飘着小雪。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The sky was sombre, and a little snow was falling.","zh":"她气喘吁吁，来到公证人栅栏门前；天色阴沉，飘着小雪。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At the sound of the bell, Theodore in a red waistcoat appeared on the steps; he came to open the door almost familiarly, as to an acquaintance, and showed her into the dining-room.","zh":"泰奥多尔听见铃响。穿着红背心，来到台阶上，一看是她，上前开门，好像迎接一位熟人一样，并不问长问短，就请进饭厅去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A large porcelain stove crackled beneath a cactus that filled up the niche in the wall, and in black wood frames against the oak-stained paper hung Steuben’s “Esmeralda” and Schopin’s “Potiphar.” The ready-laid table, the two silver chafing-dishes, the crystal door-knobs, the parquet and the furniture, all shone with a scrupulous, English cleanliness; the windows were ornamented at each corner with stained glass.","sentences":[{"en":"A large porcelain stove crackled beneath a cactus that filled up the niche in the wall, and in black wood frames against the oak-stained paper hung Steuben’s “Esmeralda” and Schopin’s “Potiphar.”","zh":"壁龛里搁着一棵仙人掌，底下有一个大瓷炉，毕毕剥剥在响，墙纸是橡树枝叶，上面挂着黑木框子，里头是斯特本的《爱斯梅拉达》和邵班的《波提乏》。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The ready-laid table, the two silver chafing-dishes, the crystal door-knobs, the parquet and the furniture, all shone with a scrupulous, English cleanliness; the windows were ornamented at each corner with stained glass.","zh":"早饭开好了，两只银火锅、水晶门球、拼花地板和家具，样样透亮，一尘不染，干干净净，像英国人的房间一样。窗户四角镶的是花玻璃。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Now this,” thought Emma, “is the dining-room I ought to have.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now this,” thought Emma, “is the dining-room I ought to have.”","zh":"爱玛心想：这才叫作饭厅，我要的正是这样一间饭厅。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The notary came in pressing his palm-leaf dressing-gown to his breast with his left arm, while with the other hand he raised and quickly put on again his brown velvet cap, pretentiously cocked on the right side, whence looked out the ends of three fair curls drawn from the back of the head, following the line of his bald skull.","sentences":[{"en":"The notary came in pressing his palm-leaf dressing-gown to his breast with his left arm, while with the other hand he raised and quickly put on again his brown velvet cap, pretentiously cocked on the right side, whence looked out the ends of three fair curls drawn from the back of the head, following the line of his bald skull.","zh":"公证人进来，左胳膊压住他的棕榈树叶图案便服，右手摘下他的栗色丝绒小帽，又迅速戴好。小帽偏右，高高在上，底下露出三根金黄头发，从后脑向前盘，兜住他的秃脑壳，绕了一匝。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"After he had offered her a seat he sat down to breakfast, apologising profusely for his rudeness.","sentences":[{"en":"After he had offered her a seat he sat down to breakfast, apologising profusely for his rudeness.","zh":"他先请她就座，然后一面坐下用早饭，一面连声道歉，说他失礼。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I have come,” she said, “to beg you, sir—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I have come,” she said, “to beg you, sir—”","zh":"“先生，我求您…”“夫人有事见教？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What, madame? I am listening.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What, madame?","zh":"她对他说起她的情形。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I am listening.”","zh":"她对他说起她的情形。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And she began explaining her position to him. Monsieur Guillaumin knew it, being secretly associated with the linendraper, from whom he always got capital for the loans on mortgages that he was asked to make.","sentences":[{"en":"And she began explaining her position to him.","zh":"她即使不说，居由曼律师也知道，因为他和布商私下有勾当，遇到有人拿东西押款的时候，布庄总有资金供他用。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Monsieur Guillaumin knew it, being secretly associated with the linendraper, from whom he always got capital for the loans on mortgages that he was asked to make.","zh":"她即使不说，居由曼律师也知道，因为他和布商私下有勾当，遇到有人拿东西押款的时候，布庄总有资金供他用。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"So he knew (and better than she herself) the long story of the bills, small at first, bearing different names as endorsers, made out at long dates, and constantly renewed up to the day, when, gathering together all the protested bills, the shopkeeper had bidden his friend Vincart take in his own name all the necessary proceedings, not wishing to pass for a tiger with his fellow-citizens.","sentences":[{"en":"So he knew (and better than she herself) the long story of the bills, small at first, bearing different names as endorsers, made out at long dates, and constantly renewed up to the day, when, gathering together all the protested bills, the shopkeeper had bidden his friend Vincart take in his own name all the necessary proceedings, not wishing to pass for a tiger with his fellow-citizens.","zh":"所以他比她还清楚这些票据的悠久历史：起先微不足道，用不同的名姓签订，期限延长，到期又不断续下去，挨到最后一天，商人把拒付的票据聚在一道，委托他的朋友万萨出面，追索欠款，因为自己不希望当地居民把他看成豺狼。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She mingled her story with recriminations against Lheureux, to which the notary replied from time to time with some insignificant word. Eating his cutlet and drinking his tea, he buried his chin in his sky-blue cravat, into which were thrust two diamond pins, held together by a small gold chain; and he smiled a singular smile, in a sugary, ambiguous fashion. But noticing that her feet were damp, he said—","sentences":[{"en":"She mingled her story with recriminations against Lheureux, to which the notary replied from time to time with some insignificant word.","zh":"她叙说中，免不了咒骂勒乐几句，公证人听见她骂，不时来一句无关痛痒的话支应。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Eating his cutlet and drinking his tea, he buried his chin in his sky-blue cravat, into which were thrust two diamond pins, held together by a small gold chain; and he smiled a singular smile, in a sugary, ambiguous fashion.","zh":"他吃他的排骨肉，喝他的茶，下巴缩进他的天蓝领带。一条小金链子连起两个金刚石别针，别住他的领带。他显出一种古怪的微笑，样子又甜，又模棱两可。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But noticing that her feet were damp, he said—","zh":"他看见她的鞋湿，就道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do get closer to the stove; put your feet up against the porcelain.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do get closer to the stove; put your feet up against the porcelain.”","zh":"“靠近炉子…脚再高些…蹬到瓷上头好了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was afraid of dirtying it. The notary replied in a gallant tone—","sentences":[{"en":"She was afraid of dirtying it.","zh":"她怕把瓷弄脏了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The notary replied in a gallant tone—","zh":"公证人用一种交际口吻道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Beautiful things spoil nothing.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Beautiful things spoil nothing.”","zh":"“漂亮的东西，无往而不相宜。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she tried to move him, and, growing moved herself, she began telling him about the poorness of her home, her worries, her wants. He could understand that; an elegant woman! and, without leaving off eating, he had turned completely round towards her, so that his knee brushed against her boot, whose sole curled round as it smoked against the stove.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she tried to move him, and, growing moved herself, she began telling him about the poorness of her home, her worries, her wants.","zh":"她听了这话，就试着拿话打动他，可是说着说着，自己动了感情，什么家庭拮据喽、艰难喽、需要喽。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He could understand that; an elegant woman! and, without leaving off eating, he had turned completely round towards her, so that his knee brushed against her boot, whose sole curled round as it smoked against the stove.","zh":"他明白这个：像她这样一位上流女子！他并不中止用饭，可是身子完全转向她，膝盖蹭着她的小靴，小靴底朝炉子弯着，一边还在冒气。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But when she asked for a thousand sous, he closed his lips, and declared he was very sorry he had not had the management of her fortune before, for there were hundreds of ways very convenient, even for a lady, of turning her money to account. They might, either in the turf-peats of Grumesnil or building-ground at Havre, almost without risk, have ventured on some excellent speculations; and he let her consume herself with rage at the thought of the fabulous sums that she would certainly have made.","sentences":[{"en":"But when she asked for a thousand sous, he closed his lips, and declared he was very sorry he had not had the management of her fortune before, for there were hundreds of ways very convenient, even for a lady, of turning her money to account.","zh":"但是临到她问他借一千埃居，他先是闭紧嘴唇，接着就讲：他很遗憾从前没有帮她料理财产，因为即使是一位女流，也有种种方法拿钱生息赢利。格吕梅尼泥炭矿也好，勒阿弗尔地皮也好，都是绝好的投机机会，万无一失。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They might, either in the turf-peats of Grumesnil or building-ground at Havre, almost without risk, have ventured on some excellent speculations; and he let her consume herself with rage at the thought of the fabulous sums that she would certainly have made.","zh":"她想到自己原有可能大发其财，心里很懊恼。他接下去道：“您先前为什么不来舍下呀？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“How was it,” he went on, “that you didn’t come to me?”","sentences":[{"en":"“How was it,” he went on, “that you didn’t come to me?”","zh":"她道：“我也不知道是怎么一回事。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I hardly know,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“I hardly know,” she said.","zh":"“为什么，嗯？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, hey? Did I frighten you so much? It is I, on the contrary, who ought to complain. We hardly know one another; yet I am very devoted to you. You do not doubt that, I hope?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, hey?","zh":"难道我就那么让您害怕？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Did I frighten you so much?","zh":"难道我就那么让您害怕？","scope":"group"},{"en":"It is I, on the contrary, who ought to complain.","zh":"正相反，应当诉苦的是我！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We hardly know one another; yet I am very devoted to you.","zh":"我们几乎连认识都说不上！可是我非常关心您；我希望，您不会再不相信了吧？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"You do not doubt that, I hope?”","zh":"我们几乎连认识都说不上！可是我非常关心您；我希望，您不会再不相信了吧？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He held out his hand, took hers, covered it with a greedy kiss, then held it on his knee; and he played delicately with her fingers whilst he murmured a thousand blandishments. His insipid voice murmured like a running brook; a light shone in his eyes through the glimmering of his spectacles, and his hand was advancing up Emma’s sleeve to press her arm. She felt against her cheek his panting breath. This man oppressed her horribly.","sentences":[{"en":"He held out his hand, took hers, covered it with a greedy kiss, then held it on his knee; and he played delicately with her fingers whilst he murmured a thousand blandishments.","zh":"他伸出手，握住她的手，饿狼般吻着，然后留在膝盖上，意兴盎然，玩弄她的手指，一面对她说着种种媚言媚语。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His insipid voice murmured like a running brook; a light shone in his eyes through the glimmering of his spectacles, and his hand was advancing up Emma’s sleeve to press her arm.","zh":"他平板的声音，嗫嗫嚅嚅，好像一条小河在流一样；他的瞳仁射出一道光，透过他闪烁的镜片；他的手伸到爱玛的袖筒，抚摸她的胳膊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She felt against her cheek his panting breath.","zh":"她觉得一股粗气吹她的脸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This man oppressed her horribly.","zh":"这人讨厌到了极点。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She sprang up and said to him—","sentences":[{"en":"She sprang up and said to him—","zh":"她跳起来向他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Sir, I am waiting.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Sir, I am waiting.”","zh":"“先生，我在等着！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For what?” said the notary, who suddenly became very pale.","sentences":[{"en":"“For what?” said the notary, who suddenly became very pale.","zh":"公证人的脸，突然之间，一点血色也没有了。他问道：“等什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“This money.”","sentences":[{"en":"“This money.”","zh":"“那笔钱。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But—” Then, yielding to the outburst of too powerful a desire, “Well, yes!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But—” Then, yielding to the outburst of too powerful a desire, “Well, yes!”","zh":"可是禁不住欲火如焚，只好认账道：“好吧，有！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He dragged himself towards her on his knees, regardless of his dressing-gown.","sentences":[{"en":"He dragged himself towards her on his knees, regardless of his dressing-gown.","zh":"他不管便袍会不会弄脏，朝她跪着走了过来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For pity’s sake, stay. I love you!”","sentences":[{"en":"“For pity’s sake, stay.","zh":"“求求您 ，待下来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I love you!”","zh":"我爱您！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He seized her by her waist. Madame Bovary’s face flushed purple. She recoiled with a terrible look, crying—","sentences":[{"en":"He seized her by her waist.","zh":"他搂她的腰。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madame Bovary’s face flushed purple.","zh":"爱玛立刻脸红了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She recoiled with a terrible look, crying—","zh":"她神情可怖，往后倒退，一面嚷道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are taking a shameless advantage of my distress, sir! I am to be pitied—not to be sold.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are taking a shameless advantage of my distress, sir!","zh":"“先生，您丧尽天良，欺负我这落难的人！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I am to be pitied—not to be sold.”","zh":"我可怜，但是并不出卖自己！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she went out.","sentences":[{"en":"And she went out.","zh":"她出去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The notary remained quite stupefied, his eyes fixed on his fine embroidered slippers. They were a love gift, and the sight of them at last consoled him. Besides, he reflected that such an adventure might have carried him too far.","sentences":[{"en":"The notary remained quite stupefied, his eyes fixed on his fine embroidered slippers.","zh":"公证人一惊之下，愣愣磕磕，眼睛死盯着他漂亮的绣花拖鞋——这是情妇送他的礼物。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were a love gift, and the sight of them at last consoled him.","zh":"公证人一惊之下，愣愣磕磕，眼睛死盯着他漂亮的绣花拖鞋——这是情妇送他的礼物。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Besides, he reflected that such an adventure might have carried him too far.","zh":"绣花拖鞋最后安慰了他。再说，他怕这事闹下去，不可收拾。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What a wretch! what a scoundrel! what an infamy!” she said to herself, as she fled with nervous steps beneath the aspens of the path. The disappointment of her failure increased the indignation of her outraged modesty; it seemed to her that Providence pursued her implacably, and, strengthening herself in her pride, she had never felt so much esteem for herself nor so much contempt for others. A spirit of warfare transformed her. She would have liked to strike all men, to spit in their faces, to crush them, and she walked rapidly straight on, pale, quivering, maddened, searching the empty horizon with tear-dimmed eyes, and as it were rejoicing in the hate that was choking her.","sentences":[{"en":"“What a wretch! what a scoundrel! what an infamy!” she said to herself, as she fled with nervous steps beneath the aspens of the path.","zh":"她飞快地逃到大路上的山杨树下，自言自语道：“多混账！多下流！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The disappointment of her failure increased the indignation of her outraged modesty; it seemed to her that Providence pursued her implacably, and, strengthening herself in her pride, she had never felt so much esteem for herself nor so much contempt for others.","zh":"多无耻！”借不到钱的失望，更加强了贞节受到侮辱的气愤。她想到上天一意同她为难，反而骄傲起来：她从来没有这样高看过自己，也从来不曾这样小看过别人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A spirit of warfare transformed her.","zh":"她产生了好斗情绪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would have liked to strike all men, to spit in their faces, to crush them, and she walked rapidly straight on, pale, quivering, maddened, searching the empty horizon with tear-dimmed eyes, and as it were rejoicing in the hate that was choking her.","zh":"恨不得打男人们一顿，啐他们的脸，把他们踏得粉碎。她快步朝前走去，脸色苍白，浑身哆嗦，怒不可遏，泪眼望着空空落落的天边，好像陶醉于满腹的憎恨一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When she saw her house a numbness came over her. She could not go on; and yet she must. Besides, whither could she flee?","sentences":[{"en":"When she saw her house a numbness came over her.","zh":"她望见她的住宅，觉得一阵麻木，再也走不过去，但又非过去不可；何况她能往哪儿逃呢？","scope":"group"},{"en":"She could not go on; and yet she must.","zh":"她望见她的住宅，觉得一阵麻木，再也走不过去，但又非过去不可；何况她能往哪儿逃呢？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Besides, whither could she flee?","zh":"她望见她的住宅，觉得一阵麻木，再也走不过去，但又非过去不可；何况她能往哪儿逃呢？","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Félicité was waiting for her at the door. “Well?”","sentences":[{"en":"Félicité was waiting for her at the door.","zh":"全福在门口等她回来。“怎么样？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Well?”","zh":"全福在门口等她回来。“怎么样？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“No!” said Emma.","sentences":[{"en":"“No!” said Emma.","zh":"爱玛道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And for a quarter of an hour the two of them went over the various persons in Yonville who might perhaps be inclined to help her. But each time that Félicité named someone Emma replied—","sentences":[{"en":"And for a quarter of an hour the two of them went over the various persons in Yonville who might perhaps be inclined to help her.","zh":"“借不到！”两个人说起永镇上可能救她的各色人等，说了足足一刻钟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But each time that Félicité named someone Emma replied—","zh":"但是全福每说一个人名，爱玛就驳道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Impossible! they will not!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Impossible! they will not!”","zh":"“不行！他们不肯的！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“And the master’ll soon be in.”","sentences":[{"en":"“And the master’ll soon be in.”","zh":"“可是老爷就要回来！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I know that well enough. Leave me alone.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I know that well enough.","zh":"“我知道…你先让我一个人待一会儿。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Leave me alone.”","zh":"“我知道…你先让我一个人待一会儿。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She had tried everything; there was nothing more to be done now; and when Charles came in she would have to say to him—","sentences":[{"en":"She had tried everything; there was nothing more to be done now; and when Charles came in she would have to say to him—","zh":"她全试过了。现在她只有束手待毙；等查理回来，她只好对他讲：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Go away! This carpet on which you are walking is no longer ours. In your own house you do not possess a chair, a pin, a straw, and it is I, poor man, who have ruined you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Go away!","zh":"“走开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This carpet on which you are walking is no longer ours.","zh":"你脚踩的这条地毯已经不是我们的了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In your own house you do not possess a chair, a pin, a straw, and it is I, poor man, who have ruined you.”","zh":"家里一件家具、一个别针、一根草，都不是你的。可怜人，害你破产的就是我！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then there would be a great sob; next he would weep abundantly, and at last, the surprise past, he would forgive her.","sentences":[{"en":"Then there would be a great sob; next he would weep abundantly, and at last, the surprise past, he would forgive her.","zh":"他听了这话，呜咽一大阵，眼泪再流一大堆，最后惊惶过去，他会宽恕的。她咬住牙，咕哝道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes,” she murmured, grinding her teeth, “he will forgive me, he who would give a million if I would forgive him for having known me! Never! never!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes,” she murmured, grinding her teeth, “he will forgive me, he who would give a million if I would forgive him for having known me!","zh":"“是啊，他会宽恕我的，可是他有一百万献给我，我也不原谅他认识我…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Never! never!”","zh":"决不！不！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This thought of Bovary’s superiority to her exasperated her. Then, whether she confessed or did not confess, presently, immediately, to-morrow, he would know the catastrophe all the same; so she must wait for this horrible scene, and bear the weight of his magnanimity. The desire to return to Lheureux’s seized her—what would be the use? To write to her father—it was too late; and perhaps, she began to repent now that she had not yielded to that other, when she heard the trot of a horse in the alley. It was he; he was opening the gate; he was whiter than the plaster wall. Rushing to the stairs, she ran out quickly to the square; and the wife of the mayor, who was talking to Lestiboudois in front of the church, saw her go in to the tax-collector’s.","sentences":[{"en":"This thought of Bovary’s superiority to her exasperated her.","zh":"想到包法利占着上风，她就怒火冲天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, whether she confessed or did not confess, presently, immediately, to-morrow, he would know the catastrophe all the same; so she must wait for this horrible scene, and bear the weight of his magnanimity.","zh":"其实她说出来也罢，不说出来也罢，迟早今明，他不会不知道的。这样看来，她非等待这可怕的场面不可，非忍受他的宽宏大量不可。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The desire to return to Lheureux’s seized her—what would be the use?","zh":"她想再去求求勒乐，不过有什么用？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To write to her father—it was too late; and perhaps, she began to repent now that she had not yielded to that other, when she heard the trot of a horse in the alley.","zh":"写信给她父亲：太晚了；也许她现在后悔没有依顺公证人。她听见小巷马蹄走动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was he; he was opening the gate; he was whiter than the plaster wall.","zh":"是他；他在开栅栏门，脸色比石墙还白。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rushing to the stairs, she ran out quickly to the square; and the wife of the mayor, who was talking to Lestiboudois in front of the church, saw her go in to the tax-collector’s.","zh":"她一步跳下楼梯，连忙逃往广场。镇长太太正在教堂前面和赖斯地布杜瓦闲谈，看见她走进税务员的住宅。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She hurried off to tell Madame Caron, and the two ladies went up to the attic, and, hidden by some linen spread across props, stationed themselves comfortably for overlooking the whole of Binet’s room.","sentences":[{"en":"She hurried off to tell Madame Caron, and the two ladies went up to the attic, and, hidden by some linen spread across props, stationed themselves comfortably for overlooking the whole of Binet’s room.","zh":"她跑去告诉卡隆太太。两位夫人走上阁楼，躲在晾在竿上的衣服后面，位置恰好望见毕耐屋里。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was alone in his garret, busy imitating in wood one of those indescribable bits of ivory, composed of crescents, of spheres hollowed out one within the other, the whole as straight as an obelisk, and of no use whatever; and he was beginning on the last piece—he was nearing his goal. In the twilight of the workshop the white dust was flying from his tools like a shower of sparks under the hoofs of a galloping horse; the two wheels were turning, droning; Binet smiled, his chin lowered, his nostrils distended, and, in a word, seemed lost in one of those complete happinesses that, no doubt, belong only to commonplace occupations, which amuse the mind with facile difficulties, and satisfy by a realisation of that beyond which such minds have not a dream.","sentences":[{"en":"He was alone in his garret, busy imitating in wood one of those indescribable bits of ivory, composed of crescents, of spheres hollowed out one within the other, the whole as straight as an obelisk, and of no use whatever; and he was beginning on the last piece—he was nearing his goal.","zh":"他独自待在顶层的小屋，正在拿木头仿制一个奇形怪状的象牙摆设：由月牙和一个套一个的空球组成、方尖碑似的无用东西；他如今做到末一环节，眼看就要大功告成！金黄木屑从他的工具飞出，在制作室的光影之间，好像快马疾驰、铁蹄底下爆出来的火星一样。两只轮子呜隆呜隆在转。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the twilight of the workshop the white dust was flying from his tools like a shower of sparks under the hoofs of a galloping horse; the two wheels were turning, droning; Binet smiled, his chin lowered, his nostrils distended, and, in a word, seemed lost in one of those complete happinesses that, no doubt, belong only to commonplace occupations, which amuse the mind with facile difficulties, and satisfy by a realisation of that beyond which such minds have not a dream.","zh":"毕耐一脸微笑，下巴朝下，鼻孔张开，似乎沉醉在美满的幸福中。这类活计，以微不足道的困难娱乐心灵，完成了，人也就心满意足，不再想它了。毕耐的幸福，毫无疑问，就是这类平庸活计的产物。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! there she is!” exclaimed Madame Tuvache.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! there she is!” exclaimed Madame Tuvache.","zh":"杜法赦太太道：“啊！那不是她！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But it was impossible because of the lathe to hear what she was saying.","sentences":[{"en":"But it was impossible because of the lathe to hear what she was saying.","zh":"但是旋床太响，她们听不见她说什么。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last these ladies thought they made out the word “francs,” and Madame Tuvache whispered in a low voice—","sentences":[{"en":"At last these ladies thought they made out the word “francs,” and Madame Tuvache whispered in a low voice—","zh":"最后，两位夫人仿佛听到法郎这个词，杜法赦太太耳语道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“She is begging him to give her time for paying her taxes.”","sentences":[{"en":"“She is begging him to give her time for paying her taxes.”","zh":"“她付不出捐税，求他许她缓付。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Apparently!” replied the other.","sentences":[{"en":"“Apparently!” replied the other.","zh":"另一位太太道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They saw her walking up and down, examining the napkin-rings, the candlesticks, the banister rails against the walls, while Binet stroked his beard with satisfaction.","sentences":[{"en":"They saw her walking up and down, examining the napkin-rings, the candlesticks, the banister rails against the walls, while Binet stroked his beard with satisfaction.","zh":"“像是！”她们望见她走来走去，看看墙边的饭巾环、蜡烛台、栏杆柱头的圆球，同时毕耐心满意足，摩弄胡须。杜法赦太太道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do you think she wants to order something of him?” said Madame Tuvache.","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you think she wants to order something of him?” said Madame Tuvache.","zh":"“她来是不是要定做什么东西？”她的女邻居反驳道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, he doesn’t sell anything,” objected her neighbour.","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, he doesn’t sell anything,” objected her neighbour.","zh":"“他什么也不卖！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The tax-collector seemed to be listening with wide-open eyes, as if he did not understand. She went on in a tender, suppliant manner. She came nearer to him, her breast heaving; they no longer spoke.","sentences":[{"en":"The tax-collector seemed to be listening with wide-open eyes, as if he did not understand.","zh":"税务员的样子仿佛在听，可是睁大眼睛，又像听不明白一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She went on in a tender, suppliant manner.","zh":"她讲话的姿态又动人，又可怜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She came nearer to him, her breast heaving; they no longer spoke.","zh":"她走近了，胸脯忽上忽下。他们不言语了。杜法赦太太道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Is she making him advances?” said Madame Tuvache. Binet was scarlet to his very ears. She took hold of his hands.","sentences":[{"en":"“Is she making him advances?” said Madame Tuvache.","zh":"“她是不是在勾搭他？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Binet was scarlet to his very ears.","zh":"毕耐连耳梢也红了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She took hold of his hands.","zh":"她抓住他的手。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, it’s too much!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it’s too much!”","zh":"“啊！太不像话！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And no doubt she was suggesting something abominable to him; for the tax-collector—yet he was brave, had fought at Bautzen and at Lutzen, had been through the French campaign, and had even been recommended for the cross—suddenly, as at the sight of a serpent, recoiled as far as he could from her, crying—","sentences":[{"en":"And no doubt she was suggesting something abominable to him; for the tax-collector—yet he was brave, had fought at Bautzen and at Lutzen, had been through the French campaign, and had even been recommended for the cross—suddenly, as at the sight of a serpent, recoiled as far as he could from her, crying—","zh":"毫无疑问，她作出非礼的建议，因为税务员——可是人家勇敢，在波岑和吕岑打过仗， 为法兰西而战，还列在“请奖名单”之中——忽然退得老远，好像看见一条蛇一样，喊道：“夫人！您真这样想？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Madame! what do you mean?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Madame! what do you mean?”","zh":"杜法赦太太道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Women like that ought to be whipped,” said Madame Tuvache.","sentences":[{"en":"“Women like that ought to be whipped,” said Madame Tuvache.","zh":"“这种女人就欠鞭子抽！”卡隆太太问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But where is she?” continued Madame Caron, for she had disappeared whilst they spoke; then catching sight of her going up the Grande Rue, and turning to the right as if making for the cemetery, they were lost in conjectures.","sentences":[{"en":"“But where is she?” continued Madame Caron, for she had disappeared whilst they spoke; then catching sight of her going up the Grande Rue, and turning to the right as if making for the cemetery, they were lost in conjectures.","zh":"“她哪儿去啦？”因为她们说话中间，她已经不见了；她们后来望见她贴大街走，好像要去公墓，又朝右转，彼此乱猜一阵，也猜不出一个所以然来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Nurse Rollet,” she said on reaching the nurse’s, “I am choking; unlace me!” She fell on the bed sobbing. Nurse Rollet covered her with a petticoat and remained standing by her side. Then, as she did not answer, the good woman withdrew, took her wheel and began spinning flax.","sentences":[{"en":"“Nurse Rollet,” she said on reaching the nurse’s, “I am choking; unlace me!”","zh":"她走到奶妈家，说道：“罗莱嫂子，我出不来气！帮我解解带子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She fell on the bed sobbing.","zh":"”她躺在床上只是哭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nurse Rollet covered her with a petticoat and remained standing by her side.","zh":"罗莱嫂子给她盖上一条围裙，站在一旁，等她说话。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, as she did not answer, the good woman withdrew, took her wheel and began spinning flax.","zh":"老实女人见她始终不回答，走开了，坐在纺车跟前纺麻。她以为是毕耐的旋床响，咕哝道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, leave off!” she murmured, fancying she heard Binet’s lathe.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, leave off!” she murmured, fancying she heard Binet’s lathe.","zh":"“嗐！停了吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What’s bothering her?” said the nurse to herself. “Why has she come here?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s bothering her?” said the nurse to herself.","zh":"奶妈纳闷道：“谁得罪她啦？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Why has she come here?”","zh":"她来这儿做什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She had rushed thither; impelled by a kind of horror that drove her from her home.","sentences":[{"en":"She had rushed thither; impelled by a kind of horror that drove her from her home.","zh":"她跑到这里，活像家里出了煞神，把她吓跑了一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Lying on her back, motionless, and with staring eyes, she saw things but vaguely, although she tried to with idiotic persistence. She looked at the scales on the walls, two brands smoking end to end, and a long spider crawling over her head in a rent in the beam. At last she began to collect her thoughts. She remembered—one day—Léon—Oh! how long ago that was—the sun was shining on the river, and the clematis were perfuming the air. Then, carried away as by a rushing torrent, she soon began to recall the day before.","sentences":[{"en":"Lying on her back, motionless, and with staring eyes, she saw things but vaguely, although she tried to with idiotic persistence.","zh":"她仰天躺着，动也不动，眼睛直瞪瞪的，好像白痴一样，死看东西，可是看到的，只是一片模糊。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She looked at the scales on the walls, two brands smoking end to end, and a long spider crawling over her head in a rent in the beam.","zh":"她望着墙上的剥蚀的墙皮、头对头冒烟的两块劈柴、一个在头上横梁缝走动的长蜘蛛。她终于集中思想，记起…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last she began to collect her thoughts.","zh":"有一天，和赖昂…唉！许久以前…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She remembered—one day—Léon—Oh! how long ago that was—the sun was shining on the river, and the clematis were perfuming the air.","zh":"太阳照耀河面，铁线莲香气扑鼻…于是回忆如同湍流一样，很快就把她带到昨天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, carried away as by a rushing torrent, she soon began to recall the day before.","zh":"她问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What time is it?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“What time is it?” she asked.","zh":"“几点钟了？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Mere Rollet went out, raised the fingers of her right hand to that side of the sky that was brightest, and came back slowly, saying—","sentences":[{"en":"Mere Rollet went out, raised the fingers of her right hand to that side of the sky that was brightest, and came back slowly, saying—","zh":"罗莱嫂子走出房间，朝天色最亮的方向，举起右手手指，慢慢腾腾回来道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Nearly three.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Nearly three.”","zh":"“快三点了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! thanks, thanks!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! thanks, thanks!”","zh":"“好！谢谢！谢谢！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For he would come; he would have found some money. But he would, perhaps, go down yonder, not guessing she was here, and she told the nurse to run to her house to fetch him.","sentences":[{"en":"For he would come; he would have found some money.","zh":"因为他就要来了。一定会来的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But he would, perhaps, go down yonder, not guessing she was here, and she told the nurse to run to her house to fetch him.","zh":"他会弄到钱的。不过他想不到她在这里，也许去了那边；她吩咐奶妈跑到她家去，把他带过来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Be quick!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Be quick!”","zh":"“快呀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But, my dear lady, I’m going, I’m going!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But, my dear lady, I’m going, I’m going!”","zh":"“我的好太太，我去！我去！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She wondered now that she had not thought of him from the first. Yesterday he had given his word; he would not break it. And she already saw herself at Lheureux’s spreading out her three bank-notes on his bureau. Then she would have to invent some story to explain matters to Bovary. What should it be?","sentences":[{"en":"She wondered now that she had not thought of him from the first.","zh":"她现在奇怪她开头怎么没想到他，昨天他赌了咒：不会爽约的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Yesterday he had given his word; he would not break it.","zh":"她现在奇怪她开头怎么没想到他，昨天他赌了咒：不会爽约的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And she already saw herself at Lheureux’s spreading out her three bank-notes on his bureau.","zh":"她看见自己像是已经到了勒乐那边，掏出三张支票，往他的书桌一丢。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she would have to invent some story to explain matters to Bovary.","zh":"事后还得捏造一篇鬼话，向包法利解释。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What should it be?","zh":"什么鬼话？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The nurse, however, was a long while gone. But, as there was no clock in the cot, Emma feared she was perhaps exaggerating the length of time. She began walking round the garden, step by step; she went into the path by the hedge, and returned quickly, hoping that the woman would have come back by another road. At last, weary of waiting, assailed by fears that she thrust from her, no longer conscious whether she had been here a century or a moment, she sat down in a corner, closed her eyes, and stopped her ears. The gate grated; she sprang up. Before she had spoken Mere Rollet said to her—","sentences":[{"en":"The nurse, however, was a long while gone.","zh":"奶妈去了许久，不见回来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But, as there was no clock in the cot, Emma feared she was perhaps exaggerating the length of time.","zh":"可是草屋里没有钟，爱玛心想，也许是自己把时间扯长了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She began walking round the garden, step by step; she went into the path by the hedge, and returned quickly, hoping that the woman would have come back by another road.","zh":"她放慢脚步，围着园子走动；她沿着篱笆，走进小径，又连忙走回，希望老实女人走别的路回来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, weary of waiting, assailed by fears that she thrust from her, no longer conscious whether she had been here a century or a moment, she sat down in a corner, closed her eyes, and stopped her ears.","zh":"最后，她等累了，起了疑心，又不相信，恍恍惚惚，不知道自己在这里待了一世纪，还是一分钟，她坐在一个角落，闭住眼睛，堵住耳朵。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The gate grated; she sprang up.","zh":"栅栏门嘎吱在响；她一跃而起，可是罗莱嫂子不等她开口，先对她道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Before she had spoken Mere Rollet said to her—","zh":"栅栏门嘎吱在响；她一跃而起，可是罗莱嫂子不等她开口，先对她道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“There is no one at your house!”","sentences":[{"en":"“There is no one at your house!”","zh":"“你们家没有人！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“怎么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, no one! And the doctor is crying. He is calling for you; they’re looking for you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, no one!","zh":"“哎呀！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And the doctor is crying.","zh":"没有人！老爷在哭。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He is calling for you; they’re looking for you.”","zh":"他在喊您。他们在找您。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma answered nothing. She gasped as she turned her eyes about her, while the peasant woman, frightened at her face, drew back instinctively, thinking her mad. Suddenly she struck her brow and uttered a cry; for the thought of Rodolphe, like a flash of lightning in a dark night, had passed into her soul. He was so good, so delicate, so generous! And besides, should he hesitate to do her this service, she would know well enough how to constrain him to it by re-waking, in a single moment, their lost love. So she set out towards La Huchette, not seeing that she was hastening to offer herself to that which but a while ago had so angered her, not in the least conscious of her prostitution.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma answered nothing.","zh":"爱玛一言不发，喘着气，眼睛向四下张望，庄稼女人让她那副脸相吓坏了，心想她疯了，出于本能，直往后退。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She gasped as she turned her eyes about her, while the peasant woman, frightened at her face, drew back instinctively, thinking her mad.","zh":"爱玛一言不发，喘着气，眼睛向四下张望，庄稼女人让她那副脸相吓坏了，心想她疯了，出于本能，直往后退。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Suddenly she struck her brow and uttered a cry; for the thought of Rodolphe, like a flash of lightning in a dark night, had passed into her soul.","zh":"爱玛猛打自己的额头，叫了起来，因为她想到了罗道耳弗；这像一道强光，闪过沉沉的黑夜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was so good, so delicate, so generous!","zh":"他那样好，那样体贴，那样慷慨！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And besides, should he hesitate to do her this service, she would know well enough how to constrain him to it by re-waking, in a single moment, their lost love.","zh":"再说，即使他一时不想帮她这个忙，她也有法子逼他这么做的，她只要眼睛一瞟，他们的爱情就活过来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So she set out towards La Huchette, not seeing that she was hastening to offer herself to that which but a while ago had so angered her, not in the least conscious of her prostitution.","zh":"这样一想，她就去了于歇特。她看不出同样的事，方才她在公证人家，怒不可遏，现在她却跑着送上门去，根本没有理会这是卖淫。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-8","part":3,"n":8,"title":"Part III · Chapter 8","titleZh":"下卷 · 8","paragraphs":[{"en":"She asked herself as she walked along, “What am I going to say? How shall I begin?” And as she went on she recognised the thickets, the trees, the sea-rushes on the hill, the château yonder. All the sensations of her first tenderness came back to her, and her poor aching heart opened out amorously. A warm wind blew in her face; the melting snow fell drop by drop from the buds to the grass.","sentences":[{"en":"She asked herself as she walked along, “What am I going to say?","zh":"她边走，边问自己：“我说什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How shall I begin?”","zh":"我先说什么？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And as she went on she recognised the thickets, the trees, the sea-rushes on the hill, the château yonder.","zh":"她一路走下去，望见灌木、树木、岭上的黄刺条、远处的庄园，仿佛旧友重逢，又有了她初恋的心情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All the sensations of her first tenderness came back to her, and her poor aching heart opened out amorously.","zh":"她的可怜的心，也枯木逢春一般，欣欣向荣。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A warm wind blew in her face; the melting snow fell drop by drop from the buds to the grass.","zh":"暖风吹拂她的脸，雪在融化，一滴一滴，从树芽落在草上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She entered, as she used to, through the small park-gate. She reached the avenue bordered by a double row of dense lime-trees. They were swaying their long whispering branches to and fro. The dogs in their kennels all barked, and the noise of their voices resounded, but brought out no one.","sentences":[{"en":"She entered, as she used to, through the small park-gate.","zh":"她像先前一样，走进草坪的小门，来到正院。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She reached the avenue bordered by a double row of dense lime-trees.","zh":"边沿两排繁茂的菩提树，窸窸窣窣，长枝摇来摇去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They were swaying their long whispering branches to and fro.","zh":"边沿两排繁茂的菩提树，窸窸窣窣，长枝摇来摇去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The dogs in their kennels all barked, and the noise of their voices resounded, but brought out no one.","zh":"狗在狗舍吠成一片，响声震天，不见有人出来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She went up the large straight staircase with wooden balusters that led to the corridor paved with dusty flags, into which several doors in a row opened, as in a monastery or an inn. His was at the top, right at the end, on the left. When she placed her fingers on the lock her strength suddenly deserted her. She was afraid, almost wished he would not be there, though this was her only hope, her last chance of salvation. She collected her thoughts for one moment, and, strengthening herself by the feeling of present necessity, went in.","sentences":[{"en":"She went up the large straight staircase with wooden balusters that led to the corridor paved with dusty flags, into which several doors in a row opened, as in a monastery or an inn.","zh":"她走上装有木栏杆、又直又宽的楼梯，来到有灰尘的石板地过道，好像修道院或者旅馆一样，并排开着几扇门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His was at the top, right at the end, on the left.","zh":"他的房间在尽里左手。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"When she placed her fingers on the lock her strength suddenly deserted her.","zh":"她拿手指搁到门扶手上，忽然感到软弱无力。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was afraid, almost wished he would not be there, though this was her only hope, her last chance of salvation.","zh":"她害怕他不在家，却又几乎希望他不在，然而这是她唯一的指望、最后的机会。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She collected her thoughts for one moment, and, strengthening herself by the feeling of present necessity, went in.","zh":"她停一分钟定了定神，想着时间紧迫，只好鼓足勇气走进去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was in front of the fire, both his feet on the mantelpiece, smoking a pipe.","sentences":[{"en":"He was in front of the fire, both his feet on the mantelpiece, smoking a pipe.","zh":"他坐在壁炉前面，两只脚放在框子上，噙着烟斗吸烟。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What! it is you!” he said, getting up hurriedly.","sentences":[{"en":"“What! it is you!” he said, getting up hurriedly.","zh":"他一看是她，连忙跳起来道：“嗐！是您！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, it is I, Rodolphe. I should like to ask your advice.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, it is I, Rodolphe.","zh":"“是呀，是我！我想，罗道耳弗，请教一个主意。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I should like to ask your advice.”","zh":"“是呀，是我！我想，罗道耳弗，请教一个主意。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And, despite all her efforts, it was impossible for her to open her lips.","sentences":[{"en":"And, despite all her efforts, it was impossible for her to open her lips.","zh":"她用尽气力，可是再也说不下去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You have not changed; you are charming as ever!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You have not changed; you are charming as ever!”","zh":"“您没变，还是那样可爱！”她伤心道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh,” she replied bitterly, “they are poor charms since you disdained them.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh,” she replied bitterly, “they are poor charms since you disdained them.”","zh":"“唉！不可爱，我的朋友，因为您没有把我搁在心上。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he began a long explanation of his conduct, excusing himself in vague terms, in default of being able to invent better.","sentences":[{"en":"Then he began a long explanation of his conduct, excusing himself in vague terms, in default of being able to invent better.","zh":"他听了这话，找话解释他的行为，不过一时编不出适当的借口，就拿泛泛的话来道歉。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She yielded to his words, still more to his voice and the sight of him, so that, she pretended to believe, or perhaps believed; in the pretext he gave for their rupture; this was a secret on which depended the honour, the very life of a third person.","sentences":[{"en":"She yielded to his words, still more to his voice and the sight of him, so that, she pretended to believe, or perhaps believed; in the pretext he gave for their rupture; this was a secret on which depended the honour, the very life of a third person.","zh":"他的语言，尤其是他的声音和他的形体，打动了她，她听到后来，装出相信——或者也许真就相信：他们破裂的原因是一个秘密，关系第三者的名誉，甚至生命也成了问题。她伤心地望着他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No matter!” she said, looking at him sadly. “I have suffered much.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No matter!” she said, looking at him sadly.","zh":"“不管怎么样，反正我受够了苦！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I have suffered much.”","zh":"他用一种达观的口吻回答道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He replied philosophically—","sentences":[{"en":"He replied philosophically—","zh":"他用一种达观的口吻回答道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Such is life!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Such is life!”","zh":"“人生就是这样！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Has life,” Emma went on, “been good to you at least, since our separation?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Has life,” Emma went on, “been good to you at least, since our separation?”","zh":"爱玛接下去道：“自从我们分手以来，人生待您总还好吧？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, neither good nor bad.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, neither good nor bad.”","zh":"“啊！不好…也不坏。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Perhaps it would have been better never to have parted.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Perhaps it would have been better never to have parted.”","zh":"“你我永不分手，也许好多了。”“是啊…也许！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, perhaps.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, perhaps.”","zh":"“你相信？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You think so?” she said, drawing nearer, and she sighed. “Oh, Rodolphe! if you but knew! I loved you so!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You think so?” she said, drawing nearer, and she sighed.","zh":"她叹气道：“哎呀！罗道耳弗！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Oh, Rodolphe! if you but knew!","zh":"你不知道…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I loved you so!”","zh":"我多爱你！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was then that she took his hand, and they remained some time, their fingers intertwined, like that first day at the Show. With a gesture of pride he struggled against this emotion. But sinking upon his breast she said to him—","sentences":[{"en":"It was then that she took his hand, and they remained some time, their fingers intertwined, like that first day at the Show.","zh":"于是她握住他的手，他们也就手指交揉，待了一会儿——仿佛第一天，在农业展览会上！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"With a gesture of pride he struggled against this emotion.","zh":"自尊心不要他心软，他正在自我挣扎，就见她倒进他的胸怀，对他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"But sinking upon his breast she said to him—","zh":"自尊心不要他心软，他正在自我挣扎，就见她倒进他的胸怀，对他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“How did you think I could live without you? One cannot lose the habit of happiness. I was desolate. I thought I should die. I will tell you about all that and you will see. And you—you fled from me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“How did you think I could live without you?","zh":"“没有你，你怎么指望我活得下去？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One cannot lose the habit of happiness.","zh":"享惯了福，不享就不成！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was desolate.","zh":"我可真叫伤心啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought I should die.","zh":"我以为我会死的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I will tell you about all that and you will see.","zh":"改天我再一五一十讲给你听。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And you—you fled from me!”","zh":"可是你呀，躲着我…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For, all the three years, he had carefully avoided her in consequence of that natural cowardice that characterises the stronger sex. Emma went on, with dainty little nods, more coaxing than an amorous kitten—","sentences":[{"en":"For, all the three years, he had carefully avoided her in consequence of that natural cowardice that characterises the stronger sex.","zh":"因为三年以来，他由于男性特有的天赋的怯懦，小心在意避她。爱玛拿头一动一动，做出娇憨的模样，比一只动情的母猫还要妖媚，继续道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Emma went on, with dainty little nods, more coaxing than an amorous kitten—","zh":"因为三年以来，他由于男性特有的天赋的怯懦，小心在意避她。爱玛拿头一动一动，做出娇憨的模样，比一只动情的母猫还要妖媚，继续道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You love others, confess it! Oh, I understand them, dear! I excuse them. You probably seduced them as you seduced me. You are indeed a man; you have everything to make one love you. But we’ll begin again, won’t we? We will love one another. See! I am laughing; I am happy! Oh, speak!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You love others, confess it!","zh":"“你实说了吧，你爱别的女人；哎！我懂，好啦！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Oh, I understand them, dear!","zh":"“你实说了吧，你爱别的女人；哎！我懂，好啦！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I excuse them.","zh":"我原谅她们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You probably seduced them as you seduced me.","zh":"你勾引她们，就像你从前勾引我一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are indeed a man; you have everything to make one love you.","zh":"你是男子，你！有种种条件博得女人欢心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But we’ll begin again, won’t we?","zh":"不过我们再好下去，对不对？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We will love one another.","zh":"我们会相爱的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"See!","zh":"看，我笑了，我快活！你倒是说话呀！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I am laughing; I am happy!","zh":"看，我笑了，我快活！你倒是说话呀！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Oh, speak!”","zh":"看，我笑了，我快活！你倒是说话呀！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And she was charming to see, with her eyes, in which trembled a tear, like the rain of a storm in a blue corolla.","sentences":[{"en":"And she was charming to see, with her eyes, in which trembled a tear, like the rain of a storm in a blue corolla.","zh":"她娇滴滴的，确实惹人心疼，眼里盈盈一颗泪珠，颤颤索索，好像花萼含了一滴雨水一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had drawn her upon his knees, and with the back of his hand was caressing her smooth hair, where in the twilight was mirrored like a golden arrow one last ray of the sun. She bent down her brow; at last he kissed her on the eyelids quite gently with the tips of his lips.","sentences":[{"en":"He had drawn her upon his knees, and with the back of his hand was caressing her smooth hair, where in the twilight was mirrored like a golden arrow one last ray of the sun.","zh":"他把她抱到膝盖上，拿手背抚摸她光滑的头发。薄暮中落日的余晖投射在她的头发上，仿佛一支金箭在闪耀。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She bent down her brow; at last he kissed her on the eyelids quite gently with the tips of his lips.","zh":"他低下头，用嘴唇尖，轻轻吻着她的眼皮。他问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why, you have been crying! What for?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why, you have been crying!","zh":"“可是你哭了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What for?”","zh":"为什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She burst into tears. Rodolphe thought this was an outburst of her love. As she did not speak, he took this silence for a last remnant of resistance, and then he cried out—","sentences":[{"en":"She burst into tears.","zh":"她反而呜咽起来了，罗道耳弗以为她的爱情爆发了；他见她不做声，错把沉默当作害羞的最后表示，嚷嚷道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Rodolphe thought this was an outburst of her love.","zh":"她反而呜咽起来了，罗道耳弗以为她的爱情爆发了；他见她不做声，错把沉默当作害羞的最后表示，嚷嚷道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"As she did not speak, he took this silence for a last remnant of resistance, and then he cried out—","zh":"她反而呜咽起来了，罗道耳弗以为她的爱情爆发了；他见她不做声，错把沉默当作害羞的最后表示，嚷嚷道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, forgive me! You are the only one who pleases me. I was imbecile and cruel. I love you. I will love you always. What is it. Tell me!” He was kneeling by her.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, forgive me!","zh":"“啊！饶恕我！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are the only one who pleases me.","zh":"我只喜欢你一个人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I was imbecile and cruel.","zh":"我是又坏又蠢！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I love you.","zh":"我爱你，我永远爱你！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I will love you always.","zh":"我爱你，我永远爱你！","scope":"group"},{"en":"What is it.","zh":"你怎么啦？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Tell me!”","zh":"说话呀！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was kneeling by her.","zh":"他跪下来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, I am ruined, Rodolphe! You must lend me three thousand francs.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, I am ruined, Rodolphe!","zh":"“好吧！我破产啦，罗道耳弗！你借我三千法郎！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"You must lend me three thousand francs.”","zh":"“好吧！我破产啦，罗道耳弗！你借我三千法郎！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“But—but—” said he, getting up slowly, while his face assumed a grave expression.","sentences":[{"en":"“But—but—” said he, getting up slowly, while his face assumed a grave expression.","zh":"他慢慢站起来，脸上显出一种严肃的表情，说道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You know,” she went on quickly, “that my husband had placed his whole fortune at a notary’s. He ran away. So we borrowed; the patients don’t pay us. Moreover, the settling of the estate is not yet done; we shall have the money later on. But to-day, for want of three thousand francs, we are to be sold up. It is to be at once, this very moment, and, counting upon your friendship, I have come to you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You know,” she went on quickly, “that my husband had placed his whole fortune at a notary’s.","zh":"“不过…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He ran away.","zh":"不过…”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So we borrowed; the patients don’t pay us.","zh":"她急促地讲下去：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Moreover, the settling of the estate is not yet done; we shall have the money later on.","zh":"“你知道，我丈夫把他的财产统统交给公证人经管；他卷逃了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But to-day, for want of three thousand francs, we are to be sold up.","zh":"我们借钱，病人不付诊费。其实，清算没有结束；我们往后还会有钱的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It is to be at once, this very moment, and, counting upon your friendship, I have come to you.”","zh":"不过今天缺三千法郎，人家就要扣押我们的动产；就在如今，就在眼前。我信得过你的友谊，所以就来了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah!” thought Rodolphe, turning very pale, “that was what she came for.” At last he said with a calm air—","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!” thought Rodolphe, turning very pale, “that was what she came for.”","zh":"罗道耳弗脸色变得十分苍白，寻思道：啊！她来是为了这个！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last he said with a calm air—","zh":"他最后显出非常安详的神气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Dear madame, I have not got them.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Dear madame, I have not got them.”","zh":"“亲爱的夫人，我没有钱。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He did not lie. If he had had them, he would, no doubt, have given them, although it is generally disagreeable to do such fine things: a demand for money being, of all the winds that blow upon love, the coldest and most destructive.","sentences":[{"en":"He did not lie.","zh":"他不是说谎。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If he had had them, he would, no doubt, have given them, although it is generally disagreeable to do such fine things: a demand for money being, of all the winds that blow upon love, the coldest and most destructive.","zh":"他要是有钱的话，不用说，他会给的，虽然这种慷慨之举，一般说来，并不愉快：摧残爱情的方式很多，不过连根拔起的狂风暴雨，却是借钱。她先是望他望了几分钟。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"First she looked at him for some moments.","sentences":[{"en":"First she looked at him for some moments.","zh":"“你没有钱！”她重复了好几次：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You have not got them!” she repeated several times. “You have not got them! I ought to have spared myself this last shame. You never loved me. You are no better than the others.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You have not got them!” she repeated several times.","zh":"“你没有钱！早知道这样的话，我也不来受这场最后的羞辱了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"“You have not got them!","zh":"“你没有钱！早知道这样的话，我也不来受这场最后的羞辱了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I ought to have spared myself this last shame.","zh":"你从来没有爱过我！你比别人好不了多少！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"You never loved me.","zh":"你从来没有爱过我！你比别人好不了多少！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"You are no better than the others.”","zh":"她出卖自己，把话扯远了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was betraying, ruining herself.","sentences":[{"en":"She was betraying, ruining herself.","zh":"是啊，一百二十分可怜你！”于是眼睛望定兵器上一管发亮的银线短铳道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe interrupted her, declaring he was “hard up” himself.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe interrupted her, declaring he was “hard up” himself.","zh":"“可是人要是穷呀，铳把子不会镶银！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! I pity you,” said Emma. “Yes—very much.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!","zh":"她指着布勒 时钟，继续道：“也不会买镶介壳的钟！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I pity you,” said Emma.","zh":"她指着布勒 时钟，继续道：“也不会买镶介壳的钟！","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Yes—very much.”","zh":"也不会给马鞭来一串镀金的银叫子！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And fixing her eyes upon an embossed carabine, that shone against its panoply, “But when one is so poor one doesn’t have silver on the butt of one’s gun. One doesn’t buy a clock inlaid with tortoise shell,” she went on, pointing to a buhl timepiece, “nor silver-gilt whistles for one’s whips,” and she touched them, “nor charms for one’s watch. Oh, he wants for nothing! even to a liqueur-stand in his room! For you love yourself; you live well. You have a château, farms, woods; you go hunting; you travel to Paris. Why, if it were but that,” she cried, taking up two studs from the mantelpiece, “but the least of these trifles, one can get money for them. Oh, I do not want them, keep them!”","sentences":[{"en":"And fixing her eyes upon an embossed carabine, that shone against its panoply, “But when one is so poor one doesn’t have silver on the butt of one’s gun.","zh":"她摸着这些银叫子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One doesn’t buy a clock inlaid with tortoise shell,” she went on, pointing to a buhl timepiece, “nor silver-gilt whistles for one’s whips,” and she touched them, “nor charms for one’s watch.","zh":"“也不会给他表上来一串小玩意儿链子！嗐！他什么也不缺！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, he wants for nothing! even to a liqueur-stand in his room!","zh":"屋里还有一顶酒橱；因为你爱你自己，你过舒服日子，你有一所庄园、几处田庄、几座树林；你骑马打猎，你远游巴黎…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"For you love yourself; you live well.","zh":"单单就是这个…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You have a château, farms, woods; you go hunting; you travel to Paris.","zh":"”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Why, if it were but that,” she cried, taking up two studs from the mantelpiece, “but the least of these trifles, one can get money for them.","zh":"她抓起壁炉上的袖口纽扣，喊道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Oh, I do not want them, keep them!”","zh":"她抓起壁炉上的袖口纽扣，喊道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And she threw the two links away from her, their gold chain breaking as it struck against the wall.","sentences":[{"en":"And she threw the two links away from her, their gold chain breaking as it struck against the wall.","zh":"“这顶小的小玩意儿，就能变出钱来！嗐！我不要你的！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But I! I would have given you everything. I would have sold all, worked for you with my hands, I would have begged on the highroads for a smile, for a look, to hear you say ‘Thanks!’ And you sit there quietly in your arm-chair, as if you had not made me suffer enough already! But for you, and you know it, I might have lived happily. What made you do it? Was it a bet? Yet you loved me—you said so. And but a moment since—Ah! it would have been better to have driven me away. My hands are hot with your kisses, and there is the spot on the carpet where at my knees you swore an eternity of love! You made me believe you; for two years you held me in the most magnificent, the sweetest dream! Eh! Our plans for the journey, do you remember? Oh, your letter! your letter! it tore my heart! And then when I come back to him—to him, rich, happy, free—to implore the help the first stranger would give, a suppliant, and bringing back to him all my tenderness, he repulses me because it would cost him three thousand francs!”","sentences":[{"en":"“But I! I would have given you everything.","zh":"她拿两个纽扣丢得老远，小金链碰在墙上，断了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I would have sold all, worked for you with my hands, I would have begged on the highroads for a smile, for a look, to hear you say ‘Thanks!’","zh":"“可是我呀，为了博得你一个微笑，让你瞧上一眼，听你说一句‘谢谢’，我什么都会给你，什么都会卖掉，做苦工，沿路乞讨！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And you sit there quietly in your arm-chair, as if you had not made me suffer enough already!","zh":"而你安安详详坐在你的扶手椅里，好像你先前没有让我受够罪？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But for you, and you know it, I might have lived happily.","zh":"没有你，你明白，我会快快活活过日子的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What made you do it?","zh":"你为什么要这样做？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Was it a bet?","zh":"难道跟谁打赌来着？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yet you loved me—you said so.","zh":"可是你从前爱我，你从前这样讲…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And but a moment since—Ah! it would have been better to have driven me away.","zh":"方才还这样讲…啊！还不如把我撵走的好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"My hands are hot with your kisses, and there is the spot on the carpet where at my knees you swore an eternity of love!","zh":"你亲我的手，手现在还是热烘烘的。你就在这地方，在这地毯上，跪在我面前，发誓爱我一辈子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You made me believe you; for two years you held me in the most magnificent, the sweetest dream!","zh":"我相信你：整整两年，你带我做着最香甜、最绮丽的梦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Eh!","zh":"嗯？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Our plans for the journey, do you remember?","zh":"我们的旅行计划，你记得不，啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Oh, your letter! your letter! it tore my heart!","zh":"你的信！你的信，撕碎了我的心！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then when I come back to him—to him, rich, happy, free—to implore the help the first stranger would give, a suppliant, and bringing back to him all my tenderness, he repulses me because it would cost him three thousand francs!”","zh":"如今我看他来了，投他来了，他又有钱，又快活，又自由！求他搭救一把，随便什么人也会帮忙，苦苦央求，把恩情统统献给他，他推开我，因为这要破费他三千法郎！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I haven’t got them,” replied Rodolphe, with that perfect calm with which resigned rage covers itself as with a shield.","sentences":[{"en":"“I haven’t got them,” replied Rodolphe, with that perfect calm with which resigned rage covers itself as with a shield.","zh":"罗道耳弗口气绝对冷静——这种冷静就像盾牌一样，掩护抑制下去的愤怒，回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She went out. The walls trembled, the ceiling was crushing her, and she passed back through the long alley, stumbling against the heaps of dead leaves scattered by the wind. At last she reached the ha-ha hedge in front of the gate; she broke her nails against the lock in her haste to open it. Then a hundred steps farther on, breathless, almost falling, she stopped. And now turning round, she once more saw the impassive château, with the park, the gardens, the three courts, and all the windows of the facade.","sentences":[{"en":"She went out.","zh":"“我没有钱！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The walls trembled, the ceiling was crushing her, and she passed back through the long alley, stumbling against the heaps of dead leaves scattered by the wind.","zh":"她出来了。墙在摇晃，天花板往下压她。她又走进悠长的林荫道，绊在随风散开的枯叶堆上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last she reached the ha-ha hedge in front of the gate; she broke her nails against the lock in her haste to open it.","zh":"她终于走到栅栏门前的壕沟；她急着开门，在门闩上碰断了指甲。然后百步开外，她气喘吁吁，眼看就要跌倒，只得站住。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then a hundred steps farther on, breathless, almost falling, she stopped.","zh":"她终于走到栅栏门前的壕沟；她急着开门，在门闩上碰断了指甲。然后百步开外，她气喘吁吁，眼看就要跌倒，只得站住。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And now turning round, she once more saw the impassive château, with the park, the gardens, the three courts, and all the windows of the facade.","zh":"她于是扭转身子，又瞥了一眼无动于衷的庄园：草坪、花园、三座院子和正面的全部窗户。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She remained lost in stupor, and having no more consciousness of herself than through the beating of her arteries, that she seemed to hear bursting forth like a deafening music filling all the fields. The earth beneath her feet was more yielding than the sea, and the furrows seemed to her immense brown waves breaking into foam. Everything in her head, of memories, ideas, went off at once like a thousand pieces of fireworks. She saw her father, Lheureux’s closet, their room at home, another landscape. Madness was coming upon her; she grew afraid, and managed to recover herself, in a confused way, it is true, for she did not in the least remember the cause of the terrible condition she was in, that is to say, the question of money. She suffered only in her love, and felt her soul passing from her in this memory; as wounded men, dying, feel their life ebb from their bleeding wounds.","sentences":[{"en":"She remained lost in stupor, and having no more consciousness of herself than through the beating of her arteries, that she seemed to hear bursting forth like a deafening music filling all the fields.","zh":"她呆呆瞪瞪站了许久，觉不出自己是在活着，只觉得听见自己的脉搏在跳动，仿佛震耳欲聋的音乐，在田野响成一片。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The earth beneath her feet was more yielding than the sea, and the furrows seemed to her immense brown waves breaking into foam.","zh":"脚底下的土比水还软；犁沟在她看来，成了掀天的棕色大浪。回忆、观念，大大小小，同时涌出，活跃在她的脑子里，像一道烟火放出无数的火花。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Everything in her head, of memories, ideas, went off at once like a thousand pieces of fireworks.","zh":"脚底下的土比水还软；犁沟在她看来，成了掀天的棕色大浪。回忆、观念，大大小小，同时涌出，活跃在她的脑子里，像一道烟火放出无数的火花。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She saw her father, Lheureux’s closet, their room at home, another landscape.","zh":"她看见她的父亲、勒乐的小屋、他们的旅馆房间、另一片风景。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Madness was coming upon her; she grew afraid, and managed to recover herself, in a confused way, it is true, for she did not in the least remember the cause of the terrible condition she was in, that is to say, the question of money.","zh":"她觉得自己要疯。她一害怕，努力收敛，但是情形混乱，也是真的；她已记不起她落到这般田地的原因，也就是说：金钱问题。她感到痛苦的，只是她的爱情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She suffered only in her love, and felt her soul passing from her in this memory; as wounded men, dying, feel their life ebb from their bleeding wounds.","zh":"她觉得她的灵魂通过这种回忆离开了她，就像受伤的人临死觉得生命从流血的伤口走掉一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Night was falling, crows were flying about.","sentences":[{"en":"Night was falling, crows were flying about.","zh":"天黑了，乌鸦在飞。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Suddenly it seemed to her that fiery spheres were exploding in the air like fulminating balls when they strike, and were whirling, whirling, to melt at last upon the snow between the branches of the trees. In the midst of each of them appeared the face of Rodolphe. They multiplied and drew near her, penetrating her. It all disappeared; she recognised the lights of the houses that shone through the fog.","sentences":[{"en":"Suddenly it seemed to her that fiery spheres were exploding in the air like fulminating balls when they strike, and were whirling, whirling, to melt at last upon the snow between the branches of the trees.","zh":"她恍惚看见天空，突然有火球出现，好像闪亮的子弹一样，在下降中间炸开，旋转向前，融在树枝之间的雪里。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"In the midst of each of them appeared the face of Rodolphe.","zh":"个个火球当中，都有罗道耳弗的脸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They multiplied and drew near her, penetrating her.","zh":"火球越来越多，越来越近，钻进她的身子，全不见了。她认出点点灯火，远远在雾里闪耀。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It all disappeared; she recognised the lights of the houses that shone through the fog.","zh":"火球越来越多，越来越近，钻进她的身子，全不见了。她认出点点灯火，远远在雾里闪耀。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Now her situation, like an abyss, rose up before her. She was panting as if her heart would burst. Then in an ecstasy of heroism, that made her almost joyous, she ran down the hill, crossed the cow-plank, the foot-path, the alley, the market, and reached the chemist’s shop. She was about to enter, but at the sound of the bell someone might come, and slipping in by the gate, holding her breath, feeling her way along the walls, she went as far as the door of the kitchen, where a candle stuck on the stove was burning. Justin in his shirt-sleeves was carrying out a dish.","sentences":[{"en":"Now her situation, like an abyss, rose up before her.","zh":"于是她的遭遇，仿佛一座深渊，来到眼前，她喘不过气来，胸脯活像要裂开了一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was panting as if her heart would burst.","zh":"于是她的遭遇，仿佛一座深渊，来到眼前，她喘不过气来，胸脯活像要裂开了一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then in an ecstasy of heroism, that made her almost joyous, she ran down the hill, crossed the cow-plank, the foot-path, the alley, the market, and reached the chemist’s shop.","zh":"接着她的心头涌起舍身的念头，她几乎喜不自胜了，跑下岭来，穿过牛走的便桥、小径、小巷、菜场，来到药房前面。没有人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was about to enter, but at the sound of the bell someone might come, and slipping in by the gate, holding her breath, feeling her way along the walls, she went as far as the door of the kitchen, where a candle stuck on the stove was burning.","zh":"她打算进去；但是门铃一响，会有人来的。她于是溜过栅栏门，屏住气，摸着墙，一直走到厨房门口。炉台上点着一支蜡烛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Justin in his shirt-sleeves was carrying out a dish.","zh":"朱斯丹穿一件衬衫，端走一盘菜。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! they are dining; I will wait.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! they are dining; I will wait.”","zh":"“啊！他们在吃晚饭。等等再说。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He returned; she tapped at the window. He went out.","sentences":[{"en":"He returned; she tapped at the window.","zh":"他回来了。她敲玻璃窗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He went out.","zh":"他出来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The key! the one for upstairs where he keeps the—”","sentences":[{"en":"“The key! the one for upstairs where he keeps the—”","zh":"“钥匙！上头那把，放…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What?”","zh":"“什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he looked at her, astonished at the pallor of her face, that stood out white against the black background of the night. She seemed to him extraordinarily beautiful and majestic as a phantom. Without understanding what she wanted, he had the presentiment of something terrible.","sentences":[{"en":"And he looked at her, astonished at the pallor of her face, that stood out white against the black background of the night.","zh":"他看着她，奇怪她的脸没有一丝血色，衬着黑黝黝的夜色，分外显得白。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She seemed to him extraordinarily beautiful and majestic as a phantom.","zh":"他觉得她异常美丽，幽灵一样庄严。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Without understanding what she wanted, he had the presentiment of something terrible.","zh":"他不明白她的意思，预先感到有什么祸事要来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But she went on quickly in a love voice; in a sweet, melting voice, “I want it; give it to me.”","sentences":[{"en":"But she went on quickly in a love voice; in a sweet, melting voice, “I want it; give it to me.”","zh":"但是她放低声音，急促地说，声音又温柔，又有软化人的力量：“我有用！给我。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As the partition wall was thin, they could hear the clatter of the forks on the plates in the dining-room.","sentences":[{"en":"As the partition wall was thin, they could hear the clatter of the forks on the plates in the dining-room.","zh":"板壁薄薄的，饭厅传来叉子和盘子的响声。她假说老鼠吵她睡觉，要药弄死老鼠。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She pretended that she wanted to kill the rats that kept her from sleeping.","sentences":[{"en":"She pretended that she wanted to kill the rats that kept her from sleeping.","zh":"“我得回禀一声老爷。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I must tell master.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I must tell master.”","zh":"“不必！别走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, stay!” Then with an indifferent air, “Oh, it’s not worth while; I’ll tell him presently. Come, light me upstairs.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, stay!”","zh":"然后神情淡漠，又道：“哎！你犯不着去，我这就告诉他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then with an indifferent air, “Oh, it’s not worth while; I’ll tell him presently.","zh":"然后神情淡漠，又道：“哎！你犯不着去，我这就告诉他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Come, light me upstairs.”","zh":"来，给我照亮！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She entered the corridor into which the laboratory door opened. Against the wall was a key labelled Capharnaum.","sentences":[{"en":"She entered the corridor into which the laboratory door opened.","zh":"她走进通实验室的过道。墙上挂着一把钥匙，标明“堆置间”。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Against the wall was a key labelled Capharnaum.","zh":"她走进通实验室的过道。墙上挂着一把钥匙，标明“堆置间”。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Justin!” called the druggist impatiently.","sentences":[{"en":"“Justin!” called the druggist impatiently.","zh":"药剂师等急了，喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Let us go up.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Let us go up.”","zh":"“朱斯丹！”“上楼！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he followed her. The key turned in the lock, and she went straight to the third shelf, so well did her memory guide her, seized the blue jar, tore out the cork, plunged in her hand, and withdrawing it full of a white powder, she began eating it.","sentences":[{"en":"And he followed her.","zh":"他跟着她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The key turned in the lock, and she went straight to the third shelf, so well did her memory guide her, seized the blue jar, tore out the cork, plunged in her hand, and withdrawing it full of a white powder, she began eating it.","zh":"钥匙在锁眼转动；她一直走向第三槅架，她记得明明白白，抓起蓝罐，拔掉塞头，伸进手去，捏了满满一把白粉，立时一口吞下。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Stop!” he cried, rushing at her.","sentences":[{"en":"“Stop!” he cried, rushing at her.","zh":"他扑过去拦她，喊道：“别吃！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Hush! someone will come.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hush! someone will come.”","zh":"“别吵！当心人来…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was in despair, was calling out.","sentences":[{"en":"He was in despair, was calling out.","zh":"他难过得不得了，打算叫唤。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Say nothing, or all the blame will fall on your master.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Say nothing, or all the blame will fall on your master.”","zh":"“不要说出去。小心连累你的主人！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then she went home, suddenly calmed, and with something of the serenity of one that had performed a duty.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she went home, suddenly calmed, and with something of the serenity of one that had performed a duty.","zh":"她走开了，忽然心平气和，差不多就像完成了任务那样恬适自在。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When Charles, distracted by the news of the distraint, returned home, Emma had just gone out. He cried aloud, wept, fainted, but she did not return. Where could she be? He sent Félicité to Homais, to Monsieur Tuvache, to Lheureux, to the “Lion d’Or,” everywhere, and in the intervals of his agony he saw his reputation destroyed, their fortune lost, Berthe’s future ruined. By what?—Not a word! He waited till six in the evening. At last, unable to bear it any longer, and fancying she had gone to Rouen, he set out along the highroad, walked a mile, met no one, again waited, and returned home. She had come back.","sentences":[{"en":"When Charles, distracted by the news of the distraint, returned home, Emma had just gone out.","zh":"查理听见扣押的消息，心慌意乱，赶回家来，爱玛正好出门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He cried aloud, wept, fainted, but she did not return.","zh":"他喊，他哭，他晕了过去，但是她不回来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Where could she be?","zh":"她有什么地方好去？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sent Félicité to Homais, to Monsieur Tuvache, to Lheureux, to the “Lion d’Or,” everywhere, and in the intervals of his agony he saw his reputation destroyed, their fortune lost, Berthe’s future ruined.","zh":"他差全福四处寻找，郝麦那边、杜法赦先生那边、勒乐那边、金狮那边，不见踪影；他一阵一阵心焦，看见自己名誉扫地、财产荡尽，白尔特前程黯淡！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"By what?—Not a word!","zh":"什么缘故？一句话也没有！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He waited till six in the evening.","zh":"他一直等到下午六点钟。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, unable to bear it any longer, and fancying she had gone to Rouen, he set out along the highroad, walked a mile, met no one, again waited, and returned home.","zh":"他最后再也等不下去了，以为她去了鲁昂，来到大路上，走了半古里，不见一个人，又等了一会儿，这才回来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She had come back.","zh":"她先回来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What was the matter? Why? Explain to me.”","sentences":[{"en":"“What was the matter?","zh":"“是怎么一回事？为什么？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Why?","zh":"“是怎么一回事？为什么？","scope":"group"},{"en":"Explain to me.”","zh":"说给我听？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She sat down at her writing-table and wrote a letter, which she sealed slowly, adding the date and the hour. Then she said in a solemn tone:","sentences":[{"en":"She sat down at her writing-table and wrote a letter, which she sealed slowly, adding the date and the hour.","zh":"她坐在她的书桌前面写信，慢条斯理封口，添补日期和时间，然后以一种庄严的口吻道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she said in a solemn tone:","zh":"她坐在她的书桌前面写信，慢条斯理封口，添补日期和时间，然后以一种庄严的口吻道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“You are to read it to-morrow; till then, I pray you, do not ask me a single question. No, not one!”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are to read it to-morrow; till then, I pray you, do not ask me a single question.","zh":"“你明天再看；从现在起，我求你一句话也不要问我！是的，一句话也不要问！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"No, not one!”","zh":"“你明天再看；从现在起，我求你一句话也不要问我！是的，一句话也不要问！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“But—”","sentences":[{"en":"“But—”","zh":"“可是…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, leave me!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, leave me!”","zh":"“哎呀！走开！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She lay down full length on her bed. A bitter taste that she felt in her mouth awakened her. She saw Charles, and again closed her eyes.","sentences":[{"en":"She lay down full length on her bed.","zh":"她躺倒在床上。她觉得嘴里有一股辛辣味道，醒过来了，她模模糊糊望见查理，又闭上眼睛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A bitter taste that she felt in her mouth awakened her.","zh":"她躺倒在床上。她觉得嘴里有一股辛辣味道，醒过来了，她模模糊糊望见查理，又闭上眼睛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She saw Charles, and again closed her eyes.","zh":"她躺倒在床上。她觉得嘴里有一股辛辣味道，醒过来了，她模模糊糊望见查理，又闭上眼睛。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She was studying herself curiously, to see if she were not suffering. But no! nothing as yet. She heard the ticking of the clock, the crackling of the fire, and Charles breathing as he stood upright by her bed.","sentences":[{"en":"She was studying herself curiously, to see if she were not suffering.","zh":"她带着好奇的心理，看自己会不会难受。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But no! nothing as yet.","zh":"是啊！还没有动静。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She heard the ticking of the clock, the crackling of the fire, and Charles breathing as he stood upright by her bed.","zh":"她听见钟走、火响、查理立在床旁呼吸。她寻思道：“啊！死真算不了一回事！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! it is but a little thing, death!” she thought. “I shall fall asleep and all will be over.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! it is but a little thing, death!” she thought.","zh":"我睡过去，就全完了！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I shall fall asleep and all will be over.”","zh":"她喝了一口水，朝墙翻转身子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She drank a mouthful of water and turned to the wall. The frightful taste of ink continued.","sentences":[{"en":"She drank a mouthful of water and turned to the wall.","zh":"那种可怕的墨水气味一直有。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The frightful taste of ink continued.","zh":"她呻吟道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I am thirsty; oh! so thirsty,” she sighed.","sentences":[{"en":"“I am thirsty; oh! so thirsty,” she sighed.","zh":"“我渴！哎呀！我好渴呀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What is it?” said Charles, who was handing her a glass.","sentences":[{"en":"“What is it?” said Charles, who was handing her a glass.","zh":"查理端水给她，问道：“你到底怎么啦？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“It is nothing! Open the window; I am choking.”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is nothing!","zh":"“没有什么！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Open the window; I am choking.”","zh":"打开窗户…我出不来气！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She was seized with a sickness so sudden that she had hardly time to draw out her handkerchief from under the pillow.","sentences":[{"en":"She was seized with a sickness so sudden that she had hardly time to draw out her handkerchief from under the pillow.","zh":"她忽然觉得恶心，几乎来不及到枕头底下掏手绢，就吐出来了。她赶快道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Take it away,” she said quickly; “throw it away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Take it away,” she said quickly; “throw it away.”","zh":"“拿开！扔掉！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He spoke to her; she did not answer. She lay motionless, afraid that the slightest movement might make her vomit. But she felt an icy cold creeping from her feet to her heart.","sentences":[{"en":"He spoke to her; she did not answer.","zh":"他问她话；她不回答。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She lay motionless, afraid that the slightest movement might make her vomit.","zh":"她躺平了，不敢移动；害怕一动，又要呕吐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she felt an icy cold creeping from her feet to her heart.","zh":"但是她觉得从脚到心像冰一样寒冷。她咕哝道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! it is beginning,” she murmured.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! it is beginning,” she murmured.","zh":"“啊！现在开始啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What did you say?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What did you say?”","zh":"“你说什么？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She turned her head from side to side with a gentle movement full of agony, while constantly opening her mouth as if something very heavy were weighing upon her tongue. At eight o’clock the vomiting began again.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned her head from side to side with a gentle movement full of agony, while constantly opening her mouth as if something very heavy were weighing upon her tongue.","zh":"她的头轻轻摇来摇去，充满痛苦，上下牙床一直张开，好像有什么很重的东西压住她的舌头一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At eight o’clock the vomiting began again.","zh":"临到八点钟，她又呕吐起来。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles noticed that at the bottom of the basin there was a sort of white sediment sticking to the sides of the porcelain.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles noticed that at the bottom of the basin there was a sort of white sediment sticking to the sides of the porcelain.","zh":"查理注意到脸盆底上，有白色颗粒似的东西，贴住瓷面。他重复道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“This is extraordinary—very singular,” he repeated.","sentences":[{"en":"“This is extraordinary—very singular,” he repeated.","zh":"“怪事！奇怪！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But she said in a firm voice, “No, you are mistaken.”","sentences":[{"en":"But she said in a firm voice, “No, you are mistaken.”","zh":"但是她以一种坚定的声音道：“不，你看错啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then gently, and almost as caressing her, he passed his hand over her stomach. She uttered a sharp cry. He fell back terror-stricken.","sentences":[{"en":"Then gently, and almost as caressing her, he passed his hand over her stomach.","zh":"他于是轻轻拿手放在她的胃上，差不多是抚摸着。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She uttered a sharp cry.","zh":"她尖声一叫，把他吓得直往后退。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He fell back terror-stricken.","zh":"她尖声一叫，把他吓得直往后退。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then she began to groan, faintly at first. Her shoulders were shaken by a strong shuddering, and she was growing paler than the sheets in which her clenched fingers buried themselves. Her unequal pulse was now almost imperceptible.","sentences":[{"en":"Then she began to groan, faintly at first.","zh":"接着她就哼唧，起初声音低微。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her shoulders were shaken by a strong shuddering, and she was growing paler than the sheets in which her clenched fingers buried themselves.","zh":"她的肩膀直抖，脸比床单还白，痉挛的手指抠着床单。她的脉搏不匀，现在几乎细到听也听不出来了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her unequal pulse was now almost imperceptible.","zh":"她的肩膀直抖，脸比床单还白，痉挛的手指抠着床单。她的脉搏不匀，现在几乎细到听也听不出来了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Drops of sweat oozed from her bluish face, that seemed as if rigid in the exhalations of a metallic vapour. Her teeth chattered, her dilated eyes looked vaguely about her, and to all questions she replied only with a shake of the head; she even smiled once or twice. Gradually, her moaning grew louder; a hollow shriek burst from her; she pretended she was better and that she would get up presently. But she was seized with convulsions and cried out—","sentences":[{"en":"Drops of sweat oozed from her bluish face, that seemed as if rigid in the exhalations of a metallic vapour.","zh":"她像在金属水汽中凝成的一样，脸色发青，汗水直往外渗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her teeth chattered, her dilated eyes looked vaguely about her, and to all questions she replied only with a shake of the head; she even smiled once or twice.","zh":"牙齿乱响；眼睛睁大，迷迷茫茫，向四下望。任凭问她什么话，只是摇头，甚至于微笑了两三次，哼唧的声音越来越响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Gradually, her moaning grew louder; a hollow shriek burst from her; she pretended she was better and that she would get up presently.","zh":"她不要叫唤，可是不由自主，还是低声叫起来了。她硬说自己好多了，马上就会起来的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she was seized with convulsions and cried out—","zh":"但是她浑身抽搐，喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! my God! It is horrible!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! my God!","zh":"“啊！难受死了，我的上帝！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It is horrible!”","zh":"“啊！难受死了，我的上帝！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He threw himself on his knees by her bed.","sentences":[{"en":"He threw himself on his knees by her bed.","zh":"他跪到床前道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Tell me! what have you eaten? Answer, for heaven’s sake!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Tell me! what have you eaten?","zh":"“说呀，你吃了什么？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Answer, for heaven’s sake!”","zh":"看在上天的分上，回答我！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he looked at her with a tenderness in his eyes such as she had never seen.","sentences":[{"en":"And he looked at her with a tenderness in his eyes such as she had never seen.","zh":"他看着她，一往情深，她先前像没有见过。她以一种微弱的声音道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Well, there—there!” she said in a faint voice. He flew to the writing-table, tore open the seal, and read aloud: “Accuse no one.” He stopped, passed his hands across his eyes, and read it over again.","sentences":[{"en":"“Well, there—there!” she said in a faint voice.","zh":"“好，那…那边！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He flew to the writing-table, tore open the seal, and read aloud: “Accuse no one.”","zh":"”他跳到书桌跟前，打开信封，大声念道：“什么人也不要怪罪…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He stopped, passed his hands across his eyes, and read it over again.","zh":"”他停住不念，拿手擦擦眼睛，再念下去。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What! help—help!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What! help—help!”","zh":"“什么！救命！来人呀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He could only keep repeating the word: “Poisoned! poisoned!” Félicité ran to Homais, who proclaimed it in the market-place; Madame Lefrancois heard it at the “Lion d’Or”; some got up to go and tell their neighbours, and all night the village was on the alert.","sentences":[{"en":"He could only keep repeating the word: “Poisoned! poisoned!”","zh":"他能重复的只有这两个字：“服毒！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Félicité ran to Homais, who proclaimed it in the market-place; Madame Lefrancois heard it at the “Lion d’Or”; some got up to go and tell their neighbours, and all night the village was on the alert.","zh":"服毒！”全福跑去找郝麦；郝麦在广场嚷得家家听见，勒弗朗索瓦太太在金狮都听见了；有人起来说给邻居知道：全镇活活闹了一整夜。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Distraught, faltering, reeling, Charles wandered about the room. He knocked against the furniture, tore his hair, and the chemist had never believed that there could be so terrible a sight.","sentences":[{"en":"Distraught, faltering, reeling, Charles wandered about the room.","zh":"查理在屋里打转，心慌意乱，话也说不清，几乎站不稳，撞家具，抓头发，药剂师做梦也想不到会看见这种恐怖场面。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He knocked against the furniture, tore his hair, and the chemist had never believed that there could be so terrible a sight.","zh":"查理在屋里打转，心慌意乱，话也说不清，几乎站不稳，撞家具，抓头发，药剂师做梦也想不到会看见这种恐怖场面。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He went home to write to Monsieur Canivet and to Doctor Lariviere. He lost his head, and made more than fifteen rough copies. Hippolyte went to Neufchâtel, and Justin so spurred Bovary’s horse that he left it foundered and three parts dead by the hill at Bois-Guillaume.","sentences":[{"en":"He went home to write to Monsieur Canivet and to Doctor Lariviere.","zh":"他回家给卡尼韦先生和拉里维耶尔博士写信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He lost his head, and made more than fifteen rough copies.","zh":"他头昏脑涨，一连起了十五次草稿，还写不好。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Hippolyte went to Neufchâtel, and Justin so spurred Bovary’s horse that he left it foundered and three parts dead by the hill at Bois-Guillaume.","zh":"伊玻立特去了新堡；朱斯丹拼命踢包法利的马，踢到后来，马跑不动，只有一口气了，只好丢在纪尧姆树林岭。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles tried to look up his medical dictionary, but could not read it; the lines were dancing.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles tried to look up his medical dictionary, but could not read it; the lines were dancing.","zh":"查理想翻医学辞典，字句跳动，看不清楚。药剂师道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Be calm,” said the druggist; “we have only to administer a powerful antidote. What is the poison?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Be calm,” said the druggist; “we have only to administer a powerful antidote.","zh":"“冷静点！只要服些高效的解毒药就成。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What is the poison?”","zh":"是什么毒药？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles showed him the letter. It was arsenic.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles showed him the letter.","zh":"查理给他看信。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was arsenic.","zh":"原来是砒霜。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Very well,” said Homais, “we must make an analysis.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Very well,” said Homais, “we must make an analysis.”","zh":"郝麦又道：“好！应该化验一下才是！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For he knew that in cases of poisoning an analysis must be made; and the other, who did not understand, answered—","sentences":[{"en":"For he knew that in cases of poisoning an analysis must be made; and the other, who did not understand, answered—","zh":"因为他知道，遇到中毒事件必须化验，查理不懂他的意思，回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, do anything! save her!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, do anything! save her!”","zh":"对！救救她…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then going back to her, he sank upon the carpet, and lay there with his head leaning against the edge of her bed, sobbing.","sentences":[{"en":"Then going back to her, he sank upon the carpet, and lay there with his head leaning against the edge of her bed, sobbing.","zh":"然后，他回到她身旁，倒在地毯上，头靠住床沿呜咽。她向他道：“别哭！用不了多久，我就不再折磨你啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Don’t cry,” she said to him. “Soon I shall not trouble you any more.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Don’t cry,” she said to him.","zh":"“你为什么服毒？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Soon I shall not trouble you any more.”","zh":"你凭什么非服毒不可？”她回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why was it? Who drove you to it?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why was it?","zh":"“我的朋友，应该这样。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Who drove you to it?”","zh":"“我的朋友，应该这样。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"She replied. “It had to be, my dear!”","sentences":[{"en":"She replied.","zh":"“难道你不快活？难道是我不好？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“It had to be, my dear!”","zh":"“难道你不快活？难道是我不好？","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Weren’t you happy? Is it my fault? I did all I could!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Weren’t you happy?","zh":"可是我尽我的力来着！”“是…","scope":"group"},{"en":"Is it my fault?","zh":"可是我尽我的力来着！”“是…","scope":"group"},{"en":"I did all I could!”","zh":"对…你是好人，你！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yes, that is true—you are good—you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes, that is true—you are good—you.”","zh":"她慢慢拿手放在他的头发上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And she passed her hand slowly over his hair. The sweetness of this sensation deepened his sadness; he felt his whole being dissolving in despair at the thought that he must lose her, just when she was confessing more love for him than ever. And he could think of nothing; he did not know, he did not dare; the urgent need for some immediate resolution gave the finishing stroke to the turmoil of his mind.","sentences":[{"en":"And she passed her hand slowly over his hair.","zh":"这种甜蜜的感觉加重了他的忧伤；就在她比从前显得更爱他的时候，他却反而非失去她不可，想到这上头，他就肝肠寸断，觉得全部生命都在崩溃。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The sweetness of this sensation deepened his sadness; he felt his whole being dissolving in despair at the thought that he must lose her, just when she was confessing more love for him than ever.","zh":"这种甜蜜的感觉加重了他的忧伤；就在她比从前显得更爱他的时候，他却反而非失去她不可，想到这上头，他就肝肠寸断，觉得全部生命都在崩溃。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And he could think of nothing; he did not know, he did not dare; the urgent need for some immediate resolution gave the finishing stroke to the turmoil of his mind.","zh":"他想不出抢救的办法，不知道该怎么着手，也不敢着手，越是情况紧急，需要立刻做出决断，他就越是不知所措。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"So she had done, she thought, with all the treachery; and meanness, and numberless desires that had tortured her. She hated no one now; a twilight dimness was settling upon her thoughts, and, of all earthly noises, Emma heard none but the intermittent lamentations of this poor heart, sweet and indistinct like the echo of a symphony dying away.","sentences":[{"en":"So she had done, she thought, with all the treachery; and meanness, and numberless desires that had tortured her.","zh":"她想，一切欺诈、卑鄙和折磨她的无数欲望，都和她不相干了。现在，她什么人也不恨了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She hated no one now; a twilight dimness was settling upon her thoughts, and, of all earthly noises, Emma heard none but the intermittent lamentations of this poor heart, sweet and indistinct like the echo of a symphony dying away.","zh":"她的思想陷入迷离境地；人世的喧嚣，爱玛听见的，只有这可怜人的间歇的啼哭，柔和而模糊，好像交响乐隐隐约约的尾声。她支起胳膊肘道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Bring me the child,” she said, raising herself on her elbow.","sentences":[{"en":"“Bring me the child,” she said, raising herself on her elbow.","zh":"“把孩子给我带来。”查理问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are not worse, are you?” asked Charles.","sentences":[{"en":"“You are not worse, are you?” asked Charles.","zh":"“你不觉得更难过，是不是？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“No, no!”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no!”","zh":"“是的！是的！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The child, serious, and still half-asleep, was carried in on the servant’s arm in her long white nightgown, from which her bare feet peeped out. She looked wonderingly at the disordered room, and half-closed her eyes, dazzled by the candles burning on the table. They reminded her, no doubt, of the morning of New Year’s day and Mid-Lent, when thus awakened early by candle-light she came to her mother’s bed to fetch her presents, for she began saying—","sentences":[{"en":"The child, serious, and still half-asleep, was carried in on the servant’s arm in her long white nightgown, from which her bare feet peeped out.","zh":"女用人把孩子抱来。她穿着长睡衣，露出两只光脚，神情严肃，差不多还在做梦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She looked wonderingly at the disordered room, and half-closed her eyes, dazzled by the candles burning on the table.","zh":"她满脸惊奇，望着凌乱的房间。桌上点着蜡烛，照花她的眼睛，不住眨动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They reminded her, no doubt, of the morning of New Year’s day and Mid-Lent, when thus awakened early by candle-light she came to her mother’s bed to fetch her presents, for she began saying—","zh":"不用说，蜡烛让她记起新年或者四旬斋狂欢节的早晨，也是点着蜡烛，老早就喊醒她，抱到母亲床头，接受礼物，她说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But where is it, mamma?” And as everybody was silent, “But I can’t see my little stocking.”","sentences":[{"en":"“But where is it, mamma?”","zh":"“妈妈，东西在哪儿？”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And as everybody was silent, “But I can’t see my little stocking.”","zh":"她见大家不做声，又说：“我看不见我的小鞋！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Félicité held her over the bed while she still kept looking towards the mantelpiece.","sentences":[{"en":"Félicité held her over the bed while she still kept looking towards the mantelpiece.","zh":"全福朝床抱她，她却一直望着壁炉那边。她问道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Has nurse taken it?” she asked.","sentences":[{"en":"“Has nurse taken it?” she asked.","zh":"“是奶妈拿走啦？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And at this name, that carried her back to the memory of her adulteries and her calamities, Madame Bovary turned away her head, as at the loathing of another bitterer poison that rose to her mouth. But Berthe remained perched on the bed.","sentences":[{"en":"And at this name, that carried her back to the memory of her adulteries and her calamities, Madame Bovary turned away her head, as at the loathing of another bitterer poison that rose to her mouth.","zh":"包法利夫人听见奶妈两个字，想起她的奸情和她的灾殃，不由得转开了头，似乎另有一种毒药，比嘴里的毒药还猛，惹她恶心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But Berthe remained perched on the bed.","zh":"白尔特站在床上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, how big your eyes are, mamma! How pale you are! how hot you are!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, how big your eyes are, mamma!","zh":"“啊！啊！妈妈，你的眼睛多大啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"How pale you are! how hot you are!”","zh":"脸多白啊！看你净出汗啦…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her mother looked at her. “I am frightened!” cried the child, recoiling.","sentences":[{"en":"Her mother looked at her.","zh":"母亲望着她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I am frightened!” cried the child, recoiling.","zh":"小孩子后退道：“我怕！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma took her hand to kiss it; the child struggled.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma took her hand to kiss it; the child struggled.","zh":"爱玛握住她的小手吻；她挣扎不肯。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That will do. Take her away,” cried Charles, who was sobbing in the alcove.","sentences":[{"en":"“That will do.","zh":"查理在床后呜咽，喊道：“行啦！把她抱走吧。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Take her away,” cried Charles, who was sobbing in the alcove.","zh":"查理在床后呜咽，喊道：“行啦！把她抱走吧。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then the symptoms ceased for a moment; she seemed less agitated; and at every insignificant word, at every respiration a little more easy, he regained hope. At last, when Canivet came in, he threw himself into his arms.","sentences":[{"en":"Then the symptoms ceased for a moment; she seemed less agitated; and at every insignificant word, at every respiration a little more easy, he regained hope.","zh":"随后病势缓和一时，看上去，她也不像先前那样难过。他听见她每说一句不关重要的话，每出一口比较匀静的气，就以为有了希望。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, when Canivet came in, he threw himself into his arms.","zh":"最后，他看见卡尼韦进来，扑过去拥抱他，哭道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! it is you. Thanks! You are good! But she is better. See! look at her.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! it is you.","zh":"“啊！是您！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thanks!","zh":"谢谢！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"You are good!","zh":"您真好！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she is better.","zh":"现在好一点了，来，看看她…”","scope":"group"},{"en":"See! look at her.”","zh":"现在好一点了，来，看看她…”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"His colleague was by no means of this opinion, and, as he said of himself, “never beating about the bush,” he prescribed, an emetic in order to empty the stomach completely.","sentences":[{"en":"His colleague was by no means of this opinion, and, as he said of himself, “never beating about the bush,” he prescribed, an emetic in order to empty the stomach completely.","zh":"同行的看法完全两样，像他自己说的，不必兜圈子，他干脆就开呕吐剂，把胃打扫干净。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She soon began vomiting blood. Her lips became drawn. Her limbs were convulsed, her whole body covered with brown spots, and her pulse slipped beneath the fingers like a stretched thread, like a harp-string nearly breaking.","sentences":[{"en":"She soon began vomiting blood.","zh":"她很快就吐起血来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Her lips became drawn.","zh":"舌头也更紧了，四肢抽搐，一身棕色点子，捺捺她的脉搏，滑溜溜的，仿佛一根绷紧了的线，又仿佛一条将断未断的琴弦。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her limbs were convulsed, her whole body covered with brown spots, and her pulse slipped beneath the fingers like a stretched thread, like a harp-string nearly breaking.","zh":"舌头也更紧了，四肢抽搐，一身棕色点子，捺捺她的脉搏，滑溜溜的，仿佛一根绷紧了的线，又仿佛一条将断未断的琴弦。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"After this she began to scream horribly. She cursed the poison, railed at it, and implored it to be quick, and thrust away with her stiffened arms everything that Charles, in more agony than herself, tried to make her drink. He stood up, his handkerchief to his lips, with a rattling sound in his throat, weeping, and choked by sobs that shook his whole body. Félicité was running hither and thither in the room. Homais, motionless, uttered great sighs; and Monsieur Canivet, always retaining his self-command, nevertheless began to feel uneasy.","sentences":[{"en":"After this she began to scream horribly.","zh":"接着她就发疯一般喊叫连天。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She cursed the poison, railed at it, and implored it to be quick, and thrust away with her stiffened arms everything that Charles, in more agony than herself, tried to make her drink.","zh":"她诅咒毒药，谩骂毒药，哀求毒药尽快发作；查理比她还痛苦，一劝她喝药，她就伸出僵硬的胳膊推开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He stood up, his handkerchief to his lips, with a rattling sound in his throat, weeping, and choked by sobs that shook his whole body.","zh":"他站直了，手绢掩住嘴唇，喉咙呼呼在响，眼泪直流，哽咽得喘不过气，连脚后跟也在抖动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Félicité was running hither and thither in the room.","zh":"全福在屋里乱跑；郝麦一动不动，只是大声叹气；卡尼韦先生虽然照样刚强，也开始心乱了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Homais, motionless, uttered great sighs; and Monsieur Canivet, always retaining his self-command, nevertheless began to feel uneasy.","zh":"全福在屋里乱跑；郝麦一动不动，只是大声叹气；卡尼韦先生虽然照样刚强，也开始心乱了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“The devil! yet she has been purged, and from the moment that the cause ceases—”","sentences":[{"en":"“The devil! yet she has been purged, and from the moment that the cause ceases—”","zh":"可是…她也用过清除剂了。病源一消灭…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The effect must cease,” said Homais, “that is evident.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The effect must cease,” said Homais, “that is evident.”","zh":"郝麦道：“后果就该消灭；理所当然。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, save her!” cried Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, save her!” cried Bovary.","zh":"包法利喊道：“救救她！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And, without listening to the chemist, who was still venturing the hypothesis, “It is perhaps a salutary paroxysm,” Canivet was about to administer some theriac, when they heard the cracking of a whip; all the windows rattled, and a post-chaise drawn by three horses abreast, up to their ears in mud, drove at a gallop round the corner of the market. It was Doctor Lariviere.","sentences":[{"en":"And, without listening to the chemist, who was still venturing the hypothesis, “It is perhaps a salutary paroxysm,” Canivet was about to administer some theriac, when they heard the cracking of a whip; all the windows rattled, and a post-chaise drawn by three horses abreast, up to their ears in mud, drove at a gallop round the corner of the market.","zh":"药剂师还在提供假定：“也许这是一种有利的发作。”卡尼韦不理他，正要使用鸦片解毒剂，就听见传来一阵马鞭的响声。玻璃窗全在摇晃。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Doctor Lariviere.","zh":"一辆柏林式驿车 驾了三匹马，浑身是泥，直到耳朵，飞也似的，从菜场拐角，冲了过来。原来是拉里维耶尔博士到了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The apparition of a god would not have caused more commotion. Bovary raised his hands; Canivet stopped short; and Homais pulled off his skull-cap long before the doctor had come in.","sentences":[{"en":"The apparition of a god would not have caused more commotion.","zh":"天神出现也不见得会引起更大的骚动。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bovary raised his hands; Canivet stopped short; and Homais pulled off his skull-cap long before the doctor had come in.","zh":"包法利举起两手；卡尼韦赶快住手；郝麦不等医生进来，先就摘下他的希腊小帽。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He belonged to that great school of surgery begotten of Bichat, to that generation, now extinct, of philosophical practitioners, who, loving their art with a fanatical love, exercised it with enthusiasm and wisdom. Everyone in his hospital trembled when he was angry; and his students so revered him that they tried, as soon as they were themselves in practice, to imitate him as much as possible. So that in all the towns about they were found wearing his long wadded merino overcoat and black frock-coat, whose buttoned cuffs slightly covered his brawny hands—very beautiful hands, and that never knew gloves, as though to be more ready to plunge into suffering. Disdainful of honours, of titles, and of academies, like one of the old Knight-Hospitallers, generous, fatherly to the poor, and practising virtue without believing in it, he would almost have passed for a saint if the keenness of his intellect had not caused him to be feared as a demon. His glance, more penetrating than his bistouries, looked straight into your soul, and dissected every lie athwart all assertions and all reticences. And thus he went along, full of that debonair majesty that is given by the consciousness of great talent, of fortune, and of forty years of a labourious and irreproachable life.","sentences":[{"en":"He belonged to that great school of surgery begotten of Bichat, to that generation, now extinct, of philosophical practitioners, who, loving their art with a fanatical love, exercised it with enthusiasm and wisdom.","zh":"他属于比夏 建立的伟大外科学派，目前已经不存在的哲学家兼手术家的一代，爱护自己的医道，如同一位狂热的教徒，行起医来，又热情，又明敏！他一发怒，整个医院发抖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Everyone in his hospital trembled when he was angry; and his students so revered him that they tried, as soon as they were themselves in practice, to imitate him as much as possible.","zh":"学生尊敬他到了这步田地，一挂牌行医，就处处模仿他，以致人们在附近城镇，到处看见他的棉里美里奴长斗篷和宽大的青燕尾服。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"So that in all the towns about they were found wearing his long wadded merino overcoat and black frock-coat, whose buttoned cuffs slightly covered his brawny hands—very beautiful hands, and that never knew gloves, as though to be more ready to plunge into suffering.","zh":"他的硬袖解开，盖住一点他胖嘟嘟的手——一双非常漂亮的手，从来不戴手套，好像为了加快救治病人一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Disdainful of honours, of titles, and of academies, like one of the old Knight-Hospitallers, generous, fatherly to the poor, and practising virtue without believing in it, he would almost have passed for a saint if the keenness of his intellect had not caused him to be feared as a demon.","zh":"他看不起奖章、头衔和科学院，他仁慈、慷慨、周济穷人，不相信道德，却又极力行善，如果不是头脑精细，使别人怕他就像怕魔鬼一样，他简直可以算是一位圣者了。他的目光比他的手术刀还要锋利，一直射到你的灵魂深处，不管是托词也好，害羞也好，藏在底下的谎话统统分解出来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"His glance, more penetrating than his bistouries, looked straight into your soul, and dissected every lie athwart all assertions and all reticences.","zh":"他看不起奖章、头衔和科学院，他仁慈、慷慨、周济穷人，不相信道德，却又极力行善，如果不是头脑精细，使别人怕他就像怕魔鬼一样，他简直可以算是一位圣者了。他的目光比他的手术刀还要锋利，一直射到你的灵魂深处，不管是托词也好，害羞也好，藏在底下的谎话统统分解出来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And thus he went along, full of that debonair majesty that is given by the consciousness of great talent, of fortune, and of forty years of a labourious and irreproachable life.","zh":"他这样活在人民当中，充满和蔼可亲的庄严气概——一种觉得自己饶有才能与财富的意识和四十年勤劳、无可非议的生涯形成的庄严气概。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He frowned as soon as he had passed the door when he saw the cadaverous face of Emma stretched out on her back with her mouth open. Then, while apparently listening to Canivet, he rubbed his fingers up and down beneath his nostrils, and repeated—","sentences":[{"en":"He frowned as soon as he had passed the door when he saw the cadaverous face of Emma stretched out on her back with her mouth open.","zh":"他一进门，望见爱玛张开口，仰天躺在床上，脸像死人一样，就皱眉头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, while apparently listening to Canivet, he rubbed his fingers up and down beneath his nostrils, and repeated—","zh":"随后他一边好像听卡尼韦解释，一边拿食指放在鼻孔底下，重复道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Good! good!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Good! good!”","zh":"“好，好。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But he made a slow gesture with his shoulders. Bovary watched him; they looked at one another; and this man, accustomed as he was to the sight of pain, could not keep back a tear that fell on his shirt-frill.","sentences":[{"en":"But he made a slow gesture with his shoulders.","zh":"但是他的肩膀慢慢上耸。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bovary watched him; they looked at one another; and this man, accustomed as he was to the sight of pain, could not keep back a tear that fell on his shirt-frill.","zh":"包法利注意到了。两个人你望我，我望你；这个人虽然看惯了痛苦，也忍不住流下一滴眼泪，落在他的胸饰上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He tried to take Canivet into the next room. Charles followed him.","sentences":[{"en":"He tried to take Canivet into the next room.","zh":"他想把卡尼韦带到外间，查理跟着他。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles followed him.","zh":"他想把卡尼韦带到外间，查理跟着他。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“She is very ill, isn’t she? If we put on sinapisms? Anything! Oh, think of something, you who have saved so many!”","sentences":[{"en":"“She is very ill, isn’t she?","zh":"“很严重，是不是？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"If we put on sinapisms?","zh":"贴芥子膏怎么样？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Anything!","zh":"我不知道怎么才好！想想办法，您救过那么多人！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Oh, think of something, you who have saved so many!”","zh":"我不知道怎么才好！想想办法，您救过那么多人！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles caught him in both his arms, and gazed at him wildly, imploringly, half-fainting against his breast.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles caught him in both his arms, and gazed at him wildly, imploringly, half-fainting against his breast.","zh":"查理拿两只胳膊围住他的身子，眼睛望他，样子又凄惶，又哀求，简直要在他的胸前昏倒。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come, my poor fellow, courage! There is nothing more to be done.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, my poor fellow, courage!","zh":"“好，可怜的孩子，拿出勇气来！没有法子救。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"There is nothing more to be done.”","zh":"“好，可怜的孩子，拿出勇气来！没有法子救。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"And Doctor Lariviere turned away.","sentences":[{"en":"And Doctor Lariviere turned away.","zh":"拉里维耶尔博士走开了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You are going?”","sentences":[{"en":"“You are going?”","zh":"“您这就走？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I will come back.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I will come back.”","zh":"“我还回来。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He went out only to give an order to the coachman, with Monsieur Canivet, who did not care either to have Emma die under his hands.","sentences":[{"en":"He went out only to give an order to the coachman, with Monsieur Canivet, who did not care either to have Emma die under his hands.","zh":"他像有话吩咐车夫，卡尼韦也走出来了，同样不高兴看爱玛死在自己手上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The chemist rejoined them on the Place. He could not by temperament keep away from celebrities, so he begged Monsieur Lariviere to do him the signal honour of accepting some breakfast.","sentences":[{"en":"The chemist rejoined them on the Place.","zh":"药剂师在广场追上他们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He could not by temperament keep away from celebrities, so he begged Monsieur Lariviere to do him the signal honour of accepting some breakfast.","zh":"他天性离不开名人。所以他恳求拉里维耶尔先生赏光，到他家里用饭。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He sent quickly to the “Lion d’Or” for some pigeons; to the butcher’s for all the cutlets that were to be had; to Tuvache for cream; and to Lestiboudois for eggs; and the druggist himself aided in the preparations, while Madame Homais was saying as she pulled together the strings of her jacket—","sentences":[{"en":"He sent quickly to the “Lion d’Or” for some pigeons; to the butcher’s for all the cutlets that were to be had; to Tuvache for cream; and to Lestiboudois for eggs; and the druggist himself aided in the preparations, while Madame Homais was saying as she pulled together the strings of her jacket—","zh":"他马上叫人到金狮去取鸽子，到肉庄去取所有的小排骨肉，到杜法郝家去取奶酪，到赖斯地布杜瓦家去取鸡蛋。药剂师亲自帮着预备；郝麦太太一边系牢罩衫带子，一边道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You must excuse us, sir, for in this poor place, when one hasn’t been told the night before—”","sentences":[{"en":"“You must excuse us, sir, for in this poor place, when one hasn’t been told the night before—”","zh":"“先生，您得原谅才是；因为在我们这小地方，头一天不先关照一声…”郝麦轻声吩咐：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Wine glasses!” whispered Homais.","sentences":[{"en":"“Wine glasses!” whispered Homais.","zh":"“高脚玻璃杯！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“If only we were in town, we could fall back upon stuffed trotters.”","sentences":[{"en":"“If only we were in town, we could fall back upon stuffed trotters.”","zh":"“在城里的话，我们起码可以弄到灌肉蹄子。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Be quiet! Sit down, doctor!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Be quiet!","zh":"“少废话！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sit down, doctor!”","zh":"博士，请。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He thought fit, after the first few mouthfuls, to give some details as to the catastrophe.","sentences":[{"en":"He thought fit, after the first few mouthfuls, to give some details as to the catastrophe.","zh":"用过几口以后，他觉得应该提供一些详细情况：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We first had a feeling of siccity in the pharynx, then intolerable pains at the epigastrium, super purgation, coma.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We first had a feeling of siccity in the pharynx, then intolerable pains at the epigastrium, super purgation, coma.”","zh":"“起初我们发现她咽喉发干，后来上腹部剧痛，呕吐不止，呈昏睡状态。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But how did she poison herself?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But how did she poison herself?”","zh":"“她怎么会服毒的？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I don’t know, doctor, and I don’t even know where she can have procured the arsenious acid.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t know, doctor, and I don’t even know where she can have procured the arsenious acid.”","zh":"“我不知道，博士，我简直不晓得她从什么地方得到这种砒霜。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Justin, who was just bringing in a pile of plates, began to tremble.","sentences":[{"en":"Justin, who was just bringing in a pile of plates, began to tremble.","zh":"朱斯丹这时正好端上一摞盘子，听见这话，不由哆嗦起来。药剂师问道：“你怎么啦？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What’s the matter?” said the chemist.","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s the matter?” said the chemist.","zh":"年轻人一听问话，稀里哗啦，把东西全摔到地上。郝麦喊道：“蠢猪！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At this question the young man dropped the whole lot on the ground with a crash.","sentences":[{"en":"At this question the young man dropped the whole lot on the ground with a crash.","zh":"笨牛！傻瓜！死驴！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Imbecile!” cried Homais, “awkward lout! block-head! confounded ass!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Imbecile!” cried Homais, “awkward lout! block-head! confounded ass!”","zh":"但是他猛然克制自己，回到原来的话题道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"But suddenly controlling himself—","sentences":[{"en":"But suddenly controlling himself—","zh":"但是他猛然克制自己，回到原来的话题道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“I wished, doctor, to make an analysis, and primo I delicately introduced a tube—”","sentences":[{"en":"“I wished, doctor, to make an analysis, and primo I delicately introduced a tube—”","zh":"“博士，我决计化验，首先我小心从事，拿一只细管搁到…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“You would have done better,” said the physician, “to introduce your fingers into her throat.”","sentences":[{"en":"“You would have done better,” said the physician, “to introduce your fingers into her throat.”","zh":"外科医生道：“顶好是拿您的手指搁进她的喉咙。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His colleague was silent, having just before privately received a severe lecture about his emetic, so that this good Canivet, so arrogant and so verbose at the time of the clubfoot, was to-day very modest. He smiled without ceasing in an approving manner.","sentences":[{"en":"His colleague was silent, having just before privately received a severe lecture about his emetic, so that this good Canivet, so arrogant and so verbose at the time of the clubfoot, was to-day very modest.","zh":"他的同行默不作声，因为方才已经为了他的呕吐剂，私下饱受训斥，所以这位好好先生卡尼韦，治跷脚时，说话滔滔不绝，气焰不可一世；今天极其谦虚，一副心服口服的模样，不断微笑。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He smiled without ceasing in an approving manner.","zh":"他的同行默不作声，因为方才已经为了他的呕吐剂，私下饱受训斥，所以这位好好先生卡尼韦，治跷脚时，说话滔滔不绝，气焰不可一世；今天极其谦虚，一副心服口服的模样，不断微笑。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Homais dilated in Amphytrionic pride, and the affecting thought of Bovary vaguely contributed to his pleasure by a kind of egotistic reflex upon himself. Then the presence of the doctor transported him. He displayed his erudition, cited pell-mell cantharides, upas, the manchineel, vipers.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais dilated in Amphytrionic pride, and the affecting thought of Bovary vaguely contributed to his pleasure by a kind of egotistic reflex upon himself.","zh":"郝麦做了东道，自尊心得到满足，心花怒放，包法利的悲痛促成他的幸福，在他心上，模模糊糊，激起一片快感。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then the presence of the doctor transported him.","zh":"而且他有博士在座，特别兴奋。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He displayed his erudition, cited pell-mell cantharides, upas, the manchineel, vipers.","zh":"他卖弄渊博，东拉西扯，说起斑蝥、乌巴斯树 、芒色尼耶树、蝰…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I have even read that various persons have found themselves under toxicological symptoms, and, as it were, thunderstricken by black-pudding that had been subjected to a too vehement fumigation. At least, this was stated in a very fine report drawn up by one of our pharmaceutical chiefs, one of our masters, the illustrious Cadet de Gassicourt!”","sentences":[{"en":"“I have even read that various persons have found themselves under toxicological symptoms, and, as it were, thunderstricken by black-pudding that had been subjected to a too vehement fumigation.","zh":"“我甚至于读到，有些香肠，熏过了头，人吃了就会中毒。博士，好像中电一样！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At least, this was stated in a very fine report drawn up by one of our pharmaceutical chiefs, one of our masters, the illustrious Cadet de Gassicourt!”","zh":"我们有一位大师，著名的卡代·德·嘉西古尔 ，我们的药物学权威，曾经写过一篇了不起的报告，就提到来着！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Homais reappeared, carrying one of those shaky machines that are heated with spirits of wine; for Homais liked to make his coffee at table, having, moreover, torrefied it, pulverised it, and mixed it himself.","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Homais reappeared, carrying one of those shaky machines that are heated with spirits of wine; for Homais liked to make his coffee at table, having, moreover, torrefied it, pulverised it, and mixed it himself.","zh":"郝麦太太又出来了，端着一个燃烧酒精的摇摇晃晃的机器；因为郝麦讲究在饭桌上熬咖啡而且事前经他亲手炒好，磨好，调好。他献糖道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Saccharum, doctor?” said he, offering the sugar.","sentences":[{"en":"“Saccharum, doctor?” said he, offering the sugar.","zh":"“Saccharum ，博士。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then he had all his children brought down, anxious to have the physician’s opinion on their constitutions.","sentences":[{"en":"Then he had all his children brought down, anxious to have the physician’s opinion on their constitutions.","zh":"他随后把子女全叫到底下，希望听听外科医生对他们的体格的意见。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last Monsieur Lariviere was about to leave, when Madame Homais asked for a consultation about her husband. He was making his blood too thick by going to sleep every evening after dinner.","sentences":[{"en":"At last Monsieur Lariviere was about to leave, when Madame Homais asked for a consultation about her husband.","zh":"最后，拉里维耶尔先生准备走了，郝麦太太请他检查检查她丈夫。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was making his blood too thick by going to sleep every evening after dinner.","zh":"他的血变稠了，每天用过晚饭，他就打盹。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, it isn’t his blood that’s too thick,” said the physician.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, it isn’t his blood that’s too thick,” said the physician.","zh":"“嗐！妨碍他的不是血。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And, smiling a little at his unnoticed joke, the doctor opened the door. But the chemist’s shop was full of people; he had the greatest difficulty in getting rid of Monsieur Tuvache, who feared his spouse would get inflammation of the lungs, because she was in the habit of spitting on the ashes; then of Monsieur Binet, who sometimes experienced sudden attacks of great hunger; and of Madame Caron, who suffered from tinglings; of Lheureux, who had vertigo; of Lestiboudois, who had rheumatism; and of Madame Lefrancois, who had heartburn. At last the three horses started; and it was the general opinion that he had not shown himself at all obliging.","sentences":[{"en":"And, smiling a little at his unnoticed joke, the doctor opened the door.","zh":"这句双关语，没有人理会，医生笑微微的，打开了门。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the chemist’s shop was full of people; he had the greatest difficulty in getting rid of Monsieur Tuvache, who feared his spouse would get inflammation of the lungs, because she was in the habit of spitting on the ashes; then of Monsieur Binet, who sometimes experienced sudden attacks of great hunger; and of Madame Caron, who suffered from tinglings; of Lheureux, who had vertigo; of Lestiboudois, who had rheumatism; and of Madame Lefrancois, who had heartburn.","zh":"可是药房挤满了人，他简直难以脱身。杜法赦先生担心太太害肺炎，因为她好对灰烬唾痰；毕耐先生，一来就饿；卡隆太太，皮肤有针扎的感觉；勒乐，常常头晕；赖斯地布杜瓦，害风湿症；还有勒弗朗索瓦太太，闹胃气病。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last the three horses started; and it was the general opinion that he had not shown himself at all obliging.","zh":"最后，三匹马出发了，人人嫌他不够和气。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Public attention was distracted by the appearance of Monsieur Bournisien, who was going across the market with the holy oil.","sentences":[{"en":"Public attention was distracted by the appearance of Monsieur Bournisien, who was going across the market with the holy oil.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生捧着圣油，走过菜场，引起公众的注意。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais, as was due to his principles, compared priests to ravens attracted by the odour of death. The sight of an ecclesiastic was personally disagreeable to him, for the cassock made him think of the shroud, and he detested the one from some fear of the other.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais, as was due to his principles, compared priests to ravens attracted by the odour of death.","zh":"郝麦根据他的原则，把教士比作死人气味招引来的乌鸦。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sight of an ecclesiastic was personally disagreeable to him, for the cassock made him think of the shroud, and he detested the one from some fear of the other.","zh":"他一看见教士，就身心不畅，因为道袍让他想到寿衣，他憎恨前者，有一点由于畏惧后者。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Nevertheless, not shrinking from what he called his mission, he returned to Bovary’s in company with Canivet whom Monsieur Lariviere, before leaving, had strongly urged to make this visit; and he would, but for his wife’s objections, have taken his two sons with him, in order to accustom them to great occasions; that this might be a lesson, an example, a solemn picture, that should remain in their heads later on.","sentences":[{"en":"Nevertheless, not shrinking from what he called his mission, he returned to Bovary’s in company with Canivet whom Monsieur Lariviere, before leaving, had strongly urged to make this visit; and he would, but for his wife’s objections, have taken his two sons with him, in order to accustom them to great occasions; that this might be a lesson, an example, a solemn picture, that should remain in their heads later on.","zh":"不过他面对他的所谓使命，并不退却，所以就又陪卡尼韦回到包法利那边——拉里维耶尔先生走前，再三嘱咐卡尼韦这样做来着。不是太太反对，他会连两个儿子也带过去，经历大事，将来留在脑海，也好成为一种教训、一个榜样、一幅严肃的图画。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The room when they went in was full of mournful solemnity. On the work-table, covered over with a white cloth, there were five or six small balls of cotton in a silver dish, near a large crucifix between two lighted candles.","sentences":[{"en":"The room when they went in was full of mournful solemnity.","zh":"他们走进房间，里面充满悲惨的仪式，女红桌上蒙了一条白饭巾，上面一只银盘，里头有五六个小棉花球，旁边是一个大十字架，一边点着一支蜡烛。","scope":"group"},{"en":"On the work-table, covered over with a white cloth, there were five or six small balls of cotton in a silver dish, near a large crucifix between two lighted candles.","zh":"他们走进房间，里面充满悲惨的仪式，女红桌上蒙了一条白饭巾，上面一只银盘，里头有五六个小棉花球，旁边是一个大十字架，一边点着一支蜡烛。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Emma, her chin sunken upon her breast, had her eyes inordinately wide open, and her poor hands wandered over the sheets with that hideous and soft movement of the dying, that seems as if they wanted already to cover themselves with the shroud. Pale as a statue and with eyes red as fire, Charles, not weeping, stood opposite her at the foot of the bed, while the priest, bending one knee, was muttering words in a low voice.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma, her chin sunken upon her breast, had her eyes inordinately wide open, and her poor hands wandered over the sheets with that hideous and soft movement of the dying, that seems as if they wanted already to cover themselves with the shroud.","zh":"爱玛的下巴靠住胸脯，眼睛睁得老大，两只可怜的手搭在床单上，姿势又难看，又柔和，好像快死的人，直盼早拿尸布盖好自己一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Pale as a statue and with eyes red as fire, Charles, not weeping, stood opposite her at the foot of the bed, while the priest, bending one knee, was muttering words in a low voice.","zh":"查理停住哭泣，脸色仿佛石像那样白，眼睛好像炭火一样红，面对着她，站在床尾；教士一条腿跪在地上，咿咿唔唔祷告。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She turned her face slowly, and seemed filled with joy on seeing suddenly the violet stole, no doubt finding again, in the midst of a temporary lull in her pain, the lost voluptuousness of her first mystical transports, with the visions of eternal beatitude that were beginning.","sentences":[{"en":"She turned her face slowly, and seemed filled with joy on seeing suddenly the violet stole, no doubt finding again, in the midst of a temporary lull in her pain, the lost voluptuousness of her first mystical transports, with the visions of eternal beatitude that were beginning.","zh":"她慢悠悠转过脸来，一眼望见教士身上的紫飘带，忽然有了笑容，不用说，她在无牵无挂之中，又体会到了早年的神秘感受，看到了正在开始的天国形象。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The priest rose to take the crucifix; then she stretched forward her neck as one who is athirst, and glueing her lips to the body of the Man-God, she pressed upon it with all her expiring strength the fullest kiss of love that she had ever given. Then he recited the Misereatur and the Indulgentiam, dipped his right thumb in the oil, and began to give extreme unction. First upon the eyes, that had so coveted all worldly pomp; then upon the nostrils, that had been greedy of the warm breeze and amorous odours; then upon the mouth, that had uttered lies, that had curled with pride and cried out in lewdness; then upon the hands that had delighted in sensual touches; and finally upon the soles of the feet, so swift of yore, when she was running to satisfy her desires, and that would now walk no more.","sentences":[{"en":"The priest rose to take the crucifix; then she stretched forward her neck as one who is athirst, and glueing her lips to the body of the Man-God, she pressed upon it with all her expiring strength the fullest kiss of love that she had ever given.","zh":"教士站起来取十字架；她好像渴了一样，伸长颈项，嘴唇贴牢基督的身体，使出就要断气的全部气力，亲着她从来没有亲过的最大的爱情的吻。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he recited the Misereatur and the Indulgentiam, dipped his right thumb in the oil, and began to give extreme unction.","zh":"接着他就诵“愿主慈悲”和“降恩”，右手拇指蘸蘸油，开始涂抹：先是眼睛，曾经贪恋人世种种浮华；其次是鼻孔，喜好温和的微风与动情的香味；再次是嘴，曾经张开了说谎，由于骄傲而呻吟，在淫欲之中喊叫；再次是手，爱接触润滑的东西；最后是脚底，从前为了满足欲望，跑起来那样快，如今行走不动了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"First upon the eyes, that had so coveted all worldly pomp; then upon the nostrils, that had been greedy of the warm breeze and amorous odours; then upon the mouth, that had uttered lies, that had curled with pride and cried out in lewdness; then upon the hands that had delighted in sensual touches; and finally upon the soles of the feet, so swift of yore, when she was running to satisfy her desires, and that would now walk no more.","zh":"接着他就诵“愿主慈悲”和“降恩”，右手拇指蘸蘸油，开始涂抹：先是眼睛，曾经贪恋人世种种浮华；其次是鼻孔，喜好温和的微风与动情的香味；再次是嘴，曾经张开了说谎，由于骄傲而呻吟，在淫欲之中喊叫；再次是手，爱接触润滑的东西；最后是脚底，从前为了满足欲望，跑起来那样快，如今行走不动了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The cure wiped his fingers, threw the bit of cotton dipped in oil into the fire, and came and sat down by the dying woman, to tell her that she must now blend her sufferings with those of Jesus Christ and abandon herself to the divine mercy.","sentences":[{"en":"The cure wiped his fingers, threw the bit of cotton dipped in oil into the fire, and came and sat down by the dying woman, to tell her that she must now blend her sufferings with those of Jesus Christ and abandon herself to the divine mercy.","zh":"堂长擦擦手指，拿蘸油的棉花球扔到火里，过来坐在病床旁边，告诉她：现在她应当把她的痛苦和基督的痛苦打成一片，等候上天怜悯。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Finishing his exhortations, he tried to place in her hand a blessed candle, symbol of the celestial glory with which she was soon to be surrounded. Emma, too weak, could not close her fingers, and the taper, but for Monsieur Bournisien would have fallen to the ground.","sentences":[{"en":"Finishing his exhortations, he tried to place in her hand a blessed candle, symbol of the celestial glory with which she was soon to be surrounded.","zh":"劝告完了，他试着拿一支祝福过的蜡烛，放在她的手心，这象征天国的光辉，眼看就要环绕她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma, too weak, could not close her fingers, and the taper, but for Monsieur Bournisien would have fallen to the ground.","zh":"爱玛太衰弱，手指拢不过来，不是布尔尼贤先生，蜡烛就掉在地上了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"However, she was not quite so pale, and her face had an expression of serenity as if the sacrament had cured her.","sentences":[{"en":"However, she was not quite so pale, and her face had an expression of serenity as if the sacrament had cured her.","zh":"但是她显出一种平静的表情，脸色不如先前那样白，好像仪式治好了她一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The priest did not fail to point this out; he even explained to Bovary that the Lord sometimes prolonged the life of persons when he thought it meet for their salvation; and Charles remembered the day when, so near death, she had received the communion. Perhaps there was no need to despair, he thought.","sentences":[{"en":"The priest did not fail to point this out; he even explained to Bovary that the Lord sometimes prolonged the life of persons when he thought it meet for their salvation; and Charles remembered the day when, so near death, she had received the communion.","zh":"教士看出这种现象，说给包法利听，甚至对他解释：主有时候认为有利于人，就延长寿命。查理记得她有一天领受圣体，也像这样快要死了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Perhaps there was no need to despair, he thought.","zh":"他寻思道：“也许还有指望。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In fact, she looked around her slowly, as one awakening from a dream; then in a distinct voice she asked for her looking-glass, and remained some time bending over it, until the big tears fell from her eyes. Then she turned away her head with a sigh and fell back upon the pillows.","sentences":[{"en":"In fact, she looked around her slowly, as one awakening from a dream; then in a distinct voice she asked for her looking-glass, and remained some time bending over it, until the big tears fell from her eyes.","zh":"说实话，她看看四周，慢条斯理，好像如梦方醒一般，然后声音清清楚楚的，要她的镜子。她照镜子照了许久，直到后来，流出许多眼泪，这才不照。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then she turned away her head with a sigh and fell back upon the pillows.","zh":"她于是仰起头来，叹了一口气，又倒在枕头上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Her chest soon began panting rapidly; the whole of her tongue protruded from her mouth; her eyes, as they rolled, grew paler, like the two globes of a lamp that is going out, so that one might have thought her already dead but for the fearful labouring of her ribs, shaken by violent breathing, as if the soul were struggling to free itself. Félicité knelt down before the crucifix, and the druggist himself slightly bent his knees, while Monsieur Canivet looked out vaguely at the Place. Bournisien had again begun to pray, his face bowed against the edge of the bed, his long black cassock trailing behind him in the room. Charles was on the other side, on his knees, his arms outstretched towards Emma. He had taken her hands and pressed them, shuddering at every beat of her heart, as at the shaking of a falling ruin. As the death-rattle became stronger the priest prayed faster; his prayers mingled with the stifled sobs of Bovary, and sometimes all seemed lost in the muffled murmur of the Latin syllables that tolled like a passing bell.","sentences":[{"en":"Her chest soon began panting rapidly; the whole of her tongue protruded from her mouth; her eyes, as they rolled, grew paler, like the two globes of a lamp that is going out, so that one might have thought her already dead but for the fearful labouring of her ribs, shaken by violent breathing, as if the soul were struggling to free itself.","zh":"她的胸脯立刻迅速起伏。舌头完全伸到嘴外；眼睛转动着，仿佛一对玻璃灯在逐渐发暗，终于熄灭了。不是肋骨拼命抽动，她已经可以说是死了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Félicité knelt down before the crucifix, and the druggist himself slightly bent his knees, while Monsieur Canivet looked out vaguely at the Place.","zh":"全福跪在十字架前；就连药剂师也曲了曲膝盖；卡尼韦漫无目标，望着广场。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bournisien had again begun to pray, his face bowed against the edge of the bed, his long black cassock trailing behind him in the room.","zh":"布尔尼贤又在祈祷，脸靠床沿，黑长道袍拖在背后地上。查理跪在对面，胳膊伸向爱玛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles was on the other side, on his knees, his arms outstretched towards Emma.","zh":"他握她的手，握得紧紧的，她一心跳，他就哆嗦，好像一所破房子在倒塌，把他震哆嗦了一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had taken her hands and pressed them, shuddering at every beat of her heart, as at the shaking of a falling ruin.","zh":"喘吼越来越急，教士的祷告也越来越快，和包法利的哽咽打成一片，有时候又像全不响了，只有拉丁字母喑喑哑哑，咿咿唔唔，好像哀祷的钟声一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As the death-rattle became stronger the priest prayed faster; his prayers mingled with the stifled sobs of Bovary, and sometimes all seemed lost in the muffled murmur of the Latin syllables that tolled like a passing bell.","zh":"人行道上忽然传来笨重的木头套鞋和手杖戳戳点点的响声。一个声音起来了，一个沙哑的声音开始歌唱：火红的太阳暖烘烘，","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Suddenly on the pavement was heard a loud noise of clogs and the clattering of a stick; and a voice rose—a raucous voice—that sang—","sentences":[{"en":"Suddenly on the pavement was heard a loud noise of clogs and the clattering of a stick; and a voice rose—a raucous voice—that sang—","zh":"小姑娘正做爱情的梦。爱玛坐了起来，好像一具尸首中了电一样，头发披散，瞳仁睁大，呆瞪瞪的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Maids in the warmth of a summer day Dream of love and of love always”","sentences":[{"en":"“Maids in the warmth of a summer day Dream of love and of love always”","zh":"地里的麦子结了穗，忙呀忙坏了大镰刀，","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma raised herself like a galvanised corpse, her hair undone, her eyes fixed, staring.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma raised herself like a galvanised corpse, her hair undone, her eyes fixed, staring.","zh":"快拾麦穗呀别嫌累，我的娜奈特弯下腰。她喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Where the sickle blades have been, Nannette, gathering ears of corn, Passes bending down, my queen, To the earth where they were born.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Where the sickle blades have been, Nannette, gathering ears of corn, Passes bending down, my queen, To the earth where they were born.”","zh":"“瞎子！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“The blind man!” she cried. And Emma began to laugh, an atrocious, frantic, despairing laugh, thinking she saw the hideous face of the poor wretch that stood out against the eternal night like a menace.","sentences":[{"en":"“The blind man!” she cried.","zh":"于是爱玛笑了起来，一种疯狂的、绝望的狞笑，她相信自己看见乞丐的丑脸，站在永恒的黑暗里面吓唬她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"And Emma began to laugh, an atrocious, frantic, despairing laugh, thinking she saw the hideous face of the poor wretch that stood out against the eternal night like a menace.","zh":"于是爱玛笑了起来，一种疯狂的、绝望的狞笑，她相信自己看见乞丐的丑脸，站在永恒的黑暗里面吓唬她。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“The wind is strong this summer day, Her petticoat has flown away.”","sentences":[{"en":"“The wind is strong this summer day, Her petticoat has flown away.”","zh":"这一天忽然起大风，她的短裙哟失了踪。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She fell back upon the mattress in a convulsion. They all drew near. She was dead.","sentences":[{"en":"She fell back upon the mattress in a convulsion.","zh":"一阵痉挛，她又倒在床褥上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They all drew near.","zh":"大家走到跟前。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was dead.","zh":"她已经咽气了。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-9","part":3,"n":9,"title":"Part III · Chapter 9","titleZh":"下卷 · 9","paragraphs":[{"en":"There is always after the death of anyone a kind of stupefaction; so difficult is it to grasp this advent of nothingness and to resign ourselves to believe in it. But still, when he saw that she did not move, Charles threw himself upon her, crying—","sentences":[{"en":"There is always after the death of anyone a kind of stupefaction; so difficult is it to grasp this advent of nothingness and to resign ourselves to believe in it.","zh":"说死就死，快得什么似的，不说相信，单是领会，活着的人就很难一下子做到，所以看见人死，起初总是目瞪口呆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But still, when he saw that she did not move, Charles threw himself upon her, crying—","zh":"可是查理一见她断气，就扑到她身上喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Farewell! farewell!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Farewell! farewell!”","zh":"“永别了！永别了！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais and Canivet dragged him from the room.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais and Canivet dragged him from the room.","zh":"郝麦和卡尼韦把他拉到卧室外。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Restrain yourself!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Restrain yourself!”","zh":"郝麦和卡尼韦把他拉到卧室外。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Yes.” said he, struggling, “I’ll be quiet. I’ll not do anything. But leave me alone. I want to see her. She is my wife!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yes.” said he, struggling, “I’ll be quiet.","zh":"“要节哀才是！”他挣扎道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ll not do anything.","zh":"“是，我懂，我不会闹出事来的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But leave me alone.","zh":"“是，我懂，我不会闹出事来的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I want to see her.","zh":"不过，放开我！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She is my wife!”","zh":"我要看看她！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he wept.","sentences":[{"en":"And he wept.","zh":"她是我太太！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Cry,” said the chemist; “let nature take her course; that will solace you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Cry,” said the chemist; “let nature take her course; that will solace you.”","zh":"他哭着。药剂师道：“哭吧，顺其自然，您就舒坦啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Weaker than a child, Charles let himself be led downstairs into the sitting-room, and Monsieur Homais soon went home. On the Place he was accosted by the blind man, who, having dragged himself as far as Yonville, in the hope of getting the antiphlogistic pomade, was asking every passer-by where the druggist lived.","sentences":[{"en":"Weaker than a child, Charles let himself be led downstairs into the sitting-room, and Monsieur Homais soon went home.","zh":"查理变得比一个小孩子还软弱，由他们拉到底下厅房。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the Place he was accosted by the blind man, who, having dragged himself as far as Yonville, in the hope of getting the antiphlogistic pomade, was asking every passer-by where the druggist lived.","zh":"郝麦先生跟着也就回家去了。他在广场遇见瞎子。瞎子希望弄到消炎膏，逢人打听药剂师的住处，一直摸索到永镇。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“There now! as if I hadn’t got other fish to fry. Well, so much the worse; you must come later on.”","sentences":[{"en":"“There now! as if I hadn’t got other fish to fry.","zh":"“去你一边的吧！倒像我手上没有别的事一样！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Well, so much the worse; you must come later on.”","zh":"啊！活该，以后再来吧！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And he entered the shop hurriedly.","sentences":[{"en":"And he entered the shop hurriedly.","zh":"他急急忙忙进了药房。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had to write two letters, to prepare a soothing potion for Bovary, to invent some lie that would conceal the poisoning, and work it up into an article for the “Fanal,” without counting the people who were waiting to get the news from him; and when the Yonvillers had all heard his story of the arsenic that she had mistaken for sugar in making a vanilla cream. Homais once more returned to Bovary’s.","sentences":[{"en":"He had to write two letters, to prepare a soothing potion for Bovary, to invent some lie that would conceal the poisoning, and work it up into an article for the “Fanal,” without counting the people who were waiting to get the news from him; and when the Yonvillers had all heard his story of the arsenic that she had mistaken for sugar in making a vanilla cream.","zh":"他得写两封信，给包法利配一副安神药水，捏造一套隐瞒服毒的谎话，写成文章，送给《烽火》登出来，还不提永镇的男男女女，等着找他打听消息。待永镇人都听说了她做香草奶油，错把砒霜当糖用的故事，郝麦便又回到包法利家。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Homais once more returned to Bovary’s.","zh":"他得写两封信，给包法利配一副安神药水，捏造一套隐瞒服毒的谎话，写成文章，送给《烽火》登出来，还不提永镇的男男女女，等着找他打听消息。待永镇人都听说了她做香草奶油，错把砒霜当糖用的故事，郝麦便又回到包法利家。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He found him alone (Monsieur Canivet had left), sitting in an arm-chair near the window, staring with an idiotic look at the flags of the floor.","sentences":[{"en":"He found him alone (Monsieur Canivet had left), sitting in an arm-chair near the window, staring with an idiotic look at the flags of the floor.","zh":"他发现只包法利一个人（卡尼韦先生才走），坐在扶手椅里，靠近窗户，白痴似的，盯着厅房的石板地看。药剂师道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Now,” said the chemist, “you ought yourself to fix the hour for the ceremony.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Now,” said the chemist, “you ought yourself to fix the hour for the ceremony.”","zh":"“现在您该规定一下举行仪式的时间。”“什么？什么仪式？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Why? What ceremony?” Then, in a stammering, frightened voice, “Oh, no! not that. No! I want to see her here.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Why?","zh":"然后，声音畏缩，结结巴巴道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What ceremony?”","zh":"“哎！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, in a stammering, frightened voice, “Oh, no! not that.","zh":"不必，是不是？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"No! I want to see her here.”","zh":"不必，我要留着她。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais, to keep himself in countenance, took up a water-bottle on the whatnot to water the geraniums.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais, to keep himself in countenance, took up a water-bottle on the whatnot to water the geraniums.","zh":"郝麦一听话不对劲，拿起摆设架上的水瓶，去浇天竺葵。查理道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah! thanks,” said Charles; “you are good.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah! thanks,” said Charles; “you are good.”","zh":"“啊！谢谢。您是好人！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But he did not finish, choking beneath the crowd of memories that this action of the druggist recalled to him.","sentences":[{"en":"But he did not finish, choking beneath the crowd of memories that this action of the druggist recalled to him.","zh":"药剂师的举动引起满头满脑的回忆，他一难过，不再说下去了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then to distract him, Homais thought fit to talk a little horticulture: plants wanted humidity. Charles bowed his head in sign of approbation.","sentences":[{"en":"Then to distract him, Homais thought fit to talk a little horticulture: plants wanted humidity.","zh":"郝麦心想谈谈园艺，可以分散分散他的悲伤，就说：“植物需要湿润。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles bowed his head in sign of approbation.","zh":"查理低下头来，表示赞成。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Besides, the fine days will soon be here again.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Besides, the fine days will soon be here again.”","zh":"“其实，春暖花开的日子，眼看也就到了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Ah!” said Bovary.","sentences":[{"en":"“Ah!” said Bovary.","zh":"包法利道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The druggist, at his wit’s end, began softly to draw aside the small window-curtain.","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist, at his wit’s end, began softly to draw aside the small window-curtain.","zh":"“啊！”药剂师无计可施，轻轻拉开玻璃窗的小帘。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Hallo! there’s Monsieur Tuvache passing.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Hallo! there’s Monsieur Tuvache passing.”","zh":"“看，杜法赦先生过来啦。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles repeated like a machine—-","sentences":[{"en":"Charles repeated like a machine—-","zh":"查理活像一架机器，重复他的话道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Monsieur Tuvache passing!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Monsieur Tuvache passing!”","zh":"查理活像一架机器，重复他的话道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Homais did not dare to speak to him again about the funeral arrangements; it was the priest who succeeded in reconciling him to them.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais did not dare to speak to him again about the funeral arrangements; it was the priest who succeeded in reconciling him to them.","zh":"“杜法赦先生过来啦。”郝麦不敢同他再谈丧葬事宜；最后还是教士劝他，起了效验。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He shut himself up in his consulting-room, took a pen, and after sobbing for some time, wrote—","sentences":[{"en":"He shut himself up in his consulting-room, took a pen, and after sobbing for some time, wrote—","zh":"他把自己关在诊室，拿起笔来，呜咽了半晌，这才写道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I wish her to be buried in her wedding-dress, with white shoes, and a wreath. Her hair is to be spread out over her shoulders. Three coffins, one of oak, one of mahogany, one of lead. Let no one say anything to me. I shall have strength. Over all there is to be placed a large piece of green velvet. This is my wish; see that it is done.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I wish her to be buried in her wedding-dress, with white shoes, and a wreath.","zh":"我希望她入殓时，身穿她的新婚礼服，脚着白鞋，头戴花冠，头发披在两肩，一棺两椁：一个用橡木，一个用桃花心木，一个用铅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Her hair is to be spread out over her shoulders.","zh":"我希望她入殓时，身穿她的新婚礼服，脚着白鞋，头戴花冠，头发披在两肩，一棺两椁：一个用橡木，一个用桃花心木，一个用铅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Three coffins, one of oak, one of mahogany, one of lead.","zh":"我希望她入殓时，身穿她的新婚礼服，脚着白鞋，头戴花冠，头发披在两肩，一棺两椁：一个用橡木，一个用桃花心木，一个用铅。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Let no one say anything to me.","zh":"我不要人和我谈话；我会硬撑起来的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I shall have strength.","zh":"我不要人和我谈话；我会硬撑起来的。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Over all there is to be placed a large piece of green velvet.","zh":"拿一大幅绿丝绒盖在她身上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This is my wish; see that it is done.”","zh":"这是我的希望。就这样做吧。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The two men were much surprised at Bovary’s romantic ideas. The chemist at once went to him and said—","sentences":[{"en":"The two men were much surprised at Bovary’s romantic ideas.","zh":"包法利的浪漫观点，两位先生看了，非常惊讶。药剂师马上劝他道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"The chemist at once went to him and said—","zh":"包法利的浪漫观点，两位先生看了，非常惊讶。药剂师马上劝他道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“This velvet seems to me a superfetation. Besides, the expense—”","sentences":[{"en":"“This velvet seems to me a superfetation.","zh":"“这幅丝绒，我看未免多余。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Besides, the expense—”","zh":"再说，开销…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What’s that to you?” cried Charles. “Leave me! You did not love her. Go!”","sentences":[{"en":"“What’s that to you?” cried Charles.","zh":"查理喊道：“关您什么事？","scope":"group"},{"en":"“Leave me!","zh":"查理喊道：“关您什么事？","scope":"group"},{"en":"You did not love her.","zh":"走开！您不爱她！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Go!”","zh":"出去！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The priest took him by the arm for a turn in the garden. He discoursed on the vanity of earthly things. God was very great, was very good: one must submit to his decrees without a murmur; nay, must even thank him.","sentences":[{"en":"The priest took him by the arm for a turn in the garden.","zh":"教士挽起他的胳膊，兜着花园散步。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He discoursed on the vanity of earthly things.","zh":"他谈起人间物事的虚空。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"God was very great, was very good: one must submit to his decrees without a murmur; nay, must even thank him.","zh":"上帝极其伟大，极其仁慈；我们就该平心静气，服从他的意旨，简直就该感谢才是。查理谩骂起来：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Charles burst out into blasphemies: “I hate your God!”","sentences":[{"en":"Charles burst out into blasphemies: “I hate your God!”","zh":"上帝极其伟大，极其仁慈；我们就该平心静气，服从他的意旨，简直就该感谢才是。查理谩骂起来：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“The spirit of rebellion is still upon you,” sighed the ecclesiastic.","sentences":[{"en":"“The spirit of rebellion is still upon you,” sighed the ecclesiastic.","zh":"“您的上帝呀，我恨透了！”教士叹息道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Bovary was far away. He was walking with great strides along by the wall, near the espalier, and he ground his teeth; he raised to heaven looks of malediction, but not so much as a leaf stirred.","sentences":[{"en":"Bovary was far away.","zh":"“您还有反抗的心情。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was walking with great strides along by the wall, near the espalier, and he ground his teeth; he raised to heaven looks of malediction, but not so much as a leaf stirred.","zh":"包法利走远了。他迈开大步，靠近墙边果树行走，咬牙切齿，朝天投出诅咒的视线，但是没有一片树叶摇动。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A fine rain was falling: Charles, whose chest was bare, at last began to shiver; he went in and sat down in the kitchen.","sentences":[{"en":"A fine rain was falling: Charles, whose chest was bare, at last began to shiver; he went in and sat down in the kitchen.","zh":"细雨蒙蒙，查理没穿外衣，临了也打冷战了，他走进厨房坐下。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At six o’clock a noise like a clatter of old iron was heard on the Place; it was the “Hirondelle” coming in, and he remained with his forehead against the windowpane, watching all the passengers get out, one after the other. Félicité put down a mattress for him in the drawing-room. He threw himself upon it and fell asleep.","sentences":[{"en":"At six o’clock a noise like a clatter of old iron was heard on the Place; it was the “Hirondelle” coming in, and he remained with his forehead against the windowpane, watching all the passengers get out, one after the other.","zh":"到六点钟，广场传来铁器的哐当声：燕子到了。他额头贴着玻璃，看着乘客一个接一个下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Félicité put down a mattress for him in the drawing-room.","zh":"全福在客厅地上给他铺了一条褥子，他往上一躺，睡着了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He threw himself upon it and fell asleep.","zh":"全福在客厅地上给他铺了一条褥子，他往上一躺，睡着了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Although a philosopher, Monsieur Homais respected the dead. So bearing no grudge to poor Charles, he came back again in the evening to sit up with the body; bringing with him three volumes and a pocket-book for taking notes.","sentences":[{"en":"Although a philosopher, Monsieur Homais respected the dead.","zh":"郝麦先生虽然哲理一大套，却也尊重死人。所以他不和可怜的查理记仇，黄昏又守尸来了，带着三本书，还有一个活叶册子，写笔记用。","scope":"group"},{"en":"So bearing no grudge to poor Charles, he came back again in the evening to sit up with the body; bringing with him three volumes and a pocket-book for taking notes.","zh":"郝麦先生虽然哲理一大套，却也尊重死人。所以他不和可怜的查理记仇，黄昏又守尸来了，带着三本书，还有一个活叶册子，写笔记用。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Monsieur Bournisien was there, and two large candles were burning at the head of the bed, that had been taken out of the alcove. The druggist, on whom the silence weighed, was not long before he began formulating some regrets about this “unfortunate young woman.” and the priest replied that there was nothing to do now but pray for her.","sentences":[{"en":"Monsieur Bournisien was there, and two large candles were burning at the head of the bed, that had been taken out of the alcove.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生也在。床已经挪到外头，床头点着两支大蜡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The druggist, on whom the silence weighed, was not long before he began formulating some regrets about this “unfortunate young woman.” and the priest replied that there was nothing to do now but pray for her.","zh":"药剂师嫌空气沉静，没有多久，就编了两句悼念的话，哀怜这“不幸的少妇”。教士回答，如今只有帮她祷告，才是正经。郝麦接下去道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yet,” Homais went on, “one of two things; either she died in a state of grace (as the Church has it), and then she has no need of our prayers; or else she departed impertinent (that is, I believe, the ecclesiastical expression), and then—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Yet,” Homais went on, “one of two things; either she died in a state of grace (as the Church has it), and then she has no need of our prayers; or else she departed impertinent (that is, I believe, the ecclesiastical expression), and then—”","zh":"“不过，二者必有其一：或者她是蒙主召归（如教会那种说法），那她根本就用不着我们祷告；或者她是至死不悟（我相信这是教士的辞令），那…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Bournisien interrupted him, replying testily that it was none the less necessary to pray.","sentences":[{"en":"Bournisien interrupted him, replying testily that it was none the less necessary to pray.","zh":"布尔尼贤打断他的话，粗声粗气驳他，说不管怎么样，都应该祷告。药剂师反对道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But,” objected the chemist, “since God knows all our needs, what can be the good of prayer?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But,” objected the chemist, “since God knows all our needs, what can be the good of prayer?”","zh":"“上帝既然知道我们的一切需要，祷告又有什么用？”教士道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“What!” cried the ecclesiastic, “prayer! Why, aren’t you a Christian?”","sentences":[{"en":"“What!” cried the ecclesiastic, “prayer!","zh":"“什么！祷告！难道您不是基督徒？”","scope":"group"},{"en":"Why, aren’t you a Christian?”","zh":"“什么！祷告！难道您不是基督徒？”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Excuse me,” said Homais; “I admire Christianity. To begin with, it enfranchised the slaves, introduced into the world a morality—”","sentences":[{"en":"“Excuse me,” said Homais; “I admire Christianity.","zh":"郝麦道：“对不住！我佩服基督教！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To begin with, it enfranchised the slaves, introduced into the world a morality—”","zh":"首先，解放奴隶，在社会树立起一种道德理论…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“That isn’t the question. All the texts-”","sentences":[{"en":"“That isn’t the question.","zh":"“不仅这个！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All the texts-”","zh":"所有经文…”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh! oh! As to texts, look at history; it, is known that all the texts have been falsified by the Jesuits.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh! oh!","zh":"“嗐！嗐！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"As to texts, look at history; it, is known that all the texts have been falsified by the Jesuits.”","zh":"说到经文，看看历史吧；人人知道，耶稣会会士篡改经文来的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles came in, and advancing towards the bed, slowly drew the curtains.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles came in, and advancing towards the bed, slowly drew the curtains.","zh":"查理进来，走到床前，慢慢腾腾，掀开幔帐。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Emma’s head was turned towards her right shoulder, the corner of her mouth, which was open, seemed like a black hole at the lower part of her face; her two thumbs were bent into the palms of her hands; a kind of white dust besprinkled her lashes, and her eyes were beginning to disappear in that viscous pallor that looks like a thin web, as if spiders had spun it over. The sheet sunk in from her breast to her knees, and then rose at the tips of her toes, and it seemed to Charles that infinite masses, an enormous load, were weighing upon her.","sentences":[{"en":"Emma’s head was turned towards her right shoulder, the corner of her mouth, which was open, seemed like a black hole at the lower part of her face; her two thumbs were bent into the palms of her hands; a kind of white dust besprinkled her lashes, and her eyes were beginning to disappear in that viscous pallor that looks like a thin web, as if spiders had spun it over.","zh":"爱玛的头歪靠右肩膀，嘴张开了，脸的下部就像开了一个黑洞。两个拇指还弯在手心。眼睫毛上仿佛撒了一层白粉。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The sheet sunk in from her breast to her knees, and then rose at the tips of her toes, and it seemed to Charles that infinite masses, an enormous load, were weighing upon her.","zh":"眼睛开始消失，像是蜘蛛在上面结了网，盖着一种细布似的黏黏的白东西。尸布先在胸脯和膝盖之间凹下去，再在脚趾尖头鼓了起来，查理觉得像有无限的体积、绝大的重量压在她身上一样。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The church clock struck two. They could hear the loud murmur of the river flowing in the darkness at the foot of the terrace. Monsieur Bournisien from time to time blew his nose noisily, and Homais’ pen was scratching over the paper.","sentences":[{"en":"The church clock struck two.","zh":"教堂的钟正敲两点。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They could hear the loud murmur of the river flowing in the darkness at the foot of the terrace.","zh":"他们听见河水潺潺，从平台一旁流入黑暗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Bournisien from time to time blew his nose noisily, and Homais’ pen was scratching over the paper.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生不时大声擤鼻涕；郝麦的笔在纸上哧哧直响。他道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come, my good friend,” he said, “withdraw; this spectacle is tearing you to pieces.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, my good friend,” he said, “withdraw; this spectacle is tearing you to pieces.”","zh":"“好啦，我的好朋友，对景伤情，您还是走开吧。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles once gone, the chemist and the cure recommenced their discussions.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles once gone, the chemist and the cure recommenced their discussions.","zh":"查理一走，药剂师和堂长又辩论起来了。一位说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Read Voltaire,” said the one, “read D’Holbach, read the ‘Encyclopaedia’!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Read Voltaire,” said the one, “read D’Holbach, read the ‘Encyclopaedia’!”","zh":"“读伏尔泰！读霍尔巴赫！读《百科全书》！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Read the ‘Letters of some Portuguese Jews,’” said the other; “read ‘The Meaning of Christianity,’ by Nicolas, formerly a magistrate.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Read the ‘Letters of some Portuguese Jews,’” said the other; “read ‘The Meaning of Christianity,’ by Nicolas, formerly a magistrate.”","zh":"另一位说：“读《葡萄牙犹太人书简》！读前任文官尼古拉写的《基督教辨》！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They grew warm, they grew red, they both talked at once without listening to each other. Bournisien was scandalized at such audacity; Homais marvelled at such stupidity; and they were on the point of insulting one another when Charles suddenly reappeared. A fascination drew him. He was continually coming upstairs.","sentences":[{"en":"They grew warm, they grew red, they both talked at once without listening to each other.","zh":"两个人争执不下，面红耳赤，同时说话，谁也不听谁说。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bournisien was scandalized at such audacity; Homais marvelled at such stupidity; and they were on the point of insulting one another when Charles suddenly reappeared.","zh":"布尔尼贤想不到对方会这样狂妄；郝麦奇怪对方会这样愚蠢。两个人就要破口对骂了，忽然看见查理又出现了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A fascination drew him.","zh":"有什么东西不断吸引他上楼。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was continually coming upstairs.","zh":"有什么东西不断吸引他上楼。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He stood opposite her, the better to see her, and he lost himself in a contemplation so deep that it was no longer painful.","sentences":[{"en":"He stood opposite her, the better to see her, and he lost himself in a contemplation so deep that it was no longer painful.","zh":"为了看她看得清楚，他待在对面，凝神观看。也正由于凝神观看，他已经不觉得痛苦了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He recalled stories of catalepsy, the marvels of magnetism, and he said to himself that by willing it with all his force he might perhaps succeed in reviving her. Once he even bent towards he, and cried in a low voice, “Emma! Emma!” His strong breathing made the flames of the candles tremble against the wall.","sentences":[{"en":"He recalled stories of catalepsy, the marvels of magnetism, and he said to himself that by willing it with all his force he might perhaps succeed in reviving her.","zh":"他想起关于感应的故事，关于催眠术的奇迹；他向自己说：精诚所至，或许能起死回生。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once he even bent towards he, and cried in a low voice, “Emma!","zh":"有一次，他甚至朝她弯过身子，低头呼唤：“爱玛！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma!”","zh":"爱玛！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His strong breathing made the flames of the candles tremble against the wall.","zh":"声急气粗，蜡烛的火焰也被吹到墙上摇晃。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At daybreak Madame Bovary senior arrived. Charles as he embraced her burst into another flood of tears. She tried, as the chemist had done, to make some remarks to him on the expenses of the funeral. He became so angry that she was silent, and he even commissioned her to go to town at once and buy what was necessary.","sentences":[{"en":"At daybreak Madame Bovary senior arrived.","zh":"天蒙蒙亮，包法利老太太就来了；查理吻抱她，悲从中来，又哭了一场。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles as he embraced her burst into another flood of tears.","zh":"天蒙蒙亮，包法利老太太就来了；查理吻抱她，悲从中来，又哭了一场。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She tried, as the chemist had done, to make some remarks to him on the expenses of the funeral.","zh":"她像药剂师一样，试着劝他撙节丧葬费用。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He became so angry that she was silent, and he even commissioned her to go to town at once and buy what was necessary.","zh":"他不但不听劝，反而大为生气，她也就只好作罢。他甚至要她立刻进城去买必需的东西。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles remained alone the whole afternoon; they had taken Berthe to Madame Homais’; Félicité was in the room upstairs with Madame Lefrancois.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles remained alone the whole afternoon; they had taken Berthe to Madame Homais’; Félicité was in the room upstairs with Madame Lefrancois.","zh":"查理独自待了一下午；白尔特交给郝麦太太照管；全福和勒弗朗索瓦太太在楼上房间守灵。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the evening he had some visitors. He rose, pressed their hands, unable to speak. Then they sat down near one another, and formed a large semicircle in front of the fire. With lowered faces, and swinging one leg crossed over the other knee, they uttered deep sighs at intervals; each one was inordinately bored, and yet none would be the first to go.","sentences":[{"en":"In the evening he had some visitors.","zh":"当天黄昏，他接见吊客。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He rose, pressed their hands, unable to speak.","zh":"他站起来，握着对方的手，说不出话，随后大家挨挨挤挤坐下，在壁炉前围成一个大半圆圈，低下头，交叠着腿。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then they sat down near one another, and formed a large semicircle in front of the fire.","zh":"他站起来，握着对方的手，说不出话，随后大家挨挨挤挤坐下，在壁炉前围成一个大半圆圈，低下头，交叠着腿。","scope":"group"},{"en":"With lowered faces, and swinging one leg crossed over the other knee, they uttered deep sighs at intervals; each one was inordinately bored, and yet none would be the first to go.","zh":"他们一边摇腿，一边不时大声叹息。人人无聊到了极点，可是谁也不肯先走。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais, when he returned at nine o’clock (for the last two days only Homais seemed to have been on the Place), was laden with a stock of camphor, of benzine, and aromatic herbs. He also carried a large jar full of chlorine water, to keep off all miasmata. Just then the servant, Madame Lefrancois, and Madame Bovary senior were busy about Emma, finishing dressing her, and they were drawing down the long stiff veil that covered her to her satin shoes.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais, when he returned at nine o’clock (for the last two days only Homais seemed to have been on the Place), was laden with a stock of camphor, of benzine, and aromatic herbs.","zh":"郝麦在九点钟又来了（两天以来，大家净在广场看见他），带来一堆樟脑、安息香和香草。他还带来一瓶含氯的药水 ，消除秽气。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He also carried a large jar full of chlorine water, to keep off all miasmata.","zh":"女用人、勒弗朗索瓦太太和包法利老太太兜着爱玛，转来转去，这时正好给她换完衣服；她们拉下又长又硬的面网，一直盖到她的缎鞋。全福呜咽道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"Just then the servant, Madame Lefrancois, and Madame Bovary senior were busy about Emma, finishing dressing her, and they were drawing down the long stiff veil that covered her to her satin shoes.","zh":"女用人、勒弗朗索瓦太太和包法利老太太兜着爱玛，转来转去，这时正好给她换完衣服；她们拉下又长又硬的面网，一直盖到她的缎鞋。全福呜咽道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Félicité was sobbing—“Ah! my poor mistress! my poor mistress!”","sentences":[{"en":"Félicité was sobbing—“Ah! my poor mistress! my poor mistress!”","zh":"“啊！我可怜的太太，我可怜的太太！”女店家叹息道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Look at her,” said the landlady, sighing; “how pretty she still is! Now, couldn’t you swear she was going to get up in a minute?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Look at her,” said the landlady, sighing; “how pretty she still is!","zh":"“看呀，她还是那样好看！谁不说，她这就要坐起来呀。”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Now, couldn’t you swear she was going to get up in a minute?”","zh":"她们接着就弯下身子，给她戴花冠。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then they bent over her to put on her wreath. They had to raise the head a little, and a rush of black liquid issued, as if she were vomiting, from her mouth.","sentences":[{"en":"Then they bent over her to put on her wreath.","zh":"头非举高一点不可，但是头一举高，就见嘴里流出一股黑水，好像又在呕吐一样。勒弗朗索瓦太太叫道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"They had to raise the head a little, and a rush of black liquid issued, as if she were vomiting, from her mouth.","zh":"头非举高一点不可，但是头一举高，就见嘴里流出一股黑水，好像又在呕吐一样。勒弗朗索瓦太太叫道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“Oh, goodness! The dress; take care!” cried Madame Lefrancois. “Now, just come and help,” she said to the chemist. “Perhaps you’re afraid?”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, goodness!","zh":"“啊！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The dress; take care!” cried Madame Lefrancois.","zh":"我的上帝！袍子，当心！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Now, just come and help,” she said to the chemist.","zh":"她转向药剂师道：“帮帮我们的忙！怎么！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Perhaps you’re afraid?”","zh":"您还害怕！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I afraid?” replied he, shrugging his shoulders. “I dare say! I’ve seen all sorts of things at the hospital when I was studying pharmacy. We used to make punch in the dissecting room! Nothingness does not terrify a philosopher; and, as I often say, I even intend to leave my body to the hospitals, in order, later on, to serve science.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I afraid?” replied he, shrugging his shoulders.","zh":"他耸肩膀驳她道：“我，害怕？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“I dare say!","zh":"看您说的！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I’ve seen all sorts of things at the hospital when I was studying pharmacy.","zh":"我念药剂学的时候，我在市立医院看到的死人，那才叫多！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"We used to make punch in the dissecting room!","zh":"我们在解剖教室配五味酒！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Nothingness does not terrify a philosopher; and, as I often say, I even intend to leave my body to the hospitals, in order, later on, to serve science.”","zh":"死人吓不倒哲学家；我常常说起，我有心要把我的身体送给医院，供科学研究用。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The cure on his arrival inquired how Monsieur Bovary was, and, on the reply of the druggist, went on—“The blow, you see, is still too recent.”","sentences":[{"en":"The cure on his arrival inquired how Monsieur Bovary was, and, on the reply of the druggist, went on—“The blow, you see, is still too recent.”","zh":"神甫一到，就问起包法利的情形，听完药剂师的回答，他讲：“您明白，刺激还太近！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Homais congratulated him on not being exposed, like other people, to the loss of a beloved companion; whence there followed a discussion on the celibacy of priests.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Homais congratulated him on not being exposed, like other people, to the loss of a beloved companion; whence there followed a discussion on the celibacy of priests.","zh":"郝麦一听这话，就恭喜他不像别人，不致有丧失娇妻的危险。他这话引起一场关于教士独身的争论。药剂师说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“For,” said the chemist, “it is unnatural that a man should do without women! There have been crimes—”","sentences":[{"en":"“For,” said the chemist, “it is unnatural that a man should do without women!","zh":"“因为男人不要女人，就不合乎自然！有人犯罪…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There have been crimes—”","zh":"”教士喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“But, good heaven!” cried the ecclesiastic, “how do you expect an individual who is married to keep the secrets of the confessional, for example?”","sentences":[{"en":"“But, good heaven!” cried the ecclesiastic, “how do you expect an individual who is married to keep the secrets of the confessional, for example?”","zh":"“不过，老天爷！一个人结了婚，您倒说说，怎么能保守忏悔的秘密啊？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais fell foul of the confessional. Bournisien defended it; he enlarged on the acts of restitution that it brought about. He cited various anecdotes about thieves who had suddenly become honest. Military men on approaching the tribunal of penitence had felt the scales fall from their eyes. At Fribourg there was a minister—","sentences":[{"en":"Homais fell foul of the confessional.","zh":"郝麦攻击忏悔。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Bournisien defended it; he enlarged on the acts of restitution that it brought about.","zh":"布尔尼贤加以辩护，说它有恢复本性的效果，举出盗贼忽然变好的种种逸事作证明。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He cited various anecdotes about thieves who had suddenly become honest.","zh":"布尔尼贤加以辩护，说它有恢复本性的效果，举出盗贼忽然变好的种种逸事作证明。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Military men on approaching the tribunal of penitence had felt the scales fall from their eyes.","zh":"有些军人走进告解座，觉得眼睛上有鳞掉下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At Fribourg there was a minister—","zh":"弗里堡 有一位教士…","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His companion was asleep. Then he felt somewhat stifled by the over-heavy atmosphere of the room; he opened the window; this awoke the chemist.","sentences":[{"en":"His companion was asleep.","zh":"他的同伴睡着了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he felt somewhat stifled by the over-heavy atmosphere of the room; he opened the window; this awoke the chemist.","zh":"房间的空气太浊，教士觉得有一点气闷，过去打开窗户，惊醒了药剂师。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come, take a pinch of snuff,” he said to him. “Take it; it’ll relieve you.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Come, take a pinch of snuff,” he said to him.","zh":"他对他道：“来，闻闻鼻烟！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Take it; it’ll relieve you.”","zh":"吸吸吧，人就清醒了。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A continual barking was heard in the distance. “Do you hear that dog howling?” said the chemist.","sentences":[{"en":"A continual barking was heard in the distance.","zh":"老远什么地方，狗不断在吠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Do you hear that dog howling?” said the chemist.","zh":"药剂师道：“您听见狗叫了吗？”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“They smell the dead,” replied the priest. “It’s like bees; they leave their hives on the decease of any person.”","sentences":[{"en":"“They smell the dead,” replied the priest.","zh":"教士回答：“据说，它们闻得到死人的气味。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“It’s like bees; they leave their hives on the decease of any person.”","zh":"好像蜜蜂一样，闻到死人气味就会离开蜂窝。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Homais made no remark upon these prejudices, for he had again dropped asleep. Monsieur Bournisien, stronger than he, went on moving his lips gently for some time, then insensibly his chin sank down, he let fall his big black boot, and began to snore.","sentences":[{"en":"Homais made no remark upon these prejudices, for he had again dropped asleep.","zh":"郝麦没有驳斥这些偏见，因为他又睡着了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Bournisien, stronger than he, went on moving his lips gently for some time, then insensibly his chin sank down, he let fall his big black boot, and began to snore.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生比较壮实，呢呢喃喃，嘴唇继续动了一阵，不知不觉，下巴一耷拉，丢开他的大黑书，也就呼噜呼噜打起鼾来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They sat opposite one another, with protruding stomachs, puffed-up faces, and frowning looks, after so much disagreement uniting at last in the same human weakness, and they moved no more than the corpse by their side, that seemed to be sleeping.","sentences":[{"en":"They sat opposite one another, with protruding stomachs, puffed-up faces, and frowning looks, after so much disagreement uniting at last in the same human weakness, and they moved no more than the corpse by their side, that seemed to be sleeping.","zh":"两个人相对而坐，肚子臌出，脸皮浮肿，眉头紧皱，争吵了那么长时间，终于在人类同一弱点之中携手了。尸体的模样像在睡觉一样，他们一动不动，比尸体强不了多少。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles coming in did not wake them. It was the last time; he came to bid her farewell.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles coming in did not wake them.","zh":"查理进来，没有惊动他们。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was the last time; he came to bid her farewell.","zh":"这是末一回。他向她告别来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The aromatic herbs were still smoking, and spirals of bluish vapour blended at the window-sash with the fog that was coming in. There were few stars, and the night was warm. The wax of the candles fell in great drops upon the sheets of the bed. Charles watched them burn, tiring his eyes against the glare of their yellow flame.","sentences":[{"en":"The aromatic herbs were still smoking, and spirals of bluish vapour blended at the window-sash with the fog that was coming in.","zh":"香草还在燃烧，浅蓝的氤氲飘到窗口，和进来的雾混合起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There were few stars, and the night was warm.","zh":"天上有几颗星宿，夜很柔和。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The wax of the candles fell in great drops upon the sheets of the bed.","zh":"大滴蜡烛油落在床单上，好像眼泪一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles watched them burn, tiring his eyes against the glare of their yellow flame.","zh":"查理望着蜡烛燃烧，可是望久了黄焰的亮光，眼睛疲倦了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The watering on the satin gown shimmered white as moonlight. Emma was lost beneath it; and it seemed to him that, spreading beyond her own self, she blended confusedly with everything around her—the silence, the night, the passing wind, the damp odours rising from the ground.","sentences":[{"en":"The watering on the satin gown shimmered white as moonlight.","zh":"缎袍如同月光一样白，波纹似的闪闪烁烁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma was lost beneath it; and it seemed to him that, spreading beyond her own self, she blended confusedly with everything around her—the silence, the night, the passing wind, the damp odours rising from the ground.","zh":"她裹在里头，好像消失了一样。他觉得她离开身体，迷迷蒙蒙，化入四周的什物，和寂静、黑夜、过往的风、升起的润泽的香气，全都混为一体。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then suddenly he saw her in the garden at Tostes, on a bench against the thorn hedge, or else at Rouen in the streets, on the threshold of their house, in the yard at Bertaux. He again heard the laughter of the happy boys beneath the apple-trees: the room was filled with the perfume of her hair; and her dress rustled in his arms with a noise like electricity. The dress was still the same.","sentences":[{"en":"Then suddenly he saw her in the garden at Tostes, on a bench against the thorn hedge, or else at Rouen in the streets, on the threshold of their house, in the yard at Bertaux.","zh":"他忽然看见她在道特的花园，坐在荆棘篱笆前面的长凳上；过了一会儿，又在鲁昂的街上，又在他们的门口，又在拜尔托的院落。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He again heard the laughter of the happy boys beneath the apple-trees: the room was filled with the perfume of her hair; and her dress rustled in his arms with a noise like electricity.","zh":"他还听见男孩子们，快快活活，在苹果树底下，连笑带舞。房间充满她的头发的香味，她的袍子在他的胳膊底下，窸窸窣窣，发出火花一样的响声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The dress was still the same.","zh":"这件袍子还是那件袍子！","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"For a long while he thus recalled all his lost joys, her attitudes, her movements, the sound of her voice. Upon one fit of despair followed another, and even others, inexhaustible as the waves of an overflowing sea.","sentences":[{"en":"For a long while he thus recalled all his lost joys, her attitudes, her movements, the sound of her voice.","zh":"他就这样久久回忆过去的种种欢乐，她的体态、她的手势、她的声调。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Upon one fit of despair followed another, and even others, inexhaustible as the waves of an overflowing sea.","zh":"他一阵一阵难过，无终无了，源源不绝，仿佛潮水上涨，喷涌一片。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A terrible curiosity seized him. Slowly, with the tips of his fingers, palpitating, he lifted her veil. But he uttered a cry of horror that awoke the other two.","sentences":[{"en":"A terrible curiosity seized him.","zh":"他起了可怕的好奇心：他一边心跳，一边慢慢腾腾，拿手指尖掀起她的面网。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Slowly, with the tips of his fingers, palpitating, he lifted her veil.","zh":"他起了可怕的好奇心：他一边心跳，一边慢慢腾腾，拿手指尖掀起她的面网。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But he uttered a cry of horror that awoke the other two.","zh":"但是他不看犹可，一看吓得叫了起来，惊醒另外两位。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"They dragged him down into the sitting-room. Then Félicité came up to say that he wanted some of her hair.","sentences":[{"en":"They dragged him down into the sitting-room.","zh":"但是他不看犹可，一看吓得叫了起来，惊醒另外两位。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then Félicité came up to say that he wanted some of her hair.","zh":"他们把他拉到底下厅房。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Cut some off,” replied the druggist.","sentences":[{"en":"“Cut some off,” replied the druggist.","zh":"全福随后上来，说他要一绺头发。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And as she did not dare to, he himself stepped forward, scissors in hand. He trembled so that he pierced the skin of the temple in several places. At last, stiffening himself against emotion, Homais gave two or three great cuts at random that left white patches amongst that beautiful black hair.","sentences":[{"en":"And as she did not dare to, he himself stepped forward, scissors in hand.","zh":"药剂师道：“剪吧！”她不敢剪；他拿起剪子，亲自去剪。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He trembled so that he pierced the skin of the temple in several places.","zh":"他直打哆嗦，两鬓扎了好几个伤口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, stiffening himself against emotion, Homais gave two or three great cuts at random that left white patches amongst that beautiful black hair.","zh":"最后，郝麦硬起头皮，乱剪了两三剪刀，给她的美丽的黑头发添了几块空白。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The chemist and the cure plunged anew into their occupations, not without sleeping from time to time, of which they accused each other reciprocally at each fresh awakening. Then Monsieur Bournisien sprinkled the room with holy water and Homais threw a little chlorine water on the floor.","sentences":[{"en":"The chemist and the cure plunged anew into their occupations, not without sleeping from time to time, of which they accused each other reciprocally at each fresh awakening.","zh":"药剂师和堂长继续干自己的事，中间免不了睡一会儿，但是每回醒来，就你怪我，我怪你，谁也不放过谁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Monsieur Bournisien sprinkled the room with holy water and Homais threw a little chlorine water on the floor.","zh":"于是布尔尼贤在房间洒圣水，郝麦拿一点含氯的药水倒在地板上。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Félicité had taken care to put on the chest of drawers, for each of them, a bottle of brandy, some cheese, and a large roll. And the druggist, who could not hold out any longer, about four in the morning sighed—","sentences":[{"en":"Félicité had taken care to put on the chest of drawers, for each of them, a bottle of brandy, some cheese, and a large roll.","zh":"全福事前在五斗柜上，给他们摆好一瓶白酒、一块干酪、一大块点心。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And the druggist, who could not hold out any longer, about four in the morning sighed—","zh":"所以临到早晨四点钟左右，药剂师熬不住了，叹气道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“My word! I should like to take some sustenance.”","sentences":[{"en":"“My word!","zh":"“说真的，我想加加养料！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I should like to take some sustenance.”","zh":"“说真的，我想加加养料！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The priest did not need any persuading; he went out to go and say mass, came back, and then they ate and hobnobbed, giggling a little without knowing why, stimulated by that vague gaiety that comes upon us after times of sadness, and at the last glass the priest said to the druggist, as he clapped him on the shoulder—","sentences":[{"en":"The priest did not need any persuading; he went out to go and say mass, came back, and then they ate and hobnobbed, giggling a little without knowing why, stimulated by that vague gaiety that comes upon us after times of sadness, and at the last glass the priest said to the druggist, as he clapped him on the shoulder—","zh":"教士不需他劝，出去做完弥撒回来，他们就碰杯吃喝起来，不知道为什么，还咯咯笑着：人在经历某些忧愁阶段之后，会生出一种泛泛的轻松感，所以教士喝到末一小杯，拍着药剂师的肩膀道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“We shall end by understanding one another.”","sentences":[{"en":"“We shall end by understanding one another.”","zh":"“我们会有一天互相了解的！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the passage downstairs they met the undertaker’s men, who were coming in. Then Charles for two hours had to suffer the torture of hearing the hammer resound against the wood. Next day they lowered her into her oak coffin, that was fitted into the other two; but as the bier was too large, they had to fill up the gaps with the wool of a mattress. At last, when the three lids had been planed down, nailed, soldered, it was placed outside in front of the door; the house was thrown open, and the people of Yonville began to flock round.","sentences":[{"en":"In the passage downstairs they met the undertaker’s men, who were coming in.","zh":"他们在底下门道遇见工人进来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Charles for two hours had to suffer the torture of hearing the hammer resound against the wood.","zh":"于是足足两小时之久，查理不得不忍受铁锤敲打木板的响声。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Next day they lowered her into her oak coffin, that was fitted into the other two; but as the bier was too large, they had to fill up the gaps with the wool of a mattress.","zh":"他们把她放进橡木棺材，再装在另外两副棺材里头，但是外椁太宽，又得拿一条褥子的毛绒塞满空当。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, when the three lids had been planed down, nailed, soldered, it was placed outside in front of the door; the house was thrown open, and the people of Yonville began to flock round.","zh":"最后三副棺盖刨平，钉牢，焊好了，就把灵柩放在大门前面。大门敞开了，永镇的男女开始集合。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Old Rouault arrived, and fainted on the Place when he saw the black cloth!","sentences":[{"en":"Old Rouault arrived, and fainted on the Place when he saw the black cloth!","zh":"卢欧老爹来了。他望见黑布 ，在广场晕死过去。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-10","part":3,"n":10,"title":"Part III · Chapter 10","titleZh":"下卷 · 10","paragraphs":[{"en":"He had only received the chemist’s letter thirty-six hours after the event; and, from consideration for his feelings, Homais had so worded it that it was impossible to make out what it was all about.","sentences":[{"en":"He had only received the chemist’s letter thirty-six hours after the event; and, from consideration for his feelings, Homais had so worded it that it was impossible to make out what it was all about.","zh":"他在出事三十六小时之后，收到药剂师的信。郝麦先生照顾他的情绪，信上含糊其辞，他看不明白到底是什么意思。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"First, the old fellow had fallen as if struck by apoplexy. Next, he understood that she was not dead, but she might be. At last, he had put on his blouse, taken his hat, fastened his spurs to his boots, and set out at full speed; and the whole of the way old Rouault, panting, was torn by anguish. Once even he was obliged to dismount. He was dizzy; he heard voices round about him; he felt himself going mad.","sentences":[{"en":"First, the old fellow had fallen as if struck by apoplexy.","zh":"老头子看完信，先像中风一样，倒了下去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Next, he understood that she was not dead, but she might be.","zh":"后来他明白她没有死，但是又可能死…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, he had put on his blouse, taken his hat, fastened his spurs to his boots, and set out at full speed; and the whole of the way old Rouault, panting, was torn by anguish.","zh":"他最后穿上工人服，戴上帽子，给鞋套上刺马距，飞也似的出发了。卢欧老爹一路焦灼万状，气喘吁吁。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Once even he was obliged to dismount.","zh":"有一会儿，他什么也看不见，只好下马；听见周围轰隆作响，觉得自己快要疯了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was dizzy; he heard voices round about him; he felt himself going mad.","zh":"有一会儿，他什么也看不见，只好下马；听见周围轰隆作响，觉得自己快要疯了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Day broke. He saw three black hens asleep in a tree. He shuddered, horrified at this omen. Then he promised the Holy Virgin three chasubles for the church, and that he would go barefooted from the cemetery at Bertaux to the chapel of Vassonville.","sentences":[{"en":"Day broke.","zh":"天破晓了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He saw three black hens asleep in a tree.","zh":"他望见三只黑母鸡在一棵树上睡觉；这是凶兆，他吓得哆嗦了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He shuddered, horrified at this omen.","zh":"他望见三只黑母鸡在一棵树上睡觉；这是凶兆，他吓得哆嗦了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he promised the Holy Virgin three chasubles for the church, and that he would go barefooted from the cemetery at Bertaux to the chapel of Vassonville.","zh":"于是他向圣母许愿，送教堂三件祭披，从拜尔托公墓，赤脚走到法松镇的圣堂。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He entered Maromme shouting for the people of the inn, burst open the door with a thrust of his shoulder, made for a sack of oats, emptied a bottle of sweet cider into the manger, and again mounted his nag, whose feet struck fire as it dashed along.","sentences":[{"en":"He entered Maromme shouting for the people of the inn, burst open the door with a thrust of his shoulder, made for a sack of oats, emptied a bottle of sweet cider into the manger, and again mounted his nag, whose feet struck fire as it dashed along.","zh":"他一进马罗默，就喊店家，一肩膀撞开店门，跑到荞麦口袋跟前，又拿一瓶新苹果酒倒进食槽，喂饱了马，又跨上他的小马。马拼命跑，四个铁掌冒出火星来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He said to himself that no doubt they would save her; the doctors would discover some remedy surely. He remembered all the miraculous cures he had been told about. Then she appeared to him dead. She was there; before his eyes, lying on her back in the middle of the road. He reined up, and the hallucination disappeared.","sentences":[{"en":"He said to himself that no doubt they would save her; the doctors would discover some remedy surely.","zh":"他向自己道：不用说，会把她救活过来的；医生一定有法子救她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He remembered all the miraculous cures he had been told about.","zh":"他想起先前听人说起的种种治病的奇迹。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then she appeared to him dead.","zh":"他想起先前听人说起的种种治病的奇迹。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She was there; before his eyes, lying on her back in the middle of the road.","zh":"接着他觉得她又像死了一样。她仰天躺在前面大路当中。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He reined up, and the hallucination disappeared.","zh":"他拉住缰绳，幻影不见了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At Quincampoix, to give himself heart, he drank three cups of coffee one after the other. He fancied they had made a mistake in the name in writing. He looked for the letter in his pocket, felt it there, but did not dare to open it.","sentences":[{"en":"At Quincampoix, to give himself heart, he drank three cups of coffee one after the other.","zh":"他来到甘冈普瓦，一连喝了三杯咖啡壮胆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He fancied they had made a mistake in the name in writing.","zh":"他心想信上写错了名姓。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He looked for the letter in his pocket, felt it there, but did not dare to open it.","zh":"他摸索衣袋，信摸索到了，可是不敢打开看。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At last he began to think it was all a joke; someone’s spite, the jest of some wag; and besides, if she were dead, one would have known it. But no! There was nothing extraordinary about the country; the sky was blue, the trees swayed; a flock of sheep passed. He saw the village; he was seen coming bending forward upon his horse, belabouring it with great blows, the girths dripping with blood.","sentences":[{"en":"At last he began to think it was all a joke; someone’s spite, the jest of some wag; and besides, if she were dead, one would have known it.","zh":"他最后猜想，这也许是一个玩笑——有人报他的仇，淘气小子寻他的开心。再说，她要是真死了的话，他会没有一点感觉？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But no! There was nothing extraordinary about the country; the sky was blue, the trees swayed; a flock of sheep passed.","zh":"然而的确没有！田野和平日没有什么两样：天是蓝的，树枝摇曳；一群羊从旁边走过。他望见村镇。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He saw the village; he was seen coming bending forward upon his horse, belabouring it with great blows, the girths dripping with blood.","zh":"大家见他伏在马背，风驰电掣，拼命打马，肚带上的血往下滴。他醒过来，倒在包法利怀里，哭道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"When he had recovered consciousness, he fell, weeping, into Bovary’s arms: “My girl! Emma! my child! tell me—”","sentences":[{"en":"When he had recovered consciousness, he fell, weeping, into Bovary’s arms: “My girl!","zh":"“我的女儿，爱玛！我的孩子！是怎么一回事，说给我听…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Emma! my child! tell me—”","zh":"”另一位抽抽噎噎回答道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The other replied, sobbing, “I don’t know! I don’t know! It’s a curse!”","sentences":[{"en":"The other replied, sobbing, “I don’t know!","zh":"“我不知道，我不知道！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I don’t know!","zh":"反正是祸事就是了！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"It’s a curse!”","zh":"反正是祸事就是了！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The druggist separated them. “These horrible details are useless. I will tell this gentleman all about it. Here are the people coming. Dignity! Come now! Philosophy!”","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist separated them.","zh":"药剂师分开他们：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“These horrible details are useless.","zh":"“这些可怕的细情，听了也没有用。我回头告诉先生好了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"I will tell this gentleman all about it.","zh":"“这些可怕的细情，听了也没有用。我回头告诉先生好了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Here are the people coming.","zh":"看，人越来越多了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Dignity!","zh":"好，沉着点！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Come now!","zh":"好，沉着点！","scope":"group"},{"en":"Philosophy!”","zh":"想开些！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The poor fellow tried to show himself brave, and repeated several times. “Yes! courage!”","sentences":[{"en":"The poor fellow tried to show himself brave, and repeated several times.","zh":"可怜的包法利表示镇静，重复了几次：“是…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Yes! courage!”","zh":"要勇敢。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh,” cried the old man, “so I will have, by God! I’ll go along o’ her to the end!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh,” cried the old man, “so I will have, by God!","zh":"老头子喊道：“好！老天在上，我一定勇敢，我送她一直送到头。”","scope":"group"},{"en":"I’ll go along o’ her to the end!”","zh":"老头子喊道：“好！老天在上，我一定勇敢，我送她一直送到头。”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The bell began tolling. All was ready; they had to start. And seated in a stall of the choir, side by side, they saw pass and repass in front of them continually the three chanting choristers.","sentences":[{"en":"The bell began tolling.","zh":"钟响了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All was ready; they had to start.","zh":"一切齐备。应当出发了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And seated in a stall of the choir, side by side, they saw pass and repass in front of them continually the three chanting choristers.","zh":"他们并肩坐在唱经堂的祷告席上，只见三位唱诗队队员，不停地在前面走来走去，唱赞美诗。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The serpent-player was blowing with all his might. Monsieur Bournisien, in full vestments, was singing in a shrill voice. He bowed before the tabernacle, raising his hands, stretched out his arms. Lestiboudois went about the church with his whalebone stick. The bier stood near the lectern, between four rows of candles. Charles felt inclined to get up and put them out.","sentences":[{"en":"The serpent-player was blowing with all his might.","zh":"蛇形风管呜嘟呜嘟在响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Bournisien, in full vestments, was singing in a shrill voice.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生全身披挂，尖声吟唱，膜拜圣龛，举高两只手，伸出一双胳膊。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He bowed before the tabernacle, raising his hands, stretched out his arms.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生全身披挂，尖声吟唱，膜拜圣龛，举高两只手，伸出一双胳膊。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Lestiboudois went about the church with his whalebone stick.","zh":"赖斯地布杜瓦拿着他的鲸骨杖，在教堂转来转去。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The bier stood near the lectern, between four rows of candles.","zh":"灵柩靠近经台，停在四排蜡烛中间。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles felt inclined to get up and put them out.","zh":"查理直想站起来，吹灭蜡烛。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Yet he tried to stir himself to a feeling of devotion, to throw himself into the hope of a future life in which he should see her again. He imagined to himself she had gone on a long journey, far away, for a long time. But when he thought of her lying there, and that all was over, that they would lay her in the earth, he was seized with a fierce, gloomy, despairful rage. At times he thought he felt nothing more, and he enjoyed this lull in his pain, whilst at the same time he reproached himself for being a wretch.","sentences":[{"en":"Yet he tried to stir himself to a feeling of devotion, to throw himself into the hope of a future life in which he should see her again.","zh":"不过他也努力激起笃信的心情，希望将来有一天再见到她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He imagined to himself she had gone on a long journey, far away, for a long time.","zh":"他想象她许久以来，就到远处旅行。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But when he thought of her lying there, and that all was over, that they would lay her in the earth, he was seized with a fierce, gloomy, despairful rage.","zh":"但是他再一想，她就在棺材里，不但休想活转来，而且就要下葬，心头立刻涌起一种绝望、悲惨、冷酷的愤怒。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At times he thought he felt nothing more, and he enjoyed this lull in his pain, whilst at the same time he reproached himself for being a wretch.","zh":"有时候他以为自己失了感觉。他一面责备自己没有心肝，一面体味他的痛苦减轻。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The sharp noise of an iron-ferruled stick was heard on the stones, striking them at irregular intervals. It came from the end of the church, and stopped short at the lower aisles. A man in a coarse brown jacket knelt down painfully. It was Hippolyte, the stable-boy at the “Lion d’Or.” He had put on his new leg.","sentences":[{"en":"The sharp noise of an iron-ferruled stick was heard on the stones, striking them at irregular intervals.","zh":"大家听见一根包铁棍子，一板一眼，顿石板地响，声音从里发出，在教堂一侧停住。一个穿一件宽大棕色上装的男人，好不容易跪了下来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It came from the end of the church, and stopped short at the lower aisles.","zh":"大家听见一根包铁棍子，一板一眼，顿石板地响，声音从里发出，在教堂一侧停住。一个穿一件宽大棕色上装的男人，好不容易跪了下来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"A man in a coarse brown jacket knelt down painfully.","zh":"大家听见一根包铁棍子，一板一眼，顿石板地响，声音从里发出，在教堂一侧停住。一个穿一件宽大棕色上装的男人，好不容易跪了下来。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was Hippolyte, the stable-boy at the “Lion d’Or.”","zh":"原来是金狮的伙计伊玻立特。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had put on his new leg.","zh":"他换上了他的新假腿。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"One of the choristers went round the nave making a collection, and the coppers chinked one after the other on the silver plate.","sentences":[{"en":"One of the choristers went round the nave making a collection, and the coppers chinked one after the other on the silver plate.","zh":"一个唱诗队队员，兜着正殿，请求布施。铜钱一个又一个，在银盘里面响动。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, make haste! I am in pain!” cried Bovary, angrily throwing him a five-franc piece. The churchman thanked him with a deep bow.","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, make haste!","zh":"包法利带怒丢给他一枚五法郎辅币，喊道：“快！","scope":"group"},{"en":"I am in pain!” cried Bovary, angrily throwing him a five-franc piece.","zh":"包法利带怒丢给他一枚五法郎辅币，喊道：“快！","scope":"group"},{"en":"The churchman thanked him with a deep bow.","zh":"我难过！我！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They sang, they knelt, they stood up; it was endless! He remembered that once, in the early times, they had been to mass together, and they had sat down on the other side, on the right, by the wall. The bell began again. There was a great moving of chairs; the bearers slipped their three staves under the coffin, and everyone left the church.","sentences":[{"en":"They sang, they knelt, they stood up; it was endless!","zh":"队员深深一躬谢他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He remembered that once, in the early times, they had been to mass together, and they had sat down on the other side, on the right, by the wall.","zh":"歌唱、跪拜、起立，简直没完没了！他记得初来永镇，他们有一回一同望弥撒，坐在右边靠墙一面…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The bell began again.","zh":"钟又响了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was a great moving of chairs; the bearers slipped their three staves under the coffin, and everyone left the church.","zh":"椅子乱动。杠夫在灵柩底下放过三根杠子。大家走出教堂。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Justin appeared at the door of the shop. He suddenly went in again, pale, staggering.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Justin appeared at the door of the shop.","zh":"朱斯丹这时在药房门口出现，面无人色，步履蹒跚，忽然又进去了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He suddenly went in again, pale, staggering.","zh":"朱斯丹这时在药房门口出现，面无人色，步履蹒跚，忽然又进去了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"People were at the windows to see the procession pass. Charles at the head walked erect. He affected a brave air, and saluted with a nod those who, coming out from the lanes or from their doors, stood amidst the crowd.","sentences":[{"en":"People were at the windows to see the procession pass.","zh":"人们站在窗口看出殡。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles at the head walked erect.","zh":"查理领头先走，挺直了腰，他装出一副勇敢模样，看见有人从小巷或者大门出来，加入行列，就点头致意。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He affected a brave air, and saluted with a nod those who, coming out from the lanes or from their doors, stood amidst the crowd.","zh":"查理领头先走，挺直了腰，他装出一副勇敢模样，看见有人从小巷或者大门出来，加入行列，就点头致意。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The six men, three on either side, walked slowly, panting a little. The priests, the choristers, and the two choirboys recited the De profundis, and their voices echoed over the fields, rising and falling with their undulations. Sometimes they disappeared in the windings of the path; but the great silver cross rose always before the trees.","sentences":[{"en":"The six men, three on either side, walked slowly, panting a little.","zh":"六个杠夫，一边三个，迈开小步，微微气喘。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The priests, the choristers, and the two choirboys recited the De profundis, and their voices echoed over the fields, rising and falling with their undulations.","zh":"教士、唱诗队队员和两个唱诗的童子，吟诵“我从深处” ，声音抑扬顿挫，散在田野。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Sometimes they disappeared in the windings of the path; but the great silver cross rose always before the trees.","zh":"有时候他们走进小路拐弯，看不见了，不过大银十字架总在树木之间举着。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The women followed in black cloaks with turned-down hoods; each of them carried in her hands a large lighted candle, and Charles felt himself growing weaker at this continual repetition of prayers and torches, beneath this oppressive odour of wax and of cassocks. A fresh breeze was blowing; the rye and colza were sprouting, little dewdrops trembled at the roadsides and on the hawthorn hedges. All sorts of joyous sounds filled the air; the jolting of a cart rolling afar off in the ruts, the crowing of a cock, repeated again and again, or the gambling of a foal running away under the apple-trees: The pure sky was fretted with rosy clouds; a bluish haze rested upon the cots covered with iris. Charles as he passed recognised each courtyard. He remembered mornings like this, when, after visiting some patient, he came out from one and returned to her.","sentences":[{"en":"The women followed in black cloaks with turned-down hoods; each of them carried in her hands a large lighted candle, and Charles felt himself growing weaker at this continual repetition of prayers and torches, beneath this oppressive odour of wax and of cassocks.","zh":"妇女跟在后头，披着风帽朝下翻的黑斗篷，拿着一支点亮的大蜡烛。查理听见祷告声翻来覆去，看见蜡烛光络绎不绝，闻见蜡油和道袍的恶心气味，觉得自己软绵绵没有气力。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A fresh breeze was blowing; the rye and colza were sprouting, little dewdrops trembled at the roadsides and on the hawthorn hedges.","zh":"一阵清风吹过，裸麦和油菜一片碧绿；露珠在道旁荆棘篱笆上颤抖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All sorts of joyous sounds filled the air; the jolting of a cart rolling afar off in the ruts, the crowing of a cock, repeated again and again, or the gambling of a foal running away under the apple-trees: The pure sky was fretted with rosy clouds; a bluish haze rested upon the cots covered with iris.","zh":"天边是一片欢乐的声音：一辆大车在车辙走动，远远传来鞭子噼啪的响声；一只公鸡啼个不住，要不然就见一匹马驹，跳跳蹦蹦，逃到苹果树底下。晴空飘着几点玫瑰色红云；淡蓝色浮光笼罩着蝴蝶花盖住的茅屋；查理走过，认出一所一所院落。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles as he passed recognised each courtyard.","zh":"天边是一片欢乐的声音：一辆大车在车辙走动，远远传来鞭子噼啪的响声；一只公鸡啼个不住，要不然就见一匹马驹，跳跳蹦蹦，逃到苹果树底下。晴空飘着几点玫瑰色红云；淡蓝色浮光笼罩着蝴蝶花盖住的茅屋；查理走过，认出一所一所院落。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He remembered mornings like this, when, after visiting some patient, he came out from one and returned to her.","zh":"他记得有些早晨如同今天一样，他看完病人，走出院落，回去看她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The black cloth bestrewn with white beads blew up from time to time, laying bare the coffin. The tired bearers walked more slowly, and it advanced with constant jerks, like a boat that pitches with every wave.","sentences":[{"en":"The black cloth bestrewn with white beads blew up from time to time, laying bare the coffin.","zh":"黑布棺罩绣了好些眼泪似的白点子，不时被风吹开，露出灵柩。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The tired bearers walked more slowly, and it advanced with constant jerks, like a boat that pitches with every wave.","zh":"杠夫走累了，放慢脚步。灵柩忽高忽低，仿佛一条小船，一个浪头打来，上下摆动。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They reached the cemetery. The men went right down to a place in the grass where a grave was dug. They ranged themselves all round; and while the priest spoke, the red soil thrown up at the sides kept noiselessly slipping down at the corners.","sentences":[{"en":"They reached the cemetery.","zh":"公墓到了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The men went right down to a place in the grass where a grave was dug.","zh":"人们继续走，一直走到草地有坟穴的地方站住，围成一个圆圈，听教士讲话。红土抛在坟穴周围，又悄悄顺着四周，不断泄了下去。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They ranged themselves all round; and while the priest spoke, the red soil thrown up at the sides kept noiselessly slipping down at the corners.","zh":"人们继续走，一直走到草地有坟穴的地方站住，围成一个圆圈，听教士讲话。红土抛在坟穴周围，又悄悄顺着四周，不断泄了下去。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Then when the four ropes were arranged the coffin was placed upon them. He watched it descend; it seemed descending for ever. At last a thud was heard; the ropes creaked as they were drawn up. Then Bournisien took the spade handed to him by Lestiboudois; with his left hand all the time sprinkling water, with the right he vigorously threw in a large spadeful; and the wood of the coffin, struck by the pebbles, gave forth that dread sound that seems to us the reverberation of eternity.","sentences":[{"en":"Then when the four ropes were arranged the coffin was placed upon them.","zh":"随后四条绳子放好，杠夫把灵柩放到上头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He watched it descend; it seemed descending for ever.","zh":"他看着它往下坠，一直下坠。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last a thud was heard; the ropes creaked as they were drawn up.","zh":"最后听见一声撞响，绳子呲呲喳喳又拉上来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then Bournisien took the spade handed to him by Lestiboudois; with his left hand all the time sprinkling water, with the right he vigorously threw in a large spadeful; and the wood of the coffin, struck by the pebbles, gave forth that dread sound that seems to us the reverberation of eternity.","zh":"于是布尔尼贤拿起赖斯地布杜瓦递给他的铁铲，一面右手洒圣水，一面左手使劲推下一大堆土去；石子碰着棺木，发出可怕的声响，听起来好像永恒的回声。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The ecclesiastic passed the holy water sprinkler to his neighbour. This was Homais. He swung it gravely, then handed it to Charles, who sank to his knees in the earth and threw in handfuls of it, crying, “Adieu!” He sent her kisses; he dragged himself towards the grave, to engulf himself with her. They led him away, and he soon grew calmer, feeling perhaps, like the others, a vague satisfaction that it was all over.","sentences":[{"en":"The ecclesiastic passed the holy water sprinkler to his neighbour.","zh":"教士把圣水壶递给他旁边的郝麦先生。","scope":"group"},{"en":"This was Homais.","zh":"教士把圣水壶递给他旁边的郝麦先生。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He swung it gravely, then handed it to Charles, who sank to his knees in the earth and threw in handfuls of it, crying, “Adieu!”","zh":"他一副庄重的模样摇了摇，又递给查理。他双膝跪在土里，掬起满把土往里扔，一面喊着：“永别了！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sent her kisses; he dragged himself towards the grave, to engulf himself with her.","zh":"一面送过吻去；他爬到坟穴跟前，要和她埋在一道。大家把他拉开了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They led him away, and he soon grew calmer, feeling perhaps, like the others, a vague satisfaction that it was all over.","zh":"他没有多久，也就安静下来。他也许跟别人一样，模模糊糊，感到结束的满足。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Old Rouault on his way back began quietly smoking a pipe, which Homais in his innermost conscience thought not quite the thing. He also noticed that Monsieur Binet had not been present, and that Tuvache had “made off” after mass, and that Theodore, the notary’s servant wore a blue coat, “as if one could not have got a black coat, since that is the custom, by Jove!” And to share his observations with others he went from group to group. They were deploring Emma’s death, especially Lheureux, who had not failed to come to the funeral.","sentences":[{"en":"Old Rouault on his way back began quietly smoking a pipe, which Homais in his innermost conscience thought not quite the thing.","zh":"出殡回来，卢欧老爹像无事人一样，吸着烟斗；郝麦看在眼里，心下觉得很不应该。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He also noticed that Monsieur Binet had not been present, and that Tuvache had “made off” after mass, and that Theodore, the notary’s servant wore a blue coat, “as if one could not have got a black coat, since that is the custom, by Jove!”","zh":"他还注意到毕耐没有露面，杜法赦听完弥撒，就“溜之大吉”，公证人的听差泰奥多尔穿一件蓝燕尾服，“倒像找不到一件青燕尾服，话说回来，这是风俗！”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And to share his observations with others he went from group to group.","zh":"他从这一群人走到另一群人，说起他的观察心得。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They were deploring Emma’s death, especially Lheureux, who had not failed to come to the funeral.","zh":"大家谈到爱玛，同声惋惜，特别是勒乐。他自然也送殡来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Poor little woman! What a trouble for her husband!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Poor little woman!","zh":"“可怜的少奶奶！她丈夫要多难过！”","scope":"group"},{"en":"What a trouble for her husband!”","zh":"“可怜的少奶奶！她丈夫要多难过！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The druggist continued, “Do you know that but for me he would have committed some fatal attempt upon himself?”","sentences":[{"en":"The druggist continued, “Do you know that but for me he would have committed some fatal attempt upon himself?”","zh":"药剂师接下去道：“不是我，您知道，他会结果自己性命的！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Such a good woman! To think that I saw her only last Saturday in my shop.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Such a good woman!","zh":"“那样善良的一位太太！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"To think that I saw her only last Saturday in my shop.”","zh":"星期六，我还在我的铺子见到她，您说说看！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I haven’t had leisure,” said Homais, “to prepare a few words that I would have cast upon her tomb.”","sentences":[{"en":"“I haven’t had leisure,” said Homais, “to prepare a few words that I would have cast upon her tomb.”","zh":"郝麦道：“我没有时间，不然的话，我会准备几句话，到她坟上演说的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles on getting home undressed, and old Rouault put on his blue blouse. It was a new one, and as he had often during the journey wiped his eyes on the sleeves, the dye had stained his face, and the traces of tears made lines in the layer of dust that covered it.","sentences":[{"en":"Charles on getting home undressed, and old Rouault put on his blue blouse.","zh":"查理回到家，脱掉衣服。卢欧老爹换上他的蓝工人服。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a new one, and as he had often during the journey wiped his eyes on the sleeves, the dye had stained his face, and the traces of tears made lines in the layer of dust that covered it.","zh":"这是新做的，他一路常拿袖子擦眼睛，脸上也有了颜色。一脸的土，眼泪流过，留下一道一道印子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Madame Bovary senior was with them. All three were silent. At last the old fellow sighed—","sentences":[{"en":"Madame Bovary senior was with them.","zh":"包法利老太太和他们在一起。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All three were silent.","zh":"三个人全不言语。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last the old fellow sighed—","zh":"老头子最后叹息道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Do you remember, my friend, that I went to Tostes once when you had just lost your first deceased? I consoled you at that time. I thought of something to say then, but now—” Then, with a loud groan that shook his whole chest, “Ah! this is the end for me, do you see! I saw my wife go, then my son, and now to-day it’s my daughter.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Do you remember, my friend, that I went to Tostes once when you had just lost your first deceased?","zh":"“您记不记得，我的朋友，我有一回到道特，正赶上您丢掉您头一位太太。当时我直安慰您！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I consoled you at that time.","zh":"我有话讲；可是现在…”","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I thought of something to say then, but now—” Then, with a loud groan that shook his whole chest, “Ah! this is the end for me, do you see!","zh":"接着就膨起胸脯，长叹了一声：“啊！您明白，这下子我完啦，我看见我女人死…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I saw my wife go, then my son, and now to-day it’s my daughter.”","zh":"后来是我儿子…今天，又是我女儿！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He wanted to go back at once to Bertaux, saying that he could not sleep in this house. He even refused to see his granddaughter.","sentences":[{"en":"He wanted to go back at once to Bertaux, saying that he could not sleep in this house.","zh":"他决计马上就回拜尔托，说他在这房子睡不着觉。他甚至拒绝看一眼他的外孙女。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He even refused to see his granddaughter.","zh":"他决计马上就回拜尔托，说他在这房子睡不着觉。他甚至拒绝看一眼他的外孙女。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“No, no! It would grieve me too much. Only you’ll kiss her many times for me. Good-bye! you’re a good fellow! And then I shall never forget that,” he said, slapping his thigh. “Never fear, you shall always have your turkey.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, no! It would grieve me too much.","zh":"“不！不！我受不了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Only you’ll kiss her many times for me.","zh":"您替我好好吻吻她！再会！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Good-bye! you’re a good fellow!","zh":"您是个好孩子！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And then I shall never forget that,” he said, slapping his thigh.","zh":"再说，我永远不会忘记这个…”他打着自己的屁股道：","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"“Never fear, you shall always have your turkey.”","zh":"“别担心！总有你的火鸡的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But when he reached the top of the hill he turned back, as he had turned once before on the road of Saint-Victor when he had parted from her. The windows of the village were all on fire beneath the slanting rays of the sun sinking behind the field. He put his hand over his eyes, and saw in the horizon an enclosure of walls, where trees here and there formed black clusters between white stones; then he went on his way at a gentle trot, for his nag had gone lame.","sentences":[{"en":"But when he reached the top of the hill he turned back, as he had turned once before on the road of Saint-Victor when he had parted from her.","zh":"但是他走到岭上，却又转回身子，如同从前在圣维克托小路和她分手，转回身子一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The windows of the village were all on fire beneath the slanting rays of the sun sinking behind the field.","zh":"太阳落在草原，光线斜射过来，村庄的窗户仿佛着了火似的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He put his hand over his eyes, and saw in the horizon an enclosure of walls, where trees here and there formed black clusters between white stones; then he went on his way at a gentle trot, for his nag had gone lame.","zh":"他拿手放在眼前，望见天边有一圈墙，里面的树木，左一堆，右一堆，夹在白石头当中，活像一束一束黑花。他继续行路，缓缓走去，因为他的小马跛了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Despite their fatigue, Charles and his mother stayed very long that evening talking together. They spoke of the days of the past and of the future. She would come to live at Yonville; she would keep house for him; they would never part again. She was ingenious and caressing, rejoicing in her heart at gaining once more an affection that had wandered from her for so many years. Midnight struck. The village as usual was silent, and Charles, awake, thought always of her.","sentences":[{"en":"Despite their fatigue, Charles and his mother stayed very long that evening talking together.","zh":"查理和母亲虽然劳累，黄昏守在一起，仍然谈了许久。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They spoke of the days of the past and of the future.","zh":"他们说起先前的日子和将来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She would come to live at Yonville; she would keep house for him; they would never part again.","zh":"她打算搬到永镇住，料理家务，母子不再离开。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She was ingenious and caressing, rejoicing in her heart at gaining once more an affection that had wandered from her for so many years.","zh":"她机敏而且体贴，儿子的感情，多少年来，溜出她的手心，如今回到身边，自然心中暗喜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Midnight struck.","zh":"半夜了，村镇和往常一样，静静悄悄，只有钟响。查理醒过来，总在想她。","scope":"group"},{"en":"The village as usual was silent, and Charles, awake, thought always of her.","zh":"半夜了，村镇和往常一样，静静悄悄，只有钟响。查理醒过来，总在想她。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe, who, to distract himself, had been rambling about the wood all day, was sleeping quietly in his château, and Léon, down yonder, always slept.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe, who, to distract himself, had been rambling about the wood all day, was sleeping quietly in his château, and Léon, down yonder, always slept.","zh":"罗道耳弗整天在树林打猎消遣，安安逸逸，睡在他的庄园；赖昂在那边，也睡着了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"There was another who at that hour was not asleep.","sentences":[{"en":"There was another who at that hour was not asleep.","zh":"这时候有一个人却没有睡。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"On the grave between the pine-trees a child was on his knees weeping, and his heart, rent by sobs, was beating in the shadow beneath the load of an immense regret, sweeter than the moon and fathomless as the night. The gate suddenly grated. It was Lestiboudois; he came to fetch his spade, that he had forgotten. He recognised Justin climbing over the wall, and at last knew who was the culprit who stole his potatoes.","sentences":[{"en":"On the grave between the pine-trees a child was on his knees weeping, and his heart, rent by sobs, was beating in the shadow beneath the load of an immense regret, sweeter than the moon and fathomless as the night.","zh":"松树中间，有一个男孩子，跪在坟头哭泣，他在黑地里，胸脯一起一伏，抽抽搭搭，上气不接下气，难过得什么似的，比月光还柔，比夜色还深。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The gate suddenly grated.","zh":"栅栏门忽然嘎吱一响。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Lestiboudois; he came to fetch his spade, that he had forgotten.","zh":"赖斯地布杜瓦方才忘记带走他的铁铲，现在寻找来了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He recognised Justin climbing over the wall, and at last knew who was the culprit who stole his potatoes.","zh":"他认出是朱斯丹爬墙：偷他的马铃薯的罪犯，总算有了下落。","scope":"sentence"}]}]},{"id":"3-11","part":3,"n":11,"title":"Part III · Chapter 11","titleZh":"下卷 · 11","paragraphs":[{"en":"The next day Charles had the child brought back. She asked for her mamma. They told her she was away; that she would bring her back some playthings. Berthe spoke of her again several times, then at last thought no more of her. The child’s gaiety broke Bovary’s heart, and he had to bear besides the intolerable consolations of the chemist.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day Charles had the child brought back.","zh":"查理第二天接回小孩子。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She asked for her mamma.","zh":"她要妈妈。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"They told her she was away; that she would bring her back some playthings.","zh":"大家回答她：妈妈出门了，会带玩具给她的。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Berthe spoke of her again several times, then at last thought no more of her.","zh":"白尔特问起好几次，不过时间一久，也就不往这上头想了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The child’s gaiety broke Bovary’s heart, and he had to bear besides the intolerable consolations of the chemist.","zh":"包法利看见孩子快活，反而伤心，还有药剂师的慰唁，听了心烦，却又非听不可。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Money troubles soon began again, Monsieur Lheureux urging on anew his friend Vincart, and Charles pledged himself for exorbitant sums; for he would never consent to let the smallest of the things that had belonged to HER be sold. His mother was exasperated with him; he grew even more angry than she did. He had altogether changed. She left the house.","sentences":[{"en":"Money troubles soon began again, Monsieur Lheureux urging on anew his friend Vincart, and Charles pledged himself for exorbitant sums; for he would never consent to let the smallest of the things that had belonged to HER be sold.","zh":"银钱事务不久又开始了，勒乐先生又唆使朋友万萨出面；查理认可惊人的数字，因为属于她的家具，再小他也不答应变卖。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"His mother was exasperated with him; he grew even more angry than she did.","zh":"母亲气得不得了。他比她的气性还大。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He had altogether changed.","zh":"他完全变了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She left the house.","zh":"她丢下他走了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then everyone began “taking advantage” of him. Mademoiselle Lempereur presented a bill for six months’ teaching, although Emma had never taken a lesson (despite the receipted bill she had shown Bovary); it was an arrangement between the two women. The man at the circulating library demanded three years’ subscriptions; Mere Rollet claimed the postage due for some twenty letters, and when Charles asked for an explanation, she had the delicacy to reply—","sentences":[{"en":"Then everyone began “taking advantage” of him.","zh":"于是人人来找便宜。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Mademoiselle Lempereur presented a bill for six months’ teaching, although Emma had never taken a lesson (despite the receipted bill she had shown Bovary); it was an arrangement between the two women.","zh":"朗玻乐小姐索讨半年学费，虽然爱玛一次钢琴课也没有上过（别瞧她拿出那张收据给包法利看：原来是她们两个人串通好的）。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The man at the circulating library demanded three years’ subscriptions; Mere Rollet claimed the postage due for some twenty letters, and when Charles asked for an explanation, she had the delicacy to reply—","zh":"租书处索讨三年租费。罗莱嫂子索讨二十来封信的寄费；查理问她细情，她不漏一丝口风：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, I don’t know. It was for her business affairs.”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, I don’t know.","zh":"“啊！我知道什么呀！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was for her business affairs.”","zh":"反正是她寄的。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"With every debt he paid Charles thought he had come to the end of them. But others followed ceaselessly. He sent in accounts for professional attendance. He was shown the letters his wife had written. Then he had to apologise.","sentences":[{"en":"With every debt he paid Charles thought he had come to the end of them.","zh":"查理每付一次账，总以为这是最后一次。但是一次又一次，没完没了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"But others followed ceaselessly.","zh":"查理每付一次账，总以为这是最后一次。但是一次又一次，没完没了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He sent in accounts for professional attendance.","zh":"他讨取拖延未付的诊费，人家拿他太太的信给他看，他只好连声道歉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He was shown the letters his wife had written.","zh":"他讨取拖延未付的诊费，人家拿他太太的信给他看，他只好连声道歉。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he had to apologise.","zh":"他讨取拖延未付的诊费，人家拿他太太的信给他看，他只好连声道歉。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Félicité now wore Madame Bovary’s gowns; not all, for he had kept some of them, and he went to look at them in her dressing-room, locking himself up there; she was about her height, and often Charles, seeing her from behind, was seized with an illusion, and cried out—","sentences":[{"en":"Félicité now wore Madame Bovary’s gowns; not all, for he had kept some of them, and he went to look at them in her dressing-room, locking himself up there; she was about her height, and often Charles, seeing her from behind, was seized with an illusion, and cried out—","zh":"全福如今穿太太的衣服，不是全穿，因为他留下几件，放在她的梳洗间，他进去观看，就把自己锁在里头。全福差不多和她一样高矮，查理望见她的背影，常常产生幻觉，喊道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Oh, stay, stay!”","sentences":[{"en":"“Oh, stay, stay!”","zh":"“喂！别走！别走！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But at Whitsuntide she ran away from Yonville, carried off by Theodore, stealing all that was left of the wardrobe.","sentences":[{"en":"But at Whitsuntide she ran away from Yonville, carried off by Theodore, stealing all that was left of the wardrobe.","zh":"可是泰奥多尔在圣灵降临节把她拐跑了。她离开永镇，偷去留在衣橱的全部东西。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"It was about this time that the widow Dupuis had the honour to inform him of the “marriage of Monsieur Léon Dupuis her son, notary at Yvetot, to Mademoiselle Leocadie Leboeuf of Bondeville.” Charles, among the other congratulations he sent him, wrote this sentence—","sentences":[{"en":"It was about this time that the widow Dupuis had the honour to inform him of the “marriage of Monsieur Léon Dupuis her son, notary at Yvetot, to Mademoiselle Leocadie Leboeuf of Bondeville.”","zh":"就在同一时期，寡妇迪皮伊夫人送了一份喜帖给他，宣布“她的儿子、伊弗托的公证人，赖昂·迪皮伊先生，和崩德镇的莱奥卡狄·勒伯夫小姐举行婚礼”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles, among the other congratulations he sent him, wrote this sentence—","zh":"查理给他写信道喜，并说：“我可怜的太太在世的话，听到您的喜讯，该多快乐呀！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“How glad my poor wife would have been!”","sentences":[{"en":"“How glad my poor wife would have been!”","zh":"查理给他写信道喜，并说：“我可怜的太太在世的话，听到您的喜讯，该多快乐呀！”","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"One day when, wandering aimlessly about the house, he had gone up to the attic, he felt a pellet of fine paper under his slipper. He opened it and read: “Courage, Emma, courage. I would not bring misery into your life.” It was Rodolphe’s letter, fallen to the ground between the boxes, where it had remained, and that the wind from the dormer window had just blown towards the door. And Charles stood, motionless and staring, in the very same place where, long ago, Emma, in despair, and paler even than he, had thought of dying. At last he discovered a small R at the bottom of the second page. What did this mean? He remembered Rodolphe’s attentions, his sudden, disappearance, his constrained air when they had met two or three times since. But the respectful tone of the letter deceived him.","sentences":[{"en":"One day when, wandering aimlessly about the house, he had gone up to the attic, he felt a pellet of fine paper under his slipper.","zh":"有一天，他在家里漫步闲走，上到阁楼，觉得鞋底踩到一个小纸球。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He opened it and read: “Courage, Emma, courage.","zh":"他打开读道：“拿出勇气来，爱玛！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"I would not bring misery into your life.”","zh":"拿出勇气来！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was Rodolphe’s letter, fallen to the ground between the boxes, where it had remained, and that the wind from the dormer window had just blown towards the door.","zh":"我不希望害您一辈子。”原来是罗道耳弗的信，掉在木箱夹缝，一直待在地上，天窗的风新近又把它吹到门口。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And Charles stood, motionless and staring, in the very same place where, long ago, Emma, in despair, and paler even than he, had thought of dying.","zh":"查理张大了嘴，一动不动，站在从前爱玛站的地方，当时她万念俱灰，直想寻死，脸色比他现在的脸色还要惨白。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last he discovered a small R at the bottom of the second page.","zh":"最后他在第二页底下看到一个小小的罗字。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What did this mean?","zh":"这是什么意思？","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He remembered Rodolphe’s attentions, his sudden, disappearance, his constrained air when they had met two or three times since.","zh":"他想起罗道耳弗的殷勤、他的忽然消失和以后有两三次遇到时，他的杌陧神情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But the respectful tone of the letter deceived him.","zh":"不过书信的尊敬口气引他往好处想。他自言自语道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Perhaps they loved one another platonically,” he said to himself.","sentences":[{"en":"“Perhaps they loved one another platonically,” he said to himself.","zh":"“他们也许是闹精神恋爱。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Besides, Charles was not of those who go to the bottom of things; he shrank from the proofs, and his vague jealousy was lost in the immensity of his woe.","sentences":[{"en":"Besides, Charles was not of those who go to the bottom of things; he shrank from the proofs, and his vague jealousy was lost in the immensity of his woe.","zh":"再说，查理不是那种追根究底的人；他看见证据，反而退缩。他的忌妒若有若无，比起他的巨大痛苦来，也就微不足道了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Everyone, he thought, must have adored her; all men assuredly must have coveted her. She seemed but the more beautiful to him for this; he was seized with a lasting, furious desire for her, that inflamed his despair, and that was boundless, because it was now unrealisable.","sentences":[{"en":"Everyone, he thought, must have adored her; all men assuredly must have coveted her.","zh":"在他看来，男人不膜拜她，就不可能。个个男子，毫无疑问，都想要她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She seemed but the more beautiful to him for this; he was seized with a lasting, furious desire for her, that inflamed his despair, and that was boundless, because it was now unrealisable.","zh":"他这样一想，越发觉得她美。他对她起了一种持久、疯狂的欲望。欲望无边无涯，加强他的绝望，因为现在失去了一切实现的可能。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"To please her, as if she were still living, he adopted her predilections, her ideas; he bought patent leather boots and took to wearing white cravats. He put cosmetics on his moustache, and, like her, signed notes of hand. She corrupted him from beyond the grave.","sentences":[{"en":"To please her, as if she were still living, he adopted her predilections, her ideas; he bought patent leather boots and took to wearing white cravats.","zh":"好像她还活着一样，他讨她的欢心，迁就她的喜好、她的见解；他买了一双漆皮鞋，系白领带，髭上洒香水，学她签发票。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He put cosmetics on his moustache, and, like her, signed notes of hand.","zh":"好像她还活着一样，他讨她的欢心，迁就她的喜好、她的见解；他买了一双漆皮鞋，系白领带，髭上洒香水，学她签发票。","scope":"group"},{"en":"She corrupted him from beyond the grave.","zh":"想不到她死了以后还败坏他。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He was obliged to sell his silver piece by piece; next he sold the drawing-room furniture. All the rooms were stripped; but the bedroom, her own room, remained as before. After his dinner Charles went up there. He pushed the round table in front of the fire, and drew up her armchair. He sat down opposite it. A candle burnt in one of the gilt candlesticks. Berthe by his side was painting prints.","sentences":[{"en":"He was obliged to sell his silver piece by piece; next he sold the drawing-room furniture.","zh":"他迫不得已，一件一件卖掉银器，接着又卖掉客厅的家具。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All the rooms were stripped; but the bedroom, her own room, remained as before.","zh":"间间屋子成了空的，只有卧室、她的房间，丝毫不动，还和先前一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"After his dinner Charles went up there.","zh":"间间屋子成了空的，只有卧室、她的房间，丝毫不动，还和先前一样。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He pushed the round table in front of the fire, and drew up her armchair.","zh":"查理用过晚饭，来到卧室，把圆桌推到壁炉前面，拉近她的扶手椅。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sat down opposite it.","zh":"他坐在对面。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A candle burnt in one of the gilt candlesticks.","zh":"有一支镀金蜡烛台点着蜡烛。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Berthe by his side was painting prints.","zh":"白尔特在他旁边，往画上涂颜色。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He suffered, poor man, at seeing her so badly dressed, with laceless boots, and the arm-holes of her pinafore torn down to the hips; for the charwoman took no care of her. But she was so sweet, so pretty, and her little head bent forward so gracefully, letting the dear fair hair fall over her rosy cheeks, that an infinite joy came upon him, a happiness mingled with bitterness, like those ill-made wines that taste of resin. He mended her toys, made her puppets from cardboard, or sewed up half-torn dolls. Then, if his eyes fell upon the workbox, a ribbon lying about, or even a pin left in a crack of the table, he began to dream, and looked so sad that she became as sad as he.","sentences":[{"en":"He suffered, poor man, at seeing her so badly dressed, with laceless boots, and the arm-holes of her pinafore torn down to the hips; for the charwoman took no care of her.","zh":"可怜人见她穿得那样破烂，好生难过。靴子没有靴带，罩衫从肩膀底下一直撕到屁股，因为女用人根本就不管她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But she was so sweet, so pretty, and her little head bent forward so gracefully, letting the dear fair hair fall over her rosy cheeks, that an infinite joy came upon him, a happiness mingled with bitterness, like those ill-made wines that taste of resin.","zh":"但是她长得又温柔，又可爱，小脑袋朝前一歪，温文尔雅，美丽的金黄头发搭在她的粉红脸蛋上，他感到无限喜悦，好像酒酿坏了，有松香气味一样，欢乐掺有悲伤。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He mended her toys, made her puppets from cardboard, or sewed up half-torn dolls.","zh":"他帮她修理玩具，用硬纸板剪小人，缝补囡囡的破肚皮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then, if his eyes fell upon the workbox, a ribbon lying about, or even a pin left in a crack of the table, he began to dream, and looked so sad that she became as sad as he.","zh":"他要是见到女红盒、一条拖在外头的缎带，或者甚至一根落在桌缝的针的话，他都会沉入遐想，模样非常忧郁，连她也变得像他一样忧郁。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"No one now came to see them, for Justin had run away to Rouen, where he was a grocer’s assistant, and the druggist’s children saw less and less of the child, Monsieur Homais not caring, seeing the difference of their social position, to continue the intimacy.","sentences":[{"en":"No one now came to see them, for Justin had run away to Rouen, where he was a grocer’s assistant, and the druggist’s children saw less and less of the child, Monsieur Homais not caring, seeing the difference of their social position, to continue the intimacy.","zh":"如今没有人看望他们了。因为朱斯丹逃到鲁昂，进杂货铺当伙计；药剂师的孩子越来越不理小姑娘，郝麦先生也不在乎友谊长存，他们的社会地位不一样了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The blind man, whom he had not been able to cure with the pomade, had gone back to the hill of Bois-Guillaume, where he told the travellers of the vain attempt of the druggist, to such an extent, that Homais when he went to town hid himself behind the curtains of the “Hirondelle” to avoid meeting him. He detested him, and wishing, in the interests of his own reputation, to get rid of him at all costs, he directed against him a secret battery, that betrayed the depth of his intellect and the baseness of his vanity. Thus, for six consecutive months, one could read in the “Fanal de Rouen” editorials such as these—","sentences":[{"en":"The blind man, whom he had not been able to cure with the pomade, had gone back to the hill of Bois-Guillaume, where he told the travellers of the vain attempt of the druggist, to such an extent, that Homais when he went to town hid himself behind the curtains of the “Hirondelle” to avoid meeting him.","zh":"他的消炎膏没能医好瞎子。瞎子回到纪尧姆树林岭，对旅客讲药剂师徒劳无功，讲到后来，郝麦进城，躲在燕子的窗帘后头，不敢见他。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He detested him, and wishing, in the interests of his own reputation, to get rid of him at all costs, he directed against him a secret battery, that betrayed the depth of his intellect and the baseness of his vanity.","zh":"他恨透了他；名誉攸关，他千方百计除他，还安装了一座隐蔽的炮位打他：显出他不但足智多谋，而且用心险恶。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Thus, for six consecutive months, one could read in the “Fanal de Rouen” editorials such as these—","zh":"一连六个月，人们在《鲁昂烽火》可以读到这样措词的短论：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“All who bend their steps towards the fertile plains of Picardy have, no doubt, remarked, by the Bois-Guillaume hill, a wretch suffering from a horrible facial wound. He importunes, persecutes one, and levies a regular tax on all travellers. Are we still living in the monstrous times of the Middle Ages, when vagabonds were permitted to display in our public places leprosy and scrofulas they had brought back from the Crusades?”","sentences":[{"en":"“All who bend their steps towards the fertile plains of Picardy have, no doubt, remarked, by the Bois-Guillaume hill, a wretch suffering from a horrible facial wound.","zh":"每一个去庇卡底肥土沃野的人，一定会在纪尧姆树林岭上，看见一个乞丐，脸上长着可怕的烂疮。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He importunes, persecutes one, and levies a regular tax on all travellers.","zh":"他纠缠你，迫害你，简直等于征收旅客一次路捐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Are we still living in the monstrous times of the Middle Ages, when vagabonds were permitted to display in our public places leprosy and scrofulas they had brought back from the Crusades?”","zh":"难道如今还是中世纪野蛮时代，流浪人参加十字军远征，带回来的癞疮和瘰疬，我们也允许公开展览？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Or—","sentences":[{"en":"Or—","zh":"要不然就是：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“In spite of the laws against vagabondage, the approaches to our great towns continue to be infected by bands of beggars. Some are seen going about alone, and these are not, perhaps, the least dangerous. What are our ediles about?”","sentences":[{"en":"“In spite of the laws against vagabondage, the approaches to our great towns continue to be infected by bands of beggars.","zh":"法律禁止流浪，可是我们的大城市近郊，依然布满成群结队的乞丐。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Some are seen going about alone, and these are not, perhaps, the least dangerous.","zh":"人们还见到踽踽独行的乞丐，他们未见得就不危险。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"What are our ediles about?”","zh":"我们的市府官长在想什么？","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Homais invented anecdotes—","sentences":[{"en":"Then Homais invented anecdotes—","zh":"郝麦还捏造了一些耸人听闻的故事：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Yesterday, by the Bois-Guillaume hill, a skittish horse—” And then followed the story of an accident caused by the presence of the blind man.","sentences":[{"en":"“Yesterday, by the Bois-Guillaume hill, a skittish horse—” And then followed the story of an accident caused by the presence of the blind man.","zh":"昨天，一匹受惊的马，在纪尧姆树林岭…接下去就讲遇见瞎子，发生了意外事件。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He managed so well that the fellow was locked up. But he was released. He began again, and Homais began again. It was a struggle. Homais won it, for his foe was condemned to life-long confinement in an asylum.","sentences":[{"en":"He managed so well that the fellow was locked up.","zh":"结果是官府把瞎子抓起来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But he was released.","zh":"可是又把他放了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He began again, and Homais began again.","zh":"他又开始，郝麦也又开始。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a struggle.","zh":"这变成一场角斗。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Homais won it, for his foe was condemned to life-long confinement in an asylum.","zh":"郝麦胜利了；因为他的仇敌被关进一家收容所，受到终身禁闭的处分。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"This success emboldened him, and henceforth there was no longer a dog run over, a barn burnt down, a woman beaten in the parish, of which he did not immediately inform the public, guided always by the love of progress and the hate of priests. He instituted comparisons between the elementary and clerical schools to the detriment of the latter; called to mind the massacre of St. Bartholomew a propos of a grant of one hundred francs to the church, and denounced abuses, aired new views. That was his phrase. Homais was digging and delving; he was becoming dangerous.","sentences":[{"en":"This success emboldened him, and henceforth there was no longer a dog run over, a barn burnt down, a woman beaten in the parish, of which he did not immediately inform the public, guided always by the love of progress and the hate of priests.","zh":"成功增加胆量。从这时候起，县里压死一条狗，烧掉一座谷仓，殴打一个女人，他一知道，就永远根据拥护进步和憎恨教士的原则，立刻公之于众。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He instituted comparisons between the elementary and clerical schools to the detriment of the latter; called to mind the massacre of St. Bartholomew a propos of a grant of one hundred francs to the church, and denounced abuses, aired new views.","zh":"他比较公立小学和教会小学，指摘后者。他看见补贴教堂一百法郎，气愤不过，提起圣巴托罗缪惨案。他揭发弊端，散布警句：这是他自己的说法。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"That was his phrase.","zh":"郝麦做的是破坏工作；他变成危险分子了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Homais was digging and delving; he was becoming dangerous.","zh":"郝麦做的是破坏工作；他变成危险分子了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"However, he was stifling in the narrow limits of journalism, and soon a book, a work was necessary to him. Then he composed “General Statistics of the Canton of Yonville, followed by Climatological Remarks.” The statistics drove him to philosophy. He busied himself with great questions: the social problem, moralisation of the poorer classes, pisciculture, caoutchouc, railways, etc. He even began to blush at being a bourgeois. He affected the artistic style, he smoked. He bought two chic Pompadour statuettes to adorn his drawing-room.","sentences":[{"en":"However, he was stifling in the narrow limits of journalism, and soon a book, a work was necessary to him.","zh":"但是新闻天地太小，不足以发挥他的大才，他需要来一部书、一部著作！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then he composed “General Statistics of the Canton of Yonville, followed by Climatological Remarks.”","zh":"于是他编了一部《永镇统计一览，附风土调查》。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The statistics drove him to philosophy.","zh":"统计学把他引向哲学。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He busied himself with great questions: the social problem, moralisation of the poorer classes, pisciculture, caoutchouc, railways, etc. He even began to blush at being a bourgeois.","zh":"他关心重大问题，例如社会问题、下层阶级的教化、养鱼法、树胶、铁路等等。他羞于做一个资产者。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He affected the artistic style, he smoked.","zh":"他摆出艺术家风度，吸起烟来了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He bought two chic Pompadour statuettes to adorn his drawing-room.","zh":"他买了两尊彭巴杜尔风格的时髦小雕像，装潢他的客厅。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He by no means gave up his shop. On the contrary, he kept well abreast of new discoveries. He followed the great movement of chocolates; he was the first to introduce “cocoa” and “revalenta” into the Seine-Inferieure. He was enthusiastic about the hydro-electric Pulvermacher chains; he wore one himself, and when at night he took off his flannel vest, Madame Homais stood quite dazzled before the golden spiral beneath which he was hidden, and felt her ardour redouble for this man more bandaged than a Scythian, and splendid as one of the Magi.","sentences":[{"en":"He by no means gave up his shop.","zh":"他不放弃药房；正相反！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"On the contrary, he kept well abreast of new discoveries.","zh":"他晓得最新发明。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He followed the great movement of chocolates; he was the first to introduce “cocoa” and “revalenta” into the Seine-Inferieure.","zh":"他注意提倡巧克力的大运动。他头一个把可可和补力多介绍到塞纳河下游州。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was enthusiastic about the hydro-electric Pulvermacher chains; he wore one himself, and when at night he took off his flannel vest, Madame Homais stood quite dazzled before the golden spiral beneath which he was hidden, and felt her ardour redouble for this man more bandaged than a Scythian, and splendid as one of the Magi.","zh":"他热烈鼓吹普韦马舍的水电链 ，自己就戴一条；晚上他脱法兰绒背心，露出金螺旋线，裹得又密又严，赛过斯基泰人 ，严实得连人都没影了。见他金碧辉煌，如同东方王爷 ，郝麦太太不禁目瞪口呆，觉得自己加倍崇拜他了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He had fine ideas about Emma’s tomb. First he proposed a broken column with some drapery, next a pyramid, then a Temple of Vesta, a sort of rotunda, or else a “mass of ruins.” And in all his plans Homais always stuck to the weeping willow, which he looked upon as the indispensable symbol of sorrow.","sentences":[{"en":"He had fine ideas about Emma’s tomb.","zh":"他对爱玛的墓碑有奇妙的见解。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"First he proposed a broken column with some drapery, next a pyramid, then a Temple of Vesta, a sort of rotunda, or else a “mass of ruins.”","zh":"他最先建议，立一根半截石柱，外加帷幔；后来又建议，立一座金字塔；再后又主张建成圆亭式样的火神庙…要不就是“一堆断垣残壁”。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"And in all his plans Homais always stuck to the weeping willow, which he looked upon as the indispensable symbol of sorrow.","zh":"他把垂柳看成忧郁的独一无二的标志 ，所以计划尽管改来改去，但是关于垂柳这一点，他决不让步。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Charles and he made a journey to Rouen together to look at some tombs at a funeral furnisher’s, accompanied by an artist, one Vaufrylard, a friend of Bridoux’s, who made puns all the time. At last, after having examined some hundred designs, having ordered an estimate and made another journey to Rouen, Charles decided in favour of a mausoleum, which on the two principal sides was to have a “spirit bearing an extinguished torch.”","sentences":[{"en":"Charles and he made a journey to Rouen together to look at some tombs at a funeral furnisher’s, accompanied by an artist, one Vaufrylard, a friend of Bridoux’s, who made puns all the time.","zh":"查理和他一同到鲁昂一家石厂，挑选墓碑——还有一位画家做伴。他是布里杜的朋友，姓沃弗里拉，一路净说双关语。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last, after having examined some hundred designs, having ordered an estimate and made another journey to Rouen, Charles decided in favour of a mausoleum, which on the two principal sides was to have a “spirit bearing an extinguished torch.”","zh":"查理看了一百多种图样，又估计了一番价钱，最后，二次去鲁昂，决计采用皇陵式样，主要两面全雕了“一位司命神，拿着一根灭了的火把”。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As to the inscription, Homais could think of nothing so fine as Sta viator, and he got no further; he racked his brain, he constantly repeated Sta viator. At last he hit upon Amabilen conjugem calcas, which was adopted.","sentences":[{"en":"As to the inscription, Homais could think of nothing so fine as Sta viator, and he got no further; he racked his brain, he constantly repeated Sta viator.","zh":"至于碑铭，郝麦觉得就数“行人止步”漂亮；他想不出下文，搜索枯肠，不断重复“行人止步”…","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"At last he hit upon Amabilen conjugem calcas, which was adopted.","zh":"最后忽然想到“勿践贤妻” ，查理采用了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"A strange thing was that Bovary, while continually thinking of Emma, was forgetting her. He grew desperate as he felt this image fading from his memory in spite of all efforts to retain it. Yet every night he dreamt of her; it was always the same dream. He drew near her, but when he was about to clasp her she fell into decay in his arms.","sentences":[{"en":"A strange thing was that Bovary, while continually thinking of Emma, was forgetting her.","zh":"奇怪的是，包法利一边不停地想念爱玛，一边却在忘记她。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He grew desperate as he felt this image fading from his memory in spite of all efforts to retain it.","zh":"他想尽方法来保留她的形象，可是他觉得这形象照样溜出了他的记忆。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Yet every night he dreamt of her; it was always the same dream.","zh":"他为这事直恨自己。其实他夜夜梦到她；梦也永远一样：他走到她跟前，然而就在搂抱的时候，她在他的胳膊中间变成了尘土。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He drew near her, but when he was about to clasp her she fell into decay in his arms.","zh":"他为这事直恨自己。其实他夜夜梦到她；梦也永远一样：他走到她跟前，然而就在搂抱的时候，她在他的胳膊中间变成了尘土。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"For a week he was seen going to church in the evening. Monsieur Bournisien even paid him two or three visits, then gave him up. Moreover, the old fellow was growing intolerant, fanatic, said Homais. He thundered against the spirit of the age, and never failed, every other week, in his sermon, to recount the death agony of Voltaire, who died devouring his excrements, as everyone knows.","sentences":[{"en":"For a week he was seen going to church in the evening.","zh":"大家看见他天天黄昏去教堂，去了一星期不去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Monsieur Bournisien even paid him two or three visits, then gave him up.","zh":"布尔尼贤先生甚至看望过他两三回，后来也就随他去了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Moreover, the old fellow was growing intolerant, fanatic, said Homais.","zh":"而且郝麦说，老堂长心地越来越褊狭，越疯狂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He thundered against the spirit of the age, and never failed, every other week, in his sermon, to recount the death agony of Voltaire, who died devouring his excrements, as everyone knows.","zh":"他大骂时代精神，每半个月，临到讲道，必定提起伏尔泰临死的情形，大家知道，他是吞自己的粪死的。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In spite of the economy with which Bovary lived, he was far from being able to pay off his old debts. Lheureux refused to renew any more bills. A distraint became imminent. Then he appealed to his mother, who consented to let him take a mortgage on her property, but with a great many recriminations against Emma; and in return for her sacrifice she asked for a shawl that had escaped the depredations of Félicité. Charles refused to give it her; they quarrelled.","sentences":[{"en":"In spite of the economy with which Bovary lived, he was far from being able to pay off his old debts.","zh":"包法利虽然省吃俭用，离还清旧债，却还远得很。勒乐拒绝改期。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Lheureux refused to renew any more bills.","zh":"扣押就在眼前了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A distraint became imminent.","zh":"事到如今，他只好写信给母亲求救。母亲答应拿她的财产作抵押，不过信上狠狠数落了爱玛一顿；她要一条全福没有偷去的披肩，酬谢她的牺牲。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Then he appealed to his mother, who consented to let him take a mortgage on her property, but with a great many recriminations against Emma; and in return for her sacrifice she asked for a shawl that had escaped the depredations of Félicité.","zh":"事到如今，他只好写信给母亲求救。母亲答应拿她的财产作抵押，不过信上狠狠数落了爱玛一顿；她要一条全福没有偷去的披肩，酬谢她的牺牲。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Charles refused to give it her; they quarrelled.","zh":"查理不肯给她。他们失和了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"She made the first overtures of reconciliation by offering to have the little girl, who could help her in the house, to live with her. Charles consented to this, but when the time for parting came, all his courage failed him. Then there was a final, complete rupture.","sentences":[{"en":"She made the first overtures of reconciliation by offering to have the little girl, who could help her in the house, to live with her.","zh":"她首先提出和解，向他建议接小女孩过去，陪她做伴。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles consented to this, but when the time for parting came, all his courage failed him.","zh":"查理同意了。但是临到动身，他又舍不得她走。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then there was a final, complete rupture.","zh":"这一回，母子决裂到底，挽救不来了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"As his affections vanished, he clung more closely to the love of his child. She made him anxious, however, for she coughed sometimes, and had red spots on her cheeks.","sentences":[{"en":"As his affections vanished, he clung more closely to the love of his child.","zh":"亲戚关系越淡，他的心也就越集中爱女儿。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She made him anxious, however, for she coughed sometimes, and had red spots on her cheeks.","zh":"偏偏她又让他不放心，因为她有时候咳嗽，脸蛋有红印子。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Opposite his house, flourishing and merry, was the family of the chemist, with whom everything was prospering. Napoleon helped him in the laboratory, Athalie embroidered him a skullcap, Irma cut out rounds of paper to cover the preserves, and Franklin recited Pythagoras’ table in a breath. He was the happiest of fathers, the most fortunate of men.","sentences":[{"en":"Opposite his house, flourishing and merry, was the family of the chemist, with whom everything was prospering.","zh":"对面是药剂师的家庭，又兴旺，又快活，事事如意。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Napoleon helped him in the laboratory, Athalie embroidered him a skullcap, Irma cut out rounds of paper to cover the preserves, and Franklin recited Pythagoras’ table in a breath.","zh":"拿破仑帮他做实验；阿塔莉给他绣了一顶希腊小帽；伊尔玛剪圆纸片，盖蜜饯罐；富兰克林一口气背完九九表。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was the happiest of fathers, the most fortunate of men.","zh":"他是最快乐的父亲，最走运的人。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Not so! A secret ambition devoured him. Homais hankered after the cross of the Legion of Honour. He had plenty of claims to it.","sentences":[{"en":"Not so!","zh":"错啦！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"A secret ambition devoured him.","zh":"有一种野心私下折磨他：郝麦热衷十字勋章。","scope":"group"},{"en":"Homais hankered after the cross of the Legion of Honour.","zh":"有一种野心私下折磨他：郝麦热衷十字勋章。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He had plenty of claims to it.","zh":"他不缺乏资格：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“First, having at the time of the cholera distinguished myself by a boundless devotion; second, by having published, at my expense, various works of public utility, such as” (and he recalled his pamphlet entitled, “Cider, its manufacture and effects,” besides observation on the lanigerous plant-louse, sent to the Academy; his volume of statistics, and down to his pharmaceutical thesis); “without counting that I am a member of several learned societies” (he was member of a single one).","sentences":[{"en":"“First, having at the time of the cholera distinguished myself by a boundless devotion; second, by having published, at my expense, various works of public utility, such as” (and he recalled his pamphlet entitled, “Cider, its manufacture and effects,” besides observation on the lanigerous plant-louse, sent to the Academy; his volume of statistics, and down to his pharmaceutical thesis); “without counting that I am a member of several learned societies” (he was member of a single one).","zh":"第一，霍乱流行时期，曾经奋不顾身，热心服务；第二，自费刊印种种造福公众的著述，例如…（他提起他的报告，题目是《论苹果酒及其酿造与效用》；还有关于密毛木虱的研究，送到法兰西学院；他的《统计》，甚至他当药剂师的考试论文）；何况“我是好几个学会的会员”（他只是一个学会的会员） 。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“In short!” he cried, making a pirouette, “if it were only for distinguishing myself at fires!”","sentences":[{"en":"“In short!” he cried, making a pirouette, “if it were only for distinguishing myself at fires!”","zh":"他打一个转身，喊道：“单说踊跃救火，我也该得！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Then Homais inclined towards the Government. He secretly did the prefect great service during the elections. He sold himself—in a word, prostituted himself. He even addressed a petition to the sovereign in which he implored him to “do him justice”; he called him “our good king,” and compared him to Henri IV.","sentences":[{"en":"Then Homais inclined towards the Government.","zh":"于是郝麦逢迎当局。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He secretly did the prefect great service during the elections.","zh":"州长先生竞选 ，他私下大帮其忙。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He sold himself—in a word, prostituted himself.","zh":"他最后卖身求荣，无所不为。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He even addressed a petition to the sovereign in which he implored him to “do him justice”; he called him “our good king,” and compared him to Henri IV.","zh":"他甚至给国王写了一封请愿书，求他主持公道；他称呼他我的好国王，把他比成亨利四世。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And every morning the druggist rushed for the paper to see if his nomination were in it. It was never there. At last, unable to bear it any longer, he had a grass plot in his garden designed to represent the Star of the Cross of Honour with two little strips of grass running from the top to imitate the ribband. He walked round it with folded arms, meditating on the folly of the Government and the ingratitude of men.","sentences":[{"en":"And every morning the druggist rushed for the paper to see if his nomination were in it.","zh":"每天早晨，药剂师接过报纸，急忙打开，在任命栏寻找他的名字，只是任命老不见下来。他最后等不及了，拿花园草地修成勋章的星形，上头来两个小条，也是草做的，代表缎带。","scope":"group"},{"en":"It was never there.","zh":"每天早晨，药剂师接过报纸，急忙打开，在任命栏寻找他的名字，只是任命老不见下来。他最后等不及了，拿花园草地修成勋章的星形，上头来两个小条，也是草做的，代表缎带。","scope":"group"},{"en":"At last, unable to bear it any longer, he had a grass plot in his garden designed to represent the Star of the Cross of Honour with two little strips of grass running from the top to imitate the ribband.","zh":"每天早晨，药剂师接过报纸，急忙打开，在任命栏寻找他的名字，只是任命老不见下来。他最后等不及了，拿花园草地修成勋章的星形，上头来两个小条，也是草做的，代表缎带。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He walked round it with folded arms, meditating on the folly of the Government and the ingratitude of men.","zh":"他交叉胳膊，围着这块草地散步，默念政府无能，世人负义。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"From respect, or from a sort of sensuality that made him carry on his investigations slowly, Charles had not yet opened the secret drawer of a rosewood desk which Emma had generally used. One day, however, he sat down before it, turned the key, and pressed the spring. All Léon’s letters were there. There could be no doubt this time. He devoured them to the very last, ransacked every corner, all the furniture, all the drawers, behind the walls, sobbing, crying aloud, distraught, mad. He found a box and broke it open with a kick. Rodolphe’s portrait flew full in his face in the midst of the overturned love-letters.","sentences":[{"en":"From respect, or from a sort of sensuality that made him carry on his investigations slowly, Charles had not yet opened the secret drawer of a rosewood desk which Emma had generally used.","zh":"爱玛常用的一张乌木书桌，查理由于尊重起见，或者由于从缓查看的一种快感，从没有打开她本人的抽屉看过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"One day, however, he sat down before it, turned the key, and pressed the spring.","zh":"终于有一天，他坐在书桌前面，转动钥匙，推开锁簧。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"All Léon’s letters were there.","zh":"赖昂的书信全在里头。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There could be no doubt this time.","zh":"这一回，没有疑问了！","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He devoured them to the very last, ransacked every corner, all the furniture, all the drawers, behind the walls, sobbing, crying aloud, distraught, mad.","zh":"他一直看到末一封信，搜索个个角落、件件家具、只只抽屉、张张画后，又是呜咽，又是嗥叫，心烦意乱，如癫如狂。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He found a box and broke it open with a kick.","zh":"他发现一只匣子，一脚踢破。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe’s portrait flew full in his face in the midst of the overturned love-letters.","zh":"情书散了一地，当中有一张罗道耳弗的画像，凝目相望。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"People wondered at his despondency. He never went out, saw no one, refused even to visit his patients. Then they said “he shut himself up to drink.”","sentences":[{"en":"People wondered at his despondency.","zh":"大家奇怪他为什么那样情绪低落。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He never went out, saw no one, refused even to visit his patients.","zh":"他不出门，不见客，甚至拒绝去看他的病人。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Then they said “he shut himself up to drink.”","zh":"大家讲他：“关在家里喝酒。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Sometimes, however, some curious person climbed on to the garden hedge, and saw with amazement this long-bearded, shabbily clothed, wild man, who wept aloud as he walked up and down.","sentences":[{"en":"Sometimes, however, some curious person climbed on to the garden hedge, and saw with amazement this long-bearded, shabbily clothed, wild man, who wept aloud as he walked up and down.","zh":"有时候，好事者耸起身子，从花园篱笆上头往里张望，大吃一惊，就见这位先生，胡须老长，衣服龌龊，容貌狰狞，边走边号啕大哭。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"In the evening in summer he took his little girl with him and led her to the cemetery. They came back at nightfall, when the only light left in the Place was that in Binet’s window.","sentences":[{"en":"In the evening in summer he took his little girl with him and led her to the cemetery.","zh":"夏季黄昏，他带领小女儿，来到公墓，直到黑夜才回，除去毕耐的天窗，广场没有亮光。","scope":"group"},{"en":"They came back at nightfall, when the only light left in the Place was that in Binet’s window.","zh":"夏季黄昏，他带领小女儿，来到公墓，直到黑夜才回，除去毕耐的天窗，广场没有亮光。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"The voluptuousness of his grief was, however, incomplete, for he had no one near him to share it, and he paid visits to Madame Lefrancois to be able to speak of her.","sentences":[{"en":"The voluptuousness of his grief was, however, incomplete, for he had no one near him to share it, and he paid visits to Madame Lefrancois to be able to speak of her.","zh":"不过他的痛苦感受并不完整，因为旁边没有人和他一起分担。他看望勒弗朗索瓦太太，为了能谈谈她。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"But the landlady only listened with half an ear, having troubles like himself. For Lheureux had at last established the “Favorites du Commerce,” and Hivert, who enjoyed a great reputation for doing errands, insisted on a rise of wages, and was threatening to go over “to the opposition shop.”","sentences":[{"en":"But the landlady only listened with half an ear, having troubles like himself.","zh":"但是女店家只用一只耳朵听：她像他一样，也有苦恼，因为勒乐先生的 “利商车行”，最近终于开张了。伊韦尔在办货方面，卓有声誉，要求加薪，还威胁她，要加入“对方”。","scope":"group"},{"en":"For Lheureux had at last established the “Favorites du Commerce,” and Hivert, who enjoyed a great reputation for doing errands, insisted on a rise of wages, and was threatening to go over “to the opposition shop.”","zh":"但是女店家只用一只耳朵听：她像他一样，也有苦恼，因为勒乐先生的 “利商车行”，最近终于开张了。伊韦尔在办货方面，卓有声誉，要求加薪，还威胁她，要加入“对方”。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"One day when he had gone to the market at Argueil to sell his horse—his last resource—he met Rodolphe.","sentences":[{"en":"One day when he had gone to the market at Argueil to sell his horse—his last resource—he met Rodolphe.","zh":"有一天，他到阿格伊市场，去卖他的马——他最后的财路，遇见罗道耳弗。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"They both turned pale when they caught sight of one another. Rodolphe, who had only sent his card, first stammered some apologies, then grew bolder, and even pushed his assurance (it was in the month of August and very hot) to the length of inviting him to have a bottle of beer at the public-house.","sentences":[{"en":"They both turned pale when they caught sight of one another.","zh":"狭路相逢，两个人脸全白了。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rodolphe, who had only sent his card, first stammered some apologies, then grew bolder, and even pushed his assurance (it was in the month of August and very hot) to the length of inviting him to have a bottle of beer at the public-house.","zh":"爱玛出殡的时候，罗道耳弗仅仅送去他的名片，所以一见之下，就期期艾艾先表歉意，随后有了胆量，居然请他（正当八月，天气炎热）到酒馆去喝一瓶啤酒。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Leaning on the table opposite him, he chewed his cigar as he talked, and Charles was lost in reverie at this face that she had loved. He seemed to see again something of her in it. It was a marvel to him. He would have liked to have been this man.","sentences":[{"en":"Leaning on the table opposite him, he chewed his cigar as he talked, and Charles was lost in reverie at this face that she had loved.","zh":"他靠住桌子，边说，边嚼他的雪茄；查理坐在她爱过的这张脸对面，出神遐想。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He seemed to see again something of her in it.","zh":"他觉得像又见到她的什么东西一样。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"It was a marvel to him.","zh":"实在意想不到。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He would have liked to have been this man.","zh":"他真想做罗道耳弗。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The other went on talking agriculture, cattle, pasturage, filling out with banal phrases all the gaps where an allusion might slip in. Charles was not listening to him; Rodolphe noticed it, and he followed the succession of memories that crossed his face. This gradually grew redder; the nostrils throbbed fast, the lips quivered. There was at last a moment when Charles, full of a sombre fury, fixed his eyes on Rodolphe, who, in something of fear, stopped talking. But soon the same look of weary lassitude came back to his face.","sentences":[{"en":"The other went on talking agriculture, cattle, pasturage, filling out with banal phrases all the gaps where an allusion might slip in.","zh":"另一位继续闲谈庄稼、牲畜、肥料，看见谈话有了间隙，唯恐对方提起隐情，赶紧找无聊的话来堵塞。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Charles was not listening to him; Rodolphe noticed it, and he followed the succession of memories that crossed his face.","zh":"查理并没有听他说话；罗道耳弗也觉出来了，单从他脸色的变化，就看出回忆正在掠过。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"This gradually grew redder; the nostrils throbbed fast, the lips quivered.","zh":"查理渐渐脸红了，鼻孔抖动，嘴唇哆嗦，甚至有一阵，气愤填胸，死盯着罗道耳弗看。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"There was at last a moment when Charles, full of a sombre fury, fixed his eyes on Rodolphe, who, in something of fear, stopped talking.","zh":"罗道耳弗似乎感到恐怖，话也中断了。但是没有多久，查理脸上又显出原先那种凄惨的无精打采的神情。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"But soon the same look of weary lassitude came back to his face.","zh":"他说：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“I don’t blame you,” he said.","sentences":[{"en":"“I don’t blame you,” he said.","zh":"“我不生您的气。”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe was dumb. And Charles, his head in his hands, went on in a broken voice, and with the resigned accent of infinite sorrow—","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe was dumb.","zh":"罗道耳弗默不作声。查理两手抱住头，好像无限的痛苦全都咽下去了一样，奄奄一息，低声道：","scope":"group"},{"en":"And Charles, his head in his hands, went on in a broken voice, and with the resigned accent of infinite sorrow—","zh":"罗道耳弗默不作声。查理两手抱住头，好像无限的痛苦全都咽下去了一样，奄奄一息，低声道：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“No, I don’t blame you now.”","sentences":[{"en":"“No, I don’t blame you now.”","zh":"“是啊，我不再生您的气啦！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"He even added a fine phrase, the only one he ever made—","sentences":[{"en":"He even added a fine phrase, the only one he ever made—","zh":"他甚至于添上一句伟大的话，有生以来，他说过的唯一伟大的话：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"“It is the fault of fatality!”","sentences":[{"en":"“It is the fault of fatality!”","zh":"他甚至于添上一句伟大的话，有生以来，他说过的唯一伟大的话：","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"Rodolphe, who had managed the fatality, thought the remark very offhand from a man in his position, comic even, and a little mean.","sentences":[{"en":"Rodolphe, who had managed the fatality, thought the remark very offhand from a man in his position, comic even, and a little mean.","zh":"“错的是命！”罗道耳弗，作为支配这一命运的人，觉得一个人处在查理这种地位，说这种话，未免过于宽厚，简直可笑，甚至有点下贱。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"The next day Charles went to sit down on the seat in the arbour. Rays of light were straying through the trellis, the vine leaves threw their shadows on the sand, the jasmines perfumed the air, the heavens were blue, Spanish flies buzzed round the lilies in bloom, and Charles was suffocating like a youth beneath the vague love influences that filled his aching heart.","sentences":[{"en":"The next day Charles went to sit down on the seat in the arbour.","zh":"第二天，查理坐到花棚底下的长凳上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"Rays of light were straying through the trellis, the vine leaves threw their shadows on the sand, the jasmines perfumed the air, the heavens were blue, Spanish flies buzzed round the lilies in bloom, and Charles was suffocating like a youth beneath the vague love influences that filled his aching heart.","zh":"阳光从空格进来；葡萄叶的影子映在沙地；素馨花芬芳扑鼻；天是蓝的；斑蝥环绕开花的百合嗡嗡地飞。查理觉得气闷，仿佛一个年轻人，心里迷迷茫茫，涨满了爱情的潮汐。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"At seven o’clock little Berthe, who had not seen him all the afternoon, went to fetch him to dinner.","sentences":[{"en":"At seven o’clock little Berthe, who had not seen him all the afternoon, went to fetch him to dinner.","zh":"小白尔特一下午没有见到他。七点钟找他去用晚饭。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"His head was thrown back against the wall, his eyes closed, his mouth open, and in his hand was a long tress of black hair.","sentences":[{"en":"His head was thrown back against the wall, his eyes closed, his mouth open, and in his hand was a long tress of black hair.","zh":"他闭住眼睛，张大了嘴，手里拿着一股又黑又长的头发，头仰靠着墙。她道：","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"“Come along, papa,” she said.","sentences":[{"en":"“Come along, papa,” she said.","zh":"“爸爸，你倒是来呀！”","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"And thinking he wanted to play; she pushed him gently. He fell to the ground. He was dead.","sentences":[{"en":"And thinking he wanted to play; she pushed him gently.","zh":"她以为他在逗她玩耍，轻轻推了他一下。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He fell to the ground.","zh":"他倒在地上。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"He was dead.","zh":"原来是死了。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Thirty-six hours after, at the druggist’s request, Monsieur Canivet came thither. He made a post-mortem and found nothing.","sentences":[{"en":"Thirty-six hours after, at the druggist’s request, Monsieur Canivet came thither.","zh":"三十六小时以后，由于药剂师的要求，卡尼韦先生跑来加以解剖，但是什么也检验不出。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He made a post-mortem and found nothing.","zh":"三十六小时以后，由于药剂师的要求，卡尼韦先生跑来加以解剖，但是什么也检验不出。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"When everything had been sold, twelve francs seventy-five centimes remained, that served to pay for Mademoiselle Bovary’s going to her grandmother. The good woman died the same year; old Rouault was paralysed, and it was an aunt who took charge of her. She is poor, and sends her to a cotton-factory to earn a living.","sentences":[{"en":"When everything had been sold, twelve francs seventy-five centimes remained, that served to pay for Mademoiselle Bovary’s going to her grandmother.","zh":"全部什物出卖，只有十二法郎七十五生丁剩下来，留给包法利小姐投奔祖母一路使用。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"The good woman died the same year; old Rouault was paralysed, and it was an aunt who took charge of her.","zh":"老太太当年去世；卢欧老爹瘫了，一个远房姨母把她收养下来。","scope":"sentence"},{"en":"She is poor, and sends her to a cotton-factory to earn a living.","zh":"姨母家道贫寒，为了谋生，如今把她送进一家纱厂。","scope":"sentence"}]},{"en":"Since Bovary’s death three doctors have followed one another at Yonville without any success, so severely did Homais attack them. He has an enormous practice; the authorities treat him with consideration, and public opinion protects him.","sentences":[{"en":"Since Bovary’s death three doctors have followed one another at Yonville without any success, so severely did Homais attack them.","zh":"自从包法利死后，一连有三个医生在永镇开业，但是经不起郝麦拼命排挤，没有一个站住了脚。他的主顾多得不得了。","scope":"group"},{"en":"He has an enormous practice; the authorities treat him with consideration, and public opinion protects him.","zh":"自从包法利死后，一连有三个医生在永镇开业，但是经不起郝麦拼命排挤，没有一个站住了脚。他的主顾多得不得了。","scope":"group"}]},{"en":"He has just received the cross of the Legion of Honour.","sentences":[{"en":"He has just received the cross of the Legion of Honour.","zh":"官方宽容他，舆论保护他。他新近得到十字勋章。","scope":"sentence"}]}]}]};
